-- ====================================================================================================
-- seat questions from part coa1 (merged by the lead on 2026-11-12; unchanged text follows)
-- ====================================================================================================
-- Companies Act 2006 (United Kingdom), Parts 2 to 4 (ss 7 to 52) -- THE SEAT LAYER (coa1).
--
-- SEAT: an individual who is, or is about to become, a director, a company secretary or a member (shareholder) of a company
-- registered under the Act, or who deals with one, asking, on facts they can state, what the Act requires or lets them do, what rights
-- they have against the company or its directors, what they must disclose, file, approve or vote on and by when, and what follows
-- (liability, offences, penalties) if it is not done. (Assumed, not ruled: the Act is addressed to companies, so the individual is
-- whoever stands in a company's management or ownership.)
--
-- This layer phrases the rules of coa1-part2-formation.l4, coa1-part3-constitution.l4 and coa1-part4-capacity.l4 as questions that
-- person asks. Nothing here is new law: each question calls the module rule that carries the section's name and never restates it.
--
-- PLAIN INPUTS. Every question takes plain inputs (yes/no, a number, a date, a choice from a list), one per fact the person can state,
-- each with an @desc worded as that person is asked. The rules' own MAYBE inputs for answers that other parts of the Act or other
-- Acts give (whether a document is "authenticated" under s 1146, whether an officer "is in default" under s 1121, whether an individual's
-- identity "is verified" under s 1110A, whether a person is "connected with" a director under Part 10, whether a resolution "is a special
-- resolution" under s 283) are built here from a yes/no answer (JUST TRUE or JUST FALSE): the person states the fact, and the borrowed
-- definition is not worked out here. The pounds that "level 3 on the standard scale" stands for are not in the Act: they are an input.
-- A record field that no rule reads gets a fixed placeholder, with a comment saying so.
--
-- HOW TO READ AN ANSWER. Every question that returns a MAYBE BOOLEAN answers
--   JUST TRUE   the Act says yes, on these facts;
--   JUST FALSE  the Act says no, on these facts, in its own words (see NOTES.md, Reading a result: FALSE and NOTHING);
--   NOTHING     the Act does not decide this case ("not covered"); NEVER read it as "no".
-- There is no seat for an official: provisions that address only the registrar or a court appear here only as what they mean to
-- the individual (what may be done to them, what they must be given, and by when).
-- Every question name begins "Under section N,", with the Act's own numbering, so that no two parts' questions can share a name.

§ `Companies Act 2006, Parts 2 to 4: the questions of a director, secretary, member or person dealing with a company`

§§ `Part 2 -- Forming a company (ss 7 to 16). These questions arise only if you are forming a company or are a subscriber or proposed officer of one`

@export Under section 7(1), is the company formed under this Act (ss 7(1), 8, 9 to 13)?
GIVEN `how many persons are subscribing their names` IS A NUMBER @desc How many persons are subscribing their names to the memorandum of association?
      `we subscribed our names to a memorandum` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Have the subscribers subscribed their names to a memorandum of association?
      `we complied with the registration requirements` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Have the requirements of the Act as to registration (sections 9 to 13) been complied with?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 7(1), is the company formed under this Act` IS
    `s 7(1) the company is formed under this Act` `how many persons are subscribing their names` `we subscribed our names to a memorandum` `we complied with the registration requirements`

@export Under section 7(2), may we form the company for this purpose (s 7(2))?
GIVEN `the purpose is unlawful` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the purpose for which the company is to be formed unlawful?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 7(2), may we form the company for this purpose` IS
    `s 7(2) the company may be formed for the purpose` `the purpose is unlawful`

@export Under section 8(1), is our document a memorandum of association (s 8(1))?
GIVEN `it states that the subscribers wish to form a company under this Act` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does the document state that the subscribers wish to form a company under this Act?
      `it states that the subscribers agree to become members` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does the document state that the subscribers agree to become members of the company?
      `the company is to have a share capital` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the company to have a share capital?
      `it states that each subscriber agrees to take at least one share` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does the document state that each subscriber agrees to take at least one share? (Answer false if the company is not to have a share capital and the document says nothing about shares.)
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 8(1), is our document a memorandum of association` IS
    `s 8(1) the document is a memorandum of association` `it states that the subscribers wish to form a company under this Act` `it states that the subscribers agree to become members` `the company is to have a share capital` `it states that each subscriber agrees to take at least one share`

@export Under section 8(2), does our memorandum meet the requirements as to form and authentication (s 8(2))?
GIVEN `it is in the prescribed form` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the memorandum in the form prescribed?
      `every subscriber has authenticated it` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has each subscriber authenticated the memorandum?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 8(2), does our memorandum meet the requirements as to form and authentication` IS
    `s 8(2) the memorandum meets the requirements as to form and authentication` `it is in the prescribed form` (JUST `every subscriber has authenticated it`)

@export Under section 9(1), have we delivered to the registrar everything the section requires (s 9(1))?
GIVEN `the memorandum is delivered` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the memorandum of association delivered to the registrar?
      `with an application for registration` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is an application for registration of the company delivered with it?
      `with the documents the section requires` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are the documents required by section 9 delivered with it?
      `with a statement of compliance` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is a statement of compliance delivered with it?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 9(1), have we delivered to the registrar everything the section requires` IS
    `s 9(1) the delivery includes what the section requires` `the memorandum is delivered` `with an application for registration` `with the documents the section requires` `with a statement of compliance`

@export Under section 9(2), does our application state what it must (s 9(2))?
GIVEN `it states the proposed name` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does the application state the company's proposed name?
      `it states where the registered office is to be` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does the application state whether the registered office is to be in England and Wales (or in Wales), in Scotland or in Northern Ireland?
      `it states the limit on members' liability` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does the application state whether the members' liability is to be limited and, if so, whether by shares or by guarantee?
      `it states private or public` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does the application state whether the company is to be a private or a public company?
      `it states the lawful purposes` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does the application state that the subscribers wish to form the company for lawful purposes?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 9(2), does our application state what it must` IS
    `s 9(2) the application states what it must` `it states the proposed name` `it states where the registered office is to be` `it states the limit on members' liability` `it states private or public` `it states the lawful purposes`

@export Under section 9(3), does our application give the agent's name and address as required (s 9(3))?
GIVEN `an agent delivers it for the subscribers` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the application delivered by a person as agent for the subscribers?
      `it states the agent's name and address` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does the application state the agent's name and address?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 9(3), does our application give the agent's name and address as required` IS
    `s 9(3) the application states the agent's name and address as required` `an agent delivers it for the subscribers` `it states the agent's name and address`

@export Under section 9(3A), does our application contain the statements about the subscribers it must contain (s 9(3A))?
GIVEN `it contains the required information about each subscriber` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does the application contain a statement of the required information about each of the subscribers (section 9A)?
      `it contains the no-disqualification statement` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does the application contain a statement that none of the subscribers is disqualified under the directors disqualification legislation?
      `a subscriber is disqualified but for a court's permission` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Would any subscriber be disqualified but for the permission of a court to act?
      `it states the court permission details` IS A BOOLEAN @desc If so, does the application say so for each of them, giving the subscriber's name, the court that gave permission and the date it was given?
      `a subscriber is disqualified but for a licence` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Would any subscriber be disqualified as a designated person under sanctions legislation but for the authority of a licence?
      `it states the licence details` IS A BOOLEAN @desc If so, does the application say so for each of them, giving the subscriber's name, the date the licence was issued and by whom?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 9(3A), does our application contain the statements about the subscribers it must contain` IS
    `s 9(3A) the application contains the statements it must` `it contains the required information about each subscriber` `it contains the no-disqualification statement` `a subscriber is disqualified but for a court's permission` `it states the court permission details` `a subscriber is disqualified but for a licence` `it states the licence details`

@export Under section 9(4), does our application contain the statements of capital, guarantee, officers and significant control it must (s 9(4))?
GIVEN `the company is to have a share capital` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the company to have a share capital?
      `it contains a statement of capital and initial shareholdings` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does the application contain a statement of capital and initial shareholdings?
      `the company is to be limited by guarantee` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the company to be limited by guarantee?
      `it contains a statement of guarantee` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does the application contain a statement of guarantee?
      `it contains a statement of proposed officers` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does the application contain a statement of the company's proposed officers?
      `it contains a statement of initial significant control` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does the application contain a statement of initial significant control?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 9(4), does our application contain the statements of capital, guarantee, officers and significant control it must` IS
    `s 9(4) the application contains the statements it must` `the company is to have a share capital` `it contains a statement of capital and initial shareholdings` `the company is to be limited by guarantee` `it contains a statement of guarantee` `it contains a statement of proposed officers` `it contains a statement of initial significant control`

@export Under section 9(5), does our application contain the registered office, email, articles and company-type statements it must (s 9(5))?
GIVEN `it states the intended registered office address` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does the application state the intended address of the company's registered office?
      `the address is an appropriate address` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is that address an appropriate address (section 86(2))?
      `it states the intended registered email address` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does the application state the intended registered email address of the company?
      `the email address is an appropriate email address` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is that an appropriate email address (section 88A(2))?
      `we propose articles beyond the model articles` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are you proposing articles of association that go beyond what the default model articles supply?
      `it contains a copy of the proposed articles` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does the application contain a copy of the proposed articles of association?
      `it states the type of company and principal business activities` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does the application state the type of company and its intended principal business activities?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 9(5), does our application contain the registered office, email, articles and company-type statements it must` IS
    `s 9(5) the application contains what it must also contain` `it states the intended registered office address` (JUST `the address is an appropriate address`) `it states the intended registered email address` (JUST `the email address is an appropriate email address`) `we propose articles beyond the model articles` `it contains a copy of the proposed articles` `it states the type of company and principal business activities`

@export Under section 9(6), which registrar must we deliver our application to (s 9(6))?
GIVEN `the registered office is to be in` IS A `Place of registration` @desc Where is the registered office to be situated? One of: England and Wales, Scotland, Northern Ireland.
GIVETH A STRING
DECIDE `Under section 9(6), which registrar must we deliver our application to` IS
    `s 9(6) the registrar to whom the application must be delivered` `the registered office is to be in`

@export Under section 9A, what information must we give about a subscriber (ss 9A(1), 9A(2))?
GIVEN `the subscriber is` IS A `Kind of person` @desc What is the subscriber? One of: an individual; a company registered under the Companies Act 2006; another body corporate incorporated in the United Kingdom; a body corporate incorporated outside the United Kingdom; a corporation sole; a partnership; an unincorporated association.
      `the subscriber is a firm that is a legal person` IS A BOOLEAN @desc If the subscriber is a firm (a partnership or other unincorporated association, or a corporation sole), is it a legal person under the law by which it is governed?
GIVETH A MAYBE (LIST OF `s 9A item of required information`)
DECIDE `Under section 9A, what information must we give about a subscriber` IS
    `s 9A(1) the required information about a subscriber` `the subscriber is` `the subscriber is a firm that is a legal person`

@export Under section 9A(4), is the name we give for a subscriber acceptable (s 9A(3), (4))?
GIVEN `the subscriber is a peer or usually known by a title` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the subscriber a peer, or an individual usually known by a title?
      `the name we state` IS A STRING @desc What name do you state in the application for the subscriber?
      `the forename` IS A STRING @desc What is the subscriber's forename?
      `the surname` IS A STRING @desc What is the subscriber's surname?
      `the title` IS A STRING @desc What is the title the subscriber is usually known by? (Any text if the subscriber is not known by a title.)
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 9A(4), is the name we give for a subscriber acceptable` IS
    `s 9A(4) the name stated for the subscriber is acceptable` `the subscriber is a peer or usually known by a title` `the name we state` `the forename` `the surname` `the title`

@export Under section 10(2), does our statement of capital and initial shareholdings state what it must (s 10(2))?
GIVEN `it states the total number of shares taken on formation` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does the statement state the total number of shares of the company to be taken on formation by the subscribers?
      `it states the aggregate nominal value` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does it state the aggregate nominal value of those shares?
      `it states the aggregate amount to be unpaid` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does it state the aggregate amount (if any) to be unpaid on those shares?
      `for every class it states the rights` IS A BOOLEAN @desc For every class of shares, does it state the prescribed particulars of the rights attached to the shares?
      `for every class it states the number of shares` IS A BOOLEAN @desc For every class of shares, does it state the total number of shares of that class?
      `for every class it states the nominal value` IS A BOOLEAN @desc For every class of shares, does it state the aggregate nominal value of shares of that class?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 10(2), does our statement of capital and initial shareholdings state what it must` IS
    `s 10(2) the statement of capital states what it must` `it states the total number of shares taken on formation` `it states the aggregate nominal value` `it states the aggregate amount to be unpaid` (LIST `s 10(2)(c) statement for a class of shares` OF `for every class it states the rights`, `for every class it states the number of shares`, `for every class it states the nominal value`)
    -- One record stands for "every class": a fact stated for every class is the same fact for each, and the rule asks it of each class in the list.

@export Under section 10(4), does our statement state what it must for each subscriber (s 10(4), (5))?
GIVEN `for each class a subscriber takes it states the number` IS A BOOLEAN @desc For each class of shares a subscriber is to take, does the statement state the number of shares to be taken by that subscriber on formation?
      `for each class it states the nominal value of each share` IS A BOOLEAN @desc For each such class, does it state the nominal value of each share?
      `for each class it states the class` IS A BOOLEAN @desc For each such class, does it state the class of the shares?
      `it states what is paid up and unpaid` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does it state the amount to be paid up and the amount (if any) to be unpaid on each share?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 10(4), does our statement state what it must for each subscriber` IS
    `s 10(4) the statement states what it must for the subscriber` (LIST `s 10(4)(a) statement for a class of shares taken by a subscriber` OF `for each class a subscriber takes it states the number`, `for each class it states the nominal value of each share`, `for each class it states the class`) `it states what is paid up and unpaid`

@export Under section 10(5), is the share information given for each class a subscriber takes (s 10(5))?
GIVEN `classes the subscriber takes` IS A NUMBER @desc How many classes of shares is the subscriber to take?
      `classes for which the information is given` IS A NUMBER @desc For how many of those classes does the statement give the number, nominal value and class of shares?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 10(5), is the share information given for each class a subscriber takes` IS
    `s 10(5) the information is given for each class` `classes the subscriber takes` `classes for which the information is given`

@export Under section 11(3), does our statement of guarantee state what it must (ss 11(2), 11(3))?
GIVEN `it states that each member undertakes to contribute` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does the statement say that each member undertakes to contribute to the assets of the company if it is wound up while he is a member, or within one year after he ceases to be a member?
      `it says the contribution is for debts` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does it say the contribution is for payment of the debts and liabilities of the company contracted before he ceases to be a member?
      `it says the contribution is for winding-up costs` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does it say the contribution is for the costs, charges and expenses of winding up?
      `it says the contribution is for adjusting the contributories' rights` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does it say the contribution is for adjustment of the rights of the contributories among themselves?
      `it states a specified amount` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does it state a specified amount that the contribution must not exceed?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 11(3), does our statement of guarantee state what it must` IS
    `s 11(3) the statement of guarantee states what it must` `it states that each member undertakes to contribute` `it says the contribution is for debts` `it says the contribution is for winding-up costs` `it says the contribution is for adjusting the contributories' rights` `it states a specified amount`

@export Under section 11(3), does a member's guarantee undertaking apply to me if the company is wound up (s 11(3))?
GIVEN `the company is wound up while I am a member` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the company wound up while you are a member?
      `I have ceased to be a member` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Have you ceased to be a member?
      `the date I ceased to be a member` IS A DATE @desc On what date did you cease to be a member? (Any date if you have not ceased.)
      `the date the winding up began` IS A DATE @desc On what date did the winding up of the company begin?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 11(3), does a member's guarantee undertaking apply to me if the company is wound up` IS
    `s 11(3) the undertaking applies to the member` (IF `I have ceased to be a member` THEN JUST `the date I ceased to be a member` ELSE NOTHING) `the date the winding up began` `the company is wound up while I am a member`

@export Under section 11(3), what is the most I can be required to contribute on a winding up, in pounds (s 11(3))?
GIVEN `the undertaking applies to me` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does the undertaking apply to you (the company is wound up while you are a member, or within one year after you cease to be one)?
      `debts contracted before I ceased to be a member` IS A NUMBER @desc How many pounds are the debts and liabilities of the company contracted before you ceased to be a member?
      `costs of winding up` IS A NUMBER @desc How many pounds are the costs, charges and expenses of winding up?
      `adjustment among contributories` IS A NUMBER @desc How many pounds are needed for adjustment of the rights of the contributories among themselves?
      `the specified amount` IS A NUMBER @desc What is the specified amount, in pounds, that your contribution cannot exceed, as stated in the company's statement of guarantee?
GIVETH A MAYBE NUMBER
DECIDE `Under section 11(3), what is the most I can be required to contribute on a winding up, in pounds` IS
    `s 11(3) the most the member can be required to contribute, in pounds` `the undertaking applies to me` `debts contracted before I ceased to be a member` `costs of winding up` `adjustment among contributories` `the specified amount`

@export Under section 12(1), does our statement of proposed officers contain the required information about the first officers (s 12(1))?
GIVEN `it contains the required information about the first director or directors` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does the statement contain the required information about the person or persons to be the first director or directors?
      `the company is to be a public company` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the company to be a public company?
      `a first secretary is proposed` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is a person (or are persons) proposed as the first secretary (or joint secretaries)?
      `it contains the required information about the first secretary` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does the statement contain the required information about the first secretary (or joint secretaries)?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 12(1), does our statement of proposed officers contain the required information about the first officers` IS
    `s 12(1) the statement contains the required information about the first officers` `it contains the required information about the first director or directors` `the company is to be a public company` `a first secretary is proposed` `it contains the required information about the first secretary`

@export Under section 12(2A), does our statement confirm that each individual named as a director has a verified identity (s 12(2A))?
GIVEN `the statement confirms identity is verified` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does the statement confirm, for each individual named as a director, that the individual's identity is verified?
      `the identity is in fact verified` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the individual's identity in fact verified (section 1110A)?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 12(2A), does our statement confirm that each individual named as a director has a verified identity` IS
    `s 12(2A) the statement confirms that an individual named as a director has a verified identity` `the statement confirms identity is verified` (JUST `the identity is in fact verified`)

@export Under section 12(3), does our statement include the subscribers' statement that each proposed officer has consented to act (s 12(3))?
GIVEN `it includes the subscribers' statement of consent` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does the statement include a statement by the subscribers that each person named as a director, as secretary or as one of the joint secretaries has consented to act in that capacity?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 12(3), does our statement include the subscribers' statement that each proposed officer has consented to act` IS
    `s 12(3) the statement includes the subscribers' statement of consent to act` `it includes the subscribers' statement of consent`

@export Under section 12(4), does our statement include the subscribers' statement that no proposed director is disqualified or ineligible (s 12(4))?
GIVEN `it states no one named as a director is disqualified` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does the statement include a statement by the subscribers that no one named as a director is disqualified under the directors disqualification legislation?
      `it states no one named as a director is otherwise ineligible` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does it also state that no one named as a director is otherwise ineligible by virtue of any enactment for appointment as a director?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 12(4), does our statement include the subscribers' statement that no proposed director is disqualified or ineligible` IS
    `s 12(4) the statement includes the subscribers' statement of no disqualification or ineligibility` `it states no one named as a director is disqualified` `it states no one named as a director is otherwise ineligible`

@export Under section 12A(1), does our statement of initial significant control state what it must (s 12A(1))?
GIVEN `there will be a registrable person or entity on incorporation` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Will there be anyone who is a registrable person or a registrable relevant legal entity in relation to the company on incorporation (section 790C)?
      `it states whether there will be one` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does the statement state whether, on incorporation, there will be anyone who is a registrable person or a registrable relevant legal entity?
      `it includes the required particulars` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does the statement include the required particulars (section 790K) of each such person?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 12A(1), does our statement of initial significant control state what it must` IS
    `s 12A(1) the statement of initial significant control states what it must` (JUST `there will be a registrable person or entity on incorporation`) `it states whether there will be one` `it includes the required particulars`

@export Under section 12A(1A), does our statement include the further statements it must where there is a registrable person (s 12A(1A))?
GIVEN `there will be a registrable person or entity on incorporation` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Will there be anyone who is a registrable person or a registrable relevant legal entity in relation to the company on incorporation (section 790C)?
      `it includes the statement that none is disqualified` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does the statement include a statement that none of them is disqualified under the directors disqualification legislation?
      `one is disqualified but for a court's permission` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Would any of them be disqualified but for the permission of a court to act?
      `it states the court permission details` IS A BOOLEAN @desc If so, does the statement say so for each of them, giving the person's name, the court that gave permission and the date it was given?
      `one is disqualified but for a licence` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Would any of them be disqualified as a designated person under sanctions legislation but for the authority of a licence?
      `it states the licence details` IS A BOOLEAN @desc If so, does the statement say so for each of them, giving the person's name, the date the licence was issued and by whom?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 12A(1A), does our statement include the further statements it must where there is a registrable person` IS
    `s 12A(1A) the statement includes what it must where there will be a registrable person` (JUST `there will be a registrable person or entity on incorporation`) `it includes the statement that none is disqualified` `one is disqualified but for a court's permission` `it states the court permission details` `one is disqualified but for a licence` `it states the licence details`

@export Under section 12A(3), does our statement say the particulars of an individual are included with the individual's knowledge (s 12A(3))?
GIVEN `it includes required particulars of an individual` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does the statement include required particulars of an individual?
      `it contains the statement of knowledge` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does the statement contain a statement that those particulars are included with the knowledge of that individual?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 12A(3), does our statement say the particulars of an individual are included with the individual's knowledge` IS
    `s 12A(3) the statement contains the statement that the particulars are included with the individual's knowledge` `it includes required particulars of an individual` `it contains the statement of knowledge`

@export Under section 12B(2), may our statement include a statement that a registrable person's identity is verified (ss 12B(1), 12B(2))?
GIVEN `the application contains a statement of initial significant control identifying a registrable person` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does the application contain a statement of initial significant control that identifies a person who will be a registrable person, or a registrable relevant legal entity, on incorporation?
      `the person will be a registrable person` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Will the person in question be a registrable person (section 790C)?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 12B(2), may our statement include a statement that a registrable person's identity is verified` IS
    `s 12B(2) the statement may include a statement that the person's identity is verified` (`s 12B(1) this section applies` `the application contains a statement of initial significant control identifying a registrable person`) (JUST `the person will be a registrable person`)

@export Under section 12B(4), is our application accompanied by the individual's confirmation that they are a relevant officer (s 12B(4))?
GIVEN `we include a statement under section 12B(3)` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is a statement under section 12B(3) (naming a relevant officer whose identity is verified) included for a registrable relevant legal entity?
      `the application comes with the individual's confirmation` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the application accompanied by a statement by the individual confirming that the individual is a relevant officer of that entity?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 12B(4), is our application accompanied by the individual's confirmation that they are a relevant officer` IS
    `s 12B(4) the application is accompanied by the individual's confirmation` `we include a statement under section 12B(3)` `the application comes with the individual's confirmation`

@export Under section 13(2), may the registrar accept our statement of compliance as sufficient evidence that the registration requirements are met (ss 13(1), 13(2))?
GIVEN `it states the requirements as to registration have been complied with` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does the document state that the requirements of the Act as to registration have been complied with?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 13(2), may the registrar accept our statement of compliance as sufficient evidence that the registration requirements are met` IS
    `s 13(2) the registrar may accept the statement of compliance as sufficient evidence of compliance` (`s 13(1) the document is a statement of compliance` `it states the requirements as to registration have been complied with`)

@export Under section 14, must the registrar register the documents we delivered (s 14)?
GIVEN `the registrar is satisfied` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the registrar satisfied that the requirements of the Act as to registration are complied with?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 14, must the registrar register the documents we delivered` IS
    `s 14 the registrar shall register the documents delivered` `the registrar is satisfied`

@export Under section 15(1), must the registrar give us a certificate that the company is incorporated (s 15(1))?
GIVEN `the company has been registered` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has the company been registered?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 15(1), must the registrar give us a certificate that the company is incorporated` IS
    `s 15(1) the registrar shall give a certificate that the company is incorporated` `the company has been registered`

@export Under section 15(2), what must our certificate of incorporation say about our members' liability (s 15(2)(c))?
GIVEN `how the members' liability is limited` IS A `Liability of members` @desc How is the members' liability limited? One of: liability not limited; liability limited to the amount, if any, unpaid on the shares held; liability limited to the amount the members undertake to contribute on a winding up; liability limited in some other way by the constitution.
GIVETH A MAYBE `s 15(2)(c) what the certificate must state about the liability of the members`
DECIDE `Under section 15(2), what must our certificate of incorporation say about our members' liability` IS
    `s 15(2)(c) what the certificate must state about the liability of the members` profile
    WHERE
        -- Placeholder fields: the rule reads only the liability of the members.
        profile MEANS `Company profile` WITH
            `place of registration` IS `England and Wales`
            `liability of the members` IS `how the members' liability is limited`
            `a share capital` IS FALSE
            `certificate of incorporation stating that it is a public company` IS FALSE

@export Under section 15(2), does our certificate of incorporation state what it must (s 15(2))?
GIVEN `it states the name and registered number` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does the certificate state the name and registered number of the company?
      `it states the date of incorporation` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does it state the date of incorporation?
      `it states limited or unlimited` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does it state whether the company is a limited or unlimited company?
      `it states by shares or by guarantee` IS A BOOLEAN @desc If the company is limited, does it state whether it is limited by shares or by guarantee?
      `it states private or public` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does it state whether the company is a private or a public company?
      `it states where the registered office is` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does it state whether the registered office is situated in England and Wales (or in Wales), in Scotland or in Northern Ireland?
      `how the members' liability is limited` IS A `Liability of members` @desc How is the members' liability limited? One of: liability not limited; liability limited to the amount, if any, unpaid on the shares held; liability limited to the amount the members undertake to contribute on a winding up; liability limited in some other way by the constitution.
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 15(2), does our certificate of incorporation state what it must` IS
    `s 15(2) the certificate states what it must` `it states the name and registered number` `it states the date of incorporation` `it states limited or unlimited` `it states by shares or by guarantee` `it states private or public` `it states where the registered office is` `how the members' liability is limited`

@export Under section 15(3), is our certificate of incorporation signed or sealed as required (s 15(3))?
GIVEN `the registrar signed it` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the certificate signed by the registrar?
      `it bears the registrar's official seal` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does the certificate bear the registrar's official seal?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 15(3), is our certificate of incorporation signed or sealed as required` IS
    `s 15(3) the certificate is signed or authenticated as required` `the registrar signed it` (JUST `it bears the registrar's official seal`)

@export Under section 15(4), is our certificate conclusive evidence that the company is duly registered (s 15(4))?
GIVEN `a certificate of incorporation has been issued` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has a certificate of incorporation been issued?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 15(4), is our certificate conclusive evidence that the company is duly registered` IS
    `s 15(4) the certificate is conclusive evidence that the requirements as to registration have been complied with and that the company is duly registered` `a certificate of incorporation has been issued`

@export Under section 16(1), have the effects of registration begun on this date (s 16(1))?
GIVEN `the date of incorporation` IS A DATE @desc What is the date of incorporation stated in the certificate?
      `the date in question` IS A DATE @desc For which date are you asking?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 16(1), have the effects of registration begun on this date` IS
    `s 16(1) the effects of registration have begun on the date` `the date of incorporation` `the date in question`

@export Under section 16(2), am I one of the body corporate that registration creates (s 16(2))?
GIVEN `the date of incorporation` IS A DATE @desc What is the date of incorporation stated in the certificate?
      `the date in question` IS A DATE @desc For which date are you asking?
      `I am a subscriber to the memorandum` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are you a subscriber to the memorandum?
      `I am a member of the company` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are you a member of the company (section 112)?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 16(2), am I one of the body corporate that registration creates` IS
    `s 16(2) the person is one of those who are the body corporate` (`s 16(1) the effects of registration have begun on the date` `the date of incorporation` `the date in question` EQUALS JUST TRUE) `I am a subscriber to the memorandum` (JUST `I am a member of the company`)

@export Under section 16(5), how many shares do I hold on registration as a subscriber (s 16(5))?
GIVEN `registration has taken effect` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has registration taken effect (is the date on or after the date of incorporation)?
      `the company has a share capital` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does the company have a share capital?
      `shares specified for me` IS A NUMBER @desc How many shares are specified for you in the statement of capital and initial shareholdings?
GIVETH A MAYBE NUMBER
DECIDE `Under section 16(5), how many shares do I hold on registration as a subscriber` IS
    `s 16(5) the number of shares the subscriber holds on registration` `registration has taken effect` `the company has a share capital` `shares specified for me`

@export Under section 16(6), am I deemed to have been appointed to the office I am named for on registration (s 16(6))?
GIVEN `registration has taken effect` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has registration taken effect (is the date on or after the date of incorporation)?
      `I am named in the statement of proposed officers` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are you named in the statement of proposed officers as director, or as secretary or joint secretary?
      `I am ineligible for the office` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are you ineligible for appointment to that office by virtue of any enactment?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 16(6), am I deemed to have been appointed to the office I am named for on registration` IS
    `s 16(6) the person is deemed to have been appointed to the office` `registration has taken effect` `I am named in the statement of proposed officers` `I am ineligible for the office`

§§ `Part 3 -- The company's constitution (ss 17 to 38)`

@export Under section 17, is this document part of the company's constitution (s 17)?
GIVEN `the context otherwise requires` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does the context of the provision you are reading otherwise require a different meaning of "constitution"?
      `it is the company's articles` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the document the company's articles of association?
      `Chapter 3 applies to it` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it a resolution or agreement to which Chapter 3 of Part 3 applies (section 29)?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 17, is this document part of the company's constitution` IS
    `s 17 the document is part of the company's constitution` `the context otherwise requires` `it is the company's articles` (JUST `Chapter 3 applies to it`)

@export Under section 18(2), must our company register articles of association (ss 18(1), 18(2), 20)?
GIVEN `how the members' liability is limited` IS A `Liability of members` @desc How is the members' liability limited? One of: liability not limited; liability limited to the amount, if any, unpaid on the shares held; liability limited to the amount the members undertake to contribute on a winding up; liability limited in some other way by the constitution.
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 18(2), must our company register articles of association` IS
    `s 18(2) the company must register articles of association` `how the members' liability is limited`

@export Under section 18(3), do our registered articles meet the requirements as to form (s 18(3))?
GIVEN `they are in a single document` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are the registered articles contained in a single document?
      `they are in numbered paragraphs` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are they divided into paragraphs numbered consecutively?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 18(3), do our registered articles meet the requirements as to form` IS
    `s 18(3) the registered articles meet the requirements as to form` `they are in a single document` `they are in numbered paragraphs`

@export Under section 20(1), does a provision of the model articles form part of our articles (s 20(1))?
GIVEN `how the members' liability is limited` IS A `Liability of members` @desc How is the members' liability limited? One of: liability not limited; liability limited to the amount, if any, unpaid on the shares held; liability limited to the amount the members undertake to contribute on a winding up; liability limited in some other way by the constitution.
      `we registered articles` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Were articles registered on formation?
      `our articles exclude or modify the provision` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Do the registered articles exclude or modify the provision of the relevant model articles?
      `the provision is applicable to us` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the provision of the model articles applicable to your company?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 20(1), does a provision of the model articles form part of our articles` IS
    `s 20(1) the provision of the relevant model articles forms part of the company's articles` `how the members' liability is limited` `we registered articles` `our articles exclude or modify the provision` `the provision is applicable to us`

@export Under section 21(1), may we amend our articles by this resolution (s 21(1))?
GIVEN `it is a special resolution` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the resolution a special resolution (section 283)?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 21(1), may we amend our articles by this resolution` IS
    `s 21(1) the company may amend its articles by the resolution` (JUST `it is a special resolution`)

@export Under section 21(2), what other enactments limit our power to amend our articles (ss 21(2), 21(3))?
GIVEN `the company is a charity` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the company a charity?
      `it is registered in the Scottish Charity Register` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the company registered in the Scottish Charity Register?
      `the company is registered in` IS A `Place of registration` @desc Where is the company registered? One of: England and Wales, Scotland, Northern Ireland.
GIVETH A LIST OF `s 21 enactment the power to amend is subject to`
DECIDE `Under section 21(2), what other enactments limit our power to amend our articles` IS
    `s 21(2) and (3) the enactments the power to amend articles is subject to` `the company is a charity` `it is registered in the Scottish Charity Register` `the company is registered in`

@export Under section 22(2), may we make provision for entrenchment in this way (s 22(2))?
GIVEN `it is made in the articles on formation` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the provision made in the company's articles on formation?
      `it is made by an amendment agreed to by all the members` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it made by an amendment of the articles agreed to by all the members of the company?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 22(2), may we make provision for entrenchment in this way` IS
    `s 22(2) provision for entrenchment may be made` `it is made in the articles on formation` `it is made by an amendment agreed to by all the members`

@export Under section 22(3), does provision for entrenchment prevent this amendment (s 22(3))?
GIVEN `all the members agree` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the amendment made by agreement of all the members of the company?
      `a court or authority orders it` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it made by order of a court or other authority having power to alter the company's articles?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 22(3), does provision for entrenchment prevent this amendment` IS
    `s 22(3) provision for entrenchment prevents the amendment` `all the members agree` `a court or authority orders it`

@export Under section 23(1), must we give the registrar notice that our articles contain or are restricted by entrenchment (s 23(1))?
GIVEN `our articles on formation contain provision for entrenchment` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Do the articles on formation contain provision for entrenchment?
      `our articles are amended to include provision for entrenchment` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are the articles amended so as to include provision for entrenchment?
      `a court order restricts or excludes our power to amend` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are the articles altered by order of a court or other authority so as to restrict or exclude the company's power to amend its articles?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 23(1), must we give the registrar notice that our articles contain or are restricted by entrenchment` IS
    `s 23(1) the company must give notice to the registrar of the entrenchment or restriction` `our articles on formation contain provision for entrenchment` `our articles are amended to include provision for entrenchment` `a court order restricts or excludes our power to amend`

@export Under section 23(2), must we give the registrar notice that entrenchment or a restriction has been removed (s 23(2))?
GIVEN `our articles are amended to remove entrenchment` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are the articles amended so as to remove provision for entrenchment?
      `a court order removes entrenchment` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are the articles altered by order so as to remove provision for entrenchment?
      `a court order removes another restriction` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are the articles altered by order so as to remove any other restriction on, or exclusion of, the company's power to amend its articles?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 23(2), must we give the registrar notice that entrenchment or a restriction has been removed` IS
    `s 23(2) the company must give notice to the registrar of the removal` `our articles are amended to remove entrenchment` `a court order removes entrenchment` `a court order removes another restriction`

@export Under section 24(2), must we deliver a statement of compliance with the document making the amendment (ss 24(1), 24(2))?
GIVEN `our articles are subject to entrenchment` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are the company's articles subject to provision for entrenchment?
      `our articles are subject to a restricting order` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are they subject to an order of a court or other authority restricting or excluding the company's power to amend them?
      `we amend our articles` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the company amending its articles?
      `we must send the registrar a document evidencing the amendment` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the company required to send the registrar a document making or evidencing the amendment?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 24(2), must we deliver a statement of compliance with the document making the amendment` IS
    `s 24(2) the company must deliver a statement of compliance with the document` (`s 24(1) this section applies` `our articles are subject to entrenchment` `our articles are subject to a restricting order`) `we amend our articles` `we must send the registrar a document evidencing the amendment`

@export Under section 24(3), is our statement the statement of compliance required (s 24(3))?
GIVEN `it certifies the amendment follows our articles` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does the statement certify that the amendment has been made in accordance with the company's articles?
      `an order applies` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does an order of a court or other authority apply?
      `it certifies the amendment follows the order` IS A BOOLEAN @desc If so, does the statement certify that the amendment has been made in accordance with the order?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 24(3), is our statement the statement of compliance required` IS
    `s 24(3) the statement is the statement of compliance required` `it certifies the amendment follows our articles` `an order applies` `it certifies the amendment follows the order`

@export Under section 25(1), am I protected from being bound by an alteration of the articles (ss 25(1), 25(2))?
GIVEN `the alteration was after I became a member` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Was the alteration made after the date on which you became a member?
      `shares the alteration requires me to hold` IS A NUMBER @desc How many shares does the alteration require you to take or subscribe for (in total)?
      `shares I hold when it is made` IS A NUMBER @desc How many shares do you hold at the date on which the alteration is made?
      `it increases my liability to pay money` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does the alteration in any way increase your liability, as at that date, to contribute to the company's share capital or otherwise to pay money to the company?
      `I agreed in writing to be bound` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Have you agreed in writing, before or after the alteration was made, to be bound by it?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 25(1), am I protected from being bound by an alteration of the articles` IS
    `s 25(1) the member is not bound by the alteration` `the alteration was after I became a member` `shares the alteration requires me to hold` `shares I hold when it is made` `it increases my liability to pay money` `I agreed in writing to be bound`
    -- JUST TRUE: the section says you are not bound by the alteration; JUST FALSE: the section does not protect you; NOTHING: the section does not decide (it takes your written agreement out of the protection but does not say you are then bound).

@export Under section 26(1), did we send the registrar the amended articles in time (s 26(1))?
GIVEN `the date the amendment takes effect` IS A DATE @desc On what date does the amendment of the articles take effect?
      `the date we sent the copy` IS A DATE @desc On what date was the copy of the articles as amended sent to the registrar?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 26(1), did we send the registrar the amended articles in time` IS
    `s 26(1) the copy of the articles as amended was sent in time` `the date the amendment takes effect` `the date we sent the copy`

@export Under section 26(3), do I commit an offence as an officer if our company did not send the amended articles in time (s 26(3))?
GIVEN `the company failed to comply with section 26` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did the company fail to comply with section 26?
      `I am an officer in default` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are you an officer of the company who is in default (section 1121)?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 26(3), do I commit an offence as an officer if our company did not send the amended articles in time` IS
    `s 26(3)(b) the officer of the company commits an offence` `the company failed to comply with section 26` (JUST `I am an officer in default`)

@export Under section 26(4), what is the most I can be fined for continued contravention each day, in pounds (s 26(4))?
GIVEN `level 3 on the standard scale in pounds` IS A NUMBER @desc How many pounds is level 3 on the standard scale? (The amount is set outside this Act.)
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `Under section 26(4), what is the most I can be fined for continued contravention each day, in pounds` IS
    `s 26(4) the most the daily default fine can be for each day of continued contravention, in pounds` `level 3 on the standard scale in pounds`

@export Under section 27(4), is our company liable to a civil penalty if it ignored the registrar's notice (ss 27(1), 27(4))?
GIVEN `the registrar gave notice` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has the registrar given the company a notice under section 27(1)?
      `the date the notice was issued` IS A DATE @desc On what date was the notice issued?
      `we complied` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has the company complied with the notice?
      `the date we complied` IS A DATE @desc On what date did the company comply? (Any date if it has not.)
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 27(4), is our company liable to a civil penalty if it ignored the registrar's notice` IS
    `s 27(4) the company is liable to a civil penalty` `the registrar gave notice` `the date the notice was issued` `we complied` `the date we complied`

@export Under section 27(3), can criminal proceedings still be brought if we complied with the registrar's notice in time (s 27(3))?
GIVEN `the date the notice was issued` IS A DATE @desc On what date was the notice issued?
      `we complied` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has the company complied with the notice?
      `the date we complied` IS A DATE @desc On what date did the company comply? (Any date if it has not.)
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 27(3), can criminal proceedings still be brought if we complied with the registrar's notice in time` IS
    `s 27(3) criminal proceedings may be brought in respect of the failure to comply` `the date the notice was issued` `we complied` `the date we complied`

@export Under section 28(1), is a provision that was in our memorandum before Part 3 began now treated as part of our articles (s 28(1))?
GIVEN `it was in our memorandum immediately before Part 3 began` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Was the provision contained in the company's memorandum immediately before the commencement of Part 3?
      `it is a provision of the kind a new-style memorandum has` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it a provision of the kind mentioned in section 8 (a new-style memorandum)?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 28(1), is a provision that was in our memorandum before Part 3 began now treated as part of our articles` IS
    `s 28(1) the provision is treated as a provision of the company's articles` `it was in our memorandum immediately before Part 3 began` `it is a provision of the kind a new-style memorandum has`

@export Under section 29(1), does Chapter 3 apply to this resolution or agreement (s 29(1))?
GIVEN `it is a special resolution` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it a special resolution (section 283)?
      `all the members agreed and it needed a special resolution` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Was it agreed to by all the members of the company, when it would not otherwise have been effective unless passed as a special resolution?
      `all the members of a class agreed and it needed a majority or manner` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Was it agreed to by all the members of a class of shareholders, when it would not otherwise have been effective unless passed by some particular majority or in some particular manner?
      `it binds a class although not all of them agreed` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does it effectively bind all members of a class of shareholders though not agreed to by all of them?
      `an enactment makes the Chapter apply` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does Chapter 3 apply to it by virtue of any enactment?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 29(1), does Chapter 3 apply to this resolution or agreement` IS
    `s 29(1) this Chapter applies to the resolution or agreement` (JUST `it is a special resolution`) `all the members agreed and it needed a special resolution` `all the members of a class agreed and it needed a majority or manner` `it binds a class although not all of them agreed` `an enactment makes the Chapter apply`

@export Under section 30(1), what must we forward to the registrar about a resolution or agreement (s 30(1))?
GIVEN `it is in writing` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the resolution or agreement in writing?
GIVETH A `s 30(1) what must be forwarded to the registrar`
DECIDE `Under section 30(1), what must we forward to the registrar about a resolution or agreement` IS
    `s 30(1) what the company must forward to the registrar` `it is in writing`

@export Under section 30(1), did we forward it to the registrar in time (s 30(1))?
GIVEN `the date it was passed or made` IS A DATE @desc On what date was the resolution or agreement passed or made?
      `the date we forwarded it` IS A DATE @desc On what date was the copy (or written memorandum) forwarded to the registrar?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 30(1), did we forward it to the registrar in time` IS
    `s 30(1) the copy or memorandum was forwarded in time` `the date it was passed or made` `the date we forwarded it`

@export Under section 30(2), do I commit an offence as an officer if our company did not forward it in time (s 30(2), (4))?
GIVEN `the company failed to comply with section 30` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did the company fail to comply with section 30?
      `I am an officer in default` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are you an officer of the company who is in default (section 1121)? A liquidator of the company counts as an officer for this section (section 30(4)).
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 30(2), do I commit an offence as an officer if our company did not forward it in time` IS
    `s 30(2)(b) the officer of the company commits an offence` `the company failed to comply with section 30` (JUST `I am an officer in default`)

@export Under section 31(1), are our company's objects unrestricted (s 31(1))?
GIVEN `our articles specifically restrict the objects` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Do the company's articles specifically restrict the objects of the company?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 31(1), are our company's objects unrestricted` IS
    `s 31(1) the company's objects are unrestricted` `our articles specifically restrict the objects`

@export Under section 31(2), is our amendment of the statement of objects still not effective (s 31(2)(c))?
GIVEN `the notice has been entered on the register` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has the registrar entered the company's notice of the amendment on the register?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 31(2), is our amendment of the statement of objects still not effective` IS
    `s 31(2)(c) the amendment cannot yet be effective` `the notice has been entered on the register`
    -- JUST TRUE means the amendment cannot yet be effective (no entry); JUST FALSE means the bar is lifted. The answer never says the amendment has become effective.

@export Under section 32(1), must the company send me its constitutional documents on my request (s 32(1))?
GIVEN `I am a member of the company` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are you a member of the company (section 112)?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 32(1), must the company send me its constitutional documents on my request` IS
    `s 32(1) the company must send the documents to the person on request` (JUST `I am a member of the company`)

@export Under section 32(1), which documents must the company send me (s 32(1))?
GIVEN `the company's liability` IS A `Liability of members` @desc How is the members' liability limited? One of: liability not limited; liability limited to the amount, if any, unpaid on the shares held; liability limited to the amount the members undertake to contribute on a winding up; liability limited in some other way by the constitution.
      `the company has a share capital` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does the company have a share capital?
      `there is a resolution or agreement in force` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is there a resolution or agreement to which Chapter 3 applies that is for the time being in force?
      `a document went to the registrar under section 34(2)` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has a document been required to be sent to the registrar under section 34(2) (constitution altered by enactment)?
      `a document went to the registrar under section 35(2)(a)` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has a document been required to be sent to the registrar under section 35(2)(a) (constitution altered by order)?
      `there is a section 899 or 900 order` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is there a court order under section 899 or 900?
      `there is a section 901F or 901J order` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is there a court order under section 901F or 901J?
      `there is a section 996 order altering the constitution` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is there a court order under section 996 that alters the company's constitution?
GIVETH A LIST OF `s 32(1) document the company must send`
DECIDE `Under section 32(1), which documents must the company send me` IS
    `s 32(1) the documents the company must send to the member` profile `there is a resolution or agreement in force` `a document went to the registrar under section 34(2)` `a document went to the registrar under section 35(2)(a)` `there is a section 899 or 900 order` `there is a section 901F or 901J order` `there is a section 996 order altering the constitution`
    WHERE
        -- Placeholder fields: the rule reads only the share capital and the liability of the members.
        profile MEANS `Company profile` WITH
            `place of registration` IS `England and Wales`
            `liability of the members` IS `the company's liability`
            `a share capital` IS `the company has a share capital`
            `certificate of incorporation stating that it is a public company` IS FALSE

@export Under section 33(1), is the party bound by the company's constitution as if by covenants (s 33(1))?
GIVEN `the party` IS A Party @desc Which party are you asking about? One of: Company, Director, Shadow director, Company secretary, Member, Subscriber to the memorandum, Officer in default, Auditor, Creditor, Debenture holder, Person with significant control, Registrar, Secretary of State, Court, Takeover Panel, Competent authority.
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 33(1), is the party bound by the company's constitution as if by covenants` IS
    `s 33(1) the provisions of the constitution bind the party as if there were covenants` `the party`

@export Under section 33(2), is money I owe the company under its constitution a debt (s 33(2))?
GIVEN `it is payable by me as a member under the constitution` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the money payable by you, as a member, to the company under its constitution?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 33(2), is money I owe the company under its constitution a debt` IS
    `s 33(2) the money is a debt due from the member to the company` `it is payable by me as a member under the constitution`

@export Under section 34(2), did we give the registrar notice in time that an enactment altered our constitution (ss 34(1), 34(2))?
GIVEN `the date the enactment came into force` IS A DATE @desc On what date did the enactment come into force?
      `the date we gave notice` IS A DATE @desc On what date did the company give the registrar notice of the alteration?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 34(2), did we give the registrar notice in time that an enactment altered our constitution` IS
    `s 34(2) the notice was given in time` `the date the enactment came into force` `the date we gave notice`

@export Under section 34(3), what must come with our notice that an enactment altered our constitution (ss 34(2), 34(3))?
GIVEN `it is a special enactment` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the enactment a special enactment (not a public general enactment, or one of the kinds section 34(4) includes)?
      `it amends our articles` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does the enactment amend the company's articles?
      `it amends a Chapter 3 resolution or agreement` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does the enactment amend a resolution or agreement to which Chapter 3 applies?
GIVETH A LIST OF `s 34 document that must accompany the notice`
DECIDE `Under section 34(3), what must come with our notice that an enactment altered our constitution` IS
    `s 34(2) and (3) the documents that must accompany the notice` `it is a special enactment` `it amends our articles` `it amends a Chapter 3 resolution or agreement`

@export Under section 35(1), did we give the registrar notice in time that a court order altered our constitution (s 35(1))?
GIVEN `the date the alteration took effect` IS A DATE @desc On what date did the alteration made by the order take effect?
      `the date we gave notice` IS A DATE @desc On what date did the company give the registrar notice of the alteration?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 35(1), did we give the registrar notice in time that a court order altered our constitution` IS
    `s 35(1) the notice was given in time` `the date the alteration took effect` `the date we gave notice`

@export Under section 35(2), what must come with our notice that a court order altered our constitution (s 35(2))?
GIVEN `the order amends our articles` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does the order amend the company's articles?
      `the order amends a Chapter 3 resolution or agreement` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does the order amend a resolution or agreement to which Chapter 3 applies?
GIVETH A LIST OF `s 35 document that must accompany the notice`
DECIDE `Under section 35(2), what must come with our notice that a court order altered our constitution` IS
    `s 35(2) the documents that must accompany the notice` `the order amends our articles` `the order amends a Chapter 3 resolution or agreement`

@export Under section 36(1), must this document or statement accompany a copy of our articles that we issue (ss 36(1), 36(2))?
GIVEN `it is one of the documents or statements section 36(1) lists` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it a Chapter 3 resolution or agreement, a statement under section 36(1)(b), a special enactment, or an order sent to the registrar under section 35(2)(a)?
      `its effect is already incorporated in the articles` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has the effect of the resolution, agreement, enactment or order on the constitution been incorporated into the articles by amendment?
      `it is not in force` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the resolution, agreement, enactment or order not for the time being in force?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 36(1), must this document or statement accompany a copy of our articles that we issue` IS
    `s 36(1) the document or statement must accompany the copy of the articles issued` `it is one of the documents or statements section 36(1) lists` `its effect is already incorporated in the articles` `it is not in force`

@export Under section 36(4), what is the most I can be fined for the occasions copies were issued or requested, in pounds (s 36(4))?
GIVEN `level 3 on the standard scale in pounds` IS A NUMBER @desc How many pounds is level 3 on the standard scale? (The amount is set outside this Act.)
      `occasions` IS A NUMBER @desc On how many occasions were copies of the articles issued, or, as the case may be, requested, without the documents that must accompany them?
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `Under section 36(4), what is the most I can be fined for the occasions copies were issued or requested, in pounds` IS
    `s 36(4) the most the person can be fined on summary conviction for the occasions, in pounds` `level 3 on the standard scale in pounds` `occasions`

@export Under section 37, is a provision in our articles giving a right to profits otherwise than as a member void (s 37)?
GIVEN `how the members' liability is limited` IS A `Liability of members` @desc How is the members' liability limited? One of: liability not limited; liability limited to the amount, if any, unpaid on the shares held; liability limited to the amount the members undertake to contribute on a winding up; liability limited in some other way by the constitution.
      `the company has a share capital` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does the company have a share capital?
      `the provision is in the articles or a resolution` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the provision in the company's articles or in a resolution of the company?
      `it gives a right to divisible profits other than as a member` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does the provision purport to give a person a right to participate in the divisible profits of the company otherwise than as a member?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 37, is a provision in our articles giving a right to profits otherwise than as a member void` IS
    `s 37 the provision is void` profile `the provision is in the articles or a resolution` `it gives a right to divisible profits other than as a member`
    WHERE
        -- Placeholder fields: the rule reads only the share capital and the liability of the members.
        profile MEANS `Company profile` WITH
            `place of registration` IS `England and Wales`
            `liability of the members` IS `how the members' liability is limited`
            `a share capital` IS `the company has a share capital`
            `certificate of incorporation stating that it is a public company` IS FALSE

@export Under section 38, does an enactment or rule of law for companies with several members apply to our one-member company (s 38)?
GIVEN `it applies to companies formed by two or more persons or with two or more members` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the enactment or rule of law one applicable to companies formed by two or more persons or having two or more members?
      `our company was formed by one person or has one member` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Was your company formed by one person, or does it have only one person as a member?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 38, does an enactment or rule of law for companies with several members apply to our one-member company` IS
    `s 38 the enactment or rule of law applies to the company with any necessary modification` `it applies to companies formed by two or more persons or with two or more members` `our company was formed by one person or has one member`

§§ `Part 4 -- A company's capacity and the power of directors to bind it (ss 39 to 52). The charity questions arise only if the company is a charity`

@export Under section 39(1), can the validity of the company's act be called into question for lack of capacity (ss 39(1), 39(2), 42)?
GIVEN `the ground is lack of capacity under the constitution` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the ground on which the act is challenged lack of capacity by reason of anything in the company's constitution?
      `the company is registered in` IS A `Place of registration` @desc Where is the company registered? One of: England and Wales, Scotland, Northern Ireland.
      `the company is a charity` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the company a charity?
      `I did not know it was a charity` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did you not know, when the act was done, that the company is a charity?
      `I gave full consideration` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did you give full consideration in money or money's worth in relation to the act?
      `I did not know the act was not permitted` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did you not know that the act is not permitted by the company's constitution?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 39(1), can the validity of the company's act be called into question for lack of capacity` IS
    `s 39(1) the validity of the act can be called into question on the ground of lack of capacity` `the ground is lack of capacity under the constitution` (`s 42(1) section 39 does not apply to the act` `the company is registered in` `the company is a charity` `I did not know it was a charity` `I gave full consideration` `I did not know the act was not permitted`)

@export Under section 40(1), is the directors' power to bind the company deemed free of constitutional limits in my favour (ss 40(1), 40(2), 42)?
GIVEN `I am a party to a transaction or act to which the company is a party` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are you a party to a transaction or other act to which the company is a party?
      `it is proved I acted in bad faith` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it proved that you did not act in good faith?
      `the company is registered in` IS A `Place of registration` @desc Where is the company registered? One of: England and Wales, Scotland, Northern Ireland.
      `the company is a charity` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the company a charity?
      `I did not know it was a charity` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did you not know, when the act was done, that the company is a charity?
      `I gave full consideration` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did you give full consideration in money or money's worth in relation to the act?
      `I did not know the act was beyond the directors' powers` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did you not know that the act is beyond the powers of the directors?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 40(1), is the directors' power to bind the company deemed free of constitutional limits in my favour` IS
    `s 40(1) the power of the directors to bind the company is deemed free of any limitation under the company's constitution in favour of the person` (`s 40(2)(a) the person deals with the company` `I am a party to a transaction or act to which the company is a party` EQUALS JUST TRUE) `it is proved I acted in bad faith` (`s 42(1) section 40 does not apply to the act` `the company is registered in` `the company is a charity` `I did not know it was a charity` `I gave full consideration` `I did not know the act was beyond the directors' powers`)

@export Under section 40(2), am I bound to enquire whether the directors' powers are limited (s 40(2)(b)(i))?
GIVEN `I am a party to a transaction or act to which the company is a party` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are you a party to a transaction or other act to which the company is a party?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 40(2), am I bound to enquire whether the directors' powers are limited` IS
    `s 40(2)(b)(i) the person dealing with the company is bound to enquire as to any limitation on the powers of the directors` (`s 40(2)(a) the person deals with the company` `I am a party to a transaction or act to which the company is a party` EQUALS JUST TRUE)

@export Under section 40(2), am I presumed to have acted in good faith when dealing with the company (s 40(2)(b)(ii), (iii))?
GIVEN `I am a party to a transaction or act to which the company is a party` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are you a party to a transaction or other act to which the company is a party?
      `the contrary is proved` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it proved that you did not act in good faith?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 40(2), am I presumed to have acted in good faith when dealing with the company` IS
    `s 40(2)(b)(ii) the person dealing with the company is presumed to have acted in good faith` (`s 40(2)(a) the person deals with the company` `I am a party to a transaction or act to which the company is a party` EQUALS JUST TRUE) `the contrary is proved`

@export Under section 41(2), is the transaction voidable at the company's instance because a director or connected person is a party (ss 41(1), 41(2), 41(7))?
GIVEN `the transaction's validity depends on section 40` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does the validity of the transaction depend on section 40 (the directors' power deemed free of limits)?
      `the company entered into it` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did the company enter into the transaction?
      `a party is a director of the company or its holding company` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is a party to the transaction a director of the company or of its holding company?
      `a party is connected with such a director` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is a party to the transaction a person connected with such a director (Part 10)?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 41(2), is the transaction voidable at the company's instance because a director or connected person is a party` IS
    `s 41(2) the transaction is voidable at the instance of the company` (`s 41(1) this section applies to the transaction` `the transaction's validity depends on section 40` EQUALS JUST TRUE) `the company entered into it` `a party is a director of the company or its holding company` (JUST `a party is connected with such a director`)

@export Under section 41(3), how much must I account to the company for, in pounds (ss 41(3), 41(5))?
GIVEN `I am a party within section 41(2)(b)` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are you a party to the transaction who is a director of the company or its holding company, or a person connected with such a director?
      `I am a director who authorised it` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are you a director of the company who authorised the transaction?
      `I am a director of the company` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are you a director of the company?
      `I can show I did not know the directors exceeded their powers` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Can you show that, when the transaction was entered into, you did not know that the directors were exceeding their powers?
      `my gain from the transaction` IS A NUMBER @desc How many pounds did you gain, directly or indirectly, from the transaction?
GIVETH A MAYBE NUMBER
DECIDE `Under section 41(3), how much must I account to the company for, in pounds` IS
    `s 41(3)(a) the amount the person must account to the company for` (IF `s 41(5) a person other than a director is liable under subsection (3)` `I am a director of the company` `I can show I did not know the directors exceeded their powers` EQUALS JUST FALSE THEN JUST FALSE ELSE `s 41(3) the person is liable under subsection (3)` `I am a party within section 41(2)(b)` `I am a director who authorised it`) `my gain from the transaction`

@export Under section 41(3), how much must I indemnify the company for, in pounds (ss 41(3), 41(5))?
GIVEN `I am a party within section 41(2)(b)` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are you a party to the transaction who is a director of the company or its holding company, or a person connected with such a director?
      `I am a director who authorised it` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are you a director of the company who authorised the transaction?
      `I am a director of the company` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are you a director of the company?
      `I can show I did not know the directors exceeded their powers` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Can you show that, when the transaction was entered into, you did not know that the directors were exceeding their powers?
      `the loss or damage to the company` IS A NUMBER @desc How many pounds is the loss or damage to the company resulting from the transaction?
GIVETH A MAYBE NUMBER
DECIDE `Under section 41(3), how much must I indemnify the company for, in pounds` IS
    `s 41(3)(b) the amount the person must indemnify the company for` (IF `s 41(5) a person other than a director is liable under subsection (3)` `I am a director of the company` `I can show I did not know the directors exceeded their powers` EQUALS JUST FALSE THEN JUST FALSE ELSE `s 41(3) the person is liable under subsection (3)` `I am a party within section 41(2)(b)` `I am a director who authorised it`) `the loss or damage to the company`

@export Under section 41(4), has the transaction ceased to be voidable (s 41(4))?
GIVEN `restitution is no longer possible` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is restitution of any money or other asset that was the subject matter of the transaction no longer possible?
      `the company is indemnified` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the company indemnified for any loss or damage resulting from the transaction?
      `third party rights would be affected` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Would rights acquired bona fide for value and without actual notice of the directors' exceeding their powers, by a person who is not a party to the transaction, be affected by avoidance?
      `the company affirmed it` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has the company affirmed the transaction? (For a charity, an affirmation is ineffective without the prior written consent in section 42(4).)
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 41(4), has the transaction ceased to be voidable` IS
    `s 41(4) the transaction has ceased to be voidable` `restitution is no longer possible` `the company is indemnified` `third party rights would be affected` `the company affirmed it`

@export Under section 42(1), is the protection of section 40 taken away in my dealing with a charity company (ss 42(1), 42(5))?
GIVEN `the company is registered in` IS A `Place of registration` @desc Where is the company registered? One of: England and Wales, Scotland, Northern Ireland.
      `the company is a charity` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the company a charity?
      `I did not know it was a charity` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did you not know, when the act was done, that the company is a charity?
      `I gave full consideration` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did you give full consideration in money or money's worth in relation to the act?
      `I did not know the act was beyond the directors' powers` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did you not know that the act is beyond the powers of the directors?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 42(1), is the protection of section 40 taken away in my dealing with a charity company` IS
    `s 42(1) section 40 does not apply to the act` `the company is registered in` `the company is a charity` `I did not know it was a charity` `I gave full consideration` `I did not know the act was beyond the directors' powers`
    -- JUST TRUE: section 40 does not apply to this act; JUST FALSE: it does (you are within the exception, or section 42 does not extend to Scotland); NOTHING: the company is not a charity, and section 42 says nothing.

@export Under section 42(2), is my title to property bought from a charity company affected by a defect in its act (s 42(2))?
GIVEN `the company is registered in` IS A `Place of registration` @desc Where is the company registered? One of: England and Wales, Scotland, Northern Ireland.
      `the company is a charity` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the company a charity?
      `the company purported to transfer or grant an interest in property` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did the company purport to transfer or grant an interest in property?
      `I acquired it later for full consideration` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did you subsequently acquire the property or an interest in it for full consideration?
      `I had no actual notice` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did you acquire it without actual notice of any circumstances affecting the validity of the company's act?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 42(2), is my title to property bought from a charity company affected by a defect in its act` IS
    `s 42(2) the title of the person who acquires the property or interest is affected` `the company is registered in` `the company is a charity` `the company purported to transfer or grant an interest in property` `I acquired it later for full consideration` `I had no actual notice`

@export Under section 42(4), is a charity company's affirmation of a transaction with a director effective (s 42(4))?
GIVEN `the company is registered in` IS A `Place of registration` @desc Where is the company registered? One of: England and Wales, Scotland, Northern Ireland.
      `the company is a charity` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the company a charity?
      `section 41 applies to the transaction` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the transaction one to which section 41 applies?
      `the prior written consent was given` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has the prior written consent of the Charity Commission (England and Wales) or the Department for Social Development (Northern Ireland) been given?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 42(4), is a charity company's affirmation of a transaction with a director effective` IS
    `s 42(4) the affirmation of the transaction is effective` `the company is registered in` `the company is a charity` `section 41 applies to the transaction` `the prior written consent was given`

@export Under section 43(1), may our contract be made this way (s 43(1))?
GIVEN `English or Northern Irish law governs` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the contract made under the law of England and Wales or Northern Ireland?
      `it is by writing under the common seal` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it made by the company, by writing under its common seal?
      `it is made by a person acting under authority` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it made on behalf of the company by a person acting under its authority, express or implied?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 43(1), may our contract be made this way` IS
    `s 43(1) the contract may be made in that way` `English or Northern Irish law governs` `it is by writing under the common seal` `it is made by a person acting under authority`

@export Under section 44(2), is our document validly executed by the signatures on it (s 44(2), (3))?
GIVEN `authorised signatories who signed` IS A NUMBER @desc How many authorised signatories (every director, and the secretary or any joint secretary of a public company or of a private company with a secretary) signed on the company's behalf?
      `a director signed before an attesting witness` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did a director of the company sign on its behalf in the presence of a witness who attests the signature?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 44(2), is our document validly executed by the signatures on it` IS
    `s 44(2) signature in that way validly executes the document for the company` `authorised signatories who signed` `a director signed before an attesting witness`

@export Under section 44(3), am I an authorised signatory for the company (s 44(3))?
GIVEN `I am a director` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are you a director of the company?
      `the company is a public company` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the company a public company?
      `the company is a private company with a secretary` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the company a private company with a secretary?
      `I am the secretary or a joint secretary` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are you the secretary (or a joint secretary) of the company?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 44(3), am I an authorised signatory for the company` IS
    `s 44(3) the person is an authorised signatory for the purposes of subsection (2)` `I am a director` `the company is a public company` `the company is a private company with a secretary` `I am the secretary or a joint secretary`

@export Under section 44(5), is the document deemed duly executed in my favour as a purchaser (s 44(5))?
GIVEN `I bought in good faith for valuable consideration` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are you a purchaser in good faith for valuable consideration?
      `I acquired an interest in property for valuable consideration` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are you a lessee, mortgagee or other person who for valuable consideration acquires an interest in property?
      `it purports to be signed under section 44(2)` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does the document purport to be signed in accordance with section 44(2)?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 44(5), is the document deemed duly executed in my favour as a purchaser` IS
    `s 44(5) the document is deemed to have been duly executed by the company in favour of the person` (`s 44(5) the person is a purchaser` `I bought in good faith for valuable consideration` `I acquired an interest in property for valuable consideration` EQUALS JUST TRUE) `it purports to be signed under section 44(2)`

@export Under section 44(6), is a document I sign for more than one company duly signed (s 44(6))?
GIVEN `it is signed by me for more than one company` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the document to be signed by you on behalf of more than one company?
      `I sign separately in each capacity` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Do you sign it separately in each capacity?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 44(6), is a document I sign for more than one company duly signed` IS
    `s 44(6) the document is duly signed by the person for the purposes of section 44` `it is signed by me for more than one company` `I sign separately in each capacity`

@export Under section 45(2), must our company have its name engraved on its common seal (ss 45(1), 45(2), 45(6))?
GIVEN `the company is registered in` IS A `Place of registration` @desc Where is the company registered? One of: England and Wales, Scotland, Northern Ireland.
      `the company has a common seal` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does the company have a common seal?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 45(2), must our company have its name engraved on its common seal` IS
    `s 45(2) the company must have its name engraved in legible characters on its common seal` `the company is registered in` `the company has a common seal`

@export Under section 45(3), do I commit an offence as an officer if our common seal lacks the company's name (s 45(3))?
GIVEN `the company is registered in` IS A `Place of registration` @desc Where is the company registered? One of: England and Wales, Scotland, Northern Ireland.
      `the company has a common seal` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does the company have a common seal?
      `the name is engraved on it` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the company's name engraved in legible characters on the seal?
      `I am an officer in default` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are you an officer of the company who is in default (section 1121)?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 45(3), do I commit an offence as an officer if our common seal lacks the company's name` IS
    `s 45(3)(b) the officer of the company commits an offence` `the company is registered in` `the company has a common seal` `the name is engraved on it` (JUST `I am an officer in default`)

@export Under section 45(4), do I commit an offence by using a seal on which the company's name is not engraved (s 45(4))?
GIVEN `the company is registered in` IS A `Place of registration` @desc Where is the company registered? One of: England and Wales, Scotland, Northern Ireland.
      `I am an officer or act for the company` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are you an officer of a company, or a person acting on behalf of a company?
      `I use or authorise the use of the seal` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Do you use, or authorise the use of, a seal purporting to be a seal of the company?
      `its name is not engraved on it` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the company's name not engraved on the seal as required by section 45(2)?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 45(4), do I commit an offence by using a seal on which the company's name is not engraved` IS
    `s 45(4) the person commits an offence` `the company is registered in` `I am an officer or act for the company` `I use or authorise the use of the seal` `its name is not engraved on it`

@export Under section 45(5), what is the most I can be fined for a seal offence, in pounds (s 45(5))?
GIVEN `level 3 on the standard scale in pounds` IS A NUMBER @desc How many pounds is level 3 on the standard scale? (The amount is set outside this Act.)
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `Under section 45(5), what is the most I can be fined for a seal offence, in pounds` IS
    `s 45(5) the most the person can be fined on summary conviction, in pounds` `level 3 on the standard scale in pounds`

@export Under section 46(1), is our document validly executed as a deed (s 46(1))?
GIVEN `it is duly executed by the company` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the document duly executed by the company?
      `it is delivered as a deed` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it delivered as a deed?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 46(1), is our document validly executed as a deed` IS
    `s 46(1) the document is validly executed by the company as a deed` `it is duly executed by the company` `it is delivered as a deed`

@export Under section 46(2), is our deed presumed to have been delivered when executed (s 46(2))?
GIVEN `it has been executed` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has the document been executed?
      `a contrary intention is proved` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is a contrary intention proved?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 46(2), is our deed presumed to have been delivered when executed` IS
    `s 46(2) the document is presumed to be delivered` `it has been executed` `a contrary intention is proved`

@export Under section 47(1), may the company empower me as its attorney by an instrument executed as a deed (ss 47(1), 47(2))?
GIVEN `English or Northern Irish law governs` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does the law of England and Wales or Northern Ireland govern the appointment?
      `it is by an instrument executed as a deed` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the empowerment by an instrument executed as a deed?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 47(1), may the company empower me as its attorney by an instrument executed as a deed` IS
    `s 47(1) the company may empower the person as its attorney to execute deeds or other documents on its behalf` `English or Northern Irish law governs` `it is by an instrument executed as a deed`

@export Under section 49(5), does an agent's authority to affix the official seal continue on this date (s 49(5))?
GIVEN `as between the company and a person dealing with the agent` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the question as between the company and a person dealing with the agent?
      `the instrument mentions a period` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does the instrument conferring the authority mention a period?
      `the period ends on` IS A DATE @desc On what date does the period mentioned in the instrument end? (Any date if none is mentioned.)
      `notice of revocation or termination has been given` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has notice of the revocation or termination of the agent's authority been given to the person dealing with the agent?
      `the notice was given on` IS A DATE @desc On what date was that notice given? (Any date if none has been given.)
      `the date in question` IS A DATE @desc For which date are you asking?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 49(5), does an agent's authority to affix the official seal continue on this date` IS
    `s 49(5) the agent's authority continues on the date` `as between the company and a person dealing with the agent` (IF `the instrument mentions a period` THEN JUST `the period ends on` ELSE NOTHING) (IF `notice of revocation or termination has been given` THEN JUST `the notice was given on` ELSE NOTHING) `the date in question`

@export Under section 49(6), have I certified the date and place as the person who affixed the official seal (s 49(6))?
GIVEN `I certified the date in writing` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did you certify in writing, on the deed or other document, the date on which the official seal was affixed?
      `I certified the place in writing` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did you certify in writing, on the deed or other document, the place at which it was affixed?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 49(6), have I certified the date and place as the person who affixed the official seal` IS
    `s 49(6) the person affixing the official seal has certified the date and place` `I certified the date in writing` `I certified the place in writing`

@export Under section 51(1), am I personally liable on a contract I made for a company that had not been formed (ss 51(1), 51(2))?
GIVEN `it purported to be made for the company` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did the contract purport to be made by or on behalf of a company?
      `the company had not been formed` IS A BOOLEAN @desc When it was made, had the company not yet been formed?
      `we agreed otherwise` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is there an agreement to the contrary?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 51(1), am I personally liable on a contract I made for a company that had not been formed` IS
    `s 51(1) the person purporting to act for the company is personally liable on the contract` `it purported to be made for the company` `the company had not been formed` `we agreed otherwise`

@export Under section 52, is a bill of exchange or promissory note I signed deemed to be made, accepted or endorsed on the company's behalf (s 52)?
GIVEN `it is a bill of exchange or promissory note` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the instrument a bill of exchange or promissory note?
      `it is in the company's name or on its behalf or account` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it made, accepted or endorsed in the name of, or by or on behalf or on account of, the company?
      `I act under the company's authority` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it so made, accepted or endorsed by a person acting under the company's authority?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 52, is a bill of exchange or promissory note I signed deemed to be made, accepted or endorsed on the company's behalf` IS
    `s 52 the bill or note is deemed to have been made, accepted or endorsed on behalf of the company` `it is a bill of exchange or promissory note` `it is in the company's name or on its behalf or account` `I act under the company's authority`

-- ====================================================================================================
-- seat questions from part coa2 (merged by the lead on 2026-11-12; unchanged text follows)
-- ====================================================================================================
-- coa2-seat.l4: the SEAT LAYER over the coa2 modules (Companies Act 2006, ss 53-111: a company's name, its registered
-- office and email address, and re-registration as a means of altering its status).
--
-- SEAT: an individual who is, or is about to become, a director, a company secretary or a member (shareholder) of a
-- company registered under the Act, or who deals with one, asking on facts they can state what the Act requires or lets
-- them do, what rights they have against the company or its directors, what they must disclose, file, approve or vote on
-- and by when, and what follows (liability, offences, penalties) if it is not done.  (Assumed, not ruled: the Act is
-- addressed to companies, so the individual is whoever stands in a company's management or ownership.)
-- There is never a seat for an official: provisions that address only the Secretary of State, the registrar, a company
-- names adjudicator or a court appear here only as what they mean for the individual (what may be done to them, what they
-- must be given, and by when).
--
-- PLAIN INPUTS.  Every question takes plain inputs, one per fact the person can state (yes/no, a number, a date, a choice
-- from a list), each with an @desc worded as that person would be asked.  The rules are the layer-1 modules'; nothing is
-- restated here.  Where a layer-1 rule takes another section's answer as an input (the keel's, or another part's), the
-- person's statement of that fact is the answer: `coa2 seat a stated fact as an answer` turns a yes/no into JUST TRUE or
-- JUST FALSE.  Where a layer-1 rule takes a date that may not have happened yet (a certificate not yet issued), a yes/no
-- and a date are asked and `coa2 seat a date if it has happened` turns them into a MAYBE DATE.
--
-- WHAT AN ANSWER MEANS (the rule of 2026-10-29, assumed, not ruled by a lawyer): a MAYBE BOOLEAN answer is
--   JUST TRUE   the Act says yes;
--   JUST FALSE  the Act says no in its own words;
--   NOTHING     the Act does not decide on these facts (silent, a list not closed, "includes", an undefined term, a rule
--               or number outside the Act, or a prohibition or grant limited by its own wording).
-- A caller must never read NOTHING as "no".  Amounts of money are never in the Act: the pounds that a level on the
-- standard scale stands for are asked as inputs where a pounds answer is wanted.
--
-- Where the layer-1 rule needs the amount of the penalty, the answer is a sentence (a STRING) that says what the Act
-- states.  The daily default fine in ss 63(3) and 64(6) is given in two wordings run together by the text converter; the
-- sentence says so (NOTES.md, fork 1).

GIVEN fact IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`coa2 seat a stated fact as an answer` MEANS
    IF fact THEN JUST TRUE ELSE JUST FALSE

GIVEN `it has happened` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the date it happened` IS A DATE
GIVETH A MAYBE DATE
`coa2 seat a date if it has happened` MEANS
    IF `it has happened` THEN JUST `the date it happened` ELSE NOTHING

GIVEN limit IS A MAYBE `Fine limit`
GIVETH A STRING
`coa2 seat describe a fine limit` MEANS
    CONSIDER limit
    WHEN NOTHING THEN "not covered by the text"
    WHEN JUST `a fine without a stated limit` THEN "a fine (no limit stated)"
    WHEN JUST (`a fine not exceeding the statutory maximum` frac) THEN CONCAT "a fine not exceeding ", TOSTRING frac, " of the statutory maximum"
    WHEN JUST (`a fine not exceeding a level on the standard scale` lvl frac) THEN CONCAT "a fine not exceeding ", TOSTRING frac, " of level ", TOSTRING lvl, " on the standard scale"
    WHEN JUST (`a fine not exceeding an amount in pounds` amt) THEN CONCAT "a fine not exceeding ", TOSTRING amt, " pounds"

GIVEN nominal IS A NUMBER, paidNominal IS A NUMBER, premium IS A NUMBER, paidPremium IS A NUMBER, date IS A DATE
      employee IS A BOOLEAN, work IS A BOOLEAN, workDone IS A BOOLEAN, nonCash IS A BOOLEAN, nonCashDone IS A BOOLEAN, contract IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A `s 91 allotment`
`coa2 seat an allotment` MEANS
    `s 91 allotment` WITH
        `nominal value of the shares in the allotment` IS nominal
        `amount paid up on those shares on account of their nominal value` IS paidNominal
        `premium on those shares` IS premium
        `amount paid up on those shares on account of the premium` IS paidPremium
        `date of the allotment` IS date
        `allotted in pursuance of an employees' share scheme` IS employee
        `paid up by an undertaking that he or another should do work or perform services` IS work
        `that undertaking has been performed or otherwise discharged` IS workDone
        `allotted otherwise than in cash, the consideration including an undertaking to the company other than one in paragraph (c)` IS nonCash
        `the undertaking to the company has been performed or otherwise discharged` IS nonCashDone
        `a contract provides for the undertaking to be performed within five years from the time the special resolution is passed` IS contract

GIVEN penalty IS A Penalty
GIVETH A STRING
`coa2 seat describe a penalty` MEANS
    CONCAT "On summary conviction: ", `coa2 seat describe a fine limit` (penalty's `fine not exceeding`),
           "; for continued contravention, a daily default fine: ", `coa2 seat describe a fine limit` (penalty's `daily default fine for continued contravention`)

§ `Companies Act 2006, Parts 5 to 7: a company's name, registered office and email address, and re-registration`

§§ `Part 5, Chapter 1: names that cannot be registered (ss 53 to 57C)`
-- Ask before incorporating, or before changing a name.

@export Under section 53, may my company be registered by this name? (JUST FALSE where the Secretary of State is of the opinion that its use would be an offence or that it is offensive)
GIVEN `use of the name would be an offence in the Secretary of State's opinion` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the Secretary of State of the opinion that your company's use of the name would constitute an offence?
      `the name is offensive in the Secretary of State's opinion` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the Secretary of State of the opinion that the name is offensive?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 53, may my company be registered by this name` IS
    `s 53 the company may be registered by the name` `use of the name would be an offence in the Secretary of State's opinion` `the name is offensive in the Secretary of State's opinion`

@export Under section 53A, may my company be registered by this name? (JUST FALSE where the Secretary of State is of the opinion that registration is intended to facilitate dishonesty or deception)
GIVEN `registration is intended to facilitate an offence involving dishonesty or deception` IS A BOOLEAN @desc In the Secretary of State's opinion, is registration by this name intended to facilitate the commission of an offence involving dishonesty or deception?
      `registration is intended to facilitate conduct that would amount to such an offence in the United Kingdom` IS A BOOLEAN @desc In the Secretary of State's opinion, is registration by this name intended to facilitate conduct that, if carried out in any part of the United Kingdom, would amount to such an offence?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 53A, may my company be registered by this name` IS
    `s 53A the company may be registered by the name` `registration is intended to facilitate an offence involving dishonesty or deception` `registration is intended to facilitate conduct that would amount to such an offence in the United Kingdom`

@export Under section 54(2), is this body a local authority?
GIVEN `local authority within the meaning of the Local Government Act 1972` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the body a local authority within the meaning of the Local Government Act 1972?
      `the Common Council of the City of London` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the body the Common Council of the City of London?
      `the Council of the Isles of Scilly` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the body the Council of the Isles of Scilly?
      `a council constituted under section 2 of the Local Government etc. (Scotland) Act 1994` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the body a council constituted under section 2 of the Local Government etc. (Scotland) Act 1994?
      `a district council in Northern Ireland` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the body a district council in Northern Ireland?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 54(2), is this body a local authority` IS
    `s 54(2) the body is a local authority` `local authority within the meaning of the Local Government Act 1972` `the Common Council of the City of London` `the Council of the Isles of Scilly` `a council constituted under section 2 of the Local Government etc. (Scotland) Act 1994` `a district council in Northern Ireland`

@export Under section 54(2), is this person or body a public authority? (the Act says a public authority includes any person or body having functions of a public nature)
GIVEN `the person or body has functions of a public nature` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does the person or body have functions of a public nature?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 54(2), is this person or body a public authority` IS
    `s 54(2) the person or body is a public authority` `the person or body has functions of a public nature`

@export Under section 54(1), do we need the approval of the Secretary of State for a name that suggests a connection with government or a public authority?
GIVEN `the name would be likely to give the impression of a connection` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Would the name be likely to give the impression that your company is connected with the body concerned?
      `the body is Her Majesty's Government or a government in the United Kingdom` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the body Her Majesty's Government, a part of the Scottish administration, the Welsh Assembly Government or Her Majesty's Government in Northern Ireland?
      `the body is a local authority` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the body a local authority (see the question on section 54(2))?
      `the body is a public authority specified in regulations` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the body a public authority specified by the Secretary of State's regulations under section 54?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 54(1), do we need the approval of the Secretary of State for a name suggesting a connection with government` IS
    `s 54(1) the approval of the Secretary of State is required` `the name would be likely to give the impression of a connection` `the body is Her Majesty's Government or a government in the United Kingdom` (`coa2 seat a stated fact as an answer` `the body is a local authority`) `the body is a public authority specified in regulations`

@export Under section 55, do we need the approval of the Secretary of State for a name that includes a sensitive word or expression?
GIVEN `the name includes a word or expression specified in the regulations` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does the name include a word or expression for the time being specified in regulations made by the Secretary of State under section 55?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 55, do we need the approval of the Secretary of State for a name including a sensitive word` IS
    `s 55(1) the approval of the Secretary of State is required` `the name includes a word or expression specified in the regulations`

@export Under section 56(2), must the applicant ask a government department or other body for its view on the proposed name?
GIVEN `regulations require the applicant to seek the view of a specified body` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Do regulations under section 54 or 55 require the applicant to seek the view of a specified Government department or other body?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 56(2), must I ask a government department for its view on the name` IS
    `s 56(2) the applicant must request the specified department or body in writing to indicate whether and why it has any objections` `regulations require the applicant to seek the view of a specified body`

@export Under section 56(3)(a), must the application to register the company include a statement that a request for the department's view has been made?
GIVEN `a request has been made in connection with the application to register` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has a request under section 56 been made in connection with the application for the registration of the company?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 56(3)(a), must the application to register include a statement that a request was made` IS
    `s 56(3)(a) the application must include a statement that a request under this section has been made` `a request has been made in connection with the application to register`

@export Under section 56(3)(b), must the application to register the company be accompanied by a copy of the department's response?
GIVEN `a request has been made in connection with the application to register` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has a request under section 56 been made in connection with the application for the registration of the company?
      `a response has been received` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Have you received a response to the request?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 56(3)(b), must the application to register be accompanied by a copy of the response` IS
    `s 56(3)(b) the application must be accompanied by a copy of the response received` `a request has been made in connection with the application to register` `a response has been received`

@export Under section 56(4)(a), must the notice of a change of the company's name be accompanied by a statement by a director or secretary that a request has been made?
GIVEN `a request has been made in connection with the change of name` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has a request under section 56 been made in connection with a change in the company's name?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 56(4)(a), must the notice of a change of name be accompanied by a statement by a director or secretary` IS
    `s 56(4)(a) the notice of the change must be accompanied by a statement by a director or secretary that a request has been made` `a request has been made in connection with the change of name`

@export Under section 56(4)(b), must the notice of a change of the company's name be accompanied by a copy of the department's response?
GIVEN `a request has been made in connection with the change of name` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has a request under section 56 been made in connection with a change in the company's name?
      `a response has been received` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Have you received a response to the request?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 56(4)(b), must the notice of a change of name be accompanied by a copy of the response` IS
    `s 56(4)(b) the notice of the change must be accompanied by a copy of the response received` `a request has been made in connection with the change of name` `a response has been received`

@export Under section 56A, may my company be registered by this name? (JUST FALSE where it would be likely to give the false impression of a connection with a foreign government or an international organisation)
GIVEN `the name suggests a connection with a foreign government` IS A BOOLEAN @desc In the Secretary of State's opinion, would the name be likely to give the false impression that the company is connected with a foreign government or an agency or authority of a foreign government?
      `the name suggests a connection with an international organisation` IS A BOOLEAN @desc In the Secretary of State's opinion, would the name be likely to give the false impression that the company is connected with an international organisation whose members include two or more countries or territories (or their governments)?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 56A, may my company be registered by this name` IS
    `s 56A the company may be registered by the name` `the name suggests a connection with a foreign government` `the name suggests a connection with an international organisation`

@export Under section 57(3), may my company be registered by a name that consists of or includes something the regulations do not permit?
GIVEN `the name includes something not permitted by the regulations` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does the name consist of or include anything that is not permitted in accordance with regulations under section 57 (letters, characters, signs, symbols or punctuation, or a standard style)?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 57(3), may my company be registered by a name with a character the regulations do not permit` IS
    `s 57(3) the company may be registered by the name` `the name includes something not permitted by the regulations`

@export Under section 57A, may my company be registered by this name? (JUST FALSE where in the Secretary of State's opinion the name consists of or includes computer code)
GIVEN `the name includes computer code in the Secretary of State's opinion` IS A BOOLEAN @desc In the Secretary of State's opinion, does the name consist of or include computer code?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 57A, may my company be registered by a name that includes computer code` IS
    `s 57A the company may be registered by the name` `the name includes computer code in the Secretary of State's opinion`

@export Under section 57B(1), may my company be registered again by the name it was made to change, or a name similar to it?
GIVEN `its name was changed following a direction under section 67, 75, 76, 76A or 76B` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has the company's name at any time been changed following a direction under section 67, 75, 76, 76A or 76B?
      `a new name was determined under section 76D after a direction was not complied with` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Was a new name determined for the company under section 76D because it failed to comply with such a direction?
      `its name was changed following an order under section 73` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has the company's name at any time been changed following an order under section 73?
      `a new name was determined under section 73(4) after an order was not complied with` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Was a new name determined for the company under section 73(4) because it failed to comply with such an order?
      `the name is the original name or a similar one` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the name you want the original name, or a name that is similar to it?
      `the name is approved by the Secretary of State` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has the Secretary of State approved the name?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 57B(1), may my company be registered again by its original name or a similar one` IS
    `s 57B(1) the company may be registered by the name` (`s 57B(3)(a) the name is treated as changed following a direction` `its name was changed following a direction under section 67, 75, 76, 76A or 76B` `a new name was determined under section 76D after a direction was not complied with`) (`s 57B(3)(b) the name is treated as changed following an order` `its name was changed following an order under section 73` `a new name was determined under section 73(4) after an order was not complied with`) `the name is the original name or a similar one` `the name is approved by the Secretary of State`

@export Under section 57C(4), do I have a "relevant relationship" with this company? (an officer, or a member or former member)
GIVEN `I am or was an officer of the company` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are you an officer of the company?
      `I am or was a member of the company` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are you a member or former member of the company?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 57C(4), do I have a relevant relationship with this company` IS
    `s 57C(4) the person has a relevant relationship with the company` `I am or was an officer of the company` `I am or was a member of the company`

@export Under section 57C(1), may another company be registered by a name that a company has been directed (or ordered) to change, or a similar name?
GIVEN `the first company was directed under section 67, 75, 76, 76A or 76B to change its name` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has a company at any time been directed under section 67, 75, 76, 76A or 76B to change its name?
      `a new name was determined for it under section 76D` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Was a new name determined for that company under section 76D because it failed to comply with the direction?
      `the first company was ordered under section 73 to change its name` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has the company been ordered under section 73 to change its name?
      `a new name was determined for it under section 73(4)` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Was a new name determined for that company under section 73(4) because it failed to comply with the order?
      `the name is that name or a similar one` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the name wanted by the other company that name, or a name similar to it?
      `the other company is an existing company` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the other company an existing company?
      `an application has been made to register the other company` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has an application been made for the registration of the other company?
      `a person has a relevant relationship with both companies now` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is there a person who has, or has had, a relevant relationship (officer, or member or former member) with both companies?
      `a person would have a relevant relationship with both on incorporation` IS A BOOLEAN @desc If the other company is registered, will there be on its incorporation a person who has, or has had, a relevant relationship with both companies?
      `the name is approved by the Secretary of State` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has the Secretary of State approved the name?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 57C(1), may another company be registered by a name that a company was directed to change` IS
    `s 57C(1) the other company may be registered by the name` (`s 57C(5)(a) the company is treated as directed to change its name` `the first company was directed under section 67, 75, 76, 76A or 76B to change its name` `a new name was determined for it under section 76D`) (`s 57C(5)(b) the company is treated as ordered to change its name` `the first company was ordered under section 73 to change its name` `a new name was determined for it under section 73(4)`) `the name is that name or a similar one` `the other company is an existing company` `an application has been made to register the other company` `a person has a relevant relationship with both companies now` `a person would have a relevant relationship with both on incorporation` `the name is approved by the Secretary of State`

§§ `Part 5, Chapter 2: "public limited company", "limited" and the exemption (ss 58 to 65)`

@export Under section 58(1), must my company's name end with "public limited company" or "p.l.c."?
GIVEN `the company is limited` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the liability of the company's members limited by its constitution?
      `the company is a public company` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the company a public company?
      `the company is a community interest company` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the company a community interest company?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 58(1), must my public company's name end with public limited company or p.l.c.` IS
    `s 58(1) the name of the company must end with public limited company or p.l.c.` `the company is limited` `the company is a public company` `the company is a community interest company`

@export Under section 58, does my public company's name end as the section requires? (a Welsh company may end with "cwmni cyfyngedig cyhoeddus" or "c.c.c.")
GIVEN `the company is limited` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the liability of the company's members limited by its constitution?
      `the company is a public company` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the company a public company?
      `the company is a community interest company` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the company a community interest company?
      `the name ends with public limited company or p.l.c.` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does the name end with "public limited company" or "p.l.c."?
      `the company is a Welsh company` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does the register state that the company's registered office is to be situated in Wales?
      `the name ends in Welsh with cwmni cyfyngedig cyhoeddus or c.c.c.` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does the name end with "cwmni cyfyngedig cyhoeddus" or "c.c.c."?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 58, does my public company's name end as the section requires` IS
    `s 58(1) the name of the company ends as the section requires` (`s 58(1) the name of the company must end with public limited company or p.l.c.` `the company is limited` `the company is a public company` `the company is a community interest company`) `the name ends with public limited company or p.l.c.` (`coa2 seat a stated fact as an answer` `the company is a Welsh company`) `the name ends in Welsh with cwmni cyfyngedig cyhoeddus or c.c.c.`

@export Under section 59(1), must my private company's name end with "limited" or "ltd."?
GIVEN `the company is limited` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the liability of the company's members limited by its constitution?
      `the company is a private company` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the company a private company?
      `the company is a community interest company` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the company a community interest company?
      `the company is exempt under section 60` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the company exempt from this requirement under section 60 (see the question on section 60(1))?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 59(1), must my private company's name end with limited or ltd.` IS
    `s 59(1) the name of the company must end with limited or ltd.` `the company is limited` `the company is a private company` `the company is a community interest company` (`coa2 seat a stated fact as an answer` `the company is exempt under section 60`)

@export Under section 59, does my private company's name end as the section requires? (a Welsh company may end with "cyfyngedig" or "cyf.")
GIVEN `the company is limited` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the liability of the company's members limited by its constitution?
      `the company is a private company` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the company a private company?
      `the company is a community interest company` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the company a community interest company?
      `the company is exempt under section 60` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the company exempt from this requirement under section 60?
      `the name ends with limited or ltd.` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does the name end with "limited" or "ltd."?
      `the company is a Welsh company` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does the register state that the company's registered office is to be situated in Wales?
      `the name ends in Welsh with cyfyngedig or cyf.` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does the name end with "cyfyngedig" or "cyf."?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 59, does my private company's name end as the section requires` IS
    `s 59(1) the name of the company ends as the section requires` (`s 59(1) the name of the company must end with limited or ltd.` `the company is limited` `the company is a private company` `the company is a community interest company` (`coa2 seat a stated fact as an answer` `the company is exempt under section 60`)) `the name ends with limited or ltd.` (`coa2 seat a stated fact as an answer` `the company is a Welsh company`) `the name ends in Welsh with cyfyngedig or cyf.`

@export Under section 61(1), does the continued exemption for a private company limited by shares apply to my company?
GIVEN `the company is a private company limited by shares` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the company a private company limited by shares?
      `it was registered in Great Britain on 25 February 1982` IS A BOOLEAN @desc On 25 February 1982 was the company registered in Great Britain?
      `on 25 February 1982 its name lacked limited by licence` IS A BOOLEAN @desc On 25 February 1982 did its name, by virtue of a licence under section 19 of the Companies Act 1948 (or corresponding earlier legislation), lack the word "limited" and every permitted alternative?
      `it was registered in Northern Ireland on 30 June 1983` IS A BOOLEAN @desc On 30 June 1983 was the company registered in Northern Ireland?
      `on 30 June 1983 its name lacked limited by licence` IS A BOOLEAN @desc On 30 June 1983 did its name, by virtue of a licence under section 19 of the Companies Act (Northern Ireland) 1960 (or corresponding earlier legislation), lack the word "limited" and every permitted alternative?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 61(1), does the old exemption for companies limited by shares apply to my company` IS
    `s 61(1) the section applies to the company` `the company is a private company limited by shares` `it was registered in Great Britain on 25 February 1982` `on 25 February 1982 its name lacked limited by licence` `it was registered in Northern Ireland on 30 June 1983` `on 30 June 1983 its name lacked limited by licence`

@export Under section 61(3), does my company meet the first condition: that its objects are the promotion of commerce, art, science, education, religion, charity or any profession?
GIVEN `the objects are the promotion of commerce, art, science, education, religion, charity or a profession` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are the company's objects the promotion of commerce, art, science, education, religion, charity or any profession, and anything incidental or conducive to any of those objects?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 61(3), does my company meet the first condition for the exemption` IS
    `s 61(3) the first condition is met` `the objects are the promotion of commerce, art, science, education, religion, charity or a profession`

@export Under section 61(4), does my company meet the second condition about its articles?
GIVEN `the articles require income to be applied in promoting the objects` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Do the articles require the company's income to be applied in promoting its objects?
      `the articles prohibit dividends and returns of capital to members` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Do the articles prohibit the payment of dividends, or any return of capital, to its members?
      `the articles send assets on winding up to a body with similar objects` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Do the articles require all the assets otherwise available to members generally to be transferred on winding up to another body with objects similar to its own?
      `the articles send assets on winding up to a charity body` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Do the articles require all those assets to be transferred on winding up to another body the objects of which are the promotion of charity and anything incidental or conducive thereto?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 61(4), does my company meet the second condition for the exemption` IS
    `s 61(4) the second condition is met` `the articles require income to be applied in promoting the objects` `the articles prohibit dividends and returns of capital to members` `the articles send assets on winding up to a body with similar objects` `the articles send assets on winding up to a charity body`

@export Under section 61(2), is my company exempt from the requirement to use "limited" (a continued exemption, so long as the two conditions are met and the name is not changed)?
GIVEN `section 61 applies to the company` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does section 61 apply to the company (see the question on section 61(1))?
      `the first condition is met` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does the company continue to meet the first condition (objects)?
      `the second condition is met` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does the company continue to meet the second condition (articles)?
      `the company has changed its name` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has the company changed its name?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 61(2), is my company exempt from using limited` IS
    `s 61(2) the company is exempt from section 59` (`coa2 seat a stated fact as an answer` `section 61 applies to the company`) (`coa2 seat a stated fact as an answer` `the first condition is met`) (`coa2 seat a stated fact as an answer` `the second condition is met`) `the company has changed its name`

@export Under section 62(1), is my private company limited by guarantee exempt from the requirement to use "limited" (a continued exemption, so long as the two conditions are met and the name is not changed)?
GIVEN `the company is a private company limited by guarantee` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the company a private company limited by guarantee?
      `it was exempt immediately before commencement` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Immediately before the commencement of Part 5 was the company exempt, by virtue of section 30 of the Companies Act 1985 or Article 40 of the Companies (Northern Ireland) Order 1986, from the requirement to have a name including "limited" or a permitted alternative?
      `its name then lacked limited` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did its name then lack the word "limited" and every permitted alternative?
      `the first condition is met` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does the company continue to meet the first condition: are its objects the promotion of commerce, art, science, education, religion, charity or any profession, and anything incidental or conducive?
      `the second condition is met` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does the company continue to meet the second condition: do its articles require income to be applied in promoting its objects, prohibit the payment of dividends to its members, and require its assets on winding up to go to a body with similar objects or to a charity body?
      `the company has changed its name` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has the company changed its name?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 62(1), is my company limited by guarantee exempt from using limited` IS
    `s 62(1) the company is exempt from section 59` `the company is a private company limited by guarantee` `it was exempt immediately before commencement` `its name then lacked limited` (`coa2 seat a stated fact as an answer` `the first condition is met`) (`coa2 seat a stated fact as an answer` `the second condition is met`) `the company has changed its name`

@export Under section 60(1), is my private company exempt from the requirement to end its name with "limited" or a permitted alternative?
GIVEN `the company is a private company` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the company a private company?
      `the company is a charity` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the company a charity?
      `the company is exempted by regulations` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has the Secretary of State's regulations under section 60 exempted the company from the requirement?
      `it meets the conditions in section 61` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does the company meet the conditions in section 61 (continuation of an existing exemption: companies limited by shares)?
      `it meets the conditions in section 62` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does the company meet the conditions in section 62 (continuation of an existing exemption: companies limited by guarantee)?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 60(1), is my private company exempt from using limited` IS
    `s 60(1) the private company is exempt from section 59` `the company is a private company` `the company is a charity` `the company is exempted by regulations` (`coa2 seat a stated fact as an answer` `it meets the conditions in section 61`) (`coa2 seat a stated fact as an answer` `it meets the conditions in section 62`)

@export Under section 60(2), may the registrar refuse to register my private limited company by a name that does not include "limited" (or a permitted alternative)?
GIVEN `the company is a private limited company` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the company a private limited company?
      `the name lacks limited` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does the name lack the word "limited" (or a permitted alternative)?
      `a statement of exemption has been delivered` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has a statement been delivered to the registrar that the company meets the conditions for exemption?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 60(2), may the registrar refuse to register my private limited company by a name without limited` IS
    `s 60(2) the registrar may refuse to register the company by the name` `the company is a private limited company` `the name lacks limited` `a statement of exemption has been delivered`

@export Under section 63(1), may my exempt company amend its articles in the way proposed? (JUST FALSE where the amendment would make it cease to comply with the conditions for exemption)
GIVEN `the company is a private company` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the company a private company?
      `the company is exempt under section 61 or 62` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the company exempt under section 61 or 62 from the requirement to use "limited" (or a permitted alternative)?
      `the name lacks limited` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does the company's name lack "limited" and every permitted alternative?
      `the amendment would end compliance with the conditions` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Would the amendment make the articles cease to comply with the conditions for exemption under that section?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 63(1), may my exempt company amend its articles as proposed` IS
    `s 63(1) the company may amend its articles as proposed` `the company is a private company` (`coa2 seat a stated fact as an answer` `the company is exempt under section 61 or 62`) `the name lacks limited` `the amendment would end compliance with the conditions`

@export Under section 63(2), would I commit an offence if the company amended its articles contrary to section 63(1)? (the company, and every officer in default; a shadow director is treated as an officer)
GIVEN `section 63(1) is contravened` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has section 63(1) been contravened (has the company amended its articles so that it ceases to comply with the conditions for exemption)?
      `who I am` IS A Party @desc What are you in relation to the company? One of: Company, Director, `Company secretary`, `Shadow director`, `Officer in default`, Member, `Subscriber to the memorandum`, Auditor, Creditor, `Debenture holder`, `Person with significant control`, Registrar, `Secretary of State`, Court, `Takeover Panel`, `Competent authority`.
      `I am in default` IS A BOOLEAN @desc If you are an officer, are you in default (see section 1121)?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 63(2), could I commit an offence if my company amends its articles contrary to section 63(1)` IS
    `s 63(2) the person commits an offence` `section 63(1) is contravened` `who I am` (`coa2 seat a stated fact as an answer` `I am in default`)

@export Under section 63(3), what is the most the company or an officer in default can be fined on summary conviction?
GIVETH A STRING
DECIDE `Under section 63(3), what is the penalty if my company is convicted of the offence` IS
    `coa2 seat describe a penalty` `s 63(3) the penalty on summary conviction`

@export Under section 63(3), what is the most the daily default fine can be, in pounds, on the first wording (one-tenth of level 5 on the standard scale)?
GIVEN `the amount of level 5 on the standard scale` IS A NUMBER @desc What is the amount in pounds of level 5 on the standard scale?
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `Under section 63(3), what is the daily default fine in pounds on the first wording` IS
    `s 63(3) the daily default fine in pounds on the first wording` `the amount of level 5 on the standard scale`

@export Under section 63(3), what is the most the daily default fine can be, in pounds, on the second wording (one-tenth of the greater of 5,000 pounds or level 4 on the standard scale)?
GIVEN `the amount of level 4 on the standard scale` IS A NUMBER @desc What is the amount in pounds of level 4 on the standard scale?
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `Under section 63(3), what is the daily default fine in pounds on the second wording` IS
    `s 63(3) the daily default fine in pounds on the second wording` `the amount of level 4 on the standard scale`

@export Under section 64(1), may the Secretary of State direct my company, whose name does not include "limited", to change its name?
GIVEN `the name lacks limited` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does the name lack "limited" and every permitted alternative?
      `it appears the company has ceased to be entitled to an exemption under section 60(1)(a) or (b)` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does it appear to the Secretary of State that the company has ceased to be entitled to exemption under section 60(1)(a) (charity) or (b) (regulations)?
      `the company is within section 61 or 62` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the company within section 61 or 62?
      `it appears the company carried on other business` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does it appear to the Secretary of State that the company has carried on any business other than the promotion of its objects?
      `it appears the company acted inconsistently with its required articles` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does it appear to the Secretary of State that the company has acted inconsistently with the provision its articles are required to have?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 64(1), may the Secretary of State direct my company to change its name` IS
    `s 64(1) the Secretary of State may direct the company to change its name` `the name lacks limited` `it appears the company has ceased to be entitled to an exemption under section 60(1)(a) or (b)` `the company is within section 61 or 62` `it appears the company carried on other business` `it appears the company acted inconsistently with its required articles`

@export Under section 64(2A), is the period the Secretary of State's direction gives the company to change its name long enough (at least 28 days beginning with the date of the direction)?
GIVEN `the date of the direction` IS A DATE @desc On what date was the direction given?
      `the last day of the period` IS A DATE @desc What is the last day of the period the direction allows?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 64(2A), is the period the direction gives us long enough` IS
    `s 64(2A) the period meets the requirement of subsection (2A)` `the date of the direction` `the last day of the period`

@export Under section 64(2B), may the Secretary of State extend the period by a further direction in writing given on this date?
GIVEN `the further direction is in writing` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the further direction in writing?
      `the date of the further direction` IS A DATE @desc On what date is the further direction given?
      `the last day of the period` IS A DATE @desc What is the last day of the period for the time being specified?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 64(2B), may the Secretary of State extend the period by a further direction` IS
    `s 64(2B) the Secretary of State may give a further direction extending the period` `the further direction is in writing` `the date of the further direction` `the last day of the period`

@export Under section 64(3), may the directors change the company's name by resolution of the directors in order to comply with the direction?
GIVEN `the change is made to comply with the direction` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the change of name made in order to comply with a direction under section 64?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 64(3), may the directors change the name by resolution to comply with the direction` IS
    `s 64(3) the company may change its name by resolution of the directors` `the change is made to comply with the direction`

@export Under section 64(4), must the company give notice to the registrar of a change of name made by resolution of the directors?
GIVEN `a resolution of the directors has been passed to comply with the direction` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has a resolution of the directors been passed to change the name in accordance with section 64(3)?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 64(4), must we give notice to the registrar of the change` IS
    `s 64(4) the company must give notice to the registrar of the change` `a resolution of the directors has been passed to comply with the direction`

@export Under section 64(5), would I commit an offence if the company failed to comply with the direction? (the company, and every officer in default)
GIVEN `the company fails to comply with the direction` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has the company failed to comply with a direction under section 64?
      `who I am` IS A Party @desc What are you in relation to the company? One of: Company, Director, `Company secretary`, `Shadow director`, `Officer in default`, Member, `Subscriber to the memorandum`, Auditor, Creditor, `Debenture holder`, `Person with significant control`, Registrar, `Secretary of State`, Court, `Takeover Panel`, `Competent authority`.
      `I am in default` IS A BOOLEAN @desc If you are an officer, are you in default (see section 1121)?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 64(5), could I commit an offence if the company fails to comply with the direction` IS
    `s 64(5) the person commits an offence` `the company fails to comply with the direction` `who I am` (`coa2 seat a stated fact as an answer` `I am in default`)

@export Under section 64(6), what is the most the company or an officer in default can be fined on summary conviction for failing to comply with the direction?
GIVETH A STRING
DECIDE `Under section 64(6), what is the penalty for failing to comply with the direction` IS
    `coa2 seat describe a penalty` `s 64(6) the penalty on summary conviction`

@export Under section 64(7), do we need the Secretary of State's approval to change the name later to one that does not include "limited"?
GIVEN `the company has been directed under section 64` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has the company been directed to change its name under section 64?
      `the new name lacks limited` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does the new name lack "limited" and every permitted alternative?
      `the change is on re-registration or conversion to a community interest company` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the change of name made on re-registration or on conversion to a community interest company?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 64(7), do we need the approval of the Secretary of State to drop limited from the name later` IS
    `s 64(7) the approval of the Secretary of State is required for the change of name` `the company has been directed under section 64` `the new name lacks limited` `the change is on re-registration or conversion to a community interest company`

@export Under section 65(3), may my company be registered by a name that consists of or includes an indication of company type or legal form that the regulations prohibit?
GIVEN `the name includes something prohibited by the regulations` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does the name consist of or include anything prohibited by regulations under section 65?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 65(3), may my company be registered by a name that includes something the regulations prohibit` IS
    `s 65(3) the company may be registered by the name` `the name includes something prohibited by the regulations`

§§ `Part 5, Chapter 3: a name too like another (ss 66 to 74)`

@export Under section 66(1), may my company be registered by a name that is the same as another name in the registrar's index of company names?
GIVEN `the name is the same as another in the index` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the name the same as another name appearing in the registrar's index of company names (disregarding what the regulations say is to be disregarded)?
      `regulations permit registration in the circumstances` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Do regulations under section 66(4) permit registration by the name in the circumstances (or with the consent given)?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 66(1), may my company be registered by a name that is the same as one on the registrar's index` IS
    `s 66(1) the company may be registered by the name` `the name is the same as another in the index` `regulations permit registration in the circumstances`

@export Under section 67(1), may the Secretary of State direct my company to change its name because it was registered in a name the same as, or too like, a name in the index?
GIVEN `the name is the same as an indexed name` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Was the company registered in a name that is the same as a name in (a) or (b)?
      `in the Secretary of State's opinion the name is too like an indexed name` IS A BOOLEAN @desc In the Secretary of State's opinion is the name too like a name in (a) or (b)?
      `the other name was in the index at the time of registration` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did the other name appear in the registrar's index of company names at the time of the registration?
      `the other name should have been in the index at that time` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Should the other name have appeared in that index at that time?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 67(1), may the Secretary of State direct my company to change its name because it is too like another` IS
    `s 67(1) the Secretary of State may direct the company to change its name` `the name is the same as an indexed name` `in the Secretary of State's opinion the name is too like an indexed name` `the other name was in the index at the time of registration` `the other name should have been in the index at that time`

@export Under section 68(2)(a), was the Secretary of State's direction to change my company's name given within twelve months of the company's registration by the name?
GIVEN `the date of registration by the name` IS A DATE @desc On what date was the company registered by the name?
      `the date of the direction` IS A DATE @desc On what date was the direction given?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 68(2)(a), was the direction given in time` IS
    `s 68(2)(a) the direction is given within twelve months of the company's registration by the name` `the date of registration by the name` `the date of the direction`

@export Under section 68(2A), is the period the direction gives the company to change its name at least 28 days beginning with the date of the direction?
GIVEN `the date of the direction` IS A DATE @desc On what date was the direction given?
      `the last day of the period` IS A DATE @desc What is the last day of the period the direction allows?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 68(2A), is the period the direction gives us long enough` IS
    `s 68(2A) the period meets the requirement of subsection (2A)` `the date of the direction` `the last day of the period`

@export Under section 68(3), may the Secretary of State extend the period by a further direction given on this date?
GIVEN `the date of the further direction` IS A DATE @desc On what date is the further direction given?
      `the last day of the period` IS A DATE @desc What is the last day of the period for the time being specified?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 68(3), may the Secretary of State extend the period by a further direction` IS
    `s 68(3) the Secretary of State may give a further direction extending the period` `the date of the further direction` `the last day of the period`

@export Under section 68(5), would I commit an offence if the company failed to comply with the direction? (the company, and every officer in default; a shadow director is treated as an officer)
GIVEN `the company fails to comply with the direction` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has the company failed to comply with the direction?
      `who I am` IS A Party @desc What are you in relation to the company? One of: Company, Director, `Company secretary`, `Shadow director`, `Officer in default`, Member, `Subscriber to the memorandum`, Auditor, Creditor, `Debenture holder`, `Person with significant control`, Registrar, `Secretary of State`, Court, `Takeover Panel`, `Competent authority`.
      `I am in default` IS A BOOLEAN @desc If you are an officer, are you in default (see section 1121)?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 68(5), could I commit an offence if the company fails to comply with the direction` IS
    `s 68(5) the person commits an offence` `the company fails to comply with the direction` `who I am` (`coa2 seat a stated fact as an answer` `I am in default`)

@export Under section 68(6), what is the most the company or an officer in default can be fined on summary conviction?
GIVETH A STRING
DECIDE `Under section 68(6), what is the penalty for failing to comply with the direction` IS
    `coa2 seat describe a penalty` `s 68(6) the penalty on summary conviction`

@export Under section 69(1), may I object to a company's registered name because it is the same as, or too like, a name in which I have goodwill?
GIVEN `the name is the same as a name associated with me in which I have goodwill` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the company's name the same as a name associated with you in which you have goodwill?
      `the name is similar enough to mislead the public about a connection with me` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the name sufficiently similar to such a name that its use in the United Kingdom or elsewhere would be likely to mislead members of the public by suggesting a connection between the company and you?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 69(1), may I object to a company's registered name` IS
    `s 69(1) the applicant may object to the company's registered name` `the name is the same as a name associated with me in which I have goodwill` `the name is similar enough to mislead the public about a connection with me`

@export Under section 69(7), is what I rely on "goodwill"? (the Act says goodwill includes reputation of any description)
GIVEN `it is reputation of any description` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it a reputation of any description?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 69(7), is what I rely on goodwill` IS
    `s 69(7) the interest is goodwill` `it is reputation of any description`

@export Under section 69(2), is my objection made as the Act requires (by application to a company names adjudicator)?
GIVEN `the objection is made by application to a company names adjudicator` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the objection made by application to a company names adjudicator?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 69(2), is my objection made in the way the Act requires` IS
    `s 69(2) the objection is made as the subsection requires` `the objection is made by application to a company names adjudicator`

@export Under section 69(3), may I be joined as a respondent to an application against a company's name?
GIVEN `I am or was a member when the name was registered` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are you a member, or were you a member at the time at which the name was registered?
      `I am or was a director when the name was registered` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are you a director, or were you a director at the time at which the name was registered?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 69(3), may I be joined as a respondent to an application` IS
    `s 69(3) the person may be joined as a respondent` `I am or was a member when the name was registered` `I am or was a director when the name was registered`

@export Under section 69(4), if the objection's ground is established, will the objection be upheld because the respondents show none of the defences?
GIVEN `the ground in section 69(1) is established` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the ground in section 69(1)(a) or (b) established?
      `the name was registered before the activities on which goodwill is based` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Do the respondents show that the name was registered before the commencement of the activities on which the applicant relies to show goodwill?
      `the name was registered in a company formation business and is for sale on standard terms` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Do the respondents show that the name was registered in the ordinary course of a company formation business and the company is available for sale to the applicant on the standard terms of that business?
      `the name was adopted in good faith` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Do the respondents show that the name was adopted in good faith?
      `the applicant's interests are not significantly affected` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Do the respondents show that the interests of the applicant are not adversely affected to any significant extent?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 69(4), will my objection be upheld at the first stage` IS
    `s 69(4) the objection is upheld under subsection (4)` `the ground in section 69(1) is established` `the name was registered before the activities on which goodwill is based` `the name was registered in a company formation business and is for sale on standard terms` `the name was adopted in good faith` `the applicant's interests are not significantly affected`

@export Under section 69(5), will my objection be upheld anyway because the main purpose in registering the name was to obtain money or to block me?
GIVEN `the facts in section 69(4)(a) or (c) are established` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are the facts mentioned in section 69(4)(a) (name registered before the activities) or (c) (company formation business) established?
      `I show the main purpose was to obtain money or to prevent my registering the name` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Do you show that the main purpose of the respondents (or any of them) in registering the name was to obtain money (or other consideration) from you or prevent you from registering the name?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 69(5), will my objection be upheld despite a defence` IS
    `s 69(5) the objection is nevertheless upheld` `the facts in section 69(4)(a) or (c) are established` `I show the main purpose was to obtain money or to prevent my registering the name`

@export Under section 69(6), will my objection be dismissed because it is not upheld under subsection (4) or (5)?
GIVEN `the objection is upheld under subsection (4)` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the objection upheld under section 69(4)?
      `the objection is upheld under subsection (5)` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the objection upheld under section 69(5)?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 69(6), will my objection be dismissed` IS
    `s 69(6) the objection is dismissed` (`coa2 seat a stated fact as an answer` `the objection is upheld under subsection (4)`) (`coa2 seat a stated fact as an answer` `the objection is upheld under subsection (5)`)

@export Under section 72(1), was the company names adjudicator's decision and reasons made available to the public within 90 days of determining the application?
GIVEN `the date of determining the application` IS A DATE @desc On what date was the application under section 69 determined?
      `the date the decision was made available` IS A DATE @desc On what date were the decision and reasons made available to the public?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 72(1), was the adjudicator's decision made available to the public in time` IS
    `s 72(1) the decision was made available within 90 days of the determination` `the date of determining the application` `the date the decision was made available`

@export Under section 73(1), if the application under section 69 is upheld, must the adjudicator make an order requiring my company to change its name?
GIVEN `the application under section 69 is upheld` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has the application under section 69 been upheld?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 73(1), must the adjudicator make an order against my company` IS
    `s 73(1) the adjudicator must make an order` `the application under section 69 is upheld`

@export Under section 73(2), is the name I propose an "offending name" (one that by its similarity to the applicant's name would be likely to be the subject of a direction under section 67 or give rise to a further application)?
GIVEN `the name is similar to the applicant's name` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the name similar to the name associated with the applicant in which he claims goodwill?
      `it would be likely to be directed to be changed under section 67` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Would it be likely to be the subject of a direction under section 67?
      `it would be likely to give rise to a further application under section 69` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Would it be likely to give rise to a further application under section 69?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 73(2), is the name I propose an offending name` IS
    `s 73(2) the name is an offending name` `the name is similar to the applicant's name` `it would be likely to be directed to be changed under section 67` `it would be likely to give rise to a further application under section 69`

@export Under section 73(3), how may the adjudicator's order be enforced in this place?
GIVEN `the place where the order is enforced` IS A `Place of registration` @desc Where is the order to be enforced? One of: `England and Wales`, Scotland, `Northern Ireland`.
GIVETH A `s 73(3) way of enforcing the order`
DECIDE `Under section 73(3), how may the adjudicator's order be enforced` IS
    `s 73(3) the order may be enforced` `the place where the order is enforced`

@export Under section 73(4), may the adjudicator determine a new name for my company because its name was not changed in accordance with the order by the specified date?
GIVEN `the company has a new certificate of incorporation` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has a new certificate of incorporation been issued on the change of name?
      `the date the new certificate was issued` IS A DATE @desc On what date was the new certificate issued? (any date if none has been issued)
      `the date the order requires the name to be changed by` IS A DATE @desc By what date does the order require the name to be changed?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 73(4), may the adjudicator determine a new name for my company` IS
    `s 73(4) the adjudicator may determine a new name for the company` (`s 73(6) the name is changed in accordance with the order by the specified date` (`coa2 seat a date if it has happened` `the company has a new certificate of incorporation` `the date the new certificate was issued`) `the date the order requires the name to be changed by`)

@export Under section 74(1), may I appeal to the court from this decision of a company names adjudicator?
GIVEN `the decision is to uphold or dismiss an application under section 69` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the decision a decision of a company names adjudicator to uphold or dismiss an application under section 69?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 74(1), may I appeal to the court from the adjudicator's decision` IS
    `s 74(1) an appeal lies to the court from the decision` `the decision is to uphold or dismiss an application under section 69`

@export Under section 74(2), is my notice of appeal against a decision upholding the application given in time (before the date the order sets for the name change)?
GIVEN `the decision upholds the application` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does the decision uphold the application?
      `the date of notice of appeal` IS A DATE @desc On what date is notice of appeal given?
      `the date specified in the order` IS A DATE @desc What is the date specified in the adjudicator's order by which the name is to be changed?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 74(2), is my notice of appeal in time` IS
    `s 74(2) notice of appeal is given in time` `the decision upholds the application` `the date of notice of appeal` `the date specified in the order`

@export Under section 74(3), is the adjudicator's order suspended because notice of appeal has been given against a decision upholding the application?
GIVEN `the decision upholds the application` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does the decision uphold the application?
      `notice of appeal has been given` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has notice of appeal been given against the decision?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 74(3), is the order suspended while I appeal` IS
    `s 74(3) the effect of the adjudicator's order is suspended` `the decision upholds the application` `notice of appeal has been given`

