@export Under section 76B(11), would I commit an offence if the company failed to comply with a direction under section 76B(1)? (the company, and every officer in default; a shadow director is treated as an officer)
GIVEN `the company fails to comply with the direction` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has the company failed to comply with the direction under subsection (1)?
      `who I am` IS A Party @desc What are you in relation to the company? One of: Company, Director, `Company secretary`, `Shadow director`, `Officer in default`, Member, `Subscriber to the memorandum`, Auditor, Creditor, `Debenture holder`, `Person with significant control`, Registrar, `Secretary of State`, Court, `Takeover Panel`, `Competent authority`.
      `I am in default` IS A BOOLEAN @desc If you are an officer, are you in default (see section 1121)?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 76B(11), could I commit an offence if the company fails to comply with the direction` IS
    `s 76B(11) the person commits an offence` `the company fails to comply with the direction` `who I am` (`coa2 seat a stated fact as an answer` `I am in default`)

@export Under section 76C(1), may the registrar determine a new name for my company because in the registrar's opinion its name consists of or includes computer code?
GIVEN `in the registrar's opinion the name includes computer code` IS A BOOLEAN @desc In the registrar's opinion, does the company's registered name consist of or include computer code?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 76C(1), may the registrar change my company's name because it contains computer code` IS
    `s 76C(1) the registrar may determine a new name for the company and remove the old name from the register` `in the registrar's opinion the name includes computer code`

@export Under section 76D(1), may the registrar determine a new name for my company because it failed to comply with a direction to change its name?
GIVEN `the company fails to comply with a direction to change its name` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has the company failed to comply with a direction to change its name?
      `the direction was one of those listed` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Was the direction one under section 64, 67, 75, 76, 76A or 76B?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 76D(1), may the registrar change my company's name because we did not comply with a direction` IS
    `s 76D(1) the registrar may determine a new name for the company` `the company fails to comply with a direction to change its name` (`coa2 seat a stated fact as an answer` `the direction was one of those listed`)

@export Under section 76E(1), does Part 5 not prevent the company being registered by the name because the Secretary of State is satisfied it is necessary for national security or to prevent or detect serious crime?
GIVEN `the Secretary of State is satisfied registration is necessary in the interests of national security` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the Secretary of State satisfied that registration by the name is necessary in the interests of national security?
      `the Secretary of State is satisfied registration is necessary to prevent or detect crime` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the Secretary of State satisfied that registration is necessary for the purposes of preventing or detecting the crime in question?
      `the crime is serious` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the crime serious (see the question on section 76E(2)(b))?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 76E(1), can Part 5 be disapplied so that my company is registered by the name` IS
    `s 76E(1) Part 5 does not prevent the registration of the company by the name` `the Secretary of State is satisfied registration is necessary in the interests of national security` `the Secretary of State is satisfied registration is necessary to prevent or detect crime` (`coa2 seat a stated fact as an answer` `the crime is serious`)

@export Under section 76E(2)(b), is this crime "serious"? (a maximum sentence of 3 years or more, or violence, substantial financial gain or a large number of persons in pursuit of a common purpose)
GIVEN `the greatest maximum term of imprisonment in years` IS A NUMBER @desc What is the greatest maximum term of imprisonment, in years, for the offence in any part of the United Kingdom?
      `the conduct involves the use of violence` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does the conduct involve the use of violence?
      `the conduct results in substantial financial gain` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does the conduct result in substantial financial gain?
      `the conduct is by a large number of persons in pursuit of a common purpose` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the conduct conduct by a large number of persons in pursuit of a common purpose?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 76E(2)(b), is this crime serious` IS
    `s 76E(2)(b) the crime is serious` `the greatest maximum term of imprisonment in years` `the conduct involves the use of violence` `the conduct results in substantial financial gain` `the conduct is by a large number of persons in pursuit of a common purpose`

§§ `Part 5, Chapters 5 and 6: changing the name and trading disclosures (ss 77 to 85)`

@export Under section 77(1), may my company change its name by special resolution?
GIVEN `the resolution is a special resolution` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the resolution a special resolution (see section 283)?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 77(1), may my company change its name by special resolution` IS
    `s 77(1) the company may change its name in that way` `s 77(1)(a) by special resolution` (`coa2 seat a stated fact as an answer` `the resolution is a special resolution`) FALSE

@export Under section 77(1), may my company change its name by other means provided for by its articles?
GIVEN `the articles provide for other means` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Do the company's articles provide for another means of changing its name?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 77(1), may my company change its name by other means in its articles` IS
    `s 77(1) the company may change its name in that way` `s 77(1)(b) by other means provided for by the company's articles` NOTHING `the articles provide for other means`

@export Under section 78(1), must the company give notice to the registrar of a change of name agreed by special resolution (as well as sending a copy of the resolution)?
GIVEN `the resolution is a special resolution` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the resolution a special resolution (see section 283)?
      `a change of name has been agreed by that resolution` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has a change of name been agreed by that resolution?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 78(1), must we give notice to the registrar of a change of name agreed by special resolution` IS
    `s 78(1) the company must give notice to the registrar` (`coa2 seat a stated fact as an answer` `the resolution is a special resolution`) `a change of name has been agreed by that resolution`

@export Under section 78(2), where the change of name is conditional on an event, must the notice say that it is conditional and whether the event has occurred?
GIVEN `the change is conditional on an event` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the change of name by special resolution conditional on the occurrence of an event?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 78(2), must the notice say that the change is conditional` IS
    `s 78(2)(a) the notice must specify that the change is conditional` `the change is conditional on an event`

@export Under section 78(3), must the company give notice to the registrar when the event occurs?
GIVEN `the notice said the event had not occurred` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did the notice state that the event had not occurred?
      `the event has occurred` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has the event occurred?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 78(3), must we tell the registrar when the event occurs` IS
    `s 78(3)(b) the company must give notice to the registrar stating that the event has occurred` `the notice said the event had not occurred` `the event has occurred`

@export Under section 79(1), must the company give notice to the registrar, with a statement, of a change of name made by other means provided for by its articles?
GIVEN `the name was changed by means provided for in the articles` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has the company's name been changed by other means provided for by its articles?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 79(1), must we give notice to the registrar of a change of name made under our articles` IS
    `s 79(1)(a) the company must give notice to the registrar` `the name was changed by means provided for in the articles`

@export Under section 80(1), must the registrar enter the new name on the register in place of the former name (where he has notice of the change and is satisfied it meets the requirements, or has determined the new name under section 76C or 76D)?
GIVEN `the registrar has received notice of the change` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has the registrar received notice of the change of the company's name?
      `the registrar is satisfied the new name complies with Part 5` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the registrar satisfied that the new name complies with the requirements of Part 5?
      `the registrar is satisfied the Acts and articles were complied with` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the registrar satisfied that the requirements of the Companies Acts, and any relevant requirements of the articles, with respect to a change of name are complied with?
      `the registrar has determined the new name under section 76C or 76D` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has the registrar determined the new name under section 76C or 76D?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 80(1), must the registrar enter our new name on the register` IS
    `s 80(2) the registrar must enter the new name on the register in place of the former name` (`s 80(1) this section applies` `the registrar has received notice of the change` `the registrar is satisfied the new name complies with Part 5` `the registrar is satisfied the Acts and articles were complied with` `the registrar has determined the new name under section 76C or 76D`)

@export Under section 81(1), has the change of the company's name taken effect on this day (from the date the new certificate of incorporation is issued)?
GIVEN `the new certificate has been issued` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has the new certificate of incorporation been issued?
      `the date the certificate was issued` IS A DATE @desc On what date was it issued? (any date if it has not been issued)
      `the day` IS A DATE @desc On what day do you ask?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 81(1), has the change of our name taken effect on this day` IS
    `s 81(1) the change of name has effect on the day` (`coa2 seat a date if it has happened` `the new certificate has been issued` `the date the certificate was issued`) `the day`

@export Under section 81(2), does a change of name affect the company's rights or obligations, or make legal proceedings by or against it defective?
GIVEN `it is a right or obligation of the company, or proceedings by or against it` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it a right or obligation of the company, or legal proceedings by or against it?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 81(2), does the change of name affect our rights or obligations or legal proceedings` IS
    `s 81(2) the change of name affects the right, the obligation or the proceedings` `it is a right or obligation of the company, or proceedings by or against it`

@export Under section 83, must proceedings brought against me by a company be dismissed because, when the contract was made, it was in breach of the trading disclosure regulations?
GIVEN `the proceedings are brought by a company to which section 82 applies` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are the proceedings brought by a company to which section 82 (requirement to disclose company name etc) applies?
      `the proceedings are to enforce a right arising out of a contract made in the course of a business` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are they brought to enforce a right arising out of a contract made in the course of a business?
      `the company was in breach of the regulations when the contract was made` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Was the company, at the time the contract was made, in breach of the regulations under section 82 in respect of that business?
      `I show a claim I could not pursue because of the breach` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Do you show that you have a claim against the claimant arising out of the contract that you have been unable to pursue by reason of its breach?
      `I show financial loss because of the breach` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Do you show that you have suffered some financial loss in connection with the contract by reason of its breach?
      `the court is satisfied it is just and equitable to let the proceedings continue` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the court satisfied that it is just and equitable to permit the proceedings to continue?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 83, must proceedings by a company be dismissed because it did not make the required disclosure` IS
    `s 83(2) the proceedings shall be dismissed` (`s 83(1) this section applies to the proceedings` `the proceedings are brought by a company to which section 82 applies` `the proceedings are to enforce a right arising out of a contract made in the course of a business` `the company was in breach of the regulations when the contract was made`) `I show a claim I could not pursue because of the breach` `I show financial loss because of the breach` `the court is satisfied it is just and equitable to let the proceedings continue`

@export Under section 85(1), is this difference between two company names left out of account when considering a name for the purposes of Chapter 6?
GIVEN `kind of difference` IS A `s 85(1) kind of difference between names` @desc Which difference? One of: `s 85(1)(a) whether upper or lower case characters (or a combination of the two) are used`, `s 85(1)(b) whether diacritical marks or punctuation are present or absent`, `s 85(1)(c) whether the name is in the same format or style as is specified under section 57(1)(b) for the purposes of registration`, `s 85(1) any other difference`.
      `there is no real likelihood the names would be taken to be different` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is there no real likelihood of names differing only in those respects being taken to be different names?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 85(1), is this difference between two names left out of account` IS
    `s 85(1) no account is taken of the difference` `kind of difference` `there is no real likelihood the names would be taken to be different`

§§ `Part 6: the registered office and the registered email address (ss 86 to 88B)`

@export Under section 86, is this address the company's registered office?
GIVEN `the address is the address entered in the register as the company's registered office` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the address the one entered in the register as the company's registered office?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 86, is this address my company's registered office` IS
    `s 86 the company has its registered office at the address` `the address is the address entered in the register as the company's registered office`

@export Under section 86(2), is my company's registered office address an "appropriate address"?
GIVEN `a document delivered by hand or by post would be expected to reach a person acting for the company` IS A BOOLEAN @desc In the ordinary course of events, would a document addressed to the company and delivered there by hand or by post be expected to come to the attention of a person acting on behalf of the company?
      `delivery there can be recorded by an acknowledgement` IS A BOOLEAN @desc In the ordinary course of events, is the delivery of documents there capable of being recorded by the obtaining of an acknowledgement of delivery?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 86(2), is my company's registered office address an appropriate address` IS
    `s 86(2) the address is an appropriate address` `a document delivered by hand or by post would be expected to reach a person acting for the company` `delivery there can be recorded by an acknowledgement`

@export Under section 86(1), must my company ensure that its registered office is at all times at an appropriate address? (not while the address is a default address nominated by the registrar)
GIVEN `the address is a default address nominated under section 1097A(3)(h)` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the address of the registered office, for the period in question, a default address nominated by virtue of section 1097A(3)(h)?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 86(1), must my company ensure its registered office is at an appropriate address` IS
    `s 86(1) the company must ensure that its registered office is at an appropriate address` (`coa2 seat a stated fact as an answer` `the address is a default address nominated under section 1097A(3)(h)`)

@export Under section 86(3), would I commit an offence if the company failed, without reasonable excuse, to keep its registered office at an appropriate address? (the company, and every officer in default)
GIVEN `the company fails to comply` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has the company failed to comply with section 86?
      `the company has a reasonable excuse` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does the company have a reasonable excuse for the failure?
      `who I am` IS A Party @desc What are you in relation to the company? One of: Company, Director, `Company secretary`, `Shadow director`, `Officer in default`, Member, `Subscriber to the memorandum`, Auditor, Creditor, `Debenture holder`, `Person with significant control`, Registrar, `Secretary of State`, Court, `Takeover Panel`, `Competent authority`.
      `I am in default` IS A BOOLEAN @desc If you are an officer, are you in default (see section 1121)?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 86(3), could I commit an offence if the company's registered office is not at an appropriate address` IS
    `s 86(3) the person commits an offence` `the company fails to comply` `the company has a reasonable excuse` `who I am` (`coa2 seat a stated fact as an answer` `I am in default`)

@export Under section 86(4), what is the most the company or an officer in default can be fined on summary conviction in this place?
GIVEN `the place where the person is convicted` IS A `Place of registration` @desc Where is the person convicted? One of: `England and Wales`, Scotland, `Northern Ireland`.
GIVETH A STRING
DECIDE `Under section 86(4), what is the penalty for failing to keep the registered office at an appropriate address` IS
    `coa2 seat describe a penalty` (`s 86(4) the penalty on summary conviction` `the place where the person is convicted`)

@export Under section 87(2), may a person still validly serve a document on the company at its previously registered address on this day (until 14 days after the change is registered)?
GIVEN `the notice of the change has been registered` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has the registrar registered the notice of the change of the registered office address?
      `the date it was registered` IS A DATE @desc On what date was it registered? (any date if it has not been registered)
      `the day` IS A DATE @desc On what day was or will the document be served?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 87(2), may a document still be validly served at our old registered office address` IS
    `s 87(2) a person may validly serve a document on the company at the address previously registered on the day` (`coa2 seat a date if it has happened` `the notice of the change has been registered` `the date it was registered`) `the day`

@export Under section 87(3), may the company act on the change of its registered office address from this date (not more than 14 days after the notice is given)?
GIVEN `the date the notice is given` IS A DATE @desc On what date was notice of the change given to the registrar?
      `the date the company will act on the change` IS A DATE @desc From what date does the company determine to act on the change?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 87(3), may the company act on the change of address from this date` IS
    `s 87(3) the company may act on the change as from that date` `the date the notice is given` `the date the company will act on the change`

@export Under section 87(4), is the company protected from being treated as having failed in a duty at its registered office because it unavoidably ceased to perform it?
GIVEN `the company unavoidably ceased to perform the duty at its registered office` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did the company unavoidably cease to perform at its registered office a duty to keep documents available for inspection there?
      `it was not practicable to give prior notice of a change of address` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Was it not practicable to give prior notice to the registrar of a change in the address of its registered office?
      `the company resumed performing the duty at other premises as soon as practicable` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did the company resume performance of the duty at other premises as soon as practicable?
      `the date it resumed` IS A DATE @desc On what date did it resume performance?
      `the date it notified the registrar` IS A DATE @desc On what date did it give notice to the registrar of the change in the situation of its registered office?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 87(4), is the company protected when it unavoidably could not keep its documents at the registered office` IS
    `s 87(4) the company is protected from being treated as having failed to comply with the duty` `the company unavoidably ceased to perform the duty at its registered office` `it was not practicable to give prior notice of a change of address` `the company resumed performing the duty at other premises as soon as practicable` `the date it resumed` `the date it notified the registrar`

@export Under section 88(1), is my company a "Welsh company"?
GIVEN `the register states the registered office is to be situated in Wales` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does the register state that the company's registered office is to be situated in Wales?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 88(1), is my company a Welsh company` IS
    `s 88(1) the company is a Welsh company` `the register states the registered office is to be situated in Wales`

@export Under section 88(2), may my company, whose registered office is in Wales and whose register entry says England and Wales, by special resolution require the register to say Wales?
GIVEN `the registered office is in Wales` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the company's registered office in Wales?
      `the register states England and Wales` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does the register state that its registered office is to be situated in England and Wales?
      `the resolution is a special resolution` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the resolution a special resolution (see section 283)?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 88(2), may my company by special resolution have the register say Wales` IS
    `s 88(2) the company may by special resolution require the register to state that its registered office is to be situated in Wales` `the registered office is in Wales` `the register states England and Wales` (`coa2 seat a stated fact as an answer` `the resolution is a special resolution`)

@export Under section 88(3), may my company, whose registered office is in Wales and whose register entry says Wales, by special resolution require the register to say England and Wales?
GIVEN `the registered office is in Wales` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the company's registered office in Wales?
      `the register states Wales` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does the register state that its registered office is to be situated in Wales?
      `the resolution is a special resolution` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the resolution a special resolution (see section 283)?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 88(3), may my company by special resolution have the register say England and Wales` IS
    `s 88(3) the company may by special resolution require the register to state that its registered office is to be situated in England and Wales` `the registered office is in Wales` `the register states Wales` (`coa2 seat a stated fact as an answer` `the resolution is a special resolution`)

@export Under section 88(4), must the company give notice to the registrar when it passes a resolution about the Welsh or England and Wales register entry?
GIVEN `the company has passed a resolution under section 88` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has the company passed a resolution under section 88?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 88(4), must we give notice to the registrar of a resolution about the Welsh register entry` IS
    `s 88(4) the company must give notice to the registrar` `the company has passed a resolution under section 88`

@export Under section 88A(2), is my company's registered email address an "appropriate email address"?
GIVEN `emails sent by the registrar would be expected to reach a person acting for the company` IS A BOOLEAN @desc In the ordinary course of events, would emails sent to it by the registrar be expected to come to the attention of a person acting on behalf of the company?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 88A(2), is my company's registered email address an appropriate email address` IS
    `s 88A(2) the email address is an appropriate email address` `emails sent by the registrar would be expected to reach a person acting for the company`

@export Under section 88A(3), would I commit an offence if the company failed, without reasonable excuse, to keep an appropriate registered email address? (the company, and every officer in default)
GIVEN `the company fails to comply` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has the company failed to comply with section 88A?
      `the company has a reasonable excuse` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does the company have a reasonable excuse for the failure?
      `who I am` IS A Party @desc What are you in relation to the company? One of: Company, Director, `Company secretary`, `Shadow director`, `Officer in default`, Member, `Subscriber to the memorandum`, Auditor, Creditor, `Debenture holder`, `Person with significant control`, Registrar, `Secretary of State`, Court, `Takeover Panel`, `Competent authority`.
      `I am in default` IS A BOOLEAN @desc If you are an officer, are you in default (see section 1121)?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 88A(3), could I commit an offence if the company's registered email address is not appropriate` IS
    `s 88A(3) the person commits an offence` `the company fails to comply` `the company has a reasonable excuse` `who I am` (`coa2 seat a stated fact as an answer` `I am in default`)

@export Under section 88A(4), what is the most the company or an officer in default can be fined on summary conviction in this place?
GIVEN `the place where the person is convicted` IS A `Place of registration` @desc Where is the person convicted? One of: `England and Wales`, Scotland, `Northern Ireland`.
GIVETH A STRING
DECIDE `Under section 88A(4), what is the penalty for not keeping an appropriate registered email address` IS
    `coa2 seat describe a penalty` (`s 88A(4) the penalty on summary conviction` `the place where the person is convicted`)

@export Under section 88B(3), has the change of the company's registered email address taken effect on this day (upon the notice being registered)?
GIVEN `the notice has been registered` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has the registrar registered the notice of the change?
      `the date it was registered` IS A DATE @desc On what date was it registered? (any date if it has not been registered)
      `the day` IS A DATE @desc On what day do you ask?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 88B(3), has the change of our registered email address taken effect on this day` IS
    `s 88B(3) the change takes effect on the day` (`coa2 seat a date if it has happened` `the notice has been registered` `the date it was registered`) `the day`

§§ `Part 7: re-registration (ss 89 to 111)`
-- Ask when the company wants to change its status.

@export Under section 89, may my company alter its status in this way by re-registration under Part 7?
GIVEN `the company is a public company` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the company a public company?
      `the company is a private company` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the company a private company?
      `the company is limited` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the liability of its members limited by its constitution?
      `the alteration` IS A `s 89 alteration of status` @desc Which alteration? One of: `s 89(a) from a private company to a public company`, `s 89(b) from a public company to a private company`, `s 89(c) from a private limited company to an unlimited company`, `s 89(d) from an unlimited private company to a limited company`, `s 89(e) from a public company to an unlimited private company`.
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 89, may my company alter its status in this way by re-registration` IS
    `s 89 the company may by re-registration under Part 7 alter its status in that way` `the company is a public company` `the company is a private company` `the company is limited` `the alteration`

§§ `Part 7, private company becoming public (ss 90 to 96)`

@export Under section 90(2), are the conditions for re-registering my private company as a public company met?
GIVEN `the company has a share capital` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does the company have a share capital?
      `the share capital requirements of section 91 are met` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are the requirements of section 91 as to share capital met (see the questions on section 91)?
      `the net assets requirements of section 92 are met` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are the requirements of section 92 as to net assets met (see the questions on section 92)?
      `section 93 applies` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does section 93 apply (shares allotted for non-cash consideration since the balance sheet date)?
      `the requirements of section 93 are met` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are the requirements of section 93 met?
      `the company has previously been re-registered as unlimited` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has the company previously been re-registered as unlimited?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 90(2), are the conditions for re-registering as a public company met` IS
    `s 90(2) the conditions are met` `the company has a share capital` (`coa2 seat a stated fact as an answer` `the share capital requirements of section 91 are met`) (`coa2 seat a stated fact as an answer` `the net assets requirements of section 92 are met`) (`coa2 seat a stated fact as an answer` `section 93 applies`) (`coa2 seat a stated fact as an answer` `the requirements of section 93 are met`) `the company has previously been re-registered as unlimited`

@export Under section 90(1), may my private company be re-registered as a public company limited by shares?
GIVEN `the company is a private company` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the company a private company (limited or unlimited)?
      `the resolution is a special resolution` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has a special resolution that the company should be re-registered as a public company been passed (see section 283)?
      `the conditions of section 90(2) are met` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are the conditions of section 90(2) met (see the question on section 90(2))?
      `the application and documents have been delivered` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has an application for re-registration been delivered to the registrar in accordance with section 94, together with the other documents required by that section?
      `a statement of compliance has been delivered` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has a statement of compliance been delivered with the application?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 90(1), may my private company be re-registered as a public company` IS
