GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 101(4), has my company become a private limited company on this day` IS
    `s 101(4)(a) the company is a private limited company on the day` (`coa2 seat a date if it has happened` `the certificate has been issued` `the date the certificate was issued`) `the day`

§§ `Part 7, private limited company becoming unlimited (ss 102 to 104)`

@export Under section 102(4), has this member's assent to the company becoming unlimited been given (a trustee in bankruptcy assents to the exclusion of the member; a personal representative may assent for a deceased member)?
GIVEN `the member has assented` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has the member assented?
      `a trustee in bankruptcy of the member is entitled to assent` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is a trustee in bankruptcy of the member entitled to assent?
      `the trustee in bankruptcy has assented` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has the trustee in bankruptcy assented?
      `the member is deceased` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the member deceased?
      `the personal representative has assented` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has the personal representative of the deceased member assented on his behalf?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 102(4), has this member's assent to the company becoming unlimited been given` IS
    `s 102(4) the member's assent is given` (`s 102(4) member` WITH `the member has assented` IS `the member has assented`, `a trustee in bankruptcy of the member is entitled to assent` IS `a trustee in bankruptcy of the member is entitled to assent`, `the trustee in bankruptcy has assented` IS `the trustee in bankruptcy has assented`, `the member is deceased` IS `the member is deceased`, `the personal representative of the deceased member has assented on behalf of the deceased` IS `the personal representative has assented`)

@export Under section 102(1), may my private limited company be re-registered as an unlimited company?
GIVEN `the company is a private company` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the company a private company?
      `the company is limited` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the company limited?
      `all the members have assented` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Have all the members assented (through trustees in bankruptcy and personal representatives where section 102(4) applies)?
      `the company has previously been re-registered as limited` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has the company previously been re-registered as limited?
      `the application and documents have been delivered` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has an application been delivered to the registrar in accordance with section 103, together with the other documents required by that section?
      `a statement of compliance has been delivered` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has a statement of compliance been delivered with the application?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 102(1), may my private limited company be re-registered as unlimited` IS
    `s 102(1) the private limited company may be re-registered as an unlimited company` `the company is a private company` `the company is limited` (`coa2 seat a stated fact as an answer` `all the members have assented`) (`s 102(2) the condition is met` `the company has previously been re-registered as limited`) `the application and documents have been delivered` `a statement of compliance has been delivered`

@export Under section 103(2), is the application for re-registration as an unlimited company accompanied by the prescribed form of assent, authenticated by or on behalf of all the members, and the articles as proposed?
GIVEN `the prescribed form of assent accompanies it` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does the prescribed form of assent accompany the application?
      `the form is authenticated by or on behalf of all the members` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the form authenticated by or on behalf of all the members of the company (section 1146)?
      `a copy of the articles as proposed accompanies it` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does a copy of the company's articles as proposed to be amended accompany the application?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 103(2), is the application accompanied by the documents required` IS
    `s 103(2) the application is accompanied by what the subsection requires` `the prescribed form of assent accompanies it` (`coa2 seat a stated fact as an answer` `the form is authenticated by or on behalf of all the members`) `a copy of the articles as proposed accompanies it`

@export Under section 103(4), does the statement of compliance contain the directors' statement that the form of assent covers the whole membership (and, where others authenticated for members, that reasonable steps were taken)?
GIVEN `the directors state the authenticators are the whole membership` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Do the directors state that the persons by whom or on whose behalf the form of assent is authenticated constitute the whole membership of the company?
      `some members did not authenticate the form themselves` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did some of the members not authenticate the form themselves?
      `the directors state they took all reasonable steps` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Do the directors state that they have taken all reasonable steps to satisfy themselves that each person who authenticated it for a member was lawfully empowered to do so?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 103(4), does the directors' statement contain what is required` IS
    `s 103(4) the statement of compliance contains the directors' statement` `the directors state the authenticators are the whole membership` `some members did not authenticate the form themselves` `the directors state they took all reasonable steps`

@export Under section 104(4), has my company become an unlimited company on this day (on the issue of the certificate of incorporation on re-registration)?
GIVEN `the certificate has been issued` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has the certificate of incorporation on re-registration been issued?
      `the date the certificate was issued` IS A DATE @desc On what date was it issued? (any date if it has not been issued)
      `the day` IS A DATE @desc On what day do you ask?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 104(4), has my company become an unlimited company on this day` IS
    `s 104(4)(a) the company is an unlimited company on the day` (`coa2 seat a date if it has happened` `the certificate has been issued` `the date the certificate was issued`) `the day`

§§ `Part 7, unlimited company becoming limited (ss 105 to 108)`

@export Under section 105(1), may my unlimited company be re-registered as a private limited company?
GIVEN `the company is unlimited` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the company an unlimited company?
      `the resolution is a special resolution` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has a special resolution that the company be re-registered as a private limited company been passed (see section 283)?
      `the company has previously been re-registered as unlimited` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has the company previously been re-registered as unlimited?
      `the application and documents have been delivered` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has an application been delivered to the registrar in accordance with section 106, together with the other documents required by that section?
      `a statement of compliance has been delivered` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has a statement of compliance been delivered with the application?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 105(1), may my unlimited company be re-registered as a private limited company` IS
    `s 105(1) the unlimited company may be re-registered as a private limited company` `the company is unlimited` (`coa2 seat a stated fact as an answer` `the resolution is a special resolution`) (`s 105(2) the condition is met` `the company has previously been re-registered as unlimited`) `the application and documents have been delivered` `a statement of compliance has been delivered`

@export Under section 105(3), does the special resolution state whether the company is to be limited by shares or by guarantee, as the subsection requires?
GIVEN `the resolution states whether limited by shares or by guarantee` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does the special resolution state whether the company is to be limited by shares or by guarantee?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 105(3), does the special resolution state whether we will be limited by shares or by guarantee` IS
    `s 105(3) the special resolution meets the requirement of subsection (3)` `the resolution states whether limited by shares or by guarantee`

@export Under section 106(2), is the application for re-registration as a limited company accompanied by the documents required (and, if limited by guarantee, a statement of guarantee)?
GIVEN `a copy of the resolution accompanies it` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does a copy of the resolution accompany the application?
      `a copy has already been forwarded to the registrar` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has a copy already been forwarded to the registrar under Chapter 3 of Part 3?
      `the company is to be limited by guarantee` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the company to be limited by guarantee?
      `a statement of guarantee accompanies it` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does a statement of guarantee accompany the application?
      `a copy of the articles as proposed accompanies it` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does a copy of the company's articles as proposed to be amended accompany the application?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 106(2), is the application accompanied by the documents required` IS
    `s 106(2) the application is accompanied by what the subsection requires` `a copy of the resolution accompanies it` `a copy has already been forwarded to the registrar` `the company is to be limited by guarantee` `a statement of guarantee accompanies it` `a copy of the articles as proposed accompanies it`

@export Under section 106(3), does a member's undertaking in the statement of guarantee cover this winding up (while he is a member, or within one year after he ceases to be a member)?
GIVEN `the company is wound up while I am a member` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the company wound up while the person is a member?
      `I have ceased to be a member` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has the person ceased to be a member?
      `the date I ceased to be a member` IS A DATE @desc On what date did the person cease to be a member? (any date if not)
      `the date of the winding up` IS A DATE @desc On what date is the company wound up?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 106(3), does my undertaking as a member of a guarantee company cover this winding up` IS
    `s 106(3) the member's undertaking covers the winding up` `the company is wound up while I am a member` (`coa2 seat a date if it has happened` `I have ceased to be a member` `the date I ceased to be a member`) `the date of the winding up`

@export Under section 107(4), has my company become a limited company on this day (on the issue of the certificate of incorporation on re-registration)?
GIVEN `the certificate has been issued` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has the certificate of incorporation on re-registration been issued?
      `the date the certificate was issued` IS A DATE @desc On what date was it issued? (any date if it has not been issued)
      `the day` IS A DATE @desc On what day do you ask?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 107(4), has my company become a limited company on this day` IS
    `s 107(4)(a) the company is a limited company on the day` (`coa2 seat a date if it has happened` `the certificate has been issued` `the date the certificate was issued`) `the day`

@export Under section 108(1), must my company deliver a statement of capital to the registrar within 15 days after re-registration as a limited company?
GIVEN `the company already has allotted share capital on re-registration` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does the company, on re-registration under section 107, already have allotted share capital?
      `the information was already sent in a statement of capital and initial shareholdings` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has the information that would be included already been sent to the registrar in a statement of capital and initial shareholdings (section 10)?
      `the information was already sent in the last statement of capital` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has the information already been sent in the last statement of capital sent by the company?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 108(1), must my company deliver a statement of capital after re-registration` IS
    `s 108(1) the company must deliver a statement of capital to the registrar` `the company already has allotted share capital on re-registration` `the information was already sent in a statement of capital and initial shareholdings` `the information was already sent in the last statement of capital`

@export Under section 108(1), was the statement of capital delivered to the registrar within 15 days after the re-registration?
GIVEN `the date of the re-registration` IS A DATE @desc On what date was the company re-registered?
      `the date the statement was delivered` IS A DATE @desc On what date was the statement of capital delivered?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 108(1), was the statement of capital delivered in time` IS
    `s 108(1) the statement of capital is delivered within 15 days after the re-registration` `the date of the re-registration` `the date the statement was delivered`

@export Under section 108(4), would I commit an offence if default were made in delivering the statement of capital? (the company, and every officer in default)
GIVEN `default is made in complying with the section` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has default been made in complying with section 108?
      `who I am` IS A Party @desc What are you in relation to the company? One of: Company, Director, `Company secretary`, `Shadow director`, `Officer in default`, Member, `Subscriber to the memorandum`, Auditor, Creditor, `Debenture holder`, `Person with significant control`, Registrar, `Secretary of State`, Court, `Takeover Panel`, `Competent authority`.
      `I am in default` IS A BOOLEAN @desc If you are an officer, are you in default (see section 1121)?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 108(4), could I commit an offence if the company fails to deliver the statement of capital` IS
    `s 108(4) the person commits an offence` `default is made in complying with the section` `who I am` (`coa2 seat a stated fact as an answer` `I am in default`)

@export Under section 108(5), what is the most the company or an officer in default can be fined on summary conviction?
GIVETH A STRING
DECIDE `Under section 108(5), what is the penalty for failing to deliver the statement of capital` IS
    `coa2 seat describe a penalty` `s 108(5) the penalty on summary conviction`

§§ `Part 7, public company becoming private and unlimited (ss 109 to 111)`

@export Under section 109(1), may my public company limited by shares be re-registered as an unlimited private company with a share capital?
GIVEN `the company is a public company` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the company a public company?
      `the company is limited by shares` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the company limited by shares?
      `all the members have assented` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Have all the members assented (through trustees in bankruptcy and personal representatives where section 109(4) applies)?
      `the company has previously been re-registered as limited` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has the company previously been re-registered as limited?
      `the company has previously been re-registered as unlimited` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has the company previously been re-registered as unlimited?
      `the application and documents have been delivered` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has an application been delivered to the registrar in accordance with section 110, together with the other documents required by that section?
      `a statement of compliance has been delivered` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has a statement of compliance been delivered with the application?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 109(1), may my public company be re-registered as an unlimited private company` IS
    `s 109(1) the public company limited by shares may be re-registered as an unlimited private company with a share capital` `the company is a public company` `the company is limited by shares` (`coa2 seat a stated fact as an answer` `all the members have assented`) (`s 109(2) the condition is met` `the company has previously been re-registered as limited` `the company has previously been re-registered as unlimited`) `the application and documents have been delivered` `a statement of compliance has been delivered`

@export Under section 110(2), is the application for re-registration as an unlimited private company accompanied by the prescribed form of assent, authenticated by or on behalf of all the members, and the articles as proposed?
GIVEN `the prescribed form of assent accompanies it` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does the prescribed form of assent accompany the application?
      `the form is authenticated by or on behalf of all the members` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the form authenticated by or on behalf of all the members of the company (section 1146)?
      `a copy of the articles as proposed accompanies it` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does a copy of the company's articles as proposed to be amended accompany the application?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 110(2), is the application accompanied by the documents required` IS
    `s 110(2) the application is accompanied by what the subsection requires` `the prescribed form of assent accompanies it` (`coa2 seat a stated fact as an answer` `the form is authenticated by or on behalf of all the members`) `a copy of the articles as proposed accompanies it`

@export Under section 111(4), has my company become an unlimited private company on this day (on the issue of the certificate of incorporation on re-registration)?
GIVEN `the certificate has been issued` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has the certificate of incorporation on re-registration been issued?
      `the date the certificate was issued` IS A DATE @desc On what date was it issued? (any date if it has not been issued)
      `the day` IS A DATE @desc On what day do you ask?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 111(4), has my company become an unlimited private company on this day` IS
    `s 111(4)(a) the company is an unlimited private company on the day` (`coa2 seat a date if it has happened` `the certificate has been issued` `the date the certificate was issued`) `the day`

-- ====================================================================================================
-- seat questions from part coa3 (merged by the lead on 2026-11-12; unchanged text follows)
-- ====================================================================================================
-- coa3-seat.l4: the SEAT LAYER over the layer-1 modules coa3-part8-members.l4, coa3-part8-inspection.l4,
-- coa3-part8-branch.l4, coa3-part8-subsidiary.l4 and coa3-part9-rights.l4 (Companies Act 2006 (United Kingdom),
-- Parts 8 and 9, ss 112 to 153).
--
-- SEAT: an individual who is, or is about to become, a director, a company secretary or a member (shareholder) of a
-- company registered under the Act, or who deals with one, asking on facts they can state what the Act requires or lets
-- them do, what rights they have against the company or its directors, what they must disclose, file, approve or vote on
-- and by when, and what follows (liability, offences, penalties) if it is not done.
-- (Assumed, not ruled: the Act is addressed to companies, so the individual is whoever stands in a company's management or ownership.)
--
-- Each question begins "Under section N," with the Act's own numbering and has @export and @desc. Each takes plain
-- inputs, one per fact the person can state, worded as the person would be asked, builds what the layer-1 rule
-- needs, and calls the layer-1 rule: no rule is restated here. Answers are the layer-1 answers: JUST TRUE (the Act says yes),
-- JUST FALSE (the Act says no in its own words), NOTHING (the Act does not decide the case): a caller must never read
-- NOTHING as no.
--
-- Where an answer of another part is needed (s 1121 "in default"; s 853E(6) "relevant market"; s 1159 "subsidiary";
-- s 1173(1) "UK regulated market"; Schedule 5), the question asks the person the fact that answers it: a yes or no that
-- the person states, or "yes", "no" or "not known" for an answer they may not have. The lead wires the other part's answer at the merge.
-- Penalty questions answer with the typed `Penalty`: the pounds that a level on the standard scale or the statutory maximum
-- stands for are not in the Act and are not asked here.
-- Where the text shows two versions of a provision (s 113(2); ss 113J and 115): there is no seat question on s 113(2) itself (the one that touches the register's contents, s 113(2A), belongs with the second version);
-- both index sections are exposed, Under section 113J(1) and Under section 115(1), and a caller who must choose should prefer s 113J (forks F1 and F2 in NOTES.md).

-- ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
-- Helpers: what the person states, turned into what the layer-1 rules take. Not questions.
-- ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------

GIVEN fact IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`Under section 112, I state this as a yes or no answer` MEANS
    IF fact THEN JUST TRUE ELSE JUST FALSE

GIVEN answer IS A STRING
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`Under section 136(1), what I know about another section's answer` MEANS
    BRANCH IF answer EQUALS "yes" THEN JUST TRUE
           IF answer EQUALS "no" THEN JUST FALSE
           OTHERWISE NOTHING

GIVEN `I am a director of the company` IS A BOOLEAN
      `I am the company secretary` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A Party
`Under section 113(7), the party I am` MEANS
    IF `I am a director of the company`
    THEN Director
    ELSE IF `I am the company secretary`
         THEN `Company secretary`
         ELSE Member

GIVEN `where the company is registered` IS A STRING
GIVETH A `Place of registration`
`Under section 126, where the company is registered` MEANS
    BRANCH IF `where the company is registered` EQUALS "Scotland" THEN Scotland
           IF `where the company is registered` EQUALS "Northern Ireland" THEN `Northern Ireland`
           OTHERWISE `England and Wales`

GIVEN `how I am convicted` IS A STRING
GIVETH A `Mode of conviction`
`Under section 113G(4), how I am convicted` MEANS
    BRANCH IF `how I am convicted` EQUALS "on indictment" THEN `on conviction on indictment`
           IF `how I am convicted` EQUALS "summary, England and Wales" THEN `on summary conviction in England and Wales`
           IF `how I am convicted` EQUALS "summary, Scotland" THEN `on summary conviction in Scotland`
           IF `how I am convicted` EQUALS "summary, Northern Ireland" THEN `on summary conviction in Northern Ireland`
           OTHERWISE `on summary conviction`

§ `Part 8: A company's members`

§§ `Chapter 1, section 112: am I a member of the company?`

@ref s 112
@export Under section 112, am I a member of the company?
GIVEN `I signed the company's memorandum` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did you sign the company's memorandum (are you a subscriber)?
      `the company has been registered` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has the company been registered?
      `I agreed to become a member` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did you agree to become a member of the company?
      `my name is entered in the register of members` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is your name entered in the company's register of members?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`Under section 112, am I a member of the company` MEANS
    `s 112 the person is a member of the company` `I signed the company's memorandum` `the company has been registered` `I agreed to become a member` `my name is entered in the register of members`

@ref s 112(4)
@export Under section 112(4), do I still become a member although my name is entered in the wrong form?
GIVEN `I agreed to become a member` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did you agree to become a member of the company?
      `my name as an individual is entered in the register` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is your name, as an individual, entered in the company's register of members?
      `my name is in the form section 113A requires` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is your name entered in the form that section 113A requires (forename and surname, or title)?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`Under section 112(4), do I still become a member although my name is entered in the wrong form` MEANS
    `s 112(4) the person becomes a member under s 112(2) although the entered name is not in the form required by s 113A` `I agreed to become a member` `my name as an individual is entered in the register` `my name is in the form section 113A requires`

§§ `Chapter 2, section 113: what the register of members must contain`

@ref s 113(1)
@export Under section 113(1), must the company keep a register of its members?
GIVEN `the body is a company formed and registered under the Companies Act 2006` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the body a company formed and registered under the Companies Act 2006?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`Under section 113(1), must the company keep a register of its members` MEANS
    `s 113(1) the company must keep a register of its members` (`Under section 112, I state this as a yes or no answer` `the body is a company formed and registered under the Companies Act 2006`)

@ref s 113(2A)
@export Under section 113(2A), must the register show the date I stopped being a member?
GIVEN `I have ceased to be a member` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Have you ceased to be a member of the company?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`Under section 113(2A), must the register show the date I stopped being a member` MEANS
    `s 113(2A) the register must contain the date at which the person's membership ceased` `I have ceased to be a member`

@ref s 113(3)
@export Under section 113(3), must the register show the shares I hold?
GIVEN `the company has a share capital` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does the company have a share capital?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`Under section 113(3), must the register show the shares I hold` MEANS
    `s 113(3) the register must contain a statement of the shares held by each member` `the company has a share capital`

@ref s 113(3)(a)(i)
@export Under section 113(3)(a)(i), must the register give each of my shares by its number?
GIVEN `the company has a share capital` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does the company have a share capital?
      `my share has a number` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the share numbered?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`Under section 113(3)(a)(i), must the register give each of my shares by its number` MEANS
    `s 113(3)(a)(i) the register must distinguish the share by its number` `the company has a share capital` `my share has a number`

@ref s 113(3)(a)(ii)
@export Under section 113(3)(a)(ii), must the register show the class of my shares?
GIVEN `the company has a share capital` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does the company have a share capital?
      `the company has more than one class of issued shares` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does the company have more than one class of issued shares?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`Under section 113(3)(a)(ii), must the register show the class of my shares` MEANS
    `s 113(3)(a)(ii) the register must distinguish the share by its class` `the company has a share capital` `the company has more than one class of issued shares`

@ref s 113(3)(b)
@export Under section 113(3)(b), must the register show the amount paid on my shares?
GIVEN `the company has a share capital` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does the company have a share capital?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`Under section 113(3)(b), must the register show the amount paid on my shares` MEANS
    `s 113(3)(b) the register must state the amount paid or agreed to be considered as paid on the shares of each member` `the company has a share capital`

@ref s 113(4)
@export Under section 113(4), must the register show stock instead of shares?
GIVEN `the company has converted shares into stock` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has the company converted any of its shares into stock?
      `the company has given notice of the conversion to the registrar` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has the company given notice of the conversion to the registrar?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`Under section 113(4), must the register show stock instead of shares` MEANS
    `s 113(4) the register must show the amount and class of stock held by each member instead of the amount of shares and the particulars relating to shares` `the company has converted shares into stock` `the company has given notice of the conversion to the registrar`

@ref s 113(5)
@export Under section 113(5), must the register name each of us as joint holders?
GIVEN `we hold the shares or stock jointly` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Do you hold the shares or stock jointly with someone else?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`Under section 113(5), must the register name each of us as joint holders` MEANS
    `s 113(5) the register must state the names of each joint holder` `we hold the shares or stock jointly`

@ref s 113(6)
@export Under section 113(6), must the register show the class of membership I belong to?
GIVEN `the company has a share capital` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does the company have a share capital?
      `the company has more than one class of members` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does the company have more than one class of members?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`Under section 113(6), must the register show the class of membership I belong to` MEANS
    `s 113(6) the register must contain a statement of the class to which each member belongs` `the company has a share capital` `the company has more than one class of members`

@ref s 113(9)
@export Under section 113(9), is the company a traded company?
GIVEN `shares are admitted to trading on a relevant market` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are any of the company's shares admitted to trading on a "relevant market" (section 853E(6))?
      `shares are admitted to trading on another market outside the United Kingdom` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are any of the company's shares admitted to trading on any other market that is outside the United Kingdom?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`Under section 113(9), is the company a traded company` MEANS
    `s 113(9) the company is a traded company` (`s 113(9) the market is a relevant market` (`Under section 112, I state this as a yes or no answer` `shares are admitted to trading on a relevant market`)) `shares are admitted to trading on another market outside the United Kingdom`

@ref s 113(6A)(b)
@export Under section 113(6A)(b), must the company keep my old information in the register?
GIVEN `my information has changed` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has information required to be entered in the register about you changed?
      `shares are admitted to trading on a relevant market` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are any of the company's shares admitted to trading on a "relevant market" (section 853E(6))?
      `shares are admitted to trading on another market outside the United Kingdom` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are any of the company's shares admitted to trading on any other market that is outside the United Kingdom?
      `removal of the old information is authorised` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has removal of the old information been authorised by section 121 (ten years after you ceased to be a member) or by a court order under section 125?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`Under section 113(6A)(b), must the company keep my old information in the register` MEANS
    `s 113(6A)(b) the old information must be retained in the register` `my information has changed` (`s 113(9) the company is a non-traded company` (`s 113(9) the company is a traded company` (`s 113(9) the market is a relevant market` (`Under section 112, I state this as a yes or no answer` `shares are admitted to trading on a relevant market`)) `shares are admitted to trading on another market outside the United Kingdom`)) `removal of the old information is authorised`

@ref s 113(6B)
@export Under section 113(6B), may a traded company drop my old information from the register?
GIVEN `my information has changed` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has information required to be entered in the register about you changed?
      `shares are admitted to trading on a relevant market` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are any of the company's shares admitted to trading on a "relevant market" (section 853E(6))?
      `shares are admitted to trading on another market outside the United Kingdom` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are any of the company's shares admitted to trading on any other market that is outside the United Kingdom?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`Under section 113(6B), may a traded company drop my old information from the register` MEANS
    `s 113(6B) the company need not include or retain the old information in the register` `my information has changed` (`s 113(9) the company is a traded company` (`s 113(9) the market is a relevant market` (`Under section 112, I state this as a yes or no answer` `shares are admitted to trading on a relevant market`)) `shares are admitted to trading on another market outside the United Kingdom`)

@ref s 113(7)
@export Under section 113(7), am I or the company guilty of an offence for failing to keep the register?
GIVEN `the company had a reasonable excuse for the default` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did the company have a reasonable excuse for the default?
      `the company made default in complying with section 113` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did the company make default in complying with section 113 (the register of members)?
      `I am a director of the company` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are you a director of the company?
      `I am the company secretary` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are you the secretary of the company?
      `I authorised or permitted the default, took part in it, or failed to take all reasonable steps to prevent it` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did you authorise or permit the default, take part in it, or fail to take all reasonable steps to prevent it? (this is what makes an officer "in default")
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`Under section 113(7), am I or the company guilty of an offence for failing to keep the register` MEANS
    `s 113(7) the person commits an offence` `the company made default in complying with section 113` (NOT `the company had a reasonable excuse for the default`) (`Under section 113(7), the party I am` `I am a director of the company` `I am the company secretary`) (`Under section 112, I state this as a yes or no answer` `I authorised or permitted the default, took part in it, or failed to take all reasonable steps to prevent it`)

@ref s 113(8)
@export Under section 113(8), what is the penalty for failing to keep the register?
GIVETH A Penalty
`Under section 113(8), what is the penalty for failing to keep the register` MEANS
    `s 113(8) the penalty for an offence under s 113`

§§ `Sections 113A to 113F: my details as a member, and the time limits (Ask only if you have become a member, or the company has written to you)`

@ref s 113A(3)
@export Under section 113A(3), may I give my title instead of my forename and surname?
GIVEN `I am a peer` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are you a peer?
      `I am usually known by a title` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are you an individual who is usually known by a title?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`Under section 113A(3), may I give my title instead of my forename and surname` MEANS
    `s 113A(3)(a) the requirement to provide the name may be satisfied by providing the title instead` `I am a peer` `I am usually known by a title`

@ref s 113D(1)
@export Under section 113D(1), must I give the company my details as a new member?
GIVEN `I have become a member of the company` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Have you become a member of the company?
      `I have already given the company my details` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Have you already given the company your name (or title) and a service address?
      `I became a member on incorporation and my details are in the application to register the company` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did you become a member when the company was incorporated, with your details in the application for its registration?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`Under section 113D(1), must I give the company my details as a new member` MEANS
    `s 113D(1) the person must provide the company with the required information about the member, subject to s 113D(2)` `I have become a member of the company` `I have already given the company my details` `I became a member on incorporation and my details are in the application to register the company`

@ref s 113D(3)
@export Under section 113D(3), by what date must I give the company my details?
GIVEN `the date I became a member` IS A DATE @desc On what date did you become a member of the company?
GIVETH A DATE
`Under section 113D(3), by what date must I give the company my details` MEANS
    `s 113D(3) the last day for providing the information` `the date I became a member`

@ref s 113D(3)
@export Under section 113D(3), did I give the company my details in time?
GIVEN `the date I became a member` IS A DATE @desc On what date did you become a member of the company?
      `the date I gave the company my details` IS A DATE @desc On what date did you give the company your details?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`Under section 113D(3), did I give the company my details in time` MEANS
    `s 113D(3) the person provided the information within the period of two months` `the date I became a member` `the date I gave the company my details`

@ref s 113E(1)
@export Under section 113E(1), must I tell the company that my details have changed?
GIVEN `I am a member of the company` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are you a member of the company?
      `my details have changed` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has there been a change in your name (or title) or your service address?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`Under section 113E(1), must I tell the company that my details have changed` MEANS
    `s 113E(1) the member must give notice to the company of the change in the required information` `I am a member of the company` `my details have changed`

@ref s 113E(3)
@export Under section 113E(3), by what date must I tell the company of the change?
GIVEN `the date my details changed` IS A DATE @desc On what date did your details change?
GIVETH A DATE
`Under section 113E(3), by what date must I tell the company of the change` MEANS
    `s 113E(3) the last day for giving notice of the change` `the date my details changed`

@ref s 113E(3)
@export Under section 113E(3), did I tell the company of the change in time?
GIVEN `the date my details changed` IS A DATE @desc On what date did your details change?
      `the date I told the company` IS A DATE @desc On what date did you give the company notice of the change?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`Under section 113E(3), did I tell the company of the change in time` MEANS
    `s 113E(3) the member gave notice of the change within the period of two months` `the date my details changed` `the date I told the company`

@ref s 113F(1)
@export Under section 113F(1), may the company require me to give my details?
GIVEN `I am a member or former member of the company` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are you a member or former member of the company?
      `the company wants to make sure its register includes the information it must include` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the company asking so that its register of members includes the information it is required to include?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`Under section 113F(1), may the company require me to give my details` MEANS
    `s 113F(1) the company may require the person to provide the required information about the person` `I am a member or former member of the company` `the company wants to make sure its register includes the information it must include`

@ref s 113F(2)
@export Under section 113F(2), by what date must I answer the company's notice?
GIVEN `the date the notice was given to me` IS A DATE @desc On what date did the company give you the notice?
GIVETH A DATE
`Under section 113F(2), by what date must I answer the company's notice` MEANS
    `s 113F(2) the last day of the period of one month for complying with the notice` `the date the notice was given to me`

§§ `Sections 113G to 113I: offences about my details (Ask only if you failed to give the details, or gave them wrongly)`

@ref s 113G(1)
@export Under section 113G(1), do I commit an offence by failing to give my details or notice of a change?
GIVEN `I failed to comply with section 113D or 113E` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did you fail to give your details within two months of becoming a member, or fail to give notice of a change within two months?
      `I failed to comply with the company's notice under section 113F` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did you fail to comply with the company's notice requiring your details?
      `I had a reasonable excuse` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did you have a reasonable excuse for the failure?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`Under section 113G(1), do I commit an offence by failing to give my details or notice of a change` MEANS
    `s 113G(1)-(2) the person commits an offence by failing to comply` `I failed to comply with section 113D or 113E` `I failed to comply with the company's notice under section 113F` (NOT `I had a reasonable excuse`)

@ref s 113G(4)
@export Under section 113G(4), what is the penalty for failing to give my details?
GIVEN `how I am convicted` IS A STRING @desc Where and how would the conviction be? One of: "on indictment", "summary, England and Wales", "summary, Scotland", "summary, Northern Ireland"
      `the general limit in a magistrates' court, in months` IS A NUMBER @desc What is the general limit in a magistrates' court on imprisonment, in months, where you are convicted summarily in England and Wales? (it is fixed by sentencing law outside the Companies Act; give 0 if you do not know)
GIVETH A MAYBE Penalty
`Under section 113G(4), what is the penalty for failing to give my details` MEANS
    `s 113G(4) the penalty for an offence under s 113G` (`Under section 113G(4), how I am convicted` `how I am convicted`) (Period OF `the general limit in a magistrates' court, in months`, Months)

@ref s 113H(1)
@export Under section 113H(1), do I commit an offence by a false statement when I give my details?
GIVEN `I made a statement in purported compliance with section 113D or 113E` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did you make a statement, in purported compliance with section 113D or 113E, when giving your details or notice of a change?
      `the statement was misleading, false or deceptive in a material particular` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Was the statement misleading, false or deceptive in a material particular?
      `I had a reasonable excuse` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did you have a reasonable excuse for making it?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`Under section 113H(1), do I commit an offence by a false statement when I give my details` MEANS
    `s 113H(1) the person commits an offence by a false statement in purported compliance with s 113D or s 113E` `I made a statement in purported compliance with section 113D or 113E` `the statement was misleading, false or deceptive in a material particular` (NOT `I had a reasonable excuse`)

@ref s 113H(4)
@export Under section 113H(4), what is the penalty for a false statement when I give my details?
GIVEN `how I am convicted` IS A STRING @desc Where and how would the conviction be? One of: "on indictment", "summary, England and Wales", "summary, Scotland", "summary, Northern Ireland"
GIVETH A MAYBE Penalty
`Under section 113H(4), what is the penalty for a false statement when I give my details` MEANS
    `s 113H(4) the penalty for an offence under s 113H` (`Under section 113G(4), how I am convicted` `how I am convicted`)

@ref s 113I(1)
@export Under section 113I(1), do I commit an offence by a statement I know to be false when I give my details?
GIVEN `I made a statement in purported compliance with section 113D or 113E` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did you make a statement, in purported compliance with section 113D or 113E, when giving your details or notice of a change?
      `I knew the statement to be misleading, false or deceptive in a material particular` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did you know the statement to be misleading, false or deceptive in a material particular?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`Under section 113I(1), do I commit an offence by a statement I know to be false when I give my details` MEANS
    `s 113I(1) the person commits an offence by a statement known to be false in purported compliance with s 113D or s 113E` `I made a statement in purported compliance with section 113D or 113E` `I knew the statement to be misleading, false or deceptive in a material particular`

@ref s 113I(4)
@export Under section 113I(4), what is the penalty for a statement known to be false when I give my details?
GIVEN `how I am convicted` IS A STRING @desc Where and how would the conviction be? One of: "on indictment", "summary, England and Wales", "summary, Scotland", "summary, Northern Ireland"
      `the general limit in a magistrates' court, in months` IS A NUMBER @desc What is the general limit in a magistrates' court on imprisonment, in months, where you are convicted summarily in England and Wales? (it is fixed by sentencing law outside the Companies Act; give 0 if you do not know)
GIVETH A MAYBE Penalty
`Under section 113I(4), what is the penalty for a statement known to be false when I give my details` MEANS
    `s 113I(4) the penalty for an offence under s 113I` (`Under section 113G(4), how I am convicted` `how I am convicted`) (Period OF `the general limit in a magistrates' court, in months`, Months)

§§ `Section 113J: the index of members (Ask only if the company has more than 50 members)`

@ref s 113J(1)
@export Under section 113J(1), must the company keep an index of its members?
GIVEN `the number of members of the company` IS A NUMBER @desc How many members does the company have?
      `the register of members is itself in the form of an index` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the register of members in such a form as to constitute in itself an index?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`Under section 113J(1), must the company keep an index of its members` MEANS
    `s 113J(1) the company must keep an index of the names or titles of its members` `the number of members of the company` `the register of members is itself in the form of an index`

@ref s 113J(2)
@export Under section 113J(2), by what date must the company alter the index?
GIVEN `the date the register was altered` IS A DATE @desc On what date was the register of members altered?
GIVETH A DATE
`Under section 113J(2), by what date must the company alter the index` MEANS
    `s 113J(2) the last day for making the alteration in the index` `the date the register was altered`

@ref s 113J(5)
@export Under section 113J(5), am I or the company guilty of an offence for defaulting on the index?
GIVEN `the company made default in complying with section 113J` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did the company make default in complying with section 113J (the index of members)?
      `I am a director of the company` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are you a director of the company?
      `I am the company secretary` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are you the secretary of the company?
      `I authorised or permitted the default, took part in it, or failed to take all reasonable steps to prevent it` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did you authorise or permit the default, take part in it, or fail to take all reasonable steps to prevent it? (this is what makes an officer "in default")
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`Under section 113J(5), am I or the company guilty of an offence for defaulting on the index` MEANS
    `s 113J(5) the person commits an offence` `the company made default in complying with section 113J` (`Under section 113(7), the party I am` `I am a director of the company` `I am the company secretary`) (`Under section 112, I state this as a yes or no answer` `I authorised or permitted the default, took part in it, or failed to take all reasonable steps to prevent it`)

@ref s 113J(6)
@export Under section 113J(6), what is the penalty for defaulting on the index?
GIVETH A Penalty
`Under section 113J(6), what is the penalty for defaulting on the index` MEANS
    `s 113J(6) the penalty for an offence under s 113J`

§§ `Sections 114 and 115: where the register is kept and telling the registrar`

@ref s 114(1)
@export Under section 114(1), is the register of members kept where it must be?
GIVEN `the register is kept at the registered office` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the register kept available for inspection at the company's registered office?
      `the register is kept at a place specified in regulations under section 1136` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it kept at a place specified in regulations under section 1136?
      `a restriction under section 120A applies` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does a restriction imposed by regulations under section 120A (protected material) apply?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`Under section 114(1), is the register of members kept where it must be` MEANS
    `s 114(1) the register of members is kept at a place that satisfies s 114(1)` (IF `the register is kept at the registered office` THEN `s 114(1)(a) at its registered office` ELSE IF `the register is kept at a place specified in regulations under section 1136` THEN `s 114(1)(b) at a place specified in regulations under section 1136` ELSE `s 114(1) at another place`) `a restriction under section 120A applies`

@ref s 114(2)
@export Under section 114(2), must the company tell the registrar where the register is kept?
GIVEN `the body is a company formed and registered under the Companies Act 2006` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the body a company formed and registered under the Companies Act 2006?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`Under section 114(2), must the company tell the registrar where the register is kept` MEANS
    `s 114(2) the company must give notice to the registrar of the place where its register is kept available and of any change in that place` (`Under section 112, I state this as a yes or no answer` `the body is a company formed and registered under the Companies Act 2006`)

@ref s 114(3)
@export Under section 114(3), is the company excused from telling the registrar where the register is kept?
GIVEN `the register was in existence on the relevant date` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Was the register in existence on 1 July 1948 (a company registered in Great Britain) or 1 April 1961 (Northern Ireland)?
      `the register has always been kept at the registered office since it came into existence` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has the register at all times since it came into existence been kept available at the registered office?
      `the register has always been kept at the registered office since the relevant date` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has the register at all times since that date been kept available at the registered office?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`Under section 114(3), is the company excused from telling the registrar where the register is kept` MEANS
    `s 114(3) no notice is required under s 114(2)` `the register was in existence on the relevant date` `the register has always been kept at the registered office since it came into existence` `the register has always been kept at the registered office since the relevant date`

@ref s 114(5)
@export Under section 114(5), am I or the company guilty of an offence for being 14 days late telling the registrar?
GIVEN `the number of days of default` IS A NUMBER @desc For how many days has the company been in default of giving the registrar notice of the place where the register is kept?
      `I am a director of the company` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are you a director of the company?
      `I am the company secretary` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are you the secretary of the company?
      `I authorised or permitted the default, took part in it, or failed to take all reasonable steps to prevent it` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did you authorise or permit the default, take part in it, or fail to take all reasonable steps to prevent it? (this is what makes an officer "in default")
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`Under section 114(5), am I or the company guilty of an offence for being 14 days late telling the registrar` MEANS
    `s 114(5) the person commits an offence` `the number of days of default` (`Under section 113(7), the party I am` `I am a director of the company` `I am the company secretary`) (`Under section 112, I state this as a yes or no answer` `I authorised or permitted the default, took part in it, or failed to take all reasonable steps to prevent it`)

@ref s 114(6)
@export Under section 114(6), what is the penalty for being late telling the registrar where the register is kept?
GIVETH A Penalty
`Under section 114(6), what is the penalty for being late telling the registrar where the register is kept` MEANS
    `s 114(6) the penalty for an offence under s 114`

@ref s 115(1)
@export Under section 115(1), must the company keep an index of the names of its members?
GIVEN `the number of members of the company` IS A NUMBER @desc How many members does the company have?
      `the register of members is itself in the form of an index` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the register of members in such a form as to constitute in itself an index?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`Under section 115(1), must the company keep an index of the names of its members` MEANS
    `s 115(1) the company must keep an index of the names of its members` `the number of members of the company` `the register of members is itself in the form of an index`

§§ `Sections 116 to 120B: inspecting the register, getting copies and protected information`

@ref s 116(1)
@export Under section 116(1), may I inspect the register of members and the index?
GIVEN `I am a member of the company` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are you a member of the company?
      `I pay the prescribed fee` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Will you pay the prescribed fee? (a member pays nothing)
      `a restriction under section 120A applies` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does a restriction imposed by regulations under section 120A (protected material) apply?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`Under section 116(1), may I inspect the register of members and the index` MEANS
    IF `I am a member of the company`
    THEN `s 116(1)(a) the register and the index of members' names must be open to the person's inspection without charge` `I am a member of the company` `a restriction under section 120A applies`
    ELSE `s 116(1)(b) the register and the index of members' names must be open to the person's inspection on payment of the prescribed fee` `I am a member of the company` `I pay the prescribed fee` `a restriction under section 120A applies`

@ref s 116(2)
@export Under section 116(2), may I require a copy of the register of members?
GIVEN `I pay the prescribed fee` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Will you pay the prescribed fee?
      `a restriction under section 120A applies` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does a restriction imposed by regulations under section 120A (protected material) apply?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`Under section 116(2), may I require a copy of the register of members` MEANS
    `s 116(2) the person may require a copy of the register of members or of any part of it` `I pay the prescribed fee` `a restriction under section 120A applies`

@ref s 116(4)
@export Under section 116(4), does my request contain everything the company can insist on?
GIVEN `I am an individual` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are you making the request as an individual (not for an organisation)?
      `the request gives a name and address` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does the request give your name and address (or, for an organisation, those of the individual responsible for making the request)?
      `the request states my purpose` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does the request say the purpose for which the information is to be used?
      `the request says whether the information will be disclosed` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does the request say whether the information will be disclosed to any other person?
      `the information will be disclosed to another person` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Will the information be disclosed to another person?
      `the other person is an individual` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is that other person an individual (not an organisation)?
      `the request gives the other person's name and address` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does the request give that person's name and address (or those of the individual responsible for receiving the information for an organisation)?
      `the request states the other person's purpose` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does the request say the purpose for which that person is to use the information?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`Under section 116(4), does my request contain everything the company can insist on` MEANS
    `s 116(4) the request contains the information that s 116(4) requires` (`s 116(4) request for inspection or a copy` OF `I am an individual`, `the request gives a name and address`, `the request states my purpose`, `the request says whether the information will be disclosed`, `the information will be disclosed to another person`, `the other person is an individual`, `the request gives the other person's name and address`, `the request states the other person's purpose`)

@ref s 117(1)
@export Under section 117(1), has the company complied with my request or applied to the court within five working days?
GIVEN `the working days between my request and the company's compliance or application to the court` IS A NUMBER @desc How many working days passed after the day the company received your request until it complied or applied to the court? (0 for the day of receipt)
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`Under section 117(1), has the company complied with my request or applied to the court within five working days` MEANS
    `s 117(1) the company acted within five working days` `the working days between my request and the company's compliance or application to the court`

@ref s 117(3)
@export Under section 117(3), can the court order me to pay the company's costs?
GIVEN `the company applied to the court` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has the company applied to the court under section 117?
      `the court is satisfied that I did not seek the inspection or copy for a proper purpose` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has the court decided that the inspection or copy was not sought for a proper purpose?
      `I am a party to the application` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are you a party to the application? (it makes no difference)
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`Under section 117(3), can the court order me to pay the company's costs` MEANS
    `s 117(3)(b) the court may order the company's costs on the application to be paid in whole or in part by the person who made the request` `the company applied to the court` `the court is satisfied that I did not seek the inspection or copy for a proper purpose` `I am a party to the application`

@ref s 117(5)
@export Under section 117(5), must the company now comply with my request?
GIVEN `the court did not direct the company not to comply` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did the court, on the company's application, decline to direct the company not to comply with your request?
      `the court has given its decision or the proceedings have been discontinued` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has the court given its decision, or have the proceedings been discontinued?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`Under section 117(5), must the company now comply with my request` MEANS
    `s 117(5) the company must comply with the request immediately` `the court did not direct the company not to comply` `the court has given its decision or the proceedings have been discontinued`

@ref s 118(1)
@export Under section 118(1), is the company or an officer guilty of an offence for refusing my inspection or copy?
GIVEN `the refusal or default was in accordance with an order of the court` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Was the refusal or default in accordance with an order of the court?
      `the inspection was refused or the copy not provided` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Was an inspection required by section 116 refused, or was there default in providing a copy?
      `I am a director of the company` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are you a director of the company?
      `I am the company secretary` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are you the secretary of the company?
      `I authorised or permitted the default, took part in it, or failed to take all reasonable steps to prevent it` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did you authorise or permit the default, take part in it, or fail to take all reasonable steps to prevent it? (this is what makes an officer "in default")
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`Under section 118(1), is the company or an officer guilty of an offence for refusing my inspection or copy` MEANS
    `s 118(1) the person commits an offence` `the inspection was refused or the copy not provided` `the refusal or default was in accordance with an order of the court` (`Under section 113(7), the party I am` `I am a director of the company` `I am the company secretary`) (`Under section 112, I state this as a yes or no answer` `I authorised or permitted the default, took part in it, or failed to take all reasonable steps to prevent it`)

@ref s 118(3)
@export Under section 118(3), can the court order the company to let me inspect or send me the copy?
GIVEN `the inspection was refused or the copy not provided` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Was an inspection required by section 116 refused, or was there default in providing a copy?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`Under section 118(3), can the court order the company to let me inspect or send me the copy` MEANS
    `s 118(3) the court may by order compel an immediate inspection or direct that the copy required be sent to the person requesting it` `the inspection was refused or the copy not provided`

@ref s 119(1)
@export Under section 119(1), do I commit an offence by a false statement in my request?
GIVEN `my request contained a misleading, false or deceptive statement in a material particular` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did your request contain a statement that was misleading, false or deceptive in a material particular?
      `I made it knowingly` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did you make it knowingly?
      `I made it recklessly` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did you make it recklessly?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`Under section 119(1), do I commit an offence by a false statement in my request` MEANS
    `s 119(1) the person commits an offence by a false statement in a request` `my request contained a misleading, false or deceptive statement in a material particular` `I made it knowingly` `I made it recklessly`

@ref s 119(2)
@export Under section 119(2), do I commit an offence by passing on the information I obtained from the register?
GIVEN `I hold information obtained from the register` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Do you hold information obtained by exercising a right under section 116?
      `I did something that resulted in its disclosure` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did you do something that resulted in the information being disclosed to another person?
      `I failed to do something with the result that it was disclosed` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did you fail to do something, with the result that the information was disclosed to another person?
      `I knew or had reason to suspect an improper purpose` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did you know, or have reason to suspect, that the other person might use the information for a purpose that is not a proper purpose?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`Under section 119(2), do I commit an offence by passing on the information I obtained from the register` MEANS
    `s 119(2) the person commits an offence by disclosure` `I hold information obtained from the register` `I did something that resulted in its disclosure` `I failed to do something with the result that it was disclosed` `I knew or had reason to suspect an improper purpose`

@ref s 119(3)
@export Under section 119(3), what is the penalty for a false statement in my request or an improper disclosure?
GIVEN `how I am convicted` IS A STRING @desc Where and how would the conviction be? One of: "on indictment", "summary, England and Wales", "summary, Scotland", "summary, Northern Ireland"
GIVETH A MAYBE Penalty
`Under section 119(3), what is the penalty for a false statement in my request or an improper disclosure` MEANS
    `s 119(3) the penalty for an offence under s 119` (`Under section 113G(4), how I am convicted` `how I am convicted`)

@ref s 120(1)
@export Under section 120(1), must the company tell me when the register was last altered?
GIVEN `I inspected the register or the company gave me a copy` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did you inspect the register, or did the company give you a copy of it or part of it?
      `the alteration relates to protected information` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does the alteration relate to information the company must refrain from disclosing under regulations under section 120A?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`Under section 120(1), must the company tell me when the register was last altered` MEANS
    `s 120(1) the company must inform the person of the most recent date on which alterations were made and whether further alterations are to be made` `I inspected the register or the company gave me a copy` `the alteration relates to protected information`

@ref s 120(3)
@export Under section 120(3), is the company or an officer guilty of an offence for not giving me that information?
GIVEN `the company failed to provide the information` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did the company fail to provide the information required under section 120(1) or (2)?
      `I am a director of the company` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are you a director of the company?
      `I am the company secretary` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are you the secretary of the company?
      `I authorised or permitted the default, took part in it, or failed to take all reasonable steps to prevent it` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did you authorise or permit the default, take part in it, or fail to take all reasonable steps to prevent it? (this is what makes an officer "in default")
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`Under section 120(3), is the company or an officer guilty of an offence for not giving me that information` MEANS
    `s 120(3) the person commits an offence` `the company failed to provide the information` (`Under section 113(7), the party I am` `I am a director of the company` `I am the company secretary`) (`Under section 112, I state this as a yes or no answer` `I authorised or permitted the default, took part in it, or failed to take all reasonable steps to prevent it`)

@ref s 120A(6)
@export Under section 120A(6), do the protection rules affect how information about me as an officer is used?
GIVEN `the information is about me in another capacity` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the information about you in a capacity other than as a member or former member (for example as an officer of the company)?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`Under section 120A(6), do the protection rules affect how information about me as an officer is used` MEANS
    `s 120A(6) s 120A or regulations under it affect the use or disclosure of information about a person in any other capacity` `the information is about me in another capacity`

@ref s 120B(1)
@export Under section 120B(1), is the company or an officer guilty of an offence for breaking a protection restriction?
GIVEN `the company broke a restriction on use or disclosure` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did the company contravene a restriction on the use or disclosure of information imposed by regulations under section 120A?
      `I am a director of the company` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are you a director of the company?
      `I am the company secretary` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are you the secretary of the company?
      `I authorised or permitted the default, took part in it, or failed to take all reasonable steps to prevent it` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did you authorise or permit the default, take part in it, or fail to take all reasonable steps to prevent it? (this is what makes an officer "in default")
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`Under section 120B(1), is the company or an officer guilty of an offence for breaking a protection restriction` MEANS
    `s 120B(1) the person commits an offence` `the company broke a restriction on use or disclosure` (`Under section 113(7), the party I am` `I am a director of the company` `I am the company secretary`) (`Under section 112, I state this as a yes or no answer` `I authorised or permitted the default, took part in it, or failed to take all reasonable steps to prevent it`)

@ref s 120B(2)
@export Under section 120B(2), what is the penalty for breaking a protection restriction?
GIVEN `how I am convicted` IS A STRING @desc Where and how would the conviction be? One of: "on indictment", "summary, England and Wales", "summary, Scotland", "summary, Northern Ireland"
GIVETH A MAYBE Penalty
`Under section 120B(2), what is the penalty for breaking a protection restriction` MEANS
    `s 120B(2) the penalty for an offence under s 120B` (`Under section 113G(4), how I am convicted` `how I am convicted`)

§§ `Sections 121 to 128ZA: removing entries, share warrants, single member companies, treasury shares, rectifying the register, evidence and time limits`

@ref s 121
