      `the warrant had been surrendered and cancelled` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Had the warrant been surrendered and cancelled?
      `I lost money because of that entry` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did you incur a loss by reason of that entry?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`Under section 122(5), is the company responsible for my loss from entering a bearer's name on the register` MEANS
    `s 122(5) the company is responsible for the person's loss` `the company entered the bearer's name in the register in respect of the shares in the warrant` `the warrant had been surrendered and cancelled` `I lost money because of that entry`

@ref s 123(1)
@export Under section 123(1), must the register state that the company has only one member?
GIVEN `the company is a limited company formed under the Companies Act 2006` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the company a limited company formed under the Companies Act 2006?
      `the company was formed with only one member` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Was it formed with only one member?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`Under section 123(1), must the register state that the company has only one member` MEANS
    `s 123(1) the register must contain a statement that the company has only one member` `the company is a limited company formed under the Companies Act 2006` `the company was formed with only one member`

@ref s 123(2)
@export Under section 123(2), must the register record that the company has become a one member company?
GIVEN `the number of members of the limited company has fallen to one` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has the number of members of the limited company fallen to one?
      `an unlimited company with one member has become a limited company on re-registration` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has an unlimited company with only one member become a limited company on re-registration?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`Under section 123(2), must the register record that the company has become a one member company` MEANS
    `s 123(2) the register must contain a statement that the company has only one member and the date on which it became a company having only one member` `the number of members of the limited company has fallen to one` `an unlimited company with one member has become a limited company on re-registration`

@ref s 123(3)
@export Under section 123(3), must the register record that the company has ceased to have only one member?
