      `I am a director of the company` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are you a director of the company?
      `I am the company secretary` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are you the secretary of the company?
      `I authorised or permitted the default, took part in it, or failed to take all reasonable steps to prevent it` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did you authorise or permit the default, take part in it, or fail to take all reasonable steps to prevent it? (this is what makes an officer "in default")
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`Under section 123(4), am I or the company guilty of an offence for failing to record a single member` MEANS
    `s 123(4) the person commits an offence` `the company made default in complying with section 123` (`Under section 113(7), the party I am` `I am a director of the company` `I am the company secretary`) (`Under section 112, I state this as a yes or no answer` `I authorised or permitted the default, took part in it, or failed to take all reasonable steps to prevent it`)

@ref s 124(1)
@export Under section 124(1), is the company excused from complying with section 113 for the shares it bought back?
GIVEN `the company purchased its own shares` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did the company purchase its own shares?
      `section 724 applies to the purchase` IS A STRING @desc Does section 724 (treasury shares) apply to the purchase? Answer "yes", "no" or "not known".
      `the company cancelled all of the shares forthwith after the purchase` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did the company cancel all of the shares forthwith after the purchase?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`Under section 124(1), is the company excused from complying with section 113 for the shares it bought back` MEANS
    `s 124(1)(a) the requirements of section 113 need not be complied with` `the company purchased its own shares` (`Under section 136(1), what I know about another section's answer` `section 724 applies to the purchase`) `the company cancelled all of the shares forthwith after the purchase`

@ref s 124(2)
@export Under section 124(2), must the company be entered in the register as the member holding its treasury shares?
GIVEN `the company holds shares as treasury shares` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does the company hold shares as treasury shares?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`Under section 124(2), must the company be entered in the register as the member holding its treasury shares` MEANS
    `s 124(2) the company must be entered in the register as the member holding those shares` `the company holds shares as treasury shares`

@ref s 125(1)
@export Under section 125(1), may I apply to the court to rectify the register?
GIVEN `the register leaves out information it must include` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does the register leave out information that it is required to include?
      `the register includes information it must not include` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does the register include information that it is not required to include?
      `I am the person aggrieved` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are you the person aggrieved?
      `I am a member of the company` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are you a member of the company?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`Under section 125(1), may I apply to the court to rectify the register` MEANS
    `s 125(1) the applicant may apply to the court for rectification of the register` `the register leaves out information it must include` `the register includes information it must not include` (IF `I am the person aggrieved` THEN `s 125(1) the person aggrieved` ELSE IF `I am a member of the company` THEN `s 125(1) any member of the company` ELSE `s 125(1) someone else`)

@ref s 125(2)
@export Under section 125(2), may the court order the company to pay me damages when it rectifies the register?
GIVEN `I have applied to the court for rectification` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Have you applied to the court for rectification of the register?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`Under section 125(2), may the court order the company to pay me damages when it rectifies the register` MEANS
    `s 125(2) the court may make the order` `I have applied to the court for rectification` `s 125(2) order payment by the company of any damages sustained by any party aggrieved`

@ref s 126
