GIVEN `where the company is registered` IS A STRING @desc Where is the company registered? One of: "England and Wales", "Scotland", "Northern Ireland"
      `the notice is of a trust` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the notice one of a trust, whether expressed, implied or constructive?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`Under section 126, may notice of a trust be entered on the register of members` MEANS
    `s 126 notice of a trust may be entered on the register of members or be received by the registrar` (`Under section 126, where the company is registered` `where the company is registered`) `the notice is of a trust`

@ref s 127(1)
@export Under section 127(1), is the register of members evidence of what it records?
GIVEN `the matter is one the Act directs or authorises to be entered in the register` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the matter one that the Companies Act directs or authorises to be inserted in the register of members?
      `the central register is evidence of the matter under section 127(2)` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the central register, kept by the registrar, prima facie evidence of the matter under section 127(2) (a company that elected to keep information there before the option was repealed)?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`Under section 127(1), is the register of members evidence of what it records` MEANS
    `s 127(1) the register of members is prima facie evidence of the matter` `the matter is one the Act directs or authorises to be entered in the register` `the central register is evidence of the matter under section 127(2)`

@ref s 128(1)
@export Under section 128(1), is a claim against the company about an entry in the register out of time?
GIVEN `the claim is for liability incurred by the company from making or deleting an entry, or failing to` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the claim for liability incurred by the company from the making or deletion of an entry in the register of members, or from a failure to make or delete one?
      `the date the entry was made or deleted or the failure first occurred` IS A DATE @desc On what date was the entry made or deleted, or did the failure first occur?
      `the date the claim is brought` IS A DATE @desc On what date is the claim brought?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`Under section 128(1), is a claim against the company about an entry in the register out of time` MEANS
    `s 128(1) the liability is not enforceable` `the claim is for liability incurred by the company from making or deleting an entry, or failing to` `the date the entry was made or deleted or the failure first occurred` `the date the claim is brought`

@ref s 128ZA(1)
@export Under section 128ZA(1), must the company enter in its register all the information it would have had to enter?
GIVEN `an election was made under section 128B before it was repealed` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did the company make an election under section 128B (the option to keep information on the central register) before that section was repealed?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`Under section 128ZA(1), must the company enter in its register all the information it would have had to enter` MEANS
    `s 128ZA(1)(a) the company must enter in its register of members all of the information that it would have had to enter if the election had never been made` `an election was made under section 128B before it was repealed`

§§ `Sections 129 to 135: overseas branch registers (Ask only if the company keeps, or wants to keep, a branch register abroad)`

@ref s 129(1)
@export Under section 129(1), may the company keep an overseas branch register in the country?
GIVEN `the company has a share capital` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does the company have a share capital?
      `the company transacts business in the country` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does the company transact business in the country or territory?
      `the name of the country or territory` IS A STRING @desc What is the name of the country or territory (for example "Singapore")?
      `it is part of the dominions outside the United Kingdom, the Channel Islands and the Isle of Man` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it a part of Her Majesty's dominions outside the United Kingdom, the Channel Islands and the Isle of Man?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`Under section 129(1), may the company keep an overseas branch register in the country` MEANS
    `s 129(1) the company may cause to be kept in the country or territory a branch register of members resident there` `the company has a share capital` `the company transacts business in the country` (`s 129(2) this Chapter applies to the country or territory` `the name of the country or territory` `it is part of the dominions outside the United Kingdom, the Channel Islands and the Isle of Man`)

@ref s 130(1)
@export Under section 130(1), by what date must the company tell the registrar it has begun to keep an overseas branch register?
GIVEN `the date the company began to keep the overseas branch register` IS A DATE @desc On what date did the company begin to keep the overseas branch register?
GIVETH A DATE
`Under section 130(1), by what date must the company tell the registrar it has begun to keep an overseas branch register` MEANS
    `s 130(1) the last day for giving notice` `the date the company began to keep the overseas branch register`

@ref s 130(1)
@export Under section 130(1), did the company tell the registrar in time that it began to keep an overseas branch register?
GIVEN `the date the company began to keep the overseas branch register` IS A DATE @desc On what date did the company begin to keep the overseas branch register?
      `the date the company gave notice to the registrar` IS A DATE @desc On what date did the company give notice to the registrar?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`Under section 130(1), did the company tell the registrar in time that it began to keep an overseas branch register` MEANS
    `s 130(1) the company gave notice within 14 days` `the date the company began to keep the overseas branch register` `the date the company gave notice to the registrar`

@ref s 130(2)
@export Under section 130(2), am I or the company guilty of an offence for not telling the registrar of the opening?
GIVEN `the company made default in complying with section 130(1)` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did the company make default in giving the registrar notice of the opening of an overseas branch register?
      `I am a director of the company` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are you a director of the company?
      `I am the company secretary` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are you the secretary of the company?
      `I authorised or permitted the default, took part in it, or failed to take all reasonable steps to prevent it` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did you authorise or permit the default, take part in it, or fail to take all reasonable steps to prevent it? (this is what makes an officer "in default")
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`Under section 130(2), am I or the company guilty of an offence for not telling the registrar of the opening` MEANS
    `s 130(2) the person commits an offence` `the company made default in complying with section 130(1)` (`Under section 113(7), the party I am` `I am a director of the company` `I am the company secretary`) (`Under section 112, I state this as a yes or no answer` `I authorised or permitted the default, took part in it, or failed to take all reasonable steps to prevent it`)

@ref s 132(1)
@export Under section 132(1), is the overseas register or a duplicate kept available as it must be?
GIVEN `the company keeps an overseas branch register` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does the company keep an overseas branch register?
      `the register itself is kept available for inspection` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the overseas branch register itself kept available for inspection?
      `a duplicate duly entered up is kept available for inspection` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is a duplicate of it, duly entered up from time to time, kept available for inspection?
      `it is kept at the place in the United Kingdom where the main register is kept` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it kept available at the place in the United Kingdom where the company's main register is kept available for inspection?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`Under section 132(1), is the overseas register or a duplicate kept available as it must be` MEANS
    `s 132(1) the register or a duplicate is kept available for inspection as s 132(1) requires` `the company keeps an overseas branch register` `the register itself is kept available for inspection` `a duplicate duly entered up is kept available for inspection` `it is kept at the place in the United Kingdom where the main register is kept`

@ref s 133(2)
@export Under section 133(2), may a transaction in my overseas shares be registered in another register?
GIVEN `my shares are registered in an overseas branch register` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are your shares registered in an overseas branch register?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`Under section 133(2), may a transaction in my overseas shares be registered in another register` MEANS
    `s 133(2) a transaction with respect to the shares may be registered in any other register` `my shares are registered in an overseas branch register`

@ref s 133(3)
@export Under section 133(3), is my transfer of overseas register shares exempt from stamp duty?
GIVEN `my instrument transfers a share registered in an overseas branch register` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the instrument one of transfer of a share registered in an overseas branch register?
      `the instrument is executed in a part of the United Kingdom` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the instrument executed in a part of the United Kingdom?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`Under section 133(3), is my transfer of overseas register shares exempt from stamp duty` MEANS
    `s 133(3)(b) the instrument is exempt from stamp duty` `my instrument transfers a share registered in an overseas branch register` `the instrument is executed in a part of the United Kingdom`

@ref s 135(2)
@export Under section 135(2), does transferring the entries to this place meet the duty when the company discontinues an overseas branch register?
GIVEN `the company discontinues an overseas branch register` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the company discontinuing an overseas branch register?
      `the entries go to another overseas branch register in the same country` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Will all the entries be transferred to some other overseas branch register kept in the same country or territory?
      `the entries go to the main register` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Will all the entries be transferred to the main register?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`Under section 135(2), does transferring the entries to this place meet the duty when the company discontinues an overseas branch register` MEANS
    `s 135(2) all the entries in the register must be transferred to the destination` `the company discontinues an overseas branch register` (IF `the entries go to another overseas branch register in the same country` THEN `s 135(2)(a) to some other overseas branch register kept in the same country or territory` ELSE IF `the entries go to the main register` THEN `s 135(2)(b) to the main register` ELSE `s 135(2) somewhere else`)

@ref s 135(3)
@export Under section 135(3), by what date must the company tell the registrar it has discontinued an overseas branch register?
GIVEN `the date of the discontinuance` IS A DATE @desc On what date was the overseas branch register discontinued?
GIVETH A DATE
`Under section 135(3), by what date must the company tell the registrar it has discontinued an overseas branch register` MEANS
    `s 135(3) the last day for giving notice of the discontinuance` `the date of the discontinuance`

§§ `Sections 136 to 144: a subsidiary as a member of its holding company (Ask only if a company holds, or is to take, shares in its own holding company)`

@ref s 136(1)
@export Under section 136(1), is the subsidiary barred from being a member of its holding company?
GIVEN `the body corporate is a subsidiary of the company` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the body corporate a subsidiary of the company (and so is the company its holding company)?
      `section 137 lets it continue as a member` IS A STRING @desc Does section 137 let the body corporate continue to be a member? Answer "yes", "no" or "not known".
      `section 138 means the prohibition does not apply` IS A STRING @desc Does section 138 (personal representative or trustee) mean the prohibition does not apply? Answer "yes", "no" or "not known".
      `section 141 means the prohibition does not apply` IS A STRING @desc Does section 141 (authorised dealer in securities) mean the prohibition does not apply? Answer "yes", "no" or "not known".
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`Under section 136(1), is the subsidiary barred from being a member of its holding company` MEANS
    `s 136(1)(a) the prohibition applies: the body corporate cannot be a member of the company` (`Under section 112, I state this as a yes or no answer` `the body corporate is a subsidiary of the company`) (`Under section 136(1), what I know about another section's answer` `section 137 lets it continue as a member`) (`Under section 136(1), what I know about another section's answer` `section 138 means the prohibition does not apply`) (`Under section 136(1), what I know about another section's answer` `section 141 means the prohibition does not apply`)

@ref s 137(1)
@export Under section 137(1), may the body corporate continue to be a member because it held the shares before the prohibition?
GIVEN `where the company is registered` IS A STRING @desc Where is the company registered? One of: "England and Wales", "Scotland", "Northern Ireland"
      `the date the body corporate became a holder of the shares` IS A DATE @desc On what date did the body corporate become a holder of shares in the company?
      `the date this Chapter came into force` IS A DATE @desc On what date did Chapter 4 of Part 8 come into force? (a date outside the Companies Act text; you supply it)
      `the earlier prohibition did not apply to it` IS A BOOLEAN @desc If it became a holder on or after the relevant date and before this Chapter came into force: did the earlier prohibition (section 23(1) of the Companies Act 1985 or Article 33(1) of the Companies (Northern Ireland) Order 1986) not apply in the circumstances?
      `the prohibition in section 136 did not apply to it` IS A BOOLEAN @desc If it became a holder on or after this Chapter came into force: did the prohibition in section 136 not apply in the circumstances?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`Under section 137(1), may the body corporate continue to be a member because it held the shares before the prohibition` MEANS
    `s 137(1) the body corporate may continue to be a member of the company` (`s 137(2) the relevant date for the purposes of s 137(1)(a)` (`Under section 126, where the company is registered` `where the company is registered`)) `the date the body corporate became a holder of the shares` `the date this Chapter came into force` `the earlier prohibition did not apply to it` `the prohibition in section 136 did not apply to it`

@ref s 138(1)
@export Under section 138(1), does the prohibition not apply because the subsidiary acts only as personal representative or trustee?
GIVEN `the subsidiary is concerned only as personal representative` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the subsidiary concerned only as a personal representative?
      `the subsidiary is concerned only as trustee` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the subsidiary concerned only as a trustee?
      `the holding company or a subsidiary of it is beneficially interested under the trust` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the holding company, or a subsidiary of it, beneficially interested under the trust (leaving out the interests that section 138(2) says to disregard)?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`Under section 138(1), does the prohibition not apply because the subsidiary acts only as personal representative or trustee` MEANS
    `s 138(1) the prohibition in section 136 does not apply to the subsidiary` `the subsidiary is concerned only as personal representative` `the subsidiary is concerned only as trustee` `the holding company or a subsidiary of it is beneficially interested under the trust`

@ref s 141(1)
@export Under section 141(1), does the prohibition not apply because the subsidiary holds the shares as an intermediary?
GIVEN `the shares are held in the ordinary course of its business` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are the shares held by the subsidiary in the ordinary course of its business?
      `it carries on a bona fide business of dealing in securities` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does it carry on a bona fide business of dealing in securities?
      `it is a member of or has access to a UK regulated market` IS A STRING @desc Is it a member of, or does it have access to, a UK regulated market? Answer "yes", "no" or "not known".
      `its business is wholly or mainly making or managing investments` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does its business consist wholly or mainly in making or managing investments?
      `its business is wholly or mainly services to connected persons` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does its business consist wholly or mainly in, or is it carried on wholly or mainly for the purposes of, providing services to persons connected with it?
      `its business is insurance business` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is its business insurance business?
      `its business is managing or acting as trustee for a pension scheme` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is its business managing, or acting as trustee in relation to, a pension scheme (or carried on by the manager or trustee of one for the purposes of the scheme)?
      `its business is operating or acting as trustee for a collective investment scheme` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is its business operating, or acting as trustee in relation to, a collective investment scheme (or carried on by the operator or trustee of one for the purposes of the scheme)?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`Under section 141(1), does the prohibition not apply because the subsidiary holds the shares as an intermediary` MEANS
    `s 141(1) the prohibition in section 136 does not apply to the subsidiary` `the shares are held in the ordinary course of its business` (`s 141(2) the person is an intermediary` `it carries on a bona fide business of dealing in securities` (`Under section 136(1), what I know about another section's answer` `it is a member of or has access to a UK regulated market`) (`s 141(3) the business is an excluded business` (`s 141(3) business facts` OF `its business is wholly or mainly making or managing investments`, `its business is wholly or mainly services to connected persons`, `its business is insurance business`, `its business is managing or acting as trustee for a pension scheme`, `its business is operating or acting as trustee for a collective investment scheme`)))

@ref s 142(1)
@export Under section 142(1), is the person who bought shares from a dealer subsidiary protected?
GIVEN `a dealer subsidiary acquired shares in its holding company in contravention` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did a subsidiary that is a dealer in securities purportedly acquire shares in its holding company in contravention of section 136?
      `I acted in good faith and agreed to acquire shares in the holding company` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did you, acting in good faith, agree to acquire shares in the holding company?
      `I agreed for value and without notice of the contravention` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did you agree for value and without notice of the contravention?
      `I acquire them from the subsidiary or from a later purported acquirer` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Do you acquire them from the subsidiary, or from someone who purportedly acquired them after the subsidiary disposed of them?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`Under section 142(1), is the person who bought shares from a dealer subsidiary protected` MEANS
    `s 142(2) the transfer to that person has the same effect as it would have had if the original acquisition by the subsidiary had not been in contravention` (`s 142(1) this section applies` `a dealer subsidiary acquired shares in its holding company in contravention` `I acted in good faith and agreed to acquire shares in the holding company` `I agreed for value and without notice of the contravention` `I acquire them from the subsidiary or from a later purported acquirer`)

@ref s 143
@export Under section 143, are references to shares read as references to members' interests in my company?
GIVEN `the company is limited by shares` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the company a company limited by shares?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`Under section 143, are references to shares read as references to members' interests in my company` MEANS
    `s 143 the references in this Chapter to shares are read as references to the interest of its members as such, whatever the form of that interest` `the company is limited by shares`

@ref s 144
@export Under section 144, does the prohibition apply to my nominee as it does to the subsidiary?
GIVEN `the person is a nominee acting on behalf of a subsidiary` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the person a nominee acting on behalf of a subsidiary?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`Under section 144, does the prohibition apply to my nominee as it does to the subsidiary` MEANS
    `s 144 the provisions of this Chapter apply to the nominee as to the subsidiary itself` `the person is a nominee acting on behalf of a subsidiary`

§ `Part 9: Exercise of members' rights`

§§ `Section 145: nominating someone else to exercise my rights as a member (Ask only if the company's articles allow a nomination)`

@ref s 145(2)
@export Under section 145(2), may the person I nominated do instead what the Companies Acts let me do as a member?
GIVEN `the articles enable a member to nominate another person to enjoy or exercise rights` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Do the company's articles enable a member to nominate another person as entitled to enjoy or exercise all or any specified rights of the member?
      `the thing is required or authorised by a provision of the Companies Acts` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the thing a provision of the Companies Acts requires or authorises to be done by or in relation to a member?
      `the Companies Acts require it of the member (not merely allow it)` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Do the Companies Acts require it to be done (answer no if they merely allow it)?
      `it is necessary to give effect to the nomination` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it necessary in order to give effect to the provision in the articles?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`Under section 145(2), may the person I nominated do instead what the Companies Acts let me do as a member` MEANS
    `s 145(2) the act is done, or may be done, by or in relation to the nominated person instead of the member` (`s 145(1) this section applies` `the articles enable a member to nominate another person to enjoy or exercise rights`) (`Under section 112, I state this as a yes or no answer` `the thing is required or authorised by a provision of the Companies Acts`) (IF `the Companies Acts require it of the member (not merely allow it)` THEN `s 145(2) an act required to be done by or in relation to the member` ELSE `s 145(2) an act that may be done by or in relation to the member`) `it is necessary to give effect to the nomination`

@ref s 145(4)
@export Under section 145(4), can the person I nominated enforce the right against the company?
GIVEN `I am the nominated person and not the member` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are you the person nominated (and not the member who nominated you)?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`Under section 145(4), can the person I nominated enforce the right against the company` MEANS
    `s 145(4)(a) the person can enforce a right against the company by virtue of s 145 or the provision in the articles` `I am the nominated person and not the member`

§§ `Sections 146 to 151: information rights for a person on whose behalf shares are held (Ask only if the company's shares are traded on a regulated market)`

@ref s 146(2)
@export Under section 146(2), may I nominate the person I hold shares for to enjoy information rights?
GIVEN `shares are admitted to trading on a UK regulated market` IS A STRING @desc Are the company's shares admitted to trading on a UK regulated market? Answer "yes", "no" or "not known".
      `shares are admitted to trading on an EU regulated market` IS A STRING @desc Are the company's shares admitted to trading on an EU regulated market? Answer "yes", "no" or "not known".
      `I am a member of the company` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are you a member of the company?
      `I hold shares on behalf of the other person` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Do you hold shares on behalf of the person you want to nominate?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`Under section 146(2), may I nominate the person I hold shares for to enjoy information rights` MEANS
    `s 146(2) the member may nominate the other person to enjoy information rights` (`s 146(1) this section applies to the company` (`Under section 136(1), what I know about another section's answer` `shares are admitted to trading on a UK regulated market`) (`Under section 136(1), what I know about another section's answer` `shares are admitted to trading on an EU regulated market`)) `I am a member of the company` `I hold shares on behalf of the other person`

@ref s 146(5)
@export Under section 146(5), is the company excused from acting on my nomination?
GIVEN `my nomination relates to certain information rights only` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does the nomination relate to certain information rights only?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`Under section 146(5), is the company excused from acting on my nomination` MEANS
    `s 146(5) the company need not act on the nomination` `my nomination relates to certain information rights only`

@ref s 147(2)
@export Under section 147(2), did the request for hard copies come before the nomination?
GIVEN `the date I made the request and gave an address` IS A DATE @desc On what date did you request the member to notify the company, and provide an address?
      `the date the nomination was made` IS A DATE @desc On what date was the nomination made?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`Under section 147(2), did the request for hard copies come before the nomination` MEANS
    `s 147(2) the request was made and the address provided before the nomination was made` `the date I made the request and gave an address` `the date the nomination was made`

@ref s 147(3)
@export Under section 147(3), am I entitled to hard copy communications?
GIVEN `the member received my request` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did the member who nominated you receive your request?
      `the member notified the company that I wish to receive hard copies` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did the member notify the company that you wish to receive hard copy communications?
      `the member gave the company my address` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did the member give the company your address?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`Under section 147(3), am I entitled to hard copy communications` MEANS
    `s 147(3) the right of the nominated person is to receive hard copy communications` `the member received my request` `the member notified the company that I wish to receive hard copies` `the member gave the company my address`

@ref s 147(5)
@export Under section 147(5), am I taken to have agreed that the company may use a website?
GIVEN `no notification was given` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Was no notification given to the company that you wish to receive hard copies?
      `no address was provided` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Was no address provided for hard copies?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`Under section 147(5), am I taken to have agreed that the company may use a website` MEANS
    `s 147(5) the nominated person is taken to have agreed that documents or information may be sent or supplied to him by means of a website` `no notification was given` `no address was provided`

@ref s 148(2)
@export Under section 148(2), may the nomination be ended at my request?
GIVEN `I am the member who made the nomination` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are you the member who made the nomination?
      `I am the nominated person` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are you the nominated person?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`Under section 148(2), may the nomination be ended at my request` MEANS
    `s 148(2) the nomination may be terminated at the request` (IF `I am the member who made the nomination` THEN `s 148(2) the member` ELSE IF `I am the nominated person` THEN `s 148(2) the nominated person` ELSE `s 148(2) someone else`)

@ref s 148(5)
@export Under section 148(5), is the effect of my nominations suspended?
GIVEN `the number of persons I have nominated` IS A NUMBER @desc How many persons have you nominated?
      `the number of shares I have in the company` IS A NUMBER @desc How many shares do you have in the company?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`Under section 148(5), is the effect of my nominations suspended` MEANS
    `s 148(5) the effect of the nominations made by the member is suspended` `the number of persons I have nominated` `the number of shares I have in the company`

@ref s 148(7)
@export Under section 148(7), has the nomination ended because I did not answer the company's enquiry?
GIVEN `the company enquired whether I wish to retain information rights` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did the company enquire of you whether you wish to retain information rights?
      `the date the company's enquiry was sent` IS A DATE @desc On what date was the company's enquiry sent?
      `I replied` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has the company received a response from you?
      `the date the company received my response` IS A DATE @desc If you replied, on what date did the company receive your response? (any date if you did not)
      `the day I am asking` IS A DATE @desc On what date are you asking this question?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`Under section 148(7), has the nomination ended because I did not answer the company's enquiry` MEANS
    `s 148(7) the nomination has ceased to have effect` `the company enquired whether I wish to retain information rights` `the date the company's enquiry was sent` (IF `I replied` THEN JUST `the date the company received my response` ELSE NOTHING) `the day I am asking`

@ref s 148(7)
@export Under section 148(7), by what date must I answer the company's enquiry?
GIVEN `the date the company's enquiry was sent` IS A DATE @desc On what date was the company's enquiry sent?
GIVETH A DATE
`Under section 148(7), by what date must I answer the company's enquiry` MEANS
    `s 148(7) the last day of the period of 28 days beginning with the date on which the enquiry was sent` `the date the company's enquiry was sent`

@ref s 149(2)
@export Under section 149(2), must the notice of a meeting I am sent come with a statement about voting?
GIVEN `the company sent me a copy of a notice of a meeting` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did the company send you a copy of a notice of a meeting as a person nominated to enjoy information rights?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`Under section 149(2), must the notice of a meeting I am sent come with a statement about voting` MEANS
    `s 149(2) the copy of the notice must be accompanied by the statement` (`s 149(1) this section applies` `the company sent me a copy of a notice of a meeting`)

@ref s 150(2)
@export Under section 150(2), can I enforce the nominated person's enjoyment of the rights against the company?
GIVEN `the nomination is under section 146` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the nomination one under section 146?
      `I am the member` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are you the member who made the nomination?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`Under section 150(2), can I enforce the nominated person's enjoyment of the rights against the company` MEANS
    `s 150(2) the nominated person's enjoyment of the rights is enforceable against the company by the member as if they were rights conferred by the company's articles` `the nomination is under section 146` `I am the member`

@ref s 150(4)
@export Under section 150(4), is the company excused from sending the document to the person I nominated?
GIVEN `the members entitled are determined as at a date before it is sent` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are the members entitled to the document or information determined as at a date or time before it is sent or supplied?
      `the date as at which the members are determined` IS A DATE @desc What is that date?
      `the date the company received the nomination` IS A DATE @desc On what date did the company receive the nomination?
      `that date falls in a period of suspension of the nomination` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does that date fall in a period of suspension of the nomination?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`Under section 150(4), is the company excused from sending the document to the person I nominated` MEANS
    `s 150(4)(a) the company need not send or supply the document or information to the nominated person` `the members entitled are determined as at a date before it is sent` `the date as at which the members are determined` `the date the company received the nomination` `that date falls in a period of suspension of the nomination`

§§ `Sections 152 and 153: holding shares for more than one person, and members' requests`

@ref s 152(2)
@export Under section 152(2), must I tell the company that I am not exercising all my rights?
GIVEN `I hold shares on behalf of more than one person` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Do you hold shares in the company on behalf of more than one person?
      `I exercise such rights` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Do you exercise the rights attached to the shares, or rights under an enactment exercisable by virtue of holding them?
      `I am not exercising all my rights` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are you not exercising all of those rights?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`Under section 152(2), must I tell the company that I am not exercising all my rights` MEANS
    `s 152(2) the member must inform the company to what extent he is exercising the rights` `I hold shares on behalf of more than one person` `I exercise such rights` `I am not exercising all my rights`

@ref s 152(3)
@export Under section 152(3), must I tell the company that I am exercising my rights in different ways?
GIVEN `I hold shares on behalf of more than one person` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Do you hold shares in the company on behalf of more than one person?
      `I exercise such rights in different ways` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Do you exercise those rights in different ways?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`Under section 152(3), must I tell the company that I am exercising my rights in different ways` MEANS
    `s 152(3) the member must inform the company of the ways in which he is exercising the rights and to what extent` `I hold shares on behalf of more than one person` `I exercise such rights in different ways`

@ref s 152(4)
@export Under section 152(4), may the company assume that I exercise all my rights in the same way?
GIVEN `I exercise such rights` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Do you exercise the rights attached to the shares, or rights under an enactment exercisable by virtue of holding them?
      `I told the company I am not exercising all my rights` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did you inform the company that you are not exercising all your rights?
      `I told the company I am exercising my rights in different ways` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did you inform the company that you are exercising your rights in different ways?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`Under section 152(4), may the company assume that I exercise all my rights in the same way` MEANS
    `s 152(4) the company is entitled to assume that the member is exercising all his rights and is exercising them in the same way` `I exercise such rights` `I told the company I am not exercising all my rights` `I told the company I am exercising my rights in different ways`

@ref s 153(2)
@export Under section 153(2), must the company act on our request?
GIVEN `the number of persons making the request` IS A NUMBER @desc How many persons make the request?
      `the request is authenticated by all of us` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the request authenticated by all the persons making it?
      `each of us who is not a member gives the member's name and address` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does each person making it who is not a member give the full name and address of the member who holds shares on that person's behalf?
      `each of us who is not a member states the member holds the shares in the course of a business` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does each such person state that the member holds those shares on that person's behalf in the course of a business?
      `each of us who is not a member states the number of shares` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does each such person state the number of shares the member holds on that person's behalf?
      `each of us who is not a member states the amount paid up` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does each such person state the total amount paid up on those shares?
      `each of us who is not a member states the shares are not held for anyone else among us` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does each such person state that the shares are not held on behalf of anyone else or, if they are, that the others are not among the persons making the request?
      `each of us who is not a member states the shares confer relevant voting rights` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does each such person state that some or all of those shares confer voting rights relevant to the section in question?
      `each of us who is not a member states a right to instruct the member` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does each such person state that the person has the right to instruct the member how to exercise those rights?
      `each member among us states he holds shares for no one else` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does each member making the request state that he holds shares otherwise than on behalf of another person?
      `each member among us states those he holds for are not among us` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does each member making the request state that he holds shares on behalf of others who are not among the persons making the request?
      `the request comes with the evidence the company reasonably requires` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the request accompanied by the evidence the company may reasonably require of those matters?
      `the total paid up on the shares, in pounds` IS A NUMBER @desc What is the total amount paid up, in pounds, on the shares held as mentioned above?
      `the request meets the requirements of the section in question` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does the request comply with any other requirements of the section in question as to contents, timing and otherwise?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`Under section 153(2), must the company act on our request` MEANS
    `s 153(2) the company is required to act under the section on the request` (`s 153(2) request` OF `the number of persons making the request`, `the request is authenticated by all of us`, `each of us who is not a member gives the member's name and address`, `each of us who is not a member states the member holds the shares in the course of a business`, `each of us who is not a member states the number of shares`, `each of us who is not a member states the amount paid up`, `each of us who is not a member states the shares are not held for anyone else among us`, `each of us who is not a member states the shares confer relevant voting rights`, `each of us who is not a member states a right to instruct the member`, `each member among us states he holds shares for no one else`, `each member among us states those he holds for are not among us`, `the request comes with the evidence the company reasonably requires`, `the total paid up on the shares, in pounds`, `the request meets the requirements of the section in question`)

-- ====================================================================================================
-- seat questions from part coa4 (merged by the lead on 2026-11-12; unchanged text follows)
-- ====================================================================================================
-- coa4-seat.l4: Companies Act 2006 (United Kingdom), Part 10, Chapter 1 (from s 154), Chapters 2, 3 and 4 (to s 204(2)):
-- THE SEAT LAYER for lines 2022-2696 of ukpga-2006-46.txt.
--
-- SEAT: an individual who is, or is about to become, a director, a company secretary or a member (shareholder) of a company
-- registered under the Act, or who deals with one, asking on facts they can state what the Act requires or lets them do, what
-- rights they have against the company or its directors, what they must disclose, file, approve or vote on and by when, and what
-- follows (liability, offences, penalties) if it is not done. (Assumed, not ruled: the Act is addressed to companies, so the
-- individual is whoever stands in a company's management or ownership.) There is never a seat for an official.
--
-- This layer asks the seat's questions of the layer-1 modules imported above and calls their rules; it restates none. Every question
-- takes plain inputs, one per fact the person can state, each with an @desc worded as that person would be asked. The answers are
-- MAYBE BOOLEAN (JUST TRUE, JUST FALSE, or NOTHING = "the Act does not say on these facts") unless the question asks for a day, a
-- number of pounds or a penalty; a caller must never turn NOTHING into FALSE. A fact another part of the Act decides (is the
-- person connected with a director, a shadow director, an officer in default, is the identity verified) is asked as a plain
-- yes/no and passed on as JUST TRUE or JUST FALSE: the form cannot ask "I do not know". The pounds a level on the standard scale
-- stands for are not in the Act: the person is asked for them. Where the text carries two wordings of one penalty, the person
-- says which is in force (NOTES.md, fork F2).
-- Every question name begins "Under section N," with the Act's own numbering.

-- A helper that is not a question: the answers of several rules taken together. JUST FALSE if any is JUST FALSE, JUST TRUE if all
-- are JUST TRUE, and NOTHING otherwise.
GIVEN answers IS A LIST OF MAYBE BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`coa4 seat all of these answers hold` MEANS
    IF any (GIVEN a YIELD a EQUALS JUST FALSE) answers
    THEN JUST FALSE
    ELSE IF all (GIVEN a YIELD a EQUALS JUST TRUE) answers
         THEN JUST TRUE
         ELSE NOTHING

-- The person in the seat, as the core's `Individual` (identity is the reference field; a placeholder, since no rule reads it).
GIVEN d IS A DATE
GIVETH A Individual
`coa4 seat the individual born on` MEANS Individual WITH `reference for the individual` IS "the person in the seat", `date of birth` IS d

§ `Part 10, Chapter 1: Appointment and removal of directors`

§§ `Requirement to have directors (ss 154 to 156)`

@export Under section 154, does my company have enough directors (s 154)?
GIVEN `my company is a public company` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the company a public company (one whose certificate of incorporation says it is a public company)?
      `the number of directors my company has` IS A NUMBER @desc How many directors does the company have?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 154, does my company have enough directors` IS
    IF `my company is a public company`
    THEN `s 154(2) the public company meets the requirement to have at least two directors` `my company is a public company` `the number of directors my company has`
    ELSE `s 154(1) the private company meets the requirement to have at least one director` (NOT (`my company is a public company`)) `the number of directors my company has`

@export Under section 155, does my company have a director who is a natural person (s 155)?
GIVEN `the number of my company's directors who are natural persons` IS A NUMBER @desc How many of the company's directors are natural persons (human beings)?
      `the office of director is held by a natural person as a corporation sole` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the office of director held by a natural person as a corporation sole?
      `the office of director is held by a natural person by virtue of another office` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the office of director otherwise held by a natural person by virtue of an office?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 155, does my company have a director who is a natural person` IS
    IF `s 155(2) the requirement is met by the office of director being held by a natural person as a corporation sole or by virtue of an office` `the office of director is held by a natural person as a corporation sole` `the office of director is held by a natural person by virtue of another office` EQUALS JUST TRUE
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE `s 155(1) the company meets the requirement to have at least one director who is a natural person` `the number of my company's directors who are natural persons`

@export Under section 156, may the Secretary of State direct my company to appoint a director (s 156(1))?
GIVEN `it appears that the company has too few directors` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does it appear to the Secretary of State that the company has fewer directors than section 154 requires?
      `it appears that the company has no director who is a natural person` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does it appear to the Secretary of State that the company has no director who is a natural person (section 155)?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 156, may the Secretary of State direct my company to appoint a director` IS
    `s 156(1) the Secretary of State may give the company a direction under section 156` `it appears that the company has too few directors` `it appears that the company has no director who is a natural person`

@export Under section 156, is the direction my company has been given valid in form (s 156(2) and (3))?
GIVEN `the direction names the requirement the company is in breach of` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does the direction say which requirement (section 154 or 155) the company appears to be in breach of?
      `the direction says what the company must do` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does the direction say what the company must do to comply?
      `the direction gives a period` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does the direction give the period within which the company must do it?
      `the direction tells the company the consequences` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does the direction tell the company what follows if it fails to comply?
      `the day the direction was given` IS A DATE @desc On what day was the direction given?
      `the last day of the period in the direction` IS A DATE @desc On what day does the period the direction allows end?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 156, is the direction my company has been given valid in form` IS
    `coa4 seat all of these answers hold` (LIST `s 156(2) the direction specifies what the section requires it to specify` `the direction names the requirement the company is in breach of` `the direction says what the company must do` `the direction gives a period`
                                                , `s 156(2) the period the direction specifies is not less than one month or more than three months after the day the direction is given` `the day the direction was given` `the last day of the period in the direction`
                                                , `s 156(3) the direction informs the company of the consequences of failing to comply as the section requires` `the direction tells the company the consequences`)

@export Under section 156, has my company complied with the direction (s 156(4) and (5))?
GIVEN `the company is in breach of section 154 or 155` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the company in breach of section 154 (too few directors) or section 155 (no natural person director)?
      `the company has already made the necessary appointments` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has the company already made the necessary appointment or appointments (so far as it has)?
      `the appointments were made in time` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Were the necessary appointments made before the end of the period the direction gave?
      `the notice under section 167G was given in time` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Was notice of them given to the registrar (under section 167G) before the end of that period?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 156, has my company complied with the direction` IS
    IF `the company has already made the necessary appointments`
    THEN `s 156(5) the company has complied with the direction by giving notice of the appointments already made` `the company has already made the necessary appointments` `the notice under section 167G was given in time`
    ELSE `s 156(4) the company has complied with the direction by making the appointments and giving notice of them` `the company is in breach of section 154 or 155` `the appointments were made in time` `the notice under section 167G was given in time`

@export Under section 156, am I guilty of an offence because my company did not comply with the direction (s 156(6))?
GIVEN `my company failed to comply with the direction` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did the company fail to comply with the direction?
      `I am an officer of the company` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are you an officer of the company (a director, manager or secretary)?
      `I am a shadow director of the company` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are you a shadow director (a person whose directions the directors are accustomed to act on)?
      `I am in default` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are you an officer in default (did you knowingly authorise or permit the failure, or take part in it)?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 156, am I guilty of an offence because my company did not comply with the direction` IS
    `s 156(6)(b) the officer in default commits the offence` `my company failed to comply with the direction` (JUST `I am an officer of the company`) (JUST `I am a shadow director of the company`) (JUST `I am in default`)

@export Under section 156, what is the most I can be fined for failing to comply with the direction, in pounds (s 156(7))?
GIVEN `how I am convicted` IS A `Mode of conviction` @desc How are you convicted: on conviction on indictment, on summary conviction, or on summary conviction in England and Wales, in Scotland or in Northern Ireland?
      `the statutory maximum in pounds` IS A NUMBER @desc How many pounds is the statutory maximum? (set outside the Companies Act)
      `level 4 in pounds` IS A NUMBER @desc How many pounds is level 4 on the standard scale? (set outside the Companies Act)
      `level 5 in pounds` IS A NUMBER @desc How many pounds is level 5 on the standard scale? (set outside the Companies Act)
GIVETH A MAYBE NUMBER
DECIDE `Under section 156, what is the most I can be fined for failing to comply with the direction` IS
    CONSIDER `s 156(7) the penalty for the offence, under the wording ending one-tenth of level 5 on the standard scale` `how I am convicted`
    WHEN NOTHING THEN NOTHING
    WHEN JUST p THEN
         CONSIDER p's `fine not exceeding`
         WHEN NOTHING THEN NOTHING
         WHEN JUST limit THEN `s 156(7) the fine limit in pounds` limit (`s 156(7) standard scale in pounds` OF `the statutory maximum in pounds`, `level 4 in pounds`, `level 5 in pounds`)

@export Under section 156, what is the most the daily default fine can be for continued failure, in pounds (s 156(7))?
GIVEN `how I am convicted` IS A `Mode of conviction` @desc How are you convicted: on conviction on indictment, on summary conviction, or on summary conviction in England and Wales, in Scotland or in Northern Ireland?
      `the statutory maximum in pounds` IS A NUMBER @desc How many pounds is the statutory maximum? (set outside the Companies Act)
      `level 4 in pounds` IS A NUMBER @desc How many pounds is level 4 on the standard scale? (set outside the Companies Act)
      `level 5 in pounds` IS A NUMBER @desc How many pounds is level 5 on the standard scale? (set outside the Companies Act)
      `the wording one-tenth of the greater of 5,000 pounds or level 4 is in force` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the wording "one-tenth of the greater of £5,000 or level 4 on the standard scale" in force? (the text shows two wordings; answer no if the wording is "one-tenth of level 5")
GIVETH A MAYBE NUMBER
DECIDE `Under section 156, what is the most the daily default fine can be for continued failure` IS
    IF `the wording one-tenth of the greater of 5,000 pounds or level 4 is in force`
    THEN IF `how I am convicted` EQUALS `on summary conviction`
         THEN JUST (`s 156(7) the daily default fine limit in pounds under the wording one-tenth of the greater of 5000 pounds or level 4 on the standard scale` (`s 156(7) standard scale in pounds` OF `the statutory maximum in pounds`, `level 4 in pounds`, `level 5 in pounds`))
         ELSE NOTHING
    ELSE CONSIDER `s 156(7) the penalty for the offence, under the wording ending one-tenth of level 5 on the standard scale` `how I am convicted`
         WHEN NOTHING THEN NOTHING
         WHEN JUST p THEN
              CONSIDER p's `daily default fine for continued contravention`
              WHEN NOTHING THEN NOTHING
              WHEN JUST limit THEN `s 156(7) the fine limit in pounds` limit (`s 156(7) standard scale in pounds` OF `the statutory maximum in pounds`, `level 4 in pounds`, `level 5 in pounds`)

§§ `Appointment (ss 156A to 161)`

@export Under section 156A, am I barred from being appointed a director because I am not a natural person (s 156A(1))?
GIVEN `the person is a natural person` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the person to be appointed a natural person (a human being)?
      `the person holds the office as a corporation sole or by virtue of an office` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the office held by a natural person as a corporation sole or otherwise by virtue of an office?
      `regulations under section 156B allow it` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Do regulations under section 156B allow a person who is not a natural person to be appointed in this case?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 156A, am I barred from being appointed a director because I am not a natural person` IS
    `s 156A(1) section 156A(1) bars the appointment of the person as a director` `the person is a natural person` `the person holds the office as a corporation sole or by virtue of an office` `regulations under section 156B allow it`

@export Under section 156A, is an appointment of a person who is not a natural person void (s 156A(3))?
GIVEN `the person is a natural person` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the person appointed a natural person (a human being)?
      `the person holds the office as a corporation sole or by virtue of an office` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the office held by a natural person as a corporation sole or otherwise by virtue of an office?
      `regulations under section 156B allow it` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Do regulations under section 156B allow a person who is not a natural person to be appointed in this case?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 156A, is an appointment of a person who is not a natural person void` IS
    `s 156A(3) the appointment made is void` (`s 156A(1) section 156A(1) bars the appointment of the person as a director` `the person is a natural person` `the person holds the office as a corporation sole or by virtue of an office` `regulations under section 156B allow it`)

@export Under section 156C, have I ceased to be a director because I am not a natural person (s 156C(2))?
GIVEN `the day section 156A came into force` IS A DATE @desc On what day did section 156A come into force?
      `I was appointed before section 156A came into force` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Were you appointed a director before section 156A came into force?
      `I am not a natural person` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are you not a natural person (a human being)?
      `regulations under section 156B except my case` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Do regulations under section 156B except your case from section 156A?
      `the day in question` IS A DATE @desc For what day are you asking?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 156C, have I ceased to be a director because I am not a natural person` IS
    `s 156C(2) the person has ceased to hold office by virtue of that appointment` `the day section 156A came into force` `I was appointed before section 156A came into force` `I am not a natural person` `regulations under section 156B except my case` `the day in question`

@export Under section 157, does section 157(1) bar the appointment of a person of my age as a director (s 157(1))?
GIVEN `the date of birth` IS A DATE @desc What is the person's date of birth?
      `the day the appointment takes effect` IS A DATE @desc On what day does the appointment take effect?
      `regulations under section 158 allow it` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Do regulations under section 158 allow a person under 16 to be appointed in this case?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 157, does section 157(1) bar the appointment of a person of my age as a director` IS
    `s 157(1) section 157(1) bars the appointment of the person as a director` (`coa4 seat the individual born on` `the date of birth`) `the day the appointment takes effect` `regulations under section 158 allow it`

@export Under section 157, is the appointment of a person under 16 void (s 157(4))?
GIVEN `the date of birth` IS A DATE @desc What is the person's date of birth?
      `the day the appointment takes effect` IS A DATE @desc On what day does the appointment take effect?
      `regulations under section 158 allow it` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Do regulations under section 158 allow a person under 16 to be appointed in this case?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 157, is the appointment of a person under 16 void` IS
    `s 157(4) the appointment made is void` (`s 157(1) section 157(1) bars the appointment of the person as a director` (`coa4 seat the individual born on` `the date of birth`) `the day the appointment takes effect` `regulations under section 158 allow it`)

@export Under section 159A, am I barred from being appointed a director of a company registered in England and Wales or Scotland (s 159A, Part 1 of the table)?
GIVEN `row 1 applies to me` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it true that you are subject to a disqualification order or undertaking under the Company Directors Disqualification Act 1986?
      `row 1 exception applies` IS A BOOLEAN @desc For what you are doing, do you have the permission of a court or the authority of a licence, or does an exception apply, by virtue of the provision named in column 2 of that row of the table in section 159A(2)?
      `row 2 applies to me` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it true that any of the circumstances in section 11 of that Act (bankruptcy and the like) apply to you?
      `row 2 exception applies` IS A BOOLEAN @desc For what you are doing, do you have the permission of a court or the authority of a licence, or does an exception apply, by virtue of the provision named in column 2 of that row of the table in section 159A(2)?
      `row 3 applies to me` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it true that you are subject to director disqualification sanctions (section 11A of that Act)?
      `row 3 exception applies` IS A BOOLEAN @desc For what you are doing, do you have the permission of a court or the authority of a licence, or does an exception apply, by virtue of the provision named in column 2 of that row of the table in section 159A(2)?
      `row 4 applies to me` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it true that section 12 of that Act applies to you (revocation of an administration order against an individual)?
      `row 4 exception applies` IS A BOOLEAN @desc For what you are doing, do you have the permission of a court or the authority of a licence, or does an exception apply, by virtue of the provision named in column 2 of that row of the table in section 159A(2)?
      `row 5 applies to me` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it true that you are subject to an order or undertaking recognised under section 12A or 12B of that Act (Northern Ireland orders)?
      `row 5 exception applies` IS A BOOLEAN @desc For what you are doing, do you have the permission of a court or the authority of a licence, or does an exception apply, by virtue of the provision named in column 2 of that row of the table in section 159A(2)?
      `row 6 applies to me` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it true that you are disqualified as mentioned in section 1184(2)(a) or (b) or subject to an undertaking under section 1184(3)?
      `row 6 exception applies` IS A BOOLEAN @desc For what you are doing, do you have the permission of a court or the authority of a licence, or does an exception apply, by virtue of the provision named in column 2 of that row of the table in section 159A(2)?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 159A, am I barred from being appointed a director of a company registered in England and Wales or Scotland` IS
    `s 159A(1) section 159A(1) bars the appointment of the person as a director` (`s 159A(2) the person is disqualified under the directors disqualification legislation` `England and Wales` (LIST (`s 159A(2) fact about a row` OF `s 159A(2) Part 1 row 1: a disqualification order or undertaking under the 1986 Act`, `row 1 applies to me`, `row 1 exception applies`) , (`s 159A(2) fact about a row` OF `s 159A(2) Part 1 row 2: the circumstances in section 11 of the 1986 Act (bankruptcy etc)`, `row 2 applies to me`, `row 2 exception applies`) , (`s 159A(2) fact about a row` OF `s 159A(2) Part 1 row 3: director disqualification sanctions (section 11A of the 1986 Act)`, `row 3 applies to me`, `row 3 exception applies`) , (`s 159A(2) fact about a row` OF `s 159A(2) Part 1 row 4: section 12 of the 1986 Act (revocation of administration order against an individual)`, `row 4 applies to me`, `row 4 exception applies`) , (`s 159A(2) fact about a row` OF `s 159A(2) Part 1 row 5: an order or undertaking mentioned in section 12A or 12B of the 1986 Act`, `row 5 applies to me`, `row 5 exception applies`) , (`s 159A(2) fact about a row` OF `s 159A(2) Part 1 row 6: disqualified as mentioned in section 1184`, `row 6 applies to me`, `row 6 exception applies`)))

@export Under section 159A, am I barred from being appointed a director of a company registered in Northern Ireland (s 159A, Part 2 of the table)?
GIVEN `row 1 applies to me` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it true that you are subject to a disqualification order or undertaking under the Company Directors Disqualification (Northern Ireland) Order 2002?
      `row 1 exception applies` IS A BOOLEAN @desc For what you are doing, do you have the permission of a court or the authority of a licence, or does an exception apply, by virtue of the provision named in column 2 of that row of the table in section 159A(2)?
      `row 2 applies to me` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it true that any of the circumstances in Article 15 of that Order (bankruptcy and the like) apply to you?
      `row 2 exception applies` IS A BOOLEAN @desc For what you are doing, do you have the permission of a court or the authority of a licence, or does an exception apply, by virtue of the provision named in column 2 of that row of the table in section 159A(2)?
      `row 3 applies to me` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it true that you are subject to director disqualification sanctions (Article 15A of that Order)?
      `row 3 exception applies` IS A BOOLEAN @desc For what you are doing, do you have the permission of a court or the authority of a licence, or does an exception apply, by virtue of the provision named in column 2 of that row of the table in section 159A(2)?
      `row 4 applies to me` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it true that Article 16 of that Order applies to you (revocation of an administration order against an individual)?
      `row 4 exception applies` IS A BOOLEAN @desc For what you are doing, do you have the permission of a court or the authority of a licence, or does an exception apply, by virtue of the provision named in column 2 of that row of the table in section 159A(2)?
      `row 5 applies to me` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it true that you are subject to an order or undertaking recognised under Article 17 of that Order (Great Britain orders)?
      `row 5 exception applies` IS A BOOLEAN @desc For what you are doing, do you have the permission of a court or the authority of a licence, or does an exception apply, by virtue of the provision named in column 2 of that row of the table in section 159A(2)?
      `row 6 applies to me` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it true that you are disqualified as mentioned in section 1184(2)(a) or (b) or subject to an undertaking under section 1184(3)?
      `row 6 exception applies` IS A BOOLEAN @desc For what you are doing, do you have the permission of a court or the authority of a licence, or does an exception apply, by virtue of the provision named in column 2 of that row of the table in section 159A(2)?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 159A, am I barred from being appointed a director of a company registered in Northern Ireland` IS
    `s 159A(1) section 159A(1) bars the appointment of the person as a director` (`s 159A(2) the person is disqualified under the directors disqualification legislation` `Northern Ireland` (LIST (`s 159A(2) fact about a row` OF `s 159A(2) Part 2 row 1: a disqualification order or undertaking under the 2002 Order`, `row 1 applies to me`, `row 1 exception applies`) , (`s 159A(2) fact about a row` OF `s 159A(2) Part 2 row 2: the circumstances in Article 15 of the 2002 Order (bankruptcy etc)`, `row 2 applies to me`, `row 2 exception applies`) , (`s 159A(2) fact about a row` OF `s 159A(2) Part 2 row 3: director disqualification sanctions (Article 15A of the 2002 Order)`, `row 3 applies to me`, `row 3 exception applies`) , (`s 159A(2) fact about a row` OF `s 159A(2) Part 2 row 4: Article 16 of the 2002 Order (revocation of administration order against an individual)`, `row 4 applies to me`, `row 4 exception applies`) , (`s 159A(2) fact about a row` OF `s 159A(2) Part 2 row 5: an order or undertaking mentioned in Article 17 of the 2002 Order`, `row 5 applies to me`, `row 5 exception applies`) , (`s 159A(2) fact about a row` OF `s 159A(2) Part 2 row 6: disqualified as mentioned in section 1184`, `row 6 applies to me`, `row 6 exception applies`)))

@export Under section 160, does section 160(1) bar a motion to appoint two or more directors of a public company by a single resolution from being made (s 160)?
GIVEN `the company is a public company` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the company a public company?
      `the motion is for the appointment of two or more persons` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the motion for the appointment of two or more persons as directors by a single resolution?
      `the motion is for approving two or more persons` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the motion for approving the appointment of two or more persons by a single resolution?
      `the motion is for nominating two or more persons` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the motion for nominating two or more persons for appointment by a single resolution?
      `the resolution amends the articles` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the resolution one amending the company's articles?
      `the meeting first agreed the motion should be made without a vote against` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has the meeting first agreed, without any vote being given against it, that the motion should be made?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 160, does section 160(1) bar a motion to appoint two or more directors of a public company by a single resolution from being made` IS
    `s 160(1) section 160(1) bars the motion being made` `the company is a public company` (`the motion is for the appointment of two or more persons` OR `s 160(3) the motion is treated as a motion for the person's appointment` `the motion is for approving two or more persons` `the motion is for nominating two or more persons` EQUALS JUST TRUE) `the resolution amends the articles` `the meeting first agreed the motion should be made without a vote against`

@export Under section 161, are the acts of a person acting as a director valid despite a defect (s 161)?
GIVEN `the person was acting as a director` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Was the person acting as a director of the company?
      `the defect discovered afterwards` IS A `s 161(1) defect discovered afterwards` @desc Which defect was afterwards discovered: a defect in the appointment, disqualification, having ceased to hold office, not being entitled to vote, the resolution for the appointment being void under section 160, or another defect?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 161, are the acts of a person acting as a director valid despite a defect` IS
    `s 161(1) the acts of the person acting as a director are valid` `the person was acting as a director` `the defect discovered afterwards`

§§ `Notifying the registrar (ss 167G to 167N)`

@export Under section 167G, by what day must my company notify the registrar of a change in directors (s 167G(6))?
GIVEN `the day the person becomes or ceases to be a director` IS A DATE @desc On what day does the person become, or cease to be, a director?
GIVETH A DATE
DECIDE `Under section 167G, by what day must my company notify the registrar of a change in directors` IS
    `s 167G(6) the last day of the period of 14 days beginning with the day the person becomes or ceases to be a director` `the day the person becomes or ceases to be a director`

@export Under section 167G, did my company give notice of the change in directors in time (s 167G(6))?
GIVEN `the day the person becomes or ceases to be a director` IS A DATE @desc On what day did the person become, or cease to be, a director?
      `the day the notice was given` IS A DATE @desc On what day did the company give notice to the registrar?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 167G, did my company give notice of the change in directors in time` IS
    `s 167G(6) the notice is given within the period of 14 days` `the day the person becomes or ceases to be a director` `the day the notice was given`

@export Under section 167G, is my company obliged to notify the registrar of a change in directors (s 167G(1))?
GIVEN `a person becomes a director` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has a person become a director of the company?
      `a person ceases to be a director` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has a person ceased to be a director of the company?
      `the person was named in the incorporation statement` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did the person become a director on the company's incorporation and is the person named as a proposed director in the statement under section 12?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 167G, is my company obliged to notify the registrar of a change in directors` IS
    `s 167G(1) the company is obliged to give notice to the registrar of the change` `a person becomes a director` `a person ceases to be a director` `the person was named in the incorporation statement`

@export Under section 167G, does the notice of a new director contain what it must (s 167G(3))?
GIVEN `the notice has the required information` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does the notice contain a statement of the required information about the new director (sections 167J and 167K)?
      `the notice has the consent statement` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does the notice contain a statement by the company that the person has consented to act?
      `the person is an individual` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the new director an individual (not a company or firm)?
      `the notice has the identity statement` IS A BOOLEAN @desc If the person is an individual, does the notice say their identity is verified?
      `the notice says not disqualified` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does the notice say the person is not disqualified under the directors disqualification legislation?
      `the notice says not ineligible` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does the notice say the person is not otherwise ineligible by virtue of any enactment?
      `the person would be disqualified but for a court permission` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Would the person be disqualified but for the permission of a court to act?
      `the notice names the court` IS A BOOLEAN @desc If so, does the notice name the court that gave permission?
      `the notice gives the date of the permission` IS A BOOLEAN @desc If so, does the notice give the date of the permission?
      `the person would be disqualified but for a licence` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Would the person be disqualified (section 11A of the 1986 Act or Article 15A of the 2002 Order) but for the authority of a licence?
      `the notice gives the licence date` IS A BOOLEAN @desc If so, does the notice give the date the licence was issued?
      `the notice gives the licence issuer` IS A BOOLEAN @desc If so, does the notice say by whom the licence was issued?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 167G, does the notice of a new director contain what it must` IS
    `s 167G(3) the notice contains what the subsection requires` (`s 167G(3) the notice of a person having become a director` OF `the notice has the required information`, `the notice has the consent statement`, `the person is an individual`, `the notice has the identity statement`, `the notice says not disqualified`, `the notice says not ineligible`, `the person would be disqualified but for a court permission`, `the notice names the court`, `the notice gives the date of the permission`, `the person would be disqualified but for a licence`, `the notice gives the licence date`, `the notice gives the licence issuer`)

@export Under section 167H, did my company give notice of a change in a director's details in time (s 167H(3))?
GIVEN `the day the change occurred` IS A DATE @desc On what day did the change in the director's required information occur?
      `the day the notice was given` IS A DATE @desc On what day did the company give notice to the registrar?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 167H, did my company give notice of a change in a director's details in time` IS
    `s 167H(3) the notice is given within the period of 14 days beginning with the day the change occurs` `the day the change occurred` `the day the notice was given`

@export Under section 167I, did my company give notice of a change before incorporation in time (s 167I(5))?
GIVEN `the day the company was incorporated` IS A DATE @desc On what day was the company incorporated?
      `the day the notice was given` IS A DATE @desc On what day did the company give notice to the registrar?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 167I, did my company give notice of a change before incorporation in time` IS
    `s 167I(5) the notice is given within the period of 14 days beginning with the day the company was incorporated` `the day the company was incorporated` `the day the notice was given`

@export Under section 167L, am I guilty of an offence because my company did not notify the registrar (s 167L)?
GIVEN `my company failed without reasonable excuse` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did the company fail, without reasonable excuse, to give a notice required by section 167G, 167H or 167I?
      `I am an officer of the company` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are you an officer of the company (a director, manager or secretary)?
      `I am a shadow director of the company` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are you a shadow director?
      `I am in default` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are you an officer in default?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 167L, am I guilty of an offence because my company did not notify the registrar` IS
    `s 167L(1)(b) the officer in default commits the offence` `my company failed without reasonable excuse` (JUST `I am an officer of the company`) (JUST `I am a shadow director of the company`) (JUST `I am in default`)

@export Under section 167M, am I committing an offence by acting as a director without my identity being verified (s 167M)?
GIVEN `I act as a director` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Do you act as a director of the company?
      `my identity is verified` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is your identity verified (section 1110A)?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 167M, am I committing an offence by acting as a director without my identity being verified` IS
    `s 167M(3) the person who contravenes subsection (1) commits an offence` (`s 167M(1) the individual contravenes subsection (1) by acting as a director` `I act as a director` (JUST `my identity is verified`))

@export Under section 167N, am I committing an offence by acting as a director before the registrar has been told (s 167N)?
GIVEN `I became a director other than on incorporation` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did you become a director of the company otherwise than on its incorporation?
      `notice was not given in time` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Was notice under section 167G not given within 14 days of your becoming a director?
      `I act as a director` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Do you act as a director?
      `notice has now been given` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has notice now been given under section 167G?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 167N, am I committing an offence by acting as a director before the registrar has been told` IS
    `s 167N(3) the person who contravenes subsection (2) commits an offence` (`s 167N(2) the person contravenes subsection (2) by acting as a director` `I became a director other than on incorporation` `notice was not given in time` `I act as a director` `notice has now been given`)

@export Under section 167N, do I have a defence to the charge of acting before the registrar was told (s 167N(5))?
GIVEN `I am charged with an offence under section 167N` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are you charged with an offence under section 167N?
      `I prove I reasonably believed notice had been given` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Do you prove that you reasonably believed that notice had been given under section 167G?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 167N, do I have a defence to the charge of acting before the registrar was told` IS
    `s 167N(5) this section gives the person a defence on these facts` `I am charged with an offence under section 167N` `I prove I reasonably believed notice had been given`

§§ `Removal (ss 168 to 169A)`

@export Under section 168, can the company remove a director by resolution (s 168(1))?
GIVEN `the resolution is an ordinary resolution` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the resolution an ordinary resolution (passed by a simple majority)?
      `the way the resolution is passed` IS A `Way a resolution is passed` @desc How is the resolution passed: as a written resolution, at a meeting on a show of hands, or at a meeting on a poll?
      `an agreement says the director may not be removed` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does an agreement between the company and the director say he cannot be removed?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 168, can the company remove a director by resolution` IS
    `s 168(1) the company may by that resolution remove the director before the expiration of the director's period of office` (JUST `the resolution is an ordinary resolution`) `the way the resolution is passed` `an agreement says the director may not be removed`

@export Under section 168, is special notice required of a resolution to remove a director (s 168(2))?
GIVEN `the resolution is to remove a director` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the resolution one to remove a director under section 168?
      `the resolution is to appoint somebody in place of the director removed` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the resolution one to appoint somebody instead of a director so removed at the meeting at which he is removed?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 168, is special notice required of a resolution to remove a director` IS
    `s 168(2) special notice is required of the resolution` `the resolution is to remove a director` `the resolution is to appoint somebody in place of the director removed`

@export Under section 169, has my company done what it must when it received notice of a resolution to remove a director (s 169(1))?
GIVEN `the company has received notice` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has the company received notice of an intended resolution to remove a director under section 168?
      `the company has forthwith sent a copy` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has the company forthwith sent a copy of the notice to the director concerned?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 169, has my company done what it must when it received notice of a resolution to remove a director` IS
    `s 169(1) the company has complied with the duty to send a copy of the notice to the director concerned` `the company has received notice` `the company has forthwith sent a copy`

@export Under section 169, is a director entitled to be heard on the resolution to remove him (s 169(2))?
GIVEN `the resolution is to remove me` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the resolution one to remove you as a director under section 168?
      `I am a member of the company` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are you a member of the company?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 169, is a director entitled to be heard on the resolution to remove him` IS
    `s 169(2) the director is entitled to be heard on the resolution at the meeting` `the resolution is to remove me` `I am a member of the company`

@export Under section 169, can I require my written representations to be read out at the meeting (s 169(4))?
GIVEN `a copy was not sent as required` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Was a copy of your representations not sent to the members as required?
      `because late or the company's default` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Was that because they were received too late or because of the company's default?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 169, can I require my written representations to be read out at the meeting` IS
    `s 169(4) the director may require that the representations be read out at the meeting` `a copy was not sent as required` `because late or the company's default`

@export Under section 169A, have I ceased to be a director because I became disqualified (s 169A(1))?
GIVEN `I was appointed a director` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Were you appointed a director of the company?
      `I have become disqualified` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Have you become disqualified under the directors disqualification legislation (section 159A(2))?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 169A, have I ceased to be a director because I became disqualified` IS
    `s 169A(1) the person has ceased to hold office by virtue of the appointment` `I was appointed a director` (JUST `I have become disqualified`)

§ `Part 10, Chapter 2: General duties of directors`

§§ `The general duties (ss 170 to 177)`

@export Under section 170, do the general duties still bind me after I cease to be a director (s 170(2))?
GIVEN `I have ceased to be a director` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Have you ceased to be a director of the company?
      `the duty in question` IS A `s 170(1) general duty` @desc Which duty is in question: section 171, 172, 173, 174, 175, 176, 177, or a duty outside sections 171 to 177?
      `the matter is exploitation learnt as a director` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the matter the exploitation of property, information or an opportunity you became aware of when you were a director?
      `the matter was done before I ceased` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the matter something you did or omitted to do before you ceased to be a director?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 170, do the general duties still bind me after I cease to be a director` IS
    `s 170(2) the former director continues to be subject to the duty` `I have ceased to be a director` `the duty in question` `the matter is exploitation learnt as a director` `the matter was done before I ceased`

@export Under section 171, have I complied with the duty to act within my powers (s 171)?
GIVEN `I act in accordance with the constitution` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Do you act in accordance with the company's constitution?
      `I only use powers for their purposes` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Do you only exercise powers for the purposes for which they are conferred?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 171, have I complied with the duty to act within my powers` IS
    `s 171 the director has complied with the duty to act within powers` `I act in accordance with the constitution` `I only use powers for their purposes`

@export Under section 172, have I complied with the duty to promote the success of the company (s 172)?
GIVEN `I acted as I considered, in good faith, would promote the object` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did you act in the way you considered, in good faith, would be most likely to promote the success of the company for the benefit of its members as a whole (or, if the company has other purposes, to achieve them)?
      `I had regard to the long term` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did you have regard to the likely consequences of any decision in the long term?
      `I had regard to employees` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did you have regard to the interests of the company's employees?
      `I had regard to business relationships` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did you have regard to the need to foster the company's business relationships with suppliers, customers and others?
      `I had regard to community and environment` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did you have regard to the impact of the company's operations on the community and the environment?
      `I had regard to reputation` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did you have regard to the desirability of the company maintaining a reputation for high standards of business conduct?
      `I had regard to fairness between members` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did you have regard to the need to act fairly as between members of the company?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 172, have I complied with the duty to promote the success of the company` IS
    `s 172(1) the director has complied with the duty to promote the success of the company` `I acted as I considered, in good faith, would promote the object` `I had regard to the long term` `I had regard to employees` `I had regard to business relationships` `I had regard to community and environment` `I had regard to reputation` `I had regard to fairness between members`

@export Under section 173, have I complied with the duty to exercise independent judgment (s 173)?
GIVEN `I exercise independent judgment` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Do you exercise independent judgment?
      `I act under an agreement restricting discretion` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are you acting in accordance with an agreement duly entered into by the company that restricts the future exercise of discretion by its directors?
      `I act as the constitution authorises` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are you acting in a way authorised by the company's constitution?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 173, have I complied with the duty to exercise independent judgment` IS
    `s 173(1) the director has complied with the duty to exercise independent judgment` `I exercise independent judgment` `I act under an agreement restricting discretion` `I act as the constitution authorises`

@export Under section 174, have I exercised reasonable care, skill and diligence (s 174)?
GIVEN `my care meets the objective standard` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Was your care, skill and diligence at least that of a reasonably diligent person with the knowledge, skill and experience reasonably expected of a person carrying out your functions?
      `my care meets my own standard` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Was it at least that of a reasonably diligent person with the knowledge, skill and experience you actually have?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 174, have I exercised reasonable care, skill and diligence` IS
    `s 174(1) the director has exercised reasonable care, skill and diligence` `my care meets the objective standard` `my care meets my own standard`

@export Under section 175, have I complied with the duty to avoid conflicts of interest (s 175(1), (3), (4))?
GIVEN `I am in a situation of conflict` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are you in a situation in which you have, or can have, a direct or indirect interest that conflicts, or possibly may conflict, with the interests of the company?
      `the conflict arises in a transaction with the company` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does the conflict arise in relation to a transaction or arrangement with the company?
      `the situation cannot reasonably be regarded as likely to give rise to a conflict` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Can the situation not reasonably be regarded as likely to give rise to a conflict of interest?
      `the matter has been authorised by the directors` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has the matter been authorised by the directors (see the next question)?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 175, have I complied with the duty to avoid conflicts of interest` IS
    `s 175(1) the director has complied with the duty to avoid conflicts of interest` `I am in a situation of conflict` `the conflict arises in a transaction with the company` `the situation cannot reasonably be regarded as likely to give rise to a conflict` `the matter has been authorised by the directors`

@export Under section 175, have the directors validly authorised the conflict (s 175(5) and (6))?
GIVEN `the company is a public company` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the company a public company?
      `nothing in the constitution invalidates authorisation` IS A BOOLEAN @desc For a private company: does nothing in the constitution invalidate such authorisation?
      `the constitution lets the directors authorise` IS A BOOLEAN @desc For a public company: does the constitution include provision enabling the directors to authorise the matter?
      `the matter was proposed to and authorised by the directors` IS A BOOLEAN @desc For a private company: was the matter proposed to and authorised by the directors?
      `the matter was proposed and authorised in accordance with the constitution` IS A BOOLEAN @desc For a public company: was it proposed to and authorised by them in accordance with the constitution?
      `the quorum was met without the interested directors` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Was any quorum requirement met without counting you or any other interested director?
      `it was agreed without their voting` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Was the matter agreed to without the interested directors voting?
      `it would have been agreed without their votes` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Would it have been agreed to if their votes had not been counted?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 175, have the directors validly authorised the conflict` IS
    `coa4 seat all of these answers hold` (LIST `s 175(5) authorisation has been given by the directors` `the company is a public company` `nothing in the constitution invalidates authorisation` `the constitution lets the directors authorise` `the matter was proposed to and authorised by the directors` `the matter was proposed and authorised in accordance with the constitution`
                                                , `s 175(6) the authorisation is effective` `the quorum was met without the interested directors` `it was agreed without their voting` `it would have been agreed without their votes`)

@export Under section 176, have I complied with the duty not to accept benefits from third parties (s 176)?
GIVEN `I accept a benefit` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Do you accept a benefit?
      `the benefit is from the company` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the benefit from the company itself?
      `the benefit is from an associated body corporate` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it from a body corporate associated with the company?
      `the benefit is from a person acting on behalf of the company` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it from a person acting on behalf of the company or an associated body corporate?
      `the benefit is from a person who provides my services` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it from a person by whom your services (as a director or otherwise) are provided to the company?
      `the benefit is conferred by reason of my being a director` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it conferred by reason of your being a director, or of your doing (or not doing) anything as director?
      `accepting it cannot reasonably be regarded as likely to give rise to a conflict` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Can your acceptance of it not reasonably be regarded as likely to give rise to a conflict of interest?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 176, have I complied with the duty not to accept benefits from third parties` IS
    `s 176(1) the director has complied with the duty not to accept benefits from third parties` `I accept a benefit` `the benefit is from a third party` `the benefit is conferred by reason of my being a director` `accepting it cannot reasonably be regarded as likely to give rise to a conflict`
    WHERE
        `the benefit is from a third party` MEANS
            IF `s 176(3) the benefit is regarded as conferred by a third party` `the benefit is from a person who provides my services` EQUALS JUST FALSE
            THEN JUST FALSE
            ELSE `s 176(2) the person is a third party` `the benefit is from the company` `the benefit is from an associated body corporate` `the benefit is from a person acting on behalf of the company`

@export Under section 177, must I declare my interest in a proposed transaction (s 177(1), (5), (6))?
GIVEN `I am interested in a proposed transaction` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are you in any way, directly or indirectly, interested in a transaction or arrangement the company proposes to enter into?
      `I am aware of the interest` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are you aware of the interest?
      `I ought reasonably to be aware of the interest` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Ought you reasonably to be aware of it?
      `I am aware of the transaction` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are you aware of the proposed transaction?
      `I ought reasonably to be aware of the transaction` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Ought you reasonably to be aware of it?
      `it cannot reasonably be regarded as likely to give rise to a conflict` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Can the interest not reasonably be regarded as likely to give rise to a conflict of interest?
      `the other directors are already aware` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are the other directors already aware of the interest?
      `the other directors ought reasonably to be aware` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Ought the other directors reasonably to be aware of it?
      `it concerns terms of my service contract considered by the directors` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does it concern terms of your service contract that have been or are to be considered by a meeting of the directors?
      `it concerns terms of my service contract considered by a committee` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does it concern terms of your service contract that have been or are to be considered by a committee of the directors appointed for the purpose?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 177, must I declare my interest in a proposed transaction` IS
    `s 177(1) the director is obliged to declare the nature and extent of the interest to the other directors` `I am interested in a proposed transaction` (`s 177(5) the section requires a declaration so far as the director's awareness goes` `I am aware of the interest` `I ought reasonably to be aware of the interest` `I am aware of the transaction` `I ought reasonably to be aware of the transaction`) (`s 177(6) the director need not declare the interest` `it cannot reasonably be regarded as likely to give rise to a conflict` `the other directors are already aware` `the other directors ought reasonably to be aware` `it concerns terms of my service contract considered by the directors` `it concerns terms of my service contract considered by a committee`)

@export Under section 177, have I made the declaration of interest the section requires (s 177(4))?
GIVEN `a declaration is required` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does section 177 require you to declare the interest (see the previous question)?
      `I declared the nature and extent of the interest` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Have you declared the nature and extent of the interest to the other directors?
      `I declared before the company entered into the transaction` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did you declare it before the company entered into the transaction or arrangement?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 177, have I made the declaration of interest the section requires` IS
    `s 177(4) the director has made the declaration the section requires` (IF `a declaration is required` THEN JUST TRUE ELSE JUST FALSE) `I declared the nature and extent of the interest` `I declared before the company entered into the transaction`

§§ `Supplementary provisions (ss 178 to 181)`

@export Under section 178, can the company enforce a general duty against me like any other fiduciary duty (s 178)?
GIVEN `the duty in question` IS A `s 170(1) general duty` @desc Which duty is in question: section 171, 172, 173, 174, 175, 176, 177, or a duty outside sections 171 to 177?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 178, can the company enforce a general duty against me like any other fiduciary duty` IS
    `s 178(2) the duty is enforceable in the same way as any other fiduciary duty owed to a company by its directors` `the duty in question`

@export Under section 180, is a transaction safe from being set aside for want of members' consent if section 175 or 177 was complied with (s 180(1))?
GIVEN `section 175 is complied with by authorisation by the directors` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is section 175 complied with by authorisation by the directors?
      `section 177 is complied with` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is section 177 complied with (the interest declared)?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 180, is a transaction safe from being set aside for want of members' consent if section 175 or 177 was complied with` IS
    `s 180(1) the transaction or arrangement is not liable to be set aside by virtue of a common law rule or equitable principle requiring the consent or approval of the members` `section 175 is complied with by authorisation by the directors` `section 177 is complied with`

@export Under section 181, have the directors validly authorised the conflict in a charitable company (s 181(2)(b))?
GIVEN `the constitution lets the directors authorise` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does the company's constitution include provision enabling the directors to authorise the matter?
      `the matter was proposed and authorised in accordance with the constitution` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Was the matter proposed to and authorised by them in accordance with the constitution?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 181, have the directors validly authorised the conflict in a charitable company` IS
    `s 181(2)(b) authorisation has been given by the directors, for a charity` `the constitution lets the directors authorise` `the matter was proposed and authorised in accordance with the constitution`

§ `Part 10, Chapter 3: Declaration of interest in existing transaction or arrangement`

@export Under section 182, must I declare my interest in a transaction the company has already entered into (s 182(1), (5), (6))?
GIVEN `I am interested in an existing transaction` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are you in any way, directly or indirectly, interested in a transaction or arrangement the company has entered into?
      `I have declared it under section 177` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Have you already declared the interest under section 177?
      `I am aware of the interest` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are you aware of the interest?
      `I ought reasonably to be aware of the interest` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Ought you reasonably to be aware of it?
      `I am aware of the transaction` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are you aware of the transaction?
      `I ought reasonably to be aware of the transaction` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Ought you reasonably to be aware of it?
      `it cannot reasonably be regarded as likely to give rise to a conflict` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Can the interest not reasonably be regarded as likely to give rise to a conflict of interest?
      `the other directors are already aware` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are the other directors already aware of the interest?
      `the other directors ought reasonably to be aware` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Ought they reasonably to be aware of it?
      `it concerns terms of my service contract considered by the directors` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does it concern terms of your service contract considered by a meeting of the directors?
      `it concerns terms of my service contract considered by a committee` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does it concern terms of your service contract considered by a committee of the directors appointed for the purpose?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 182, must I declare my interest in a transaction the company has already entered into` IS
    `s 182(1) the director is obliged to declare the nature and extent of the interest to the other directors` `I am interested in an existing transaction` `I have declared it under section 177` (`s 182(5) the section requires a declaration so far as the director's awareness goes` `I am aware of the interest` `I ought reasonably to be aware of the interest` `I am aware of the transaction` `I ought reasonably to be aware of the transaction`) (`s 182(6) the director need not declare the interest under section 182` `it cannot reasonably be regarded as likely to give rise to a conflict` `the other directors are already aware` `the other directors ought reasonably to be aware` `it concerns terms of my service contract considered by the directors` `it concerns terms of my service contract considered by a committee`)

@export Under section 182, have I made the declaration in the way and at the time the section requires (s 182(2) and (4))?
GIVEN `a declaration is required` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does section 182 require you to declare the interest (see the previous question)?
      `I declared the nature and extent of the interest` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Have you declared the nature and extent of the interest to the other directors?
      `I declared at a meeting of the directors` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did you declare it at a meeting of the directors?
      `I am a shadow director` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are you a shadow director?
      `my notice in writing is in accordance with section 184` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did you declare it by a notice in writing that is in accordance with section 184?
      `my general notice is in accordance with section 185` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did you declare it by a general notice that is in accordance with section 185?
      `I declared as soon as reasonably practicable` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did you declare it as soon as was reasonably practicable?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 182, have I made the declaration in the way and at the time the section requires` IS
    `s 182 the director has complied with the requirements of section 182` (IF `a declaration is required` THEN JUST TRUE ELSE JUST FALSE) `I declared the nature and extent of the interest` (`s 182(2) the declaration is made in a way the subsection requires` `I declared at a meeting of the directors` `I am a shadow director` (JUST `my notice in writing is in accordance with section 184`) (JUST `my general notice is in accordance with section 185`)) (`s 182(4) the declaration was made as soon as is reasonably practicable` `I declared as soon as reasonably practicable`)

@export Under section 183, am I guilty of an offence for failing to declare my interest (s 183)?
GIVEN `I complied with section 182` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did you comply with the requirements of section 182?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 183, am I guilty of an offence for failing to declare my interest` IS
    `s 183(1) the director commits an offence` (IF `I complied with section 182` THEN JUST TRUE ELSE JUST FALSE)

@export Under section 184, is my notice in writing of my interest in accordance with the section (s 184)?
GIVEN `I sent the notice to the other directors` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did you send the notice to the other directors?
      `the form of the notice` IS A `Form of document` @desc Was the notice sent in hard copy form or in electronic form?
      `the recipient agreed to receive it in electronic form` IS A BOOLEAN @desc If it was in electronic form, had the recipient agreed to receive it in electronic form?
      `the notice is in an agreed electronic form` IS A BOOLEAN @desc If so, is it in an agreed electronic form?
      `the means of sending` IS A `s 184(4) means of sending the notice` @desc How was it sent: by hand, by post, by electronic means, or by another means?
      `the recipient agreed to electronic means` IS A BOOLEAN @desc If by electronic means, had the recipient agreed to receive it by electronic means?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 184, is my notice in writing of my interest in accordance with the section` IS
    `s 184 the notice in writing is in accordance with section 184` (`s 184(2) the director has sent the notice to the other directors` `I sent the notice to the other directors`) (`s 184(3) the notice is sent in a form the subsection allows` `the form of the notice` `the recipient agreed to receive it in electronic form` `the notice is in an agreed electronic form`) (`s 184(4) the notice is sent by a means the subsection allows` `the means of sending` `the recipient agreed to electronic means`)

@export Under section 185, is my general notice of my interests in accordance with the section (s 185)?
GIVEN `my notice says I have an interest in a body corporate or firm` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does the notice say you have an interest (as member, officer, employee or otherwise) in a specified body corporate or firm and are to be regarded as interested in any transaction it may make with it?
      `my notice says I am connected with a person` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does it say you are connected with a specified person (other than a body corporate or firm) and are to be regarded as interested in any transaction made with that person?
      `that person is connected with me` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is that person connected with you (section 252)?
      `my notice states the nature and extent` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does it state the nature and extent of your interest in the body corporate or firm or, as the case may be, the nature of your connection with the person?
      `the notice was given at a meeting of the directors` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Was it given at a meeting of the directors?
      `I took reasonable steps to have it read at the next meeting` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did you take reasonable steps to secure that it was brought up and read at the next meeting of the directors after it was given?
      `I am a shadow director` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are you a shadow director?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 185, is my general notice of my interests in accordance with the section` IS
    `s 185 the general notice is in accordance with section 185` (`s 185(2) the notice is general notice` `my notice says I have an interest in a body corporate or firm` `my notice says I am connected with a person` (JUST `that person is connected with me`)) (`s 185(3) the notice states what the subsection requires` `my notice states the nature and extent`) (`s 185(4) section 185(4) makes the general notice ineffective` `the notice was given at a meeting of the directors` `I took reasonable steps to have it read at the next meeting` `I am a shadow director`)

@export Under section 186, have I recorded my declaration of interest in writing as a sole director must (s 186(1)(a))?
GIVEN `a declaration is required of a sole director` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is a declaration of interest under section 182 required of you as the sole director of a company that is required to have more than one director?
      `I recorded the declaration in writing` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Have you recorded the declaration in writing?
