§ `Part 10, Chapter 4: Transactions with directors requiring approval of members`

§§ `Service contracts (ss 188 and 189)`

@export Under section 188, does section 188(2) bar my company from agreeing a long-term service contract without its members' approval (s 188(2))?
GIVEN `the first day of the employment` IS A DATE @desc On what day does the director's employment begin?
      `the months the employment is to continue` IS A NUMBER @desc For how many months is the employment to continue (or may it be continued otherwise than at the company's instance) and not be terminable by the company by notice? (0 if there is no such period)
      `the months of notice` IS A NUMBER @desc How many months of notice must the company give to end the employment? (0 if it is not terminable by notice)
      `the employment is with the company or within the group` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the employment with the company of which he is a director or, where he is a director of a holding company, within the group of that company and its subsidiaries?
      `the company agrees to the provision` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does the company agree to the provision?
      `the members of the company approved it` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Have the members of the company approved it by resolution?
      `the company is a UK-registered company` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the company a UK-registered company?
      `the company is a wholly-owned subsidiary` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the company a wholly-owned subsidiary of another body corporate?
      `he is a director of a holding company` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is he a director of a holding company?
      `the members of the holding company approved it` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Have the members of the holding company approved it by resolution?
      `the holding company is a UK-registered company` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the holding company a UK-registered company?
      `the holding company is a wholly-owned subsidiary` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the holding company a wholly-owned subsidiary of another body corporate?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 188, does section 188(2) bar my company from agreeing a long-term service contract without its members' approval` IS
    CONSIDER `s 188(3) the day on which the guaranteed term of the director's employment ends` `the first day of the employment` (IF `the months the employment is to continue` GREATER THAN 0 THEN JUST (Period OF `the months the employment is to continue`, Months) ELSE NOTHING) (IF `the months of notice` GREATER THAN 0 THEN JUST (Period OF `the months of notice`, Months) ELSE NOTHING)
    WHEN NOTHING THEN NOTHING
    WHEN JUST end THEN
         `s 188(2) section 188(2) bars the company from agreeing to the provision` (`s 188(1) section 188 applies to the provision` `the employment is with the company or within the group` `the first day of the employment` end) `the company agrees to the provision` `the members of the company approved it` (`s 188(6) approval is required on the part of the members of the body corporate` `the company is a UK-registered company` `the company is a wholly-owned subsidiary`) `he is a director of a holding company` `the members of the holding company approved it` (`s 188(6) approval is required on the part of the members of the body corporate` `the holding company is a UK-registered company` `the holding company is a wholly-owned subsidiary`)

@export Under section 188, has the memorandum been made available to members as required (s 188(5))?
GIVEN `the way the resolution is passed` IS A `Way a resolution is passed` @desc How is the resolution passed: as a written resolution, at a meeting on a show of hands, or at a meeting on a poll?
      `the memorandum sets out the proposed contract` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does the memorandum set out the proposed contract incorporating the provision?
      `it was sent to every eligible member` IS A BOOLEAN @desc For a written resolution: was the memorandum sent or submitted to every eligible member at or before the time the resolution was sent or submitted to him?
      `the first day it was available at the registered office` IS A DATE @desc For a meeting: on what day did the memorandum first become available for inspection at the company's registered office?
      `the day of the meeting` IS A DATE @desc On what day is the meeting?
      `it is available at the meeting` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the memorandum available for inspection at the meeting itself?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 188, has the memorandum been made available to members as required` IS
    `s 188(5) the memorandum has been made available to members as the subsection requires` `the way the resolution is passed` `the memorandum sets out the proposed contract` `it was sent to every eligible member` `the first day it was available at the registered office` `the day of the meeting` `it is available at the meeting`

@export Under section 189, is a long-term service provision void if the company agreed to it without approval (s 189)?
