    `s 189(b) the contract is deemed to contain a term entitling the company to terminate it at any time by the giving of reasonable notice` `the company agreed to the provision` (IF `section 188 barred it` THEN JUST TRUE ELSE JUST FALSE)

§§ `Substantial property transactions (ss 190 to 196)`

@export Under section 190, does section 190(1) bar my company from entering into an arrangement for a substantial non-cash asset with a director without members' approval (s 190(1))?
GIVEN `the company disposes of an asset to the other party` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does the company dispose of a non-cash asset to the other party?
      `the company acquires an asset from the other party` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does the company acquire a non-cash asset from the other party?
      `the other party is a director` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the other party a director of the company or of its holding company?
      `the other party is connected with a director` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the other party a person connected with such a director (section 252)?
      `the value of the asset` IS A NUMBER @desc What is the value of the asset (or the aggregate value of the assets in the arrangement or series), in pounds?
      `statutory accounts have been prepared` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Have the company's statutory accounts been prepared?
      `the day the accounts are to be sent to members` IS A DATE @desc On what day does the time for sending the most recent statutory accounts out to members fall?
      `the net assets by the accounts` IS A NUMBER @desc What are the net assets by those accounts, in pounds?
      `the called-up share capital` IS A NUMBER @desc What is the called-up share capital, in pounds?
      `the arrangement has been approved` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has the arrangement been approved by a resolution of the members of the company?
      `the arrangement is conditional on approval` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it conditional on such approval being obtained?
      `the company is a UK-registered company` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the company a UK-registered company?
      `the company is a wholly-owned subsidiary` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the company a wholly-owned subsidiary of another body corporate?
      `an exception applies` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does an exception apply (section 190(6), 192, 193 or 194)?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 190, does section 190(1) bar my company from entering into an arrangement for a substantial non-cash asset with a director without members' approval` IS
    `s 190(1) section 190(1) bars the company from entering into the arrangement` `the company disposes of an asset to the other party` `the company acquires an asset from the other party` `the other party is a director` (JUST `the other party is connected with a director`) (`s 191(2) the asset is a substantial asset in relation to the company` `the value of the asset` (`s 191(3) the company's asset value` (IF `statutory accounts have been prepared` THEN LIST (`s 191(4) statutory accounts` OF `the day the accounts are to be sent to members`, `the net assets by the accounts`) ELSE EMPTY) `the called-up share capital`)) `the arrangement has been approved` `the arrangement is conditional on approval` (`s 190(4) approval is required on the part of the members of the body corporate` `the company is a UK-registered company` `the company is a wholly-owned subsidiary`) `an exception applies`

@export Under section 190, must the members of my company's holding company also approve an arrangement for a substantial non-cash asset (s 190(2))?
GIVEN `the person is of the holding company` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the director or connected person a director of the company's holding company, or a person connected with such a director?
      `the holding company's members approved` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Have the members of the holding company approved the arrangement by resolution?
      `the arrangement is conditional on approval` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the arrangement conditional on such approval being obtained?
      `the holding company is a UK-registered company` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the holding company a UK-registered company?
      `the holding company is a wholly-owned subsidiary` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the holding company a wholly-owned subsidiary of another body corporate?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 190, must the members of my company's holding company also approve an arrangement for a substantial non-cash asset` IS
    `s 190(2) section 190(2) requires the approval of the members of the holding company` `the person is of the holding company` `the holding company's members approved` `the arrangement is conditional on approval` (`s 190(4) approval is required on the part of the members of the body corporate` `the holding company is a UK-registered company` `the holding company is a wholly-owned subsidiary`)

@export Under section 191, is an asset substantial for the purposes of section 190 (s 191)?
GIVEN `the value of the asset` IS A NUMBER @desc What is the value of the non-cash asset, in pounds?
      `statutory accounts have been prepared` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Have the company's statutory accounts been prepared?
      `the day the accounts are to be sent to members` IS A DATE @desc On what day does (or did) the time for sending the most recent statutory accounts out to members fall?
      `the net assets by the accounts` IS A NUMBER @desc What are the company's net assets by its most recent statutory accounts, in pounds?
      `the called-up share capital` IS A NUMBER @desc What is the company's called-up share capital, in pounds?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 191, is an asset substantial for the purposes of section 190` IS
    `s 191(2) the asset is a substantial asset in relation to the company` `the value of the asset` (`s 191(3) the company's asset value` (IF `statutory accounts have been prepared` THEN LIST (`s 191(4) statutory accounts` OF `the day the accounts are to be sent to members`, `the net assets by the accounts`) ELSE EMPTY) `the called-up share capital`)

@export Under section 192, is approval under section 190 needed for a transaction with a member or between group companies (s 192)?
GIVEN `the transaction is with a person in his character as a member` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the transaction between the company and a person in his character as a member of that company?
      `it is between a holding company and its wholly-owned subsidiary` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it between a holding company and its wholly-owned subsidiary?
      `it is between two wholly-owned subsidiaries of the same holding company` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it between two wholly-owned subsidiaries of the same holding company?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 192, is approval under section 190 needed for a transaction with a member or between group companies` IS
    `s 192 approval is required under section 190 for the transaction` `the transaction is with a person in his character as a member` `it is between a holding company and its wholly-owned subsidiary` `it is between two wholly-owned subsidiaries of the same holding company`

@export Under section 193, is approval under section 190 needed while my company is being wound up or is in administration (s 193)?
GIVEN `the company is being wound up` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the company being wound up?
      `the winding up is a members' voluntary winding up` IS A BOOLEAN @desc If so, is it a members' voluntary winding up?
      `the company is in administration` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the company in administration within the meaning of Schedule B1 to the Insolvency Act 1986 or the Insolvency (Northern Ireland) Order 1989?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 193, is approval under section 190 needed while my company is being wound up or is in administration` IS
    `s 193(2) approval is required under section 190` (`s 193(1) section 193 applies to the company` `the company is being wound up` `the winding up is a members' voluntary winding up` `the company is in administration`)

@export Under section 194, is approval under section 190 needed for a transaction on a recognised investment exchange (s 194)?
GIVEN `the exchange is a recognised investment exchange` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the exchange a recognised investment exchange (Part 18 of the Financial Services and Markets Act 2000)?
      `the transaction is effected by a director or a person connected with him` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the transaction effected by a director, or a person connected with him?
      `the broker selects the other party` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does the person through whose agency it is effected select the person with whom the transaction is to be effected?
      `the broker does so independently` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does that person do so independently of the director or any person connected with him?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 194, is approval under section 190 needed for a transaction on a recognised investment exchange` IS
    `s 194(1) approval is required under section 190 for the transaction` (JUST `the exchange is a recognised investment exchange`) `the transaction is effected by a director or a person connected with him` (`s 194(2) the person is an independent broker` `the broker selects the other party` `the broker does so independently`)

@export Under section 195, is an arrangement made without the approval section 190 requires voidable by the company (s 195(2))?
GIVEN `the company entered into the arrangement` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did the company enter into the arrangement?
      `it contravened section 190` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did it contravene section 190 (approval was needed and was not obtained)?
      `restitution is no longer possible` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is restitution of any money or other asset that was the subject matter no longer possible?
      `the company has been indemnified` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has the company been indemnified under section 195 by any other persons for its loss?
      `good faith rights would be affected` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Would rights acquired in good faith, for value and without actual notice by a person who is not a party be affected by avoiding it?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 195, is an arrangement made without the approval section 190 requires voidable by the company` IS
    `s 195(2) the arrangement and any transaction entered into in pursuance of it is voidable at the instance of the company` `the company entered into the arrangement` (IF `it contravened section 190` THEN JUST TRUE ELSE JUST FALSE) `restitution is no longer possible` `the company has been indemnified` `good faith rights would be affected`

@export Under section 195, am I liable to account to the company and indemnify it for an arrangement made in contravention of section 190 (s 195(3) and (4))?
GIVEN `the arrangement contravened section 190` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Was the arrangement entered into in contravention of section 190?
      `who I am in relation to the arrangement` IS A `s 195(4) person who may be liable` @desc Who are you: a director with whom the company entered into the arrangement; a connected person with whom it did; the director with whom such a person is connected; another director who authorised it; or anyone else?
      `I took all reasonable steps` IS A BOOLEAN @desc If you are the director with whom a connected person is connected: do you show you took all reasonable steps to secure the company's compliance?
      `I did not know the circumstances` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Do you show that, when the arrangement was entered into, you did not know the relevant circumstances constituting the contravention?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 195, am I liable to account to the company and indemnify it for an arrangement made in contravention of section 190` IS
    `s 195(3) the person is liable to account to the company for any gain and to indemnify the company for any loss or damage` `the arrangement contravened section 190` `who I am in relation to the arrangement` `I took all reasonable steps` `I did not know the circumstances`

@export Under section 196, may an arrangement made without approval no longer be avoided because the members have affirmed it (s 196)?
GIVEN `the contravention is of section 190(1)` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Was section 190(1) (approval of the company's members) contravened?
      `the contravention is of section 190(2)` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Was section 190(2) (approval of the holding company's members) contravened?
      `the company's members affirmed it in a reasonable period` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did the company's members affirm it by resolution within a reasonable period?
      `the holding company's members affirmed it in a reasonable period` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did the holding company's members affirm it by resolution within a reasonable period?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 196, may an arrangement made without approval no longer be avoided because the members have affirmed it` IS
    `s 196 the transaction or arrangement may no longer be avoided under section 195` `the contravention is of section 190(1)` `the contravention is of section 190(2)` `the company's members affirmed it in a reasonable period` `the holding company's members affirmed it in a reasonable period`

