@export Under section 202, is the transaction a credit transaction (s 202)?
GIVEN `goods supplied or land sold under hire-purchase or conditional sale` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does the creditor supply goods or sell land under a hire-purchase agreement or a conditional sale agreement?
      `land or goods leased or hired for periodical payments` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does the creditor lease or hire land or goods in return for periodical payments?
      `land disposed of or goods or services supplied on deferred payment` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does the creditor otherwise dispose of land or supply goods or services on the understanding that payment is to be deferred?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 202, is the transaction a credit transaction` IS
    `s 202(1) the transaction is a credit transaction` `goods supplied or land sold under hire-purchase or conditional sale` `land or goods leased or hired for periodical payments` `land disposed of or goods or services supplied on deferred payment`

@export Under section 203, does section 203(1) bar my company from taking part in a related arrangement without its members' approval (s 203(1))?
GIVEN `the arrangement is for a transaction that would have needed approval` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the arrangement one under which another person enters into a transaction that, if the company had entered into it, would have needed approval under section 197, 198, 200 or 201?
      `that person obtains a benefit from the company` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does that person, in pursuance of the arrangement, obtain a benefit from the company or an associated body corporate?
      `the arrangement is for an assignment or assumption` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does the company arrange for the assignment to it, or assumption by it, of rights, obligations or liabilities under such a transaction?
      `the arrangement has been approved` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has the arrangement been approved by a resolution of the members of the company?
      `the company is a UK-registered company` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the company a UK-registered company?
      `the company is a wholly-owned subsidiary` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the company a wholly-owned subsidiary of another body corporate?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 203, does section 203(1) bar my company from taking part in a related arrangement without its members' approval` IS
    `s 203(1) section 203(1) bars the company from the arrangement` (JUST `the arrangement is for a transaction that would have needed approval`) `that person obtains a benefit from the company` (JUST `the arrangement is for an assignment or assumption`) `the arrangement has been approved` (`s 203(5) approval is required on the part of the members of the body corporate` `the company is a UK-registered company` `the company is a wholly-owned subsidiary`)

@export Under section 203, must the members of my company's holding company also approve a related arrangement (s 203(2))?
GIVEN `the person is of the holding company` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the director or connected person for whom the transaction is entered into a director of the company's holding company or a person connected with such a director?
      `the holding company's members approved` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Have the members of the holding company approved the arrangement by resolution?
      `the holding company is a UK-registered company` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the holding company a UK-registered company?
      `the holding company is a wholly-owned subsidiary` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the holding company a wholly-owned subsidiary of another body corporate?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 203, must the members of my company's holding company also approve a related arrangement` IS
    `s 203(2) the section requires the approval of the members of the holding company` `the person is of the holding company` `the holding company's members approved` (`s 203(5) approval is required on the part of the members of the body corporate` `the holding company is a UK-registered company` `the holding company is a wholly-owned subsidiary`)

@export Under section 204, does my company need members' approval for funds for expenditure on company business (s 204)?
GIVEN `the funds are for the purposes of the company` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the company providing a director (or a person connected with one) with funds to meet expenditure for the purposes of the company?
      `the funds are to perform duties as an officer` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it providing funds to meet expenditure for enabling him properly to perform his duties as an officer of the company?
      `the thing done is to avoid incurring such expenditure` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the company enabling such a person to avoid incurring such expenditure?
      `the value of the transaction` IS A NUMBER @desc What is the value of the transaction, in pounds?
      `the value of other relevant transactions` IS A NUMBER @desc What is the total value of any other relevant transactions or arrangements, in pounds?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 204, does my company need members' approval for funds for expenditure on company business` IS
    IF `s 204(2) section 204 authorises the company to enter into the transaction` `the value of the transaction` `the value of other relevant transactions` EQUALS JUST FALSE
    THEN NOTHING
    ELSE `s 204(1) approval is required under section 197, 198, 200 or 201 for the thing done` `the funds are for the purposes of the company` `the funds are to perform duties as an officer` `the thing done is to avoid incurring such expenditure`

-- ====================================================================================================
-- seat questions from part coa5 (merged by the lead on 2026-11-12; unchanged text follows)
-- ====================================================================================================
-- coa5-seat.l4: THE SEAT LAYER for Part 10 (ss 205 to 259, from the second half of Chapter 4) and Part 11 (ss 260 to 269) of the Companies Act 2006 (United Kingdom).
-- Generated by a script from a table of questions (the script is scratch and is not shipped); every question calls a layer-1 rule and restates none.
--
-- SEAT: an individual who is, or is about to become, a director, a company secretary or a member (shareholder) of a company registered under the Act, or who deals with one,
-- asking on facts they can state what the Act requires or lets them do, what rights they have against the company or its directors, what they must disclose, file, approve or vote on
-- and by when, and what follows (liability, offences, penalties) if it is not done. (Assumed, not ruled: the Act is addressed to companies, so the individual is whoever stands in a
-- company's management or ownership.) No official (registrar, court, Secretary of State) has a seat: their provisions are asked only for what they mean to this person.
--
-- PLAIN INPUTS. Every question takes plain inputs (yes/no, a number, a date), each with a @desc worded as the person would be asked. A question that needs another question's answer (whether
-- the person is a shadow director, a connected person, a member) builds it inside, from plain facts, by calling the layer-1 rule. The answers other parts give (section 1121 "in default",
-- section 112 "member", section 1159 "subsidiary", Schedule 1) are asked as plain facts and passed to the layer-1 rule as JUST answers; the person cannot state "NOTHING", so a question here
-- answers NOTHING only where the layer-1 rule does for the facts stated.
-- A result is JUST TRUE, JUST FALSE or NOTHING (see NOTES.md, "Reading a result: FALSE and NOTHING"): NOTHING is "not covered by this Act's words on these facts", never "no".
-- What a "level" on the standard scale stands for in pounds is not in the sources: the penalty questions (ss 228(6), 229(4), 231(4), 237(7), 238(4)) take it as a number.
-- The money sums the Act itself states (ss 207, 211 and 221) are used as the Act states them; section 258 lets the Secretary of State substitute larger ones, which would change those answers (NOTES.md, finding 2).

§ `Helper shared by the penalty questions`

-- A fine limit in pounds, from the pounds a level on the standard scale stands for (an input: the sources do not give it). Used by sections 229(4), 237(7) and 238(4), whose penalty constants this layer reads.
GIVEN lim IS A `Fine limit`
      `the pounds the level stands for` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A MAYBE NUMBER
`s 229(4) the most in pounds that a fine limit allows` MEANS
    CONSIDER lim
    WHEN `a fine not exceeding a level on the standard scale` lvl frac THEN JUST (`the pounds the level stands for` TIMES frac)
    WHEN `a fine not exceeding an amount in pounds` pounds THEN JUST pounds
    OTHERWISE NOTHING

§ `Chapter 4: loans, quasi-loans and credit transactions with directors: exceptions to the need for members' approval (ss 205 to 214)`

-- Asked by a director (or a person connected with one) about a loan, guarantee or credit transaction the company makes: is members' approval not needed, what is the value, and what follows if it was needed and not obtained.

-- section 205(1)

@export Under section 205(1), is members' approval for a loan or other funds the company provides me to meet defence costs not required (the exception for expenditure on defending proceedings)?
GIVEN `I am a director of the company or of its holding company` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are you a director of the company or of its holding company?
      `the funds are to meet my expenditure in defending criminal or civil proceedings` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are the funds to meet your expenditure in defending criminal or civil proceedings?
      `the funds are to meet my expenditure in connection with an application for relief under section 661(3) or (4) or section 1157` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are the funds to meet your expenditure in connection with an application for relief under section 661(3) or (4) or section 1157?
      `the funds are to enable me to avoid incurring such expenditure` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are the funds to enable you to avoid incurring such expenditure?
      `the proceedings concern alleged negligence, default, breach of duty or breach of trust by me in relation to the company or an associated company` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Do the proceedings concern alleged negligence, default, breach of duty or breach of trust by you in relation to the company or an associated company?
      `the terms require the loan to be repaid (or the liability discharged) if I am convicted, judgment is given against me or the court refuses me relief` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Do the terms require the loan to be repaid (or any liability of the company under a connected transaction discharged) if you are convicted, judgment is given against you or the court refuses you relief?
      `the latest date the terms allow for repayment` IS A DATE @desc What is the latest date by which the terms require repayment or discharge?
      `the date the conviction, judgment or refusal of relief becomes final` IS A DATE @desc On what date does the conviction, judgment or refusal of relief become final (the end of the time for appeal, or when any appeal is disposed of)?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 205(1), is member approval for the company's loan to fund my defence not required` IS
    (`s 205(1) approval under sections 197, 198, 200 and 201 is not required by this section` `what the company does` `I am a director of the company or of its holding company` `the proceedings concern alleged negligence, default, breach of duty or breach of trust by me in relation to the company or an associated company` `the terms are met`)
    WHERE
        `what the company does` MEANS
            BRANCH
                IF `the funds are to meet my expenditure in connection with an application for relief under section 661(3) or (4) or section 1157` THEN `s 205(1)(a)(ii) provides funds to meet expenditure in connection with an application for relief` `s 205(5) section 661(3) or (4)`
                IF `the funds are to meet my expenditure in defending criminal or civil proceedings` THEN `s 205(1)(a)(i) provides funds to meet expenditure in defending criminal or civil proceedings`
                IF `the funds are to enable me to avoid incurring such expenditure` THEN `s 205(1)(b) enables the director to avoid incurring such expenditure`
                OTHERWISE `s 205(1) does something else`
        `the terms are met` MEANS
            (`s 205(2) the terms are met` `the terms require the loan to be repaid (or the liability discharged) if I am convicted, judgment is given against me or the court refuses me relief` `the latest date the terms allow for repayment` `the date the conviction, judgment or refusal of relief becomes final`) EQUALS JUST TRUE

-- section 206

@export Under section 206, is members' approval for funds the company provides me to meet my costs of an investigation by, or action proposed by, a regulatory authority not required?
GIVEN `I am a director of the company or of its holding company` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are you a director of the company or of its holding company?
      `the funds are to meet my expenditure in defending myself in an investigation by a regulatory authority` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are the funds to meet your expenditure in defending yourself in an investigation by a regulatory authority?
      `the funds are to meet my expenditure in defending myself against action proposed to be taken by a regulatory authority` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are the funds to meet your expenditure in defending yourself against action proposed to be taken by a regulatory authority?
      `the funds are to enable me to avoid incurring such expenditure` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are the funds to enable you to avoid incurring such expenditure?
      `the matter is in connection with alleged negligence, default, breach of duty or breach of trust by me in relation to the company or an associated company` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the matter in connection with alleged negligence, default, breach of duty or breach of trust by you in relation to the company or an associated company?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 206, is member approval for the company's funds for my defence in a regulatory investigation not required` IS
    (`s 206 approval under sections 197, 198, 200 and 201 is not required by this section` `what the company does` `I am a director of the company or of its holding company` `the matter is in connection with alleged negligence, default, breach of duty or breach of trust by me in relation to the company or an associated company`)
    WHERE
        `what the company does` MEANS
            BRANCH
                IF `the funds are to meet my expenditure in defending myself in an investigation by a regulatory authority` THEN `s 206(a)(i) provides funds to meet expenditure in defending himself in an investigation by a regulatory authority`
                IF `the funds are to meet my expenditure in defending myself against action proposed to be taken by a regulatory authority` THEN `s 206(a)(ii) provides funds to meet expenditure in defending himself against action proposed to be taken by a regulatory authority`
                IF `the funds are to enable me to avoid incurring such expenditure` THEN `s 206(b) enables the director to avoid incurring such expenditure`
                OTHERWISE `s 206 does something else`

-- section 207(1)

@export Under section 207(1), is members' approval under sections 197, 198 and 200 for a small loan, quasi-loan or guarantee not required because the transaction and other relevant transactions together do not exceed 10,000 pounds?
GIVEN `the transaction is a loan` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it a loan?
      `the transaction is a quasi-loan` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it a quasi-loan (the company pays or agrees to pay a sum for you, to be reimbursed)?
      `the transaction is a guarantee or security in connection with a loan or quasi-loan` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it a guarantee given, or security provided, in connection with a loan or quasi-loan?
      `the transaction is a credit transaction` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it a credit transaction (goods, services or land supplied on deferred payment)?
      `the transaction is a guarantee or security in connection with a credit transaction` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it a guarantee given, or security provided, in connection with a credit transaction?
      `the value of the transaction in pounds` IS A NUMBER @desc What is the value of the transaction in pounds (the principal of a loan; the amount you are liable to reimburse for a quasi-loan; the price it is reasonable to expect for goods, services or land under a credit transaction; the amount guaranteed or secured)?
      `the value cannot be expressed as a specific sum of money` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the value of the transaction not capable of being expressed as a specific sum of money?
      `the value in pounds of any other relevant transactions or arrangements` IS A NUMBER @desc What is the total value in pounds of any other relevant transactions or arrangements (section 210)?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 207(1), is member approval for a small loan not required` IS
    (`s 207(1) approval under sections 197, 198 and 200 is not required by this section` `the transaction` `the value of the transaction` `the value of other relevant transactions`)
    WHERE
        `the transaction` MEANS
            BRANCH
                IF `the transaction is a loan` THEN `s 207 a loan`
                IF `the transaction is a quasi-loan` THEN `s 207 a quasi-loan`
                IF `the transaction is a guarantee or security in connection with a loan or quasi-loan` THEN `s 207 a guarantee or security in connection with a loan or quasi-loan`
                IF `the transaction is a credit transaction` THEN `s 207 a credit transaction`
                IF `the transaction is a guarantee or security in connection with a credit transaction` THEN `s 207 a guarantee or security in connection with a credit transaction`
                OTHERWISE `s 207 another kind of transaction`
        `the value of the transaction` MEANS
            IF `the value cannot be expressed as a specific sum of money` THEN `s 211 deemed to exceed 50000 pounds` ELSE `s 211 a specific sum` `the value of the transaction in pounds`
        `the value of other relevant transactions` MEANS
            `s 211 a specific sum` `the value in pounds of any other relevant transactions or arrangements`

-- section 207(2)

@export Under section 207(2), is members' approval under section 201 for a small credit transaction, guarantee or security not required because it and other relevant transactions together do not exceed 15,000 pounds?
GIVEN `the transaction is a loan` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it a loan?
      `the transaction is a quasi-loan` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it a quasi-loan (the company pays or agrees to pay a sum for you, to be reimbursed)?
      `the transaction is a guarantee or security in connection with a loan or quasi-loan` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it a guarantee given, or security provided, in connection with a loan or quasi-loan?
      `the transaction is a credit transaction` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it a credit transaction (goods, services or land supplied on deferred payment)?
      `the transaction is a guarantee or security in connection with a credit transaction` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it a guarantee given, or security provided, in connection with a credit transaction?
      `the value of the transaction in pounds` IS A NUMBER @desc What is the value of the transaction in pounds (the principal of a loan; the amount you are liable to reimburse for a quasi-loan; the price it is reasonable to expect for goods, services or land under a credit transaction; the amount guaranteed or secured)?
      `the value cannot be expressed as a specific sum of money` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the value of the transaction not capable of being expressed as a specific sum of money?
      `the value in pounds of any other relevant transactions or arrangements` IS A NUMBER @desc What is the total value in pounds of any other relevant transactions or arrangements (section 210)?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 207(2), is member approval for a small credit transaction not required` IS
    (`s 207(2) approval under section 201 is not required by this section` `the transaction` `the value of the transaction` `the value of other relevant transactions`)
    WHERE
        `the transaction` MEANS
            BRANCH
                IF `the transaction is a loan` THEN `s 207 a loan`
                IF `the transaction is a quasi-loan` THEN `s 207 a quasi-loan`
                IF `the transaction is a guarantee or security in connection with a loan or quasi-loan` THEN `s 207 a guarantee or security in connection with a loan or quasi-loan`
                IF `the transaction is a credit transaction` THEN `s 207 a credit transaction`
                IF `the transaction is a guarantee or security in connection with a credit transaction` THEN `s 207 a guarantee or security in connection with a credit transaction`
                OTHERWISE `s 207 another kind of transaction`
        `the value of the transaction` MEANS
            IF `the value cannot be expressed as a specific sum of money` THEN `s 211 deemed to exceed 50000 pounds` ELSE `s 211 a specific sum` `the value of the transaction in pounds`
        `the value of other relevant transactions` MEANS
            `s 211 a specific sum` `the value in pounds of any other relevant transactions or arrangements`

-- section 208

@export Under section 208, is members' approval not required for the company to lend to, give a guarantee or security for, or enter into a credit transaction for the benefit of, an associated body corporate?
GIVEN `the transaction is the making of a loan or quasi-loan to the other body corporate` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it the making of a loan or quasi-loan to the other body corporate?
      `the transaction is a guarantee or security in connection with a loan or quasi-loan made to the other body corporate` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it a guarantee or security in connection with a loan or quasi-loan made to the other body corporate?
      `the transaction is a credit transaction entered into as creditor for the benefit of the other body corporate` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it a credit transaction the company enters into as creditor for the benefit of the other body corporate?
      `the transaction is a guarantee or security in connection with a credit transaction entered into for the benefit of the other body corporate` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it a guarantee or security in connection with a credit transaction entered into by any person for the benefit of the other body corporate?
      `one body corporate is a subsidiary of the other` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is one of the two bodies corporate a subsidiary of the other?
      `both bodies corporate are subsidiaries of the same body corporate` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are both bodies corporate subsidiaries of the same body corporate?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 208, is member approval for a loan, guarantee or credit transaction within the corporate group not required` IS
    (`s 208 approval is not required by this section` `the transaction` `associated`)
    WHERE
        `the transaction` MEANS
            BRANCH
                IF `the transaction is the making of a loan or quasi-loan to the other body corporate` THEN `s 208(1)(a) the making of a loan or quasi-loan to the other body corporate`
                IF `the transaction is a guarantee or security in connection with a loan or quasi-loan made to the other body corporate` THEN `s 208(1)(b) a guarantee or security in connection with a loan or quasi-loan made to the other body corporate`
                IF `the transaction is a credit transaction entered into as creditor for the benefit of the other body corporate` THEN `s 208(2)(a) a credit transaction entered into as creditor for the benefit of the other body corporate`
                IF `the transaction is a guarantee or security in connection with a credit transaction entered into for the benefit of the other body corporate` THEN `s 208(2)(b) a guarantee or security in connection with a credit transaction entered into by any person for the benefit of the other body corporate`
                OTHERWISE `s 208 another kind of transaction`
        `associated` MEANS
            (`s 256(a) the bodies corporate are associated` (JUST `one body corporate is a subsidiary of the other`) (JUST `both bodies corporate are subsidiaries of the same body corporate`))

-- section 209(1)

@export Under section 209(1), is members' approval under sections 197, 198 and 200 not required for a loan, quasi-loan, guarantee or security made by a money-lending company in the ordinary course of its business?
GIVEN `the transaction is a loan` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it a loan?
      `the transaction is a quasi-loan` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it a quasi-loan (the company pays or agrees to pay a sum for you, to be reimbursed)?
      `the transaction is a guarantee or security in connection with a loan or quasi-loan` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it a guarantee given, or security provided, in connection with a loan or quasi-loan?
      `the company's ordinary business includes making loans or quasi-loans` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does the company's ordinary business include the making of loans or quasi-loans?
      `the company's ordinary business includes giving guarantees or providing security in connection with loans or quasi-loans` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does the company's ordinary business include giving guarantees or providing security in connection with loans or quasi-loans?
      `the transaction is entered into in the ordinary course of the company's business` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the transaction entered into by the company in the ordinary course of its business?
      `the value is not greater and the terms are not more favourable than for an unconnected person of the same financial standing` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the value of the transaction not greater, and are its terms not more favourable, than it is reasonable to expect the company would have offered to a person of the same financial standing but unconnected with the company?
      `it is a loan to a director of the company or its holding company` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it a loan to a director of the company or of its holding company?
      `it is a loan to an employee of the company` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it a loan to an employee of the company?
      `the loan is to buy a dwelling-house for my only or main residence` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the loan to buy a dwelling-house (with land to be occupied with it) for use as the borrower's only or main residence?
      `the loan is to improve a dwelling-house used as my only or main residence` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the loan to improve a dwelling-house (or its land) used as the borrower's only or main residence?
      `the loan replaces a loan made for either of those purposes` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does the loan replace a loan made by any person for either of those purposes?
      `loans of that description are ordinarily made by the company to its employees` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are loans of that description ordinarily made by the company to its employees?
      `the terms are no more favourable than those on which such loans are ordinarily made` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are the terms no more favourable than those on which such loans are ordinarily made?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 209(1), is member approval for my money-lending company's loan not required` IS
    (`s 209(1) approval under sections 197, 198 and 200 is not required by this section` `the transaction` `money-lending` `the transaction is entered into in the ordinary course of the company's business` `the value is not greater and the terms are not more favourable than for an unconnected person of the same financial standing` `home loan condition`)
    WHERE
        `the transaction` MEANS
            BRANCH
                IF `the transaction is a loan` THEN `s 207 a loan`
                IF `the transaction is a quasi-loan` THEN `s 207 a quasi-loan`
                IF `the transaction is a guarantee or security in connection with a loan or quasi-loan` THEN `s 207 a guarantee or security in connection with a loan or quasi-loan`
                OTHERWISE `s 207 another kind of transaction`
        `money-lending` MEANS
            (`s 209(2) the company is a money-lending company` `the company's ordinary business includes making loans or quasi-loans` `the company's ordinary business includes giving guarantees or providing security in connection with loans or quasi-loans`)
        `the purpose` MEANS
            BRANCH
                IF `the loan is to buy a dwelling-house for my only or main residence` THEN `s 209(4)(a) purchase of the whole or part of a dwelling-house, with land to be occupied and enjoyed with it`
                IF `the loan is to improve a dwelling-house used as my only or main residence` THEN `s 209(4)(b) improving a dwelling-house or part of one so used, or land occupied and enjoyed with it`
                IF `the loan replaces a loan made for either of those purposes` THEN `s 209(4)(c) substitution for a loan made by any person and falling within paragraph (a) or (b)`
                OTHERWISE `s 209(4) some other purpose`
        `home loan` MEANS
            (`s 209(4) the loan is a home loan` `the purpose` TRUE)
        `the borrower` MEANS
            BRANCH
                IF `it is a loan to a director of the company or its holding company` THEN `s 209(3)(a) a director of the company or of its holding company`
                IF `it is a loan to an employee of the company` THEN `s 209(3)(b) an employee of the company`
                OTHERWISE `s 209(3) someone else`
        `home loan condition` MEANS
            (`s 209(3) the condition in subsection (1)(b) does not of itself prevent the company from making the home loan` `the borrower` `home loan` `loans of that description are ordinarily made by the company to its employees` `the terms are no more favourable than those on which such loans are ordinarily made`)

-- section 209(2)

@export Under section 209(2), is the company a money-lending company (its ordinary business includes making loans or quasi-loans, or giving guarantees or security for them)?
GIVEN `the company's ordinary business includes making loans or quasi-loans` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does the company's ordinary business include the making of loans or quasi-loans?
      `the company's ordinary business includes giving guarantees or providing security in connection with loans or quasi-loans` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does the company's ordinary business include giving guarantees or providing security in connection with loans or quasi-loans?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 209(2), is my company a money-lending company` IS
    (`s 209(2) the company is a money-lending company` `the company's ordinary business includes making loans or quasi-loans` `the company's ordinary business includes giving guarantees or providing security in connection with loans or quasi-loans`)

-- section 210(2)

@export Under section 210(2), is another transaction or arrangement one of the 'other relevant transactions or arrangements' that count with this one towards an exception from members' approval?
GIVEN `the other transaction was entered into previously or at the same time as this one` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Was the other transaction or arrangement entered into previously, or at the same time as the one in question?
      `this transaction is for a director of the company entering into it` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the transaction in question entered into for a director of the company entering into it?
      `this transaction is for a person connected with a director of the company entering into it` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it entered into for a person connected with such a director?
      `this transaction is for a director of the holding company of the company entering into it` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it entered into for a director of the holding company of the company entering into it?
      `this transaction is for a person connected with a director of the holding company` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it entered into for a person connected with such a director of the holding company?
      `the other transaction was entered into for that director or connected person by virtue of the relevant exception` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Was the other transaction entered into for that director, or a person connected with him, by virtue of the relevant exception?
      `the other transaction was entered into by the company or one of its subsidiaries` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Was the other transaction entered into by the company entering into the transaction in question, or by one of its subsidiaries?
      `the other transaction was entered into by the holding company or one of its subsidiaries` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Was it entered into by the holding company, or by one of its subsidiaries?
      `its maker was then a subsidiary of the company or of its holding company` IS A BOOLEAN @desc At the time the other transaction was entered into, was its maker a subsidiary of the company entering into the transaction in question, or of that company's holding company?
      `its maker is still such a subsidiary` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is its maker still such a subsidiary now?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 210(2), is my other loan or arrangement a relevant transaction for an exception` IS
    (`s 210(2) the other transaction or arrangement is a relevant transaction or arrangement` `the other transaction was entered into previously or at the same time as this one` `three` `four` `five`)
    WHERE
        `for whom` MEANS
            BRANCH
                IF `this transaction is for a director of the company entering into it` THEN `s 210(3)(a) a director of the company entering into it`
                IF `this transaction is for a person connected with a director of the company entering into it` THEN `s 210(3)(b) a person connected with a director of the company entering into it`
                IF `this transaction is for a director of the holding company of the company entering into it` THEN `s 210(4)(a) a director of the holding company of the company entering into it`
                IF `this transaction is for a person connected with a director of the holding company` THEN `s 210(4)(b) a person connected with a director of the holding company of the company entering into it`
                OTHERWISE `s 210 someone else`
        `by whom` MEANS
            BRANCH
                IF `the other transaction was entered into by the company or one of its subsidiaries` THEN `s 210 the company entering into the transaction in question`
                IF `the other transaction was entered into by the holding company or one of its subsidiaries` THEN `s 210 the holding company of the company entering into the transaction in question`
                OTHERWISE `s 210 someone else`
        `three` MEANS
            (`s 210(3) the conditions are met` `for whom` `the other transaction was entered into for that director or connected person by virtue of the relevant exception` `by whom`)
        `four` MEANS
            (`s 210(4) the conditions are met` `for whom` `the other transaction was entered into for that director or connected person by virtue of the relevant exception` `by whom`)
        `five` MEANS
            (`s 210(5) the transaction or arrangement is not a relevant transaction or arrangement` `its maker was then a subsidiary of the company or of its holding company` `its maker is still such a subsidiary`)

-- section 211(1)

@export Under section 211(1), what is the value in pounds of a loan, quasi-loan, credit transaction, guarantee, security or related arrangement for the exceptions to members' approval (nothing if its value cannot be expressed as a specific sum)?
GIVEN `it is a loan` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it a loan?
      `it is a quasi-loan` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it a quasi-loan?
      `it is a credit transaction` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it a credit transaction?
      `it is a guarantee or security` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it a guarantee or security?
      `the amount in pounds` IS A NUMBER @desc What is its amount in pounds: the principal of a loan; the most the person is liable to reimburse for a quasi-loan; the price it is reasonable to expect for the goods, services or land; the amount guaranteed or secured; or the value of the transaction a related arrangement relates to?
      `its value is capable of being expressed as a specific sum of money` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Can its value be expressed as a specific sum of money?
GIVETH A MAYBE NUMBER
DECIDE `Under section 211(1), what is the value of my loan, guarantee or credit transaction in pounds` IS
    CONSIDER (`s 211(1)(a) the value of the transaction or arrangement` `the transaction` `its value is capable of being expressed as a specific sum of money`)
    WHEN `s 211 a specific sum` x THEN JUST x
    WHEN `s 211 deemed to exceed 50000 pounds` THEN NOTHING
    WHERE
        `the transaction` MEANS
            BRANCH
                IF `it is a loan` THEN `s 211(2) a loan` `the amount in pounds`
                IF `it is a quasi-loan` THEN `s 211(3) a quasi-loan` `the amount in pounds`
                IF `it is a credit transaction` THEN `s 211(4) a credit transaction` `the amount in pounds`
                IF `it is a guarantee or security` THEN `s 211(5) a guarantee or security` `the amount in pounds`
                OTHERWISE `s 211(6) an arrangement to which section 203 applies` `the amount in pounds`

-- section 211(7)

@export Under section 211(7), is the value of the transaction or arrangement deemed to exceed 50,000 pounds because it cannot be expressed as a specific sum of money?
GIVEN `its value is capable of being expressed as a specific sum of money` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Can its value be expressed as a specific sum of money (for example, is the liability under it ascertainable)?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 211(7), is the value of my transaction deemed to exceed 50,000 pounds` IS
    (`s 211(7) the value is deemed to exceed 50,000 pounds` `its value is capable of being expressed as a specific sum of money`)

-- section 211(1)(b)

@export Under section 211(1)(b), what is the value in pounds of another relevant transaction once the liabilities of the person it was made for have been reduced?
GIVEN `the value so determined in pounds` IS A NUMBER @desc What is the value of the earlier transaction in pounds, worked out under section 211?
      `the amount by which the liabilities have been reduced in pounds` IS A NUMBER @desc By how much in pounds have the liabilities of the person it was made for been reduced?
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `Under section 211(1)(b), what is the value of an earlier transaction after my liabilities were reduced` IS
    (`s 211(1)(b) the value of an other relevant transaction or arrangement` `the value so determined in pounds` `the amount by which the liabilities have been reduced in pounds`)

-- section 212

@export Under section 212, who is the person for whom a loan, quasi-loan, credit transaction, guarantee, security or related arrangement is entered into?
GIVEN `it is a loan or quasi-loan` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it a loan or quasi-loan?
      `it is a credit transaction` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it a credit transaction?
      `it is a guarantee or security` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it a guarantee or security?
      `the person to whom the loan is made, the goods are supplied, or for whom the transaction guaranteed or related to is made` IS A STRING @desc Who is the person to whom the loan or quasi-loan is made, to whom the goods, land or services are supplied, or for whom the transaction is made in connection with which the guarantee, security or arrangement is given?
GIVETH A STRING
DECIDE `Under section 212, for whom is the transaction entered into` IS
    (`s 212 the person for whom the transaction or arrangement is entered into` `the transaction`)
    WHERE
        `the transaction` MEANS
            BRANCH
                IF `it is a loan or quasi-loan` THEN `s 212(a) a loan or quasi-loan` `the person to whom the loan is made, the goods are supplied, or for whom the transaction guaranteed or related to is made`
                IF `it is a credit transaction` THEN `s 212(b) a credit transaction` `the person to whom the loan is made, the goods are supplied, or for whom the transaction guaranteed or related to is made`
                IF `it is a guarantee or security` THEN `s 212(c) a guarantee or security` `the person to whom the loan is made, the goods are supplied, or for whom the transaction guaranteed or related to is made`
                OTHERWISE `s 212(d) an arrangement within section 203` `the person to whom the loan is made, the goods are supplied, or for whom the transaction guaranteed or related to is made`

-- section 213(2)

@export Under section 213(2), is a transaction made without the members' approval that sections 197 to 203 require voidable at the instance of the company?
GIVEN `it was entered into without the members' approval that section 197 requires (loans to directors)` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Was the transaction or arrangement entered into without the members' approval that section 197 requires (loans to directors?)
      `it was entered into without the members' approval that section 198 requires (quasi-loans to directors)` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Was the transaction or arrangement entered into without the members' approval that section 198 requires (quasi-loans to directors?)
      `it was entered into without the members' approval that section 200 requires (loans or quasi-loans to persons connected with directors)` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Was the transaction or arrangement entered into without the members' approval that section 200 requires (loans or quasi-loans to persons connected with directors?)
      `it was entered into without the members' approval that section 201 requires (credit transactions)` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Was the transaction or arrangement entered into without the members' approval that section 201 requires (credit transactions?)
      `it was entered into without the members' approval that section 203 requires (related arrangements)` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Was the transaction or arrangement entered into without the members' approval that section 203 requires (related arrangements?)
      `restitution of any money or other asset that was the subject matter is no longer possible` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is restitution of any money or other asset that was the subject matter of the transaction no longer possible?
      `the company has been indemnified for any loss or damage resulting from the transaction` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has the company been indemnified for any loss or damage resulting from the transaction or arrangement?
      `rights acquired in good faith, for value and without actual notice by an outsider would be affected by the avoidance` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Would rights acquired in good faith, for value and without actual notice of the contravention by a person who is not a party to the transaction be affected by the avoidance?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 213(2), can the company avoid the transaction` IS
    (`s 213(2) the transaction or arrangement is voidable at the instance of the company` (`s 213(1) this section applies` (JUST `it was entered into without the members' approval that section 197 requires (loans to directors)`) (JUST `it was entered into without the members' approval that section 198 requires (quasi-loans to directors)`) (JUST `it was entered into without the members' approval that section 200 requires (loans or quasi-loans to persons connected with directors)`) (JUST `it was entered into without the members' approval that section 201 requires (credit transactions)`) (JUST `it was entered into without the members' approval that section 203 requires (related arrangements)`)) `restitution of any money or other asset that was the subject matter is no longer possible` `the company has been indemnified for any loss or damage resulting from the transaction` `rights acquired in good faith, for value and without actual notice by an outsider would be affected by the avoidance`)

-- section 213(3)

@export Under section 213(3) and (4), am I, as a director, a connected person or the director of a connected person, liable to account to the company for any gain and to indemnify it for loss because it made a transaction without the members' approval?
GIVEN `it was entered into without the members' approval that section 197 requires (loans to directors)` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Was the transaction or arrangement entered into without the members' approval that section 197 requires (loans to directors?)
      `it was entered into without the members' approval that section 198 requires (quasi-loans to directors)` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Was the transaction or arrangement entered into without the members' approval that section 198 requires (quasi-loans to directors?)
      `it was entered into without the members' approval that section 200 requires (loans or quasi-loans to persons connected with directors)` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Was the transaction or arrangement entered into without the members' approval that section 200 requires (loans or quasi-loans to persons connected with directors?)
      `it was entered into without the members' approval that section 201 requires (credit transactions)` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Was the transaction or arrangement entered into without the members' approval that section 201 requires (credit transactions?)
      `it was entered into without the members' approval that section 203 requires (related arrangements)` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Was the transaction or arrangement entered into without the members' approval that section 203 requires (related arrangements?)
      `I am a director with whom the company entered into the transaction` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are you a director of the company (or of its holding company) with whom the company entered into the transaction?
      `I am a person with whom the company entered into it who is connected with a director` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are you a person with whom the company entered into the transaction who is connected with a director of the company or of its holding company?
      `I am the director with whom such a connected person is connected` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are you the director of the company (or of its holding company) with whom such a connected person is connected?
      `I am another director who authorised the transaction` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are you another director of the company who authorised the transaction?
      `the transaction was with a person connected with a director` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Was the transaction made with a person connected with a director of the company or of its holding company?
      `I show that I took all reasonable steps to secure the company's compliance` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Can you show that you took all reasonable steps to secure the company's compliance with the section concerned?
      `I show that I did not know the relevant circumstances constituting the contravention` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Can you show that, when the transaction was entered into, you did not know the relevant circumstances constituting the contravention?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 213(3), am I liable to account for my gain and indemnify the company` IS
    (`s 213(3) the person is liable to account to the company for any gain and to indemnify it for any loss` `four` `six` `seven`)
    WHERE
        `position` MEANS
            BRANCH
                IF `I am a director with whom the company entered into the transaction` THEN `s 213(4)(a) a director of the company or of its holding company with whom the company entered into the transaction or arrangement`
                IF `I am a person with whom the company entered into it who is connected with a director` THEN `s 213(4)(b) a person with whom the company entered into the transaction or arrangement who is connected with a director of the company or of its holding company`
                IF `I am the director with whom such a connected person is connected` THEN `s 213(4)(c) the director of the company or of its holding company with whom any such person is connected`
                IF `I am another director who authorised the transaction` THEN `s 213(4)(d) any other director of the company who authorised the transaction or arrangement`
                OTHERWISE `s 213(4) none of these`
        `contravened` MEANS
            BRANCH
                IF `it was entered into without the members' approval that section 200 requires (loans or quasi-loans to persons connected with directors)` THEN `s 213 section 200`
                IF `it was entered into without the members' approval that section 201 requires (credit transactions)` THEN `s 213 section 201`
                IF `it was entered into without the members' approval that section 203 requires (related arrangements)` THEN `s 213 section 203`
                IF `it was entered into without the members' approval that section 198 requires (quasi-loans to directors)` THEN `s 213 section 198`
                OTHERWISE `s 213 section 197`
        `four` MEANS
            (`s 213(4) the person is one of the persons liable` `position` `contravened`)
        `six` MEANS
            (`s 213(6) the director is not liable by virtue of subsection (4)(c)` `position` `contravened` `the transaction was with a person connected with a director` `I show that I took all reasonable steps to secure the company's compliance`)
        `seven` MEANS
            (`s 213(7) the person is not liable by virtue of subsection (4)(b) or (d)` `position` `I show that I did not know the relevant circumstances constituting the contravention`)

-- section 213(3)(a)

@export Under section 213(3)(a), how much in pounds must I account to the company for the gain I made directly or indirectly by a transaction made without the members' approval (nothing if the answer depends on facts not stated)?
GIVEN `I am liable under section 213(3)` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are you liable under section 213(3) (see the question on liability)?
      `the gain I made directly or indirectly by the transaction in pounds` IS A NUMBER @desc What gain in pounds did you make, directly or indirectly, by the transaction or arrangement?
GIVETH A MAYBE NUMBER
DECIDE `Under section 213(3)(a), how much must I account to the company for my gain` IS
    (`s 213(3)(a) the amount the person must account to the company for` (JUST `I am liable under section 213(3)`) `the gain I made directly or indirectly by the transaction in pounds`)

-- section 214

@export Under section 214, may a transaction made without the members' approval that sections 197 to 203 require no longer be avoided under section 213 because the members affirmed it within a reasonable period?
GIVEN `it was entered into without the members' approval that section 197 requires (loans to directors)` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Was the transaction or arrangement entered into without the members' approval that section 197 requires (loans to directors?)
      `it was entered into without the members' approval that section 198 requires (quasi-loans to directors)` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Was the transaction or arrangement entered into without the members' approval that section 198 requires (quasi-loans to directors?)
      `it was entered into without the members' approval that section 200 requires (loans or quasi-loans to persons connected with directors)` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Was the transaction or arrangement entered into without the members' approval that section 200 requires (loans or quasi-loans to persons connected with directors?)
      `it was entered into without the members' approval that section 201 requires (credit transactions)` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Was the transaction or arrangement entered into without the members' approval that section 201 requires (credit transactions?)
      `it was entered into without the members' approval that section 203 requires (related arrangements)` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Was the transaction or arrangement entered into without the members' approval that section 203 requires (related arrangements?)
      `it was affirmed within a reasonable period` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Was it affirmed within a reasonable period?
      `the contravention was of the requirement for a resolution of the members of the company` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Was the contravention of the requirement for a resolution of the members of the company?
      `it was affirmed by a resolution of the members of the company` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Was it affirmed by a resolution of the members of the company?
      `the contravention was of the requirement for a resolution of the members of the holding company` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Was the contravention of the requirement for a resolution of the members of the company's holding company?
      `it was affirmed by a resolution of the members of the holding company` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Was it affirmed by a resolution of the members of the holding company?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 214, is the transaction one that may no longer be avoided because the members affirmed it` IS
    (`s 214 the transaction or arrangement may no longer be avoided under section 213` (`s 213(1) this section applies` (JUST `it was entered into without the members' approval that section 197 requires (loans to directors)`) (JUST `it was entered into without the members' approval that section 198 requires (quasi-loans to directors)`) (JUST `it was entered into without the members' approval that section 200 requires (loans or quasi-loans to persons connected with directors)`) (JUST `it was entered into without the members' approval that section 201 requires (credit transactions)`) (JUST `it was entered into without the members' approval that section 203 requires (related arrangements)`)) `it was affirmed within a reasonable period` `the contravention was of the requirement for a resolution of the members of the company` `it was affirmed by a resolution of the members of the company` `the contravention was of the requirement for a resolution of the members of the holding company` `it was affirmed by a resolution of the members of the holding company`)

§ `Chapter 4, payments for loss of office (ss 215 to 222) and the supplementary sections (ss 223 to 226)`

-- Asked by a director who is leaving or has left, by a member asked to approve a payment, or by the company's officers.

-- section 215(1)

@export Under section 215(1), is a payment made to me a payment for loss of office (compensation for losing, or consideration for retiring from, my office as director or a related office or employment)?
GIVEN `the payment is compensation for my loss of office as director of the company` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it compensation for your loss of office as director of the company?
      `the payment is compensation for my loss of another office or employment in connection with the management of the company's affairs` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it compensation for your loss of another office or employment in connection with the management of the company's affairs?
      `the payment is compensation for my loss of an office or employment in connection with the management of a subsidiary undertaking's affairs` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it compensation for your loss of an office or employment in connection with the management of a subsidiary undertaking's affairs?
      `the payment is consideration for my retirement from office as director of the company` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it consideration for your retirement from office as director of the company?
      `the payment is consideration for my retirement from another office or employment in connection with the management of the company's affairs` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it consideration for your retirement from another office or employment in connection with the management of the company's affairs?
      `the payment is consideration for my retirement from an office or employment in connection with the management of a subsidiary undertaking's affairs` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it consideration for your retirement from an office or employment in connection with the management of a subsidiary undertaking's affairs?
      `the payment is made to a director or past director of the company` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the payment made to a director or past director of the company?
      `the loss or retirement was while I was director or in connection with my ceasing to be a director` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did the loss, or the retirement, happen while you were a director or in connection with your ceasing to be one?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 215(1), is the payment to me a payment for loss of office` IS
    (`s 215(1) the payment is a payment for loss of office` `the nature` `the payment is made to a director or past director of the company` `the loss or retirement was while I was director or in connection with my ceasing to be a director`)
    WHERE
        `the nature` MEANS
            BRANCH
                IF `the payment is compensation for my loss of office as director of the company` THEN `s 215(1)(a) compensation for loss of office as director of the company`
                IF `the payment is compensation for my loss of another office or employment in connection with the management of the company's affairs` THEN `s 215(1)(b)(i) compensation for loss of any other office or employment in connection with the management of the affairs of the company`
                IF `the payment is compensation for my loss of an office or employment in connection with the management of a subsidiary undertaking's affairs` THEN `s 215(1)(b)(ii) compensation for loss of any office (as director or otherwise) or employment in connection with the management of the affairs of a subsidiary undertaking of the company`
                IF `the payment is consideration for my retirement from office as director of the company` THEN `s 215(1)(c) consideration for or in connection with retirement from office as director of the company`
                IF `the payment is consideration for my retirement from another office or employment in connection with the management of the company's affairs` THEN `s 215(1)(d)(i) consideration for or in connection with retirement from any other office or employment in connection with the management of the affairs of the company`
                IF `the payment is consideration for my retirement from an office or employment in connection with the management of a subsidiary undertaking's affairs` THEN `s 215(1)(d)(ii) consideration for or in connection with retirement from any office (as director or otherwise) or employment in connection with the management of the affairs of a subsidiary undertaking of the company`
                OTHERWISE `s 215(1) some other payment`

-- section 215(3)

@export Under section 215(3), for the approval rules in sections 217 to 221, is a payment made to a person connected with me, or to someone at my direction or for my benefit, treated as a payment to me?
GIVEN `the payment is one within sections 217 to 221` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the payment one that sections 217 to 221 deal with (a payment for loss of office needing members' approval)?
      `the payment is to a person connected with a director` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the payment made to a person connected with a director?
      `the payment is to someone at the direction of, or for the benefit of, a director or a person connected with him` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the payment made to someone at the direction of, or for the benefit of, a director or a person connected with him?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 215(3), is a payment to someone connected with me treated as a payment to me` IS
    (`s 215(3) the payment is treated as payment to the director` `recipient` `the payment is one within sections 217 to 221`)
    WHERE
        `recipient` MEANS
            BRANCH
                IF `the payment is to a person connected with a director` THEN `s 215(3)(a) a person connected with a director`
                IF `the payment is to someone at the direction of, or for the benefit of, a director or a person connected with him` THEN `s 215(3)(b) any person at the direction of, or for the benefit of, a director or a person connected with him`
                OTHERWISE `s 215(3) someone else`

-- section 216(2)

@export Under section 216(2)(a), when I am to leave office in connection with a transfer of the company's business or shares, how much of the price paid to me above what other holders could have obtained is taken to be a payment for loss of office?
GIVEN `it is in connection with a transfer under section 218 or 219` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it in connection with a transfer of the company's undertaking or property (section 218) or of shares resulting from a takeover bid (section 219)?
      `I am to cease to hold office as director` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are you to cease to hold office as director?
      `the price to be paid to me for my shares in pounds` IS A NUMBER @desc What price in pounds is to be paid to you for your shares in the company?
      `the price other holders of like shares could have obtained in pounds` IS A NUMBER @desc What price in pounds could other holders of like shares have obtained at the time?
GIVETH A MAYBE NUMBER
DECIDE `Under section 216(2), how much of the price I am paid for my shares is taken to be a payment for loss of office` IS
    (`s 216(2)(a) the excess taken to have been a payment for loss of office` (`s 216(1) this section applies` `it is in connection with a transfer under section 218 or 219` `I am to cease to hold office as director` FALSE) `the price to be paid to me for my shares in pounds` `the price other holders of like shares could have obtained in pounds`)

-- section 217(1)

@export Under section 217(1), is the company barred from paying me a payment for loss of office because the members have not approved it by resolution?
GIVEN `the payment is a payment for loss of office to a director of the company` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the payment a payment for loss of office to a director of the company?
      `the payment has been approved by a resolution of the members of the company` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has the payment been approved by a resolution of the members of the company?
      `the company is a UK-registered company` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the company a UK-registered company?
      `the company is a wholly-owned subsidiary of another body corporate` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the company a wholly-owned subsidiary of another body corporate?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 217(1), is my company barred from paying me for loss of office without members' approval` IS
    (`s 217(1) the company may not make the payment` `the payment is a payment for loss of office to a director of the company` `the payment has been approved by a resolution of the members of the company` (`s 217(4) no approval is required under section 217 on the part of the members of the body corporate` `the company is a UK-registered company` `the company is a wholly-owned subsidiary of another body corporate`))

-- section 217(3)

@export Under section 217(3), must the resolution approving a payment for loss of office not be passed because the memorandum of particulars was not made available as required (a written resolution: sent to every eligible member in time; a meeting: available for inspection for 15 days ending with the meeting date, and at the meeting)?
GIVEN `the resolution is a written resolution` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the resolution a written resolution (not passed at a meeting)?
      `a memorandum setting out particulars of the proposed payment, including its amount, was made available to the members` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Was a memorandum setting out particulars of the proposed payment, including its amount, made available to the members?
      `it was sent or submitted to every eligible member at or before the time the proposed written resolution was sent to him` IS A BOOLEAN @desc For a written resolution: was the memorandum sent or submitted to every eligible member at or before the time the proposed resolution was sent or submitted to him?
      `the first day it was available for inspection at the registered office` IS A DATE @desc For a meeting: on what date was the memorandum first available for inspection at the company's registered office?
      `the date of the meeting` IS A DATE @desc For a meeting: what is the date of the meeting?
      `it was also available for inspection at the meeting itself` IS A BOOLEAN @desc For a meeting: was the memorandum also available for inspection at the meeting itself?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 217(3), must the resolution approving the payment not be passed for want of a memorandum` IS
    (`s 217(3) the resolution approving the payment must not be passed` (IF `the resolution is a written resolution` THEN `as a written resolution` ELSE `at a meeting on a show of hands`) TRUE (`s 217(3) memorandum` OF `a memorandum setting out particulars of the proposed payment, including its amount, was made available to the members`, `it was sent or submitted to every eligible member at or before the time the proposed written resolution was sent to him`, `the first day it was available for inspection at the registered office`, `the date of the meeting`, `it was also available for inspection at the meeting itself`))

-- section 218(3)

@export Under section 218(3), must the resolution approving a payment for loss of office not be passed because the memorandum of particulars was not made available as required (a written resolution: sent to every eligible member in time; a meeting: available for inspection for 15 days ending with the meeting date, and at the meeting)?
GIVEN `the resolution is a written resolution` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the resolution a written resolution (not passed at a meeting)?
      `a memorandum setting out particulars of the proposed payment, including its amount, was made available to the members` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Was a memorandum setting out particulars of the proposed payment, including its amount, made available to the members?
      `it was sent or submitted to every eligible member at or before the time the proposed written resolution was sent to him` IS A BOOLEAN @desc For a written resolution: was the memorandum sent or submitted to every eligible member at or before the time the proposed resolution was sent or submitted to him?
      `the first day it was available for inspection at the registered office` IS A DATE @desc For a meeting: on what date was the memorandum first available for inspection at the company's registered office?
      `the date of the meeting` IS A DATE @desc For a meeting: what is the date of the meeting?
      `it was also available for inspection at the meeting itself` IS A BOOLEAN @desc For a meeting: was the memorandum also available for inspection at the meeting itself?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 218(3), must the resolution approving the payment not be passed for want of a memorandum` IS
    (`s 218(3) the resolution approving the payment must not be passed` (IF `the resolution is a written resolution` THEN `as a written resolution` ELSE `at a meeting on a show of hands`) TRUE (`s 218(3) memorandum` OF `a memorandum setting out particulars of the proposed payment, including its amount, was made available to the members`, `it was sent or submitted to every eligible member at or before the time the proposed written resolution was sent to him`, `the first day it was available for inspection at the registered office`, `the date of the meeting`, `it was also available for inspection at the meeting itself`))

-- section 219(3)

@export Under section 219(3), must the resolution approving a payment for loss of office not be passed because the memorandum of particulars was not made available as required (a written resolution: sent to every eligible member in time; a meeting: available for inspection for 15 days ending with the meeting date, and at the meeting)?
GIVEN `the resolution is a written resolution` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the resolution a written resolution (not passed at a meeting)?
      `a memorandum setting out particulars of the proposed payment, including its amount, was made available to the members` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Was a memorandum setting out particulars of the proposed payment, including its amount, made available to the members?
      `it was sent or submitted to every eligible member at or before the time the proposed written resolution was sent to him` IS A BOOLEAN @desc For a written resolution: was the memorandum sent or submitted to every eligible member at or before the time the proposed resolution was sent or submitted to him?
      `the first day it was available for inspection at the registered office` IS A DATE @desc For a meeting: on what date was the memorandum first available for inspection at the company's registered office?
      `the date of the meeting` IS A DATE @desc For a meeting: what is the date of the meeting?
      `it was also available for inspection at the meeting itself` IS A BOOLEAN @desc For a meeting: was the memorandum also available for inspection at the meeting itself?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 219(3), must the resolution approving the payment not be passed for want of a memorandum` IS
    (`s 219(3) the resolution approving the payment must not be passed` (IF `the resolution is a written resolution` THEN `as a written resolution` ELSE `at a meeting on a show of hands`) TRUE (`s 219(3) memorandum` OF `a memorandum setting out particulars of the proposed payment, including its amount, was made available to the members`, `it was sent or submitted to every eligible member at or before the time the proposed written resolution was sent to him`, `the first day it was available for inspection at the registered office`, `the date of the meeting`, `it was also available for inspection at the meeting itself`))

-- section 218(1)

@export Under section 218(1), is no person allowed to pay me for loss of office in connection with a transfer of the company's undertaking or property because the members have not approved it?
GIVEN `the payment is made to me in connection with the transfer of the whole or any part of the company's undertaking or property` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the payment made to you, a director, in connection with the transfer of the whole or any part of the company's undertaking or property?
      `the payment has been approved by a resolution of the members of the company` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has the payment been approved by a resolution of the members of the company?
      `the company is a UK-registered company` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the company a UK-registered company?
      `the company is a wholly-owned subsidiary of another body corporate` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the company a wholly-owned subsidiary of another body corporate?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 218(1), is no person allowed to pay me for loss of office in connection with a transfer of the company's business without approval` IS
    (`s 218(1) no person may make the payment` `the payment is made to me in connection with the transfer of the whole or any part of the company's undertaking or property` `the payment has been approved by a resolution of the members of the company` (`s 218(4) no approval is required under section 218 on the part of the members of the body corporate` `the company is a UK-registered company` `the company is a wholly-owned subsidiary of another body corporate`))

-- section 218(5)

@export Under section 218(5), is a payment made under an arrangement connected with the transfer of the company's undertaking or property presumed to be a payment needing members' approval?
GIVEN `the arrangement was entered into as part of the agreement for the transfer` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Was the arrangement entered into as part of the agreement for the transfer?
      `the date the arrangement was entered into` IS A DATE @desc On what date was the arrangement entered into?
      `the date of the agreement for the transfer` IS A DATE @desc On what date was the agreement for the transfer made?
      `the company whose undertaking is transferred, or a person to whom it is transferred, is privy to the arrangement` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the company whose undertaking or property is transferred, or any person to whom the transfer is made, privy to the arrangement?
      `the contrary is shown` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has it been shown that the payment is not one to which section 218 applies?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 218(5), is a payment under an arrangement for a transfer presumed to need approval` IS
    (`s 218(5) the payment is presumed to be a payment to which section 218 applies` `the arrangement was entered into as part of the agreement for the transfer` `the date the arrangement was entered into` `the date of the agreement for the transfer` `the company whose undertaking is transferred, or a person to whom it is transferred, is privy to the arrangement` `the contrary is shown`)

-- section 219(1)

@export Under section 219(1), is no person allowed to pay me for loss of office in connection with a transfer of shares resulting from a takeover bid because the relevant shareholders have not approved it?
GIVEN `the payment is made to me in connection with a transfer of shares resulting from a takeover bid` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the payment made to you, a director, in connection with a transfer of shares in the company, or in a subsidiary, resulting from a takeover bid?
      `the payment has been approved by a resolution of the relevant shareholders` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has the payment been approved by a resolution of the relevant shareholders (the holders of the shares the bid relates to, and holders of shares of the same class)?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 219(1), is no person allowed to pay me for loss of office in connection with a takeover bid without approval of the shareholders` IS
    (`s 219(1) no person may make the payment` `the payment is made to me in connection with a transfer of shares resulting from a takeover bid` `the payment has been approved by a resolution of the relevant shareholders`)

-- section 219(4)

@export Under section 219(4), is a person who makes the takeover offer, or an associate of that person, entitled to vote on the resolution approving a payment to me?
GIVEN `the person is the person making the offer` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the person the one making the takeover offer?
      `the person is an associate of the person making the offer` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the person an associate (within section 988) of the person making the offer?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 219(4), may the bidder vote on the resolution approving my payment` IS
    (`s 219(4) the person is entitled to vote on the resolution` `the person is the person making the offer` (JUST `the person is an associate of the person making the offer`))

-- section 219(5)

@export Under section 219(5), is a payment deemed approved because no quorum was present at the meeting and again after it was adjourned?
GIVEN `a quorum is not present at the meeting to consider the resolution` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Was a quorum not present at the meeting to consider the resolution?
      `the meeting was adjourned to a later date and a quorum was again not present` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Was the meeting adjourned to a later date, and was a quorum again not present?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 219(5), is my payment deemed approved if the meeting was twice inquorate` IS
    (`s 219(5) the payment is deemed to have been approved` `a quorum is not present at the meeting to consider the resolution` `the meeting was adjourned to a later date and a quorum was again not present`)

-- section 220(1)

@export Under section 220(1), is members' approval for a payment not required because it was made in good faith in discharge of an existing legal obligation, as damages for breach of one, in settlement of a claim on termination, or as a pension for past services?
GIVEN `the payment was made in good faith` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Was the payment made in good faith?
      `it is made in discharge of an existing legal obligation` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it made in discharge of an existing legal obligation?
      `it is made by way of damages for breach of such an obligation` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it made by way of damages for breach of such an obligation?
      `it is made by way of settlement or compromise of a claim arising in connection with the termination of an office or employment` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it made by way of settlement or compromise of any claim arising in connection with the termination of a person's office or employment?
      `it is made by way of pension in respect of past services` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it made by way of pension in respect of past services?
      `the payment is a payment by the company within section 217` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the payment one the company makes to a director, within section 217?
      `the payment is in connection with a transfer of the undertaking or property, within section 218` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the payment made in connection with a transfer of the company's undertaking or property, within section 218?
      `the payment is in connection with a transfer of shares resulting from a takeover bid, within section 219` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the payment made in connection with a transfer of shares resulting from a takeover bid, within section 219?
      `it is an obligation of the company` IS A BOOLEAN @desc For a payment by the company: is the obligation one of the company?
      `it was not entered into in connection with, or in consequence of, the event giving rise to the payment for loss of office` IS A BOOLEAN @desc For a payment by the company: was the obligation not entered into in connection with, or in consequence of, the event giving rise to the payment?
      `it is an obligation of the person making the payment` IS A BOOLEAN @desc For a payment in connection with a transfer: is the obligation one of the person making the payment?
      `it was not entered into for the purposes of, in connection with or in consequence of, the transfer in question` IS A BOOLEAN @desc For a payment in connection with a transfer: was the obligation not entered into for the purposes of, in connection with or in consequence of, the transfer?
      `one body corporate is a subsidiary of the other` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is one of the two bodies corporate a subsidiary of the other?
      `both bodies corporate are subsidiaries of the same body corporate` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are both bodies corporate subsidiaries of the same body corporate?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 220(1), is approval for my payment not needed because it is in discharge of a legal obligation or a pension` IS
    BRANCH
        IF NOT (`the payment is a payment by the company within section 217` OR `the payment is in connection with a transfer of the undertaking or property, within section 218` OR `the payment is in connection with a transfer of shares resulting from a takeover bid, within section 219`) THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "Approval is not required under section 217, 218 or 219"
        OTHERWISE (`s 220(1) approval under section 217, 218 or 219 is not required by this section` `the ground` `the payment was made in good faith` `the obligation`)
    WHERE
        `the ground` MEANS
            BRANCH
                IF `it is made in discharge of an existing legal obligation` THEN `s 220(1)(a) in discharge of an existing legal obligation`
                IF `it is made by way of damages for breach of such an obligation` THEN `s 220(1)(b) by way of damages for breach of such an obligation`
                IF `it is made by way of settlement or compromise of a claim arising in connection with the termination of an office or employment` THEN `s 220(1)(c) by way of settlement or compromise of any claim arising in connection with the termination of a person's office or employment`
                IF `it is made by way of pension in respect of past services` THEN `s 220(1)(d) by way of pension in respect of past services`
                OTHERWISE `s 220(1) some other ground`
        `associated` MEANS
            (`s 256(a) the bodies corporate are associated` (JUST `one body corporate is a subsidiary of the other`) (JUST `both bodies corporate are subsidiaries of the same body corporate`))
        `within` MEANS
            BRANCH
                IF `the payment is a payment by the company within section 217` AND `the payment is in connection with a transfer of the undertaking or property, within section 218` THEN `s 220(4) both section 217 and section 218`
                IF `the payment is a payment by the company within section 217` AND `the payment is in connection with a transfer of shares resulting from a takeover bid, within section 219` THEN `s 220(4) both section 217 and section 219`
                IF `the payment is a payment by the company within section 217` THEN `s 220(4) section 217 only`
                IF `the payment is in connection with a transfer of the undertaking or property, within section 218` THEN `s 220(4) section 218 only`
                OTHERWISE `s 220(4) section 219 only`
        `the obligation` MEANS
            CONSIDER (`s 220(4) which definition of an existing legal obligation applies` `within`)
            WHEN `s 220(4) subsection (2) applies` THEN (`s 220(2) the obligation is an existing legal obligation` `associated` `it is an obligation of the company` `it was not entered into in connection with, or in consequence of, the event giving rise to the payment for loss of office`)
            WHEN `s 220(4) subsection (3) applies` THEN (`s 220(3) the obligation is an existing legal obligation` `it is an obligation of the person making the payment` `it was not entered into for the purposes of, in connection with or in consequence of, the transfer in question`)

-- section 221(1)

@export Under section 221(1), is members' approval for a payment for loss of office not required because it, with other relevant payments, does not exceed 200 pounds?
GIVEN `the payment is made by the company or one of its subsidiaries` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the payment made by the company or any of its subsidiaries?
      `the amount or value of the payment in pounds` IS A NUMBER @desc What is the amount or value of the payment in pounds?
      `the amount or value of any other relevant payments in pounds` IS A NUMBER @desc What is the total amount or value in pounds of any other relevant payments (to you, by the company or its subsidiaries, in connection with the same event or transfer)?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 221(1), is approval for my small payment not needed` IS
    (`s 221(1) approval under section 217, 218 or 219 is not required by this section` `the payment is made by the company or one of its subsidiaries` `the amount or value of the payment in pounds` `the amount or value of any other relevant payments in pounds`)

-- section 222

@export Under section 222, for whom does the recipient hold on trust a payment for loss of office made in contravention of section 217, 218 or 219 (nothing if the court's direction decides it)?
GIVEN `the payment contravened section 217 (payment by the company without members' approval)` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did the payment contravene section 217 (the company paid without its members' approval)?
      `the payment contravened section 218 (in connection with a transfer of the undertaking or property)` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did the payment contravene section 218 (made in connection with a transfer of the undertaking or property without approval)?
      `the payment contravened section 219 (in connection with a takeover bid)` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did the payment contravene section 219 (made in connection with a takeover bid without approval)?
      `the court directs otherwise` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has the court directed otherwise (where sections 217 and 219 are both contravened)?
GIVETH A MAYBE STRING
DECIDE `Under section 222, for whom does the recipient hold a payment made without approval` IS
    CONSIDER (`s 222 the payment is held by the recipient on trust for` (`s 222(1) subsection (1) applies to the payment` `the payment contravened section 217 (payment by the company without members' approval)` `the payment contravened section 218 (in connection with a transfer of the undertaking or property)` `the payment contravened section 219 (in connection with a takeover bid)` `the court directs otherwise`) (`s 222(2) subsection (2) applies to the payment` `the payment contravened section 218 (in connection with a transfer of the undertaking or property)`) (`s 222(3) subsection (3) applies to the payment` `the payment contravened section 217 (payment by the company without members' approval)` `the payment contravened section 219 (in connection with a takeover bid)` `the court directs otherwise`))
    WHEN JUST `s 222(1)(a) the company making the payment` THEN JUST "the company that made the payment"
    WHEN JUST `s 222(2) the company whose undertaking or property is or is proposed to be transferred` THEN JUST "the company whose undertaking or property is or is proposed to be transferred"
    WHEN JUST `s 222(3)(a) the persons who have sold their shares as a result of the offer made` THEN JUST "the persons who sold their shares as a result of the offer made"
    OTHERWISE NOTHING

-- section 223(1)

@export Under section 223(1), is a shadow director treated as a director for the rules on service contracts (ss 188, 189), property transactions (ss 190 to 196), loans etc (ss 197 to 214) and payments for loss of office (ss 215 to 222)?
GIVEN `the directors are accustomed to act in accordance with my directions or instructions` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are the directors of the company accustomed to act in accordance with your directions or instructions?
      `the only reason is that they act on my advice given in a professional capacity` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the only reason that the directors act on advice you give in a professional capacity?
      `the only reason is that they act on my directions, guidance or advice in the exercise of a function under an enactment` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the only reason that the directors act on directions, instructions, guidance or advice you give in the exercise of a function conferred by or under an enactment?
      `the only reason is that they act on my guidance or advice as a Minister of the Crown` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the only reason that the directors act on guidance or advice you give as a Minister of the Crown?
      `I am a body corporate, the company is my subsidiary and that is the only reason` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are you a body corporate, is the company your subsidiary, and is the only reason the directors act on your directions that they are accustomed to?
      `the provision is one of sections 188 and 189` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the question under sections 188 and 189 (directors' long-term service contracts)?
      `the provision is one of sections 190 to 196` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the question under sections 190 to 196 (substantial property transactions)?
      `the provision is one of sections 197 to 214` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the question under sections 197 to 214 (loans, quasi-loans and credit transactions)?
      `the provision is one of sections 215 to 222` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the question under sections 215 to 222 (payments for loss of office)?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 223(1), am I, a shadow director, treated as a director for the approval rules` IS
    (`s 223(1) the shadow director is treated as a director for the provision` `the provision` (`s 251 the person is a shadow director` (`s 251(1) the directors act in accordance with the person's directions or instructions` `the directors are accustomed to act in accordance with my directions or instructions`) (`s 251(2) the person is not to be regarded as a shadow director by reason only of that` (BRANCH IF `the only reason is that they act on my advice given in a professional capacity` THEN `s 251(2)(a) advice given by that person in a professional capacity` IF `the only reason is that they act on my directions, guidance or advice in the exercise of a function under an enactment` THEN `s 251(2)(b) instructions, a direction, guidance or advice given by that person in the exercise of a function conferred by or under an enactment` IF `the only reason is that they act on my guidance or advice as a Minister of the Crown` THEN `s 251(2)(c) guidance or advice given by that person in that person's capacity as a Minister of the Crown (within the meaning of the Ministers of the Crown Act 1975)` OTHERWISE `s 251(2) some other reason`)) (`s 251(3) the body corporate is not to be regarded as a shadow director of the subsidiary company for the purpose` `I am a body corporate, the company is my subsidiary and that is the only reason` (JUST `I am a body corporate, the company is my subsidiary and that is the only reason`) `s 251(3)(b) Chapter 4 (transactions requiring members' approval)` `I am a body corporate, the company is my subsidiary and that is the only reason`)))
    WHERE
        `the provision` MEANS
            BRANCH
                IF `the provision is one of sections 188 and 189` THEN `s 223(1)(a) sections 188 and 189 (directors' service contracts)`
                IF `the provision is one of sections 190 to 196` THEN `s 223(1)(b) sections 190 to 196 (property transactions)`
                IF `the provision is one of sections 197 to 214` THEN `s 223(1)(c) sections 197 to 214 (loans etc)`
                IF `the provision is one of sections 215 to 222` THEN `s 223(1)(d) sections 215 to 222 (payments for loss of office)`
                OTHERWISE `s 223(1) some other provision`

-- section 224(1)

@export Under section 224(1), where approval is sought by written resolution, is an accidental failure to send the required memorandum to one or more members disregarded in deciding whether the requirement was met?
GIVEN `approval under Chapter 4 is sought by written resolution` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is approval under Chapter 4 sought by written resolution?
      `a memorandum is required to be sent or submitted to every eligible member before the resolution is passed` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is a memorandum required to be sent or submitted to every eligible member before the resolution is passed?
      `the failure to send it to one or more members was accidental` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Was the failure to send or submit it to one or more members accidental?
      `a provision of the company's articles deals with the matter` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does a provision of the company's articles deal with the matter?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 224(1), is the accidental failure to send me the memorandum disregarded` IS
    (`s 224(1) the failure is disregarded in determining whether the requirement has been met` `approval under Chapter 4 is sought by written resolution` `a memorandum is required to be sent or submitted to every eligible member before the resolution is passed` `the failure to send it to one or more members was accidental` (`s 224(2) subsection (1) has effect subject to a provision of the articles` `a provision of the company's articles deals with the matter`))

-- section 225(2)

@export Under section 225(2), where approval is required under more than one provision of Chapter 4, has approval been given as the Chapter requires (the requirements of each met, and a separate resolution for each)?
GIVEN `the number of provisions of this Chapter under which approval is required` IS A NUMBER @desc Under how many provisions of Chapter 4 is approval required?
      `the requirements of each applicable provision have been met` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Have the requirements of each applicable provision been met?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 225(2), has approval been given as Chapter 4 requires where it is needed under more than one provision` IS
    (`s 225(2) approval has been given as this Chapter requires` (`s 225(1) approval is required under more than one provision of this Chapter` `the number of provisions of this Chapter under which approval is required`) `the requirements of each applicable provision have been met`)

§ `Chapter 4A: directors of quoted companies: special provision (ss 226A to 226F)`

-- Asked by a director of a quoted company, or by a member asked to vote on a remuneration or loss of office payment.

-- section 226B(1)

@export Under section 226B(1), is a quoted company barred from making me a remuneration payment because it is neither consistent with the approved directors' remuneration policy nor approved by the members?
GIVEN `the company is a quoted company` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the company a quoted company (as Part 15 defines it)?
      `the payment is to a person who is, or is to be or has been, a director of the company` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the payment to a person who is, is to be or has been a director of the company?
      `the payment is consistent with the approved directors' remuneration policy` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the payment consistent with the approved directors' remuneration policy (the most recent policy approved by the members in general meeting)?
      `the payment is approved by resolution of the members of the company` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has the payment been approved by a resolution of the members of the company?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 226B(1), is my quoted company barred from making me a remuneration payment` IS
    (`s 226B(1) the quoted company may not make the remuneration payment` (JUST `the company is a quoted company`) `the payment is to a person who is, or is to be or has been, a director of the company` `the payment is consistent with the approved directors' remuneration policy` `the payment is approved by resolution of the members of the company`)

-- section 226C(1)

@export Under section 226C(1), is no person allowed to pay me, a present or past director of a quoted company, a payment for loss of office unless consistent with the approved directors' remuneration policy or approved by the members?
GIVEN `the company is a quoted company` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the company a quoted company (as Part 15 defines it)?
      `the payment for loss of office is to a person who is, or has been, a director of the company` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the payment for loss of office to a person who is, or has been, a director of the company?
      `the payment is consistent with the approved directors' remuneration policy` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the payment consistent with the approved directors' remuneration policy (the most recent policy approved by the members in general meeting)?
      `the payment is approved by resolution of the members of the company` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has the payment been approved by a resolution of the members of the company?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 226C(1), is no person allowed to pay me for loss of office from a quoted company unless the payment is consistent with the policy or approved` IS
    (`s 226C(1) no person may make the payment for loss of office` (JUST `the company is a quoted company`) `the payment for loss of office is to a person who is, or has been, a director of the company` `the payment is consistent with the approved directors' remuneration policy` `the payment is approved by resolution of the members of the company`)

-- section 226D(1)

@export Under section 226D(1), must a resolution approving a remuneration or loss of office payment under sections 226B and 226C not be passed because the memorandum was not available for inspection for 15 days ending with the meeting and at the meeting?
GIVEN `a memorandum of particulars of the proposed payment, including its amount, is made available for inspection by the members` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is a memorandum setting out particulars of the proposed payment, including its amount, made available for inspection by the members?
      `the first day it was available for inspection at the registered office` IS A DATE @desc On what date was it first available for inspection at the company's registered office?
      `the date of the meeting at which the resolution is to be considered` IS A DATE @desc What is the date of the meeting at which the resolution is to be considered?
      `it is available for inspection at the meeting itself` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it also available for inspection at the meeting itself?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 226D(1), must the resolution approving my quoted company payment not be passed for want of a memorandum` IS
    (`s 226D(1) the resolution approving the payment must not be passed` TRUE `a memorandum of particulars of the proposed payment, including its amount, is made available for inspection by the members` `the first day it was available for inspection at the registered office` `the date of the meeting at which the resolution is to be considered` `it is available for inspection at the meeting itself`)

-- section 226D(6)

@export Under section 226D(6), do sections 226B and 226C apply to a payment made before the earlier of the end of the company's first financial year as a quoted company and the date its first approved remuneration policy takes effect?
GIVEN `the date of the payment` IS A DATE @desc On what date was the payment made?
      `the end of the first financial year of the company to begin on or after the day it becomes a quoted company` IS A DATE @desc When does the first financial year of the company that begins on or after the day it becomes a quoted company end?
      `the first remuneration policy has been approved` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has the company's first directors' remuneration policy been approved under section 439A?
      `the date from which the first policy takes effect` IS A DATE @desc From what date does the first policy take effect (any date if it has not been approved)?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 226D(6), do the quoted company rules apply to my payment made before the first policy` IS
    (`s 226D(6) sections 226B and 226C apply to the payment` `the date of the payment` `the end of the first financial year of the company to begin on or after the day it becomes a quoted company` (IF `the first remuneration policy has been approved` THEN JUST `the date from which the first policy takes effect` ELSE NOTHING))

-- section 226E(5)

@export Under section 226E(5), may the court relieve me, wholly or in part, from liability to indemnify the company for a payment I authorised in contravention of section 226B or 226C because I acted honestly and reasonably?
GIVEN `the proceedings are for the enforcement of a liability under section 226E(2)(b)` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are the proceedings against you for the enforcement of your liability to indemnify the company under section 226E(2)(b)?
      `I show that I acted honestly and reasonably` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Can you show that you acted honestly and reasonably?
      `the court considers that I ought to be relieved of liability` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does the court consider, having regard to all the circumstances, that you ought to be relieved of liability?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 226E(5), may the court relieve me of liability for an unapproved quoted company payment` IS
    (`s 226E(5) the court may relieve the director from liability` `the proceedings are for the enforcement of a liability under section 226E(2)(b)` `I show that I acted honestly and reasonably` `the court considers that I ought to be relieved of liability`)

-- section 226F(2)

@export Under section 226F(2), does the members' approval I obtained for a payment under Chapter 4 also satisfy the approval limb of sections 226B(1)(b) and 226C(1)(b)?
GIVEN `the payment is one to which section 226B or 226C applies` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the payment one to which section 226B or 226C applies?
      `the payment also requires approval by a resolution of the members under Chapter 4` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does the payment also require approval by a resolution of the members under Chapter 4?
      `approval has been obtained for the purposes of Chapter 4` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has that approval been obtained for the purposes of Chapter 4?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 226F(2), does the approval already obtained under Chapter 4 also satisfy the quoted company rules` IS
    (`s 226F(2) the approval obtained for Chapter 4 is treated as satisfying section 226B(1)(b) or 226C(1)(b)` `the payment is one to which section 226B or 226C applies` `the payment also requires approval by a resolution of the members under Chapter 4` `approval has been obtained for the purposes of Chapter 4`)

§ `Chapter 5: directors' service contracts (ss 227 to 230) and contracts with a sole member who is also a director (s 231)`

-- Asked by a director about the terms of their own service contract, by a member wanting to see it, and by the company's officers about keeping it.

-- section 227(1)

@export Under section 227(1), is a contract a director's service contract (one where a director undertakes personally to perform services for the company or a subsidiary, or those services are made available by a third party)?
GIVEN `a director of the company undertakes personally to perform services for the company or a subsidiary` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does a director of the company undertake personally to perform services (as director or otherwise) for the company, or for a subsidiary of the company?
      `services a director undertakes personally to perform are made available by a third party to the company or a subsidiary` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are services (as director or otherwise) that a director of the company undertakes personally to perform made available by a third party to the company, or to a subsidiary of the company?
      `the arrangement is a contract` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the arrangement a contract?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 227(1), is my contract a director's service contract` IS
    (`s 227(1) the contract is a director's service contract` `the arrangement` `the arrangement is a contract`)
    WHERE
        `the arrangement` MEANS
            BRANCH
                IF `a director of the company undertakes personally to perform services for the company or a subsidiary` THEN `s 227(1)(a) a director of the company undertakes personally to perform services (as director or otherwise) for the company, or for a subsidiary of the company`
                IF `services a director undertakes personally to perform are made available by a third party to the company or a subsidiary` THEN `s 227(1)(b) services that a director of the company undertakes personally to perform are made available by a third party to the company, or to a subsidiary of the company`
                OTHERWISE `s 227(1) some other arrangement`

-- section 227(2)

@export Under section 227(2), do the provisions of this Part about directors' service contracts apply to the terms of my appointment as a director, and not only to contracts for services outside a director's ordinary duties?
GIVEN `the terms are the terms of a person's appointment as a director of the company` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are these the terms of a person's appointment as a director of the company?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 227(2), do the service contract rules apply to my appointment as a director` IS
    (`s 227(2) the provisions of this Part relating to directors' service contracts apply to the terms` `the terms are the terms of a person's appointment as a director of the company`)

-- section 228(1)

@export Under section 228(1), has the company kept available for inspection a copy of every director's service contract, or if it is not in writing a written memorandum of its terms?
GIVEN `the contract is in writing` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the contract in writing?
      `a copy of the contract is kept available for inspection` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is a copy of the contract kept available for inspection?
      `a written memorandum setting out the terms is kept available for inspection` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is a written memorandum setting out its terms kept available for inspection?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 228(1), has my company kept the copy or memorandum of my service contract available` IS
    (`s 228(1) the company has kept the copy or memorandum available for inspection` `the contract is in writing` `a copy of the contract is kept available for inspection` `a written memorandum setting out the terms is kept available for inspection`)

-- section 228(2)

@export Under section 228(2), are the copies and memoranda kept at the company's registered office, or at a place specified in regulations under section 1136?
GIVEN `the place is the company's registered office` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the place where the copies and memoranda are kept the company's registered office?
      `the place is one specified in regulations under section 1136` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the place one specified in regulations under section 1136?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 228(2), are the copies kept at a permitted place` IS
    (`s 228(2) the copies and memoranda are kept at a permitted place` `the place` (JUST `the place is one specified in regulations under section 1136`))
    WHERE
        `the place` MEANS
            BRANCH
                IF `the place is the company's registered office` THEN `s 228(2)(a) the company's registered office`
                IF `the place is one specified in regulations under section 1136` THEN `s 228(2)(b) a place specified in regulations under section 1136`
                OTHERWISE `s 228(2) some other place`

-- section 228(3)

@export Under section 228(3), must the company still retain, and keep available for inspection, the copies and memoranda on a given date, because it is within one year from the date my contract ended or expired?
GIVEN `the date of termination or expiry of the contract` IS A DATE @desc On what date did the contract terminate or expire?
      `the date in question` IS A DATE @desc What is the date you ask about?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 228(3), must the company still have my contract on a given date after it ends` IS
    (`s 228(3) the copies and memoranda must still be retained and kept available on the date` `the date of termination or expiry of the contract` `the date in question`)

-- section 228(4)

@export Under section 228(4), must the company give notice to the registrar of the place where the copies and memoranda are kept and of any change, unless they have always been kept at the registered office?
GIVEN `the copies and memoranda have at all times been kept at the company's registered office` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Have the copies and memoranda at all times been kept at the company's registered office?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 228(4), must my company tell the registrar where the contracts are kept` IS
    (`s 228(4) the company must give notice to the registrar of the place and of any change in it` `the copies and memoranda have at all times been kept at the company's registered office`)

-- section 228(5)

@export Under section 228(5), am I, an officer of the company, guilty of an offence because the company failed to keep the contracts available, at a permitted place, or for the required time, or failed for 14 days to notify the registrar?
GIVEN `default is made in complying with subsection (1), (2) or (3)` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has the company defaulted in keeping the contracts available (subsection (1)), at a permitted place (subsection (2)) or for the required time (subsection (3))?
      `the number of days default has been made in complying with subsection (4)` IS A NUMBER @desc For how many days has the company defaulted in notifying the registrar of the place and of any change (subsection (4))?
      `the officer is in default` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are you an officer of the company who is in default (section 1121)?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 228(5), have I committed an offence over my company's records of directors' service contracts` IS
    (`s 228(5) the officer commits an offence` `default is made in complying with subsection (1), (2) or (3)` `the number of days default has been made in complying with subsection (4)` (JUST `the officer is in default`))

-- section 228(6)

@export Under section 228(6), what is the most in pounds I can be fined on summary conviction for the offence under section 228 (level 3 on the standard scale)?
GIVEN `the pounds that level 3 on the standard scale stands for` IS A NUMBER @desc How many pounds does level 3 on the standard scale stand for (the Act does not say: it is in the Criminal Justice Act 1982 and later changes)?
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `Under section 228(6), what is the most I can be fined for that offence` IS
    (`s 228(6) the largest fine in pounds` `the pounds that level 3 on the standard scale stands for`)

-- section 228(6)

@export Under section 228(6), what is the most in pounds I can be fined for each day the contravention continues (one-tenth of level 3 on the standard scale)?
GIVEN `the pounds that level 3 on the standard scale stands for` IS A NUMBER @desc How many pounds does level 3 on the standard scale stand for?
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `Under section 228(6), what is the most I can be fined for each day the offence continues` IS
    (`s 228(6) the largest daily default fine in pounds` `the pounds that level 3 on the standard scale stands for`)

-- section 228(7)

@export Under section 228(7), do the provisions of section 228 apply to a variation of a director's service contract as they apply to the original contract?
GIVEN `the change is a variation of a director's service contract` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the change a variation of a director's service contract?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 228(7), do the contract-keeping rules apply when my service contract is varied` IS
    (`s 228(7) the provisions of this section apply to the variation as to the original contract` `the change is a variation of a director's service contract`)

-- section 229(1)

@export Under section 229(1), as a member of the company, may I inspect without charge the copies and memoranda the company must keep under section 228?
GIVEN `the person is a member of the company` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are you a member of the company?
      `the copy or memorandum is one required to be kept under section 228` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the copy or memorandum one the company is required to keep under section 228?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 229(1), may I inspect my company's directors' service contracts without charge` IS
    (`s 229(1) the person may inspect the copy or memorandum without charge` (JUST `the person is a member of the company`) `the copy or memorandum is one required to be kept under section 228`)

-- section 229(2)

@export Under section 229(2), as a member, am I entitled on request and on paying the prescribed fee to be provided with a copy of a director's service contract or memorandum?
GIVEN `the person is a member of the company` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are you a member of the company?
      `the member has made a request` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Have you made a request?
      `the prescribed fee has been paid` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Have you paid the prescribed fee?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 229(2), am I entitled to a copy of a director's service contract` IS
    (`s 229(2) the member is entitled to be provided with a copy` (JUST `the person is a member of the company`) `the member has made a request` `the prescribed fee has been paid`)

-- section 229(2)

@export Under section 229(2), was the copy provided within seven days after the company received my request?
GIVEN `the date the request is received by the company` IS A DATE @desc On what date did the company receive the request?
      `the date the copy is provided` IS A DATE @desc On what date was the copy provided?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 229(2), was my copy provided in time` IS
    (`s 229(2) the copy has been provided in time` `the date the request is received by the company` `the date the copy is provided`)

-- section 229(3)

@export Under section 229(3), am I, an officer in default, guilty of an offence because an inspection was refused or the company defaulted in providing a copy?
GIVEN `an inspection required under subsection (1) is refused` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Was an inspection required under subsection (1) refused?
      `default is made in complying with subsection (2)` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has the company defaulted in providing a copy under subsection (2)?
      `the officer is in default` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are you an officer of the company who is in default (section 1121)?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 229(3), have I committed an offence over a member's inspection or copy` IS
    (`s 229(3) the officer commits an offence` `an inspection required under subsection (1) is refused` `default is made in complying with subsection (2)` (JUST `the officer is in default`))

-- section 229(5)

@export Under section 229(5), where inspection was refused or the company defaulted in providing a copy, may the court by order compel an immediate inspection or direct that the copy be sent to me?
GIVEN `an inspection is refused, or default is made in complying with subsection (2)` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Was an inspection refused, or did the company default in providing a copy?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 229(5), may the court order the inspection or a copy to be sent` IS
    (`s 229(5) the court may by order compel an immediate inspection or direct that the copy be sent` `an inspection is refused, or default is made in complying with subsection (2)`)

-- section 230

@export Under section 230, is a shadow director treated as a director for the provisions of Chapter 5?
GIVEN `the directors are accustomed to act in accordance with my directions or instructions` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are the directors of the company accustomed to act in accordance with your directions or instructions?
      `the only reason is that they act on my advice given in a professional capacity` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the only reason that the directors act on advice you give in a professional capacity?
      `the only reason is that they act on my directions, guidance or advice in the exercise of a function under an enactment` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the only reason that the directors act on directions, instructions, guidance or advice you give in the exercise of a function conferred by or under an enactment?
      `the only reason is that they act on my guidance or advice as a Minister of the Crown` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the only reason that the directors act on guidance or advice you give as a Minister of the Crown?
      `I am a body corporate, the company is my subsidiary and that is the only reason` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are you a body corporate, is the company your subsidiary, and is the only reason the directors act on your directions that they are accustomed to?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 230, am I, a shadow director, treated as a director for this Chapter` IS
    (`s 230 the shadow director is treated as a director for the provisions of this Chapter` (`s 251 the person is a shadow director` (`s 251(1) the directors act in accordance with the person's directions or instructions` `the directors are accustomed to act in accordance with my directions or instructions`) (`s 251(2) the person is not to be regarded as a shadow director by reason only of that` (BRANCH IF `the only reason is that they act on my advice given in a professional capacity` THEN `s 251(2)(a) advice given by that person in a professional capacity` IF `the only reason is that they act on my directions, guidance or advice in the exercise of a function under an enactment` THEN `s 251(2)(b) instructions, a direction, guidance or advice given by that person in the exercise of a function conferred by or under an enactment` IF `the only reason is that they act on my guidance or advice as a Minister of the Crown` THEN `s 251(2)(c) guidance or advice given by that person in that person's capacity as a Minister of the Crown (within the meaning of the Ministers of the Crown Act 1975)` OTHERWISE `s 251(2) some other reason`)) (`s 251(3) the body corporate is not to be regarded as a shadow director of the subsidiary company for the purpose` `I am a body corporate, the company is my subsidiary and that is the only reason` (JUST `I am a body corporate, the company is my subsidiary and that is the only reason`) `s 251(3) some other purpose` `I am a body corporate, the company is my subsidiary and that is the only reason`)))

-- section 231(1)

@export Under section 231(1), does section 231 apply to a contract between a limited company with only one member and that sole member, who is also a director, entered into outside the ordinary course of business?
GIVEN `a limited company having only one member enters into a contract with the sole member` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it a limited company with only one member that enters into a contract with its sole member?
      `the sole member is also a director of the company` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the sole member also a director of the company?
      `the contract is entered into in the ordinary course of the company's business` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the contract entered into in the ordinary course of the company's business?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 231(1), does the sole member contract section apply to me` IS
    (`s 231(1) this section applies` `a limited company having only one member enters into a contract with the sole member` `the sole member is also a director of the company` `the contract is entered into in the ordinary course of the company's business`)

-- section 231(2)

@export Under section 231(2), unless the contract is in writing, must the company ensure its terms are set out in a written memorandum or recorded in the minutes of the first directors' meeting following the contract?
GIVEN `a limited company having only one member enters into a contract with the sole member` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it a limited company with only one member that enters into a contract with its sole member?
      `the sole member is also a director of the company` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the sole member also a director of the company?
      `the contract is entered into in the ordinary course of the company's business` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the contract entered into in the ordinary course of the company's business?
      `the contract is in writing` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the contract in writing?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 231(2), must my company set down the terms of my contract with it` IS
    (`s 231(2) the company must ensure the terms are set out or recorded` (`s 231(1) this section applies` `a limited company having only one member enters into a contract with the sole member` `the sole member is also a director of the company` `the contract is entered into in the ordinary course of the company's business`) `the contract is in writing`)

-- section 231(2)

@export Under section 231(2), has the company complied by setting the terms out in a written memorandum or recording them in the minutes of the first directors' meeting following the contract?
GIVEN `a limited company having only one member enters into a contract with the sole member` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it a limited company with only one member that enters into a contract with its sole member?
      `the sole member is also a director of the company` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the sole member also a director of the company?
      `the contract is entered into in the ordinary course of the company's business` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the contract entered into in the ordinary course of the company's business?
      `the contract is in writing` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the contract in writing?
      `the terms are set out in a written memorandum` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are the terms set out in a written memorandum?
      `the terms are recorded in the minutes of the first meeting of the directors following the making of the contract` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are the terms recorded in the minutes of the first directors' meeting following the making of the contract?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 231(2), has my company complied by setting down the terms` IS
    (`s 231(2) the company has complied` (`s 231(2) the company must ensure the terms are set out or recorded` (`s 231(1) this section applies` `a limited company having only one member enters into a contract with the sole member` `the sole member is also a director of the company` `the contract is entered into in the ordinary course of the company's business`) `the contract is in writing`) `the terms are set out in a written memorandum` `the terms are recorded in the minutes of the first meeting of the directors following the making of the contract`)

-- section 231(3)

@export Under section 231(3), am I, an officer in default, guilty of an offence because the company failed to comply with section 231?
GIVEN `a limited company having only one member enters into a contract with the sole member` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it a limited company with only one member that enters into a contract with its sole member?
      `the sole member is also a director of the company` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the sole member also a director of the company?
      `the contract is entered into in the ordinary course of the company's business` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the contract entered into in the ordinary course of the company's business?
      `the contract is in writing` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the contract in writing?
      `the terms are set out in a written memorandum` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are the terms set out in a written memorandum?
      `the terms are recorded in the minutes of the first meeting of the directors following the making of the contract` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are the terms recorded in the minutes of the first directors' meeting following the making of the contract?
      `the officer is in default` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are you an officer of the company who is in default (section 1121)?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 231(3), have I committed an offence by my company not recording its contract with me` IS
    (`s 231(3) the officer commits an offence` (`s 231(2) the company has complied` (`s 231(2) the company must ensure the terms are set out or recorded` (`s 231(1) this section applies` `a limited company having only one member enters into a contract with the sole member` `the sole member is also a director of the company` `the contract is entered into in the ordinary course of the company's business`) `the contract is in writing`) `the terms are set out in a written memorandum` `the terms are recorded in the minutes of the first meeting of the directors following the making of the contract`) (JUST `the officer is in default`))

-- section 231(4)

@export Under section 231(4), what is the most in pounds I can be fined on summary conviction (level 5 on the standard scale)?
GIVEN `the pounds that level 5 on the standard scale stands for` IS A NUMBER @desc How many pounds does level 5 on the standard scale stand for?
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `Under section 231(4), what is the most I can be fined for that offence` IS
    (`s 231(4) the largest fine in pounds` `the pounds that level 5 on the standard scale stands for`)

-- section 231(5)

@export Under section 231(5), is a shadow director treated as a director for section 231?
GIVEN `the directors are accustomed to act in accordance with my directions or instructions` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are the directors of the company accustomed to act in accordance with your directions or instructions?
      `the only reason is that they act on my advice given in a professional capacity` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the only reason that the directors act on advice you give in a professional capacity?
      `the only reason is that they act on my directions, guidance or advice in the exercise of a function under an enactment` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the only reason that the directors act on directions, instructions, guidance or advice you give in the exercise of a function conferred by or under an enactment?
      `the only reason is that they act on my guidance or advice as a Minister of the Crown` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the only reason that the directors act on guidance or advice you give as a Minister of the Crown?
      `I am a body corporate, the company is my subsidiary and that is the only reason` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are you a body corporate, is the company your subsidiary, and is the only reason the directors act on your directions that they are accustomed to?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 231(5), am I, a shadow director, treated as a director for this section` IS
    (`s 231(5) the shadow director is treated as a director` (`s 251 the person is a shadow director` (`s 251(1) the directors act in accordance with the person's directions or instructions` `the directors are accustomed to act in accordance with my directions or instructions`) (`s 251(2) the person is not to be regarded as a shadow director by reason only of that` (BRANCH IF `the only reason is that they act on my advice given in a professional capacity` THEN `s 251(2)(a) advice given by that person in a professional capacity` IF `the only reason is that they act on my directions, guidance or advice in the exercise of a function under an enactment` THEN `s 251(2)(b) instructions, a direction, guidance or advice given by that person in the exercise of a function conferred by or under an enactment` IF `the only reason is that they act on my guidance or advice as a Minister of the Crown` THEN `s 251(2)(c) guidance or advice given by that person in that person's capacity as a Minister of the Crown (within the meaning of the Ministers of the Crown Act 1975)` OTHERWISE `s 251(2) some other reason`)) (`s 251(3) the body corporate is not to be regarded as a shadow director of the subsidiary company for the purpose` `I am a body corporate, the company is my subsidiary and that is the only reason` (JUST `I am a body corporate, the company is my subsidiary and that is the only reason`) `s 251(3)(c) Chapter 6 (contract with sole member who is also a director)` `I am a body corporate, the company is my subsidiary and that is the only reason`)))

-- section 231(6)

@export Under section 231(6), does the company's failure to comply with section 231 affect the validity of the contract?
GIVEN `the company has failed to comply with this section in relation to the contract` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has the company failed to comply with section 231 in relation to the contract?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 231(6), does my company's failure to record the contract affect its validity` IS
    (`s 231(6) the failure affects the validity of the contract` `the company has failed to comply with this section in relation to the contract`)

-- section 229(4)

@export Under section 229(4), what is the most in pounds a person guilty of the section 229 offence can be fined on summary conviction (level 3 on the standard scale)?
GIVEN `the pounds that level 3 on the standard scale stands for` IS A NUMBER @desc How many pounds does level 3 on the standard scale stand for (the Act does not say: it is in the Criminal Justice Act 1982 and later changes)?
GIVETH A MAYBE NUMBER
DECIDE `Under section 229(4), what is the most I can be fined for refusing a member inspection or a copy` IS
    CONSIDER (`s 229(4) the penalty`'s `fine not exceeding`)
    WHEN NOTHING THEN NOTHING
    WHEN JUST lim THEN (`s 229(4) the most in pounds that a fine limit allows` lim `the pounds that level 3 on the standard scale stands for`)

-- section 229(4)

@export Under section 229(4), what is the most in pounds a person guilty of the section 229 offence can be fined for each day of continued contravention (one-tenth of level 3)?
GIVEN `the pounds that level 3 on the standard scale stands for` IS A NUMBER @desc How many pounds does level 3 on the standard scale stand for (the Act does not say: it is in the Criminal Justice Act 1982 and later changes)?
GIVETH A MAYBE NUMBER
DECIDE `Under section 229(4), what is the most I can be fined for each day of continued refusal` IS
    CONSIDER (`s 229(4) the penalty`'s `daily default fine for continued contravention`)
    WHEN NOTHING THEN NOTHING
    WHEN JUST lim THEN (`s 229(4) the most in pounds that a fine limit allows` lim `the pounds that level 3 on the standard scale stands for`)

§ `Chapter 7: directors' liabilities (ss 232 to 239)`

-- Asked by a director about exemption from, and indemnity against, liability; by the company's officers about records of indemnity; and by members asked to ratify a director's conduct.

-- section 232(1)

@export Under section 232(1), is a provision that purports to exempt a director from a liability for negligence, default, breach of duty or breach of trust in relation to the company void?
GIVEN `the provision purports to exempt a director of a company (to any extent) from a liability that would otherwise attach to him in connection with negligence, default, breach of duty or breach of trust in relation to the company` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does the provision purport to exempt a director (to any extent) from a liability that would otherwise attach to him in connection with negligence, default, breach of duty or breach of trust in relation to the company?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 232(1), is a clause that exempts me from liability to the company void` IS
    (`s 232(1) the provision is void` `the provision purports to exempt a director of a company (to any extent) from a liability that would otherwise attach to him in connection with negligence, default, breach of duty or breach of trust in relation to the company`)

-- section 232(2)

@export Under section 232(2), is a provision by which the company indemnifies a director against a liability for negligence, default, breach of duty or breach of trust in relation to the company void, unless it is insurance (s 233), a qualifying third party indemnity (s 234) or a qualifying pension scheme indemnity (s 235)?
GIVEN `the company directly or indirectly provides an indemnity (to any extent)` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does the company directly or indirectly provide an indemnity (to any extent)?
      `for a director of the company, or of an associated company` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it for a director of the company, or of an associated company?
      `against a liability attaching to him in connection with negligence, default, breach of duty or breach of trust in relation to the company of which he is a director` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it against a liability attaching to him in connection with negligence, default, breach of duty or breach of trust in relation to the company of which he is a director?
      `the company purchases and maintains insurance` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it so that the company purchases and maintains insurance?
      `against a liability mentioned in section 232(2)` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it so that against a liability mentioned in section 232(2)?
      `it is provision for indemnity against liability incurred by the director to a person other than the company or an associated company` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it so that it is provision for indemnity against liability incurred by the director to a person other than the company or an associated company?
      `it indemnifies a fine imposed in criminal proceedings` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it so that it indemnifies a fine imposed in criminal proceedings?
      `it indemnifies a sum payable to a regulatory authority by way of a penalty in respect of non-compliance with a requirement of a regulatory nature (however arising)` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it so that it indemnifies a sum payable to a regulatory authority by way of a penalty in respect of non-compliance with a requirement of a regulatory nature (however arising)?
      `it indemnifies a liability incurred in defending criminal proceedings in which he is convicted` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it so that it indemnifies a liability incurred in defending criminal proceedings in which he is convicted?
      `it indemnifies a liability incurred in defending civil proceedings brought by the company, or an associated company, in which judgment is given against him` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it so that it indemnifies a liability incurred in defending civil proceedings brought by the company, or an associated company, in which judgment is given against him?
      `it indemnifies a liability incurred in connection with an application for relief in which the court refuses to grant him relief` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it so that it indemnifies a liability incurred in connection with an application for relief in which the court refuses to grant him relief?
      `it is an occupational pension scheme as defined in section 150(5) of the Finance Act 2004` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it so that it is an occupational pension scheme as defined in section 150(5) of the Finance Act 2004?
      `it is established under a trust` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it so that it is established under a trust?
      `the company is a trustee of the scheme` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it so that the company is a trustee of the scheme?
      `it is provision indemnifying a director of the company against liability incurred in connection with the company's activities as trustee of the scheme` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it so that it is provision indemnifying a director of the company against liability incurred in connection with the company's activities as trustee of the scheme?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 232(2), is a clause that indemnifies me against liability to the company void` IS
    (`s 232(2) the provision is void` `the company directly or indirectly provides an indemnity (to any extent)` `for a director of the company, or of an associated company` `against a liability attaching to him in connection with negligence, default, breach of duty or breach of trust in relation to the company of which he is a director` (`s 233 the insurance is permitted` `the company purchases and maintains insurance` `for a director of the company, or of an associated company` `against a liability mentioned in section 232(2)`) (`s 234(1) the provision is permitted as qualifying third party indemnity provision` (`s 234(2) the provision is qualifying third party indemnity provision` (`s 234(2) the provision is third party indemnity provision` `it is provision for indemnity against liability incurred by the director to a person other than the company or an associated company`) (`s 234(3) the provision provides no indemnity against the excluded liabilities` `it indemnifies a fine imposed in criminal proceedings` `it indemnifies a sum payable to a regulatory authority by way of a penalty in respect of non-compliance with a requirement of a regulatory nature (however arising)` `it indemnifies a liability incurred in defending criminal proceedings in which he is convicted` `it indemnifies a liability incurred in defending civil proceedings brought by the company, or an associated company, in which judgment is given against him` `it indemnifies a liability incurred in connection with an application for relief in which the court refuses to grant him relief`))) (`s 235(1) the provision is permitted as qualifying pension scheme indemnity provision` (`s 235(2) the provision is qualifying pension scheme indemnity provision` (`s 235(2) the provision is pension scheme indemnity provision` (`s 235(6) the scheme is an occupational pension scheme` `it is an occupational pension scheme as defined in section 150(5) of the Finance Act 2004` `it is established under a trust`) `the company is a trustee of the scheme` `it is provision indemnifying a director of the company against liability incurred in connection with the company's activities as trustee of the scheme`) (`s 235(3) the provision provides no indemnity against the excluded liabilities` `it indemnifies a fine imposed in criminal proceedings` `it indemnifies a sum payable to a regulatory authority by way of a penalty in respect of non-compliance with a requirement of a regulatory nature (however arising)` `it indemnifies a liability incurred in defending criminal proceedings in which he is convicted`))))

