            BRANCH
                IF `the report is for a director of the company, when it is approved` THEN `s 236(2) when the directors' report is approved, for a director of the company`
                IF `the report is for a person who was a director of the company at a time during the financial year` THEN `s 236(3) at a time during the financial year, for a person then a director of the company`
                IF `the report is for a director of an associated company, when it is approved` THEN `s 236(4) when the directors' report is approved, provision made by the company for a director of an associated company`
                IF `the report is for a person who was a director of an associated company at a time during the financial year` THEN `s 236(5) at a time during the financial year, for a person then a director of an associated company`
                OTHERWISE `s 236(2) when the directors' report is approved, for a director of the company`
        `the kind of provision` MEANS
            BRANCH
                IF `the provision is a third party indemnity` THEN `s 236(1)(a) qualifying third party indemnity provision`
                IF `the provision is a pension scheme indemnity` THEN `s 236(1)(b) qualifying pension scheme indemnity provision`
                OTHERWISE `s 236(1) some other provision`

-- section 236

@export Under section 236, does the directors' report meet the requirement to state that a qualifying indemnity provision is or was in force?
GIVEN `the report is for a director of the company, when it is approved` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it so that the report is for a director of the company, when it is approved?
      `the report is for a person who was a director of the company at a time during the financial year` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it so that the report is for a person who was a director of the company at a time during the financial year?
      `the report is for a director of an associated company, when it is approved` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it so that the report is for a director of an associated company, when it is approved?
      `the report is for a person who was a director of an associated company at a time during the financial year` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it so that the report is for a person who was a director of an associated company at a time during the financial year?
      `the provision is a third party indemnity` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the provision a third party indemnity (s 234)?
      `the provision is a pension scheme indemnity` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the provision a pension scheme indemnity (s 235)?
      `it is provision for indemnity against liability incurred by the director to a person other than the company or an associated company` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it so that it is provision for indemnity against liability incurred by the director to a person other than the company or an associated company?
      `it indemnifies a fine imposed in criminal proceedings` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it so that it indemnifies a fine imposed in criminal proceedings?
      `it indemnifies a sum payable to a regulatory authority by way of a penalty in respect of non-compliance with a requirement of a regulatory nature (however arising)` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it so that it indemnifies a sum payable to a regulatory authority by way of a penalty in respect of non-compliance with a requirement of a regulatory nature (however arising)?
      `it indemnifies a liability incurred in defending criminal proceedings in which he is convicted` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it so that it indemnifies a liability incurred in defending criminal proceedings in which he is convicted?
      `it indemnifies a liability incurred in defending civil proceedings brought by the company, or an associated company, in which judgment is given against him` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it so that it indemnifies a liability incurred in defending civil proceedings brought by the company, or an associated company, in which judgment is given against him?
      `it indemnifies a liability incurred in connection with an application for relief in which the court refuses to grant him relief` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it so that it indemnifies a liability incurred in connection with an application for relief in which the court refuses to grant him relief?
      `it is an occupational pension scheme as defined in section 150(5) of the Finance Act 2004` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it so that it is an occupational pension scheme as defined in section 150(5) of the Finance Act 2004?
      `it is established under a trust` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it so that it is established under a trust?
      `the company is a trustee of the scheme` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it so that the company is a trustee of the scheme?
      `it is provision indemnifying a director of the company against liability incurred in connection with the company's activities as trustee of the scheme` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it so that it is provision indemnifying a director of the company against liability incurred in connection with the company's activities as trustee of the scheme?
      `the provision is in force at that time for the benefit of one or more directors of the kind` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the provision in force at that time for the benefit of one or more directors of the kind in question?
      `the provision was made by the company` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Was the provision made by the company?
      `the report states it` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does the directors' report state it?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 236, does my company's directors' report meet the requirement about indemnity` IS
    (`s 236 the directors' report meets the requirement` (`s 236(2) to (5) the directors' report must state that the provision is in force or was in force` `the time` (`s 236(1) the provision is qualifying indemnity provision` `the kind of provision` (`s 234(2) the provision is qualifying third party indemnity provision` (`s 234(2) the provision is third party indemnity provision` `it is provision for indemnity against liability incurred by the director to a person other than the company or an associated company`) (`s 234(3) the provision provides no indemnity against the excluded liabilities` `it indemnifies a fine imposed in criminal proceedings` `it indemnifies a sum payable to a regulatory authority by way of a penalty in respect of non-compliance with a requirement of a regulatory nature (however arising)` `it indemnifies a liability incurred in defending criminal proceedings in which he is convicted` `it indemnifies a liability incurred in defending civil proceedings brought by the company, or an associated company, in which judgment is given against him` `it indemnifies a liability incurred in connection with an application for relief in which the court refuses to grant him relief`)) (`s 235(2) the provision is qualifying pension scheme indemnity provision` (`s 235(2) the provision is pension scheme indemnity provision` (`s 235(6) the scheme is an occupational pension scheme` `it is an occupational pension scheme as defined in section 150(5) of the Finance Act 2004` `it is established under a trust`) `the company is a trustee of the scheme` `it is provision indemnifying a director of the company against liability incurred in connection with the company's activities as trustee of the scheme`) (`s 235(3) the provision provides no indemnity against the excluded liabilities` `it indemnifies a fine imposed in criminal proceedings` `it indemnifies a sum payable to a regulatory authority by way of a penalty in respect of non-compliance with a requirement of a regulatory nature (however arising)` `it indemnifies a liability incurred in defending criminal proceedings in which he is convicted`))) `the provision is in force at that time for the benefit of one or more directors of the kind` `the provision was made by the company`) `the report states it`)
    WHERE
        `the time` MEANS
            BRANCH
                IF `the report is for a director of the company, when it is approved` THEN `s 236(2) when the directors' report is approved, for a director of the company`
                IF `the report is for a person who was a director of the company at a time during the financial year` THEN `s 236(3) at a time during the financial year, for a person then a director of the company`
                IF `the report is for a director of an associated company, when it is approved` THEN `s 236(4) when the directors' report is approved, provision made by the company for a director of an associated company`
                IF `the report is for a person who was a director of an associated company at a time during the financial year` THEN `s 236(5) at a time during the financial year, for a person then a director of an associated company`
                OTHERWISE `s 236(2) when the directors' report is approved, for a director of the company`
        `the kind of provision` MEANS
            BRANCH
                IF `the provision is a third party indemnity` THEN `s 236(1)(a) qualifying third party indemnity provision`
                IF `the provision is a pension scheme indemnity` THEN `s 236(1)(b) qualifying pension scheme indemnity provision`
                OTHERWISE `s 236(1) some other provision`

-- section 237(1)

@export Under section 237(1), does section 237 apply to a company because a qualifying indemnity provision is made for a director of that company or of an associated company?
GIVEN `the company is the one of which the director concerned is a director` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the company the one of which the director concerned is a director (whether the provision is made by that company or by an associated company)?
      `the company is an associated company that made the provision` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the company an associated company that made the provision?
      `qualifying indemnity provision is made for a director of a company` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is a qualifying indemnity provision made for a director of a company?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 237(1), does the record-keeping rule for my indemnity apply to my company` IS
    (`s 237(1) this section applies to the company` `the company` `qualifying indemnity provision is made for a director of a company`)
    WHERE
        `the company` MEANS
            BRANCH
                IF `the company is the one of which the director concerned is a director` THEN `s 237(1)(a) the company of which he is a director (whether the provision is made by that company or an associated company)`
                IF `the company is an associated company that made the provision` THEN `s 237(1)(b) an associated company that made the provision`
                OTHERWISE `s 237(1) some other company`

-- section 237(2)

@export Under section 237(2), has the company kept available for inspection a copy of the qualifying indemnity provision, or if it is not in writing a written memorandum of its terms?
GIVEN `the provision is in writing` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it so that the provision is in writing?
      `a copy of the provision is kept available for inspection` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it so that a copy of the provision is kept available for inspection?
      `a written memorandum setting out its terms is kept available for inspection` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it so that a written memorandum setting out its terms is kept available for inspection?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 237(2), has my company kept the copy or memorandum of the indemnity available` IS
    (`s 237(2) the company has kept the copy or memorandum available for inspection` `the provision is in writing` `a copy of the provision is kept available for inspection` `a written memorandum setting out its terms is kept available for inspection`)

-- section 237(3)

@export Under section 237(3), are the copies and memoranda kept at the company's registered office or at a place specified in regulations under section 1136?
GIVEN `the place is the company's registered office` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the place where the copies and memoranda are kept the company's registered office?
      `the place is one specified in regulations under section 1136` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the place one specified in regulations under section 1136?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 237(3), are the copies of the indemnity kept at a permitted place` IS
    (`s 237(3) the copy or memorandum is kept at a permitted place` `the place` (JUST `the place is one specified in regulations under section 1136`))
    WHERE
        `the place` MEANS
            BRANCH
                IF `the place is the company's registered office` THEN `s 237(3)(a) the company's registered office`
                IF `the place is one specified in regulations under section 1136` THEN `s 237(3)(b) a place specified in regulations under section 1136`
                OTHERWISE `s 237(3) some other place`

-- section 237(4)

@export Under section 237(4), must the copy or memorandum still be retained and kept available on a given date, being within one year from the termination or expiry of the provision?
GIVEN `the date of termination or expiry of the provision` IS A DATE @desc On what date did the provision terminate or expire?
      `the date in question` IS A DATE @desc What is the date you ask about?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 237(4), must the company still keep the indemnity copy on a given date` IS
    (`s 237(4) the copy or memorandum must still be retained and kept available on the date` `the date of termination or expiry of the provision` `the date in question`)

-- section 237(5)

@export Under section 237(5), must the company notify the registrar of the place where the copies are kept, and of any change, unless they have always been at the registered office?
GIVEN `the copy or memorandum has at all times been kept at the company's registered office` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Have the copies at all times been kept at the company's registered office?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 237(5), must my company tell the registrar where the indemnity records are kept` IS
    (`s 237(5) the company must give notice to the registrar of the place and of any change in it` `the copy or memorandum has at all times been kept at the company's registered office`)

-- section 237(6)

@export Under section 237(6), am I, an officer in default, guilty of an offence because the company defaulted in keeping the records or for 14 days in notifying the registrar?
GIVEN `default is made in complying with subsection (2), (3) or (4)` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has the company defaulted in subsection (2), (3) or (4) (keeping a copy, at a permitted place, for the required time)?
      `the number of days default has been made in complying with subsection (5)` IS A NUMBER @desc For how many days has the company defaulted in notifying the registrar (subsection (5))?
      `the officer is in default` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are you an officer of the company who is in default (section 1121)?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 237(6), have I committed an offence over my company's records of indemnities` IS
    (`s 237(6) the officer commits an offence` `default is made in complying with subsection (2), (3) or (4)` `the number of days default has been made in complying with subsection (5)` (JUST `the officer is in default`))

-- section 237(7)

@export Under section 237(7), what is the most in pounds a person guilty of the section 237 offence can be fined on summary conviction (level 3 on the standard scale)?
GIVEN `the pounds that level 3 on the standard scale stands for` IS A NUMBER @desc How many pounds does level 3 on the standard scale stand for (the Act does not say: it is in the Criminal Justice Act 1982 and later changes)?
GIVETH A MAYBE NUMBER
DECIDE `Under section 237(7), what is the most I can be fined for that offence` IS
    CONSIDER (`s 237(7) the penalty`'s `fine not exceeding`)
    WHEN NOTHING THEN NOTHING
    WHEN JUST lim THEN (`s 229(4) the most in pounds that a fine limit allows` lim `the pounds that level 3 on the standard scale stands for`)

-- section 237(8)

@export Under section 237(8), do the provisions of section 237 apply to a variation of a qualifying indemnity provision as they apply to the original?
GIVEN `the change is a variation of a qualifying indemnity provision` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the change a variation of a qualifying indemnity provision?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 237(8), do the indemnity record rules apply when the indemnity is varied` IS
    (`s 237(8) the provisions of this section apply to the variation as to the original provision` `the change is a variation of a qualifying indemnity provision`)

-- section 238(1)

@export Under section 238(1), as a member of the company, may I inspect without charge the copies and memoranda the company must keep under section 237?
GIVEN `the person is a member of the company` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are you a member of the company?
      `the copy or memorandum is one required to be kept by the company under section 237` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the copy or memorandum one the company is required to keep under section 237?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 238(1), may I inspect my company's indemnity records without charge` IS
    (`s 238(1) the person may inspect the copy or memorandum without charge` (JUST `the person is a member of the company`) `the copy or memorandum is one required to be kept by the company under section 237`)

-- section 238(2)

@export Under section 238(2), as a member, am I entitled on request and on paying the prescribed fee to be provided with a copy?
GIVEN `the person is a member of the company` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are you a member of the company?
      `the member has made a request` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Have you made a request?
      `the prescribed fee has been paid` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Have you paid the prescribed fee?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 238(2), am I entitled to a copy of the indemnity provision` IS
    (`s 238(2) the member is entitled to be provided with a copy` (JUST `the person is a member of the company`) `the member has made a request` `the prescribed fee has been paid`)

-- section 238(2)

@export Under section 238(2), was the copy provided within seven days after the company received my request?
GIVEN `the date the request is received by the company` IS A DATE @desc On what date did the company receive the request?
      `the date the copy is provided` IS A DATE @desc On what date was the copy provided?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 238(2), was my copy of the indemnity provision provided in time` IS
    (`s 238(2) the copy has been provided in time` `the date the request is received by the company` `the date the copy is provided`)

-- section 238(3)

@export Under section 238(3), am I, an officer in default, guilty of an offence because an inspection was refused or a copy was not provided?
GIVEN `an inspection required under subsection (1) is refused` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Was an inspection required under subsection (1) refused?
      `default is made in complying with subsection (2)` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has the company defaulted in providing a copy under subsection (2)?
      `the officer is in default` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are you an officer of the company who is in default (section 1121)?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 238(3), have I committed an offence over a member's inspection of indemnity records` IS
    (`s 238(3) the officer commits an offence` `an inspection required under subsection (1) is refused` `default is made in complying with subsection (2)` (JUST `the officer is in default`))

-- section 238(4)

@export Under section 238(4), what is the most in pounds a person guilty of the section 238 offence can be fined on summary conviction (level 3 on the standard scale)?
GIVEN `the pounds that level 3 on the standard scale stands for` IS A NUMBER @desc How many pounds does level 3 on the standard scale stand for (the Act does not say: it is in the Criminal Justice Act 1982 and later changes)?
GIVETH A MAYBE NUMBER
DECIDE `Under section 238(4), what is the most I can be fined for refusing an inspection of indemnity records` IS
    CONSIDER (`s 238(4) the penalty`'s `fine not exceeding`)
    WHEN NOTHING THEN NOTHING
    WHEN JUST lim THEN (`s 229(4) the most in pounds that a fine limit allows` lim `the pounds that level 3 on the standard scale stands for`)

-- section 238(5)

@export Under section 238(5), where inspection was refused or a copy was not provided, may the court order an immediate inspection or direct that the copy be sent?
GIVEN `an inspection is refused, or default is made in complying with subsection (2)` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Was an inspection refused, or did the company default in providing a copy?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 238(5), may the court order the indemnity records to be shown or sent` IS
    (`s 238(5) the court may by order compel an immediate inspection or direct that the copy be sent` `an inspection is refused, or default is made in complying with subsection (2)`)

-- section 239(1)

@export Under section 239(1), does section 239 apply because the company ratifies conduct by a director that amounts to negligence, default, breach of duty or breach of trust in relation to the company?
GIVEN `the company ratifies conduct by a director amounting to negligence, default, breach of duty or breach of trust in relation to the company` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the company ratifying conduct by a director that amounts to negligence, default, breach of duty or breach of trust in relation to the company?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 239(1), does the ratification rule apply to my company's ratification of a director's conduct` IS
    (`s 239(1) this section applies to the ratification` `the company ratifies conduct by a director amounting to negligence, default, breach of duty or breach of trust in relation to the company`)

-- section 239(2)

@export Under section 239(2), has the decision to ratify been made as this subsection requires, by resolution of the members?
GIVEN `the company ratifies conduct by a director amounting to negligence, default, breach of duty or breach of trust in relation to the company` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it so that the company ratifies conduct by a director amounting to negligence, default, breach of duty or breach of trust in relation to the company?
      `the decision to ratify was made by resolution of the members of the company` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it so that the decision to ratify was made by resolution of the members of the company?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 239(2), has my company's decision to ratify been made as required` IS
    (`s 239(2) the decision to ratify has been made as this subsection requires` (`s 239(1) this section applies to the ratification` `the company ratifies conduct by a director amounting to negligence, default, breach of duty or breach of trust in relation to the company`) `the decision to ratify was made by resolution of the members of the company`)

-- section 239(3)

@export Under section 239(3), where the ratification resolution is proposed as a written resolution, am I, a member, an eligible member (not the director, nor a member connected with the director)?
GIVEN `the resolution is proposed as a written resolution` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the resolution proposed as a written resolution?
      `the member is the director (if a member of the company)` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are you the director concerned (a member of the company)?
      `the member is connected with the director` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are you a member connected with the director (section 252)?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 239(3), am I an eligible member for a written resolution to ratify a director's conduct` IS
    (`s 239(3) the member is an eligible member` `the resolution is proposed as a written resolution` `the member is the director (if a member of the company)` (JUST `the member is connected with the director`))

-- section 239(4)

@export Under section 239(4), at a meeting to ratify a director's conduct, does my vote count towards the necessary majority (not if I am the director or a member connected with the director)?
GIVEN `the resolution is proposed at a meeting` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the resolution proposed at a meeting?
      `the voter is the director (if a member of the company)` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are you the director concerned (a member of the company)?
      `the voter is a member connected with the director` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are you a member connected with the director (section 252)?
      `the vote is in favour of the resolution` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is your vote in favour of the resolution?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 239(4), does my vote count towards the majority to ratify a director's conduct` IS
    (`s 239(4) the vote counts towards the necessary majority` `the resolution is proposed at a meeting` `the voter is the director (if a member of the company)` (JUST `the voter is a member connected with the director`) `the vote is in favour of the resolution`)

-- section 239(4)

@export Under section 239(4), am I, as the director or a member connected with the director, prevented from attending, being counted towards the quorum and taking part in the proceedings at the meeting to ratify?
GIVEN `the resolution is proposed at a meeting` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the resolution proposed at a meeting?
      `the person is the director (if a member of the company)` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are you the director concerned (a member of the company)?
      `the person is a member connected with the director` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are you a member connected with the director (section 252)?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 239(4), am I prevented from attending and taking part in the meeting that ratifies a director's conduct` IS
    (`s 239(4) the director or the connected member is prevented from attending, being counted towards the quorum and taking part in the proceedings` `the resolution is proposed at a meeting` `the person is the director (if a member of the company)` (JUST `the person is a member connected with the director`))

-- section 239(5)(a)

@export Under section 239(5)(a), for the ratification rules, is the conduct an act or an omission (conduct includes both)?
GIVEN `the conduct is an act` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the conduct an act?
      `the conduct is an omission` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the conduct an omission?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 239(5)(a), is the conduct I am ratifying an act or omission` IS
    (`s 239(5)(a) the matter is conduct` `the kind of conduct`)
    WHERE
        `the kind of conduct` MEANS
            BRANCH
                IF `the conduct is an act` THEN `s 239(5)(a) an act`
                IF `the conduct is an omission` THEN `s 239(5)(a) an omission`
                OTHERWISE `s 239(5)(a) something else`

-- section 239(5)(b)

@export Under section 239(5)(b), is a former director a director for the purposes of section 239?
GIVEN `the person is a former director` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are you a former director?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 239(5)(b), am I, a former director, a director for the ratification rules` IS
    (`s 239(5)(b) the person is a director for this section` `the person is a former director`)

-- section 239(5)(c)

@export Under section 239(5)(c), is a shadow director treated as a director for the purposes of section 239?
GIVEN `the directors are accustomed to act in accordance with my directions or instructions` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are the directors of the company accustomed to act in accordance with your directions or instructions?
      `the only reason is that they act on my advice given in a professional capacity` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the only reason that the directors act on advice you give in a professional capacity?
      `the only reason is that they act on my directions, guidance or advice in the exercise of a function under an enactment` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the only reason that the directors act on directions, instructions, guidance or advice you give in the exercise of a function conferred by or under an enactment?
      `the only reason is that they act on my guidance or advice as a Minister of the Crown` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the only reason that the directors act on guidance or advice you give as a Minister of the Crown?
      `I am a body corporate, the company is my subsidiary and that is the only reason` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are you a body corporate, is the company your subsidiary, and is the only reason the directors act on your directions that they are accustomed to?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 239(5)(c), am I, a shadow director, treated as a director for the ratification rules` IS
    (`s 239(5)(c) the shadow director is treated as a director` (`s 251 the person is a shadow director` (`s 251(1) the directors act in accordance with the person's directions or instructions` `the directors are accustomed to act in accordance with my directions or instructions`) (`s 251(2) the person is not to be regarded as a shadow director by reason only of that` (BRANCH IF `the only reason is that they act on my advice given in a professional capacity` THEN `s 251(2)(a) advice given by that person in a professional capacity` IF `the only reason is that they act on my directions, guidance or advice in the exercise of a function under an enactment` THEN `s 251(2)(b) instructions, a direction, guidance or advice given by that person in the exercise of a function conferred by or under an enactment` IF `the only reason is that they act on my guidance or advice as a Minister of the Crown` THEN `s 251(2)(c) guidance or advice given by that person in that person's capacity as a Minister of the Crown (within the meaning of the Ministers of the Crown Act 1975)` OTHERWISE `s 251(2) some other reason`)) (`s 251(3) the body corporate is not to be regarded as a shadow director of the subsidiary company for the purpose` `I am a body corporate, the company is my subsidiary and that is the only reason` (JUST `I am a body corporate, the company is my subsidiary and that is the only reason`) `s 251(3) some other purpose` `I am a body corporate, the company is my subsidiary and that is the only reason`)))

-- section 239(6)

@export Under section 239(6), does section 239 affect the validity of a decision taken by unanimous consent of the members, or any power of the directors to agree not to sue, or to settle or release a claim?
GIVEN `the matter is the validity of a decision taken by unanimous consent of the members` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the matter the validity of a decision taken by the unanimous consent of the members of the company?
      `the matter is a power of the directors to agree not to sue, or to settle or release a claim made on behalf of the company` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the matter any power of the directors to agree not to sue, or to settle or release a claim made by them on behalf of the company?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 239(6), does the ratification section affect a unanimous decision or the directors' power to settle claims` IS
    (`s 239(6) this section affects it` `the matter`)
    WHERE
        `the matter` MEANS
            BRANCH
                IF `the matter is the validity of a decision taken by unanimous consent of the members` THEN `s 239(6)(a) the validity of a decision taken by unanimous consent of the members of the company`
                IF `the matter is a power of the directors to agree not to sue, or to settle or release a claim made on behalf of the company` THEN `s 239(6)(b) any power of the directors to agree not to sue, or to settle or release a claim made by them on behalf of the company`
                OTHERWISE `s 239(6) something else`

§ `Chapter 8: directors' residential addresses: protection from disclosure (ss 240 to 246)`

-- Asked by a director about their own residential address, by the company about using or disclosing it, and by anyone seeking it.

-- section 240(2)

@export Under section 240(2), is information about a director's usual residential address, or that the service address is the usual residential address, protected information?
GIVEN `it concerns a company director who is an individual` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does the information concern a company director who is an individual?
      `the information is as to his usual residential address` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it information as to the director's usual residential address?
      `the information is that his service address is his usual residential address` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it the information that the director's service address is his usual residential address?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 240(2), is information about my address protected information` IS
    (`s 240(2) the information is protected information` `the information` `it concerns a company director who is an individual`)
    WHERE
        `the information` MEANS
            BRANCH
                IF `the information is as to his usual residential address` THEN `s 240(1)(a) information as to his usual residential address`
                IF `the information is that his service address is his usual residential address` THEN `s 240(1)(b) the information that his service address is his usual residential address`
                OTHERWISE `s 240(1) other information`

-- section 240(3)

@export Under section 240(3), does information that was protected while I was a director stop being protected once I cease to be a director?
GIVEN `the information was protected information while he was a director` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Was the information protected information while you were a director?
      `the individual has ceased to be a director of the company` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Have you ceased to be a director of the company?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 240(3), does my address stop being protected when I stop being a director` IS
    (`s 240(3) the information ceases to be protected information` `the information was protected information while he was a director` `the individual has ceased to be a director of the company`)

-- section 240(3)

@export Under section 240(3), does a reference in Chapter 8 to a director include a former director?
GIVEN `the person is a former director` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are you a former director?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 240(3), am I, a former director, a director for this Chapter` IS
    (`s 240(3) a reference in this Chapter to a director includes the person` `the person is a former director`)

-- section 241(2)

@export Under section 241(2), does subsection (1) prohibit the use or disclosure of protected information with the consent of the director concerned?
GIVEN `the director concerned has consented to the use or disclosure` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has the director concerned consented to the use or disclosure?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 241(2), does section 241(1) prohibit use or disclosure of protected information where the director has consented` IS
    (`s 241(2) subsection (1) prohibits the use or disclosure` `the director concerned has consented to the use or disclosure`)

-- section 241(1)

@export Under section 241(1), is a company barred from using or disclosing protected information about one of its directors, except to communicate with the director, to comply with a requirement to send particulars to the registrar, or under a court order, or with the director's consent?
GIVEN `it is for communicating with the director concerned` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the use or disclosure for communicating with the director concerned?
      `it is to comply with a requirement of the Companies Acts as to particulars to be sent to the registrar` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it to comply with a requirement of the Companies Acts as to particulars to be sent to the registrar?
      `it is a disclosure in accordance with section 244 (court order)` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it a disclosure in accordance with section 244 (disclosure under a court order)?
      `the information is protected information about one of the company's directors` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the information protected information about one of the company's directors?
      `the director concerned has consented to the use or disclosure` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has the director concerned consented to the use or disclosure?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 241(1), is my company barred from using or disclosing my residential address` IS
    (`s 241(1) the company may not use or disclose the protected information` `the purpose` `the information is protected information about one of the company's directors` (`s 241(2) subsection (1) prohibits the use or disclosure` `the director concerned has consented to the use or disclosure`))
    WHERE
        `the purpose` MEANS
            BRANCH
                IF `it is for communicating with the director concerned` THEN `s 241(1)(a) communicating with the director concerned`
                IF `it is to comply with a requirement of the Companies Acts as to particulars to be sent to the registrar` THEN `s 241(1)(b) complying with a requirement of the Companies Acts as to particulars to be sent to the registrar`
                IF `it is a disclosure in accordance with section 244 (court order)` THEN `s 241(1)(c) disclosure in accordance with section 244 (disclosure under court order)`
                OTHERWISE `s 241(1) another purpose`

-- section 241(3)(a)

@export Under section 241(3)(a), does a company commit an offence by using or disclosing protected information in contravention of section 241?
GIVEN `it is for communicating with the director concerned` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the use or disclosure for communicating with the director concerned?
      `it is to comply with a requirement of the Companies Acts as to particulars to be sent to the registrar` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it to comply with a requirement of the Companies Acts as to particulars to be sent to the registrar?
      `it is a disclosure in accordance with section 244 (court order)` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it a disclosure in accordance with section 244 (disclosure under a court order)?
      `the information is protected information about one of the company's directors` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the information protected information about one of the company's directors?
      `the director concerned has consented to the use or disclosure` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has the director concerned consented to the use or disclosure?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 241(3)(a), has my company committed an offence by using or disclosing a director's address` IS
    (`s 241(3)(a) the company commits an offence` (`s 241(1) the company may not use or disclose the protected information` `the purpose` `the information is protected information about one of the company's directors` (`s 241(2) subsection (1) prohibits the use or disclosure` `the director concerned has consented to the use or disclosure`)))
    WHERE
        `the purpose` MEANS
            BRANCH
                IF `it is for communicating with the director concerned` THEN `s 241(1)(a) communicating with the director concerned`
                IF `it is to comply with a requirement of the Companies Acts as to particulars to be sent to the registrar` THEN `s 241(1)(b) complying with a requirement of the Companies Acts as to particulars to be sent to the registrar`
                IF `it is a disclosure in accordance with section 244 (court order)` THEN `s 241(1)(c) disclosure in accordance with section 244 (disclosure under court order)`
                OTHERWISE `s 241(1) another purpose`

-- section 241(3)(b)

@export Under section 241(3)(b), am I, an officer of the company in default, guilty of an offence because the company used or disclosed protected information in contravention of section 241?
GIVEN `it is for communicating with the director concerned` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the use or disclosure for communicating with the director concerned?
      `it is to comply with a requirement of the Companies Acts as to particulars to be sent to the registrar` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it to comply with a requirement of the Companies Acts as to particulars to be sent to the registrar?
      `it is a disclosure in accordance with section 244 (court order)` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it a disclosure in accordance with section 244 (disclosure under a court order)?
      `the information is protected information about one of the company's directors` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the information protected information about one of the company's directors?
      `the director concerned has consented to the use or disclosure` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has the director concerned consented to the use or disclosure?
      `the officer is in default` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are you an officer of the company who is in default (section 1121)?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 241(3)(b), have I committed an offence as an officer by my company's disclosure` IS
    (`s 241(3)(b) the officer commits an offence` (`s 241(1) the company may not use or disclose the protected information` `the purpose` `the information is protected information about one of the company's directors` (`s 241(2) subsection (1) prohibits the use or disclosure` `the director concerned has consented to the use or disclosure`)) (JUST `the officer is in default`))
    WHERE
        `the purpose` MEANS
            BRANCH
                IF `it is for communicating with the director concerned` THEN `s 241(1)(a) communicating with the director concerned`
                IF `it is to comply with a requirement of the Companies Acts as to particulars to be sent to the registrar` THEN `s 241(1)(b) complying with a requirement of the Companies Acts as to particulars to be sent to the registrar`
                IF `it is a disclosure in accordance with section 244 (court order)` THEN `s 241(1)(c) disclosure in accordance with section 244 (disclosure under court order)`
                OTHERWISE `s 241(1) another purpose`

-- section 242(1)

@export Under section 242(1), must the registrar omit protected information from the material on the register available for public inspection, where it is in a part of a document in which such information is required to be stated?
GIVEN `it is contained in a document delivered to the registrar in which such information is required to be stated` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the information contained in a document delivered to the registrar in which such information is required to be stated?
      `the document has more than one part` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does the document have more than one part?
      `it is contained in a part of the document in which such information is required to be stated` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it contained in a part of the document in which such information is required to be stated?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 242(1), must the registrar keep my residential address off the public register` IS
    (`s 242(1) the registrar must omit the protected information from the material available for inspection` `it is contained in a document delivered to the registrar in which such information is required to be stated` `the document has more than one part` `it is contained in a part of the document in which such information is required to be stated`)

-- section 242(2)

@export Under section 242(2), is the registrar obliged to check other documents or other parts of a document to ensure the absence of protected information, or to omit from public inspection anything registered before the Chapter came into force?
GIVEN `the registrar is asked to check other documents or parts to ensure the absence of protected information` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the registrar being asked to check other documents, or other parts of the document, to ensure the absence of protected information?
      `the registrar is asked to omit anything registered before this Chapter came into force` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the registrar being asked to omit from public inspection anything registered before this Chapter came into force?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 242(2), must the registrar check other parts or old records for my address` IS
    (`s 242(2) the registrar is obliged to do it` `the task`)
    WHERE
        `the task` MEANS
            BRANCH
                IF `the registrar is asked to check other documents or parts to ensure the absence of protected information` THEN `s 242(2)(a) to check other documents or other parts of the document to ensure the absence of protected information`
                IF `the registrar is asked to omit anything registered before this Chapter came into force` THEN `s 242(2)(b) to omit from the material available for public inspection anything registered before this Chapter comes into force`
                OTHERWISE `s 242(2) something else`

-- section 242(3)

@export Under section 242(3), must the registrar not disclose protected information except as permitted by section 243, in accordance with section 244, or as section 1110F permits?
GIVEN `the disclosure is as permitted by section 243` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the disclosure as permitted by section 243 (permitted disclosure by the registrar)?
      `the disclosure is in accordance with section 244 (court order)` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the disclosure in accordance with section 244 (disclosure under a court order)?
      `the disclosure is as permitted by section 1110F` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the disclosure as permitted by section 1110F (general powers of disclosure by the registrar)?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 242(3), is the registrar barred from making this disclosure of my protected information` IS
    (`s 242(3) the registrar must not make the disclosure` `the disclosure`)
    WHERE
        `the disclosure` MEANS
            BRANCH
                IF `the disclosure is as permitted by section 243` THEN `s 242(3)(a) as permitted by section 243 (permitted disclosure by the registrar)`
                IF `the disclosure is in accordance with section 244 (court order)` THEN `s 242(3)(b) in accordance with section 244 (disclosure under court order)`
                IF `the disclosure is as permitted by section 1110F` THEN `s 242(3)(c) as permitted by section 1110F (general powers of disclosure by the registrar)`
                OTHERWISE `s 242(3) in some other way`

-- section 243(7)

@export Under section 243(7), is a person a credit reference agency, because they carry on a business of furnishing information relevant to the financial standing of individuals, information the agency collects for that purpose?
GIVEN `the person carries on a business comprising the furnishing of information relevant to the financial standing of individuals` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does the person carry on a business comprising the furnishing of information relevant to the financial standing of individuals?
      `the information is collected by the agency for that purpose` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the information collected by the agency for that purpose?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 243(7), is the person a credit reference agency` IS
    (`s 243(7) the person is a credit reference agency` `the person carries on a business comprising the furnishing of information relevant to the financial standing of individuals` `the information is collected by the agency for that purpose`)

-- section 243(2)

@export Under section 243(2), may the registrar disclose protected information to a credit reference agency?
GIVEN `the person carries on a business comprising the furnishing of information relevant to the financial standing of individuals` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it so that the person carries on a business comprising the furnishing of information relevant to the financial standing of individuals?
      `the information is collected by the agency for that purpose` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it so that the information is collected by the agency for that purpose?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 243(2), may the registrar disclose my protected information to a credit reference agency` IS
    (`s 243(2) the registrar may disclose protected information to the person` (`s 243(7) the person is a credit reference agency` `the person carries on a business comprising the furnishing of information relevant to the financial standing of individuals` `the information is collected by the agency for that purpose`))

-- section 243(4)

@export Under section 243(4), if regulations so require, must the registrar, on my application, refrain from disclosing protected information about me to a credit reference agency?
GIVEN `regulations under subsection (4) require the registrar, on application, to refrain from disclosing protected information relating to the director to a credit reference agency` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Do regulations under subsection (4) require the registrar, on application, to refrain from disclosing protected information about you to a credit reference agency?
      `an application has been made as the regulations require` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Have you applied as the regulations require?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 243(4), must the registrar hold back my address from credit reference agencies once I apply` IS
    (`s 243(4) the registrar must refrain from disclosing the protected information to a credit reference agency` (JUST `regulations under subsection (4) require the registrar, on application, to refrain from disclosing protected information relating to the director to a credit reference agency`) `an application has been made as the regulations require`)

-- section 244(1)

@export Under section 244(1), may the court order disclosure of a director's protected information, where service at the service address is shown ineffective or disclosure is needed to enforce a court order or decree, and the court is satisfied it is appropriate?
GIVEN `there is evidence that service of documents at a service address other than the director's usual residential address is not effective to bring them to the notice of the director` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is there evidence that service of documents at a service address other than the director's usual residential address is not effective to bring them to the director's notice?
      `it is necessary or expedient for the information to be provided in connection with the enforcement of an order or decree of the court` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it necessary or expedient for the information to be provided in connection with the enforcement of an order or decree of the court?
      `the court is otherwise satisfied that it is appropriate to make the order` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the court otherwise satisfied that it is appropriate to make the order?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 244(1), may the court order disclosure of my residential address` IS
    (`s 244(1) the court may make an order for the disclosure of protected information` `there is evidence that service of documents at a service address other than the director's usual residential address is not effective to bring them to the notice of the director` `it is necessary or expedient for the information to be provided in connection with the enforcement of an order or decree of the court` `the court is otherwise satisfied that it is appropriate to make the order`)

-- section 244(2)

@export Under section 244(2), may an order for disclosure by the registrar be made only if the company does not have the director's usual residential address, or has been dissolved?
GIVEN `the company does not have the director's usual residential address` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does the company not have the director's usual residential address?
      `the company has been dissolved` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has the company been dissolved?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 244(2), may an order for disclosure be made against the registrar` IS
    (`s 244(2) an order for disclosure by the registrar may be made` `the company does not have the director's usual residential address` `the company has been dissolved`)

-- section 244(3)

@export Under section 244(3), may the order be made on my application as a liquidator, creditor or member of the company, or as another person who appears to the court to have a sufficient interest?
GIVEN `the applicant is a liquidator of the company` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the applicant a liquidator of the company?
      `the applicant is a creditor of the company` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the applicant a creditor of the company?
      `the applicant is a member of the company` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the applicant a member of the company?
      `the person appears to the court to have a sufficient interest` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does the person appear to the court to have a sufficient interest?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 244(3), may I apply for an order disclosing a director's residential address` IS
    (`s 244(3) the order may be made on the application of the person` `the applicant` `the person appears to the court to have a sufficient interest`)
    WHERE
        `the applicant` MEANS
            BRANCH
                IF `the applicant is a liquidator of the company` THEN `s 244(3) a liquidator of the company`
                IF `the applicant is a creditor of the company` THEN `s 244(3) a creditor of the company`
                IF `the applicant is a member of the company` THEN `s 244(3) a member of the company`
                OTHERWISE `s 244(3) any other person`

-- section 244(4)

@export Under section 244(4), must the order specify the persons to whom, and the purposes for which, disclosure is authorised?
GIVEN `the order specifies the persons to whom disclosure is authorised` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does the order specify the persons to whom disclosure is authorised?
      `the order specifies the purposes for which disclosure is authorised` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does the order specify the purposes for which disclosure is authorised?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 244(4), does the court's disclosure order meet the requirement` IS
    (`s 244(4) the order meets the requirement` `the order specifies the persons to whom disclosure is authorised` `the order specifies the purposes for which disclosure is authorised`)

-- section 245(1)

@export Under section 245(1), may the registrar put a director's usual residential address on the public record, where communications requiring a response go unanswered, or service at the service address is shown ineffective?
GIVEN `communications sent by the registrar to the director and requiring a response within a specified period remain unanswered` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Have communications sent by the registrar to the director and requiring a response within a specified period remained unanswered?
      `there is evidence that service of documents at a service address provided in place of the director's usual residential address is not effective to bring them to the notice of the director` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is there evidence that service of documents at a service address provided in place of the director's usual residential address is not effective to bring them to the director's notice?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 245(1), may the registrar put my residential address on the public record` IS
    (`s 245(1) the registrar may put the director's usual residential address on the public record` `communications sent by the registrar to the director and requiring a response within a specified period remain unanswered` `there is evidence that service of documents at a service address provided in place of the director's usual residential address is not effective to bring them to the notice of the director`)

-- section 245(2)

@export Under section 245(2), must the registrar give notice of the proposal to the director and to every company of which the registrar has been notified that the individual is a director?
GIVEN `the notice is to be given to the director` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the notice to be given to the director?
      `the notice is to be given to every company of which the registrar has been notified that the individual is a director` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the notice to be given to every company of which the registrar has been notified that the individual is a director?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 245(2), must the registrar tell me of a proposal to publish my address` IS
    (`s 245(2) the registrar must give notice of the proposal to the recipient` `the recipient`)
    WHERE
        `the recipient` MEANS
            BRANCH
                IF `the notice is to be given to the director` THEN `s 245(2)(a) the director`
                IF `the notice is to be given to every company of which the registrar has been notified that the individual is a director` THEN `s 245(2)(b) every company of which the registrar has been notified that the individual is a director`
                OTHERWISE `s 245(2) someone else`

-- section 245(3)

@export Under section 245(3), must the notice state the grounds for the proposal and specify a period within which representations may be made?
GIVEN `the notice states the grounds on which it is proposed to put the director's usual residential address on the public record` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does the notice state the grounds on which it is proposed to put the director's usual residential address on the public record?
      `the notice specifies a period within which representations may be made before that is done` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does the notice specify a period within which representations may be made before that is done?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 245(3), does the registrar's notice meet the requirement` IS
    (`s 245(3) the notice meets the requirement` `the notice states the grounds on which it is proposed to put the director's usual residential address on the public record` `the notice specifies a period within which representations may be made before that is done`)

-- section 245(4)

@export Under section 245(4), must the notice be sent to the director at his usual residential address, unless it appears to the registrar that service there may be ineffective?
GIVEN `it appears to the registrar that service at the usual residential address may be ineffective to bring the notice to the individual's notice` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does it appear to the registrar that service at the usual residential address may be ineffective to bring the notice to the individual's notice?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 245(4), must the registrar send the notice to my usual residential address` IS
    (`s 245(4) the notice must be sent to the director at his usual residential address` `it appears to the registrar that service at the usual residential address may be ineffective to bring the notice to the individual's notice`)

-- section 245(4)

@export Under section 245(4), may the notice be sent to a service address provided in place of the usual residential address, where it appears service at the usual residential address may be ineffective?
GIVEN `it appears to the registrar that service at the usual residential address may be ineffective to bring the notice to the individual's notice` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does it appear to the registrar that service at the usual residential address may be ineffective to bring the notice to the individual's notice?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 245(4), may the registrar send the notice to my service address instead` IS
    (`s 245(4) the notice may be sent to a service address provided in place of the usual residential address` `it appears to the registrar that service at the usual residential address may be ineffective to bring the notice to the individual's notice`)

-- section 245(5)

@export Under section 245(5), must the registrar take account of any representations received within the specified period?
GIVEN `the representations were received within the specified period` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Were the representations received within the specified period?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 245(5), must the registrar take account of my representations` IS
    (`s 245(5) the registrar must take account of the representations` `the representations were received within the specified period`)

-- section 246(1)

@export Under section 246(1), where the registrar has decided that my usual residential address is to be put on the public record, must the registrar proceed as if each relevant company had given notice of a change under section 167H?
GIVEN `the registrar has decided in accordance with section 245 that the director's usual residential address is to be put on the public record` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has the registrar decided, in accordance with section 245, that the director's usual residential address is to be put on the public record?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 246(1), must the registrar treat my companies as having given notice under section 167H` IS
    (`s 246(1) the registrar must proceed as if each relevant company had given notice under section 167H` `the registrar has decided in accordance with section 245 that the director's usual residential address is to be put on the public record`)

-- section 246(2)

@export Under section 246(2), must the registrar give notice of having done so to the director and to every relevant company?
GIVEN `the notice is to be given to the director` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the notice to be given to the director?
      `the notice is to be given to every relevant company` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the notice to be given to every relevant company?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 246(2), must the registrar tell me and my companies the address has been put on the record` IS
    (`s 246(2) the registrar must give notice of having done so to the recipient` `the recipient`)
    WHERE
        `the recipient` MEANS
            BRANCH
                IF `the notice is to be given to the director` THEN `s 246(2)(a) the director`
                IF `the notice is to be given to every relevant company` THEN `s 246(2)(b) every relevant company`
                OTHERWISE `s 246(2) someone else`

-- section 246(3)

@export Under section 246(3), must the notice state the date of the registrar's decision to put the address on the public record?
GIVEN `the notice states the date of the registrar's decision to put the director's usual residential address on the public record` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does the notice state the date of the registrar's decision to put the director's usual residential address on the public record?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 246(3), does the registrar's notice of the decision meet the requirement` IS
    (`s 246(3) the notice meets the requirement` `the notice states the date of the registrar's decision to put the director's usual residential address on the public record`)

-- section 246(6)

@export Under section 246(6), is a company a relevant company because it was given notice under section 245(2)(b)?
GIVEN `the company was given notice under section 245(2)(b)` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Was the company given notice under section 245(2)(b)?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 246(6), is my company a relevant company` IS
    (`s 246(6) the company is a relevant company` `the company was given notice under section 245(2)(b)`)

-- section 246(4)

@export Under section 246(4), is no service address other than the usual residential address allowed to be registered for a director, for five years from the registrar's decision, unless a new one is registered under regulations under section 1097B?
GIVEN `the date of the registrar's decision` IS A DATE @desc On what date did the registrar decide to put the usual residential address on the public record?
      `the date in question` IS A DATE @desc What is the date you ask about?
      `a new service address is registered for the director under regulations under section 1097B` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is a new service address registered for the director under regulations under section 1097B?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 246(4), is no service address other than my usual residential address allowed to be registered for me after my address was published` IS
    (`s 246(4) no service address may be registered for the director other than the usual residential address` `the date of the registrar's decision` `the date in question` `a new service address is registered for the director under regulations under section 1097B`)

-- section 246(5)

@export Under section 246(5)(a), does subsection (4) limit the service address that may be registered where it is registered under regulations under section 1097B?
GIVEN `the service address is registered under regulations under section 1097B` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the service address registered under regulations under section 1097B?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 246(5), does the five-year bar limit a service address registered under the regulations` IS
    (`s 246(5)(a) subsection (4) limits the service address that may be registered` `the service address is registered under regulations under section 1097B`)

§ `Chapter 9: supplementary provisions regarding directors (ss 247 to 249)`

-- Asked by a director or a member about the directors' power to provide for employees, and about the minutes of directors' meetings.

-- section 247(1)

@export Under section 247(1), do the powers of the directors include the power to make provision for the benefit of employees or former employees of the company or a subsidiary on the cessation or transfer of the business?
GIVEN `the provision is for the benefit of persons employed or formerly employed by the company, or any of its subsidiaries` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the provision for the benefit of persons employed or formerly employed by the company, or any of its subsidiaries?
      `it is made in connection with the cessation or the transfer to any person of the whole or part of the undertaking of the company or that subsidiary` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it made in connection with the cessation, or the transfer to any person, of the whole or part of the undertaking of the company or that subsidiary?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 247(1), may the directors provide for employees when the business ceases or is transferred` IS
    (`s 247(1) the powers of the directors include the power to make the provision` `the provision is for the benefit of persons employed or formerly employed by the company, or any of its subsidiaries` `it is made in connection with the cessation or the transfer to any person of the whole or part of the undertaking of the company or that subsidiary`)

-- section 247(2)

@export Under section 247(2), does the general duty in section 172 (to promote the success of the company) prevent the directors exercising that power?
GIVEN `the provision is for the benefit of persons employed or formerly employed by the company, or any of its subsidiaries` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it so that the provision is for the benefit of persons employed or formerly employed by the company, or any of its subsidiaries?
      `it is made in connection with the cessation or the transfer to any person of the whole or part of the undertaking of the company or that subsidiary` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it so that it is made in connection with the cessation or the transfer to any person of the whole or part of the undertaking of the company or that subsidiary?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 247(2), does the general duty to promote the company's success stop the directors making that provision` IS
    (`s 247(2) the general duty in section 172 prevents the exercise of the power` (`s 247(1) the powers of the directors include the power to make the provision` `the provision is for the benefit of persons employed or formerly employed by the company, or any of its subsidiaries` `it is made in connection with the cessation or the transfer to any person of the whole or part of the undertaking of the company or that subsidiary`))

-- section 247(3)

@export Under section 247(3), where the company is a charity, does a restriction on the directors' powers (or the company's capacity) flowing from its objects prevent the exercise of the power?
GIVEN `the provision is for the benefit of persons employed or formerly employed by the company, or any of its subsidiaries` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it so that the provision is for the benefit of persons employed or formerly employed by the company, or any of its subsidiaries?
      `it is made in connection with the cessation or the transfer to any person of the whole or part of the undertaking of the company or that subsidiary` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it so that it is made in connection with the cessation or the transfer to any person of the whole or part of the undertaking of the company or that subsidiary?
      `the company is a charity` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the company a charity?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 247(3), does a restriction from the company's objects stop a charity's directors` IS
    (`s 247(3) a restriction flowing from the company's objects prevents the exercise of the power` (`s 247(1) the powers of the directors include the power to make the provision` `the provision is for the benefit of persons employed or formerly employed by the company, or any of its subsidiaries` `it is made in connection with the cessation or the transfer to any person of the whole or part of the undertaking of the company or that subsidiary`) `the company is a charity`)

-- section 247(5)

@export Under section 247(5), is a resolution of the directors sufficient sanction for the exercise of the power, if the articles authorise it and the payments are not to or for directors, former directors or shadow directors?
GIVEN `the resolution of the directors is authorised by the company's articles` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the resolution of the directors authorised by the company's articles?
      `the payments are to or for the benefit of directors, former directors or shadow directors` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are the payments to or for the benefit of directors, former directors or shadow directors?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 247(5), is a resolution of the directors sufficient sanction` IS
    (`s 247(5) the resolution of the directors is sufficient sanction` `the resolution of the directors is authorised by the company's articles` `the payments are to or for the benefit of directors, former directors or shadow directors`)

-- section 247(4)

@export Under section 247(4), may the power be exercised only if sanctioned by a resolution of the company or a sufficient resolution of the directors?
GIVEN `the power is sanctioned by a resolution of the company` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the power sanctioned by a resolution of the company?
      `the resolution of the directors is authorised by the company's articles` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it so that the resolution of the directors is authorised by the company's articles?
      `the payments are to or for the benefit of directors, former directors or shadow directors` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it so that the payments are to or for the benefit of directors, former directors or shadow directors?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 247(4), may the directors exercise the power` IS
    (`s 247(4) the power may be exercised` `the power is sanctioned by a resolution of the company` (`s 247(5) the resolution of the directors is sufficient sanction` `the resolution of the directors is authorised by the company's articles` `the payments are to or for the benefit of directors, former directors or shadow directors`))

-- section 247(6)

@export Under section 247(6), have any other requirements of the company's articles as to the exercise of the power been complied with?
GIVEN `any other requirements of the company's articles as to the exercise of the power have been complied with` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Have any other requirements of the company's articles as to the exercise of the power been complied with?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 247(6), have the other requirements of my articles been complied with for that power` IS
    (`s 247(6) the other requirements of the articles have been complied with` `any other requirements of the company's articles as to the exercise of the power have been complied with`)

-- section 247(7)

@export Under section 247(7), may a payment under this section be made before the winding up begins, out of profits available for dividend?
GIVEN `the payment is made before the commencement of any winding up of the company` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the payment made before the commencement of any winding up of the company?
      `the payment is made out of profits of the company that are available for dividend` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the payment made out of profits of the company that are available for dividend?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 247(7), may the payment be made` IS
    (`s 247(7) the payment may be made` `the payment is made before the commencement of any winding up of the company` `the payment is made out of profits of the company that are available for dividend`)

-- section 248(1)

@export Under section 248(1), has the company caused minutes of all proceedings at meetings of its directors to be recorded?
GIVEN `minutes of all proceedings at meetings of the company's directors have been recorded` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Have minutes of all proceedings at meetings of the company's directors been recorded?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 248(1), has my company caused the minutes of directors' meetings to be recorded` IS
    (`s 248(1) the company has caused minutes of all proceedings at meetings of its directors to be recorded` `minutes of all proceedings at meetings of the company's directors have been recorded`)

-- section 248(2)

@export Under section 248(2), must the records of a meeting still be kept on a given date, being within ten years from the date of the meeting?
GIVEN `the date of the meeting` IS A DATE @desc On what date was the meeting held?
      `the date in question` IS A DATE @desc What is the date you ask about?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 248(2), must the company still keep the minutes on a given date` IS
    (`s 248(2) the records must still be kept on the date` `the date of the meeting` `the date in question`)

-- section 248(3)

@export Under section 248(3), am I, an officer in default, guilty of an offence because the company failed to cause minutes to be recorded or to keep them for at least ten years?
GIVEN `minutes of all proceedings at meetings of the company's directors have been recorded` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it so that minutes of all proceedings at meetings of the company's directors have been recorded?
      `the company has kept the records for at least ten years` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has the company kept the records for at least ten years?
      `the officer is in default` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are you an officer of the company who is in default (section 1121)?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 248(3), have I committed an offence over the company's minutes` IS
    (`s 248(3) the officer commits an offence` (`s 248(1) the company has caused minutes of all proceedings at meetings of its directors to be recorded` `minutes of all proceedings at meetings of the company's directors have been recorded`) `the company has kept the records for at least ten years` (JUST `the officer is in default`))

-- section 249(1)

@export Under section 249(1), are minutes recorded under section 248, purporting to be authenticated by the chairman, evidence of the proceedings at the meeting?
GIVEN `the minutes were recorded in accordance with section 248` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Were the minutes recorded in accordance with section 248?
      `the minutes purport to be authenticated by the chairman of the meeting or by the chairman of the next directors' meeting` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Do the minutes purport to be authenticated by the chairman of the meeting or by the chairman of the next directors' meeting?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 249(1), are the minutes evidence of the proceedings` IS
    (`s 249(1) the minutes are evidence of the proceedings at the meeting` `the minutes were recorded in accordance with section 248` `the minutes purport to be authenticated by the chairman of the meeting or by the chairman of the next directors' meeting`)

-- section 249(1)

@export Under section 249(1), in Scotland, are the minutes sufficient evidence of the proceedings at the meeting?
GIVEN `the minutes were recorded in accordance with section 248` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it so that the minutes were recorded in accordance with section 248?
      `the minutes purport to be authenticated by the chairman of the meeting or by the chairman of the next directors' meeting` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it so that the minutes purport to be authenticated by the chairman of the meeting or by the chairman of the next directors' meeting?
      `the proceedings are in Scotland` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are the proceedings in Scotland?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 249(1), are the minutes sufficient evidence in Scotland` IS
    (`s 249(1) the minutes are sufficient evidence of the proceedings at the meeting` (`s 249(1) the minutes are evidence of the proceedings at the meeting` `the minutes were recorded in accordance with section 248` `the minutes purport to be authenticated by the chairman of the meeting or by the chairman of the next directors' meeting`) `the proceedings are in Scotland`)

-- section 249(2)(a)

@export Under section 249(2)(a), where minutes have been made in accordance with section 248, is it deemed, until the contrary is proved, that the meeting was duly held and convened?
GIVEN `minutes have been made in accordance with section 248 of the proceedings of a meeting of directors` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Have minutes been made in accordance with section 248 of the proceedings of the directors' meeting?
      `the contrary is proved` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has the contrary been proved?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 249(2)(a), is it deemed that my directors' meeting was duly held and convened` IS
    (`s 249(2)(a) the meeting is deemed duly held and convened` `minutes have been made in accordance with section 248 of the proceedings of a meeting of directors` `the contrary is proved`)

-- section 249(2)(b)

@export Under section 249(2)(b), where minutes have been made in accordance with section 248, is it deemed, until the contrary is proved, that all proceedings at the meeting duly took place?
GIVEN `minutes have been made in accordance with section 248 of the proceedings of a meeting of directors` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Have minutes been made in accordance with section 248 of the proceedings of the directors' meeting?
      `the contrary is proved` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has the contrary been proved?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 249(2)(b), is it deemed that all proceedings at my directors' meeting duly took place` IS
    (`s 249(2)(b) all proceedings at the meeting are deemed to have duly taken place` `minutes have been made in accordance with section 248 of the proceedings of a meeting of directors` `the contrary is proved`)

-- section 249(2)(c)

@export Under section 249(2)(c), where minutes have been made in accordance with section 248, is it deemed, until the contrary is proved, that all appointments at the meeting are valid?
GIVEN `minutes have been made in accordance with section 248 of the proceedings of a meeting of directors` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Have minutes been made in accordance with section 248 of the proceedings of the directors' meeting?
      `the contrary is proved` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has the contrary been proved?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 249(2)(c), is it deemed that all appointments at my directors' meeting are valid` IS
    (`s 249(2)(c) all appointments at the meeting are deemed valid` `minutes have been made in accordance with section 248 of the proceedings of a meeting of directors` `the contrary is proved`)

§ `Chapter 10: interpretation of Part 10 (ss 250 to 259)`

-- Asked by anyone who needs to know whether a person is a director, a shadow director, connected with a director, or a member of a director's family, and by a member or officer about control of a body corporate and what the company's constitution includes.

-- section 250

@export Under section 250, is a person who occupies the position of director, by whatever name called, a director?
GIVEN `the person holds a post in the company that carries the position of director, by whatever name it is called` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Do you hold a post in the company that carries the position of director, by whatever name it is called?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 250, do I occupy the position of director` IS
    (`s 250 the person occupies the position of director` `the person holds a post in the company that carries the position of director, by whatever name it is called`)

-- section 251

@export Under section 251, am I a shadow director of the company (a person in accordance with whose directions or instructions the directors are accustomed to act), allowing for the exceptions for professional advice, enactment functions, Ministers, and a parent body corporate?
GIVEN `the directors are accustomed to act in accordance with my directions or instructions` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are the directors of the company accustomed to act in accordance with your directions or instructions?
      `the only reason is that they act on my advice given in a professional capacity` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the only reason that the directors act on advice you give in a professional capacity?
      `the only reason is that they act on my directions, guidance or advice in the exercise of a function under an enactment` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the only reason that the directors act on directions, instructions, guidance or advice you give in the exercise of a function conferred by or under an enactment?
      `the only reason is that they act on my guidance or advice as a Minister of the Crown` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the only reason that the directors act on guidance or advice you give as a Minister of the Crown?
      `I am a body corporate, the company is my subsidiary and that is the only reason` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are you a body corporate, is the company your subsidiary, and is the only reason the directors act on your directions that they are accustomed to?
      `the question is under Chapter 2 of Part 10 (general duties of directors)` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the question one under Chapter 2 (general duties of directors)?
      `the question is under Chapter 4 of Part 10 (transactions requiring members' approval)` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the question one under Chapter 4 (transactions requiring members' approval)?
      `the question is under Chapter 6 of Part 10 (contract with sole member who is also a director)` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the question one under Chapter 6 (contract with a sole member who is also a director)?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 251, am I a shadow director` IS
    (`s 251 the person is a shadow director` (`s 251(1) the directors act in accordance with the person's directions or instructions` `the directors are accustomed to act in accordance with my directions or instructions`) (`s 251(2) the person is not to be regarded as a shadow director by reason only of that` (BRANCH IF `the only reason is that they act on my advice given in a professional capacity` THEN `s 251(2)(a) advice given by that person in a professional capacity` IF `the only reason is that they act on my directions, guidance or advice in the exercise of a function under an enactment` THEN `s 251(2)(b) instructions, a direction, guidance or advice given by that person in the exercise of a function conferred by or under an enactment` IF `the only reason is that they act on my guidance or advice as a Minister of the Crown` THEN `s 251(2)(c) guidance or advice given by that person in that person's capacity as a Minister of the Crown (within the meaning of the Ministers of the Crown Act 1975)` OTHERWISE `s 251(2) some other reason`)) (`s 251(3) the body corporate is not to be regarded as a shadow director of the subsidiary company for the purpose` `I am a body corporate, the company is my subsidiary and that is the only reason` (JUST `I am a body corporate, the company is my subsidiary and that is the only reason`) `the purpose` `I am a body corporate, the company is my subsidiary and that is the only reason`))
    WHERE
        `the purpose` MEANS
            BRANCH
                IF `the question is under Chapter 2 of Part 10 (general duties of directors)` THEN `s 251(3)(a) Chapter 2 (general duties of directors)`
                IF `the question is under Chapter 4 of Part 10 (transactions requiring members' approval)` THEN `s 251(3)(b) Chapter 4 (transactions requiring members' approval)`
                IF `the question is under Chapter 6 of Part 10 (contract with sole member who is also a director)` THEN `s 251(3)(c) Chapter 6 (contract with sole member who is also a director)`
                OTHERWISE `s 251(3) some other purpose`

-- section 251(3)

@export Under section 251(3), is a body corporate not to be regarded as a shadow director of its subsidiary companies for the purposes of Chapter 2, 4 or 6, where that is only because the subsidiary's directors are accustomed to act on its directions?
GIVEN `I am a body corporate, the company is my subsidiary and that is the only reason` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are you a body corporate, is the company your subsidiary, and is the only reason the directors act on your directions that they are accustomed to?
      `the question is under Chapter 2 of Part 10 (general duties of directors)` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the question one under Chapter 2 (general duties of directors)?
      `the question is under Chapter 4 of Part 10 (transactions requiring members' approval)` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the question one under Chapter 4 (transactions requiring members' approval)?
      `the question is under Chapter 6 of Part 10 (contract with sole member who is also a director)` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the question one under Chapter 6 (contract with a sole member who is also a director)?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 251(3), is my parent company not a shadow director of its subsidiary for this purpose` IS
    (`s 251(3) the body corporate is not to be regarded as a shadow director of the subsidiary company for the purpose` `I am a body corporate, the company is my subsidiary and that is the only reason` (JUST `I am a body corporate, the company is my subsidiary and that is the only reason`) `the purpose` `I am a body corporate, the company is my subsidiary and that is the only reason`)
    WHERE
        `the purpose` MEANS
            BRANCH
                IF `the question is under Chapter 2 of Part 10 (general duties of directors)` THEN `s 251(3)(a) Chapter 2 (general duties of directors)`
                IF `the question is under Chapter 4 of Part 10 (transactions requiring members' approval)` THEN `s 251(3)(b) Chapter 4 (transactions requiring members' approval)`
                IF `the question is under Chapter 6 of Part 10 (contract with sole member who is also a director)` THEN `s 251(3)(c) Chapter 6 (contract with sole member who is also a director)`
                OTHERWISE `s 251(3) some other purpose`

-- section 253(2)

@export Under section 253(2), is a person a member of a director's family (spouse or civil partner, a partner in an enduring family relationship other than a close relative, children and step-children, a partner's children, parents)?
GIVEN `the person is the director's spouse or civil partner` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the person the director's spouse or civil partner?
      `the person lives with the director as partner in an enduring family relationship` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does the person live with the director as partner in an enduring family relationship (of the same or a different sex)?
      `the person is the director's child or step-child` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the person the director's child or step-child?
      `the person is a child or step-child of the director's partner, and not of the director` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the person a child or step-child of the director's partner (see the line above) who is not a child or step-child of the director?
      `the person is the director's parent` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the person the director's parent?
      `the other person is the director's grandparent or grandchild, sister, brother, aunt or uncle, or nephew or niece` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the other person the director's grandparent or grandchild, sister, brother, aunt or uncle, or nephew or niece?
      `the child or step-child lives with the director and has not attained the age of 18` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does the child or step-child live with the director and not yet have reached the age of 18?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 253(2), is the person a member of the director's family` IS
    (`s 253(2) the person is a member of the director's family` `the relationship` (`s 253(3) subsection (2)(b) applies to the person` `the other person is the director's grandparent or grandchild, sister, brother, aunt or uncle, or nephew or niece`) `the child or step-child lives with the director and has not attained the age of 18`)
    WHERE
        `the relationship` MEANS
            BRANCH
                IF `the person is the director's spouse or civil partner` THEN `s 253(2)(a) the director's spouse or civil partner`
                IF `the person lives with the director as partner in an enduring family relationship` THEN `s 253(2)(b) any other person (whether of a different sex or the same sex) with whom the director lives as partner in an enduring family relationship`
                IF `the person is the director's child or step-child` THEN `s 253(2)(c) the director's children or step-children`
                IF `the person is a child or step-child of the director's partner, and not of the director` THEN `s 253(2)(d) a child or step-child of a person within paragraph (b), who is not a child or step-child of the director`
                IF `the person is the director's parent` THEN `s 253(2)(e) the director's parents`
                OTHERWISE `s 253(2) some other relationship`

-- section 253(3)

@export Under section 253(3), is a person excluded from paragraph (2)(b) because they are the director's grandparent or grandchild, sister, brother, aunt or uncle, or nephew or niece?
GIVEN `the other person is the director's grandparent or grandchild, sister, brother, aunt or uncle, or nephew or niece` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the other person the director's grandparent or grandchild, sister, brother, aunt or uncle, or nephew or niece?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 253(3), is a relative excluded from being my partner for the family rules` IS
    (`s 253(3) subsection (2)(b) applies to the person` `the other person is the director's grandparent or grandchild, sister, brother, aunt or uncle, or nephew or niece`)

-- section 254(2)

@export Under section 254(2), is a director connected with a body corporate if he and persons connected with him together hold at least 20% of the nominal value of its equity share capital, or are entitled to exercise or control more than 20% of the voting power?
GIVEN `the nominal value of the shares comprised in the equity share capital of the body corporate in which he and the persons connected with him together are interested` IS A NUMBER @desc What is the nominal value, in pounds, of the shares in the equity share capital of the body corporate in which the director and persons connected with him together are interested?
      `the nominal value of the equity share capital of the body corporate` IS A NUMBER @desc What is the nominal value of the equity share capital of the body corporate, in pounds?
      `the share of the voting power at any general meeting of the body that he and the persons connected with him together are entitled to exercise or control` IS A NUMBER @desc What is the share of the voting power at any general meeting of the body that he and the persons connected with him together are entitled to exercise or control?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 254(2), am I connected with a body corporate` IS
    (`s 254(2) the director is connected with the body corporate` `the nominal value of the shares comprised in the equity share capital of the body corporate in which he and the persons connected with him together are interested` `the nominal value of the equity share capital of the body corporate` `the share of the voting power at any general meeting of the body that he and the persons connected with him together are entitled to exercise or control`)

-- section 254(3)

@export Under section 254(3), do the rules in Schedule 1 (rules for the interpretation of section 254) apply for the purposes of the section where the interest is one to which a rule in that Schedule applies?
GIVEN `the interest is one to which a rule in Schedule 1 applies` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the interest one to which a rule in Schedule 1 applies?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 254(3), do the Schedule 1 rules on interests apply to this question` IS
    (`s 254(3) the rules in Schedule 1 apply for the purposes of this section` `the interest is one to which a rule in Schedule 1 applies`)

-- section 254(5)

@export Under section 254(5), are shares held as treasury shares, and their voting rights, disregarded for section 254?
GIVEN `the shares are held as treasury shares` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are the shares held as treasury shares?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 254(5), are treasury shares disregarded when working out my connection with a body corporate` IS
    (`s 254(5) the shares and their voting rights are disregarded` `the shares are held as treasury shares`)

-- section 255(3)

@export Under section 255(3), do the rules in Schedule 1 apply for the purposes of section 255 where the interest is one to which a rule in that Schedule applies?
GIVEN `the interest is one to which a rule in Schedule 1 applies` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the interest one to which a rule in Schedule 1 applies?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 255(3), do the Schedule 1 rules on interests apply to the question of control` IS
    (`s 255(3) the rules in Schedule 1 apply for the purposes of this section` `the interest is one to which a rule in Schedule 1 applies`)

-- section 255(5)

@export Under section 255(5), are shares held as treasury shares, and their voting rights, disregarded for section 255?
GIVEN `the shares are held as treasury shares` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are the shares held as treasury shares?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 255(5), are treasury shares disregarded when working out whether I control a body corporate` IS
    (`s 255(5) the shares and their voting rights are disregarded` `the shares are held as treasury shares`)

-- section 254(6)

@export Under section 254(6)(a), is a body corporate with which the director is connected under section 254 not treated as connected with him for this section, unless also connected as trustee or partner?
GIVEN `the body corporate is one with which the director is connected under section 254` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the body corporate one with which the director is connected under section 254?
      `it is also connected with him by virtue of section 252(2)(c) or (d) (connection as trustee or partner)` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it also connected with the director as trustee or partner (section 252(2)(c) or (d))?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 254(6), is a body corporate not treated as connected with me under this section when connected another way` IS
    (`s 254(6)(a) the body corporate is not treated as connected with the director for the purposes of this section` `the body corporate is one with which the director is connected under section 254` `it is also connected with him by virtue of section 252(2)(c) or (d) (connection as trustee or partner)`)

-- section 254(6)

@export Under section 254(6)(b), is a trustee of a trust not treated as connected with the director only because the beneficiaries include a body corporate with which the director is connected?
GIVEN `the beneficiaries of the trust include (or may include) a body corporate with which the director is connected` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Do the beneficiaries of the trust include (or may they include) a body corporate with which the director is connected?
      `that fact is the only reason the trustee would be treated as connected with the director` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is that fact the only reason the trustee would be treated as connected with the director?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 254(6), is a trustee not treated as connected with me merely because the trust benefits my company` IS
    (`s 254(6)(b) the trustee is not treated as connected with the director` `the beneficiaries of the trust include (or may include) a body corporate with which the director is connected` `that fact is the only reason the trustee would be treated as connected with the director`)

-- section 255(2)

@export Under section 255(2), does a director control a body corporate if he, with connected persons and the other directors, is interested in more than half of its equity share capital or entitled to exercise or control more than half of its voting power?
GIVEN `he or a person connected with him is interested in any part of the equity share capital of the body` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are you, or a person connected with you, interested in any part of the equity share capital of the body?
      `he or a person connected with him is entitled to exercise or control the exercise of any part of the voting power at any general meeting of the body` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are you, or a person connected with you, entitled to exercise or control any part of the voting power at any general meeting of the body?
      `the share of the equity share capital in which he, the persons connected with him and the other directors of the company together are interested` IS A NUMBER @desc What fraction (0 to 1) of the equity share capital are you, persons connected with you and the other directors of the company together interested in?
      `the share of the voting power that he, the persons connected with him and the other directors of the company together are entitled to exercise or control` IS A NUMBER @desc What fraction (0 to 1) of the voting power are you, persons connected with you and the other directors of the company together entitled to exercise or control?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 255(2), do I control a body corporate` IS
    (`s 255(2) the director controls the body corporate` `he or a person connected with him is interested in any part of the equity share capital of the body` `he or a person connected with him is entitled to exercise or control the exercise of any part of the voting power at any general meeting of the body` `the share of the equity share capital in which he, the persons connected with him and the other directors of the company together are interested` `the share of the voting power that he, the persons connected with him and the other directors of the company together are entitled to exercise or control`)

-- section 254(4)

@export Under section 254(4), does voting power that a body corporate controlled by the director is entitled to exercise or control count as controlled by the director?
GIVEN `he or a person connected with him is interested in any part of the equity share capital of the body` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are you, or a person connected with you, interested in any part of the equity share capital of the body that holds the voting power?
      `he or a person connected with him is entitled to exercise or control the exercise of any part of the voting power at any general meeting of the body` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are you, or a person connected with you, entitled to exercise or control any part of the voting power at any general meeting of the body that holds the voting power?
      `the share of the equity share capital in which he, the persons connected with him and the other directors of the company together are interested` IS A NUMBER @desc What fraction (0 to 1) of that body's equity share capital are you, persons connected with you and the other directors together interested in?
      `the share of the voting power that he, the persons connected with him and the other directors of the company together are entitled to exercise or control` IS A NUMBER @desc What fraction (0 to 1) of that body's voting power are you, persons connected with you and the other directors together entitled to exercise or control?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 254(4), does voting power held by a body corporate I control count as mine for the connection test` IS
    (`s 254(4) voting power controlled by a body corporate controlled by the director counts as controlled by the director` (`s 255(2) the director controls the body corporate` `he or a person connected with him is interested in any part of the equity share capital of the body` `he or a person connected with him is entitled to exercise or control the exercise of any part of the voting power at any general meeting of the body` `the share of the equity share capital in which he, the persons connected with him and the other directors of the company together are interested` `the share of the voting power that he, the persons connected with him and the other directors of the company together are entitled to exercise or control`))

-- section 255(4)

@export Under section 255(4), does voting power that a body corporate controlled by the director is entitled to exercise or control count as controlled by the director?
GIVEN `he or a person connected with him is interested in any part of the equity share capital of the body` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are you, or a person connected with you, interested in any part of the equity share capital of the body that holds the voting power?
      `he or a person connected with him is entitled to exercise or control the exercise of any part of the voting power at any general meeting of the body` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are you, or a person connected with you, entitled to exercise or control any part of the voting power at any general meeting of the body that holds the voting power?
      `the share of the equity share capital in which he, the persons connected with him and the other directors of the company together are interested` IS A NUMBER @desc What fraction (0 to 1) of that body's equity share capital are you, persons connected with you and the other directors together interested in?
      `the share of the voting power that he, the persons connected with him and the other directors of the company together are entitled to exercise or control` IS A NUMBER @desc What fraction (0 to 1) of that body's voting power are you, persons connected with you and the other directors together entitled to exercise or control?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 255(4), does voting power held by a body corporate I control count as mine for the control test` IS
    (`s 255(4) voting power controlled by a body corporate controlled by the director counts as controlled by the director` (`s 255(2) the director controls the body corporate` `he or a person connected with him is interested in any part of the equity share capital of the body` `he or a person connected with him is entitled to exercise or control the exercise of any part of the voting power at any general meeting of the body` `the share of the equity share capital in which he, the persons connected with him and the other directors of the company together are interested` `the share of the voting power that he, the persons connected with him and the other directors of the company together are entitled to exercise or control`))

-- section 255(6)

@export Under section 255(6)(a), is a body corporate with which the director is connected under section 254 not treated as connected with him for the purposes of section 255, unless also connected as trustee or partner?
GIVEN `the body corporate is one with which the director is connected under section 254` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the body corporate one with which the director is connected under section 254?
      `it is also connected with him by virtue of section 252(2)(c) or (d) (connection as trustee or partner)` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it also connected with the director as trustee or partner (section 252(2)(c) or (d))?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
