    (`s 256(b) the companies are associated` (JUST `one company is a subsidiary of the other`) (JUST `both companies are subsidiaries of the same body corporate`))

-- section 257

@export Under section 257, do references in Part 10 to a company's constitution include a resolution or other decision come to in accordance with the constitution, and a decision of the members or a class of members treated as a decision of the company?
GIVEN `the matter is a resolution or other decision come to in accordance with the constitution` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the matter a resolution or other decision come to in accordance with the constitution?
      `the matter is a decision by the members, or a class of members, treated by an enactment or rule of law as equivalent to a decision by the company` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the matter a decision by the members, or a class of members, that is treated by any enactment or rule of law as equivalent to a decision by the company?
      `the matter is one mentioned in section 17 (the constitution)` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the matter one mentioned in section 17 (what the company's constitution includes)?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 257, is a decision part of my company's constitution for this Part` IS
    (`s 257 the matter is part of the company's constitution for the purposes of this Part` `the matter` (JUST `the matter is one mentioned in section 17 (the constitution)`))
    WHERE
        `the matter` MEANS
            BRANCH
                IF `the matter is a resolution or other decision come to in accordance with the constitution` THEN `s 257(1)(a) a resolution or other decision come to in accordance with the constitution`
                IF `the matter is a decision by the members, or a class of members, treated by an enactment or rule of law as equivalent to a decision by the company` THEN `s 257(1)(b) a decision by the members, or a class of members, that is treated by virtue of any enactment or rule of law as equivalent to a decision by the company`
                OTHERWISE `s 257(1) some other matter`

