§ `Part 11, Chapter 1: derivative claims in England and Wales or Northern Ireland (ss 260 to 264)`

-- Asked by a member of a company who is thinking of suing, or has sued, on the company's behalf, and by a director who may be sued.

-- section 260(1)

@export Under section 260(1), are my proceedings a derivative claim (proceedings in England and Wales or Northern Ireland by a member of a company in respect of a cause of action vested in the company, seeking relief on its behalf)?
GIVEN `the proceedings are in England and Wales or Northern Ireland` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are the proceedings in England and Wales or Northern Ireland?
      `the person is a member of the company` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are you a member of the company?
      `shares in the company have been transferred or transmitted to the person by operation of law` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Have shares in the company been transferred or transmitted to you by operation of law?
      `the proceedings are in respect of a cause of action vested in the company` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are the proceedings in respect of a cause of action vested in the company?
      `the proceedings seek relief on behalf of the company` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Do the proceedings seek relief on behalf of the company?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 260(1), is my claim a derivative claim` IS
    (`s 260(1) the proceedings are a derivative claim` `the proceedings are in England and Wales or Northern Ireland` (`s 260(5)(c) the person is a member for this Chapter` (JUST `the person is a member of the company`) `shares in the company have been transferred or transmitted to the person by operation of law`) `the proceedings are in respect of a cause of action vested in the company` `the proceedings seek relief on behalf of the company`)

-- section 260(2)

@export Under section 260(2), may a derivative claim be brought by this route, given that the Act allows only Chapter 1 or an order of the court in proceedings under section 994 (unfair prejudice)?
GIVEN `it is brought under this Chapter` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it so that it is brought under this Chapter?
      `it is brought in pursuance of an order of the court in proceedings under section 994 (proceedings for protection of members against unfair prejudice)` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it so that it is brought in pursuance of an order of the court in proceedings under section 994 (proceedings for protection of members against unfair prejudice)?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 260(2), may my derivative claim be brought by this route, which the Act allows only under Chapter 1 or a section 994 order` IS
    (`s 260(2) the derivative claim may be brought` `it is brought under this Chapter` `it is brought in pursuance of an order of the court in proceedings under section 994 (proceedings for protection of members against unfair prejudice)`)

-- section 260(3)

@export Under section 260(3), may a derivative claim be brought only in respect of a cause of action arising from an actual or proposed act or omission involving negligence, default, breach of duty or breach of trust by a director?
GIVEN `the cause of action arises from an actual or proposed act or omission` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it so that the cause of action arises from an actual or proposed act or omission?
      `the act or omission involves negligence, default, breach of duty or breach of trust` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it so that the act or omission involves negligence, default, breach of duty or breach of trust?
      `by a director of the company` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it so that by a director of the company?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 260(3), may I bring a derivative claim for this cause of action` IS
    (`s 260(3) a derivative claim under this Chapter may be brought in respect of the cause of action` `the cause of action arises from an actual or proposed act or omission` `the act or omission involves negligence, default, breach of duty or breach of trust` `by a director of the company`)

-- section 260(3)

@export Under section 260(3), may the cause of action be against the director, another person, or both?
GIVEN `the defendant is the director only` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the defendant the director only?
      `the defendant is another person only` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the defendant another person only?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 260(3), may I sue the director, another person, or both` IS
    (`s 260(3) the cause of action may be against the defendant` `the defendant`)
    WHERE
        `the defendant` MEANS
            BRANCH
                IF `the defendant is the director only` THEN `s 260(3) the director`
                IF `the defendant is another person only` THEN `s 260(3) another person`
                OTHERWISE `s 260(3) both the director and another person`

-- section 260(4)

@export Under section 260(4), does it matter whether the cause of action arose before or after the person seeking to bring or continue the claim became a member of the company?
GIVEN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 260(4), does it matter that the cause of action arose before I became a member` IS
    `s 260(4) it matters whether the cause of action arose before or after the person became a member of the company`

-- section 260(5)

@export Under section 260(5)(a), is a former director a director for the purposes of Chapter 1?
GIVEN `the person is a former director` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are you a former director?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 260(5), am I, a former director, a director for this Chapter` IS
    (`s 260(5)(a) the person is a director for this Chapter` `the person is a former director`)

-- section 260(5)

@export Under section 260(5)(b), is a shadow director treated as a director for the purposes of Chapter 1?
GIVEN `the directors are accustomed to act in accordance with my directions or instructions` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are the directors of the company accustomed to act in accordance with your directions or instructions?
      `the only reason is that they act on my advice given in a professional capacity` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the only reason that the directors act on advice you give in a professional capacity?
      `the only reason is that they act on my directions, guidance or advice in the exercise of a function under an enactment` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the only reason that the directors act on directions, instructions, guidance or advice you give in the exercise of a function conferred by or under an enactment?
      `the only reason is that they act on my guidance or advice as a Minister of the Crown` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the only reason that the directors act on guidance or advice you give as a Minister of the Crown?
      `I am a body corporate, the company is my subsidiary and that is the only reason` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are you a body corporate, is the company your subsidiary, and is the only reason the directors act on your directions that they are accustomed to?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 260(5), am I, a shadow director, treated as a director for this Chapter` IS
    (`s 260(5)(b) the shadow director is treated as a director` (`s 251 the person is a shadow director` (`s 251(1) the directors act in accordance with the person's directions or instructions` `the directors are accustomed to act in accordance with my directions or instructions`) (`s 251(2) the person is not to be regarded as a shadow director by reason only of that` (BRANCH IF `the only reason is that they act on my advice given in a professional capacity` THEN `s 251(2)(a) advice given by that person in a professional capacity` IF `the only reason is that they act on my directions, guidance or advice in the exercise of a function under an enactment` THEN `s 251(2)(b) instructions, a direction, guidance or advice given by that person in the exercise of a function conferred by or under an enactment` IF `the only reason is that they act on my guidance or advice as a Minister of the Crown` THEN `s 251(2)(c) guidance or advice given by that person in that person's capacity as a Minister of the Crown (within the meaning of the Ministers of the Crown Act 1975)` OTHERWISE `s 251(2) some other reason`)) (`s 251(3) the body corporate is not to be regarded as a shadow director of the subsidiary company for the purpose` `I am a body corporate, the company is my subsidiary and that is the only reason` (JUST `I am a body corporate, the company is my subsidiary and that is the only reason`) `s 251(3) some other purpose` `I am a body corporate, the company is my subsidiary and that is the only reason`)))

-- section 260(5)

@export Under section 260(5)(c), does a member include a person to whom shares have been transferred or transmitted by operation of law?
GIVEN `the person is a member of the company` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are you a member of the company?
      `shares in the company have been transferred or transmitted to the person by operation of law` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Have shares in the company been transferred or transmitted to you by operation of law?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 260(5), am I, a transferee of shares, a member for this Chapter` IS
    (`s 260(5)(c) the person is a member for this Chapter` (JUST `the person is a member of the company`) `shares in the company have been transferred or transmitted to the person by operation of law`)

-- section 261(1)

@export Under section 261(1), must a member who brings a derivative claim apply to the court for permission (in Northern Ireland, leave) to continue it?
GIVEN `a member of a company brings a derivative claim under this Chapter` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Have you, a member of a company, brought a derivative claim under Chapter 1?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 261(1), must I apply for permission to continue my derivative claim` IS
    (`s 261(1) the member must apply to the court for permission to continue the claim` `a member of a company brings a derivative claim under this Chapter`)

-- section 261(2)

@export Under section 261(2), must the court dismiss the application, and may it make any consequential order, because the application and my evidence do not disclose a prima facie case for permission (leave)?
GIVEN `it appears to the court that the application and the evidence filed by the applicant in support of it do not disclose a prima facie case for giving permission (or leave)` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does it appear to the court that the application and the evidence you filed in support of it do not disclose a prima facie case for giving permission (or leave)?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 261(2), must the court dismiss my application at once` IS
    (`s 261(2) the court must dismiss the application` `it appears to the court that the application and the evidence filed by the applicant in support of it do not disclose a prima facie case for giving permission (or leave)`)

-- section 261(3)

@export Under section 261(3), if the application is not dismissed, may the court give directions as to the evidence to be provided by the company and adjourn the proceedings to obtain it?
GIVEN `it appears to the court that the application and the evidence filed by the applicant in support of it do not disclose a prima facie case for giving permission (or leave)` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does it appear to the court that the application and the evidence you filed in support of it do not disclose a prima facie case for giving permission (or leave)?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 261(3), may the court give directions about evidence and adjourn` IS
    (`s 261(3) the court may give directions as to the evidence and may adjourn the proceedings` (`s 261(2) the court must dismiss the application` `it appears to the court that the application and the evidence filed by the applicant in support of it do not disclose a prima facie case for giving permission (or leave)`))

-- section 261(4)

@export Under section 261(4), on hearing the application, may the court give permission (leave) on such terms as it thinks fit, refuse and dismiss, or adjourn and give directions?
GIVEN `the court is hearing the application` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the court hearing the application?
      `the court give permission (or leave) to continue the claim on such terms as it thinks fit` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does the court give permission (or leave) to continue the claim on such terms as it thinks fit?
      `the court refuse permission (or leave) and dismiss the claim` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does the court refuse permission (or leave) and dismiss the claim?
      `the court adjourn the proceedings on the application and give such directions as it thinks fit` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does the court adjourn the proceedings on the application and give such directions as it thinks fit?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 261(4), what may the court do on hearing my application` IS
    (`s 261(4) the court's course on hearing the application` `the course` `the court is hearing the application`)
    WHERE
        `the course` MEANS
            BRANCH
                IF `the court give permission (or leave) to continue the claim on such terms as it thinks fit` THEN `s 261(4)(a) give permission (or leave) to continue the claim on such terms as it thinks fit`
                IF `the court refuse permission (or leave) and dismiss the claim` THEN `s 261(4)(b) refuse permission (or leave) and dismiss the claim`
                IF `the court adjourn the proceedings on the application and give such directions as it thinks fit` THEN `s 261(4)(c) adjourn the proceedings on the application and give such directions as it thinks fit`
                OTHERWISE `s 261(4) some other course`

-- section 262(1)

@export Under section 262(1), does section 262 apply because the company has brought a claim and its cause of action could be pursued as a derivative claim?
GIVEN `a company has brought a claim` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has the company brought a claim?
      `the cause of action on which the claim is based could be pursued as a derivative claim under this Chapter` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Could the cause of action on which the claim is based be pursued as a derivative claim under Chapter 1?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 262(1), does section 262 apply to the company's own claim` IS
    (`s 262(1) this section applies` `a company has brought a claim` `the cause of action on which the claim is based could be pursued as a derivative claim under this Chapter`)

-- section 262(2)

@export Under section 262(2), may I, a member, apply for permission to continue the company's claim as a derivative claim on the ground that the company abused the process, failed to prosecute it diligently, and it is appropriate for me to continue?
GIVEN `a company has brought a claim` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has the company brought a claim?
      `the cause of action on which the claim is based could be pursued as a derivative claim under this Chapter` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Could the cause of action on which the claim is based be pursued as a derivative claim under Chapter 1?
      `the manner in which the company commenced or continued the claim amounts to an abuse of the process of the court` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does the manner in which the company commenced or continued the claim amount to an abuse of the process of the court?
      `the company has failed to prosecute the claim diligently` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has the company failed to prosecute the claim diligently?
      `it is appropriate for the member to continue the claim as a derivative claim` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it appropriate for you to continue the claim as a derivative claim?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 262(2), may I, a member, apply for permission to continue the company's claim as a derivative claim` IS
    (`s 262(2) the member may apply to the court for permission to continue the claim as a derivative claim` (`s 262(1) this section applies` `a company has brought a claim` `the cause of action on which the claim is based could be pursued as a derivative claim under this Chapter`) `the manner in which the company commenced or continued the claim amounts to an abuse of the process of the court` `the company has failed to prosecute the claim diligently` `it is appropriate for the member to continue the claim as a derivative claim`)

-- section 262(3)

@export Under section 262(3), must the court dismiss the application, and may it make any consequential order, because the application and my evidence do not disclose a prima facie case for permission (leave)?
GIVEN `it appears to the court that the application and the evidence filed by the applicant in support of it do not disclose a prima facie case for giving permission (or leave)` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does it appear to the court that the application and the evidence you filed in support of it do not disclose a prima facie case for giving permission (or leave)?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 262(3), must the court dismiss my application at once` IS
    (`s 262(3) the court must dismiss the application` `it appears to the court that the application and the evidence filed by the applicant in support of it do not disclose a prima facie case for giving permission (or leave)`)

-- section 262(4)

@export Under section 262(4), if the application is not dismissed, may the court give directions as to the evidence to be provided by the company and adjourn the proceedings to obtain it?
GIVEN `it appears to the court that the application and the evidence filed by the applicant in support of it do not disclose a prima facie case for giving permission (or leave)` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does it appear to the court that the application and the evidence you filed in support of it do not disclose a prima facie case for giving permission (or leave)?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 262(4), may the court give directions about evidence and adjourn` IS
    (`s 262(4) the court may give directions as to the evidence and may adjourn the proceedings` (`s 262(3) the court must dismiss the application` `it appears to the court that the application and the evidence filed by the applicant in support of it do not disclose a prima facie case for giving permission (or leave)`))

-- section 262(5)

@export Under section 262(5), on hearing the application, may the court give permission (leave) on such terms as it thinks fit, refuse and dismiss, or adjourn and give directions?
GIVEN `the court is hearing the application` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the court hearing the application?
      `the court give permission (or leave) to continue the claim as a derivative claim on such terms as it thinks fit` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does the court give permission (or leave) to continue the claim as a derivative claim on such terms as it thinks fit?
      `the court refuse permission (or leave) and dismiss the application` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does the court refuse permission (or leave) and dismiss the application?
      `the court adjourn the proceedings on the application and give such directions as it thinks fit` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does the court adjourn the proceedings on the application and give such directions as it thinks fit?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 262(5), what may the court do on hearing my application` IS
    (`s 262(5) the court's course on hearing the application` `the course` `the court is hearing the application`)
    WHERE
        `the course` MEANS
            BRANCH
                IF `the court give permission (or leave) to continue the claim as a derivative claim on such terms as it thinks fit` THEN `s 262(5)(a) give permission (or leave) to continue the claim as a derivative claim on such terms as it thinks fit`
                IF `the court refuse permission (or leave) and dismiss the application` THEN `s 262(5)(b) refuse permission (or leave) and dismiss the application`
                IF `the court adjourn the proceedings on the application and give such directions as it thinks fit` THEN `s 262(5)(c) adjourn the proceedings on the application and give such directions as it thinks fit`
                OTHERWISE `s 262(5) some other course`

-- section 263(1)

@export Under section 263(1), do the provisions of section 263 have effect where a member applies for permission (leave) under section 261 or 262?
GIVEN `a member of a company applies for permission (in Northern Ireland, leave) under section 261 or 262` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is a member of a company applying for permission (in Northern Ireland, leave) under section 261 or 262?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 263(1), does the test for giving permission apply to my application` IS
    (`s 263(1) the provisions of this section have effect` `a member of a company applies for permission (in Northern Ireland, leave) under section 261 or 262`)

-- section 263(2)

@export Under section 263(2), must permission (leave) be refused if the court is satisfied that a person acting under section 172 would not continue the claim, or that the act or omission was authorised, or has been ratified?
GIVEN `the act or omission has already occurred` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has the act or omission already occurred (answer no if it is still to occur)?
      `the court is satisfied that a person acting in accordance with section 172 (duty to promote the success of the company) would not seek to continue the claim` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the court satisfied that a person acting in accordance with section 172 (duty to promote the success of the company) would not seek to continue the claim?
      `the court is satisfied that the act or omission has been authorised by the company (before it occurs, where it is yet to occur)` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the court satisfied that the act or omission has been authorised by the company (before it occurs, where it is yet to occur)?
      `the court is satisfied that the act or omission was authorised by the company before it occurred` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the court satisfied that the act or omission was authorised by the company before it occurred?
      `the court is satisfied that the act or omission has been ratified by the company since it occurred` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the court satisfied that the act or omission has been ratified by the company since it occurred?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 263(2), must the court refuse me permission` IS
    (`s 263(2) permission (or leave) must be refused` `when` `the court is satisfied that a person acting in accordance with section 172 (duty to promote the success of the company) would not seek to continue the claim` `the court is satisfied that the act or omission has been authorised by the company (before it occurs, where it is yet to occur)` `the court is satisfied that the act or omission was authorised by the company before it occurred` `the court is satisfied that the act or omission has been ratified by the company since it occurred`)
    WHERE
        `when` MEANS
            IF `the act or omission has already occurred` THEN `s 263(2)(c) the act or omission has already occurred` ELSE `s 263(2)(b) the act or omission is yet to occur`

-- section 263(3)

@export Under section 263(3), what matters must the court take into account in particular (the list differs for an act yet to occur and one that has occurred)?
GIVEN `the act or omission has already occurred` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has the act or omission already occurred (answer no if it is still to occur)?
GIVETH A LIST OF STRING
DECIDE `Under section 263(3), what must the court take into account when deciding whether to give me permission` IS
    (`s 263(3) the matters the court must take into account in particular` `when`)
    WHERE
        `when` MEANS
            IF `the act or omission has already occurred` THEN `s 263(2)(c) the act or omission has already occurred` ELSE `s 263(2)(b) the act or omission is yet to occur`

-- section 263(4)

@export Under section 263(4), must the court have particular regard to any evidence before it as to the views of members who have no personal interest, direct or indirect, in the matter?
GIVEN `there is evidence before the court as to the views of members of the company who have no personal interest, direct or indirect, in the matter` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is there evidence before the court as to the views of members of the company who have no personal interest, direct or indirect, in the matter?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 263(4), must the court have particular regard to other members' views` IS
    (`s 263(4) the court must have particular regard to the evidence` `there is evidence before the court as to the views of members of the company who have no personal interest, direct or indirect, in the matter`)

-- section 264(1)

@export Under section 264(1), does section 264 apply where a member (the claimant) has brought a derivative claim, continued a company's claim as a derivative claim, or continued a derivative claim under section 264?
GIVEN `a member of the company (“the claimant”) has brought a derivative claim` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it so that a member of the company (“the claimant”) has brought a derivative claim?
      `the claimant has continued as a derivative claim a claim brought by the company` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it so that the claimant has continued as a derivative claim a claim brought by the company?
      `the claimant has continued a derivative claim under this section` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it so that the claimant has continued a derivative claim under this section?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 264(1), does section 264 apply to a claim another member has brought` IS
    (`s 264(1) this section applies` `a member of the company (“the claimant”) has brought a derivative claim` `the claimant has continued as a derivative claim a claim brought by the company` `the claimant has continued a derivative claim under this section`)

-- section 264(2)

@export Under section 264(2), may I, another member, apply for permission to continue the claim on the ground that the claimant's manner of proceeding is an abuse, the claimant has failed to prosecute it diligently, and it is appropriate for me to continue?
GIVEN `a member of the company (“the claimant”) has brought a derivative claim` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it so that a member of the company (“the claimant”) has brought a derivative claim?
      `the claimant has continued as a derivative claim a claim brought by the company` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it so that the claimant has continued as a derivative claim a claim brought by the company?
      `the claimant has continued a derivative claim under this section` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it so that the claimant has continued a derivative claim under this section?
      `the manner in which the proceedings have been commenced or continued by the claimant amounts to an abuse of the process of the court` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it so that the manner in which the proceedings have been commenced or continued by the claimant amounts to an abuse of the process of the court?
      `the claimant has failed to prosecute the claim diligently` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it so that the claimant has failed to prosecute the claim diligently?
      `it is appropriate for the applicant to continue the claim as a derivative claim` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it so that it is appropriate for the applicant to continue the claim as a derivative claim?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 264(2), may I, another member, apply for permission to continue the claim the claimant is running` IS
    (`s 264(2) another member may apply to the court for permission to continue the claim` (`s 264(1) this section applies` `a member of the company (“the claimant”) has brought a derivative claim` `the claimant has continued as a derivative claim a claim brought by the company` `the claimant has continued a derivative claim under this section`) `the manner in which the proceedings have been commenced or continued by the claimant amounts to an abuse of the process of the court` `the claimant has failed to prosecute the claim diligently` `it is appropriate for the applicant to continue the claim as a derivative claim`)

-- section 264(3)

@export Under section 264(3), must the court dismiss the application, and may it make any consequential order, because the application and my evidence do not disclose a prima facie case for permission (leave)?
GIVEN `it appears to the court that the application and the evidence filed by the applicant in support of it do not disclose a prima facie case for giving permission (or leave)` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does it appear to the court that the application and the evidence you filed in support of it do not disclose a prima facie case for giving permission (or leave)?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 264(3), must the court dismiss my application at once` IS
    (`s 264(3) the court must dismiss the application` `it appears to the court that the application and the evidence filed by the applicant in support of it do not disclose a prima facie case for giving permission (or leave)`)

-- section 264(4)

@export Under section 264(4), if the application is not dismissed, may the court give directions as to the evidence to be provided by the company and adjourn the proceedings to obtain it?
GIVEN `it appears to the court that the application and the evidence filed by the applicant in support of it do not disclose a prima facie case for giving permission (or leave)` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does it appear to the court that the application and the evidence you filed in support of it do not disclose a prima facie case for giving permission (or leave)?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 264(4), may the court give directions about evidence and adjourn` IS
    (`s 264(4) the court may give directions as to the evidence and may adjourn the proceedings` (`s 264(3) the court must dismiss the application` `it appears to the court that the application and the evidence filed by the applicant in support of it do not disclose a prima facie case for giving permission (or leave)`))

-- section 264(5)

@export Under section 264(5), on hearing the application, may the court give permission (leave) on such terms as it thinks fit, refuse and dismiss, or adjourn and give directions?
GIVEN `the court is hearing the application` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the court hearing the application?
      `the court give permission (or leave) to continue the claim on such terms as it thinks fit` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does the court give permission (or leave) to continue the claim on such terms as it thinks fit?
      `the court refuse permission (or leave) and dismiss the application` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does the court refuse permission (or leave) and dismiss the application?
      `the court adjourn the proceedings on the application and give such directions as it thinks fit` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does the court adjourn the proceedings on the application and give such directions as it thinks fit?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 264(5), what may the court do on hearing my application` IS
    (`s 264(5) the court's course on hearing the application` `the course` `the court is hearing the application`)
    WHERE
        `the course` MEANS
            BRANCH
                IF `the court give permission (or leave) to continue the claim on such terms as it thinks fit` THEN `s 264(5)(a) give permission (or leave) to continue the claim on such terms as it thinks fit`
                IF `the court refuse permission (or leave) and dismiss the application` THEN `s 264(5)(b) refuse permission (or leave) and dismiss the application`
                IF `the court adjourn the proceedings on the application and give such directions as it thinks fit` THEN `s 264(5)(c) adjourn the proceedings on the application and give such directions as it thinks fit`
                OTHERWISE `s 264(5) some other course`

§ `Part 11, Chapter 2: derivative proceedings in Scotland (ss 265 to 269)`

-- Asked by a member of a company who is thinking of raising proceedings in Scotland on the company's behalf, and by a director who may be sued.

-- section 265(3)

@export Under section 265(3), is the act or omission any actual or proposed act or omission involving negligence, default, breach of duty or breach of trust by a director of the company?
GIVEN `the act or omission is actual or proposed` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the act or omission actual or proposed?
      `it involves negligence, default, breach of duty or breach of trust` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does it involve negligence, default, breach of duty or breach of trust?
      `by a director of the company` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it by a director of the company?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 265(3), is the act or omission one I can raise derivative proceedings about` IS
    (`s 265(3) the act or omission is one specified in subsection (3)` `the act or omission is actual or proposed` `it involves negligence, default, breach of duty or breach of trust` `by a director of the company`)

-- section 265(1)

@export Under section 265(1), may I, a member, raise proceedings in Scotland in respect of an act or omission specified in subsection (3), to protect the company's interests and obtain a remedy on its behalf?
GIVEN `the proceedings are raised in Scotland` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are the proceedings raised in Scotland?
      `the person is a member of the company` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are you a member of the company?
      `shares in the company have been transferred or transmitted to the person by operation of law` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Have shares in the company been transferred or transmitted to you by operation of law?
      `the act or omission is actual or proposed` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the act or omission actual or proposed?
      `it involves negligence, default, breach of duty or breach of trust` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does it involve negligence, default, breach of duty or breach of trust?
      `by a director of the company` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it by a director of the company?
      `it is in order to protect the interests of the company and obtain a remedy on its behalf` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it in order to protect the interests of the company and obtain a remedy on its behalf?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 265(1), may I raise derivative proceedings in Scotland` IS
    (`s 265(1) the member may raise the proceedings` `the proceedings are raised in Scotland` (`s 265(7)(e) the person is a member for this Chapter` (JUST `the person is a member of the company`) `shares in the company have been transferred or transmitted to the person by operation of law`) (`s 265(3) the act or omission is one specified in subsection (3)` `the act or omission is actual or proposed` `it involves negligence, default, breach of duty or breach of trust` `by a director of the company`) `it is in order to protect the interests of the company and obtain a remedy on its behalf`)

-- section 265(2)

@export Under section 265(2), may a member raise proceedings of this kind in the way chosen, given that the Act allows only subsection (1)?
GIVEN `the proceedings are proceedings in respect of an act or omission specified in subsection (3) to protect the interests of the company` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are the proceedings in respect of an act or omission specified in subsection (3), to protect the interests of the company?
      `they are raised under subsection (1)` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are they raised under subsection (1)?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 265(2), may I raise such proceedings in this way, which the Act allows only under section 265(1)` IS
    (`s 265(2) a member may raise such proceedings` `the proceedings are proceedings in respect of an act or omission specified in subsection (3) to protect the interests of the company` `they are raised under subsection (1)`)

-- section 265(4)

@export Under section 265(4), may proceedings be raised against the director, another person, or both?
GIVEN `the defendant is the director only` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the defendant the director only?
      `the defendant is another person only` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the defendant another person only?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 265(4), may I raise proceedings against the director, another person, or both` IS
    (`s 265(4) proceedings may be raised against the defendant` `the defendant`)
    WHERE
        `the defendant` MEANS
            BRANCH
                IF `the defendant is the director only` THEN `s 265(4)(a) the director referred to in subsection (3)`
                IF `the defendant is another person only` THEN `s 265(4)(b) another person`
                OTHERWISE `s 265(4) both`

-- section 265(5)

@export Under section 265(5), does it matter whether the act or omission arose before or after the person seeking to raise or continue the proceedings became a member?
GIVEN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 265(5), does it matter that the act arose before I became a member` IS
    `s 265(5) it matters whether the act or omission arose before or after the person became a member of the company`

-- section 265(6)

@export Under section 265(6), does section 265 affect a member's right to raise proceedings to protect his own interests, or the court's power to make an order under section 996(2)(c)?
GIVEN `the matter is a member's right to raise proceedings to protect his own interests` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the matter a member's right to raise proceedings in respect of an act or omission specified in subsection (3) to protect his own interests and obtain a remedy on his own behalf?
      `the matter is the court's power to make an order under section 996(2)(c)` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the matter the court's power to make an order under section 996(2)(c), or anything done under such an order?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 265(6), does section 265 affect my own right to sue or the court's power under section 996` IS
    (`s 265(6) this section affects it` `the matter`)
    WHERE
        `the matter` MEANS
            BRANCH
                IF `the matter is a member's right to raise proceedings to protect his own interests` THEN `s 265(6)(a) any right of a member to raise proceedings in respect of an act or omission specified in subsection (3) in order to protect his own interests and obtain a remedy on his own behalf`
                IF `the matter is the court's power to make an order under section 996(2)(c)` THEN `s 265(6)(b) the court's power to make an order under section 996(2)(c) or anything done under such an order`
                OTHERWISE `s 265(6) something else`

-- section 265(7)

@export Under section 265(7)(c), does a reference to a director include a former director?
GIVEN `the person is a former director` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are you a former director?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 265(7), am I, a former director, a director for this Chapter` IS
    (`s 265(7)(c) the person is a director for this Chapter` `the person is a former director`)

-- section 265(7)

@export Under section 265(7)(d), do references to a director include a shadow director?
GIVEN `the directors are accustomed to act in accordance with my directions or instructions` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are the directors of the company accustomed to act in accordance with your directions or instructions?
      `the only reason is that they act on my advice given in a professional capacity` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the only reason that the directors act on advice you give in a professional capacity?
      `the only reason is that they act on my directions, guidance or advice in the exercise of a function under an enactment` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the only reason that the directors act on directions, instructions, guidance or advice you give in the exercise of a function conferred by or under an enactment?
      `the only reason is that they act on my guidance or advice as a Minister of the Crown` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the only reason that the directors act on guidance or advice you give as a Minister of the Crown?
      `I am a body corporate, the company is my subsidiary and that is the only reason` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are you a body corporate, is the company your subsidiary, and is the only reason the directors act on your directions that they are accustomed to?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 265(7), am I, a shadow director, included among the references to a director` IS
    (`s 265(7)(d) the shadow director is included among the references to a director` (`s 251 the person is a shadow director` (`s 251(1) the directors act in accordance with the person's directions or instructions` `the directors are accustomed to act in accordance with my directions or instructions`) (`s 251(2) the person is not to be regarded as a shadow director by reason only of that` (BRANCH IF `the only reason is that they act on my advice given in a professional capacity` THEN `s 251(2)(a) advice given by that person in a professional capacity` IF `the only reason is that they act on my directions, guidance or advice in the exercise of a function under an enactment` THEN `s 251(2)(b) instructions, a direction, guidance or advice given by that person in the exercise of a function conferred by or under an enactment` IF `the only reason is that they act on my guidance or advice as a Minister of the Crown` THEN `s 251(2)(c) guidance or advice given by that person in that person's capacity as a Minister of the Crown (within the meaning of the Ministers of the Crown Act 1975)` OTHERWISE `s 251(2) some other reason`)) (`s 251(3) the body corporate is not to be regarded as a shadow director of the subsidiary company for the purpose` `I am a body corporate, the company is my subsidiary and that is the only reason` (JUST `I am a body corporate, the company is my subsidiary and that is the only reason`) `s 251(3) some other purpose` `I am a body corporate, the company is my subsidiary and that is the only reason`)))

-- section 265(7)

@export Under section 265(7)(e), does a reference to a member include a person to whom shares have been transferred or transmitted by operation of law?
GIVEN `the person is a member of the company` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are you a member of the company?
      `shares in the company have been transferred or transmitted to the person by operation of law` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Have shares in the company been transferred or transmitted to you by operation of law?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 265(7), am I, a transferee, a member for this Chapter` IS
    (`s 265(7)(e) the person is a member for this Chapter` (JUST `the person is a member of the company`) `shares in the company have been transferred or transmitted to the person by operation of law`)

-- section 266(1)

@export Under section 266(1), may derivative proceedings be raised by the member, given that the Act allows it only with the leave of the court?
GIVEN `the court has granted leave` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has the court granted leave?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 266(1), may I raise derivative proceedings, which the Act allows only with the court's leave` IS
    (`s 266(1) derivative proceedings may be raised by the member` `the court has granted leave`)

-- section 266(2)

@export Under section 266(2), must my application for leave specify the cause of action and summarise the facts on which the derivative proceedings are to be based?
GIVEN `the application specifies the cause of action` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does the application specify the cause of action?
      `the application summarises the facts on which the derivative proceedings are to be based` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does the application summarise the facts on which the derivative proceedings are to be based?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 266(2), does my application for leave say what it must` IS
    (`s 266(2) the application meets the requirement` `the application specifies the cause of action` `the application summarises the facts on which the derivative proceedings are to be based`)

-- section 266(3)

@export Under section 266(3), must the court refuse the application, and may it make any consequential order, because the application and my evidence do not disclose a prima facie case?
GIVEN `it appears to the court that the application and the evidence produced by the applicant in support of it do not disclose a prima facie case for granting it` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does it appear to the court that the application and the evidence you produced in support of it do not disclose a prima facie case for granting it?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 266(3), must the court refuse my application at once` IS
    (`s 266(3) the court must refuse the application` `it appears to the court that the application and the evidence produced by the applicant in support of it do not disclose a prima facie case for granting it`)

-- section 266(4)(a)

@export Under section 266(4)(a), must the applicant serve the application on the company, if the application is not refused?
GIVEN `it appears to the court that the application and the evidence produced by the applicant in support of it do not disclose a prima facie case for granting it` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does it appear to the court that the application and the evidence you produced in support of it do not disclose a prima facie case for granting it?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 266(4)(a), must I serve my application on the company` IS
    (`s 266(4)(a) the applicant must serve the application on the company` (`s 266(3) the court must refuse the application` `it appears to the court that the application and the evidence produced by the applicant in support of it do not disclose a prima facie case for granting it`))

-- section 266(4)(b)

@export Under section 266(4)(b), may the court order the company to produce evidence and adjourn the proceedings, if the application is not refused?
GIVEN `it appears to the court that the application and the evidence produced by the applicant in support of it do not disclose a prima facie case for granting it` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does it appear to the court that the application and the evidence you produced in support of it do not disclose a prima facie case for granting it?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 266(4)(b), may the court order the company to produce evidence and adjourn` IS
    (`s 266(4)(b) the court may make an order requiring evidence to be produced by the company and may adjourn the proceedings` (`s 266(3) the court must refuse the application` `it appears to the court that the application and the evidence produced by the applicant in support of it do not disclose a prima facie case for granting it`))

-- section 266(4)(c)

@export Under section 266(4)(c), is the company entitled to take part in the further proceedings on the application, if it is not refused?
GIVEN `it appears to the court that the application and the evidence produced by the applicant in support of it do not disclose a prima facie case for granting it` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does it appear to the court that the application and the evidence you produced in support of it do not disclose a prima facie case for granting it?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 266(4)(c), may the company take part in the further proceedings` IS
    (`s 266(4)(c) the company is entitled to take part in the further proceedings on the application` (`s 266(3) the court must refuse the application` `it appears to the court that the application and the evidence produced by the applicant in support of it do not disclose a prima facie case for granting it`))

-- section 266(5)

@export Under section 266(5), on hearing the application, may the court grant it on such terms as it thinks fit, refuse it, or adjourn and make an order as to further procedure?
GIVEN `the court is hearing the application` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the court hearing the application?
      `the court grant the application on such terms as it thinks fit` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does the court grant the application on such terms as it thinks fit?
      `the court refuse the application` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does the court refuse the application?
      `the court adjourn the proceedings on the application and make such order as to further procedure as it thinks fit` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does the court adjourn the proceedings on the application and make such order as to further procedure as it thinks fit?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 266(5), what may the court do on hearing my application` IS
    (`s 266(5) the court's course on hearing the application` `the course` `the court is hearing the application`)
    WHERE
        `the course` MEANS
            BRANCH
                IF `the court grant the application on such terms as it thinks fit` THEN `s 266(5)(a) grant the application on such terms as it thinks fit`
                IF `the court refuse the application` THEN `s 266(5)(b) refuse the application`
                IF `the court adjourn the proceedings on the application and make such order as to further procedure as it thinks fit` THEN `s 266(5)(c) adjourn the proceedings on the application and make such order as to further procedure as it thinks fit`
                OTHERWISE `s 266(5) some other course`

-- section 267(1)

@export Under section 267(1), does section 267 apply because the company has raised proceedings in respect of an act or omission that could be the basis for derivative proceedings?
GIVEN `a company has raised proceedings` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has the company raised proceedings?
      `the proceedings are in respect of an act or omission which could be the basis for derivative proceedings` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are the proceedings in respect of an act or omission which could be the basis for derivative proceedings?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
