-- section 267(2)

@export Under section 267(2), may I, a member, apply to be substituted for the company on the ground that the company abused the process, failed to prosecute diligently, and it is appropriate for me to be substituted?
GIVEN `a company has raised proceedings` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has the company raised proceedings?
      `the proceedings are in respect of an act or omission which could be the basis for derivative proceedings` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are the proceedings in respect of an act or omission which could be the basis for derivative proceedings?
      `the manner in which the company commenced or continued the proceedings amounts to an abuse of the process of the court` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it so that the manner in which the company commenced or continued the proceedings amounts to an abuse of the process of the court?
      `the company has failed to prosecute the proceedings diligently` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it so that the company has failed to prosecute the proceedings diligently?
      `it is appropriate for the member to be substituted for the company in the proceedings` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it so that it is appropriate for the member to be substituted for the company in the proceedings?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 267(2), may I, a member, apply to be substituted for the company in its proceedings` IS
    (`s 267(2) the member may apply to the court to be substituted for the company` (`s 267(1) this section applies` `a company has raised proceedings` `the proceedings are in respect of an act or omission which could be the basis for derivative proceedings`) `the manner in which the company commenced or continued the proceedings amounts to an abuse of the process of the court` `the company has failed to prosecute the proceedings diligently` `it is appropriate for the member to be substituted for the company in the proceedings`)

