-- section 267(5)

@export Under section 267(5), on hearing the application, may the court grant it on such terms as it thinks fit, refuse it, or adjourn and make an order as to further procedure?
GIVEN `the court is hearing the application` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the court hearing the application?
      `the court grant the application on such terms as it thinks fit` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does the court grant the application on such terms as it thinks fit?
      `the court refuse the application` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does the court refuse the application?
      `the court adjourn the proceedings on the application and make such order as to further procedure as it thinks fit` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does the court adjourn the proceedings on the application and make such order as to further procedure as it thinks fit?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 267(5), what may the court do on hearing my application` IS
    (`s 267(5) the court's course on hearing the application` `the course` `the court is hearing the application`)
    WHERE
        `the course` MEANS
            BRANCH
                IF `the court grant the application on such terms as it thinks fit` THEN `s 267(5)(a) grant the application on such terms as it thinks fit`
                IF `the court refuse the application` THEN `s 267(5)(b) refuse the application`
                IF `the court adjourn the proceedings on the application and make such order as to further procedure as it thinks fit` THEN `s 267(5)(c) adjourn the proceedings on the application and make such order as to further procedure as it thinks fit`
                OTHERWISE `s 267(5) some other course`

-- section 268(1)

@export Under section 268(1), must the court refuse leave to raise derivative proceedings (or an application under section 267) if satisfied that a person acting under section 172 would not continue them, or that the act or omission was authorised, or has been ratified?
GIVEN `the act or omission has already occurred` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has the act or omission already occurred (answer no if it is still to occur)?
      `the court is satisfied that a person acting in accordance with section 172 (duty to promote the success of the company) would not seek to raise or continue the proceedings` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the court satisfied that a person acting in accordance with section 172 (duty to promote the success of the company) would not seek to raise or continue the proceedings?
      `the court is satisfied that the act or omission has been authorised by the company (before it occurs, where it is yet to occur)` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the court satisfied that the act or omission has been authorised by the company (before it occurs, where it is yet to occur)?
      `the court is satisfied that the act or omission was authorised by the company before it occurred` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the court satisfied that the act or omission was authorised by the company before it occurred?
      `the court is satisfied that the act or omission has been ratified by the company since it occurred` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the court satisfied that the act or omission has been ratified by the company since it occurred?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 268(1), must the court refuse me leave` IS
    (`s 268(1) leave to raise derivative proceedings or an application under section 267 must be refused` `when` `the court is satisfied that a person acting in accordance with section 172 (duty to promote the success of the company) would not seek to raise or continue the proceedings` `the court is satisfied that the act or omission has been authorised by the company (before it occurs, where it is yet to occur)` `the court is satisfied that the act or omission was authorised by the company before it occurred` `the court is satisfied that the act or omission has been ratified by the company since it occurred`)
    WHERE
        `when` MEANS
            IF `the act or omission has already occurred` THEN `s 268(1)(c) the act or omission has already occurred` ELSE `s 268(1)(b) the act or omission is yet to occur`

-- section 268(2)

@export Under section 268(2), what matters must the court take into account in particular (the list differs for an act yet to occur and one that has occurred)?
GIVEN `the act or omission has already occurred` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has the act or omission already occurred (answer no if it is still to occur)?
GIVETH A LIST OF STRING
DECIDE `Under section 268(2), what must the court take into account when deciding whether to give me leave` IS
    (`s 268(2) the matters the court must take into account in particular` `when`)
    WHERE
        `when` MEANS
            IF `the act or omission has already occurred` THEN `s 268(1)(c) the act or omission has already occurred` ELSE `s 268(1)(b) the act or omission is yet to occur`

-- section 268(3)

@export Under section 268(3), must the court have particular regard to any evidence before it as to the views of members who have no personal interest, direct or indirect, in the matter?
GIVEN `there is evidence before the court as to the views of members of the company who have no personal interest, direct or indirect, in the matter` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is there evidence before the court as to the views of members of the company who have no personal interest, direct or indirect, in the matter?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 268(3), must the court have particular regard to other members' views` IS
    (`s 268(3) the court must have particular regard to the evidence` `there is evidence before the court as to the views of members of the company who have no personal interest, direct or indirect, in the matter`)

