      `the court grant the application on such terms as it thinks fit` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does the court grant the application on such terms as it thinks fit?
      `the court refuse the application` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does the court refuse the application?
      `the court adjourn the proceedings on the application and make such order as to further procedure as it thinks fit` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does the court adjourn the proceedings on the application and make such order as to further procedure as it thinks fit?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 269(5), what may the court do on hearing my application` IS
    (`s 269(5) the court's course on hearing the application` `the course` `the court is hearing the application`)
    WHERE
        `the course` MEANS
            BRANCH
                IF `the court grant the application on such terms as it thinks fit` THEN `s 269(5)(a) grant the application on such terms as it thinks fit`
                IF `the court refuse the application` THEN `s 269(5)(b) refuse the application`
                IF `the court adjourn the proceedings on the application and make such order as to further procedure as it thinks fit` THEN `s 269(5)(c) adjourn the proceedings on the application and make such order as to further procedure as it thinks fit`
                OTHERWISE `s 269(5) some other course`

-- ====================================================================================================
-- seat questions from part coa6 (merged by the lead on 2026-11-12; unchanged text follows)
-- ====================================================================================================
-- coa6-seat.l4: the seat layer of the part agent coa6 over the Companies Act 2006 (United Kingdom), Part 12 (Company secretaries),
-- ss 270 to 280. Layer 2: it calls the rules of the layer-1 modules imported above and restates none of them.
--
-- SEAT: an individual who is, or is about to become, a director, a company secretary or a member (shareholder) of a company
-- registered under the Act, or who deals with one, asking on facts they can state what the Act requires or lets them do, what rights
-- they have against the company or its directors, what they must disclose, file, approve or vote on and by when, and what follows
-- (liability, offences, penalties) if it is not done. (Assumed, not ruled: the Act is addressed to companies, so the individual is
-- whoever stands in a company's management or ownership.) Part 12 is addressed to the company and its directors, so most questions
-- are asked "from inside" the company by a director or secretary (the questions say "my company"); an official (the Secretary of
-- State, the registrar, a court) appears only as the party the text names, never as a seat.
--
-- PLAIN INPUTS. Every question takes plain inputs (yes/no, a number, a date, a choice) one for each fact the person can state, each
-- with an @desc worded as that person would be asked. The records and the keel's answers the layer-1 rules expect are built inside
-- each question, in its WHERE, from those answers. Where a rule takes the answer of another section (a seam: s 4, s 12, s 9, s 250,
-- s 251, s 1088, s 1121, s 1141, s 1173(1)) the person is asked the underlying fact, and the keel's own function (coa-definitions) is
-- called where the keel has one (s 4(1), s 4(2), s 3(1), s 1158, s 1173(1) "officer"); otherwise the fact is passed as JUST TRUE or
-- JUST FALSE, with a comment saying which section's answer it stands for. A record field that no rule reads is given a fixed
-- placeholder with a comment.
--
-- THE FOUR COMPANY-TYPE FACTS. Whether a company is public or private is s 4(2) and s 4(1): four facts (the certificate, how the
-- members' liability is limited, a share capital, and compliance with the registration requirements on or after the relevant date).
-- Questions that turn on it ask all four; the service asks only those that still matter.
--
-- HOW TO READ AN ANSWER. Every answer is a MAYBE BOOLEAN, MAYBE NUMBER, a date or a list:
--   true / false   the Act says yes / says no, in its own words;
--   null (NOTHING) the Act does not decide the case on these facts. null is NOT false: never read it as "no".
-- A question about a permission or power answers null (not false) where an "if" condition of the grant is not met (s 272(1), the "if"
-- of s 274(b)) or the case falls outside the grant's own description; where the section's own "where" or "in the case of" gate is not met
-- (ss 270(3)(a)(i) and (b), 274(a) and (b)) it answers false (name-test sweep of 2026-11-12: assumed, not ruled; NOTES.md F-grants).

§ `Companies Act 2006 -- Part 12 -- the questions of a director, secretary or member`

§§ `Private companies (s 270)`

-- s 270(1): "A private company is not required to have a secretary." The answer is false for a private company, null for a company
-- that is not one (the section speaks of a private company only).
@export Under section 270(1), is my company required to have a secretary, if it is a private company?
GIVEN `my company's certificate of incorporation states that it is a public company` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does your company's certificate of incorporation state that it is a public company?
      `how the liability of my company's members is limited` IS A `Liability of members` @desc How is the liability of your company's members limited? Exactly one of: liability not limited; liability limited to the amount, if any, unpaid on the shares held; liability limited to the amount the members undertake to contribute on a winding up; liability limited in some other way by the constitution
      `my company has a share capital` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does your company have a share capital?
      `the requirements as to registration as a public company have been complied with on or after the relevant date` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Have the requirements of the Companies Acts, or of the former Companies Acts, as to registration or re-registration of your company as a public company been complied with on or after the relevant date (22 December 1980 for registration in Great Britain, 1 July 1983 for registration in Northern Ireland)?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 270(1), is my company required to have a secretary, if it is a private company` IS
    `s 270(1) the private company is required to have a secretary` `my company is a private company`
    WHERE
        `my company profile` MEANS `Company profile` WITH
            `place of registration` IS `England and Wales` -- placeholder: s 4(1) and s 4(2) do not read it (only s 4(3) does, and these questions do not call it)
            `liability of the members` IS `how the liability of my company's members is limited`
            `a share capital` IS `my company has a share capital`
            `certificate of incorporation stating that it is a public company` IS `my company's certificate of incorporation states that it is a public company`
        `my company is a public company` MEANS `s 4(2) the company is a public company` `my company profile` `the requirements as to registration as a public company have been complied with on or after the relevant date`
        `my company is a private company` MEANS `s 4(1) the company is a private company` `my company profile` `the requirements as to registration as a public company have been complied with on or after the relevant date`

-- s 270(2): a private company "without a secretary" is one that for the time being is taking advantage of the exemption in
-- subsection (1), that is, one that has none.
@export Under section 270(2), is my company a private company without a secretary?
GIVEN `my company's certificate of incorporation states that it is a public company` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does your company's certificate of incorporation state that it is a public company?
      `how the liability of my company's members is limited` IS A `Liability of members` @desc How is the liability of your company's members limited? Exactly one of: liability not limited; liability limited to the amount, if any, unpaid on the shares held; liability limited to the amount the members undertake to contribute on a winding up; liability limited in some other way by the constitution
      `my company has a share capital` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does your company have a share capital?
      `the requirements as to registration as a public company have been complied with on or after the relevant date` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Have the requirements of the Companies Acts, or of the former Companies Acts, as to registration or re-registration of your company as a public company been complied with on or after the relevant date (22 December 1980 for registration in Great Britain, 1 July 1983 for registration in Northern Ireland)?
      `my company for the time being has a secretary` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does your company, for the time being, have a secretary (or joint secretaries)?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 270(2), is my company a private company without a secretary` IS
    `s 270(2) the company is a private company without a secretary` `my company is a private company` `my company for the time being has a secretary`
    WHERE
        `my company profile` MEANS `Company profile` WITH
            `place of registration` IS `England and Wales` -- placeholder: s 4(1) and s 4(2) do not read it (only s 4(3) does, and these questions do not call it)
            `liability of the members` IS `how the liability of my company's members is limited`
            `a share capital` IS `my company has a share capital`
            `certificate of incorporation stating that it is a public company` IS `my company's certificate of incorporation states that it is a public company`
        `my company is a public company` MEANS `s 4(2) the company is a public company` `my company profile` `the requirements as to registration as a public company have been complied with on or after the relevant date`
        `my company is a private company` MEANS `s 4(1) the company is a private company` `my company profile` `the requirements as to registration as a public company have been complied with on or after the relevant date`

@export Under section 270(2), is my company a private company with a secretary?
GIVEN `my company's certificate of incorporation states that it is a public company` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does your company's certificate of incorporation state that it is a public company?
      `how the liability of my company's members is limited` IS A `Liability of members` @desc How is the liability of your company's members limited? Exactly one of: liability not limited; liability limited to the amount, if any, unpaid on the shares held; liability limited to the amount the members undertake to contribute on a winding up; liability limited in some other way by the constitution
      `my company has a share capital` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does your company have a share capital?
      `the requirements as to registration as a public company have been complied with on or after the relevant date` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Have the requirements of the Companies Acts, or of the former Companies Acts, as to registration or re-registration of your company as a public company been complied with on or after the relevant date (22 December 1980 for registration in Great Britain, 1 July 1983 for registration in Northern Ireland)?
      `my company for the time being has a secretary` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does your company, for the time being, have a secretary (or joint secretaries)?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 270(2), is my company a private company with a secretary` IS
    `s 270(2) the company is a private company with a secretary` `my company is a private company` `my company for the time being has a secretary`
    WHERE
        `my company profile` MEANS `Company profile` WITH
            `place of registration` IS `England and Wales` -- placeholder: s 4(1) and s 4(2) do not read it (only s 4(3) does, and these questions do not call it)
            `liability of the members` IS `how the liability of my company's members is limited`
            `a share capital` IS `my company has a share capital`
            `certificate of incorporation stating that it is a public company` IS `my company's certificate of incorporation states that it is a public company`
        `my company is a public company` MEANS `s 4(2) the company is a public company` `my company profile` `the requirements as to registration as a public company have been complied with on or after the relevant date`
        `my company is a private company` MEANS `s 4(1) the company is a private company` `my company profile` `the requirements as to registration as a public company have been complied with on or after the relevant date`

-- s 270(3)(a)(i): in a private company without a secretary, anything authorised or required to be given or sent to, or served on,
-- the company by being sent to its secretary may be given or sent to, or served on, the company itself.
@export Under section 270(3)(a)(i), does the subsection let a thing that the law requires or lets people send to my company's secretary be given or sent to, or served on, my company itself?
GIVEN `my company's certificate of incorporation states that it is a public company` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does your company's certificate of incorporation state that it is a public company?
      `how the liability of my company's members is limited` IS A `Liability of members` @desc How is the liability of your company's members limited? Exactly one of: liability not limited; liability limited to the amount, if any, unpaid on the shares held; liability limited to the amount the members undertake to contribute on a winding up; liability limited in some other way by the constitution
      `my company has a share capital` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does your company have a share capital?
      `the requirements as to registration as a public company have been complied with on or after the relevant date` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Have the requirements of the Companies Acts, or of the former Companies Acts, as to registration or re-registration of your company as a public company been complied with on or after the relevant date (22 December 1980 for registration in Great Britain, 1 July 1983 for registration in Northern Ireland)?
      `my company for the time being has a secretary` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does your company, for the time being, have a secretary (or joint secretaries)?
      `the thing is authorised or required to be given or sent to, or served on, the company by being sent to its secretary` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the thing (a notice, document or other communication) one that the law authorises or requires to be given or sent to, or served on, your company by being sent to its secretary?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 270(3)(a)(i), does the subsection let a thing that the law requires or lets people send to my company's secretary be given or sent to, or served on, my company itself` IS
    `s 270(3)(a)(i) the thing may be given or sent to, or served on, the company itself` `my company is a private company` `my company for the time being has a secretary` `the thing is authorised or required to be given or sent to, or served on, the company by being sent to its secretary`
    WHERE
        `my company profile` MEANS `Company profile` WITH
            `place of registration` IS `England and Wales` -- placeholder: s 4(1) and s 4(2) do not read it (only s 4(3) does, and these questions do not call it)
            `liability of the members` IS `how the liability of my company's members is limited`
            `a share capital` IS `my company has a share capital`
            `certificate of incorporation stating that it is a public company` IS `my company's certificate of incorporation states that it is a public company`
        `my company is a public company` MEANS `s 4(2) the company is a public company` `my company profile` `the requirements as to registration as a public company have been complied with on or after the relevant date`
        `my company is a private company` MEANS `s 4(1) the company is a private company` `my company profile` `the requirements as to registration as a public company have been complied with on or after the relevant date`

-- s 270(3)(a)(ii): in a private company without a secretary, such a thing addressed to the secretary is treated as addressed to the company.
@export Under section 270(3)(a)(ii), is a thing addressed to my company's secretary treated as addressed to my company?
GIVEN `my company's certificate of incorporation states that it is a public company` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does your company's certificate of incorporation state that it is a public company?
      `how the liability of my company's members is limited` IS A `Liability of members` @desc How is the liability of your company's members limited? Exactly one of: liability not limited; liability limited to the amount, if any, unpaid on the shares held; liability limited to the amount the members undertake to contribute on a winding up; liability limited in some other way by the constitution
      `my company has a share capital` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does your company have a share capital?
      `the requirements as to registration as a public company have been complied with on or after the relevant date` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Have the requirements of the Companies Acts, or of the former Companies Acts, as to registration or re-registration of your company as a public company been complied with on or after the relevant date (22 December 1980 for registration in Great Britain, 1 July 1983 for registration in Northern Ireland)?
      `my company for the time being has a secretary` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does your company, for the time being, have a secretary (or joint secretaries)?
      `the thing is authorised or required to be given or sent to, or served on, the company by being sent to its secretary` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the thing (a notice, document or other communication) one that the law authorises or requires to be given or sent to, or served on, your company by being sent to its secretary?
      `the thing is addressed to the secretary` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the thing addressed to the secretary?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 270(3)(a)(ii), is a thing addressed to my company's secretary treated as addressed to my company` IS
    `s 270(3)(a)(ii) the thing addressed to the secretary is treated as addressed to the company` `my company is a private company` `my company for the time being has a secretary` `the thing is authorised or required to be given or sent to, or served on, the company by being sent to its secretary` `the thing is addressed to the secretary`
    WHERE
        `my company profile` MEANS `Company profile` WITH
            `place of registration` IS `England and Wales` -- placeholder: s 4(1) and s 4(2) do not read it (only s 4(3) does, and these questions do not call it)
            `liability of the members` IS `how the liability of my company's members is limited`
            `a share capital` IS `my company has a share capital`
            `certificate of incorporation stating that it is a public company` IS `my company's certificate of incorporation states that it is a public company`
        `my company is a public company` MEANS `s 4(2) the company is a public company` `my company profile` `the requirements as to registration as a public company have been complied with on or after the relevant date`
        `my company is a private company` MEANS `s 4(1) the company is a private company` `my company profile` `the requirements as to registration as a public company have been complied with on or after the relevant date`

-- s 270(3)(b): in a private company without a secretary, anything else required or authorised to be done by or to the secretary may
-- be done by or to a director, or a person authorised generally or specifically in that behalf by the directors.
@export Under section 270(3)(b), does the subsection let me do or receive, in place of my company's secretary, anything else that the law requires or lets the secretary do or receive?
GIVEN `my company's certificate of incorporation states that it is a public company` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does your company's certificate of incorporation state that it is a public company?
      `how the liability of my company's members is limited` IS A `Liability of members` @desc How is the liability of your company's members limited? Exactly one of: liability not limited; liability limited to the amount, if any, unpaid on the shares held; liability limited to the amount the members undertake to contribute on a winding up; liability limited in some other way by the constitution
      `my company has a share capital` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does your company have a share capital?
      `the requirements as to registration as a public company have been complied with on or after the relevant date` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Have the requirements of the Companies Acts, or of the former Companies Acts, as to registration or re-registration of your company as a public company been complied with on or after the relevant date (22 December 1980 for registration in Great Britain, 1 July 1983 for registration in Northern Ireland)?
      `my company for the time being has a secretary` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does your company, for the time being, have a secretary (or joint secretaries)?
      `the thing is required or authorised to be done by or to the secretary` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the thing one that the law requires or authorises to be done by or to the secretary of your company?
      `the thing is one of those described in paragraph (a)` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the thing a notice, document or communication that is to be given or sent to, or served on, your company by being sent to its secretary (the things that section 270(3)(a) deals with)?
      `I occupy the position of director` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Do you occupy the position of director of your company, by whatever name called?
      `the directors have authorised me` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Have the directors authorised you, generally or specifically, to do or receive the thing in place of the secretary?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 270(3)(b), does the subsection let me do or receive, in place of my company's secretary, anything else that the law requires or lets the secretary do or receive` IS
    `s 270(3)(b) the thing may be done by or to the person` `my company is a private company` `my company for the time being has a secretary` `the thing is required or authorised to be done by or to the secretary` `the thing is one of those described in paragraph (a)` (JUST `I occupy the position of director`) `the directors have authorised me`
    WHERE
        `my company profile` MEANS `Company profile` WITH
            `place of registration` IS `England and Wales` -- placeholder: s 4(1) and s 4(2) do not read it (only s 4(3) does, and these questions do not call it)
            `liability of the members` IS `how the liability of my company's members is limited`
            `a share capital` IS `my company has a share capital`
            `certificate of incorporation stating that it is a public company` IS `my company's certificate of incorporation states that it is a public company`
        `my company is a public company` MEANS `s 4(2) the company is a public company` `my company profile` `the requirements as to registration as a public company have been complied with on or after the relevant date`
        `my company is a private company` MEANS `s 4(1) the company is a private company` `my company profile` `the requirements as to registration as a public company have been complied with on or after the relevant date`
        -- (JUST ...) above stands for s 250: "director" includes any person occupying the position of director, by whatever name called.

§§ `Public companies (ss 271 to 273)`

-- s 271: "A public company must have a secretary."
@export Under section 271, must my company have a secretary?
GIVEN `my company's certificate of incorporation states that it is a public company` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does your company's certificate of incorporation state that it is a public company?
      `how the liability of my company's members is limited` IS A `Liability of members` @desc How is the liability of your company's members limited? Exactly one of: liability not limited; liability limited to the amount, if any, unpaid on the shares held; liability limited to the amount the members undertake to contribute on a winding up; liability limited in some other way by the constitution
      `my company has a share capital` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does your company have a share capital?
      `the requirements as to registration as a public company have been complied with on or after the relevant date` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Have the requirements of the Companies Acts, or of the former Companies Acts, as to registration or re-registration of your company as a public company been complied with on or after the relevant date (22 December 1980 for registration in Great Britain, 1 July 1983 for registration in Northern Ireland)?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 271, must my company have a secretary` IS
    `s 271 the public company must have a secretary` `my company is a public company`
    WHERE
        `my company profile` MEANS `Company profile` WITH
            `place of registration` IS `England and Wales` -- placeholder: s 4(1) and s 4(2) do not read it (only s 4(3) does, and these questions do not call it)
            `liability of the members` IS `how the liability of my company's members is limited`
            `a share capital` IS `my company has a share capital`
            `certificate of incorporation stating that it is a public company` IS `my company's certificate of incorporation states that it is a public company`
        `my company is a public company` MEANS `s 4(2) the company is a public company` `my company profile` `the requirements as to registration as a public company have been complied with on or after the relevant date`
        `my company is a private company` MEANS `s 4(1) the company is a private company` `my company profile` `the requirements as to registration as a public company have been complied with on or after the relevant date`

@export Under section 271, is my company in breach of the requirement to have a secretary?
GIVEN `my company's certificate of incorporation states that it is a public company` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does your company's certificate of incorporation state that it is a public company?
      `how the liability of my company's members is limited` IS A `Liability of members` @desc How is the liability of your company's members limited? Exactly one of: liability not limited; liability limited to the amount, if any, unpaid on the shares held; liability limited to the amount the members undertake to contribute on a winding up; liability limited in some other way by the constitution
      `my company has a share capital` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does your company have a share capital?
      `the requirements as to registration as a public company have been complied with on or after the relevant date` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Have the requirements of the Companies Acts, or of the former Companies Acts, as to registration or re-registration of your company as a public company been complied with on or after the relevant date (22 December 1980 for registration in Great Britain, 1 July 1983 for registration in Northern Ireland)?
      `my company has a secretary` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does your company have a secretary (or joint secretaries)?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 271, is my company in breach of the requirement to have a secretary` IS
    `s 271 the public company is in breach of section 271` `my company is a public company` `my company has a secretary`
    WHERE
        `my company profile` MEANS `Company profile` WITH
            `place of registration` IS `England and Wales` -- placeholder: s 4(1) and s 4(2) do not read it (only s 4(3) does, and these questions do not call it)
            `liability of the members` IS `how the liability of my company's members is limited`
            `a share capital` IS `my company has a share capital`
            `certificate of incorporation stating that it is a public company` IS `my company's certificate of incorporation states that it is a public company`
        `my company is a public company` MEANS `s 4(2) the company is a public company` `my company profile` `the requirements as to registration as a public company have been complied with on or after the relevant date`
        `my company is a private company` MEANS `s 4(1) the company is a private company` `my company profile` `the requirements as to registration as a public company have been complied with on or after the relevant date`

-- s 272(1): if it appears to the Secretary of State that a public company is in breach of s 271, the Secretary of State may give the
-- company a direction. A power: the answer is null where its conditions are not met.
@export Under section 272(1), may the Secretary of State give my company a direction to appoint a secretary?
GIVEN `my company's certificate of incorporation states that it is a public company` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does your company's certificate of incorporation state that it is a public company?
      `how the liability of my company's members is limited` IS A `Liability of members` @desc How is the liability of your company's members limited? Exactly one of: liability not limited; liability limited to the amount, if any, unpaid on the shares held; liability limited to the amount the members undertake to contribute on a winding up; liability limited in some other way by the constitution
      `my company has a share capital` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does your company have a share capital?
      `the requirements as to registration as a public company have been complied with on or after the relevant date` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Have the requirements of the Companies Acts, or of the former Companies Acts, as to registration or re-registration of your company as a public company been complied with on or after the relevant date (22 December 1980 for registration in Great Britain, 1 July 1983 for registration in Northern Ireland)?
      `it appears to the Secretary of State that my company is in breach of section 271` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does it appear to the Secretary of State that your public company is in breach of section 271 (the requirement to have a secretary)?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 272(1), may the Secretary of State give my company a direction to appoint a secretary` IS
    `s 272(1) the Secretary of State may give the company a direction under section 272` `my company is a public company` `it appears to the Secretary of State that my company is in breach of section 271`
    WHERE
        `my company profile` MEANS `Company profile` WITH
            `place of registration` IS `England and Wales` -- placeholder: s 4(1) and s 4(2) do not read it (only s 4(3) does, and these questions do not call it)
            `liability of the members` IS `how the liability of my company's members is limited`
            `a share capital` IS `my company has a share capital`
            `certificate of incorporation stating that it is a public company` IS `my company's certificate of incorporation states that it is a public company`
        `my company is a public company` MEANS `s 4(2) the company is a public company` `my company profile` `the requirements as to registration as a public company have been complied with on or after the relevant date`
        `my company is a private company` MEANS `s 4(1) the company is a private company` `my company profile` `the requirements as to registration as a public company have been complied with on or after the relevant date`

-- s 272(2): what a direction must state and specify.
@export Under section 272(2), does the direction my company received state and specify what the subsection requires?
GIVEN `the direction states that my company appears to be in breach of section 271` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does the direction state that your company appears to be in breach of section 271?
      `the direction specifies what my company must do in order to comply` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does the direction specify what your company must do in order to comply with it?
      `the direction specifies the period within which my company must do so` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does the direction specify the period within which your company must do it?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 272(2), does the direction my company received state and specify what the subsection requires` IS
    `s 272(2) the direction states and specifies what the subsection requires` `the direction states that my company appears to be in breach of section 271` `the direction specifies what my company must do in order to comply` `the direction specifies the period within which my company must do so`

@export Under section 272(2), is the period the direction gives my company within the limits the subsection sets (not less than one month and not more than three months after the date the direction is given)?
GIVEN `the date on which the direction was given` IS A DATE @desc On what date was the direction given to your company?
      `the last day of the period specified in the direction` IS A DATE @desc What is the last day of the period the direction gives your company to comply?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 272(2), is the period the direction gives my company within the limits the subsection sets (not less than one month and not more than three months after the date the direction is given)` IS
    `s 272(2) the period specified is not less than one month or more than three months after the date the direction is given` `the date on which the direction was given` `the last day of the period specified in the direction`

-- s 272(3): the direction must also inform the company of the consequences of failing to comply.
@export Under section 272(3), does the direction my company received inform it of the consequences of failing to comply?
GIVEN `the direction informs my company of the consequences of failing to comply` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does the direction inform your company of the consequences of failing to comply with it?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 272(3), does the direction my company received inform it of the consequences of failing to comply` IS
    `s 272(3) the direction informs the company of the consequences of failing to comply` `the direction informs my company of the consequences of failing to comply`

-- s 272(4) and (5): the duty to comply by the end of the period.
@export Under section 272(4), must my company comply with the direction by making the necessary appointment and giving notice of it before the end of the period?
GIVEN `my company was in breach of section 271 when the direction was given` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Was your company in breach of section 271 (a public company with no secretary) when the direction was given?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 272(4), must my company comply with the direction by making the necessary appointment and giving notice of it before the end of the period` IS
    `s 272(4) the company must comply with the direction by making the appointment and giving notice of it` `my company was in breach of section 271 when the direction was given`

@export Under section 272(5), must my company comply with the direction by giving notice of the appointment before the end of the period?
GIVEN `my company had already made the necessary appointment when the direction was given` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Had your company already made the necessary appointment (of a secretary) when the direction was given?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 272(5), must my company comply with the direction by giving notice of the appointment before the end of the period` IS
    `s 272(5) the company must comply with the direction by giving notice of the appointment` `my company had already made the necessary appointment when the direction was given`

-- s 272(4) and (5) together: has the company complied? The notice is the one "under section 276", which this text shows as repealed
-- (finding F-276 in NOTES.md); the person states when notice of the appointment was given to the registrar.
@export Under section 272(4) and (5), has my company complied with the direction?
GIVEN `my company was in breach of section 271 when the direction was given` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Was your company in breach of section 271 (a public company with no secretary) when the direction was given?
      `my company had already made the necessary appointment when the direction was given` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Had your company already made the necessary appointment (of a secretary) when the direction was given?
      `my company has made the necessary appointment since` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has your company made the necessary appointment since the direction was given? (Answer no if it had already made it, or has not made it yet.)
      `the day my company made the necessary appointment` IS A DATE @desc On what date did your company make the necessary appointment? (Any date if it has not.)
      `my company has given notice of the appointment` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has your company given notice of the appointment to the registrar?
      `the day my company gave notice of the appointment` IS A DATE @desc On what date did your company give that notice? (Any date if it has not.)
      `the last day of the period specified in the direction` IS A DATE @desc What is the last day of the period the direction gives your company to comply?
      `the day of the question` IS A DATE @desc What is today's date?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 272(4) and (5), has my company complied with the direction` IS
    `s 272(4)-(5) the company has complied with the direction`
        `my company was in breach of section 271 when the direction was given`
        `my company had already made the necessary appointment when the direction was given`
        (IF `my company has made the necessary appointment since` THEN JUST `the day my company made the necessary appointment` ELSE NOTHING)
        (IF `my company has given notice of the appointment` THEN JUST `the day my company gave notice of the appointment` ELSE NOTHING)
        `the last day of the period specified in the direction`
        `the day of the question`

-- s 272(6)(a): the company commits an offence if it fails to comply with the direction.
@export Under section 272(6)(a), does my company commit an offence by failing to comply with the direction?
GIVEN `my company has failed to comply with the direction` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has your company failed to comply with the direction (it did not make the appointment and give notice before the end of the period the direction specified)?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 272(6)(a), does my company commit an offence by failing to comply with the direction` IS
    `s 272(6)(a) the company commits an offence` (JUST (NOT (`my company has failed to comply with the direction`)))
    -- the input of s 272(6)(a) is the answer of s 272(4)-(5) (has the company COMPLIED), here the negation of the fact the person states

-- s 272(6)(b): every officer of the company who is in default commits the offence; for this purpose a shadow director is treated as an officer.
@export Under section 272(6)(b), do I commit an offence as an officer of my company that failed to comply with the direction?
GIVEN `my company has failed to comply with the direction` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has your company failed to comply with the direction (it did not make the appointment and give notice before the end of the period the direction specified)?
      `I am a director of my company` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are you a director of your company?
      `I am a manager of my company` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are you a manager of your company?
      `I am the secretary of my company` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are you the secretary of your company?
      `I am a shadow director of my company` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are you a person in accordance with whose directions or instructions the directors of your company are accustomed to act (a shadow director)?
      `I am in default` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did you authorise or permit, participate in, or fail to take all reasonable steps to prevent, the failure of your company to comply with the direction?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 272(6)(b), do I commit an offence as an officer of my company that failed to comply with the direction` IS
    `s 272(6)(b) the officer commits an offence`
        (JUST (NOT (`my company has failed to comply with the direction`)))
        (`s 1173(1) the holder of the position is an officer of the body corporate` `my position in my company`)
        (JUST `I am a shadow director of my company`)
        (JUST `I am in default`)
    WHERE
        `my position in my company` MEANS
            IF `I am a director of my company`
            THEN `s 1173(1) director`
            ELSE IF `I am a manager of my company`
                 THEN `s 1173(1) manager`
                 ELSE IF `I am the secretary of my company`
                      THEN `s 1173(1) secretary`
                      ELSE `s 1173(1) another position`
    -- (JUST `I am a shadow director ...`) stands for s 251; (JUST `I am in default`) stands for s 1121 (the person states the facts s 1121(3) names)

-- s 272(7): the penalty. The Act does not say what a level on the standard scale stands for in pounds: the person supplies it.
@export Under section 272(7), what is the most I can be fined on summary conviction for the offence, in pounds?
GIVEN `the amount in pounds that level 5 on the standard scale stands for` IS A NUMBER @desc How many pounds is level 5 on the standard scale?
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `Under section 272(7), what is the most I can be fined on summary conviction for the offence, in pounds` IS
    `s 272(7) the most a person guilty of an offence may be fined on summary conviction, in pounds` `the amount in pounds that level 5 on the standard scale stands for`

-- s 272(7): the text carries two wordings of the daily default fine run together (finding F-272-7 in NOTES.md); a question for each.
@export Under section 272(7), on the first wording (one-tenth of level 5 on the standard scale), what is the most the daily default fine can be, in pounds?
GIVEN `the amount in pounds that level 5 on the standard scale stands for` IS A NUMBER @desc How many pounds is level 5 on the standard scale?
GIVETH A MAYBE NUMBER
DECIDE `Under section 272(7), on the first wording (one-tenth of level 5 on the standard scale), what is the most the daily default fine can be, in pounds` IS
    `s 272(7) the most the daily default fine may be, in pounds`
        (JUST `s 272(7) one-tenth of level 5 on the standard scale`)
        `the amount in pounds that level 5 on the standard scale stands for`
        0 -- placeholder: the first wording does not read level 4

@export Under section 272(7), on the second wording (one-tenth of the greater of £5,000 or level 4 on the standard scale), what is the most the daily default fine can be, in pounds?
GIVEN `the amount in pounds that level 4 on the standard scale stands for` IS A NUMBER @desc How many pounds is level 4 on the standard scale?
GIVETH A MAYBE NUMBER
DECIDE `Under section 272(7), on the second wording (one-tenth of the greater of £5,000 or level 4 on the standard scale), what is the most the daily default fine can be, in pounds` IS
    `s 272(7) the most the daily default fine may be, in pounds`
        (JUST `s 272(7) one-tenth of the greater of £5,000 or level 4 on the standard scale`)
        0 -- placeholder: the second wording does not read level 5
        `the amount in pounds that level 4 on the standard scale stands for`

-- s 273(1): the duty of the directors of a public company.
@export Under section 273(1), are the directors of my company under a duty to take all reasonable steps to secure a suitably qualified secretary?
GIVEN `my company's certificate of incorporation states that it is a public company` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does your company's certificate of incorporation state that it is a public company?
      `how the liability of my company's members is limited` IS A `Liability of members` @desc How is the liability of your company's members limited? Exactly one of: liability not limited; liability limited to the amount, if any, unpaid on the shares held; liability limited to the amount the members undertake to contribute on a winding up; liability limited in some other way by the constitution
      `my company has a share capital` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does your company have a share capital?
      `the requirements as to registration as a public company have been complied with on or after the relevant date` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Have the requirements of the Companies Acts, or of the former Companies Acts, as to registration or re-registration of your company as a public company been complied with on or after the relevant date (22 December 1980 for registration in Great Britain, 1 July 1983 for registration in Northern Ireland)?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 273(1), are the directors of my company under a duty to take all reasonable steps to secure a suitably qualified secretary` IS
    `s 273(1) the directors are under a duty to take all reasonable steps` `my company is a public company`
    WHERE
        `my company profile` MEANS `Company profile` WITH
            `place of registration` IS `England and Wales` -- placeholder: s 4(1) and s 4(2) do not read it (only s 4(3) does, and these questions do not call it)
            `liability of the members` IS `how the liability of my company's members is limited`
            `a share capital` IS `my company has a share capital`
            `certificate of incorporation stating that it is a public company` IS `my company's certificate of incorporation states that it is a public company`
        `my company is a public company` MEANS `s 4(2) the company is a public company` `my company profile` `the requirements as to registration as a public company have been complied with on or after the relevant date`
        `my company is a private company` MEANS `s 4(1) the company is a private company` `my company profile` `the requirements as to registration as a public company have been complied with on or after the relevant date`

@export Under section 273(1), have the directors of my company performed their duty to take all reasonable steps to secure a suitably qualified secretary?
GIVEN `my company's certificate of incorporation states that it is a public company` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does your company's certificate of incorporation state that it is a public company?
      `how the liability of my company's members is limited` IS A `Liability of members` @desc How is the liability of your company's members limited? Exactly one of: liability not limited; liability limited to the amount, if any, unpaid on the shares held; liability limited to the amount the members undertake to contribute on a winding up; liability limited in some other way by the constitution
      `my company has a share capital` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does your company have a share capital?
      `the requirements as to registration as a public company have been complied with on or after the relevant date` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Have the requirements of the Companies Acts, or of the former Companies Acts, as to registration or re-registration of your company as a public company been complied with on or after the relevant date (22 December 1980 for registration in Great Britain, 1 July 1983 for registration in Northern Ireland)?
      `the directors have taken all reasonable steps to secure that the secretary has what subsection (1) describes` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Have the directors taken all reasonable steps to secure that the secretary (or each joint secretary) appears to them to have the requisite knowledge and experience to discharge the functions of secretary and has one or more of the qualifications in section 273(2)?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 273(1), have the directors of my company performed their duty to take all reasonable steps to secure a suitably qualified secretary` IS
    `s 273(1) the directors have performed their duty` `my company is a public company` `the directors have taken all reasonable steps to secure that the secretary has what subsection (1) describes`
    WHERE
        `my company profile` MEANS `Company profile` WITH
            `place of registration` IS `England and Wales` -- placeholder: s 4(1) and s 4(2) do not read it (only s 4(3) does, and these questions do not call it)
            `liability of the members` IS `how the liability of my company's members is limited`
            `a share capital` IS `my company has a share capital`
            `certificate of incorporation stating that it is a public company` IS `my company's certificate of incorporation states that it is a public company`
        `my company is a public company` MEANS `s 4(2) the company is a public company` `my company profile` `the requirements as to registration as a public company have been complied with on or after the relevant date`
        `my company is a private company` MEANS `s 4(1) the company is a private company` `my company profile` `the requirements as to registration as a public company have been complied with on or after the relevant date`

-- s 273(2) and (3): the qualifications of a secretary of a public company. The person states, for one secretary (or one joint
-- secretary at a time), the facts each limb of (2) turns on.
@export Under section 273(3), is the body one of the bodies the section specifies?
GIVEN body IS A `s 273(3) body` @desc Which body is it? Exactly one of: s 273(3)(a) the Institute of Chartered Accountants in England and Wales; s 273(3)(b) the Institute of Chartered Accountants of Scotland; s 273(3)(c) the Association of Chartered Certified Accountants; s 273(3)(d) the Institute of Chartered Accountants in Ireland; s 273(3)(e) the Institute of Chartered Secretaries and Administrators; s 273(3)(f) the Chartered Institute of Management Accountants; s 273(3)(g) the Chartered Institute of Public Finance and Accountancy; s 273(3) any other body
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 273(3), is the body one of the bodies the section specifies` IS
    `s 273(3) the body is one of the bodies specified in subsection (3)` body

@export Under section 273(2), does the person have one or more of the qualifications the subsection lists?
GIVEN `the years in the five years before the appointment that the person held the office of secretary of a public company` IS A NUMBER @desc Added together, for how many of the five years immediately preceding the appointment as secretary did the person hold the office of secretary of a public company? (a number from 0 to 5; 2.5 means two and a half years)
      `the person is a member of the Institute of Chartered Accountants in England and Wales` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the person a member of the Institute of Chartered Accountants in England and Wales?
      `the person is a member of the Institute of Chartered Accountants of Scotland` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the person a member of the Institute of Chartered Accountants of Scotland?
      `the person is a member of the Association of Chartered Certified Accountants` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the person a member of the Association of Chartered Certified Accountants?
      `the person is a member of the Institute of Chartered Accountants in Ireland` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the person a member of the Institute of Chartered Accountants in Ireland?
      `the person is a member of the Institute of Chartered Secretaries and Administrators` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the person a member of the Institute of Chartered Secretaries and Administrators?
      `the person is a member of the Chartered Institute of Management Accountants` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the person a member of the Chartered Institute of Management Accountants?
      `the person is a member of the Chartered Institute of Public Finance and Accountancy` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the person a member of the Chartered Institute of Public Finance and Accountancy?
      `the person is a barrister` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the person a barrister?
      `the person is an advocate` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the person an advocate?
      `the person is a solicitor` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the person a solicitor?
      `the person is called or admitted in a part of the United Kingdom` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the person called or admitted as a barrister, advocate or solicitor in any part of the United Kingdom?
      `it appears to the directors that the person is capable of discharging the functions of secretary` IS A BOOLEAN @desc By virtue of the person's holding or having held any other position, or being a member of any other body, does it appear to the directors that the person is capable of discharging the functions of secretary of the company?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 273(2), does the person have one or more of the qualifications the subsection lists` IS
    `s 273(2) the person has one or more of the qualifications` `limb (a)` `limb (b)` `limb (c)` `limb (d)`
    WHERE
        `limb (a)` MEANS `s 273(2)(a) the person has held the office of secretary of a public company for at least three of the five years immediately preceding the appointment` `the years in the five years before the appointment that the person held the office of secretary of a public company`
        `limb (b)` MEANS `s 273(2)(b) the person is a member of any of the bodies specified in subsection (3)` `coa6 seat the bodies of which the person is a member`
        `limb (c)` MEANS `s 273(2)(c) the person is a barrister, advocate or solicitor called or admitted in any part of the United Kingdom` `coa6 seat the calling of the person` `the person is called or admitted in a part of the United Kingdom`
        `limb (d)` MEANS `s 273(2)(d) the person is a person who appears to the directors to be capable of discharging the functions of secretary` `it appears to the directors that the person is capable of discharging the functions of secretary`
        `coa6 seat the bodies of which the person is a member` MEANS concat (LIST `ICAEW if a member`, `ICAS if a member`, `ACCA if a member`, `ICAI if a member`, `ICSA if a member`, `CIMA if a member`, `CIPFA if a member`)
        `ICAEW if a member` MEANS IF `the person is a member of the Institute of Chartered Accountants in England and Wales` THEN LIST `s 273(3)(a) the Institute of Chartered Accountants in England and Wales` ELSE EMPTY
        `ICAS if a member` MEANS IF `the person is a member of the Institute of Chartered Accountants of Scotland` THEN LIST `s 273(3)(b) the Institute of Chartered Accountants of Scotland` ELSE EMPTY
        `ACCA if a member` MEANS IF `the person is a member of the Association of Chartered Certified Accountants` THEN LIST `s 273(3)(c) the Association of Chartered Certified Accountants` ELSE EMPTY
        `ICAI if a member` MEANS IF `the person is a member of the Institute of Chartered Accountants in Ireland` THEN LIST `s 273(3)(d) the Institute of Chartered Accountants in Ireland` ELSE EMPTY
        `ICSA if a member` MEANS IF `the person is a member of the Institute of Chartered Secretaries and Administrators` THEN LIST `s 273(3)(e) the Institute of Chartered Secretaries and Administrators` ELSE EMPTY
        `CIMA if a member` MEANS IF `the person is a member of the Chartered Institute of Management Accountants` THEN LIST `s 273(3)(f) the Chartered Institute of Management Accountants` ELSE EMPTY
        `CIPFA if a member` MEANS IF `the person is a member of the Chartered Institute of Public Finance and Accountancy` THEN LIST `s 273(3)(g) the Chartered Institute of Public Finance and Accountancy` ELSE EMPTY
        `coa6 seat the calling of the person` MEANS
            IF `the person is a barrister`
            THEN `s 273(2)(c) a barrister`
            ELSE IF `the person is an advocate`
                 THEN `s 273(2)(c) an advocate`
                 ELSE IF `the person is a solicitor`
                      THEN `s 273(2)(c) a solicitor`
                      ELSE `s 273(2)(c) another calling`

@export Under section 273(1), does the secretary have what the directors must take all reasonable steps to secure (the requisite knowledge and experience in their view, and one of the qualifications in section 273(2))?
GIVEN `it appears to the directors that the person has the requisite knowledge and experience to discharge the functions of secretary of the company` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does it appear to the directors that the secretary has the requisite knowledge and experience to discharge the functions of secretary of the company?
      `the person has one or more of the qualifications in section 273(2)` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has the secretary one or more of the qualifications in section 273(2)? (Section 273(2) asks about the person's years as secretary of a public company, membership of the listed bodies, calling as barrister, advocate or solicitor, and the directors' view of the person's capability.)
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 273(1), does the secretary have what the directors must take all reasonable steps to secure (the requisite knowledge and experience in their view, and one of the qualifications in section 273(2))` IS
    `s 273(1) the secretary has what the directors must take all reasonable steps to secure`
        (`s 273(1)(a) the secretary is a person who appears to the directors to have the requisite knowledge and experience` `it appears to the directors that the person has the requisite knowledge and experience to discharge the functions of secretary of the company`)
        (JUST `the person has one or more of the qualifications in section 273(2)`)
    -- (JUST ...) stands for the answer of s 273(2), which the person states as the fact "has one or more of the qualifications"

§§ `Provisions applying to private companies with a secretary and to public companies (s 274)`

-- s 274: where the office of secretary is vacant, or there is for any other reason no secretary capable of acting, anything required or
-- authorised to be done by or to the secretary may be done (a) by or to an assistant or deputy secretary, or (b) if there is none, by or
-- to a person authorised by the directors. Both are permissions: the answer is null where the conditions are not met.
@export Under section 274(a), does the section let a thing the law requires or lets my company's secretary do or receive be done by or to an assistant or deputy secretary, where the office is vacant or no secretary can act?
GIVEN `the office of secretary is vacant` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the office of secretary of your company vacant?
      `there is for any other reason no secretary capable of acting` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is there, for any other reason, no secretary of your company capable of acting?
      `the thing is required or authorised to be done by or to the secretary` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the thing one that the law requires or authorises to be done by or to the secretary of your company?
      `the person is an assistant or deputy secretary` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the person who is to do or receive the thing an assistant or deputy secretary of your company?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 274(a), does the section let a thing the law requires or lets my company's secretary do or receive be done by or to an assistant or deputy secretary, where the office is vacant or no secretary can act` IS
    `s 274(a) the thing may be done by or to an assistant or deputy secretary` `the office of secretary is vacant` `there is for any other reason no secretary capable of acting` `the thing is required or authorised to be done by or to the secretary` `the person is an assistant or deputy secretary`

@export Under section 274(b), does the section let a thing the law requires or lets my company's secretary do or receive be done by or to a person the directors have authorised, where the office is vacant or no secretary can act and there is no assistant or deputy secretary capable of acting?
GIVEN `the office of secretary is vacant` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the office of secretary of your company vacant?
      `there is for any other reason no secretary capable of acting` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is there, for any other reason, no secretary of your company capable of acting?
      `the thing is required or authorised to be done by or to the secretary` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the thing one that the law requires or authorises to be done by or to the secretary of your company?
      `there is no assistant or deputy secretary or none capable of acting` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is there no assistant or deputy secretary of your company, or none capable of acting?
      `the person is authorised generally or specifically in that behalf by the directors` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the person who is to do or receive the thing authorised, generally or specifically, in that behalf by the directors?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 274(b), does the section let a thing the law requires or lets my company's secretary do or receive be done by or to a person the directors have authorised, where the office is vacant or no secretary can act and there is no assistant or deputy secretary capable of acting` IS
    `s 274(b) the thing may be done by or to a person authorised by the directors` `the office of secretary is vacant` `there is for any other reason no secretary capable of acting` `the thing is required or authorised to be done by or to the secretary` `there is no assistant or deputy secretary or none capable of acting` `the person is authorised generally or specifically in that behalf by the directors`

§§ `Notification of information about secretaries (ss 279G to 279M)`

-- Helper (not exported): the kind of change in the secretaries, from the person's two yes/no facts. If both are yes the change is
-- taken to be a person BECOMING secretary (the questions say to answer yes to one only).
GIVEN becomes IS A BOOLEAN
      ceases IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A `s 279G change in the secretaries`
`s 279G(1) the change in the secretaries from the person's two facts` MEANS
    IF becomes
    THEN `s 279G(1)(a) a person becomes the secretary or one of the joint secretaries of the company`
    ELSE IF ceases
         THEN `s 279G(1)(b) a person ceases to be the secretary or one of the joint secretaries of the company`
         ELSE `s 279G no such change`

-- s 279G(1) and (4): a company must give notice to the registrar when a person becomes or ceases to be the secretary or a joint
-- secretary, but is not required to on its incorporation for a person named in the statement under section 12.
@export Under section 279G(1), must my company give notice to the registrar of a change in its secretary or joint secretary?
GIVEN `a person has become the secretary or one of the joint secretaries of my company` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has a person become the secretary, or one of the joint secretaries, of your company? (Answer yes to only one of this question and the next.)
      `a person has ceased to be the secretary or one of the joint secretaries of my company` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has a person ceased to be the secretary, or one of the joint secretaries, of your company?
      `the person became the secretary or a joint secretary on my company's incorporation` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did the person become the secretary (or a joint secretary) on your company's incorporation?
      `the person is named in the statement of proposed officers as the proposed secretary or a proposed joint secretary` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the person named, in the statement of the company's proposed officers delivered to the registrar under section 12, as the proposed secretary or one of the proposed joint secretaries?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 279G(1), must my company give notice to the registrar of a change in its secretary or joint secretary` IS
    `s 279G(1) the company must give notice to the registrar`
        (`s 279G(1) the change in the secretaries from the person's two facts` `a person has become the secretary or one of the joint secretaries of my company` `a person has ceased to be the secretary or one of the joint secretaries of my company`)
        `the person became the secretary or a joint secretary on my company's incorporation`
        `the person is named in the statement of proposed officers as the proposed secretary or a proposed joint secretary`

@export Under section 279G(2), does the notice my company gave specify the date on which the person became or ceased to be the secretary or a joint secretary?
GIVEN `the notice specifies the date on which the person became or ceased to be the secretary or one of the joint secretaries` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does the notice specify the date on which the person became or ceased to be the secretary, or one of the joint secretaries, of your company?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 279G(2), does the notice my company gave specify the date on which the person became or ceased to be the secretary or a joint secretary` IS
    `s 279G(2) the notice specifies the date` `the notice specifies the date on which the person became or ceased to be the secretary or one of the joint secretaries`

@export Under section 279G(3), does my company's notice that a person became its secretary contain the statements the subsection requires?
GIVEN `the notice is a notice that a person has become the secretary or a joint secretary` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the notice a notice that a person has become the secretary, or one of the joint secretaries, of your company? (Answer no for a notice that a person has ceased to be one.)
      `the notice contains a statement of the required information about the secretary` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does the notice contain a statement of the required information about the secretary or joint secretary (sections 279J and 279K)?
      `the notice contains a statement by my company that the person has consented to act` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does the notice contain a statement by your company that the person has consented to act in that capacity?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 279G(3), does my company's notice that a person became its secretary contain the statements the subsection requires` IS
    `s 279G(3) the notice under subsection (1)(a) contains the statements required`
        (`s 279G(1) the change in the secretaries from the person's two facts` `the notice is a notice that a person has become the secretary or a joint secretary` (NOT (`the notice is a notice that a person has become the secretary or a joint secretary`)))
        `the notice contains a statement of the required information about the secretary`
        `the notice contains a statement by my company that the person has consented to act`

@export Under section 279G(5), what is the last day for my company to give the notice?
GIVEN `the day on which the person became or ceased to be the secretary or a joint secretary` IS A DATE @desc On what date did the person become, or cease to be, the secretary or one of the joint secretaries of your company?
GIVETH A DATE
DECIDE `Under section 279G(5), what is the last day for my company to give the notice` IS
    `s 279G(5) the last day of the period` `the day on which the person became or ceased to be the secretary or a joint secretary`

@export Under section 279G(5), did my company give the notice within the period of 14 days beginning with the day of the change?
GIVEN `the day on which the person became or ceased to be the secretary or a joint secretary` IS A DATE @desc On what date did the person become, or cease to be, the secretary or one of the joint secretaries of your company?
      `the day the notice was given` IS A DATE @desc On what date did your company give the notice to the registrar?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 279G(5), did my company give the notice within the period of 14 days beginning with the day of the change` IS
    `s 279G(5) the notice was given within the period` `the day on which the person became or ceased to be the secretary or a joint secretary` `the day the notice was given`

-- Has the company failed to comply with section 279G (the failure on which the offence of s 279M(1) rests)?
@export Under section 279G, has my company failed to comply with section 279G?
GIVEN `a person has become the secretary or one of the joint secretaries of my company` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has a person become the secretary, or one of the joint secretaries, of your company? (Answer yes to only one of this question and the next.)
      `a person has ceased to be the secretary or one of the joint secretaries of my company` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has a person ceased to be the secretary, or one of the joint secretaries, of your company?
      `the person became the secretary or a joint secretary on my company's incorporation` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did the person become the secretary (or a joint secretary) on your company's incorporation?
      `the person is named in the statement of proposed officers as the proposed secretary or a proposed joint secretary` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the person named, in the statement of the company's proposed officers delivered to the registrar under section 12, as the proposed secretary or one of the proposed joint secretaries?
      `the day on which the person became or ceased to be the secretary or a joint secretary` IS A DATE @desc On what date did the person become, or cease to be, the secretary or one of the joint secretaries of your company?
      `my company has given notice to the registrar` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has your company given notice of the change to the registrar?
      `the day the notice was given` IS A DATE @desc On what date did your company give the notice? (Any date if it has not.)
      `the notice specifies the date of the change` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does the notice specify the date of the change? (Any answer if no notice has been given.)
      `the notice contains a statement of the required information` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does the notice contain a statement of the required information about the secretary (sections 279J and 279K)? (Any answer if no notice has been given, or if the person ceased to be secretary.)
      `the notice contains a statement of consent` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does the notice contain a statement by your company that the person consented to act? (Any answer if no notice has been given, or if the person ceased to be secretary.)
      `the day of the question` IS A DATE @desc What is today's date?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 279G, has my company failed to comply with section 279G` IS
    `s 279G the company has failed to comply with section 279G`
        (`s 279G(1) the change in the secretaries from the person's two facts` `a person has become the secretary or one of the joint secretaries of my company` `a person has ceased to be the secretary or one of the joint secretaries of my company`)
        `the person became the secretary or a joint secretary on my company's incorporation`
        `the person is named in the statement of proposed officers as the proposed secretary or a proposed joint secretary`
        `the day on which the person became or ceased to be the secretary or a joint secretary`
        (IF `my company has given notice to the registrar`
         THEN JUST (`s 279G notice given` OF `the day the notice was given`, `the notice specifies the date of the change`, `the notice contains a statement of the required information`, `the notice contains a statement of consent`)
         ELSE NOTHING)
        `the day of the question`

-- s 279H: notice of a change in the required information.
@export Under section 279H(1), must my company give notice to the registrar of a change in the required information about its secretary?
GIVEN `there is a change in the required information about the secretary or one of the joint secretaries of my company` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is there a change in the required information (sections 279J and 279K) about the secretary, or one of the joint secretaries, of your company?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 279H(1), must my company give notice to the registrar of a change in the required information about its secretary` IS
    `s 279H(1) the company must give notice to the registrar of the change` `there is a change in the required information about the secretary or one of the joint secretaries of my company`

@export Under section 279H(2), does the notice my company gave specify the date on which the change occurred?
GIVEN `the notice specifies the date on which the change occurred` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does the notice specify the date on which the change occurred?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 279H(2), does the notice my company gave specify the date on which the change occurred` IS
    `s 279H(2) the notice specifies the date` `the notice specifies the date on which the change occurred`

@export Under section 279H(3), what is the last day for my company to give the notice?
GIVEN `the day on which the change occurs` IS A DATE @desc On what date did the change in the required information occur?
GIVETH A DATE
DECIDE `Under section 279H(3), what is the last day for my company to give the notice` IS
    `s 279H(3) the last day of the period` `the day on which the change occurs`

@export Under section 279H(3), did my company give the notice within the period of 14 days beginning with the day the change occurred?
GIVEN `the day on which the change occurs` IS A DATE @desc On what date did the change in the required information occur?
      `the day the notice was given` IS A DATE @desc On what date did your company give the notice to the registrar?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 279H(3), did my company give the notice within the period of 14 days beginning with the day the change occurred` IS
    `s 279H(3) the notice was given within the period` `the day on which the change occurs` `the day the notice was given`

@export Under section 279H, has my company failed to comply with section 279H?
GIVEN `there is a change in the required information about the secretary or one of the joint secretaries of my company` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is there a change in the required information (sections 279J and 279K) about the secretary, or one of the joint secretaries, of your company?
      `the day on which the change occurs` IS A DATE @desc On what date did the change occur?
      `my company has given notice to the registrar` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has your company given notice of the change to the registrar?
      `the day the notice was given` IS A DATE @desc On what date did your company give the notice? (Any date if it has not.)
      `the notice specifies the date on which the change occurred` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does the notice specify the date on which the change occurred? (Any answer if no notice has been given.)
      `the day of the question` IS A DATE @desc What is today's date?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 279H, has my company failed to comply with section 279H` IS
    `s 279H the company has failed to comply with section 279H`
        (`s 279H(1) the company must give notice to the registrar of the change` `there is a change in the required information about the secretary or one of the joint secretaries of my company`)
        `the day on which the change occurs`
        (IF `my company has given notice to the registrar` THEN JUST (`s 279H notice given` OF `the day the notice was given`, `the notice specifies the date on which the change occurred`) ELSE NOTHING)
        `the day of the question`

-- s 279I: changes occurring before the company's incorporation.
@export Under section 279I(1), must my company give notice to the registrar that a person named as its proposed secretary (or one of its proposed joint secretaries) did not become its secretary (or one of its joint secretaries) on incorporation?
GIVEN `the person is named in the statement of proposed officers as the proposed secretary or one of the proposed joint secretaries` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the person named, in the statement of the company's proposed officers delivered to the registrar under section 12, as the proposed secretary or one of the proposed joint secretaries?
      `the person did not become the secretary or one of the joint secretaries on my company's incorporation` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did the person not become the secretary, or one of the joint secretaries, of your company on its incorporation?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 279I(1), must my company give notice to the registrar that a person named as its proposed secretary (or one of its proposed joint secretaries) did not become its secretary (or one of its joint secretaries) on incorporation` IS
    `s 279I(1) the company must give notice to the registrar that a proposed secretary did not become the secretary` `the person is named in the statement of proposed officers as the proposed secretary or one of the proposed joint secretaries` `the person did not become the secretary or one of the joint secretaries on my company's incorporation`

@export Under section 279I(2), must my company give notice to the registrar of a change in the required information about a proposed secretary (or proposed joint secretary) that occurred after the application for its registration was delivered and before it was incorporated?
GIVEN `the person is a proposed secretary or one of the proposed joint secretaries of my company` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the person a proposed secretary, or one of the proposed joint secretaries, of your company?
      `there was a change in the required information about the person` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Was there a change in the required information (sections 279J and 279K) about the person?
      `the day on which the change occurred` IS A DATE @desc On what date did the change occur?
      `the day the application for my company's registration was delivered to the registrar` IS A DATE @desc On what date was the application for your company's registration under section 9 delivered to the registrar?
      `the day on which my company was incorporated` IS A DATE @desc On what date was your company incorporated?
      `my company gives notice under subsection (1) in respect of the person` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does your company give notice under section 279I(1) in respect of the person?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 279I(2), must my company give notice to the registrar of a change in the required information about a proposed secretary (or proposed joint secretary) that occurred after the application for its registration was delivered and before it was incorporated` IS
    `s 279I(2) the company must give notice to the registrar of the change in the required information` `the person is a proposed secretary or one of the proposed joint secretaries of my company` `there was a change in the required information about the person` `the day on which the change occurred` `the day the application for my company's registration was delivered to the registrar` `the day on which my company was incorporated` `my company gives notice under subsection (1) in respect of the person`

@export Under section 279I(4), does the notice my company gave of a change before incorporation specify the date on which the change occurred?
GIVEN `the notice specifies the date on which the change occurred` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does the notice specify the date on which the change occurred?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 279I(4), does the notice my company gave of a change before incorporation specify the date on which the change occurred` IS
    `s 279I(4) the notice under subsection (2) specifies the date` `the notice specifies the date on which the change occurred`

@export Under section 279I(5), what is the last day for my company to give the notice?
GIVEN `the day on which my company was incorporated` IS A DATE @desc On what date was your company incorporated?
GIVETH A DATE
DECIDE `Under section 279I(5), what is the last day for my company to give the notice` IS
    `s 279I(5) the last day of the period` `the day on which my company was incorporated`

@export Under section 279I(5), did my company give the notice within the period of 14 days beginning with the day it was incorporated?
GIVEN `the day on which my company was incorporated` IS A DATE @desc On what date was your company incorporated?
      `the day the notice was given` IS A DATE @desc On what date did your company give the notice to the registrar?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 279I(5), did my company give the notice within the period of 14 days beginning with the day it was incorporated` IS
    `s 279I(5) the notice was given within the period` `the day on which my company was incorporated` `the day the notice was given`

@export Under section 279I, has my company failed to comply with section 279I?
GIVEN `the person is named in the statement of proposed officers as the proposed secretary or one of the proposed joint secretaries` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the person named, in the statement of the company's proposed officers delivered to the registrar under section 12, as the proposed secretary or one of the proposed joint secretaries?
      `the person did not become the secretary or one of the joint secretaries on my company's incorporation` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did the person not become the secretary, or one of the joint secretaries, of your company on its incorporation?
      `the person is a proposed secretary or one of the proposed joint secretaries of my company` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the person a proposed secretary, or one of the proposed joint secretaries, of your company?
      `there was a change in the required information about the person` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Was there a change in the required information (sections 279J and 279K) about the person?
      `the day on which the change occurred` IS A DATE @desc On what date did the change occur? (Any date if there was none.)
      `the day the application for my company's registration was delivered to the registrar` IS A DATE @desc On what date was the application for your company's registration under section 9 delivered to the registrar?
      `the day on which my company was incorporated` IS A DATE @desc On what date was your company incorporated?
      `my company gives notice under subsection (1) in respect of the person` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does your company give notice under section 279I(1) in respect of the person?
      `my company has given notice to the registrar` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has your company given notice to the registrar under section 279I?
      `the day the notice was given` IS A DATE @desc On what date did your company give the notice? (Any date if it has not.)
      `the notice specifies the date on which the change occurred` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does the notice specify the date on which the change occurred? (Any answer if no notice has been given.)
      `the day of the question` IS A DATE @desc What is today's date?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 279I, has my company failed to comply with section 279I` IS
    `s 279I the company has failed to comply with section 279I`
        (`s 279I(1) the company must give notice to the registrar that a proposed secretary did not become the secretary` `the person is named in the statement of proposed officers as the proposed secretary or one of the proposed joint secretaries` `the person did not become the secretary or one of the joint secretaries on my company's incorporation`)
        (`s 279I(2) the company must give notice to the registrar of the change in the required information` `the person is a proposed secretary or one of the proposed joint secretaries of my company` `there was a change in the required information about the person` `the day on which the change occurred` `the day the application for my company's registration was delivered to the registrar` `the day on which my company was incorporated` `my company gives notice under subsection (1) in respect of the person`)
        `the day on which my company was incorporated`
        (IF `my company has given notice to the registrar` THEN JUST (`s 279I notice given` OF `the day the notice was given`, `the notice specifies the date on which the change occurred`) ELSE NOTHING)
        `the day of the question`

-- s 279J(1): what must be given about a secretary who is an individual (the individual's name, any relevant former names, a service address).
@export Under section 279J(1), what is the required information about a secretary or joint secretary who is an individual?
GIVEN `the secretary or joint secretary is an individual` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the secretary (or joint secretary, or proposed one) an individual? (Answer no for a body corporate or a firm.)
GIVETH A MAYBE (LIST OF `s 279J(1) item of the required information about an individual`)
DECIDE `Under section 279J(1), what is the required information about a secretary or joint secretary who is an individual` IS
    `s 279J(1) the required information about a secretary or joint secretary who is an individual` `the kind of person the secretary is`
    WHERE
        `the kind of person the secretary is` MEANS
            IF `the secretary or joint secretary is an individual`
            THEN `an individual`
            ELSE `another body corporate incorporated in the United Kingdom` -- placeholder for "not an individual": s 279J(1) answers null for every kind of person but an individual

@export Under section 279J(1)(c), is the address I have given an acceptable statement of the service address (which may be stated as "The company's registered office")?
GIVEN `the statement of the service address` IS A STRING @desc What have you stated as the service address? (To state your company's registered office, write: The company's registered office; the Act's own apostrophe is accepted too)
      `the address is an address at which documents may be effectively served` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the address you have given an address at which documents may be effectively served on you?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 279J(1)(c), is the address I have given an acceptable statement of the service address (which may be stated as "The company's registered office")` IS
    `s 279J(1)(c) the statement given is an acceptable statement of the service address` `the statement as printed in the Act` (JUST `the address is an address at which documents may be effectively served`)
    WHERE
        -- the Act prints the phrase with a curly apostrophe; a person typing a straight one has stated the same words
        `the statement as printed in the Act` MEANS
            IF `the statement of the service address` EQUALS "The company's registered office"
            THEN "The company’s registered office"
            ELSE `the statement of the service address`
    -- (JUST ...) stands for s 1141: a "service address" means an address at which documents may be effectively served on that person

@export Under section 279J(2), is a name I used before a "relevant former name"?
GIVEN `the name is a name by which I was formerly known for business purposes` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it a name by which you were formerly known for business purposes?
      `I am a peer or am normally known by a British title` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are you a peer, or an individual normally known by a British title?
      `the name is the one I was known by before I adopted or succeeded to the title` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it the name by which you were known previous to the adoption of, or succession to, the title?
      `my date of birth` IS A DATE @desc What is your date of birth?
      `the day the name was changed or disused` IS A DATE @desc On what date was the name changed or disused?
      `the day of the question` IS A DATE @desc What is today's date?
      `the registrar is required to refrain from making the name available for public inspection or from disclosing it` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the registrar required, by regulations under section 1088(1)(a) or (b), to refrain from making the former name available for public inspection or from disclosing it (or both)?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 279J(2), is a name I used before a "relevant former name"` IS
    `s 279J(2) the former name is a relevant former name` `the name is a name by which I was formerly known for business purposes` `I am a peer or am normally known by a British title` `the name is the one I was known by before I adopted or succeeded to the title` `my date of birth` `the day the name was changed or disused` `the day of the question` (JUST `the registrar is required to refrain from making the name available for public inspection or from disclosing it`)
    -- (JUST ...) stands for the answer of s 1088

@export Under section 279J(3), is a name I used before a "former name"?
GIVEN `the name is a name by which I was formerly known for business purposes` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it a name by which you were formerly known for business purposes?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 279J(3), is a name I used before a "former name"` IS
    `s 279J(3) the name is a former name` `the name is a name by which I was formerly known for business purposes`

@export Under section 279J(4), is the requirement to give my name satisfied by giving my title instead of my forename and surname?
GIVEN `I am a peer or am usually known by a title` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are you a peer, or an individual usually known by a title?
      `the title is provided instead of my forename and surname` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the title being provided instead of your forename and surname?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 279J(4), is the requirement to give my name satisfied by giving my title instead of my forename and surname` IS
    `s 279J(4) the requirement to provide the name is satisfied by providing the title` `I am a peer or am usually known by a title` `the title is provided instead of my forename and surname`

-- s 279K(1): what must be given about a secretary that is a body corporate (or a firm that is a legal person). Whether the body is "a
-- limited company that is a UK-registered company" is s 3(1) and s 1158, answered here by the keel's functions.
@export Under section 279K(1), what is the required information about a secretary or joint secretary that is a body corporate or a firm that is a legal person?
GIVEN `the secretary is a body corporate, or a firm that is a legal person under the law by which it is governed` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the secretary (or joint secretary, or proposed one) a body corporate, or a firm that is a legal person under the law by which it is governed?
      `how the liability of the body's members is limited` IS A `Liability of members` @desc How is the liability of the body's members limited? Exactly one of: liability not limited; liability limited to the amount, if any, unpaid on the shares held; liability limited to the amount the members undertake to contribute on a winding up; liability limited in some other way by the constitution
      `the body is registered under the Companies Act 2006` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the body a company registered under the Companies Act 2006?
      `the body is an overseas company that has registered particulars under section 1046` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the body an overseas company that has registered particulars under section 1046?
      `the body or firm is entered in a register` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the body or firm entered in a register (for the particulars the section asks for, "if applicable")?
GIVETH A MAYBE (LIST OF `s 279K(1) item of the required information about a body corporate or firm`)
DECIDE `Under section 279K(1), what is the required information about a secretary or joint secretary that is a body corporate or a firm that is a legal person` IS
    `s 279K(1) the required information about a secretary or joint secretary that is a body corporate or a firm that is a legal person`
        `the secretary is a body corporate, or a firm that is a legal person under the law by which it is governed`
        (`s 3(1) the company is a limited company` `how the liability of the body's members is limited`)
        (`s 1158 the company is a UK-registered company` `the body is registered under the Companies Act 2006` `the body is an overseas company that has registered particulars under section 1046`)
        `the body or firm is entered in a register`

-- s 279L: a firm that is not a legal person, all of whose members are joint secretaries.
@export Under section 279L(1), does section 279L apply to a firm all of whose members are joint secretaries of my company?
GIVEN `all the members in the firm are joint secretaries (or proposed joint secretaries) of my company` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are all the members in the firm joint secretaries (or proposed joint secretaries) of your company?
      `the firm is not a legal person under the law by which it is governed` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the firm not a legal person under the law by which it is governed?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 279L(1), does section 279L apply to a firm all of whose members are joint secretaries of my company` IS
    `s 279L(1) this section applies` `all the members in the firm are joint secretaries (or proposed joint secretaries) of my company` `the firm is not a legal person under the law by which it is governed`

@export Under section 279L(2), is the requirement to provide the required information about the members as joint secretaries satisfied by providing the firm's information instead?
GIVEN `all the members in the firm are joint secretaries (or proposed joint secretaries) of my company` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are all the members in the firm joint secretaries (or proposed joint secretaries) of your company?
      `the firm is not a legal person under the law by which it is governed` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the firm not a legal person under the law by which it is governed?
      `the information provided is the information that would be required if the firm were a legal person and had been appointed as secretary` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the information you provide the information that would be required if the firm were a legal person and the firm had been appointed as secretary?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 279L(2), is the requirement to provide the required information about the members as joint secretaries satisfied by providing the firm's information instead` IS
    `s 279L(2) the requirement is satisfied by providing the firm's information instead` `all the members in the firm are joint secretaries (or proposed joint secretaries) of my company` `the firm is not a legal person under the law by which it is governed` `the information provided is the information that would be required if the firm were a legal person and had been appointed as secretary`

@export Under section 279L(2), what is the information that would be required about the firm if the firm were a legal person appointed as secretary?
GIVEN `the firm is entered in a register` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the firm entered in a register (for the particulars section 279K(1)(e)(ii) asks for, "if applicable")?
GIVETH A MAYBE (LIST OF `s 279K(1) item of the required information about a body corporate or firm`)
DECIDE `Under section 279L(2), what is the information that would be required about the firm if the firm were a legal person appointed as secretary` IS
    `s 279L(2) the information that would be required if the firm were a legal person and had been appointed as secretary` `the firm is entered in a register`

-- s 279M: the offence of failing to notify.
@export Under section 279M(1)(a), does my company commit an offence by failing, without reasonable excuse, to comply with section 279G, 279H or 279I?
GIVEN `my company has failed to comply with section 279G` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has your company failed to comply with section 279G (notice of a change in its secretary or joint secretary)?
      `my company has failed to comply with section 279H` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has your company failed to comply with section 279H (notice of a change in the required information about its secretary)?
      `my company has failed to comply with section 279I` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has your company failed to comply with section 279I (notice of changes occurring before its incorporation)?
      `my company had a reasonable excuse for the failure` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did your company have a reasonable excuse for the failure?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 279M(1)(a), does my company commit an offence by failing, without reasonable excuse, to comply with section 279G, 279H or 279I` IS
    `s 279M(1)(a) the company commits an offence`
        (`s 279M(1) the company has failed to comply with section 279G, 279H or 279I`
            (JUST `my company has failed to comply with section 279G`) (JUST `my company has failed to comply with section 279H`) (JUST `my company has failed to comply with section 279I`))
        `my company had a reasonable excuse for the failure`

@export Under section 279M(1)(b), do I commit an offence as an officer of my company that failed, without reasonable excuse, to comply with section 279G, 279H or 279I?
GIVEN `my company has failed to comply with section 279G` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has your company failed to comply with section 279G (notice of a change in its secretary or joint secretary)?
      `my company has failed to comply with section 279H` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has your company failed to comply with section 279H (notice of a change in the required information about its secretary)?
      `my company has failed to comply with section 279I` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has your company failed to comply with section 279I (notice of changes occurring before its incorporation)?
      `my company had a reasonable excuse for the failure` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did your company have a reasonable excuse for the failure?
      `I am a director of my company` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are you a director of your company?
      `I am a manager of my company` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are you a manager of your company?
      `I am the secretary of my company` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are you the secretary of your company?
      `I am a shadow director of my company` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are you a person in accordance with whose directions or instructions the directors of your company are accustomed to act (a shadow director)?
      `I am in default` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did you authorise or permit, participate in, or fail to take all reasonable steps to prevent, the failure of your company to comply?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 279M(1)(b), do I commit an offence as an officer of my company that failed, without reasonable excuse, to comply with section 279G, 279H or 279I` IS
    `s 279M(1)(b) the officer commits an offence`
        (`s 279M(1) the company has failed to comply with section 279G, 279H or 279I`
            (JUST `my company has failed to comply with section 279G`) (JUST `my company has failed to comply with section 279H`) (JUST `my company has failed to comply with section 279I`))
        `my company had a reasonable excuse for the failure`
        (`s 1173(1) the holder of the position is an officer of the body corporate` `my position in my company`)
        (JUST `I am a shadow director of my company`)
        (JUST `I am in default`)
    WHERE
        `my position in my company` MEANS
            IF `I am a director of my company`
            THEN `s 1173(1) director`
            ELSE IF `I am a manager of my company`
                 THEN `s 1173(1) manager`
                 ELSE IF `I am the secretary of my company`
                      THEN `s 1173(1) secretary`
                      ELSE `s 1173(1) another position`
    -- (JUST `I am a shadow director ...`) stands for s 251; (JUST `I am in default`) stands for s 1121 (the person states the facts s 1121(3) names)

@export Under section 279M(3), what penalty am I liable to on summary conviction of the offence?
GIVEN `where I am convicted` IS A `Mode of conviction` @desc Where are you convicted? Exactly one of: on summary conviction in England and Wales; on summary conviction in Scotland; on summary conviction in Northern Ireland; on summary conviction; on conviction on indictment
GIVETH A MAYBE Penalty
DECIDE `Under section 279M(3), what penalty am I liable to on summary conviction of the offence` IS
    `s 279M(3) the penalty on a person guilty of an offence under section 279M` `where I am convicted`

@export Under section 279M(3), what is the most I can be fined for the offence, in pounds?
GIVEN `where I am convicted` IS A `Mode of conviction` @desc Where are you convicted? Exactly one of: on summary conviction in England and Wales; on summary conviction in Scotland; on summary conviction in Northern Ireland; on summary conviction; on conviction on indictment
      `the amount in pounds that level 5 on the standard scale stands for` IS A NUMBER @desc How many pounds is level 5 on the standard scale?
GIVETH A MAYBE NUMBER
DECIDE `Under section 279M(3), what is the most I can be fined for the offence, in pounds` IS
    `s 279M(3) the most the person may be fined, in pounds` `where I am convicted` `the amount in pounds that level 5 on the standard scale stands for`

@export Under section 279M(3), what is the most the daily default fine can be for the offence, in pounds?
GIVEN `where I am convicted` IS A `Mode of conviction` @desc Where are you convicted? Exactly one of: on summary conviction in England and Wales; on summary conviction in Scotland; on summary conviction in Northern Ireland; on summary conviction; on conviction on indictment
      `the amount in pounds that level 5 on the standard scale stands for` IS A NUMBER @desc How many pounds is level 5 on the standard scale?
GIVETH A MAYBE NUMBER
DECIDE `Under section 279M(3), what is the most the daily default fine can be for the offence, in pounds` IS
    `s 279M(3) the most the daily default fine may be, in pounds` `where I am convicted` `the amount in pounds that level 5 on the standard scale stands for`

§§ `Person acting in dual capacity (s 280)`

-- s 280: a provision requiring or authorising a thing to be done by or to a director and the secretary is not satisfied by its being
-- done by or to the same person acting both as director and as, or in place of, the secretary. The answer is false where the section
-- applies ("is not satisfied") and null where it does not.
@export Under section 280, is a provision that requires or lets a thing be done by or to a director and the secretary satisfied by its being done by or to one person acting as both?
GIVEN `the provision requires or authorises a thing to be done by or to a director and the secretary of a company` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does the provision require or authorise a thing to be done by or to a director and the secretary of a company?
      `the thing is done by or to the same person` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the thing done by or to one and the same person?
      `that person acts both as director and as, or in place of, the secretary` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does that person act both as director and as, or in place of, the secretary?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 280, is a provision that requires or lets a thing be done by or to a director and the secretary satisfied by its being done by or to one person acting as both` IS
    `s 280 the provision is satisfied by the thing being done by or to the one person` `the provision requires or authorises a thing to be done by or to a director and the secretary of a company` `the thing is done by or to the same person` `that person acts both as director and as, or in place of, the secretary`

-- ====================================================================================================
-- seat questions from part coa7 (merged by the lead on 2026-11-12; unchanged text follows)
-- ====================================================================================================
-- coa7-seat.l4: the seat layer for Part 13 of the Companies Act 2006 (United Kingdom), ss 281 to 361
-- (resolutions and meetings), over the layer-1 modules coa7-ch1 .. coa7-ch7. Nothing here is new law: each question
-- builds the layer-1 records from plain facts and calls the layer-1 rule.
--
-- SEAT (assumed, not ruled: the Act is addressed to companies, so the individual is whoever stands in a company's
-- management or ownership): an individual who is, or is about to become, a director, a company secretary or a member
-- (shareholder) of a company registered under the Act, or who deals with one, asking on facts they can state what
-- the Act requires or lets them do, what rights they have against the company or its directors, what they must
-- disclose, file, approve or vote on and by when, and what follows (liability, offences, penalties) if it is not done.
-- Every question begins "Under section N," (the Act's own numbering) and says the scope its answer claims.
--
-- HOW TO READ AN ANSWER (the rule of 2026-10-29, assumed, not ruled by a lawyer): a question that answers a yes/no is
-- JUST TRUE (the Act says yes), JUST FALSE (the Act says no in its own words) or NOTHING (the Act does not decide the
-- case, or points outside the text). A "no" is never turned into "not covered" and "not covered" is never turned into
-- "no". A question about a number or a date answers JUST a value, or NOTHING where the Act does not say.
--
-- PLAIN INPUTS. Facts the person can state are yes/no, a number, a date, or a choice from a list. A fact that another
-- part of the Act decides (is the officer "in default" under s 1121; is the company "quoted", s 385; is the meeting
-- held under s 969) is asked as the plain yes/no the person can give, and is passed to the layer-1 rule as JUST that
-- answer; a person who does not know should not answer, and the layer-1 rule answers NOTHING for such a case.
-- A question that depends on a conclusion of ANOTHER section (s 339 on s 338, s 343(3) on s 344(1)) asks for
-- that conclusion as a yes/no, to be answered from the question under the other section. A question that depends on
-- a rule in its OWN section (s 292(1) on s 292(2), s 316(2) on s 316(1), s 319A(1) on s 319A(2), s 320(1) on s 320(3), s 326(1) on s 326(2), s 340(2) on s 340(1), s 344(1) on s 344(2), s 346(3) on s 346(4), s 357(3) on s 357(2) on s 357(1), s 360BA(1) on s 360BA(2)) asks the
-- plain facts and builds the helper rule's answer inside the question, so it can never be given a combination the rule
-- itself would not produce.
-- Fractions are written as decimals (0.05 is 5%). Hours are hours; "the hours of that period that fall on a day that is
-- not a working day" are asked as a number (the keel's working-day rule, s 1173(1), decides which days those are).
-- Amounts the Act leaves to regulations or orders (a level on the standard scale in pounds, the prescribed fee) are not
-- computed: a penalty answer gives the level and fraction, never a number of pounds.


§ `Part 13 of the Companies Act 2006 -- resolutions and meetings`
-- Seat: an individual who is or is about to become a director, company secretary or member of a company, or who deals with one.
-- The groups below follow the Act's chapters; each question says which section it asks about.

§§ `Chapter 1 -- how a resolution is passed and what votes count (ss 281 to 287)`
-- Asked of any member, director or secretary whose company has passed, or is about to pass, a resolution.

@export Has my private company's resolution been passed in a way the Act allows (section 281(1))?
GIVEN `the company is a public company` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is your company a public company? (A public company's certificate of incorporation says that it is one; any other company is a private company.)
      `the resolution was passed as a written resolution in accordance with Chapter 2` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Was the resolution passed as a written resolution in accordance with Chapter 2 of Part 13?
      `the resolution was passed at a meeting of the members to which Chapter 3 applies` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Was the resolution passed at a meeting of the members?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`Under section 281, has my private company's resolution been passed in a way the Act allows` MEANS
    `s 281(1) a private company's resolution is passed in a way this section allows` `the company is a public company` `the resolution was passed as a written resolution in accordance with Chapter 2` `the resolution was passed at a meeting of the members to which Chapter 3 applies`

@export Has my public company's resolution been passed in the way the Act requires (section 281(2))?
GIVEN `the company is a public company` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is your company a public company? (A public company's certificate of incorporation says that it is one; any other company is a private company.)
      `the resolution was passed at a meeting of the members to which Chapter 3 applies` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Was the resolution passed at a meeting of the members?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`Under section 281, has my public company's resolution been passed in the way the Act requires` MEANS
    `s 281(2) a public company's resolution is passed in the way this section requires` `the company is a public company` `the resolution was passed at a meeting of the members to which Chapter 3 applies`

@export Where a provision of the Companies Acts requires a resolution without saying what kind, what does the Act require (section 281(3))?
GIVEN `the provision requires a resolution` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does a provision of the Companies Acts require a resolution of the company or of its members?
      `the provision specifies what kind of resolution is required` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does that provision say what kind of resolution is required?
      `the company's articles require a higher majority or unanimity` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Do your company's articles require a higher majority (or unanimity)?
GIVETH A MAYBE `s 281(3) what is required`
`Under section 281, what kind of resolution does the Act require where the provision does not say` MEANS
    `s 281(3) what the Companies Acts require where the kind of resolution is not specified` `the provision requires a resolution` `the provision specifies what kind of resolution is required` `the company's articles require a higher majority or unanimity`

@export Was my ordinary resolution passed by a simple majority (section 282)?
GIVEN `how my resolution was passed` IS A `Way a resolution is passed` @desc How was the resolution passed: as a written resolution, at a meeting on a show of hands, or at a meeting on a poll?
      `votes or voting rights in favour` IS A NUMBER @desc How many votes (show of hands), or how much voting right (written resolution or poll), were in favour?
      `votes or voting rights against` IS A NUMBER @desc How many votes or how much voting right were against? (Leave 0 for a written resolution.)
      `total voting rights of eligible members` IS A NUMBER @desc For a written resolution: what is the total voting right of all the eligible members? (Leave 0 otherwise.)
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`Under section 282, was my ordinary resolution passed` MEANS
    `s 282(1) the resolution is an ordinary resolution` `how my resolution was passed` (`s 282 vote count` OF `votes or voting rights in favour`, `votes or voting rights against`, `total voting rights of eligible members`)

@export Was my special resolution passed by a majority of not less than 75% (section 283(1))?
GIVEN `how my resolution was passed` IS A `Way a resolution is passed` @desc How was the resolution passed: as a written resolution, at a meeting on a show of hands, or at a meeting on a poll?
      `votes or voting rights in favour` IS A NUMBER @desc How many votes (show of hands), or how much voting right (written resolution or poll), were in favour?
      `votes or voting rights against` IS A NUMBER @desc How many votes or how much voting right were against? (Leave 0 for a written resolution.)
      `total voting rights of eligible members` IS A NUMBER @desc For a written resolution: what is the total voting right of all the eligible members? (Leave 0 otherwise.)
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`Under section 283, was my special resolution passed` MEANS
    `s 283(1) the resolution is a special resolution` `how my resolution was passed` (`s 282 vote count` OF `votes or voting rights in favour`, `votes or voting rights against`, `total voting rights of eligible members`)

@export Is my private company's written resolution barred from being a special resolution because it did not say it was proposed as one (section 283(3)(a))?
GIVEN `the company is a public company` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is your company a public company? (A public company's certificate of incorporation says that it is one; any other company is a private company.)
      `the resolution was passed as a written resolution` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Was the resolution passed as a written resolution?
      `the resolution stated that it was proposed as a special resolution` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did the resolution state that it was proposed as a special resolution?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`Under section 283, is my private company's written resolution barred from being a special resolution` MEANS
    `s 283(3)(a) the written resolution of the private company is not a special resolution` `the company is a public company` `the resolution was passed as a written resolution` `the resolution stated that it was proposed as a special resolution`

@export Is a resolution passed at a meeting barred from being a special resolution because the notice did not include its text and say it was proposed as one (section 283(6)(a))?
GIVEN `the resolution was passed at a meeting` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Was the resolution passed at a meeting?
      `the notice of the meeting included the text of the resolution` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did the notice of the meeting include the text of the resolution?
      `the notice of the meeting specified the intention to propose the resolution as a special resolution` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did the notice of the meeting specify the intention to propose the resolution as a special resolution?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`Under section 283, is the resolution passed at the meeting barred from being a special resolution` MEANS
    `s 283(6)(a) the resolution passed at the meeting is not a special resolution` `the resolution was passed at a meeting` `the notice of the meeting included the text of the resolution` `the notice of the meeting specified the intention to propose the resolution as a special resolution`

@export How many votes do I have, as a member, on a poll at a meeting (section 284(3))?
GIVEN `the articles contain a provision on the number of votes` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Do your company's articles contain a provision on the number of votes a member has?
      `the company has a share capital` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does your company have a share capital?
      `shares held by the member` IS A NUMBER @desc How many shares do you hold?
      `pounds of stock held by the member` IS A NUMBER @desc How many pounds of stock do you hold? (Each £10 of stock counts as one vote.)
GIVETH A MAYBE NUMBER
`Under section 284, how many votes do I have on a poll` MEANS
    `s 284(3) the member's votes on a poll` `the articles contain a provision on the number of votes` `the company has a share capital` `shares held by the member` `pounds of stock held by the member`

@export How many votes do I have, as a member, on a show of hands at a meeting (section 284(2))?
GIVEN `the articles contain a provision on the number of votes` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Do your company's articles contain a provision on the number of votes a member has?
      `the member is present in person` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are you present in person at the meeting?
GIVETH A MAYBE NUMBER
`Under section 284, how many votes do I have on a show of hands` MEANS
    `s 284(2) the member's votes on a show of hands` `the articles contain a provision on the number of votes` `the member is present in person`

@export How many votes do I have, as a member, on a written resolution (section 284(1))?
GIVEN `the articles contain a provision on the number of votes` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Do your company's articles contain a provision on the number of votes a member has?
      `the company has a share capital` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does your company have a share capital?
      `shares held by the member` IS A NUMBER @desc How many shares do you hold?
      `pounds of stock held by the member` IS A NUMBER @desc How many pounds of stock do you hold? (Each £10 of stock counts as one vote.)
GIVETH A MAYBE NUMBER
`Under section 284, how many votes do I have on a written resolution` MEANS
    `s 284(1) the member's votes on a written resolution` `the articles contain a provision on the number of votes` `the company has a share capital` `shares held by the member` `pounds of stock held by the member`

@export How many votes does a proxy have on a show of hands (section 285(1))?
GIVEN `the proxy is present` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the proxy present at the meeting?
      `the proxy has been duly appointed by one or more members entitled to vote on the resolution` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has the proxy been duly appointed by one or more members entitled to vote on the resolution?
GIVETH A MAYBE NUMBER
`Under section 285, how many votes does my proxy have on a show of hands` MEANS
    `s 285(1) the proxy's votes on a show of hands` `the proxy is present` `the proxy has been duly appointed by one or more members entitled to vote on the resolution`

@export Does a proxy appointed by several members have one vote for and one vote against on a show of hands (section 285(2))?
GIVEN `members who duly appointed the proxy and are entitled to vote on the resolution` IS A NUMBER @desc How many members entitled to vote duly appointed the proxy?
      `of those members, the number who instructed the proxy to vote for the resolution` IS A NUMBER @desc Of those members, how many instructed the proxy to vote for the resolution?
      `of those members, the number who instructed the proxy to vote against the resolution` IS A NUMBER @desc Of those members, how many instructed the proxy to vote against the resolution?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`Under section 285, does my proxy have one vote for and one vote against the resolution` MEANS
    `s 285(2) the proxy has one vote for and one vote against the resolution` `members who duly appointed the proxy and are entitled to vote on the resolution` `of those members, the number who instructed the proxy to vote for the resolution` `of those members, the number who instructed the proxy to vote against the resolution`

-- RECONCILED 2026-11-12 (seat audit, direction mismatch): was named `Under section 285, do my proxies together have more voting rights than I would in person`; the old name asked a comparison of fact (TRUE for more) but s 285(4) answers whether subsection (3) authorises it (JUST FALSE for more).
@export Does section 285(3) authorise my proxies, taken together, to exercise more voting rights on a poll than I could in person (section 285(4))?
GIVEN `the member appoints more than one proxy` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Do you appoint more than one proxy?
      `voting rights the proxies exercise taken together` IS A NUMBER @desc How many voting rights do your proxies exercise taken together?
      `voting rights the member could exercise in person` IS A NUMBER @desc How many voting rights could you exercise in person?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`Under section 285, does section 285(3) authorise my proxies together to exercise more voting rights than I could in person` MEANS
    `s 285(4) subsection (3) authorises the proxies together to exercise these rights` `the member appoints more than one proxy` `voting rights the proxies exercise taken together` `voting rights the member could exercise in person`

@export Where my private company's articles give a different number of votes on a poll and on a written resolution, how many votes do I have on the poll (section 285A)?
GIVEN `the company is a public company` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is your company a public company? (A public company's certificate of incorporation says that it is one; any other company is a private company.)
      `the resolution is required or authorised by an enactment` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the resolution one required or authorised by an enactment?
      `the articles give a different number of votes on a poll and on a written resolution` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Do your company's articles give a member a different number of votes on a poll and on a written resolution?
      `votes the member has on the written resolution` IS A NUMBER @desc How many votes do you have on the written resolution?
GIVETH A MAYBE NUMBER
`Under section 285A, how many votes do I have on a poll where my private company's articles give a different number` MEANS
    `s 285A the member's votes on a poll` `the company is a public company` `the resolution is required or authorised by an enactment` `the articles give a different number of votes on a poll and on a written resolution` `votes the member has on the written resolution`

@export Where shares are held jointly, may the company count my vote (section 286(1))?
GIVEN `the holder whose vote is in question` IS A STRING @desc What is your name, as it appears in the register of members?
      `the articles contain a provision on the votes of joint holders` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Do your company's articles contain a provision on the votes of joint holders?
      `joint holders in the order their names appear in the register of members` IS A LIST OF STRING @desc List the joint holders' names in the order they appear in the register of members.
      `joint holders who vote` IS A LIST OF STRING @desc List the names of the joint holders who vote.
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`Under section 286, may the company count my vote as a joint holder of shares` MEANS
    `s 286(1) the holder's own vote may be counted by the company` `the holder whose vote is in question` `the articles contain a provision on the votes of joint holders` `joint holders in the order their names appear in the register of members` `joint holders who vote`

@export Does Chapter 1 of Part 13 leave unaffected a provision of my company's articles on how objections to a person's entitlement to vote are made and decided (section 287)?
GIVEN `matter` IS A `s 287 matter` @desc What is the matter: an articles provision requiring an objection to a person's entitlement to vote to be made as the articles say, with its determination final and conclusive; or the grounds on which such a determination may be questioned in legal proceedings; or another matter?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`Under section 287, does Chapter 1 leave an articles provision on objections to votes unaffected` MEANS
    `s 287 this Chapter leaves the matter unaffected` `matter`

§§ `Chapter 2 -- written resolutions of private companies (ss 288 to 300)`
-- Asked of a member or director of a private company that is proposing or voting on a written resolution.

@export Is my resolution one that may not be passed as a written resolution (section 288(2): removing a director or an auditor before the end of the term of office)?
GIVEN `s 168 the resolution removes a director before the expiration of his period of office` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it a resolution under section 168 removing a director before the expiration of his period of office?
      `s 510 the resolution removes an auditor before the expiration of his term of office` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it a resolution under section 510 removing an auditor before the expiration of his term of office?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`Under section 288, is my resolution one that may not be passed as a written resolution` MEANS
    `s 288(2) the resolution may not be passed as a written resolution` (JUST `s 168 the resolution removes a director before the expiration of his period of office`) (JUST `s 510 the resolution removes an auditor before the expiration of his term of office`)

@export Am I an eligible member for a written resolution (section 289(1))?
GIVEN `the resolution is proposed as a written resolution of a private company` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the resolution proposed as a written resolution of a private company?
      `the member would have been entitled to vote on the resolution on the circulation date` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Would you have been entitled to vote on the resolution on the date copies were first sent or submitted to members (the circulation date)?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`Under section 289, am I an eligible member for the written resolution` MEANS
    `s 289(1) the member is an eligible member` `the resolution is proposed as a written resolution of a private company` `the member would have been entitled to vote on the resolution on the circulation date`

@export What is the circulation date of a written resolution, the first day on which copies were sent or submitted to members (section 290)?
GIVEN `the first day on which a copy was sent or submitted to a member` IS A DATE @desc On what date was the first copy of the resolution sent or submitted to a member?
      `the last day on which a copy was sent or submitted to a member` IS A DATE @desc On what date was the last copy of the resolution sent or submitted to a member? (The same date if all were sent on one day.)
GIVETH A MAYBE DATE
`Under section 290, what is the circulation date of the written resolution` MEANS
    `s 290 the circulation date` (LIST `the first day on which a copy was sent or submitted to a member`, `the last day on which a copy was sent or submitted to a member`)

@export Has the company sent or submitted a copy of the directors' written resolution to every eligible member (section 291(2))?
GIVEN `the resolution was proposed as a written resolution by the directors of the company` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Was the resolution proposed as a written resolution by the directors of the company?
      `eligible members` IS A NUMBER @desc How many eligible members are there?
      `eligible members to whom a copy of the resolution was sent or submitted` IS A NUMBER @desc To how many eligible members was a copy sent or submitted?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`Under section 291, has the company sent every eligible member a copy of the directors' written resolution` MEANS
    `s 291(2) the company has sent or submitted a copy of the resolution to every eligible member` `the resolution was proposed as a written resolution by the directors of the company` `eligible members` `eligible members to whom a copy of the resolution was sent or submitted`

@export Was the copy of the directors' resolution accompanied by a statement of how to signify agreement and of the date by which it must be passed (section 291(4))?
GIVEN `the copy is accompanied by a statement informing the member how to signify agreement to the resolution` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did the statement tell the member how to signify agreement to the resolution?
      `the copy is accompanied by a statement informing the member of the date by which the resolution must be passed if it is not to lapse` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did the statement tell the member the date by which the resolution must be passed if it is not to lapse?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`Under section 291, was the copy of the resolution accompanied by the statement the Act requires` MEANS
    `s 291(4) the copy is accompanied by the statement this subsection requires` `the copy is accompanied by a statement informing the member how to signify agreement to the resolution` `the copy is accompanied by a statement informing the member of the date by which the resolution must be passed if it is not to lapse`

@export Am I, as an officer of the company, guilty of an offence because the company did not circulate the directors' written resolution properly (section 291(5))?
GIVEN `the company is in default in complying with this section` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the company in default in complying with section 291?
      `s 1121 the officer is in default` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are you an officer of the company who is in default (section 1121)?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`Under section 291, am I guilty of an offence as an officer of the company in default` MEANS
    `s 291(5) the officer of the company commits an offence` `the company is in default in complying with this section` (JUST `s 1121 the officer is in default`)

@export What penalty could I face if I am convicted of the offence under section 291 (section 291(6))?
GIVEN `how the person is convicted` IS A `Mode of conviction` @desc How will the person be convicted: on conviction on indictment, on summary conviction in England and Wales, in Scotland, in Northern Ireland, or on summary conviction without saying where?
GIVETH A MAYBE Penalty
`Under section 291, what penalty could I face on conviction` MEANS
    `s 291(6) the penalty on conviction` `how the person is convicted`

@export May the members of my private company require the company to circulate a resolution as a written resolution (section 292(1))?
GIVEN `the company is a public company` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is your company a public company? (A public company's certificate of incorporation says that it is one; any other company is a private company.)
      `the resolution would, if passed, be ineffective` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Would the resolution, if passed, be ineffective (whether by reason of inconsistency with any enactment or the company's constitution or otherwise)?
      `the resolution is defamatory of any person` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the resolution defamatory of any person?
      `the resolution is frivolous or vexatious` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the resolution frivolous or vexatious?
      `the resolution is proposed to be moved as a written resolution` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the resolution proposed to be moved as a written resolution?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`Under section 292, may the members of my private company require it to circulate a resolution` MEANS
    `s 292(1) the members may require the company to circulate the resolution` `the company is a public company` (`s 292(2) the resolution may properly be moved as a written resolution` `the resolution would, if passed, be ineffective` `the resolution is defamatory of any person` `the resolution is frivolous or vexatious`) `the resolution is proposed to be moved as a written resolution`

@export Is the company required to circulate the members' resolution and any statement, given the percentage of voting rights that asked (section 292(4))?
GIVEN `fraction of the total voting rights of all members entitled to vote on the resolution held by the members who have requested circulation` IS A NUMBER @desc What fraction of the total voting rights of all members entitled to vote on the resolution do the members who asked for circulation hold? (0.05 is 5%.)
      `the requisite percentage` IS A NUMBER @desc What is the requisite percentage as a fraction? (0.05 unless your articles specify a lower one.)
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`Under section 292, is the company required to circulate the members' resolution` MEANS
    `s 292(4) the company is required to circulate the resolution and any accompanying statement` `fraction of the total voting rights of all members entitled to vote on the resolution held by the members who have requested circulation` `the requisite percentage`

@export Did the company send or submit the copies of the members' resolution not more than 21 days after it became subject to the requirement (section 293(3))?
GIVEN `the date the company became subject to the requirement under section 292 to circulate the resolution` IS A DATE @desc On what date did the company become subject to the requirement under section 292 to circulate the resolution?
      `the date the copies (or the first of them) were sent or submitted` IS A DATE @desc On what date were the copies (or the first of them) sent or submitted?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`Under section 293, did the company circulate the members' resolution in time` MEANS
    `s 293(3) the copies were sent or submitted in time` `the date the company became subject to the requirement under section 292 to circulate the resolution` `the date the copies (or the first of them) were sent or submitted`

@export Am I, as an officer of the company, guilty of an offence because the company did not circulate the members' written resolution properly (section 293(5))?
GIVEN `the company is in default in complying with this section` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the company in default in complying with section 293?
      `s 1121 the officer is in default` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are you an officer of the company who is in default (section 1121)?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`Under section 293, am I guilty of an offence as an officer of the company in default` MEANS
    `s 293(5) the officer of the company commits an offence` `the company is in default in complying with this section` (JUST `s 1121 the officer is in default`)

@export Must the members who requested the circulation of a resolution pay the company's expenses of circulating it (section 294(1))?
GIVEN `the company has resolved otherwise` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has the company resolved that it will bear the expenses?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`Under section 294, must the members who requested the circulation pay the company's expenses` MEANS
    `s 294(1) the expenses of complying with section 293 must be paid by the members who requested the circulation` `the company has resolved otherwise`

-- RECONCILED 2026-11-12 (seat audit, subject mismatch): was named `Under section 294, is the company bound to circulate the resolution without a deposit`; the old name said "without a deposit", but the function answers whether the company is bound given what it resolved or what was deposited (JUST FALSE when neither).
@export Is the company bound to circulate the members' resolution, given whether it resolved to meet the expenses or a sum was deposited or tendered for them (section 294(2))?
GIVEN `the company has previously resolved to meet the expenses` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has the company previously resolved to meet the expenses?
      `there is deposited with or tendered to the company a sum reasonably sufficient to meet its expenses` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has a sum reasonably sufficient to meet the company's expenses been deposited with or tendered to it?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`Under section 294, is the company bound to circulate the resolution, given any deposit or its own resolution to meet the expenses` MEANS
    `s 294(2) the company is bound to comply with section 293` `the company has previously resolved to meet the expenses` `there is deposited with or tendered to the company a sum reasonably sufficient to meet its expenses`

@export Is the company excused from circulating a members' statement because the court found the right to circulate it is being abused (section 295(1))?
GIVEN `an application was made by the company or by another person who claims to be aggrieved` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Was an application made by the company or by another person who claims to be aggrieved?
      `the court is satisfied that the rights conferred by sections 292 and 293 are being abused` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the court satisfied that the rights conferred by sections 292 and 293 are being abused?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`Under section 295, is the company excused from circulating the members' statement` MEANS
    `s 295(1) the company is not required to circulate the members' statement` `an application was made by the company or by another person who claims to be aggrieved` `the court is satisfied that the rights conferred by sections 292 and 293 are being abused`

@export Have I signified my agreement to a proposed written resolution (section 296(1))?
GIVEN `the company has received a document from the member or from someone acting on his behalf` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has the company received a document from you (or from someone acting on your behalf)?
      `the document is authenticated` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the document authenticated?
      `the document identifies the resolution to which it relates` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does the document identify the resolution to which it relates?
      `the document indicates the member's agreement to the resolution` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does the document indicate your agreement to the resolution?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`Under section 296, have I signified my agreement to the written resolution` MEANS
    `s 296(1) the member has signified agreement to the proposed written resolution` `the company has received a document from the member or from someone acting on his behalf` `the document is authenticated` `the document identifies the resolution to which it relates` `the document indicates the member's agreement to the resolution`

@export May I revoke my agreement to a written resolution once I have signified it (section 296(3))?
GIVEN `the member's agreement has been signified` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Have you already signified your agreement to the resolution?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`Under section 296, may I revoke my agreement to a written resolution` MEANS
    `s 296(3) the member's agreement may be revoked` `the member's agreement has been signified`

@export What is the last day on which members can agree to a written resolution before it lapses (section 297(1))?
GIVEN `the circulation date` IS A DATE @desc On what date were copies of the resolution first sent or submitted to members?
      `the company's articles specify a period` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Do your company's articles specify the period for agreeing to a written resolution?
      `the day on which the period specified in the company's articles ends` IS A DATE @desc If so, on what date does that period end? (Ignored if the articles specify no period.)
GIVETH A DATE
`Under section 297, what is the last day for agreeing to the written resolution` MEANS
    `s 297(1) the last day of the period for agreeing to the written resolution` `the circulation date` (IF `the company's articles specify a period` THEN JUST `the day on which the period specified in the company's articles ends` ELSE NOTHING)

@export Is my agreement to a written resolution ineffective because I signified it after the period ended (section 297(2))?
GIVEN `the day on which the member's agreement was signified` IS A DATE @desc On what date did you signify your agreement?
      `the last day of the period` IS A DATE @desc What is the last day of the period for agreeing to the resolution?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`Under section 297, is my agreement ineffective because I signified it too late` MEANS
    `s 297(2) the member's agreement is ineffective` `the day on which the member's agreement was signified` `the last day of the period`

@export Where the company gave an electronic address in a document with a proposed written resolution, is it deemed to agree that documents about that resolution may be sent there (section 298(1))?
GIVEN `the company has given an electronic address in a document containing or accompanying the proposed written resolution` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did the company give an electronic address in a document containing or accompanying the proposed written resolution?
      `the document or information relates to that resolution` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does the document or information relate to that resolution?
      `the sending is within any conditions or limitations specified in the document` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the sending within any conditions or limitations specified in the document?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`Under section 298, is the company deemed to accept documents about a written resolution by electronic means` MEANS
    `s 298(1) the company is deemed to have agreed that the document or information may be sent by electronic means to the address` `the company has given an electronic address in a document containing or accompanying the proposed written resolution` `the document or information relates to that resolution` `the sending is within any conditions or limitations specified in the document`

@export Is a written resolution (or statement) sent to me by means of a website not validly sent because it was not available on the website throughout the period (section 299(2))?
GIVEN `the company sends the resolution or statement to a person by means of a website` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did the company send the resolution or statement to you by means of a website?
      `the resolution is available on the website throughout the period beginning with the circulation date and ending on the date on which it lapses under section 297` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Was the resolution available on the website throughout the period beginning with the circulation date and ending on the date it lapses under section 297?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`Under section 299, is a resolution sent to me by website not validly sent` MEANS
    `s 299(2) the resolution or statement is not validly sent for the purposes of this Chapter` `the company sends the resolution or statement to a person by means of a website` `the resolution is available on the website throughout the period beginning with the circulation date and ending on the date on which it lapses under section 297`

@export Is a provision of my private company's articles void because it stops a resolution required by an enactment being passed as a written resolution (section 300)?
GIVEN `the company is a public company` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is your company a public company? (A public company's certificate of incorporation says that it is one; any other company is a private company.)
      `the provision would have the effect that a resolution required by or otherwise provided for in an enactment could not be proposed and passed as a written resolution` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Would the provision have the effect that a resolution required by or provided for in an enactment could not be proposed and passed as a written resolution?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`Under section 300, is a provision of my private company's articles void` MEANS
    `s 300 the provision of the articles is void` `the company is a public company` `the provision would have the effect that a resolution required by or otherwise provided for in an enactment could not be proposed and passed as a written resolution`

§§ `Chapter 3 -- resolutions at meetings (ss 301 to 335)`
-- Asked of a member, director or company secretary who is calling, attending, or voting at a general meeting.

@export Was a resolution validly passed at a general meeting (section 301)?
GIVEN `notice of the meeting and of the resolution is given in accordance with this Chapter (and, where relevant, Chapter 4) and the company's articles` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Was notice of the meeting and of the resolution given in accordance with Chapters 3 and 4 and the company's articles?
      `the meeting is held and conducted in accordance with this Chapter (and, where relevant, Chapter 4) and the company's articles` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Was the meeting held and conducted in accordance with Chapters 3 and 4 and the company's articles?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`Under section 301, was the resolution validly passed at the general meeting` MEANS
    `s 301 the resolution is validly passed at the general meeting` `notice of the meeting and of the resolution is given in accordance with this Chapter (and, where relevant, Chapter 4) and the company's articles` `the meeting is held and conducted in accordance with this Chapter (and, where relevant, Chapter 4) and the company's articles`

@export May the directors of a company call a general meeting (section 302)?
GIVEN `the person calling the meeting is a director of the company acting as one of its directors` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are you a director of the company, acting as one of its directors?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`Under section 302, may I call a general meeting as a director` MEANS
    `s 302 the directors may call a general meeting` `the person calling the meeting is a director of the company acting as one of its directors`

@export Are the directors required to call a general meeting because enough members asked for one (section 303(2))?
GIVEN `the company has a share capital` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does your company have a share capital?
      `paid-up capital held by the requesting members that carries the right of voting at general meetings (excluding treasury shares)` IS A NUMBER @desc How much paid-up capital that carries the right to vote at general meetings (excluding treasury shares) do the members who asked for the meeting hold?
      `paid-up capital of the company that carries the right of voting at general meetings (excluding treasury shares)` IS A NUMBER @desc How much paid-up capital carrying the right to vote at general meetings (excluding treasury shares) does the company have in all?
      `voting rights represented by the requesting members` IS A NUMBER @desc For a company without a share capital: how much voting right do the requesting members represent?
      `total voting rights of all the members having a right to vote at general meetings` IS A NUMBER @desc For a company without a share capital: what is the total voting right of all the members who may vote at general meetings?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`Under section 303, are the directors required to call a general meeting on our requests` MEANS
    `s 303(2) the directors are required to call a general meeting` `the company has a share capital` `paid-up capital held by the requesting members that carries the right of voting at general meetings (excluding treasury shares)` `paid-up capital of the company that carries the right of voting at general meetings (excluding treasury shares)` `voting rights represented by the requesting members` `total voting rights of all the members having a right to vote at general meetings`

@export May our resolution properly be moved at the general meeting (section 303(5))?
GIVEN `the resolution would, if passed, be ineffective (whether by reason of inconsistency with any enactment or the company's constitution or otherwise)` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Would the resolution, if passed, be ineffective (for example by inconsistency with an enactment or the company's constitution)?
      `the resolution is defamatory of any person` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the resolution defamatory of any person?
      `the resolution is frivolous or vexatious` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the resolution frivolous or vexatious?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`Under section 303, may our resolution properly be moved at the meeting` MEANS
    `s 303(5) the resolution may properly be moved at the meeting` `the resolution would, if passed, be ineffective (whether by reason of inconsistency with any enactment or the company's constitution or otherwise)` `the resolution is defamatory of any person` `the resolution is frivolous or vexatious`

@export Did the directors call the meeting members required within 21 days (section 304(1)(a))?
GIVEN `the date on which the directors became subject to the requirement under section 303` IS A DATE @desc On what date did the directors become subject to the requirement under section 303?
      `the date on which the directors called the meeting` IS A DATE @desc On what date did the directors call the meeting?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`Under section 304, did the directors call the meeting we required in time` MEANS
    `s 304(1)(a) the directors called the meeting in time` `the date on which the directors became subject to the requirement under section 303` `the date on which the directors called the meeting`

@export Is the meeting members required to be held on a date not more than 28 days after the date of the notice convening it (section 304(1)(b))?
GIVEN `the date of the notice convening the meeting` IS A DATE @desc What is the date of the notice convening the meeting?
      `the date on which the meeting is to be held` IS A DATE @desc On what date is the meeting to be held?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`Under section 304, is the meeting we required to be held in time` MEANS
    `s 304(1)(b) the meeting is to be held in time` `the date of the notice convening the meeting` `the date on which the meeting is to be held`

@export May the members who requested a meeting call it themselves because the directors did not (section 305(1))?
GIVEN `the directors are required under section 303 to call a meeting` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are the directors required under section 303 to call a meeting?
      `the directors do not call the meeting in accordance with section 304` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did the directors fail to call the meeting in accordance with section 304?
      `voting rights represented by the members who call the meeting` IS A NUMBER @desc How much voting right do the members who will call the meeting represent?
      `total voting rights of all the members who requested the meeting` IS A NUMBER @desc What is the total voting right of all the members who requested the meeting?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`Under section 305, may we call the general meeting ourselves` MEANS
    `s 305(1) the members may themselves call a general meeting` `the directors are required under section 303 to call a meeting` `the directors do not call the meeting in accordance with section 304` `voting rights represented by the members who call the meeting` `total voting rights of all the members who requested the meeting`

@export Is a meeting called by the members for a date not more than three months after the directors became subject to the requirement (section 305(3))?
GIVEN `the date on which the directors became subject to the requirement to call a meeting` IS A DATE @desc On what date did the directors become subject to the requirement to call a meeting?
      `the date for which the meeting is called` IS A DATE @desc For what date is the meeting called?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`Under section 305, is the meeting we call ourselves called for a date in time` MEANS
    `s 305(3) the meeting is called for a date in time` `the date on which the directors became subject to the requirement to call a meeting` `the date for which the meeting is called`

@export Must the company reimburse the reasonable expenses I incurred in calling a meeting because the directors failed to (section 305(6))?
GIVEN `the expenses were incurred by the members requesting the meeting by reason of the failure of the directors duly to call a meeting` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Were the expenses incurred by the members requesting the meeting by reason of the failure of the directors duly to call a meeting?
      `the expenses are reasonable` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are the expenses reasonable?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`Under section 305, must the company reimburse my expenses of calling the meeting` MEANS
    `s 305(6) the company must reimburse the expenses` `the expenses were incurred by the members requesting the meeting by reason of the failure of the directors duly to call a meeting` `the expenses are reasonable`

@export May the court order a meeting to be called, held and conducted in any manner it thinks fit, on my application (section 306)?
GIVEN `it is impracticable to call a meeting of the company in any manner in which meetings may be called` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it impracticable to call a meeting of the company in any manner in which meetings of that company may be called?
      `it is impracticable to conduct the meeting in the manner prescribed by the articles or the Act` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it impracticable to conduct the meeting in the manner prescribed by the company's articles or the Act?
      `who asks the court` IS A `s 306(2) who moves the court` @desc Who asks the court: a director of the company, a member who would be entitled to vote at the meeting, or someone else?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`Under section 306, may the court order a meeting on my application` MEANS
    `s 306(2) the court may order a meeting to be called, held and conducted in any manner the court thinks fit` (`s 306(1) this section applies` `it is impracticable to call a meeting of the company in any manner in which meetings may be called` `it is impracticable to conduct the meeting in the manner prescribed by the articles or the Act`) `who asks the court`

@export How many days of notice must a general meeting of a private company be called by (section 307(1))?
GIVEN `the company is a public company` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is your company a public company? (A public company's certificate of incorporation says that it is one; any other company is a private company.)
      `the meeting is an adjourned meeting` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it an adjourned meeting?
GIVETH A MAYBE NUMBER
`Under section 307, how many days of notice must be given of a general meeting of my private company` MEANS
    `s 307(1) the days of notice required of a general meeting of a private company` `the company is a public company` `the meeting is an adjourned meeting`

@export How many days of notice must a general meeting of a public company be called by (section 307(2))?
GIVEN `the company is a public company` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is your company a public company? (A public company's certificate of incorporation says that it is one; any other company is a private company.)
      `the meeting is an adjourned meeting` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it an adjourned meeting?
      `the meeting is an annual general meeting` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it an annual general meeting?
GIVETH A MAYBE NUMBER
`Under section 307, how many days of notice must be given of a general meeting of my public company` MEANS
    `s 307(2) the days of notice required of a general meeting of a public company` `the company is a public company` `the meeting is an adjourned meeting` `the meeting is an annual general meeting`

@export Is the notice I was given of the general meeting long enough, counting clear days (sections 307(1) to (3) and 360)?
GIVEN `the days of notice required` IS A NUMBER @desc How many days of notice does the Act (or your company's longer articles) require?
      `the day on which notice of the meeting is given` IS A DATE @desc On what date was notice of the meeting given?
      `the day of the meeting` IS A DATE @desc On what date is the meeting?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`Under section 307, is the notice given long enough` MEANS
    `s 307(3) the notice given is at least the notice required` `the days of notice required` `the day on which notice of the meeting is given` `the day of the meeting`

@export May the general meeting be called by shorter notice because the members agreed (section 307(4))?
GIVEN `shorter notice is agreed by the members` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Do the members agree to shorter notice?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`Under section 307, may the meeting be called by shorter notice` MEANS
    `s 307(4) the meeting may be called by shorter notice than otherwise required` `shorter notice is agreed by the members`

@export Have enough members agreed to shorter notice of the general meeting (section 307(5))?
GIVEN `the company has a share capital` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does your company have a share capital?
      `members having a right to attend and vote at the meeting` IS A NUMBER @desc How many members have a right to attend and vote at the meeting?
      `of those members, the number who agree to the shorter notice` IS A NUMBER @desc How many of them agree to the shorter notice?
      `nominal value of the shares held by the agreeing members` IS A NUMBER @desc What is the nominal value of the shares the agreeing members hold?
      `nominal value of all the shares giving a right to attend and vote at the meeting (excluding treasury shares)` IS A NUMBER @desc What is the nominal value of all the shares giving a right to attend and vote (excluding treasury shares)?
      `voting rights represented by the agreeing members` IS A NUMBER @desc For a company without a share capital: how much voting right do the agreeing members represent?
      `total voting rights at the meeting of all the members` IS A NUMBER @desc For a company without a share capital: what is the total voting right at the meeting?
      `the requisite percentage` IS A NUMBER @desc What is the requisite percentage as a fraction? (0.9 is 90%.)
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`Under section 307, have enough members agreed to shorter notice` MEANS
    `s 307(5) the shorter notice has been agreed to as this subsection requires` `the company has a share capital` `members having a right to attend and vote at the meeting` `of those members, the number who agree to the shorter notice` `nominal value of the shares held by the agreeing members` `nominal value of all the shares giving a right to attend and vote at the meeting (excluding treasury shares)` `voting rights represented by the agreeing members` `total voting rights at the meeting of all the members` `the requisite percentage`

@export What percentage of the shares (or voting rights) must agree to shorter notice (section 307(6))?
GIVEN `the company is a public company` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is your company a public company? (A public company's certificate of incorporation says that it is one; any other company is a private company.)
      `the company's articles specify a higher percentage` IS A BOOLEAN @desc For a private company: do your articles specify a percentage higher than 90% (not above 95%)?
      `that percentage as a fraction` IS A NUMBER @desc If so, what is it as a fraction? (0.92 is 92%; ignored if your articles specify none.)
GIVETH A MAYBE NUMBER
`Under section 307, what is the requisite percentage for agreeing to shorter notice` MEANS
    `s 307(6) the requisite percentage` `the company is a public company` (IF `the company's articles specify a higher percentage` THEN JUST `that percentage as a fraction` ELSE NOTHING)

@export How many days of notice must a general meeting of a traded company be called by (section 307A(1))?
GIVEN `the meeting is an adjourned meeting` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it an adjourned meeting?
      `s 307A(2) condition A is met` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is condition A met: the meeting is not an annual general meeting (section 307A(2))?
      `s 307A(3) condition B is met` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is condition B met: the company offers every member with voting shares a facility to vote by electronic means or to appoint a proxy by a website (section 307A(3))?
      `condition C is met (s 307A(4), or s 307A(5) for a company that has not yet held an annual general meeting)` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is condition C met: a special resolution reducing the notice to not less than 14 days was passed at the last AGM or since (section 307A(4) or (5))?
GIVETH A MAYBE NUMBER
`Under section 307A, how many days of notice must a traded company give of a general meeting` MEANS
    `s 307A(1) the days of notice required of a general meeting of a traded company` `the meeting is an adjourned meeting` `s 307A(2) condition A is met` `s 307A(3) condition B is met` `condition C is met (s 307A(4), or s 307A(5) for a company that has not yet held an annual general meeting)`

@export May notice of a general meeting be given in this way (section 308)?
GIVEN `manner` IS A `s 308 manner of giving notice` @desc How is the notice given: in hard copy form, in electronic form, by means of a website, partly by one means and partly by another, or in some other manner?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`Under section 308, may notice of the general meeting be given in this way` MEANS
    `s 308 the notice of the general meeting is given in a manner this section allows` `manner`

@export Does the notification I was sent about a notice published on a website meet the requirements of section 309(2)?
GIVEN `the notification states that it concerns a notice of a company meeting` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does the notification state that it concerns a notice of a company meeting?
      `the notification specifies the place, date and time of the meeting` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does the notification specify the place, date and time of the meeting?
      `the company is a public company` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the company a public company?
      `the notification states whether the meeting will be an annual general meeting` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does the notification state whether the meeting will be an annual general meeting?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`Under section 309, did the notification of a notice on a website meet the requirements` MEANS
    `s 309(2) the notification to the member meets the requirements of this subsection` `the notification states that it concerns a notice of a company meeting` `the notification specifies the place, date and time of the meeting` `the company is a public company` `the notification states whether the meeting will be an annual general meeting`

@export Was a notice of a meeting given by means of a website available on the website throughout the period section 309(3) requires?
GIVEN `the date of the notification` IS A DATE @desc On what date was the notification given?
      `the first day on which the notice was available on the website` IS A DATE @desc On what date did the notice first become available on the website?
      `the last day on which the notice was available on the website` IS A DATE @desc What was the last day on which the notice was available on the website?
      `the day of the conclusion of the meeting` IS A DATE @desc On what day did the meeting conclude?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`Under section 309, was the notice available on the website for the whole period required` MEANS
    `s 309(3) the notice was available on the website throughout the period this subsection requires` `the date of the notification` `the first day on which the notice was available on the website` `the last day on which the notice was available on the website` `the day of the conclusion of the meeting`

@export Is a notice of a meeting given by means of a website not validly given because it was not given in accordance with section 309 (section 309(1))?
GIVEN `the notice is given in accordance with this section` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Was the notice given in accordance with section 309?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`Under section 309, is a notice given by website not validly given` MEANS
    `s 309(1) notice given by means of a website is not validly given` `the notice is given in accordance with this section`

@export Must notice of a general meeting be sent to me (section 310(1))?
GIVEN `the person is a member of the company` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are you a member of the company?
      `the person is a director` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are you a director of the company?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`Under section 310, must notice of the general meeting be sent to me` MEANS
    `s 310(1) notice of a general meeting must be sent to the person` `the person is a member of the company` `the person is a director`

@export Does the notice of the general meeting state what section 311(1) requires: the time, date and place?
GIVEN `the notice states the time and date of the meeting` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does the notice state the time and date of the meeting?
      `the notice states the place of the meeting` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does the notice state the place of the meeting?
