@export Where more than one person authorised by a corporation purport to exercise a power over the same shares, how is the power treated (section 323(4))?
GIVEN `subsection (3) applies` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does section 323(3) apply (a vote on a show of hands)?
      `more than one authorised person purport to exercise a power under subsection (2) in respect of the same shares` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Do more than one authorised person purport to exercise a power in respect of the same shares?
      `they purport to exercise the power in the same way as each other` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Do they purport to exercise the power in the same way as each other?
GIVETH A MAYBE `s 323(4) how the power is treated`
`Under section 323, how is the power treated where my corporation's representatives disagree` MEANS
    `s 323(4) the power is treated` `subsection (3) applies` `more than one authorised person purport to exercise a power under subsection (2) in respect of the same shares` `they purport to exercise the power in the same way as each other`

@export May I appoint more than one proxy to attend and vote at a meeting (section 324(2))?
GIVEN `the company has a share capital` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does your company have a share capital?
      `each proxy is appointed to exercise the rights attached to a different share or shares held by the member (or a different £10, or multiple of £10, of stock)` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is each proxy appointed to exercise the rights attached to a different share or shares (or a different £10, or multiple of £10, of stock) that you hold?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`Under section 324, may I appoint more than one proxy` MEANS
    `s 324(2) the member may appoint more than one proxy in relation to the meeting` `the company has a share capital` `each proxy is appointed to exercise the rights attached to a different share or shares held by the member (or a different £10, or multiple of £10, of stock)`

@export Has a proxy voted in accordance with the instructions the member gave (section 324A)?
GIVEN `the member gave the proxy instructions` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did the member give the proxy instructions?
      `the proxy voted in accordance with those instructions` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did the proxy vote in accordance with those instructions?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`Under section 324A, has my proxy complied with my instructions` MEANS
    `s 324A the proxy has complied with the instructions given by the member` `the member gave the proxy instructions` `the proxy voted in accordance with those instructions`

@export Does the notice calling the meeting contain the statement of my rights to appoint proxies (section 325(1))?
GIVEN `the notice appears with reasonable prominence in every notice calling the meeting` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does the statement appear with reasonable prominence in every notice calling the meeting?
      `the statement informs the member of his rights under section 324` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does it inform the member of his rights under section 324?
      `the articles confer more extensive rights to appoint more than one proxy` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Do the articles confer more extensive rights to appoint more than one proxy?
      `the statement informs the member of those more extensive rights` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does it inform the member of those more extensive rights?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`Under section 325, does the notice of the meeting contain the statement of my proxy rights` MEANS
    `s 325(1) the notice contains the statement this subsection requires` `the notice appears with reasonable prominence in every notice calling the meeting` `the statement informs the member of his rights under section 324` `the articles confer more extensive rights to appoint more than one proxy` `the statement informs the member of those more extensive rights`

-- RECONCILED 2026-11-12 (seat audit, subject mismatch): was named `Under section 326, were the proxy invitations issued in breach of the Act`; the old name said breach of the Act, but s 326(1) answers whether the invitations contravene that subsection only.
@export Do the company-sponsored invitations to appoint proxies contravene section 326(1)?
GIVEN `invitations are issued at the company's expense to appoint a specified person as proxy` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Were invitations issued at the company's expense to members to appoint as proxy a specified person or persons?
      `the invitations are issued to all members entitled to vote at the meeting` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Were the invitations issued to all members entitled to vote at the meeting?
      `a form naming the proxy, or a list of willing persons, is issued to a member at his request` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is a form of appointment naming the proxy, or a list of persons willing to act, issued to a member at his request?
      `the form or list is available on request to all members entitled to vote` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the form or list available on request to all members entitled to vote at the meeting?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`Under section 326, do the company's proxy invitations contravene subsection (1)` MEANS
    `s 326(1) the invitations contravene this subsection` `invitations are issued at the company's expense to appoint a specified person as proxy` `the invitations are issued to all members entitled to vote at the meeting` (`s 326(2) subsection (1) is not contravened` `a form naming the proxy, or a list of willing persons, is issued to a member at his request` `the form or list is available on request to all members entitled to vote`)

@export Is a provision of my company's articles void because it requires a proxy appointment to be received earlier than the Act allows (section 327(2))?
GIVEN `case` IS A `s 327(2) when the document must be received` @desc Is it for a meeting or adjourned meeting (48 hours), or a poll taken more than 48 hours after it was demanded (24 hours), or another case?
      `hours before the relevant time that the articles require the appointment or document to be received` IS A NUMBER @desc How many hours before the relevant time do the articles require the appointment or document to be received?
      `of those hours, the hours that fall on a day that is not a working day` IS A NUMBER @desc Of those hours, how many fall on a day that is not a working day?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`Under section 327, is a provision of the articles on the time for receiving a proxy appointment void` MEANS
    `s 327(2) the provision of the articles is void` `case` `hours before the relevant time that the articles require the appointment or document to be received` `of those hours, the hours that fall on a day that is not a working day`

@export May a proxy be elected chairman of a general meeting by a resolution passed at the meeting (section 328(1))?
GIVEN `the person is a proxy` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the person a proxy?
      `the person is elected chairman of the general meeting by a resolution of the company passed at the meeting` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the person elected chairman by a resolution of the company passed at the meeting?
      `the company's articles state who may or who may not be chairman` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Do the company's articles state who may or may not be chairman?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`Under section 328, may my proxy be elected chairman of the general meeting` MEANS
    `s 328(1) the proxy may be elected chairman of the general meeting` `the person is a proxy` `the person is elected chairman of the general meeting by a resolution of the company passed at the meeting` `the company's articles state who may or who may not be chairman`

@export Is a proxy authorised to demand, or join in demanding, a poll on a matter he is appointed to vote on (section 329(1))?
GIVEN `the person is appointed as proxy to vote on the matter at a meeting of the company` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are you appointed as proxy to vote on the matter at a meeting of the company?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`Under section 329, may my proxy demand a poll` MEANS
    `s 329(1) the proxy is authorised to demand, or join in demanding, a poll on the matter` `the person is appointed as proxy to vote on the matter at a meeting of the company`

-- RECONCILED 2026-11-12 (seat audit, direction mismatch): was named `Under section 330, does the termination of my proxy's authority affect his vote`; the old name asked whether the termination affects the vote, but s 330(3) answers that it does NOT affect its validity (JUST TRUE means valid).
@export Does the termination of a proxy's authority leave his vote valid (section 330(3))?
GIVEN `the company receives notice of the termination before the commencement of the meeting or adjourned meeting at which the vote is given` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did the company receive notice of the termination before the commencement of the meeting or adjourned meeting at which the vote is given?
      `the vote is given on a poll taken more than 48 hours after it was demanded` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the vote given on a poll taken more than 48 hours after it was demanded?
      `the company receives notice of the termination before the time appointed for taking the poll` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did the company receive notice of the termination before the time appointed for taking the poll?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`Under section 330, does the termination of my proxy's authority leave the vote my proxy gave valid` MEANS
    `s 330(3) the termination of the authority of the person to act as proxy does not affect the validity of the vote` `the company receives notice of the termination before the commencement of the meeting or adjourned meeting at which the vote is given` `the vote is given on a poll taken more than 48 hours after it was demanded` `the company receives notice of the termination before the time appointed for taking the poll`

-- RECONCILED 2026-11-12 (seat audit, direction mismatch): was named `Under section 331, may the articles give members or proxies more rights than sections 324 to 330`; the old name asked a permission (may the articles) but s 331 answers whether sections 324 to 330 prevent it, a bar (JUST FALSE means they do not).
@export Do sections 324 to 330 prevent my company's articles from giving members or proxies more extensive rights than those sections give (section 331)?
GIVEN `the articles confer more extensive rights on members or proxies than are conferred by sections 324 to 330` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Do the articles confer more extensive rights on members or proxies than sections 324 to 330 confer?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`Under section 331, do sections 324 to 330 prevent my company's articles from giving members or proxies more extensive rights` MEANS
    `s 331 sections 324 to 330 prevent the articles from conferring the rights` `the articles confer more extensive rights on members or proxies than are conferred by sections 324 to 330`

@export On what date is a resolution passed at an adjourned meeting treated as passed (section 332)?
GIVEN `the resolution is passed at an adjourned meeting of the company` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Was the resolution passed at an adjourned meeting of the company?
      `the date on which the resolution was in fact passed` IS A DATE @desc On what date was the resolution in fact passed?
GIVETH A MAYBE DATE
`Under section 332, on what date is a resolution passed at an adjourned meeting treated as passed` MEANS
    `s 332 the date on which the resolution is treated as having been passed` `the resolution is passed at an adjourned meeting of the company` `the date on which the resolution was in fact passed`

@export Where the company gave an electronic address in a notice calling a meeting, is it deemed to agree that documents about the meeting may be sent there (section 333(1))?
GIVEN `the company has given an electronic address in a notice calling a meeting` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did the company give an electronic address in a notice calling a meeting?
      `the document or information relates to proceedings at the meeting` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does the document or information relate to proceedings at the meeting?
      `the sending is within any conditions or limitations specified in the notice` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the sending within any conditions or limitations specified in the notice?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`Under section 333, is the company deemed to accept documents about the meeting by electronic means` MEANS
    `s 333(1) the company is deemed to have agreed that the document or information may be sent by electronic means to the address` `the company has given an electronic address in a notice calling a meeting` `the document or information relates to proceedings at the meeting` `the sending is within any conditions or limitations specified in the notice`

@export Has a traded company provided an electronic address for the receipt of documents about proxies for a general meeting (section 333A(1))?
GIVEN `the company is a traded company` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the company a traded company?
      `the company has provided an electronic address for the receipt of any document or information relating to proxies for the general meeting` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has the company provided an electronic address for the receipt of any document or information relating to proxies for the general meeting?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`Under section 333A, has the traded company provided an electronic address for proxies` MEANS
    `s 333A(1) the traded company has provided an electronic address` `the company is a traded company` `the company has provided an electronic address for the receipt of any document or information relating to proxies for the general meeting`

@export Was the traded company's electronic address for proxies provided in one of the two ways section 333A(2) allows?
GIVEN `the address was given when sending out an instrument of proxy for the purposes of the meeting or issuing an invitation to appoint a proxy for those purposes` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Was the address given when sending out an instrument of proxy, or issuing an invitation to appoint a proxy, for the meeting?
      `the address was made available, throughout the period beginning with the first date on which notice of the meeting was given and ending with the conclusion of the meeting, on the website on which the information required by section 311A(1) is made available` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Was the address made available on the website (where the section 311A(1) information is published) throughout the period from the first date of notice of the meeting to its conclusion?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`Under section 333A, was the electronic address provided in the way the Act requires` MEANS
    `s 333A(2) the address was provided in a way this subsection requires` `the address was given when sending out an instrument of proxy for the purposes of the meeting or issuing an invitation to appoint a proxy for those purposes` `the address was made available, throughout the period beginning with the first date on which notice of the meeting was given and ending with the conclusion of the meeting, on the website on which the information required by section 311A(1) is made available`

@export Where a traded company provided an electronic address for proxies, is it deemed to agree that documents about proxies may be sent there (section 333A(3))?
GIVEN `the company has provided an electronic address under this section` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has the company provided an electronic address under section 333A?
      `the document or information relates to proxies for the meeting` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does the document or information relate to proxies for the meeting?
      `the sending is within any limitations specified by the company when providing the address` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the sending within any limitations the company specified when providing the address?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`Under section 333A, is the traded company deemed to accept documents about proxies by electronic means` MEANS
    `s 333A(3) the company is deemed to have agreed that the document or information may be sent by electronic means to the address` `the company has provided an electronic address under this section` `the document or information relates to proxies for the meeting` `the sending is within any limitations specified by the company when providing the address`

@export Does a provision of Chapter 3 apply to a meeting of holders of a class of shares (section 334(1))?
GIVEN `provision` IS A STRING @desc Which provision of the Chapter (for example "303", "318", "321")?
      `the meeting is a variation of class rights meeting` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the meeting a variation of class rights meeting?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`Under section 334, does a provision of Chapter 3 apply to a meeting of holders of a class of shares` MEANS
    `s 334(1) the provision of this Chapter applies (with necessary modifications) to a meeting of holders of a class of shares` `provision` `the meeting is a variation of class rights meeting`

@export Is there a quorum at a meeting to vary the rights of a class of shares (section 334(4))?
GIVEN `the meeting is a variation of class rights meeting` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the meeting a variation of class rights meeting?
      `the meeting is an adjourned meeting` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it an adjourned meeting?
      `persons present holding shares of the class in question` IS A NUMBER @desc How many persons present hold shares of the class?
      `nominal value of the issued shares of the class held by the persons present` IS A NUMBER @desc What is the nominal value of the issued shares of the class they hold?
      `nominal value of the issued shares of the class in question (excluding treasury shares)` IS A NUMBER @desc What is the nominal value of all the issued shares of the class (excluding treasury shares)?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`Under section 334, is there a quorum at a variation of class rights meeting of shareholders` MEANS
    `s 334(4) the quorum for the variation of class rights meeting is present` `the meeting is a variation of class rights meeting` `the meeting is an adjourned meeting` `persons present holding shares of the class in question` `nominal value of the issued shares of the class held by the persons present` `nominal value of the issued shares of the class in question (excluding treasury shares)`

@export Is there a quorum at a meeting to vary the rights of a class of members of a company without a share capital (section 335(4))?
GIVEN `the meeting is a variation of class rights meeting` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the meeting a variation of class rights meeting?
      `the meeting is an adjourned meeting` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it an adjourned meeting?
      `members of the class present (in person or by proxy)` IS A NUMBER @desc How many members of the class are present (in person or by proxy)?
      `voting rights of the class represented by the members of the class present` IS A NUMBER @desc How much of the voting rights of the class do they represent?
      `total voting rights of the class` IS A NUMBER @desc What is the total voting right of the class?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`Under section 335, is there a quorum at a variation of class rights meeting of members` MEANS
    `s 335(4) the quorum for the variation of class rights meeting is present` `the meeting is a variation of class rights meeting` `the meeting is an adjourned meeting` `members of the class present (in person or by proxy)` `voting rights of the class represented by the members of the class present` `total voting rights of the class`

§§ `Chapter 4 -- annual general meetings of public companies and traded companies (ss 336 to 340B)`
-- Asked of a director or secretary of a public company (or a private traded company), or of a member who wants an item on its annual general meeting agenda.

@export Was my public company's annual general meeting held within the period of 6 months beginning with the day after its accounting reference date (section 336(1))?
GIVEN `the company is a public company` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is your company a public company? (A public company's certificate of incorporation says that it is one; any other company is a private company.)
      `the accounting reference date` IS A DATE @desc What is your company's accounting reference date?
      `the day on which the general meeting was held as the annual general meeting` IS A DATE @desc On what date was the general meeting held as the annual general meeting?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`Under section 336, was my public company's annual general meeting held in time` MEANS
    `s 336(1) the annual general meeting was held in the period of 6 months` `the company is a public company` `the accounting reference date` `the day on which the general meeting was held as the annual general meeting`

@export Was my private company that is a traded company's annual general meeting held within 9 months beginning with the day after its accounting reference date (section 336(1A))?
GIVEN `the company is a private company that is a traded company` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is your company a private company that is a traded company?
      `the accounting reference date` IS A DATE @desc What is your company's accounting reference date?
      `the day on which the general meeting was held as the annual general meeting` IS A DATE @desc On what date was the general meeting held as the annual general meeting?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`Under section 336, was my private traded company's annual general meeting held in time` MEANS
    `s 336(1A) the annual general meeting was held in the period of 9 months` `the company is a private company that is a traded company` `the accounting reference date` `the day on which the general meeting was held as the annual general meeting`

@export Am I, as an officer of the company, guilty of an offence because the company did not hold its annual general meeting in time (section 336(3))?
GIVEN `the company fails to comply with subsection (1) or (1A)` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did the company fail to comply with section 336(1) or (1A)?
      `s 1121 the officer is in default` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are you an officer of the company who is in default (section 1121)?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`Under section 336, am I guilty of an offence as an officer of the company in default` MEANS
    `s 336(3) the officer of the company commits an offence` `the company fails to comply with subsection (1) or (1A)` (JUST `s 1121 the officer is in default`)

@export What penalty could I face if convicted of the offence under section 336 (section 336(4))?
GIVEN `how the person is convicted` IS A `Mode of conviction` @desc How will the person be convicted: on conviction on indictment, on summary conviction in England and Wales, in Scotland, in Northern Ireland, or on summary conviction without saying where?
GIVETH A MAYBE Penalty
`Under section 336, what penalty could I face on conviction` MEANS
    `s 336(4) the penalty on conviction` `how the person is convicted`

@export Does the notice calling a traded company's annual general meeting include the statements of the members' rights to require a resolution or a matter (section 337(3))?
GIVEN `the company is a traded company` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the company a traded company?
      `the company is a public company` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the company a public company?
      `the day on which notice calling the annual general meeting is given` IS A DATE @desc On what date was the notice calling the annual general meeting given?
      `the day of the annual general meeting` IS A DATE @desc On what date is the annual general meeting?
      `the notice includes a statement of the right under section 338 to require the company to give notice of a resolution to be moved at the meeting` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does the notice include a statement of the right under section 338 to require notice of a resolution?
      `the notice includes a statement of the right under section 338A to require the company to include a matter in the business to be dealt with at the meeting` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does the notice include a statement of the right under section 338A to require a matter to be included in the business?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`Under section 337, does the notice of a traded company's annual general meeting include the statements of members' rights` MEANS
    `s 337(3) the notice includes the statements this subsection requires` `the company is a traded company` `the company is a public company` `the day on which notice calling the annual general meeting is given` `the day of the annual general meeting` `the notice includes a statement of the right under section 338 to require the company to give notice of a resolution to be moved at the meeting` `the notice includes a statement of the right under section 338A to require the company to include a matter in the business to be dealt with at the meeting`

@export Is my public company required to give notice of the members' resolution for its annual general meeting (section 338(3))?
GIVEN `voting rights represented by the requesting members who have a right to vote on the resolution at the annual general meeting` IS A NUMBER @desc How much voting right do the requesting members who have a right to vote on the resolution at the AGM represent?
      `total voting rights of all the members who have a right to vote on the resolution at the annual general meeting (excluding treasury shares)` IS A NUMBER @desc What is the total voting right of all the members who have a right to vote on the resolution at the AGM (excluding treasury shares)?
      `number of requesting members who have a right to vote on the resolution at the annual general meeting and hold shares in the company` IS A NUMBER @desc How many requesting members have a right to vote on the resolution and hold shares in the company?
      `total sum paid up on the shares those members hold` IS A NUMBER @desc What is the total sum paid up on the shares those members hold, in pounds?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`Under section 338, is the public company required to give notice of our resolution for the annual general meeting` MEANS
    `s 338(3) the company is required to give notice of the resolution` `voting rights represented by the requesting members who have a right to vote on the resolution at the annual general meeting` `total voting rights of all the members who have a right to vote on the resolution at the annual general meeting (excluding treasury shares)` `number of requesting members who have a right to vote on the resolution at the annual general meeting and hold shares in the company` `total sum paid up on the shares those members hold`

-- RECONCILED 2026-11-12 (seat audit, subject mismatch): was named `Under section 338, did we make our request for the annual general meeting resolution in time`; the old name asked only about time, but s 338(4) answers whether the request meets all the requirements of the subsection.
@export Does our request to give notice of a resolution at the annual general meeting meet the Act's requirements, including the time (section 338(4))?
GIVEN `the request is in hard copy form or in electronic form` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the request in hard copy form or electronic form?
      `the request identifies the resolution of which notice is to be given` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does the request identify the resolution of which notice is to be given?
      `the request is authenticated by the person or persons making it` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the request authenticated by the person or persons making it?
      `the day on which the company received the request` IS A DATE @desc On what date did the company receive the request?
      `the day of the annual general meeting to which the requests relate` IS A DATE @desc On what date is the annual general meeting?
      `the day on which notice of that meeting is given` IS A DATE @desc On what date is notice of that meeting given?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`Under section 338, does our request for the annual general meeting resolution meet the requirements, including the time` MEANS
    `s 338(4) the request meets the requirements of this subsection` `the request is in hard copy form or in electronic form` `the request identifies the resolution of which notice is to be given` `the request is authenticated by the person or persons making it` `the day on which the company received the request` `the day of the annual general meeting to which the requests relate` `the day on which notice of that meeting is given`

@export Is a traded company required to include the members' matter in the business to be dealt with at its annual general meeting (section 338A(3))?
GIVEN `voting rights represented by the requesting members who have a right to vote at the meeting` IS A NUMBER @desc How much voting right do the requesting members who have a right to vote at the meeting represent?
      `total voting rights of all the members who have a right to vote at the meeting` IS A NUMBER @desc What is the total voting right of all the members who have a right to vote at the meeting?
      `number of requesting members who have a right to vote at the meeting and hold shares in the company` IS A NUMBER @desc How many requesting members have a right to vote at the meeting and hold shares in the company?
      `total sum paid up on the shares those members hold` IS A NUMBER @desc What is the total sum paid up on the shares those members hold, in pounds?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`Under section 338A, is the traded company required to include our matter in the annual general meeting business` MEANS
    `s 338A(3) the company is required to include the matter` `voting rights represented by the requesting members who have a right to vote at the meeting` `total voting rights of all the members who have a right to vote at the meeting` `number of requesting members who have a right to vote at the meeting and hold shares in the company` `total sum paid up on the shares those members hold`

@export Did the company receive our request to include a matter in the AGM business in time (section 338A(5))?
GIVEN `the day on which the company received the request` IS A DATE @desc On what date did the company receive the request?
      `the day of the meeting` IS A DATE @desc On what date is the meeting?
      `the day on which notice of the meeting is given` IS A DATE @desc On what date is notice of the meeting given?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`Under section 338A, did we make our request to include a matter in time` MEANS
    `s 338A(5) the request was received in time` `the day on which the company received the request` `the day of the meeting` `the day on which notice of the meeting is given`

@export Must the company send each member entitled to receive notice a copy of the members' resolution for the annual general meeting (section 339(1))?
GIVEN `the company is required under section 338 to give notice of the resolution` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the company required under section 338 to give notice of the resolution?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`Under section 339, must the company send us a copy of the members' resolution for the annual general meeting` MEANS
    `s 339(1) the company must send a copy of the resolution to each member entitled to receive notice of the annual general meeting` (JUST `the company is required under section 338 to give notice of the resolution`)

-- RECONCILED 2026-11-12 (seat audit, subject mismatch): was named `Under section 340, is the public company bound to circulate our resolution without a deposit`; the old name said "without a deposit", but the function answers whether the company is bound given what it resolved or what was deposited (JUST FALSE when neither).
@export Is the company bound to circulate the members' AGM resolution, given whether it resolved to meet the expenses or a sum was deposited or tendered for them (section 340(2))?
GIVEN `the day on which requests sufficient to require the company to circulate the resolution were received` IS A DATE @desc On what date did the company receive requests sufficient to require it to circulate the resolution?
      `the last day of the financial year preceding the meeting` IS A DATE @desc What was the last day of the financial year before the meeting?
      `the company has previously resolved to meet the expenses` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has the company previously resolved to meet the expenses?
      `a sum reasonably sufficient was deposited or tendered` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Was a sum reasonably sufficient to meet the company's expenses deposited with or tendered to it?
      `the day on which the sum was deposited or tendered` IS A DATE @desc On what date was the sum deposited or tendered?
      `the day of the annual general meeting` IS A DATE @desc On what date is the annual general meeting?
      `the day on which notice of that meeting is given` IS A DATE @desc On what date is notice of that meeting given?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`Under section 340, is the public company bound to circulate our resolution, given any deposit or its own resolution to meet the expenses` MEANS
    `s 340(2) the company is bound to comply with section 339` (`s 340(1) the expenses need not be paid by the members who requested the circulation` `the day on which requests sufficient to require the company to circulate the resolution were received` `the last day of the financial year preceding the meeting` EQUALS JUST TRUE) `the company has previously resolved to meet the expenses` `a sum reasonably sufficient was deposited or tendered` `the day on which the sum was deposited or tendered` `the day of the annual general meeting` `the day on which notice of that meeting is given`

-- RECONCILED 2026-11-12 (seat audit, subject mismatch): was named `Under section 340A, has the traded company given notice of our matter and published it`; the old name asked about notice and publication, but s 340A(1)(a) answers notice only (publication is s 340A(1)(b), its own question).
@export Has the traded company given notice of the members' matter to each member in the way section 340A(1)(a) requires?
GIVEN `notice of the matter is given in the same manner as notice of the meeting` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Was notice of the matter given in the same manner as notice of the meeting?
      `notice of the matter is given at the same time as, or as soon as reasonably practicable after, the company gives notice of the meeting` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Was notice of the matter given at the same time as, or as soon as reasonably practicable after, the company gave notice of the meeting?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`Under section 340A, has the traded company given notice of our matter in the way the Act requires` MEANS
    `s 340A(1)(a) the notice of the matter was given as this paragraph requires` `notice of the matter is given in the same manner as notice of the meeting` `notice of the matter is given at the same time as, or as soon as reasonably practicable after, the company gives notice of the meeting`

@export Has the traded company published the members' matter on the same website as the section 311A information (section 340A(1)(b))?
GIVEN `the matter is published on the same website as that on which the company published the information required by section 311A` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the matter published on the same website as that on which the company published the information required by section 311A?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`Under section 340A, has the traded company published our matter on its website` MEANS
    `s 340A(1)(b) the matter was published as this paragraph requires` `the matter is published on the same website as that on which the company published the information required by section 311A`

@export Am I, as an officer of the company, guilty of an offence because the company did not circulate the members' matter (section 340A(3))?
GIVEN `the company is in default in complying with this section` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the company in default in complying with section 340A?
      `s 1121 the officer is in default` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are you an officer of the company who is in default (section 1121)?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`Under section 340A, am I guilty of an offence as an officer of the company in default` MEANS
    `s 340A(3) the officer of the company commits an offence` `the company is in default in complying with this section` (JUST `s 1121 the officer is in default`)

@export What penalty could I face if convicted of the offence under section 340A (section 340A(4))?
GIVEN `how the person is convicted` IS A `Mode of conviction` @desc How will the person be convicted: on conviction on indictment, on summary conviction in England and Wales, in Scotland, in Northern Ireland, or on summary conviction without saying where?
GIVETH A MAYBE Penalty
`Under section 340A, what penalty could I face on conviction` MEANS
    `s 340A(4) the penalty on conviction` `how the person is convicted`

-- RECONCILED 2026-11-12 (seat audit, subject mismatch): was named `Under section 340B, is the traded company bound to circulate our matter without a deposit`; the old name said "without a deposit", but the function answers whether the company is bound given what it resolved or what was deposited (JUST FALSE when neither).
@export Is the traded company bound to circulate the members' AGM matter, given whether it resolved to meet the expenses or a sum was deposited or tendered for them (section 340B(2))?
GIVEN `the day on which requests sufficient to require the company to include the matter were received` IS A DATE @desc On what date did the company receive requests sufficient to require it to include the matter?
      `the last day of the financial year preceding the meeting` IS A DATE @desc What was the last day of the financial year before the meeting?
      `the company has previously resolved to meet the expenses` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has the company previously resolved to meet the expenses?
      `a sum reasonably sufficient was deposited or tendered` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Was a sum reasonably sufficient to meet the company's expenses deposited with or tendered to it?
      `the day on which the sum was deposited or tendered` IS A DATE @desc On what date was the sum deposited or tendered?
      `the day of the annual general meeting` IS A DATE @desc On what date is the annual general meeting?
      `the day on which notice of that meeting is given` IS A DATE @desc On what date is notice of that meeting given?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`Under section 340B, is the traded company bound to circulate our matter, given any deposit or its own resolution to meet the expenses` MEANS
    `s 340B(2) the company is bound to comply with section 340A` (`s 340B(1) the expenses need not be paid by the members who requested the inclusion of the matter` `the day on which requests sufficient to require the company to include the matter were received` `the last day of the financial year preceding the meeting` EQUALS JUST TRUE) `the company has previously resolved to meet the expenses` `a sum reasonably sufficient was deposited or tendered` `the day on which the sum was deposited or tendered` `the day of the annual general meeting` `the day on which notice of that meeting is given`

§§ `Chapter 5 -- quoted companies and traded companies: poll results and independent reports (ss 341 to 354)`
-- Asked of a director or secretary of a quoted or traded company, of a member of one who wants an independent report on a poll, or of a person asked to act as the independent assessor.

@export Has a quoted company that is not a traded company made the results of a poll available on a website (section 341(1))?
GIVEN `s 361 the company is a quoted company` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the company a quoted company (Part 15, section 385)?
      `the company is a traded company` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the company a traded company?
      `a poll is taken at a general meeting of the company` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Was a poll taken at a general meeting of the company?
      `the date of the meeting is made available on a website` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the date of the meeting made available on a website?
      `the text of the resolution or a description of the subject matter of the poll is made available on a website` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are the text of the resolution (or a description of the subject matter of the poll) made available on a website?
      `the number of votes cast in favour is made available on a website` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the number of votes cast in favour made available on a website?
      `the number of votes cast against is made available on a website` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the number of votes cast against made available on a website?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`Under section 341, has the quoted company published the results of the poll on a website` MEANS
    `s 341(1) the quoted company has made the information available on a website` (JUST `s 361 the company is a quoted company`) `the company is a traded company` `a poll is taken at a general meeting of the company` `the date of the meeting is made available on a website` `the text of the resolution or a description of the subject matter of the poll is made available on a website` `the number of votes cast in favour is made available on a website` `the number of votes cast against is made available on a website`

@export Did the traded company make the poll results available on a website by the end of 16 days beginning with the day of the meeting (or, if later, the end of the first working day after the result was declared) (section 341(1B))?
GIVEN `the day of the meeting` IS A DATE @desc On what date was the meeting?
      `the first working day after the day on which the result of the poll is declared` IS A DATE @desc What is the first working day after the day on which the result of the poll was declared?
      `the day on which the information was made available on a website` IS A DATE @desc On what date was the information made available on a website?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`Under section 341, has the traded company published the results of the poll in time` MEANS
    `s 341(1B) the traded company has complied with subsection (1A) in time` `the day of the meeting` `the first working day after the day on which the result of the poll is declared` `the day on which the information was made available on a website`

@export Am I, as an officer of the company, guilty of an offence because the company did not publish the poll results (section 341(3))?
GIVEN `the company is in default in complying with this section (or with the requirements of section 353 as it applies for the purposes of this section)` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the company in default in complying with section 341 (or with the requirements of section 353 as it applies for this purpose)?
      `s 1121 the officer is in default` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are you an officer of the company who is in default (section 1121)?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`Under section 341, am I guilty of an offence as an officer of the company in default` MEANS
    `s 341(3) the officer of the company commits an offence` `the company is in default in complying with this section (or with the requirements of section 353 as it applies for the purposes of this section)` (JUST `s 1121 the officer is in default`)

-- RECONCILED 2026-11-12 (seat audit, subject mismatch): was named `Under section 342, may the members of a quoted company require an independent report on a poll`; the old name asked about the members' power (s 342(1)), but the function answers s 342(2), whether the directors are required.
@export Are the directors required to obtain an independent report on a poll because enough members asked for one (section 342(2))?
GIVEN `voting rights represented by the requesting members who have a right to vote on the matter to which the poll relates` IS A NUMBER @desc How much voting right do the requesting members who have a right to vote on the matter to which the poll relates represent?
      `total voting rights of all the members who have a right to vote on the matter to which the poll relates (excluding treasury shares)` IS A NUMBER @desc What is the total voting right of all the members who have a right to vote on that matter (excluding treasury shares)?
      `number of requesting members who have a right to vote on the matter to which the poll relates and hold shares in the company` IS A NUMBER @desc How many requesting members have a right to vote on that matter and hold shares in the company?
      `total sum paid up on the shares those members hold` IS A NUMBER @desc What is the total sum paid up on the shares those members hold, in pounds?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`Under section 342, are the directors required to obtain an independent report on a poll because enough members asked` MEANS
    `s 342(2) the directors are required to obtain an independent report` `voting rights represented by the requesting members who have a right to vote on the matter to which the poll relates` `total voting rights of all the members who have a right to vote on the matter to which the poll relates (excluding treasury shares)` `number of requesting members who have a right to vote on the matter to which the poll relates and hold shares in the company` `total sum paid up on the shares those members hold`

@export Did the directors appoint the independent assessor within one week after the company was required to obtain the report (section 343(2))?
GIVEN `the day on which the company became required to obtain the report` IS A DATE @desc On what date did the company become required to obtain the report?
      `the day on which the appointment was made` IS A DATE @desc On what date was the appointment made?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`Under section 343, did the directors appoint the independent assessor in time` MEANS
    `s 343(2) the appointment was made in time` `the day on which the company became required to obtain the report` `the day on which the appointment was made`

@export May the directors appoint this person as the independent assessor (section 343(3))?
GIVEN `s 344(1) the person may not be appointed as an independent assessor` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the person barred from appointment by the independence requirement of section 344(1)?
      `the person has another role in relation to any poll on which he is to report (including a role in connection with collecting or counting votes or with the appointment of proxies)` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does the person have another role in relation to any poll on which he is to report (for example collecting or counting votes or appointing proxies)?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`Under section 343, may the directors appoint this person as the independent assessor` MEANS
    `s 343(3) the directors may appoint the person` (JUST `s 344(1) the person may not be appointed as an independent assessor`) `the person has another role in relation to any poll on which he is to report (including a role in connection with collecting or counting votes or with the appointment of proxies)`

@export Am I, as an officer of the company, guilty of an offence because the directors did not comply with section 343 (section 343(4))?
GIVEN `the directors are in default in complying with this section` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are the directors in default in complying with section 343?
      `s 1121 the officer is in default` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are you an officer of the company who is in default (section 1121)?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`Under section 343, am I guilty of an offence as an officer of the company in default` MEANS
    `s 343(4) the officer of the company commits an offence` `the directors are in default in complying with this section` (JUST `s 1121 the officer is in default`)

@export What penalty could I face if convicted of the offence under section 343 (section 343(5))?
GIVEN `how the person is convicted` IS A `Mode of conviction` @desc How will the person be convicted: on conviction on indictment, on summary conviction in England and Wales, in Scotland, in Northern Ireland, or on summary conviction without saying where?
GIVETH A MAYBE Penalty
`Under section 343, what penalty could I face on conviction` MEANS
    `s 343(5) the penalty on conviction` `how the person is convicted`

@export Is this person barred from appointment as the independent assessor by the independence requirement (section 344(1))?
GIVEN `the person is an auditor of the company` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the person an auditor of the company? (An auditor is not regarded as an officer or employee of the company for this purpose: section 344(2).)
      `the person is otherwise an officer or employee of the company` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the person otherwise an officer or employee of the company?
      `the person is a partner or employee of an officer or employee of the company, or a partnership of which such a person is a partner` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the person a partner or employee of an officer or employee of the company, or a partnership of which such a person is a partner?
      `the person is an officer or employee of an associated undertaking of the company` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the person an officer or employee of an associated undertaking of the company?
      `the person is a partner or employee of an officer or employee of an associated undertaking, or a partnership of which such a person is a partner` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the person a partner or employee of an officer or employee of an associated undertaking, or a partnership of which such a person is a partner?
      `a connection of a description specified by regulations exists` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does a connection of a description specified by regulations made by the Secretary of State exist between the person (or an associate of his) and the company or an associated undertaking of the company?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`Under section 344, may this person not be appointed as the independent assessor` MEANS
    `s 344(1) the person may not be appointed as an independent assessor` (`s 344(2) the person is regarded as an officer or employee of the company for this purpose` `the person is an auditor of the company` `the person is otherwise an officer or employee of the company`) `the person is a partner or employee of an officer or employee of the company, or a partnership of which such a person is a partner` `the person is an officer or employee of an associated undertaking of the company` `the person is a partner or employee of an officer or employee of an associated undertaking, or a partnership of which such a person is a partner` `a connection of a description specified by regulations exists`

@export Is an auditor of the company regarded as an officer or employee of the company for the independence requirement (section 344(2))?
GIVEN `the person is an auditor of the company` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the person an auditor of the company?
      `the person is otherwise an officer or employee of the company` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the person otherwise an officer or employee of the company?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`Under section 344, is an auditor regarded as an officer or employee of the company` MEANS
    `s 344(2) the person is regarded as an officer or employee of the company for this purpose` `the person is an auditor of the company` `the person is otherwise an officer or employee of the company`

@export Is this person an associate of an individual for the independence requirement (section 345(2))?
GIVEN `the person is the individual's spouse or civil partner or minor child or step-child` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the person the individual's spouse or civil partner or minor child or step-child?
      `the person is a body corporate of which the individual counts as a director (s 345(6))` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the person a body corporate of which the individual is a director (or, for a limited liability partnership, a member)?
      `the person is an employee or partner of the individual` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the person an employee or partner of the individual?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`Under section 345, is this person an associate of the individual` MEANS
    `s 345(2) the person is an associate of the individual` `the person is the individual's spouse or civil partner or minor child or step-child` `the person is a body corporate of which the individual counts as a director (s 345(6))` `the person is an employee or partner of the individual`

@export Where a partnership appointed as independent assessor ceases, is the appointment treated as extending to its successor (section 346(3))?
GIVEN `the partnership ceases` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has the partnership appointed as independent assessor ceased?
      `the successor` IS A `s 346(3) successor` @desc Is the successor a partnership that succeeds to the practice, or another person who succeeds to that practice having previously carried it on in partnership?
      `the members of the successor partnership are substantially the same as those of the former partnership` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are the members of the successor partnership substantially the same as those of the former partnership?
      `the successor succeeds to the whole or substantially the whole of the business` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does the successor succeed to the whole or substantially the whole of the business of the former partnership?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`Under section 346, is the appointment of a partnership as independent assessor extended to its successor` MEANS
    `s 346(3) the appointment is treated as extending to the successor` `the partnership ceases` `the successor` (`s 346(4)(a) the partnership is regarded as succeeding to the practice of the former partnership` `the members of the successor partnership are substantially the same as those of the former partnership` `the successor succeeds to the whole or substantially the whole of the business`) (`s 346(4)(b) the partnership or other person is regarded as succeeding to the practice of a partnership` `the successor succeeds to the whole or substantially the whole of the business`)

@export Does the independent assessor's report state his opinion on every matter section 347(1) requires?
GIVEN `the report states his opinion whether the procedures adopted in connection with the poll or polls were adequate` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does it state his opinion whether the procedures adopted for the poll were adequate?
      `the report states his opinion whether the votes cast (including proxy votes) were fairly and accurately recorded and counted` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does it state his opinion whether the votes cast (including proxy votes) were fairly and accurately recorded and counted?
      `the report states his opinion whether the validity of members' appointments of proxies was fairly assessed` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does it state his opinion whether the validity of members' appointments of proxies was fairly assessed?
      `the report states his opinion whether the notice of the meeting complied with section 325` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does it state his opinion whether the notice of the meeting complied with section 325?
      `the report states his opinion whether section 326 was complied with in relation to the meeting` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does it state his opinion whether section 326 was complied with in relation to the meeting?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`Under section 347, does the independent assessor's report state the opinions required` MEANS
    `s 347(1) the report states the opinions this subsection requires` `the report states his opinion whether the procedures adopted in connection with the poll or polls were adequate` `the report states his opinion whether the votes cast (including proxy votes) were fairly and accurately recorded and counted` `the report states his opinion whether the validity of members' appointments of proxies was fairly assessed` `the report states his opinion whether the notice of the meeting complied with section 325` `the report states his opinion whether section 326 was complied with in relation to the meeting`

@export Is an independent assessor entitled to attend the meeting, and any later proceedings, on a poll he is to report on (section 348(1))?
GIVEN `an independent assessor has been appointed to report on the poll` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has an independent assessor been appointed to report on the poll?
      `occasion` IS A `s 348(1) occasion` @desc Which occasion: the meeting at which the poll may be taken, any subsequent proceedings in connection with the poll, or another occasion?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`Under section 348, am I entitled to attend the meeting as the independent assessor` MEANS
    `s 348(1) the independent assessor is entitled to attend` `an independent assessor has been appointed to report on the poll` `occasion`

@export May the independent assessor require me to provide information or explanations for his report (section 349(2))?
GIVEN `person` IS A `s 349(2) person` @desc Which describes you at a material time: a director or secretary, an employee, a person holding or accountable for records, a member, an agent of the company, or someone else?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`Under section 349, may the independent assessor require me to provide information or explanations` MEANS
    `s 349(2) the independent assessor may require the person to provide information or explanations` `person`

@export May a statement I made in response to the independent assessor's requirement be used in evidence against me in criminal proceedings (section 349(4))?
GIVEN `the statement was made in response to a requirement under this section` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Was the statement made in response to a requirement under section 349?
      `the proceedings are criminal proceedings` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are the proceedings criminal proceedings?
      `the proceedings are for an offence under section 350 (offences relating to provision of information)` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are the proceedings for an offence under section 350?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`Under section 349, may my statement to the independent assessor be used against me in criminal proceedings` MEANS
    `s 349(4) the statement may be used in evidence against the person` `the statement was made in response to a requirement under this section` `the proceedings are criminal proceedings` `the proceedings are for an offence under section 350 (offences relating to provision of information)`

@export Am I required by section 349 to disclose information that is subject to legal professional privilege (section 349(5))?
GIVEN `a claim to legal professional privilege (in Scotland, to confidentiality of communications) could be maintained in legal proceedings in respect of the information` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Could a claim to legal professional privilege (in Scotland, confidentiality of communications) be maintained in respect of the information?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`Under section 349, am I required to disclose privileged information to the independent assessor` MEANS
    `s 349(5) the person is required by this section to disclose the information` `a claim to legal professional privilege (in Scotland, to confidentiality of communications) could be maintained in legal proceedings in respect of the information`

@export Do I commit an offence by failing to comply with the independent assessor's requirement without delay (section 350(1))?
GIVEN `the person fails to comply without delay with a requirement under section 349` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did you fail to comply without delay with a requirement under section 349?
      `it was not reasonably practicable for him to provide the required information or explanation` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Was it not reasonably practicable for you to provide the required information or explanation?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`Under section 350, am I guilty of an offence for failing to give the independent assessor the information` MEANS
    `s 350(1) the person commits an offence` `the person fails to comply without delay with a requirement under section 349` `it was not reasonably practicable for him to provide the required information or explanation`

@export Do I commit an offence by knowingly or recklessly making a misleading, false or deceptive statement to the independent assessor (section 350(3))?
GIVEN `the person knowingly or recklessly makes to an independent assessor a statement (oral or written)` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did you knowingly or recklessly make a statement (oral or written) to the independent assessor?
      `the statement conveys or purports to convey information or explanations which the independent assessor requires, or is entitled to require, under section 349` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did the statement convey or purport to convey information the assessor requires, or is entitled to require, under section 349?
      `the statement is misleading, false or deceptive in a material particular` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the statement misleading, false or deceptive in a material particular?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`Under section 350, am I guilty of an offence for a false statement to the independent assessor` MEANS
    `s 350(3) the person commits an offence` `the person knowingly or recklessly makes to an independent assessor a statement (oral or written)` `the statement conveys or purports to convey information or explanations which the independent assessor requires, or is entitled to require, under section 349` `the statement is misleading, false or deceptive in a material particular`

@export What penalty could I face on conviction of the offence of making a false statement to the independent assessor (section 350(4))?
GIVEN `how the person is convicted` IS A `Mode of conviction` @desc How will the person be convicted: on conviction on indictment, on summary conviction in England and Wales, in Scotland, in Northern Ireland, or on summary conviction without saying where?
GIVETH A MAYBE Penalty
`Under section 350, what penalty could I face for a false statement to the independent assessor` MEANS
    `s 350(4) the penalty on conviction` `how the person is convicted`

@export Has the company made the independent assessor's appointment, identity, the poll and his report available on a website (section 351(1))?
GIVEN `an independent assessor has been appointed to report on a poll` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has an independent assessor been appointed to report on a poll?
      `the fact of his appointment is made available on a website` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the fact of his appointment made available on a website?
      `his identity is made available on a website` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is his identity made available on a website?
      `the text of the resolution or a description of the subject matter of the poll to which his appointment relates is made available on a website` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are the text of the resolution (or a description of the subject matter of the poll) made available on a website?
      `a copy of a report by him which complies with section 347 is made available on a website` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is a copy of his report that complies with section 347 made available on a website?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`Under section 351, has the company published the independent assessor's appointment and report on a website` MEANS
    `s 351(1) the company has made the information available on a website` `an independent assessor has been appointed to report on a poll` `the fact of his appointment is made available on a website` `his identity is made available on a website` `the text of the resolution or a description of the subject matter of the poll to which his appointment relates is made available on a website` `a copy of a report by him which complies with section 347 is made available on a website`

@export Do the poll-results rules of section 341 apply to a meeting of holders of a class of shares called to vary the rights attached to them (section 352(1))?
GIVEN `the company is a quoted company or a traded company` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the company a quoted company or a traded company?
      `the meeting is a meeting of holders of a class of shares in connection with the variation of the rights attached to such shares` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the meeting a meeting of holders of a class of shares in connection with the variation of the rights attached to such shares?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`Under section 352, does section 341 apply to a class meeting on a variation of rights` MEANS
    `s 352(1) section 341 applies (with any necessary modifications) to the class meeting` `the company is a quoted company or a traded company` `the meeting is a meeting of holders of a class of shares in connection with the variation of the rights attached to such shares`

@export Do the independent-report rules of sections 342 to 351 apply to a meeting of holders of a class of shares of a quoted company called to vary the rights attached to them (section 352(1A))?
GIVEN `the company is a quoted company` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the company a quoted company (Part 15, section 385)?
      `the meeting is a variation of class rights meeting` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the meeting a meeting of holders of a class of shares in connection with the variation of the rights attached to such shares?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`Under section 352, do the independent-report rules apply to a class meeting on a variation of rights` MEANS
    `s 352(1A) sections 342 to 351 apply (with any necessary modifications) to the class meeting` (JUST `the company is a quoted company`) `the meeting is a variation of class rights meeting`

@export Is this act treated as a variation of the rights attached to a class of shares for section 352 (section 352(2))?
GIVEN `act` IS A `s 352(2) act` @desc What is the act: an amendment of the articles' provision for varying class rights (or the insertion of such a provision), the abrogation of the rights, or another act?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`Under section 352, is this change treated as a variation of the rights attached to a class of shares` MEANS
    `s 352(2) the act is treated as a variation of the rights attached to a class of shares` `act`

@export Was the information kept available on a website throughout the period of two years beginning with the date it was first made available (section 353(4)(b))?
GIVEN `the date on which the information was first made available on a website` IS A DATE @desc On what date was the information first made available on a website?
      `the last day on which the information was kept available` IS A DATE @desc What was the last day on which it was kept available?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`Under section 353, has the information been kept on the website for two years` MEANS
    `s 353(4)(b) the information was kept available throughout the two years` `the date on which the information was first made available on a website` `the last day on which the information was kept available`

§§ `Chapter 6 -- records of resolutions and meetings (ss 355 to 359)`
-- Asked of a director or secretary who keeps the company's records, a member who wants to inspect them, or a sole member who takes decisions.

-- RECONCILED 2026-11-12 (seat audit, subject mismatch): was named `Under section 355, must my company keep this record`; the old name asked about the duty, but s 355(1) as encoded answers whether the company has kept the record.
@export Has my company kept the records of resolutions and meetings that section 355(1) requires?
GIVEN `record` IS A `s 355(1) record` @desc Which record: copies of resolutions of members passed otherwise than at general meetings, minutes of proceedings of general meetings, details of a sole member's decisions, or another record?
      `the company has kept the record` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has the company kept the record?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`Under section 355, has my company kept this record` MEANS
    `s 355(1) the company has kept the record this subsection requires` `record` `the company has kept the record`

@export Was the record kept for at least ten years from the date of the resolution, meeting or decision (section 355(2))?
GIVEN `the date of the resolution, meeting or decision` IS A DATE @desc What is the date of the resolution, meeting or decision?
      `the last day on which the record was kept` IS A DATE @desc What was the last day on which the record was kept?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`Under section 355, were the records kept for at least ten years` MEANS
    `s 355(2) the record was kept for at least ten years` `the date of the resolution, meeting or decision` `the last day on which the record was kept`

@export Am I, as an officer of the company, guilty of an offence because the company did not keep the records (section 355(3))?
GIVEN `the company fails to comply with this section` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did the company fail to comply with section 355?
      `s 1121 the officer is in default` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are you an officer of the company who is in default (section 1121)?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`Under section 355, am I guilty of an offence as an officer of the company in default` MEANS
    `s 355(3) the officer of the company commits an offence` `the company fails to comply with this section` (JUST `s 1121 the officer is in default`)

@export What penalty could I face if convicted of the offence under section 355, including the daily default fine (section 355(4))?
GIVEN `how the person is convicted` IS A `Mode of conviction` @desc How will the person be convicted: on conviction on indictment, on summary conviction in England and Wales, in Scotland, in Northern Ireland, or on summary conviction without saying where?
GIVETH A MAYBE Penalty
`Under section 355, what penalty could I face on conviction` MEANS
    `s 355(4) the penalty on conviction` `how the person is convicted`

@export Are minutes of a general meeting, purporting to be signed by the chairman of the meeting or of the next one, evidence of the proceedings (section 356(4))?
GIVEN `the minutes are of proceedings of a general meeting` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are the minutes of proceedings of a general meeting?
      `the minutes purport to be signed by the chairman of that meeting or by the chairman of the next general meeting` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Do they purport to be signed by the chairman of that meeting or of the next general meeting?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`Under section 356, is the signed minute of the meeting evidence of what happened` MEANS
    `s 356(4) the minutes are evidence (in Scotland, sufficient evidence) of the proceedings at the meeting` `the minutes are of proceedings of a general meeting` `the minutes purport to be signed by the chairman of that meeting or by the chairman of the next general meeting`

@export Where there is a record of a private company's written resolution, are the Act's requirements for passing it deemed complied with (section 356(3))?
GIVEN `there is a record of a written resolution of a private company` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is there a record of a written resolution of a private company?
      `the contrary is proved` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has the contrary been proved?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`Under section 356, are the requirements for passing the written resolution deemed complied with` MEANS
    `s 356(3) the requirements of this Act with respect to the passing of the resolution are deemed to be complied with` `there is a record of a written resolution of a private company` `the contrary is proved`

@export Must I, as the sole member of a company limited by shares or by guarantee, give the company details of a decision I take (section 357(2))?
GIVEN `the company is limited by shares or by guarantee` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the company limited by shares or by guarantee?
      `the company has only one member` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does the company have only one member?
      `the decision may be taken by the company in general meeting` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the decision one that may be taken by the company in general meeting?
      `the decision has effect as if agreed by the company in general meeting` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does the decision have effect as if agreed by the company in general meeting?
      `the decision is taken by way of a written resolution` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the decision taken by way of a written resolution?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`Under section 357, must I give my company details of my decision as its sole member` MEANS
    `s 357(2) the member must provide the company with details of the decision` (`s 357(1) this section applies to the company` `the company is limited by shares or by guarantee` `the company has only one member`) `the decision may be taken by the company in general meeting` `the decision has effect as if agreed by the company in general meeting` `the decision is taken by way of a written resolution`

@export Do I commit an offence by failing to give my company details of a sole member's decision (section 357(3))?
GIVEN `the company is limited by shares or by guarantee` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the company limited by shares or by guarantee?
      `the company has only one member` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does the company have only one member?
      `the decision may be taken by the company in general meeting` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the decision one that may be taken by the company in general meeting?
      `the decision has effect as if agreed by the company in general meeting` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does the decision have effect as if agreed by the company in general meeting?
      `the decision is taken by way of a written resolution` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the decision taken by way of a written resolution?
      `the member fails to provide the details` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did you fail to provide the company with details of the decision?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`Under section 357, do I commit an offence if I do not give my company details of my decision` MEANS
    `s 357(3) the person commits an offence` (`s 357(2) the member must provide the company with details of the decision` (`s 357(1) this section applies to the company` `the company is limited by shares or by guarantee` `the company has only one member`) `the decision may be taken by the company in general meeting` `the decision has effect as if agreed by the company in general meeting` `the decision is taken by way of a written resolution`) `the member fails to provide the details`

@export What penalty could I face if convicted of the offence under section 357 (section 357(4))?
GIVEN `how the person is convicted` IS A `Mode of conviction` @desc How will the person be convicted: on conviction on indictment, on summary conviction in England and Wales, in Scotland, in Northern Ireland, or on summary conviction without saying where?
GIVETH A MAYBE Penalty
`Under section 357, what penalty could I face on conviction` MEANS
    `s 357(4) the penalty on conviction` `how the person is convicted`

@export Are the records of resolutions and meetings kept available for inspection where section 358(1) allows?
GIVEN `place` IS A `s 358(1) place` @desc Where are they kept: at the registered office, at a place specified in regulations under section 1136, or elsewhere?
      `s 1136 the place is specified in regulations under section 1136` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the place specified in regulations under section 1136?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`Under section 358, are the company's records of resolutions kept where the Act allows` MEANS
    `s 358(1) the records relating to the previous ten years are kept available for inspection at a place this subsection allows` `place` (JUST `s 1136 the place is specified in regulations under section 1136`)

@export Must the company let me, as a member, inspect the records of resolutions and meetings without charge (section 358(3))?
GIVEN `the person is a member of the company` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are you a member of the company?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`Under section 358, must the company let me inspect the records of resolutions without charge` MEANS
    `s 358(3) the records must be open to the inspection of the person without charge` `the person is a member of the company`

@export May I, as a member, require a copy of any of the records of resolutions and meetings on payment of the prescribed fee (section 358(4))?
GIVEN `the person is a member of the company` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are you a member of the company?
      `the person has paid such fee as may be prescribed` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Have you paid such fee as may be prescribed?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`Under section 358, may I require a copy of the records of resolutions` MEANS
    `s 358(4) the member may require a copy of any of the records` `the person is a member of the company` `the person has paid such fee as may be prescribed`

@export Am I, as an officer of the company, guilty of an offence because the company failed to give notice of the place, or refused inspection, or did not send a copy (section 358(5))?
GIVEN `the days for which default has been made in complying with subsection (2)` IS A NUMBER @desc For how many days has default been made in complying with section 358(2) (notice to the registrar)?
      `an inspection required under subsection (3) is refused` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Was an inspection required under section 358(3) refused?
      `a copy requested under subsection (4) is not sent` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Was a copy requested under section 358(4) not sent?
      `s 1121 the officer is in default` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are you an officer of the company who is in default (section 1121)?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`Under section 358, am I guilty of an offence as an officer of the company in default` MEANS
    `s 358(5) the officer of the company commits an offence` `the days for which default has been made in complying with subsection (2)` `an inspection required under subsection (3) is refused` `a copy requested under subsection (4) is not sent` (JUST `s 1121 the officer is in default`)

@export What penalty could I face if convicted of the offence under section 358, including the daily default fine (section 358(6))?
GIVEN `how the person is convicted` IS A `Mode of conviction` @desc How will the person be convicted: on conviction on indictment, on summary conviction in England and Wales, in Scotland, in Northern Ireland, or on summary conviction without saying where?
GIVETH A MAYBE Penalty
`Under section 358, what penalty could I face on conviction` MEANS
    `s 358(6) the penalty on conviction` `how the person is convicted`

@export May the court order an immediate inspection of the records, or that copies be sent, where inspection was refused or a copy not sent (section 358(7))?
GIVEN `an inspection required under subsection (3) is refused or a copy requested under subsection (4) is not sent` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Was an inspection required under section 358(3) refused, or a copy requested under section 358(4) not sent?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`Under section 358, may the court compel an inspection or order copies to be sent` MEANS
    `s 358(7) the court may by order compel an immediate inspection of the records or direct that the copies required be sent` `an inspection required under subsection (3) is refused or a copy requested under subsection (4) is not sent`

@export Does Chapter 6 apply (with necessary modifications) to the resolutions and meetings of holders of a class of shares, or of a class of members of a company without a share capital (section 359)?
GIVEN `group` IS A `s 359 resolutions and meetings of` @desc Whose resolutions and meetings: holders of a class of shares, a class of members of a company without a share capital, or another group?
      `the company has a share capital` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does your company have a share capital?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`Under section 359, does Chapter 6 apply to the resolutions and meetings of a class of members` MEANS
    `s 359 this Chapter applies (with necessary modifications) to the resolutions and meetings` `group` `the company has a share capital`

§§ `Chapter 7 -- counting periods of notice, electronic meetings and traded companies (ss 360 to 361)`
-- Asked of any director, secretary or member counting a period of notice, or of a member of a traded company about voting.

@export How many clear days lie between the day notice was given (or a request received, or a sum deposited) and the day of the meeting, excluding both (section 360(2))?
GIVEN `the day on which the notice is given, the request received or the sum deposited or tendered` IS A DATE @desc On what day was the notice given, the request received or the sum deposited or tendered?
      `the day of the meeting` IS A DATE @desc On what day is the meeting?
GIVETH A NUMBER
`Under section 360, how many clear days of notice were given` MEANS
    `s 360(2) the clear days between the day the notice is given and the day of the meeting` `the day on which the notice is given, the request received or the sum deposited or tendered` `the day of the meeting`

@export Is the period of the specified length satisfied, counting clear days (section 360(2))?
GIVEN `the length of the period` IS A NUMBER @desc How many days is the required period?
      `the day on which the notice is given, the request received or the sum deposited or tendered` IS A DATE @desc On what day was the notice given, the request received or the sum deposited or tendered?
      `the day of the meeting` IS A DATE @desc On what day is the meeting?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`Under section 360, is the period of notice long enough counting clear days` MEANS
    `s 360(2) the period of the specified length is satisfied` `the length of the period` `the day on which the notice is given, the request received or the sum deposited or tendered` `the day of the meeting`

-- RECONCILED 2026-11-12 (seat audit, direction mismatch): was named `Under section 360A, may a meeting be held so that members attend electronically`; the old name asked a permission (may a meeting be held) but s 360A(1) answers whether this Part precludes it, a bar (JUST FALSE means it does not).
@export Does Part 13 stop a meeting being held so that members who are not present together attend, speak and vote by electronic means (section 360A(1))?
GIVEN `persons who are not present together at the same place attend, speak and vote at the meeting by electronic means` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Do persons who are not present together at the same place attend, speak and vote at the meeting by electronic means?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`Under section 360A, does Part 13 stop a meeting being held so that members attend electronically` MEANS
    `s 360A(1) this Part precludes the holding and conducting of the meeting in that way` `persons who are not present together at the same place attend, speak and vote at the meeting by electronic means`

@export Has the traded company sent confirmation that my electronic vote on a poll was received (section 360AA(1))?
GIVEN `the company is a traded company` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the company a traded company?
      `the vote is cast on a poll by electronic means` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Was the vote cast on a poll by electronic means?
      `who cast the vote` IS A `s 360AA(1) who cast the vote` @desc Who cast the vote: the member, the proxy, or the representative of a corporation?
      `confirmation of receipt was sent by electronic means to that person as soon as reasonably practicable after the vote was received` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Was confirmation of receipt sent by electronic means as soon as reasonably practicable?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`Under section 360AA, has the traded company confirmed receipt of my electronic vote` MEANS
    `s 360AA(1) the company has sent confirmation of receipt of the vote` `the company is a traded company` `the vote is cast on a poll by electronic means` `who cast the vote` `confirmation of receipt was sent by electronic means to that person as soon as reasonably practicable after the vote was received`

@export Is a provision of a traded company's articles void because it restricts my right to participate and vote unless my shares were deposited with, or transferred to, someone else (section 360B(1)(a))?
GIVEN `the company is a traded company` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the company a traded company?
      `the provision imposes a restriction on a member's right to participate in and vote at a general meeting unless the member's shares have, after being acquired and before the meeting, been deposited with, transferred to or registered in the name of another person` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does the provision restrict a member's right to participate in and vote at a general meeting unless the shares have been deposited with, transferred to or registered in the name of another person?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`Under section 360B, is a provision of the traded company's articles void for restricting my right to vote` MEANS
    `s 360B(1)(a) the provision of the articles is void` `the company is a traded company` `the provision imposes a restriction on a member's right to participate in and vote at a general meeting unless the member's shares have, after being acquired and before the meeting, been deposited with, transferred to or registered in the name of another person`

-- RECONCILED 2026-11-12 (seat audit, subject mismatch): was named `Under section 360B, may the traded company fix the time for who may vote`; the old name asked a general permission, but s 360B(2) answers whether the time actually fixed is one the subsection allows.
@export Is the time a traded company fixed for determining the right to vote not more than 48 hours before the meeting (section 360B(2))?
GIVEN `the company is a traded company` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the company a traded company?
      `hours before the time for holding the meeting at which the register of members was taken as the basis of the right to vote` IS A NUMBER @desc How many hours before the time for holding the meeting is the time at which the register of members was taken as the basis of the right to vote?
      `hours of that period that fall on a day that is not a working day` IS A NUMBER @desc Of those hours, how many fall on a day that is not a working day?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`Under section 360B, is the time the traded company fixed for who may vote one the Act allows` MEANS
    `s 360B(2) the time determined by the company is one this subsection allows` `the company is a traded company` `hours before the time for holding the meeting at which the register of members was taken as the basis of the right to vote` `hours of that period that fall on a day that is not a working day`

@export Must a traded company give me information to confirm that my vote on a poll was validly recorded and counted (section 360BA(1))?
GIVEN `the company is a traded company` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the company a traded company?
      `a poll has been taken on the resolution at the general meeting` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Was a poll taken on the resolution at the general meeting?
      `the date of the general meeting` IS A DATE @desc On what date was the general meeting?
      `the date on which the member's request was received by the company` IS A DATE @desc On what date did the company receive your request for the information?
      `the member has another reasonable means to determine that the vote was counted` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Do you have another reasonable means by which to determine that your vote has been validly recorded and counted by the company?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`Under section 360BA, must the traded company give me information to confirm my vote was counted` MEANS
    `s 360BA(1) the company must provide the information to the member` `the company is a traded company` `a poll has been taken on the resolution at the general meeting` (`s 360BA(2)(a) the request was received in time` `the date of the general meeting` `the date on which the member's request was received by the company`) (`s 360BA(2)(b) the member has no other reasonable means` `the member has another reasonable means to determine that the vote was counted`)

@export What is the last day for a traded company to give me the information confirming my vote (section 360BA(3))?
GIVEN `the first working day after the day on which the result of the poll is declared for the resolution` IS A DATE @desc What is the first working day after the day on which the result of the poll was declared?
      `the first working day after the day on which the request is received by the company` IS A DATE @desc What is the first working day after the day on which your request was received?
GIVETH A DATE
`Under section 360BA, by what date must the traded company give me the information` MEANS
    `s 360BA(3) the last day for providing the information` `the first working day after the day on which the result of the poll is declared for the resolution` `the first working day after the day on which the request is received by the company`

@export Is my company a traded company, one any of whose shares carry the right to vote at general meetings and are admitted to trading on a UK or EU regulated market (section 360C)?
GIVEN `any of the company's shares both carry rights to vote at general meetings and are admitted to trading` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Do any of your company's shares both carry the right to vote at general meetings and are they admitted to trading on a UK regulated market or an EU regulated market by or with the company's consent?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`Under section 360C, is my company a traded company` MEANS
    `s 360C the company is a traded company` (IF `any of the company's shares both carry rights to vote at general meetings and are admitted to trading` THEN LIST (`s 360C class of shares` OF TRUE, TRUE) ELSE EMPTY)

@export Is my company a quoted company for the purposes of Part 13, as defined in Part 15 (section 361)?
GIVEN `s 385 the company is a quoted company` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is your company a quoted company as defined in Part 15 (section 385)?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`Under section 361, is my company a quoted company for Part 13` MEANS
    `s 361 the company is a quoted company` (JUST `s 385 the company is a quoted company`)

-- ====================================================================================================
-- seat questions from part coa8 (merged by the lead on 2026-11-12; unchanged text follows)
-- ====================================================================================================
-- coa8-seat.l4: THE SEAT LAYER over the layer-1 modules of coa8 (Companies Act 2006, ss 362 to 414B: Part 14, political donations and
-- expenditure, and Part 15 up to section 414B, accounts and reports).
-- Written by a script (work/genseat.py) from the signatures of the layer-1 rules, so that every call passes its inputs in the order
-- the rule declares them; it restates no rule.
--
-- SEAT: an individual who is, or is about to become, a director, a company secretary or a member (shareholder) of a company registered
-- under the Act, or who deals with one, asking on facts they can state what the Act requires or lets them do, what rights they have
-- against the company or its directors, what they must disclose, file, approve or vote on and by when, and what follows (liability,
-- offences, penalties) if it is not done. (Assumed, not ruled: the Act is addressed to companies, so the individual is whoever stands in
-- a company's management or ownership.) There is no seat for an official: the court, the registrar and the Secretary of State appear only
-- as what the text lets them do to the person.
--
-- PLAIN INPUTS. Every question takes plain inputs (true or false, a number, a date, a list of numbers or a choice of words), each with an
-- @desc worded as the person would be asked. Where a layer-1 rule takes a borrowed or other-section answer as MAYBE BOOLEAN, the seat asks
-- true or false and passes JUST the answer: a person who does not know such a fact cannot answer the question (assumed, not ruled; the layer-1
-- rules still answer NOTHING where another part passes NOTHING). The answers are MAYBE BOOLEAN, MAYBE NUMBER, MAYBE DATE or MAYBE STRING:
--   JUST TRUE / JUST FALSE   the text says yes, or says no in its own words;
--   NOTHING                  the Act does not decide the case on the facts given ("not covered"; never to be read as no).
-- The figures the text states (the small-company limits, the 5,000 pounds, the 28 days) are the Act's own; a substitution by regulations
-- would change the answers.

-- A list with one answer for each subsidiary undertaking, for section 402: the first k are excludable, the rest are not.
GIVEN n IS A NUMBER
      k IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A LIST OF MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 402 the answer for each subsidiary undertaking` MEANS
    IF n AT MOST 0
    THEN EMPTY
    ELSE (IF k GREATER THAN 0 THEN JUST TRUE ELSE JUST FALSE) FOLLOWED BY (`s 402 the answer for each subsidiary undertaking` (n MINUS 1) (k MINUS 1))

-- Words for a penalty, so that a person can read it: the layer-1 rules answer with the core's Penalty record.
GIVEN m IS A `Mode of conviction`
GIVETH A STRING
`s 387(3) the mode of conviction in words` MEANS
    CONSIDER m
    WHEN `on conviction on indictment` THEN "on conviction on indictment"
    WHEN `on summary conviction` THEN "on summary conviction"
    WHEN `on summary conviction in England and Wales` THEN "on summary conviction in England and Wales"
    WHEN `on summary conviction in Scotland` THEN "on summary conviction in Scotland"
    WHEN `on summary conviction in Northern Ireland` THEN "on summary conviction in Northern Ireland"

GIVEN how IS A STRING
GIVETH A `Mode of conviction`
`s 387(3) the mode of conviction named` MEANS
    BRANCH IF how EQUALS "on indictment" THEN `on conviction on indictment`
           IF how EQUALS "summary conviction in England and Wales" THEN `on summary conviction in England and Wales`
           IF how EQUALS "summary conviction in Scotland" THEN `on summary conviction in Scotland`
           IF how EQUALS "summary conviction in Northern Ireland" THEN `on summary conviction in Northern Ireland`
           OTHERWISE `on summary conviction`

GIVEN p IS A Period
GIVETH A STRING
`s 387(3) the period in words` MEANS
    CONCAT (TOSTRING (p's `number of units`)), " ", unitWord
    WHERE
        unitWord MEANS
            CONSIDER p's unit
            WHEN Days THEN "days"
            WHEN `Working days` THEN "working days"
            WHEN Weeks THEN "weeks"
            WHEN Months THEN "months"
            WHEN Years THEN "years"

GIVEN f IS A `Fine limit`
GIVETH A STRING
`s 387(3) the fine in words` MEANS
    CONSIDER f
    WHEN `a fine without a stated limit` THEN "a fine"
    WHEN `a fine not exceeding the statutory maximum` ofMaximum THEN
        IF ofMaximum EQUALS 1
        THEN "a fine not exceeding the statutory maximum"
        ELSE CONCAT "a fine not exceeding ", (TOSTRING ofMaximum), " of the statutory maximum"
    WHEN `a fine not exceeding a level on the standard scale` levelNumber ofLevel THEN
        IF ofLevel EQUALS 1
        THEN CONCAT "a fine not exceeding level ", (TOSTRING levelNumber), " on the standard scale"
        ELSE CONCAT "a fine not exceeding ", (TOSTRING ofLevel), " of level ", (TOSTRING levelNumber), " on the standard scale"
    WHEN `a fine not exceeding an amount in pounds` amount THEN CONCAT "a fine not exceeding ", (TOSTRING amount), " pounds"

GIVEN p IS A MAYBE Penalty
GIVETH A MAYBE STRING
`s 387(3) the penalty in words` MEANS
    CONSIDER p
    WHEN NOTHING THEN NOTHING
    WHEN JUST x THEN
        JUST (CONCAT (`s 387(3) the mode of conviction in words` (x's `how convicted`)), ": ", imprisonment, fine, daily, together)
        WHERE
            imprisonment MEANS
                CONSIDER x's `imprisonment not exceeding`
                WHEN NOTHING THEN "no imprisonment"
                WHEN JUST per THEN CONCAT "imprisonment for a term not exceeding ", (`s 387(3) the period in words` per)
            fine MEANS
                CONSIDER x's `fine not exceeding`
                WHEN NOTHING THEN ""
                WHEN JUST fl THEN CONCAT "; ", (`s 387(3) the fine in words` fl)
            daily MEANS
                CONSIDER x's `daily default fine for continued contravention`
                WHEN NOTHING THEN ""
                WHEN JUST fl THEN CONCAT "; and, for continued contravention, ", (`s 387(3) the fine in words` fl), " a day"
            together MEANS
                IF x's `imprisonment and fine together`
                THEN " (or both)"
                ELSE ""


§ `Companies Act 2006, Part 14: control of political donations and expenditure`
-- Has a company made, or does it want to make, a gift or a payment to a political party, organisation or election candidate, or spend money on political publicity or activities?


§§ `Which parties and organisations the Part covers, and what a political donation and political expenditure are (ss 363 to 365)`

@export Under section 363, is this political party one to which Part 14 (political donations and expenditure) applies?
GIVEN `registered under Part 2 of the Political Parties, Elections and Referendums Act 2000` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it true that registered under Part 2 of the Political Parties, Elections and Referendums Act 2000? (true or false)
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 363, is this political party one to which the political donations rules apply` IS
    `s 363(1) this Part applies to the political party` `registered under Part 2 of the Political Parties, Elections and Referendums Act 2000`

@export Under section 363, do the rules on political donations apply to this independent election candidate?
GIVEN `standing at an election to public office held in the United Kingdom` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it true that standing at an election to public office held in the United Kingdom? (true or false)
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 363, do the political donations rules apply to this independent election candidate` IS
    `s 363(3) this Part applies to the independent election candidate` `standing at an election to public office held in the United Kingdom`

@export Under section 363, is this organisation a political organisation, so that the political donations rules cover it?
GIVEN `it carries on, or proposes to carry on, activities` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does the organisation carry on, or propose to carry on, activities? (true or false)
      `capable of affecting public support` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are those activities capable of being reasonably regarded as intended to affect public support for a political party or an independent election candidate? (true or false)
      `that party or candidate is covered` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is that party registered under Part 2 of the Political Parties, Elections and Referendums Act 2000, or is that candidate standing at an election to public office held in the United Kingdom? (true or false)
      `capable of influencing a referendum` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are those activities capable of being reasonably regarded as intended to influence voters in a national or regional referendum held under the law of the United Kingdom? (true or false)
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 363, is this organisation a political organisation` IS
    `s 363(2) the organisation is a political organisation` `it carries on, or proposes to carry on, activities`
        (`s 363(2)(a) the activities are intended to affect public support for a party or candidate to which this Part applies` `capable of affecting public support` (JUST `that party or candidate is covered`))
        (`s 363(2)(b) the activities are intended to influence voters in a referendum` `capable of influencing a referendum`)

@export Under section 364, is this payment or gift a political donation, so that the political donations rules apply to it?
GIVEN `the recipient is an independent election candidate` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the recipient an independent election candidate (rather than a political party or other political organisation)? (true or false)
      `it is a donation under the 2000 Act as unamended` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Would the payment or gift be a donation under sections 50 to 52 of the Political Parties, Elections and Referendums Act 2000, read as if the Electoral Administration Act 2006 amendments had not been made? (true or false)
      `it would be a donation reading the recipient as a registered party` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Would it be such a donation if the Act's references to a registered party were read as references to the recipient (the party or other political organisation, or the independent election candidate)? (true or false)
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 364, is this payment or gift a political donation` IS
    IF `the recipient is an independent election candidate`
    THEN `s 364(3)(a) the thing is a political donation to the independent election candidate` (`s 364(4) the answer under sections 50 and 53 to use for this section` NOTHING (JUST `it would be a donation reading the recipient as a registered party`))
    ELSE `s 364(2)(a) the thing is a political donation to the political party or other political organisation` (`s 364(4) the answer under sections 50 and 53 to use for this section` NOTHING (JUST `it is a donation under the 2000 Act as unamended`)) (JUST `it would be a donation reading the recipient as a registered party`)

@export Under section 365, is this spending political expenditure, so that the political donations rules require it to be authorised?
GIVEN `incurred by the company` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the money spent by the company? (true or false)
      `on advertising or publicity material` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it spent on preparing, publishing or disseminating advertising or other promotional or publicity material? (true or false)
      `the material is capable of affecting public support` IS A BOOLEAN @desc At the time of publication or dissemination, is that material capable of being reasonably regarded as intended to affect public support for a political party or other political organisation, or an independent election candidate? (true or false)
      `on activities of the company` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it spent on activities on the part of the company? (true or false)
      `the activities are capable of affecting public support` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are those activities capable of being reasonably regarded as intended to affect public support for a political party or other political organisation, or an independent election candidate? (true or false)
      `the activities are capable of influencing a referendum` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are those activities capable of being reasonably regarded as intended to influence voters in a national or regional referendum held under the law of the United Kingdom? (true or false)
      `the party, organisation or candidate is covered` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the party, organisation or candidate one to which Part 14 applies (see the section 363 questions)? (true or false)
      `it is a political donation` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the payment a political donation (see the section 364 question)? (true or false)
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 365, is this spending political expenditure` IS
    `s 365(2) the spending counts as political expenditure` (JUST `it is a political donation`)
        (`s 365(1) the expenditure is political expenditure`
            (`s 365(1)(a) the expenditure is on advertising or publicity material intended to affect public support` `incurred by the company` `on advertising or publicity material` `the material is capable of affecting public support` (JUST `the party, organisation or candidate is covered`))
            (`s 365(1)(b) the expenditure is on activities intended to affect public support or to influence referendum voters` `incurred by the company` `on activities of the company` `the activities are capable of affecting public support` (JUST `the party, organisation or candidate is covered`) `the activities are capable of influencing a referendum`))


§§ `Authorisation needed before a donation or expenditure (ss 366 to 368)`

@export Under section 366, is this company forbidden to make this political donation or incur this political expenditure, taking its members' authorisation and the exemptions of sections 374 to 378 into account?
GIVEN `the company makes a political donation` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the company making a political donation to a political party, other political organisation or independent election candidate? (true or false)
      `the company incurs political expenditure` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the company incurring political expenditure? (true or false)
      `an exemption in sections 374 to 378 applies` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does an exemption apply under section 374 (trade unions), 375 (trade association subscriptions), 376 (all-party parliamentary groups), 377 (an order) or 378 (not more than 5,000 pounds in twelve months)? (true or false)
      `the company is a subsidiary of another company` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the company a subsidiary of another company? (true or false)
      `a resolution of the company's members has been passed` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has a resolution of the members of the company been passed? (true or false)
      `it is a wholly-owned subsidiary of a UK-registered company` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the company a wholly-owned subsidiary of a UK-registered company? (true or false)
      `every relevant holding company's members have passed a resolution` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Have the members of every relevant holding company (a UK-registered holding company that is not itself a subsidiary of another UK-registered company) passed a resolution? Answer true if there is none. (true or false)
      `the resolution is in the form section 367 requires` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the resolution in the form section 367 requires (see the section 367 question)? (true or false)
      `the date on which the resolution was passed` IS A DATE @desc On what date was the resolution passed (the latest, if there are several)? (a date)
      `the date on which the donation is made or the expenditure incurred` IS A DATE @desc On what date is the donation made or the expenditure incurred (or, if under a contract, the earlier date the contract was entered into: see section 379)? (a date)
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 366, is this company forbidden to make this political donation or incur this political expenditure` IS
    `s 366(1) the company is forbidden to make the donation or incur the expenditure` `the company makes a political donation` `the company incurs political expenditure` authorisedOrExempt
    WHERE
        authorisedOrExempt MEANS
            `s 362 helper either answer` (JUST `an exemption in sections 374 to 378 applies`)
                (`s 362 helper both answers`
                    (`s 366(2) the donation or expenditure is authorised as section 366(2) requires` (JUST `the company is a subsidiary of another company`) (JUST `a resolution of the company's members has been passed`) (`s 366(3) no resolution is required on the part of the company` `it is a wholly-owned subsidiary of a UK-registered company` TRUE) (LIST (JUST `every relevant holding company's members have passed a resolution`)))
                    (`s 366(5) the resolution or resolutions meet the requirements of subsection (5)` (JUST `the resolution is in the form section 367 requires`) (LIST `the date on which the resolution was passed`) `the date on which the donation is made or the expenditure incurred`))

@export Under section 366, is this other company a relevant holding company of the company that made the donation or incurred the expenditure?
GIVEN `the company by which the donation was made or the expenditure was incurred is a subsidiary of the other company` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it true that the company by which the donation was made or the expenditure was incurred is a subsidiary of the other company? (true or false)
      `the other company is a UK-registered company` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it true that the other company is a UK-registered company? (true or false)
      `the other company is a subsidiary of another UK-registered company` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it true that the other company is a subsidiary of another UK-registered company? (true or false)
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 366, is this other company a relevant holding company of ours` IS
    `s 366(4) the other company is a relevant holding company` (JUST `the company by which the donation was made or the expenditure was incurred is a subsidiary of the other company`) `the other company is a UK-registered company` (JUST `the other company is a subsidiary of another UK-registered company`)

@export Under section 366, does section 366 enable the company to be authorised to do this thing, given whether the company could lawfully do it apart from the section?
GIVEN `the company could lawfully do it apart from this section` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it true that the company could lawfully do it apart from this section? (true or false)
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 366, does section 366 enable the company to be authorised to do this thing` IS
    `s 366(6) section 366 enables the company to be authorised to do it` `the company could lawfully do it apart from this section`

@export Under section 367, does this authorising resolution have the form the Act requires?
GIVEN `it relates to some other company` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does the resolution relate to a company other than the company passing it and its subsidiaries? (true or false)
      `it is a resolution under subsection (2)` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it expressed to relate to all the company's subsidiaries without identifying them individually (section 367(2))? (true or false)
      `heads are specified for all the companies together` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does it specify the head or heads (donations to parties or candidates; donations to other political organisations; political expenditure) for all the companies it relates to taken together? (true or false)
      `heads are specified for each company` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does it specify the head or heads for each company it relates to? (true or false)
      `it is expressed in general terms` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it expressed in general terms conforming with section 367(3)? (true or false)
      `it purports to authorise particular donations or expenditure` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does it purport to authorise particular donations or particular expenditure? (true or false)
      `it authorises up to a specified amount for each head` IS A BOOLEAN @desc For each specified head, does it authorise donations or expenditure up to a specified amount in the period for which it has effect? (true or false)
      `amounts are specified for all the companies together` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are the amounts specified for all the companies it relates to taken together? (true or false)
      `amounts are specified for each company` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are the amounts specified for each company it relates to? (true or false)
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 367, does this authorising resolution have the form the Act requires` IS
    `s 367 the resolution is in the form section 367 requires`
        (`s 367(1) the resolution may relate to` (IF `it relates to some other company` THEN `s 367(1) some other company` ELSE `s 367(1)(c) the company passing the resolution and one or more subsidiaries of that company`))
        (`s 367(4) the resolution specifies the head or heads as required` `it is a resolution under subsection (2)` `heads are specified for all the companies together` `heads are specified for each company`)
        (`s 367(5) the resolution is expressed in general terms as required` `it is expressed in general terms` `it purports to authorise particular donations or expenditure`)
        (`s 367(6) the resolution authorises up to a specified amount for each head` `it authorises up to a specified amount for each head`)
        (`s 367(7) the resolution specifies the amounts as required` `it is a resolution under subsection (2)` `amounts are specified for all the companies together` `amounts are specified for each company`)

@export Under section 368, on what date does this authorising resolution stop having effect?
GIVEN `the date on which the resolution was passed` IS A DATE @desc On what date was the resolution passed? (a date)
      `the directors determined a shorter period` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did the directors determine that the resolution is to have effect for a shorter period than four years? (true or false)
      `the period the directors determined, in months` IS A NUMBER @desc If so, how long is it, in months? (a number; 0 if they determined none)
      `the articles require a shorter period` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Do the articles require a shorter period than four years? (true or false)
      `the period the articles require, in months` IS A NUMBER @desc If so, how long is it, in months? (a number; 0 if they require none)
      `the articles prevent the directors from determining a shorter period` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does a provision of the articles operate to prevent the directors from determining a shorter period? (true or false)
GIVETH A MAYBE DATE
DECIDE `Under section 368, on what date does this authorising resolution stop having effect` IS
    `s 368(1) the last day on which the resolution has effect` `the date on which the resolution was passed`
        (IF `the directors determined a shorter period` THEN JUST (Period OF `the period the directors determined, in months`, Months) ELSE NOTHING)
        (JUST (NOT `the articles prevent the directors from determining a shorter period`))
        (IF `the articles require a shorter period` THEN JUST (Period OF `the period the articles require, in months`, Months) ELSE NOTHING)

@export Under section 368, can the directors determine that the authorisation lasts for a shorter period than four years?
GIVEN `a provision of the articles operates to prevent the directors from determining a shorter period` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it true that a provision of the articles operates to prevent the directors from determining a shorter period? (true or false)
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 368, can the directors determine a shorter period for the authorisation` IS
    `s 368(2) the directors have power to determine a shorter period` `a provision of the articles operates to prevent the directors from determining a shorter period`


§§ `If a donation or expenditure was not authorised: directors' liability and shareholder action (ss 369 to 373)`
-- Has a company made a political donation or incurred political expenditure that was not authorised as the Act requires?

@export Under section 369, am I, as a director, jointly and severally liable to make good this unauthorised political donation or expenditure to the company and to compensate it for loss or damage?
GIVEN `the company made the donation or incurred the expenditure` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has the company made a political donation or incurred political expenditure? (true or false)
      `it was authorised as the Part requires` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Was it authorised in accordance with Part 14 (see the section 366 question)? (true or false)
      `I was a director of that company at the time` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Were you a director of the company (including a shadow director) at the time the donation was made or the expenditure incurred? (true or false)
      `the company was a subsidiary of a relevant holding company` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Was the company a subsidiary of a relevant holding company at that time? (true or false)
      `I was a director of that relevant holding company` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Were you a director of that relevant holding company (including a shadow director) at that time? (true or false)
      `its directors failed to take all reasonable steps` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did the directors of the relevant holding company fail to take all reasonable steps to prevent the donation being made or the expenditure being incurred? (true or false)
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 369, am I jointly and severally liable to make good this unauthorised donation or expenditure to the company and to compensate it for loss or damage` IS
    `s 369(2) the person is jointly and severally liable to make good and to compensate the company`
        (`s 369(1) section 369 applies` `the company made the donation or incurred the expenditure` (JUST `it was authorised as the Part requires`))
        (`s 369(3) the person is one of the directors in default` (JUST `I was a director of that company at the time`) (JUST `the company was a subsidiary of a relevant holding company`) (JUST `I was a director of that relevant holding company`) `its directors failed to take all reasonable steps`)

@export Under section 369, how much of the political donation or expenditure was unauthorised, in pounds?
GIVEN `the amount of the donation or expenditure` IS A NUMBER @desc What is the amount of the donation or expenditure? (a number)
      `the part of it that was authorised` IS A NUMBER @desc What is the part of it that was authorised? (a number)
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `Under section 369, how much of the donation or expenditure was unauthorised, in pounds` IS
    `s 369(6) the amount of the donation or expenditure to which this section applies` `the amount of the donation or expenditure` `the part of it that was authorised`

@export Under section 369, how much of the unauthorised donation or expenditure is still to be made good to the company, before interest, in pounds?
GIVEN `the amount of the unauthorised donation or expenditure` IS A NUMBER @desc What is the amount of the unauthorised donation or expenditure? (a number)
      `the amount already made good to the company` IS A NUMBER @desc What is the amount already made good to the company? (a number)
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `Under section 369, how much of the unauthorised donation or expenditure is still to be made good to the company, before interest, in pounds` IS
    `s 369(2)(a) the amount of the unauthorised donation or expenditure still to be made good to the company` `the amount of the unauthorised donation or expenditure` `the amount already made good to the company`

@export Under section 370, are these members an authorised group (5% of the issued share capital by nominal value, 5% of the members if the company is not limited by shares, or 50 members)?
GIVEN `the nominal value of the issued share capital held by the members in the group` IS A NUMBER @desc What is the nominal value of the issued share capital held by the members in the group? (a number)
      `the nominal value of the company's issued share capital` IS A NUMBER @desc What is the nominal value of the company's issued share capital? (a number)
      `the company is limited by shares` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it true that the company is limited by shares? (true or false)
      `the number of members in the group` IS A NUMBER @desc What is the number of members in the group? (a number)
      `the number of members of the company` IS A NUMBER @desc What is the number of members of the company? (a number)
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 370, are these members an authorised group` IS
    `s 370(3) the members are an authorised group` `the nominal value of the issued share capital held by the members in the group` `the nominal value of the company's issued share capital` `the company is limited by shares` `the number of members in the group` `the number of members of the company`

@export Under section 371, has our group given the company written notice and waited at least 28 days before bringing proceedings under section 370?
GIVEN `the group has given written notice to the company` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it true that the group has given written notice to the company? (true or false)
      `the notice states the cause of action and a summary of the facts on which the proceedings are to be based` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it true that the notice states the cause of action and a summary of the facts on which the proceedings are to be based? (true or false)
      `the notice states the names and addresses of the members comprising the group` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it true that the notice states the names and addresses of the members comprising the group? (true or false)
      `the notice states the grounds on which it is alleged that those members constitute an authorised group` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it true that the notice states the grounds on which it is alleged that those members constitute an authorised group? (true or false)
      `the date of the giving of the notice to the company` IS A DATE @desc What is the date of the giving of the notice to the company? (a date)
      `the date of the bringing of the proceedings` IS A DATE @desc What is the date of the bringing of the proceedings? (a date)
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 371, has our group met the notice requirements for bringing proceedings under section 370` IS
    `s 371(1) the notice requirements are met` `the group has given written notice to the company` `the notice states the cause of action and a summary of the facts on which the proceedings are to be based` `the notice states the names and addresses of the members comprising the group` `the notice states the grounds on which it is alleged that those members constitute an authorised group` `the date of the giving of the notice to the company` `the date of the bringing of the proceedings`

@export Under section 371, may I, as a director, apply to the court for an order that the members' proposed proceedings are not to be brought?
GIVEN `I am a director of the company` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are you a director of the company? (true or false)
      `notice has been given to the company` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has a group of members given the company notice of proposed proceedings under section 370? (true or false)
      `the date the notice was given` IS A DATE @desc On what date was the notice given? (a date)
      `the date of my application` IS A DATE @desc On what date would you apply to the court? (a date)
      `my ground` IS A STRING @desc The ground of your application. One of: "made good" (the unauthorised amount has been made good to the company), "company proceeding" (the company has brought proceedings and is pursuing them with due diligence), "not an authorised group" (the members do not constitute an authorised group), or "other".
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 371, may I apply to the court for an order that the proposed proceedings are not to be brought` IS
    `s 371(2) the director may apply to the court for an order that the proposed proceedings shall not be brought` `I am a director of the company` `notice has been given to the company` `the date the notice was given` `the date of my application` ground
    WHERE
        ground MEANS
            BRANCH IF `my ground` EQUALS "made good" THEN `s 371(2)(a) the unauthorised amount has been made good to the company`
                   IF `my ground` EQUALS "company proceeding" THEN `s 371(2)(b) proceedings to enforce the liability have been brought, and are being pursued with due diligence, by the company`
                   IF `my ground` EQUALS "not an authorised group" THEN `s 371(2)(c) the members proposing to bring proceedings do not constitute an authorised group`
                   OTHERWISE `s 371(2) some other ground`

@export Under section 371, may the court give the alternative directions section 371(3) allows (the members' proceedings may be brought on terms; the company's proceedings are discontinued or continued on terms), where the application is on the ground that the company is already pursuing proceedings?
GIVEN `an application is made on the ground mentioned in subsection (2)(b)` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it true that an application is made on the ground mentioned in subsection (2)(b)? (true or false)
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 371, may the court give the alternative directions section 371(3) allows, where the application is on the ground that the company is already pursuing proceedings` IS
    `s 371(3) the court may make the alternative directions` `an application is made on the ground mentioned in subsection (2)(b)`

@export Under section 371, may the company bring proceedings to enforce the duties the members owe it, and does it have the court's permission?
GIVEN `the court has given permission` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it true that the court has given permission? (true or false)
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 371, may the company bring proceedings against the members who sued in its name` IS
    `s 371(4) the company may bring proceedings to enforce those duties` `the court has given permission`

@export Under section 371, has the court given permission for our group to discontinue or settle the proceedings?
GIVEN `the court has given permission` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it true that the court has given permission? (true or false)
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 371, may our group discontinue or settle the proceedings` IS
    `s 371(5) the group may discontinue or settle the proceedings` `the court has given permission`

@export Under section 372, has the court made an order directing the company to indemnify our group for its costs?
GIVEN `an order under subsection (2) has been made` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it true that an order under subsection (2) has been made? (true or false)
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 372, is our group entitled to be paid its costs out of the company's assets` IS
    `s 372(3) the group is entitled to be paid costs out of the assets of the company` `an order under subsection (2) has been made`

@export Under section 372, no indemnity order having been made, will costs awarded to the company be paid to our group?
GIVEN `an order under subsection (2) has been made` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it true that an order under subsection (2) has been made? (true or false)
      `the company is awarded costs in connection with the proceedings, or it is agreed that costs incurred by the company should be paid by any defendant` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it true that the company is awarded costs in connection with the proceedings, or it is agreed that costs incurred by the company should be paid by any defendant? (true or false)
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 372, will costs awarded to the company be paid to our group` IS
    `s 372(4)(a) the costs shall be paid to the group` `an order under subsection (2) has been made` `the company is awarded costs in connection with the proceedings, or it is agreed that costs incurred by the company should be paid by any defendant`

@export Under section 372, no indemnity order having been made, must our group pay costs awarded to a defendant?
GIVEN `an order under subsection (2) has been made` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it true that an order under subsection (2) has been made? (true or false)
      `any defendant is awarded costs in connection with the proceedings, or it is agreed that any defendant should be paid costs incurred by him in connection with the proceedings` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it true that any defendant is awarded costs in connection with the proceedings, or it is agreed that any defendant should be paid costs incurred by him in connection with the proceedings? (true or false)
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 372, must our group pay a defendant's costs` IS
    `s 372(4)(b) the costs shall be paid by the group` `an order under subsection (2) has been made` `any defendant is awarded costs in connection with the proceedings, or it is agreed that any defendant should be paid costs incurred by him in connection with the proceedings`

@export Under section 373, is our group entitled to require the company to provide information about the proceedings?
GIVEN `proceedings have been brought under section 370 in the name of the company by an authorised group` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it true that proceedings have been brought under section 370 in the name of the company by an authorised group? (true or false)
      `the information relates to the subject matter of the proceedings` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it true that the information relates to the subject matter of the proceedings? (true or false)
      `the information is in the company's possession or under its control or is reasonably obtainable by it` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it true that the information is in the company's possession or under its control or is reasonably obtainable by it? (true or false)
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 373, is our group entitled to require the company to give it information about the proceedings` IS
    `s 373(1) the group is entitled to require the company to provide the information` `proceedings have been brought under section 370 in the name of the company by an authorised group` `the information relates to the subject matter of the proceedings` `the information is in the company's possession or under its control or is reasonably obtainable by it`

@export Under section 373, may the court order the company, and officers or employees we name, to give our group the information?
GIVEN `the company, having been required by the group to do so, refuses to provide all or any of that information` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it true that the company, having been required by the group to do so, refuses to provide all or any of that information? (true or false)
      `the group has applied to the court` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it true that the group has applied to the court? (true or false)
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 373, may the court order the company and named officers or employees to give us the information` IS
    `s 373(2) the court may order the company and specified officers or employees to provide the information` `the company, having been required by the group to do so, refuses to provide all or any of that information` `the group has applied to the court`


§§ `Exemptions and minor definitions (ss 374 to 379)`
-- Is the payment to a trade union, a trade association or an all-party parliamentary group, covered by an order, or small?

@export Under section 374, is this donation to a trade union a political donation for the purposes of Part 14?
GIVEN `the payee is a trade union` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the payee a trade union (within section 1 of the Trade Union and Labour Relations (Consolidation) Act 1992 or Article 3 of the Industrial Relations (Northern Ireland) Order 1992)? (true or false)
      `the donation is a contribution to the union's political fund` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the donation a contribution to the union's political fund? (true or false)
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 374, is this donation to a trade union a political donation` IS
    `s 374(1) the donation to the trade union is a political donation for the purposes of this Part` (JUST `the payee is a trade union`) (JUST `the donation is a contribution to the union's political fund`)

@export Under section 375, is this subscription to a trade association a political donation for the purposes of Part 14?
GIVEN `the organisation is a trade association` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the payee an organisation formed for the purpose of furthering the trade interests of its members, or of persons represented by its members? (true or false)
      `the sum is a subscription paid for membership of the association` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it true that the sum is a subscription paid for membership of the association? (true or false)
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 375, is this subscription to a trade association a political donation` IS
    `s 375(1) the subscription is a political donation for the purposes of this Part` (JUST `the organisation is a trade association`) `the sum is a subscription paid for membership of the association`

@export Under section 375, how much of this payment to a trade association counts as a subscription, in pounds?
GIVEN `the payment` IS A NUMBER @desc What is the payment? (a number)
      `the part of it made for the purpose of financing any particular activity of the association` IS A NUMBER @desc What is the part of it made for the purpose of financing any particular activity of the association? (a number)
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `Under section 375, how much of this payment is a subscription, in pounds` IS
    `s 375(2) the part of the payment that is a subscription` `the payment` `the part of it made for the purpose of financing any particular activity of the association`

@export Under section 376, is this all-party parliamentary group a political organisation for the purposes of Part 14?
GIVEN `it is an all-party group` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it an all-party group? (true or false)
      `it is composed of members of Parliament` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it composed of members of one or both of the Houses of Parliament (or of such members and other persons)? (true or false)
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 376, is this all-party parliamentary group a political organisation` IS
    `s 376(1) the group is a political organisation for the purposes of this Part` (`s 376(2) the group is an all-party parliamentary group` `it is an all-party group` `it is composed of members of Parliament`)

@export Under section 377, is authorisation not needed for this political expenditure?
GIVEN `the expenditure is exempt by virtue of an order of the Secretary of State under this section` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the expenditure exempt by virtue of an order of the Secretary of State under section 377 (the order must cover the company or the expenditure)? (true or false)
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 377, is authorisation not needed for this political expenditure` IS
    `s 377(1) authorisation under this Part is not needed for the political expenditure` (JUST `the expenditure is exempt by virtue of an order of the Secretary of State under this section`)

@export Under section 378, how much of this donation needs authorisation, in pounds (authorisation is needed only to the extent that the donation and other relevant donations in twelve months exceed 5,000 pounds)?
GIVEN `this donation` IS A NUMBER @desc What is this donation? (a number)
      `the total of the other relevant donations made in the period of 12 months ending with the date of this donation` IS A NUMBER @desc What is the total of the other relevant donations made in the period of 12 months ending with the date of this donation? (a number)
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `Under section 378, how much of this donation needs authorisation, in pounds` IS
    `s 378(1) the part of this donation for which authorisation is needed` `this donation` `the total of the other relevant donations made in the period of 12 months ending with the date of this donation`

@export Under section 378, does the other donation fall in the period of 12 months ending with the date of this donation?
GIVEN `the date of the other donation` IS A DATE @desc What is the date of the other donation? (a date)
      `the date of this donation` IS A DATE @desc What is the date of this donation? (a date)
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 378, does this earlier donation fall in the twelve months ending with the date of this donation` IS
    `s 378(1)(b) the other donation falls in the period of 12 months ending with the date of this donation` `the date of the other donation` `the date of this donation`

@export Under section 378, does another donation count towards the 5,000 pounds limit on this donation?
GIVEN `the company making this donation is a subsidiary` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the company making this donation a subsidiary of another company? (true or false)
      `who made the other donation` IS A STRING @desc Who made the other donation, in relation to the company making this donation? One of: "the company itself", "a subsidiary of the company", "a holding company of the company", "another subsidiary of a holding company of the company", or "none of those".
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 378, does another donation count towards the 5,000 pounds limit on this donation` IS
    `s 378(2) the other donation is an other relevant donation` (JUST `the company making this donation is a subsidiary`) relation
    WHERE
        relation MEANS
            BRANCH IF `who made the other donation` EQUALS "the company itself" THEN `s 378(2) the company itself`
                   IF `who made the other donation` EQUALS "a subsidiary of the company" THEN `s 378(2) a subsidiary of the company`
                   IF `who made the other donation` EQUALS "a holding company of the company" THEN `s 378(2) a holding company of the company`
                   IF `who made the other donation` EQUALS "another subsidiary of a holding company of the company" THEN `s 378(2) another subsidiary of a holding company of the company`
                   OTHERWISE `s 378(2) none of those`

@export Under section 379, is this person a director for the purposes of Part 14 (a director includes a shadow director)?
GIVEN `the person occupies the position of director` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it true that the person occupies the position of director? (true or false)
      `the person is a shadow director` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it true that the person is a shadow director? (true or false)
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 379, is this person a director for the purposes of Part 14` IS
    `s 379(1) the person is a director for the purposes of this Part` (JUST `the person occupies the position of director`) (JUST `the person is a shadow director`)

@export Under section 379, on what date is the donation treated as made or the expenditure as incurred (the earlier date on which a contract for it was entered into, if it was made under a contract)?
GIVEN `the date on which the donation is made or the expenditure is incurred` IS A DATE @desc What is the date on which the donation is made or the expenditure is incurred? (a date)
      `it is made or incurred in pursuance of a contract` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it true that it is made or incurred in pursuance of a contract? (true or false)
      `the date on which that contract is entered into by the company` IS A DATE @desc What is the date on which that contract is entered into by the company? (a date)
GIVETH A DATE
DECIDE `Under section 379, on what date is the donation treated as made or the expenditure as incurred` IS
    `s 379(2) the time at which the donation is made or the expenditure is incurred` `the date on which the donation is made or the expenditure is incurred` `it is made or incurred in pursuance of a contract` `the date on which that contract is entered into by the company`


§ `Companies Act 2006, Part 15: accounts and reports`
-- Is this company a small company, a micro-entity or a quoted company? Which records, year-end, accounts, notes, approvals and reports does the Act require of its directors, and what happens if they are not done?


§§ `Chapter 1: Introductory (ss 380 to 385)`

@export Under section 380, do the requirements of Part 15 on accounts and reports apply to this period
GIVEN `the period is a financial year of a company` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it true that the period is a financial year of a company? (true or false)
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 380, do the requirements of Part 15 on accounts and reports apply to this period` IS
    `s 380(1) the requirements of this Part as to accounts and reports apply in relation to the period` `the period is a financial year of a company`

@export Under section 381, does the small companies regime apply to this company for the financial year
GIVEN `the company qualifies as small` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it true that the company qualifies as small? (true or false)
      `the company is excluded from the small companies regime` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it true that the company is excluded from the small companies regime? (true or false)
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 381, does the small companies regime apply to this company for the financial year` IS
    `s 381 the small companies regime applies to the company for the financial year` (JUST `the company qualifies as small`) (JUST `the company is excluded from the small companies regime`)

@export Under section 382, does this company meet the qualifying conditions for a small company in this year (at least two of: turnover, balance sheet total, employees, each within its limit)
GIVEN `turnover` IS A NUMBER @desc What is turnover? (a number)
      `balance sheet total` IS A NUMBER @desc What is balance sheet total? (a number)
      `number of employees` IS A NUMBER @desc What is number of employees? (a number)
      `the length of the financial year as a proportion of a year` IS A NUMBER @desc What is the length of the financial year as a proportion of a year? (a number)
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 382, does this company meet the qualifying conditions for a small company in this year` IS
    `s 382(3) the qualifying conditions are met in the year` `turnover` `balance sheet total` `number of employees` `the length of the financial year as a proportion of a year`

@export Under section 382, does this company qualify as small in a financial year after its first
GIVEN `the qualifying conditions are met in this year` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it true that the qualifying conditions are met in this year? (true or false)
      `the qualifying conditions were met in the previous year` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it true that the qualifying conditions were met in the previous year? (true or false)
      `the company qualified as small in the previous year` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it true that the company qualified as small in the previous year? (true or false)
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 382, does this company qualify as small in this financial year, after its first` IS
    `s 382(1A) the company qualifies as small in a subsequent financial year` `the qualifying conditions are met in this year` `the qualifying conditions were met in the previous year` `the company qualified as small in the previous year`

@export Under section 382, does this company qualify as small in its first financial year
GIVEN `the qualifying conditions are met in that year` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it true that the qualifying conditions are met in that year? (true or false)
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 382, does this company qualify as small in its first financial year` IS
    `s 382(1) the company qualifies as small in its first financial year` (JUST `the qualifying conditions are met in that year`)

@export Under section 382, what is this company's number of employees for the year (the average of the number employed in each month)
GIVEN `the number of persons employed under contracts of service by the company in each month of the financial year` IS A LIST OF NUMBER @desc What is the number of persons employed under contracts of service by the company in each month of the financial year? (a list of numbers, one per item)
GIVETH A MAYBE NUMBER
DECIDE `Under section 382, what is this company's number of employees for the year` IS
    `s 382(6) the number of employees` `the number of persons employed under contracts of service by the company in each month of the financial year`

@export Under section 383, does this group meet the qualifying conditions for a small group in this year (at least two of: aggregate turnover, aggregate balance sheet total, aggregate employees, each within its limit)
GIVEN `the aggregate turnover, net` IS A NUMBER @desc What is the aggregate turnover, net? (a number)
      `the aggregate turnover, gross` IS A NUMBER @desc What is the aggregate turnover, gross? (a number)
      `the aggregate balance sheet total, net` IS A NUMBER @desc What is the aggregate balance sheet total, net? (a number)
      `the aggregate balance sheet total, gross` IS A NUMBER @desc What is the aggregate balance sheet total, gross? (a number)
      `the aggregate number of employees` IS A NUMBER @desc What is the aggregate number of employees? (a number)
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 383, does this group meet the qualifying conditions for a small group in this year` IS
    `s 383(4) the qualifying conditions are met by the group in the year` `the aggregate turnover, net` `the aggregate turnover, gross` `the aggregate balance sheet total, net` `the aggregate balance sheet total, gross` `the aggregate number of employees`

@export Under section 383, does this group qualify as small in a financial year of the parent company after its first
GIVEN `the qualifying conditions are met by the group in this year` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it true that the qualifying conditions are met by the group in this year? (true or false)
      `the qualifying conditions were met by the group in the previous year` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it true that the qualifying conditions were met by the group in the previous year? (true or false)
      `the group qualified as small in the previous year` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it true that the group qualified as small in the previous year? (true or false)
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 383, does this group qualify as small in this financial year of the parent company, after its first` IS
    `s 383(2A) the group qualifies as small in a subsequent financial year` `the qualifying conditions are met by the group in this year` `the qualifying conditions were met by the group in the previous year` `the group qualified as small in the previous year`

@export Under section 383, does this parent company qualify as a small company (it must qualify as small itself and the group must qualify as small)
GIVEN `the parent company qualifies as small under section 382 on its own figures` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it true that the parent company qualifies as small under section 382 on its own figures? (true or false)
      `the group headed by it qualifies as a small group` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it true that the group headed by it qualifies as a small group? (true or false)
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 383, does this parent company qualify as a small company` IS
    `s 383(1) the parent company qualifies as a small company` (JUST `the parent company qualifies as small under section 382 on its own figures`) (JUST `the group headed by it qualifies as a small group`)

@export Under section 384, is this company excluded from the small companies regime (a public company, a banking or insurance company, a company in an ineligible group and the other kinds the section lists)
GIVEN `the company was at any time within the financial year a public company` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it true that the company was at any time within the financial year a public company? (true or false)
      `the company was at any time within the financial year an authorised insurance company` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it true that the company was at any time within the financial year an authorised insurance company? (true or false)
      `the company was at any time within the financial year a banking company` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it true that the company was at any time within the financial year a banking company? (true or false)
      `the company was at any time within the financial year an e-money issuer, a MiFID investment firm or a UCITS management company` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it true that the company was at any time within the financial year an e-money issuer, a MiFID investment firm or a UCITS management company? (true or false)
      `the company at any time within the financial year carried on insurance market activity` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it true that the company at any time within the financial year carried on insurance market activity? (true or false)
      `the company was at any time within the financial year a scheme funder of a Master Trust scheme` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it true that the company was at any time within the financial year a scheme funder of a Master Trust scheme? (true or false)
      `the company was at any time within the financial year a member of an ineligible group` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it true that the company was at any time within the financial year a member of an ineligible group? (true or false)
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 384, is this company excluded from the small companies regime` IS
    `s 384(1) the company is excluded from the small companies regime` `the company was at any time within the financial year a public company` `the company was at any time within the financial year an authorised insurance company` `the company was at any time within the financial year a banking company` (JUST `the company was at any time within the financial year an e-money issuer, a MiFID investment firm or a UCITS management company`) (JUST `the company at any time within the financial year carried on insurance market activity`) (JUST `the company was at any time within the financial year a scheme funder of a Master Trust scheme`) (JUST `the company was at any time within the financial year a member of an ineligible group`)

@export Under section 384A, does this company meet the qualifying conditions for a micro-entity in this year (at least two of: turnover, balance sheet total, employees, each within its limit)
GIVEN `turnover` IS A NUMBER @desc What is turnover? (a number)
      `balance sheet total` IS A NUMBER @desc What is balance sheet total? (a number)
      `number of employees` IS A NUMBER @desc What is number of employees? (a number)
      `the length of the financial year as a proportion of a year` IS A NUMBER @desc What is the length of the financial year as a proportion of a year? (a number)
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 384A, does this company meet the qualifying conditions for a micro-entity in this year` IS
    `s 384A(4) the qualifying conditions are met in the year` `turnover` `balance sheet total` `number of employees` `the length of the financial year as a proportion of a year`

@export Under section 384A, does this company qualify as a micro-entity in a financial year after its first
GIVEN `the qualifying conditions are met in this year` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it true that the qualifying conditions are met in this year? (true or false)
      `the qualifying conditions were met in the previous year` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it true that the qualifying conditions were met in the previous year? (true or false)
      `the company qualified as a micro-entity in the previous year` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it true that the company qualified as a micro-entity in the previous year? (true or false)
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 384A, does this company qualify as a micro-entity in this financial year, after its first` IS
    `s 384A(2) the company qualifies as a micro-entity in a subsequent financial year` `the qualifying conditions are met in this year` `the qualifying conditions were met in the previous year` `the company qualified as a micro-entity in the previous year`

@export Under section 384B, do the micro-entity provisions not apply to this company's accounts because of what the company is (an investment undertaking, a financial holding undertaking, a credit institution, an insurance undertaking, a charity and so on)
GIVEN `the company was at any time within the year excluded from the small companies regime` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it true that the company was at any time within the year excluded from the small companies regime? (true or false)
      `would have been an investment undertaking as defined in Article 2(14) of Directive 2013/34/EU were the United Kingdom a member State` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it true that would have been an investment undertaking as defined in Article 2(14) of Directive 2013/34/EU were the United Kingdom a member State? (true or false)
      `would have been a financial holding undertaking as defined in Article 2(15) of that Directive were the United Kingdom a member State` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it true that would have been a financial holding undertaking as defined in Article 2(15) of that Directive were the United Kingdom a member State? (true or false)
      `was a credit institution within the meaning given by Article 4(1)(1) of Regulation (EU) No. 575/2013 which is a CRR firm within the meaning of Article 4(1)(2A) of that Regulation` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it true that was a credit institution within the meaning given by Article 4(1)(1) of Regulation (EU) No. 575/2013 which is a CRR firm within the meaning of Article 4(1)(2A) of that Regulation? (true or false)
      `would have been an insurance undertaking as defined in Article 2(1) of Council Directive 91/674/EEC were the United Kingdom a member State` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it true that would have been an insurance undertaking as defined in Article 2(1) of Council Directive 91/674/EEC were the United Kingdom a member State? (true or false)
      `was a charity` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it true that was a charity? (true or false)
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 384B, do the micro-entity provisions not apply to this company's accounts because of what the company is` IS
    `s 384B(1) the micro-entity provisions do not apply to the company's accounts` (JUST `the company was at any time within the year excluded from the small companies regime`) (JUST `would have been an investment undertaking as defined in Article 2(14) of Directive 2013/34/EU were the United Kingdom a member State`) (JUST `would have been a financial holding undertaking as defined in Article 2(15) of that Directive were the United Kingdom a member State`) (JUST `was a credit institution within the meaning given by Article 4(1)(1) of Regulation (EU) No. 575/2013 which is a CRR firm within the meaning of Article 4(1)(2A) of that Regulation`) (JUST `would have been an insurance undertaking as defined in Article 2(1) of Council Directive 91/674/EEC were the United Kingdom a member State`) (JUST `was a charity`)

@export Under section 384B, do the micro-entity provisions also not apply to this company's accounts because the company is a parent company or is included in consolidated group accounts
GIVEN `the company is a parent company` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it true that the company is a parent company? (true or false)
      `the company prepares group accounts for that year as permitted by section 399(4)` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it true that the company prepares group accounts for that year as permitted by section 399(4)? (true or false)
      `the company's accounts are included in consolidated group accounts for that year` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it true that the company's accounts are included in consolidated group accounts for that year? (true or false)
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 384B, do the micro-entity provisions also not apply because the company is part of a group` IS
    `s 384B(2) the micro-entity provisions also do not apply to the company's accounts` (JUST `the company is a parent company`) `the company prepares group accounts for that year as permitted by section 399(4)` `the company's accounts are included in consolidated group accounts for that year`

@export Under section 385, is this company a quoted company (its equity share capital is included in the UK official list, officially listed in a European Economic Area state, or admitted to dealing on the New York Stock Exchange or Nasdaq)
GIVEN `its equity share capital has been included in the official list in accordance with the provisions of Part 6 of the Financial Services and Markets Act 2000` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it true that its equity share capital has been included in the official list in accordance with the provisions of Part 6 of the Financial Services and Markets Act 2000? (true or false)
      `its equity share capital is officially listed in an EEA State` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it true that its equity share capital is officially listed in an EEA State? (true or false)
      `its equity share capital is admitted to dealing on either the New York Stock Exchange or the exchange known as Nasdaq` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it true that its equity share capital is admitted to dealing on either the New York Stock Exchange or the exchange known as Nasdaq? (true or false)
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 385, is this company a quoted company` IS
    `s 385(2) the company is a quoted company` `its equity share capital has been included in the official list in accordance with the provisions of Part 6 of the Financial Services and Markets Act 2000` `its equity share capital is officially listed in an EEA State` `its equity share capital is admitted to dealing on either the New York Stock Exchange or the exchange known as Nasdaq`

@export Under section 385, is this company a quoted company in relation to this financial year (it was a quoted company immediately before the end of the accounting reference period)
GIVEN `the company is a quoted company immediately before the end of the accounting reference period by reference to which that financial year was determined` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it true that the company is a quoted company immediately before the end of the accounting reference period by reference to which that financial year was determined? (true or false)
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 385, is this company a quoted company in relation to this financial year` IS
    `s 385(1) the company is a quoted company in relation to the financial year` (JUST `the company is a quoted company immediately before the end of the accounting reference period by reference to which that financial year was determined`)

@export Under section 385, is this company an unquoted company (a company that is not a quoted company)
GIVEN `the company is a quoted company` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it true that the company is a quoted company? (true or false)
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 385, is this company an unquoted company` IS
    `s 385(3) the company is an unquoted company` (JUST `the company is a quoted company`)


§§ `Chapter 2: Accounting records (ss 386 to 389)`
-- Is the company keeping the accounting records the Act requires, and are they kept for long enough?

@export Under section 386, is this company required to keep adequate accounting records
GIVEN `the body is a company` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it true that the body is a company? (true or false)
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 386, is this company required to keep adequate accounting records` IS
    `s 386(1) the company is required to keep adequate accounting records` (JUST `the body is a company`)

@export Under section 386, are these records adequate accounting records
GIVEN `sufficient to show and explain the company's transactions` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it true that sufficient to show and explain the company's transactions? (true or false)
      `sufficient to disclose with reasonable accuracy, at any time, the financial position of the company at that time` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it true that sufficient to disclose with reasonable accuracy, at any time, the financial position of the company at that time? (true or false)
      `sufficient to enable the directors to ensure that any accounts required to be prepared comply with the requirements of this Act` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it true that sufficient to enable the directors to ensure that any accounts required to be prepared comply with the requirements of this Act? (true or false)
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 386, are these records adequate accounting records` IS
    `s 386(2) the records are adequate accounting records` `sufficient to show and explain the company's transactions` `sufficient to disclose with reasonable accuracy, at any time, the financial position of the company at that time` `sufficient to enable the directors to ensure that any accounts required to be prepared comply with the requirements of this Act`

@export Under section 386, do these records contain the entries and the record of assets and liabilities that the section requires
GIVEN `entries from day to day of all sums of money received and expended by the company and the matters in respect of which the receipt and expenditure takes place` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it true that entries from day to day of all sums of money received and expended by the company and the matters in respect of which the receipt and expenditure takes place? (true or false)
      `a record of the assets and liabilities of the company` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it true that a record of the assets and liabilities of the company? (true or false)
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 386, do these records contain the entries and the record of assets and liabilities that the section requires` IS
    `s 386(3) the records contain what subsection (3) requires` `entries from day to day of all sums of money received and expended by the company and the matters in respect of which the receipt and expenditure takes place` `a record of the assets and liabilities of the company`

@export Under section 386, must these records contain statements of stock held, stocktakings and goods sold and purchased
GIVEN `the company's business involves dealing in goods` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it true that the company's business involves dealing in goods? (true or false)
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 386, must these records contain statements of stock and of goods sold and purchased` IS
    `s 386(4) the records are required to contain the stock and goods statements` `the company's business involves dealing in goods`

@export Under section 386, do these records contain the stock and goods statements the section requires
GIVEN `the company's business involves dealing in goods` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it true that the company's business involves dealing in goods? (true or false)
      `statements of stock held by the company at the end of each financial year` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it true that statements of stock held by the company at the end of each financial year? (true or false)
      `all statements of stocktakings from which any such statement of stock has been or is to be prepared` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it true that all statements of stocktakings from which any such statement of stock has been or is to be prepared? (true or false)
      `every sale is of goods sold by way of ordinary retail trade` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it true that every sale is of goods sold by way of ordinary retail trade? (true or false)
      `statements of all goods sold and purchased show the goods and the buyers and sellers in sufficient detail to enable all these to be identified` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it true that statements of all goods sold and purchased show the goods and the buyers and sellers in sufficient detail to enable all these to be identified? (true or false)
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 386, do these records contain the stock and goods statements the section requires` IS
    `s 386(4) the records contain the statements subsection (4) requires` `the company's business involves dealing in goods` `statements of stock held by the company at the end of each financial year` `all statements of stocktakings from which any such statement of stock has been or is to be prepared` `every sale is of goods sold by way of ordinary retail trade` `statements of all goods sold and purchased show the goods and the buyers and sellers in sufficient detail to enable all these to be identified`

@export Under section 386, must this parent company take reasonable steps to secure that its subsidiary undertaking keeps accounting records
GIVEN `the company is a parent company` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it true that the company is a parent company? (true or false)
      `it has a subsidiary undertaking in relation to which the above requirements do not apply` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it true that it has a subsidiary undertaking in relation to which the above requirements do not apply? (true or false)
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 386, must this parent company take reasonable steps to secure that its subsidiary undertaking keeps accounting records` IS
    `s 386(5) the parent company is required to take reasonable steps to secure that the subsidiary undertaking keeps accounting records` (JUST `the company is a parent company`) `it has a subsidiary undertaking in relation to which the above requirements do not apply`

@export Under section 387, does this officer commit an offence because the company has failed to comply with a provision of section 386?
GIVEN `the company fails to comply with a provision of section 386` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it true that the company fails to comply with a provision of section 386? (true or false)
      `the officer is in default` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it true that the officer is in default? (true or false)
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 387, does this officer commit an offence because the company has failed to comply with a provision of section 386` IS
    `s 387(1) the officer commits an offence` (JUST `the company fails to comply with a provision of section 386`) (JUST `the officer is in default`)

@export Under section 387, does this officer have a defence to the accounting records offence
GIVEN `the person acted honestly` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it true that the person acted honestly? (true or false)
      `in the circumstances in which the company's business was carried on the default was excusable` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it true that in the circumstances in which the company's business was carried on the default was excusable? (true or false)
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 387, does this officer have a defence to the accounting records offence` IS
    `s 387(2) this subsection gives the person a defence on these facts` `the person acted honestly` `in the circumstances in which the company's business was carried on the default was excusable`

@export Under section 387, what is the penalty for the accounting records offence?
GIVEN `how I would be convicted` IS A STRING @desc How would the person be convicted? One of: "on indictment", "summary conviction", "summary conviction in England and Wales", "summary conviction in Scotland", "summary conviction in Northern Ireland".
GIVETH A MAYBE STRING
DECIDE `Under section 387, what is the penalty for the accounting records offence` IS
    `s 387(3) the penalty in words` (`s 387(3) the penalty on conviction` (`s 387(3) the mode of conviction named` `how I would be convicted`))

@export Under section 388, are the accounting records kept where and as the section requires
GIVEN `kept at the company's registered office` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it true that kept at the company's registered office? (true or false)
      `kept at such other place as the directors think fit` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it true that kept at such other place as the directors think fit? (true or false)
      `at all times open to inspection by the company's officers` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it true that at all times open to inspection by the company's officers? (true or false)
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 388, are the accounting records kept where and as the section requires` IS
    `s 388(1) the accounting records are kept as subsection (1) requires` `kept at the company's registered office` `kept at such other place as the directors think fit` `at all times open to inspection by the company's officers`

@export Under section 388, for records kept outside the United Kingdom, are the accounts and returns kept as the section requires
GIVEN `the accounting records are kept at a place outside the United Kingdom` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it true that the accounting records are kept at a place outside the United Kingdom? (true or false)
      `accounts and returns with respect to the business dealt with in those records are sent to, and kept at, a place in the United Kingdom` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it true that accounts and returns with respect to the business dealt with in those records are sent to, and kept at, a place in the United Kingdom? (true or false)
      `those accounts and returns are at all times open to such inspection` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it true that those accounts and returns are at all times open to such inspection? (true or false)
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 388, for records kept outside the United Kingdom, are the accounts and returns kept as the section requires` IS
    `s 388(2) the accounts and returns for records kept outside the United Kingdom are kept as subsection (2) requires` `the accounting records are kept at a place outside the United Kingdom` `accounts and returns with respect to the business dealt with in those records are sent to, and kept at, a place in the United Kingdom` `those accounts and returns are at all times open to such inspection`

@export Under section 388, are the accounts and returns sent to the United Kingdom such as the section requires
GIVEN `the accounting records are kept at a place outside the United Kingdom` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it true that the accounting records are kept at a place outside the United Kingdom? (true or false)
      `the longest interval between the dates at which the accounts and returns disclose the financial position of the business, in months` IS A NUMBER @desc What is the longest interval between the dates at which the accounts and returns disclose the financial position of the business, in months? (a number)
      `they disclose it with reasonable accuracy` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it true that they disclose it with reasonable accuracy? (true or false)
      `they enable the directors to ensure that the accounts required to be prepared under this Part comply with the requirements of this Act` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it true that they enable the directors to ensure that the accounts required to be prepared under this Part comply with the requirements of this Act? (true or false)
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 388, are the accounts and returns sent to the United Kingdom such as the section requires` IS
    `s 388(3) the accounts and returns sent to the United Kingdom are such as subsection (3) requires` `the accounting records are kept at a place outside the United Kingdom` `the longest interval between the dates at which the accounts and returns disclose the financial position of the business, in months` `they disclose it with reasonable accuracy` `they enable the directors to ensure that the accounts required to be prepared under this Part comply with the requirements of this Act`

@export Under section 388, for how long must the company keep its accounting records?
GIVEN `the company is a public company` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the company a public company? (true or false)
GIVETH A STRING
DECIDE `Under section 388, for how long must the company keep its accounting records` IS
    `s 387(3) the period in words` (`s 388(4) the period for which the accounting records must be preserved` `the company is a public company`)

@export Under section 388, must the company still keep its accounting records on this day (a rule of insolvency law may displace the usual period)
GIVEN `the company is a public company` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it true that the company is a public company? (true or false)
      `the date on which the records were made` IS A DATE @desc What is the date on which the records were made? (a date)
      `day` IS A DATE @desc On what date are you asking whether the records must still be kept? (a date)
      `a provision of insolvency rules displaces subsection (4)` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it true that a provision of insolvency rules displaces subsection (4)? (true or false)
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 388, must the company still keep its accounting records on this day` IS
    `s 388(4) the accounting records must still be preserved on the day` `the company is a public company` `the date on which the records were made` `day` (JUST `a provision of insolvency rules displaces subsection (4)`)

@export Under section 389, does this officer commit an offence because the company has failed to comply with a provision of section 388(1) to (3)?
GIVEN `the company fails to comply with a provision of subsections (1) to (3) of section 388` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it true that the company fails to comply with a provision of subsections (1) to (3) of section 388? (true or false)
      `the officer is in default` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it true that the officer is in default? (true or false)
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 389, does this officer commit an offence because the company has failed to comply with a provision of section 388(1) to (3)` IS
    `s 389(1) the officer commits an offence` (JUST `the company fails to comply with a provision of subsections (1) to (3) of section 388`) (JUST `the officer is in default`)

@export Under section 389, does this officer have a defence to the offence under section 389(1)
GIVEN `the person acted honestly` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it true that the person acted honestly? (true or false)
      `in the circumstances in which the company's business was carried on the default was excusable` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it true that in the circumstances in which the company's business was carried on the default was excusable? (true or false)
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 389, does this officer have a defence to the offence under section 389(1)` IS
    `s 389(2) this subsection gives the person a defence on these facts` `the person acted honestly` `in the circumstances in which the company's business was carried on the default was excusable`

@export Under section 389, does this officer commit an offence by failing to take all reasonable steps to secure that the accounting records are preserved for the period section 388(4) requires, or by intentionally causing a default in preserving them?
GIVEN `the person is an officer of the company` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are you an officer of the company? (true or false)
      `fails to take all reasonable steps for securing compliance by the company with subsection (4) of that section` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it true that fails to take all reasonable steps for securing compliance by the company with subsection (4) of that section? (true or false)
      `intentionally causes any default by the company under that subsection` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did you intentionally cause any default by the company in preserving its accounting records for that period? (true or false)
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 389, does this officer commit an offence by failing to take all reasonable steps to secure that the accounting records are preserved as section 388(4) requires, or by intentionally causing a default in preserving them` IS
    `s 389(3) the officer commits an offence` `the person is an officer of the company` `fails to take all reasonable steps for securing compliance by the company with subsection (4) of that section` `intentionally causes any default by the company under that subsection`

@export Under section 389, what is the penalty for an offence under that section?
GIVEN `how I would be convicted` IS A STRING @desc How would the person be convicted? One of: "on indictment", "summary conviction", "summary conviction in England and Wales", "summary conviction in Scotland", "summary conviction in Northern Ireland".
GIVETH A MAYBE STRING
DECIDE `Under section 389, what is the penalty for an offence under that section` IS
    `s 387(3) the penalty in words` (`s 389(4) the penalty on conviction` (`s 387(3) the mode of conviction named` `how I would be convicted`))


§§ `Chapter 3: A company's financial year (ss 390 to 392)`
-- When does the company's financial year begin and end, and may it change its accounting reference date?

@export Under section 390, on what date does the company's first financial year begin
GIVEN `the first day of its first accounting reference period` IS A DATE @desc What is the first day of its first accounting reference period? (a date)
GIVETH A DATE
DECIDE `Under section 390, on what date does the company's first financial year begin` IS
    `s 390(2)(a) the first day of the first financial year` `the first day of its first accounting reference period`

@export Under section 390, on what date does the company's first financial year end?
GIVEN `the last day of the first accounting reference period` IS A DATE @desc What is the last day of the company's first accounting reference period? (a date)
      `the directors determine a different date` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Have the directors determined that the financial year ends on a different date, not more than seven days before or after that last day? (true or false)
      `the date the directors determine` IS A DATE @desc If so, what date have they determined? (a date; any date if they have determined none)
GIVETH A MAYBE DATE
DECIDE `Under section 390, on what date does the company's first financial year end` IS
    `s 390(2)(b) the last day of the first financial year` `the last day of the first accounting reference period` (IF `the directors determine a different date` THEN JUST `the date the directors determine` ELSE NOTHING)

@export Under section 390, on what date does a financial year after the first begin
GIVEN `the last day of the company's previous financial year` IS A DATE @desc What is the last day of the company's previous financial year? (a date)
GIVETH A DATE
DECIDE `Under section 390, on what date does a later financial year begin` IS
    `s 390(3)(a) the first day of a subsequent financial year` `the last day of the company's previous financial year`

@export Under section 390, on what date does a later financial year end?
GIVEN `the last day of its next accounting reference period` IS A DATE @desc What is the last day of the company's next accounting reference period? (a date)
      `the directors determine a different date` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Have the directors determined that the financial year ends on a different date, not more than seven days before or after that last day? (true or false)
      `the date the directors determine` IS A DATE @desc If so, what date have they determined? (a date; any date if they have determined none)
GIVETH A MAYBE DATE
DECIDE `Under section 390, on what date does a later financial year end` IS
    `s 390(3)(b) the last day of a subsequent financial year` `the last day of its next accounting reference period` (IF `the directors determine a different date` THEN JUST `the date the directors determine` ELSE NOTHING)

@export Under section 390, is this period the financial year of an undertaking that is not a company
GIVEN `a profit and loss account of the undertaking is required to be made up for the period (by its constitution or by the law under which it is established)` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it true that a profit and loss account of the undertaking is required to be made up for the period (by its constitution or by the law under which it is established)? (true or false)
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 390, is this period the financial year of an undertaking that is not a company` IS
    `s 390(4) the period is the financial year of the undertaking that is not a company` `a profit and loss account of the undertaking is required to be made up for the period (by its constitution or by the law under which it is established)`

@export Under section 390, must the directors secure that the financial year of each subsidiary undertaking coincides with the company's own
GIVEN `the company is a parent company` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it true that the company is a parent company? (true or false)
      `in their opinion there are good reasons against it` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it true that in their opinion there are good reasons against it? (true or false)
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 390, must the directors secure that the financial year of each subsidiary undertaking coincides with the company's own` IS
    `s 390(5) the directors are required to secure that the financial year of each subsidiary undertaking coincides with the company's own` (JUST `the company is a parent company`) `in their opinion there are good reasons against it`

@export Under section 391, on what date does the company's first accounting reference period end?
GIVEN `the date of incorporation` IS A DATE @desc On what date was the company incorporated? (a date)
      `its reference date is a fixed day and month` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the accounting reference date a fixed day and month (true), or the last day of a month (false)? (true or false)
      `the month of the fixed day, or of the last day` IS A NUMBER @desc The month (1 to 12) of the accounting reference date. (a number)
      `the day of the month of the fixed day` IS A NUMBER @desc If a fixed day and month, the day of that month. Enter 0 if the date is the last day of a month. (a number)
GIVETH A DATE
DECIDE `Under section 391, on what date does the company's first accounting reference period end` IS
    `s 391(5) the last day of the first accounting reference period` `the date of incorporation`
        (IF `its reference date is a fixed day and month`
         THEN `s 391 a fixed day and month` `the day of the month of the fixed day` `the month of the fixed day, or of the last day`
         ELSE `s 391 the last day of a month` `the month of the fixed day, or of the last day`)

@export Under section 392, is a notice to change the accounting reference date ineffective because an earlier extension was too recent?
GIVEN `the notice extends the company's current or previous accounting reference period` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does the notice extend the company's current or previous accounting reference period? (true or false)
      `the date on which the notice is given` IS A DATE @desc On what date is the notice given? (a date)
      `an earlier accounting reference period of the company was extended under this section` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Was an earlier accounting reference period of the company extended under section 392? (true or false)
      `the end of the earlier extended accounting reference period` IS A DATE @desc If so, on what date did that earlier accounting reference period end? (a date; any date if there was none)
      `the company is a subsidiary undertaking or parent undertaking of another UK undertaking` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the company a subsidiary undertaking or a parent undertaking of another UK undertaking? (true or false)
      `the new accounting reference date coincides with that of the other UK undertaking` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does the new accounting reference date coincide with that of the other UK undertaking or, if that undertaking is not a company, with the last day of its financial year? (true or false)
      `the company is in administration` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the company in administration under Part 2 of the Insolvency Act 1986 or Part 3 of the Insolvency (Northern Ireland) Order 1989? (true or false)
      `the Secretary of State directs that the bar should not apply` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has the Secretary of State directed that the bar should not apply? (true or false)
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 392, is a notice to change the accounting reference date ineffective because an earlier extension was too recent` IS
    `s 392(3) the notice is ineffective because it is given less than five years after an earlier extension`
        `the notice extends the company's current or previous accounting reference period`
        `the date on which the notice is given`
        (IF `an earlier accounting reference period of the company was extended under this section` THEN JUST `the end of the earlier extended accounting reference period` ELSE NOTHING)
        (JUST `the company is a subsidiary undertaking or parent undertaking of another UK undertaking`)
        `the new accounting reference date coincides with that of the other UK undertaking`
        `the company is in administration`
        `the Secretary of State directs that the bar should not apply`

@export Under section 392, may a notice be given in respect of the previous accounting reference period
GIVEN `the period for filing accounts and reports for the financial year determined by reference to that accounting reference period has already expired` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it true that the period for filing accounts and reports for the financial year determined by reference to that accounting reference period has already expired? (true or false)
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 392, may a notice be given in respect of the previous accounting reference period` IS
    `s 392(4) a notice may be given in respect of the previous accounting reference period` `the period for filing accounts and reports for the financial year determined by reference to that accounting reference period has already expired`

@export Under section 392, is a notice ineffective because the period as extended would exceed 18 months
GIVEN `the first day of the period` IS A DATE @desc What is the first day of the period? (a date)
      `the last day of the period as extended in accordance with the notice` IS A DATE @desc What is the last day of the period as extended in accordance with the notice? (a date)
      `the company is in administration under Part 2 of the Insolvency Act 1986 or Part 3 of the Insolvency (Northern Ireland) Order 1989` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it true that the company is in administration under Part 2 of the Insolvency Act 1986 or Part 3 of the Insolvency (Northern Ireland) Order 1989? (true or false)
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 392, is a notice ineffective because the extended period would exceed 18 months` IS
    `s 392(5) the notice is ineffective because the period as extended would exceed 18 months` `the first day of the period` `the last day of the period as extended in accordance with the notice` `the company is in administration under Part 2 of the Insolvency Act 1986 or Part 3 of the Insolvency (Northern Ireland) Order 1989`

@export Under section 392, is this undertaking a UK undertaking
GIVEN `it is an undertaking established under the law of any part of the United Kingdom` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it true that it is an undertaking established under the law of any part of the United Kingdom? (true or false)
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 392, is this undertaking a UK undertaking` IS
    `s 392(6) the undertaking is a UK undertaking` `it is an undertaking established under the law of any part of the United Kingdom`


§§ `Chapter 4: Annual accounts (ss 393 to 414)`


§§§ `Individual accounts (ss 393 to 398)`
-- What must the directors satisfy themselves of before approving the accounts, and which accounts must they prepare?

@export Under section 393, are the conditions for the directors to approve the individual accounts met
GIVEN `the directors are satisfied that the accounts give a true and fair view of the assets, liabilities, financial position and profit or loss of the company` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it true that the directors are satisfied that the accounts give a true and fair view of the assets, liabilities, financial position and profit or loss of the company? (true or false)
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 393, are the conditions for the directors to approve the individual accounts met` IS
    `s 393(1)(a) the condition for approving the company's individual accounts is met` `the directors are satisfied that the accounts give a true and fair view of the assets, liabilities, financial position and profit or loss of the company`

@export Under section 393, are the conditions for the directors to approve the group accounts met
GIVEN `the directors are satisfied that the accounts give a true and fair view of the assets, liabilities, financial position and profit or loss of the undertakings included in the consolidation as a whole, so far as concerns members of the company` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it true that the directors are satisfied that the accounts give a true and fair view of the assets, liabilities, financial position and profit or loss of the undertakings included in the consolidation as a whole, so far as concerns members of the company? (true or false)
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 393, are the conditions for the directors to approve the group accounts met` IS
    `s 393(1)(b) the condition for approving the company's group accounts is met` `the directors are satisfied that the accounts give a true and fair view of the assets, liabilities, financial position and profit or loss of the undertakings included in the consolidation as a whole, so far as concerns members of the company`

@export Under section 393, must the auditor have regard to the directors' duty not to approve accounts that do not give a true and fair view
GIVEN `the auditor is carrying out functions under this Act in relation to the company's annual accounts` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it true that the auditor is carrying out functions under this Act in relation to the company's annual accounts? (true or false)
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 393, must the auditor have regard to the directors' duty not to approve accounts that do not give a true and fair view` IS
    `s 393(2) the auditor is required to have regard to the directors' duty under subsection (1)` `the auditor is carrying out functions under this Act in relation to the company's annual accounts`

@export Under section 394, are the directors required to prepare individual accounts for the financial year
GIVEN `the company is exempt from the requirement under section 394A` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it true that the company is exempt from the requirement under section 394A? (true or false)
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 394, are the directors required to prepare individual accounts for the financial year` IS
    `s 394 the directors are required to prepare individual accounts for the financial year` (JUST `the company is exempt from the requirement under section 394A`)

@export Under section 394A, is this subsidiary company exempt from the requirement to prepare individual accounts
GIVEN `the company is a subsidiary undertaking` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it true that the company is a subsidiary undertaking? (true or false)
      `the company has been dormant throughout the whole of the year` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it true that the company has been dormant throughout the whole of the year? (true or false)
      `its parent undertaking is established under the law of any part of the United Kingdom` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it true that its parent undertaking is established under the law of any part of the United Kingdom? (true or false)
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 394A, is this subsidiary company exempt from the requirement to prepare individual accounts` IS
    `s 394A(1) the company is exempt from the requirement to prepare individual accounts for the financial year` (JUST `the company is a subsidiary undertaking`) `the company has been dormant throughout the whole of the year` `its parent undertaking is established under the law of any part of the United Kingdom`

@export Under section 394A, are all the conditions of the subsidiary company's exemption from preparing individual accounts complied with
GIVEN `all members of the company agree to the exemption in respect of the financial year in question` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it true that all members of the company agree to the exemption in respect of the financial year in question? (true or false)
      `a guarantee is given by the parent undertaking in respect of that year` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it true that a guarantee is given by the parent undertaking in respect of that year? (true or false)
      `the company is included in the consolidated accounts drawn up for that year or to an earlier date in that year by the parent undertaking in accordance with the requirements of this Part or the legal requirements that apply to it, or UK-adopted international accounting standards` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it true that the company is included in the consolidated accounts drawn up for that year or to an earlier date in that year by the parent undertaking in accordance with the requirements of this Part or the legal requirements that apply to it, or UK-adopted international accounting standards? (true or false)
      `the parent undertaking discloses in the notes to the consolidated accounts that the company is exempt from the requirement to prepare individual accounts by virtue of section 394A` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it true that the parent undertaking discloses in the notes to the consolidated accounts that the company is exempt from the requirement to prepare individual accounts by virtue of section 394A? (true or false)
      `the directors have delivered to the registrar a written notice of the agreement referred to in subsection (2)(a)` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it true that the directors have delivered to the registrar a written notice of the agreement referred to in subsection (2)(a)? (true or false)
      `the directors have delivered to the registrar the statement referred to in section 394C(1)` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it true that the directors have delivered to the registrar the statement referred to in section 394C(1)? (true or false)
      `the directors have delivered to the registrar a copy of the consolidated accounts referred to in subsection (2)(c)` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it true that the directors have delivered to the registrar a copy of the consolidated accounts referred to in subsection (2)(c)? (true or false)
      `the directors have delivered to the registrar a copy of the auditor's report on those accounts` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it true that the directors have delivered to the registrar a copy of the auditor's report on those accounts? (true or false)
      `the directors have delivered to the registrar a copy of the consolidated annual report drawn up by the parent undertaking` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it true that the directors have delivered to the registrar a copy of the consolidated annual report drawn up by the parent undertaking? (true or false)
      `the date on which the directors delivered the documents` IS A DATE @desc What is the date on which the directors delivered the documents? (a date)
      `the last day of the period for filing the company's accounts and reports for that year` IS A DATE @desc What is the last day of the period for filing the company's accounts and reports for that year? (a date)
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 394A, are all the conditions of the subsidiary company's exemption complied with` IS
    `s 394A(2) the conditions of the exemption are all complied with` `all members of the company agree to the exemption in respect of the financial year in question` (JUST `a guarantee is given by the parent undertaking in respect of that year`) `the company is included in the consolidated accounts drawn up for that year or to an earlier date in that year by the parent undertaking in accordance with the requirements of this Part or the legal requirements that apply to it, or UK-adopted international accounting standards` `the parent undertaking discloses in the notes to the consolidated accounts that the company is exempt from the requirement to prepare individual accounts by virtue of section 394A` `the directors have delivered to the registrar a written notice of the agreement referred to in subsection (2)(a)` `the directors have delivered to the registrar the statement referred to in section 394C(1)` `the directors have delivered to the registrar a copy of the consolidated accounts referred to in subsection (2)(c)` `the directors have delivered to the registrar a copy of the auditor's report on those accounts` `the directors have delivered to the registrar a copy of the consolidated annual report drawn up by the parent undertaking` `the date on which the directors delivered the documents` `the last day of the period for filing the company's accounts and reports for that year`

@export Under section 394B, is this company, so far as section 394B goes, entitled to the exemption conferred by section 394A (it is not if it is one of the excluded kinds; if it is none of them, section 394A decides)?
GIVEN `the company was at any time within the financial year a traded company` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it true that the company was at any time within the financial year a traded company? (true or false)
      `the company was at any time within the financial year an authorised insurance company` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it true that the company was at any time within the financial year an authorised insurance company? (true or false)
      `the company was at any time within the financial year a banking company` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it true that the company was at any time within the financial year a banking company? (true or false)
      `the company was at any time within the financial year an e-money issuer, a MiFID investment firm or a UCITS management company` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it true that the company was at any time within the financial year an e-money issuer, a MiFID investment firm or a UCITS management company? (true or false)
      `the company at any time within the financial year carried on insurance market activity` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it true that the company at any time within the financial year carried on insurance market activity? (true or false)
      `the company was at any time within the financial year a special register body as defined in section 117(1) of the Trade Union and Labour Relations (Consolidation) Act 1992 or an employers' association as defined in section 122 of that Act or Article 4 of the Industrial Relations (Northern Ireland) Order 1992` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it true that the company was at any time within the financial year a special register body as defined in section 117(1) of the Trade Union and Labour Relations (Consolidation) Act 1992 or an employers' association as defined in section 122 of that Act or Article 4 of the Industrial Relations (Northern Ireland) Order 1992? (true or false)
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 394B, is this company, so far as section 394B goes, entitled to the exemption conferred by section 394A` IS
    `s 394B the company is entitled to the exemption conferred by section 394A` (JUST `the company was at any time within the financial year a traded company`) `the company was at any time within the financial year an authorised insurance company` `the company was at any time within the financial year a banking company` (JUST `the company was at any time within the financial year an e-money issuer, a MiFID investment firm or a UCITS management company`) (JUST `the company at any time within the financial year carried on insurance market activity`) (JUST `the company was at any time within the financial year a special register body as defined in section 117(1) of the Trade Union and Labour Relations (Consolidation) Act 1992 or an employers' association as defined in section 122 of that Act or Article 4 of the Industrial Relations (Northern Ireland) Order 1992`)

@export Under section 394C, does the parent undertaking's statement of guarantee meet the requirements of the section
GIVEN `the statement is authenticated by the parent undertaking` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it true that the statement is authenticated by the parent undertaking? (true or false)
      `it specifies the name of the parent undertaking` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it true that it specifies the name of the parent undertaking? (true or false)
      `it specifies the registered number (if any) of the parent undertaking` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it true that it specifies the registered number (if any) of the parent undertaking? (true or false)
      `it specifies the name and registered number of the subsidiary company in respect of which the guarantee is being given` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it true that it specifies the name and registered number of the subsidiary company in respect of which the guarantee is being given? (true or false)
