@export Under section 401, is this company within one of the cases that carry the exemption for a subsidiary whose parent undertaking is not established in the United Kingdom
GIVEN `the company is itself a subsidiary undertaking` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it true that the company is itself a subsidiary undertaking? (true or false)
      `its parent undertaking is not established under the law of any part of the United Kingdom` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it true that its parent undertaking is not established under the law of any part of the United Kingdom? (true or false)
      `case (a)` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the company a wholly-owned subsidiary of that parent undertaking? (true or false)
      `case (b)` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does that parent undertaking hold 90% or more of the allotted shares in the company, and have the remaining shareholders approved the exemption? (true or false)
      `case (c)` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does that parent undertaking hold more than 50% (but less than 90%) of the allotted shares, with no notice requesting group accounts served on the company by shareholders holding at least 5% in aggregate (or 5% of the shares not held by the parent) at least six months before the end of the financial year? (true or false)
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 401, is this company within one of the cases that carry the exemption for a subsidiary of a parent undertaking not established in the United Kingdom` IS
    `s 401(1) the company is within one of the cases that carry the exemption` (JUST `the company is itself a subsidiary undertaking`) `its parent undertaking is not established under the law of any part of the United Kingdom` (JUST `case (a)`) (JUST `case (b)`) (JUST `case (c)`)

@export Under section 401, are all the conditions of the exemption complied with
GIVEN `the company and all of its subsidiary undertakings are included in consolidated accounts for a larger group drawn up to the same date, or to an earlier date in the same financial year, by a parent undertaking` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it true that the company and all of its subsidiary undertakings are included in consolidated accounts for a larger group drawn up to the same date, or to an earlier date in the same financial year, by a parent undertaking? (true or false)
      `those accounts and, where appropriate, the group's annual report are drawn up in a manner equivalent to this Part, or in accordance with UK-adopted international accounting standards or equivalent standards` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it true that those accounts and, where appropriate, the group's annual report are drawn up in a manner equivalent to this Part, or in accordance with UK-adopted international accounting standards or equivalent standards? (true or false)
      `the group accounts are audited by one or more persons authorised to audit accounts under the law under which the parent undertaking is established` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it true that the group accounts are audited by one or more persons authorised to audit accounts under the law under which the parent undertaking is established? (true or false)
      `the company discloses in its individual accounts that it is exempt from the obligation to prepare and deliver group accounts` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it true that the company discloses in its individual accounts that it is exempt from the obligation to prepare and deliver group accounts? (true or false)
      `the company states in its individual accounts the name of the parent undertaking that draws up the group accounts and the address of its registered office (whether in or outside the United Kingdom) or, if it is unincorporated, of its principal place of business` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it true that the company states in its individual accounts the name of the parent undertaking that draws up the group accounts and the address of its registered office (whether in or outside the United Kingdom) or, if it is unincorporated, of its principal place of business? (true or false)
      `the company delivers to the registrar, within the period for filing its accounts and reports for the financial year, copies of the group accounts and, where appropriate, the consolidated annual report, together with the auditor's report on them` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it true that the company delivers to the registrar, within the period for filing its accounts and reports for the financial year, copies of the group accounts and, where appropriate, the consolidated annual report, together with the auditor's report on them? (true or false)
      `any requirement of Part 35 as to the delivery of a certified translation into English is met` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it true that any requirement of Part 35 as to the delivery of a certified translation into English is met? (true or false)
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 401, are all the conditions of the exemption complied with` IS
    `s 401(2) the conditions of the exemption are all complied with` `the company and all of its subsidiary undertakings are included in consolidated accounts for a larger group drawn up to the same date, or to an earlier date in the same financial year, by a parent undertaking` `those accounts and, where appropriate, the group's annual report are drawn up in a manner equivalent to this Part, or in accordance with UK-adopted international accounting standards or equivalent standards` `the group accounts are audited by one or more persons authorised to audit accounts under the law under which the parent undertaking is established` `the company discloses in its individual accounts that it is exempt from the obligation to prepare and deliver group accounts` `the company states in its individual accounts the name of the parent undertaking that draws up the group accounts and the address of its registered office (whether in or outside the United Kingdom) or, if it is unincorporated, of its principal place of business` `the company delivers to the registrar, within the period for filing its accounts and reports for the financial year, copies of the group accounts and, where appropriate, the consolidated annual report, together with the auditor's report on them` `any requirement of Part 35 as to the delivery of a certified translation into English is met`

