    `s 411(1A) the notes must also disclose the average number of persons within each category` (JUST `the company is subject to the small companies regime`)

@export Under section 411, what is the average number of persons employed (the relevant annual number divided by the number of months in the financial year)
GIVEN `the relevant annual number` IS A NUMBER @desc What is the relevant annual number? (a number)
      `the number of months in the financial year` IS A NUMBER @desc What is the number of months in the financial year? (a number)
GIVETH A MAYBE NUMBER
DECIDE `Under section 411, what is the average number of persons employed` IS
    `s 411(3) the average number` `the relevant annual number` `the number of months in the financial year`

@export Under section 411, must the notes or the profit and loss account disclose the total staff costs (a company not subject to the small companies regime)
GIVEN `the company is subject to the small companies regime` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it true that the company is subject to the small companies regime? (true or false)
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 411, must the notes or the profit and loss account disclose the total staff costs` IS
    `s 411(5) the notes or the profit and loss account must disclose the total staff costs` (JUST `the company is subject to the small companies regime`)

@export Under section 411, what are the total staff costs, in pounds (wages and salaries, social security costs and other pension costs)
GIVEN `wages and salaries paid or payable in respect of the year to those persons` IS A NUMBER @desc What is wages and salaries paid or payable in respect of the year to those persons? (a number)
      `social security costs incurred by the company on their behalf` IS A NUMBER @desc What is social security costs incurred by the company on their behalf? (a number)
      `other pension costs so incurred` IS A NUMBER @desc What is other pension costs so incurred? (a number)
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `Under section 411, what are the total staff costs, in pounds` IS
    `s 411(5) the total staff costs` `wages and salaries paid or payable in respect of the year to those persons` `social security costs incurred by the company on their behalf` `other pension costs so incurred`

@export Under section 411, is this cost a pension cost
GIVEN `costs in respect of a pension scheme established for the purpose of providing pensions for persons currently or formerly employed by the company` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it true that costs in respect of a pension scheme established for the purpose of providing pensions for persons currently or formerly employed by the company? (true or false)
      `costs in respect of sums set aside for the future payment of pensions directly by the company to current or former employees` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it true that costs in respect of sums set aside for the future payment of pensions directly by the company to current or former employees? (true or false)
      `costs in respect of pensions paid directly to such persons without having first been set aside` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it true that costs in respect of pensions paid directly to such persons without having first been set aside? (true or false)
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 411, is this cost a pension cost` IS
    `s 411(6) the cost is a pension cost` `costs in respect of a pension scheme established for the purpose of providing pensions for persons currently or formerly employed by the company` `costs in respect of sums set aside for the future payment of pensions directly by the company to current or former employees` `costs in respect of pensions paid directly to such persons without having first been set aside`

@export Under section 411, is this cost a social security cost
GIVEN `it is a contribution by the company to a state social security or pension scheme, fund or arrangement` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it true that it is a contribution by the company to a state social security or pension scheme, fund or arrangement? (true or false)
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 411, is this cost a social security cost` IS
    `s 411(6) the cost is a social security cost` `it is a contribution by the company to a state social security or pension scheme, fund or arrangement`

@export Under section 412, is this amount treated as paid to or receivable by the director (it is paid to a person connected with the director or to a body corporate the director controls)
GIVEN `the amount is paid to or receivable by a person connected with the director` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it true that the amount is paid to or receivable by a person connected with the director? (true or false)
      `the amount is paid to or receivable by a body corporate controlled by the director` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it true that the amount is paid to or receivable by a body corporate controlled by the director? (true or false)
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 412, is this amount treated as paid to or receivable by the director` IS
    `s 412(4) the amount is treated as paid to or receivable by the director` (JUST `the amount is paid to or receivable by a person connected with the director`) (JUST `the amount is paid to or receivable by a body corporate controlled by the director`)

@export Under section 412, am I, as a director or a director of the last five years, under a duty to give the company notice of matters about myself?
GIVEN `I am a director of the company` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are you a director of the company now? (true or false)
      `I have been a director of the company at some time` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Have you ever been a director of the company? (true or false)
      `the last day on which I was a director of the company` IS A DATE @desc If you have been a director, on what date did you last cease to be one (or today's date, if you still are)? (a date; any date if you never were)
      `the day on which the question is asked` IS A DATE @desc On what date are you asking? (a date)
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 412, am I under a duty to give the company notice of matters relating to myself` IS
    `s 412(5) the person is under the duty to give notice to the company of such matters relating to himself as regulations require` (JUST `I am a director of the company`) (IF `I have been a director of the company at some time` THEN JUST `the last day on which I was a director of the company` ELSE NOTHING) `the day on which the question is asked`

@export Under section 412, do I commit an offence by making default in giving the notice
GIVEN `the person is under the duty to give notice to the company of such matters relating to himself as regulations require` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it true that the person is under the duty to give notice to the company of such matters relating to himself as regulations require? (true or false)
      `the person makes default in complying with subsection (5)` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it true that the person makes default in complying with subsection (5)? (true or false)
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 412, do I commit an offence by making default in giving the notice` IS
    `s 412(6) the person commits an offence` (JUST `the person is under the duty to give notice to the company of such matters relating to himself as regulations require`) `the person makes default in complying with subsection (5)`

@export Under section 412, what is the penalty for the offence of failing to give the company notice?
GIVEN `how I would be convicted` IS A STRING @desc How would the person be convicted? One of: "on indictment", "summary conviction", "summary conviction in England and Wales", "summary conviction in Scotland", "summary conviction in Northern Ireland".
GIVETH A MAYBE STRING
DECIDE `Under section 412, what is the penalty for the offence of failing to give the company notice` IS
    `s 387(3) the penalty in words` (`s 412(6) the penalty on conviction` (`s 387(3) the mode of conviction named` `how I would be convicted`))

@export Under section 413, must the details of advances, credit and guarantees to directors be shown in the notes to the company's individual accounts (a company that does not prepare group accounts)
GIVEN `the company does not prepare group accounts` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it true that the company does not prepare group accounts? (true or false)
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 413, must the details of advances, credit and guarantees be shown in the notes to the individual accounts` IS
    `s 413(1) the details must be shown in the notes to the company's individual accounts` `the company does not prepare group accounts`

@export Under section 413, must the details of advances, credit and guarantees to directors be shown in the notes to the group accounts (a parent company that prepares group accounts)
GIVEN `the company is a parent company` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it true that the company is a parent company? (true or false)
      `the company prepares group accounts` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it true that the company prepares group accounts? (true or false)
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 413, must the details be shown in the notes to the group accounts` IS
    `s 413(2) the details must be shown in the notes to the group accounts` (JUST `the company is a parent company`) `the company prepares group accounts`

@export Under section 413, are the details of the advance or credit given as the section requires (amount, interest rate, main conditions, amounts repaid, written off and waived)
GIVEN `its amount` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it true that its amount? (true or false)
      `an indication of the interest rate` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it true that an indication of the interest rate? (true or false)
      `its main conditions` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it true that its main conditions? (true or false)
      `any amounts repaid` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it true that any amounts repaid? (true or false)
      `any amounts written off` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it true that any amounts written off? (true or false)
      `any amounts waived` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it true that any amounts waived? (true or false)
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 413, are the details of an advance or credit given as the section requires` IS
    `s 413(3) the details of an advance or credit are given as subsection (3) requires` `its amount` `an indication of the interest rate` `its main conditions` `any amounts repaid` `any amounts written off` `any amounts waived`

@export Under section 413, are the details of the guarantee given as the section requires (main terms, maximum liability, amounts paid or liabilities incurred)
GIVEN `its main terms` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it true that its main terms? (true or false)
      `the amount of the maximum liability that may be incurred by the company (or its subsidiary)` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it true that the amount of the maximum liability that may be incurred by the company (or its subsidiary)? (true or false)
      `any amount paid and any liability incurred by the company (or its subsidiary) for the purpose of fulfilling the guarantee (including any loss incurred by reason of enforcement of the guarantee)` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it true that any amount paid and any liability incurred by the company (or its subsidiary) for the purpose of fulfilling the guarantee (including any loss incurred by reason of enforcement of the guarantee)? (true or false)
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 413, are the details of a guarantee given as the section requires` IS
    `s 413(4) the details of a guarantee are given as subsection (4) requires` `its main terms` `the amount of the maximum liability that may be incurred by the company (or its subsidiary)` `any amount paid and any liability incurred by the company (or its subsidiary) for the purpose of fulfilling the guarantee (including any loss incurred by reason of enforcement of the guarantee)`

@export Under section 413, is this person one of the directors for the purposes of the section (a person who was a director at any time in the financial year)
GIVEN `the person was a director at any time in the financial year to which the accounts relate` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it true that the person was a director at any time in the financial year to which the accounts relate? (true or false)
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 413, is this person one of the directors for the purposes of the section` IS
    `s 413(6) the person is one of the directors for the purposes of this section` `the person was a director at any time in the financial year to which the accounts relate`

@export Under section 413, do the requirements of the section apply to this advance, credit or guarantee (it subsists at any time in the financial year)
GIVEN `it subsists at any time in the financial year to which the accounts relate` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it true that it subsists at any time in the financial year to which the accounts relate? (true or false)
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 413, do the requirements of the section apply to this advance, credit or guarantee` IS
    `s 413(7) the requirements of the section apply to the advance, credit or guarantee` `it subsists at any time in the financial year to which the accounts relate`


§§§ `Approval and signing of accounts (s 414)`
-- Have the directors approved and signed the accounts as required?

@export Under section 414, have the annual accounts been approved by the board of directors and signed on its behalf by a director
GIVEN `the accounts are approved by the board of directors` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it true that the accounts are approved by the board of directors? (true or false)
      `they are signed on behalf of the board by a director of the company` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it true that they are signed on behalf of the board by a director of the company? (true or false)
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 414, have the annual accounts been approved and signed as the section requires` IS
    `s 414(1) the annual accounts are approved and signed as subsection (1) requires` `the accounts are approved by the board of directors` `they are signed on behalf of the board by a director of the company`

@export Under section 414, is the signature on the company's balance sheet
GIVEN `the signature is on the company's balance sheet` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it true that the signature is on the company's balance sheet? (true or false)
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 414, is the signature on the balance sheet` IS
    `s 414(2) the signature is placed as subsection (2) requires` `the signature is on the company's balance sheet`

@export Under section 414, does the balance sheet contain the required statement in a prominent position above the signature
GIVEN `the balance sheet contains the statement the subsection requires` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it true that the balance sheet contains the statement the subsection requires? (true or false)
      `it is in a prominent position above the signature` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it true that it is in a prominent position above the signature? (true or false)
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 414, does the balance sheet contain the required statement in a prominent position above the signature` IS
    `s 414(3) the balance sheet contains the statement as subsection (3) requires` `the balance sheet contains the statement the subsection requires` `it is in a prominent position above the signature`

@export Under section 414, does this director commit an offence by approving accounts that do not comply with this Act
GIVEN `annual accounts are approved` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it true that annual accounts are approved? (true or false)
      `they do not comply with the requirements of this Act` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it true that they do not comply with the requirements of this Act? (true or false)
      `the director knew that they did not comply, or was reckless as to whether they complied` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it true that the director knew that they did not comply, or was reckless as to whether they complied? (true or false)
      `the director failed to take reasonable steps to secure compliance with those requirements or, as the case may be, to prevent the accounts from being approved` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it true that the director failed to take reasonable steps to secure compliance with those requirements or, as the case may be, to prevent the accounts from being approved? (true or false)
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 414, does this director commit an offence by approving accounts that do not comply with this Act` IS
    `s 414(4) the director commits an offence` `annual accounts are approved` (JUST `they do not comply with the requirements of this Act`) `the director knew that they did not comply, or was reckless as to whether they complied` `the director failed to take reasonable steps to secure compliance with those requirements or, as the case may be, to prevent the accounts from being approved`

@export Under section 414, what is the penalty for approving accounts that do not comply?
GIVEN `how I would be convicted` IS A STRING @desc How would the person be convicted? One of: "on indictment", "summary conviction", "summary conviction in England and Wales", "summary conviction in Scotland", "summary conviction in Northern Ireland".
GIVETH A MAYBE STRING
DECIDE `Under section 414, what is the penalty for approving accounts that do not comply` IS
    `s 387(3) the penalty in words` (`s 414(5) the penalty on conviction` (`s 387(3) the mode of conviction named` `how I would be convicted`))


§§ `Chapter 4A: Strategic report (ss 414A to 414B)`
-- Must the directors prepare a strategic report, and is the company entitled to the small companies exemption from it?

@export Under section 414A, are the directors required to prepare a strategic report for the financial year
GIVEN `the company is entitled to the small companies exemption in relation to the strategic report` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it true that the company is entitled to the small companies exemption in relation to the strategic report? (true or false)
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 414A, are the directors required to prepare a strategic report for the financial year` IS
    `s 414A(1) the directors are required to prepare a strategic report for the financial year` (JUST `the company is entitled to the small companies exemption in relation to the strategic report`)

@export Under section 414A, must the strategic report be a group strategic report relating to the undertakings included in the consolidation
GIVEN `in the financial year the company is a parent company` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it true that in the financial year the company is a parent company? (true or false)
      `the directors of the company prepare group accounts` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it true that the directors of the company prepare group accounts? (true or false)
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 414A, must the strategic report be a group strategic report` IS
    `s 414A(3) the strategic report must be a group strategic report relating to the undertakings included in the consolidation` (JUST `in the financial year the company is a parent company`) `the directors of the company prepare group accounts`

@export Under section 414A, may the group strategic report give greater emphasis to the matters that are significant to the undertakings included in the consolidation taken as a whole
GIVEN `it is a group strategic report` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it true that it is a group strategic report? (true or false)
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 414A, may the group strategic report give greater emphasis to the matters significant to the group as a whole` IS
    `s 414A(4) the group strategic report may, where appropriate, give greater emphasis to the matters that are significant to the undertakings included in the consolidation taken as a whole` `it is a group strategic report`

@export Under section 414A, does this person commit an offence by failing to secure that a strategic report is prepared
GIVEN `there is a failure to comply with the requirement to prepare a strategic report` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it true that there is a failure to comply with the requirement to prepare a strategic report? (true or false)
      `the person was a director of the company immediately before the end of the period for filing accounts and reports for the financial year in question` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it true that the person was a director of the company immediately before the end of the period for filing accounts and reports for the financial year in question? (true or false)
      `the person failed to take all reasonable steps for securing compliance with that requirement` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it true that the person failed to take all reasonable steps for securing compliance with that requirement? (true or false)
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 414A, does this director commit an offence by failing to prepare a strategic report` IS
    `s 414A(5) the person commits an offence` `there is a failure to comply with the requirement to prepare a strategic report` `the person was a director of the company immediately before the end of the period for filing accounts and reports for the financial year in question` `the person failed to take all reasonable steps for securing compliance with that requirement`

@export Under section 414A, what is the penalty for failing to prepare a strategic report?
GIVEN `how I would be convicted` IS A STRING @desc How would the person be convicted? One of: "on indictment", "summary conviction", "summary conviction in England and Wales", "summary conviction in Scotland", "summary conviction in Northern Ireland".
GIVETH A MAYBE STRING
DECIDE `Under section 414A, what is the penalty for failing to prepare a strategic report` IS
    `s 387(3) the penalty in words` (`s 414A(6) the penalty on conviction` (`s 387(3) the mode of conviction named` `how I would be convicted`))

@export Under section 414B, is this company entitled to the small companies exemption in relation to the strategic report
GIVEN `the company is entitled to prepare accounts for the year in accordance with the small companies regime` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it true that the company is entitled to prepare accounts for the year in accordance with the small companies regime? (true or false)
      `the company would be so entitled but for being or having been a member of an ineligible group` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it true that the company would be so entitled but for being or having been a member of an ineligible group? (true or false)
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 414B, is this company entitled to the small companies exemption in relation to the strategic report` IS
    `s 414B the company is entitled to the small companies exemption in relation to the strategic report` (JUST `the company is entitled to prepare accounts for the year in accordance with the small companies regime`) (JUST `the company would be so entitled but for being or having been a member of an ineligible group`)

-- ====================================================================================================
-- seat questions from part coa9 (merged by the lead on 2026-11-12; unchanged text follows)
-- ====================================================================================================
-- coa9-seat.l4: THE SEAT LAYER over coa9-penalties, coa9-strategic, coa9-directors-report, coa9-remuneration, coa9-circulation,
-- coa9-publication, coa9-laying and coa9-approval: Companies Act 2006 (UK), Part 15 from section 414C to section 440
-- (lines 5418-5894 of ukpga-2006-46.txt: the strategic report from 414C, the directors' report, the directors' remuneration report,
-- publication of accounts and reports, the laying of accounts before a public company's general meeting, and quoted companies' approval
-- of the remuneration report and policy).
--
-- SEAT: an individual who is, or is about to become, a director, a company secretary or a member (shareholder) of a company
-- registered under the Act, or who deals with one, asking on facts they can state what the Act requires or lets them do,
-- what rights they have against the company or its directors, what they must disclose, file, approve or vote on and by when,
-- and what follows (liability, offences, penalties) if it is not done.
-- (Assumed, not ruled: the Act is addressed to companies, so the individual is whoever stands in a company's management or ownership.)
-- Each question below says whose question it is: a director's, a company secretary's, a member's (or debenture holder's), or that of someone who deals with the company.
--
-- Nothing here is new law. Each question takes plain inputs, one for each fact the person can state (yes or no, a number, a date, or a choice
-- from a short list written out in the input's description), builds the answer by calling the layer-1 rule of the section named in the
-- question, and restates no rule. Where a layer-1 rule takes an answer that another part of the Act decides (is the company a quoted company? is
-- it medium-sized? is this officer in default?) the person states it as a plain yes or no and this layer passes it on as a stated answer.
--
-- HOW TO READ AN ANSWER: every question answers JUST TRUE (the section says yes), JUST FALSE (the section says no in its own words, or a
-- choice recorded in NOTES.md) or NOTHING (the section does not decide: "not covered"). NOTHING is never FALSE. Questions that ask for an amount
-- or a date answer NOTHING where the section states none. Section 1121 (who is an officer in default), the amounts that "the statutory maximum"
-- and the levels of the standard scale stand for, and the end of the period for filing (section 442) are not in this part's text: they are inputs.
--
-- DIRECTION. A question is titled in the direction its answer runs: "is the company barred ..." where the rule is a bar; "does the section excuse ..."
-- where it is an exemption; "am I entitled ..." where it is an entitlement; "do I commit an offence ..." where it defines an offence.


§ `Strategic report (sections 414C to 414D)`
-- Whose questions: a director's (the directors prepare, approve and sign the strategic report) and a company secretary's (who may sign it).
-- These questions arise only in a financial year for which the company prepares a strategic report; a form may first ask "Is your company preparing a strategic report for a financial year?"
-- The questions about quoted companies, about the non-financial and sustainability information statement and about the climate-related disclosures apply only to companies of those kinds.

-- Whose question: a director's.
@export Does the strategic report contain the fair review and the description of principal risks and uncertainties that section 414C(2) requires?
GIVEN `my strategic report contains a fair review of the company's business` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does your strategic report contain a fair review of the company's business?
      `my strategic report contains a description of the principal risks and uncertainties facing the company` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does your strategic report contain a description of the principal risks and uncertainties facing the company?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 414C(2), does my strategic report contain a fair review of the company's business and a description of the principal risks and uncertainties?` IS
    `s 414C(2) the strategic report contains the required items` `my strategic report contains a fair review of the company's business` `my strategic report contains a description of the principal risks and uncertainties facing the company`

-- Whose question: a director's.
@export Is the review in the strategic report the balanced and comprehensive analysis of the company's business that section 414C(3) requires?
GIVEN `my review analyses the development and performance of the company's business during the financial year` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does your review analyse the development and performance of the company's business during the financial year?
      `my review analyses the position of the company's business at the end of that year` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does your review analyse the position of the company's business at the end of that year?
      `my analysis is balanced and comprehensive` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is your analysis balanced and comprehensive? (This is your judgment.)
      `my analysis is consistent with the size and complexity of the business` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is your analysis consistent with the size and complexity of the business? (This is your judgment.)
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 414C(3), is the review in my strategic report the balanced and comprehensive analysis that the section requires?` IS
    `s 414C(3) the review is the required balanced and comprehensive analysis` `my review analyses the development and performance of the company's business during the financial year` `my review analyses the position of the company's business at the end of that year` `my analysis is balanced and comprehensive` `my analysis is consistent with the size and complexity of the business`

-- Whose question: a director's.
@export Must the review include analysis using financial key performance indicators, to the extent necessary for an understanding of the business (section 414C(4)(a))?
GIVEN `analysis using financial key performance indicators is necessary for an understanding of the company's business` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is analysis using financial key performance indicators necessary for an understanding of the development, performance or position of the company's business? (This is your judgment.)
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 414C(4)(a), must the review in my strategic report include analysis using financial key performance indicators?` IS
    `s 414C(4)(a) the review must include analysis using financial key performance indicators` `analysis using financial key performance indicators is necessary for an understanding of the company's business`

-- Whose question: a director's.
@export Must the review include analysis using other key performance indicators, including environmental and employee matters, where appropriate (section 414C(4)(b))?
GIVEN `analysis using other key performance indicators is necessary for an understanding of the company's business` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is analysis using other key performance indicators necessary for an understanding of the development, performance or position of the company's business? (This is your judgment.)
      `it is appropriate to analyse using other key performance indicators` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it appropriate to analyse using other key performance indicators? (This is your judgment.)
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 414C(4)(b), must the review in my strategic report include analysis using other key performance indicators?` IS
    `s 414C(4)(b) the review must include analysis using other key performance indicators` `analysis using other key performance indicators is necessary for an understanding of the company's business` `it is appropriate to analyse using other key performance indicators`

-- Whose question: a director's.
@export Is the review excused from the requirements of section 414C(4) so far as they relate to non-financial information because the company qualifies as medium-sized (section 414C(6))?
GIVEN `my company qualifies as medium-sized for the financial year` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does your company qualify as medium-sized in relation to the financial year (sections 465 to 467)?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 414C(6), is the review in my company's strategic report excused from the non-financial part of subsection (4) because my company qualifies as medium-sized?` IS
    `s 414C(6) the review need not comply with subsection (4) so far as it relates to non-financial information` (JUST `my company qualifies as medium-sized for the financial year`)

-- Whose question: a director's of a quoted company.
@export Must the strategic report of a quoted company include this kind of information (section 414C(7))?
GIVEN `my company is a quoted company` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is your company a quoted company for the financial year?
      `the information is necessary for an understanding of the company's business` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the information necessary for an understanding of the development, performance or position of the company's business? (This is your judgment.)
      `which kind of information` IS A STRING @desc Which kind of information? One of: trends (the main trends and factors likely to affect future development), environmental, employees, social (social, community and human rights issues).
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 414C(7), must the strategic report of my quoted company include this kind of information?` IS
    CONSIDER `which kind of information`
    WHEN "trends" THEN `s 414C(7) the strategic report of a quoted company must include the information` (JUST `my company is a quoted company`) `the information is necessary for an understanding of the company's business` `s 414C(7)(a) the main trends and factors likely to affect the future development, performance and position of the company's business`
    WHEN "environmental" THEN `s 414C(7) the strategic report of a quoted company must include the information` (JUST `my company is a quoted company`) `the information is necessary for an understanding of the company's business` `s 414C(7)(b)(i) environmental matters (including the impact of the company's business on the environment)`
    WHEN "employees" THEN `s 414C(7) the strategic report of a quoted company must include the information` (JUST `my company is a quoted company`) `the information is necessary for an understanding of the company's business` `s 414C(7)(b)(ii) the company's employees`
    WHEN "social" THEN `s 414C(7) the strategic report of a quoted company must include the information` (JUST `my company is a quoted company`) `the information is necessary for an understanding of the company's business` `s 414C(7)(b)(iii) social, community and human rights issues`
    OTHERWISE NOTHING

-- Whose question: a director's of a quoted company.
@export Which of the environmental, employee and social kinds of information must the strategic report of a quoted company state it does not contain (section 414C(7))?
GIVEN `my company is a quoted company` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is your company a quoted company for the financial year?
      `my report contains information about environmental matters` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does your strategic report contain information about environmental matters?
      `my report contains information about the company's employees` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does your strategic report contain information about the company's employees?
      `my report contains information about social, community and human rights issues` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does your strategic report contain information about social, community and human rights issues?
GIVETH A MAYBE (LIST OF `s 414C(7) kind of information`)
DECIDE `Under section 414C(7), which kinds of information must the strategic report of my quoted company say that it does not contain?` IS
    `s 414C(7) the kinds of information the report must state it does not contain` (JUST `my company is a quoted company`) `my report contains information about environmental matters` `my report contains information about the company's employees` `my report contains information about social, community and human rights issues`

-- Whose question: a director's of a quoted company.
@export Must the strategic report of a quoted company include this item: strategy, business model, or a breakdown by sex (section 414C(8))?
GIVEN `my company is a quoted company` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is your company a quoted company for the financial year?
      `which item` IS A STRING @desc Which item? One of: strategy, business model, directors by sex, senior managers by sex, employees by sex.
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 414C(8), must the strategic report of my quoted company include this item?` IS
    CONSIDER `which item`
    WHEN "strategy" THEN `s 414C(8) the strategic report of a quoted company must include the item` (JUST `my company is a quoted company`) `s 414C(8)(a) a description of the company's strategy`
    WHEN "business model" THEN `s 414C(8) the strategic report of a quoted company must include the item` (JUST `my company is a quoted company`) `s 414C(8)(b) a description of the company's business model`
    WHEN "directors by sex" THEN `s 414C(8) the strategic report of a quoted company must include the item` (JUST `my company is a quoted company`) `s 414C(8)(c)(i) the number of persons of each sex who were directors of the company`
    WHEN "senior managers by sex" THEN `s 414C(8) the strategic report of a quoted company must include the item` (JUST `my company is a quoted company`) `s 414C(8)(c)(ii) the number of persons of each sex who were senior managers of the company`
    WHEN "employees by sex" THEN `s 414C(8) the strategic report of a quoted company must include the item` (JUST `my company is a quoted company`) `s 414C(8)(c)(iii) the number of persons of each sex who were employees of the company`
    OTHERWISE NOTHING

-- Whose question: a director's of a quoted company.
@export Is this person counted among the senior managers in the breakdown by sex (section 414C(8)(c)(ii))?
GIVEN `the person is a senior manager of the company` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the person a senior manager of the company (section 414C(9))?
      `the person is a director of the company` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the person a director of the company (a director is counted under sub-paragraph (i) instead)?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 414C(8)(c)(ii), is this person counted among my company's senior managers in the breakdown by sex?` IS
    `s 414C(8)(c)(ii) the person is counted among the senior managers` `the person is a senior manager of the company` `the person is a director of the company`

-- Whose question: a director's of a quoted company.
@export Is this person a senior manager of the company, for the breakdown by sex (section 414C(9))?
GIVEN `the person has responsibility for planning, directing or controlling the activities of the company, or a strategically significant part of it` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does the person have responsibility for planning, directing or controlling the activities of the company, or a strategically significant part of the company?
      `the person is an employee of the company` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the person an employee of the company?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 414C(9), is this person a senior manager of my company?` IS
    `s 414C(9) the person is a senior manager` `the person has responsibility for planning, directing or controlling the activities of the company, or a strategically significant part of it` `the person is an employee of the company`

-- Whose question: a director's.
@export Does section 414C require disclosure of information about impending developments or matters in the course of negotiation that the directors think would be seriously prejudicial (section 414C(14))?
GIVEN `the information is about impending developments or matters in the course of negotiation` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the information about impending developments or matters in the course of negotiation?
      `in the directors' opinion the disclosure would be seriously prejudicial to the interests of the company` IS A BOOLEAN @desc In the directors' opinion, would the disclosure be seriously prejudicial to the interests of the company?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 414C(14), does section 414C require my company to disclose information about impending developments or matters in the course of negotiation that the directors think would be seriously prejudicial to the company's interests?` IS
    `s 414C(14) this section requires the disclosure of the information` `the information is about impending developments or matters in the course of negotiation` `in the directors' opinion the disclosure would be seriously prejudicial to the interests of the company`

-- Whose question: a director's.
@export Does the strategic report include the statement of how the directors have had regard to the section 172(1) matters (section 414CZA(1))?
GIVEN `my strategic report includes a statement` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does your strategic report include a statement about how the directors have had regard to the matters in section 172(1)(a) to (f)?
      `the statement describes how the directors have had regard to the matters set out in section 172(1)(a) to (f) when performing their duty under section 172` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does the statement describe how the directors have had regard to the matters set out in section 172(1)(a) to (f) when performing their duty under section 172?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 414CZA(1), does my strategic report include the section 172(1) statement that the section requires?` IS
    `s 414CZA(1) the strategic report includes the required section 172(1) statement` `my strategic report includes a statement` (`s 414CZA(1) the statement is a section 172(1) statement` `the statement describes how the directors have had regard to the matters set out in section 172(1)(a) to (f) when performing their duty under section 172`)

-- Whose question: a director's.
@export Does section 414CZA(2) excuse the company from including a section 172(1) statement because it qualifies as medium-sized?
GIVEN `my company qualifies as medium-sized for the financial year` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does your company qualify as medium-sized in relation to the financial year (sections 465 to 467)?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 414CZA(2), is my company excused from including a section 172(1) statement in its strategic report because it qualifies as medium-sized?` IS
    `s 414CZA(2) subsection (1) does not apply to the company` (JUST `my company qualifies as medium-sized for the financial year`)

-- Whose question: a director's.
@export Does subsection (A1) of section 414CA, the requirement to include a non-financial and sustainability information statement in the strategic report, apply to the company, subject to the exclusions in subsections (3) to (7)?
GIVEN `my company was a traded company at any time within the financial year` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Was your company a traded company at any time within the financial year to which the report relates?
      `my company was a banking company at any time within the financial year` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Was your company a banking company at any time within the financial year?
      `my company was an authorised insurance company at any time within the financial year` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Was your company an authorised insurance company at any time within the financial year?
      `my company carried on insurance market activity at any time within the financial year` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did your company carry on insurance market activity at any time within the financial year?
      `securities of my company were admitted to trading on the Alternative Investment Market at any time within the financial year` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Were any securities of your company admitted to trading on the Alternative Investment Market at any time within the financial year?
      `my company was a parent company at any time within the financial year` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Was your company a parent company at any time within the financial year?
      `my company's own turnover in the year, in pounds` IS A NUMBER @desc What was your company's own turnover in the financial year, in pounds?
      `the aggregate turnover of the group headed by my company, net, in pounds` IS A NUMBER @desc If your company was a parent company, what was the aggregate turnover of the group it headed in the financial year, net, in pounds? (Enter 0 if it was not a parent company.)
      `the length of my company's financial year as a proportion of a year` IS A NUMBER @desc How long was the financial year as a proportion of a year? (1 for a full year, 0.5 for six months.)
      `my company is subject to the small companies regime for the financial year` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is your company subject to the small companies regime in relation to the financial year (sections 382 to 384)?
      `my company qualifies as medium-sized for the financial year` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does your company qualify as medium-sized in relation to the financial year (sections 465 to 467)?
      `the number of persons my company employed under contracts of service in each month of the financial year` IS A LIST OF NUMBER @desc How many persons did your company employ under contracts of service in each month of the financial year (whether throughout the month or not)? Give one number for each month, as a list.
      `the aggregate number of employees for the group headed by my company in the financial year` IS A NUMBER @desc If your company was a parent company, what was the aggregate number of employees for the group it headed in the financial year? (Enter 0 if it was not a parent company.)
      `my company is a subsidiary undertaking at the end of the financial year` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is your company a subsidiary undertaking at the end of the financial year?
      `my company is included in a group strategic report of a parent undertaking of the company` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is your company included in a group strategic report of a parent undertaking of the company?
      `that group strategic report relates to undertakings that include my company and its subsidiary undertakings` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does that group strategic report relate to undertakings that include your company and its subsidiary undertakings (if any)?
      `that report is prepared for a financial year of the parent undertaking that ends at the same time as, or before the end of, my company's financial year` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is that report prepared for a financial year of the parent undertaking that ends at the same time as, or before the end of, your company's financial year?
      `that report includes a group non-financial and sustainability information statement in respect of all the undertakings included in the consolidation` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does that report include a group non-financial and sustainability information statement in respect of all the undertakings included in the consolidation?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 414CA(1B), does the requirement to include a non-financial and sustainability information statement apply to my company?` IS
    CONSIDER `s 414CA(5) the number of employees` `the number of persons my company employed under contracts of service in each month of the financial year`
    WHEN NOTHING THEN NOTHING
    WHEN JUST employees THEN
        `s 414CA(1B) subsection (A1) applies to the company`
            (`s 414CA(1) subsection (A1) applies to the company because of its kind` (`s 414CA(1)(a) to (d) the company is of a kind described` (JUST `my company was a traded company at any time within the financial year`) `my company was a banking company at any time within the financial year` `my company was an authorised insurance company at any time within the financial year` `my company carried on insurance market activity at any time within the financial year`) `securities of my company were admitted to trading on the Alternative Investment Market at any time within the financial year`)
            (`s 414CA(1A) subsection (A1) also applies to the company because it was a high turnover company` (`s 414CA(2A) the company is a high turnover company in relation to the financial year` (JUST `my company was a parent company at any time within the financial year`) `my company's own turnover in the year, in pounds` `the aggregate turnover of the group headed by my company, net, in pounds` `the length of my company's financial year as a proportion of a year`))
            (`s 414CA(3) subsection (A1) does not apply because of the company's size` (JUST `my company is subject to the small companies regime for the financial year`) (JUST `my company qualifies as medium-sized for the financial year`))
            (`s 414CA(4) subsection (A1) does not apply because of the number of employees` (JUST `my company was a parent company at any time within the financial year`) employees `the aggregate number of employees for the group headed by my company in the financial year`)
            (`s 414CA(7) subsection (A1) does not apply because the company is included in a group strategic report` `my company is a subsidiary undertaking at the end of the financial year` `my company is included in a group strategic report of a parent undertaking of the company` (`s 414CA(8) the requirements in this subsection are satisfied` `that group strategic report relates to undertakings that include my company and its subsidiary undertakings` `that report is prepared for a financial year of the parent undertaking that ends at the same time as, or before the end of, my company's financial year` `that report includes a group non-financial and sustainability information statement in respect of all the undertakings included in the consolidation`))

-- Whose question: a director's.
@export Is the company a high turnover company in relation to the financial year (section 414CA(2A))?
GIVEN `my company was a parent company at any time within the financial year` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Was your company a parent company at any time within the financial year?
      `my company's own turnover in the year, in pounds` IS A NUMBER @desc What was your company's own turnover in the financial year, in pounds?
      `the aggregate turnover of the group headed by my company, net, in pounds` IS A NUMBER @desc If your company was a parent company, what was the aggregate turnover of the group it headed in the financial year, net, in pounds? (Enter 0 if it was not a parent company.)
      `the length of my company's financial year as a proportion of a year` IS A NUMBER @desc How long was the financial year as a proportion of a year? (1 for a full year, 0.5 for six months.)
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 414CA(2A), is my company a high turnover company for the financial year?` IS
    `s 414CA(2A) the company is a high turnover company in relation to the financial year` (JUST `my company was a parent company at any time within the financial year`) `my company's own turnover in the year, in pounds` `the aggregate turnover of the group headed by my company, net, in pounds` `the length of my company's financial year as a proportion of a year`

-- Whose question: a director's.
@export What is the company's number of employees, the average of the monthly numbers of persons employed under contracts of service (section 414CA(5))?
GIVEN `the number of persons my company employed under contracts of service in each month of the financial year` IS A LIST OF NUMBER @desc How many persons did your company employ under contracts of service in each month of the financial year (whether throughout the month or not)? Give one number for each month, as a list.
GIVETH A MAYBE NUMBER
DECIDE `Under section 414CA(5), what is my company's number of employees for the financial year?` IS
    `s 414CA(5) the number of employees` `the number of persons my company employed under contracts of service in each month of the financial year`

-- Whose question: a director's.
@export Does the non-financial and sustainability information statement contain all eight climate-related financial disclosures of section 414CB(2A) (section 414CB(A1))?
GIVEN `my statement contains a description of the company's governance arrangements in relation to assessing and managing climate-related risks and opportunities` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does your statement contain a description of the company's governance arrangements in relation to assessing and managing climate-related risks and opportunities?
      `my statement contains a description of how the company identifies, assesses and manages climate-related risks and opportunities` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does your statement contain a description of how the company identifies, assesses and manages climate-related risks and opportunities?
      `my statement contains a description of how the processes for identifying, assessing and managing climate-related risks are integrated into the company's overall risk management process` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does your statement contain a description of how the processes for identifying, assessing and managing climate-related risks are integrated into the company's overall risk management process?
      `my statement contains a description of the principal climate-related risks and opportunities and the time periods by reference to which they are assessed` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does your statement contain a description of the principal climate-related risks and opportunities and the time periods by reference to which they are assessed?
      `my statement contains a description of the actual and potential impacts of the principal climate-related risks and opportunities on the business model and strategy` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does your statement contain a description of the actual and potential impacts of the principal climate-related risks and opportunities on the business model and strategy?
      `my statement contains an analysis of the resilience of the business model and strategy, taking into consideration different climate-related scenarios` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does your statement contain an analysis of the resilience of the business model and strategy, taking into consideration different climate-related scenarios?
      `my statement contains a description of the targets used to manage climate-related risks and to realise climate-related opportunities, and of performance against those targets` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does your statement contain a description of the targets used to manage climate-related risks and to realise climate-related opportunities, and of performance against those targets?
      `my statement contains a description of the key performance indicators used to assess progress against those targets and of the calculations on which they are based` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does your statement contain a description of the key performance indicators used to assess progress against those targets and of the calculations on which they are based?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 414CB(A1), does my statement contain all eight of the climate-related financial disclosures listed in section 414CB(2A)?` IS
    `s 414CB(A1) the statement contains the climate-related financial disclosures` (filter (GIVEN k YIELD `the statement contains` k) (LIST `s 414CB(2A)(a) governance arrangements in relation to assessing and managing climate-related risks and opportunities`, `s 414CB(2A)(b) how the company identifies, assesses and manages climate-related risks and opportunities`, `s 414CB(2A)(c) how those processes are integrated into the company's overall risk management process`, `s 414CB(2A)(d) the principal climate-related risks and opportunities and the time periods by reference to which they are assessed`, `s 414CB(2A)(e) the actual and potential impacts of the principal climate-related risks and opportunities on the business model and strategy`, `s 414CB(2A)(f) the resilience of the business model and strategy in different climate-related scenarios`, `s 414CB(2A)(g) the targets used to manage climate-related risks and to realise opportunities, and performance against them`, `s 414CB(2A)(h) the key performance indicators used to assess progress against those targets, and the calculations behind them`))
    WHERE
        `the statement contains` k MEANS
            CONSIDER k
            WHEN `s 414CB(2A)(a) governance arrangements in relation to assessing and managing climate-related risks and opportunities` THEN `my statement contains a description of the company's governance arrangements in relation to assessing and managing climate-related risks and opportunities`
            WHEN `s 414CB(2A)(b) how the company identifies, assesses and manages climate-related risks and opportunities` THEN `my statement contains a description of how the company identifies, assesses and manages climate-related risks and opportunities`
            WHEN `s 414CB(2A)(c) how those processes are integrated into the company's overall risk management process` THEN `my statement contains a description of how the processes for identifying, assessing and managing climate-related risks are integrated into the company's overall risk management process`
            WHEN `s 414CB(2A)(d) the principal climate-related risks and opportunities and the time periods by reference to which they are assessed` THEN `my statement contains a description of the principal climate-related risks and opportunities and the time periods by reference to which they are assessed`
            WHEN `s 414CB(2A)(e) the actual and potential impacts of the principal climate-related risks and opportunities on the business model and strategy` THEN `my statement contains a description of the actual and potential impacts of the principal climate-related risks and opportunities on the business model and strategy`
            WHEN `s 414CB(2A)(f) the resilience of the business model and strategy in different climate-related scenarios` THEN `my statement contains an analysis of the resilience of the business model and strategy, taking into consideration different climate-related scenarios`
            WHEN `s 414CB(2A)(g) the targets used to manage climate-related risks and to realise opportunities, and performance against them` THEN `my statement contains a description of the targets used to manage climate-related risks and to realise climate-related opportunities, and of performance against those targets`
            WHEN `s 414CB(2A)(h) the key performance indicators used to assess progress against those targets, and the calculations behind them` THEN `my statement contains a description of the key performance indicators used to assess progress against those targets and of the calculations on which they are based`
            OTHERWISE FALSE

-- Whose question: a director's.
@export Must the non-financial and sustainability information statement contain information on this matter, one of environmental matters, employees, social matters, human rights, or anti-corruption and anti-bribery matters, to the extent necessary for an understanding of the company's development, performance and position and the impact of its activity (section 414CB(1))?
GIVEN `my company was a traded company at any time within the financial year` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Was your company a traded company at any time within the financial year to which the report relates?
      `my company was a banking company at any time within the financial year` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Was your company a banking company at any time within the financial year?
      `my company was an authorised insurance company at any time within the financial year` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Was your company an authorised insurance company at any time within the financial year?
      `my company carried on insurance market activity at any time within the financial year` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did your company carry on insurance market activity at any time within the financial year?
      `the information is necessary for an understanding of the company's development, performance and position and the impact of its activity` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the information on that matter necessary for an understanding of the company's development, performance and position and the impact of its activity? (This is your judgment.)
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 414CB(1), must the statement of my company contain information on this matter (one of environmental matters, the company's employees, social matters, respect for human rights, or anti-corruption and anti-bribery matters)?` IS
    `s 414CB(1) the statement must contain information on the matter` (`s 414CA(1)(a) to (d) the company is of a kind described` (JUST `my company was a traded company at any time within the financial year`) `my company was a banking company at any time within the financial year` `my company was an authorised insurance company at any time within the financial year` `my company carried on insurance market activity at any time within the financial year`) `the information is necessary for an understanding of the company's development, performance and position and the impact of its activity`

-- Whose question: a director's.
@export May the directors omit the whole or part of a climate-related financial disclosure under (2A)(e), (f), (g) or (h) because they reasonably believe it is not necessary for an understanding of the company's business (section 414CB(4A))?
GIVEN `which disclosure` IS A STRING @desc Which disclosure of section 414CB(2A)? One of the letters a to h (a governance, b identifying and managing, c integration, d principal risks and time periods, e impacts, f resilience, g targets, h key performance indicators).
      `the directors reasonably believe that the disclosure is not necessary for an understanding of the company's business` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Do the directors reasonably believe that, having regard to the nature of the company's business and the manner in which it is carried on, the whole or a part of the disclosure is not necessary for an understanding of the company's business?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 414CB(4A), may the directors omit this climate-related financial disclosure or part of it?` IS
    CONSIDER `which disclosure`
    WHEN "a" THEN `s 414CB(4A) the directors may omit the disclosure or the relevant part of it` `s 414CB(2A)(a) governance arrangements in relation to assessing and managing climate-related risks and opportunities` `the directors reasonably believe that the disclosure is not necessary for an understanding of the company's business`
    WHEN "b" THEN `s 414CB(4A) the directors may omit the disclosure or the relevant part of it` `s 414CB(2A)(b) how the company identifies, assesses and manages climate-related risks and opportunities` `the directors reasonably believe that the disclosure is not necessary for an understanding of the company's business`
    WHEN "c" THEN `s 414CB(4A) the directors may omit the disclosure or the relevant part of it` `s 414CB(2A)(c) how those processes are integrated into the company's overall risk management process` `the directors reasonably believe that the disclosure is not necessary for an understanding of the company's business`
    WHEN "d" THEN `s 414CB(4A) the directors may omit the disclosure or the relevant part of it` `s 414CB(2A)(d) the principal climate-related risks and opportunities and the time periods by reference to which they are assessed` `the directors reasonably believe that the disclosure is not necessary for an understanding of the company's business`
    WHEN "e" THEN `s 414CB(4A) the directors may omit the disclosure or the relevant part of it` `s 414CB(2A)(e) the actual and potential impacts of the principal climate-related risks and opportunities on the business model and strategy` `the directors reasonably believe that the disclosure is not necessary for an understanding of the company's business`
    WHEN "f" THEN `s 414CB(4A) the directors may omit the disclosure or the relevant part of it` `s 414CB(2A)(f) the resilience of the business model and strategy in different climate-related scenarios` `the directors reasonably believe that the disclosure is not necessary for an understanding of the company's business`
    WHEN "g" THEN `s 414CB(4A) the directors may omit the disclosure or the relevant part of it` `s 414CB(2A)(g) the targets used to manage climate-related risks and to realise opportunities, and performance against them` `the directors reasonably believe that the disclosure is not necessary for an understanding of the company's business`
    WHEN "h" THEN `s 414CB(4A) the directors may omit the disclosure or the relevant part of it` `s 414CB(2A)(h) the key performance indicators used to assess progress against those targets, and the calculations behind them` `the directors reasonably believe that the disclosure is not necessary for an understanding of the company's business`
    OTHERWISE NOTHING

-- Whose question: a director's or the company secretary's.
@export Has the strategic report been approved by the board and signed on its behalf by a director or the secretary (section 414D(1))?
GIVEN `the strategic report has been approved by the board of directors` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has the strategic report been approved by the board of directors?
      `the strategic report has been signed on behalf of the board by a director` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has the strategic report been signed on behalf of the board by a director?
      `the strategic report has been signed on behalf of the board by the secretary of the company` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has the strategic report been signed on behalf of the board by the secretary of the company?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 414D(1), has my strategic report been approved and signed as the section requires?` IS
    `s 414D(1) the strategic report has been approved and signed as required` `the strategic report has been approved by the board of directors` `the strategic report has been signed on behalf of the board by a director` `the strategic report has been signed on behalf of the board by the secretary of the company`

-- Whose question: a director's.
@export Does a director commit an offence under section 414D(2) because a strategic report that does not comply with the requirements of the Act was approved?
GIVEN `a strategic report has been approved` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has a strategic report been approved?
      `the approved report does not comply with the requirements of this Act` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does the approved strategic report fail to comply with the requirements of the Companies Act?
      `I am a director of the company` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are you a director of the company?
      `I knew that it did not comply` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did you know that it did not comply?
      `I was reckless as to whether it complied` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Were you reckless as to whether it complied?
      `I failed to take reasonable steps to secure compliance or to prevent the report from being approved` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did you fail to take reasonable steps to secure compliance with those requirements or to prevent the report from being approved?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 414D(2), do I commit an offence as a director because a strategic report that does not comply was approved?` IS
    `s 414D(2) the director commits an offence` `a strategic report has been approved` `the approved report does not comply with the requirements of this Act` `I am a director of the company` `I knew that it did not comply` `I was reckless as to whether it complied` `I failed to take reasonable steps to secure compliance or to prevent the report from being approved`

-- Whose question: a director's.
@export What is the most the director can be fined on summary conviction of an offence under section 414D, in pounds (section 414D(3))?
GIVEN `the statutory maximum, in pounds` IS A NUMBER @desc What is the amount of the statutory maximum fine, in pounds? (The Act does not state it; it is set outside the Act.)
GIVETH A MAYBE NUMBER
DECIDE `Under section 414D(3), what is the most I can be fined on summary conviction for that offence, in pounds?` IS
    CONSIDER `s 414D(3) the penalty for an offence under section 414D` `on summary conviction`
    WHEN NOTHING THEN NOTHING
    WHEN JUST penalty THEN
        CONSIDER penalty's `fine not exceeding`
        WHEN NOTHING THEN NOTHING
        WHEN JUST limit THEN `s 414D(3) the most a fine limit allows in pounds` limit `the statutory maximum, in pounds` 0 -- placeholder: no level on the standard scale is used by this section, so a fixed 0 is passed

§ `Directors' report (sections 415 to 419A)`
-- Whose questions: a director's, and a company secretary's for signing.
-- The questions about the statement as to disclosure to auditors (section 418) arise only where the company is not exempt from audit.

-- Whose question: a director's.
@export Have the directors prepared a directors' report for the financial year (section 415(1))?
GIVEN `the directors have prepared a directors' report for the financial year` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Have the directors prepared a directors' report for the financial year?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 415(1), have the directors prepared the directors' report for the financial year?` IS
    `s 415(1) the directors have prepared the directors' report for the financial year` `the directors have prepared a directors' report for the financial year`

-- Whose question: a director's.
@export Does section 415(1A) excuse the company from preparing a directors' report because it qualifies as a micro-entity?
GIVEN `my company qualifies as a micro-entity for the financial year` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does your company qualify as a micro-entity in relation to the financial year (sections 384A and 384B)?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 415(1A), is my company excused from preparing a directors' report because it qualifies as a micro-entity?` IS
    `s 415(1A) subsection (1) does not apply to the company` (JUST `my company qualifies as a micro-entity for the financial year`)

-- Whose question: a director's.
@export Must the directors' report be a consolidated report relating to the undertakings included in the consolidation (section 415(2))?
GIVEN `my company was a parent company in the financial year` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Was your company a parent company in the financial year?
      `the directors of my company prepare group accounts for the financial year` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Do the directors of your company prepare group accounts for the financial year?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 415(2), must my company's directors' report be a consolidated report?` IS
    `s 415(2) the directors' report must be a consolidated report` (JUST `my company was a parent company in the financial year`) `the directors of my company prepare group accounts for the financial year`

-- Whose question: a director's.
@export Does a director commit an offence under section 415(4) because the company failed to prepare a directors' report?
GIVEN `the company has failed to comply with the requirement to prepare a directors' report` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did the company fail to prepare a directors' report for the financial year?
      `I was a director of the company immediately before the end of the period for filing accounts and reports` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Were you a director of the company immediately before the end of the period for filing accounts and reports for the financial year?
      `I failed to take all reasonable steps for securing compliance with that requirement` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did you fail to take all reasonable steps for securing that a directors' report was prepared?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 415(4), do I commit an offence as a director because no directors' report was prepared?` IS
    `s 415(4) the person commits an offence` `the company has failed to comply with the requirement to prepare a directors' report` `I was a director of the company immediately before the end of the period for filing accounts and reports` `I failed to take all reasonable steps for securing compliance with that requirement`

-- Whose question: a director's.
@export What is the most a director can be fined on summary conviction of an offence under section 415, in pounds (section 415(5))?
GIVEN `the statutory maximum, in pounds` IS A NUMBER @desc What is the amount of the statutory maximum fine, in pounds? (The Act does not state it; it is set outside the Act.)
GIVETH A MAYBE NUMBER
DECIDE `Under section 415(5), what is the most I can be fined on summary conviction for that offence, in pounds?` IS
    CONSIDER `s 415(5) the penalty for an offence under section 415` `on summary conviction`
    WHEN NOTHING THEN NOTHING
    WHEN JUST penalty THEN
        CONSIDER penalty's `fine not exceeding`
        WHEN NOTHING THEN NOTHING
        WHEN JUST limit THEN `s 414D(3) the most a fine limit allows in pounds` limit `the statutory maximum, in pounds` 0 -- placeholder: no level on the standard scale is used by this section, so a fixed 0 is passed

-- Whose question: a director's.
@export Is the company entitled to small companies exemption in relation to the directors' report (section 415A(1))?
GIVEN `my company is entitled to prepare accounts for the year in accordance with the small companies regime` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is your company entitled to prepare accounts for the year in accordance with the small companies regime (sections 381 to 384)?
      `my company would be so entitled but for being or having been a member of an ineligible group` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Would your company be so entitled but for being or having been a member of an ineligible group?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 415A(1), is my company entitled to small companies exemption in relation to the directors' report?` IS
    `s 415A(1) the company is entitled to small companies exemption in relation to the directors' report` (JUST `my company is entitled to prepare accounts for the year in accordance with the small companies regime`) `my company would be so entitled but for being or having been a member of an ineligible group`

-- Whose question: a director's.
@export Must the directors' report state the amount (if any) that the directors recommend should be paid by way of dividend (section 416(3))?
GIVEN `my company is entitled to the small companies exemption` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is your company entitled to small companies exemption in relation to the directors' report (section 415A)?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 416(3), must the directors' report of my company state the amount recommended by way of dividend?` IS
    `s 416(3) the directors' report must state the amount (if any) that the directors recommend should be paid by way of dividend` (JUST `my company is entitled to the small companies exemption`)

-- Whose question: a director's.
@export Does section 418, the directors' statement as to disclosure to the company's auditor, apply to the company (section 418(1))?
GIVEN `my company is exempt for the financial year from the requirements of Part 16 as to audit of accounts` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is your company exempt for the financial year from the requirements of Part 16 as to audit of accounts?
      `the directors take advantage of that exemption` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Do the directors take advantage of that exemption?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 418(1), does the section on the statement as to disclosure to auditors apply to my company?` IS
    `s 418(1) this section applies to the company` `my company is exempt for the financial year from the requirements of Part 16 as to audit of accounts` `the directors take advantage of that exemption`

-- Whose question: a director's.
@export Does the directors' report contain the statement that, for each director, there is no relevant audit information of which the auditor is unaware and that the director has taken all the steps he ought to have taken (section 418(2))?
GIVEN `the report contains a statement as to each director that, so far as the director is aware, there is no relevant audit information of which the company's auditor is unaware` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does the report contain a statement, for each person who is a director when the report is approved, that so far as the director is aware there is no relevant audit information of which the company's auditor is unaware?
      `the report contains a statement as to each director that he has taken all the steps that he ought to have taken` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does the report contain a statement, for each of those directors, that he has taken all the steps that he ought to have taken as a director to make himself aware of any relevant audit information and to establish that the company's auditor is aware of it?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 418(2), does the directors' report contain the statement as to disclosure to the auditor that the section requires?` IS
    `s 418(2) the directors' report contains the required statement` `the report contains a statement as to each director that, so far as the director is aware, there is no relevant audit information of which the company's auditor is unaware` `the report contains a statement as to each director that he has taken all the steps that he ought to have taken`

-- Whose question: a director's.
@export Is a director regarded as having taken all the steps he ought to have taken, having made the enquiries and taken the steps required by his duty of care (section 418(4))?
GIVEN `I have made such enquiries of my fellow directors and of the company's auditors as are required by my duty as a director` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Have you made such enquiries of your fellow directors and of the company's auditors for that purpose as are required by your duty as a director of the company to exercise reasonable care, skill and diligence?
      `I have taken such other steps for that purpose as are required by that duty` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Have you taken such other steps (if any) for that purpose as are required by that duty?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 418(4), am I regarded as having taken all the steps that I ought to have taken as a director to make myself aware of relevant audit information?` IS
    `s 418(4) the director is regarded as having taken all the steps that he ought to have taken as a director` `I have made such enquiries of my fellow directors and of the company's auditors as are required by my duty as a director` `I have taken such other steps for that purpose as are required by that duty`

-- Whose question: a director's.
@export Does a director commit an offence under section 418(5) because a directors' report containing a false statement as to disclosure to the auditor was approved?
GIVEN `a directors' report containing the statement required by section 418 has been approved` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has a directors' report containing the statement required by section 418 been approved?
      `the statement is false` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the statement false?
      `I am a director of the company` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are you a director of the company?
      `I knew that the statement was false` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did you know that the statement was false?
      `I was reckless as to whether the statement was false` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Were you reckless as to whether the statement was false?
      `I failed to take reasonable steps to prevent the report from being approved` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did you fail to take reasonable steps to prevent the report from being approved?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 418(5), do I commit an offence as a director because the statement as to disclosure to the auditor in the directors' report was false?` IS
    `s 418(5) the director commits an offence` `a directors' report containing the statement required by section 418 has been approved` `the statement is false` `I am a director of the company` `I knew that the statement was false` `I was reckless as to whether the statement was false` `I failed to take reasonable steps to prevent the report from being approved`

-- Whose question: a director's.
@export What is the longest term of imprisonment, in months, for an offence under section 418(5), depending on how and where the person is convicted (section 418(6))?
GIVEN `how I am convicted` IS A STRING @desc How would you be convicted? One of: on indictment, summary conviction in England and Wales, summary conviction in Scotland, summary conviction in Northern Ireland.
GIVETH A MAYBE NUMBER
DECIDE `Under section 418(6), what is the longest term of imprisonment I can be sentenced to for that offence, in months?` IS
    CONSIDER `how I am convicted`
    WHEN "on indictment" THEN `months for` `on conviction on indictment`
    WHEN "summary conviction in England and Wales" THEN `months for` `on summary conviction in England and Wales`
    WHEN "summary conviction in Scotland" THEN `months for` `on summary conviction in Scotland`
    WHEN "summary conviction in Northern Ireland" THEN `months for` `on summary conviction in Northern Ireland`
    OTHERWISE NOTHING
    WHERE
        `months for` mode MEANS
            CONSIDER `s 418(6) the penalty for an offence under section 418(5)` mode
            WHEN NOTHING THEN NOTHING
            WHEN JUST penalty THEN
                CONSIDER penalty's `imprisonment not exceeding`
                WHEN NOTHING THEN NOTHING
                WHEN JUST term THEN
                    CONSIDER term's unit
                    WHEN Years THEN JUST (term's `number of units` TIMES 12)
                    WHEN Months THEN JUST (term's `number of units`)
                    OTHERWISE NOTHING

-- Whose question: a director's or the company secretary's.
@export Has the directors' report been approved by the board and signed on its behalf by a director or the secretary (section 419(1))?
GIVEN `the directors' report has been approved by the board of directors` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has the directors' report been approved by the board of directors?
      `the directors' report has been signed on behalf of the board by a director` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has the directors' report been signed on behalf of the board by a director?
      `the directors' report has been signed on behalf of the board by the secretary of the company` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has the directors' report been signed on behalf of the board by the secretary of the company?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 419(1), has the directors' report been approved and signed as the section requires?` IS
    `s 419(1) the directors' report has been approved and signed as required` `the directors' report has been approved by the board of directors` `the directors' report has been signed on behalf of the board by a director` `the directors' report has been signed on behalf of the board by the secretary of the company`

-- Whose question: a director's or the company secretary's.
@export Must the directors' report contain a statement, in a prominent position above the signature, that advantage is taken of the small companies exemption (section 419(2))?
GIVEN `in preparing the report advantage is taken of the small companies exemption` IS A BOOLEAN @desc In preparing the directors' report, is advantage taken of the small companies exemption?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 419(2), must the directors' report state, above the signature, that advantage is taken of the small companies exemption?` IS
    `s 419(2) the report must contain a statement that advantage is taken of the small companies exemption in a prominent position above the signature` `in preparing the report advantage is taken of the small companies exemption`

-- Whose question: a director's.
@export Does a director commit an offence under section 419(3) because a directors' report that does not comply with the requirements of the Act was approved?
GIVEN `a directors' report has been approved` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has a directors' report been approved?
      `the approved report does not comply with the requirements of this Act` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does the approved directors' report fail to comply with the requirements of the Companies Act?
      `I am a director of the company` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are you a director of the company?
      `I knew that it did not comply` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did you know that it did not comply?
      `I was reckless as to whether it complied` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Were you reckless as to whether it complied?
      `I failed to take reasonable steps to secure compliance or to prevent the report from being approved` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did you fail to take reasonable steps to secure compliance with those requirements or to prevent the report from being approved?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 419(3), do I commit an offence as a director because a directors' report that does not comply was approved?` IS
    `s 419(3) the director commits an offence` `a directors' report has been approved` `the approved report does not comply with the requirements of this Act` `I am a director of the company` `I knew that it did not comply` `I was reckless as to whether it complied` `I failed to take reasonable steps to secure compliance or to prevent the report from being approved`

-- Whose question: a director's.
@export What is the most a director can be fined on summary conviction of an offence under section 419, in pounds (section 419(4))?
GIVEN `the statutory maximum, in pounds` IS A NUMBER @desc What is the amount of the statutory maximum fine, in pounds? (The Act does not state it; it is set outside the Act.)
GIVETH A MAYBE NUMBER
DECIDE `Under section 419(4), what is the most I can be fined on summary conviction for that offence, in pounds?` IS
    CONSIDER `s 419(4) the penalty for an offence under section 419` `on summary conviction`
    WHEN NOTHING THEN NOTHING
    WHEN JUST penalty THEN
        CONSIDER penalty's `fine not exceeding`
        WHEN NOTHING THEN NOTHING
        WHEN JUST limit THEN `s 414D(3) the most a fine limit allows in pounds` limit `the statutory maximum, in pounds` 0 -- placeholder: no level on the standard scale is used by this section, so a fixed 0 is passed

-- Whose question: a director's or the company secretary's.
@export Has the separate corporate governance statement been approved by the board and signed on its behalf by a director or the secretary (section 419A)?
GIVEN `the statement is a separate corporate governance statement` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the statement a separate corporate governance statement (one that is not included in the directors' report)?
      `the statement has been approved by the board of directors` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has the statement been approved by the board of directors?
      `the statement has been signed on behalf of the board by a director` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has the statement been signed on behalf of the board by a director?
      `the statement has been signed on behalf of the board by the secretary of the company` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has the statement been signed on behalf of the board by the secretary of the company?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 419A, has the separate corporate governance statement been approved and signed as the section requires?` IS
    `s 419A the separate corporate governance statement has been approved and signed as required` `the statement is a separate corporate governance statement` `the statement has been approved by the board of directors` `the statement has been signed on behalf of the board by a director` `the statement has been signed on behalf of the board by the secretary of the company`

§ `Directors' remuneration report (sections 420 to 422A)`
-- Whose questions: a director's (also a former director's within five years, under section 421(3)).
-- These questions arise only for a quoted company, except section 421(3), which runs to any director of any company and to a former director.

-- Whose question: a director's of a quoted company.
@export Have the directors of the quoted company prepared a directors' remuneration report for the financial year (section 420(1))?
GIVEN `my company is a quoted company` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is your company a quoted company for the financial year?
      `the directors have prepared a directors' remuneration report for the financial year` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Have the directors prepared a directors' remuneration report for the financial year?
