GIVETH A MAYBE NUMBER
DECIDE `Under section 420(3), what is the most I can be fined on summary conviction for that offence, in pounds?` IS
    CONSIDER `s 420(3) the penalty for an offence under section 420` `on summary conviction`
    WHEN NOTHING THEN NOTHING
    WHEN JUST penalty THEN
        CONSIDER penalty's `fine not exceeding`
        WHEN NOTHING THEN NOTHING
        WHEN JUST limit THEN `s 414D(3) the most a fine limit allows in pounds` limit `the statutory maximum, in pounds` 0 -- placeholder: no level on the standard scale is used by this section, so a fixed 0 is passed

-- Whose question: a director's, or a former director's within five years.
@export Is a director, or a person who has been a director within the preceding five years, under a duty to give the company notice of matters relating to himself that the remuneration regulations need (section 421(3))?
GIVEN `I am a director of the company on the day I ask` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are you a director of the company today?
      `I have been a director of the company at some time` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Have you ever been a director of the company?
      `the last day on which I was a director of the company` IS A DATE @desc If you are no longer a director, on what day were you last a director of the company? (ISO 8601, for example 2024-03-31. If you still are a director, give today's date.)
      `the day I ask` IS A DATE @desc What is today's date? (ISO 8601, for example 2026-11-13.)
      `the matter relates to me and is necessary for the purposes of regulations under section 421` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does the matter relate to you, and is it necessary for the purposes of regulations made under section 421?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 421(3), must I give notice to my company of matters relating to myself for the purposes of the remuneration regulations?` IS
    `s 421(3) the person must give notice to the company of the matter` `I am a director of the company on the day I ask` (IF `I have been a director of the company at some time` THEN JUST `the last day on which I was a director of the company` ELSE NOTHING) `the day I ask` `the matter relates to me and is necessary for the purposes of regulations under section 421`

-- Whose question: a director's, or a former director's within five years.
@export Does a person who makes default in complying with section 421(3) commit an offence (section 421(4))?
GIVEN `I am a director of the company on the day I ask` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are you a director of the company today?
      `I have been a director of the company at some time` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Have you ever been a director of the company?
      `the last day on which I was a director of the company` IS A DATE @desc If you are no longer a director, on what day were you last a director of the company? (ISO 8601, for example 2024-03-31. If you still are a director, give today's date.)
      `the day I ask` IS A DATE @desc What is today's date? (ISO 8601, for example 2026-11-13.)
      `the matter relates to me and is necessary for the purposes of regulations under section 421` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does the matter relate to you, and is it necessary for the purposes of regulations made under section 421?
      `I have made default in complying with section 421(3)` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Have you made default in giving the company that notice?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 421(4), do I commit an offence because I made default in giving notice to my company?` IS
    `s 421(4) the person commits an offence` (`s 421(3) the person must give notice to the company of the matter` `I am a director of the company on the day I ask` (IF `I have been a director of the company at some time` THEN JUST `the last day on which I was a director of the company` ELSE NOTHING) `the day I ask` `the matter relates to me and is necessary for the purposes of regulations under section 421`) `I have made default in complying with section 421(3)`

-- Whose question: a director's, or a former director's within five years.
