      `the revised policy is set out in a document` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the revised policy set out in a document?
      `the document is signed on behalf of the board by a director` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the document signed on behalf of the board by a director?
      `the document is signed on behalf of the board by the secretary of the company` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the document signed on behalf of the board by the secretary of the company?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 422A(3), has the revised policy been set out in a document signed on behalf of the board as the section requires?` IS
    `s 422A(3) the revised policy has been set out in a document signed as required` `the directors' remuneration policy has been revised` `the revised policy is set out in a document` `the document is signed on behalf of the board by a director` `the document is signed on behalf of the board by the secretary of the company`

§ `Circulating the annual accounts and reports (sections 423 to 426A)`
-- Whose questions: a member's or a debenture holder's (what the company must send, and by when), and a director's or company secretary's (what the company must do, and what follows if it does not).

-- Whose question: a member's or debenture holder's.
@export Must the company send this person a copy of its annual accounts and reports for the financial year (section 423(1))?
GIVEN `I am a member of the company` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are you a member of the company?
      `I am a holder of the company's debentures` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Do you hold debentures of the company?
      `I am entitled to receive notice of general meetings of the company` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are you entitled to receive notice of general meetings of the company?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 423(1), must my company send me a copy of its annual accounts and reports for the financial year?` IS
    `s 423(1) the company must send the person a copy of its annual accounts and reports for the financial year` (JUST `I am a member of the company`) `I am a holder of the company's debentures` `I am entitled to receive notice of general meetings of the company`

-- Whose question: a member's or debenture holder's.
@export Does the company not need to send this person a copy because it does not have a current address for them (section 423(2))?
GIVEN `an address has been notified to the company by me as one at which documents may be sent to me` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Have you notified the company of an address at which documents may be sent to you?
      `the company has no reason to believe that documents sent to me at that address will not reach me` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does the company have no reason to believe that documents sent to you at that address will not reach you?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 423(2), does my company not need to send me a copy because it has no current address for me?` IS
    `s 423(2) copies need not be sent to the person` (`s 423(3) the company has a current address for the person` `an address has been notified to the company by me as one at which documents may be sent to me` `the company has no reason to believe that documents sent to me at that address will not reach me`)

-- Whose question: a member's or debenture holder's.
@export Does the company have a current address for this person (section 423(3))?
GIVEN `an address has been notified to the company by me as one at which documents may be sent to me` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Have you notified the company of an address at which documents may be sent to you?
      `the company has no reason to believe that documents sent to me at that address will not reach me` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does the company have no reason to believe that documents sent to you at that address will not reach you?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 423(3), does my company have a current address for me?` IS
    `s 423(3) the company has a current address for the person` `an address has been notified to the company by me as one at which documents may be sent to me` `the company has no reason to believe that documents sent to me at that address will not reach me`

-- Whose question: a member's.
@export Does a company without a share capital not need to send a copy to a person who is not entitled to receive notices of general meetings (section 423(4))?
GIVEN `the company does not have a share capital` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does the company have no share capital?
      `I am entitled to receive notices of general meetings of the company` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are you entitled to receive notices of general meetings of the company?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 423(4), does my company, which has no share capital, not need to send me a copy because I am not entitled to notices of general meetings?` IS
    `s 423(4) copies need not be sent to the person` `the company does not have a share capital` `I am entitled to receive notices of general meetings of the company`

-- Whose question: a director's or the company secretary's.
@export Did the company send out copies of its annual accounts and reports within the time allowed: for a private company by the end of the period for filing (or, if earlier, the day it delivered them to the registrar), for a public company at least 21 days before the accounts meeting (section 424)?
GIVEN `my company was a public company immediately before the end of the accounting reference period` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Was your company a public company immediately before the end of the accounting reference period by reference to which the financial year was determined?
      `the day on which copies were sent out` IS A DATE @desc On what day were the copies sent out? (If they were sent out over several days, give the last day. ISO 8601, for example 2027-10-01.)
      `the end of the period for filing accounts and reports` IS A DATE @desc On what day does the period for filing the accounts and reports end? (Section 442 sets it. ISO 8601.)
      `my company has delivered its accounts and reports to the registrar` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has the company delivered its accounts and reports to the registrar?
      `the date the company delivered its accounts and reports to the registrar` IS A DATE @desc If so, on what day? (ISO 8601. If not, give any date: it is not used.)
      `the date of the relevant accounts meeting` IS A DATE @desc On what date is the accounts meeting at which the accounts and reports are to be laid? (ISO 8601. For a private company give any date: it is not used.)
      `all the members entitled to attend and vote at the relevant accounts meeting agreed that copies sent later were duly sent` IS A BOOLEAN @desc If a public company sent copies out late, did all the members entitled to attend and vote at the accounts meeting agree that they should be taken as duly sent? (If not, or if they were sent in time, answer no.)
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 424, did my company send out the copies of the accounts and reports within the time allowed?` IS
    `s 424(2) to (5) the company sent the copies out within the time allowed` `my company was a public company immediately before the end of the accounting reference period` `the day on which copies were sent out` `the end of the period for filing accounts and reports` (IF `my company has delivered its accounts and reports to the registrar` THEN JUST `the date the company delivered its accounts and reports to the registrar` ELSE NOTHING) `the date of the relevant accounts meeting` `all the members entitled to attend and vote at the relevant accounts meeting agreed that copies sent later were duly sent`

-- Whose question: a director's or the company secretary's.
@export By what day must a public company send out copies of its annual accounts and reports, which is 21 days before the accounts meeting (section 424(3))?
GIVEN `the date of the relevant accounts meeting` IS A DATE @desc On what date is the accounts meeting at which the accounts and reports are to be laid? (ISO 8601, for example 2027-12-22.)
GIVETH A DATE
DECIDE `Under section 424(3), by what day must my public company send out the copies of the accounts and reports?` IS
    `s 424(3) the last day on which a public company may send out copies` `the date of the relevant accounts meeting`

-- Whose question: a director's or the company secretary's.
@export Does the company commit an offence under section 425(1)(a) because default was made in complying with section 423 or 424?
GIVEN `default is made in complying with section 423 or 424` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has default been made in complying with section 423 or 424 (sending out copies, or sending them in time)?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 425(1)(a), does my company commit an offence because default was made in sending out copies?` IS
    `s 425(1)(a) the company commits an offence` `default is made in complying with section 423 or 424`

-- Whose question: a director's or the company secretary's.
@export Does an officer of the company who is in default commit an offence under section 425(1)(b) because default was made in complying with section 423 or 424?
GIVEN `default is made in complying with section 423 or 424` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has default been made in complying with section 423 or 424?
      `I am an officer of the company who is in default` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are you an officer of the company who is in default for this purpose? (Section 1121 says who is.)
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 425(1)(b), do I commit an offence as an officer of the company in default because default was made in sending out copies?` IS
    `s 425(1)(b) the officer of the company commits an offence` `default is made in complying with section 423 or 424` (JUST `I am an officer of the company who is in default`)

-- Whose question: a director's or the company secretary's.
@export What is the most that can be imposed on summary conviction of an offence under section 425, in pounds (section 425(2))?
GIVEN `the statutory maximum, in pounds` IS A NUMBER @desc What is the amount of the statutory maximum fine, in pounds? (The Act does not state it; it is set outside the Act.)
GIVETH A MAYBE NUMBER
DECIDE `Under section 425(2), what is the most I can be fined on summary conviction for that offence, in pounds?` IS
    CONSIDER `s 425(2) the penalty for an offence under section 425` `on summary conviction`
    WHEN NOTHING THEN NOTHING
    WHEN JUST penalty THEN
        CONSIDER penalty's `fine not exceeding`
        WHEN NOTHING THEN NOTHING
        WHEN JUST limit THEN `s 414D(3) the most a fine limit allows in pounds` limit `the statutory maximum, in pounds` 0 -- placeholder: no level on the standard scale is used by this section, so a fixed 0 is passed

-- Whose question: a director's or the company secretary's.
@export May the company provide a copy of the strategic report with the supplementary material instead of copies of the accounts and reports (section 426(1))?
GIVEN `the case is one specified by regulations made by the Secretary of State` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the case one specified by regulations made by the Secretary of State?
      `any conditions so specified are complied with` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are any conditions the regulations specify complied with?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 426(1), may my company provide a copy of the strategic report with supplementary material instead of copies of the accounts and reports?` IS
    `s 426(1) the company may provide a copy of the strategic report with the supplementary material instead of copies of the accounts and reports` `the case is one specified by regulations made by the Secretary of State` `any conditions so specified are complied with`

-- Whose question: a member's.
@export Must the company still send this person copies of the accounts and reports because they are entitled and wish to receive them (section 426(2))?
GIVEN `the company has provided the strategic report with the supplementary material instead of copies of the accounts and reports` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has the company sent you only the strategic report with the supplementary material instead of the accounts and reports?
      `I am entitled to be sent copies in accordance with section 423` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are you entitled to be sent copies under section 423?
      `I wish to receive them` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Do you wish to receive them?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 426(2), must my company still send me copies of the accounts and reports if I am entitled to them and wish to receive them?` IS
    `s 426(2) the company must send the person copies of the accounts and reports` `the company has provided the strategic report with the supplementary material instead of copies of the accounts and reports` `I am entitled to be sent copies in accordance with section 423` `I wish to receive them`

-- Whose question: a director's or the company secretary's, or a member's who has received it.
@export Does the supplementary material sent with the strategic report contain the statements that section 426A(2) requires?
GIVEN `my company is a quoted company` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is your company a quoted company?
      `the material states that the strategic report is only part of the company's annual accounts and reports` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does the material state that the strategic report is only part of the company's annual accounts and reports?
      `the material states how a person entitled to them can obtain a full copy` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does the material state how a person entitled to them can obtain a full copy of the annual accounts and reports?
      `the material states whether the auditor's report on the annual accounts was unqualified or qualified` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does the material state whether the auditor's report on the annual accounts was unqualified or qualified?
      `the auditor's report on the annual accounts was qualified` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Was the auditor's report on the annual accounts qualified?
      `the material sets out that report in full with any further material needed to understand the qualification` IS A BOOLEAN @desc If it was qualified, does the material set out that report in full together with any further material needed to understand the qualification?
      `the material states whether the auditor's statement under section 496 was unqualified or qualified` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does the material state whether the auditor's statement under section 496 (on the strategic report and directors' report) was unqualified or qualified?
      `the auditor's statement under section 496 was qualified` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Was that statement qualified?
      `the material sets out the qualified statement in full with any further material needed to understand the qualification` IS A BOOLEAN @desc If it was qualified, does the material set out the qualified statement in full together with any further material needed to understand the qualification?
      `the material contains a copy of the part of the directors' remuneration report that sets out the single total figure table` IS A BOOLEAN @desc If your company is quoted, does the material contain a copy of that part of the directors' remuneration report which sets out the single total figure table?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 426A(2), does the supplementary material contain everything that the section requires?` IS
    `s 426A(2) the supplementary material contains what the subsection requires` (JUST `my company is a quoted company`) `the material states that the strategic report is only part of the company's annual accounts and reports` `the material states how a person entitled to them can obtain a full copy` `the material states whether the auditor's report on the annual accounts was unqualified or qualified` `the auditor's report on the annual accounts was qualified` `the material sets out that report in full with any further material needed to understand the qualification` `the material states whether the auditor's statement under section 496 was unqualified or qualified` `the auditor's statement under section 496 was qualified` `the material sets out the qualified statement in full with any further material needed to understand the qualification` `the material contains a copy of the part of the directors' remuneration report that sets out the single total figure table`

§ `Website publication, copies on demand and publication requirements (sections 426B to 436)`
-- Whose questions: a member's or a debenture holder's (the right to a copy on demand under sections 431 and 432), a director's or company secretary's (the website, signatory and publication duties), and, for sections 433 to 436, the questions of anyone who deals with a company and reads or relies on what it publishes.
-- The website questions under section 426B arise only for an unquoted company required to include a section 172(1) statement; section 430 questions arise only for a quoted company.
-- Sections 427, 428 and 429 are blank in this text.

-- Whose question: a director's or the company secretary's.
@export Does section 426B, the requirement to make the section 172(1) statement available on a website, apply to the company (section 426B(1))?
GIVEN `my company qualifies as medium-sized for the financial year` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does your company qualify as medium-sized in relation to the financial year (sections 465 to 467)?
      `my company is a quoted company` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is your company a quoted company in relation to the financial year?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 426B(1), does the requirement to put the section 172(1) statement on a website apply to my company?` IS
    `s 426B(1) this section applies to the company` (`s 414CZA(2) subsection (1) does not apply to the company` (JUST `my company qualifies as medium-sized for the financial year`)) (JUST (NOT (`my company is a quoted company`)))

-- Whose question: a director's or the company secretary's.
@export Until what day must the section 172(1) statement remain available on the website: until the next statement is made available, or the end of the next financial year (section 426B(2))?
GIVEN `the section 172(1) statement for the next financial year has been made available` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has the section 172(1) statement for the company's next financial year been made available on the website?
      `the date the next section 172(1) statement was made available` IS A DATE @desc If so, on what day? (ISO 8601. If not, give any date: it is not used.)
      `the obligation to make a section 172(1) statement available does not arise for the next financial year` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does the obligation to make a section 172(1) statement available not arise for the company's next financial year?
      `the end of the company's next financial year` IS A DATE @desc On what day does the company's next financial year end? (ISO 8601.)
GIVETH A MAYBE DATE
DECIDE `Under section 426B(2), until what day must my company keep the section 172(1) statement available on its website?` IS
    `s 426B(2)(b) the last day until which the statement must remain available on a website` (IF `the section 172(1) statement for the next financial year has been made available` THEN JUST `the date the next section 172(1) statement was made available` ELSE NOTHING) `the obligation to make a section 172(1) statement available does not arise for the next financial year` `the end of the company's next financial year`

-- Whose question: a director's or the company secretary's.
@export Is the website maintained by or on behalf of the company and does it identify the company (section 426B(3))?
GIVEN `the website is maintained by or on behalf of the company` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the website maintained by or on behalf of the company?
      `the website identifies the company in question` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does the website identify the company in question?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 426B(3), is my company's website maintained by or on behalf of the company and does it identify the company?` IS
    `s 426B(3) the website meets the requirements of the subsection` `the website is maintained by or on behalf of the company` `the website identifies the company in question`

-- Whose question: a director's or the company secretary's.
@export Is access to the statement, and the ability to obtain a hard copy, free of any fee and unrestricted (except so far as necessary to comply with an enactment or regulatory requirement) (section 426B(4))?
GIVEN `access to the statement, or to a hard copy of it, is conditional on the payment of a fee` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is access to the statement, or the ability to obtain a hard copy of it from the website, conditional on the payment of a fee?
      `access or the ability to obtain a hard copy is otherwise restricted` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is access, or the ability to obtain a hard copy, otherwise restricted?
      `the restriction is necessary to comply with an enactment or regulatory requirement` IS A BOOLEAN @desc If it is restricted, is the restriction necessary to comply with an enactment or regulatory requirement (in the United Kingdom or elsewhere)?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 426B(4), does access to the section 172(1) statement on my company's website meet the requirement that it be free and unrestricted?` IS
    `s 426B(4) access to the statement meets the requirements of the subsection` `access to the statement, or to a hard copy of it, is conditional on the payment of a fee` `access or the ability to obtain a hard copy is otherwise restricted` `the restriction is necessary to comply with an enactment or regulatory requirement`

-- Whose question: a director's or the company secretary's.
@export Does an officer of the company who is in default commit an offence under section 426B(7)?
GIVEN `default is made in complying with section 426B` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has default been made in complying with section 426B?
      `I am an officer of the company who is in default` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are you an officer of the company who is in default for this purpose? (Section 1121 says who is.)
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 426B(7), do I commit an offence as an officer of the company in default in making the statement available on a website?` IS
    `s 426B(7) the officer of the company commits an offence` `default is made in complying with section 426B` (JUST `I am an officer of the company who is in default`)

-- Whose question: a director's or the company secretary's.
@export What is the most that can be imposed on summary conviction of an offence under section 426B(7), in pounds (section 426B(8))?
GIVEN `level 3 on the standard scale, in pounds` IS A NUMBER @desc What is the amount of level 3 on the standard scale, in pounds? (The Act does not state it; it is set outside the Act.)
GIVETH A MAYBE NUMBER
DECIDE `Under section 426B(8), what is the most I can be fined on summary conviction for that offence, in pounds?` IS
    CONSIDER `s 426B(8) the penalty for an offence under section 426B(7)` `on summary conviction`
    WHEN NOTHING THEN NOTHING
    WHEN JUST penalty THEN
        CONSIDER penalty's `fine not exceeding`
        WHEN NOTHING THEN NOTHING
        WHEN JUST limit THEN `s 414D(3) the most a fine limit allows in pounds` limit 0 `level 3 on the standard scale, in pounds` -- placeholder: the statutory maximum is not used by this section, so a fixed 0 is passed

-- Whose question: a director's or the company secretary's, of a quoted company.
@export Has the quoted company ensured that its annual accounts and reports are made available on a website and remain so available until the next ones are (section 430(1))?
GIVEN `my company is a quoted company` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is your company a quoted company?
      `the annual accounts and reports are made available on a website` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are the annual accounts and reports made available on a website?
      `they remain so available until the next financial year's are made available` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Do they remain available until the annual accounts and reports for the next financial year are made available?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 430(1), has my quoted company ensured that its annual accounts and reports are available on a website?` IS
    `s 430(1) the quoted company has ensured that its annual accounts and reports are available on a website` (JUST `my company is a quoted company`) `the annual accounts and reports are made available on a website` `they remain so available until the next financial year's are made available`

-- Whose question: a director's or the company secretary's, of a quoted company.
@export Must the quoted company ensure that a revised directors' remuneration policy is made available on the website on which its annual accounts and reports are made available (section 430(2A))?
GIVEN `my company is a quoted company` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is your company a quoted company?
      `the directors' remuneration policy of the company is revised in accordance with section 422A` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has the company's directors' remuneration policy been revised in accordance with section 422A?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 430(2A), must my quoted company make the revised remuneration policy available on the website where its annual accounts are?` IS
    `s 430(2A) the quoted company must ensure that the revised policy is made available on the website on which its annual accounts and reports are made available` (JUST `my company is a quoted company`) `the directors' remuneration policy of the company is revised in accordance with section 422A`

-- Whose question: a director's or the company secretary's, of a quoted company.
@export Must the quoted company make this information about a person who has ceased to be a director available on its website: the name, particulars of remuneration payments, or particulars of payments for loss of office (section 430(2B))?
GIVEN `my company is a quoted company` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is your company a quoted company?
      `a person ceases to be a director of the company` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has a person ceased to be a director of the company?
      `such a payment has been made or is to be made to the person` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has a payment of that kind been made, or is it to be made, to the person after ceasing to be a director?
      `which information` IS A STRING @desc Which information? One of: name, remuneration payments, loss of office payments.
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 430(2B), must my quoted company make this information about a person who has ceased to be a director available on its website?` IS
    CONSIDER `which information`
    WHEN "name" THEN `s 430(2B) the quoted company must ensure that the information is made available on the website` (JUST `my company is a quoted company`) `a person ceases to be a director of the company` `such a payment has been made or is to be made to the person` `s 430(2B)(a) the name of the person concerned`
    WHEN "remuneration payments" THEN `s 430(2B) the quoted company must ensure that the information is made available on the website` (JUST `my company is a quoted company`) `a person ceases to be a director of the company` `such a payment has been made or is to be made to the person` `s 430(2B)(b) particulars of any remuneration payment made or to be made to the person after ceasing to be a director, including its amount and how it was calculated`
    WHEN "loss of office payments" THEN `s 430(2B) the quoted company must ensure that the information is made available on the website` (JUST `my company is a quoted company`) `a person ceases to be a director of the company` `such a payment has been made or is to be made to the person` `s 430(2B)(c) particulars of any payment for loss of office made or to be made to the person, including its amount and how it was calculated`
    OTHERWISE NOTHING

-- Whose question: a director's or the company secretary's, of a quoted company.
@export Is access to the material, and the ability to obtain a hard copy, free of any fee and unrestricted (except so far as necessary to comply with an enactment or regulatory requirement) (section 430(3))?
GIVEN `access to the material, or to a hard copy of it, is conditional on the payment of a fee` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is access to the material, or the ability to obtain a hard copy of it from the website, conditional on the payment of a fee?
      `access or the ability to obtain a hard copy is otherwise restricted` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is access, or the ability to obtain a hard copy, otherwise restricted?
      `the restriction is necessary to comply with an enactment or regulatory requirement` IS A BOOLEAN @desc If it is restricted, is the restriction necessary to comply with an enactment or regulatory requirement (in the United Kingdom or elsewhere)?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 430(3), does access to the material on my company's website meet the requirement that it be free and unrestricted?` IS
    `s 430(3) access to the material meets the requirements of the subsection` `access to the material, or to a hard copy of it, is conditional on the payment of a fee` `access or the ability to obtain a hard copy is otherwise restricted` `the restriction is necessary to comply with an enactment or regulatory requirement`

-- Whose question: a director's or the company secretary's, of a quoted company.
@export Does an officer of the quoted company who is in default commit an offence under section 430(6)?
GIVEN `default is made in complying with section 430` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has default been made in complying with section 430?
      `I am an officer of the company who is in default` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are you an officer of the company who is in default for this purpose? (Section 1121 says who is.)
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 430(6), do I commit an offence as an officer of the company in default in making material available on a website?` IS
    `s 430(6) the officer of the company commits an offence` `default is made in complying with section 430` (JUST `I am an officer of the company who is in default`)

-- Whose question: a director's or the company secretary's, of a quoted company.
@export What is the most that can be imposed on summary conviction of an offence under section 430(6), in pounds (section 430(7))?
GIVEN `level 3 on the standard scale, in pounds` IS A NUMBER @desc What is the amount of level 3 on the standard scale, in pounds? (The Act does not state it; it is set outside the Act.)
GIVETH A MAYBE NUMBER
DECIDE `Under section 430(7), what is the most I can be fined on summary conviction for that offence, in pounds?` IS
    CONSIDER `s 430(7) the penalty for an offence under section 430(6)` `on summary conviction`
    WHEN NOTHING THEN NOTHING
    WHEN JUST penalty THEN
        CONSIDER penalty's `fine not exceeding`
        WHEN NOTHING THEN NOTHING
        WHEN JUST limit THEN `s 414D(3) the most a fine limit allows in pounds` limit 0 `level 3 on the standard scale, in pounds` -- placeholder: the statutory maximum is not used by this section, so a fixed 0 is passed

-- Whose question: a member's or debenture holder's.
@export Is a member or debenture holder of an unquoted company entitled to be provided, on demand and without charge, with a copy of this document (section 431(1))?
GIVEN `my company is a quoted company` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the company a quoted company?
      `I am a member of the company` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are you a member of the company?
      `I am a holder of debentures of the company` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Do you hold debentures of the company?
      `the company has a strategic report for the last financial year` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does the company have a strategic report for the last financial year?
      `which document` IS A STRING @desc Which document? One of: annual accounts, strategic report, directors' report, auditor's report.
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 431(1), am I entitled, as a member or debenture holder of an unquoted company, to a copy of this document on demand and without charge?` IS
    CONSIDER `which document`
    WHEN "annual accounts" THEN `s 431(1) the person is entitled to be provided, on demand and without charge, with a copy of the document` (JUST (NOT (`my company is a quoted company`))) (JUST `I am a member of the company`) `I am a holder of debentures of the company` `the company has a strategic report for the last financial year` `s 431(1)(a) the company's last annual accounts`
    WHEN "strategic report" THEN `s 431(1) the person is entitled to be provided, on demand and without charge, with a copy of the document` (JUST (NOT (`my company is a quoted company`))) (JUST `I am a member of the company`) `I am a holder of debentures of the company` `the company has a strategic report for the last financial year` `s 431(1)(aa) the strategic report (if any) for the last financial year`
    WHEN "directors' report" THEN `s 431(1) the person is entitled to be provided, on demand and without charge, with a copy of the document` (JUST (NOT (`my company is a quoted company`))) (JUST `I am a member of the company`) `I am a holder of debentures of the company` `the company has a strategic report for the last financial year` `s 431(1)(b) the last directors' report`
    WHEN "auditor's report" THEN `s 431(1) the person is entitled to be provided, on demand and without charge, with a copy of the document` (JUST (NOT (`my company is a quoted company`))) (JUST `I am a member of the company`) `I am a holder of debentures of the company` `the company has a strategic report for the last financial year` `s 431(1)(c) the auditor's report on those accounts`
    OTHERWISE NOTHING

-- Whose question: a member's or debenture holder's.
@export How many copies of the documents is the person entitled to in all: a single copy under section 431, in addition to any copy under section 423 (section 431(2))?
GIVEN `the number of copies I am entitled to under section 423` IS A NUMBER @desc How many copies are you entitled to under section 423?
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `Under section 431(2), how many copies of the documents am I entitled to in all, counting any copy under section 423?` IS
    `s 431(2) the total number of copies of the documents the person is entitled to under sections 423 and 431` `the number of copies I am entitled to under section 423`

-- Whose question: a member's or debenture holder's.
@export Was the demand complied with within seven days of the company's receiving it (section 431(3))?
GIVEN `the date the company received the demand` IS A DATE @desc On what date did the company receive your demand? (ISO 8601, for example 2027-03-01.)
      `the company has complied with the demand` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has the company complied with your demand?
      `the date the company complied with the demand` IS A DATE @desc If so, on what date? (ISO 8601. If not, give any date: it is not used.)
      `today's date` IS A DATE @desc What is today's date? (ISO 8601.)
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 431(3), was my demand for a copy complied with within seven days of receipt?` IS
    `s 431(3) the demand was complied with within seven days of receipt` `the date the company received the demand` (IF `the company has complied with the demand` THEN JUST `the date the company complied with the demand` ELSE NOTHING) `today's date`

-- Whose question: a director's or the company secretary's, or a member's who made the demand.
@export Does the company commit an offence under section 431(3)(a) because a demand was not complied with within seven days of receipt?
GIVEN `a demand made under section 431 was not complied with within seven days of receipt by the company` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Was a demand made under section 431 not complied with within seven days of receipt by the company?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 431(3)(a), does my company commit an offence because it did not comply with a demand within seven days?` IS
    `s 431(3)(a) the company commits an offence` `a demand made under section 431 was not complied with within seven days of receipt by the company`

-- Whose question: a director's or the company secretary's.
@export Does an officer of the company who is in default commit an offence under section 431(3)(b)?
GIVEN `a demand made under section 431 was not complied with within seven days of receipt by the company` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Was a demand made under section 431 not complied with within seven days of receipt by the company?
      `I am an officer of the company who is in default` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are you an officer of the company who is in default for this purpose? (Section 1121 says who is.)
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 431(3)(b), do I commit an offence as an officer of the company in default because a demand was not complied with?` IS
    `s 431(3)(b) the officer of the company commits an offence` `a demand made under section 431 was not complied with within seven days of receipt by the company` (JUST `I am an officer of the company who is in default`)

-- Whose question: a director's or the company secretary's.
@export What is the most that can be imposed on summary conviction of an offence under section 431, in pounds (section 431(4))?
GIVEN `level 3 on the standard scale, in pounds` IS A NUMBER @desc What is the amount of level 3 on the standard scale, in pounds? (The Act does not state it; it is set outside the Act.)
GIVETH A MAYBE NUMBER
DECIDE `Under section 431(4), what is the most I can be fined on summary conviction for that offence, in pounds?` IS
    CONSIDER `s 431(4) the penalty for an offence under section 431` `on summary conviction`
    WHEN NOTHING THEN NOTHING
    WHEN JUST penalty THEN
        CONSIDER penalty's `fine not exceeding`
        WHEN NOTHING THEN NOTHING
        WHEN JUST limit THEN `s 414D(3) the most a fine limit allows in pounds` limit 0 `level 3 on the standard scale, in pounds` -- placeholder: the statutory maximum is not used by this section, so a fixed 0 is passed

