GIVETH A MAYBE NUMBER
DECIDE `Under section 432(4), what is the most I can be fined on summary conviction for that offence, in pounds?` IS
    CONSIDER `s 432(4) the penalty for an offence under section 432` `on summary conviction`
    WHEN NOTHING THEN NOTHING
    WHEN JUST penalty THEN
        CONSIDER penalty's `fine not exceeding`
        WHEN NOTHING THEN NOTHING
        WHEN JUST limit THEN `s 414D(3) the most a fine limit allows in pounds` limit 0 `level 3 on the standard scale, in pounds` -- placeholder: the statutory maximum is not used by this section, so a fixed 0 is passed

-- Whose question: a director's or the company secretary's, or anyone who reads or relies on what the company publishes.
@export Does the published copy of a document to which section 433 applies state the name of the person who signed it on behalf of the board, as section 433(1) requires?
GIVEN `my company is a quoted company` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the company a quoted company?
      `which document` IS A STRING @desc Which document? One of: balance sheet, strategic report, directors' report, directors' remuneration report.
      `the copy is published by or on behalf of the company` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the copy published by or on behalf of the company?
      `the copy states the name of the person who signed it on behalf of the board` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does the copy state the name of the person who signed it on behalf of the board?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 433(1), does the published copy of this document state the name of the person who signed it on behalf of the board, as the section requires?` IS
    CONSIDER `which document`
    WHEN NOTHING THEN NOTHING
    WHEN JUST d THEN
        `s 433(1) the published copy states the name of the signatory as required`
            (IF `my company is a quoted company` THEN `s 433(3) this section applies to copies of the document in the case of a quoted company` (JUST `my company is a quoted company`) d ELSE `s 433(2) this section applies to copies of the document in the case of an unquoted company` (JUST (NOT (`my company is a quoted company`))) d)
            `the copy is published by or on behalf of the company` `the copy states the name of the person who signed it on behalf of the board`
    WHERE
        `which document` MEANS
            CONSIDER `which document`
            WHEN "balance sheet" THEN JUST `s 433 the company's balance sheet`
            WHEN "strategic report" THEN JUST `s 433 the strategic report`
            WHEN "directors' report" THEN JUST `s 433 the directors' report`
            WHEN "directors' remuneration report" THEN JUST `s 433 the directors' remuneration report`
            OTHERWISE NOTHING

