GIVETH A MAYBE NUMBER
DECIDE `Under section 434(5), what is the most I can be fined on summary conviction for that offence, in pounds?` IS
    CONSIDER `s 434(5) the penalty for an offence under section 434` `on summary conviction`
    WHEN NOTHING THEN NOTHING
    WHEN JUST penalty THEN
        CONSIDER penalty's `fine not exceeding`
        WHEN NOTHING THEN NOTHING
        WHEN JUST limit THEN `s 414D(3) the most a fine limit allows in pounds` limit 0 `level 3 on the standard scale, in pounds` -- placeholder: the statutory maximum is not used by this section, so a fixed 0 is passed

-- Whose question: a director's or the company secretary's.
@export Must a company that publishes non-statutory accounts publish with them a statement indicating this matter (section 435(1))?
GIVEN `the company publishes non-statutory accounts` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does the company publish non-statutory accounts?
      `an auditor's report has been made on the company's statutory accounts for a financial year the non-statutory accounts purport to deal with` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has an auditor's report been made on the company's statutory accounts for a financial year that the non-statutory accounts purport to deal with?
      `which matter` IS A STRING @desc Which matter? One of: not statutory accounts, delivered to the registrar, auditor's report made, auditor's report qualified, section 498 statement.
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 435(1), must my company publish with its non-statutory accounts a statement indicating this matter?` IS
    CONSIDER `which matter`
    WHEN "not statutory accounts" THEN `s 435(1) the company must publish with the non-statutory accounts a statement indicating the matter` `the company publishes non-statutory accounts` `an auditor's report has been made on the company's statutory accounts for a financial year the non-statutory accounts purport to deal with` `s 435(1)(a) that they are not the company's statutory accounts`
    WHEN "delivered to the registrar" THEN `s 435(1) the company must publish with the non-statutory accounts a statement indicating the matter` `the company publishes non-statutory accounts` `an auditor's report has been made on the company's statutory accounts for a financial year the non-statutory accounts purport to deal with` `s 435(1)(b) whether statutory accounts dealing with any financial year with which the non-statutory accounts purport to deal have been delivered to the registrar`
    WHEN "auditor's report made" THEN `s 435(1) the company must publish with the non-statutory accounts a statement indicating the matter` `the company publishes non-statutory accounts` `an auditor's report has been made on the company's statutory accounts for a financial year the non-statutory accounts purport to deal with` `s 435(1)(c) whether an auditor's report has been made on the company's statutory accounts for any such financial year`
    WHEN "auditor's report qualified" THEN `s 435(1) the company must publish with the non-statutory accounts a statement indicating the matter` `the company publishes non-statutory accounts` `an auditor's report has been made on the company's statutory accounts for a financial year the non-statutory accounts purport to deal with` `s 435(1)(c)(i) whether the report was qualified or unqualified, or included a reference to any matters to which the auditor drew attention by way of emphasis without qualifying the report`
    WHEN "section 498 statement" THEN `s 435(1) the company must publish with the non-statutory accounts a statement indicating the matter` `the company publishes non-statutory accounts` `an auditor's report has been made on the company's statutory accounts for a financial year the non-statutory accounts purport to deal with` `s 435(1)(c)(ii) whether the report contained a statement under section 498(2) or section 498(3)`
    OTHERWISE NOTHING

-- Whose question: a director's or the company secretary's.
@export Is the company barred from publishing with non-statutory accounts the auditor's report on its statutory accounts (section 435(2))?
GIVEN `the company publishes non-statutory accounts` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does the company publish non-statutory accounts?
      `the document is the auditor's report on the company's statutory accounts` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the document the auditor's report on the company's statutory accounts?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 435(2), is my company barred from publishing the auditor's report on its statutory accounts with its non-statutory accounts?` IS
    `s 435(2) the company is barred from publishing the auditor's report on its statutory accounts with the non-statutory accounts` `the company publishes non-statutory accounts` `the document is the auditor's report on the company's statutory accounts`

-- Whose question: anyone who deals with the company.
@export Is the publication the publication of non-statutory accounts: a balance sheet or profit and loss account, or a group account, otherwise than as part of the statutory accounts (section 435(3))?
GIVEN `the document is a balance sheet or profit and loss account relating to, or purporting to deal with, a financial year of the company` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the document a balance sheet or profit and loss account relating to, or purporting to deal with, a financial year of the company?
      `the document is an account in any form purporting to be a balance sheet or profit and loss account for a group headed by the company` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the document an account in any form purporting to be a balance sheet or profit and loss account for a group headed by the company?
      `the document is published as part of the company's statutory accounts` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the document published as part of the company's statutory accounts?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 435(3), is what the company publishes the publication of non-statutory accounts?` IS
    `s 435(3) the publication is the publication of non-statutory accounts` `the document is a balance sheet or profit and loss account relating to, or purporting to deal with, a financial year of the company` `the document is an account in any form purporting to be a balance sheet or profit and loss account for a group headed by the company` `the document is published as part of the company's statutory accounts`

-- Whose question: anyone who deals with the company.
@export Is the group a group headed by the company: the company and any other undertaking, other than a parent undertaking of the company (section 435(4))?
GIVEN `the group consists of the company and any other undertaking` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does the group consist of the company and any other undertaking (whether or not it is a subsidiary undertaking of the company)?
      `the group includes a parent undertaking of the company` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does the group include a parent undertaking of the company?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 435(4), is this group a group headed by my company?` IS
    `s 435(4) the group is a group headed by the company` `the group consists of the company and any other undertaking` `the group includes a parent undertaking of the company`

