GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 435(5)(a), does my company commit an offence because it contravened a provision of section 435?` IS
    `s 435(5)(a) the company commits an offence` `the company contravenes a provision of section 435`

-- Whose question: a director's or the company secretary's.
@export Does an officer of the company who is in default commit an offence under section 435(5)(b)?
GIVEN `the company contravenes a provision of section 435` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has the company contravened a provision of section 435?
      `I am an officer of the company who is in default` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are you an officer of the company who is in default for this purpose? (Section 1121 says who is.)
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 435(5)(b), do I commit an offence as an officer of the company in default because it contravened section 435?` IS
    `s 435(5)(b) the officer of the company commits an offence` `the company contravenes a provision of section 435` (JUST `I am an officer of the company who is in default`)

-- Whose question: a director's or the company secretary's.
@export What is the most that can be imposed on summary conviction of an offence under section 435, in pounds (section 435(6))?
GIVEN `level 3 on the standard scale, in pounds` IS A NUMBER @desc What is the amount of level 3 on the standard scale, in pounds? (The Act does not state it; it is set outside the Act.)
GIVETH A MAYBE NUMBER
DECIDE `Under section 435(6), what is the most I can be fined on summary conviction for that offence, in pounds?` IS
    CONSIDER `s 435(6) the penalty for an offence under section 435` `on summary conviction`
    WHEN NOTHING THEN NOTHING
    WHEN JUST penalty THEN
        CONSIDER penalty's `fine not exceeding`
        WHEN NOTHING THEN NOTHING
        WHEN JUST limit THEN `s 414D(3) the most a fine limit allows in pounds` limit 0 `level 3 on the standard scale, in pounds` -- placeholder: the statutory maximum is not used by this section, so a fixed 0 is passed

-- Whose question: anyone who deals with the company.
@export Is the company regarded as publishing the document for the purposes of sections 433 to 435: it publishes, issues or circulates it or otherwise makes it available for public inspection in a manner calculated to invite the public to read it (section 436(2))?
GIVEN `the company publishes the document` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does the company publish the document?
      `the company issues the document` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does the company issue the document?
      `the company circulates the document` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does the company circulate the document?
      `the company otherwise makes the document available for public inspection` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does the company otherwise make the document available for public inspection?
      `it does so in a manner calculated to invite members of the public generally, or any class of them, to read it` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does it do so in a manner calculated to invite members of the public generally, or any class of members of the public, to read it?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 436(2), is my company regarded as publishing this document?` IS
    `s 436(2) the company is regarded as publishing the document` `the company publishes the document` `the company issues the document` `the company circulates the document` `the company otherwise makes the document available for public inspection` `it does so in a manner calculated to invite members of the public generally, or any class of them, to read it`

§ `Laying the accounts before a public company's general meeting (sections 437 and 438)`
-- Whose questions: a director's of a public company (the directors must lay the accounts and reports before the company in general meeting, and each director at the end of the period commits an offence if they are not laid) and a member's (who attends the accounts meeting).

-- Whose question: a director's of a public company.
@export Have the directors of the public company laid copies of its annual accounts and reports before the company in general meeting (section 437(1))?
GIVEN `my company is a public company` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is your company a public company?
      `the directors have laid before the company in general meeting copies of its annual accounts and reports` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Have the directors laid copies of the company's annual accounts and reports before the company in general meeting?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 437(1), have the directors of my public company laid the annual accounts and reports before the company in general meeting?` IS
    `s 437(1) the directors of the public company have laid copies of the annual accounts and reports before the company in general meeting` `my company is a public company` `the directors have laid before the company in general meeting copies of its annual accounts and reports`

-- Whose question: a director's of a public company.
@export Were the copies laid not later than the end of the period for filing the accounts and reports (section 437(2))?
GIVEN `the day the copies were laid before the company in general meeting` IS A DATE @desc On what day were the copies laid before the company in general meeting? (ISO 8601, for example 2028-06-30.)
      `the end of the period for filing accounts and reports` IS A DATE @desc On what day does the period for filing the accounts and reports end? (Section 442 sets it. ISO 8601.)
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 437(2), did the directors lay the copies before the end of the period for filing?` IS
    `s 437(2) the directors laid the copies in time` `the day the copies were laid before the company in general meeting` `the end of the period for filing accounts and reports`

-- Whose question: a director's or a member's of a public company.
@export Is the meeting an accounts meeting: a general meeting of the public company at which its annual accounts and reports are, or are to be, laid (section 437(3))?
GIVEN `my company is a public company` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is your company a public company?
      `the meeting is a general meeting of the company at which the annual accounts and reports are or are to be laid` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the meeting a general meeting of the company at which the company's annual accounts and reports are (or are to be) laid?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 437(3), is this meeting an accounts meeting of my public company?` IS
    `s 437(3) the meeting is an accounts meeting` `my company is a public company` `the meeting is a general meeting of the company at which the annual accounts and reports are or are to be laid`

-- Whose question: a director's of a public company.
@export Does a person who was a director immediately before the end of the period allowed commit an offence under section 438(1) if section 437 was not complied with in time?
GIVEN `the requirements of section 437 were not complied with before the end of the period allowed` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Were the requirements of section 437 (laying the accounts and reports before the company in general meeting) not complied with before the end of the period allowed?
      `I was a director of the company immediately before the end of that period` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Were you a director of the company immediately before the end of that period?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 438(1), do I commit an offence as a director because the accounts and reports were not laid in time?` IS
    `s 438(1) the person commits an offence` `the requirements of section 437 were not complied with before the end of the period allowed` `I was a director of the company immediately before the end of that period`

-- Whose question: a director's of a public company.
@export Does section 438(2) give the person charged a defence on these facts: that he took all reasonable steps for securing that section 437 would be complied with in time?
GIVEN `I am charged with an offence under section 438` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are you charged with an offence under section 438?
      `I prove that I took all reasonable steps for securing that those requirements would be complied with before the end of that period` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Can you prove that you took all reasonable steps for securing that the requirements of section 437 would be complied with before the end of that period?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 438(2), does the Act give me a defence on these facts?` IS
    `s 438(2) this section gives the person a defence on these facts` `I am charged with an offence under section 438` `I prove that I took all reasonable steps for securing that those requirements would be complied with before the end of that period`

-- Whose question: a director's of a public company.
@export Is it a defence to prove that the documents in question were not in fact prepared as required by Part 15 (section 438(3))?
GIVEN `I prove that the documents in question were not in fact prepared as required by this Part` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Can you prove that the documents in question were not in fact prepared as required by Part 15?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 438(3), is it a defence that the documents were not in fact prepared as the Part requires?` IS
    `s 438(3) proof that the documents were not in fact prepared as required is a defence` `I prove that the documents in question were not in fact prepared as required by this Part`

-- Whose question: a director's of a public company.
-- The daily default fine of section 438(4) appears in two versions in this text and the text does not say which is in force: see the next question and fork F30 in NOTES.md.
@export What is the most that can be imposed on summary conviction of an offence under section 438, in pounds (section 438(4))?
GIVEN `level 5 on the standard scale, in pounds` IS A NUMBER @desc What is the amount of level 5 on the standard scale, in pounds? (The Act does not state it; it is set outside the Act.)
GIVETH A MAYBE NUMBER
DECIDE `Under section 438(4), what is the most I can be fined on summary conviction for that offence, in pounds?` IS
    CONSIDER `s 438(4) the penalty for an offence under section 438` `on summary conviction`
    WHEN NOTHING THEN NOTHING
    WHEN JUST penalty THEN
        CONSIDER penalty's `fine not exceeding`
        WHEN NOTHING THEN NOTHING
        WHEN JUST limit THEN `s 414D(3) the most a fine limit allows in pounds` limit 0 `level 5 on the standard scale, in pounds` -- placeholder: the statutory maximum is not used by this section, so a fixed 0 is passed

-- Whose question: a director's of a public company.
@export What is the most the daily default fine can be, in pounds, on each of the two versions of section 438(4) that this text carries (section 438(4))?
GIVEN `which version of section 438(4)` IS A STRING @desc Which version of the daily default fine? One of: first (one-tenth of level 5 on the standard scale), second (one-tenth of the greater of 5,000 pounds or level 4 on the standard scale).
      `level 4 on the standard scale, in pounds` IS A NUMBER @desc What is the amount of level 4 on the standard scale, in pounds? (The Act does not state it; it is set outside the Act.)
      `level 5 on the standard scale, in pounds` IS A NUMBER @desc What is the amount of level 5 on the standard scale, in pounds? (The Act does not state it; it is set outside the Act.)
GIVETH A MAYBE NUMBER
DECIDE `Under section 438(4), what is the most the daily default fine for continued contravention can be, in pounds, on a version of the text?` IS
    CONSIDER `which version of section 438(4)`
    WHEN "first" THEN JUST (`s 438(4) the most the daily default fine may be in pounds on the version` `s 438(4) the first version: one-tenth of level 5 on the standard scale` `level 4 on the standard scale, in pounds` `level 5 on the standard scale, in pounds`)
    WHEN "second" THEN JUST (`s 438(4) the most the daily default fine may be in pounds on the version` `s 438(4) the second version: one-tenth of the greater of £5,000 or level 4 on the standard scale` `level 4 on the standard scale, in pounds` `level 5 on the standard scale, in pounds`)
    OTHERWISE NOTHING

§ `Members' approval of the directors' remuneration report and policy (sections 439 to 440)`
-- Whose questions: a director's (the existing directors must ensure the resolution is put to the vote), a company secretary's or officer's (notice) and a member's (what is put to the vote, and whether remuneration entitlements depend on the result).
-- These questions arise only for a quoted company.

-- Whose question: a company secretary's or director's, of a quoted company.
@export Has the quoted company, prior to the accounts meeting, given its members notice of the intention to move an ordinary resolution approving the directors' remuneration report (section 439(1))?
GIVEN `my company is a quoted company` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is your company a quoted company?
      `the company has given notice of the intention to move the resolution approving the directors' remuneration report` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has the company given the members entitled to be sent notice of the meeting, before the accounts meeting, notice of the intention to move an ordinary resolution approving the directors' remuneration report (other than the policy part)?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 439(1), has my quoted company, prior to the accounts meeting, given its members notice of the intention to move the resolution approving the directors' remuneration report?` IS
    `s 439(1) the quoted company has given notice of the resolution approving the directors' remuneration report` (JUST `my company is a quoted company`) `the company has given notice of the intention to move the resolution approving the directors' remuneration report`

-- Whose question: a company secretary's or director's, of a quoted company.
@export By what day must the quoted company give notice, prior to the accounts meeting: the day before the accounts meeting (section 439(1))?
GIVEN `the date of the accounts meeting` IS A DATE @desc On what date is the accounts meeting? (ISO 8601, for example 2028-09-15.)
GIVETH A DATE
DECIDE `Under section 439(1), by what day must my quoted company give notice of the resolution, prior to the accounts meeting?` IS
    `s 439(1) the last day on which the quoted company may give notice` `the date of the accounts meeting`

-- Whose question: a company secretary's or director's, of a quoted company.
@export Was notice given prior to the accounts meeting (section 439(1))?
GIVEN `the day notice was given` IS A DATE @desc On what day was notice given? (ISO 8601.)
      `the date of the accounts meeting` IS A DATE @desc On what date is the accounts meeting? (ISO 8601.)
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 439(1), did my quoted company give notice prior to the accounts meeting?` IS
    `s 439(1) the quoted company gave notice prior to the accounts meeting` `the day notice was given` `the date of the accounts meeting`

-- Whose question: a company secretary's or director's, of a quoted company.
@export May the notice be given in this manner: any manner permitted for the service on the member of notice of the meeting (section 439(2))?
GIVEN `the manner is one permitted for the service on the member of notice of the meeting` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the manner one permitted for the service on the member of notice of the meeting?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 439(2), may the notice be given in this manner?` IS
    `s 439(2) the notice may be given in the manner` `the manner is one permitted for the service on the member of notice of the meeting`

-- Whose question: a director's of a quoted company.
@export Has the existing director ensured that the resolution approving the directors' remuneration report is put to the vote of the meeting (section 439(4))?
GIVEN `I am a director of the company immediately before that meeting` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are you a director of the company immediately before the accounts meeting?
      `the resolution was put to the vote of the meeting` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Was the resolution put to the vote of the meeting?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 439(4), have I, as an existing director, ensured that the resolution is put to the vote of the meeting?` IS
    `s 439(4) the existing director has ensured that the resolution is put to the vote of the meeting` (`s 439(6) the person is an existing director` `I am a director of the company immediately before that meeting`) `the resolution was put to the vote of the meeting`

-- Whose question: a director's or a member's.
@export Is a person's entitlement to remuneration made conditional on the resolution being passed by reason only of the provision made by section 439 (section 439(5))?
GIVEN `the entitlement is made conditional on the resolution being passed by reason only of the provision made by section 439` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it only because of section 439 that your entitlement to remuneration would depend on the resolution being passed?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 439(5), is my entitlement to remuneration made conditional on the resolution being passed by reason only of section 439?` IS
    `s 439(5) the entitlement to remuneration is made conditional on the resolution being passed` `the entitlement is made conditional on the resolution being passed by reason only of the provision made by section 439`

-- Whose question: a company secretary's or director's, of a quoted company.
@export Must the quoted company give notice of the intention to move a resolution approving the relevant directors' remuneration policy at the accounts meeting held in the first financial year that begins on or after the day it becomes quoted (section 439A(1)(a))?
GIVEN `my company is a quoted company` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is your company a quoted company?
      `the accounts meeting is held in the first financial year which begins on or after the day on which the company becomes a quoted company` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the accounts meeting held in the first financial year which begins on or after the day on which the company becomes a quoted company?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 439A(1)(a), must my quoted company give notice of the intention to move a resolution approving the directors' remuneration policy at this accounts meeting?` IS
    `s 439A(1)(a) the quoted company must give notice of the intention to move the resolution approving the relevant directors' remuneration policy at the accounts meeting` (JUST `my company is a quoted company`) `the accounts meeting is held in the first financial year which begins on or after the day on which the company becomes a quoted company`

-- Whose question: a company secretary's or director's, of a quoted company.
@export Is the accounts or other general meeting held no later than the end of the period of three financial years beginning with the first financial year after the last meeting for which notice was given (section 439A(1)(b))?
GIVEN `the number of the financial year of the last meeting for which notice was given under section 439A(1)` IS A NUMBER @desc Number your company's financial years consecutively. What is the number of the financial year in which the last meeting for which notice was given under section 439A(1) was held?
      `the number of the financial year of this meeting` IS A NUMBER @desc What is the number of the financial year in which this meeting is held?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 439A(1)(b), is this meeting held no later than the end of the period of three financial years after the last notice?` IS
    `s 439A(1)(b) the meeting is held no later than the end of the period of three financial years` `the number of the financial year of the last meeting for which notice was given under section 439A(1)` `the number of the financial year of this meeting`

-- Whose question: a company secretary's or director's, of a quoted company.
@export Must the quoted company give notice of the intention to move at an accounts meeting a resolution approving the relevant directors' remuneration policy because a section 439 resolution was not passed and no notice has been given (section 439A(2))?
GIVEN `my company is a quoted company` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is your company a quoted company?
      `a resolution required to be put to the vote under section 439 was not passed at the last accounts meeting` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Was a resolution required to be put to the vote under section 439 not passed at the last accounts meeting?
      `no notice under section 439A was given in relation to that meeting or any other general meeting held before the next accounts meeting` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Was no notice under section 439A given in relation to that meeting or any other general meeting held before the next accounts meeting?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 439A(2), must my quoted company give notice of a resolution approving the remuneration policy at an accounts meeting?` IS
    `s 439A(2) the quoted company must give notice of the intention to move the resolution approving the relevant directors' remuneration policy at an accounts meeting` (JUST `my company is a quoted company`) `a resolution required to be put to the vote under section 439 was not passed at the last accounts meeting` `no notice under section 439A was given in relation to that meeting or any other general meeting held before the next accounts meeting`

-- Whose question: a company secretary's or director's, of a quoted company.
@export Must the quoted company give notice of the intention to move at an accounts or other general meeting a resolution approving the relevant directors' remuneration policy because a resolution was not passed and no notice has been given (section 439A(2A))?
GIVEN `my company is a quoted company` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is your company a quoted company?
      `a resolution required to be put to the vote under subsection (1) or (2) or (2A) was not passed at the last accounts or other general meeting` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Was a resolution required to be put to the vote under subsection (1), (2) or (2A) not passed at the last accounts or other general meeting?
      `no notice under section 439A was given in relation to any other general meeting held before the next accounts meeting` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Was no notice under section 439A given in relation to any other general meeting held before the next accounts meeting?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 439A(2A), must my quoted company give notice of a resolution approving the remuneration policy at an accounts or other general meeting?` IS
    `s 439A(2A) the quoted company must give notice of the intention to move the resolution approving the relevant directors' remuneration policy at an accounts or other general meeting` (JUST `my company is a quoted company`) `a resolution required to be put to the vote under subsection (1) or (2) or (2A) was not passed at the last accounts or other general meeting` `no notice under section 439A was given in relation to any other general meeting held before the next accounts meeting`

-- Whose question: a company secretary's or director's, of a quoted company.
@export Was notice of the intention to move the policy resolution given, prior to the meeting, to the members entitled to be sent notice of the meeting (section 439A(5))?
GIVEN `the resolution is one to which section 439A applies` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the resolution one to which section 439A applies (one approving the directors' remuneration policy)?
      `notice was given prior to the meeting to the members entitled to be sent notice of the meeting` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Was notice given, prior to the meeting in question, to the members of the company entitled to be sent notice of the meeting?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 439A(5), was notice of the policy resolution given as the subsection requires?` IS
    `s 439A(5) notice of the intention to move the resolution was given as the subsection requires` `the resolution is one to which section 439A applies` `notice was given prior to the meeting to the members entitled to be sent notice of the meeting`

-- Whose question: a director's or the company secretary's, of a quoted company.
@export Does an officer of the company who is in default commit an offence under section 440(1) because notice of the remuneration report or policy resolution was not given as sections 439 and 439A require?
GIVEN `default is made in complying with section 439(1) or 439A(1), (2) or (2A)` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has default been made in giving notice as section 439(1) or 439A(1), (2) or (2A) requires?
      `I am an officer of the company who is in default` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are you an officer of the company who is in default for this purpose? (Section 1121 says who is.)
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 440(1), do I commit an offence as an officer in default because notice of the resolution was not given?` IS
    `s 440(1) the officer of the company commits an offence` `default is made in complying with section 439(1) or 439A(1), (2) or (2A)` (JUST `I am an officer of the company who is in default`)

-- Whose question: a director's of a quoted company.
@export Does each existing director commit an offence under section 440(2) because the resolution was not put to the vote of the meeting to which it relates?
GIVEN `the resolution is not put to the vote of the meeting to which it relates` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Was the resolution not put to the vote of the meeting to which it relates?
      `I am a director of the company immediately before that meeting` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are you a director of the company immediately before that meeting?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 440(2), do I commit an offence as an existing director because the resolution was not put to the vote?` IS
    `s 440(2) the existing director commits an offence` `the resolution is not put to the vote of the meeting to which it relates` (`s 440(5) the person is an existing director` `I am a director of the company immediately before that meeting`)

-- Whose question: a director's of a quoted company.
@export Does section 440(3) give the person charged a defence on these facts: that he took all reasonable steps for securing that the resolution was put to the vote (section 440(3))?
GIVEN `I am charged with an offence under section 440(2)` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are you charged with an offence under section 440(2)?
      `I prove that I took all reasonable steps for securing that the resolution was put to the vote of the meeting` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Can you prove that you took all reasonable steps for securing that the resolution was put to the vote of the meeting?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 440(3), does the Act give me a defence on these facts?` IS
    `s 440(3) this section gives the person a defence on these facts` `I am charged with an offence under section 440(2)` `I prove that I took all reasonable steps for securing that the resolution was put to the vote of the meeting`

-- Whose question: a director's or the company secretary's, of a quoted company.
@export What is the most that can be imposed on summary conviction of an offence under section 440, in pounds (section 440(4))?
GIVEN `level 3 on the standard scale, in pounds` IS A NUMBER @desc What is the amount of level 3 on the standard scale, in pounds? (The Act does not state it; it is set outside the Act.)
GIVETH A MAYBE NUMBER
DECIDE `Under section 440(4), what is the most I can be fined on summary conviction for that offence, in pounds?` IS
    CONSIDER `s 440(4) the penalty for an offence under section 440` `on summary conviction`
    WHEN NOTHING THEN NOTHING
    WHEN JUST penalty THEN
        CONSIDER penalty's `fine not exceeding`
        WHEN NOTHING THEN NOTHING
        WHEN JUST limit THEN `s 414D(3) the most a fine limit allows in pounds` limit 0 `level 3 on the standard scale, in pounds` -- placeholder: the statutory maximum is not used by this section, so a fixed 0 is passed

-- ====================================================================================================
-- seat questions from part coa10 (merged by the lead on 2026-11-12; unchanged text follows)
-- ====================================================================================================
-- Companies Act 2006 (United Kingdom), Part 15 Chapters 10 to 12 (ss 441 to 474), as a plain-text rendering from
-- legislation.gov.uk made by a converter script (not the official text) -- THE SEAT LAYER, part coa10.
--
-- SEAT: an individual who is, or is about to become, a director, a company secretary or a member (shareholder) of a company
-- registered under the Act, or who deals with one, asking on facts they can state what the Act requires or lets them do, what
-- rights they have against the company or its directors, what they must disclose, file, approve or vote on and by when, and
-- what follows (liability, offences, penalties) if it is not done. (Assumed, not ruled: the Act is addressed to companies, so
-- the individual is whoever stands in a company's management or ownership.)
--
-- This layer phrases the rules of the layer-1 modules imported above as the questions that person asks about their own
-- company's accounts and reports: by when the accounts must be filed, what must be filed, whether the company is exempt, what
-- follows if the accounts are late, whether accounts may be revised and what a notice or an application to court means for the
-- directors, who may ask for documents and what may be done with them, how a company qualifies as medium-sized, and what the
-- Part's defined terms mean. Nothing here is new law: each question calls one layer-1 function and restates no rule.
--
-- PLAIN INPUTS. Every question takes plain inputs (yes/no, a number, a date, or a choice from the Act's own list), one for each
-- fact the person states, each with an @desc worded as that person would be asked. The records and MAYBE answers that the
-- layer-1 rules expect are built inside each question, in its WHERE, from those answers; a "no" from another part of the Act
-- is passed as JUST FALSE and a "yes" as JUST TRUE (the person states a fact, so "not known" is not asked).
--
-- READING A RESULT. A MAYBE BOOLEAN answer is JUST TRUE (the Act says yes), JUST FALSE (the Act says no in its own words) or
-- NOTHING (the Act does not decide the case: it is silent, lists without closing the list, or limits its rule by its own
-- wording). NOTHING is "not covered", never "no".
--
-- WHERE THE PERSON MUST CHOOSE A TEXT. The text of the Act this encoding was written from prints two texts of section 444
-- (and of section 445(7), section 446(5) and the daily default fine in section 451(4)) and does not say which is in force. The
-- questions that depend on the choice ask it as `which text`; a different choice can change the answer.
--
-- Amounts the Act leaves to regulations or to another instrument (the late-filing penalty, the pounds that levels 4 and 5 on
-- the standard scale stand for) are asked as numbers; this layer never supplies them.

§ `Companies Act 2006, Part 15, Chapter 10 -- filing accounts and reports with the registrar`

§§ `Duty to file and the period allowed (ss 441 to 443)`

-- s 441(2). The duty to deliver accounts and reports is subject to the exemptions of ss 448 and 448A.
@export Under section 441(2), must the directors deliver the accounts and reports for the financial year to the registrar?
GIVEN `the directors of my company are not required to deliver accounts and reports under section 448 (unlimited companies)` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is your company an unlimited company whose directors are exempt from delivering accounts under section 448? (See the section 448 question.)
      `the directors of my company are not required to deliver a copy of the individual accounts under section 448A (dormant subsidiaries)` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is your company a dormant subsidiary whose directors are exempt from delivering its individual accounts under section 448A? (See the section 448A question.)
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 441(2), must the directors deliver the accounts and reports for the financial year to the registrar` IS
    `s 441(2) the directors must deliver the accounts and reports for the financial year`
        (JUST `the directors of my company are not required to deliver accounts and reports under section 448 (unlimited companies)`)
        (JUST `the directors of my company are not required to deliver a copy of the individual accounts under section 448A (dormant subsidiaries)`)

-- s 441(1). Which of ss 443A to 447 sets out the accounts and reports the directors must deliver.
@export Under section 441(1), which of sections 443A to 447 sets out the accounts and reports required of the directors of my company?
GIVEN `which text of sections 444, 445 and 446 you rely on` IS A `s 441 text of the sections the file prints twice` @desc The Act as we hold it prints two texts of section 444 (and of subsection (7) of section 445 and subsection (5) of section 446). Choose the first text if you rely on the version in which a small company delivers only a balance sheet (and may deliver its profit and loss account and directors' report); choose the second if you rely on the version in which a company subject to the small companies regime delivers its annual accounts and directors' report.
      `my company qualifies as a micro-entity` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does your company qualify as a micro-entity for the financial year (sections 384A and 384B)?
      `my company would qualify as a micro-entity but for being or having been a member of an ineligible group` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Would your company qualify as a micro-entity but for being, or having been, a member of an ineligible group?
      `my company is subject to the small companies regime` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is your company subject to the small companies regime for the financial year (section 381)?
      `my company would be subject to the small companies regime but for being or having been a member of an ineligible group` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Would your company be subject to the small companies regime but for being, or having been, a member of an ineligible group (section 384)?
      `my company is entitled to the small companies exemption in relation to the directors' report` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is your company entitled to the small companies exemption in relation to the directors' report (section 415A)?
      `my company qualifies as medium-sized` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does your company qualify as medium-sized for the financial year (sections 465 to 467; see the section 465 question)?
      `my company is a quoted company` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is your company a quoted company (section 385)? Answer false for an unquoted company.
GIVETH A MAYBE `s 441 filing section`
DECIDE `Under section 441(1), which of sections 443A to 447 sets out the accounts and reports required of the directors of my company` IS
    `s 441(1) the filing section that applies to the company` facts
    WHERE
        facts MEANS
            `s 441 facts about the company` OF
                `which text of sections 444, 445 and 446 you rely on`,
                (JUST `my company qualifies as a micro-entity`),
                (JUST `my company would qualify as a micro-entity but for being or having been a member of an ineligible group`),
                (JUST `my company is subject to the small companies regime`),
                (JUST `my company would be subject to the small companies regime but for being or having been a member of an ineligible group`),
                (JUST `my company is entitled to the small companies exemption in relation to the directors' report`),
                (JUST `my company qualifies as medium-sized`),
                (JUST (NOT `my company is a quoted company`)),
                (JUST `my company is a quoted company`)

-- s 441(1) with the section that applies: what the directors must or may deliver as to one document.
@export Under section 441(1), does the filing section that applies to my company make it a duty, a permission or not required for the directors to deliver this document to the registrar?
GIVEN `which text of sections 444, 445 and 446 you rely on` IS A `s 441 text of the sections the file prints twice` @desc Which text of section 444 (and of subsection (7) of section 445 and subsection (5) of section 446) do you rely on? The first text lets a small company deliver only a balance sheet; the second requires its annual accounts and directors' report.
      `my company qualifies as a micro-entity` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does your company qualify as a micro-entity for the financial year (sections 384A and 384B)?
      `my company would qualify as a micro-entity but for being or having been a member of an ineligible group` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Would your company qualify as a micro-entity but for being, or having been, a member of an ineligible group?
      `my company is subject to the small companies regime` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is your company subject to the small companies regime for the financial year (section 381)?
      `my company would be subject to the small companies regime but for being or having been a member of an ineligible group` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Would your company be subject to the small companies regime but for being, or having been, a member of an ineligible group (section 384)?
      `my company is entitled to the small companies exemption in relation to the directors' report` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is your company entitled to the small companies exemption in relation to the directors' report (section 415A)?
      `my company qualifies as medium-sized` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does your company qualify as medium-sized for the financial year (sections 465 to 467)?
      `my company is a quoted company` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is your company a quoted company (section 385)? Answer false for an unquoted company.
      `the document` IS A `s 441 document` @desc Which document do you ask about: the annual accounts, the balance sheet, the profit and loss account, the directors' report, the strategic report, the directors' remuneration report, a separate corporate governance statement, the auditor's report, or the statement that all the members consented to the abridgement?
      `my company is exempt from audit and the directors have taken advantage of that exemption` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is your company exempt from audit, and have the directors taken advantage of that exemption (Part 16, section 475)?
      `the directors deliver a copy of the profit and loss account` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Will the directors deliver a copy of the company's profit and loss account to the registrar? (This matters to a small company under the first text of section 444.)
      `the accounts are abridged under paragraph 1A of Schedule 1 to the Small Companies and Groups (Accounts and Directors' Report) Regulations 2008` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the balance sheet or profit and loss account abridged under paragraph 1A of Schedule 1 to the Small Companies and Groups (Accounts and Directors' Report) Regulations 2008?
      `there is a separate corporate governance statement` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does the company have a corporate governance statement that is separate from the directors' report?
GIVETH A MAYBE `s 441 requirement`
DECIDE `Under section 441(1), does the filing section that applies to my company make it a duty, a permission or not required for the directors to deliver this document to the registrar` IS
    `s 441(1) what the filing section that applies requires of the directors for the document` facts `the document` delivery
    WHERE
        facts MEANS
            `s 441 facts about the company` OF
                `which text of sections 444, 445 and 446 you rely on`,
                (JUST `my company qualifies as a micro-entity`),
                (JUST `my company would qualify as a micro-entity but for being or having been a member of an ineligible group`),
                (JUST `my company is subject to the small companies regime`),
                (JUST `my company would be subject to the small companies regime but for being or having been a member of an ineligible group`),
                (JUST `my company is entitled to the small companies exemption in relation to the directors' report`),
                (JUST `my company qualifies as medium-sized`),
                (JUST (NOT `my company is a quoted company`)),
                (JUST `my company is a quoted company`)
        delivery MEANS
            `s 441 facts about what is delivered` OF
                `my company is exempt from audit and the directors have taken advantage of that exemption`,
                `the directors deliver a copy of the profit and loss account`,
                `the accounts are abridged under paragraph 1A of Schedule 1 to the Small Companies and Groups (Accounts and Directors' Report) Regulations 2008`,
                `there is a separate corporate governance statement`

-- ss 441, 442, 451: were the requirements complied with before the end of the period for filing?
@export Under section 441(1), were the accounts and reports delivered before the end of the period for filing?
GIVEN `the first day of the accounting reference period` IS A DATE @desc On what date did the accounting reference period for these accounts begin? (For a company's first period this is usually the date of incorporation.)
      `the last day of the accounting reference period` IS A DATE @desc On what date did the accounting reference period end?
      `this is my company's first accounting reference period` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is this your company's first accounting reference period?
      `the date my company was incorporated` IS A DATE @desc On what date was your company incorporated?
      `my company was a public company immediately before the end of that period` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Was your company a public company immediately before the end of the accounting reference period? (False for a private company.)
      `the period was shortened by a notice under section 392` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Was the accounting reference period treated as shortened by a notice your company gave under section 392 (alteration of accounting reference date)?
      `the date of that notice` IS A DATE @desc If so, what is the date of the notice? (Give any date if there was no such notice.)
      `the Secretary of State has extended the period for filing` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has the Secretary of State, by notice in writing, extended the period for filing?
      `the date to which the notice extends the period` IS A DATE @desc If so, to what date does the notice extend it? (Give any date if there was no such notice.)
      `the accounts and reports have been delivered` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Have the accounts and reports been delivered to the registrar?
      `the date they were delivered` IS A DATE @desc If so, on what date were they delivered? (Give any date if they have not been.)
      `today's date` IS A DATE @desc What is today's date?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 441(1), were the accounts and reports delivered before the end of the period for filing` IS
    CONSIDER `s 442(1) the number of days from the end of the accounting reference period to the end of the period for filing` facts
    WHEN NOTHING THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (silent): section 442(5A) gives no period for filing when an extension passes the limit
    WHEN JUST allowed THEN
        `s 441(1) the requirements were complied with before the end of the period for filing`
            allowed
            (IF `the accounts and reports have been delivered` THEN JUST ((Day `the date they were delivered`) MINUS (Day `the last day of the accounting reference period`)) ELSE NOTHING)
            ((Day `today's date`) MINUS (Day `the last day of the accounting reference period`) GREATER THAN allowed)
    WHERE
        facts MEANS
            `s 442 facts about the accounting reference period` OF
                `the first day of the accounting reference period`,
                `the last day of the accounting reference period`,
                `this is my company's first accounting reference period`,
                `the date my company was incorporated`,
                `my company was a public company immediately before the end of that period`,
                `the period was shortened by a notice under section 392`,
                `the date of that notice`,
                `the Secretary of State has extended the period for filing`,
                `the date to which the notice extends the period`

-- s 442(1) to (7): on what date does the period for filing end?
@export Under section 442(1), on what date does the period for filing the accounts and reports end?
GIVEN `the first day of the accounting reference period` IS A DATE @desc On what date did the accounting reference period for these accounts begin? (For a company's first period this is usually the date of incorporation.)
      `the last day of the accounting reference period` IS A DATE @desc On what date did the accounting reference period end?
      `this is my company's first accounting reference period` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is this your company's first accounting reference period?
      `the date my company was incorporated` IS A DATE @desc On what date was your company incorporated?
      `my company was a public company immediately before the end of that period` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Was your company a public company immediately before the end of the accounting reference period? (False for a private company. A company that changed status during the period is judged by its status immediately before the period ended.)
      `the period was shortened by a notice under section 392` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Was the accounting reference period treated as shortened by a notice your company gave under section 392 (alteration of accounting reference date)?
      `the date of that notice` IS A DATE @desc If so, what is the date of the notice? (Give any date if there was no such notice.)
      `the Secretary of State has extended the period for filing` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has the Secretary of State, by notice in writing, extended the period for filing?
      `the date to which the notice extends the period` IS A DATE @desc If so, to what date does the notice extend it? (Give any date if there was no such notice.)
GIVETH A MAYBE DATE
DECIDE `Under section 442(1), on what date does the period for filing the accounts and reports end` IS
    `s 442(1) the period for filing ends on` facts
    WHERE
        facts MEANS
            `s 442 facts about the accounting reference period` OF
                `the first day of the accounting reference period`,
                `the last day of the accounting reference period`,
                `this is my company's first accounting reference period`,
                `the date my company was incorporated`,
                `my company was a public company immediately before the end of that period`,
                `the period was shortened by a notice under section 392`,
                `the date of that notice`,
                `the Secretary of State has extended the period for filing`,
                `the date to which the notice extends the period`

@export Under section 442(2), on what date does the period for filing end for an ordinary accounting reference period?
GIVEN `the last day of the accounting reference period` IS A DATE @desc On what date did the accounting reference period for these accounts end?
      `my company was a public company immediately before the end of that period` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Was your company a public company immediately before the end of the accounting reference period? (False for a private company.)
GIVETH A DATE
DECIDE `Under section 442(2), on what date does the period for filing end for an ordinary accounting reference period` IS
    `s 442(2) the period for filing ends on` `the last day of the accounting reference period` `my company was a public company immediately before the end of that period`

@export Under section 442(3), on what date does the period for filing end for a first accounting reference period of more than twelve months?
GIVEN `the date my company was incorporated` IS A DATE @desc On what date was your company incorporated?
      `the last day of the accounting reference period` IS A DATE @desc On what date did your first accounting reference period end?
      `my company was a public company immediately before the end of that period` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Was your company a public company immediately before the end of that period? (False for a private company.)
GIVETH A DATE
DECIDE `Under section 442(3), on what date does the period for filing end for a first accounting reference period of more than twelve months` IS
    `s 442(3) the period for filing ends on for a first accounting reference period of more than twelve months`
        `the date my company was incorporated` `the last day of the accounting reference period` `my company was a public company immediately before the end of that period`

@export Under section 442(3), is the accounting reference period a period of more than twelve months?
GIVEN `the first day of the accounting reference period` IS A DATE @desc On what date did the accounting reference period begin?
      `the last day of the accounting reference period` IS A DATE @desc On what date did it end?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 442(3), is the accounting reference period a period of more than twelve months` IF
    `s 442(3) the relevant accounting reference period is a period of more than twelve months` `the first day of the accounting reference period` `the last day of the accounting reference period`

@export Under section 442(4), on what date does the period for filing end, allowing for any notice under section 392 that shortened the accounting reference period?
GIVEN `the period for filing without the shortening` IS A DATE @desc On what date would the period for filing end under subsections (2) and (3), ignoring the notice?
      `the period was shortened by a notice under section 392` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Was the accounting reference period treated as shortened by a notice your company gave under section 392?
      `the date of that notice` IS A DATE @desc What is the date of the notice? (Give any date if there was no notice.)
GIVETH A DATE
DECIDE `Under section 442(4), on what date does the period for filing end, allowing for any notice under section 392 that shortened the accounting reference period` IS
    `s 442(4) the period for filing ends on where the accounting reference period is treated as shortened` `the period for filing without the shortening` `the period was shortened by a notice under section 392` `the date of that notice`

@export Under section 442(5), leaving aside the limit in subsection (5A), may the Secretary of State extend the period for filing on my application?
GIVEN `the date on which the period for filing would otherwise end` IS A DATE @desc On what date would the period for filing otherwise end?
      `the date you applied for an extension` IS A DATE @desc On what date did you apply to the Secretary of State for an extension?
      `the Secretary of State thinks fit for a special reason` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does the Secretary of State think fit, for some special reason, to extend the period? (This is his judgment; answer what he has said or you expect.)
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 442(5), leaving aside the limit in subsection (5A), may the Secretary of State extend the period for filing on my application` IS
    `s 442(5) the Secretary of State may extend the period for filing` `the date on which the period for filing would otherwise end` `the date you applied for an extension` `the Secretary of State thinks fit for a special reason`

@export Under section 442(5A), does the extension comply with the limit of twelve months after the end of the accounting reference period?
GIVEN `the last day of the accounting reference period` IS A DATE @desc On what date did the accounting reference period end?
      `the date to which the notice extends the period` IS A DATE @desc To what date does the Secretary of State's notice extend the period for filing?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 442(5A), does the extension comply with the limit of twelve months after the end of the accounting reference period` IS
    `s 442(5A) the extension complies with the limit of twelve months after the end of the accounting reference period` `the last day of the accounting reference period` `the date to which the notice extends the period`

@export Under section 442(6), does the period for a public company apply?
GIVEN `my company was a public company immediately before the end of the accounting reference period` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Was your company a public company immediately before the end of the accounting reference period? (False for a private company.)
      `my company was a public company at some other time` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Was your company a public company at some other time, for instance at the start of the period or today?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 442(6), does the period for a public company apply` IF
    `s 442(6) the period for a public company applies` `my company was a public company immediately before the end of the accounting reference period` `my company was a public company at some other time`

@export Under section 443, on what date does a period of a stated number of months from a given date end?
GIVEN `the specified date` IS A DATE @desc From what date, or after the end of what period, is the number of months counted? (For a period after an accounting reference period, give its last day.)
      `the number of months` IS A NUMBER @desc How many months is the period? (For example 9 for a private company's period for filing, 6 for a public company's.)
GIVETH A DATE
DECIDE `Under section 443, on what date does a period of a stated number of months from a given date end` IS
    `s 443(2) the period ends with` `the specified date` `the number of months`

§§ `What each section requires of the directors (ss 443A to 447)`

@export Under section 443A(1), is delivering this document to the registrar a duty, a permission or not required of the directors of a micro-entity?
GIVEN `the document` IS A `s 441 document` @desc Which document do you ask about: the annual accounts, the directors' report, the auditor's report, or another document?
      `my company is exempt from audit and the directors have taken advantage of that exemption` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is your company exempt from audit, and have the directors taken advantage of that exemption (Part 16, section 475)?
GIVETH A MAYBE `s 441 requirement`
DECIDE `Under section 443A(1), is delivering this document to the registrar a duty, a permission or not required of the directors of a micro-entity` IS
    `s 443A(1) what section 443A requires of the directors for the document` `the document` delivery
    WHERE
        -- Placeholders: section 443A reads only the audit-exemption fact; the other three fields are fixed.
        delivery MEANS
            `s 441 facts about what is delivered` OF
                `my company is exempt from audit and the directors have taken advantage of that exemption`,
                FALSE,
                FALSE,
                FALSE

@export Under section 444(1), is delivering this document to the registrar a duty, a permission or not required of the directors of a company subject to the small companies regime?
GIVEN `which text of section 444 you rely on` IS A `s 441 text of the sections the file prints twice` @desc The Act as we hold it prints two texts of section 444. Choose the first if you rely on the version in which the directors must deliver the balance sheet (and may deliver the profit and loss account and the directors' report); choose the second if you rely on the version in which they must deliver the annual accounts and the directors' report.
      `the document` IS A `s 441 document` @desc Which document do you ask about: the annual accounts, the balance sheet, the profit and loss account, the directors' report, the auditor's report, or the statement that all the members consented to the abridgement?
      `my company is exempt from audit and the directors have taken advantage of that exemption` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is your company exempt from audit, and have the directors taken advantage of that exemption (Part 16, section 475)?
      `the directors deliver a copy of the profit and loss account` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Will the directors deliver a copy of the company's profit and loss account to the registrar? (Only the first text turns on this.)
      `the accounts are abridged under paragraph 1A of Schedule 1 to the Small Companies and Groups (Accounts and Directors' Report) Regulations 2008` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the balance sheet or profit and loss account abridged under paragraph 1A of Schedule 1 to the Small Companies and Groups (Accounts and Directors' Report) Regulations 2008? (Only the first text turns on this.)
GIVETH A MAYBE `s 441 requirement`
DECIDE `Under section 444(1), is delivering this document to the registrar a duty, a permission or not required of the directors of a company subject to the small companies regime` IS
    `s 444(1) what section 444 requires of the directors for the document` `which text of section 444 you rely on` `the document` delivery
    WHERE
        -- Placeholder: section 444 does not read the corporate governance statement field; it is fixed.
        delivery MEANS
            `s 441 facts about what is delivered` OF
                `my company is exempt from audit and the directors have taken advantage of that exemption`,
                `the directors deliver a copy of the profit and loss account`,
                `the accounts are abridged under paragraph 1A of Schedule 1 to the Small Companies and Groups (Accounts and Directors' Report) Regulations 2008`,
                FALSE

@export Under section 444A(1), is delivering this document to the registrar a duty, a permission or not required of the directors of a company entitled to the small companies exemption in relation to the directors' report?
GIVEN `the document` IS A `s 441 document` @desc Which document do you ask about: the annual accounts, the directors' report, the auditor's report, or another document?
      `my company is exempt from audit and the directors have taken advantage of that exemption` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is your company exempt from audit, and have the directors taken advantage of that exemption (Part 16, section 475)?
GIVETH A MAYBE `s 441 requirement`
DECIDE `Under section 444A(1), is delivering this document to the registrar a duty, a permission or not required of the directors of a company entitled to the small companies exemption in relation to the directors' report` IS
    `s 444A(1) what section 444A requires of the directors for the document` `the document` delivery
    WHERE
        -- Placeholders: section 444A reads only the audit-exemption fact; the other three fields are fixed.
        delivery MEANS
            `s 441 facts about what is delivered` OF
                `my company is exempt from audit and the directors have taken advantage of that exemption`,
                FALSE,
                FALSE,
                FALSE

@export Under section 445(1), must the directors of a medium-sized company deliver this document to the registrar?
GIVEN `the document` IS A `s 441 document` @desc Which document do you ask about: the annual accounts, the strategic report, the directors' report, the auditor's report, or another document?
      `my company is exempt from audit and the directors have taken advantage of that exemption` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is your company exempt from audit, and have the directors taken advantage of that exemption (Part 16, section 475)?
GIVETH A MAYBE `s 441 requirement`
DECIDE `Under section 445(1), must the directors of a medium-sized company deliver this document to the registrar` IS
    `s 445(1) what section 445 requires of the directors for the document` `the document` delivery
    WHERE
        -- Placeholders: section 445 reads only the audit-exemption fact; the other three fields are fixed.
        delivery MEANS
            `s 441 facts about what is delivered` OF
                `my company is exempt from audit and the directors have taken advantage of that exemption`,
                FALSE,
                FALSE,
                FALSE

@export Under section 446(1), must the directors of an unquoted company deliver this document to the registrar?
GIVEN `the document` IS A `s 441 document` @desc Which document do you ask about: the annual accounts, the strategic report, the directors' report, a separate corporate governance statement, the auditor's report, or another document?
      `my company is exempt from audit and the directors have taken advantage of that exemption` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is your company exempt from audit, and have the directors taken advantage of that exemption (Part 16, section 475)?
      `there is a separate corporate governance statement` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does the company have a corporate governance statement that is separate from the directors' report?
GIVETH A MAYBE `s 441 requirement`
DECIDE `Under section 446(1), must the directors of an unquoted company deliver this document to the registrar` IS
    `s 446(1) what section 446 requires of the directors for the document` `the document` delivery
    WHERE
        -- Placeholders: section 446 does not read the profit and loss account or abridgement fields; they are fixed.
        delivery MEANS
            `s 441 facts about what is delivered` OF
                `my company is exempt from audit and the directors have taken advantage of that exemption`,
                FALSE,
                FALSE,
                `there is a separate corporate governance statement`

@export Under section 447(1), must the directors of a quoted company deliver this document to the registrar?
GIVEN `the document` IS A `s 441 document` @desc Which document do you ask about: the annual accounts, the directors' remuneration report, the strategic report, the directors' report, a separate corporate governance statement, the auditor's report, or another document?
      `there is a separate corporate governance statement` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does the company have a corporate governance statement that is separate from the directors' report?
GIVETH A MAYBE `s 441 requirement`
DECIDE `Under section 447(1), must the directors of a quoted company deliver this document to the registrar` IS
    `s 447(1) what section 447 requires of the directors for the document` `the document` delivery
    WHERE
        -- Placeholders: section 447 reads only the corporate governance statement field; the other three are fixed.
        delivery MEANS
            `s 441 facts about what is delivered` OF
                FALSE,
                FALSE,
                FALSE,
                `there is a separate corporate governance statement`

-- The copy of the balance sheet, directors' report and so on must state who signed it on behalf of the board (ss 443A(3), 444(6), 444A(3), 445(5), 446(3), 447(3)).
@export Under section 443A(3), does the copy of this document meet the requirement to state who signed it on behalf of the board?
GIVEN `the document` IS A `s 441 document` @desc Which document is the copy of: the balance sheet or the directors' report (the documents section 443A(3) names), or another document?
      `the copy states the name of the person who signed it on behalf of the board` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does the copy delivered state the name of the person who signed it on behalf of the board?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 443A(3), does the copy of this document meet the requirement to state who signed it on behalf of the board` IS
    `s 443A(3) the copy meets the requirement to state who signed it` `the document` `the copy states the name of the person who signed it on behalf of the board`

@export Under section 444(6), in the first text of section 444, does the copy of this document meet the requirement to state who signed it on behalf of the board?
GIVEN `the document` IS A `s 441 document` @desc Which document is the copy of: the balance sheet or the directors' report (the documents section 444(6) names), or another document?
      `the copy states the name of the person who signed it on behalf of the board` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does the copy delivered state the name of the person who signed it on behalf of the board?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 444(6), in the first text of section 444, does the copy of this document meet the requirement to state who signed it on behalf of the board` IS
    `s 444(6) the copy meets the requirement to state who signed it` `the document` `the copy states the name of the person who signed it on behalf of the board`

@export Under section 445(5), does the copy of this document meet the requirement to state who signed it on behalf of the board?
GIVEN `the document` IS A `s 441 document` @desc Which document is the copy of: the balance sheet, the strategic report or the directors' report (the documents section 445(5) names), or another document?
      `the copy states the name of the person who signed it on behalf of the board` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does the copy delivered state the name of the person who signed it on behalf of the board?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 445(5), does the copy of this document meet the requirement to state who signed it on behalf of the board` IS
    `s 445(5) the copy meets the requirement to state who signed it` `the document` `the copy states the name of the person who signed it on behalf of the board`

@export Under section 446(3), does the copy of this document meet the requirement to state who signed it on behalf of the board?
GIVEN `the document` IS A `s 441 document` @desc Which document is the copy of: the balance sheet, the strategic report, the directors' report or a separate corporate governance statement (the documents section 446(3) names), or another document?
      `the copy states the name of the person who signed it on behalf of the board` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does the copy delivered state the name of the person who signed it on behalf of the board?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 446(3), does the copy of this document meet the requirement to state who signed it on behalf of the board` IS
    `s 446(3) the copy meets the requirement to state who signed it` `the document` `the copy states the name of the person who signed it on behalf of the board`

@export Under section 447(3), does the copy of this document meet the requirement to state who signed it on behalf of the board?
GIVEN `the document` IS A `s 441 document` @desc Which document is the copy of: the balance sheet, the directors' remuneration report, the strategic report, the directors' report or a separate corporate governance statement (the documents section 447(3) names), or another document?
      `the copy states the name of the person who signed it on behalf of the board` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does the copy delivered state the name of the person who signed it on behalf of the board?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 447(3), does the copy of this document meet the requirement to state who signed it on behalf of the board` IS
    `s 447(3) the copy meets the requirement to state who signed it` `the document` `the copy states the name of the person who signed it on behalf of the board`

-- The copy of the auditor's report (ss 443A(4) and (5), 444(7), 444A(4), 445(6), 446(4), 447(4)).
@export Under section 443A(4), does the copy of the auditor's report state what the section requires?
GIVEN `more than one person is appointed as auditor` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is more than one person appointed as auditor?
      `the copy states the name of the auditor` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does the copy state the name of the auditor?
      `the copy states the names of all the auditors` IS A BOOLEAN @desc If more than one person is appointed, does the copy state the names of all the auditors?
      `the auditor is a firm` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the auditor a firm?
      `the copy states the name of the person who signed it as senior statutory auditor` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does the copy state the name of the person who signed it as senior statutory auditor?
      `the conditions in section 506 for omitting the names are met` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are the conditions in section 506 for omitting the auditor's names met (a resolution has been passed and notified to the Secretary of State)?
      `the copy states that a resolution has been passed and notified to the Secretary of State under section 506` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does the copy state that a resolution has been passed and notified to the Secretary of State in accordance with section 506?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 443A(4), does the copy of the auditor's report state what the section requires` IS
    `s 443A(4) the copy of the auditor's report states what the section requires` copy
    WHERE
        copy MEANS
            `s 443A facts about the copy of the auditor's report` OF
                `more than one person is appointed as auditor`,
                `the copy states the name of the auditor`,
                `the copy states the names of all the auditors`,
                `the auditor is a firm`,
                `the copy states the name of the person who signed it as senior statutory auditor`,
                JUST `the conditions in section 506 for omitting the names are met`,
                `the copy states that a resolution has been passed and notified to the Secretary of State under section 506`

@export Under section 445(6), does the copy of the auditor's report state what the section requires?
GIVEN `more than one person is appointed as auditor` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is more than one person appointed as auditor?
      `the copy states the name of the auditor` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does the copy state the name of the auditor?
      `the copy states the names of all the auditors` IS A BOOLEAN @desc If more than one person is appointed, does the copy state the names of all the auditors?
      `the auditor is a firm` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the auditor a firm?
      `the copy states the name of the person who signed it as senior statutory auditor` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does the copy state the name of the person who signed it as senior statutory auditor?
      `the conditions in section 506 for omitting the names are met` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are the conditions in section 506 for omitting the auditor's names met (a resolution has been passed and notified to the Secretary of State)?
      `the copy states that a resolution has been passed and notified to the Secretary of State under section 506` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does the copy state that a resolution has been passed and notified to the Secretary of State in accordance with section 506?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 445(6), does the copy of the auditor's report state what the section requires` IS
    `s 445(6) the copy of the auditor's report states what the section requires` copy
    WHERE
        copy MEANS
            `s 443A facts about the copy of the auditor's report` OF
                `more than one person is appointed as auditor`,
                `the copy states the name of the auditor`,
                `the copy states the names of all the auditors`,
                `the auditor is a firm`,
                `the copy states the name of the person who signed it as senior statutory auditor`,
                JUST `the conditions in section 506 for omitting the names are met`,
                `the copy states that a resolution has been passed and notified to the Secretary of State under section 506`

@export Under section 447(4), does the copy of the auditor's report state what the section requires?
GIVEN `more than one person is appointed as auditor` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is more than one person appointed as auditor?
      `the copy states the name of the auditor` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does the copy state the name of the auditor?
      `the copy states the names of all the auditors` IS A BOOLEAN @desc If more than one person is appointed, does the copy state the names of all the auditors?
      `the auditor is a firm` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the auditor a firm?
      `the copy states the name of the person who signed it as senior statutory auditor` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does the copy state the name of the person who signed it as senior statutory auditor?
      `the conditions in section 506 for omitting the names are met` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are the conditions in section 506 for omitting the auditor's names met (a resolution has been passed and notified to the Secretary of State)?
      `the copy states that a resolution has been passed and notified to the Secretary of State under section 506` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does the copy state that a resolution has been passed and notified to the Secretary of State in accordance with section 506?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 447(4), does the copy of the auditor's report state what the section requires` IS
    `s 447(4) the copy of the auditor's report states what the section requires` copy
    WHERE
        copy MEANS
            `s 443A facts about the copy of the auditor's report` OF
                `more than one person is appointed as auditor`,
                `the copy states the name of the auditor`,
                `the copy states the names of all the auditors`,
                `the auditor is a firm`,
                `the copy states the name of the person who signed it as senior statutory auditor`,
                JUST `the conditions in section 506 for omitting the names are met`,
                `the copy states that a resolution has been passed and notified to the Secretary of State under section 506`

-- s 444(5) to (5C), first text: what a small company's balance sheet must carry when it files less.
@export Under section 444(5), in the first text of section 444, must the copy of the balance sheet contain a statement that the accounts and reports have been delivered under the small companies regime provisions?
GIVEN `the directors do not deliver a copy of the profit and loss account` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Will the directors not deliver a copy of the company's profit and loss account?
      `the directors do not deliver a copy of the directors' report` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Will the directors not deliver a copy of the directors' report?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 444(5), in the first text of section 444, must the copy of the balance sheet contain a statement that the accounts and reports have been delivered under the small companies regime provisions` IS
    `s 444(5) the section requires the copy of the balance sheet to contain the statement` `the directors do not deliver a copy of the profit and loss account` `the directors do not deliver a copy of the directors' report`

@export Under section 444(5C), in the first text of section 444, does subsection (5A) apply to my company?
GIVEN `the directors do not deliver a copy of the profit and loss account` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Will the directors not deliver a copy of the company's profit and loss account?
      `my company qualifies as a micro-entity for the financial year` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does your company qualify as a micro-entity for the financial year (sections 384A and 384B)?
      `my company's accounts are prepared for that year in accordance with any of the micro-entity provisions` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are the company's accounts prepared for that year in accordance with any of the micro-entity provisions?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 444(5C), in the first text of section 444, does subsection (5A) apply to my company` IS
    `s 444(5C) subsection (5A) applies to the company` `the directors do not deliver a copy of the profit and loss account` (JUST `my company qualifies as a micro-entity for the financial year`) `my company's accounts are prepared for that year in accordance with any of the micro-entity provisions`

@export Under section 444(5B), in the first text of section 444, do the notes to the balance sheet satisfy the requirements of that subsection?
GIVEN `the auditor's report was qualified` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Was the auditor's report qualified?
      `the notes state whether the auditor's report was qualified or unqualified` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Do the notes state whether the auditor's report was qualified or unqualified?
      `the notes disclose the basis of the qualification` IS A BOOLEAN @desc If it was qualified, do the notes disclose the basis of the qualification (reproducing any statement under section 498(2)(a) or (b) or 498(3))?
      `the notes refer to matters the auditor drew attention to by way of emphasis` IS A BOOLEAN @desc If it was unqualified, do the notes include a reference to any matters to which the auditor drew attention by way of emphasis?
      `the notes state the name of the auditor` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Do the notes state the name of the auditor (the names of all the auditors, if more than one)?
      `the auditor is a firm` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the auditor a firm?
      `the notes state the senior statutory auditor` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Do the notes state the name of the person who signed the auditor's report as senior statutory auditor?
      `the conditions in section 506 for omitting the names are met` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are the conditions in section 506 for omitting the auditor's names met?
      `the notes state that a section 506 resolution has been passed and notified` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Do the notes state that a resolution has been passed and notified to the Secretary of State in accordance with section 506?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 444(5B), in the first text of section 444, do the notes to the balance sheet satisfy the requirements of that subsection` IS
    `s 444(5B) the notes to the balance sheet satisfy the requirements`
        `the auditor's report was qualified`
        `the notes state whether the auditor's report was qualified or unqualified`
        `the notes disclose the basis of the qualification`
        `the notes refer to matters the auditor drew attention to by way of emphasis`
        auditor
    WHERE
        -- Placeholders: paragraph (d) reads one name, whether the auditor is a firm, the senior statutory auditor and the section 506 facts; the field for more than one auditor and for all the names are fixed to match the single answer.
        auditor MEANS
            `s 443A facts about the copy of the auditor's report` OF
                FALSE,
                `the notes state the name of the auditor`,
                `the notes state the name of the auditor`,
                `the auditor is a firm`,
                `the notes state the senior statutory auditor`,
                JUST `the conditions in section 506 for omitting the names are met`,
                `the notes state that a section 506 resolution has been passed and notified`

§§ `Exemptions from filing (ss 448 to 448C)`

@export Under section 448(1), does the unlimited company exemption mean the directors of my company are not required to deliver accounts and reports?
GIVEN `my company is an unlimited company` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is your company an unlimited company?
      `at some time during the accounting reference period my company has been, to its knowledge, a subsidiary undertaking of an undertaking which was then limited` IS A BOOLEAN @desc At any time during the relevant accounting reference period, has your company been (to its knowledge) a subsidiary undertaking of an undertaking whose members' liability was then limited?
      `at some time during the accounting reference period two or more undertakings which were then limited had, to its knowledge, rights which would have made my company a subsidiary undertaking` IS A BOOLEAN @desc At any time during that period, were rights exercisable (to its knowledge) by or on behalf of two or more limited undertakings which, if exercisable by one of them, would have made your company a subsidiary undertaking of it?
      `at some time during the accounting reference period my company has been a parent company of an undertaking which was then limited` IS A BOOLEAN @desc At any time during that period, has your company been a parent company of an undertaking whose members' liability was then limited?
      `my company is a banking company` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is your company a banking company (section 1164)?
      `my company is an insurance company` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is your company an insurance company (section 1165)?
      `my company is the parent company of a banking group` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is your company the parent company of a banking group (section 1164)?
      `my company is the parent company of an insurance group` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is your company the parent company of an insurance group (section 1165)?
      `the kinds of the company's members` IS A LIST OF `s 448 kind of member` @desc For each member of the company, which kind is it: a limited company; another unlimited company each of whose members is a limited company; a Scottish partnership that is not a limited partnership each of whose members is a limited company; a Scottish limited partnership each of whose general partners is a limited company; or any other kind? (A comparable undertaking formed outside the United Kingdom counts as the kind it is comparable to.)
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 448(1), does the unlimited company exemption mean the directors of my company are not required to deliver accounts and reports` IS
    `s 448(1) the directors of the unlimited company are not required to deliver accounts and reports`
        `my company is an unlimited company`
        (`s 448(2) the conditions are met`
            (`s 448(2)(a) the condition is met` `at some time during the accounting reference period my company has been, to its knowledge, a subsidiary undertaking of an undertaking which was then limited`)
            (`s 448(2)(b) the condition is met` `at some time during the accounting reference period two or more undertakings which were then limited had, to its knowledge, rights which would have made my company a subsidiary undertaking`)
            (`s 448(2)(c) the condition is met` `at some time during the accounting reference period my company has been a parent company of an undertaking which was then limited`))
        (`s 448(3) the section bars the exemption`
            (`s 448(3)(a) the company is a banking or insurance company or the parent company of a banking or insurance group` `my company is a banking company` `my company is an insurance company` `my company is the parent company of a banking group` `my company is the parent company of an insurance group`)
            (`s 448(3)(b) each of the members of the company is of a kind that paragraph (b) names` `the kinds of the company's members`))

@export Under section 448A(1), does the dormant subsidiaries exemption mean the directors of my company are not required to deliver a copy of the individual accounts?
GIVEN `my company is a subsidiary undertaking` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is your company a subsidiary undertaking?
      `my company has been dormant throughout the whole of the financial year` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has your company been dormant throughout the whole of the financial year (section 1169)?
      `my company's parent undertaking is established under the law of a part of the United Kingdom` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is your company's parent undertaking established under the law of any part of the United Kingdom?
      `all the members of my company agree to the exemption` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Do all the members of your company agree to the exemption for this financial year?
      `the parent undertaking has given a guarantee under section 448C` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has the parent undertaking given a guarantee under section 448C for this year (the directors have delivered its statement to the registrar)?
      `my company is included in the parent's consolidated accounts` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is your company included in the consolidated accounts the parent undertaking draws up for that year, or to an earlier date in that year?
      `those accounts follow the Act, the parent's own law or UK-adopted international accounting standards` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are those consolidated accounts drawn up in accordance with this Part (if the parent is a company), or the legal requirements for the parent undertaking (if it is not), or UK-adopted international accounting standards?
      `the parent undertaking discloses the exemption in the notes to the consolidated accounts` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does the parent undertaking disclose in the notes to the consolidated accounts that your company's directors are exempt from delivering its individual accounts under section 448A?
      `the five documents have been delivered` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Have the directors delivered all five documents to the registrar (the written notice of the members' agreement, the parent's guarantee statement, a copy of the consolidated accounts, a copy of the auditor's report on them and a copy of the consolidated annual report)?
      `the days from the end of the accounting reference period to the last delivery` IS A NUMBER @desc How many days after the end of the accounting reference period was the last of those documents delivered?
      `the days from the end of the accounting reference period to the end of the period for filing` IS A NUMBER @desc How many days after the end of the accounting reference period does the period for filing end? (See section 442.)
      `my company is excluded from the dormant subsidiaries exemption` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is your company within paragraph (b) or (c) of section 448B, so excluded from the dormant subsidiaries exemption (see the section 448B question)? Answer false if it is within neither: the text we hold shows only those two paragraphs, so a company within neither is not shown to be outside the exclusion.
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
-- The five documents of s 448A(2)(e) are asked as one input (all five delivered), which each of that function's five document parameters receives.
-- Limbs (i) and (ii) of s 448A(2)(c) are asked as one input ("follow the Act, the parent's own law or UK-adopted international accounting standards", either suffices), so limb (i) carries the answer and limb (ii) is fixed FALSE.
DECIDE `Under section 448A(1), does the dormant subsidiaries exemption mean the directors of my company are not required to deliver a copy of the individual accounts` IS
    `s 448A(1) the directors of the dormant subsidiary are not required to deliver a copy of the individual accounts`
        `my company is a subsidiary undertaking`
        `my company has been dormant throughout the whole of the financial year`
        `my company's parent undertaking is established under the law of a part of the United Kingdom`
        (`s 448A(2) the conditions for the exemption are complied with`
            `all the members of my company agree to the exemption`
            (`s 448C(1) a guarantee is given by the parent undertaking` `the parent undertaking has given a guarantee under section 448C`)
            (`s 448A(2)(c) the company is included in consolidated accounts drawn up as the paragraph requires` `my company is included in the parent's consolidated accounts` `those accounts follow the Act, the parent's own law or UK-adopted international accounting standards` FALSE)
            `the parent undertaking discloses the exemption in the notes to the consolidated accounts`
            (`s 448A(2)(e) the directors have delivered the documents within the period for filing` `the five documents have been delivered` `the five documents have been delivered` `the five documents have been delivered` `the five documents have been delivered` `the five documents have been delivered` `the days from the end of the accounting reference period to the last delivery` `the days from the end of the accounting reference period to the end of the period for filing`))
        -- Section 448B shows paragraphs (b) and (c) only, so "not within them" is not "not excluded": the seat passes NOTHING (fork F9).
        (IF `my company is excluded from the dormant subsidiaries exemption` THEN JUST TRUE ELSE NOTHING)

@export Under section 448B, is my company excluded from the dormant subsidiaries exemption?
GIVEN `my company is an authorised insurance company` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is your company an authorised insurance company?
      `my company is a banking company` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is your company a banking company?
      `my company is an e-money issuer` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is your company an e-money issuer (an electronic money institution, or a person with permission under Part 4A of the Financial Services and Markets Act 2000 to issue electronic money)?
      `my company is a MiFID investment firm` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is your company a MiFID investment firm?
      `my company is a UCITS management company` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is your company a UCITS management company?
      `my company carries on insurance market activity` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does your company carry on insurance market activity?
      `my company is a special register body` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is your company a special register body as defined in section 117(1) of the Trade Union and Labour Relations (Consolidation) Act 1992?
      `my company is an employers' association` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is your company an employers' association as defined in section 122 of that Act or Article 4 of the Industrial Relations (Northern Ireland) Order 1992?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 448B, is my company excluded from the dormant subsidiaries exemption` IS
    `s 448B the company is excluded from the dormant subsidiaries exemption`
        `my company is an authorised insurance company`
        `my company is a banking company`
        `my company is an e-money issuer`
        `my company is a MiFID investment firm`
        `my company is a UCITS management company`
        `my company carries on insurance market activity`
        (JUST `my company is a special register body`)
        (JUST `my company is an employers' association`)

@export Under section 448C(2), does the parent undertaking's statement meet the requirements of the section?
GIVEN `the statement is authenticated by the parent undertaking` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the statement authenticated by the parent undertaking?
      `the statement gives the name of the parent undertaking` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does the statement give the name of the parent undertaking?
      `the statement gives the registered number of the parent undertaking, if it has one` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does the statement give the registered number of the parent undertaking (if it has one)?
      `the statement gives the name and registered number of the subsidiary company` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does the statement give the name and registered number of the subsidiary company the guarantee is given for?
      `the statement gives its date` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does the statement give its date?
      `the statement gives the financial year to which the guarantee relates` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does the statement give the financial year to which the guarantee relates?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 448C(2), does the parent undertaking's statement meet the requirements of the section` IS
    `s 448C(2) the statement meets the requirements of the section`
        `the statement is authenticated by the parent undertaking`
        `the statement gives the name of the parent undertaking`
        `the statement gives the registered number of the parent undertaking, if it has one`
        `the statement gives the name and registered number of the subsidiary company`
        `the statement gives its date`
        `the statement gives the financial year to which the guarantee relates`

@export Under section 448C(3), if a parent undertaking has given a guarantee under section 448C, how much of the subsidiary company's outstanding liabilities does it still guarantee, in pounds?
GIVEN `the parent undertaking has given a guarantee under section 448C` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has the parent undertaking given a guarantee under section 448C (the directors have delivered its statement to the registrar)?
      `the subsidiary's liabilities at the end of the financial year` IS A NUMBER @desc What were the subsidiary company's liabilities at the end of the financial year to which the guarantee relates, in pounds?
      `the part of them that has been satisfied` IS A NUMBER @desc How much of those liabilities has been satisfied, in pounds?
GIVETH A MAYBE NUMBER
DECIDE `Under section 448C(3), if a parent undertaking has given a guarantee under section 448C, how much of the subsidiary company's outstanding liabilities does it still guarantee, in pounds` IS
    `s 448C(3)(a) the amount of the outstanding liabilities that the parent undertaking still guarantees`
        (`s 448C(1) a guarantee is given by the parent undertaking` `the parent undertaking has given a guarantee under section 448C`)
        `the subsidiary's liabilities at the end of the financial year`
        `the part of them that has been satisfied`

@export Under section 448C(3), may I enforce against a parent undertaking a guarantee under section 448C?
GIVEN `the parent undertaking has given a guarantee under section 448C` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has the parent undertaking given a guarantee under section 448C (the directors have delivered its statement to the registrar)?
      `the subsidiary company is liable to me in respect of liabilities outstanding at the end of the financial year` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the subsidiary company liable to you in respect of liabilities that were outstanding at the end of the financial year to which the guarantee relates?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 448C(3), may I enforce against a parent undertaking a guarantee under section 448C` IS
    `s 448C(3)(b) the person may enforce the guarantee against the parent undertaking`
        (`s 448C(1) a guarantee is given by the parent undertaking` `the parent undertaking has given a guarantee under section 448C`)
        `the subsidiary company is liable to me in respect of liabilities outstanding at the end of the financial year`

§§ `If the accounts and reports are not filed in time (ss 451 to 453)`

@export Under section 451(1), have I committed an offence in relation to the delivery of the company's accounts and reports before the end of the period for filing?
GIVEN `the accounts and reports were delivered before the end of the period for filing` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Were the accounts and reports delivered to the registrar before the end of the period for filing?
      `I was a director of the company immediately before the end of the period for filing` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Were you a director of the company immediately before the end of the period for filing?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 451(1), have I committed an offence in relation to the delivery of the company's accounts and reports before the end of the period for filing` IS
    `s 451(1) the person commits an offence` (JUST `the accounts and reports were delivered before the end of the period for filing`) `I was a director of the company immediately before the end of the period for filing`

@export Under section 451(2), does section 451 give me a defence on these facts?
GIVEN `I prove that I took all reasonable steps for securing that the requirements would be complied with before the end of the period` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Can you prove that you took all reasonable steps for securing that the accounts and reports would be delivered before the end of the period for filing?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 451(2), does section 451 give me a defence on these facts` IS
    `s 451(2) this section gives the person a defence on these facts` `I prove that I took all reasonable steps for securing that the requirements would be complied with before the end of the period`

@export Under section 451(3), is it a defence to the offence to prove that the documents were not in fact prepared as the Act requires?
GIVEN `I prove that the documents were not in fact prepared as required by Part 15` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Can you prove that the documents were not in fact prepared as Part 15 requires?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 451(3), is it a defence to the offence to prove that the documents were not in fact prepared as the Act requires` IS
    `s 451(3) proving that the documents were not prepared as required is a defence to the offence` `I prove that the documents were not in fact prepared as required by Part 15`

@export Under section 451(4), am I guilty of an offence under section 451?
GIVEN `the accounts and reports were delivered before the end of the period for filing` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Were the accounts and reports delivered to the registrar before the end of the period for filing?
      `I was a director of the company immediately before the end of the period for filing` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Were you a director of the company immediately before the end of the period for filing?
      `I prove that I took all reasonable steps for securing that the requirements would be complied with before the end of the period` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Can you prove that you took all reasonable steps for securing that the accounts and reports would be delivered before the end of the period for filing?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 451(4), am I guilty of an offence under section 451` IS
    `s 451(4) the person is guilty of an offence under section 451`
        (`s 451(1) the person commits an offence` (JUST `the accounts and reports were delivered before the end of the period for filing`) `I was a director of the company immediately before the end of the period for filing`)
        (`s 451(2) this section gives the person a defence on these facts` `I prove that I took all reasonable steps for securing that the requirements would be complied with before the end of the period`)

@export Under section 451(4), what is the greatest fine on summary conviction for the offence, in pounds?
GIVEN `the amount of level 5 on the standard scale in pounds` IS A NUMBER @desc How many pounds is level 5 on the standard scale? (The Act does not say; it is fixed elsewhere.)
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `Under section 451(4), what is the greatest fine on summary conviction for the offence, in pounds` IS
    `s 451(4) the greatest fine on summary conviction in pounds` `the amount of level 5 on the standard scale in pounds`

@export Under section 451(4), what is the greatest daily default fine for continued contravention, in pounds?
GIVEN `which text of section 451(4) you rely on` IS A `s 441 text of the sections the file prints twice` @desc The Act as we hold it prints two daily default fines in section 451(4): the first text says one-tenth of level 5, the second one-tenth of the greater of 5,000 pounds and level 4. Which do you rely on?
      `the amount of level 4 on the standard scale in pounds` IS A NUMBER @desc How many pounds is level 4 on the standard scale? (The Act does not say; it is fixed elsewhere.)
      `the amount of level 5 on the standard scale in pounds` IS A NUMBER @desc How many pounds is level 5 on the standard scale? (The Act does not say; it is fixed elsewhere.)
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `Under section 451(4), what is the greatest daily default fine for continued contravention, in pounds` IS
    `s 451(4) the greatest daily default fine in pounds` `which text of section 451(4) you rely on` `the amount of level 4 on the standard scale in pounds` `the amount of level 5 on the standard scale in pounds`

@export Under section 452(1), may the court order the directors to make good a default in filing the accounts and reports?
GIVEN `the accounts and reports were delivered before the end of the period for filing` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Were the accounts and reports delivered to the registrar before the end of the period for filing?
      `the date the notice requiring compliance was served on the directors` IS A DATE @desc On what date was a notice requiring the directors to comply served on them?
      `the default has been made good` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has the default been made good (the accounts and reports delivered)?
      `the date it was made good` IS A DATE @desc If so, on what date? (Give any date if it has not been.)
      `the day on which you ask` IS A DATE @desc What is today's date?
      `the applicant is a member or creditor of the company or the registrar` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the person applying to the court a member or creditor of the company, or the registrar?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 452(1), may the court order the directors to make good a default in filing the accounts and reports` IS
    `s 452(1) the court may order the directors to make good the default`
        (JUST `the accounts and reports were delivered before the end of the period for filing`)
        (`s 452(1)(b) the directors failed to make good the default within 14 days after the service of the notice`
            `the date the notice requiring compliance was served on the directors`
            (IF `the default has been made good` THEN JUST `the date it was made good` ELSE NOTHING)
            `the day on which you ask`)
        `the applicant is a member or creditor of the company or the registrar`

@export Under section 452(2), if the court makes an order under section 452(1), may the order provide that the costs are borne by the directors?
GIVEN `the court makes an order under section 452(1)` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has the court made an order under section 452(1) directing the directors to make good the default?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 452(2), if the court makes an order under section 452(1), may the order provide that the costs are borne by the directors` IS
    `s 452(2) the court's order may provide that all the costs are borne by the directors` `the court makes an order under section 452(1)`

@export Under section 453(1), is the company liable to a civil penalty for filing late?
GIVEN `the accounts and reports were delivered before the end of the period for filing` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Were the accounts and reports delivered to the registrar before the end of the period for filing?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 453(1), is the company liable to a civil penalty for filing late` IS
    `s 453(1) the company is liable to a civil penalty` (JUST `the accounts and reports were delivered before the end of the period for filing`)

@export Under section 453(2), how many days after the end of the period for filing were the accounts and reports delivered, for the civil penalty?
GIVEN `the day on which the period for filing ended` IS A DATE @desc On what date did the period for filing end?
      `the day on which the requirements were complied with` IS A DATE @desc On what date were the accounts and reports delivered?
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `Under section 453(2), how many days after the end of the period for filing were the accounts and reports delivered, for the civil penalty` IS
    `s 453(2)(a) the number of days between the end of the period for filing and the day on which the requirements are complied with` `the day on which the period for filing ended` `the day on which the requirements were complied with`

@export Under section 453(2), if the company is liable to a civil penalty, what is its amount, in pounds?
GIVEN `the accounts and reports were delivered before the end of the period for filing` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Were the accounts and reports delivered to the registrar before the end of the period for filing?
      `the penalty the regulations fix for this company and this delay` IS A NUMBER @desc What penalty, in pounds, do the Secretary of State's regulations fix for a company of this kind (private or public) that is this many days late? (The Act leaves the amount to those regulations.)
GIVETH A MAYBE NUMBER
DECIDE `Under section 453(2), if the company is liable to a civil penalty, what is its amount, in pounds` IS
    `s 453(2) the amount of the civil penalty` (`s 453(1) the company is liable to a civil penalty` (JUST `the accounts and reports were delivered before the end of the period for filing`)) `the penalty the regulations fix for this company and this delay`

@export Under section 453(3), may the registrar recover a civil penalty under section 453 from the company?
GIVEN `the accounts and reports were delivered before the end of the period for filing` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Were the accounts and reports delivered to the registrar before the end of the period for filing?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 453(3), may the registrar recover a civil penalty under section 453 from the company` IS
    `s 453(3) the registrar may recover the penalty from the company` (`s 453(1) the company is liable to a civil penalty` (JUST `the accounts and reports were delivered before the end of the period for filing`))

@export Under section 453(4), is it a defence to the civil penalty to prove that the documents were not in fact prepared as the Act requires?
GIVEN `the company proves that the documents were not in fact prepared as required by Part 15` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Can the company prove that the documents were not in fact prepared as Part 15 requires?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 453(4), is it a defence to the civil penalty to prove that the documents were not in fact prepared as the Act requires` IS
    `s 453(4) proving that the documents were not prepared as required is a defence to the civil penalty` `the company proves that the documents were not in fact prepared as required by Part 15`

§ `Companies Act 2006, Part 15, Chapter 11 -- revision of defective accounts and reports`

§§ `Voluntary revision and the Secretary of State's notice (ss 454 and 455)`

@export Under section 454(1), may the directors prepare revised accounts or a revised report or statement?
