      `it appears to the directors that the document did not comply with the requirements of the Act` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does it appear to the directors that the document did not comply with the requirements of the Act?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 454(1), may the directors prepare revised accounts or a revised report or statement` IS
    `s 454(1) the directors may prepare revised accounts or a revised report or statement` `the document` `it appears to the directors that the document did not comply with the requirements of the Act`

@export Under section 454(2), are the revisions I am making confined to the correction of the respects in which the previous accounts or report did not comply and necessary consequential alterations?
GIVEN `copies have been sent out to members` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Have copies of the previous accounts or report been sent out to members?
      `a copy has been delivered to the registrar` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has a copy been delivered to the registrar?
      `my company is a public company` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is your company a public company?
      `the previous accounts or report have been laid before the company in general meeting` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Have the previous accounts or report been laid before the company in general meeting?
      `the revisions are only the correction of what did not comply and necessary consequential alterations` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Do the revisions consist only of the correction of the respects in which the previous accounts or report did not comply with the Act, and any necessary consequential alterations?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 454(2), are the revisions I am making confined to the correction of the respects in which the previous accounts or report did not comply and necessary consequential alterations` IS
    `s 454(2) the revision is within the limit the section sets`
        (`s 454(2) the revisions are confined to correction and consequential alterations` `copies have been sent out to members` `a copy has been delivered to the registrar` `my company is a public company` `the previous accounts or report have been laid before the company in general meeting`)
        `the revisions are only the correction of what did not comply and necessary consequential alterations`

@export Under section 455(1), does section 455 apply to the company's accounts or report?
GIVEN `copies have been sent out under section 423` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Have copies of the company's annual accounts, strategic report or directors' report been sent out under section 423?
      `a copy has been delivered to the registrar or laid before the company in general meeting` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has a copy of the company's annual accounts, strategic report or directors' report been delivered to the registrar or (for a public company) laid before the company in general meeting?
      `it appears to the Secretary of State that there is, or may be, a question` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does it appear to the Secretary of State that there is, or may be, a question whether the accounts or report comply with the requirements of the Act?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 455(1), does section 455 apply to the company's accounts or report` IS
    `s 455(1) section 455 applies` `copies have been sent out under section 423` `a copy has been delivered to the registrar or laid before the company in general meeting` `it appears to the Secretary of State that there is, or may be, a question`

@export Under section 455(3), does the notice specify a period of not less than one month for the directors?
GIVEN `the date of the notice` IS A DATE @desc What is the date of the Secretary of State's notice?
      `the last day of the period the notice specifies` IS A DATE @desc What is the last day of the period the notice gives the directors to explain the accounts or report or to prepare revised ones?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 455(3), does the notice specify a period of not less than one month for the directors` IS
    `s 455(3) the period the notice specifies is not less than one month` `the date of the notice` `the last day of the period the notice specifies`

@export Under section 455(4), may the Secretary of State apply to the court?
