GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 463(4), is a person subject to liability to someone other than the company for relying on the information in a report or statement` IS
    `s 463(4) a person is subject to liability to the claimant` (`s 463(1) the section applies to the report or statement` `the document`) `the claimant is a person other than the company` `the liability results from reliance on information in the report or statement`

@export Under section 463(6), does section 463 affect this other liability?
GIVEN `the other liability` IS A `s 463 kind of other liability` @desc Which liability: liability for a civil penalty, liability for a criminal offence, or any other liability?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 463(6), does section 463 affect this other liability` IS
    `s 463(6) the section affects the liability` `the other liability`

§§ `Medium-sized companies (ss 465 to 467)`

@export Under section 465(3), are the qualifying conditions for a medium-sized company met in the year?
GIVEN `the company's turnover in the year in pounds` IS A NUMBER @desc What was the company's turnover for the financial year, in pounds?
      `the length of the financial year in months` IS A NUMBER @desc How many months long was the financial year? (12 for a full year; the turnover limit is adjusted in proportion for a shorter or longer year.)
      `the company's balance sheet total in pounds` IS A NUMBER @desc What is the company's balance sheet total (the aggregate of the amounts shown as assets in its balance sheet), in pounds?
      `the company's average number of employees` IS A NUMBER @desc What was the average number of persons employed under contracts of service by the company in the year (the total of each month's number, divided by the number of months)?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 465(3), are the qualifying conditions for a medium-sized company met in the year` IS
    `s 465(3) the qualifying conditions are met` `the company's turnover in the year in pounds` `the length of the financial year in months` `the company's balance sheet total in pounds` `the company's average number of employees`

@export Under section 465(5), what is the company's balance sheet total, in pounds?
GIVEN `the amounts shown as assets in the balance sheet in pounds` IS A LIST OF NUMBER @desc List the amounts shown as assets in the company's balance sheet, in pounds, one per item.
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `Under section 465(5), what is the company's balance sheet total, in pounds` IS
    `s 465(5) the balance sheet total` `the amounts shown as assets in the balance sheet in pounds`

@export Under section 465(6), what is the company's number of employees?
GIVEN `the number of persons employed in each month of the financial year` IS A LIST OF NUMBER @desc For each month of the financial year, give the number of persons employed under contracts of service by the company in that month (whether throughout the month or not), one number per month.
GIVETH A MAYBE NUMBER
DECIDE `Under section 465(6), what is the company's number of employees` IS
    `s 465(6) the number of employees` `the number of persons employed in each month of the financial year`

@export Under section 465(1), does the company qualify as medium-sized in its first financial year?
GIVEN `the qualifying conditions are met in that year` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are the qualifying conditions for a medium-sized company met in the company's first financial year (two or more of: turnover not more than 54 million pounds, balance sheet total not more than 27 million pounds, not more than 250 employees)?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 465(1), does the company qualify as medium-sized in its first financial year` IS
    `s 465(1) the company qualifies as medium-sized in relation to its first financial year` `the qualifying conditions are met in that year`

@export Under section 465(2), does the company qualify as medium-sized in a later financial year?
GIVEN `the qualifying conditions are met in this year` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are the qualifying conditions for a medium-sized company met in this financial year?
      `the qualifying conditions were met in the preceding year` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Were the qualifying conditions met in the preceding financial year?
      `the company qualified as medium-sized in the preceding year` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did the company qualify as medium-sized in relation to the preceding financial year?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 465(2), does the company qualify as medium-sized in a later financial year` IS
    `s 465(2) the company qualifies as medium-sized in relation to a subsequent financial year` `the qualifying conditions are met in this year` `the qualifying conditions were met in the preceding year` `the company qualified as medium-sized in the preceding year`

@export Under section 465(7), does the company qualify as medium-sized, taking account of section 466 if it is a parent company?
GIVEN `the company's own answer under section 465(1) or (2)` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does the company qualify as medium-sized under section 465(1) or (2) (see the section 465 questions)?
      `the company is a parent company` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the company a parent company?
      `the group headed by it qualifies as a medium-sized group` IS A BOOLEAN @desc If it is a parent company, does the group headed by it qualify as a medium-sized group (see the section 466 questions)? (Give any answer if it is not a parent company.)
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 465(7), does the company qualify as medium-sized, taking account of section 466 if it is a parent company` IS
    `s 465(7) the company qualifies as medium-sized, subject to section 466` (JUST `the company's own answer under section 465(1) or (2)`) (JUST `the company is a parent company`) (JUST `the group headed by it qualifies as a medium-sized group`)

@export Under section 466(4), are the qualifying conditions for a medium-sized group met in the year?
GIVEN `the group's aggregate turnover, net, in pounds` IS A NUMBER @desc What is the group's aggregate turnover for the year after set-offs and other adjustments made to eliminate group transactions (net), in pounds?
      `the group's aggregate turnover, gross, in pounds` IS A NUMBER @desc What is the group's aggregate turnover without those set-offs and adjustments (gross), in pounds?
      `the group's aggregate balance sheet total, net, in pounds` IS A NUMBER @desc What is the group's aggregate balance sheet total, net, in pounds?
      `the group's aggregate balance sheet total, gross, in pounds` IS A NUMBER @desc What is the group's aggregate balance sheet total, gross, in pounds?
      `the group's aggregate number of employees` IS A NUMBER @desc What is the group's aggregate number of employees?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 466(4), are the qualifying conditions for a medium-sized group met in the year` IS
    `s 466(4) the qualifying conditions are met by the group` `the group's aggregate turnover, net, in pounds` `the group's aggregate turnover, gross, in pounds` `the group's aggregate balance sheet total, net, in pounds` `the group's aggregate balance sheet total, gross, in pounds` `the group's aggregate number of employees`

@export Under section 466(7), on what date does the financial year of the subsidiary undertaking whose figures are used end?
GIVEN `the end of the parent company's financial year` IS A DATE @desc On what date does the parent company's financial year end?
      `the ends of the subsidiary undertaking's financial years` IS A LIST OF DATE @desc List the dates on which the subsidiary undertaking's financial years end.
GIVETH A MAYBE DATE
DECIDE `Under section 466(7), on what date does the financial year of the subsidiary undertaking whose figures are used end` IS
    `s 466(7) the end of the subsidiary undertaking's financial year whose figures are used` `the end of the parent company's financial year` `the ends of the subsidiary undertaking's financial years`

@export Under section 466(3), does the group qualify as medium-sized in a later financial year of the parent company?
GIVEN `the qualifying conditions are met in this year` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are the qualifying conditions for a medium-sized group met in this financial year of the parent company?
      `the qualifying conditions were met in the preceding year` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Were the qualifying conditions met in the preceding financial year?
      `the group qualified as medium-sized in the preceding year` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did the group qualify as medium-sized in relation to the preceding financial year?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 466(3), does the group qualify as medium-sized in a later financial year of the parent company` IS
    `s 466(3) the group qualifies as medium-sized in relation to a subsequent financial year` `the qualifying conditions are met in this year` `the qualifying conditions were met in the preceding year` `the group qualified as medium-sized in the preceding year`

@export Under section 467(1), is the company barred from taking advantage of the medium-sized provisions?
GIVEN `the company was at some time within the financial year a public company` IS A BOOLEAN @desc At any time within the financial year in question, was the company a public company?
      `the company was at some time within the year a company with permission under Part 4A of the Financial Services and Markets Act 2000 to carry on a regulated activity` IS A BOOLEAN @desc At any time within that year, did the company have permission under Part 4A of the Financial Services and Markets Act 2000 to carry on a regulated activity?
      `the company carried on insurance market activity at some time within the year` IS A BOOLEAN @desc At any time within that year, did the company carry on insurance market activity?
      `the company was a Master Trust scheme funder at some time within the year` IS A BOOLEAN @desc At any time within that year, was the company a scheme funder of a Master Trust scheme (section 39(1) of the Pension Schemes Act 2017 or of the Pension Schemes Act (Northern Ireland) 2021)?
      `the company was an e-money issuer at some time within the year` IS A BOOLEAN @desc At any time within that year, was the company an e-money issuer?
      `the company's group is ineligible` IS A BOOLEAN @desc At any time within that year, was the company a member of an ineligible group (see the section 467(2) question)?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 467(1), is the company barred from taking advantage of the medium-sized provisions` IS
    `s 467(1) the section bars the company from taking advantage of the medium-sized provisions`
        `the company was at some time within the financial year a public company`
        `the company was at some time within the year a company with permission under Part 4A of the Financial Services and Markets Act 2000 to carry on a regulated activity`
        `the company carried on insurance market activity at some time within the year`
        `the company was a Master Trust scheme funder at some time within the year`
        `the company was an e-money issuer at some time within the year`
        (JUST `the company's group is ineligible`)

@export Under section 467(2), is the group ineligible because of one of its members?
GIVEN `a member is a traded company` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the member you describe a traded company? (Describe one member of the group and ask again for each of the others: the group is ineligible if any one of them is within the section.)
      `a member is a body corporate other than a company whose shares are admitted to trading on a UK regulated market` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is that member a body corporate (other than a company) whose shares are admitted to trading on a UK regulated market?
      `a member has permission under Part 4A of the Financial Services and Markets Act 2000` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does that member have permission under Part 4A of the Financial Services and Markets Act 2000 to carry on a regulated activity?
      `a member is a small company for the purposes of section 467(2)` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is that member a small company for the purposes of section 467(2), that is, did it qualify as small in relation to its last financial year ending on or before the end of the financial year in question (section 467(3))?
      `a member is an e-money issuer` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is that member an e-money issuer?
      `a member is an authorised insurance company, a banking company, a MiFID investment firm or a UCITS management company` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is that member an authorised insurance company, a banking company, a MiFID investment firm or a UCITS management company?
      `a member carries on insurance market activity` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does that member carry on insurance market activity?
      `a member is a Master Trust scheme funder` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is that member a scheme funder of a Master Trust scheme?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 467(2), is the group ineligible because of one of its members` IS
    `s 467(2) the group is ineligible` (LIST one)
    WHERE
        -- One record stands for the member: each paragraph of section 467(2) is stated for "any of its members".
        one MEANS
            `s 467 member of a group` OF
                `a member is a traded company`,
                `a member is a body corporate other than a company whose shares are admitted to trading on a UK regulated market`,
                `a member has permission under Part 4A of the Financial Services and Markets Act 2000`,
                JUST `a member is a small company for the purposes of section 467(2)`,
                `a member is an e-money issuer`,
                `a member is an authorised insurance company, a banking company, a MiFID investment firm or a UCITS management company`,
                `a member carries on insurance market activity`,
                `a member is a Master Trust scheme funder`

@export Under section 467(4), does section 467 prevent the company taking advantage of section 417(7) by reason only of membership of an ineligible group?
GIVEN `the only reason is that the company was a member of an ineligible group` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the only reason the company might be prevented from taking advantage of section 417(7) that it was a member of an ineligible group at some time within the financial year?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 467(4), does section 467 prevent the company taking advantage of section 417(7) by reason only of membership of an ineligible group` IS
    `s 467(4) the section prevents the company from taking advantage of section 417(7)` `the only reason is that the company was a member of an ineligible group`

§§ `Accounts in euros (s 469)`

@export Under section 469(3), does the translation of the accounts into euros meet the requirements of the section?
GIVEN `the amounts were translated at the rate prevailing on the date to which the balance sheet is made up` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Were the amounts translated at the exchange rate prevailing on the date to which the balance sheet is made up?
      `the rate is disclosed in the notes to the accounts` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is that rate disclosed in the notes to the accounts?
      `these are the Companies Act individual accounts of a company that qualifies as a micro-entity` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are these the Companies Act individual accounts of a company that qualifies as a micro-entity for the financial year (sections 384A and 384B)?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 469(3), does the translation of the accounts into euros meet the requirements of the section` IS
    `s 469(3) the translation meets the requirements of the section` `the amounts were translated at the rate prevailing on the date to which the balance sheet is made up` `the rate is disclosed in the notes to the accounts` `these are the Companies Act individual accounts of a company that qualifies as a micro-entity`

@export Under section 469(2), may the directors deliver an additional copy of the annual accounts in euros to the registrar?
GIVEN `the directors are complying with section 441` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are the directors delivering accounts and reports to the registrar to comply with section 441?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 469(2), may the directors deliver an additional copy of the annual accounts in euros to the registrar` IS
    `s 469(2) the directors may deliver to the registrar an additional copy of the annual accounts translated into euros` `the directors are complying with section 441`

§§ `Meaning of "annual accounts" and the minor definitions (ss 464, 471, 472A, 474)`

@export Under section 471(2), is this document among the annual accounts and reports of an unquoted company?
GIVEN `the document` IS A `s 471 item` @desc Which document: the annual accounts, the strategic report, the directors' report, the directors' remuneration report, or the auditor's report?
      `the company has a strategic report` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does the company have a strategic report for the year?
      `the company is exempt from audit` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the company exempt from audit?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 471(2), is this document among the annual accounts and reports of an unquoted company` IS
    `s 471(2) the item is among the annual accounts and reports of the unquoted company` `the document` `the company has a strategic report` `the company is exempt from audit`

@export Under section 471(3), is this document among the annual accounts and reports of a quoted company?
GIVEN `the document` IS A `s 471 item` @desc Which document: the annual accounts, the strategic report, the directors' report, the directors' remuneration report, or the auditor's report?
      `the company has a strategic report` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does the company have a strategic report for the year?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 471(3), is this document among the annual accounts and reports of a quoted company` IS
    `s 471(3) the item is among the annual accounts and reports of the quoted company` `the document` `the company has a strategic report`

@export Under section 474(1), what is the turnover of the company, in pounds?
GIVEN `the amounts derived from the provision of goods and services in pounds` IS A NUMBER @desc What are the amounts the company derived from the provision of goods and services, in pounds?
      `trade discounts in pounds` IS A NUMBER @desc How much were the trade discounts, in pounds?
      `value added tax in pounds` IS A NUMBER @desc How much was the value added tax, in pounds?
      `any other taxes based on those amounts in pounds` IS A NUMBER @desc How much were any other taxes based on the amounts so derived, in pounds?
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `Under section 474(1), what is the turnover of the company, in pounds` IS
    `s 474(1) the turnover of the company` `the amounts derived from the provision of goods and services in pounds` `trade discounts in pounds` `value added tax in pounds` `any other taxes based on those amounts in pounds`

@export Under section 474(1), is the company a traded company?
GIVEN `the context otherwise requires` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does the context in which the term appears otherwise require a different meaning of "traded company"?
      `any of the company's transferable securities are admitted to trading on a UK regulated market` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are any of the company's transferable securities admitted to trading on a UK regulated market?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 474(1), is the company a traded company` IS
    `s 474(1) the company is a traded company` `the context otherwise requires` `any of the company's transferable securities are admitted to trading on a UK regulated market`

@export Under section 474(1), is the auditor's report qualified?
GIVEN `the report states the auditor's unqualified opinion that the accounts have been properly prepared in accordance with the Act` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does the auditor's report state the auditor's unqualified opinion that the accounts have been properly prepared in accordance with the Companies Act 2006?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 474(1), is the auditor's report qualified` IS
    `s 474(1) the auditor's report is qualified` `the report states the auditor's unqualified opinion that the accounts have been properly prepared in accordance with the Act`

@export Under section 474(1), is the person an e-money issuer?
GIVEN `the person is an electronic money institution within the meaning of the Electronic Money Regulations 2011` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the person an electronic money institution within the meaning of the Electronic Money Regulations 2011?
      `the person has permission under Part 4A of the Financial Services and Markets Act 2000 to issue electronic money` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does the person have permission under Part 4A of the Financial Services and Markets Act 2000 to carry on the activity of issuing electronic money?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 474(1), is the person an e-money issuer` IS
    `s 474(1) the person is an e-money issuer` `the person is an electronic money institution within the meaning of the Electronic Money Regulations 2011` `the person has permission under Part 4A of the Financial Services and Markets Act 2000 to issue electronic money`

@export Under section 474(1), is the person a MiFID investment firm?
GIVEN `the person is an investment firm within the meaning of Article 2.1A of Regulation (EU) No. 600/2014` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the person an investment firm within the meaning of Article 2.1A of Regulation (EU) No. 600/2014?
      `the person is exempted from the definition of investment firm by Schedule 3 to the Regulated Activities Order` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the person a company exempted from the definition of "investment firm" by Schedule 3 to the Financial Services and Markets Act 2000 (Regulated Activities) Order 2001?
      `the person is an exempt investment firm under regulation 8 of the 2017 Regulations` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the person an exempt investment firm as defined by regulation 8 of the Financial Services and Markets Act 2000 (Markets in Financial Instruments) Regulations 2017?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 474(1), is the person a MiFID investment firm` IS
    `s 474(1) the person is a MiFID investment firm` `the person is an investment firm within the meaning of Article 2.1A of Regulation (EU) No. 600/2014` `the person is exempted from the definition of investment firm by Schedule 3 to the Regulated Activities Order` `the person is an exempt investment firm under regulation 8 of the 2017 Regulations`

@export Under section 464(1), is this statement an accounting standard?
GIVEN `the statement is a statement of standard accounting practice` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it a statement of standard accounting practice?
      `the body that issued it is prescribed by regulations` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Was it issued by a body prescribed by regulations for this purpose?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 464(1), is this statement an accounting standard` IS
    `s 464(1) the statement is an accounting standard` `the statement is a statement of standard accounting practice` (JUST `the body that issued it is prescribed by regulations`)

@export Under section 472A(3), is this a separate corporate governance statement?
GIVEN `the statement is the statement required by rules 7.2.1 to 7.2.11 of the Disclosure Rules and Transparency Rules sourcebook` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it the corporate governance statement required by rules 7.2.1 to 7.2.11 in the Disclosure Rules and Transparency Rules sourcebook made by the Financial Conduct Authority?
      `the statement is included in the directors' report` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the statement included in the directors' report?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 472A(3), is this a separate corporate governance statement` IS
    `s 472A(3) the statement is a separate corporate governance statement` (`s 472A(1) the statement is a corporate governance statement` `the statement is the statement required by rules 7.2.1 to 7.2.11 of the Disclosure Rules and Transparency Rules sourcebook`) `the statement is included in the directors' report`

@export Under section 474(1), is this activity a regulated activity for the purposes of Part 15?
GIVEN `the activity is a regulated activity within section 22 of the Financial Services and Markets Act 2000` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the activity a regulated activity within section 22 of the Financial Services and Markets Act 2000?
      `the kind of activity` IS A `s 474 kind of activity` @desc Which kind of activity is it: one of the kinds Part 15 leaves out (arranging or advising on regulated mortgage contracts, home reversion plans, home purchase plans or sale and rent back agreements; assisting administration of a contract of insurance; dealing as agent, arranging deals, advising on investments and the like; agreeing to carry on one of those), or another kind?
      `it concerns relevant investments that are not contractually based investments` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does the activity concern relevant investments that are not contractually based investments (within the meaning of article 3 of that Order)?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 474(1), is this activity a regulated activity for the purposes of Part 15` IS
    `s 474(1) the activity is a regulated activity for the purposes of this Part` (JUST `the activity is a regulated activity within section 22 of the Financial Services and Markets Act 2000`) `the kind of activity` `it concerns relevant investments that are not contractually based investments`

-- ====================================================================================================
-- seat questions from part coa11 (merged by the lead on 2026-11-12; unchanged text follows)
-- ====================================================================================================
-- coa11-seat.l4: Companies Act 2006 (United Kingdom), Part 16 (Audit), Chapters 1 and 2, ss 475 to 494A: THE SEAT LAYER.
--
-- SEAT: an individual who is, or is about to become, a director, a company secretary or a member (shareholder) of a company
-- registered under the Act, or who deals with one, asking on facts they can state what the Act requires or lets them do, what
-- rights they have against the company or its directors, what they must disclose, file, approve or vote on and by when, and what
-- follows (liability, offences, penalties) if it is not done.  (Assumed, not ruled: the Act is addressed to companies, so the
-- individual is whoever stands in a company's management or ownership.)
--
-- This layer asks the questions Part 16 Chapters 1 and 2 answer for that person: must my company's accounts be audited and does
-- an exemption apply, may the members force an audit, who may appoint the auditor and by when, what a public interest entity
-- must do, what happens if it does not, and when an auditor's term ends.  Nothing here is new law: every question builds the
-- layer-1 inputs from plain facts and calls the layer-1 rule; no rule is restated.  A fact the layer-1 function does not read
-- is given a fixed placeholder with a comment.
--
-- HOW TO READ AN ANSWER.  A question answers MAYBE BOOLEAN (or a date, a number, or a named "not covered" value):
-- JUST TRUE = the answer the question's own words ask for; JUST FALSE = the text says no on these facts, in its own
-- words; NOTHING = not covered by the text (it is silent, lists without closing the list, points to a definition outside the
-- sources, or limits its own grant and the facts fall outside the limit).  A "no" is never a "not covered", and a caller must
-- never turn NOTHING into FALSE.  Every question is named for what its body answers, in the same direction: a question about
-- a bar ("is my company barred ...") returns JUST TRUE for barred, a question about an entitlement returns JUST TRUE for
-- entitled.  See NOTES.md, "Reading a result: FALSE and NOTHING".
--
-- AMOUNTS AND PERCENTAGES.  A percentage is asked as a percentage (10 means 10%) and divided by 100 here.  The pounds that
-- "level 3 on the standard scale" stands for are not in the Act: they are asked.  A day is a date.
--
-- Questions that arise only in a situation the person may not be in (the group questions, the public interest entity questions,
-- the default power of the Secretary of State, the deemed re-appointment of an auditor, the members' notice) say so in the
-- comment above their heading, so that a form can ask "has this happened to you?" first.

DECLARE `coa11 seat answer` IS ONE OF
    `coa11 seat yes`
    `coa11 seat no`
    `coa11 seat not sure`

GIVEN answer IS A `coa11 seat answer`
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`coa11 seat the answer given as an answer of the text` MEANS
    CONSIDER answer
    WHEN `coa11 seat yes` THEN JUST TRUE
    WHEN `coa11 seat no` THEN JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): the answer given is the answer of the section's own question
    WHEN `coa11 seat not sure` THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (silent): the person is not sure, so the question is not answered

-- Section 475(2) is printed twice in the text with different words (NOTES.md, finding 1 and fork F2): the seat gives an
-- answer only where the two printed versions agree.
GIVEN one IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
      other IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`coa11 seat the answer where the two printed versions of section 475(2) agree` MEANS
    IF one EQUALS other
    THEN one
    ELSE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (silent): the text prints two versions of section 475(2) and does not say which is in force

-- The first printed version asks for "a statement by the directors to that effect": taken as a statement that confirms the
-- company qualifies for the exemption.
GIVEN `the statement identifies the exemption in question` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the statement confirms that the company qualifies for the exemption` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`coa11 seat section 475(2) bar` MEANS
    `coa11 seat the answer where the two printed versions of section 475(2) agree`
        (`s 475(2) (first printed version) the company is barred from the exemption for want of the directors' statement` `the statement confirms that the company qualifies for the exemption`)
        (`s 475(2) (second printed version) the company is barred from the exemption for want of the directors' statement` `the statement identifies the exemption in question` `the statement confirms that the company qualifies for the exemption`)

-- The statements the directors must make, and the notice the members may give, are asked in the same words by every
-- exemption question below.

§ `Companies Act 2006, Part 16 Chapters 1 and 2 -- the questions of a director, secretary or member (ss 475 to 494A)`

§§ `Section 475: must my company's accounts be audited, and what must its balance sheet say`

-- Ask this after the exemption questions below: it gathers their answers, as section 475(1) does ("unless the company is exempt").
@export Under section 475(1), must my company's annual accounts for the year be audited?
GIVEN `my company is exempt from audit under section 477 (small companies)` IS A `coa11 seat answer` @desc Is your company entitled to the small companies exemption from audit for the year (answer of the section 477 question): yes, no, or not sure?
      `my company is exempt from audit under section 479A (subsidiary companies)` IS A `coa11 seat answer` @desc Is your company entitled to the subsidiary companies exemption from audit for the year (answer of the section 479A question): yes, no, or not sure?
      `my company is exempt from audit under section 480 (dormant companies)` IS A `coa11 seat answer` @desc Is your company entitled to the dormant companies exemption from audit for the year (answer of the section 480 question): yes, no, or not sure?
      `my company is exempt from the audit requirements under section 482 (public sector audit)` IS A `coa11 seat answer` @desc Is your company, being non-profit-making and subject to public sector audit, exempt under section 482 (answer of the section 482 question): yes, no, or not sure?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 475(1), must my company's annual accounts for the year be audited` IS
    `s 475(1) the company's annual accounts for the financial year must be audited in accordance with Part 16`
        (`coa11 seat the answer given as an answer of the text` `my company is exempt from audit under section 477 (small companies)`)
        (`coa11 seat the answer given as an answer of the text` `my company is exempt from audit under section 479A (subsidiary companies)`)
        (`coa11 seat the answer given as an answer of the text` `my company is exempt from audit under section 480 (dormant companies)`)
        (`coa11 seat the answer given as an answer of the text` `my company is exempt from the audit requirements under section 482 (public sector audit)`)

@export Under section 475(2), is my company barred from an audit exemption for want of the directors' statement on the balance sheet?
GIVEN `the balance sheet's statement identifies the exemption in question` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does the directors' statement on your company's balance sheet identify the exemption the company relies on?
      `the balance sheet's statement confirms that the company qualifies for the exemption` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does the directors' statement on your company's balance sheet confirm that the company qualifies for that exemption?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 475(2), is my company barred from an audit exemption for want of the directors' statement on the balance sheet` IS
    `coa11 seat section 475(2) bar` `the balance sheet's statement identifies the exemption in question` `the balance sheet's statement confirms that the company qualifies for the exemption`

@export Under section 475(3), is my company barred from an audit exemption for want of the directors' statements about the members' right and the directors' responsibilities?
GIVEN exemption IS A `s 475 exemption` @desc Which exemption does your company rely on: section 477 (small companies), 479A (subsidiary companies), 480 (dormant companies) or 482 (public sector audit)?
      `the statement says the members have not required an audit under section 476` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does the directors' statement on the balance sheet say that the members have not required the company to obtain an audit of its accounts for the year under section 476?
      `the statement says the directors acknowledge their responsibilities` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does it say that the directors acknowledge their responsibilities for complying with the Act with respect to accounting records and the preparation of accounts?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 475(3), is my company barred from an audit exemption for want of the directors' statements about the members' right and the directors' responsibilities` IS
    `s 475(3) the company is barred from the exemption for want of the directors' statements` exemption `the statement says the members have not required an audit under section 476` `the statement says the directors acknowledge their responsibilities`

@export Under section 475(4), does the directors' statement appear on my company's balance sheet above the signature required by section 414?
GIVEN `the statement appears on the balance sheet above the signature required by section 414` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does the directors' statement appear on the balance sheet above the signature required by section 414 (the signature approving the accounts)?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 475(4), does the directors' statement appear on my company's balance sheet above the signature required by section 414` IS
    `s 475(4) the statement appears on the balance sheet above the signature required by section 414` `the statement appears on the balance sheet above the signature required by section 414`

§§ `Section 476: may the members of my company force an audit`

-- Only for a company that would otherwise be exempt from audit under section 477, 479A or 480.
@export Under section 476, may the members who give this notice require my company to obtain an audit of its accounts for the year?
GIVEN `my company would otherwise be entitled to an audit exemption under section 477, 479A or 480` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Would your company otherwise be entitled to exemption from audit under section 477, 479A or 480?
      `my company has a share capital` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does your company have a share capital?
      `percentage of the nominal value of the issued share capital held by the members giving notice` IS A NUMBER @desc What percentage (for example 10) of the nominal value of the company's issued share capital do the members giving the notice hold in total? (0 if the company has no share capital)
      `largest percentage of the nominal value of one class held by the members giving notice` IS A NUMBER @desc What is the largest percentage (for example 10) of the nominal value of any one class of the company's issued share capital that the members giving the notice hold in total? (0 if the company has no share capital)
      `percentage of the members who give the notice` IS A NUMBER @desc What percentage (for example 10) of the members of the company, by number, give the notice? (Used only if the company has no share capital.)
      `first day of the financial year` IS A DATE @desc What is the first day of the financial year to which the notice relates? (Date, for example 2025-01-01)
      `last day of the financial year` IS A DATE @desc What is the last day of that financial year? (Date, for example 2025-12-31)
      `day the notice is given` IS A DATE @desc On what day is the notice given to the company? (Date, for example 2025-11-30)
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 476, may the members who give this notice require my company to obtain an audit of its accounts for the year` IS
    `s 476(1) the members may by notice require the company to obtain an audit of its accounts for the financial year`
        (JUST `my company would otherwise be entitled to an audit exemption under section 477, 479A or 480`)
        (`s 476(2) the notice is given by enough members` `my company has a share capital` (`percentage of the nominal value of the issued share capital held by the members giving notice` DIVIDED BY 100) (`largest percentage of the nominal value of one class held by the members giving notice` DIVIDED BY 100) (`percentage of the members who give the notice` DIVIDED BY 100))
        (`s 476(3) the notice is given in time` `first day of the financial year` `last day of the financial year` `day the notice is given`)

@export Under section 476(3), what is the latest day by which the members of my company must give notice requiring an audit?
GIVEN `last day of the financial year` IS A DATE @desc What is the last day of the financial year to which the notice will relate? (Date, for example 2025-12-31)
GIVETH A DATE
DECIDE `Under section 476(3), what is the latest day by which the members of my company must give notice requiring an audit` IS
    `s 476(3) the last day on which the notice may be given` `last day of the financial year`

§§ `Sections 477 to 481: is my company exempt from audit as a small, subsidiary or dormant company`

-- Section 477: a small company.  The group questions apply only if the company was a parent company or a subsidiary undertaking
-- at some time in the year.
@export Under section 477, is my company entitled to the small companies exemption from audit for the year?
GIVEN `my company qualifies as a small company in relation to the year (section 382)` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does your company qualify as a small company for the financial year, determined under section 382(1) to (6)?
      `my company was a parent company at some time in the year` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Was your company a parent company at any time in the financial year?
      `my company was a subsidiary undertaking at some time in the year` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Was your company a subsidiary undertaking at any time in the financial year?
      `my company's group qualifies as a small group for the year (section 383)` IS A BOOLEAN @desc If your company was a group company: does its group qualify as a small group for the year, determined under section 383 as if all the bodies corporate in the group were companies? (No if not a group company.)
      `my company's group was an ineligible group at some time in the year (section 384)` IS A BOOLEAN @desc If your company was a group company: was its group an ineligible group at any time in the year, under section 384(2) and (3)? (No if not a group company.)
      `my company was throughout its time as a group company a subsidiary undertaking` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Was your company a subsidiary undertaking throughout the whole of the period or periods in the year when it was a group company?
      `my company was throughout its time as a group company dormant` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Was your company dormant (section 1169) throughout the whole of the period or periods in the year when it was a group company?
      `my company was at some time in the year a public company` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Was your company a public company at any time in the financial year?
      `my company was at some time in the year an authorised insurance company` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Was your company an authorised insurance company (section 1165) at any time in the financial year?
      `my company was at some time in the year a banking company` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Was your company a banking company (section 1164) at any time in the financial year?
      `my company was at some time in the year an e-money issuer` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Was your company an e-money issuer (as defined in section 474(1)) at any time in the financial year?
      `my company was at some time in the year a MiFID investment firm` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Was your company a MiFID investment firm (as defined in section 474(1)) at any time in the financial year?
      `my company was at some time in the year a UCITS management company` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Was your company a UCITS management company (as defined in section 474(1)) at any time in the financial year?
      `my company carried on insurance market activity at some time in the year` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did your company carry on insurance market activity (section 1165) at any time in the financial year?
      `my company was at some time in the year a Master Trust scheme funder` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Was your company a scheme funder of a Master Trust scheme (section 39(1) of the Pension Schemes Act 2017 or the Northern Ireland Act of 2021) at any time in the financial year?
      `my company was at some time in the year a special register body` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Was your company a special register body as defined in section 117(1) of the Trade Union and Labour Relations (Consolidation) Act 1992 at any time in the financial year?
      `my company was at some time in the year an employers' association` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Was your company an employers' association as defined in section 122 of that Act or Article 4 of the Industrial Relations (Northern Ireland) Order 1992 at any time in the financial year?
      `the directors' statement identifies the exemption` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does the directors' statement on the balance sheet identify the exemption in question?
      `the directors' statement confirms that the company qualifies` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does the directors' statement on the balance sheet confirm that the company qualifies for the exemption?
      `the directors' statement says the members have not required an audit` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does the balance sheet say that the members have not required the company to obtain an audit for the year under section 476?
      `the directors' statement says the directors acknowledge their responsibilities` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does the balance sheet say that the directors acknowledge their responsibilities for accounting records and the preparation of accounts?
      `the statement is above the signature required by section 414` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does the statement appear on the balance sheet above the signature required by section 414?
      `a valid notice requiring an audit has been given under section 476` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Have the members given your company a valid notice requiring an audit for the year (see the section 476 question)?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 477, is my company entitled to the small companies exemption from audit for the year` IS
    `s 477(5) the company is entitled to the exemption conferred by section 477`
        (`s 477(1) the company is exempt from audit under section 477` (JUST `my company qualifies as a small company in relation to the year (section 382)`))
        (`s 478 the company is barred from the small companies exemption` `my company was at some time in the year a public company` `my company was at some time in the year an authorised insurance company` `my company was at some time in the year a banking company` (JUST `my company was at some time in the year an e-money issuer`) (JUST `my company was at some time in the year a MiFID investment firm`) (JUST `my company was at some time in the year a UCITS management company`) `my company carried on insurance market activity at some time in the year` `my company was at some time in the year a Master Trust scheme funder` `my company was at some time in the year a special register body` `my company was at some time in the year an employers' association`)
        (`s 479(1) the company is barred from the small companies exemption as a group company`
            (`s 479(4)(a) the company is a group company` (JUST `my company was a parent company at some time in the year`) (JUST `my company was a subsidiary undertaking at some time in the year`))
            (JUST `my company's group qualifies as a small group for the year (section 383)`)
            (JUST `my company's group was an ineligible group at some time in the year (section 384)`)
            (`s 479(3) subsection (3) applies: the company is not excluded by subsection (1)` (JUST `my company was throughout its time as a group company a subsidiary undertaking`) (JUST `my company was throughout its time as a group company dormant`)))
        (`coa11 seat section 475(2) bar` `the directors' statement identifies the exemption` `the directors' statement confirms that the company qualifies`)
        (`s 475(3) the company is barred from the exemption for want of the directors' statements` `s 475 the small companies exemption (section 477)` `the directors' statement says the members have not required an audit` `the directors' statement says the directors acknowledge their responsibilities`)
        (`s 475(4) the statement appears on the balance sheet above the signature required by section 414` `the statement is above the signature required by section 414`)
        (JUST `a valid notice requiring an audit has been given under section 476`)

@export Under section 478, is my company barred from the small companies exemption by the kind of company it is?
GIVEN `my company was at some time in the year a public company` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Was your company a public company at any time in the financial year?
      `my company was at some time in the year an authorised insurance company` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Was your company an authorised insurance company (section 1165) at any time in the financial year?
      `my company was at some time in the year a banking company` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Was your company a banking company (section 1164) at any time in the financial year?
      `my company was at some time in the year an e-money issuer` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Was your company an e-money issuer (as defined in section 474(1)) at any time in the financial year?
      `my company was at some time in the year a MiFID investment firm` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Was your company a MiFID investment firm (as defined in section 474(1)) at any time in the financial year?
      `my company was at some time in the year a UCITS management company` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Was your company a UCITS management company (as defined in section 474(1)) at any time in the financial year?
      `my company carried on insurance market activity at some time in the year` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did your company carry on insurance market activity (section 1165) at any time in the financial year?
      `my company was at some time in the year a Master Trust scheme funder` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Was your company a scheme funder of a Master Trust scheme (section 39(1) of the Pension Schemes Act 2017 or the Northern Ireland Act of 2021) at any time in the financial year?
      `my company was at some time in the year a special register body` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Was your company a special register body as defined in section 117(1) of the Trade Union and Labour Relations (Consolidation) Act 1992 at any time in the financial year?
      `my company was at some time in the year an employers' association` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Was your company an employers' association as defined in section 122 of that Act or Article 4 of the Industrial Relations (Northern Ireland) Order 1992 at any time in the financial year?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 478, is my company barred from the small companies exemption by the kind of company it is` IS
    `s 478 the company is barred from the small companies exemption` `my company was at some time in the year a public company` `my company was at some time in the year an authorised insurance company` `my company was at some time in the year a banking company` (JUST `my company was at some time in the year an e-money issuer`) (JUST `my company was at some time in the year a MiFID investment firm`) (JUST `my company was at some time in the year a UCITS management company`) `my company carried on insurance market activity at some time in the year` `my company was at some time in the year a Master Trust scheme funder` `my company was at some time in the year a special register body` `my company was at some time in the year an employers' association`

-- Section 479: only for a company that was a parent company or a subsidiary undertaking at some time in the year.
@export Under section 479(1), is my company barred from the small companies exemption by the rule on group companies?
GIVEN `my company was a parent company at some time in the year` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Was your company a parent company at any time in the financial year?
      `my company was a subsidiary undertaking at some time in the year` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Was your company a subsidiary undertaking at any time in the financial year?
      `my company's group qualifies as a small group for the year (section 383)` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does your company's group qualify as a small group for the year, determined under section 383 as if all the bodies corporate in the group were companies?
      `my company's group was an ineligible group at some time in the year (section 384)` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Was your company's group an ineligible group at any time in the year, under section 384(2) and (3)?
      `my company was throughout its time as a group company a subsidiary undertaking` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Was your company a subsidiary undertaking throughout the whole of the period or periods in the year when it was a group company?
      `my company was throughout its time as a group company dormant` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Was your company dormant (section 1169) throughout the whole of the period or periods in the year when it was a group company?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 479(1), is my company barred from the small companies exemption by the rule on group companies` IS
    `s 479(1) the company is barred from the small companies exemption as a group company`
        (`s 479(4)(a) the company is a group company` (JUST `my company was a parent company at some time in the year`) (JUST `my company was a subsidiary undertaking at some time in the year`))
        (JUST `my company's group qualifies as a small group for the year (section 383)`)
        (JUST `my company's group was an ineligible group at some time in the year (section 384)`)
        (`s 479(3) subsection (3) applies: the company is not excluded by subsection (1)` (JUST `my company was throughout its time as a group company a subsidiary undertaking`) (JUST `my company was throughout its time as a group company dormant`))

-- Section 479A: only for a company that is itself a subsidiary undertaking whose parent undertaking is established in the United Kingdom.
@export Under section 479A, is my company entitled to the subsidiary companies exemption from the audit of its individual accounts for the year?
GIVEN `my company is itself a subsidiary undertaking` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is your company itself a subsidiary undertaking (section 1162)?
      `its parent undertaking is established under the law of any part of the United Kingdom` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is its parent undertaking established under the law of any part of the United Kingdom?
      `all members of my company agree to the exemption for the year` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Do all the members of your company agree to the exemption in respect of the financial year?
      `the parent undertaking has given a guarantee under section 479C for the year` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has the parent undertaking given a guarantee under section 479C in respect of the year (see the section 479C questions)?
      `my company is included in the parent undertaking's consolidated accounts for the year` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is your company included in the consolidated accounts drawn up for that year, or to an earlier date in that year, by the parent undertaking?
      `the parent undertaking is a company` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the parent undertaking a company?
      `the consolidated accounts follow the requirements of Part 15` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Were the consolidated accounts drawn up in accordance with the requirements of Part 15 of the Act?
      `the consolidated accounts follow the legal requirements for a parent that is not a company` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Were the consolidated accounts drawn up in accordance with the legal requirements that apply to the drawing up of consolidated accounts for a parent that is not a company?
      `the consolidated accounts follow UK-adopted international accounting standards` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Were the consolidated accounts drawn up in accordance with UK-adopted international accounting standards (within the meaning given by section 474(1))?
      `the parent discloses the exemption in the notes to the consolidated accounts` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does the parent undertaking disclose in the notes to the consolidated accounts that your company is exempt from audit of its individual accounts under section 479A?
      `the day the directors file the accounts for the year` IS A MAYBE DATE @desc On what day did (or will) the directors file the accounts for the year with the registrar? (Date, for example 2025-09-30; leave empty if they have not yet been filed)
      `the day the written notice of the members' agreement was delivered to the registrar` IS A MAYBE DATE @desc On what day did the directors deliver to the registrar a written notice of the members' agreement? (Date; leave empty if not yet delivered)
      `the day the statement of guarantee was delivered to the registrar` IS A MAYBE DATE @desc On what day did the directors deliver to the registrar the statement referred to in section 479C(1)? (Date; leave empty if not yet delivered)
      `the day the copy of the consolidated accounts was delivered to the registrar` IS A MAYBE DATE @desc On what day did the directors deliver to the registrar a copy of the consolidated accounts? (Date; leave empty if not yet delivered)
      `the day the copy of the auditor's report on the consolidated accounts was delivered to the registrar` IS A MAYBE DATE @desc On what day did the directors deliver to the registrar a copy of the auditor's report on those accounts? (Date; leave empty if not yet delivered)
      `the day the copy of the consolidated annual report was delivered to the registrar` IS A MAYBE DATE @desc On what day did the directors deliver to the registrar a copy of the consolidated annual report drawn up by the parent undertaking? (Date; leave empty if not yet delivered)
      `my company was at some time in the year a traded company` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Was your company a traded company (as defined in section 474(1)) at any time in the financial year?
      `my company was at some time in the year an authorised insurance company` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Was your company an authorised insurance company (section 1165) at any time in the financial year?
      `my company was at some time in the year a banking company` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Was your company a banking company (section 1164) at any time in the financial year?
      `my company was at some time in the year an e-money issuer` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Was your company an e-money issuer (as defined in section 474(1)) at any time in the financial year?
      `my company was at some time in the year a MiFID investment firm` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Was your company a MiFID investment firm (as defined in section 474(1)) at any time in the financial year?
      `my company was at some time in the year a UCITS management company` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Was your company a UCITS management company (as defined in section 474(1)) at any time in the financial year?
      `my company carried on insurance market activity at some time in the year` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did your company carry on insurance market activity (section 1165) at any time in the financial year?
      `my company was at some time in the year a Master Trust scheme funder` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Was your company a scheme funder of a Master Trust scheme (section 39(1) of the Pension Schemes Act 2017 or the Northern Ireland Act of 2021) at any time in the financial year?
      `my company was at some time in the year a special register body` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Was your company a special register body as defined in section 117(1) of the Trade Union and Labour Relations (Consolidation) Act 1992 at any time in the financial year?
      `my company was at some time in the year an employers' association` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Was your company an employers' association as defined in section 122 of that Act or Article 4 of the Industrial Relations (Northern Ireland) Order 1992 at any time in the financial year?
      `the directors' statement identifies the exemption` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does the directors' statement on the balance sheet identify the exemption in question?
      `the directors' statement confirms that the company qualifies` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does the directors' statement on the balance sheet confirm that the company qualifies for the exemption?
      `the directors' statement says the members have not required an audit` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does the balance sheet say that the members have not required the company to obtain an audit for the year under section 476?
      `the directors' statement says the directors acknowledge their responsibilities` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does the balance sheet say that the directors acknowledge their responsibilities for accounting records and the preparation of accounts?
      `the statement is above the signature required by section 414` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does the statement appear on the balance sheet above the signature required by section 414?
      `a valid notice requiring an audit has been given under section 476` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Have the members given your company a valid notice requiring an audit for the year (see the section 476 question)?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 479A, is my company entitled to the subsidiary companies exemption from the audit of its individual accounts for the year` IS
    `s 479A(3) the company is entitled to the exemption conferred by section 479A`
        (`s 479A(1) the company is within the subsidiary companies audit exemption` `my company is itself a subsidiary undertaking` `its parent undertaking is established under the law of any part of the United Kingdom`)
        (`s 479A(2) the conditions of the exemption are complied with` `all members of my company agree to the exemption for the year` `the parent undertaking has given a guarantee under section 479C for the year` `my company is included in the parent undertaking's consolidated accounts for the year` `the parent undertaking is a company` `the consolidated accounts follow the requirements of Part 15` `the consolidated accounts follow the legal requirements for a parent that is not a company` `the consolidated accounts follow UK-adopted international accounting standards` `the parent discloses the exemption in the notes to the consolidated accounts` (`s 479A(2)(e) the five documents were delivered on or before the date the directors file the accounts` `the documents delivered`))
        (`s 479B the company is barred from the subsidiary companies audit exemption` (JUST `my company was at some time in the year a traded company`) `my company was at some time in the year an authorised insurance company` `my company was at some time in the year a banking company` (JUST `my company was at some time in the year an e-money issuer`) (JUST `my company was at some time in the year a MiFID investment firm`) (JUST `my company was at some time in the year a UCITS management company`) `my company carried on insurance market activity at some time in the year` `my company was at some time in the year a Master Trust scheme funder` `my company was at some time in the year a special register body` `my company was at some time in the year an employers' association`)
        (`coa11 seat section 475(2) bar` `the directors' statement identifies the exemption` `the directors' statement confirms that the company qualifies`)
        (`s 475(3) the company is barred from the exemption for want of the directors' statements` `s 475 the subsidiary companies exemption (section 479A)` `the directors' statement says the members have not required an audit` `the directors' statement says the directors acknowledge their responsibilities`)
        (`s 475(4) the statement appears on the balance sheet above the signature required by section 414` `the statement is above the signature required by section 414`)
        (JUST `a valid notice requiring an audit has been given under section 476`)
    WHERE
        -- the layer-1 module takes the five deliveries and the filing day as one record
        `the documents delivered` MEANS
            `s 479A(2)(e) documents delivered to the registrar` OF `the day the directors file the accounts for the year`, `the day the written notice of the members' agreement was delivered to the registrar`, `the day the statement of guarantee was delivered to the registrar`, `the day the copy of the consolidated accounts was delivered to the registrar`, `the day the copy of the auditor's report on the consolidated accounts was delivered to the registrar`, `the day the copy of the consolidated annual report was delivered to the registrar`

@export Under section 479B, is my company barred from the subsidiary companies exemption by the kind of company it is?
GIVEN `my company was at some time in the year a traded company` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Was your company a traded company (as defined in section 474(1)) at any time in the financial year?
      `my company was at some time in the year an authorised insurance company` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Was your company an authorised insurance company (section 1165) at any time in the financial year?
      `my company was at some time in the year a banking company` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Was your company a banking company (section 1164) at any time in the financial year?
      `my company was at some time in the year an e-money issuer` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Was your company an e-money issuer (as defined in section 474(1)) at any time in the financial year?
      `my company was at some time in the year a MiFID investment firm` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Was your company a MiFID investment firm (as defined in section 474(1)) at any time in the financial year?
