    `s 479B the company is barred from the subsidiary companies audit exemption` (JUST `my company was at some time in the year a traded company`) `my company was at some time in the year an authorised insurance company` `my company was at some time in the year a banking company` (JUST `my company was at some time in the year an e-money issuer`) (JUST `my company was at some time in the year a MiFID investment firm`) (JUST `my company was at some time in the year a UCITS management company`) `my company carried on insurance market activity at some time in the year` `my company was at some time in the year a Master Trust scheme funder` `my company was at some time in the year a special register body` `my company was at some time in the year an employers' association`

-- Section 479C: only if a parent undertaking is giving a guarantee so that its subsidiary can use the section 479A exemption.
@export Under section 479C(2), does the parent undertaking's statement meet the requirements of section 479C(2) (authentication and the listed particulars)?
GIVEN `the statement is authenticated by the parent undertaking` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the statement authenticated by the parent undertaking?
      `the parent undertaking has a registered number` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does the parent undertaking have a registered number?
      `the statement gives the name of the parent undertaking` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does the statement give the name of the parent undertaking?
      `the statement gives the registered number of the parent undertaking` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does the statement give the registered number of the parent undertaking?
      `the statement gives the name and registered number of the subsidiary company` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does the statement give the name and registered number of the subsidiary company for which the guarantee is given?
      `the statement gives its date` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does the statement give the date of the statement?
      `the statement gives the financial year to which the guarantee relates` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does the statement give the financial year to which the guarantee relates?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 479C(2), does the parent undertaking's statement meet the requirements of section 479C(2) (authentication and the listed particulars)` IS
    `s 479C(2) the statement meets the requirements` `the statement is authenticated by the parent undertaking` `the parent undertaking has a registered number` `the statement gives the name of the parent undertaking` `the statement gives the registered number of the parent undertaking` `the statement gives the name and registered number of the subsidiary company` `the statement gives its date` `the statement gives the financial year to which the guarantee relates`

@export Under section 479C(3)(a), does the parent undertaking's guarantee cover this liability of the subsidiary company?
GIVEN `a guarantee has been given under section 479C` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has a guarantee been given under section 479C (the directors of the subsidiary have delivered to the registrar the parent undertaking's statement)?
      `the liability is one the subsidiary was subject to at the end of the financial year to which the guarantee relates` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Was the subsidiary subject to the liability at the end of the financial year to which the guarantee relates?
      `the liability has been satisfied in full` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has the liability been satisfied in full?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 479C(3)(a), does the parent undertaking's guarantee cover this liability of the subsidiary company` IS
    `s 479C(3)(a) the parent undertaking guarantees the liability` `a guarantee has been given under section 479C` `the liability is one the subsidiary was subject to at the end of the financial year to which the guarantee relates` `the liability has been satisfied in full`

-- Section 480: only for a company that has been dormant since its formation or since the end of the previous financial year.
@export Under section 480, is my company entitled to the dormant companies exemption from audit for the year?
GIVEN `my company has been dormant since its formation` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has your company been dormant (section 1169) since its formation?
      `my company has been dormant since the end of the previous financial year` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has your company been dormant (section 1169) since the end of the previous financial year?
      `my company is entitled to prepare accounts under the small companies regime` IS A BOOLEAN @desc As regards its individual accounts for the year, is your company entitled to prepare accounts in accordance with the small companies regime (sections 381 to 384)?
      `my company would be so entitled but for being a public company or in an ineligible group` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Would it be so entitled but for having been a public company or a member of an ineligible group?
      `my company is required to prepare group accounts for the year` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is your company required to prepare group accounts for the year?
      `my company was at some time in the year a traded company` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Was your company a traded company (as defined in section 474(1)) at any time in the financial year?
      `my company was at some time in the year an authorised insurance company` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Was your company an authorised insurance company (section 1165) at any time in the financial year?
      `my company was at some time in the year a banking company` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Was your company a banking company (section 1164) at any time in the financial year?
      `my company was at some time in the year an e-money issuer` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Was your company an e-money issuer (as defined in section 474(1)) at any time in the financial year?
      `my company was at some time in the year a MiFID investment firm` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Was your company a MiFID investment firm (as defined in section 474(1)) at any time in the financial year?
      `my company was at some time in the year a UCITS management company` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Was your company a UCITS management company (as defined in section 474(1)) at any time in the financial year?
      `my company carried on insurance market activity at some time in the year` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did your company carry on insurance market activity (section 1165) at any time in the financial year?
      `the directors' statement identifies the exemption` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does the directors' statement on the balance sheet identify the exemption in question?
      `the directors' statement confirms that the company qualifies` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does the directors' statement on the balance sheet confirm that the company qualifies for the exemption?
      `the directors' statement says the members have not required an audit` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does the balance sheet say that the members have not required the company to obtain an audit for the year under section 476?
      `the directors' statement says the directors acknowledge their responsibilities` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does the balance sheet say that the directors acknowledge their responsibilities for accounting records and the preparation of accounts?
      `the statement is above the signature required by section 414` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does the statement appear on the balance sheet above the signature required by section 414?
      `a valid notice requiring an audit has been given under section 476` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Have the members given your company a valid notice requiring an audit for the year (see the section 476 question)?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 480, is my company entitled to the dormant companies exemption from audit for the year` IS
    `s 480(3) the company is entitled to the exemption conferred by section 480`
        (`s 480(1) the company is exempt from audit under section 480`
            (JUST `my company has been dormant since its formation`)
            (JUST `my company has been dormant since the end of the previous financial year`)
            (`s 480(2) the conditions for the dormant companies exemption are met` (JUST `my company is entitled to prepare accounts under the small companies regime`) `my company would be so entitled but for being a public company or in an ineligible group` `my company is required to prepare group accounts for the year`))
        (`s 481 the company is barred from the dormant companies exemption` (JUST `my company was at some time in the year a traded company`) `my company was at some time in the year an authorised insurance company` `my company was at some time in the year a banking company` (JUST `my company was at some time in the year an e-money issuer`) (JUST `my company was at some time in the year a MiFID investment firm`) (JUST `my company was at some time in the year a UCITS management company`) `my company carried on insurance market activity at some time in the year`)
        (`coa11 seat section 475(2) bar` `the directors' statement identifies the exemption` `the directors' statement confirms that the company qualifies`)
        (`s 475(3) the company is barred from the exemption for want of the directors' statements` `s 475 the dormant companies exemption (section 480)` `the directors' statement says the members have not required an audit` `the directors' statement says the directors acknowledge their responsibilities`)
        (`s 475(4) the statement appears on the balance sheet above the signature required by section 414` `the statement is above the signature required by section 414`)
        (JUST `a valid notice requiring an audit has been given under section 476`)

@export Under section 481, is my company barred from the dormant companies exemption by the kind of company it is?
GIVEN `my company was at some time in the year a traded company` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Was your company a traded company (as defined in section 474(1)) at any time in the financial year?
      `my company was at some time in the year an authorised insurance company` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Was your company an authorised insurance company (section 1165) at any time in the financial year?
      `my company was at some time in the year a banking company` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Was your company a banking company (section 1164) at any time in the financial year?
      `my company was at some time in the year an e-money issuer` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Was your company an e-money issuer (as defined in section 474(1)) at any time in the financial year?
      `my company was at some time in the year a MiFID investment firm` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Was your company a MiFID investment firm (as defined in section 474(1)) at any time in the financial year?
      `my company was at some time in the year a UCITS management company` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Was your company a UCITS management company (as defined in section 474(1)) at any time in the financial year?
      `my company carried on insurance market activity at some time in the year` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did your company carry on insurance market activity (section 1165) at any time in the financial year?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 481, is my company barred from the dormant companies exemption by the kind of company it is` IS
    `s 481 the company is barred from the dormant companies exemption` (JUST `my company was at some time in the year a traded company`) `my company was at some time in the year an authorised insurance company` `my company was at some time in the year a banking company` (JUST `my company was at some time in the year an e-money issuer`) (JUST `my company was at some time in the year a MiFID investment firm`) (JUST `my company was at some time in the year a UCITS management company`) `my company carried on insurance market activity at some time in the year`

§§ `Sections 482 and 483: non-profit-making companies subject to public sector audit`

-- Only for a non-profit-making company whose accounts are audited by the Comptroller and Auditor General or an Auditor General.
@export Under section 482, is my company entitled to the exemption from audit for non-profit-making companies subject to public sector audit for the year?
GIVEN route IS A `s 482(1) route of public sector audit` @desc By what route are your company's accounts subject to public sector audit: an order under section 25(6) of the Government Resources and Accounts Act 2000, an order under section 144 of the Government of Wales Act 1998, paragraph 18 of Schedule 8 to the Government of Wales Act 2006, section 21 of the Public Finance and Accountability (Scotland) Act 2000, an order under section 483, an order under Article 5(3) of the Audit and Accountability (Northern Ireland) Order 2003, or none of these?
      `my company is non-profit-making` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is your company non-profit-making, in the sense of Article 54 of the Treaty on the Functioning of the European Union?
      `my company is a parent company or a subsidiary undertaking` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is your company a parent company or a subsidiary undertaking?
      `every group undertaking is non-profit-making` IS A BOOLEAN @desc If it is, is every group undertaking non-profit-making?
      `the directors' statement identifies the exemption` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does the directors' statement on the balance sheet identify the exemption in question?
      `the directors' statement confirms that the company qualifies` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does the directors' statement on the balance sheet confirm that the company qualifies for the exemption?
      `the statement is above the signature required by section 414` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does the statement appear on the balance sheet above the signature required by section 414?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 482, is my company entitled to the exemption from audit for non-profit-making companies subject to public sector audit for the year` IS
    `s 482(4) the company is entitled to the exemption conferred by section 482`
        (`s 482(1) the requirements of Part 16 as to audit of accounts do not apply to the company` route `my company is non-profit-making` `my company is a parent company or a subsidiary undertaking` `every group undertaking is non-profit-making`)
        (`coa11 seat section 475(2) bar` `the directors' statement identifies the exemption` `the directors' statement confirms that the company qualifies`)
        (`s 475(4) the statement appears on the balance sheet above the signature required by section 414` `the statement is above the signature required by section 414`)

-- Only for a company with its registered office in Scotland.
@export Under section 483(1) and (2), is my company one in relation to which the Scottish Ministers may make an order providing for its accounts to be audited by the Auditor General for Scotland?
GIVEN `my company has its registered office in Scotland` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does your company have its registered office in Scotland?
      `it appears to the Scottish Ministers that the company exercises functions of a public nature in or as regards Scotland, none relating to reserved matters` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does it appear to the Scottish Ministers that your company exercises in or as regards Scotland functions of a public nature none of which relate to reserved matters (within the meaning of the Scotland Act 1998)?
      `it appears to the Scottish Ministers that the company is entirely or substantially funded from such a body` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does it appear to the Scottish Ministers that your company is entirely or substantially funded from a body whose accounts are audited by the Auditor General for Scotland (section 21 of the Public Finance and Accountability (Scotland) Act 2000, or an order under section 483)?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 483(1) and (2), is my company one in relation to which the Scottish Ministers may make an order providing for its accounts to be audited by the Auditor General for Scotland` IS
    `s 483(1) the Scottish Ministers may by order provide for the company's accounts to be audited by the Auditor General for Scotland` `my company has its registered office in Scotland` `it appears to the Scottish Ministers that the company exercises functions of a public nature in or as regards Scotland, none relating to reserved matters` `it appears to the Scottish Ministers that the company is entirely or substantially funded from such a body`

-- Only for a company in relation to which an order under section 483(1) is proposed.  JUST TRUE means barred: the order is not to be made yet.
@export Under section 483(5), is an order under section 483(1) barred until a draft of it has been laid before, and approved by resolution of, the Scottish Parliament?
GIVEN `a draft of the statutory instrument containing the order has been laid before the Scottish Parliament` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has a draft of the statutory instrument containing the order been laid before the Scottish Parliament?
      `the draft has been approved by resolution of the Scottish Parliament` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has the Scottish Parliament approved that draft by resolution?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 483(5), is an order under section 483(1) barred until a draft of it has been laid before, and approved by resolution of, the Scottish Parliament` IS
    `s 483(5) the order may not yet be made` `a draft of the statutory instrument containing the order has been laid before the Scottish Parliament` `the draft has been approved by resolution of the Scottish Parliament`

§§ `Sections 485 to 488: appointing the auditor of a private company, and the auditor's term`

-- Chapter 2 on private companies: ask only if your company is a private company.
@export Under section 485(1), must an auditor be appointed for my company for the financial year, if it is a private company?
GIVEN `my company is a private company` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is your company a private company (section 4(1))?
      `the directors have resolved that no auditor be appointed because audited accounts are unlikely to be required` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Have the directors resolved that no auditor be appointed for the financial year on the ground that audited accounts are unlikely to be required?
      `that resolution was reasonable` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Was that resolution a reasonable one?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 485(1), must an auditor be appointed for my company for the financial year, if it is a private company` IS
    `s 485(1) an auditor or auditors of the private company must be appointed for the financial year` `my company is a private company` `the directors have resolved that no auditor be appointed because audited accounts are unlikely to be required` `that resolution was reasonable`

@export Under section 485(2), what is the last day of my private company's period for appointing auditors?
GIVEN `the end of the time allowed for sending out the previous year's accounts and reports (section 424)` IS A DATE @desc On what day does the time allowed for sending out copies of the company's annual accounts and reports for the previous financial year end (section 424)? (Date, for example 2025-09-30)
      `the day the previous year's accounts and reports were sent out (section 423)` IS A MAYBE DATE @desc On what day were copies of the previous year's annual accounts and reports sent out under section 423? (Date; leave empty if they have not yet been sent out)
GIVETH A DATE
DECIDE `Under section 485(2), what is the last day of my private company's period for appointing auditors` IS
    (`s 485(2) the period for appointing auditors` `the end of the time allowed for sending out the previous year's accounts and reports (section 424)` `the day the previous year's accounts and reports were sent out (section 423)`)'s `s 485(2) last day of the period for appointing auditors`

@export Under section 485(2), is my private company's appointment of an auditor made before the end of the period for appointing auditors?
GIVEN `this is my company's first financial year` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is this the company's first financial year?
      `the end of the time allowed for sending out the previous year's accounts and reports (section 424)` IS A DATE @desc On what day does the time allowed for sending out copies of the company's annual accounts and reports for the previous financial year end (section 424)? (Date, for example 2025-09-30)
      `the day the previous year's accounts and reports were sent out (section 423)` IS A MAYBE DATE @desc On what day were copies of the previous year's annual accounts and reports sent out under section 423? (Date; leave empty if they have not yet been sent out)
      `the day the appointment was made` IS A DATE @desc On what day was (or will) the auditor be appointed? (Date, for example 2025-10-12)
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 485(2), is my private company's appointment of an auditor made before the end of the period for appointing auditors` IS
    `s 485(2) the appointment is made before the end of the period for appointing auditors` `this is my company's first financial year`
        (`s 485(2) the period for appointing auditors` `the end of the time allowed for sending out the previous year's accounts and reports (section 424)` `the day the previous year's accounts and reports were sent out (section 423)`)
        `the day the appointment was made`

@export Under section 485(3), may the directors of my private company appoint an auditor?
GIVEN `it is before my company's first period for appointing auditors` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the appointment being made at a time before the company's first period for appointing auditors?
      `the company was exempt from audit and had no auditor, and the appointment is before its next period` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Following a period during which the company, being exempt from audit, had no auditor, is the appointment being made before the company's next period for appointing auditors?
      `the appointment fills a casual vacancy` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the appointment to fill a casual vacancy in the office of auditor?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 485(3), may the directors of my private company appoint an auditor` IS
    `s 485(3) the directors may appoint an auditor or auditors of the company` `it is before my company's first period for appointing auditors` `the company was exempt from audit and had no auditor, and the appointment is before its next period` `the appointment fills a casual vacancy`

@export Under section 485(4), may the members of my private company appoint an auditor by ordinary resolution?
GIVEN `the appointment is during a period for appointing auditors` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the appointment being made during a period for appointing auditors?
      `the company should have appointed during a period but failed to do so` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Should the company have appointed an auditor during a period for appointing auditors but failed to do so?
      `the directors had power to appoint but failed to make an appointment` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did the directors have power to appoint under section 485(3) but fail to make an appointment?
      `the resolution is an ordinary resolution` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the resolution an ordinary resolution (passed by a simple majority, section 282)?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 485(4), may the members of my private company appoint an auditor by ordinary resolution` IS
    `s 485(4) the members may appoint an auditor or auditors of the company by ordinary resolution` `the appointment is during a period for appointing auditors` `the company should have appointed during a period but failed to do so` `the directors had power to appoint but failed to make an appointment` (JUST `the resolution is an ordinary resolution`)

-- Section 485(5) "may only be appointed" is a limit on every appointment, not a power: outside the routes it lists the answer is JUST FALSE, where the questions on subsections (3) and (4) answer NOTHING for an occasion they do not name.
@export Under section 485(5), is the appointment of an auditor of my private company made in accordance with a route the subsection allows (section 485, 486 or 486A)?
GIVEN `the appointment is made in accordance with section 485` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the appointment made in accordance with section 485 (by the directors under subsection (3), or by the members under subsection (4))?
      `the appointment is made in accordance with section 486 or 486A` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the appointment made in accordance with section 486 or 486A (the Secretary of State's default powers)?
      `the appointment is a deemed re-appointment under section 487` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the appointment a deemed re-appointment of the existing auditor under section 487?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 485(5), is the appointment of an auditor of my private company made in accordance with a route the subsection allows (section 485, 486 or 486A)` IS
    `s 485(5) the appointment is made in accordance with a route the section allows` `the appointment is made in accordance with section 485` `the appointment is made in accordance with section 486 or 486A` `the appointment is a deemed re-appointment under section 487`

-- Sections 485A, 485B and 485C: only if the company is a public interest entity.
@export Under section 485A(4), if section 485A applies to the appointment, must the audit committee or directors of my company carry out a selection procedure?
GIVEN `the appointment is made under section 485(4)` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the appointment one made by the members under section 485(4)?
      `my company is a private company` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is your company a private company (section 4(1))?
      `my company is a public interest entity` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is your company a public interest entity (section 494A)?
      `my company has an audit committee` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does your company have an audit committee (section 494A)?
      `the appointment is of an Auditor General` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the appointment of an Auditor General as auditor or one of the auditors?
      `my company is a small or medium sized enterprise` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is your company a small or medium sized enterprise within the meaning in Article 2(1)(f) of Directive 2003/71/EC?
      `the audit committee recommends re-appointment and the directors agree` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does the audit committee recommend re-appointment of the company's existing auditor or auditors, and do the directors agree?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 485A(4), if section 485A applies to the appointment, must the audit committee or directors of my company carry out a selection procedure` IS
    `s 485A(4) the audit committee or the directors must carry out a selection procedure in accordance with Article 16(3) of the Audit Regulation`
        (`s 485A(1) the section applies to the appointment` `the appointment is made under section 485(4)` `my company is a private company` (JUST `my company is a public interest entity`) (JUST `my company has an audit committee`) `the appointment is of an Auditor General`)
        `my company is a small or medium sized enterprise`
        `the audit committee recommends re-appointment and the directors agree`

@export Under section 485A(5), does the audit committee's recommendation meet the requirements of section 485A(5)?
GIVEN `the recommendation identifies a first and second choice drawn from the selection procedure` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does the recommendation identify its first and second choice candidates, drawn from those auditors who participated in a selection procedure under section 485A(4)?
      `the recommendation gives reasons for the choices` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does it give reasons for those choices?
      `the recommendation states it is free from influence by a third party` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does it state that the recommendation is free from influence by a third party?
      `the recommendation states no Article 16(6) contractual term has been imposed` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does it state that no contractual term of the kind mentioned in Article 16(6) of the Audit Regulation has been imposed on the company?
      `the audit committee recommends re-appointment and the directors agree` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does the audit committee recommend re-appointment of the company's existing auditor or auditors, and do the directors agree?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 485A(5), does the audit committee's recommendation meet the requirements of section 485A(5)` IS
    `s 485A(5) the audit committee's recommendation meets the requirements` `the recommendation identifies a first and second choice drawn from the selection procedure` `the recommendation gives reasons for the choices` `the recommendation states it is free from influence by a third party` `the recommendation states no Article 16(6) contractual term has been imposed` `the audit committee recommends re-appointment and the directors agree`

@export Under section 485A(6), does the directors' proposal meet the requirements of section 485A(6)?
GIVEN `the proposal includes the audit committee's recommendation` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does the directors' proposal include the recommendation made by the audit committee?
      `the proposal departs from the audit committee's preference` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does the proposal depart from the preference of the audit committee?
      `the proposal recommends a candidate drawn from the selection procedure` IS A BOOLEAN @desc If it departs: does it include a recommendation for a candidate drawn from those auditors who participated in a selection procedure under section 485A(4)?
      `the proposal gives the reasons for not following the recommendation` IS A BOOLEAN @desc If it departs: does it include the reasons for not following the audit committee's recommendation?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 485A(6), does the directors' proposal meet the requirements of section 485A(6)` IS
    `s 485A(6) the directors' proposal meets the requirements` `the proposal includes the audit committee's recommendation` `the proposal departs from the audit committee's preference` `the proposal recommends a candidate drawn from the selection procedure` `the proposal gives the reasons for not following the recommendation`

@export Under section 485B(4), if section 485B applies to the appointment, must the directors of my company carry out a selection procedure?
GIVEN `the appointment is made under section 485(4)` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the appointment one made by the members under section 485(4)?
      `my company is a private company` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is your company a private company (section 4(1))?
      `my company is a public interest entity` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is your company a public interest entity (section 494A)?
      `my company has an audit committee` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does your company have an audit committee (section 494A)?
      `the appointment is of an Auditor General` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the appointment of an Auditor General as auditor or one of the auditors?
      `my company is a small or medium sized enterprise` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is your company a small or medium sized enterprise within the meaning in Article 2(1)(f) of Directive 2003/71/EC?
      `the proposal is to re-appoint the existing auditor` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the directors' proposal to re-appoint the company's existing auditor or auditors?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 485B(4), if section 485B applies to the appointment, must the directors of my company carry out a selection procedure` IS
    `s 485B(4) the directors must carry out a selection procedure in accordance with Article 16(3) of the Audit Regulation`
        (`s 485B(1) the section applies to the appointment` `the appointment is made under section 485(4)` `my company is a private company` (JUST `my company is a public interest entity`) (JUST `my company has an audit committee`) `the appointment is of an Auditor General`)
        `my company is a small or medium sized enterprise`
        `the proposal is to re-appoint the existing auditor`

@export Under section 485C(1), is a person barred from appointment as auditor of my company for the financial year, if it is a private company that is a public interest entity?
GIVEN `my company is a private company that is a public interest entity` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is your company a private company that is a public interest entity (section 494A)?
      `the person has been auditor for every year of the maximum engagement period` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has the person been, or will the person have been, auditor of the company for every financial year comprised in the maximum engagement period (section 494ZA)?
      `the last day of the last financial year of the maximum engagement period` IS A DATE @desc What is the last day of the last financial year of that maximum engagement period (section 494ZA)? (Date, for example 2024-12-31)
      `the first day of the financial year for which the appointment is proposed` IS A DATE @desc What is the first day of the financial year for which the appointment is proposed? (Date, for example 2026-01-01)
      `the appointment is of an Auditor General` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the appointment of an Auditor General?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 485C(1), is a person barred from appointment as auditor of my company for the financial year, if it is a private company that is a public interest entity` IS
    `s 485C(1) the person is barred from appointment as auditor of the company for the financial year` (JUST `my company is a private company that is a public interest entity`) `the person has been auditor for every year of the maximum engagement period` `the last day of the last financial year of the maximum engagement period` `the first day of the financial year for which the appointment is proposed` `the appointment is of an Auditor General`

@export Under section 485C(2), is a person barred from appointment as auditor of my company for the financial year under the network rule of section 485C(2), if it is a private company that is a public interest entity?
GIVEN `my company is a private company that is a public interest entity` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is your company a private company that is a public interest entity (section 494A)?
      `that auditor has been auditor for every year of the maximum engagement period` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has the auditor mentioned in section 485C(1) been, or will that auditor have been, auditor of the company for every financial year comprised in the maximum engagement period (section 494ZA)?
      `the person is a member of the same network as that auditor` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the person a member of the same network (section 494A) as that auditor?
      `the last day of the last financial year of the maximum engagement period` IS A DATE @desc What is the last day of the last financial year of that maximum engagement period (section 494ZA)? (Date, for example 2024-12-31)
      `the first day of the financial year for which the appointment is proposed` IS A DATE @desc What is the first day of the financial year for which the appointment is proposed? (Date, for example 2026-01-01)
      `the appointment is of an Auditor General` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the appointment of an Auditor General?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 485C(2), is a person barred from appointment as auditor of my company for the financial year under the network rule of section 485C(2), if it is a private company that is a public interest entity` IS
    `s 485C(2) the person is barred as a member of the same network as the auditor mentioned in subsection (1)` (JUST `my company is a private company that is a public interest entity`) `that auditor has been auditor for every year of the maximum engagement period` `the person is a member of the same network as that auditor` `the last day of the last financial year of the maximum engagement period` `the first day of the financial year for which the appointment is proposed` `the appointment is of an Auditor General`

-- Sections 486 and 486A: only if the company failed to appoint an auditor (or appointed one in breach of section 485A, 485B or 485C).
@export Under section 486(2), must my private company give the Secretary of State notice that his power to appoint an auditor has become exercisable?
GIVEN `section 485(2) applies: this is not my company's first financial year` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is this a financial year other than the company's first?
      `my company failed to make the necessary appointment before the end of the period for appointing auditors` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did the company fail to make the necessary appointment before the end of the period for appointing auditors?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 486(2), must my private company give the Secretary of State notice that his power to appoint an auditor has become exercisable` IS
    `s 486(2) the company must give the Secretary of State notice that his power has become exercisable` `section 485(2) applies: this is not my company's first financial year` `my company failed to make the necessary appointment before the end of the period for appointing auditors`

@export Under section 486(2), did my private company give that notice within one week of the end of the period for appointing auditors?
GIVEN `the last day of the period for appointing auditors` IS A DATE @desc What was the last day of the company's period for appointing auditors? (Date, for example 2025-10-12)
      `the day the company gave the notice` IS A MAYBE DATE @desc On what day did the company give the Secretary of State notice that his power had become exercisable? (Date; leave empty if it has not yet given notice)
      `the day now` IS A DATE @desc What is today's date? (Date)
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 486(2), did my private company give that notice within one week of the end of the period for appointing auditors` IS
    `s 486(2) the company gave the notice within one week of the end of the period for appointing auditors` `the last day of the period for appointing auditors` `the day the company gave the notice` `the day now`

@export Under section 486(3)(b), does an officer of my private company commit an offence under section 486?
GIVEN `the company failed to give the notice required by section 486` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did the company fail to give the notice required by section 486?
      `the officer is in default (section 1121)` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the officer an officer in default (section 1121)?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 486(3)(b), does an officer of my private company commit an offence under section 486` IS
    `s 486(3)(b) the officer commits an offence` `the company failed to give the notice required by section 486` (JUST `the officer is in default (section 1121)`)

@export Under section 486(4), what is the most the company or an officer can be fined on summary conviction for that offence, in pounds?
GIVEN `the amount of level 3 on the standard scale, in pounds` IS A NUMBER @desc How many pounds is level 3 on the standard scale? (The Act does not say; ask the current figure.)
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `Under section 486(4), what is the most the company or an officer can be fined on summary conviction for that offence, in pounds` IS
    `s 486(4) the most the person can be fined on summary conviction, in pounds` `the amount of level 3 on the standard scale, in pounds`

@export Under section 486(4), what is the most the company or an officer can be fined for each day of continued contravention, in pounds?
GIVEN `the amount of level 3 on the standard scale, in pounds` IS A NUMBER @desc How many pounds is level 3 on the standard scale? (The Act does not say; ask the current figure.)
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `Under section 486(4), what is the most the company or an officer can be fined for each day of continued contravention, in pounds` IS
    `s 486(4) the most the person can be fined for each day of continued contravention, in pounds` `the amount of level 3 on the standard scale, in pounds`

@export Under section 486A(4), did my private company give the Secretary of State notice within one week of becoming aware of the breach?
GIVEN `the day the company became aware of the breach` IS A MAYBE DATE @desc On what day did the company become aware of the breach of section 485A, 485B or 485C? (Date; leave empty if it is not yet aware)
      `the day the company gave the notice` IS A MAYBE DATE @desc On what day did the company give the Secretary of State notice that his power under section 486A(1) had become exercisable? (Date; leave empty if it has not yet given notice)
      `the day now` IS A DATE @desc What is today's date? (Date)
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 486A(4), did my private company give the Secretary of State notice within one week of becoming aware of the breach` IS
    `s 486A(4) the company gave the notice within one week of becoming aware of the breach` `the day the company became aware of the breach` `the day the company gave the notice` `the day now`

@export Under section 487(1)(b), has the auditor of my private company ceased to hold office at the end of the next period for appointing auditors?
GIVEN `the day now` IS A DATE @desc What is today's date? (Date, for example 2026-10-30)
      `the last day of the next period for appointing auditors` IS A DATE @desc What is the last day of the next period for appointing auditors? (Date, for example 2026-10-12)
      `the auditor has been re-appointed` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has the auditor been re-appointed?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 487(1)(b), has the auditor of my private company ceased to hold office at the end of the next period for appointing auditors` IS
    `s 487(1)(b) the auditor or auditors have ceased to hold office` `the day now` `the last day of the next period for appointing auditors` `the auditor has been re-appointed`

-- Section 487: only if no auditor has been appointed by the end of the next period for appointing auditors.
@export Under section 487(2), is the auditor of my private company deemed to be re-appointed?
GIVEN `no auditor has been appointed by the end of the next period for appointing auditors` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has no auditor been appointed by the end of the next period for appointing auditors?
      `an auditor was in office immediately before that time` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Was an auditor in office immediately before that time?
      `that auditor was appointed by the directors` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Was that auditor appointed by the directors?
      `the articles require actual re-appointment` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Do the company's articles require actual re-appointment?
      `the members have prevented the deemed re-appointment under section 488` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Have members prevented the deemed re-appointment by notices under section 488 (see the section 488 question)?
      `the members have resolved that the auditor should not be re-appointed` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Have the members resolved that the auditor should not be re-appointed?
      `the directors have resolved that no auditor should be appointed for the year` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Have the directors resolved that no auditor or auditors should be appointed for the financial year in question?
      `the auditor's appointment would breach section 485C` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Would the auditor's appointment be in breach of section 485C?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 487(2), is the auditor of my private company deemed to be re-appointed` IS
    `s 487(2) the auditor in office is deemed to be re-appointed` `no auditor has been appointed by the end of the next period for appointing auditors` `an auditor was in office immediately before that time` `that auditor was appointed by the directors` `the articles require actual re-appointment` (JUST `the members have prevented the deemed re-appointment under section 488`) `the members have resolved that the auditor should not be re-appointed` `the directors have resolved that no auditor should be appointed for the year` (JUST `the auditor's appointment would breach section 485C`)

@export Under section 488(1), is the deemed re-appointment of the auditor of my private company prevented by the members' notices?
GIVEN `the percentage of the total voting rights represented by the members who gave valid notices` IS A NUMBER @desc What percentage (for example 5) of the total voting rights of all members who would be entitled to vote on a resolution that the auditor should not be re-appointed do the members who gave valid notices to the company represent?
      `the articles specify a lower percentage` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Do the company's articles specify, for this purpose, a percentage lower than 5%?
      `the percentage the articles specify` IS A NUMBER @desc If so, what percentage (for example 3)? (0 if the articles specify none)
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 488(1), is the deemed re-appointment of the auditor of my private company prevented by the members' notices` IS
    `s 488(1) the deemed re-appointment is prevented by the members`
        (`the percentage of the total voting rights represented by the members who gave valid notices` DIVIDED BY 100)
        (`s 488(2) the requisite percentage` (IF `the articles specify a lower percentage` THEN JUST (`the percentage the articles specify` DIVIDED BY 100) ELSE NOTHING))

@export Under section 488(3), is the members' notice to my private company a valid notice under section 488?
GIVEN form IS A `Form of document` @desc In what form was the notice given: hard copy form or electronic form?
      `the notice is authenticated by the people who gave it` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the notice authenticated by the person or persons giving it?
      `the day the company received the notice` IS A DATE @desc On what day did the company receive the notice? (Date, for example 2025-12-30)
      `the last day of the accounting reference period immediately preceding the deemed re-appointment` IS A DATE @desc What is the last day of the accounting reference period immediately preceding the time when the deemed re-appointment would have effect? (Date, for example 2025-12-31)
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 488(3), is the members' notice to my private company a valid notice under section 488` IS
    `s 488(3) the notice is a notice under section 488` form `the notice is authenticated by the people who gave it` `the day the company received the notice` `the last day of the accounting reference period immediately preceding the deemed re-appointment`

§§ `Sections 489 to 491: appointing the auditor of a public company, and the auditor's term`

-- Chapter 2 on public companies: ask only if your company is a public company.  Sections 489A to 490A repeat sections 485A to 486A for a public company.

-- Chapter 2 on private companies: ask only if your company is a public company.
@export Under section 489(1), must an auditor be appointed for my company for the financial year, if it is a public company?
GIVEN `my company is a public company` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is your company a public company (section 4(2))?
      `the directors have resolved that no auditor be appointed because audited accounts are unlikely to be required` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Have the directors resolved that no auditor be appointed for the financial year on the ground that audited accounts are unlikely to be required?
      `that resolution was reasonable` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Was that resolution a reasonable one?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 489(1), must an auditor be appointed for my company for the financial year, if it is a public company` IS
    `s 489(1) an auditor or auditors of the public company must be appointed for the financial year` `my company is a public company` `the directors have resolved that no auditor be appointed because audited accounts are unlikely to be required` `that resolution was reasonable`

@export Under section 489(2), is my public company's appointment of an auditor made before the end of the accounts meeting at which the previous year's accounts and reports are laid?
GIVEN `this is my company's first financial year` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is this the company's first financial year?
      `the day the accounts meeting ended` IS A DATE @desc On what day does (or did) the accounts meeting of the company, at which its annual accounts and reports for the previous financial year are laid, end? (Date, for example 2025-06-20)
      `the day the appointment was made` IS A DATE @desc On what day was (or will) the auditor be appointed? (Date, for example 2025-06-20)
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 489(2), is my public company's appointment of an auditor made before the end of the accounts meeting at which the previous year's accounts and reports are laid` IS
    `s 489(2) the appointment is made before the end of the accounts meeting` `this is my company's first financial year` `the day the accounts meeting ended` `the day the appointment was made`

@export Under section 489(3), may the directors of my public company appoint an auditor?
GIVEN `it is before my company's first accounts meeting` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the appointment being made at a time before the company's first accounts meeting?
      `the company was exempt from audit and had no auditor, and the appointment is before its next accounts meeting` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Following a period during which the company, being exempt from audit, had no auditor, is the appointment being made before the company's next accounts meeting?
      `the appointment fills a casual vacancy` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the appointment to fill a casual vacancy in the office of auditor?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 489(3), may the directors of my public company appoint an auditor` IS
    `s 489(3) the directors may appoint an auditor or auditors of the company` `it is before my company's first accounts meeting` `the company was exempt from audit and had no auditor, and the appointment is before its next accounts meeting` `the appointment fills a casual vacancy`

@export Under section 489(4), may the members of my public company appoint an auditor by ordinary resolution?
GIVEN `the appointment is at an accounts meeting` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the appointment being made at an accounts meeting?
      `the company should have appointed at an accounts meeting but failed to do so` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Should the company have appointed an auditor at an accounts meeting but failed to do so?
      `the directors had power to appoint but failed to make an appointment` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did the directors have power to appoint under section 489(3) but fail to make an appointment?
      `the resolution is an ordinary resolution` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the resolution an ordinary resolution (passed by a simple majority, section 282)?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 489(4), may the members of my public company appoint an auditor by ordinary resolution` IS
    `s 489(4) the members may appoint an auditor or auditors of the company by ordinary resolution` `the appointment is at an accounts meeting` `the company should have appointed at an accounts meeting but failed to do so` `the directors had power to appoint but failed to make an appointment` (JUST `the resolution is an ordinary resolution`)

@export Under section 489(5), is the appointment of an auditor of my public company made in accordance with a route the subsection allows (section 489, 490 or 490A)?
GIVEN `the appointment is made in accordance with section 489` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the appointment made in accordance with section 489 (by the directors under subsection (3), or by the members under subsection (4))?
      `the appointment is made in accordance with section 490 or 490A` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the appointment made in accordance with section 490 or 490A (the Secretary of State's default powers)?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 489(5), is the appointment of an auditor of my public company made in accordance with a route the subsection allows (section 489, 490 or 490A)` IS
    `s 489(5) the appointment is made in accordance with a route the section allows` `the appointment is made in accordance with section 489` `the appointment is made in accordance with section 490 or 490A`

-- Sections 489A, 489B and 489C: only if the company is a public interest entity.
@export Under section 489A(4), if section 489A applies to the appointment, must the audit committee or directors of my company carry out a selection procedure?
GIVEN `the appointment is made under section 489(4)` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the appointment one made by the members under section 489(4)?
      `my company is a public company` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is your company a public company (section 4(2))?
      `my company is a public interest entity` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is your company a public interest entity (section 494A)?
      `my company has an audit committee` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does your company have an audit committee (section 494A)?
      `the appointment is of an Auditor General` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the appointment of an Auditor General as auditor or one of the auditors?
      `my company is a small or medium sized enterprise` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is your company a small or medium sized enterprise within the meaning in Article 2(1)(f) of Directive 2003/71/EC?
      `my company has reduced market capitalisation` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is your company a company with reduced market capitalisation within the meaning in Article 2(1)(t) of that Directive?
      `the audit committee recommends re-appointment and the directors agree` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does the audit committee recommend re-appointment of the company's existing auditor or auditors, and do the directors agree?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 489A(4), if section 489A applies to the appointment, must the audit committee or directors of my company carry out a selection procedure` IS
    `s 489A(4) the audit committee or the directors must carry out a selection procedure in accordance with Article 16(3) of the Audit Regulation`
        (`s 489A(1) the section applies to the appointment` `the appointment is made under section 489(4)` `my company is a public company` (JUST `my company is a public interest entity`) (JUST `my company has an audit committee`) `the appointment is of an Auditor General`)
        `my company is a small or medium sized enterprise`
        `my company has reduced market capitalisation`
        `the audit committee recommends re-appointment and the directors agree`

@export Under section 489A(5), does the audit committee's recommendation meet the requirements of section 489A(5)?
GIVEN `the recommendation identifies a first and second choice drawn from the selection procedure` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does the recommendation identify its first and second choice candidates, drawn from those auditors who participated in a selection procedure under section 489A(4)?
      `the recommendation gives reasons for the choices` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does it give reasons for those choices?
      `the recommendation states it is free from influence by a third party` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does it state that the recommendation is free from influence by a third party?
      `the recommendation states no Article 16(6) contractual term has been imposed` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does it state that no contractual term of the kind mentioned in Article 16(6) of the Audit Regulation has been imposed on the company?
      `the audit committee recommends re-appointment and the directors agree` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does the audit committee recommend re-appointment of the company's existing auditor or auditors, and do the directors agree?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 489A(5), does the audit committee's recommendation meet the requirements of section 489A(5)` IS
    `s 489A(5) the audit committee's recommendation meets the requirements` `the recommendation identifies a first and second choice drawn from the selection procedure` `the recommendation gives reasons for the choices` `the recommendation states it is free from influence by a third party` `the recommendation states no Article 16(6) contractual term has been imposed` `the audit committee recommends re-appointment and the directors agree`

@export Under section 489A(6), does the directors' proposal meet the requirements of section 489A(6)?
GIVEN `the proposal includes the audit committee's recommendation` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does the directors' proposal include the recommendation made by the audit committee?
      `the proposal departs from the audit committee's preference` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does the proposal depart from the preference of the audit committee?
      `the proposal recommends a candidate drawn from the selection procedure` IS A BOOLEAN @desc If it departs: does it include a recommendation for a candidate drawn from those auditors who participated in a selection procedure under section 489A(4)?
      `the proposal gives the reasons for not following the recommendation` IS A BOOLEAN @desc If it departs: does it include the reasons for not following the audit committee's recommendation?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 489A(6), does the directors' proposal meet the requirements of section 489A(6)` IS
    `s 489A(6) the directors' proposal meets the requirements` `the proposal includes the audit committee's recommendation` `the proposal departs from the audit committee's preference` `the proposal recommends a candidate drawn from the selection procedure` `the proposal gives the reasons for not following the recommendation`

@export Under section 489B(4), if section 489B applies to the appointment, must the directors of my company carry out a selection procedure?
GIVEN `the appointment is made under section 489(4)` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the appointment one made by the members under section 489(4)?
      `my company is a public company` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is your company a public company (section 4(2))?
      `my company is a public interest entity` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is your company a public interest entity (section 494A)?
      `my company has an audit committee` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does your company have an audit committee (section 494A)?
      `the appointment is of an Auditor General` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the appointment of an Auditor General as auditor or one of the auditors?
      `my company is a small or medium sized enterprise` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is your company a small or medium sized enterprise within the meaning in Article 2(1)(f) of Directive 2003/71/EU?
      `my company has reduced market capitalisation` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is your company a company with reduced market capitalisation within the meaning in Article 2(1)(t) of that Directive?
      `the proposal is to re-appoint the existing auditor` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the directors' proposal to re-appoint the company's existing auditor or auditors?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 489B(4), if section 489B applies to the appointment, must the directors of my company carry out a selection procedure` IS
    `s 489B(4) the directors must carry out a selection procedure in accordance with Article 16(3) of the Audit Regulation`
        (`s 489B(1) the section applies to the appointment` `the appointment is made under section 489(4)` `my company is a public company` (JUST `my company is a public interest entity`) (JUST `my company has an audit committee`) `the appointment is of an Auditor General`)
        `my company is a small or medium sized enterprise`
        `my company has reduced market capitalisation`
        `the proposal is to re-appoint the existing auditor`

@export Under section 489C(1), is a person barred from appointment as auditor of my company for the financial year, if it is a public company that is a public interest entity?
GIVEN `my company is a public company that is a public interest entity` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is your company a public company that is a public interest entity (section 494A)?
      `the person has been auditor for every year of the maximum engagement period` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has the person been, or will the person have been, auditor of the company for every financial year comprised in the maximum engagement period (section 494ZA)?
      `the last day of the last financial year of the maximum engagement period` IS A DATE @desc What is the last day of the last financial year of that maximum engagement period (section 494ZA)? (Date, for example 2024-12-31)
      `the first day of the financial year for which the appointment is proposed` IS A DATE @desc What is the first day of the financial year for which the appointment is proposed? (Date, for example 2026-01-01)
      `the appointment is of an Auditor General` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the appointment of an Auditor General?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 489C(1), is a person barred from appointment as auditor of my company for the financial year, if it is a public company that is a public interest entity` IS
    `s 489C(1) the person is barred from appointment as auditor of the company for the financial year` (JUST `my company is a public company that is a public interest entity`) `the person has been auditor for every year of the maximum engagement period` `the last day of the last financial year of the maximum engagement period` `the first day of the financial year for which the appointment is proposed` `the appointment is of an Auditor General`

@export Under section 489C(2), is a person barred from appointment as auditor of my company for the financial year under the network rule of section 489C(2), if it is a public company that is a public interest entity?
GIVEN `my company is a public company that is a public interest entity` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is your company a public company that is a public interest entity (section 494A)?
      `that auditor has been auditor for every year of the maximum engagement period` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has the auditor mentioned in section 489C(1) been, or will that auditor have been, auditor of the company for every financial year comprised in the maximum engagement period (section 494ZA)?
      `the person is a member of the same network as that auditor` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the person a member of the same network (section 494A) as that auditor?
      `the last day of the last financial year of the maximum engagement period` IS A DATE @desc What is the last day of the last financial year of that maximum engagement period (section 494ZA)? (Date, for example 2024-12-31)
      `the first day of the financial year for which the appointment is proposed` IS A DATE @desc What is the first day of the financial year for which the appointment is proposed? (Date, for example 2026-01-01)
      `the appointment is of an Auditor General` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the appointment of an Auditor General?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 489C(2), is a person barred from appointment as auditor of my company for the financial year under the network rule of section 489C(2), if it is a public company that is a public interest entity` IS
    `s 489C(2) the person is barred as a member of the same network as the auditor mentioned in subsection (1)` (JUST `my company is a public company that is a public interest entity`) `that auditor has been auditor for every year of the maximum engagement period` `the person is a member of the same network as that auditor` `the last day of the last financial year of the maximum engagement period` `the first day of the financial year for which the appointment is proposed` `the appointment is of an Auditor General`

-- Sections 490 and 490A: only if the company failed to appoint an auditor (or appointed one in breach of section 489A, 489B or 489C).
@export Under section 490(2), must my public company give the Secretary of State notice that his power to appoint an auditor has become exercisable?
GIVEN `section 489(2) applies: this is not my company's first financial year` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is this a financial year other than the company's first?
      `my company failed to make the necessary appointment before the end of the accounts meeting` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did the company fail to make the necessary appointment before the end of the accounts meeting?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 490(2), must my public company give the Secretary of State notice that his power to appoint an auditor has become exercisable` IS
    `s 490(2) the company must give the Secretary of State notice that his power has become exercisable` `section 489(2) applies: this is not my company's first financial year` `my company failed to make the necessary appointment before the end of the accounts meeting`

@export Under section 490(2), did my public company give that notice within one week of the end of the accounts meeting?
GIVEN `the day the accounts meeting ended` IS A DATE @desc On what day did the accounts meeting end? (Date, for example 2025-06-20)
      `the day the company gave the notice` IS A MAYBE DATE @desc On what day did the company give the Secretary of State notice that his power had become exercisable? (Date; leave empty if it has not yet given notice)
      `the day now` IS A DATE @desc What is today's date? (Date)
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 490(2), did my public company give that notice within one week of the end of the accounts meeting` IS
    `s 490(2) the company gave the notice within one week of the end of the accounts meeting` `the day the accounts meeting ended` `the day the company gave the notice` `the day now`

@export Under section 490(3)(b), does an officer of my public company commit an offence under section 490?
GIVEN `the company failed to give the notice required by section 490` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did the company fail to give the notice required by section 490?
      `the officer is in default (section 1121)` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the officer an officer in default (section 1121)?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 490(3)(b), does an officer of my public company commit an offence under section 490` IS
    `s 490(3)(b) the officer commits an offence` `the company failed to give the notice required by section 490` (JUST `the officer is in default (section 1121)`)

@export Under section 490(4), what is the most the company or an officer can be fined on summary conviction for that offence, in pounds?
GIVEN `the amount of level 3 on the standard scale, in pounds` IS A NUMBER @desc How many pounds is level 3 on the standard scale? (The Act does not say; ask the current figure.)
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `Under section 490(4), what is the most the company or an officer can be fined on summary conviction for that offence, in pounds` IS
    `s 490(4) the most the person can be fined on summary conviction, in pounds` `the amount of level 3 on the standard scale, in pounds`

@export Under section 490(4), what is the most the company or an officer can be fined for each day of continued contravention, in pounds?
GIVEN `the amount of level 3 on the standard scale, in pounds` IS A NUMBER @desc How many pounds is level 3 on the standard scale? (The Act does not say; ask the current figure.)
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `Under section 490(4), what is the most the company or an officer can be fined for each day of continued contravention, in pounds` IS
    `s 490(4) the most the person can be fined for each day of continued contravention, in pounds` `the amount of level 3 on the standard scale, in pounds`

@export Under section 490A(4), did my public company give the Secretary of State notice within one week of becoming aware of the breach?
GIVEN `the day the company became aware of the breach` IS A MAYBE DATE @desc On what day did the company become aware of the breach of section 489A, 489B or 489C? (Date; leave empty if it is not yet aware)
      `the day the company gave the notice` IS A MAYBE DATE @desc On what day did the company give the Secretary of State notice that his power under section 490A(1) had become exercisable? (Date; leave empty if it has not yet given notice)
      `the day now` IS A DATE @desc What is today's date? (Date)
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 490A(4), did my public company give the Secretary of State notice within one week of becoming aware of the breach` IS
    `s 490A(4) the company gave the notice within one week of becoming aware of the breach` `the day the company became aware of the breach` `the day the company gave the notice` `the day now`

-- Section 491: a public company's auditor holds office until the conclusion of the next accounts meeting.
@export Under section 491(1)(b), has the auditor of my public company ceased to hold office at the conclusion of the accounts meeting next following their appointment?
GIVEN `the accounts meeting next following their appointment has concluded` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has the accounts meeting next following the auditor's appointment concluded?
      `the auditor has been re-appointed` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has the auditor been re-appointed?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 491(1)(b), has the auditor of my public company ceased to hold office at the conclusion of the accounts meeting next following their appointment` IS
    `s 491(1)(b) the auditor or auditors have ceased to hold office` `the accounts meeting next following their appointment has concluded` `the auditor has been re-appointed`

§§ `Section 492: who fixes the auditor's remuneration`

@export Under section 492, who must fix the remuneration of my company's auditor?
GIVEN way IS A `s 492 way the auditor was appointed` @desc Was your company's auditor appointed by the members, by the directors, by the Secretary of State, or in some other way?
GIVETH A `s 492 who fixes the remuneration`
DECIDE `Under section 492, who must fix the remuneration of my company's auditor` IS
    `s 492(1) to (3) who must fix the auditor's remuneration` way

@export Under section 492(4), is a sum paid in respect of expenses part of the auditor's remuneration?
GIVEN `the sum is paid in respect of expenses` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the sum paid in respect of the auditor's expenses?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 492(4), is a sum paid in respect of expenses part of the auditor's remuneration` IS
    `s 492(4) the sum is part of the auditor's remuneration` `the sum is paid in respect of expenses`

§§ `Section 494ZA: how long may an auditor stay (the maximum engagement period)`

-- The company's financial years are taken to begin on the same day of every calendar year (so each year is twelve months long);
-- if they do not, use the layer-1 rule with the company's real financial years (NOTES.md, fork F20).  An answer needs the years to
-- run past the cut-off the Table names (for the last year for which the auditor was appointed after a qualifying selection
-- procedure, ten years later; for the first year, twenty): supply the last calendar year in which a financial year has begun
-- or is expected to begin.
GIVEN day IS A NUMBER
      month IS A NUMBER
      `first year` IS A NUMBER
      `last year` IS A NUMBER
      `years with a qualifying selection procedure` IS A LIST OF NUMBER
GIVETH A LIST OF `s 494ZA financial year`
`coa11 seat the company's financial years` MEANS
    IF `first year` GREATER THAN `last year`
    THEN EMPTY
    ELSE (`s 494ZA financial year` OF (Date day month `first year`), (Date (Day (Date day month (`first year` PLUS 1)) MINUS 1)), (elem `first year` `years with a qualifying selection procedure`))
         FOLLOWED BY `coa11 seat the company's financial years` day month (`first year` PLUS 1) `last year` `years with a qualifying selection procedure`

@export Under section 494ZA(1), what is the last day of the last financial year of the maximum engagement period of my company's auditor, before any extension?
GIVEN `day of the month on which my company's financial years begin` IS A NUMBER @desc On what day of the month do your company's financial years begin? (For example 1)
      `month in which my company's financial years begin` IS A NUMBER @desc In what month (1 to 12) do your company's financial years begin? (For example 1 for January)
      `calendar year in which the first financial year of the maximum engagement period began` IS A NUMBER @desc In what calendar year did the first financial year of the auditor's run of consecutive years as your company's auditor begin? (For example 2010)
      `last calendar year in which a financial year of my company has begun or will begin` IS A NUMBER @desc What is the last calendar year in which a financial year of your company has begun, or will begin (at least 20 years after the first year if you want a complete answer)? (For example 2035)
      `calendar years in which a financial year began for which the auditor was appointed after a qualifying selection procedure` IS A LIST OF NUMBER @desc List every calendar year in which a financial year of your company began for which the auditor was appointed following a qualifying selection procedure (section 494ZA(5)). (For example [2005, 2017]; an empty list if there has been none)
GIVETH A MAYBE DATE
DECIDE `Under section 494ZA(1), what is the last day of the last financial year of the maximum engagement period of my company's auditor, before any extension` IS
    CONSIDER `s 494ZA(1) the last financial year of the maximum engagement period` years
    WHEN NOTHING THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (silent): the years supplied do not settle the Table, or none applies
    WHEN JUST year THEN JUST (year's `s 494ZA last day of the financial year`)
    WHERE
        years MEANS `coa11 seat the company's financial years` `day of the month on which my company's financial years begin` `month in which my company's financial years begin` `calendar year in which the first financial year of the maximum engagement period began` `last calendar year in which a financial year of my company has begun or will begin` `calendar years in which a financial year began for which the auditor was appointed after a qualifying selection procedure`

@export Under section 494ZA(2), may the maximum engagement period of my company's auditor be extended by the period I have in mind?
GIVEN `the first day of the first financial year of the maximum engagement period` IS A DATE @desc What is the first day of the first financial year of the maximum engagement period? (Date, for example 2010-01-01)
      `the length of the extension in years` IS A NUMBER @desc For how many years (at most 2) is an extension proposed?
      `the competent authority has approved the extension` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has the competent authority approved the extension?
      `the competent authority is satisfied that exceptional circumstances exist` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the competent authority satisfied that exceptional circumstances exist?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 494ZA(2), may the maximum engagement period of my company's auditor be extended by the period I have in mind` IS
    `s 494ZA(2) the maximum engagement period may be extended by the period` `the first day of the first financial year of the maximum engagement period` `the length of the extension in years` `the competent authority has approved the extension` (`s 494ZA(3) the competent authority may give its approval` `the competent authority is satisfied that exceptional circumstances exist`)

@export Under section 494ZA(3), may the competent authority give its approval to an extension of the maximum engagement period of my company's auditor?
GIVEN `the competent authority is satisfied that exceptional circumstances exist` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the competent authority satisfied that exceptional circumstances exist?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 494ZA(3), may the competent authority give its approval to an extension of the maximum engagement period of my company's auditor` IS
    `s 494ZA(3) the competent authority may give its approval` `the competent authority is satisfied that exceptional circumstances exist`

§§ `Section 494A: public interest entities, audit committees, networks and Auditors General`

@export Under section 494A, is my company a public interest entity?
GIVEN `my company is an issuer within the meaning of Part 6 of the Financial Services and Markets Act 2000` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is your company an issuer within the meaning of Part 6 of the Financial Services and Markets Act 2000 (see section 102A(6))?
      `its transferable securities are admitted to trading on a UK regulated market` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are its transferable securities admitted to trading on a UK regulated market?
      `my company is a credit institution that is a CRR firm` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is your company a credit institution within the meaning given by Article 4(1)(1) of Regulation (EU) No. 575/2013 which is a CRR firm within the meaning of Article 4(1)(2A) of that Regulation?
      `my company would be an insurance undertaking were the United Kingdom a member State` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Would your company be an insurance undertaking as defined in Article 2(1) of Council Directive 91/674/EEC (as that Article had effect immediately before IP completion day), were the United Kingdom a member State?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 494A, is my company a public interest entity` IS
    `s 494A "public interest entity" the entity is a public interest entity`
        (`s 494A "issuer" the person is an issuer` (JUST `my company is an issuer within the meaning of Part 6 of the Financial Services and Markets Act 2000`))
        `its transferable securities are admitted to trading on a UK regulated market`
        (JUST `my company is a credit institution that is a CRR firm`)
        (JUST `my company would be an insurance undertaking were the United Kingdom a member State`)

@export Under section 494A, is this body an audit committee?
GIVEN `the body performs the functions in rule 7.1.3 of the Disclosure Guidance and Transparency Rules` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does the body perform the functions referred to in rule 7.1.3 of the Disclosure Guidance and Transparency Rules sourcebook of the Financial Conduct Authority, as they have effect on IP completion day?
      `the body performs the functions in rule 2.4 of the Audit Committee Part of the PRA Rulebook` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does the body perform the functions referred to in rule 2.4 of the Audit Committee Part of the Rulebook of the Prudential Regulation Authority, as they have effect on IP completion day?
      `the body performs equivalent functions` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does the body perform equivalent functions?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 494A, is this body an audit committee` IS
    `s 494A "audit committee" the body is an audit committee` `the body performs the functions in rule 7.1.3 of the Disclosure Guidance and Transparency Rules` `the body performs the functions in rule 2.4 of the Audit Committee Part of the PRA Rulebook` `the body performs equivalent functions`

@export Under section 494A, do these persons form a network?
GIVEN `the persons form an association of persons other than a firm` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Do the persons form an association of persons other than a firm?
      `they share profits` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Do they co-operate in audit work by profit-sharing?
      `they share costs` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Do they co-operate in audit work by cost sharing?
      `they have common ownership, control or management` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Do they co-operate in audit work by common ownership, control or management?
      `they have common quality control policies and procedures` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Do they co-operate in audit work by common quality control policies and procedures?
      `they have a common business strategy` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Do they co-operate in audit work by a common business strategy?
      `they use a common name` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Do they co-operate in audit work by use of a common name?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 494A, do these persons form a network` IS
    `s 494A "network" the association is a network` `the persons form an association of persons other than a firm` `they share profits` `they share costs` `they have common ownership, control or management` `they have common quality control policies and procedures` `they have a common business strategy` `they use a common name`

@export Under section 494A, is this person an Auditor General?
GIVEN `the person is the Comptroller and Auditor General` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the person the Comptroller and Auditor General?
      `the person is the Auditor General for Scotland` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the person the Auditor General for Scotland?
      `the person is the Auditor General for Wales` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the person the Auditor General for Wales?
      `the person is the Comptroller and Auditor General for Northern Ireland` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the person the Comptroller and Auditor General for Northern Ireland?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 494A, is this person an Auditor General` IS
    `s 494A "Auditor General" the person is an Auditor General` `the person is the Comptroller and Auditor General` `the person is the Auditor General for Scotland` `the person is the Auditor General for Wales` `the person is the Comptroller and Auditor General for Northern Ireland`

-- ====================================================================================================
-- seat questions from part coa12 (merged by the lead on 2026-11-12; unchanged text follows)
-- ====================================================================================================
-- coa12-seat.l4: the SEAT LAYER for the Companies Act 2006, Part 16 (Audit), Chapters 3 to 7 (ss 495 to 539).
--
-- SEAT: an individual who is, or is about to become, a director, a company secretary or a member (shareholder) of a company registered
-- under the Act, or who deals with one, asking on facts they can state what the Act requires or lets them do, what rights they have
-- against the company or its directors, what they must disclose, file, approve or vote on and by when, and what follows (liability,
-- offences, penalties) if it is not done. (Assumed, not ruled: the Act is addressed to companies, so the individual is whoever stands in
-- a company's management or ownership. Assumed, not ruled: the individual auditor, officer or employee who deals with the company is
-- "who deals with one"; questions in the auditor's voice are marked in their comments.) There is never a seat for an official: sections
-- 508, 509 and 524 address only officials and have no question here (layer 1 records them).
--
-- This layer asks questions and calls the rules of the layer-1 modules; it restates no rule. Each question takes plain inputs, one for each
-- fact the person can state, each with an @desc worded as that person would be asked. Keel and other-part answers (private or public
-- company, quoted company, officer in default, ordinary or special resolution, authenticated, subsidiary) are asked as yes/no facts.
-- A yes/no fact is passed to the layer-1 rule as JUST TRUE or JUST FALSE, so this layer never answers NOTHING because of a fact asked.
--
-- HOW TO READ AN ANSWER (the rule of 2026-10-29 and the rulings of 2026-11-04/05, assumed, not ruled by a lawyer):
--   JUST TRUE = the Act says yes (or, for a question named as a bar, the Act bars); JUST FALSE = the Act says no in its own words;
--   NOTHING = not covered: the Act does not decide the case. A caller must never turn NOTHING into "no".
-- The Act does not state the pounds a "level on the standard scale" or "the statutory maximum" stands for: they are inputs.
--
-- A question whose name and body differ in direction (the audit the brief asks for) is listed in NOTES.md under "Seat questions: name and direction".

-- The mode of conviction, named by the person in words. An answer that is none of the five is not recognised: NOTHING, never a guess.
GIVEN how IS A STRING
GIVETH A MAYBE (`Mode of conviction`)
`coa12 seat the mode of conviction named` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF how EQUALS "on indictment" THEN JUST `on conviction on indictment`
        IF how EQUALS "summary, England and Wales" THEN JUST `on summary conviction in England and Wales`
        IF how EQUALS "summary, Scotland" THEN JUST `on summary conviction in Scotland`
        IF how EQUALS "summary, Northern Ireland" THEN JUST `on summary conviction in Northern Ireland`
        IF how EQUALS "summary, place not stated" THEN JUST `on summary conviction`
        OTHERWISE NOTHING

-- The words for an audit authority, for the answer to section 525(1).
GIVEN a IS A `s 525(1) audit authority`
GIVETH A STRING
`coa12 seat the words for the audit authority` MEANS
    CONSIDER a
    WHEN `s 525(1)(a)(i) the Secretary of State` THEN "the Secretary of State"
    WHEN `s 525(1)(a)(ii) the body to which the Secretary of State has delegated functions under section 1252` THEN "the body to which the Secretary of State has delegated functions under section 1252"
    WHEN `s 525(1)(a) the Financial Reporting Council Limited` THEN "the Financial Reporting Council Limited"
    WHEN `s 525(1)(b) the relevant supervisory body` THEN "the relevant supervisory body"
    WHEN `s 525(1)(c) the Independent Supervisor` THEN "the Independent Supervisor"


§ `Companies Act 2006, Part 16 (Audit), Chapters 3 to 7 -- the questions of a director, secretary, member or person who deals with a company`

-- SEAT: an individual who is, or is about to become, a director, a company secretary or a member (shareholder) of a company registered under the Act, or who deals with one (including, assumed not ruled, the individual auditor, officer or employee who deals with the company). Every question begins "Under section N,".

§§ `Chapter 3 -- the auditor's report and the auditor's rights (ss 495 to 509)`

-- Ask these of any set of annual accounts. Where a group only arises in a situation you may not be in (an offence, a misleading statement, a guidance), the form should first ask "Has this happened to you?".

-- Seat question (member or director): Under section 495(1), must the auditor make a report to the members on these annual accounts.
@export Under section 495(1), must the auditor make a report to the members on these annual accounts?
GIVEN `Is the company a public company` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the company a public company?
      `Are copies of the annual accounts, during the auditor's tenure of office, to be sent out to members under section 423` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are copies of the annual accounts, during the auditor's tenure of office, to be sent out to members under section 423?
      `Are copies of the annual accounts, during the auditor's tenure of office, to be laid before the company in general meeting under section 437` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are copies of the annual accounts, during the auditor's tenure of office, to be laid before the company in general meeting under section 437?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 495(1), must the auditor make a report to the members on these annual accounts` IS
    `s 495(1) the auditor must make a report to the members on the annual accounts` (NOT `Is the company a public company`) `Are copies of the annual accounts, during the auditor's tenure of office, to be sent out to members under section 423` `Is the company a public company` `Are copies of the annual accounts, during the auditor's tenure of office, to be laid before the company in general meeting under section 437`

-- Seat question (auditor, director): Under section 495(2), does the auditor's report include what the subsection requires.
@export Under section 495(2), does the auditor's report include what the subsection requires?
GIVEN `Does the report identify the company whose annual accounts were audited` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does the report identify the company whose annual accounts were audited?
      `Does the report describe the annual accounts audited, including the period they cover` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does the report describe the annual accounts audited, including the period they cover?
      `Does the report describe the financial reporting framework applied in preparing the accounts` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does the report describe the financial reporting framework applied in preparing the accounts?
      `Does the report describe the scope of the audit, identifying the auditing standards used` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does the report describe the scope of the audit, identifying the auditing standards used?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 495(2), does the auditor's report include what the subsection requires` IS
    `s 495(2) the auditor's report includes what the subsection requires` `Does the report identify the company whose annual accounts were audited` `Does the report describe the annual accounts audited, including the period they cover` `Does the report describe the financial reporting framework applied in preparing the accounts` `Does the report describe the scope of the audit, identifying the auditing standards used`

-- Seat question (auditor, director): Under section 495(5), must the person or persons appointed as auditor jointly make the report.
@export Under section 495(5), must the person or persons appointed as auditor jointly make the report?
GIVEN `Is more than one person appointed as auditor` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is more than one person appointed as auditor?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 495(5), must the person or persons appointed as auditor jointly make the report` IS
    `s 495(5) the persons appointed must jointly make a report` `Is more than one person appointed as auditor`

-- Seat question (member, director): Under section 497(1), must the auditor report on the auditable part of the directors' remuneration report.
@export Under section 497(1), must the auditor report on the auditable part of the directors' remuneration report?
GIVEN `Is the company a quoted company` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the company a quoted company?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 497(1), must the auditor report on the auditable part of the directors' remuneration report` IS
    `s 497(1) the auditor must report on the auditable part of the directors' remuneration report` (`coa12 the answer for the fact` `Is the company a quoted company`)

-- Seat question (auditor): Under section 498(2)(b), must the auditor state in his report that the individual accounts are not in agreement with the accounting records and returns.
@export Under section 498(2)(b), must the auditor state in his report that the individual accounts are not in agreement with the accounting records and returns?
GIVEN `Is the auditor of the opinion that the company's individual accounts are not in agreement with the accounting records and returns` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the auditor of the opinion that the company's individual accounts are not in agreement with the accounting records and returns?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 498(2)(b), must the auditor state in his report that the individual accounts are not in agreement with the accounting records and returns` IS
    `s 498(2)(b) the auditor shall state in his report that the individual accounts are not in agreement with the records and returns` `Is the auditor of the opinion that the company's individual accounts are not in agreement with the accounting records and returns`

-- Seat question (auditor, director): Under section 498(3), must the auditor state in his report that he did not obtain all the information and explanations he needs.
@export Under section 498(3), must the auditor state in his report that he did not obtain all the information and explanations he needs?
GIVEN `Has the auditor failed to obtain all the information and explanations which, to the best of his knowledge and belief, are necessary for the purposes of his audit` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has the auditor failed to obtain all the information and explanations which, to the best of his knowledge and belief, are necessary for the purposes of his audit?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 498(3), must the auditor state in his report that he did not obtain all the information and explanations he needs` IS
    `s 498(3) the auditor shall state in his report that he did not obtain all the information and explanations` `Has the auditor failed to obtain all the information and explanations which, to the best of his knowledge and belief, are necessary for the purposes of his audit`

-- Seat question (auditor, director): Under section 498(5), must the auditor state in his report that the directors were not entitled to the small companies regime or exemption.
@export Under section 498(5), must the auditor state in his report that the directors were not entitled to the small companies regime or exemption?
GIVEN `Have the directors prepared accounts in accordance with the small companies regime` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Have the directors prepared accounts in accordance with the small companies regime?
      `Have the directors taken advantage of small companies exemption from the requirement to prepare a strategic report, or in preparing the directors' report` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Have the directors taken advantage of small companies exemption from the requirement to prepare a strategic report, or in preparing the directors' report?
      `In the auditor's opinion, were the directors not entitled to do so` IS A BOOLEAN @desc In the auditor's opinion, were the directors not entitled to do so?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 498(5), must the auditor state in his report that the directors were not entitled to the small companies regime or exemption` IS
    `s 498(5) the auditor shall state in his report that the directors were not entitled to do so` `Have the directors prepared accounts in accordance with the small companies regime` `Have the directors taken advantage of small companies exemption from the requirement to prepare a strategic report, or in preparing the directors' report` `In the auditor's opinion, were the directors not entitled to do so`

-- Seat question (officer, employee): Under section 499(1)(b), may the person asking require me to provide information or explanations.
@export Under section 499(1)(b), may the person asking require me to provide information or explanations?
GIVEN `Is the person asking an auditor of the company` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the person asking an auditor of the company?
      `Are you an officer or employee of the company` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are you an officer or employee of the company?
      `Do you hold, or are you accountable for, any of the company's books, accounts or vouchers` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Do you hold, or are you accountable for, any of the company's books, accounts or vouchers?
      `Are you a subsidiary undertaking of the company that is a body corporate incorporated in the United Kingdom` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are you a subsidiary undertaking of the company that is a body corporate incorporated in the United Kingdom?
      `Are you an officer, employee or auditor of such a subsidiary undertaking` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are you an officer, employee or auditor of such a subsidiary undertaking?
      `Do you hold, or are you accountable for, any books, accounts or vouchers of such a subsidiary undertaking` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Do you hold, or are you accountable for, any books, accounts or vouchers of such a subsidiary undertaking?
      `Were you any of those at a time to which the information or explanations the auditor wants relate` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Were you any of those at a time to which the information or explanations the auditor wants relate?
      `Does the auditor think the information or explanations necessary for the performance of his duties as auditor` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does the auditor think the information or explanations necessary for the performance of his duties as auditor?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 499(1)(b), may the person asking require me to provide information or explanations` IS
    `s 499(1)(b) the auditor may require the person to provide the information or explanations` `Is the person asking an auditor of the company` (`s 499(2) the person is one the auditor may require to provide information or explanations` `Are you an officer or employee of the company` `Do you hold, or are you accountable for, any of the company's books, accounts or vouchers` `Are you a subsidiary undertaking of the company that is a body corporate incorporated in the United Kingdom` `Are you an officer, employee or auditor of such a subsidiary undertaking` `Do you hold, or are you accountable for, any books, accounts or vouchers of such a subsidiary undertaking` `Were you any of those at a time to which the information or explanations the auditor wants relate`) `Does the auditor think the information or explanations necessary for the performance of his duties as auditor`

-- Seat question (officer, employee): Under section 499(3), may a statement I made be used in evidence against me.
@export Under section 499(3), may a statement I made be used in evidence against me?
GIVEN `Was the statement made in response to a requirement under section 499` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Was the statement made in response to a requirement under section 499?
      `Are the proceedings criminal proceedings` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are the proceedings criminal proceedings?
      `Are the proceedings for an offence under section 501` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are the proceedings for an offence under section 501?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 499(3), may a statement I made be used in evidence against me` IS
    `s 499(3) the statement may be used in evidence against the person` `Was the statement made in response to a requirement under section 499` `Are the proceedings criminal proceedings` `Are the proceedings for an offence under section 501`

-- Seat question (officer, employee): Under section 499(4), does section 499 compel me to disclose this information.
@export Under section 499(4), does section 499 compel me to disclose this information?
GIVEN `Could a claim to legal professional privilege (in Scotland, to confidentiality of communications) be maintained in legal proceedings in respect of the information` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Could a claim to legal professional privilege (in Scotland, to confidentiality of communications) be maintained in legal proceedings in respect of the information?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 499(4), does section 499 compel me to disclose this information` IS
    `s 499(4) the section compels the person to disclose the information` `Could a claim to legal professional privilege (in Scotland, to confidentiality of communications) be maintained in legal proceedings in respect of the information`

-- Seat question (director): Under section 500(1), may the auditor require the company to obtain information or explanations from a subsidiary undertaking.
@export Under section 500(1), may the auditor require the company to obtain information or explanations from a subsidiary undertaking?
GIVEN `Is the company a parent company (section 1173(1))` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the company a parent company (section 1173(1))?
      `Is the subsidiary undertaking not a body corporate incorporated in the United Kingdom` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the subsidiary undertaking not a body corporate incorporated in the United Kingdom?
      `Is the person requiring the auditor of the parent company` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the person requiring the auditor of the parent company?
      `Does the auditor reasonably require the information or explanations for the purposes of his duties as auditor` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does the auditor reasonably require the information or explanations for the purposes of his duties as auditor?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 500(1), may the auditor require the company to obtain information or explanations from a subsidiary undertaking` IS
    `s 500(1) the auditor of the parent company may require it to obtain information or explanations` (`coa12 the answer for the fact` `Is the company a parent company (section 1173(1))`) `Is the subsidiary undertaking not a body corporate incorporated in the United Kingdom` `Is the person requiring the auditor of the parent company` `Does the auditor reasonably require the information or explanations for the purposes of his duties as auditor`

-- Seat question (officer, employee): Under section 501(1), do I commit an offence by making a misleading statement to an auditor.
@export Under section 501(1), do I commit an offence by making a misleading statement to an auditor?
GIVEN `Did you make to an auditor of a company a statement (oral or written)` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did you make to an auditor of a company a statement (oral or written)?
      `Did you do so knowingly or recklessly` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did you do so knowingly or recklessly?
      `Did the statement convey, or purport to convey, information or explanations which the auditor requires, or is entitled to require, under section 499` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did the statement convey, or purport to convey, information or explanations which the auditor requires, or is entitled to require, under section 499?
      `Was the statement misleading, false or deceptive in a material particular` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Was the statement misleading, false or deceptive in a material particular?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 501(1), do I commit an offence by making a misleading statement to an auditor` IS
    `s 501(1) the person commits an offence by a misleading statement to an auditor` `Did you make to an auditor of a company a statement (oral or written)` `Did you do so knowingly or recklessly` `Did the statement convey, or purport to convey, information or explanations which the auditor requires, or is entitled to require, under section 499` `Was the statement misleading, false or deceptive in a material particular`

-- Seat question (officer, employee): Under section 501(2), what is the most I can be fined in pounds for a misleading statement to an auditor.
@export Under section 501(2), what is the most I can be fined in pounds for a misleading statement to an auditor?
GIVEN `How were you convicted? One of: "on indictment", "summary, England and Wales", "summary, Scotland", "summary, Northern Ireland", "summary, place not stated".` IS A STRING @desc How were you convicted? One of: "on indictment", "summary, England and Wales", "summary, Scotland", "summary, Northern Ireland", "summary, place not stated".
      `What is the statutory maximum in pounds, as currently set? (The Act does not state it.)` IS A NUMBER @desc What is the statutory maximum in pounds, as currently set? (The Act does not state it.)
      `What is level 3 on the standard scale in pounds, as currently set? (The Act does not state it.)` IS A NUMBER @desc What is level 3 on the standard scale in pounds, as currently set? (The Act does not state it.)
GIVETH A MAYBE NUMBER
DECIDE `Under section 501(2), what is the most I can be fined in pounds for a misleading statement to an auditor` IS
    CONSIDER `coa12 seat the mode of conviction named` `How were you convicted? One of: "on indictment", "summary, England and Wales", "summary, Scotland", "summary, Northern Ireland", "summary, place not stated".`
        WHEN NOTHING THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (silent): the answer names no mode of conviction the Act recognises
        WHEN JUST m THEN
            CONSIDER `s 501(2) the penalty for an offence under subsection (1)` m
            WHEN NOTHING THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): the section states no penalty for this mode of conviction
            WHEN JUST p THEN `coa12 the largest fine the penalty allows, in pounds` p `What is the statutory maximum in pounds, as currently set? (The Act does not state it.)` `What is level 3 on the standard scale in pounds, as currently set? (The Act does not state it.)`

-- Seat question (officer, employee): Under section 501(2), what is the longest term of imprisonment in months for a misleading statement to an auditor.
@export Under section 501(2), what is the longest term of imprisonment in months for a misleading statement to an auditor?
GIVEN `How were you convicted? One of: "on indictment", "summary, England and Wales", "summary, Scotland", "summary, Northern Ireland", "summary, place not stated".` IS A STRING @desc How were you convicted? One of: "on indictment", "summary, England and Wales", "summary, Scotland", "summary, Northern Ireland", "summary, place not stated".
GIVETH A MAYBE NUMBER
DECIDE `Under section 501(2), what is the longest term of imprisonment in months for a misleading statement to an auditor` IS
    CONSIDER `coa12 seat the mode of conviction named` `How were you convicted? One of: "on indictment", "summary, England and Wales", "summary, Scotland", "summary, Northern Ireland", "summary, place not stated".`
        WHEN NOTHING THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (silent): the answer names no mode of conviction the Act recognises
        WHEN JUST m THEN
            CONSIDER `s 501(2) the penalty for an offence under subsection (1)` m
            WHEN NOTHING THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): the section states no penalty for this mode of conviction
            WHEN JUST p THEN
                CONSIDER p's `imprisonment not exceeding`
                WHEN NOTHING THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (silent): no imprisonment is stated
                WHEN JUST per THEN
                    CONSIDER per's unit
                    WHEN Months THEN JUST (per's `number of units`)
                    WHEN Years THEN JUST ((per's `number of units`) TIMES 12)
                    OTHERWISE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (silent): the period is not in months or years

-- Seat question (officer, employee): Under section 501(3), do I commit an offence by failing to comply without delay with an auditor's requirement under section 499.
@export Under section 501(3), do I commit an offence by failing to comply without delay with an auditor's requirement under section 499?
GIVEN `Did you fail to comply with the requirement without delay` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did you fail to comply with the requirement without delay?
      `Was it not reasonably practicable for you to provide the required information or explanations` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Was it not reasonably practicable for you to provide the required information or explanations?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 501(3), do I commit an offence by failing to comply without delay with an auditor's requirement under section 499` IS
    `s 501(3) the person commits an offence by failing to comply with a requirement under section 499` `Did you fail to comply with the requirement without delay` `Was it not reasonably practicable for you to provide the required information or explanations`

-- Seat question (member, director, secretary): Under section 502(2)(a), is the auditor entitled to receive this notice or communication.
@export Under section 502(2)(a), is the auditor entitled to receive this notice or communication?
GIVEN `Does the notice or communication relate to a general meeting of the company` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does the notice or communication relate to a general meeting of the company?
      `Is a member of the company entitled to receive it` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is a member of the company entitled to receive it?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 502(2)(a), is the auditor entitled to receive this notice or communication` IS
    `s 502(2)(a) the auditor is entitled to receive the notice or communication` `Does the notice or communication relate to a general meeting of the company` `Is a member of the company entitled to receive it`

-- Seat question (member, director, secretary): Under section 502(2)(b), is the auditor entitled to attend this meeting.
@export Under section 502(2)(b), is the auditor entitled to attend this meeting?
GIVEN `Is it a general meeting of the company` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it a general meeting of the company?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 502(2)(b), is the auditor entitled to attend this meeting` IS
    `s 502(2)(b) the auditor is entitled to attend the meeting` `Is it a general meeting of the company`

-- Seat question (member, director, secretary): Under section 502(2)(c), is the auditor entitled to be heard at this meeting.
@export Under section 502(2)(c), is the auditor entitled to be heard at this meeting?
GIVEN `Is it a general meeting of the company` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it a general meeting of the company?
      `Does the auditor attend the meeting` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does the auditor attend the meeting?
      `Does that part of the business of the meeting concern him as auditor` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does that part of the business of the meeting concern him as auditor?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 502(2)(c), is the auditor entitled to be heard at this meeting` IS
    `s 502(2)(c) the auditor is entitled to be heard at the meeting on that part of the business` `Is it a general meeting of the company` `Does the auditor attend the meeting` `Does that part of the business of the meeting concern him as auditor`

-- Seat question (auditor, director): Under section 503(3), must the auditor's report be signed by the senior statutory auditor in his own name, for and on behalf of the auditor.
@export Under section 503(3), must the auditor's report be signed by the senior statutory auditor in his own name, for and on behalf of the auditor?
GIVEN `Is the auditor a firm` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the auditor a firm?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 503(3), must the auditor's report be signed by the senior statutory auditor in his own name, for and on behalf of the auditor` IS
    `s 503(3) the report must be signed by the senior statutory auditor in his own name, for and on behalf of the auditor` `Is the auditor a firm`

-- Seat question (auditor): Under section 504(3), am I, as senior statutory auditor, subject to civil liability by reason of being named or having signed the auditor's report.
@export Under section 504(3), am I, as senior statutory auditor, subject to civil liability by reason of being named or having signed the auditor's report?
GIVEN `Would the liability arise only by reason of your being named or identified as senior statutory auditor or your having signed the auditor's report` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Would the liability arise only by reason of your being named or identified as senior statutory auditor or your having signed the auditor's report?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 504(3), am I, as senior statutory auditor, subject to civil liability by reason of being named or having signed the auditor's report` IS
    `s 504(3) the senior statutory auditor is subject to civil liability by reason of being named or having signed` `Would the liability arise only by reason of your being named or identified as senior statutory auditor or your having signed the auditor's report`

-- Seat question (director, secretary): Under section 505(1), does the published copy of the auditor's report have the statement the subsection requires.
@export Under section 505(1), does the published copy of the auditor's report have the statement the subsection requires?
GIVEN `Does the copy state the name of the auditor (where more than one person is appointed, the names of all the auditors)` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does the copy state the name of the auditor (where more than one person is appointed, the names of all the auditors)?
      `Is the auditor a firm` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the auditor a firm?
      `Does the copy state the name of the person who signed it as senior statutory auditor` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does the copy state the name of the person who signed it as senior statutory auditor?
      `Does the copy state that a resolution has been passed and notified to the Secretary of State in accordance with section 506` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does the copy state that a resolution has been passed and notified to the Secretary of State in accordance with section 506?
      `Are the conditions in section 506 for leaving the names out met` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are the conditions in section 506 for leaving the names out met?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 505(1), does the published copy of the auditor's report have the statement the subsection requires` IS
    `s 505(1) the published copy of the auditor's report has the statement the subsection requires` `Does the copy state the name of the auditor (where more than one person is appointed, the names of all the auditors)` `Is the auditor a firm` `Does the copy state the name of the person who signed it as senior statutory auditor` `Does the copy state that a resolution has been passed and notified to the Secretary of State in accordance with section 506` (`coa12 the answer for the fact` `Are the conditions in section 506 for leaving the names out met`)

-- Seat question (director, secretary): Under section 505(3)(a), does the company commit an offence by publishing a copy of the auditor's report without the required statement.
@export Under section 505(3)(a), does the company commit an offence by publishing a copy of the auditor's report without the required statement?
GIVEN `Was a copy of the auditor's report published without the statement required by section 505` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Was a copy of the auditor's report published without the statement required by section 505?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 505(3)(a), does the company commit an offence by publishing a copy of the auditor's report without the required statement` IS
    `s 505(3)(a) the company commits an offence` `Was a copy of the auditor's report published without the statement required by section 505`

-- Seat question (director, secretary): Under section 505(3)(b), does an officer of the company commit an offence by the publication of a copy without the required statement.
@export Under section 505(3)(b), does an officer of the company commit an offence by the publication of a copy without the required statement?
GIVEN `Was a copy of the auditor's report published without the statement required by section 505` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Was a copy of the auditor's report published without the statement required by section 505?
      `Is the officer in default (section 1121)` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the officer in default (section 1121)?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 505(3)(b), does an officer of the company commit an offence by the publication of a copy without the required statement` IS
    `s 505(3)(b) the officer of the company commits an offence` `Was a copy of the auditor's report published without the statement required by section 505` (`coa12 the answer for the fact` `Is the officer in default (section 1121)`)

-- Seat question (director, secretary): Under section 506(2), are the conditions met for leaving the auditor's name out of published copies of the report.
@export Under section 506(2), are the conditions met for leaving the auditor's name out of published copies of the report?
GIVEN `Does the company consider, on reasonable grounds, that stating the name would create or be likely to create a serious risk that the auditor, the senior statutory auditor or any other person would be subject to violence or intimidation` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does the company consider, on reasonable grounds, that stating the name would create or be likely to create a serious risk that the auditor, the senior statutory auditor or any other person would be subject to violence or intimidation?
      `Has the company resolved that the name should not be stated` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has the company resolved that the name should not be stated?
      `Has the company given notice of the resolution to the Secretary of State` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has the company given notice of the resolution to the Secretary of State?
      `Does the notice state the name and registered number of the company` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does the notice state the name and registered number of the company?
      `Does the notice state the financial year of the company to which the report relates` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does the notice state the financial year of the company to which the report relates?
      `Does the notice state the name of the auditor and (where the auditor is a firm) the name of the person who signed the report as senior statutory auditor` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does the notice state the name of the auditor and (where the auditor is a firm) the name of the person who signed the report as senior statutory auditor?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 506(2), are the conditions met for leaving the auditor's name out of published copies of the report` IS
    `s 506(2) the conditions for omitting the names are met` `Does the company consider, on reasonable grounds, that stating the name would create or be likely to create a serious risk that the auditor, the senior statutory auditor or any other person would be subject to violence or intimidation` `Has the company resolved that the name should not be stated` `Has the company given notice of the resolution to the Secretary of State` `Does the notice state the name and registered number of the company` `Does the notice state the financial year of the company to which the report relates` `Does the notice state the name of the auditor and (where the auditor is a firm) the name of the person who signed the report as senior statutory auditor`

-- Seat question (auditor, employee of auditor): Under section 507(1), do I commit an offence by causing the auditor's report to include a misleading matter.
@export Under section 507(1), do I commit an offence by causing the auditor's report to include a misleading matter?
GIVEN `Is the auditor an individual` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the auditor an individual?
      `Are you that individual` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are you that individual?
      `Are you an employee or agent of that individual` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are you an employee or agent of that individual?
      `Is the auditor a firm` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the auditor a firm?
      `Are you a director, member, employee or agent of the firm` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are you a director, member, employee or agent of the firm?
      `Are you eligible for appointment as auditor of the company` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are you eligible for appointment as auditor of the company?
      `Did you cause a report under section 495 to include a matter that is misleading, false or deceptive in a material particular` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did you cause a report under section 495 to include a matter that is misleading, false or deceptive in a material particular?
      `Did you do so knowingly or recklessly` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did you do so knowingly or recklessly?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 507(1), do I commit an offence by causing the auditor's report to include a misleading matter` IS
    `s 507(1) the person commits an offence by causing the report to include a misleading matter` (`s 507(3) the person is a person to whom section 507 applies` `Is the auditor an individual` `Are you that individual` `Are you an employee or agent of that individual` `Is the auditor a firm` `Are you a director, member, employee or agent of the firm` (`coa12 the answer for the fact` `Are you eligible for appointment as auditor of the company`)) `Did you cause a report under section 495 to include a matter that is misleading, false or deceptive in a material particular` `Did you do so knowingly or recklessly`

-- Seat question (auditor, employee of auditor): Under section 507(4), what is the most I can be fined in pounds for an offence in connection with the auditor's report.
@export Under section 507(4), what is the most I can be fined in pounds for an offence in connection with the auditor's report?
GIVEN `How were you convicted? One of: "on indictment", "summary, England and Wales", "summary, Scotland", "summary, Northern Ireland", "summary, place not stated".` IS A STRING @desc How were you convicted? One of: "on indictment", "summary, England and Wales", "summary, Scotland", "summary, Northern Ireland", "summary, place not stated".
      `What is the statutory maximum in pounds, as currently set? (The Act does not state it.)` IS A NUMBER @desc What is the statutory maximum in pounds, as currently set? (The Act does not state it.)
      `What is level 3 on the standard scale in pounds, as currently set? (The Act does not state it.)` IS A NUMBER @desc What is level 3 on the standard scale in pounds, as currently set? (The Act does not state it.)
GIVETH A MAYBE NUMBER
DECIDE `Under section 507(4), what is the most I can be fined in pounds for an offence in connection with the auditor's report` IS
    CONSIDER `coa12 seat the mode of conviction named` `How were you convicted? One of: "on indictment", "summary, England and Wales", "summary, Scotland", "summary, Northern Ireland", "summary, place not stated".`
        WHEN NOTHING THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (silent): the answer names no mode of conviction the Act recognises
        WHEN JUST m THEN
            CONSIDER `s 507(4) the penalty for an offence under section 507` m
            WHEN NOTHING THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): the section states no penalty for this mode of conviction
            WHEN JUST p THEN `coa12 the largest fine the penalty allows, in pounds` p `What is the statutory maximum in pounds, as currently set? (The Act does not state it.)` `What is level 3 on the standard scale in pounds, as currently set? (The Act does not state it.)`

§§ `Chapter 4 -- removal, resignation, etc of auditors (ss 510 to 526)`

-- Ask these when an auditor is being removed, is not being re-appointed, resigns or otherwise ceases to hold office. A form should first ask "Is an auditor ceasing to hold office?".

-- Seat question (member, director): Under section 510(2), have the members exercised the power to remove the auditor in the way the subsection requires.
@export Under section 510(2), have the members exercised the power to remove the auditor in the way the subsection requires?
GIVEN `Was the resolution passed as an ordinary resolution` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Was the resolution passed as an ordinary resolution?
      `Was the resolution passed as a special resolution` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Was the resolution passed as a special resolution?
      `Was the resolution passed at a meeting` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Was the resolution passed at a meeting?
      `Was special notice given in accordance with section 511` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Was special notice given in accordance with section 511?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 510(2), have the members exercised the power to remove the auditor in the way the subsection requires` IS
    `s 510(2) the power to remove the auditor has been exercised as the subsection requires` (`coa12 the answer for the fact` `Was the resolution passed as an ordinary resolution`) (`coa12 the answer for the fact` `Was the resolution passed as a special resolution`) `Was the resolution passed at a meeting` `Was special notice given in accordance with section 511`

-- Seat question (member, director): Under section 510(4), is the auditor barred from removal from office before the expiration of his term of office.
@export Under section 510(4), is the auditor barred from removal from office before the expiration of his term of office?
GIVEN `Would the removal be before the expiration of his term of office` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Would the removal be before the expiration of his term of office?
      `Is the auditor removed by resolution under section 510` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the auditor removed by resolution under section 510?
      `Is the auditor removed in accordance with section 511A` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the auditor removed in accordance with section 511A?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 510(4), is the auditor barred from removal from office before the expiration of his term of office` IS
    `s 510(4) the auditor is barred from removal before the expiration of his term of office` `Would the removal be before the expiration of his term of office` `Is the auditor removed by resolution under section 510` `Is the auditor removed in accordance with section 511A`

-- Seat question (director, secretary): Under section 511(2), must the company immediately send a copy of the notice to the auditor proposed to be removed.
@export Under section 511(2), must the company immediately send a copy of the notice to the auditor proposed to be removed?
GIVEN `Has the company received notice of an intended resolution to remove an auditor from office` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has the company received notice of an intended resolution to remove an auditor from office?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 511(2), must the company immediately send a copy of the notice to the auditor proposed to be removed` IS
    `s 511(2) the company must immediately send a copy of the notice to the auditor proposed to be removed` `Has the company received notice of an intended resolution to remove an auditor from office`

-- Seat question (director, secretary): Under section 511(4), must the company state the fact of any representations in its notice and send a copy to every member to whom notice is sent.
@export Under section 511(4), must the company state the fact of any representations in its notice and send a copy to every member to whom notice is sent?
GIVEN `Has the auditor made representations under section 511(3)` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has the auditor made representations under section 511(3)?
      `Were the representations received by the company too late for it to do so` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Were the representations received by the company too late for it to do so?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 511(4), must the company state the fact of any representations in its notice and send a copy to every member to whom notice is sent` IS
    `s 511(4) the company must state the fact of the representations in its notice and send a copy to every member to whom notice is sent` `Has the auditor made representations under section 511(3)` `Were the representations received by the company too late for it to do so`

-- Seat question (member): Under section 511A(3), may the applicants apply to the court for an order removing the auditor.
@export Under section 511A(3), may the applicants apply to the court for an order removing the auditor?
GIVEN `Is the company a public interest company (section 519A)` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the company a public interest company (section 519A)?
      `Are the applicants members of the company` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are the applicants members of the company?
      `Do the applicant or applicants consider that there are proper grounds for removing the auditor from office` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Do the applicant or applicants consider that there are proper grounds for removing the auditor from office?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 511A(3), may the applicants apply to the court for an order removing the auditor` IS
    `s 511A(3) the members may apply to the court for an order removing the auditor` (`s 511A(1) the section applies to the company` (`coa12 the answer for the fact` `Is the company a public interest company (section 519A)`)) `Are the applicants members of the company` `Do the applicant or applicants consider that there are proper grounds for removing the auditor from office`

-- Seat question (member): Under section 511A(5), may the court make an order removing the auditor on the members' application.
@export Under section 511A(5), may the court make an order removing the auditor on the members' application?
GIVEN `As a fraction of the voting rights of all the members having a right to vote at a general meeting (for 5%, write 0.05), how much do the applicants represent in total` IS A NUMBER @desc As a fraction of the voting rights of all the members having a right to vote at a general meeting (for 5%, write 0.05), how much do the applicants represent in total?
      `As a fraction of the company's share capital in nominal value (for 5%, write 0.05), how much do the applicants represent in total` IS A NUMBER @desc As a fraction of the company's share capital in nominal value (for 5%, write 0.05), how much do the applicants represent in total?
      `Is the court satisfied that there are proper grounds for removing the auditor from office` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the court satisfied that there are proper grounds for removing the auditor from office?
      `Is the ground only a divergence of opinions on accounting treatments or audit procedures` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the ground only a divergence of opinions on accounting treatments or audit procedures?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 511A(5), may the court make an order removing the auditor on the members' application` IS
    `s 511A(5) the court may make an order removing the auditor on the members' application` `As a fraction of the voting rights of all the members having a right to vote at a general meeting (for 5%, write 0.05), how much do the applicants represent in total` `As a fraction of the company's share capital in nominal value (for 5%, write 0.05), how much do the applicants represent in total` `Is the court satisfied that there are proper grounds for removing the auditor from office` `Is the ground only a divergence of opinions on accounting treatments or audit procedures`

-- Seat question (member, director, secretary): Under section 513(1), does the auditor have the rights conferred by section 502(2) in relation to this meeting.
@export Under section 513(1), does the auditor have the rights conferred by section 502(2) in relation to this meeting?
GIVEN `Was the auditor removed by resolution under section 510` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Was the auditor removed by resolution under section 510?
      `Was the auditor removed by order of the court under section 511A` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Was the auditor removed by order of the court under section 511A?
      `Is it a general meeting at which his term of office would otherwise have expired` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it a general meeting at which his term of office would otherwise have expired?
      `Is it a general meeting at which it is proposed to fill the vacancy caused by his removal` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it a general meeting at which it is proposed to fill the vacancy caused by his removal?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 513(1), does the auditor have the rights conferred by section 502(2) in relation to this meeting` IS
    `s 513(1) the removed auditor has the rights conferred by section 502(2) in relation to the meeting` `Was the auditor removed by resolution under section 510` `Was the auditor removed by order of the court under section 511A` `Is it a general meeting at which his term of office would otherwise have expired` `Is it a general meeting at which it is proposed to fill the vacancy caused by his removal`

-- Seat question (director, secretary, member): Under section 514(1), does section 514 apply to this proposed resolution.
@export Under section 514(1), does section 514 apply to this proposed resolution?
GIVEN `Is the company a private company` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the company a private company?
      `Is the resolution proposed as a written resolution` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the resolution proposed as a written resolution?
      `Would the resolution appoint a person as auditor in place of the outgoing auditor` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Would the resolution appoint a person as auditor in place of the outgoing auditor?
      `Is the outgoing auditor, at the time the resolution is proposed, an auditor of the company` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the outgoing auditor, at the time the resolution is proposed, an auditor of the company?
      `Is the outgoing auditor to cease to hold office at the end of a period for appointing auditors` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the outgoing auditor to cease to hold office at the end of a period for appointing auditors?
      `Is the auditor to cease to hold office by virtue of section 510, 511A or 516` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the auditor to cease to hold office by virtue of section 510, 511A or 516?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 514(1), does section 514 apply to this proposed resolution` IS
    `s 514(1) the section applies where the outgoing auditor is to cease to hold office at the end of a period for appointing auditors` `Is the company a private company` (`coa12 the answer for the fact` `Is the resolution proposed as a written resolution`) `Would the resolution appoint a person as auditor in place of the outgoing auditor` `Is the outgoing auditor, at the time the resolution is proposed, an auditor of the company` `Is the outgoing auditor to cease to hold office at the end of a period for appointing auditors` `Is the auditor to cease to hold office by virtue of section 510, 511A or 516`

-- Seat question (director, secretary, member): Under section 514(8), is the resolution ineffective.
@export Under section 514(8), is the resolution ineffective?
GIVEN `Is any requirement of section 514 not complied with` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is any requirement of section 514 not complied with?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 514(8), is the resolution ineffective` IS
    `s 514(8) the resolution is ineffective` `Is any requirement of section 514 not complied with`

-- Seat question (director, secretary, member): Under section 515(1), is special notice required for this resolution.
@export Under section 515(1), is special notice required for this resolution?
GIVEN `Is the company a private company` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the company a private company?
      `Is the resolution one at a general meeting` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the resolution one at a general meeting?
      `Would the resolution appoint a person as auditor in place of the outgoing auditor` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Would the resolution appoint a person as auditor in place of the outgoing auditor?
      `Is the outgoing auditor, at the time the notice is given, an auditor of the company` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the outgoing auditor, at the time the notice is given, an auditor of the company?
      `Is the outgoing auditor to cease to hold office at the end of a period for appointing auditors` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the outgoing auditor to cease to hold office at the end of a period for appointing auditors?
      `Is the auditor to cease to hold office by virtue of section 510, 511A or 516` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the auditor to cease to hold office by virtue of section 510, 511A or 516?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 515(1), is special notice required for this resolution` IS
    `s 515(1) special notice is required for the resolution of a private company` `Is the company a private company` `Is the resolution one at a general meeting` `Would the resolution appoint a person as auditor in place of the outgoing auditor` `Is the outgoing auditor, at the time the notice is given, an auditor of the company` `Is the outgoing auditor to cease to hold office at the end of a period for appointing auditors` `Is the auditor to cease to hold office by virtue of section 510, 511A or 516`

-- Seat question (auditor, director): Under section 516(2), is the auditor's notice of resignation not effective.
@export Under section 516(2), is the auditor's notice of resignation not effective?
GIVEN `Is the company a public interest company` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the company a public interest company?
      `Is the notice accompanied by the statement required by section 519` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the notice accompanied by the statement required by section 519?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 516(2), is the auditor's notice of resignation not effective` IS
    `s 516(2) the notice of resignation is not effective` (`coa12 the answer for the fact` `Is the company a public interest company`) `Is the notice accompanied by the statement required by section 519`

-- Seat question (auditor, director): Under section 516(3), on what day does the auditor's term of office end.
@export Under section 516(3), on what day does the auditor's term of office end?
GIVEN `Is the notice of resignation effective` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the notice of resignation effective?
      `On what date does the company receive the notice` IS A DATE @desc On what date does the company receive the notice?
      `Does the notice specify a later date` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does the notice specify a later date?
      `What later date does the notice specify? (Any date if it specifies none.)` IS A DATE @desc What later date does the notice specify? (Any date if it specifies none.)
GIVETH A MAYBE DATE
DECIDE `Under section 516(3), on what day does the auditor's term of office end` IS
    `s 516(3) the day on which the auditor's term of office ends` `Is the notice of resignation effective` `On what date does the company receive the notice` (IF `Does the notice specify a later date` THEN JUST `What later date does the notice specify? (Any date if it specifies none.)` ELSE NOTHING)

-- Seat question (director): Under section 518(5), must the directors convene the meeting.
@export Under section 518(5), must the directors convene the meeting?
GIVEN `Is the auditor's notice of resignation accompanied by a statement under section 519` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the auditor's notice of resignation accompanied by a statement under section 519?
      `Is the company a non-public interest company` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the company a non-public interest company?
      `Does the statement say that the auditor considers that none of the reasons for his ceasing to hold office, and no matters connected with it, need to be brought to the attention of members or creditors` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does the statement say that the auditor considers that none of the reasons for his ceasing to hold office, and no matters connected with it, need to be brought to the attention of members or creditors?
      `Has the company received a requisition under section 518` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has the company received a requisition under section 518?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 518(5), must the directors convene the meeting` IS
    `s 518(5) the directors must convene the meeting` (`s 518(1) the section applies to the resigning auditor` `Is the auditor's notice of resignation accompanied by a statement under section 519` (`coa12 the answer for the fact` `Is the company a non-public interest company`) `Does the statement say that the auditor considers that none of the reasons for his ceasing to hold office, and no matters connected with it, need to be brought to the attention of members or creditors`) `Has the company received a requisition under section 518`

-- Seat question (director): Under section 518(5), have the directors convened the meeting within the periods the subsection allows.
@export Under section 518(5), have the directors convened the meeting within the periods the subsection allows?
GIVEN `On what date did the company receive the requisition` IS A DATE @desc On what date did the company receive the requisition?
      `Has a notice convening the meeting been given` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has a notice convening the meeting been given?
      `On what date was the notice convening the meeting given? (Any date if none.)` IS A DATE @desc On what date was the notice convening the meeting given? (Any date if none.)
      `For what day is the meeting convened` IS A DATE @desc For what day is the meeting convened?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 518(5), have the directors convened the meeting within the periods the subsection allows` IS
    `s 518(5) the directors convened the meeting within the periods the subsection allows` `On what date did the company receive the requisition` (IF `Has a notice convening the meeting been given` THEN JUST `On what date was the notice convening the meeting given? (Any date if none.)` ELSE NOTHING) `For what day is the meeting convened`

-- Seat question (director): Under section 518(6), does a director commit an offence by default in convening the meeting.
@export Under section 518(6), does a director commit an offence by default in convening the meeting?
GIVEN `Is default made in complying with section 518(5)` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is default made in complying with section 518(5)?
      `Did the director fail to take all reasonable steps to secure that a meeting was convened` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did the director fail to take all reasonable steps to secure that a meeting was convened?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 518(6), does a director commit an offence by default in convening the meeting` IS
    `s 518(6) the director commits an offence` `Is default made in complying with section 518(5)` `Did the director fail to take all reasonable steps to secure that a meeting was convened`

-- Seat question (auditor): Under section 519(1), must the auditor send the company a statement of the reasons.
@export Under section 519(1), must the auditor send the company a statement of the reasons?
GIVEN `Is the company a public interest company` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the company a public interest company?
      `Is the auditor ceasing to hold office (at any time and for any reason)` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the auditor ceasing to hold office (at any time and for any reason)?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 519(1), must the auditor send the company a statement of the reasons` IS
    `s 519(1) the auditor of a public interest company must send the company a statement of the reasons` (`coa12 the answer for the fact` `Is the company a public interest company`) `Is the auditor ceasing to hold office (at any time and for any reason)`

-- Seat question (auditor): Under section 519(2), must the auditor send the company a statement of the reasons.
@export Under section 519(2), must the auditor send the company a statement of the reasons?
GIVEN `Is the company a non-public interest company` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the company a non-public interest company?
      `Is the auditor ceasing to hold office` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the auditor ceasing to hold office?
      `Is the auditor ceasing at the end of a private company's period for appointing auditors, or at the end of a public company's accounts meeting` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the auditor ceasing at the end of a private company's period for appointing auditors, or at the end of a public company's accounts meeting?
      `Are all his reasons for ceasing exempt reasons and are there no matters he considers need to be brought to the attention of members or creditors` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are all his reasons for ceasing exempt reasons and are there no matters he considers need to be brought to the attention of members or creditors?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 519(2), must the auditor send the company a statement of the reasons` IS
    `s 519(2) the auditor of a non-public interest company must send the company a statement of the reasons` (`coa12 the answer for the fact` `Is the company a non-public interest company`) `Is the auditor ceasing to hold office` (`coa12 the answer for the fact` `Is the auditor ceasing at the end of a private company's period for appointing auditors, or at the end of a public company's accounts meeting`) (`coa12 the answer for the fact` `Are all his reasons for ceasing exempt reasons and are there no matters he considers need to be brought to the attention of members or creditors`)

-- Seat question (auditor): Under section 519(4)(b), was the statement sent in time on a failure to seek re-appointment.
@export Under section 519(4)(b), was the statement sent in time on a failure to seek re-appointment?
GIVEN `On what date was the statement sent` IS A DATE @desc On what date was the statement sent?
      `What is the end of the time allowed for next appointing an auditor` IS A DATE @desc What is the end of the time allowed for next appointing an auditor?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 519(4)(b), was the statement sent in time on a failure to seek re-appointment` IS
    `s 519(4)(b) the statement was sent in time on a failure to seek re-appointment` `On what date was the statement sent` `What is the end of the time allowed for next appointing an auditor`

-- Seat question (auditor): Under section 519(4)(c), was the statement sent in time in any other case.
@export Under section 519(4)(c), was the statement sent in time in any other case?
GIVEN `On what date did he cease to hold office` IS A DATE @desc On what date did he cease to hold office?
      `On what date was the statement sent` IS A DATE @desc On what date was the statement sent?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 519(4)(c), was the statement sent in time in any other case` IS
    `s 519(4)(c) the statement was sent in time in any other case` `On what date did he cease to hold office` `On what date was the statement sent`

-- Seat question (director, secretary, member, auditor): Under section 519A(1), is the company a public interest company.
@export Under section 519A(1), is the company a public interest company?
GIVEN `Is the company an issuer within the meaning of Part 6 of the Financial Services and Markets Act 2000 (section 102A(6))` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the company an issuer within the meaning of Part 6 of the Financial Services and Markets Act 2000 (section 102A(6))?
      `Are its transferable securities admitted to trading on a UK regulated market` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are its transferable securities admitted to trading on a UK regulated market?
      `Is it a credit institution within the meaning given by Article 4(1)(1) of Regulation (EU) No. 575/2013` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it a credit institution within the meaning given by Article 4(1)(1) of Regulation (EU) No. 575/2013?
      `Is it a CRR firm within the meaning of Article 4(1)(2A) of that Regulation` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it a CRR firm within the meaning of Article 4(1)(2A) of that Regulation?
      `Is it a person who would be an insurance undertaking as defined in Article 2(1) of Council Directive 91/674/EEC were the United Kingdom a member State` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it a person who would be an insurance undertaking as defined in Article 2(1) of Council Directive 91/674/EEC were the United Kingdom a member State?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 519A(1), is the company a public interest company` IS
    `s 519A(1) the company is a public interest company` (`coa12 the answer for the fact` `Is the company an issuer within the meaning of Part 6 of the Financial Services and Markets Act 2000 (section 102A(6))`) `Are its transferable securities admitted to trading on a UK regulated market` (`coa12 the answer for the fact` `Is it a credit institution within the meaning given by Article 4(1)(1) of Regulation (EU) No. 575/2013`) (`coa12 the answer for the fact` `Is it a CRR firm within the meaning of Article 4(1)(2A) of that Regulation`) (`coa12 the answer for the fact` `Is it a person who would be an insurance undertaking as defined in Article 2(1) of Council Directive 91/674/EEC were the United Kingdom a member State`)

-- Seat question (director, secretary): Under section 520(2), must the company send a copy of the auditor's statement to the persons entitled to the accounts or apply to the court.
@export Under section 520(2), must the company send a copy of the auditor's statement to the persons entitled to the accounts or apply to the court?
GIVEN `Has the company received from an auditor who is ceasing to hold office a statement under section 519` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has the company received from an auditor who is ceasing to hold office a statement under section 519?
      `Is the company a non-public interest company` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the company a non-public interest company?
      `Does the statement say that the auditor considers that none of the reasons for his ceasing to hold office, and no matters connected with it, need to be brought to the attention of members or creditors` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does the statement say that the auditor considers that none of the reasons for his ceasing to hold office, and no matters connected with it, need to be brought to the attention of members or creditors?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 520(2), must the company send a copy of the auditor's statement to the persons entitled to the accounts or apply to the court` IS
    `s 520(2) the company must either send a copy of the statement or apply to the court` (`s 520(1) the section applies to the company` `Has the company received from an auditor who is ceasing to hold office a statement under section 519` (`coa12 the answer for the fact` `Is the company a non-public interest company`) `Does the statement say that the auditor considers that none of the reasons for his ceasing to hold office, and no matters connected with it, need to be brought to the attention of members or creditors`)

-- Seat question (director, secretary): Under section 520(2), did the company act within 14 days of receiving the auditor's statement.
@export Under section 520(2), did the company act within 14 days of receiving the auditor's statement?
GIVEN `On what date did the company receive the statement` IS A DATE @desc On what date did the company receive the statement?
      `Did the company send a copy of it to the persons entitled to the accounts, or apply to the court` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did the company send a copy of it to the persons entitled to the accounts, or apply to the court?
      `On what date did it do so? (Any date if it did neither.)` IS A DATE @desc On what date did it do so? (Any date if it did neither.)
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 520(2), did the company act within 14 days of receiving the auditor's statement` IS
    `s 520(2) the company acted within 14 days of the receipt of the statement` `On what date did the company receive the statement` (IF `Did the company send a copy of it to the persons entitled to the accounts, or apply to the court` THEN JUST `On what date did it do so? (Any date if it did neither.)` ELSE NOTHING) NOTHING

-- Seat question (director, secretary): Under section 520(6), does an officer of the company commit an offence by default in complying with section 520.
@export Under section 520(6), does an officer of the company commit an offence by default in complying with section 520?
GIVEN `Is default made in complying with section 520` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is default made in complying with section 520?
      `Is the officer in default (section 1121)` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the officer in default (section 1121)?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 520(6), does an officer of the company commit an offence by default in complying with section 520` IS
    `s 520(6) the officer of the company commits an offence` `Is default made in complying with section 520` (`coa12 the answer for the fact` `Is the officer in default (section 1121)`)

-- Seat question (auditor): Under section 521(1), must the auditor send a copy of the statement to the registrar.
@export Under section 521(1), must the auditor send a copy of the statement to the registrar?
GIVEN `Has the auditor of a company sent a statement to the company under section 519` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has the auditor of a company sent a statement to the company under section 519?
      `Is the company a non-public interest company` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the company a non-public interest company?
      `Does the statement say that the auditor considers that none of the reasons for his ceasing to hold office, and no matters connected with it, need to be brought to the attention of members or creditors` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does the statement say that the auditor considers that none of the reasons for his ceasing to hold office, and no matters connected with it, need to be brought to the attention of members or creditors?
      `Within 21 days beginning with the day he sent the statement, did the auditor receive notice of an application to the court under section 520` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Within 21 days beginning with the day he sent the statement, did the auditor receive notice of an application to the court under section 520?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 521(1), must the auditor send a copy of the statement to the registrar` IS
    `s 521(1) the auditor must send a copy of the statement to the registrar` (`s 521(A1) the section applies to the auditor` `Has the auditor of a company sent a statement to the company under section 519` (`coa12 the answer for the fact` `Is the company a non-public interest company`) `Does the statement say that the auditor considers that none of the reasons for his ceasing to hold office, and no matters connected with it, need to be brought to the attention of members or creditors`) `Within 21 days beginning with the day he sent the statement, did the auditor receive notice of an application to the court under section 520`

-- Seat question (auditor): Under section 522(1), must the auditor send a copy of the statement to the appropriate audit authority at the same time.
@export Under section 522(1), must the auditor send a copy of the statement to the appropriate audit authority at the same time?
GIVEN `Does an auditor of a company send a statement under section 519` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does an auditor of a company send a statement under section 519?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 522(1), must the auditor send a copy of the statement to the appropriate audit authority at the same time` IS
    `s 522(1) the auditor must at the same time send a copy of the statement to the appropriate audit authority` `Does an auditor of a company send a statement under section 519`

-- Seat question (director, secretary): Under section 523(2), must the company give notice to the appropriate audit authority that the auditor is ceasing to hold office.
@export Under section 523(2), must the company give notice to the appropriate audit authority that the auditor is ceasing to hold office?
GIVEN `Is the company a public company` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the company a public company?
      `Is the auditor ceasing at the end of a period for appointing auditors` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the auditor ceasing at the end of a period for appointing auditors?
      `Is the auditor ceasing at the end of an accounts meeting` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the auditor ceasing at the end of an accounts meeting?
      `Does the company reasonably believe that the only reasons for the auditor's ceasing to hold office are exempt reasons (section 519A(3))` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does the company reasonably believe that the only reasons for the auditor's ceasing to hold office are exempt reasons (section 519A(3))?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 523(2), must the company give notice to the appropriate audit authority that the auditor is ceasing to hold office` IS
    `s 523(2) the company must give notice to the appropriate audit authority that the auditor is ceasing to hold office` (`s 523(1) the section applies where the auditor is ceasing to hold office` (NOT `Is the company a public company`) (`coa12 the answer for the fact` `Is the auditor ceasing at the end of a period for appointing auditors`) `Is the company a public company` (`coa12 the answer for the fact` `Is the auditor ceasing at the end of an accounts meeting`)) (`s 523(1A) the section does not apply` `Does the company reasonably believe that the only reasons for the auditor's ceasing to hold office are exempt reasons (section 519A(3))`)

-- Seat question (director, secretary): Under section 523(3), did the company give the notice within the period of 28 days beginning with the day the auditor ceased to hold office.
@export Under section 523(3), did the company give the notice within the period of 28 days beginning with the day the auditor ceased to hold office?
GIVEN `On what day did the auditor cease to hold office` IS A DATE @desc On what day did the auditor cease to hold office?
      `Did the company give the notice` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did the company give the notice?
      `On what date was the notice given? (Any date if it was not given.)` IS A DATE @desc On what date was the notice given? (Any date if it was not given.)
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 523(3), did the company give the notice within the period of 28 days beginning with the day the auditor ceased to hold office` IS
    `s 523(3) the notice was given within the period of 28 days beginning with the day on which the auditor ceases to hold office` `On what day did the auditor cease to hold office` (IF `Did the company give the notice` THEN JUST `On what date was the notice given? (Any date if it was not given.)` ELSE NOTHING)

-- Seat question (director, secretary, auditor): Under section 525(1), who is the appropriate audit authority.
@export Under section 525(1), who is the appropriate audit authority?
GIVEN `Is the company a public interest company` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the company a public interest company?
      `Is the auditor an Auditor General` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the auditor an Auditor General?
      `Has the Secretary of State delegated functions under section 1252 to a body whose functions include receiving the statement or notice` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has the Secretary of State delegated functions under section 1252 to a body whose functions include receiving the statement or notice?
      `Is the audit a major audit` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the audit a major audit?
GIVETH A MAYBE (LIST OF STRING)
DECIDE `Under section 525(1), who is the appropriate audit authority` IS
    CONSIDER `s 525(1) the appropriate audit authority` (`coa12 the answer for the fact` `Is the company a public interest company`) `Is the auditor an Auditor General` `Has the Secretary of State delegated functions under section 1252 to a body whose functions include receiving the statement or notice` `Is the audit a major audit`
        WHEN NOTHING THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (points outside the text): carried from section 525(1)
        WHEN JUST authorities THEN JUST (map `coa12 seat the words for the audit authority` authorities)

-- Seat question (auditor): Under section 526, may the auditor continue to act.
@export Under section 526, may the auditor continue to act?
GIVEN `Has an auditor ceased to hold office for any reason` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has an auditor ceased to hold office for any reason?
      `Are you a surviving or continuing auditor` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are you a surviving or continuing auditor?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 526, may the auditor continue to act` IS
    `s 526 the surviving or continuing auditor may continue to act` `Has an auditor ceased to hold office for any reason` `Are you a surviving or continuing auditor`

§§ `Chapter 5 -- quoted companies: right of members to raise audit concerns at accounts meeting (ss 527 to 531)`

-- Ask these of a quoted company only; a form should first ask "Is the company a quoted company?".

-- Seat question (member): Under section 527(1), may the members require the company to publish a statement on a website.
@export Under section 527(1), may the members require the company to publish a statement on a website?
GIVEN `Is the company a quoted company` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the company a quoted company?
      `Does the statement set out a matter relating to the audit of the accounts to be laid before the next accounts meeting (including the auditor's report and the conduct of the audit)` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does the statement set out a matter relating to the audit of the accounts to be laid before the next accounts meeting (including the auditor's report and the conduct of the audit)?
      `Does the statement set out a matter relating to circumstances connected with an auditor ceasing to hold office since the previous accounts meeting` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does the statement set out a matter relating to circumstances connected with an auditor ceasing to hold office since the previous accounts meeting?
      `Do the members propose to raise the matter at the next accounts meeting` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Do the members propose to raise the matter at the next accounts meeting?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 527(1), may the members require the company to publish a statement on a website` IS
    `s 527(1) the members may require the company to publish the statement on a website` (`coa12 the answer for the fact` `Is the company a quoted company`) `Does the statement set out a matter relating to the audit of the accounts to be laid before the next accounts meeting (including the auditor's report and the conduct of the audit)` `Does the statement set out a matter relating to circumstances connected with an auditor ceasing to hold office since the previous accounts meeting` `Do the members propose to raise the matter at the next accounts meeting`

-- Seat question (member, director): Under section 527(2), is the company required to publish the statement on a website.
@export Under section 527(2), is the company required to publish the statement on a website?
GIVEN `As a fraction of the total voting rights of all the members who have a right to vote at the accounts meeting (treasury shares left out; for 5%, write 0.05), how much do the requesting members represent` IS A NUMBER @desc As a fraction of the total voting rights of all the members who have a right to vote at the accounts meeting (treasury shares left out; for 5%, write 0.05), how much do the requesting members represent?
      `How many of the requesting members have a right to vote at the accounts meeting and hold shares in the company` IS A NUMBER @desc How many of the requesting members have a right to vote at the accounts meeting and hold shares in the company?
      `What average sum, in pounds, has been paid up per member on the shares those members hold` IS A NUMBER @desc What average sum, in pounds, has been paid up per member on the shares those members hold?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 527(2), is the company required to publish the statement on a website` IS
    `s 527(2) the company is required to publish the statement on a website` `As a fraction of the total voting rights of all the members who have a right to vote at the accounts meeting (treasury shares left out; for 5%, write 0.05), how much do the requesting members represent` `How many of the requesting members have a right to vote at the accounts meeting and hold shares in the company` `What average sum, in pounds, has been paid up per member on the shares those members hold`

-- Seat question (member, director): Under section 527(4), is the request a valid request.
@export Under section 527(4), is the request a valid request?
GIVEN `Was the request sent in electronic form (rather than hard copy)` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Was the request sent in electronic form (rather than hard copy)?
      `Does the request identify the statement to which it relates` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does the request identify the statement to which it relates?
      `Is the request authenticated by the person or persons making it (section 1146)` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the request authenticated by the person or persons making it (section 1146)?
      `On what date did the company receive the request` IS A DATE @desc On what date did the company receive the request?
      `On what date is the meeting to which the request relates` IS A DATE @desc On what date is the meeting to which the request relates?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 527(4), is the request a valid request` IS
    `s 527(4) the request is a valid request` (IF `Was the request sent in electronic form (rather than hard copy)` THEN `electronic form` ELSE `hard copy form`) `Does the request identify the statement to which it relates` (`coa12 the answer for the fact` `Is the request authenticated by the person or persons making it (section 1146)`) `On what date did the company receive the request` `On what date is the meeting to which the request relates`

-- Seat question (member, director): Under section 527(5), is the quoted company required to place the statement on a website.
@export Under section 527(5), is the quoted company required to place the statement on a website?
GIVEN `On an application by the company or another person claiming to be aggrieved, is the court satisfied that the rights conferred by section 527 are being abused` IS A BOOLEAN @desc On an application by the company or another person claiming to be aggrieved, is the court satisfied that the rights conferred by section 527 are being abused?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 527(5), is the quoted company required to place the statement on a website` IS
    `s 527(5) the quoted company is required to place the statement on a website` `On an application by the company or another person claiming to be aggrieved, is the court satisfied that the rights conferred by section 527 are being abused`

-- Seat question (director, secretary): Under section 528(3), does the access to the information meet the requirement of being free and unrestricted.
@export Under section 528(3), does the access to the information meet the requirement of being free and unrestricted?
GIVEN `Is access to the information on the website, or the ability to obtain a hard copy from it, conditional on the payment of a fee or otherwise restricted` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is access to the information on the website, or the ability to obtain a hard copy from it, conditional on the payment of a fee or otherwise restricted?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 528(3), does the access to the information meet the requirement of being free and unrestricted` IS
    `s 528(3) the access to the information meets the requirement` `Is access to the information on the website, or the ability to obtain a hard copy from it, conditional on the payment of a fee or otherwise restricted`

-- Seat question (director, secretary): Under section 528(4)(a), was the statement made available within three working days of the company being required to publish it.
@export Under section 528(4)(a), was the statement made available within three working days of the company being required to publish it?
GIVEN `How many working days after the day the company was required to publish the statement was it made available` IS A NUMBER @desc How many working days after the day the company was required to publish the statement was it made available?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 528(4)(a), was the statement made available within three working days of the company being required to publish it` IS
    `s 528(4)(a) the statement was made available within three working days of the company being required to publish it` `How many working days after the day the company was required to publish the statement was it made available`

-- Seat question (member, director): Under section 529(2), may the company require the members who requested website publication to pay these expenses.
@export Under section 529(2), may the company require the members who requested website publication to pay these expenses?
GIVEN `Are the expenses the company's expenses in complying with section 527 or section 528` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are the expenses the company's expenses in complying with section 527 or section 528?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 529(2), may the company require the members who requested website publication to pay these expenses` IS
    `s 529(2) the company may require the members requesting website publication to pay its expenses` `Are the expenses the company's expenses in complying with section 527 or section 528`

-- Seat question (director, secretary): Under section 530(1), does an officer of the company commit an offence by default in complying with section 528 or 529.
@export Under section 530(1), does an officer of the company commit an offence by default in complying with section 528 or 529?
GIVEN `Is default made in complying with section 528` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is default made in complying with section 528?
      `Is default made in complying with section 529` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is default made in complying with section 529?
      `Is the officer in default (section 1121)` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the officer in default (section 1121)?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 530(1), does an officer of the company commit an offence by default in complying with section 528 or 529` IS
    `s 530(1) the officer of the company commits an offence` `Is default made in complying with section 528` `Is default made in complying with section 529` (`coa12 the answer for the fact` `Is the officer in default (section 1121)`)

§§ `Chapter 6 -- auditors' liability (ss 532 to 538A)`

-- Ask these when a provision of the articles or a contract exempts, indemnifies or limits the liability of the auditor.

-- Seat question (director, member, auditor): Under section 532(2), is the provision void.
@export Under section 532(2), is the provision void?
GIVEN `Does the provision exempt an auditor (to any extent) from liability for negligence, default, breach of duty or breach of trust in relation to the company in the course of the audit` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does the provision exempt an auditor (to any extent) from liability for negligence, default, breach of duty or breach of trust in relation to the company in the course of the audit?
      `Does the provision have the company directly or indirectly indemnify an auditor of the company, or of an associated company, against such liability` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does the provision have the company directly or indirectly indemnify an auditor of the company, or of an associated company, against such liability?
      `Is the liability one the auditor incurs in defending proceedings (civil or criminal) in which judgment is given in his favour or he is acquitted` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the liability one the auditor incurs in defending proceedings (civil or criminal) in which judgment is given in his favour or he is acquitted?
      `Is the liability one the auditor incurs in connection with an application under section 1157 in which the court grants him relief` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the liability one the auditor incurs in connection with an application under section 1157 in which the court grants him relief?
      `Is the provision a liability limitation agreement that section 534(2) leaves valid (a "yes" to the section 534(2) question)` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the provision a liability limitation agreement that section 534(2) leaves valid (a "yes" to the section 534(2) question)?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 532(2), is the provision void` IS
    `s 532(2) the provision is void` (`s 532(1) the section applies to the provision` `Does the provision exempt an auditor (to any extent) from liability for negligence, default, breach of duty or breach of trust in relation to the company in the course of the audit` `Does the provision have the company directly or indirectly indemnify an auditor of the company, or of an associated company, against such liability`) (`s 533 section 532 does not prevent the indemnity` `Is the liability one the auditor incurs in defending proceedings (civil or criminal) in which judgment is given in his favour or he is acquitted` `Is the liability one the auditor incurs in connection with an application under section 1157 in which the court grants him relief`) (`coa12 the answer for the fact` `Is the provision a liability limitation agreement that section 534(2) leaves valid (a "yes" to the section 534(2) question)`)

-- Seat question (director, member, auditor): Under section 533, does section 532 leave the company free to indemnify the auditor against this liability.
@export Under section 533, does section 532 leave the company free to indemnify the auditor against this liability?
GIVEN `Is the liability one the auditor incurs in defending proceedings (civil or criminal) in which judgment is given in his favour or he is acquitted` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the liability one the auditor incurs in defending proceedings (civil or criminal) in which judgment is given in his favour or he is acquitted?
      `Is the liability one the auditor incurs in connection with an application under section 1157 in which the court grants him relief` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the liability one the auditor incurs in connection with an application under section 1157 in which the court grants him relief?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 533, does section 532 leave the company free to indemnify the auditor against this liability` IS
    `s 533 section 532 does not prevent the indemnity` `Is the liability one the auditor incurs in defending proceedings (civil or criminal) in which judgment is given in his favour or he is acquitted` `Is the liability one the auditor incurs in connection with an application under section 1157 in which the court grants him relief`

-- Seat question (director, member, auditor): Under section 534(2), does section 532 leave the liability limitation agreement valid.
@export Under section 534(2), does section 532 leave the liability limitation agreement valid?
GIVEN `For how many financial years does the agreement apply in respect of acts or omissions in the course of the audit of accounts` IS A NUMBER @desc For how many financial years does the agreement apply in respect of acts or omissions in the course of the audit of accounts?
      `Does the agreement specify the financial year in relation to which it applies` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does the agreement specify the financial year in relation to which it applies?
      `Does the agreement comply with any regulations under section 535(2)` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does the agreement comply with any regulations under section 535(2)?
      `Is the company a private company? (No means a public company.)` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the company a private company? (No means a public company.)
      `Did the company pass a resolution before it entered into the agreement waiving the need for approval? (Private company only.)` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did the company pass a resolution before it entered into the agreement waiving the need for approval? (Private company only.)
      `Did the company pass a resolution before it entered into the agreement approving its principal terms? (In general meeting, for a public company.)` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did the company pass a resolution before it entered into the agreement approving its principal terms? (In general meeting, for a public company.)
      `Did the company pass a resolution after it entered into the agreement approving it? (In general meeting, for a public company.)` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did the company pass a resolution after it entered into the agreement approving it? (In general meeting, for a public company.)
      `Has the authorisation been withdrawn` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has the authorisation been withdrawn?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 534(2), does section 532 leave the liability limitation agreement valid` IS
    `s 534(2) section 532 does not affect the validity of the agreement` (`s 535(1) the agreement complies with section 535 and any regulations under that section` `For how many financial years does the agreement apply in respect of acts or omissions in the course of the audit of accounts` `Does the agreement specify the financial year in relation to which it applies` (`coa12 the answer for the fact` `Does the agreement comply with any regulations under section 535(2)`)) (`s 536(1) the agreement is authorised by the members of the company` (IF `Is the company a private company? (No means a public company.)` THEN `s 536(2) the agreement between a private company and its auditor has been authorised under this section` `Is the company a private company? (No means a public company.)` `Did the company pass a resolution before it entered into the agreement waiving the need for approval? (Private company only.)` `Did the company pass a resolution before it entered into the agreement approving its principal terms? (In general meeting, for a public company.)` `Did the company pass a resolution after it entered into the agreement approving it? (In general meeting, for a public company.)` ELSE `s 536(3) the agreement between a public company and its auditor has been authorised under this section` (NOT `Is the company a private company? (No means a public company.)`) `Did the company pass a resolution before it entered into the agreement approving its principal terms? (In general meeting, for a public company.)` `Did the company pass a resolution after it entered into the agreement approving it? (In general meeting, for a public company.)`) `Has the authorisation been withdrawn`)

-- Seat question (director, member, auditor): Under section 535(1), does the liability limitation agreement comply with section 535.
@export Under section 535(1), does the liability limitation agreement comply with section 535?
GIVEN `For how many financial years does the agreement apply in respect of acts or omissions in the course of the audit of accounts` IS A NUMBER @desc For how many financial years does the agreement apply in respect of acts or omissions in the course of the audit of accounts?
      `Does the agreement specify the financial year in relation to which it applies` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does the agreement specify the financial year in relation to which it applies?
      `Does it comply with any regulations under section 535(2)` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does it comply with any regulations under section 535(2)?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 535(1), does the liability limitation agreement comply with section 535` IS
    `s 535(1) the agreement complies with section 535 and any regulations under that section` `For how many financial years does the agreement apply in respect of acts or omissions in the course of the audit of accounts` `Does the agreement specify the financial year in relation to which it applies` (`coa12 the answer for the fact` `Does it comply with any regulations under section 535(2)`)

-- Seat question (director, member): Under section 536(1), is the liability limitation agreement authorised by the members of the company.
@export Under section 536(1), is the liability limitation agreement authorised by the members of the company?
GIVEN `Is the company a private company? (No means a public company.)` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the company a private company? (No means a public company.)
      `Did the company pass a resolution before it entered into the agreement waiving the need for approval? (Private company only.)` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did the company pass a resolution before it entered into the agreement waiving the need for approval? (Private company only.)
      `Did the company pass a resolution before it entered into the agreement approving its principal terms? (In general meeting, for a public company.)` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did the company pass a resolution before it entered into the agreement approving its principal terms? (In general meeting, for a public company.)
      `Did the company pass a resolution after it entered into the agreement approving it? (In general meeting, for a public company.)` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did the company pass a resolution after it entered into the agreement approving it? (In general meeting, for a public company.)
      `Has the authorisation been withdrawn` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has the authorisation been withdrawn?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 536(1), is the liability limitation agreement authorised by the members of the company` IS
    `s 536(1) the agreement is authorised by the members of the company` (IF `Is the company a private company? (No means a public company.)` THEN `s 536(2) the agreement between a private company and its auditor has been authorised under this section` `Is the company a private company? (No means a public company.)` `Did the company pass a resolution before it entered into the agreement waiving the need for approval? (Private company only.)` `Did the company pass a resolution before it entered into the agreement approving its principal terms? (In general meeting, for a public company.)` `Did the company pass a resolution after it entered into the agreement approving it? (In general meeting, for a public company.)` ELSE `s 536(3) the agreement between a public company and its auditor has been authorised under this section` (NOT `Is the company a private company? (No means a public company.)`) `Did the company pass a resolution before it entered into the agreement approving its principal terms? (In general meeting, for a public company.)` `Did the company pass a resolution after it entered into the agreement approving it? (In general meeting, for a public company.)`) `Has the authorisation been withdrawn`

-- Seat question (member, director): Under section 536(5), may the company withdraw the authorisation by the resolution.
@export Under section 536(5), may the company withdraw the authorisation by the resolution?
GIVEN `Is the resolution an ordinary resolution` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the resolution an ordinary resolution?
      `Has the company already entered into the agreement` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has the company already entered into the agreement?
      `Is the resolution passed before the company enters into the agreement` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the resolution passed before the company enters into the agreement?
      `Is the resolution passed before the beginning of the financial year to which the agreement relates` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the resolution passed before the beginning of the financial year to which the agreement relates?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 536(5), may the company withdraw the authorisation by the resolution` IS
    `s 536(5) the authorisation may be withdrawn by the resolution` (`coa12 the answer for the fact` `Is the resolution an ordinary resolution`) `Has the company already entered into the agreement` `Is the resolution passed before the company enters into the agreement` `Is the resolution passed before the beginning of the financial year to which the agreement relates`

-- Seat question (director, member, auditor): Under section 537(2), to what amount, in pounds, is the auditor's liability limited.
@export Under section 537(2), to what amount, in pounds, is the auditor's liability limited?
GIVEN `To what amount, in pounds, does the agreement purport to limit the auditor's liability` IS A NUMBER @desc To what amount, in pounds, does the agreement purport to limit the auditor's liability?
      `What amount, in pounds, is fair and reasonable in all the circumstances of the case? (The court's judgment.)` IS A NUMBER @desc What amount, in pounds, is fair and reasonable in all the circumstances of the case? (The court's judgment.)
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `Under section 537(2), to what amount, in pounds, is the auditor's liability limited` IS
    `s 537(2) the amount to which the auditor's liability is limited` `To what amount, in pounds, does the agreement purport to limit the auditor's liability` `What amount, in pounds, is fair and reasonable in all the circumstances of the case? (The court's judgment.)`

-- Seat question (director, secretary): Under section 538(1), must the company make a disclosure.
@export Under section 538(1), must the company make a disclosure?
GIVEN `Has the company entered into a liability limitation agreement` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has the company entered into a liability limitation agreement?
      `Do regulations made by the Secretary of State require the disclosure` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Do regulations made by the Secretary of State require the disclosure?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 538(1), must the company make a disclosure` IS
    `s 538(1) the company must make the disclosure the regulations require` `Has the company entered into a liability limitation agreement` (`coa12 the answer for the fact` `Do regulations made by the Secretary of State require the disclosure`)

§§ `Chapter 7 -- supplementary provisions: minor definitions (s 539)`

-- Ask these when a figure or a description in the audit provisions depends on a defined term.

-- Seat question (director, member): Under section 539, what is the company's turnover in pounds.
@export Under section 539, what is the company's turnover in pounds?
GIVEN `What amounts, in pounds, did the company derive from the provision of goods and services falling within its ordinary activities` IS A NUMBER @desc What amounts, in pounds, did the company derive from the provision of goods and services falling within its ordinary activities?
      `How much, in pounds, was deducted in trade discounts` IS A NUMBER @desc How much, in pounds, was deducted in trade discounts?
      `How much, in pounds, was deducted in value added tax` IS A NUMBER @desc How much, in pounds, was deducted in value added tax?
      `How much, in pounds, was deducted in any other taxes based on the amounts so derived` IS A NUMBER @desc How much, in pounds, was deducted in any other taxes based on the amounts so derived?
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `Under section 539, what is the company's turnover in pounds` IS
    `s 539 the turnover of the company` `What amounts, in pounds, did the company derive from the provision of goods and services falling within its ordinary activities` `How much, in pounds, was deducted in trade discounts` `How much, in pounds, was deducted in value added tax` `How much, in pounds, was deducted in any other taxes based on the amounts so derived`

-- Seat question (member, director): Under section 539, is the auditor's report qualified.
@export Under section 539, is the auditor's report qualified?
GIVEN `Does the report state the auditor's unqualified opinion that the accounts have been properly prepared in accordance with this Act` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does the report state the auditor's unqualified opinion that the accounts have been properly prepared in accordance with this Act?
      `Is the undertaking not required to prepare accounts in accordance with this Act` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the undertaking not required to prepare accounts in accordance with this Act?
      `Does the report state the auditor's unqualified opinion that the accounts have been properly prepared under the corresponding legislation` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does the report state the auditor's unqualified opinion that the accounts have been properly prepared under the corresponding legislation?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 539, is the auditor's report qualified` IS
    `s 539 the report or statement is qualified` `Does the report state the auditor's unqualified opinion that the accounts have been properly prepared in accordance with this Act` `Is the undertaking not required to prepare accounts in accordance with this Act` `Does the report state the auditor's unqualified opinion that the accounts have been properly prepared under the corresponding legislation`

-- ====================================================================================================
-- seat questions from part coa13 (merged by the lead on 2026-11-12; unchanged text follows)
-- ====================================================================================================
-- coa13-seat.l4: the Companies Act 2006 (United Kingdom), Part 17 (ss 540 to 609), a company's share capital, first half: THE SEAT LAYER.
--
-- SEAT: an individual who is, or is about to become, a director, a company secretary or a member (shareholder) of a company registered
-- under the Act, or who deals with one, asking on facts they can state what the Act requires or lets them do, what rights they have
-- against the company or its directors, what they must disclose, file, approve or vote on and by when, and what follows (liability,
-- offences, penalties) if it is not done. (Assumed, not ruled: the Act is addressed to companies, so the individual is whoever stands in
-- a company's management or ownership.) There is never a seat for an official: the provisions that address only the registrar or the
-- court are answered here for what they mean to this person (what they may apply for, what may be done to them).
--
-- HOW A QUESTION READS. Every question is named "Under section N, ..." with the Act's own numbering, takes plain inputs (one per fact the
-- person can state, each with an @desc worded as that person would be asked) and calls the layer-1 rule; no rule is restated here.
-- The answer is "yes" (JUST TRUE), "no" (JUST FALSE: the text says no in its own words) or "not covered" (NOTHING: the text does not decide
-- the case; a caller must never read it as "no"). A question that gives a sum answers a number, or a date.
-- Seams to other parts of the Act are asked as yes/no facts and passed as JUST TRUE or JUST FALSE (the merged answer of the part that owns
-- the section would replace the input): s 1121 "officer in default" is asked as "I am an officer in default", s 1166 "employees' share
-- scheme" and Part 26A "sanctioned" are asked as facts, s 283 "special resolution" is asked as a fact. Sections of this Part that answer
-- one another (s 550 and s 551(1) into s 549(1), s 553 into s 552(1), ss 561(1)(a)/(b) and 564 to 576 into s 561(1), ss 599 and 601 into
-- s 598(1)) are computed in the question, not asked.
-- The Act's own figures that a Minister may substitute (the 14-day minimum of s 562(5), the 5% rate of ss 592 and 609) are used as the Act
-- states them, and a substitution would change the answers; the rate asks whether an order specifies another rate.

§ `Companies Act 2006, Part 17 (ss 540 to 609): the questions of a director, secretary or member`

-- A stated fact as an answer: the person's yes or no, passed on where a layer-1 rule takes a MAYBE BOOLEAN.
GIVEN `the fact` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`coa13 seat a stated fact as an answer` MEANS
    IF `the fact` THEN JUST TRUE ELSE JUST FALSE

§§ `Chapter 1: Shares and share capital (ss 540 to 548)`

@export Under section 542(1), does each share of my company meet the requirement of a fixed nominal value?
GIVEN `my company is a limited company` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is your company a limited company (the liability of its members is limited by its constitution)?
      `my company has power under its constitution to issue shares` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does your company's constitution give it power to issue shares (is it a company having a share capital)?
      `the share has a fixed nominal value` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does the share have a fixed nominal value?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 542(1), does each share of my company meet the requirement of a fixed nominal value` IS
    `s 542(1) the share meets the requirement of a fixed nominal value` `my company is a limited company` `my company has power under its constitution to issue shares` `the share has a fixed nominal value`

@export Under section 542(2), is an allotment of a share that has no fixed nominal value void?
GIVEN `the share allotted has a fixed nominal value` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does the share that was (or is to be) allotted have a fixed nominal value?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 542(2), is an allotment of a share that has no fixed nominal value void` IS
    `s 542(2) the allotment is void` `the share allotted has a fixed nominal value`

@export Under section 543, must each share of my company be distinguished by its number?
GIVEN `my company has power under its constitution to issue shares` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does your company's constitution give it power to issue shares?
      `all the issued shares are fully paid up and rank pari passu for all purposes` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are all the issued shares of the company fully paid up and ranking equally (pari passu) for all purposes?
      `all the issued shares of this class are fully paid up and rank pari passu for all purposes` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are all the issued shares of this particular class fully paid up and ranking equally (pari passu) for all purposes?
      `this share remains fully paid up and ranks pari passu with all shares of its class` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does this share remain fully paid up and rank equally for all purposes with all shares of the same class issued and fully paid up?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 543, must each share of my company be distinguished by its number` IS
    `s 543(1) the share must be distinguished by its appropriate number` `my company has power under its constitution to issue shares` `no number needed`
    WHERE
        `no number needed` MEANS
            `s 543(2) the share need not have a distinguishing number` `all the issued shares are fully paid up and rank pari passu for all purposes` `all the issued shares of this class are fully paid up and rank pari passu for all purposes` `this share remains fully paid up and ranks pari passu with all shares of its class`

@export Under section 546, are these shares part of my company's issued share capital?
GIVEN `the shares have been issued` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Have the shares been issued?
      `the shares were taken by the subscribers to the memorandum on the formation of the company` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Were the shares taken by the subscribers to the company's memorandum when the company was formed?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 546, are these shares part of my company's issued share capital` IS
    `s 546(1)(a) the shares are issued share capital` `the shares have been issued` `the shares were taken by the subscribers to the memorandum on the formation of the company`

@export Under section 547, what is my company's called-up share capital, in pounds?
GIVEN `the calls made on the company's shares, whether or not paid` IS A NUMBER @desc What is the total amount of the calls made on the company's shares, whether or not those calls have been paid, in pounds?
      `the share capital paid up without being called` IS A NUMBER @desc How much share capital has been paid up without being called, in pounds?
      `the share capital to be paid on a specified future date` IS A NUMBER @desc How much share capital is to be paid on a specified future date under the articles, the terms of allotment or any other arrangement, in pounds?
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `Under section 547, what is my company's called-up share capital` IS
    `s 547 the company's called-up share capital` `the calls made on the company's shares, whether or not paid` `the share capital paid up without being called` `the share capital to be paid on a specified future date`

@export Under section 548, what is my company's equity share capital, in pounds?
GIVEN `the company's issued share capital` IS A NUMBER @desc What is the company's issued share capital, in pounds?
      `the part that carries no right to participate beyond a specified amount in dividends or capital` IS A NUMBER @desc How much of that issued share capital carries, neither as respects dividends nor as respects capital, any right to participate beyond a specified amount in a distribution, in pounds?
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `Under section 548, what is my company's equity share capital` IS
    `s 548 the company's equity share capital` `the company's issued share capital` `the part that carries no right to participate beyond a specified amount in dividends or capital`

§§ `Chapter 2: Allotment of shares: general provisions (ss 549 to 559)`

@export Under section 549, are the directors prohibited from exercising a power to allot shares or grant rights to subscribe for or convert into shares?
GIVEN `the power is to allot shares in the company or to grant rights to subscribe for or to convert any security into shares` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the power one to allot shares in the company, or to grant rights to subscribe for, or to convert any security into, shares in the company?
      `my company is a private company` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is your company a private company?
      `my company has only one class of shares` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does your company have only one class of shares?
      `the articles prohibit the directors from exercising the power` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Do your company's articles prohibit the directors from exercising the power?
      `the articles authorise the directors to exercise the power` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Do your company's articles authorise the directors to exercise the power?
      `a resolution of the company authorises the directors to exercise the power` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has the company passed a resolution authorising the directors to exercise the power?
      `the scheme is an employees' share scheme` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the scheme under which the shares are allotted an employees' share scheme (a scheme for encouraging or facilitating the holding of shares in the company by or for the benefit of its employees)?
      `the exercise is the allotment of shares in pursuance of that scheme` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the exercise an allotment of shares in pursuance of that employees' share scheme?
      `the exercise is the grant of a right to subscribe for or convert into shares so allotted` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the exercise the grant of a right to subscribe for, or to convert any security into, shares allotted under that scheme?
      `the allotment is pursuant to an existing right to subscribe or convert` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the allotment of shares pursuant to a right to subscribe for, or to convert any security into, shares in the company?
      `it is done for the purposes of a compromise or arrangement` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it done for the purposes of a compromise or arrangement?
      `the compromise or arrangement is sanctioned under Part 26A` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is that compromise or arrangement sanctioned in accordance with Part 26A (arrangements and reconstructions: companies in financial difficulty)?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 549, are the directors prohibited from exercising a power to allot shares or grant rights to subscribe for or convert into shares` IS
    `s 549(1) the directors are prohibited from exercising the power`
        `the power is to allot shares in the company or to grant rights to subscribe for or to convert any security into shares`
        `answer of s 550` `answer of s 551(1)` `answer of s 549(2)` `answer of s 549(3)` `answer of s 549(3A)`
    WHERE
        `answer of s 550` MEANS
            `s 550 the directors may exercise the power under section 550` `my company is a private company` `my company has only one class of shares` `the power is to allot shares in the company or to grant rights to subscribe for or to convert any security into shares` `the articles prohibit the directors from exercising the power`
        `answer of s 551(1)` MEANS
            `s 551(1) the directors may exercise the power under section 551` `the power is to allot shares in the company or to grant rights to subscribe for or to convert any security into shares` `the articles authorise the directors to exercise the power` `a resolution of the company authorises the directors to exercise the power`
        `answer of s 549(2)` MEANS
            `s 549(2) subsection (1) does not apply to the exercise` (`coa13 seat a stated fact as an answer` `the scheme is an employees' share scheme`) `the exercise is the allotment of shares in pursuance of that scheme` `the exercise is the grant of a right to subscribe for or convert into shares so allotted`
        `answer of s 549(3)` MEANS
            `s 549(3) subsection (1) does not apply to the allotment` `the allotment is pursuant to an existing right to subscribe or convert`
        `answer of s 549(3A)` MEANS
            `s 549(3A) subsection (1) does not apply to the thing done` `it is done for the purposes of a compromise or arrangement` (`coa13 seat a stated fact as an answer` `the compromise or arrangement is sanctioned under Part 26A`)

@export Under section 549(4), does a director commit an offence by knowingly contravening section 549, or permitting or authorising a contravention of it?
GIVEN `I knowingly contravene section 549, or permit or authorise a contravention of it` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did you (as a director) knowingly contravene section 549, or permit or authorise a contravention of it?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 549(4), does a director commit an offence by knowingly contravening section 549, or permitting or authorising a contravention of it` IS
    `s 549(4) the director commits an offence` `I knowingly contravene section 549, or permit or authorise a contravention of it`

@export Under section 551(3), does the authorisation to allot meet the requirements as to the maximum amount and the expiry date?
GIVEN `the authorisation states the maximum amount of shares that may be allotted under it` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does the authorisation state the maximum amount of shares that may be allotted under it?
      `the authorisation specifies the date on which it will expire` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does the authorisation specify the date on which it will expire?
      `the authorisation is in the articles at the time of the original incorporation` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the authorisation contained in the company's articles at the time of its original incorporation (rather than given later by resolution)?
      `the date of the company's incorporation` IS A DATE @desc On what date was the company incorporated? (a date, for example 2026-03-10)
      `the date the resolution giving the authorisation is passed` IS A DATE @desc On what date is the resolution giving the authorisation passed? (a date, for example 2026-03-10; any date if the authorisation is in the articles at incorporation)
      `the date of expiry the authorisation specifies` IS A DATE @desc What date of expiry does the authorisation specify? (a date, for example 2031-03-10)
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 551(3), does the authorisation to allot meet the requirements as to the maximum amount and the expiry date` IS
    `s 551(3) the authorisation meets the requirements of subsection (3)` `the authorisation states the maximum amount of shares that may be allotted under it` `the authorisation specifies the date on which it will expire` `the authorisation is in the articles at the time of the original incorporation` `the date of the company's incorporation` `the date the resolution giving the authorisation is passed` `the date of expiry the authorisation specifies`

@export Under section 551(4), may the authorisation be renewed for this further period?
GIVEN `the renewal is by resolution of the company` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the renewal to be made by a resolution of the company?
      `the date the renewing resolution is passed` IS A DATE @desc On what date is the renewing resolution passed? (a date, for example 2026-03-10)
      `the date the renewed authorisation will expire` IS A DATE @desc On what date will the renewed authorisation expire? (a date, for example 2031-03-10)
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 551(4), may the authorisation be renewed for this further period` IS
    `s 551(4)(a) the authorisation may be renewed or further renewed` `the renewal is by resolution of the company` `the date the renewing resolution is passed` `the date the renewed authorisation will expire`

@export Under section 551(7), may the directors allot shares after the authorisation has expired?
GIVEN `the shares are allotted in pursuance of an offer or agreement made before the authorisation expired` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are the shares being allotted (or the rights granted) in pursuance of an offer or agreement the company made before the authorisation expired?
      `the authorisation allowed such an offer or agreement` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did the authorisation allow the company to make an offer or agreement that would or might require shares to be allotted, or rights granted, after the authorisation expired?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 551(7), may the directors allot shares after the authorisation has expired` IS
    `s 551(7) the directors may allot shares or grant rights after the authorisation has expired` `the shares are allotted in pursuance of an offer or agreement made before the authorisation expired` `the authorisation allowed such an offer or agreement`

@export Under section 552, is my company prohibited from paying this commission, discount or allowance out of its shares or capital money?
GIVEN `the company applies shares or capital money in payment of a commission, discount or allowance` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does the company apply any of its shares or capital money, directly or indirectly, in payment of a commission, discount or allowance?
      `it is for the person subscribing or agreeing to subscribe for shares` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it in consideration of the person subscribing, or agreeing to subscribe (absolutely or conditionally), for shares in the company?
      `it is for the person procuring or agreeing to procure subscriptions for shares` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it in consideration of the person procuring, or agreeing to procure, subscriptions (absolute or conditional) for shares in the company?
      `the payment is authorised by the articles` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does your company's articles authorise the payment of the commission?
      `the commission paid or agreed to be paid` IS A NUMBER @desc How much commission has been paid or agreed to be paid, in pounds?
      `the price at which the shares are issued` IS A NUMBER @desc At what price are the shares issued, in pounds?
      `the amount the articles authorise` IS A NUMBER @desc What is the most the articles authorise as commission, in pounds (worked out from the rate if they state a rate)?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 552, is my company prohibited from paying this commission, discount or allowance out of its shares or capital money` IS
    `s 552(1) the company is prohibited from applying its shares or capital money in payment` `the company applies shares or capital money in payment of a commission, discount or allowance` `it is for the person subscribing or agreeing to subscribe for shares` `it is for the person procuring or agreeing to procure subscriptions for shares` `answer of s 553(1)`
    WHERE
        `answer of s 553(1)` MEANS
            `s 553(1) the company may pay the commission`
                (`it is for the person subscribing or agreeing to subscribe for shares` OR `it is for the person procuring or agreeing to procure subscriptions for shares`)
                (`s 553(2)(a) the condition that the articles authorise the commission is satisfied` `the payment is authorised by the articles`)
                (`s 553(2)(b) the condition that the commission does not exceed the limit is satisfied` `the commission paid or agreed to be paid` `the price at which the shares are issued` `the amount the articles authorise`)

@export Under section 553, may my company pay this commission to a person for subscribing for or procuring subscriptions for shares?
GIVEN `it is for the person subscribing or agreeing to subscribe for shares, or procuring or agreeing to procure subscriptions for them` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the commission in consideration of the person subscribing, or agreeing to subscribe, for shares in the company, or procuring or agreeing to procure subscriptions for them?
      `the payment is authorised by the articles` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does your company's articles authorise the payment of the commission?
      `the commission paid or agreed to be paid` IS A NUMBER @desc How much commission has been paid or agreed to be paid, in pounds?
      `the price at which the shares are issued` IS A NUMBER @desc At what price are the shares issued, in pounds?
      `the amount the articles authorise` IS A NUMBER @desc What is the most the articles authorise as commission, in pounds (worked out from the rate if they state a rate)?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 553, may my company pay this commission to a person for subscribing for or procuring subscriptions for shares` IS
    `s 553(1) the company may pay the commission` `it is for the person subscribing or agreeing to subscribe for shares, or procuring or agreeing to procure subscriptions for them`
        (`s 553(2)(a) the condition that the articles authorise the commission is satisfied` `the payment is authorised by the articles`)
        (`s 553(2)(b) the condition that the commission does not exceed the limit is satisfied` `the commission paid or agreed to be paid` `the price at which the shares are issued` `the amount the articles authorise`)

@export Under section 554(1), has my company complied with its duty to register the allotment of shares as soon as practicable, and within two months of the allotment?
GIVEN `my company has issued a share warrant in respect of the shares` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has your company issued a share warrant in respect of the shares?
      `the date of the allotment` IS A DATE @desc On what date were the shares allotted (the date a person acquired the unconditional right to be included in the register of members)? (a date, for example 2026-01-15)
      `the company has registered the allotment` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has the company registered the allotment?
      `the date the company registered the allotment` IS A DATE @desc On what date did the company register the allotment? (a date; any date if it has not)
      `the company registered it as soon as practicable` IS A BOOLEAN @desc In your judgment, did the company register it as soon as practicable?
      `the date today` IS A DATE @desc What is today's date? (a date, for example 2026-03-20)
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 554(1), has my company complied with its duty to register the allotment of shares as soon as practicable, and within two months of the allotment` IS
    `s 554(1) the company has complied with the duty to register the allotment` (`s 554(2) the duty in section 554(1) does not apply` `my company has issued a share warrant in respect of the shares`) `the date of the allotment` `the company has registered the allotment` `the date the company registered the allotment` `the company registered it as soon as practicable` `the date today`

@export Under section 554(3), do I commit an offence as an officer of the company if the allotment was not registered in time?
GIVEN `my company has issued a share warrant in respect of the shares` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has your company issued a share warrant in respect of the shares?
      `the date of the allotment` IS A DATE @desc On what date were the shares allotted? (a date, for example 2026-01-15)
      `the company has registered the allotment` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has the company registered the allotment?
      `the date the company registered the allotment` IS A DATE @desc On what date did the company register the allotment? (a date; any date if it has not)
      `the company registered it as soon as practicable` IS A BOOLEAN @desc In your judgment, did the company register it as soon as practicable?
      `the date today` IS A DATE @desc What is today's date? (a date, for example 2026-03-20)
      `I am an officer of the company who is in default` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are you an officer of the company who is in default (within section 1121)?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 554(3), do I commit an offence as an officer of the company if the allotment was not registered in time` IS
    `s 554(3)(b) the officer of the company commits an offence` `complied` (`coa13 seat a stated fact as an answer` `I am an officer of the company who is in default`)
    WHERE
        `complied` MEANS
            `s 554(1) the company has complied with the duty to register the allotment` (`s 554(2) the duty in section 554(1) does not apply` `my company has issued a share warrant in respect of the shares`) `the date of the allotment` `the company has registered the allotment` `the date the company registered the allotment` `the company registered it as soon as practicable` `the date today`

@export Under section 554(4), what is the most a person guilty of an offence under section 554 can be fined on summary conviction, in pounds?
GIVEN `level 3 on the standard scale in pounds` IS A NUMBER @desc What amount in pounds does level 3 on the standard scale stand for? (the Act does not state it)
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `Under section 554(4), what is the most a person guilty of an offence under section 554 can be fined on summary conviction` IS
    `s 554(4) the most the fine can be, in pounds` `level 3 on the standard scale in pounds`

@export Under section 554(4), what is the most the daily default fine can be for continued contravention, in pounds?
GIVEN `level 3 on the standard scale in pounds` IS A NUMBER @desc What amount in pounds does level 3 on the standard scale stand for? (the Act does not state it)
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `Under section 554(4), what is the most the daily default fine can be for continued contravention` IS
    `s 554(4) the most the daily default fine can be, in pounds` `level 3 on the standard scale in pounds`

@export Under section 555, does the rule on returns of allotment apply to my company?
GIVEN `the liability of my members is limited by shares` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the liability of your company's members limited to the amount, if any, unpaid on the shares they hold (a company limited by shares)?
      `the liability of my members is limited by guarantee` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the liability of your company's members limited to the amount they undertake to contribute if the company is wound up (a company limited by guarantee)?
      `my company has a share capital` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does your company have a share capital (power under its constitution to issue shares)?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 555, does the rule on returns of allotment apply to my company` IS
    `s 555(1) section 555 applies to the company` `my company's profile`
    WHERE
        `my company's profile` MEANS `Company profile` WITH
            `place of registration` IS `England and Wales` -- Placeholder: the rule does not read this field.
            `liability of the members` IS
                IF `the liability of my members is limited by shares`
                THEN `liability limited to the amount, if any, unpaid on the shares held`
                ELSE IF `the liability of my members is limited by guarantee`
                     THEN `liability limited to the amount the members undertake to contribute on a winding up`
                     ELSE `liability not limited`
            `a share capital` IS `my company has a share capital`
            `certificate of incorporation stating that it is a public company` IS FALSE -- Placeholder: the rule does not read this field.

@export Under section 555(2), has my company delivered the return of allotment to the registrar in time?
GIVEN `the return was properly delivered` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has the return of allotment been properly delivered to the registrar (in the form, with the content and by the means the registrar requires)?
      `the day the registrar received the return` IS A DATE @desc On what day did the registrar receive the return? (a date; any date if it has not been delivered)
      `the date of the allotment` IS A DATE @desc On what date were the shares allotted? (a date, for example 2026-01-15)
      `the date today` IS A DATE @desc What is today's date? (a date, for example 2026-03-20)
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 555(2), has my company delivered the return of allotment to the registrar in time` IS
    `s 555(2) the company has delivered the return of the allotment in time` (`coa13 seat a stated fact as an answer` `the return was properly delivered`) `the day the registrar received the return` `the date of the allotment` `the date today`

@export Under section 556, does the rule on returns of an allotment of a new class of shares apply to my company?
GIVEN `my company is an unlimited company` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is your company an unlimited company (there is no limit on the liability of its members)?
      `the shares are of a class with rights not in all respects uniform with shares previously allotted` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are the shares of a class with rights that are not in all respects uniform with shares previously allotted?
      `the only difference is the dividend rights in the first twelve months` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the only difference that the new shares do not carry the same rights to dividends as the earlier shares during the twelve months immediately following the new shares' allotment?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 556, does the rule on returns of an allotment of a new class of shares apply to my company` IS
    `s 556(1) section 556 applies to the allotment` `my company is an unlimited company` `the shares are of a class with rights not in all respects uniform with shares previously allotted` (`s 556(4) the difference in rights is disregarded` `the only difference is the dividend rights in the first twelve months`)

@export Under section 557(1), do I commit an offence as an officer of the company if the return of allotment was not delivered in time?
GIVEN `the company is a company limited by shares (or by guarantee with a share capital), to which section 555 applies` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the return one that section 555 requires (your company is limited by shares, or by guarantee with a share capital), rather than one of an unlimited company under section 556?
      `the return was properly delivered` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has the return of allotment been properly delivered to the registrar?
      `the day the registrar received the return` IS A DATE @desc On what day did the registrar receive the return? (a date; any date if it has not been delivered)
      `the date of the allotment` IS A DATE @desc On what date were the shares allotted? (a date, for example 2026-01-15)
      `the date today` IS A DATE @desc What is today's date? (a date, for example 2026-03-20)
      `I am an officer of the company who is in default` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are you an officer of the company who is in default (within section 1121)?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 557(1), do I commit an offence as an officer of the company if the return of allotment was not delivered in time` IS
    `s 557(1) the officer of the company commits an offence` `answer of s 555(2)` `answer of s 556(2)` (`coa13 seat a stated fact as an answer` `I am an officer of the company who is in default`)
    WHERE
        `answer of s 555(2)` MEANS
            IF `the company is a company limited by shares (or by guarantee with a share capital), to which section 555 applies`
            THEN `s 555(2) the company has delivered the return of the allotment in time` (`coa13 seat a stated fact as an answer` `the return was properly delivered`) `the day the registrar received the return` `the date of the allotment` `the date today`
            ELSE NOTHING
        `answer of s 556(2)` MEANS
            IF `the company is a company limited by shares (or by guarantee with a share capital), to which section 555 applies`
            THEN NOTHING
            ELSE `s 556(2) the company has delivered the return of the allotment in time` (`coa13 seat a stated fact as an answer` `the return was properly delivered`) `the day the registrar received the return` `the date of the allotment` `the date today`

@export Under section 557(3), may I apply to the court for relief for a late return of allotment?
GIVEN `I am liable for the default` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are you a person liable for the default?
      `the default is in delivering the return within one month after the allotment` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the default one in delivering to the registrar, within one month after the allotment, the return required by section 555 or 556?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 557(3), may I apply to the court for relief for a late return of allotment` IS
    `s 557(3)(a) the person may apply to the court for relief` `I am liable for the default` `the default is in delivering the return within one month after the allotment`

@export Under section 557(3), may the court extend the time for delivering the return if it is satisfied of one of the grounds?
GIVEN `the court is satisfied that the omission was accidental or due to inadvertence` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the court satisfied that the omission to deliver the document was accidental or due to inadvertence?
      `the court is satisfied that it is just and equitable to grant relief` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the court satisfied that it is just and equitable to grant relief?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 557(3), may the court extend the time for delivering the return if it is satisfied of one of the grounds` IS
    `s 557(3)(b) the court may make an order extending the time for delivery` `the court is satisfied that the omission was accidental or due to inadvertence` `the court is satisfied that it is just and equitable to grant relief`

@export Under section 558, on what date are my shares taken to be allotted?
GIVEN `the date I acquired the unconditional right to be included in the company's register of members` IS A DATE @desc On what date did you acquire the unconditional right to be included in the company's register of members in respect of the shares? (a date, for example 2026-01-15)
GIVETH A DATE
DECIDE `Under section 558, on what date are my shares taken to be allotted` IS
    `s 558 the date on which the shares are taken to be allotted` `the date I acquired the unconditional right to be included in the company's register of members`

§§ `Chapter 3: Allotment of equity securities: existing shareholders' right of pre-emption (ss 560 to 577)`

@export Under section 561, is my company prohibited from allotting these equity securities to a person without first offering them to existing shareholders?
GIVEN `it is a share in the company` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is what the company is allotting a share in the company?
      `it is a right to subscribe for, or to convert securities into, ordinary shares` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is what the company is allotting a right to subscribe for, or to convert securities into, ordinary shares in the company?
      `the shares carry a limited right to dividends` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Do the shares carry, as respects dividends, a right to participate only up to a specified amount in a distribution?
      `the shares carry a limited right to capital` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Do the shares carry, as respects capital, a right to participate only up to a specified amount in a distribution?
      `an offer has been made to each holder of ordinary shares` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has the company made an offer to each person who holds ordinary shares in the company?
      `on the same or more favourable terms` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is each offer to allot to him on the same or more favourable terms?
      `of a proportion as nearly as practicable equal to his nominal-value proportion` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is each offer of a proportion of the securities as nearly as practicable equal to the proportion in nominal value that he holds of the company's ordinary share capital?
      `the offer period has expired` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has the period during which the offers may be accepted expired?
      `every offer has been accepted or refused` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has the company received notice of the acceptance or refusal of every offer made?
      `the allotment is of bonus shares` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the allotment of bonus shares?
      `the securities are paid up wholly or partly otherwise than in cash` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are the securities to be wholly or partly paid up otherwise than in cash? (section 565; for this purpose, cash paid to someone other than the company counts as cash)
      `the securities are held or allotted under an employees' share scheme` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Would the securities, apart from any renunciation or assignment, be held under or allotted or transferred pursuant to an employees' share scheme?
      `the scheme is an employees' share scheme` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is that scheme an employees' share scheme?
      `the allotment is part of a compromise or arrangement` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the allotment carried out as part of a compromise or arrangement?
      `the compromise or arrangement is sanctioned under Part 26A` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is that compromise or arrangement sanctioned in accordance with Part 26A?
      `my company is a private company` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is your company a private company?
      `the articles exclude the requirement` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Do the company's articles exclude the requirements of section 561 (generally or for allotments of this description)?
      `the articles give the shareholders a corresponding right which the company has followed` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Do the articles contain a provision prohibiting allotment of ordinary shares unless the company offers them to each holder, and has the company offered them and the holder accepted (section 568)?
      `the power to allot is given by the articles or a special resolution as if section 561 did not apply` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has the power to allot been given by the articles or a special resolution (sections 569 to 571 or 573) as if section 561 did not apply, and is the allotment made under it?
      `an older pre-emption requirement saved by section 576 applies` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the allotment of securities subject to a pre-emption requirement saved by section 576(1) (a public company; the 1985 Act's section 96(1) applied immediately before the Chapter began)?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 561, is my company prohibited from allotting these equity securities to a person without first offering them to existing shareholders` IS
    `s 561(1) the company is prohibited from allotting the equity securities to the person` `these are equity securities` `the offers required` `the period or the answers` `section 561 is displaced`
    WHERE
        `these are equity securities` MEANS
            `s 560(1) the thing is an equity security` (`s 560(1) the shares are ordinary shares` `the shares carry a limited right to dividends` `the shares carry a limited right to capital`) `it is a share in the company` `it is a right to subscribe for, or to convert securities into, ordinary shares` EQUALS JUST TRUE
        `the offers required` MEANS
            `s 561(1)(a) the company has made the offers required` `an offer has been made to each holder of ordinary shares` `on the same or more favourable terms` `of a proportion as nearly as practicable equal to his nominal-value proportion`
        `the period or the answers` MEANS
            `s 561(1)(b) the period has expired or every offer has been accepted or refused` `the offer period has expired` `every offer has been accepted or refused`
        `answer of s 564` MEANS
            `s 564 section 561(1) does not apply to the allotment of bonus shares` `the allotment is of bonus shares`
        `answer of s 565` MEANS
            `s 565 section 561(1) does not apply to the allotment for non-cash consideration` `the securities are paid up wholly or partly otherwise than in cash`
        `answer of s 566` MEANS
            `s 566 section 561 does not apply to the allotment under an employees' share scheme` (`coa13 seat a stated fact as an answer` `the scheme is an employees' share scheme`) `the securities are held or allotted under an employees' share scheme`
        `answer of s 566A` MEANS
            `s 566A section 561(1) does not apply to the allotment in a compromise or arrangement under Part 26A` `the allotment is part of a compromise or arrangement` (`coa13 seat a stated fact as an answer` `the compromise or arrangement is sanctioned under Part 26A`)
        `answer of s 567` MEANS
            `s 567(1) the requirements may be excluded` `my company is a private company` TRUE `the articles exclude the requirement`
        `answer of s 568(2)` MEANS
            IF `the articles give the shareholders a corresponding right which the company has followed` THEN JUST TRUE ELSE NOTHING
        `answer of ss 569 to 573` MEANS
            IF `the power to allot is given by the articles or a special resolution as if section 561 did not apply` THEN JUST TRUE ELSE NOTHING
        `answer of s 576` MEANS
            IF `an older pre-emption requirement saved by section 576 applies` THEN JUST TRUE ELSE NOTHING
        `the sections to which section 561 is subject` MEANS `s 561(5) the sections to which section 561 is subject` WITH
            `s 561(5)(a) the answer of section 564` IS `answer of s 564`
            `s 561(5)(a) the answer of section 565` IS `answer of s 565`
            `s 561(5)(a) the answer of section 566` IS `answer of s 566`
            `s 561(5)(a) the answer of section 566A` IS `answer of s 566A`
            `s 561(5)(b) the answer of section 567` IS `answer of s 567`
            `s 561(5)(b) the answer of section 568(2)` IS `answer of s 568(2)`
            `s 561(5)(c) the answer of sections 569 to 573` IS `answer of ss 569 to 573`
            `s 561(5)(d) the answer of section 576` IS `answer of s 576`
        `section 561 is displaced` MEANS
            `s 561(5) section 561 is displaced by one of the sections to which it is subject` `the sections to which section 561 is subject`

@export Under section 561(1), how many of the securities must my company offer to a holder of ordinary shares?
GIVEN `the number of the equity securities to be allotted` IS A NUMBER @desc How many equity securities is the company going to allot?
      `the nominal value of the ordinary shares the holder holds` IS A NUMBER @desc What is the nominal value, in pounds, of the ordinary shares this holder holds?
      `the nominal value of the company's ordinary share capital` IS A NUMBER @desc What is the nominal value, in pounds, of the company's ordinary share capital, leaving out any treasury shares?
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `Under section 561(1), how many of the securities must my company offer to a holder of ordinary shares` IS
    `s 561(1)(a) the number of the equity securities to be offered to the holder` `the number of the equity securities to be allotted` `the nominal value of the ordinary shares the holder holds` `the nominal value of the company's ordinary share capital`

@export Under section 562(5), is the period my company gives for accepting the pre-emption offer long enough?
GIVEN `the way the offer is made` IS A STRING @desc How is the offer made? One of: "hard copy" (sent or supplied in hard copy form), "electronic" (sent in electronic form) or "Gazette" (published in the Gazette)
      `the date the offer is sent, supplied or published` IS A DATE @desc On what date is the offer sent or supplied (hard copy), sent (electronic form) or published (Gazette)? (a date, for example 2026-03-01)
      `the last day on which the offer may be accepted` IS A DATE @desc What is the last day on which the offer may be accepted? (a date, for example 2026-03-14)
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 562(5), is the period my company gives for accepting the pre-emption offer long enough` IS
    CONSIDER `the way the offer is made`
    WHEN "hard copy" THEN `s 562(5) the period meets the requirement of at least 14 days` `s 562(5)(a) in hard copy form` `the date the offer is sent, supplied or published` `the last day on which the offer may be accepted`
    WHEN "electronic" THEN `s 562(5) the period meets the requirement of at least 14 days` `s 562(5)(b) in electronic form` `the date the offer is sent, supplied or published` `the last day on which the offer may be accepted`
    WHEN "Gazette" THEN `s 562(5) the period meets the requirement of at least 14 days` `s 562(5)(c) by publication in the Gazette` `the date the offer is sent, supplied or published` `the last day on which the offer may be accepted`
    OTHERWISE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): the subsection names three ways of making the offer

@export Under section 562(3), may my company make the pre-emption offer by publication in the Gazette?
GIVEN `the holder has a registered address in the United Kingdom or an EEA State` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does the holder have a registered address in the United Kingdom or an EEA State?
      `the holder has given the company an address in the United Kingdom or an EEA State for service of notices` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has the holder given the company an address in the United Kingdom or an EEA State for the service of notices on him?
      `the holder holds a share warrant` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the holder the holder of a share warrant?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 562(3), may my company make the pre-emption offer by publication in the Gazette` IS
    `s 562(3) the offer may be made by causing it, or a notice of where it can be obtained, to be published in the Gazette` `the holder has a registered address in the United Kingdom or an EEA State` `the holder has given the company an address in the United Kingdom or an EEA State for service of notices` `the holder holds a share warrant`

@export Under section 563, is my company liable to compensate a person to whom an offer should have been made?
GIVEN `there is a contravention of section 561 or section 562` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is there a contravention of section 561 or section 562?
      `I am a person to whom an offer should have been made` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are you (or is the claimant) a person to whom an offer should have been made in accordance with those sections?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 563, is my company liable to compensate a person to whom an offer should have been made` IS
    `s 563(2) the company is liable to compensate the person` `there is a contravention of section 561 or section 562` `I am a person to whom an offer should have been made`

@export Under section 563, am I, as an officer, liable to compensate a person to whom an offer should have been made?
GIVEN `there is a contravention of section 561 or section 562` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is there a contravention of section 561 or section 562?
      `the claimant is a person to whom an offer should have been made` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the claimant a person to whom an offer should have been made in accordance with those sections?
      `I knowingly authorised or permitted the contravention` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did you (as an officer) knowingly authorise or permit the contravention?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 563, am I, as an officer, liable to compensate a person to whom an offer should have been made` IS
    `s 563(2) the officer is liable, jointly and severally with the company, to compensate the person` `there is a contravention of section 561 or section 562` `the claimant is a person to whom an offer should have been made` `I knowingly authorised or permitted the contravention`

@export Under section 563(3), may proceedings to recover the loss still be commenced?
GIVEN `equity securities other than shares were granted` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Were equity securities other than shares granted (rather than shares allotted)?
      `the date the return of allotment was delivered to the registrar` IS A DATE @desc On what date was the return of allotment delivered to the registrar of companies? (a date)
      `the date of the grant` IS A DATE @desc On what date were the securities granted? (a date; any date if shares were allotted)
      `the date proceedings are to be commenced` IS A DATE @desc On what date will the proceedings be commenced? (a date)
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 563(3), may proceedings to recover the loss still be commenced` IS
    `s 563(3) proceedings to recover the loss may be commenced` `equity securities other than shares were granted` `the date the return of allotment was delivered to the registrar` `the date of the grant` `the date proceedings are to be commenced`

@export Under section 571, is the proposal of the special resolution disapplying pre-emption rights barred?
GIVEN `the directors recommend the special resolution` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Do the directors recommend the special resolution?
      `the directors made a written statement before it is proposed` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Have the directors made a written statement before the resolution is proposed?
      `it sets out their reasons for the recommendation` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does the statement set out their reasons for making the recommendation?
      `it sets out the amount to be paid to the company` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does the statement set out the amount to be paid to the company in respect of the equity securities to be allotted?
      `it sets out the directors' justification of that amount` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does the statement set out the directors' justification of that amount?
      `the way the resolution is proposed` IS A STRING @desc How is the resolution proposed? One of: "written resolution", "general meeting"
      `the statement was sent or submitted to every eligible member in time` IS A BOOLEAN @desc If a written resolution: was the statement sent or submitted to every eligible member at or before the time the proposed resolution was sent or submitted to him?
      `the statement was circulated with the notice of the meeting` IS A BOOLEAN @desc If a general meeting: was the statement circulated to the members entitled to notice of the meeting with that notice?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 571, is the proposal of the special resolution disapplying pre-emption rights barred` IS
    CONSIDER `the way the resolution is proposed`
    WHEN "written resolution" THEN `the answer for a written resolution`
    WHEN "general meeting" THEN `the answer for a general meeting`
    OTHERWISE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): section 571(7) names a written resolution and a general meeting
    WHERE
        `the statement as written` MEANS
            `s 571(6) the directors have made the written statement required` `the directors made a written statement before it is proposed` `it sets out their reasons for the recommendation` `it sets out the amount to be paid to the company` `it sets out the directors' justification of that amount`
        `the answer for a written resolution` MEANS
            `s 571(5) the proposal of the special resolution is barred` `the directors recommend the special resolution` `the statement as written`
                (`s 571(7) the directors' statement has been sent, submitted or circulated as required` `as a written resolution` `the statement was sent or submitted to every eligible member in time` `the statement was circulated with the notice of the meeting`)
        `the answer for a general meeting` MEANS
            `s 571(5) the proposal of the special resolution is barred` `the directors recommend the special resolution` `the statement as written`
                (`s 571(7) the directors' statement has been sent, submitted or circulated as required` `at a meeting on a show of hands` `the statement was sent or submitted to every eligible member in time` `the statement was circulated with the notice of the meeting`)

@export Under section 572, do I commit an offence by knowingly or recklessly authorising or permitting a misleading matter in the directors' statement?
GIVEN `the statement is a directors' statement under section 571` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it a directors' statement under section 571 that is sent, submitted or circulated with a special resolution disapplying pre-emption rights?
      `I knowingly or recklessly authorise or permit the inclusion of the matter` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did you knowingly or recklessly authorise or permit the inclusion of the matter in the statement?
      `the matter is misleading, false or deceptive in a material particular` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the matter misleading, false or deceptive in a material particular?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 572, do I commit an offence by knowingly or recklessly authorising or permitting a misleading matter in the directors' statement` IS
    `s 572(2) the person commits an offence` `the statement is a directors' statement under section 571` `I knowingly or recklessly authorise or permit the inclusion of the matter` `the matter is misleading, false or deceptive in a material particular`

@export Under section 574(2), does the date specified in the pre-emption offer fall within the 28 days before the offer?
GIVEN `the date specified in the offer` IS A DATE @desc What is the date specified in the offer (the date at the close of business on which holders are identified)? (a date, for example 2026-05-10)
      `the date of the offer` IS A DATE @desc What is the date of the offer? (a date, for example 2026-06-01)
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 574(2), does the date specified in the pre-emption offer fall within the 28 days before the offer` IS
    `s 574(2) the specified date falls within the period of 28 days immediately before the date of the offer` `the date specified in the offer` `the date of the offer`

§§ `Chapter 4: Public companies: allotment where issue not fully subscribed (ss 578 and 579)`

@export Under section 578(1), is my public company prohibited from allotting shares offered for subscription?
GIVEN `my company is a public company` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is your company a public company?
      `the shares are offered for subscription` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are the shares offered for subscription?
      `the shares are offered as wholly or partly payable otherwise than in cash` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are the shares offered as wholly or partly payable otherwise than in cash?
      `the issue is subscribed for in full` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has the issue been subscribed for in full?
      `the offer allows allotment in any event` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the offer made on terms that the shares subscribed for may be allotted in any event?
      `the offer allows allotment if specified conditions are met` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the offer made on terms that the shares subscribed for may be allotted if specified conditions are met?
      `those conditions are met` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are those conditions met?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 578(1), is my public company prohibited from allotting shares offered for subscription` IS
    `s 578(1) the allotment of the shares is prohibited` `my company is a public company` `the shares are offered for subscription` (`s 578(4) section 578 applies to the shares as it applies to shares offered for subscription` `the shares are offered as wholly or partly payable otherwise than in cash`) `the issue is subscribed for in full` `the offer allows allotment in any event` `the offer allows allotment if specified conditions are met` `those conditions are met`

@export Under section 578(2), must my public company repay the money received from applicants?
GIVEN `my company is a public company` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is your company a public company?
      `the shares are offered for subscription` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are the shares offered for subscription?
      `the issue is subscribed for in full` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has the issue been subscribed for in full?
      `the offer allows allotment in any event` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the offer made on terms that the shares subscribed for may be allotted in any event?
      `the offer allows allotment if specified conditions are met` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the offer made on terms that the shares may be allotted if specified conditions are met?
      `those conditions are met` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are those conditions met?
      `the date of the first making of the offer` IS A DATE @desc On what date was the offer first made? (a date, for example 2026-03-01)
      `the date today` IS A DATE @desc What is today's date? (a date)
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 578(2), must my public company repay the money received from applicants` IS
    `s 578(2) the company must repay the money received from applicants` `prohibited` `the date of the first making of the offer` `the date today`
    WHERE
        `prohibited` MEANS
            `s 578(1) the allotment of the shares is prohibited` `my company is a public company` `the shares are offered for subscription` NOTHING `the issue is subscribed for in full` `the offer allows allotment in any event` `the offer allows allotment if specified conditions are met` `those conditions are met`

@export Under section 578(3), am I, as a director, liable to repay the money with interest?
GIVEN `my company is a public company` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is your company a public company?
      `the shares are offered for subscription` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are the shares offered for subscription?
      `the issue is subscribed for in full` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has the issue been subscribed for in full?
      `the offer allows allotment in any event` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the offer made on terms that the shares subscribed for may be allotted in any event?
      `the offer allows allotment if specified conditions are met` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the offer made on terms that the shares may be allotted if specified conditions are met?
      `those conditions are met` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are those conditions met?
      `the date of the first making of the offer` IS A DATE @desc On what date was the offer first made? (a date, for example 2026-03-01)
      `the money has been repaid` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has the money been repaid to the applicants?
      `the date the money was repaid` IS A DATE @desc On what date was the money repaid? (a date; any date if it has not been)
      `the date today` IS A DATE @desc What is today's date? (a date)
      `I can prove the default was not due to my misconduct or negligence` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Can you prove that the default in the repayment of the money was not due to any misconduct or negligence on your part?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 578(3), am I, as a director, liable to repay the money with interest` IS
    `s 578(3) the director is liable to repay the money, with interest` `prohibited` `the date of the first making of the offer` `the money has been repaid` `the date the money was repaid` `the date today` (`s 578(3) the director has the defence in subsection (3)` `I can prove the default was not due to my misconduct or negligence`)
    WHERE
        `prohibited` MEANS
            `s 578(1) the allotment of the shares is prohibited` `my company is a public company` `the shares are offered for subscription` NOTHING `the issue is subscribed for in full` `the offer allows allotment in any event` `the offer allows allotment if specified conditions are met` `those conditions are met`

@export Under section 579(1), may an applicant avoid an allotment made in contravention of section 578?
GIVEN `my company is a public company` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the company a public company?
      `the allotment was made to an applicant in contravention of section 578` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Was the allotment made to the applicant in contravention of section 578?
      `the date of the allotment` IS A DATE @desc On what date was the allotment made? (a date, for example 2026-01-15)
      `the date the applicant avoids the allotment` IS A DATE @desc On what date does the applicant avoid the allotment? (a date, for example 2026-02-10)
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 579(1), may an applicant avoid an allotment made in contravention of section 578` IS
    `s 579(1) the allotment is voidable at the instance of the applicant` `my company is a public company` `the allotment was made to an applicant in contravention of section 578` `the date of the allotment` `the date the applicant avoids the allotment`

@export Under section 579(3), is a director liable to compensate the company and the allottee for a contravention of section 578?
GIVEN `my company is a public company` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the company a public company?
      `the director knowingly contravened, or permitted or authorised the contravention of, section 578` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did the director knowingly contravene, or permit or authorise the contravention of, a provision of section 578 with respect to allotment?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 579(3), is a director liable to compensate the company and the allottee for a contravention of section 578` IS
    `s 579(3) the director is liable to compensate the company and the allottee` `my company is a public company` `the director knowingly contravened, or permitted or authorised the contravention of, section 578`

§§ `Chapter 5: Payment for shares (ss 580 to 592)`

@export Under section 580(1), is the allotment of my company's shares prohibited because it is at a discount?
GIVEN `the nominal value of the shares` IS A NUMBER @desc What is the nominal value of the shares, in pounds?
      `the value of the consideration received for the shares, including any premium` IS A NUMBER @desc What is the value of the consideration the company receives for the shares, including any premium, in pounds?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 580(1), is the allotment of my company's shares prohibited because it is at a discount` IS
    `s 580(1) the allotment of the shares is prohibited because it is at a discount` `the nominal value of the shares` `the value of the consideration received for the shares, including any premium`

@export Under section 580(2), what is the amount of the discount the allottee must pay the company, in pounds?
GIVEN `the nominal value of the shares` IS A NUMBER @desc What is the nominal value of the shares, in pounds?
      `the value of the consideration received for the shares, including any premium` IS A NUMBER @desc What is the value of the consideration the company receives for the shares, including any premium, in pounds?
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `Under section 580(2), what is the amount of the discount the allottee must pay the company` IS
    `s 580(2) the amount of the discount` `the nominal value of the shares` `the value of the consideration received for the shares, including any premium`

@export Under section 583(3), is the consideration for the shares a cash consideration?
GIVEN `the company receives cash` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does the company receive cash?
      `the company receives a cheque in good faith that the directors have no reason for suspecting will not be paid` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does the company receive a cheque in good faith that the directors have no reason for suspecting will not be paid?
      `a liability of the company for a liquidated sum is released` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is a liability of the company for a liquidated sum released?
      `an undertaking to pay cash to the company at a future date is given` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is an undertaking to pay cash to the company at a future date given?
      `payment is by another means giving a present or future entitlement to cash` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is payment by any other means giving rise to a present or future entitlement (of the company or a person acting on its behalf) to a payment, or credit equivalent to payment, in cash?
      `an order of the Secretary of State specifies the means of payment` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does an order of the Secretary of State under section 583(4) specify the means of payment as falling within that last category?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 583(3), is the consideration for the shares a cash consideration` IS
    `s 583(3) the consideration is a cash consideration` `the company receives cash` `the company receives a cheque in good faith that the directors have no reason for suspecting will not be paid` `a liability of the company for a liquidated sum is released` `an undertaking to pay cash to the company at a future date is given` `payment is by another means giving a present or future entitlement to cash` `an order of the Secretary of State specifies the means of payment`

@export Under section 585(1), is my public company prohibited from accepting an undertaking to do work or perform services in payment for its shares?
GIVEN `my company is a public company` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is your company a public company?
      `the undertaking is that a person or another should do work or perform services` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the undertaking one given by a person that he or another should do work or perform services for the company or any other person?
      `the company accepts it in payment up of its shares or any premium` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does the company accept it in payment up of its shares or any premium on them?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 585(1), is my public company prohibited from accepting an undertaking to do work or perform services in payment for its shares` IS
    `s 585(1) the public company is prohibited from accepting the undertaking` `my company is a public company` `the undertaking is that a person or another should do work or perform services` `the company accepts it in payment up of its shares or any premium`

@export Under section 586(1), is my public company prohibited from allotting a share that is not paid up at least as to one-quarter of its nominal value and the whole of any premium?
GIVEN `my company is a public company` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is your company a public company?
      `the nominal value of the share` IS A NUMBER @desc What is the nominal value of the share, in pounds?
      `the amount paid up on the share as to its nominal value` IS A NUMBER @desc How much of the nominal value is paid up, in pounds?
      `the premium on the share` IS A NUMBER @desc What is the premium on the share, in pounds (0 if none)?
      `the amount paid up as to the premium` IS A NUMBER @desc How much of the premium is paid up, in pounds?
      `the share is allotted in pursuance of an employees' share scheme` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the share allotted in pursuance of an employees' share scheme?
      `the scheme is an employees' share scheme` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is that scheme an employees' share scheme?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 586(1), is my public company prohibited from allotting a share that is not paid up at least as to one-quarter of its nominal value and the whole of any premium` IS
    `s 586(1) the allotment of the share is prohibited` `my company is a public company` `the nominal value of the share` `the amount paid up on the share as to its nominal value` `the premium on the share` `the amount paid up as to the premium`
        (`s 586(2) subsection (1) does not apply to the share` (`coa13 seat a stated fact as an answer` `the scheme is an employees' share scheme`) `the share is allotted in pursuance of an employees' share scheme`)

@export Under section 587(1), is my public company prohibited from allotting shares in return for an undertaking to be performed more than five years after the allotment?
GIVEN `my company is a public company` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is your company a public company?
      `the shares are allotted as paid up otherwise than in cash` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are the shares allotted as fully or partly paid up otherwise than in cash?
      `the date of the allotment` IS A DATE @desc On what date are the shares allotted? (a date, for example 2026-01-01)
      `the latest date the undertaking is to be or may be performed` IS A DATE @desc What is the latest date on which the undertaking forming (or included in) the consideration is to be, or may be, performed? (a date)
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 587(1), is my public company prohibited from allotting shares in return for an undertaking to be performed more than five years after the allotment` IS
    `s 587(1) the allotment of the shares is prohibited` `my company is a public company` `the shares are allotted as paid up otherwise than in cash` `the date of the allotment` `the latest date the undertaking is to be or may be performed`

@export Under section 588, am I, as a later holder of the shares, liable to pay the amount another person owes the company?
GIVEN `there has been a contravention of a provision of Chapter 5 in respect of the shares` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has there been a contravention of a provision of Chapter 5 (payment for shares) in respect of the shares?
      `another person is liable to pay an amount because of that contravention` IS A BOOLEAN @desc By virtue of that contravention, is another person liable to pay an amount under the provision contravened?
      `I am a purchaser for value` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are you a purchaser for value of the shares?
      `I did not have actual notice of the contravention when I purchased` IS A BOOLEAN @desc At the time of the purchase, did you not have actual notice of the contravention?
      `I derived title from a person who became a holder after the contravention` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did you derive title to the shares (directly or indirectly) from a person who became a holder of them after the contravention?
      `that person was not liable` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Was that person not liable under section 588(1)?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 588, am I, as a later holder of the shares, liable to pay the amount another person owes the company` IS
    `s 588(1) the person who becomes a holder is also liable to pay the amount` `there has been a contravention of a provision of Chapter 5 in respect of the shares` `another person is liable to pay an amount because of that contravention`
        (`s 588(2) the person is exempted from the liability` `I am a purchaser for value` `I did not have actual notice of the contravention when I purchased` `I derived title from a person who became a holder after the contravention` `that person was not liable`)

@export Under section 589, may I apply to the court to be exempted from a liability for shares that were not properly paid for?
GIVEN `the liability is under section 585(2), 587(2) or (4), or 588` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the liability one under section 585(2), section 587(2) or (4), or section 588?
      `I am subject to the liability in relation to payment in respect of the shares` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are you subject to the liability to the company in relation to payment in respect of the shares?
      `I am subject to the liability by virtue of an undertaking given to the company` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are you subject to the liability to the company by virtue of an undertaking given to it in connection with payment for the shares?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 589, may I apply to the court to be exempted from a liability for shares that were not properly paid for` IS
    `s 589(2) the person may apply to the court to be exempted from the liability in whole or in part` (`s 589(1) section 589 applies to the liability` `the liability is under section 585(2), 587(2) or (4), or 588`) `I am subject to the liability in relation to payment in respect of the shares` `I am subject to the liability by virtue of an undertaking given to the company`

@export Under section 590, do I commit an offence as an officer of the company if the company contravenes Chapter 5?
GIVEN `the company contravenes a provision of Chapter 5` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does the company contravene a provision of Chapter 5 (payment for shares)?
      `I am an officer of the company who is in default` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are you an officer of the company who is in default (within section 1121)?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 590, do I commit an offence as an officer of the company if the company contravenes Chapter 5` IS
    `s 590(1)(b) the officer of the company commits an offence` `the company contravenes a provision of Chapter 5` (`coa13 seat a stated fact as an answer` `I am an officer of the company who is in default`)

@export Under section 592, what is the appropriate rate of interest for Chapter 5, as a fraction per annum?
GIVEN `an order specifies another rate` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has the Secretary of State made an order specifying a rate other than 5% a year?
      `the rate the order specifies` IS A NUMBER @desc If so, what rate does the order specify, as a fraction per year (for example 0.04 for 4%)? (0 if there is no order)
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `Under section 592, what is the appropriate rate of interest for Chapter 5, as a fraction per annum` IS
    `s 592(1) the appropriate rate of interest, as a fraction per annum` (IF `an order specifies another rate` THEN JUST `the rate the order specifies` ELSE NOTHING)

§§ `Chapter 6: Public companies: independent valuation of non-cash consideration (ss 593 to 609)`

@export Under section 593(1), is my public company prohibited from allotting shares for non-cash consideration without an independent valuation?
GIVEN `my company is a public company` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is your company a public company?
      `the shares are allotted as paid up otherwise than in cash` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are the shares allotted as fully or partly paid up (as to nominal value or any premium) otherwise than in cash?
      `reserves or profits are applied in paying up shares allotted to members` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the consideration the application of an amount standing to the credit of a reserve account or the profit and loss account in paying up shares allotted to members?
      `section 594 or 595 exempts the allotment` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does section 594 (arrangement with another company) or section 595 (merger or division) exempt the allotment?
      `the consideration has been independently valued` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has the consideration for the allotment been independently valued in accordance with Chapter 6?
      `the date the valuer's report was made to the company` IS A DATE @desc On what date was the valuer's report made to the company? (a date, for example 2026-01-01)
      `the date of the allotment` IS A DATE @desc On what date are the shares allotted? (a date, for example 2026-03-01)
      `a copy of the report has been sent to the proposed allottee` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has a copy of the report been sent to the proposed allottee?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 593(1), is my public company prohibited from allotting shares for non-cash consideration without an independent valuation` IS
    `s 593(1) the allotment of the shares is prohibited` `my company is a public company` `the shares are allotted as paid up otherwise than in cash`
        (`s 593(2) subsection (1) applies to the allotment` `reserves or profits are applied in paying up shares allotted to members` `reserves or profits are applied in paying up shares allotted to members`)
        (IF `section 594 or 595 exempts the allotment` THEN JUST TRUE ELSE NOTHING) NOTHING
        `the consideration has been independently valued` `the date the valuer's report was made to the company` `the date of the allotment` `a copy of the report has been sent to the proposed allottee`

@export Under section 593(3), must the allottee pay the company the nominal value and premium of shares allotted without the valuation the Chapter requires?
GIVEN `the company allotted shares in contravention of section 593(1)` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did the company allot shares in contravention of section 593(1)?
      `the allottee has not received the valuer's report` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has the allottee not received the valuer's report required to be sent to him?
      `the allottee knew or ought to have known of another contravention` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has there been some other contravention of the requirements of section 593 or 596 that the allottee knew or ought to have known amounted to a contravention?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 593(3), must the allottee pay the company the nominal value and premium of shares allotted without the valuation the Chapter requires` IS
    `s 593(3) the allottee is liable to pay the company` `the company allotted shares in contravention of section 593(1)` `the allottee has not received the valuer's report` `the allottee knew or ought to have known of another contravention`

@export Under section 594(4), is the arrangement with another company one to which the exception from valuation applies?
GIVEN `the arrangement is for the allotment of shares in my company (company A)` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the arrangement for the allotment of shares in your company (company A)?
      `the consideration is provided by the transfer to company A of shares in company B` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the whole or part of the consideration to be provided by the transfer to company A of all or some of the shares (or of a class of shares) in another company (company B)?
      `the consideration is provided by the cancellation of shares in company B` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the whole or part of the consideration to be provided by the cancellation of all or some of the shares (or of a class of shares) in company B?
      `it is open to all the holders of the shares in company B to take part` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it open to all the holders of the shares in company B (or of the class the arrangement applies to), leaving out shares held by company A, its holding company or subsidiaries and treasury shares of company B, to take part?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 594(4), is the arrangement with another company one to which the exception from valuation applies` IS
    `s 594(4) the arrangement is one to which section 594 applies`
        (`s 594(2) the arrangement is of the kind to which section 594 applies` `the arrangement is for the allotment of shares in my company (company A)` `the consideration is provided by the transfer to company A of shares in company B` `the consideration is provided by the cancellation of shares in company B`)
        `it is open to all the holders of the shares in company B to take part`

@export Under section 598(1), is my public company prohibited from entering into this agreement to acquire a non-cash asset from a subscriber in its initial period?
GIVEN `my company is a public company formed as such` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is your company a public company formed as such (or re-registered as public: then answer for a company re-registered, below)?
      `the other party is a subscriber to the memorandum (or, if re-registered, a member on the date of re-registration)` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the other party a subscriber to the company's memorandum (for a company re-registered as public: a person who was a member on the date of re-registration)?
      `the agreement is for the transfer of non-cash assets` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the agreement for the transfer by him to the company, or another, of one or more non-cash assets?
      `the date by which the transfer is to be made` IS A DATE @desc By what date is the transfer to be made? (a date)
      `the date the company's trading certificate was issued (or the date of re-registration)` IS A DATE @desc On what date was the company issued with a certificate under section 761 (trading certificate), or, for a re-registered company, on what date was it re-registered as public? (a date)
      `the value of the consideration the company gives` IS A NUMBER @desc What is, at the time of the agreement, the value of the consideration the company is to give, in pounds?
      `the company's issued share capital` IS A NUMBER @desc What is the company's issued share capital, in pounds?
      `it is part of the company's ordinary business to acquire such assets and the agreement is in the ordinary course` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it part of the company's ordinary business to acquire assets of this description, and is the agreement entered into in the ordinary course of that business?
      `the agreement is entered into under the supervision of the court` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the agreement entered into under the supervision of the court, or of an officer authorised by the court for the purpose?
      `the consideration has been independently valued, within the six months, and the report sent` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Have the conditions of independent valuation (section 599) been complied with: valued, the report made within the six months before the agreement, and a copy sent in time to the other party?
      `the agreement is approved by members as section 601 requires` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Have the conditions of approval by members (section 601) been complied with: an ordinary resolution, the report circulated, and the resolution sent to the other party?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 598(1), is my public company prohibited from entering into this agreement to acquire a non-cash asset from a subscriber in its initial period` IS
    `s 598(1) the public company is prohibited from entering into the agreement` `my company is a public company formed as such` `the other party is a subscriber to the memorandum (or, if re-registered, a member on the date of re-registration)` `the agreement is for the transfer of non-cash assets` `the date by which the transfer is to be made`
        (`s 598(2) the last day of the company's initial period` `the date the company's trading certificate was issued (or the date of re-registration)`)
        `the value of the consideration the company gives` `the company's issued share capital`
        (`s 598(4) section 598 does not apply to the agreement` `it is part of the company's ordinary business to acquire such assets and the agreement is in the ordinary course` `it is part of the company's ordinary business to acquire such assets and the agreement is in the ordinary course`)
        (`s 598(5) section 598 does not apply to the agreement because of the court's supervision` `the agreement is entered into under the supervision of the court`)
        (`coa13 seat a stated fact as an answer` `the consideration has been independently valued, within the six months, and the report sent`)
        (`coa13 seat a stated fact as an answer` `the agreement is approved by members as section 601 requires`)

@export Under section 602(1), has my company delivered the copy of the resolution and the valuer's report to the registrar in time?
GIVEN `the copy and the report were properly delivered` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Have the copy of the resolution and the valuer's report been properly delivered to the registrar?
      `the day the registrar received them` IS A DATE @desc On what day did the registrar receive them? (a date; any date if they have not been delivered)
      `the date the company passed the resolution` IS A DATE @desc On what date did the company pass the resolution under section 601? (a date, for example 2026-03-01)
      `the date today` IS A DATE @desc What is today's date? (a date)
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 602(1), has my company delivered the copy of the resolution and the valuer's report to the registrar in time` IS
    `s 602(1) the company has delivered the copy of the resolution and the valuer's report in time` (`coa13 seat a stated fact as an answer` `the copy and the report were properly delivered`) `the day the registrar received them` `the date the company passed the resolution` `the date today`

@export Under section 604, may my company recover what it gave under an agreement made in contravention of section 598?
GIVEN `a public company entered into an agreement in contravention of section 598` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did the public company enter into the agreement in contravention of section 598?
      `the other party has not received the valuer's report` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has the other party to the agreement not received the valuer's report required to be sent to him?
      `the other party knew or ought to have known of another contravention` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has there been some other contravention of the requirements of Chapter 6 that the other party knew or ought to have known amounted to a contravention?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 604, may my company recover what it gave under an agreement made in contravention of section 598` IS
    `s 604(2)(a) the company is entitled to recover from that person the consideration it gave, or its value` (`s 604(1) section 604 applies` `a public company entered into an agreement in contravention of section 598` `the other party has not received the valuer's report` `the other party knew or ought to have known of another contravention`)

@export Under section 605, am I, as a later holder of the shares, liable to pay the amount another person owes the company?
GIVEN `there has been a contravention of section 593 in respect of the shares` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has there been a contravention of section 593 in respect of the shares?
      `another person is liable to pay an amount because of that contravention` IS A BOOLEAN @desc By virtue of that contravention, is another person liable to pay an amount under the provision contravened?
      `I am a purchaser for value` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are you a purchaser for value of the shares?
      `I did not have actual notice of the contravention when I purchased` IS A BOOLEAN @desc At the time of the purchase, did you not have actual notice of the contravention?
      `I derived title from a person who became a holder after the contravention` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did you derive title to the shares (directly or indirectly) from a person who became a holder of them after the contravention?
      `that person was not liable` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Was that person not liable under section 605(1) or (2)?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 605, am I, as a later holder of the shares, liable to pay the amount another person owes the company` IS
    `s 605(1) the person who becomes a holder is also liable to pay the amount` `there has been a contravention of section 593 in respect of the shares` `another person is liable to pay an amount because of that contravention`
        (`s 605(3) the person is exempted from the liability` `I am a purchaser for value` `I did not have actual notice of the contravention when I purchased` `I derived title from a person who became a holder after the contravention` `that person was not liable`)

@export Under section 606, may I apply to the court to be exempted from a liability under Chapter 6?
GIVEN `I am liable to a company under a provision of Chapter 6 in relation to payment in respect of its shares` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are you liable to a company under a provision of Chapter 6 in relation to payment in respect of shares in the company?
      `I am liable to a company by virtue of an undertaking given in connection with payment for its shares` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are you liable to a company by virtue of an undertaking given to it in, or in connection with, payment for shares in the company?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 606, may I apply to the court to be exempted from a liability under Chapter 6` IS
    `s 606(1) the person may apply to the court to be exempted from the liability in whole or in part` `I am liable to a company under a provision of Chapter 6 in relation to payment in respect of its shares` `I am liable to a company by virtue of an undertaking given in connection with payment for its shares`

@export Under section 607, do I commit an offence as an officer of the company if it contravenes section 593 or section 598?
GIVEN `the company contravenes section 593 or section 598` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does the company contravene section 593 (allotting shares for non-cash consideration without valuation) or section 598 (agreement for transfer of a non-cash asset in the initial period)?
      `I am an officer of the company who is in default` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are you an officer of the company who is in default (within section 1121)?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 607, do I commit an offence as an officer of the company if it contravenes section 593 or section 598` IS
    `s 607(2)(b) the officer of the company commits an offence` (`s 607(1) section 607 applies` `the company contravenes section 593 or section 598`) (`coa13 seat a stated fact as an answer` `I am an officer of the company who is in default`)

@export Under section 609, what is the appropriate rate of interest for Chapter 6, as a fraction per annum?
GIVEN `an order specifies another rate` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has the Secretary of State made an order specifying a rate other than 5% a year?
      `the rate the order specifies` IS A NUMBER @desc If so, what rate does the order specify, as a fraction per year (for example 0.04 for 4%)? (0 if there is no order)
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `Under section 609, what is the appropriate rate of interest for Chapter 6, as a fraction per annum` IS
    `s 609(1) the appropriate rate of interest, as a fraction per annum` (IF `an order specifies another rate` THEN JUST `the rate the order specifies` ELSE NOTHING)

-- ====================================================================================================
-- seat questions from part coa14 (merged by the lead on 2026-11-12; unchanged text follows)
-- ====================================================================================================
-- coa14-seat.l4: Companies Act 2006, Part 17 Chapters 7 to 11 (ss 610 to 657), THE SEAT LAYER.
--
-- SEAT: an individual who is, or is about to become, a director, a company secretary or a member (shareholder) of a company
-- registered under the Act, or who deals with one, asking on facts they can state what the Act requires or lets them do, what
-- rights they have against the company or its directors, what they must disclose, file, approve or vote on and by when, and what
-- follows (liability, offences, penalties) if it is not done. (Assumed, not ruled: the Act is addressed to companies, so the
-- individual is whoever stands in a company's management or ownership.) There is never a seat for an official: where a section
-- addresses only the registrar or the court, a question asks what it means for this person.
--
-- PLAIN INPUTS. Every question takes plain inputs (yes/no, a number, a date, a choice written out in the @desc), one for each
-- fact the person can state, each with an @desc worded as that person would be asked. The records and lists the layer-1
-- modules expect are built inside each question, in its WHERE, from those answers, and the SAME layer-1 rule is then called;
-- no rule is restated here. Where a fact is another part's answer (is the resolution a special resolution, is the person an
-- officer in default) the layer-1 module takes it as a MAYBE input and this layer passes `JUST` the person's yes or no.
-- The pounds a level of the standard scale or the statutory maximum stands for are not in the Act: they are asked.
--
-- HOW TO READ AN ANSWER (the rule of 2026-10-29, assumed, not ruled by a lawyer): a MAYBE BOOLEAN answer JUST TRUE is a yes
-- the text gives in its own words; JUST FALSE is a no the text gives in its own words; NOTHING means the Act, as encoded, does
-- not say on these facts (not covered). A question titled as a bar ("does the Act bar ...") answers JUST TRUE where the text
-- says no to the act. NOTHING is never a no.

§ `Companies Act 2006, Part 17 Chapters 7 to 11 -- the questions of a director, secretary or member`

-- =========================================================================================================
-- CHAPTER 7: SHARE PREMIUMS
-- =========================================================================================================

§§ `Section 610: Application of share premiums`

@export Under section 610, must the company transfer a sum to the share premium account?
GIVEN `the company issues shares at a premium, whether for cash or otherwise` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the company issuing shares for more than their nominal value (at a premium), whether for cash or otherwise?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 610, must the company transfer a sum to the share premium account` IS
    `s 610(1) the company must transfer a sum to the share premium account` `the company issues shares at a premium, whether for cash or otherwise`

@export Under section 610, how much must the company transfer to the share premium account once any relief is taken into account?
GIVEN `the company issues shares at a premium, whether for cash or otherwise` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the company issuing shares for more than their nominal value (at a premium), whether for cash or otherwise?
      `the aggregate amount or value of the premiums on those shares` IS A NUMBER @desc What is the total amount (or, for a non-cash issue, the value) of the premiums on the shares, in pounds?
      `group reconstruction relief applies` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did your answer to the section 611 question say that group reconstruction relief applies to these shares?
      `the minimum premium value` IS A NUMBER @desc If group reconstruction relief applies: what is the minimum premium value under section 611(3), in pounds? (Any number if it does not apply.)
      `merger relief applies` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did your answer to the section 612 question say that section 610 does not apply to the premiums on these shares?
      `a regulation under section 614 relieves the company` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has a regulation made under section 614 relieved the company from section 610 for these premiums?
GIVETH A MAYBE NUMBER
DECIDE `Under section 610, how much must the company transfer to the share premium account once any relief is taken into account` IS
    `s 610(5) the sum that must be transferred to the share premium account, subject to sections 611, 612 and 614`
        `the company issues shares at a premium, whether for cash or otherwise`
        `the aggregate amount or value of the premiums on those shares`
        (JUST `group reconstruction relief applies`)
        (JUST `the minimum premium value`)
        (JUST `merger relief applies`)
        `a regulation under section 614 relieves the company`

@export Under section 610, may the company use the sum in the share premium account to write off expenses of the issue or commission paid on it?
GIVEN `the company has transferred a sum to the share premium account on issuing the shares` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has the company, on issuing the shares, transferred a sum to the share premium account?
      `what the sum would be used for` IS A STRING @desc What would the sum be used to write off? One of: "expenses of the issue", "commission paid on the issue", "something else".
      `the item relates to the issue of those shares` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does the expense or commission relate to the issue of those same shares?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 610, may the company use the sum in the share premium account to write off expenses of the issue or commission paid on it` IS
    `s 610(2) the company may use the sum to write off the item` `the company has transferred a sum to the share premium account on issuing the shares` use `the item relates to the issue of those shares`
    WHERE
        use MEANS
            BRANCH
                IF `what the sum would be used for` EQUALS "expenses of the issue" THEN `s 610(2)(a) writing off the expenses of the issue of those shares`
                IF `what the sum would be used for` EQUALS "commission paid on the issue" THEN `s 610(2)(b) writing off any commission paid on the issue of those shares`
                OTHERWISE `s 610(2) some other use of the sum`

@export Under section 610, may the company use the share premium account to pay up new shares as fully paid bonus shares for its members?
GIVEN `the shares are new shares to be allotted to members` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are the shares new shares that are to be allotted to the company's members?
      `they are to be allotted as fully paid bonus shares` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are they to be allotted as fully paid bonus shares?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 610, may the company use the share premium account to pay up new shares as fully paid bonus shares for its members` IS
    `s 610(3) the company may use the share premium account to pay up the shares` `the shares are new shares to be allotted to members` `they are to be allotted as fully paid bonus shares`

@export Under section 610, do the reduction provisions treat the share premium account as if it were part of the company's paid up share capital?
GIVEN `the account is used as subsection (2) or (3) allows` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the company using the share premium account in a way that section 610(2) or (3) allows (writing off the expenses or commission of the issue, or paying up bonus shares)?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 610, do the reduction provisions treat the share premium account as if it were part of the company's paid up share capital` IS
    `s 610(4) the reduction provisions treat the share premium account as paid up share capital` `the account is used as subsection (2) or (3) allows`

§§ `Section 611: Group reconstruction relief`

@export Under section 611, does group reconstruction relief apply to the shares the company is allotting?
GIVEN `the issuing company is a wholly-owned subsidiary of another company` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the company issuing the shares a wholly-owned subsidiary of another company (the holding company)? (Section 1159(2).)
      `the shares are allotted to the holding company itself` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are the shares allotted to the holding company itself?
      `the shares are allotted to a nominee of the holding company` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are the shares allotted to a nominee of the holding company?
      `the shares are allotted to another wholly-owned subsidiary of the holding company itself` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are the shares allotted to another wholly-owned subsidiary of the holding company?
      `the shares are allotted to a nominee of another wholly-owned subsidiary` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are the shares allotted to a nominee of another wholly-owned subsidiary of the holding company?
      `what is transferred is non-cash assets` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are the assets transferred to the issuing company non-cash assets (section 1163(1))?
      `the allotment is in consideration for the transfer of non-cash assets of the transferor company` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are the shares allotted in consideration for the transfer to the issuing company of those assets of the transferor company?
      `the transferor company is a member of the group` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the transferor company a member of the group of companies made up of the holding company and all its wholly-owned subsidiaries?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 611, does group reconstruction relief apply to the shares the company is allotting` IS
    `s 611(1) section 611 applies`
        `the issuing company is a wholly-owned subsidiary of another company`
        `the shares are allotted to the holding company itself`
        `the shares are allotted to a nominee of the holding company`
        `the shares are allotted to another wholly-owned subsidiary of the holding company itself`
        `the shares are allotted to a nominee of another wholly-owned subsidiary`
        `what is transferred is non-cash assets`
        `the allotment is in consideration for the transfer of non-cash assets of the transferor company`
        `the transferor company is a member of the group`

@export Under section 611, what is the minimum premium value of the shares being allotted?
GIVEN `the cost of the assets to the transferor company` IS A NUMBER @desc What did the assets cost the transferor company, in pounds?
      `the assets are stated in the transferor company's accounting records` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Were the assets stated in the transferor company's accounting records immediately before the transfer?
      `the amount at which the assets are stated` IS A NUMBER @desc At what amount were the assets stated there, in pounds? (Ignored if they were not stated.)
      `the amount at which the liabilities assumed are stated` IS A NUMBER @desc At what amount were the liabilities of the transferor company that the issuing company assumed stated in its accounting records immediately before the transfer, in pounds? (0 if none.)
      `the aggregate nominal value of the shares` IS A NUMBER @desc What is the aggregate nominal value of the shares allotted, in pounds?
GIVETH A MAYBE NUMBER
DECIDE `Under section 611, what is the minimum premium value of the shares being allotted` IS
    `s 611(3) the minimum premium value`
        (`s 611(4) the base value of the consideration for the shares allotted`
            (`s 611(5)(a) the base value of the assets transferred` `the cost of the assets to the transferor company` stated)
            (`s 611(5)(b) the base value of the liabilities assumed` `the amount at which the liabilities assumed are stated`))
        `the aggregate nominal value of the shares`
    WHERE
        stated MEANS IF `the assets are stated in the transferor company's accounting records` THEN JUST `the amount at which the assets are stated` ELSE NOTHING

§§ `Section 612: Merger relief`

@export Under section 612, does merger relief apply to the company that is issuing the shares?
GIVEN `the issuing company has secured at least a 90% equity holding in the other company` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has the issuing company secured at least a 90% equity holding in the other company? (See your answer to the section 613 question.)
      `the arrangement provides for the allotment of equity shares in the issuing company` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does the arrangement provide for the allotment of equity shares in the issuing company?
      `the equity shares in the other company are issued or transferred to the issuing company itself` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the consideration for those shares to be provided by the issue or transfer to the issuing company of equity shares in the other company?
      `the equity shares in the other company are issued or transferred to a nominee of the issuing company` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Or by the issue or transfer of those equity shares to a nominee of the issuing company?
      `any such shares not held by the issuing company are cancelled` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Or is the consideration to be provided by the cancellation of any such shares that the issuing company does not hold?
      `the case also falls within group reconstruction relief` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does the case also fall within group reconstruction relief (your answer to the section 611 question)?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 612, does merger relief apply to the company that is issuing the shares` IS
    `s 612(1) and (4) section 612 applies to the case` (JUST `the case also falls within group reconstruction relief`)
        (`s 612(1) section 612 applies` (JUST `the issuing company has secured at least a 90% equity holding in the other company`) `the arrangement provides for the allotment of equity shares in the issuing company` `the equity shares in the other company are issued or transferred to the issuing company itself` `the equity shares in the other company are issued or transferred to a nominee of the issuing company` `any such shares not held by the issuing company are cancelled`)

@export Under section 612, does section 610 not apply to the premiums on the shares the company is allotting?
GIVEN `merger relief applies` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did your answer to the section 612 merger relief question say that merger relief applies to the issuing company?
      `the shares are equity shares in the issuing company allotted in pursuance of the arrangement in consideration for the acquisition or cancellation of equity shares in the other company` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are these equity shares in the issuing company allotted under the arrangement in consideration for the acquisition or cancellation of equity shares in the other company?
      `they are issued at a premium` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are they issued at a premium?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 612, does section 610 not apply to the premiums on the shares the company is allotting` IS
    `s 612(2) section 610 does not apply to the premiums on those shares` (JUST `merger relief applies`) `the shares are equity shares in the issuing company allotted in pursuance of the arrangement in consideration for the acquisition or cancellation of equity shares in the other company` `they are issued at a premium`

@export Under section 612, does the relief extend to shares allotted for non-equity shares of the other company?
GIVEN `merger relief applies to the company` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does merger relief apply to the company that is issuing the shares (your answer to the section 612 question)?
      `the arrangement also provides for allotment on terms that the consideration is non-equity shares of the other company` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does the arrangement also provide for the allotment of shares in the issuing company on terms that the consideration is the issue or transfer to it of non-equity shares in the other company?
      `the arrangement also provides for allotment on terms that the consideration is the cancellation of such shares` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does the arrangement also provide for the allotment of shares on terms that the consideration is the cancellation of any such shares in the other company not held by the issuing company?
      `the shares are allotted on those terms in pursuance of the arrangement` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are the shares in question allotted on those terms in pursuance of the arrangement?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 612, does the relief extend to shares allotted for non-equity shares of the other company` IS
    `s 612(3) the relief under subsection (2) extends to the shares` (JUST `merger relief applies to the company`) `the arrangement also provides for allotment on terms that the consideration is non-equity shares of the other company` `the arrangement also provides for allotment on terms that the consideration is the cancellation of such shares` `the shares are allotted on those terms in pursuance of the arrangement`

§§ `Section 613: Merger relief: meaning of 90% equity holding`

@export Under section 613, has company A secured at least a 90% equity holding in company B?
GIVEN `the holding is in consequence of an acquisition or cancellation of equity shares in company B in pursuance of the arrangement` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does company A hold its equity shares in company B in consequence of an acquisition or cancellation of equity shares in company B under the arrangement?
      `company B has a second class of equity shares` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is company B's equity share capital divided into two classes? (If it has more than two, ask once for each pair of classes taken together as two, or take legal advice: this question handles two.)
      `class 1: nominal value held by company A` IS A NUMBER @desc First class: the nominal value of the equity shares that company A itself holds, in pounds.
      `class 1: nominal value held by A's holding company or subsidiary` IS A NUMBER @desc First class: the nominal value held by a company that is company A's holding company or subsidiary, in pounds.
      `class 1: nominal value held by a subsidiary of A's holding company` IS A NUMBER @desc First class: the nominal value held by a subsidiary of company A's holding company, in pounds.
      `class 1: nominal value held by their nominees` IS A NUMBER @desc First class: the nominal value held by the nominees of those companies, in pounds.
      `class 1: nominal value in company B's equity share capital` IS A NUMBER @desc First class: the nominal value of the whole class, treasury shares included, in pounds.
      `class 1: nominal value held by company B as treasury shares` IS A NUMBER @desc First class: the nominal value of it that company B holds as treasury shares, in pounds.
      `class 2: nominal value held by company A` IS A NUMBER @desc Second class (0 if there is none): the nominal value of the equity shares that company A itself holds, in pounds.
      `class 2: nominal value held by A's holding company or subsidiary` IS A NUMBER @desc Second class (0 if none): the nominal value held by a company that is company A's holding company or subsidiary, in pounds.
      `class 2: nominal value held by a subsidiary of A's holding company` IS A NUMBER @desc Second class (0 if none): the nominal value held by a subsidiary of company A's holding company, in pounds.
      `class 2: nominal value held by their nominees` IS A NUMBER @desc Second class (0 if none): the nominal value held by the nominees of those companies, in pounds.
      `class 2: nominal value in company B's equity share capital` IS A NUMBER @desc Second class (0 if none): the nominal value of the whole class, treasury shares included, in pounds.
      `class 2: nominal value held by company B as treasury shares` IS A NUMBER @desc Second class (0 if none): the nominal value of it that company B holds as treasury shares, in pounds.
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 613, has company A secured at least a 90% equity holding in company B` IS
    `s 613(2) and (4) company A has secured at least a 90% equity holding in company B, each class taken separately` `the holding is in consequence of an acquisition or cancellation of equity shares in company B in pursuance of the arrangement` classes
    WHERE
        classes MEANS
            IF `company B has a second class of equity shares`
            THEN LIST first, second
            ELSE LIST first
        first MEANS `s 613(2) class of company B's equity share capital` OF `class 1: nominal value held by company A`, `class 1: nominal value held by A's holding company or subsidiary`, `class 1: nominal value held by a subsidiary of A's holding company`, `class 1: nominal value held by their nominees`, `class 1: nominal value in company B's equity share capital`, `class 1: nominal value held by company B as treasury shares`
        second MEANS `s 613(2) class of company B's equity share capital` OF `class 2: nominal value held by company A`, `class 2: nominal value held by A's holding company or subsidiary`, `class 2: nominal value held by a subsidiary of A's holding company`, `class 2: nominal value held by their nominees`, `class 2: nominal value in company B's equity share capital`, `class 2: nominal value held by company B as treasury shares`

§§ `Section 615: Relief may be reflected in company's balance sheet`

@export Under section 615, how much of the premiums may be disregarded in determining the balance sheet amount of the shares or the consideration for them?
GIVEN `the premiums are not included in the share premium account by virtue of relief under this Chapter` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are the premiums (or part of them) left out of the share premium account because of relief under this Chapter (sections 611, 612 or regulations under section 614)?
      `the amount representing those premiums` IS A NUMBER @desc How much is the amount of those premiums that is not included in the account, in pounds?
GIVETH A MAYBE NUMBER
DECIDE `Under section 615, how much of the premiums may be disregarded in determining the balance sheet amount of the shares or the consideration for them` IS
    `s 615 the amount that may be disregarded in determining the balance sheet amount` `the premiums are not included in the share premium account by virtue of relief under this Chapter` `the amount representing those premiums`

§§ `Section 616: Interpretation of this Chapter`

@export Under section 616, is this act treated as an act of the company for this Chapter?
GIVEN `the kind of act` IS A STRING @desc What kind of act is it? One of: "acquisition of shares in another company", "issue, allotment or transfer of shares to or by a company", "something else".
      `the act is done by the company itself` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the act done by the company itself?
      `the act is done by a nominee of that company` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the act done by a nominee of that company?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 616, is this act treated as an act of the company for this Chapter` IS
    `s 616(2) the act is treated as an act of the company` kind `the act is done by the company itself` `the act is done by a nominee of that company`
    WHERE
        kind MEANS
            BRANCH
                IF `the kind of act` EQUALS "acquisition of shares in another company" THEN `s 616(2)(a) the acquisition by a company of shares in another company`
                IF `the kind of act` EQUALS "issue, allotment or transfer of shares to or by a company" THEN `s 616(2)(b) the issue or allotment of shares to, or the transfer of shares to or by, a company`
                OTHERWISE `s 616(2) some other act`

@export Under section 616, are these shares equity shares for this Chapter?
GIVEN `the shares are comprised in the company's equity share capital` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are the shares comprised in the company's equity share capital (your answer to the section 548 question)?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 616, are these shares equity shares for this Chapter` IS
    `s 616(1) the shares are equity shares` (JUST `the shares are comprised in the company's equity share capital`)

@export Under section 616, are these shares non-equity shares for this Chapter?
GIVEN `the shares are comprised in the company's equity share capital` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are the shares comprised in the company's equity share capital (your answer to the section 548 question)?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 616, are these shares non-equity shares for this Chapter` IS
    `s 616(1) the shares are non-equity shares` (JUST `the shares are comprised in the company's equity share capital`)

@export Under section 616, does a reference in this Chapter to the transfer of shares in the company cover this transaction?
GIVEN `it is a transfer of shares in the company` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it a transfer of shares in the company?
      `it is a transfer of a right to be included in the company's register of members in respect of those shares` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it a transfer of a right to be included in the company's register of members in respect of those shares?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 616, does a reference in this Chapter to the transfer of shares in the company cover this transaction` IS
    `s 616(3) the transaction is a transfer of shares in the company for this Chapter` `it is a transfer of shares in the company` `it is a transfer of a right to be included in the company's register of members in respect of those shares`

-- =========================================================================================================
-- CHAPTER 8: ALTERATION OF SHARE CAPITAL
-- =========================================================================================================

§§ `Section 617: Alteration of share capital of limited company`

@export Under section 617, does the Act bar the company from altering its share capital in this way?
GIVEN `the company is a limited company having a share capital` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the company a limited company that has a share capital?
      `the way the share capital is altered` IS A STRING @desc How is the share capital to be altered? One of: "increase by allotting new shares in accordance with this Part", "reduce in accordance with Chapter 10", "sub-divide or consolidate in accordance with section 618", "reconvert stock into shares in accordance with section 620", "redenominate in accordance with section 622", "reduce in accordance with section 626 in connection with a redenomination", "purchase or redeem shares in accordance with Part 18", "purchase shares in pursuance of a court order under section 98, 721(6), 759 or Part 30", "forfeit shares or accept shares surrendered in lieu, under the articles", "cancel shares under section 662", "compromise or arrangement under Part 26 or 26A, or compliance with a court order on it", "cancel a share warrant under Schedule 4 to the Small Business, Enterprise and Employment Act 2015", "cancel a share warrant under section 1028A(2) or 1032A(2)", "some other way".
      `the alteration is made in accordance with the provision that names the way` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it made in accordance with the section or Part named in that way (for example Chapter 10, section 618, Part 18)?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 617, does the Act bar the company from altering its share capital in this way` IS
    `s 617(1) the section bars the company from altering its share capital in this way` `the company is a limited company having a share capital` (`s 617(1) alteration of share capital` OF way, `the alteration is made in accordance with the provision that names the way`)
    WHERE
        way MEANS
            BRANCH
                IF `the way the share capital is altered` EQUALS "increase by allotting new shares in accordance with this Part" THEN `s 617(2)(a) increase the share capital by allotting new shares in accordance with this Part`
                IF `the way the share capital is altered` EQUALS "reduce in accordance with Chapter 10" THEN `s 617(2)(b) reduce the share capital in accordance with Chapter 10`
                IF `the way the share capital is altered` EQUALS "sub-divide or consolidate in accordance with section 618" THEN `s 617(3)(a) sub-divide or consolidate the share capital in accordance with section 618`
                IF `the way the share capital is altered` EQUALS "reconvert stock into shares in accordance with section 620" THEN `s 617(3)(b) reconvert stock into shares in accordance with section 620`
                IF `the way the share capital is altered` EQUALS "redenominate in accordance with section 622" THEN `s 617(4)(a) redenominate shares in accordance with section 622`
                IF `the way the share capital is altered` EQUALS "reduce in accordance with section 626 in connection with a redenomination" THEN `s 617(4)(b) reduce the share capital in accordance with section 626 in connection with a redenomination`
                IF `the way the share capital is altered` EQUALS "purchase or redeem shares in accordance with Part 18" THEN `s 617(5)(a) purchase or redeem shares in accordance with Part 18`
                IF `the way the share capital is altered` EQUALS "purchase shares in pursuance of a court order under section 98, 721(6), 759 or Part 30" THEN `s 617(5)(b) purchase shares in pursuance of an order of the court under section 98, 721(6), 759 or Part 30`
                IF `the way the share capital is altered` EQUALS "forfeit shares or accept shares surrendered in lieu, under the articles" THEN `s 617(5)(c) forfeit shares, or accept shares surrendered in lieu, in pursuance of the articles`
                IF `the way the share capital is altered` EQUALS "cancel shares under section 662" THEN `s 617(5)(d) cancel shares under section 662`
                IF `the way the share capital is altered` EQUALS "compromise or arrangement under Part 26 or 26A, or compliance with a court order on it" THEN `s 617(5)(e) compromise or arrangement under Part 26 or 26A, or compliance with a court order on an application under that Part`
                IF `the way the share capital is altered` EQUALS "cancel a share warrant under Schedule 4 to the Small Business, Enterprise and Employment Act 2015" THEN `s 617(5)(f) cancel a share warrant and its shares under paragraph 6 of Schedule 4 to the Small Business, Enterprise and Employment Act 2015`
                IF `the way the share capital is altered` EQUALS "cancel a share warrant under section 1028A(2) or 1032A(2)" THEN `s 617(5)(g) cancel a share warrant and its shares under section 1028A(2) or 1032A(2)`
                OTHERWISE `s 617 some other way of altering share capital`

§§ `Section 618: Sub-division or consolidation of shares`

@export Under section 618, may the company sub-divide or consolidate its shares?
GIVEN `the company is a limited company having a share capital` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the company a limited company that has a share capital?
      `the change is a sub-division` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the change a sub-division into shares of a smaller nominal amount? (Answer no if it is a consolidation and division into shares of a larger nominal amount.)
      `the nominal amount of each resulting share` IS A NUMBER @desc What will be the nominal amount of each resulting share, in pounds?
      `the nominal amount of the existing shares` IS A NUMBER @desc What is the nominal amount of each existing share, in pounds?
      `the amount paid on the share before` IS A NUMBER @desc How much has been paid on an existing share, in pounds?
      `the amount unpaid on the share before` IS A NUMBER @desc How much is unpaid on an existing share, in pounds? (0 if none.)
      `the amount paid on the resulting share` IS A NUMBER @desc How much will be treated as paid on a resulting share, in pounds?
      `the amount unpaid on the resulting share` IS A NUMBER @desc How much will be unpaid on a resulting share, in pounds? (0 if none.)
      `members have passed a resolution authorising the company to exercise the power` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Have the members passed a resolution authorising the company to do this?
      `the articles exclude or restrict the exercise of the power in the way proposed` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Do the company's articles exclude or restrict the exercise of this power in the way proposed?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 618, may the company sub-divide or consolidate its shares` IS
    `s 618 the company may exercise the power conferred by section 618`
        (`s 618(1) the company may use the power to change its shares in this way` `the company is a limited company having a share capital` change `the nominal amount of each resulting share` `the nominal amount of the existing shares`)
        (`s 618(2) the proportion between the amount paid and the amount unpaid is the same as before` `the amount paid on the share before` `the amount unpaid on the share before` `the amount paid on the resulting share` `the amount unpaid on the resulting share`)
        (`s 618(3) the section bars the company from exercising the power for want of a resolution` `members have passed a resolution authorising the company to exercise the power`)
        (`s 618(5) the company's articles bar the exercise of the power` `the articles exclude or restrict the exercise of the power in the way proposed`)
    WHERE
        change MEANS
            IF `the change is a sub-division`
            THEN `s 618(1)(a) sub-division into shares of a smaller nominal amount`
            ELSE `s 618(1)(b) consolidation and division into shares of a larger nominal amount`

@export Under section 618, may the resolution authorise the company to do this?
GIVEN `the resolution is a resolution under subsection (3)` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the resolution one passed by the members under section 618(3), authorising the company to sub-divide or consolidate its shares?
      `what the resolution would authorise` IS A STRING @desc What would the resolution authorise? One of: "the exercise of more than one of the powers", "the exercise of a power on more than one occasion", "the exercise of a power at a specified time or in specified circumstances", "something else".
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 618, may the resolution authorise the company to do this` IS
    `s 618(4) the resolution may authorise this` `the resolution is a resolution under subsection (3)` authorises
    WHERE
        authorises MEANS
            BRANCH
                IF `what the resolution would authorise` EQUALS "the exercise of more than one of the powers" THEN `s 618(4)(a) the exercise of more than one of the powers`
                IF `what the resolution would authorise` EQUALS "the exercise of a power on more than one occasion" THEN `s 618(4)(b) the exercise of a power on more than one occasion`
                IF `what the resolution would authorise` EQUALS "the exercise of a power at a specified time or in specified circumstances" THEN `s 618(4)(c) the exercise of a power at a specified time or in specified circumstances`
                OTHERWISE `s 618(4) something else`

§§ `Section 619: Notice to registrar of sub-division or consolidation`
@export Under section 619, by what day must the company give notice of the sub-division or consolidation to the registrar?
GIVEN `the date the company exercised the power conferred by section 618` IS A DATE @desc On what day did the company exercise its power to sub-divide or consolidate its shares?
GIVETH A DATE
DECIDE `Under section 619, by what day must the company give notice of the sub-division or consolidation to the registrar` IS
    `s 619(1) the last day for the notice` `the date the company exercised the power conferred by section 618`

@export Under section 619, am I committing an offence as an officer of the company by the way it has dealt with the notice?
GIVEN `the date the company exercised the power conferred by section 618` IS A DATE @desc On what day did the company exercise its power to sub-divide or consolidate its shares?
      `the company has given the notice to the registrar` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has the company given the notice to the registrar?
      `the date the notice reached the registrar` IS A DATE @desc On what day did the company give the notice to the registrar? (Ignored if it has not given it.)
      `today's date` IS A DATE @desc What day are you asking about (normally today)?
      `the notice specifies the shares affected` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does the notice specify the shares affected?
      `the notice is accompanied by a statement of capital` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the notice accompanied by a statement of capital?
      `the statement of capital states everything the section requires` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does the statement of capital state everything this section requires: the total number of shares, their aggregate nominal value, the aggregate amount unpaid, and for each class the particulars of the rights, the number of shares and their aggregate nominal value, as at the time the section names?
      `I am an officer of the company who is in default` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are you an officer of the company who is in default, that is, someone who authorised or permitted the default, took part in it, or failed to take all reasonable steps to prevent it (section 1121)?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 619, am I committing an offence as an officer of the company by the way it has dealt with the notice` IS
    `s 619(4)(b) the officer commits an offence` default (JUST `I am an officer of the company who is in default`)
    WHERE
        `the notice date, if there is one` MEANS
            IF `the company has given the notice to the registrar` THEN JUST `the date the notice reached the registrar` ELSE NOTHING
        timely MEANS `s 619(1) the company gave notice to the registrar in time` `the date the company exercised the power conferred by section 618` `the notice date, if there is one` `today's date`
        `my statement of capital` MEANS `s 619(3) statement of capital` OF `the statement of capital states everything the section requires`, TRUE, TRUE, (LIST (`s 619(3)(c) class entry in a statement of capital` OF TRUE, TRUE, TRUE)), TRUE
        default MEANS `s 619(4) default is made in complying with this section` (LIST timely, (`s 619(1) the notice specifies the shares affected` `the notice specifies the shares affected`), (`s 619(2) the notice is accompanied by a statement of capital` `the notice is accompanied by a statement of capital`), (`s 619(3) the statement of capital states what the section requires` `my statement of capital`))

@export Under section 619, what is the most that a person guilty of the offence can be fined on summary conviction, not counting the daily default fine for continued contravention, in pounds?
GIVEN `the pounds that level 3 on the standard scale stands for` IS A NUMBER @desc How many pounds is level 3 on the standard scale? (The Act does not say; it is set outside the Act.)
GIVETH A MAYBE NUMBER
DECIDE `Under section 619, what is the most that a person guilty of the offence can be fined on summary conviction, not counting the daily default fine for continued contravention, in pounds` IS
    CONSIDER `s 619(5) the penalty for a person guilty of an offence under this section` TRUE
    WHEN NOTHING THEN NOTHING
    WHEN JUST p THEN
        CONSIDER p's `fine not exceeding`
        WHEN NOTHING THEN NOTHING
        WHEN JUST f THEN `s 619(5) the most a fine can be, in pounds` f `the pounds that level 3 on the standard scale stands for` 0


§§ `Section 620: Reconversion of stock into shares`

@export Under section 620, may the company reconvert stock into shares?
GIVEN `the company is a limited company` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the company a limited company?
      `it converted paid-up shares into stock before the repeal by this Act of the power to do so` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did the company convert paid-up shares into stock before this Act repealed the power to do so?
      `members have passed a resolution authorising the company to exercise the power` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Have the members passed a resolution authorising the company to reconvert the stock?
      `the resolution is an ordinary resolution` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is that resolution an ordinary resolution (or a special resolution, which also serves)?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 620, may the company reconvert stock into shares` IS
    `s 620 the company may exercise the power conferred by section 620`
        (`s 620(1) the company may reconvert the stock into paid-up shares of any nominal value` `the company is a limited company` `it converted paid-up shares into stock before the repeal by this Act of the power to do so`)
        (`s 620(2) the section bars the company from exercising the power for want of an ordinary resolution` `members have passed a resolution authorising the company to exercise the power` (JUST `the resolution is an ordinary resolution`))

@export Under section 620, may the resolution authorise the company to do this?
GIVEN `the resolution is a resolution under subsection (2)` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the resolution one passed by the members under section 620(2), authorising the company to reconvert stock into shares?
      `what the resolution would authorise` IS A STRING @desc What would the resolution authorise? One of: "the exercise of the power on more than one occasion", "the exercise of the power at a specified time or in specified circumstances", "something else".
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 620, may the resolution authorise the company to do this` IS
    `s 620(3) the resolution may authorise this` `the resolution is a resolution under subsection (2)` authorises
    WHERE
        authorises MEANS
            BRANCH
                IF `what the resolution would authorise` EQUALS "the exercise of the power on more than one occasion" THEN `s 620(3)(a) the exercise of the power on more than one occasion`
                IF `what the resolution would authorise` EQUALS "the exercise of the power at a specified time or in specified circumstances" THEN `s 620(3)(b) the exercise of the power at a specified time or in specified circumstances`
                OTHERWISE `s 620(3) something else`

§§ `Section 621: Notice to registrar of reconversion of stock into shares`
@export Under section 621, by what day must the company give notice of the reconversion to the registrar?
GIVEN `the date the company exercised a power conferred by section 620` IS A DATE @desc On what day did the company reconvert stock into shares?
GIVETH A DATE
DECIDE `Under section 621, by what day must the company give notice of the reconversion to the registrar` IS
    `s 621(1) the last day for the notice` `the date the company exercised a power conferred by section 620`

@export Under section 621, am I committing an offence as an officer of the company by the way it has dealt with the notice?
GIVEN `the date the company exercised a power conferred by section 620` IS A DATE @desc On what day did the company reconvert stock into shares?
      `the company has given the notice to the registrar` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has the company given the notice to the registrar?
      `the date the notice reached the registrar` IS A DATE @desc On what day did the company give the notice to the registrar? (Ignored if it has not given it.)
      `today's date` IS A DATE @desc What day are you asking about (normally today)?
      `the notice specifies the stock affected` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does the notice specify the stock affected?
      `the notice is accompanied by a statement of capital` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the notice accompanied by a statement of capital?
      `the statement of capital states everything the section requires` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does the statement of capital state everything this section requires: the total number of shares, their aggregate nominal value, the aggregate amount unpaid, and for each class the particulars of the rights, the number of shares and their aggregate nominal value, as at the time the section names?
      `I am an officer of the company who is in default` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are you an officer of the company who is in default, that is, someone who authorised or permitted the default, took part in it, or failed to take all reasonable steps to prevent it (section 1121)?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 621, am I committing an offence as an officer of the company by the way it has dealt with the notice` IS
    `s 621(4)(b) the officer commits an offence` default (JUST `I am an officer of the company who is in default`)
    WHERE
        `the notice date, if there is one` MEANS
            IF `the company has given the notice to the registrar` THEN JUST `the date the notice reached the registrar` ELSE NOTHING
        timely MEANS `s 621(1) the company gave notice to the registrar in time` `the date the company exercised a power conferred by section 620` `the notice date, if there is one` `today's date`
        `my statement of capital` MEANS `s 619(3) statement of capital` OF `the statement of capital states everything the section requires`, TRUE, TRUE, (LIST (`s 619(3)(c) class entry in a statement of capital` OF TRUE, TRUE, TRUE)), TRUE
        default MEANS `s 621(4) default is made in complying with this section` (LIST timely, (`s 621(1) the notice specifies the stock affected` `the notice specifies the stock affected`), (`s 621(2) the notice is accompanied by a statement of capital` `the notice is accompanied by a statement of capital`), (`s 621(3) the statement of capital states what the section requires` `my statement of capital`))

@export Under section 621, what is the most that a person guilty of the offence can be fined on summary conviction, not counting the daily default fine for continued contravention, in pounds?
GIVEN `the pounds that level 3 on the standard scale stands for` IS A NUMBER @desc How many pounds is level 3 on the standard scale? (The Act does not say; it is set outside the Act.)
GIVETH A MAYBE NUMBER
DECIDE `Under section 621, what is the most that a person guilty of the offence can be fined on summary conviction, not counting the daily default fine for continued contravention, in pounds` IS
    CONSIDER `s 621(5) the penalty for a person guilty of an offence under this section` TRUE
    WHEN NOTHING THEN NOTHING
    WHEN JUST p THEN
        CONSIDER p's `fine not exceeding`
        WHEN NOTHING THEN NOTHING
        WHEN JUST f THEN `s 619(5) the most a fine can be, in pounds` f `the pounds that level 3 on the standard scale stands for` 0


§§ `Section 622: Redenomination of share capital`

@export Under section 622, is the company's redenomination within the section?
GIVEN `the company is a limited company having a share capital` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the company a limited company that has a share capital?
      `the redenomination is of its share capital or a class of its share capital` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the redenomination of all its share capital or of a whole class of it?
      `the redenomination is made by resolution` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it made by a resolution of the company?
      `the rate is an appropriate spot rate of exchange` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the rate of exchange an appropriate spot rate?
      `the rate is specified in the resolution` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the rate specified in the resolution?
      `the rate is of the first kind` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the rate the rate prevailing on a day the resolution specifies? (Answer no if it is the average of the rates over a period the resolution specifies.)
      `the day the resolution is passed` IS A DATE @desc On what day is the resolution passed?
      `the day specified in the resolution` IS A DATE @desc If the rate is that of a day: which day does the resolution specify? (Any date if it is an average.)
      `the first day of the period specified in the resolution` IS A DATE @desc If the rate is an average: the first day of the period the resolution specifies. (Any date if it is a day.)
      `the last day of the period specified in the resolution` IS A DATE @desc If the rate is an average: the last day of the period. (Any date if it is a day.)
      `the articles prohibit or restrict the exercise of the power in the way proposed` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Do the company's articles prohibit or restrict the exercise of this power in the way proposed?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 622, is the company's redenomination within the section` IS
    `s 622 the redenomination is within the section`
        (`s 622(1) the company may redenominate its share capital` `the company is a limited company having a share capital` `the redenomination is of its share capital or a class of its share capital` `the redenomination is made by resolution`)
        (`s 622(2) the conversion is made at a rate the section requires` `the rate is an appropriate spot rate of exchange` `the rate is specified in the resolution`)
        (`s 622(3) the rate is of a kind the section allows` kind)
        (`s 622(3) the day or period specified is within the 28 days ending on the day before the resolution is passed` `the day the resolution is passed` kind `the day specified in the resolution` `the first day of the period specified in the resolution` `the last day of the period specified in the resolution`)
        (`s 622(7) the company's articles bar the exercise of the power` `the articles prohibit or restrict the exercise of the power in the way proposed`)
    WHERE
        kind MEANS
            IF `the rate is of the first kind`
            THEN `s 622(3)(a) a rate prevailing on a day specified in the resolution`
            ELSE `s 622(3)(b) the average of the rates prevailing on each consecutive day of a period specified in the resolution`

@export Under section 622, on what day does the redenomination take effect?
GIVEN `the day the resolution is passed` IS A DATE @desc On what day was the resolution passed?
      `the resolution determines a later day` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does the resolution determine a later day on which the redenomination takes effect?
      `the later day determined in accordance with the resolution` IS A DATE @desc If so, which day? (Ignored if not.)
GIVETH A MAYBE DATE
DECIDE `Under section 622, on what day does the redenomination take effect` IS
    `s 622(5) the day the redenomination takes effect` `the day the resolution is passed` later
    WHERE
        later MEANS IF `the resolution determines a later day` THEN JUST `the later day determined in accordance with the resolution` ELSE NOTHING

@export Under section 622, has the redenomination resolution lapsed?
GIVEN `the day the resolution is passed` IS A DATE @desc On what day was the resolution passed?
      `the redenomination has taken effect` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has the redenomination taken effect?
      `the day the redenomination took effect` IS A DATE @desc If so, on what day? (Ignored if not.)
      `the date being asked about` IS A DATE @desc What day are you asking about (normally today)?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 622, has the redenomination resolution lapsed` IS
    `s 622(6) the resolution has lapsed` `the day the resolution is passed` effect `the date being asked about`
    WHERE
        effect MEANS IF `the redenomination has taken effect` THEN JUST `the day the redenomination took effect` ELSE NOTHING

@export Under section 622, does a condition in the resolution hold the redenomination back?
GIVEN `the resolution specifies conditions which must be met before the redenomination takes effect` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does the resolution specify conditions that must be met before the redenomination takes effect?
      `all those conditions have been met` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Have all those conditions been met?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 622, does a condition in the resolution hold the redenomination back` IS
    `s 622(4) a condition in the resolution holds the redenomination back` `the resolution specifies conditions which must be met before the redenomination takes effect` `all those conditions have been met`

§§ `Section 623: Calculation of new nominal values`

@export Under section 623, what is the new nominal value of each share of the class after the redenomination, in the new currency?
GIVEN `the number of shares in the class` IS A NUMBER @desc How many shares are in the class?
      `the old nominal value of each share` IS A NUMBER @desc What is the old nominal value of each share of the class, in the old currency?
      `the rate of exchange specified in the resolution` IS A NUMBER @desc How many units of the new currency does the resolution give for one unit of the old currency?
GIVETH A MAYBE NUMBER
DECIDE `Under section 623, what is the new nominal value of each share of the class after the redenomination, in the new currency` IS
    `s 623 the new nominal value of each share of the class` (replicate `the number of shares in the class` `the old nominal value of each share`) `the rate of exchange specified in the resolution`

§§ `Section 624: Effect of redenomination`

@export Under section 624, does the redenomination affect this right, restriction or liability of a member?
GIVEN `the matter` IS A STRING @desc What is the matter? One of: "a right or obligation of a member under the company's constitution", "a restriction affecting a member under the company's constitution", "entitlement to dividends", "entitlement to dividends in a particular currency", "voting rights", "liability in respect of amounts unpaid on shares", "something else".
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 624, does the redenomination affect this right, restriction or liability of a member` IS
    `s 624(1) the redenomination affects the matter` m
    WHERE
        m MEANS
            BRANCH
                IF `the matter` EQUALS "a right or obligation of a member under the company's constitution" THEN `s 624(1) a right or obligation of a member under the company's constitution`
                IF `the matter` EQUALS "a restriction affecting a member under the company's constitution" THEN `s 624(1) a restriction affecting a member under the company's constitution`
                IF `the matter` EQUALS "entitlement to dividends" THEN `s 624(1) entitlement to dividends`
                IF `the matter` EQUALS "entitlement to dividends in a particular currency" THEN `s 624(1) entitlement to dividends in a particular currency`
                IF `the matter` EQUALS "voting rights" THEN `s 624(1) voting rights`
                IF `the matter` EQUALS "liability in respect of amounts unpaid on shares" THEN `s 624(1) liability in respect of amounts unpaid on shares`
                OTHERWISE `s 624(1) some other matter`

@export Under section 624, is a reference to the old nominal value of the shares read as a reference to the new nominal value?
GIVEN `the reference is in an agreement, statement, deed, instrument or document` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the reference in an agreement, statement, deed, instrument or other document?
      `the resolution has taken effect` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has the redenomination resolution taken effect?
      `the context otherwise requires` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does the context of the document require the reference to stay a reference to the old nominal value?
      `reading it as a reference to the new nominal value would affect a right, obligation or restriction protected by subsection (1)` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Would reading it as a reference to the new nominal value affect a right, obligation or restriction of a member that the redenomination does not touch (section 624(1))?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 624, is a reference to the old nominal value of the shares read as a reference to the new nominal value` IS
    `s 624(3) the reference to the old nominal value is read as a reference to the new nominal value` `the reference is in an agreement, statement, deed, instrument or document` `the resolution has taken effect` `the context otherwise requires` `reading it as a reference to the new nominal value would affect a right, obligation or restriction protected by subsection (1)`

§§ `Section 625: Notice to registrar of redenomination`
@export Under section 625, by what day must the company give notice of the redenomination to the registrar?
GIVEN `the date the company redenominated its share capital` IS A DATE @desc On what day did the company redenominate its share capital?
GIVETH A DATE
DECIDE `Under section 625, by what day must the company give notice of the redenomination to the registrar` IS
    `s 625(1) the last day for the notice` `the date the company redenominated its share capital`

@export Under section 625, am I committing an offence as an officer of the company by the way it has dealt with the notice?
GIVEN `the date the company redenominated its share capital` IS A DATE @desc On what day did the company redenominate its share capital?
      `the company has given the notice to the registrar` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has the company given the notice to the registrar?
      `the date the notice reached the registrar` IS A DATE @desc On what day did the company give the notice to the registrar? (Ignored if it has not given it.)
      `today's date` IS A DATE @desc What day are you asking about (normally today)?
      `the company is a limited company having a share capital` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the company a limited company that has a share capital?
      `the notice specifies the shares redenominated` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does the notice specify the shares redenominated?
      `the notice states the date on which the resolution was passed` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does the notice state the date on which the resolution was passed?
      `the notice is accompanied by a statement of capital` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the notice accompanied by a statement of capital?
      `the statement of capital states everything the section requires` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does the statement of capital state everything this section requires: the total number of shares, their aggregate nominal value, the aggregate amount unpaid, and for each class the particulars of the rights, the number of shares and their aggregate nominal value, as at the time the section names?
      `I am an officer of the company who is in default` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are you an officer of the company who is in default, that is, someone who authorised or permitted the default, took part in it, or failed to take all reasonable steps to prevent it (section 1121)?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 625, am I committing an offence as an officer of the company by the way it has dealt with the notice` IS
    `s 625(4)(b) the officer commits an offence` default (JUST `I am an officer of the company who is in default`)
    WHERE
        `the notice date, if there is one` MEANS
            IF `the company has given the notice to the registrar` THEN JUST `the date the notice reached the registrar` ELSE NOTHING
        timely MEANS `s 625(1) the company gave notice to the registrar in time` `the date the company redenominated its share capital` `the notice date, if there is one` `today's date` `the company is a limited company having a share capital`
        `my statement of capital` MEANS `s 619(3) statement of capital` OF `the statement of capital states everything the section requires`, TRUE, TRUE, (LIST (`s 619(3)(c) class entry in a statement of capital` OF TRUE, TRUE, TRUE)), TRUE
        default MEANS `s 625(4) default is made in complying with this section` (LIST timely, (`s 625(1) the notice specifies the shares redenominated` `the notice specifies the shares redenominated`), (`s 625(2)(a) the notice states the date on which the resolution was passed` `the notice states the date on which the resolution was passed`), (`s 625(2)(b) the notice is accompanied by a statement of capital` `the notice is accompanied by a statement of capital`), (`s 625(3) the statement of capital states what the section requires` `my statement of capital`))

@export Under section 625, what is the most that a person guilty of the offence can be fined on summary conviction, not counting the daily default fine for continued contravention, in pounds?
GIVEN `the pounds that level 3 on the standard scale stands for` IS A NUMBER @desc How many pounds is level 3 on the standard scale? (The Act does not say; it is set outside the Act.)
GIVETH A MAYBE NUMBER
DECIDE `Under section 625, what is the most that a person guilty of the offence can be fined on summary conviction, not counting the daily default fine for continued contravention, in pounds` IS
    CONSIDER `s 625(5) the penalty for a person guilty of an offence under this section` TRUE
    WHEN NOTHING THEN NOTHING
    WHEN JUST p THEN
        CONSIDER p's `fine not exceeding`
        WHEN NOTHING THEN NOTHING
        WHEN JUST f THEN `s 619(5) the most a fine can be, in pounds` f `the pounds that level 3 on the standard scale stands for` 0


§§ `Section 626: Reduction of capital in connection with redenomination`

@export Under section 626, is the company's reduction of capital within the section?
GIVEN `the company is a limited company` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the company a limited company?
      `it has passed a resolution redenominating some or all of its shares` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has the company passed a resolution redenominating some or all of its shares?
      `the reduction is for the purpose of adjusting the nominal values` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the reduction for the purpose of adjusting the nominal values of the redenominated shares to values that are, in the company's opinion, more suitable?
      `the resolution is a special resolution` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the resolution for the reduction a special resolution?
      `the day the redenomination resolution was passed` IS A DATE @desc On what day was the resolution effecting the redenomination passed?
      `the day the reduction resolution was passed` IS A DATE @desc On what day was the resolution for the reduction passed?
      `the amount by which the share capital is reduced` IS A NUMBER @desc By how much is the share capital reduced, in pounds?
      `the nominal value of the company's allotted share capital immediately after the reduction` IS A NUMBER @desc What is the nominal value of the company's allotted share capital immediately after the reduction, in pounds?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 626, is the company's reduction of capital within the section` IS
    `s 626 the reduction is within the section`
        (`s 626(1) the company may reduce its share capital under this section` `the company is a limited company` `it has passed a resolution redenominating some or all of its shares` `the reduction is for the purpose of adjusting the nominal values`)
        (`s 626(2) the section bars the reduction for want of a special resolution` (JUST `the resolution is a special resolution`))
        (`s 626(3) the reduction resolution was passed in time` `the day the redenomination resolution was passed` `the day the reduction resolution was passed`)
        (`s 626(4) the amount of the reduction is within the limit` `the amount by which the share capital is reduced` `the nominal value of the company's allotted share capital immediately after the reduction`)

@export Under section 626, does a reduction of capital under this section extinguish or reduce any liability in respect of share capital not paid up?
GIVEN `the reduction is a reduction of capital under this section` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the reduction one made under section 626 in connection with a redenomination?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 626, does a reduction of capital under this section extinguish or reduce any liability in respect of share capital not paid up` IS
    `s 626(5) the reduction extinguishes or reduces liability in respect of share capital not paid up` `the reduction is a reduction of capital under this section`

§§ `Section 627: Notice to registrar of reduction of capital in connection with redenomination`
@export Under section 627, by what day must the company give notice of the reduction to the registrar?
GIVEN `the date the company passed a resolution under section 626` IS A DATE @desc On what day did the company pass the resolution for the reduction of capital in connection with the redenomination?
GIVETH A DATE
DECIDE `Under section 627, by what day must the company give notice of the reduction to the registrar` IS
    `s 627(1) the last day for the notice` `the date the company passed a resolution under section 626`

@export Under section 627, am I committing an offence as an officer of the company by the way it has dealt with the notice?
GIVEN `the date the company passed a resolution under section 626` IS A DATE @desc On what day did the company pass the resolution for the reduction of capital in connection with the redenomination?
      `the company has given the notice to the registrar` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has the company given the notice to the registrar?
      `the date the notice reached the registrar` IS A DATE @desc On what day did the company give the notice to the registrar? (Ignored if it has not given it.)
      `today's date` IS A DATE @desc What day are you asking about (normally today)?
      `the notice states the date of the resolution` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does the notice state the date of the resolution?
      `the notice states the date of the resolution under section 622 in connection with which the reduction resolution was passed` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does the notice state the date of the section 622 resolution in connection with which it was passed?
      `the notice is accompanied by a statement of capital` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the notice accompanied by a statement of capital?
      `the statement of capital states everything the section requires` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does the statement of capital state everything this section requires: the total number of shares, their aggregate nominal value, the aggregate amount unpaid, and for each class the particulars of the rights, the number of shares and their aggregate nominal value, as at the time the section names?
      `I am an officer of the company who is in default` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are you an officer of the company who is in default, that is, someone who authorised or permitted the default, took part in it, or failed to take all reasonable steps to prevent it (section 1121)?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 627, am I committing an offence as an officer of the company by the way it has dealt with the notice` IS
    `s 627(7)(b) the officer commits an offence` default (JUST `I am an officer of the company who is in default`)
    WHERE
        `the notice date, if there is one` MEANS
            IF `the company has given the notice to the registrar` THEN JUST `the date the notice reached the registrar` ELSE NOTHING
        timely MEANS `s 627(1) the company gave notice to the registrar in time` `the date the company passed a resolution under section 626` `the notice date, if there is one` `today's date`
        `my statement of capital` MEANS `s 619(3) statement of capital` OF `the statement of capital states everything the section requires`, TRUE, TRUE, (LIST (`s 619(3)(c) class entry in a statement of capital` OF TRUE, TRUE, TRUE)), TRUE
        default MEANS `s 627(7) default is made in complying with this section` (LIST timely, (`s 627(1)(a) the notice states the date of the resolution` `the notice states the date of the resolution`), (`s 627(1)(b) the notice states the date of the resolution under section 622` `the notice states the date of the resolution under section 622 in connection with which the reduction resolution was passed`), (`s 627(2) the notice is accompanied by a statement of capital` `the notice is accompanied by a statement of capital`), (`s 627(3) the statement of capital states what the section requires` `my statement of capital`))

@export Under section 627, what is the most that a person guilty of the offence can be fined on summary conviction, in pounds?
GIVEN `the pounds that the statutory maximum stands for` IS A NUMBER @desc How many pounds is the statutory maximum? (The Act does not say; it is set outside the Act.)
GIVETH A MAYBE NUMBER
DECIDE `Under section 627, what is the most that a person guilty of the offence can be fined on summary conviction, in pounds` IS
    CONSIDER `s 627(8) the penalty for a person guilty of an offence under this section` TRUE
    WHEN NOTHING THEN NOTHING
    WHEN JUST ps THEN
        CONSIDER (at ps 1)'s `fine not exceeding`
        WHEN NOTHING THEN NOTHING
        WHEN JUST f THEN `s 619(5) the most a fine can be, in pounds` f 0 `the pounds that the statutory maximum stands for`


@export Under section 627, by what day must the company deliver the directors' statement to the registrar?
GIVEN `the date the company passed a resolution under section 626` IS A DATE @desc On what day did the company pass the resolution for the reduction?
GIVETH A DATE
DECIDE `Under section 627, by what day must the company deliver the directors' statement to the registrar` IS
    `s 627(6) the last day for the directors' statement` `the date the company passed a resolution under section 626`

@export Under section 627, does the Act still stop the reduction of capital from being effective?
GIVEN `the notice and the statement have been registered` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has the registrar registered the notice and the statement of capital?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 627, does the Act still stop the reduction of capital from being effective` IS
    `s 627(5) the reduction of capital cannot yet be effective` `the notice and the statement have been registered`

§§ `Section 628: Redenomination reserve`

@export Under section 628, how much must the company transfer to the redenomination reserve?
GIVEN `the reduction is a reduction of capital under section 626` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the reduction one made under section 626 (in connection with a redenomination)?
      `the amount by which the share capital is reduced` IS A NUMBER @desc By how much was the share capital reduced, in pounds?
GIVETH A MAYBE NUMBER
DECIDE `Under section 628, how much must the company transfer to the redenomination reserve` IS
    `s 628(1) the sum that must be transferred to the redenomination reserve` `the reduction is a reduction of capital under section 626` `the amount by which the share capital is reduced`

@export Under section 628, may the company apply the redenomination reserve in paying up shares?
GIVEN `the shares are to be allotted to members as fully paid bonus shares` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are the shares to be allotted to members as fully paid bonus shares?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 628, may the company apply the redenomination reserve in paying up shares` IS
    `s 628(2) the company may apply the redenomination reserve in paying up the shares` `the shares are to be allotted to members as fully paid bonus shares`

@export Under section 628, do the reduction provisions treat the redenomination reserve as if it were paid-up share capital?
GIVEN `the reserve is applied as subsection (2) allows` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the company applying the redenomination reserve in paying up bonus shares for members, as section 628(2) allows?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 628, do the reduction provisions treat the redenomination reserve as if it were paid-up share capital` IS
    `s 628(3) the reduction provisions treat the redenomination reserve as paid-up share capital` `the reserve is applied as subsection (2) allows`

-- =========================================================================================================
-- CHAPTER 9: CLASSES OF SHARE AND CLASS RIGHTS
-- =========================================================================================================

§§ `Section 629: Classes of shares`

@export Under section 629, are these shares of the same class?
GIVEN `the rights attached to the shares are in all respects uniform` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are the rights attached to the shares in all respects uniform?
      `the only reason the rights differ is the dividend difference` IS A BOOLEAN @desc If they are not uniform: is the only difference that they do not carry the same rights to dividends in the twelve months immediately following their allotment?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 629, are these shares of the same class` IS
    `s 629 the shares are of the same class` `the rights attached to the shares are in all respects uniform` `the only reason the rights differ is the dividend difference`

§§ `Section 630: Variation of class rights: companies having a share capital`

@export Under section 630, has the consent required from the holders of the class of shares been given?
GIVEN `the nominal value of the issued shares of the class` IS A NUMBER @desc What is the nominal value of the issued shares of the class, in pounds?
      `the nominal value of those shares held as treasury shares` IS A NUMBER @desc How much of that nominal value is held as treasury shares, in pounds? (0 if none.)
      `the nominal value of the shares whose holders consented in writing` IS A NUMBER @desc What is the nominal value of the shares whose holders have consented in writing, in pounds?
      `the resolution was passed at a separate general meeting of the holders of that class` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Was a resolution passed at a separate general meeting of the holders of that class?
      `the resolution sanctions the variation` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does that resolution sanction the variation?
      `the resolution is a special resolution` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Was that resolution passed as a special resolution?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 630, has the consent required from the holders of the class of shares been given` IS
    `s 630(4) the consent required is given` `the nominal value of the issued shares of the class` `the nominal value of those shares held as treasury shares` `the nominal value of the shares whose holders consented in writing` `the resolution was passed at a separate general meeting of the holders of that class` `the resolution sanctions the variation` (JUST `the resolution is a special resolution`)

@export Under section 630, may the rights attached to the class of shares be varied in this way?
GIVEN `the articles contain provision for the variation of those rights` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Do the company's articles contain a provision for the variation of those rights?
      `the variation is made in accordance with that provision` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the variation made in accordance with that provision?
      `the nominal value of the issued shares of the class` IS A NUMBER @desc What is the nominal value of the issued shares of the class, in pounds?
      `the nominal value of those shares held as treasury shares` IS A NUMBER @desc How much of that nominal value is held as treasury shares, in pounds? (0 if none.)
      `the nominal value of the shares whose holders consented in writing` IS A NUMBER @desc What is the nominal value of the shares whose holders have consented in writing, in pounds?
      `the resolution was passed at a separate general meeting of the holders of that class` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Was a resolution passed at a separate general meeting of the holders of that class?
      `the resolution sanctions the variation` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does that resolution sanction the variation?
      `the resolution is a special resolution` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Was that resolution passed as a special resolution?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 630, may the rights attached to the class of shares be varied in this way` IS
    `s 630(2) the rights attached to the class may be varied in this way` `the articles contain provision for the variation of those rights` `the variation is made in accordance with that provision` consent
    WHERE
        consent MEANS `s 630(4) the consent required is given` `the nominal value of the issued shares of the class` `the nominal value of those shares held as treasury shares` `the nominal value of the shares whose holders consented in writing` `the resolution was passed at a separate general meeting of the holders of that class` `the resolution sanctions the variation` (JUST `the resolution is a special resolution`)

@export Under section 630, is this change to the articles treated as a variation of the rights attached to the class?
GIVEN `the change is an amendment of a provision in the articles for the variation of the rights attached to a class of shares` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the change an amendment of a provision in the articles for the variation of the rights attached to a class of shares?
      `the change is the insertion of such a provision into the articles` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the change the insertion of such a provision into the articles?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 630, is this change to the articles treated as a variation of the rights attached to the class` IS
    `s 630(5) the change is treated as a variation of those rights` `the change is an amendment of a provision in the articles for the variation of the rights attached to a class of shares` `the change is the insertion of such a provision into the articles`

@export Under section 630, does this act count as a variation of the rights attached to the class, abrogation included?
GIVEN `the act is a variation of the rights` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the act a variation of the rights attached to the class?
      `the act is the abrogation of the rights` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the act the abrogation of those rights?
      `the reference is in a provision in the articles for the variation of the rights` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the reference in a provision in the company's articles for the variation of those rights?
      `the context otherwise requires` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does the context require the reference to leave out abrogation?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 630, does this act count as a variation of the rights attached to the class, abrogation included` IS
    `s 630(6) the act counts as a variation of the rights` `the act is a variation of the rights` `the act is the abrogation of the rights` `the reference is in a provision in the articles for the variation of the rights` `the context otherwise requires`

§§ `Section 631: Variation of class rights: companies without a share capital`

@export Under section 631, has the consent required from the members of the class been given?
GIVEN `the number of members of the class` IS A NUMBER @desc How many members are in the class?
      `the number of those members who consented in writing` IS A NUMBER @desc How many of them have consented in writing?
      `the resolution was passed at a separate general meeting of the members of that class` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Was a resolution passed at a separate general meeting of the members of that class?
      `the resolution sanctions the variation` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does that resolution sanction the variation?
      `the resolution is a special resolution` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Was that resolution passed as a special resolution?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 631, has the consent required from the members of the class been given` IS
    `s 631(4) the consent required is given` `the number of members of the class` `the number of those members who consented in writing` `the resolution was passed at a separate general meeting of the members of that class` `the resolution sanctions the variation` (JUST `the resolution is a special resolution`)

@export Under section 631, may the rights of the class of members be varied in this way?
GIVEN `the articles contain provision for the variation of those rights` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Do the company's articles contain a provision for the variation of those rights?
      `the variation is made in accordance with that provision` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the variation made in accordance with that provision?
      `the number of members of the class` IS A NUMBER @desc How many members are in the class?
      `the number of those members who consented in writing` IS A NUMBER @desc How many of them have consented in writing?
      `the resolution was passed at a separate general meeting of the members of that class` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Was a resolution passed at a separate general meeting of the members of that class?
      `the resolution sanctions the variation` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does that resolution sanction the variation?
      `the resolution is a special resolution` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Was that resolution passed as a special resolution?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 631, may the rights of the class of members be varied in this way` IS
    `s 631(2) the rights of the class of members may be varied in this way` `the articles contain provision for the variation of those rights` `the variation is made in accordance with that provision` consent
    WHERE
        consent MEANS `s 631(4) the consent required is given` `the number of members of the class` `the number of those members who consented in writing` `the resolution was passed at a separate general meeting of the members of that class` `the resolution sanctions the variation` (JUST `the resolution is a special resolution`)

@export Under section 631, is this change to the articles treated as a variation of the rights of the class of members?
GIVEN `the change is an amendment of a provision in the articles for the variation of the rights of a class of members` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the change an amendment of a provision in the articles for the variation of the rights of a class of members?
      `the change is the insertion of such a provision into the articles` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the change the insertion of such a provision into the articles?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 631, is this change to the articles treated as a variation of the rights of the class of members` IS
    `s 631(5) the change is treated as a variation of those rights` `the change is an amendment of a provision in the articles for the variation of the rights of a class of members` `the change is the insertion of such a provision into the articles`

§§ `Section 632: Variation of class rights: saving for court's powers under other provisions`

@export Under section 632, do sections 630 and 631 affect the court's power under another provision?
GIVEN `the power of the court` IS A STRING @desc Which power of the court? One of: "section 98", "Part 26", "Part 26A", "Part 30", "some other power".
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 632, do sections 630 and 631 affect the court's power under another provision` IS
    `s 632 section 630 or 631 affects the power of the court` power
    WHERE
        power MEANS
            BRANCH
                IF `the power of the court` EQUALS "section 98" THEN `s 632 the power of the court under section 98`
                IF `the power of the court` EQUALS "Part 26" THEN `s 632 the power of the court under Part 26`
                IF `the power of the court` EQUALS "Part 26A" THEN `s 632 the power of the court under Part 26A`
                IF `the power of the court` EQUALS "Part 30" THEN `s 632 the power of the court under Part 30`
                OTHERWISE `s 632 some other power of the court`

§§ `Section 633: Right to object to variation: companies having a share capital`

@export Under section 633, may I and the other holders of the class apply to the court to have the variation cancelled?
GIVEN `the rights attached to a class of shares in the company were varied under section 630` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Were the rights attached to the class varied under section 630?
      `the number of the issued shares of the class` IS A NUMBER @desc How many shares of the class have been issued?
      `the number of those shares that the company holds as treasury shares` IS A NUMBER @desc How many of them does the company hold as treasury shares? (0 if none.)
      `the number of shares held by the applicants` IS A NUMBER @desc How many shares of the class do you and those applying with you hold?
      `none of the applicants consented to or voted in favour of the resolution for the variation` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it true that none of you consented to the variation or voted in favour of the resolution for it?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 633, may I and the other holders of the class apply to the court to have the variation cancelled` IS
    `s 633(2) the holders may apply to the court to have the variation cancelled` (`s 633(1) section 633 applies` `the rights attached to a class of shares in the company were varied under section 630`) `the number of the issued shares of the class` `the number of those shares that the company holds as treasury shares` `the number of shares held by the applicants` `none of the applicants consented to or voted in favour of the resolution for the variation`

@export Under section 633, by what day must the application to the court be made?
GIVEN `the date the consent was given or the resolution was passed` IS A DATE @desc On what day was the consent given or the resolution passed?
GIVETH A DATE
DECIDE `Under section 633, by what day must the application to the court be made` IS
    `s 633(4)(a) the last day for the application` `the date the consent was given or the resolution was passed`

@export Under section 633, was the application made in time?
GIVEN `the date the consent was given or the resolution was passed` IS A DATE @desc On what day was the consent given or the resolution passed?
      `the date the application was made` IS A DATE @desc On what day was (or will) the application be made?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 633, was the application made in time` IS
    `s 633(4)(a) the application was made in time` `the date the consent was given or the resolution was passed` `the date the application was made`

@export Under section 633, is the variation without effect unless and until the court confirms it?
GIVEN `an application has been made` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has an application been made to the court to have the variation cancelled?
      `the court has confirmed the variation` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has the court confirmed the variation?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 633, is the variation without effect unless and until the court confirms it` IS
    `s 633(3) the variation is without effect unless and until the court confirms it` `an application has been made` `the court has confirmed the variation`

§§ `Section 634: Right to object to variation: companies without a share capital`

@export Under section 634, may I and the other members of the class apply to the court to have the variation cancelled?
GIVEN `the rights of a class of members of the company were varied under section 631` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Were the rights of the class of members varied under section 631?
      `the number of members of the class in question` IS A NUMBER @desc How many members are in the class?
      `the number of members applying` IS A NUMBER @desc How many members of the class are applying (you and those applying with you)?
      `none of the applicants consented to or voted in favour of the resolution for the variation` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it true that none of you consented to the variation or voted in favour of the resolution for it?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 634, may I and the other members of the class apply to the court to have the variation cancelled` IS
    `s 634(2) the members may apply to the court to have the variation cancelled` (`s 634(1) section 634 applies` `the rights of a class of members of the company were varied under section 631`) `the number of members of the class in question` `the number of members applying` `none of the applicants consented to or voted in favour of the resolution for the variation`

@export Under section 634, by what day must the application to the court be made?
GIVEN `the date the consent was given or the resolution was passed` IS A DATE @desc On what day was the consent given or the resolution passed?
GIVETH A DATE
DECIDE `Under section 634, by what day must the application to the court be made` IS
    `s 634(4) the last day for the application` `the date the consent was given or the resolution was passed`

@export Under section 634, is the variation without effect unless and until the court confirms it?
GIVEN `an application has been made` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has an application been made to the court to have the variation cancelled?
      `the court has confirmed the variation` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has the court confirmed the variation?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 634, is the variation without effect unless and until the court confirms it` IS
    `s 634(3) the variation is without effect unless and until the court confirms it` `an application has been made` `the court has confirmed the variation`

§§ `Section 635: Copy of court order to be forwarded to the registrar`
@export Under section 635, by what day must the company forward a copy of the court's order to the registrar?
GIVEN `the date the court made an order on an application under section 633 or 634` IS A DATE @desc On what day did the court make the order on the application to cancel the variation of class rights?
GIVETH A DATE
DECIDE `Under section 635, by what day must the company forward a copy of the court's order to the registrar` IS
    `s 635(1) the last day for the copy of the order` `the date the court made an order on an application under section 633 or 634`

@export Under section 635, am I committing an offence as an officer of the company by the way it has dealt with the copy of the order?
GIVEN `the date the court made an order on an application under section 633 or 634` IS A DATE @desc On what day did the court make the order on the application to cancel the variation of class rights?
      `the company has given the copy of the order to the registrar` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has the company given the copy of the order to the registrar?
      `the date the copy of the order reached the registrar` IS A DATE @desc On what day did the company give the copy of the order to the registrar? (Ignored if it has not given it.)
      `today's date` IS A DATE @desc What day are you asking about (normally today)?
      `I am an officer of the company who is in default` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are you an officer of the company who is in default, that is, someone who authorised or permitted the default, took part in it, or failed to take all reasonable steps to prevent it (section 1121)?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 635, am I committing an offence as an officer of the company by the way it has dealt with the copy of the order` IS
    `s 635(2)(b) the officer commits an offence` default (JUST `I am an officer of the company who is in default`)
    WHERE
        `the copy of the order date, if there is one` MEANS
            IF `the company has given the copy of the order to the registrar` THEN JUST `the date the copy of the order reached the registrar` ELSE NOTHING
        timely MEANS `s 635(1) the company forwarded a copy of the order to the registrar in time` `the date the court made an order on an application under section 633 or 634` `the copy of the order date, if there is one` `today's date`
        default MEANS `s 635(2) default is made in complying with this section` (LIST timely)

@export Under section 635, what is the most that a person guilty of the offence can be fined on summary conviction, not counting the daily default fine for continued contravention, in pounds?
GIVEN `the pounds that level 3 on the standard scale stands for` IS A NUMBER @desc How many pounds is level 3 on the standard scale? (The Act does not say; it is set outside the Act.)
GIVETH A MAYBE NUMBER
DECIDE `Under section 635, what is the most that a person guilty of the offence can be fined on summary conviction, not counting the daily default fine for continued contravention, in pounds` IS
    CONSIDER `s 635(3) the penalty for a person guilty of an offence under this section` TRUE
    WHEN NOTHING THEN NOTHING
    WHEN JUST p THEN
        CONSIDER p's `fine not exceeding`
        WHEN NOTHING THEN NOTHING
        WHEN JUST f THEN `s 619(5) the most a fine can be, in pounds` f `the pounds that level 3 on the standard scale stands for` 0


§§ `Section 636: Notice of name or other designation of class of shares`
@export Under section 636, by what day must the company deliver a notice of the name or designation of a class of shares to the registrar?
GIVEN `the date the company assigned a name or other designation to a class or description of its shares` IS A DATE @desc On what day did the company assign the name or designation to the class of shares?
GIVETH A DATE
DECIDE `Under section 636, by what day must the company deliver a notice of the name or designation of a class of shares to the registrar` IS
    `s 636(1) the last day for the notice` `the date the company assigned a name or other designation to a class or description of its shares`

@export Under section 636, am I committing an offence as an officer of the company by the way it has dealt with the notice?
GIVEN `the date the company assigned a name or other designation to a class or description of its shares` IS A DATE @desc On what day did the company assign the name or designation to the class of shares?
      `the company has given the notice to the registrar` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has the company given the notice to the registrar?
      `the date the notice reached the registrar` IS A DATE @desc On what day did the company give the notice to the registrar? (Ignored if it has not given it.)
      `today's date` IS A DATE @desc What day are you asking about (normally today)?
      `the notice gives particulars of the name or designation so assigned` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does the notice give particulars of the name or designation assigned?
      `I am an officer of the company who is in default` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are you an officer of the company who is in default, that is, someone who authorised or permitted the default, took part in it, or failed to take all reasonable steps to prevent it (section 1121)?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 636, am I committing an offence as an officer of the company by the way it has dealt with the notice` IS
    `s 636(2)(b) the officer commits an offence` default (JUST `I am an officer of the company who is in default`)
    WHERE
        `the notice date, if there is one` MEANS
            IF `the company has given the notice to the registrar` THEN JUST `the date the notice reached the registrar` ELSE NOTHING
        timely MEANS `s 636(1) the company delivered the notice to the registrar in time` `the date the company assigned a name or other designation to a class or description of its shares` `the notice date, if there is one` `today's date`
        default MEANS `s 636(2) default is made in complying with this section` (LIST timely, (`s 636(1) the notice gives particulars of the name or designation` `the notice gives particulars of the name or designation so assigned`))

@export Under section 636, what is the most that a person guilty of the offence can be fined on summary conviction, not counting the daily default fine for continued contravention, in pounds?
GIVEN `the pounds that level 3 on the standard scale stands for` IS A NUMBER @desc How many pounds is level 3 on the standard scale? (The Act does not say; it is set outside the Act.)
GIVETH A MAYBE NUMBER
DECIDE `Under section 636, what is the most that a person guilty of the offence can be fined on summary conviction, not counting the daily default fine for continued contravention, in pounds` IS
    CONSIDER `s 636(3) the penalty for a person guilty of an offence under this section` TRUE
    WHEN NOTHING THEN NOTHING
    WHEN JUST p THEN
        CONSIDER p's `fine not exceeding`
        WHEN NOTHING THEN NOTHING
        WHEN JUST f THEN `s 619(5) the most a fine can be, in pounds` f `the pounds that level 3 on the standard scale stands for` 0


