-- =========================================================================================================
-- CHAPTER 10: REDUCTION OF SHARE CAPITAL
-- =========================================================================================================

§§ `Section 641: Circumstances in which a company may reduce its share capital`

@export Under section 641, is the company's reduction of its share capital by this route within the section?
GIVEN `the company is a limited company having a share capital` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the company a limited company that has a share capital?
      `the route is a special resolution supported by a solvency statement` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the route a special resolution supported by a solvency statement? (Answer no if it is a special resolution confirmed by the court.)
      `the company is a private company` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the company a private company (section 4(1))?
      `the company is limited by shares` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the company limited by shares (section 3(2))?
      `the resolution is a special resolution` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the resolution for the reduction a special resolution?
      `the resolution is supported by a solvency statement` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the resolution supported by a solvency statement (your answer to the section 642 question)?
      `the resolution is confirmed by the court` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has the court confirmed the resolution?
      `after the reduction no member would hold shares other than redeemable shares` IS A BOOLEAN @desc As a result of the reduction, would there no longer be any member holding shares other than redeemable shares?
      `the reduction is part of a scheme` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the reduction part of a compromise or arrangement sanctioned by the court under Part 26 or 26A?
      `a person is to acquire all the shares in the company` IS A BOOLEAN @desc By virtue of that scheme, is a person (or a person together with its associates) to acquire all the shares in the company, other than shares it or its associates already hold?
      `the company has more than one class of shares` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does the company have more than one class of shares?
      `a person is to acquire all the shares of one or more classes` IS A BOOLEAN @desc By virtue of that scheme, is a person (or a person together with its associates) to acquire all the shares of one or more classes, other than shares it or its associates already hold?
      `the company is to have a new parent undertaking` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Under the scheme, is the company to have a new parent undertaking?
      `all or substantially all of the members become members of the parent undertaking` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Under the scheme, do all or substantially all of the company's members become members of the parent undertaking?
      `the members hold the same or substantially the same proportions` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Under the scheme, will the members hold the same or substantially the same proportions of the equity share capital of the parent undertaking as they hold of the company?
      `the articles contain a provision restricting or prohibiting the reduction of the company's share capital` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Do the company's articles contain a provision restricting or prohibiting the reduction?
      `the reduction is one that provision restricts or prohibits` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is this reduction one that provision restricts or prohibits?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 641, is the company's reduction of its share capital by this route within the section` IS
    `s 641 the reduction of share capital is within the section`
        (`s 641(1) the company may reduce its share capital by this route` `the company is a limited company having a share capital` route `the company is a private company` `the company is limited by shares` (JUST `the resolution is a special resolution`) (JUST `the resolution is supported by a solvency statement`) `the resolution is confirmed by the court`)
        (`s 641(3) the company may reduce its share capital in the way proposed` route
            (`s 641(2) the section bars the reduction under subsection (1)(a)` route `after the reduction no member would hold shares other than redeemable shares`)
            (`s 641(2A) the section bars the reduction as part of the scheme` (JUST `the reduction is part of a scheme`) `a person is to acquire all the shares in the company` `the company has more than one class of shares` `a person is to acquire all the shares of one or more classes` (`s 641(2B) subsection (2A) does not apply to the scheme` `the company is to have a new parent undertaking` `all or substantially all of the members become members of the parent undertaking` `the members hold the same or substantially the same proportions`)))
        (`s 641(6) the company's articles bar the reduction` `the articles contain a provision restricting or prohibiting the reduction of the company's share capital` `the reduction is one that provision restricts or prohibits`)
    WHERE
        route MEANS
            IF `the route is a special resolution supported by a solvency statement`
            THEN `s 641(1)(a) special resolution supported by a solvency statement`
            ELSE `s 641(1)(b) special resolution confirmed by the court`

@export Under section 641, does the Act bar the company from reducing its share capital as part of a takeover scheme?
GIVEN `the reduction is part of a scheme` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the reduction part of a compromise or arrangement sanctioned by the court under Part 26 or 26A?
      `a person is to acquire all the shares in the company` IS A BOOLEAN @desc By virtue of that scheme, is a person (or a person together with its associates) to acquire all the shares in the company, other than shares it or its associates already hold?
      `the company has more than one class of shares` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does the company have more than one class of shares?
      `a person is to acquire all the shares of one or more classes` IS A BOOLEAN @desc By virtue of that scheme, is a person (or a person together with its associates) to acquire all the shares of one or more classes, other than shares it or its associates already hold?
      `the company is to have a new parent undertaking` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Under the scheme, is the company to have a new parent undertaking?
      `all or substantially all of the members become members of the parent undertaking` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Under the scheme, do all or substantially all of the company's members become members of the parent undertaking?
      `the members hold the same or substantially the same proportions` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Under the scheme, will the members hold the same or substantially the same proportions of the equity share capital of the parent undertaking as they hold of the company?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 641, does the Act bar the company from reducing its share capital as part of a takeover scheme` IS
    `s 641(2A) the section bars the reduction as part of the scheme` (JUST `the reduction is part of a scheme`) `a person is to acquire all the shares in the company` `the company has more than one class of shares` `a person is to acquire all the shares of one or more classes` (`s 641(2B) subsection (2A) does not apply to the scheme` `the company is to have a new parent undertaking` `all or substantially all of the members become members of the parent undertaking` `the members hold the same or substantially the same proportions`)

@export Under section 641, may the company make a reduction of this kind?
GIVEN `the kind of reduction` IS A STRING @desc What kind of reduction is it? One of: "extinguishing or reducing the liability on shares in respect of share capital not paid up", "cancelling paid-up share capital that is lost or unrepresented by available assets", "repaying paid-up share capital in excess of the company's wants", "some other kind of reduction".
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 641, may the company make a reduction of this kind` IS
    `s 641(4) the reduction is of a kind the section names` kind
    WHERE
        kind MEANS
            BRANCH
                IF `the kind of reduction` EQUALS "extinguishing or reducing the liability on shares in respect of share capital not paid up" THEN `s 641(4)(a) extinguishing or reducing the liability on shares in respect of share capital not paid up`
                IF `the kind of reduction` EQUALS "cancelling paid-up share capital that is lost or unrepresented by available assets" THEN `s 641(4)(b)(i) cancelling paid-up share capital that is lost or unrepresented by available assets`
                IF `the kind of reduction` EQUALS "repaying paid-up share capital in excess of the company's wants" THEN `s 641(4)(b)(ii) repaying paid-up share capital in excess of the company's wants`
                OTHERWISE `s 641(4) some other kind of reduction`

@export Under section 641, does the Act bar the special resolution from providing for the reduction to take effect on this date?
GIVEN `the date the resolution provides for the reduction to take effect` IS A DATE @desc On what date does the special resolution provide for the reduction to take effect?
      `the date the resolution has effect in accordance with this Chapter` IS A DATE @desc On what date does the resolution have effect in accordance with Chapter 10 (for the solvency statement route, section 644(4); for the court route, section 649(3))?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 641, does the Act bar the special resolution from providing for the reduction to take effect on this date` IS
    `s 641(5) the resolution is barred from providing for that date` `the date the resolution provides for the reduction to take effect` `the date the resolution has effect in accordance with this Chapter`

§§ `Section 642: Reduction of capital supported by solvency statement`

@export Under section 642, is the resolution supported by a solvency statement?
GIVEN `the company is a private company limited by shares` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the company a private company limited by shares?
      `the date the directors made the statement` IS A DATE @desc On what day did the directors make the solvency statement?
      `the date the resolution is passed` IS A DATE @desc On what day is (or was) the resolution passed?
      `the statement is made in accordance with section 643` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the statement made in accordance with section 643 (your answer to the section 643 question)?
      `the resolution and the solvency statement are registered in accordance with section 644` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Have the resolution and the solvency statement been registered in accordance with section 644?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 642, is the resolution supported by a solvency statement` IS
    `s 642(1) the resolution is supported by a solvency statement` `the company is a private company limited by shares` `the date the directors made the statement` `the date the resolution is passed` (JUST `the statement is made in accordance with section 643`) `the resolution and the solvency statement are registered in accordance with section 644`

@export Under section 642, was I, as an eligible member, sent or shown a copy of the solvency statement as the section requires?
GIVEN `the resolution is proposed as a written resolution` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the resolution proposed as a written resolution?
      `a copy was sent or submitted to me at or before the time the proposed resolution was` IS A BOOLEAN @desc If so: was a copy of the solvency statement sent or submitted to you at or before the time the proposed resolution was sent or submitted to you?
      `the resolution is proposed at a general meeting` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the resolution proposed at a general meeting?
      `a copy was available for inspection throughout the meeting` IS A BOOLEAN @desc If so: was a copy of the solvency statement made available for inspection by members throughout the meeting?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 642, was I, as an eligible member, sent or shown a copy of the solvency statement as the section requires` IS
    BRANCH
        IF `the resolution is proposed as a written resolution`
        THEN `s 642(2) the copy of the solvency statement was sent or submitted to the eligible member in time` `the resolution is proposed as a written resolution` `a copy was sent or submitted to me at or before the time the proposed resolution was`
        IF `the resolution is proposed at a general meeting`
        THEN `s 642(3) the copy of the solvency statement was made available for inspection throughout the meeting` `the resolution is proposed at a general meeting` `a copy was available for inspection throughout the meeting`
        OTHERWISE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (silent): neither a written resolution nor a general meeting is proposed, and subsections (2) and (3) speak of those two

@export Under section 642, does a failure to give members the solvency statement affect the validity of the resolution?
GIVEN `there was a failure to comply with subsection (2) or (3)` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Was there a failure to send or submit the copy (written resolution) or to make it available (meeting)?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 642, does a failure to give members the solvency statement affect the validity of the resolution` IS
    `s 642(4) the failure affects the validity of the resolution` `there was a failure to comply with subsection (2) or (3)`

§§ `Section 643: Solvency statement`

@export Under section 643, is the statement made in accordance with section 643?
GIVEN `it is intended to commence the winding up of the company within twelve months of the date of the statement` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it intended to commence the winding up of the company within twelve months of the date of the statement?
      `each director has formed the opinion in paragraph (a)` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has each director formed the opinion that there is no ground on which the company could then be found to be unable to pay (or otherwise discharge) its debts?
      `each director has formed the opinion in paragraph (b) that applies` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has each director formed the other opinion that applies: if a winding up is intended within twelve months, that the company will pay its debts in full within twelve months of its commencement; otherwise, that it will pay its debts as they fall due during the year after the date?
      `the directors took into account all of the company's liabilities` IS A BOOLEAN @desc In forming those opinions, did the directors take into account all of the company's liabilities?
      `they included any contingent or prospective liabilities` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did that include any contingent or prospective liabilities?
      `the statement is in the prescribed form` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the statement in the prescribed form?
      `the statement states the date on which it is made` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does the statement state the date on which it is made?
      `the statement states the name of each director of the company` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does the statement state the name of each director of the company?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 643, is the statement made in accordance with section 643` IS
    `s 643 the statement is made in accordance with section 643`
        (`s 643(1) the statement is a solvency statement` `it is intended to commence the winding up of the company within twelve months of the date of the statement` (LIST opinions))
        (`s 643(2) the directors took into account what the section requires` `the directors took into account all of the company's liabilities` `they included any contingent or prospective liabilities`)
        (`s 643(3) the solvency statement is in the form and states what the section requires` `the statement is in the prescribed form` `the statement states the date on which it is made` `the statement states the name of each director of the company`)
    WHERE
        -- the answers are for "each of the directors": one record stands for them all; the (b) answer is entered for both (b)(i) and (b)(ii), the one that applies being the one the section reads
        opinions MEANS `s 643(1) director's opinions` OF `each director has formed the opinion in paragraph (a)`, `each director has formed the opinion in paragraph (b) that applies`, `each director has formed the opinion in paragraph (b) that applies`

@export Under section 643, am I, as a director, committing an offence by making the solvency statement?
GIVEN `the directors made the solvency statement without having reasonable grounds for the opinions expressed in it` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did the directors make the solvency statement without having reasonable grounds for the opinions expressed in it?
      `the statement is delivered to the registrar` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has the statement been delivered to the registrar?
      `I am a director who is in default` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are you a director who is in default, that is, someone who authorised or permitted the default, took part in it, or failed to take all reasonable steps to prevent it (section 1121)?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 643, am I, as a director, committing an offence by making the solvency statement` IS
    `s 643(4) the director commits an offence` `the directors made the solvency statement without having reasonable grounds for the opinions expressed in it` `the statement is delivered to the registrar` (JUST `I am a director who is in default`)

@export Under section 643, what penalties does the Act give a person guilty of the offence under subsection (4)?
GIVEN `I am guilty of an offence under subsection (4)` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the person guilty of the offence under section 643(4) (a solvency statement made without reasonable grounds and delivered to the registrar, by a director in default)?
GIVETH A MAYBE (LIST OF Penalty)
DECIDE `Under section 643, what penalties does the Act give a person guilty of the offence under subsection (4)` IS
    `s 643(5) the penalty for a person guilty of an offence under subsection (4)` `I am guilty of an offence under subsection (4)`

§§ `Section 644: Registration of resolution and supporting documents`
@export Under section 644, by what day must the company deliver the solvency statement and a statement of capital to the registrar?
GIVEN `the date the resolution for reducing share capital was passed` IS A DATE @desc On what day was the resolution for reducing share capital passed?
GIVETH A DATE
DECIDE `Under section 644, by what day must the company deliver the solvency statement and a statement of capital to the registrar` IS
    `s 644(1) the last day for the documents` `the date the resolution for reducing share capital was passed`

@export Under section 644, am I committing an offence as an officer of the company by the way it has dealt with the documents?
GIVEN `the date the resolution for reducing share capital was passed` IS A DATE @desc On what day was the resolution for reducing share capital passed?
      `the company has given the documents to the registrar` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has the company given the documents to the registrar?
      `the date the documents reached the registrar` IS A DATE @desc On what day did the company give the documents to the registrar? (Ignored if it has not given it.)
      `today's date` IS A DATE @desc What day are you asking about (normally today)?
      `a copy of the solvency statement was delivered` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has a copy of the solvency statement been delivered?
      `a statement of capital was delivered` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has a statement of capital been delivered?
      `the statement of capital states everything the section requires` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does the statement of capital state everything this section requires: the total number of shares, their aggregate nominal value, the aggregate amount unpaid, and for each class the particulars of the rights, the number of shares and their aggregate nominal value, as at the time the section names?
      `I am an officer of the company who is in default` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are you an officer of the company who is in default, that is, someone who authorised or permitted the default, took part in it, or failed to take all reasonable steps to prevent it (section 1121)?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 644, am I committing an offence as an officer of the company by the way it has dealt with the documents` IS
    `s 644(8)(b) the officer commits an offence` default (JUST `I am an officer of the company who is in default`)
    WHERE
        `the documents date, if there is one` MEANS
            IF `the company has given the documents to the registrar` THEN JUST `the date the documents reached the registrar` ELSE NOTHING
        timely MEANS `s 644(1) the company delivered the documents to the registrar in time` `the date the resolution for reducing share capital was passed` `the documents date, if there is one` `today's date`
        `my statement of capital` MEANS `s 619(3) statement of capital` OF `the statement of capital states everything the section requires`, TRUE, TRUE, (LIST (`s 619(3)(c) class entry in a statement of capital` OF TRUE, TRUE, TRUE)), TRUE
        default MEANS `s 644(8) default is made in complying with this section` (LIST timely, (`s 644(1)(a) a copy of the solvency statement was delivered` `a copy of the solvency statement was delivered`), (`s 644(1)(b) a statement of capital was delivered` `a statement of capital was delivered`), (`s 644(2) the statement of capital states what the section requires` `my statement of capital`))

@export Under section 644, what is the most that a person guilty of the offence can be fined on summary conviction, in pounds?
GIVEN `the pounds that the statutory maximum stands for` IS A NUMBER @desc How many pounds is the statutory maximum? (The Act does not say; it is set outside the Act.)
GIVETH A MAYBE NUMBER
DECIDE `Under section 644, what is the most that a person guilty of the offence can be fined on summary conviction, in pounds` IS
    CONSIDER `s 644(9) the penalty for a person guilty of an offence under subsection (7) or (8)` TRUE
    WHEN NOTHING THEN NOTHING
    WHEN JUST ps THEN
        CONSIDER (at ps 1)'s `fine not exceeding`
        WHEN NOTHING THEN NOTHING
        WHEN JUST f THEN `s 619(5) the most a fine can be, in pounds` f 0 `the pounds that the statutory maximum stands for`


@export Under section 644, by what day must the company deliver the directors' statement to the registrar?
GIVEN `the date the resolution for reducing share capital was passed` IS A DATE @desc On what day was the resolution for reducing share capital passed?
GIVETH A DATE
DECIDE `Under section 644, by what day must the company deliver the directors' statement to the registrar` IS
    `s 644(5) the last day for the directors' statement` `the date the resolution for reducing share capital was passed`

@export Under section 644, does the Act still stop the resolution from taking effect?
GIVEN `those documents have been registered` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Have the documents delivered to the registrar been registered?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 644, does the Act still stop the resolution from taking effect` IS
    `s 644(4) the resolution cannot yet take effect` `those documents have been registered`

@export Under section 644, am I committing an offence as an officer of the company in connection with a solvency statement that was not provided to members?
GIVEN `the company delivers to the registrar a solvency statement that was not provided to members in accordance with section 642(2) or (3)` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has the company delivered to the registrar a solvency statement that was not provided to members as section 642(2) or (3) requires?
      `I am an officer of the company who is in default` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are you an officer of the company who is in default (section 1121)?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 644, am I committing an offence as an officer of the company in connection with a solvency statement that was not provided to members` IS
    `s 644(7) the officer commits an offence` `the company delivers to the registrar a solvency statement that was not provided to members in accordance with section 642(2) or (3)` (JUST `I am an officer of the company who is in default`)

@export Under section 644, does a failure to deliver the documents in time, or to deliver the directors' statement, affect the validity of the resolution?
GIVEN `there was a failure to deliver the documents required by subsection (1) within the time specified` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Was there a failure to deliver the solvency statement and the statement of capital within 15 days after the resolution was passed?
      `there was a failure to comply with subsection (5)` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Was there a failure to deliver the directors' statement required by section 644(5)?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 644, does a failure to deliver the documents in time, or to deliver the directors' statement, affect the validity of the resolution` IS
    `s 644(6) the failure affects the validity of the resolution` `there was a failure to deliver the documents required by subsection (1) within the time specified` `there was a failure to comply with subsection (5)`

§§ `Section 645: Application to court for order of confirmation`

@export Under section 645, may the company apply to the court for an order confirming the reduction?
GIVEN `the company has passed a resolution for reducing share capital` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has the company passed a resolution for reducing share capital?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 645, may the company apply to the court for an order confirming the reduction` IS
    `s 645(1) the company may apply to the court for an order confirming the reduction` `the company has passed a resolution for reducing share capital`

@export Under section 645, does section 646 (creditors' right to object) apply to the reduction? (Answer NOTHING means not covered: the reduction involves neither relief from unpaid share capital nor a payment of paid-up capital to a shareholder, and the court has given no direction under section 645(4), so the Act does not say either way; it is not a no.)
GIVEN `the proposed reduction involves diminution of liability in respect of unpaid share capital` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does the proposed reduction involve diminution of liability in respect of unpaid share capital?
      `the proposed reduction involves the payment to a shareholder of any paid-up share capital` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does it involve the payment to a shareholder of any paid-up share capital?
      `the court directs otherwise` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has the court directed that section 646 is not to apply (as regards a class of creditors, or at all)?
      `the court has directed under subsection (4) that section 646 is to apply` IS A BOOLEAN @desc In any other case, one that involves neither of the two things above: has the court directed under section 645(4) that section 646 is to apply? (If it has not, the Act does not say whether section 646 applies.)
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 645, does section 646 (creditors' right to object) apply to the reduction` IS
    `s 645 section 646 applies to the reduction` (`s 645(2) section 646 applies to the reduction, unless the court directs otherwise` `the proposed reduction involves diminution of liability in respect of unpaid share capital` `the proposed reduction involves the payment to a shareholder of any paid-up share capital` `the court directs otherwise`) `the court has directed under subsection (4) that section 646 is to apply`

§§ `Section 646: Creditors entitled to object to reduction`

@export Under section 646, am I, as a creditor, entitled to object to the reduction of capital?
GIVEN `section 646 applies to the reduction` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does section 646 apply to this reduction (your answer to the section 645 question)? (If that question was not covered, the Act does not say whether section 646 applies; do not use this question.)
      `at the date fixed by the court I am entitled to a debt or claim that would be admissible in proof` IS A BOOLEAN @desc At the date fixed by the court, are you entitled to a debt or claim that would be admissible in proof against the company if that date were the commencement of its winding up?
      `I can show a real likelihood that the reduction would result in the company being unable to discharge my debt or claim` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Can you show a real likelihood that the reduction would result in the company being unable to discharge your debt or claim when it fell due?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 646, am I, as a creditor, entitled to object to the reduction of capital` IS
    `s 646(1) the creditor is entitled to object to the reduction of capital` (JUST `section 646 applies to the reduction`) `at the date fixed by the court I am entitled to a debt or claim that would be admissible in proof` `I can show a real likelihood that the reduction would result in the company being unable to discharge my debt or claim`

@export Under section 646, may the court dispense with a creditor's consent to the reduction?
GIVEN `the creditor is entered on the list of creditors` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the creditor entered on the court's list of creditors entitled to object?
      `the creditor's debt or claim is not discharged or has not determined` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the creditor's debt or claim neither discharged nor determined?
      `the creditor does not consent to the reduction` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does the creditor decline to consent to the reduction?
      `the company secures payment of the creditor's debt or claim` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does the company secure payment of the creditor's debt or claim?
      `the court thinks fit` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does the court think it fit to dispense with the creditor's consent?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 646, may the court dispense with a creditor's consent to the reduction` IS
    `s 646(4) the court may dispense with the creditor's consent` `the creditor is entered on the list of creditors` `the creditor's debt or claim is not discharged or has not determined` `the creditor does not consent to the reduction` `the company secures payment of the creditor's debt or claim` `the court thinks fit`

@export Under section 646, how much must be appropriated to secure my debt or claim?
GIVEN `the company admits the full amount of the debt or claim or is willing to provide for it` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does the company admit the full amount of your debt or claim or, though not admitting it, is it willing to provide for it?
      `the amount is contingent or not ascertained` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the amount of your debt or claim contingent or not ascertained?
      `the full amount of the debt or claim` IS A NUMBER @desc What is the full amount of your debt or claim, in pounds?
      `the court has fixed an amount` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has the court fixed an amount after the like enquiry and adjudication as if the company were being wound up by the court?
      `the amount fixed by the court` IS A NUMBER @desc What amount did the court fix, in pounds? (Ignored if it has not.)
GIVETH A MAYBE NUMBER
DECIDE `Under section 646, how much must be appropriated to secure my debt or claim` IS
    `s 646(5) the amount the debt or claim must be secured by appropriating` `the company admits the full amount of the debt or claim or is willing to provide for it` `the amount is contingent or not ascertained` `the full amount of the debt or claim` fixed
    WHERE
        fixed MEANS IF `the court has fixed an amount` THEN JUST `the amount fixed by the court` ELSE NOTHING

§§ `Section 647: Offences in connection with list of creditors`

@export Under section 647, am I committing an offence as an officer of the company in connection with the list of creditors?
GIVEN `I am an officer of the company` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are you an officer of the company (a director, manager or secretary, or another officer: section 1173(1))?
      `I intentionally or recklessly conceal the name of a creditor entitled to object` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Do you intentionally or recklessly conceal the name of a creditor entitled to object to the reduction of capital?
      `I intentionally or recklessly misrepresent the nature or amount of a creditor's debt or claim` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Do you intentionally or recklessly misrepresent the nature or amount of the debt or claim of a creditor?
      `I am knowingly concerned in such a concealment or misrepresentation` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are you knowingly concerned in any such concealment or misrepresentation?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 647, am I committing an offence as an officer of the company in connection with the list of creditors` IS
    `s 647(1) the officer commits an offence` (JUST `I am an officer of the company`) `I intentionally or recklessly conceal the name of a creditor entitled to object` `I intentionally or recklessly misrepresent the nature or amount of a creditor's debt or claim` `I am knowingly concerned in such a concealment or misrepresentation`

@export Under section 647, what is the most that a person guilty of the offence can be fined on summary conviction, in pounds?
GIVEN `the pounds that the statutory maximum stands for` IS A NUMBER @desc How many pounds is the statutory maximum? (The Act does not say; it is set outside the Act.)
GIVETH A MAYBE NUMBER
DECIDE `Under section 647, what is the most that a person guilty of the offence can be fined on summary conviction, in pounds` IS
    CONSIDER `s 647(2) the penalty for a person guilty of an offence under this section` TRUE
    WHEN NOTHING THEN NOTHING
    WHEN JUST ps THEN
        CONSIDER (at ps 1)'s `fine not exceeding`
        WHEN NOTHING THEN NOTHING
        WHEN JUST f THEN `s 619(5) the most a fine can be, in pounds` f 0 `the pounds that the statutory maximum stands for`


§§ `Section 648: Court order confirming reduction`

@export Under section 648, does the Act bar the court from confirming the reduction?
GIVEN `a creditor entitled to object has neither consented nor had the debt or claim discharged, determined or secured` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is there a creditor entitled to object to the reduction whose consent has not been obtained and whose debt or claim has not been discharged, has not determined and has not been secured?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 648, does the Act bar the court from confirming the reduction` IS
    `s 648(2) the section bars the court from confirming the reduction` creditors
    WHERE
        creditors MEANS
            IF `a creditor entitled to object has neither consented nor had the debt or claim discharged, determined or secured`
            THEN LIST (`s 648(2) creditor entitled to object` OF FALSE, FALSE, FALSE, FALSE)
            ELSE LIST (`s 648(2) creditor entitled to object` OF TRUE, FALSE, FALSE, FALSE) -- every creditor entitled to object has consented (or been paid or secured): one stands for them all

@export Under section 648, are the words "and reduced" part of the company's name on this day?
GIVEN `the court has made an order that the company add "and reduced" to its name` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has the court made an order that the company add the words "and reduced" to its name?
      `the date being asked about` IS A DATE @desc What day are you asking about (normally today)?
      `the last day of the period specified in the order` IS A DATE @desc What is the last day of the period the order specifies?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 648, are the words "and reduced" part of the company's name on this day` IS
    `s 648(4) the words "and reduced" are deemed to be part of the company's name` `the court has made an order that the company add "and reduced" to its name` `the date being asked about` `the last day of the period specified in the order`

§§ `Section 649: Registration of order and statement of capital`

@export Under section 649, on what day does the resolution for reducing share capital take effect?
GIVEN `the kind of reduction` IS A STRING @desc What kind of reduction is it? One of: "part of a compromise or arrangement sanctioned under Part 26", "part of a compromise or arrangement sanctioned under Part 26A, a company other than an overseas company not required to register particulars under section 1046", "part of a compromise or arrangement sanctioned under Part 26A, an overseas company not required to register particulars under section 1046", "any other case".
      `the court so orders that it takes effect on registration` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has the court ordered that it takes effect on the registration of the order and statement of capital?
      `they have been delivered to the registrar` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Have the order and statement of capital been delivered to the registrar?
      `the day they were delivered` IS A DATE @desc If so, on what day? (Ignored if not.)
      `they have been registered` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Have the order and statement of capital been registered?
      `the day they were registered` IS A DATE @desc If so, on what day? (Ignored if not.)
      `they have been published in the Gazette` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Have the order and statement of capital been published in the Gazette?
      `the day they were published in the Gazette` IS A DATE @desc If so, on what day? (Ignored if not.)
GIVETH A MAYBE DATE
DECIDE `Under section 649, on what day does the resolution for reducing share capital take effect` IS
    `s 649(3) the day the resolution takes effect` kind `the court so orders that it takes effect on registration` (maybe `they have been delivered to the registrar` `the day they were delivered`) (maybe `they have been registered` `the day they were registered`) (maybe `they have been published in the Gazette` `the day they were published in the Gazette`)
    WHERE
        maybe flag day MEANS IF flag THEN JUST day ELSE NOTHING
        kind MEANS
            BRANCH
                IF `the kind of reduction` EQUALS "part of a compromise or arrangement sanctioned under Part 26" THEN `s 649(3)(a) part of a compromise or arrangement sanctioned under Part 26`
                IF `the kind of reduction` EQUALS "part of a compromise or arrangement sanctioned under Part 26A, a company other than an overseas company not required to register particulars under section 1046" THEN `s 649(3)(aa)(i) part of a compromise or arrangement sanctioned under Part 26A, a company other than an overseas company not required to register particulars under section 1046`
                IF `the kind of reduction` EQUALS "part of a compromise or arrangement sanctioned under Part 26A, an overseas company not required to register particulars under section 1046" THEN `s 649(3)(aa)(ii) part of a compromise or arrangement sanctioned under Part 26A, an overseas company not required to register particulars under section 1046`
                OTHERWISE `s 649(3)(b) any case not within paragraph (a) or (aa)`

@export Under section 649, is the registrar's certificate conclusive evidence of this matter?
GIVEN `a certificate has been given under subsection (5)` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has the registrar given a certificate of the registration of the order and statement of capital?
      `the matter` IS A STRING @desc What is the matter? One of: "the requirements of this Act with respect to the reduction of share capital have been complied with", "the company's share capital is as stated in the statement of capital", "some other matter".
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 649, is the registrar's certificate conclusive evidence of this matter` IS
    `s 649(6)(b) the certificate is conclusive evidence of the matter` `a certificate has been given under subsection (5)` matter
    WHERE
        matter MEANS
            BRANCH
                IF `the matter` EQUALS "the requirements of this Act with respect to the reduction of share capital have been complied with" THEN `s 649(6)(b)(i) the requirements of this Act with respect to the reduction of share capital have been complied with`
                IF `the matter` EQUALS "the company's share capital is as stated in the statement of capital" THEN `s 649(6)(b)(ii) the company's share capital is as stated in the statement of capital`
                OTHERWISE `s 649(6)(b) some other matter`

§§ `Section 650: Public company reducing capital below authorised minimum`

@export Under section 650, does the Act bar the registrar from registering the court's order?
GIVEN `the company is a public company` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the company a public company (section 4(2))?
      `the court makes an order confirming a reduction of the company's capital` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has the court made an order confirming a reduction of the company's capital?
      `the nominal value of the company's allotted share capital after the reduction` IS A NUMBER @desc What will be the nominal value of the company's allotted share capital after the reduction, in pounds?
      `the authorised minimum` IS A NUMBER @desc What is the authorised minimum nominal value of a public company's allotted share capital (section 763), in pounds?
      `the court so directs` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has the court directed that the order may be registered?
      `the company is first re-registered as a private company` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has the company first been re-registered as a private company?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 650, does the Act bar the registrar from registering the court's order` IS
    `s 650(2) the registrar is barred from registering the order` (`s 650(1) section 650 applies` `the company is a public company` `the court makes an order confirming a reduction of the company's capital` `the nominal value of the company's allotted share capital after the reduction` `the authorised minimum`) `the court so directs` `the company is first re-registered as a private company`

§§ `Section 651: Expedited procedure for re-registration as a private company`

@export Under section 651, may the company now be re-registered as a private company?
GIVEN `the court has authorised the re-registration` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has the court authorised the company to be re-registered as a private company without a section 97 special resolution?
      `an application to that effect is delivered to the registrar` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has an application to that effect been delivered to the registrar?
      `it is delivered with a copy of the court's order` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Was it delivered with a copy of the court's order?
      `it is delivered with notice of the company's name and a copy of its articles as altered` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Was it delivered with notice of the company's name and a copy of its articles, as altered by the court's order?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 651, may the company now be re-registered as a private company` IS
    `s 651(3) the company may be re-registered as a private company` `the court has authorised the re-registration` `an application to that effect is delivered to the registrar` `it is delivered with a copy of the court's order` `it is delivered with notice of the company's name and a copy of its articles as altered`

§§ `Section 652: Liability of members following reduction of capital`

@export Under section 652, what is the most that I, as a member, can be called on to contribute in respect of the share?
GIVEN `the nominal amount of the share as notified to the registrar in the statement of capital` IS A NUMBER @desc What is the nominal amount of the share as notified to the registrar in the statement of capital, in pounds?
      `the amount paid on the share or the reduced amount deemed to have been paid on it` IS A NUMBER @desc How much has been paid on the share, or is deemed to have been paid on it after the reduction, in pounds?
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `Under section 652, what is the most that I, as a member, can be called on to contribute in respect of the share` IS
    `s 652(1) the most a member can be called on to contribute in respect of the share` `the nominal amount of the share as notified to the registrar in the statement of capital` `the amount paid on the share or the reduced amount deemed to have been paid on it`

@export Under section 652, am I liable to this call or contribution on the share?
GIVEN `the amount of the call or contribution` IS A NUMBER @desc How much is the call or contribution asked of you, in pounds?
      `the nominal amount of the share as notified to the registrar in the statement of capital` IS A NUMBER @desc What is the nominal amount of the share as notified to the registrar in the statement of capital, in pounds?
      `the amount paid on the share or the reduced amount deemed to have been paid on it` IS A NUMBER @desc How much has been paid on the share, or is deemed to have been paid on it after the reduction, in pounds?
      `the call is for the debt or claim of a creditor omitted from the list` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the call or contribution for the payment of the debt or claim of a creditor who was left off the list of creditors (section 653)?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 652, am I liable to this call or contribution on the share` IS
    `s 652(1) the member is liable to the call or contribution` `the amount of the call or contribution` `the nominal amount of the share as notified to the registrar in the statement of capital` `the amount paid on the share or the reduced amount deemed to have been paid on it` `the call is for the debt or claim of a creditor omitted from the list`

§§ `Section 653: Liability to creditor in case of omission from list of creditors`

@export Under section 653, am I liable to contribute for the payment of a creditor's debt or claim?
GIVEN `the reduction of capital was confirmed by the court` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Was the reduction of capital confirmed by the court?
      `a creditor entitled to object is not entered on the list of creditors` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Was a creditor entitled to object to the reduction left off the list of creditors?
      `that is by reason of his ignorance of the proceedings` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Was that because he was ignorant of the proceedings for reduction of share capital?
      `that is by reason of his ignorance of their nature and effect` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Or because he was ignorant of their nature and effect with respect to his debt or claim?
      `the company is unable to pay the debt or claim` IS A BOOLEAN @desc After the reduction, is the company unable to pay the amount of his debt or claim (as section 123 of the Insolvency Act 1986 or Article 103 of the Insolvency (Northern Ireland) Order 1989 uses that expression)?
      `I was a member of the company at the date the resolution took effect` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Were you a member of the company at the date on which the resolution for reducing capital took effect under section 649(3)?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 653, am I liable to contribute for the payment of a creditor's debt or claim` IS
    `s 653(2) the person is liable to contribute for the payment of the debt or claim` applies `I was a member of the company at the date the resolution took effect`
    WHERE
        applies MEANS `s 653(1) section 653 applies` `the reduction of capital was confirmed by the court` `a creditor entitled to object is not entered on the list of creditors` `that is by reason of his ignorance of the proceedings` `that is by reason of his ignorance of their nature and effect` (JUST `the company is unable to pay the debt or claim`)

@export Under section 653, what is the most that I could be liable to contribute for the creditor's debt or claim?
GIVEN `the reduction of capital was confirmed by the court` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Was the reduction of capital confirmed by the court?
      `a creditor entitled to object is not entered on the list of creditors` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Was a creditor entitled to object to the reduction left off the list of creditors?
      `that is by reason of his ignorance of the proceedings` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Was that because he was ignorant of the proceedings for reduction of share capital?
      `that is by reason of his ignorance of their nature and effect` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Or because he was ignorant of their nature and effect with respect to his debt or claim?
      `the company is unable to pay the debt or claim` IS A BOOLEAN @desc After the reduction, is the company unable to pay the amount of his debt or claim (as section 123 of the Insolvency Act 1986 or Article 103 of the 1989 Order uses that expression)?
      `I was a member of the company at the date the resolution took effect` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Were you a member of the company at the date on which the resolution for reducing capital took effect under section 649(3)?
      `the amount I would have been liable to contribute had the company begun to be wound up the day before` IS A NUMBER @desc How much would you have been liable to contribute if the company had commenced to be wound up on the day before that date, in pounds?
GIVETH A MAYBE NUMBER
DECIDE `Under section 653, what is the most that I could be liable to contribute for the creditor's debt or claim` IS
    `s 653(2) the most the person is liable to contribute` liable `the amount I would have been liable to contribute had the company begun to be wound up the day before`
    WHERE
        applies MEANS `s 653(1) section 653 applies` `the reduction of capital was confirmed by the court` `a creditor entitled to object is not entered on the list of creditors` `that is by reason of his ignorance of the proceedings` `that is by reason of his ignorance of their nature and effect` (JUST `the company is unable to pay the debt or claim`)
        liable MEANS `s 653(2) the person is liable to contribute for the payment of the debt or claim` applies `I was a member of the company at the date the resolution took effect`

@export Under section 653, may the court settle a list of persons liable to contribute and make and enforce calls on them?
GIVEN `the company is wound up` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has the company been wound up (is it being wound up)?
      `the creditor in question applies to the court` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has the creditor in question applied to the court?
      `ignorance as mentioned in subsection (1)(a) is proved` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has it been proved that the creditor was ignorant of the proceedings for reduction, or of their nature and effect on the debt or claim (section 653(1)(a))?
      `the court thinks fit` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does the court think fit to do so?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 653, may the court settle a list of persons liable to contribute and make and enforce calls on them` IS
    `s 653(3) the court may settle a list of persons liable to contribute and make and enforce calls` `the company is wound up` `the creditor in question applies to the court` `ignorance as mentioned in subsection (1)(a) is proved` `the court thinks fit`

-- =========================================================================================================
-- CHAPTER 11: MISCELLANEOUS AND SUPPLEMENTARY PROVISIONS
-- =========================================================================================================

§§ `Section 654: Treatment of reserve arising from reduction of capital`

@export Under section 654, is a reserve arising from the reduction of the company's share capital distributable?
GIVEN `the reserve arises from the reduction of the company's share capital` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does the reserve arise from the reduction of the company's share capital?
      `an order under this section provides that the prohibition does not apply to it` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has the Secretary of State made an order under section 654 providing that the prohibition does not apply to this reserve?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 654, is a reserve arising from the reduction of the company's share capital distributable` IS
    `s 654(1) the reserve is distributable` `the reserve arises from the reduction of the company's share capital` `an order under this section provides that the prohibition does not apply to it`

§§ `Section 655: Shares no bar to damages against company`

@export Under section 655, am I debarred from obtaining damages or other compensation from the company by reason only of my holding or having held shares in it?
GIVEN `the only reason is that I hold or have held shares in the company` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the only reason offered for denying you damages or compensation that you hold or have held shares in the company?
      `the only reason is that I hold or have held a right to apply or subscribe for shares` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the only reason that you hold or have held a right to apply or subscribe for shares?
      `the only reason is that I hold or have held a right to be included in the register of members in respect of shares` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the only reason that you hold or have held a right to be included in the company's register of members in respect of shares?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 655, am I debarred from obtaining damages or other compensation from the company by reason only of my holding or having held shares in it` IS
    `s 655 the person is debarred from obtaining damages or other compensation from the company` `the only reason is that I hold or have held shares in the company` `the only reason is that I hold or have held a right to apply or subscribe for shares` `the only reason is that I hold or have held a right to be included in the register of members in respect of shares`

§§ `Section 656: Public companies: duty of directors to call meeting on serious loss of capital`

@export Under section 656, must the directors call a general meeting?
GIVEN `the company is a public company` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the company a public company (section 4(2))?
      `the net assets of the company` IS A NUMBER @desc What are the company's net assets, in pounds?
      `the called-up share capital of the company` IS A NUMBER @desc What is the company's called-up share capital, in pounds?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 656, must the directors call a general meeting` IS
    `s 656(1) the directors must call a general meeting` `the company is a public company` `the net assets of the company` `the called-up share capital of the company`

@export Under section 656, by what day must the directors call the general meeting?
GIVEN `the date the fact is first known to a director` IS A DATE @desc On what is the earliest day on which a director of the company knew that the net assets are half or less of the called-up share capital?
GIVETH A DATE
DECIDE `Under section 656, by what day must the directors call the general meeting` IS
    `s 656(2) the last day for the call of the meeting` `the date the fact is first known to a director`

@export Under section 656, for what date at the latest must the general meeting be convened?
GIVEN `the date the fact is first known to a director` IS A DATE @desc On what is the earliest day on which a director of the company knew that the net assets are half or less of the called-up share capital?
GIVETH A DATE
DECIDE `Under section 656, for what date at the latest must the general meeting be convened` IS
    `s 656(3) the last day for which the meeting may be convened` `the date the fact is first known to a director`

@export Under section 656, am I, as a director, committing an offence by the way the meeting has been dealt with?
GIVEN `the company is a public company` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the company a public company (section 4(2))?
      `the net assets of the company` IS A NUMBER @desc What are the company's net assets, in pounds?
      `the called-up share capital of the company` IS A NUMBER @desc What is the company's called-up share capital, in pounds?
      `the date the fact is first known to a director` IS A DATE @desc What is the earliest day on which a director of the company knew that the net assets are half or less of the called-up share capital?
      `the directors have called the meeting` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Have the directors called the general meeting?
      `the date the directors called it` IS A DATE @desc If so, on what day? (Ignored if not.)
      `the date for which the meeting is convened` IS A DATE @desc For what date is the meeting convened?
      `today's date` IS A DATE @desc What day are you asking about (normally today)?
      `I knowingly authorise or permit the failure` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Do you knowingly authorise or permit the failure to convene the meeting?
      `after the period I knowingly authorise or permit the failure to continue` IS A BOOLEAN @desc After the period during which the meeting should have been convened, do you knowingly authorise or permit the failure to continue?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 656, am I, as a director, committing an offence by the way the meeting has been dealt with` IS
    `s 656(4) the director commits an offence` failure `I knowingly authorise or permit the failure` `after the period I knowingly authorise or permit the failure to continue`
    WHERE
        called MEANS IF `the directors have called the meeting` THEN JUST `the date the directors called it` ELSE NOTHING
        failure MEANS
            `s 656(4) there is a failure to convene a meeting as required by this section`
                (`s 656(1) the directors must call a general meeting` `the company is a public company` `the net assets of the company` `the called-up share capital of the company`)
                (`s 656(2) the directors called the general meeting in time` `the date the fact is first known to a director` called `today's date`)
                (`s 656(3) the meeting is convened for a date in time` `the date the fact is first known to a director` `the date for which the meeting is convened`)

@export Under section 656, what is the most that a person guilty of the offence can be fined on summary conviction, in pounds?
GIVEN `the pounds that the statutory maximum stands for` IS A NUMBER @desc How many pounds is the statutory maximum? (The Act does not say; it is set outside the Act.)
GIVETH A MAYBE NUMBER
DECIDE `Under section 656, what is the most that a person guilty of the offence can be fined on summary conviction, in pounds` IS
    CONSIDER `s 656(5) the penalty for a person guilty of an offence under this section` TRUE
    WHEN NOTHING THEN NOTHING
    WHEN JUST ps THEN
        CONSIDER (at ps 1)'s `fine not exceeding`
        WHEN NOTHING THEN NOTHING
        WHEN JUST f THEN `s 619(5) the most a fine can be, in pounds` f 0 `the pounds that the statutory maximum stands for`


@export Under section 656, does the section authorise the meeting to consider a matter that could not have been considered at it apart from this section?
GIVEN `the matter could not have been considered at that meeting apart from this section` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the matter one that could not have been considered at that meeting apart from section 656?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 656, does the section authorise the meeting to consider a matter that could not have been considered at it apart from this section` IS
    `s 656(6) the section authorises the consideration of the matter at the meeting` `the matter could not have been considered at that meeting apart from this section`

-- ====================================================================================================
-- seat questions from part coa15 (merged by the lead on 2026-11-12; unchanged text follows)
-- ====================================================================================================
-- coa15-seat.l4: THE SEAT LAYER for Part 18 of the Companies Act 2006 (United Kingdom), ss 658 to 736 (the Act's own numbering).
--
-- SEAT: an individual who is, or is about to become, a director, a company secretary or a member (shareholder) of a company registered under
-- the Act, or who deals with one (a creditor, say), asking on facts they can state what the Act requires or lets them do, what rights they have
-- against the company or its directors, what they must disclose, file, approve or vote on and by when, and what follows (liability, offences,
-- penalties) if it is not done. (Assumed, not ruled: the Act is addressed to companies, so the individual is whoever stands in a company's
-- management or ownership.) There is never a seat for an official: the registrar, the court and the Secretary of State appear only in what they
-- mean for this person.
--
-- PLAIN INPUTS. Every question takes yes/no, number, date or choice inputs, one for each fact the person can state, each with an @desc worded as
-- that person would be asked. The records the layer-1 modules expect are built inside each question, in its WHERE, from those answers, and the same
-- layer-1 rule is then called: no rule is restated here. Where a layer-1 rule takes another part's answer as a MAYBE BOOLEAN seam (whether an officer
-- is in default (s 1121), whether a resolution is a special resolution (s 283), whether a scheme is an employees' share scheme (s 1166), whether a
-- solvency statement was made (s 643)), the seat asks the person for that fact as a yes/no, and passes it in as JUST TRUE or JUST FALSE.
--
-- AMOUNTS. The statutory maximum and the standard scale are not in the Act, so a fine is answered as a limit (a fraction of the statutory maximum,
-- or a level on the standard scale) and never as pounds. Where a question asks for the sterling figure of a limit, the Act's own figures are used
-- only where the Act states them (the 15,000 pounds and 5% of s 692(1ZA), the 5,000 pounds and level 4 of ss 707(7) and 728(5)).
--
-- HOW TO READ AN ANSWER: JUST TRUE is the Act's yes; JUST FALSE is the Act's no, in its own words; NOTHING is "the Act does not decide this case on
-- these facts" (it never means no). The questions are grouped under § headings in the order of the text.

§ `The Companies Act 2006, Part 18: a limited company acquiring its own shares`

§§ `Chapter 1: the general rule, nominees and shares in public companies (ss 658 to 676)`

-- s 658: a limited company must not acquire its own shares except as Part 18 allows.
@export Under section 658(1), must my limited company not acquire its own shares in this way?
GIVEN `my company is a limited company` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is your company a limited company?
      `the acquisition is in accordance with the provisions of Part 18` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the acquisition one that Part 18 of the Act allows (for example a lawful purchase, redemption or reduction of capital)?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 658(1), must my limited company not acquire its own shares in this way` IS
    `s 658(1) a limited company must not make the acquisition` `my company is a limited company` (JUST `the acquisition is in accordance with the provisions of Part 18`)

@export Under section 658(2), am I guilty of an offence because my company acquired its own shares in contravention of section 658?
GIVEN `my company purported to acquire its own shares in contravention of section 658` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did your company purport to acquire its own shares in a way section 658 forbids?
      `I am a director of the company` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are you a director of the company?
      `I am an officer of the company who is in default` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are you an officer of the company who is in default (section 1121: you authorised, permitted, took part in or failed to take reasonable steps to prevent the contravention)?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 658(2), am I guilty of an offence because my company acquired its own shares in contravention of section 658` IS
    `s 658(2)(a) the person commits an offence` `my company purported to acquire its own shares in contravention of section 658`
        (IF `I am a director of the company` THEN `s 658(2) a director of the company` ELSE `s 658(2) an officer of the company`)
        (JUST `I am an officer of the company who is in default`)

@export Under section 658(2), is the purported acquisition of its own shares by my company void?
GIVEN `my company purported to acquire its own shares in contravention of section 658` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did your company purport to acquire its own shares in a way section 658 forbids?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 658(2), is the purported acquisition of its own shares by my company void` IS
    `s 658(2)(b) the purported acquisition is void` `my company purported to acquire its own shares in contravention of section 658`

@export Under section 658(3), what is the most I can be sentenced to if convicted of the offence?
GIVEN `where I am convicted` IS A `Mode of conviction` @desc Where would you be convicted? One of: on conviction on indictment; on summary conviction in England and Wales; on summary conviction in Scotland; on summary conviction in Northern Ireland
GIVETH A MAYBE Penalty
DECIDE `Under section 658(3), what is the most I can be sentenced to if convicted of the offence` IS
    `s 658(3) the penalty on conviction` `where I am convicted`

-- s 659: exceptions.
@export Under section 659(1), may my limited company acquire some of its own shares for nothing?
GIVEN `the shares are fully paid` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are the shares fully paid?
      `my company gives valuable consideration for them` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is your company giving anything of value for the shares?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 659(1), may my limited company acquire some of its own shares for nothing` IS
    `s 659(1) a limited company may acquire its own shares` `the shares are fully paid` `my company gives valuable consideration for them`

@export Under section 659(2), does section 658 not prohibit this acquisition?
GIVEN `how the shares are acquired` IS A `s 659(2) kind of acquisition` @desc How are the shares acquired? One of the kinds listed in section 659(2): a reduction of capital duly made; a purchase under a court order under section 98, 721(6), 759 or Part 30; a forfeiture or surrender in lieu for failure to pay a sum due on the shares; or any other acquisition
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 659(2), does section 658 not prohibit this acquisition` IS
    `s 659(2) section 658 does not prohibit the acquisition` `how the shares are acquired`

-- ss 660 and 661: shares held by the company's nominee.
@export Under section 660, are the shares held by my company's nominee treated as held by him on his own account, with the company having no beneficial interest?
GIVEN `the company is a limited company` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the company a limited company?
      `how the nominee came to hold the shares` IS A `s 660(1) how the shares come to the nominee` @desc How did the nominee come to hold the shares? One of: taken by a subscriber to the memorandum as nominee of the company; issued to a nominee of the company; acquired by a nominee of the company, partly paid up, from a third person; in another way
      `the nominee acquired them otherwise than by subscription as nominee of a public company` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did the nominee of a public company acquire the shares otherwise than by subscription?
      `a person acquired shares with financial assistance given by the company` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did a person acquire shares in the company with financial assistance the company gave him for the acquisition?
      `the company has a beneficial interest in the shares` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does the company have a beneficial interest in the shares (leaving out interests under sections 672 to 674)?
      `the shares were acquired by a nominee of the company` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Were the shares acquired by a nominee of the company?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 660, are the shares held by my company's nominee treated as held by him on his own account` IS
    `s 660(2)(a) the shares are treated as held by the nominee on his own account` `the nominee's shares`
    WHERE
        `the nominee's shares` MEANS `s 660(1) shares held by a nominee` WITH
            `s 660(1) the company is a limited company` IS `the company is a limited company`
            `s 660(1) how the shares come to the nominee` IS `how the nominee came to hold the shares`
            `s 660(3)(a) the shares were acquired otherwise than by subscription by a nominee of a public company` IS `the nominee acquired them otherwise than by subscription as nominee of a public company`
            `s 660(3)(a)(i) a person acquires shares in the company with financial assistance given to him by the company for the purpose of or in connection with the acquisition` IS `a person acquired shares with financial assistance given by the company`
            `s 660(3)(a)(ii) the company has a beneficial interest in the shares` IS `the company has a beneficial interest in the shares`
            `s 660(3)(b) the shares were acquired by a nominee of the company` IS `the shares were acquired by a nominee of the company`

@export Under section 661(2), am I jointly and severally liable with the nominee to pay the amount he failed to pay on the shares?
GIVEN `how the nominee came to hold the shares` IS A `s 660(1) how the shares come to the nominee` @desc How did the nominee come to hold the shares? One of: taken by a subscriber to the memorandum as nominee of the company; issued to a nominee of the company; acquired by a nominee of the company, partly paid up, from a third person; in another way
      `the company has a beneficial interest in the shares` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does the company have a beneficial interest in the shares?
      `I am another subscriber to the memorandum` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are you another subscriber to the company's memorandum?
      `I was a director when the shares were issued to or acquired by the nominee` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Were you a director of the company when the shares were issued to or acquired by the nominee?
      `the date the nominee was called on to pay` IS A DATE @desc On what date was the nominee called on to pay the amount?
      `the date the nominee paid, if he has` IS A MAYBE DATE @desc On what date did the nominee pay the amount (leave out if he has not)?
      `the date as of which I am asking` IS A DATE @desc As of what date are you asking?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 661(2), am I jointly and severally liable with the nominee to pay the amount he failed to pay on the shares` IS
    `s 661(2) the person is jointly and severally liable with the nominee to pay the amount` `the nominee's shares` `who I am` `the date the nominee was called on to pay` `the date the nominee paid, if he has` `the date as of which I am asking`
    WHERE
        `who I am` MEANS
            IF `I am another subscriber to the memorandum`
            THEN `s 661(2)(a) another subscriber to the memorandum`
            ELSE IF `I was a director when the shares were issued to or acquired by the nominee`
                 THEN `s 661(2)(b) a director of the company when the shares were issued to or acquired by the nominee`
                 ELSE `s 661(2) any other person`
        `the nominee's shares` MEANS `s 660(1) shares held by a nominee` WITH
            `s 660(1) the company is a limited company` IS TRUE
            `s 660(1) how the shares come to the nominee` IS `how the nominee came to hold the shares`
            -- Placeholder: section 661 does not read this field.
            `s 660(3)(a) the shares were acquired otherwise than by subscription by a nominee of a public company` IS FALSE
            -- Placeholder: section 661 does not read this field.
            `s 660(3)(a)(i) a person acquires shares in the company with financial assistance given to him by the company for the purpose of or in connection with the acquisition` IS FALSE
            `s 660(3)(a)(ii) the company has a beneficial interest in the shares` IS `the company has a beneficial interest in the shares`
            -- The exception of s 661(5) reads "acquired by a nominee of the company": every route of s 661(1) is a nominee's holding, so this is TRUE.
            `s 660(3)(b) the shares were acquired by a nominee of the company` IS TRUE

@export Under section 661(3), may the court relieve me from liability for the nominee's unpaid amount?
GIVEN `the proceedings are for the recovery of the amount under section 661(2)` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are there proceedings against you for recovery of the amount?
      `I acted honestly and reasonably` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did you act honestly and reasonably?
      `I ought fairly to be relieved having regard to all the circumstances` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Having regard to all the circumstances of the case, ought you fairly to be relieved from liability?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 661(3), may the court relieve me from liability for the nominee's unpaid amount` IS
    `s 661(3) the court may relieve the subscriber or director from his liability` `the proceedings are for the recovery of the amount under section 661(2)` `I acted honestly and reasonably` `I ought fairly to be relieved having regard to all the circumstances`

@export Under section 661(4), may I apply to the court for relief before any claim is made against me?
GIVEN `I am a subscriber to the memorandum or a director of the company` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are you a subscriber to the company's memorandum or a director of the company?
      `I have reason to apprehend that a claim will or might be made against me` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Do you have reason to apprehend that a claim will or might be made against you for the unpaid amount?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 661(4), may I apply to the court for relief before any claim is made against me` IS
    `s 661(4)(a) the subscriber or director may apply to the court for relief` `I am a subscriber to the memorandum or a director of the company` `I have reason to apprehend that a claim will or might be made against me`

-- s 662: a public company must cancel shares it holds, or has a beneficial interest in, in the cases the section lists.
@export Under section 662(2), must my public company cancel these shares and reduce its share capital?
GIVEN `my company is a public company` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is your company a public company?
      `how the company came to hold the shares` IS A `s 662(1) how the shares come to be held` @desc How did the shares come to be held? One of: forfeited or surrendered in lieu of forfeiture for failure to pay a sum due on them; surrendered under section 102C(1)(b) of the Building Societies Act 1986; acquired by the company otherwise than in accordance with Part 18 or Part 30; acquired by a nominee of the company from a third party without financial assistance; acquired by a person with financial assistance from the company; in another way
      `the company has a beneficial interest in the shares` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does the company have a beneficial interest in the shares (where the cases of section 662(1)(c) to (e) ask for it)?
      `the shares or the company's interest in them have been disposed of` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Have the shares, or the company's interest in them, already been disposed of?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 662(2), must my public company cancel these shares and reduce its share capital` IS
    `s 662(2)(a) the company must cancel the shares` `the shares held by the public company`
    WHERE
        `the shares held by the public company` MEANS `s 662(1) shares held by or for a public company` WITH
            `s 662(1) the company is a public company` IS `my company is a public company`
            `s 662(1) how the shares come to be held` IS `how the company came to hold the shares`
            `s 662(1)(c) to (e) the company has a beneficial interest in the shares` IS `the company has a beneficial interest in the shares`
            `s 662(2) the shares or any interest of the company in them have been previously disposed of` IS `the shares or the company's interest in them have been disposed of`
            -- Placeholder: s 662(2)(a) does not read this field.
            `s 662(2)(b) the cancellation brings the nominal value of the company's allotted share capital below the authorised minimum` IS FALSE

@export Under section 662(2)(b), must my public company also apply to re-register as a private company?
GIVEN `my company is a public company` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is your company a public company?
      `how the company came to hold the shares` IS A `s 662(1) how the shares come to be held` @desc How did the shares come to be held? One of: forfeited or surrendered in lieu of forfeiture for failure to pay a sum due on them; surrendered under section 102C(1)(b) of the Building Societies Act 1986; acquired by the company otherwise than in accordance with Part 18 or Part 30; acquired by a nominee of the company from a third party without financial assistance; acquired by a person with financial assistance from the company; in another way
      `the company has a beneficial interest in the shares` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does the company have a beneficial interest in the shares?
      `the shares or the company's interest in them have been disposed of` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Have the shares, or the company's interest in them, already been disposed of?
      `cancelling the shares brings the allotted share capital below the authorised minimum` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Would cancelling the shares bring the nominal value of the company's allotted share capital below the authorised minimum?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 662(2)(b), must my public company also apply to re-register as a private company` IS
    `s 662(2)(b) the company must apply for re-registration as a private company` `the shares held by the public company`
    WHERE
        `the shares held by the public company` MEANS `s 662(1) shares held by or for a public company` WITH
            `s 662(1) the company is a public company` IS `my company is a public company`
            `s 662(1) how the shares come to be held` IS `how the company came to hold the shares`
            `s 662(1)(c) to (e) the company has a beneficial interest in the shares` IS `the company has a beneficial interest in the shares`
            `s 662(2) the shares or any interest of the company in them have been previously disposed of` IS `the shares or the company's interest in them have been disposed of`
            `s 662(2)(b) the cancellation brings the nominal value of the company's allotted share capital below the authorised minimum` IS `cancelling the shares brings the allotted share capital below the authorised minimum`

@export Under section 662(3), by what date must my public company cancel the shares (and apply for re-registration if it must)?
GIVEN `my company is a public company` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is your company a public company?
      `how the company came to hold the shares` IS A `s 662(1) how the shares come to be held` @desc How did the shares come to be held? One of: forfeited or surrendered in lieu of forfeiture for failure to pay a sum due on them; surrendered under section 102C(1)(b) of the Building Societies Act 1986; acquired by the company otherwise than in accordance with Part 18 or Part 30; acquired by a nominee of the company from a third party without financial assistance; acquired by a person with financial assistance from the company; in another way
      `the date of the forfeiture, surrender or acquisition` IS A DATE @desc On what date were the shares forfeited, surrendered or acquired?
GIVETH A MAYBE DATE
DECIDE `Under section 662(3), by what date must my public company cancel the shares (and apply for re-registration if it must)` IS
    `s 662(3) the last day for cancelling the shares and for applying for re-registration` `the shares held by the public company` `the date of the forfeiture, surrender or acquisition`
    WHERE
        `the shares held by the public company` MEANS `s 662(1) shares held by or for a public company` WITH
            `s 662(1) the company is a public company` IS `my company is a public company`
            `s 662(1) how the shares come to be held` IS `how the company came to hold the shares`
            -- Placeholder: s 662(3) does not read this field.
            `s 662(1)(c) to (e) the company has a beneficial interest in the shares` IS TRUE
            -- Placeholder: s 662(3) does not read this field.
            `s 662(2) the shares or any interest of the company in them have been previously disposed of` IS FALSE
            -- Placeholder: s 662(3) does not read this field.
            `s 662(2)(b) the cancellation brings the nominal value of the company's allotted share capital below the authorised minimum` IS FALSE

@export Under section 662(5), may the company, or its nominee or other shareholder, vote the shares?
GIVEN `how the company came to hold the shares` IS A `s 662(1) how the shares come to be held` @desc How did the shares come to be held? One of: forfeited or surrendered in lieu of forfeiture for failure to pay a sum due on them; surrendered under section 102C(1)(b) of the Building Societies Act 1986; acquired by the company otherwise than in accordance with Part 18 or Part 30; acquired by a nominee of the company from a third party without financial assistance; acquired by a person with financial assistance from the company; in another way
      `the company has a beneficial interest in the shares` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does the company have a beneficial interest in the shares?
      `the person voting is the nominee or other shareholder` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the person voting the nominee or other shareholder (answer no if it is the company itself)?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 662(5), may the company, or its nominee or other shareholder, vote the shares` IS
    `s 662(5) the person may exercise voting rights in respect of the shares` `the shares held by the public company` `who votes`
    WHERE
        `who votes` MEANS IF `the person voting is the nominee or other shareholder` THEN `s 662(5) the nominee or other shareholder` ELSE `s 662(5) the company`
        `the shares held by the public company` MEANS `s 662(1) shares held by or for a public company` WITH
            `s 662(1) the company is a public company` IS TRUE
            `s 662(1) how the shares come to be held` IS `how the company came to hold the shares`
            `s 662(1)(c) to (e) the company has a beneficial interest in the shares` IS `the company has a beneficial interest in the shares`
            -- Placeholder: s 662(5) does not read this field.
            `s 662(2) the shares or any interest of the company in them have been previously disposed of` IS FALSE
            -- Placeholder: s 662(5) does not read this field.
            `s 662(2)(b) the cancellation brings the nominal value of the company's allotted share capital below the authorised minimum` IS FALSE

-- s 663: notice of cancellation, within one month.
@export Under section 663(1), by what date must my company give the registrar notice of the cancellation of the shares?
GIVEN `the date the shares were cancelled` IS A DATE @desc On what date were the shares cancelled?
GIVETH A DATE
DECIDE `Under section 663(1), by what date must my company give the registrar notice of the cancellation of the shares` IS
    `s 663(1) the last day for giving notice to the registrar` `the date the shares were cancelled`

@export Under section 663(3), does my company's statement of capital state everything the section requires?
GIVEN `it states the total number of shares of the company` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does the statement state the total number of shares of the company?
      `it states the aggregate nominal value of those shares` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does it state their aggregate nominal value?
      `it states the aggregate amount unpaid on those shares` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does it state the aggregate amount (if any) unpaid on those shares, whether on account of nominal value or by way of premium?
      `for every class it states prescribed particulars of the rights attached to the shares` IS A BOOLEAN @desc For every class of shares, does it state the prescribed particulars of the rights attached to the shares?
      `for every class it states the total number of shares of that class` IS A BOOLEAN @desc For every class, does it state the total number of shares of that class?
      `for every class it states the aggregate nominal value of the shares of that class` IS A BOOLEAN @desc For every class, does it state the aggregate nominal value of the shares of that class?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 663(3), does my company's statement of capital state everything the section requires` IS
    `s 663(3) the statement of capital states what the section requires` `the statement`
    WHERE
        -- One class entry stands for every class: the answer is yes only if every class states all three items.
        `the statement` MEANS `s 663(3) statement of capital` WITH
            `s 663(3) states the total number of shares of the company` IS `it states the total number of shares of the company`
            `s 663(3) states the aggregate nominal value of those shares` IS `it states the aggregate nominal value of those shares`
            `s 663(3) states the aggregate amount unpaid on those shares` IS `it states the aggregate amount unpaid on those shares`
            `s 663(3) entries for the classes of shares` IS LIST (`s 663(3) class entry` WITH
                `s 663(3) states prescribed particulars of the rights attached to the shares of the class` IS `for every class it states prescribed particulars of the rights attached to the shares`
                `s 663(3) states the total number of shares of the class` IS `for every class it states the total number of shares of that class`
                `s 663(3) states the aggregate nominal value of the shares of the class` IS `for every class it states the aggregate nominal value of the shares of that class`)

@export Under section 663(4), am I guilty of an offence because my company did not comply with section 663?
GIVEN `default was made in complying with section 663` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did your company make default in complying with section 663 (notice of the cancellation, with a statement of capital)?
      `I am an officer of the company who is in default` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are you an officer of the company who is in default (section 1121)?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 663(4), am I guilty of an offence because my company did not comply with section 663` IS
    `s 663(4) the person commits an offence` `default was made in complying with section 663` `s 658(2) an officer of the company` (JUST `I am an officer of the company who is in default`)

@export Under section 663(5), what is the most I can be fined if convicted of that offence?
GIVEN `where I am convicted` IS A `Mode of conviction` @desc Where would you be convicted? One of: on conviction on indictment; on summary conviction; on summary conviction in England and Wales; on summary conviction in Scotland; on summary conviction in Northern Ireland
GIVETH A MAYBE Penalty
DECIDE `Under section 663(5), what is the most I can be fined if convicted of that offence` IS
    `s 663(5) the penalty on conviction` `where I am convicted`

-- ss 664 to 668: re-registration as a private company.
@export Under section 664(1), may the directors resolve that my public company be re-registered as a private company?
GIVEN `my company is obliged to re-register as a private company to comply with section 662` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is your company obliged to re-register as a private company to comply with section 662?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 664(1), may the directors resolve that my public company be re-registered as a private company` IS
    `s 664(1) the directors may resolve that the company should be re-registered as a private company` `my company is obliged to re-register as a private company to comply with section 662`

@export Under section 664(4), is my company's application for re-registration accompanied by everything the section requires?
GIVEN `a copy of the resolution accompanies it` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does a copy of the resolution accompany the application?
      `a copy of the resolution has already been forwarded under Chapter 3 of Part 3` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has a copy of the resolution already been forwarded to the registrar under Chapter 3 of Part 3?
      `a copy of the articles as amended accompanies it` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does a copy of the articles as amended by the resolution accompany it?
      `a statement of compliance accompanies it` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does a statement of compliance accompany it?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 664(4), is my company's application for re-registration accompanied by everything the section requires` IS
    `s 664(4) the application is accompanied as the section requires` `a copy of the resolution accompanies it` `a copy of the resolution has already been forwarded under Chapter 3 of Part 3` `a copy of the articles as amended accompanies it` `a statement of compliance accompanies it`

@export Under section 665(4), does my company become a private company when the registrar issues the certificate?
GIVEN `the certificate has been issued` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has the registrar issued the certificate of incorporation on re-registration?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 665(4), does my company become a private company when the registrar issues the certificate` IS
    `s 665(4)(a) the company becomes a private company by virtue of the issue of the certificate` `the certificate has been issued`

@export Under section 666, does Chapter 1 of Part 20 apply to my public company as if it were a private company because it failed to re-register?
GIVEN `my company is a public company` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is your company a public company?
      `section 662 requires it to apply to be re-registered as a private company` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does section 662 require your company to apply to be re-registered as a private company?
      `the end of the period in section 662(3)` IS A DATE @desc What is the last day of the period section 662(3) allows?
      `the date it applied for re-registration, if it did` IS A MAYBE DATE @desc On what date did your company apply for re-registration (leave out if it did not)?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 666, does Chapter 1 of Part 20 apply to my public company as if it were a private company because it failed to re-register` IS
    `s 666(1) Chapter 1 of Part 20 applies to the company as if it were a private company` `my company is a public company` `section 662 requires it to apply to be re-registered as a private company` `the end of the period in section 662(3)` `the date it applied for re-registration, if it did`

@export Under section 667, am I guilty of an offence because my public company did not cancel the shares or re-register in time?
GIVEN `my company failed to cancel the shares or to apply for re-registration within the time section 662(3) allows` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did your company, when required by section 662, fail to cancel any shares or to apply for re-registration as a private company within the time section 662(3) allows?
      `I am an officer of the company who is in default` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are you an officer of the company who is in default (section 1121)?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 667, am I guilty of an offence because my public company did not cancel the shares or re-register in time` IS
    `s 667(2) the person commits an offence` `my company failed to cancel the shares or to apply for re-registration within the time section 662(3) allows` `s 658(2) an officer of the company` (JUST `I am an officer of the company who is in default`)

@export Under section 667(3), what is the most I can be fined if convicted of the offence of failing to cancel the shares or to re-register in time?
GIVEN `where I am convicted` IS A `Mode of conviction` @desc Where would you be convicted? One of: on summary conviction; on summary conviction in England and Wales; on summary conviction in Scotland; on summary conviction in Northern Ireland; on conviction on indictment (the Act states no penalty on indictment for this offence)
GIVETH A MAYBE Penalty
DECIDE `Under section 667(3), what is the most I can be fined if convicted of the offence of failing to cancel the shares or to re-register in time` IS
    `s 667(3) the penalty on conviction` `where I am convicted`

@export Under section 668, from what date does the period in section 662(3) run for my company that re-registered as a public company?
GIVEN `how the shares came to be held by the then private company` IS A `s 668(1) how the shares came to be held by or for the private company` @desc How did the shares come to be held while the company was private? One of: forfeited or surrendered in lieu of forfeiture; acquired by the company otherwise than by a method Part 18 or Part 30 permits; acquired by a nominee of the company without financial assistance; acquired by a person with financial assistance from the company; in another way
      `the company has a beneficial interest in the shares` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does the company have a beneficial interest in the shares?
      `the company has since been re-registered as a public company` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has the company since been re-registered as a public company?
      `the date of re-registration as a public company` IS A DATE @desc On what date was the company re-registered as a public company?
GIVETH A MAYBE DATE
DECIDE `Under section 668, from what date does the period in section 662(3) run for my company that re-registered as a public company` IS
    `s 668(3) the date from which the period specified in section 662(3) runs` `the shares held by the private company` `the date of re-registration as a public company`
    WHERE
        `the shares held by the private company` MEANS `s 668(1) shares held by or for a private company` WITH
            `s 668(1) how the shares came to be held` IS `how the shares came to be held by the then private company`
            `s 668(1)(b) to (d) the company has a beneficial interest in the shares` IS `the company has a beneficial interest in the shares`
            `s 668(1) the company is re-registered as a public company after that` IS `the company has since been re-registered as a public company`

-- s 669: transfer to a reserve.
@export Under section 669(1), how much must my public company transfer out of profits available for dividend to a reserve fund?
GIVEN `a public company, or its nominee, acquired shares in the company` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did a public company, or a nominee of a public company, acquire shares in the company?
      `those shares are shown in the balance sheet as an asset` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are those shares shown in the company's balance sheet as an asset?
      `I am asking about an interest in the shares and not the shares themselves` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are you asking about an interest in shares (so that the value to the company of its interest counts) rather than the shares themselves?
      `the value of the shares, or of the company's interest in them` IS A NUMBER @desc What is the value of the shares (or, for an interest in them, the value to the company of its interest), in pounds?
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `Under section 669(1), how much must my public company transfer out of profits available for dividend to a reserve fund` IS
    `s 669(1) the amount to be transferred to the reserve fund` `a public company, or its nominee, acquired shares in the company` `those shares are shown in the balance sheet as an asset` `what the company holds`
    WHERE
        `what the company holds` MEANS
            IF `I am asking about an interest in the shares and not the shares themselves`
            THEN `s 669(2) an interest in shares in the company` `the value of the shares, or of the company's interest in them`
            ELSE `s 669(2) shares in the company` `the value of the shares, or of the company's interest in them`

-- s 670: lien or charge of a public company on its own shares.
@export Under section 670, is a lien or charge my public company holds on its own shares void?
GIVEN `the company is a public company` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the company a public company?
      `the shares are not fully paid up` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are the shares not fully paid up?
      `the charge is for an amount payable in respect of the shares` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the charge for an amount payable in respect of the shares?
      `its ordinary business includes the lending of money` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does the company's ordinary business include the lending of money?
      `its ordinary business is credit or hire-purchase` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does the company's ordinary business consist of the provision of credit or the bailment (in Scotland, hiring) of goods under hire-purchase agreements, or both?
      `the charge arose in a transaction in the ordinary course of that business` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did the charge arise in connection with a transaction entered into in the ordinary course of that business?
      `the company has been re-registered as a public company` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has the company been re-registered as a public company?
      `the charge existed before the application for re-registration` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Was the charge in existence immediately before the application for re-registration?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 670, is a lien or charge my public company holds on its own shares void` IS
    `s 670(1) the lien or charge is void` `the charge`
    WHERE
        `the charge` MEANS `s 670(1) lien or charge of a company on its own shares` WITH
            `s 670(1) the company is a public company` IS `the company is a public company`
            `s 670(2) the shares are not fully paid up` IS `the shares are not fully paid up`
            `s 670(2) the charge is for an amount payable in respect of the shares` IS `the charge is for an amount payable in respect of the shares`
            `s 670(3)(a) the company's ordinary business includes the lending of money` IS `its ordinary business includes the lending of money`
            `s 670(3)(b) the company's ordinary business consists of the provision of credit or the bailment of goods under a hire-purchase agreement, or both` IS `its ordinary business is credit or hire-purchase`
            `s 670(3) the charge arises in connection with a transaction entered into in the ordinary course of that business` IS `the charge arose in a transaction in the ordinary course of that business`
            `s 670(4) the company has been re-registered as a public company` IS `the company has been re-registered as a public company`
            `s 670(4) the charge was in existence immediately before the application for re-registration` IS `the charge existed before the application for re-registration`

-- ss 671 to 676: interests disregarded, and the meanings the Chapter gives.
@export Under section 671, is the company's interest one to be disregarded in deciding whether it has a beneficial interest in the shares?
GIVEN `the shares are held on trust for a pension scheme or employees' share scheme` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are the shares held on trust for the purposes of a pension scheme or employees' share scheme?
      `the company's residual interest has vested in possession` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has the company's residual interest under the scheme vested in possession?
      `it is a charge, lien or set-off for the employer's monetary obligation under a scheme` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the interest a charge or lien on, or set-off against, a benefit under the scheme to let the employer or former employer recover a monetary obligation due from the member?
      `the company is a personal representative or trustee` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the company a personal representative or trustee?
      `the right` IS A `s 674 right of the company` @desc What is the right? One of: a right to recover its expenses or be remunerated out of the estate or trust property; a right to be indemnified out of that property for a liability incurred in performing its duties; any other right the company has as personal representative or trustee; a right the company does not have in that capacity
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 671, is the company's interest one to be disregarded in deciding whether it has a beneficial interest in the shares` IS
    `s 671 the interest is to be disregarded in determining whether the company has a beneficial interest`
        (`s 672(1) the residual interest is to be disregarded` `the shares are held on trust for a pension scheme or employees' share scheme` `the company's residual interest has vested in possession`)
        (`s 673(1)(a) the charge, lien or set-off is to be disregarded` `the shares are held on trust for a pension scheme or employees' share scheme` `it is a charge, lien or set-off for the employer's monetary obligation under a scheme`)
        (`s 674 the right is to be disregarded` `the company is a personal representative or trustee` `the right`)

@export Under section 675, is this scheme a pension scheme for the purposes of Chapter 1?
GIVEN `it provides benefits that are or include relevant benefits` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does the scheme provide benefits consisting of or including pensions, lump sums, gratuities or other like benefits given on retirement or death, or in anticipation of retirement, or in connection with past service after retirement or death?
      `the benefits are for or in respect of employees or former employees` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are the benefits for or in respect of employees or former employees?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 675, is this scheme a pension scheme for the purposes of Chapter 1` IS
    `s 675(1) the scheme is a pension scheme` `it provides benefits that are or include relevant benefits` `the benefits are for or in respect of employees or former employees`

@export Under section 676, is a director treated as employed by the company in a pension scheme or employees' share scheme?
GIVEN `the reference is to an employer or employee in the context of such a scheme` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the reference to an employer or employee in the context of a pension scheme or employees' share scheme?
      `the person is a director of the company` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the person a director of the company?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 676, is a director treated as employed by the company in a pension scheme or employees' share scheme` IS
    `s 676 the director is treated as employed by the company` `the reference is to an employer or employee in the context of such a scheme` `the person is a director of the company`

§§ `Chapter 2: financial assistance for the purchase of own shares (ss 677 to 683)`

@export Under section 677, is what my company is giving financial assistance for the purposes of Chapter 2?
GIVEN `the form the assistance takes` IS A `s 677(1) form of assistance` @desc What form does the assistance take? One of: a gift; a guarantee, security or indemnity; an indemnity in respect of the indemnifier's own neglect or default; a release or waiver; a loan, or another agreement under which the giver's obligations are fulfilled while another party's remain unfulfilled; a novation or assignment of rights under such a loan or agreement; any other financial assistance
      `the assistance reduces the company's net assets to a material extent` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does giving the assistance reduce the company's net assets to a material extent?
      `the company's assets in pounds` IS A NUMBER @desc What is the aggregate amount of the company's assets, in pounds?
      `the company's liabilities apart from provisions in pounds` IS A NUMBER @desc What is the aggregate amount of the company's liabilities, leaving out provisions, in pounds?
      `the company draws up Companies Act individual accounts` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does the company draw up Companies Act individual accounts?
      `the provisions of the kind specified under section 396 in pounds` IS A NUMBER @desc If so, what are the provisions of the kind specified by regulations under section 396, in pounds (0 if none)?
      `the company draws up IAS individual accounts` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does the company draw up IAS individual accounts?
      `the provisions made in the IAS accounts in pounds` IS A NUMBER @desc If so, what are the provisions made in those accounts, in pounds (0 if none)?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 677, is what my company is giving financial assistance for the purposes of Chapter 2` IS
    `s 677(1) the assistance given by the company is financial assistance` `the form the assistance takes` `the assistance reduces the company's net assets to a material extent`
        (`s 677(2) the net assets of the company` `the company's assets in pounds`
            (`s 677(3) the aggregate amount of the company's liabilities` `the company's liabilities apart from provisions in pounds` `the company draws up Companies Act individual accounts` `the provisions of the kind specified under section 396 in pounds` `the company draws up IAS individual accounts` `the provisions made in the IAS accounts in pounds`))

@export Under section 678(1), is it unlawful for my public company, or its subsidiary, to give this financial assistance for an acquisition of its shares?
GIVEN `a person is acquiring or proposing to acquire shares in the public company` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is a person acquiring, or proposing to acquire, shares in the public company?
      `the giver is the public company itself` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the company giving the assistance the public company whose shares are acquired?
      `the giver is a subsidiary of that public company` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the company giving the assistance a subsidiary of that public company?
      `it is financial assistance within section 677` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it financial assistance as section 677 defines it?
      `given for the purpose of the acquisition` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it given, directly or indirectly, for the purpose of the acquisition?
      `before or at the same time as the acquisition` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it given before or at the same time as the acquisition takes place?
      `principal purpose is not the acquisition` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the company's principal purpose in giving it not to give it for the purpose of the acquisition?
      `only an incidental part of a larger purpose` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is giving it for that purpose only an incidental part of some larger purpose of the company?
      `given in good faith in the interests of the company` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it given in good faith in the interests of the company?
      `a transaction listed in section 681(2)` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it a transaction listed in section 681(2) (a lawful dividend, a distribution in a winding up, bonus shares, a reduction of capital, a redemption or purchase under Chapters 3 or 4, a court-sanctioned arrangement, and so on)?
      `a transaction section 682 allows` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it a transaction listed in section 682(2) that meets the conditions of section 682(1) (for example a lender's ordinary lending, or help for an employees' share scheme)?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 678(1), is it unlawful for my public company, or its subsidiary, to give this financial assistance for an acquisition of its shares` IS
    `s 678(5) the assistance is prohibited by section 678 as it has effect subject to sections 681 and 682`
        (`s 678(1) it is not lawful for the company to give the financial assistance` `a person is acquiring or proposing to acquire shares in the public company` `the giver` (JUST `it is financial assistance within section 677`) `given for the purpose of the acquisition` `before or at the same time as the acquisition`)
        (`s 678(2) subsection (1) does not prohibit the assistance` `principal purpose is not the acquisition` `only an incidental part of a larger purpose` `given in good faith in the interests of the company`)
        (JUST `a transaction listed in section 681(2)`)
        (JUST `a transaction section 682 allows`)
    WHERE
        `the giver` MEANS
            IF `the giver is the public company itself` THEN `s 678(1) the company whose shares are acquired`
            ELSE IF `the giver is a subsidiary of that public company` THEN `s 678(1) a company that is a subsidiary of that company`
                 ELSE `s 678(1) another company`

@export Under section 678(3), is it unlawful for my company to give financial assistance to reduce or discharge a liability incurred for an acquisition of its shares while it is a public company?
GIVEN `a person has acquired shares in the company` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has a person acquired shares in the company?
      `a liability was incurred for the purpose of the acquisition` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Was a liability incurred (by that person or another) for the purpose of the acquisition?
      `the giver is the company or its subsidiary` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the company giving the assistance that company or a subsidiary of it?
      `it is financial assistance within section 677` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it financial assistance as section 677 defines it?
      `given to reduce or discharge the liability` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it given, directly or indirectly, for the purpose of reducing or discharging the liability?
      `the company is a public company when the assistance is given` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the company in which the shares were acquired a public company at the time the assistance is given?
      `principal purpose is not the liability` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the company's principal purpose in giving it not to reduce or discharge the liability?
      `only an incidental part of a larger purpose` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is reducing or discharging the liability only an incidental part of some larger purpose of the company?
      `given in good faith in the interests of the company` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it given in good faith in the interests of the company?
      `a transaction listed in section 681(2)` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it a transaction listed in section 681(2)?
      `a transaction section 682 allows` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it a transaction listed in section 682(2) that meets the conditions of section 682(1)?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 678(3), is it unlawful for my company to give financial assistance to reduce or discharge a liability incurred for an acquisition of its shares while it is a public company` IS
    `s 678(5) the assistance is prohibited by section 678 as it has effect subject to sections 681 and 682`
        (`s 678(3) it is not lawful for the company to give the financial assistance to reduce or discharge the liability` `a person has acquired shares in the company` `a liability was incurred for the purpose of the acquisition`
            (IF `the giver is the company or its subsidiary` THEN `s 678(1) the company whose shares are acquired` ELSE `s 678(1) another company`)
            (JUST `it is financial assistance within section 677`) `given to reduce or discharge the liability` `the company is a public company when the assistance is given`)
        (`s 678(4) subsection (3) does not prohibit the assistance` `principal purpose is not the liability` `only an incidental part of a larger purpose` `given in good faith in the interests of the company`)
        (JUST `a transaction listed in section 681(2)`)
        (JUST `a transaction section 682 allows`)

@export Under section 679(1), is it unlawful for my public company, a subsidiary of a private company, to give this financial assistance for an acquisition of shares in its private holding company?
GIVEN `a person is acquiring or proposing to acquire shares in the private holding company` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is a person acquiring, or proposing to acquire, shares in the private holding company?
      `the giver is a public company that is a subsidiary of that private company` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the company giving the assistance a public company that is a subsidiary of that private company?
      `it is financial assistance within section 677` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it financial assistance as section 677 defines it?
      `given for the purpose of the acquisition` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it given, directly or indirectly, for the purpose of the acquisition?
      `before or at the same time as the acquisition` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it given before or at the same time as the acquisition takes place?
      `principal purpose is not the acquisition` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the company's principal purpose in giving it not to give it for the purpose of the acquisition?
      `only an incidental part of a larger purpose` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is giving it for that purpose only an incidental part of some larger purpose of the company?
      `given in good faith in the interests of the company` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it given in good faith in the interests of the company?
      `a transaction listed in section 681(2)` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it a transaction listed in section 681(2)?
      `a transaction section 682 allows` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it a transaction listed in section 682(2) that meets the conditions of section 682(1)?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 679(1), is it unlawful for my public company, a subsidiary of a private company, to give this financial assistance for an acquisition of shares in its private holding company` IS
    `s 679(5) the assistance is prohibited by section 679 as it has effect subject to sections 681 and 682`
        (`s 679(1) it is not lawful for the public company to give the financial assistance` `a person is acquiring or proposing to acquire shares in the private holding company` `the giver is a public company that is a subsidiary of that private company`
            (JUST `it is financial assistance within section 677`) `given for the purpose of the acquisition` `before or at the same time as the acquisition`)
        (`s 679(2) subsection (1) does not prohibit the assistance` `principal purpose is not the acquisition` `only an incidental part of a larger purpose` `given in good faith in the interests of the company`)
        (JUST `a transaction listed in section 681(2)`)
        (JUST `a transaction section 682 allows`)

@export Under section 679(3), is it unlawful for my public company to give financial assistance to reduce or discharge a liability incurred for an acquisition of shares in its private holding company?
GIVEN `a person has acquired shares in the private holding company` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has a person acquired shares in the private holding company?
      `a liability was incurred for the purpose of the acquisition` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Was a liability incurred (by that person or another) for the purpose of the acquisition?
      `the giver is a public company that is a subsidiary of that private company` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the company giving the assistance a public company that is a subsidiary of that private company?
      `it is financial assistance within section 677` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it financial assistance as section 677 defines it?
      `given to reduce or discharge the liability` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it given, directly or indirectly, for the purpose of reducing or discharging the liability?
      `principal purpose is not the liability` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the company's principal purpose in giving it not to reduce or discharge the liability?
      `only an incidental part of a larger purpose` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is reducing or discharging the liability only an incidental part of some larger purpose of the company?
      `given in good faith in the interests of the company` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it given in good faith in the interests of the company?
      `a transaction listed in section 681(2)` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it a transaction listed in section 681(2)?
      `a transaction section 682 allows` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it a transaction listed in section 682(2) that meets the conditions of section 682(1)?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 679(3), is it unlawful for my public company to give financial assistance to reduce or discharge a liability incurred for an acquisition of shares in its private holding company` IS
    `s 679(5) the assistance is prohibited by section 679 as it has effect subject to sections 681 and 682`
        (`s 679(3) it is not lawful for the public company to give the financial assistance to reduce or discharge the liability` `a person has acquired shares in the private holding company` `a liability was incurred for the purpose of the acquisition` `the giver is a public company that is a subsidiary of that private company`
            (JUST `it is financial assistance within section 677`) `given to reduce or discharge the liability`)
        (`s 679(4) subsection (3) does not prohibit the assistance` `principal purpose is not the liability` `only an incidental part of a larger purpose` `given in good faith in the interests of the company`)
        (JUST `a transaction listed in section 681(2)`)
        (JUST `a transaction section 682 allows`)

@export Under section 680, am I guilty of an offence because my company gave prohibited financial assistance?
GIVEN `my company contravened section 678(1) or (3) or section 679(1) or (3)` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did your company contravene section 678(1) or (3) or section 679(1) or (3) (prohibited financial assistance)?
      `I am an officer of the company who is in default` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are you an officer of the company who is in default (section 1121)?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 680, am I guilty of an offence because my company gave prohibited financial assistance` IS
    `s 680(1) the person commits an offence` `my company contravened section 678(1) or (3) or section 679(1) or (3)` `s 658(2) an officer of the company` (JUST `I am an officer of the company who is in default`)

@export Under section 680(2), what is the most I can be sentenced to if convicted of that offence?
GIVEN `where I am convicted` IS A `Mode of conviction` @desc Where would you be convicted? One of: on conviction on indictment; on summary conviction in England and Wales; on summary conviction in Scotland; on summary conviction in Northern Ireland
GIVETH A MAYBE Penalty
DECIDE `Under section 680(2), what is the most I can be sentenced to if convicted of that offence` IS
    `s 680(2) the penalty on conviction` `where I am convicted`

@export Under section 681, does section 681 let my company do this despite sections 678 and 679?
GIVEN `the kind of transaction` IS A `s 681(2) transaction` @desc What kind of transaction is it? One of the kinds in section 681(2): a distribution by lawful dividend; a distribution in a winding up; an allotment of bonus shares; a reduction of capital under Chapter 10 of Part 17; a redemption under Chapter 3 of this Part; a purchase under Chapter 4 of this Part; anything done under a court order under Part 26 or 26A; anything done under an arrangement under section 110 of the Insolvency Act 1986 (or Article 96 of the 1989 Order); anything done under a binding arrangement with creditors under Part 1 of that Act (or Part 2 of the 1989 Order); any other transaction
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 681, does section 681 let my company do this despite sections 678 and 679` IS
    `s 681(1) neither section 678 nor section 679 prohibits the transaction` `the kind of transaction`

@export Under section 682, does section 682 let my company give this financial assistance despite sections 678 and 679?
GIVEN `lending of money is part of the ordinary business of my company` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the lending of money part of the ordinary business of your company?
      `this is the lending of money in the ordinary course of that business` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the transaction the lending of money in the ordinary course of your company's business?
      `the scheme is an employees' share scheme` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the assistance for the purposes of an employees' share scheme (as section 1166 defines it)?
      `the assistance is given in good faith in the interests of the company or its holding company` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the assistance given in good faith in the interests of the company or its holding company?
      `it is for or in connection with something done to enable or facilitate transactions in shares` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the assistance for the purposes of or in connection with anything done by the company (or another company in its group) to enable or facilitate transactions in shares in the company or its holding company?
      `the transactions are between bona fide employees or former employees` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are those transactions between, and do they involve beneficial ownership by, bona fide employees or former employees of the company (or another company in its group)?
      `the transactions are between their spouses, civil partners, widows, widowers or minor children` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are those transactions between, and do they involve beneficial ownership by, spouses or civil partners, widows, widowers or surviving civil partners, or minor children or step-children of such employees or former employees?
      `it is a loan to a person employed in good faith by the company` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it a loan to a person employed in good faith by the company?
      `that person is a director` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is that person a director?
      `the loan is to enable the person to acquire fully paid shares to be held beneficially` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the loan made with a view to enabling the person to acquire fully paid shares in the company or its holding company to be held by him by way of beneficial ownership?
      `the company giving the assistance is a private company` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the company giving the assistance a private company?
      `the company giving the assistance is a public company` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the company giving the assistance a public company?
      `its net assets are not reduced by the giving of the assistance` IS A BOOLEAN @desc If it is public: does the company have net assets that are not reduced by giving the assistance?
      `to the extent they are reduced, the assistance is provided out of distributable profits` IS A BOOLEAN @desc If it is public: to the extent its net assets are so reduced, is the assistance provided out of distributable profits?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 682, does section 682 let my company give this financial assistance despite sections 678 and 679` IS
    `s 682(1) neither section 678 nor section 679 prohibits the transaction`
        (`s 682(2) the transaction is one to which section 682 applies`
            (`s 682(2)(a) the transaction is a lending of money in the ordinary course` `lending of money is part of the ordinary business of my company` `this is the lending of money in the ordinary course of that business`)
            (`s 682(2)(b) the transaction is the provision of assistance for the purposes of an employees' share scheme` (JUST `the scheme is an employees' share scheme`) `the assistance is given in good faith in the interests of the company or its holding company`)
            (`s 682(2)(c) the transaction is assistance in connection with transactions in shares by employees or their families` `it is for or in connection with something done to enable or facilitate transactions in shares` `the transactions are between bona fide employees or former employees` `the transactions are between their spouses, civil partners, widows, widowers or minor children`)
            (`s 682(2)(d) the transaction is a loan to a person other than a director to acquire fully paid shares` `it is a loan to a person employed in good faith by the company` `that person is a director` `the loan is to enable the person to acquire fully paid shares to be held beneficially`))
        `the company giving the assistance is a private company` `the company giving the assistance is a public company` `its net assets are not reduced by the giving of the assistance` `to the extent they are reduced, the assistance is provided out of distributable profits`

@export Under section 683(1), how much are my company's distributable profits for this financial assistance?
GIVEN `the profits available for distribution in pounds` IS A NUMBER @desc What are the company's profits available for distribution (section 830), in pounds?
      `the assistance is a sale, transfer or other disposition of a non-cash asset` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does the assistance consist of or include (or arise in consequence of) a sale, transfer or other disposition of a non-cash asset?
      `the profit available for a distribution of that character in pounds` IS A NUMBER @desc If so, what profit would be available for a distribution of that character (section 846), in pounds (0 if none)?
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `Under section 683(1), how much are my company's distributable profits for this financial assistance` IS
    `s 683(1) the distributable profits in relation to the giving of the financial assistance` `the profits available for distribution in pounds` `the assistance is a sale, transfer or other disposition of a non-cash asset` `the profit available for a distribution of that character in pounds`

§§ `Chapter 3: redeemable shares (ss 684 to 689)`

@export Under section 684(1), may my limited company having a share capital issue redeemable shares?
GIVEN `the company is a limited company having a share capital` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is your company a limited company having a share capital?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 684(1), may my limited company having a share capital issue redeemable shares` IS
    `s 684(1) the company may issue redeemable shares` `the company is a limited company having a share capital`

@export Under section 684(2), may the articles of my private limited company exclude or restrict the issue of redeemable shares?
GIVEN `the company is a private limited company` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is your company a private limited company?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 684(2), may the articles of my private limited company exclude or restrict the issue of redeemable shares` IS
    `s 684(2) the articles may exclude or restrict the issue of redeemable shares` `the company is a private limited company`

@export Under section 684(3), may my public limited company issue redeemable shares?
GIVEN `the company is a public limited company` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is your company a public limited company?
      `the company is authorised to issue redeemable shares by its articles` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Do the company's articles authorise it to issue redeemable shares?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 684(3), may my public limited company issue redeemable shares` IS
    `s 684(3) the public limited company may issue redeemable shares` `the company is a public limited company` `the company is authorised to issue redeemable shares by its articles`

@export Under section 684(4), is the issue of redeemable shares barred because there are no issued shares that are not redeemable?
GIVEN `there are no issued shares of the company that are not redeemable` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are there at present no issued shares of the company that are not redeemable?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 684(4), is the issue of redeemable shares barred because there are no issued shares that are not redeemable` IS
    `s 684(4) the issue of redeemable shares is barred` `there are no issued shares of the company that are not redeemable`

@export Under section 685(1), may the directors of my company determine the terms, conditions and manner of redemption of the shares?
GIVEN `the company is a limited company` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is your company a limited company?
      `the articles authorise the directors to do so` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Do the company's articles authorise the directors to determine them?
      `a resolution of the company authorises the directors to do so` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has a resolution of the company authorised the directors to determine them?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 685(1), may the directors of my company determine the terms, conditions and manner of redemption of the shares` IS
    `s 685(1) the directors may determine the terms, conditions and manner of redemption` `the company is a limited company` `the articles authorise the directors to do so` `a resolution of the company authorises the directors to do so`

@export Under section 685(3), did the directors determine the terms of redemption in time, before the shares were allotted?
GIVEN `the directors are authorised to determine the terms` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are the directors authorised, under section 685(1), to determine the terms, conditions and manner of redemption?
      `the date the directors determined them` IS A DATE @desc On what date did the directors determine the terms, conditions and manner of redemption?
      `the date the shares are allotted` IS A DATE @desc On what date are the shares allotted?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 685(3), did the directors determine the terms of redemption in time, before the shares were allotted` IS
    `s 685(3)(a) the directors determined the terms before the shares were allotted` `the directors are authorised to determine the terms` `the date the directors determined them` `the date the shares are allotted`

@export Under section 686(1), is the redemption of these redeemable shares barred because they are not fully paid?
GIVEN `the shares are fully paid` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are the shares fully paid?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 686(1), is the redemption of these redeemable shares barred because they are not fully paid` IS
    `s 686(1) the redemption is barred` `the shares are fully paid`

@export Under section 687, may my company redeem the shares out of this source of money?
GIVEN `the company is a private limited company` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is your company a private limited company?
      `the redemption is in accordance with Chapter 5` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the redemption a payment out of capital made in accordance with Chapter 5?
      `it is paid out of distributable profits` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it paid out of the company's distributable profits?
      `it is paid out of the proceeds of a fresh issue made for the redemption` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it paid out of the proceeds of a fresh issue of shares made for the purposes of the redemption?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 687, may my company redeem the shares out of this source of money` IS
    `s 687(2) the redemption is out of a source the section permits`
        (`s 687(1) the private limited company may redeem the shares out of capital` `the company is a private limited company` (JUST `the redemption is in accordance with Chapter 5`))
        `it is paid out of distributable profits` `it is paid out of the proceeds of a fresh issue made for the redemption`

@export Under section 687(3) and (4), how much of the premium on redemption must come out of distributable profits?
GIVEN `the premium payable on redemption in pounds` IS A NUMBER @desc What premium is payable on redemption, in pounds?
      `the shares were issued at a premium` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Were the redeemable shares issued at a premium?
      `the premiums received on the issue of the shares redeemed in pounds` IS A NUMBER @desc What was the aggregate of the premiums received on the issue of the shares redeemed, in pounds?
      `the share premium account in pounds` IS A NUMBER @desc What is the current amount of the share premium account (including any sum transferred to it for premiums on the new shares), in pounds?
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `Under section 687(3) and (4), how much of the premium on redemption must come out of distributable profits` IS
    `s 687(3) the part of the premium that must be paid out of distributable profits` `the premium payable on redemption in pounds`
        (`s 687(4) the most of the premium that may be paid out of the proceeds of a fresh issue` `the shares were issued at a premium` `the premiums received on the issue of the shares redeemed in pounds` `the share premium account in pounds`)

@export Under section 688, what is my company's issued share capital after redeeming these shares?
GIVEN `the shares are redeemed` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are the shares being redeemed?
      `the issued share capital before in pounds` IS A NUMBER @desc What is the amount of the company's issued share capital before the redemption, in pounds?
      `the nominal value of the shares redeemed in pounds` IS A NUMBER @desc What is the nominal value of the shares redeemed, in pounds?
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `Under section 688, what is my company's issued share capital after redeeming these shares` IS
    `s 688(b) the amount of the company's issued share capital after the redemption` `the shares are redeemed` `the issued share capital before in pounds` `the nominal value of the shares redeemed in pounds`

@export Under section 689(1), by what date must my company give the registrar notice of the redemption?
GIVEN `the date the company redeemed the shares` IS A DATE @desc On what date did your company redeem the shares?
GIVETH A DATE
DECIDE `Under section 689(1), by what date must my company give the registrar notice of the redemption` IS
    `s 689(1) the last day for giving notice to the registrar` `the date the company redeemed the shares`

@export Under section 689(4), am I guilty of an offence because my company did not comply with section 689?
GIVEN `default was made in complying with section 689` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did your company make default in complying with section 689 (notice of the redemption, with a statement of capital)?
      `I am an officer of the company who is in default` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are you an officer of the company who is in default (section 1121)?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 689(4), am I guilty of an offence because my company did not comply with section 689` IS
    `s 689(4) the person commits an offence` `default was made in complying with section 689` `s 658(2) an officer of the company` (JUST `I am an officer of the company who is in default`)

@export Under section 689(5), what is the most I can be fined if convicted of the offence of failing to give notice of the redemption?
GIVEN `where I am convicted` IS A `Mode of conviction` @desc Where would you be convicted? One of: on summary conviction; on summary conviction in England and Wales; on summary conviction in Scotland; on summary conviction in Northern Ireland; on conviction on indictment (the Act states no penalty on indictment for this offence)
GIVETH A MAYBE Penalty
DECIDE `Under section 689(5), what is the most I can be fined if convicted of the offence of failing to give notice of the redemption` IS
    `s 689(5) the penalty on conviction` `where I am convicted`

§§ `Chapter 4: purchase of own shares (ss 690 to 708)`

@export Under section 690(1), may my limited company having a share capital purchase its own shares?
GIVEN `the company is a limited company having a share capital` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is your company a limited company having a share capital?
      `the articles restrict or prohibit the purchase` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Do the company's articles restrict or prohibit the purchase?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 690(1), may my limited company having a share capital purchase its own shares` IS
    `s 690(1) the limited company may purchase its own shares` `the company is a limited company having a share capital` `the articles restrict or prohibit the purchase`

@export Under section 690(2), is this purchase barred because no issued shares other than redeemable or treasury shares would remain?
GIVEN `no issued shares other than redeemable or treasury shares would remain` IS A BOOLEAN @desc As a result of the purchase, would there no longer be any issued shares of the company other than redeemable shares or shares held as treasury shares?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 690(2), is this purchase barred because no issued shares other than redeemable or treasury shares would remain` IS
    `s 690(2) the purchase is barred` `no issued shares other than redeemable or treasury shares would remain`

@export Under section 691(1), is the purchase barred because the shares are not fully paid?
GIVEN `the shares are fully paid` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are the shares fully paid?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 691(1), is the purchase barred because the shares are not fully paid` IS
    `s 691(1) the purchase is barred` `the shares are fully paid`

@export Under section 691(2), must my limited company pay for the shares on the purchase?
GIVEN `the company is a private limited company` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is your company a private limited company?
      `the purchase is for an employees' share scheme` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the purchase for the purposes of or pursuant to an employees' share scheme (as section 1166 defines it)?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 691(2), must my limited company pay for the shares on the purchase` IS
    `s 691(2) the shares must be paid for on purchase` (`s 691(3) subsection (2) does not apply` `the company is a private limited company` (JUST `the purchase is for an employees' share scheme`))

@export Under section 692(1ZA), how much may my private limited company pay out of capital for its own shares in this financial year without following Chapter 5?
GIVEN `the company is a private limited company` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is your company a private limited company?
      `the articles authorise purchases out of capital outside Chapter 5` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Do the company's articles authorise it to purchase its own shares out of capital otherwise than under Chapter 5?
      `the share capital is in sterling` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the company's share capital denominated in sterling?
      `the nominal value of the fully paid share capital at the start of the financial year` IS A NUMBER @desc What was the nominal value of the company's fully paid share capital at the beginning of the financial year, in the currency it is denominated in?
      `the spot rate to pounds` IS A NUMBER @desc If it is not in sterling: what is the spot rate of exchange, in pounds for one unit, on a day specified in the resolution authorising the purchase (1 if it is in sterling)?
GIVETH A MAYBE NUMBER
DECIDE `Under section 692(1ZA), how much may my private limited company pay out of capital for its own shares in this financial year without following Chapter 5` IS
    `s 692(1ZA) the most the company may pay out of capital in the financial year` `the company is a private limited company` `the articles authorise purchases out of capital outside Chapter 5`
        (`s 692(1A) the value in sterling of the share capital` `the share capital is in sterling` `the nominal value of the fully paid share capital at the start of the financial year` `the spot rate to pounds`)

@export Under section 692(2), may my company pay for the purchase out of this source of money?
GIVEN `the company is a private limited company` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is your company a private limited company?
      `the purchase is in accordance with Chapter 5` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the purchase paid for out of capital in accordance with Chapter 5?
      `the payment is within the section 692(1ZA) amount` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the payment within the amount section 692(1ZA) allows out of capital this financial year?
      `it is paid out of distributable profits` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it paid out of the company's distributable profits?
      `it is paid out of the proceeds of a fresh issue made to finance the purchase` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it paid out of the proceeds of a fresh issue of shares made for the purpose of financing the purchase?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 692(2), may my company pay for the purchase out of this source of money` IS
    `s 692(2)(a) the purchase is out of a source the section permits`
        (`s 692(1) the private limited company may purchase its own shares out of capital` `the company is a private limited company` (JUST `the purchase is in accordance with Chapter 5`))
        `the payment is within the section 692(1ZA) amount` `it is paid out of distributable profits` `it is paid out of the proceeds of a fresh issue made to finance the purchase`

@export Under section 692(2)(b) and (3), how much of the premium on the purchase must come out of distributable profits?
GIVEN `the premium payable on the purchase in pounds` IS A NUMBER @desc What premium is payable on the purchase, in pounds?
      `the shares were issued at a premium` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Were the shares to be purchased issued at a premium?
      `the premiums received on their issue in pounds` IS A NUMBER @desc What was the aggregate of the premiums received on the issue of the shares purchased, in pounds?
      `the share premium account in pounds` IS A NUMBER @desc What is the current amount of the share premium account (including any sum transferred to it for premiums on the new shares), in pounds?
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `Under section 692(2)(b) and (3), how much of the premium on the purchase must come out of distributable profits` IS
    `s 692(2)(b) the part of the premium that must be paid out of distributable profits` `the premium payable on the purchase in pounds`
        (`s 692(3) the most of the premium that may be paid out of the proceeds of a fresh issue` `the shares were issued at a premium` `the premiums received on their issue in pounds` `the share premium account in pounds`)

@export Under section 693, may my limited company make this purchase of its own shares, given how it was authorised?
GIVEN `the purchase is off-market and not a market purchase` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it an off-market purchase (answer no for a market purchase)?
      `an employees' share scheme resolution under section 693A authorised it` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Was it authorised by a resolution under section 693A (for an employees' share scheme)?
      `a contract approved in advance under section 694 covers it` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it made in pursuance of a contract approved in advance under section 694?
      `a resolution under section 701 authorised it` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Was it authorised by a resolution of the company under section 701 (market purchase)?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 693, may my limited company make this purchase of its own shares, given how it was authorised` IS
    `s 693(1) the limited company may make the purchase`
        (IF `the purchase is off-market and not a market purchase` THEN `s 693(1)(a) an off-market purchase` ELSE `s 693(1)(b) a market purchase`)
        (JUST `an employees' share scheme resolution under section 693A authorised it`) (JUST `a contract approved in advance under section 694 covers it`) (JUST `a resolution under section 701 authorised it`)

@export Under section 693(2), is this purchase of my company's own shares an off-market purchase?
GIVEN `the shares are purchased on a recognised investment exchange` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are the shares purchased on a recognised investment exchange (one within Part 18 of the Financial Services and Markets Act 2000, other than an overseas investment exchange)?
      `the shares are listed under Part 6 of the Financial Services and Markets Act 2000` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are the company's shares listed under Part 6 of the Financial Services and Markets Act 2000?
      `the company has been afforded facilities for dealings on the exchange` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has the company been afforded facilities for dealings in the shares to take place on the exchange?
      `the facilities are afforded without prior permission for individual transactions` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are the facilities afforded without prior permission for individual transactions from the authority governing the exchange?
      `the facilities are afforded without limit as to time` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are the facilities afforded without limit as to the time during which they are to be available?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 693(2), is this purchase of my company's own shares an off-market purchase` IS
    `s 693(2) the purchase is an off-market purchase` `the shares are purchased on a recognised investment exchange`
        (`s 693(3) the shares are subject to a marketing arrangement on the exchange` `the shares are listed under Part 6 of the Financial Services and Markets Act 2000` `the company has been afforded facilities for dealings on the exchange` `the facilities are afforded without prior permission for individual transactions` `the facilities are afforded without limit as to time`)

@export Under section 693(4), is this purchase of my company's own shares a market purchase?
GIVEN `the shares are purchased on a recognised investment exchange` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are the shares purchased on a recognised investment exchange (one within Part 18 of the Financial Services and Markets Act 2000, other than an overseas investment exchange)?
      `the shares are listed under Part 6 of the Financial Services and Markets Act 2000` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are the company's shares listed under Part 6 of the Financial Services and Markets Act 2000?
      `the company has been afforded facilities for dealings on the exchange` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has the company been afforded facilities for dealings in the shares to take place on the exchange?
      `the facilities are afforded without prior permission for individual transactions` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are the facilities afforded without prior permission for individual transactions from the authority governing the exchange?
      `the facilities are afforded without limit as to time` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are the facilities afforded without limit as to the time during which they are to be available?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 693(4), is this purchase of my company's own shares a market purchase` IS
    `s 693(4) the purchase is a market purchase` `the shares are purchased on a recognised investment exchange`
        (`s 693(2) the purchase is an off-market purchase` `the shares are purchased on a recognised investment exchange`
            (`s 693(3) the shares are subject to a marketing arrangement on the exchange` `the shares are listed under Part 6 of the Financial Services and Markets Act 2000` `the company has been afforded facilities for dealings on the exchange` `the facilities are afforded without prior permission for individual transactions` `the facilities are afforded without limit as to time`))

@export Under section 693A(5), is the expiry date in the resolution authorising a purchase one the Act allows (not later than five years after it is passed)?
GIVEN `the date the resolution is passed` IS A DATE @desc On what date is the resolution passed?
      `the expiry date the resolution specifies, if it specifies one` IS A MAYBE DATE @desc What expiry date does the resolution specify (leave out if it specifies none)?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 693A(5), is the expiry date in the resolution authorising a purchase one the Act allows (not later than five years after it is passed)` IS
    `s 693A(5) the resolution specifies a date of expiry that is not later than five years after it is passed` `the date the resolution is passed` `the expiry date the resolution specifies, if it specifies one`

@export Under section 694(2), is the contract for my company's off-market purchase approved in the way the section requires?
GIVEN `its terms were authorised by a resolution before the contract was entered into` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Were the terms of the contract authorised by a resolution of the company before the contract was entered into?
      `the contract provides that no shares may be purchased until its terms are authorised` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does the contract provide that no shares may be purchased under it until its terms have been authorised by a resolution of the company?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 694(2), is the contract for my company's off-market purchase approved in the way the section requires` IS
    `s 694(2) the contract is approved in the way the subsection requires` `its terms were authorised by a resolution before the contract was entered into` `the contract provides that no shares may be purchased until its terms are authorised`

@export Under section 695(3), is the resolution authorising the purchase not effective because of how members holding the shares voted?
GIVEN `the resolution is proposed at a meeting` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the resolution proposed at a meeting (answer no for a written resolution)?
      `a member holding shares to which the resolution relates voted on it` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did a member holding shares to which the resolution relates vote on it (on a poll or otherwise)?
      `it would not have passed without that vote` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Would the resolution not have been passed if he had not voted?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 695(3), is the resolution authorising the purchase not effective because of how members holding the shares voted` IS
    `s 695(3) the resolution is not effective` `the resolution is proposed at a meeting` `a member holding shares to which the resolution relates voted on it` `it would not have passed without that vote`

@export Under section 696, was the contract disclosed to members as the section requires for a resolution at a meeting?
GIVEN `the first day the copy or memorandum was available at the registered office` IS A DATE @desc On what day did the copy of the contract (or memorandum of its terms) first become available for inspection by members at the registered office (and stay available to the meeting)?
      `the date of the meeting` IS A DATE @desc On what date is the meeting?
      `it was also available at the meeting` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Was it also available for inspection at the meeting itself?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 696, was the contract disclosed to members as the section requires for a resolution at a meeting` IS
    `s 696(2)(b) the copy or memorandum was made available to members for a resolution at a meeting` `the first day the copy or memorandum was available at the registered office` `the date of the meeting` `it was also available at the meeting`

@export Under section 696, was the contract disclosed to members as the section requires for a written resolution?
GIVEN `it was sent or submitted to every eligible member` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Was a copy of the contract (or memorandum of its terms) sent or submitted to every eligible member?
      `the date it was sent or submitted` IS A DATE @desc On what date was it sent or submitted?
      `the date the proposed resolution was sent or submitted` IS A DATE @desc On what date was the proposed resolution sent or submitted?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 696, was the contract disclosed to members as the section requires for a written resolution` IS
    `s 696(2)(a) the copy or memorandum was made available to members for a written resolution` `it was sent or submitted to every eligible member` `the date it was sent or submitted` `the date the proposed resolution was sent or submitted`

@export Under section 696(5), is the resolution not validly passed because section 696 was not complied with?
GIVEN `the requirements of section 696 were complied with` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Were all the requirements of section 696 complied with?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 696(5), is the resolution not validly passed because section 696 was not complied with` IS
    `s 696(5) the resolution is not validly passed` `the requirements of section 696 were complied with`

@export Under section 697(1), may my company agree to a variation of the contract?
GIVEN `the contract is one authorised under section 694` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the contract one authorised under section 694?
      `the variation is approved in advance in accordance with section 697` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has the variation been approved in advance in accordance with section 697 (terms authorised by a resolution before it is agreed to)?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 697(1), may my company agree to a variation of the contract` IS
    `s 697(1) the company may agree to the variation` `the contract is one authorised under section 694` `the variation is approved in advance in accordance with section 697`

@export Under section 700(1), is the agreement releasing my company's rights under the contract void?
GIVEN `the terms of the release are approved in advance in accordance with section 700` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Were the terms of the release agreement approved in advance in accordance with section 700 (authorised by a resolution before the agreement was entered into)?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 700(1), is the agreement releasing my company's rights under the contract void` IS
    `s 700(1) the release agreement is void` `the terms of the release are approved in advance in accordance with section 700`

@export Under section 701(1), may my company make this market purchase of its own shares?
GIVEN `a resolution of the company has first authorised the purchase` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has the purchase first been authorised by a resolution of the company?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 701(1), may my company make this market purchase of its own shares` IS
    `s 701(1) the company may make the market purchase` `a resolution of the company has first authorised the purchase`

@export Under section 701(5), is the expiry date in the resolution authorising a market purchase one the Act allows?
GIVEN `the date the resolution is passed` IS A DATE @desc On what date is the resolution passed?
      `the expiry date the resolution specifies, if it specifies one` IS A MAYBE DATE @desc What expiry date does the resolution specify (leave out if it specifies none)?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 701(5), is the expiry date in the resolution authorising a market purchase one the Act allows` IS
    `s 701(5) the resolution specifies a date of expiry that is not later than five years after it is passed` `the date the resolution is passed` `the expiry date the resolution specifies, if it specifies one`

@export Under section 702(3), until what date must my company keep the copy of the contract or memorandum available for inspection?
GIVEN `the date the purchase of all the shares was completed, if it was` IS A MAYBE DATE @desc On what date was the purchase of all the shares in pursuance of the contract completed (leave out if it has not been)?
      `the date the contract otherwise determined, if it did` IS A MAYBE DATE @desc On what date did the contract otherwise determine (leave out if it has not)?
GIVETH A MAYBE DATE
DECIDE `Under section 702(3), until what date must my company keep the copy of the contract or memorandum available for inspection` IS
    `s 702(3) the last day on which the copy or memorandum must be kept available` `the date the purchase of all the shares was completed, if it was` `the date the contract otherwise determined, if it did`

@export Under section 702(6), may I inspect the copy of the contract or memorandum without charge?
GIVEN `I am a member of the company` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are you a member of the company?
      `the company is a public company` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the company a public company?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 702(6), may I inspect the copy of the contract or memorandum without charge` IS
    `s 702(6) the person may inspect the copy or memorandum without charge` (IF `I am a member of the company` THEN `s 702(6)(a) a member of the company` ELSE `s 702(6)(b) any other person`) `the company is a public company`

@export Under section 703, am I guilty of an offence because my company did not keep the contract available or refused inspection?
GIVEN `default was made in complying with section 702(2), (3) or (4)` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did your company make default in complying with section 702(2), (3) or (4) (keeping the copy or memorandum, for the period, at a permitted place)?
      `the days of default in giving notice of the place under section 702(5)` IS A NUMBER @desc For how many days has the company made default in giving the registrar notice of the place (section 702(5))?
      `an inspection was refused` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Was an inspection required under section 702(6) refused?
      `I am an officer of the company who is in default` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are you an officer of the company who is in default (section 1121)?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 703, am I guilty of an offence because my company did not keep the contract available or refused inspection` IS
    CONSIDER `s 703(1) the company is in default as the subsection describes` `default was made in complying with section 702(2), (3) or (4)` `the days of default in giving notice of the place under section 702(5)` `an inspection was refused`
    WHEN JUST TRUE THEN `s 703(1) the person commits an offence` TRUE `s 658(2) an officer of the company` (JUST `I am an officer of the company who is in default`)
    WHEN JUST FALSE THEN `s 703(1) the person commits an offence` FALSE `s 658(2) an officer of the company` (JUST `I am an officer of the company who is in default`)
    WHEN NOTHING THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (points outside the text): whether the company is in default is not known

@export Under section 703(2), what is the most I can be fined if convicted of the offence of failing to keep the contract available or refusing inspection?
GIVEN `where I am convicted` IS A `Mode of conviction` @desc Where would you be convicted? One of: on summary conviction; on summary conviction in England and Wales; on summary conviction in Scotland; on summary conviction in Northern Ireland; on conviction on indictment (the Act states no penalty on indictment for this offence)
GIVETH A MAYBE Penalty
DECIDE `Under section 703(2), what is the most I can be fined if convicted of the offence of failing to keep the contract available or refusing inspection` IS
    `s 703(2) the penalty on conviction` `where I am convicted`

@export Under section 704, can my company assign its right to purchase its own shares under this contract?
GIVEN `the authority the contract was made under` IS A `s 704 the section under which the contract is authorised` @desc Under which section is the contract authorised? One of: section 693A (employees' share scheme); section 694 (off-market purchase); section 701 (market purchase); none of those
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 704, can my company assign its right to purchase its own shares under this contract` IS
    `s 704 the company's right under the contract is capable of being assigned` `the authority the contract was made under`

@export Under section 705(2), what follows if a payment for a right, a variation or a release is not paid out of distributable profits?
GIVEN `what the payment is for` IS A `s 705(1) what the payment is in consideration of` @desc What is the payment for? One of: acquiring a right with respect to the purchase of its own shares under a contingent purchase contract approved under section 694; the variation of a contract approved under section 694; the release of an obligation of the company under a contract approved under section 694 or authorised under section 701; something else
      `it is paid out of distributable profits` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the payment made out of the company's distributable profits?
GIVETH A `s 705(2) consequence of the requirement not being met`
DECIDE `Under section 705(2), what follows if a payment for a right, a variation or a release is not paid out of distributable profits` IS
    `s 705(2) the consequence of the requirement not being met` `what the payment is for` `it is paid out of distributable profits`

@export Under section 706(a), may the shares my company purchased be held and dealt with as treasury shares?
GIVEN `the purchase was made in accordance with Chapter 4` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Was the purchase made in accordance with Chapter 4?
      `the purchase was made out of distributable profits` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Was the purchase made out of distributable profits?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 706(a), may the shares my company purchased be held and dealt with as treasury shares` IS
    `s 706(a) the shares may be held and dealt with in accordance with Chapter 6` `the purchase was made in accordance with Chapter 4` `the purchase was made out of distributable profits`

@export Under section 706(b)(i), are the shares my company purchased treated as cancelled?
GIVEN `the purchase was made in accordance with Chapter 4` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Was the purchase made in accordance with Chapter 4?
      `the purchase was made out of distributable profits` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Was the purchase made out of distributable profits?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 706(b)(i), are the shares my company purchased treated as cancelled` IS
    `s 706(b)(i) the shares are treated as cancelled` `the purchase was made in accordance with Chapter 4` `the purchase was made out of distributable profits`

@export Under section 706(b)(ii), what is my company's issued share capital after a purchase that cancels the shares?
GIVEN `the purchase was made in accordance with Chapter 4` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Was the purchase made in accordance with Chapter 4?
      `the purchase was made out of distributable profits` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Was the purchase made out of distributable profits?
      `the issued share capital before the purchase in pounds` IS A NUMBER @desc What is the company's issued share capital before the purchase, in pounds?
      `the nominal value of the shares cancelled in pounds` IS A NUMBER @desc What is the nominal value of the shares cancelled, in pounds?
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `Under section 706(b)(ii), what is my company's issued share capital after a purchase that cancels the shares` IS
    `s 706(b)(ii) the amount of the company's issued share capital after the purchase` `the purchase was made in accordance with Chapter 4` `the purchase was made out of distributable profits` `the issued share capital before the purchase in pounds` `the nominal value of the shares cancelled in pounds`

@export Under section 707(1), by what date must my company deliver the return of its purchase to the registrar?
GIVEN `the date the shares were delivered to the company` IS A DATE @desc On what date were the shares delivered to the company?
GIVETH A DATE
DECIDE `Under section 707(1), by what date must my company deliver the return of its purchase to the registrar` IS
    `s 707(1) the last day for delivering the return to the registrar` `the date the shares were delivered to the company`

@export Under section 707(6), am I guilty of an offence because my company did not deliver the return?
GIVEN `default was made in complying with section 707` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did your company make default in complying with section 707 (the return of the purchase)?
      `I am an officer of the company who is in default` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are you an officer of the company who is in default (section 1121)?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 707(6), am I guilty of an offence because my company did not deliver the return` IS
    `s 707(6) the person commits an offence` `default was made in complying with section 707` `s 658(2) an officer of the company` (JUST `I am an officer of the company who is in default`)

@export Under section 707(7), what is the most I can be fined if convicted of that offence?
GIVEN `where I am convicted` IS A `Mode of conviction` @desc Where would you be convicted? One of: on conviction on indictment; on summary conviction; on summary conviction in England and Wales; on summary conviction in Scotland; on summary conviction in Northern Ireland
      `the amended wording of the daily fine is in force` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN @desc Is the wording that substitutes one-tenth of the greater of 5,000 pounds and the level 4 amount for one-tenth of the statutory maximum in force? (leave out if you do not know)
GIVETH A MAYBE `s 707(7) penalty`
DECIDE `Under section 707(7), what is the most I can be fined if convicted of that offence` IS
    `s 707(7) the penalty on conviction` `where I am convicted` `the amended wording of the daily fine is in force`

@export Under section 708, by what date must my company give the registrar notice of the cancellation of the shares it purchased?
GIVEN `the date the shares were delivered to the company` IS A DATE @desc On what date were the shares delivered to the company?
GIVETH A DATE
DECIDE `Under section 708, by what date must my company give the registrar notice of the cancellation of the shares it purchased` IS
    `s 708(1) the last day for giving notice of cancellation to the registrar` `the date the shares were delivered to the company`

@export Under section 708(1), must my company give the registrar notice of the cancellation of the shares it purchased?
GIVEN `the purchase was made out of distributable profits` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Was the purchase made out of distributable profits?
      `the shares are cancelled forthwith` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are the shares cancelled forthwith (under section 729)?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 708(1), must my company give the registrar notice of the cancellation of the shares it purchased` IS
    `s 708(1) the company must give notice of cancellation to the registrar` TRUE `the purchase was made out of distributable profits` `the shares are cancelled forthwith`

@export Under section 708(4), am I guilty of an offence because my company did not give notice of the cancellation?
GIVEN `default was made in complying with section 708` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did your company make default in complying with section 708 (notice of the cancellation)?
      `I am an officer of the company who is in default` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are you an officer of the company who is in default (section 1121)?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 708(4), am I guilty of an offence because my company did not give notice of the cancellation` IS
    `s 708(4) the person commits an offence` `default was made in complying with section 708` `s 658(2) an officer of the company` (JUST `I am an officer of the company who is in default`)

@export Under section 708(5), what is the most I can be fined if convicted of the offence of failing to give notice of the cancellation of purchased shares?
GIVEN `where I am convicted` IS A `Mode of conviction` @desc Where would you be convicted? One of: on summary conviction; on summary conviction in England and Wales; on summary conviction in Scotland; on summary conviction in Northern Ireland; on conviction on indictment (the Act states no penalty on indictment for this offence)
GIVETH A MAYBE Penalty
DECIDE `Under section 708(5), what is the most I can be fined if convicted of the offence of failing to give notice of the cancellation of purchased shares` IS
    `s 708(5) the penalty on conviction` `where I am convicted`

§§ `Chapter 5: redemption or purchase by a private company out of capital (ss 709 to 723)`

@export Under section 709(1), may my private limited company make a payment out of capital for redeeming or purchasing its own shares?
GIVEN `the company is a private limited company` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is your company a private limited company?
      `the payment is in accordance with Chapter 5` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the payment made in accordance with Chapter 5 (the statements, resolution, notices and inspection it requires)?
      `the articles restrict or prohibit the payment` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Do the company's articles restrict or prohibit such a payment?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 709(1), may my private limited company make a payment out of capital for redeeming or purchasing its own shares` IS
    `s 709(1) the private limited company may make the payment out of capital` `the company is a private limited company` (JUST `the payment is in accordance with Chapter 5`) `the articles restrict or prohibit the payment`

@export Under section 710, how much is the permissible capital payment for the shares?
GIVEN `the price of the redemption or purchase in pounds` IS A NUMBER @desc What is the price of the redemption or purchase, in pounds?
      `the available profits in pounds` IS A NUMBER @desc What are the company's available profits for this purpose (section 712), in pounds?
      `the proceeds of a fresh issue in pounds` IS A NUMBER @desc What are the proceeds of any fresh issue of shares made for the purposes of the redemption or purchase, in pounds (0 if none)?
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `Under section 710, how much is the permissible capital payment for the shares` IS
    `s 710(1) the permissible capital payment` `the price of the redemption or purchase in pounds` `the available profits in pounds` `the proceeds of a fresh issue in pounds`

@export Under section 712, what are my company's available profits for a payment out of capital?
GIVEN `the profits determined from the relevant accounts in pounds` IS A NUMBER @desc What are the company's profits determined by reference to the items stated in the relevant accounts (profits, losses, assets and liabilities, provisions, share capital and reserves), in pounds?
      `the date of the relevant accounts` IS A DATE @desc As at what date are the relevant accounts prepared?
      `the date of the statement` IS A DATE @desc On what date is the directors' statement (section 714) or the solvency statement (section 720A) made?
      `a distribution lawfully made in pounds` IS A NUMBER @desc What distribution did the company lawfully make after the date of the accounts and before the end of the period, in pounds (0 if none)?
      `the date of that distribution` IS A DATE @desc On what date was that distribution made?
      `financial assistance lawfully given out of distributable profits in pounds` IS A NUMBER @desc What financial assistance did the company lawfully give out of distributable profits (Chapter 2) after the date of the accounts and before the end of the period, in pounds (0 if none)?
      `the date of that assistance` IS A DATE @desc On what date was that assistance given?
GIVETH A MAYBE NUMBER
DECIDE `Under section 712, what are my company's available profits for a payment out of capital` IS
    `s 711(2) the available profits of the company for the purposes of Chapter 5` `the profits determined from the relevant accounts in pounds` `the date of the relevant accounts` `the date of the statement`
        (LIST `the distribution` , `the assistance`)
    WHERE
        `the distribution` MEANS `s 712(3) payment` WITH
            `s 712(3) kind of payment` IS `s 712(3)(a) a distribution lawfully made by the company`
            `s 712(3) amount of the payment` IS `a distribution lawfully made in pounds`
            `s 712(3) date of the payment` IS `the date of that distribution`
            `s 712(3) the payment was lawfully made by the company out of distributable profits` IS TRUE
        `the assistance` MEANS `s 712(3) payment` WITH
            `s 712(3) kind of payment` IS `s 712(4)(a) financial assistance lawfully given out of distributable profits in accordance with Chapter 2`
            `s 712(3) amount of the payment` IS `financial assistance lawfully given out of distributable profits in pounds`
            `s 712(3) date of the payment` IS `the date of that assistance`
            `s 712(3) the payment was lawfully made by the company out of distributable profits` IS TRUE

@export Under section 713, is my private company's payment out of capital not lawful because a requirement was not met?
GIVEN `the company is a private company` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is your company a private company?
      `the directors' statement and auditor's report requirements of section 714 are met` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are the requirements of section 714 (directors' statement and auditor's report) met?
      `the special resolution requirements of section 716 are met` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are the requirements of section 716 (approval by special resolution) met?
      `the public notice requirements of section 719 are met` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are the requirements of section 719 (public notice of the proposed payment) met?
      `the inspection requirements of section 720 are met` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are the requirements of section 720 (statement and report available for inspection) met?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 713, is my private company's payment out of capital not lawful because a requirement was not met` IS
    `s 713(1) the payment out of capital is not lawful` `the company is a private company`
        (JUST `the directors' statement and auditor's report requirements of section 714 are met`) (JUST `the special resolution requirements of section 716 are met`)
        (JUST `the public notice requirements of section 719 are met`) (JUST `the inspection requirements of section 720 are met`)

@export Under section 714, does the directors' statement and auditor's report contain everything the section requires?
GIVEN `the amount the statement specifies in pounds` IS A NUMBER @desc What amount does the statement specify as the permissible capital payment, in pounds?
      `the permissible capital payment worked out under section 710 in pounds` IS A NUMBER @desc What is the permissible capital payment worked out under section 710, in pounds?
      `it says the directors made full inquiry and formed an opinion` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does it state that, having made full inquiry into the company's affairs and prospects, the directors have formed the opinion mentioned in section 714(3)?
      `the opinion covers the initial situation` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does the opinion say that, immediately after the date of the proposed payment, there will be no grounds on which the company could be found unable to pay its debts?
      `the opinion covers the prospects for the year` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does the opinion say that, having regard to the directors' intentions and the financial resources available, the company will be able to carry on business as a going concern throughout the following year?
      `all liabilities including contingent and prospective ones were taken into account` IS A BOOLEAN @desc In forming the opinion about the initial situation, did the directors take into account all the company's liabilities, including contingent or prospective ones?
      `it is in the prescribed form` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the statement in the prescribed form?
      `it contains the prescribed information about the company's business` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does it contain the prescribed information about the nature of the company's business?
      `an auditor's report is annexed` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is a report addressed to the directors by the company's auditor annexed to it?
      `the report says the auditor inquired into the company's affairs` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does the report state that the auditor has inquired into the company's state of affairs?
      `the report says the amount is properly determined` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does the report state that the amount specified is in the auditor's view properly determined under sections 710 to 712?
      `the report says he is not aware the opinion is unreasonable` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does the report state that the auditor is not aware of anything to indicate the directors' opinion is unreasonable in all the circumstances?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 714, does the directors' statement and auditor's report contain everything the section requires` IS
    `s 714 the statement and report contain everything section 714 requires` `the statement` `the permissible capital payment worked out under section 710 in pounds`
    WHERE
        `the statement` MEANS `s 714(1) directors' statement` WITH
            `s 714(1) the amount of the permissible capital payment the statement specifies` IS `the amount the statement specifies in pounds`
            `s 714(3) the statement says the directors made full inquiry into the affairs and prospects of the company and formed the opinion` IS `it says the directors made full inquiry and formed an opinion`
            `s 714(3)(a) the statement says the opinion is that, as regards its initial situation immediately following the date on which the payment out of capital is proposed to be made, there will be no grounds on which the company could then be found unable to pay its debts` IS `the opinion covers the initial situation`
            `s 714(3)(b) the statement says the opinion is that, as regards its prospects for the year immediately following that date, the company will be able to continue to carry on business as a going concern throughout that year` IS `the opinion covers the prospects for the year`
            `s 714(4) in forming their opinion under subsection (3)(a) the directors took into account all of the company's liabilities (including any contingent or prospective liabilities)` IS `all liabilities including contingent and prospective ones were taken into account`
            `s 714(5) the statement is in the prescribed form` IS `it is in the prescribed form`
            `s 714(5) the statement contains the prescribed information with respect to the nature of the company's business` IS `it contains the prescribed information about the company's business`
            `s 714(6) a report addressed to the directors by the company's auditor is annexed to the statement` IS `an auditor's report is annexed`
            `s 714(6)(a) the report states that the auditor has inquired into the company's state of affairs` IS `the report says the auditor inquired into the company's affairs`
            `s 714(6)(b) the report states that the amount specified as the permissible capital payment is in his view properly determined in accordance with sections 710 to 712` IS `the report says the amount is properly determined`
            `s 714(6)(c) the report states that he is not aware of anything to indicate that the opinion expressed by the directors as to any of the matters mentioned in subsection (3) is unreasonable in all the circumstances` IS `the report says he is not aware the opinion is unreasonable`

@export Under section 715, am I, a director, guilty of an offence because the statement was made without reasonable grounds for the opinion?
GIVEN `the directors made a statement under section 714 without reasonable grounds for the opinion` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did the directors make a statement under section 714 without having reasonable grounds for the opinion expressed in it?
      `I am a director who is in default` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are you a director who is in default (section 1121)?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 715, am I, a director, guilty of an offence because the statement was made without reasonable grounds for the opinion` IS
    `s 715(1) the person commits an offence` `the directors made a statement under section 714 without reasonable grounds for the opinion` `s 658(2) a director of the company` (JUST `I am a director who is in default`)

@export Under section 715(2), what is the most I can be sentenced to if convicted of that offence?
GIVEN `where I am convicted` IS A `Mode of conviction` @desc Where would you be convicted? One of: on conviction on indictment; on summary conviction in England and Wales; on summary conviction in Scotland; on summary conviction in Northern Ireland
GIVETH A MAYBE Penalty
DECIDE `Under section 715(2), what is the most I can be sentenced to if convicted of that offence` IS
    `s 715(2) the penalty on conviction` `where I am convicted`

@export Under section 716, by what date must my private company pass the special resolution approving the payment out of capital?
GIVEN `the date the directors make the statement` IS A DATE @desc On what date do the directors make the statement required by section 714?
GIVETH A DATE
DECIDE `Under section 716, by what date must my private company pass the special resolution approving the payment out of capital` IS
    `s 716(2) the last day for passing the resolution` `the date the directors make the statement`

@export Under section 716(1), is the payment out of capital approved as the section requires?
GIVEN `a resolution of the company approved the payment` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did a resolution of the company approve the payment?
      `it was passed as a special resolution` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Was it passed as a special resolution?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 716(1), is the payment out of capital approved as the section requires` IS
    `s 716(1) the payment is approved as the subsection requires` `a resolution of the company approved the payment` (JUST `it was passed as a special resolution`)

@export Under section 717, is the resolution approving the payment not effective because of how members holding the shares voted?
GIVEN `the resolution is proposed at a meeting` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the resolution proposed at a meeting (answer no for a written resolution)?
      `a member holding shares to which the resolution relates voted on it` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did a member holding shares to which the resolution relates vote on it (on a poll or otherwise)?
      `it would not have passed without that vote` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Would the resolution not have been passed if he had not voted?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 717, is the resolution approving the payment not effective because of how members holding the shares voted` IS
    `s 717(3) the resolution is not effective` `the resolution is proposed at a meeting` `a member holding shares to which the resolution relates voted on it` `it would not have passed without that vote`

@export Under section 718, is the resolution ineffective because the directors' statement and auditor's report were not made available to members?
GIVEN `the requirement of section 718(2) is complied with` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Was a copy of the directors' statement and auditor's report made available to members as section 718(2) requires (sent to every eligible member with a written resolution, or available for inspection at the meeting)?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 718, is the resolution ineffective because the directors' statement and auditor's report were not made available to members` IS
    `s 718(3) the resolution is ineffective` `the requirement of section 718(2) is complied with`

@export Under section 719, by what date must my company publish the notice of the proposed payment in the Gazette?
GIVEN `the date of the resolution` IS A DATE @desc On what date was the special resolution passed?
GIVETH A DATE
DECIDE `Under section 719, by what date must my company publish the notice of the proposed payment in the Gazette` IS
    `s 719(1) the last day for publishing the notice in the Gazette` `the date of the resolution`

@export Under section 719(4), by what day must my company deliver a copy of the directors' statement and auditor's report to the registrar?
GIVEN `the day the company first publishes the Gazette notice` IS A DATE @desc On what day does the company first publish the Gazette notice (section 719(1))?
      `the day the company first publishes or gives the second notice` IS A DATE @desc On what day does the company first publish the newspaper notice or give written notice to creditors (section 719(2))?
GIVETH A DATE
DECIDE `Under section 719(4), by what day must my company deliver a copy of the directors' statement and auditor's report to the registrar` IS
    `s 719(4) the last day for delivering the copy to the registrar` `the day the company first publishes the Gazette notice` `the day the company first publishes or gives the second notice`

@export Under section 720(1), from what day must the directors' statement and auditor's report be kept available for inspection?
GIVEN `the day the company first publishes the Gazette notice` IS A DATE @desc On what day does the company first publish the Gazette notice (section 719(1))?
      `the day the company first publishes or gives the second notice` IS A DATE @desc On what day does the company first publish the newspaper notice or give written notice to creditors (section 719(2))?
GIVETH A DATE
DECIDE `Under section 720(1), from what day must the directors' statement and auditor's report be kept available for inspection` IS
    `s 720(1) the first day of the period` `the day the company first publishes the Gazette notice` `the day the company first publishes or gives the second notice`

@export Under section 720(1), until what day must the directors' statement and auditor's report be kept available for inspection?
GIVEN `the date of the resolution` IS A DATE @desc On what date was the special resolution passed?
GIVETH A DATE
DECIDE `Under section 720(1), until what day must the directors' statement and auditor's report be kept available for inspection` IS
    `s 720(1) the last day of the period` `the date of the resolution`

@export Under section 720(4), may I inspect the directors' statement and auditor's report without charge?
GIVEN `I am a member of the company` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are you a member of the company?
      `I am a creditor of the company` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are you a creditor of the company?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 720(4), may I inspect the directors' statement and auditor's report without charge` IS
    `s 720(4) the person may inspect the statement and report without charge`
        (IF `I am a member of the company` THEN `s 720(4) a member of the company` ELSE IF `I am a creditor of the company` THEN `s 720(4) a creditor of the company` ELSE `s 720(4) any other person`)

@export Under section 720(5), am I guilty of an offence because my company did not comply with section 720 or refused inspection?
GIVEN `the days of default in giving notice of the place under section 720(3)` IS A NUMBER @desc For how many days has the company made default in giving the registrar notice of the place (section 720(3))?
      `an inspection under section 720(4) was refused` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Was an inspection under section 720(4) refused?
      `I am an officer of the company who is in default` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are you an officer of the company who is in default (section 1121)?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 720(5), am I guilty of an offence because my company did not comply with section 720 or refused inspection` IS
    CONSIDER `s 720(5) the company is in default as the subsection describes` `the days of default in giving notice of the place under section 720(3)` `an inspection under section 720(4) was refused`
    WHEN JUST TRUE THEN `s 720(5) the person commits an offence` TRUE `s 658(2) an officer of the company` (JUST `I am an officer of the company who is in default`)
    WHEN JUST FALSE THEN `s 720(5) the person commits an offence` FALSE `s 658(2) an officer of the company` (JUST `I am an officer of the company who is in default`)
    WHEN NOTHING THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (points outside the text): whether the company is in default is not known

@export Under section 720(6), what is the most I can be fined if convicted of the offence of failing to keep the statement and report available or refusing inspection?
GIVEN `where I am convicted` IS A `Mode of conviction` @desc Where would you be convicted? One of: on summary conviction; on summary conviction in England and Wales; on summary conviction in Scotland; on summary conviction in Northern Ireland; on conviction on indictment (the Act states no penalty on indictment for this offence)
GIVETH A MAYBE Penalty
DECIDE `Under section 720(6), what is the most I can be fined if convicted of the offence of failing to keep the statement and report available or refusing inspection` IS
    `s 720(6) the penalty on conviction` `where I am convicted`

@export Under section 720A, does section 713(1) not apply to my private company's purchase out of capital for an employees' share scheme?
GIVEN `the company is a private company` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is your company a private company?
      `the purchase is for an employees' share scheme` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the purchase for the purposes of or pursuant to an employees' share scheme?
      `it is approved by special resolution` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it approved by special resolution?
      `the directors made a solvency statement` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did the directors make a solvency statement (section 643)?
      `the date of the solvency statement` IS A DATE @desc On what date did the directors make the solvency statement?
      `the date the resolution is passed` IS A DATE @desc On what date is the resolution passed?
      `the resolution and statement are registered in accordance with section 720B` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are the resolution and solvency statement registered in accordance with section 720B?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 720A, does section 713(1) not apply to my private company's purchase out of capital for an employees' share scheme` IS
    `s 720A(1) section 713(1) does not apply` `the company is a private company` (JUST `the purchase is for an employees' share scheme`) (JUST `it is approved by special resolution`)
        (`s 720A(2) the resolution is supported by a solvency statement` (JUST `the directors made a solvency statement`) `the date of the solvency statement` `the date the resolution is passed` `the resolution and statement are registered in accordance with section 720B`)

@export Under section 720B(1), by what date must my company deliver the solvency statement, the resolution and a statement of capital to the registrar?
GIVEN `the date the resolution was passed` IS A DATE @desc On what date was the resolution passed?
GIVETH A DATE
DECIDE `Under section 720B(1), by what date must my company deliver the solvency statement, the resolution and a statement of capital to the registrar` IS
    `s 720B(1) the last day for delivering the documents to the registrar` `the date the resolution was passed`

@export Under section 720B(4), is the resolution still unable to take effect?
GIVEN `the documents delivered under section 720B(1) have been registered` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has the registrar registered the documents delivered under section 720B(1)?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 720B(4), is the resolution still unable to take effect` IS
    `s 720B(4) the resolution cannot yet take effect` `the documents delivered under section 720B(1) have been registered`

@export Under section 720B(7), am I guilty of an offence because my company delivered a solvency statement that was not provided to members?
GIVEN `the company delivered a solvency statement not provided to members in accordance with section 720A(3) or (4)` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did the company deliver to the registrar a solvency statement that was not provided to members in accordance with section 720A(3) or (4)?
      `I am an officer of the company who is in default` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are you an officer of the company who is in default (section 1121)?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 720B(7), am I guilty of an offence because my company delivered a solvency statement that was not provided to members` IS
    `s 720B(7) the person commits an offence` `the company delivered a solvency statement not provided to members in accordance with section 720A(3) or (4)` `s 658(2) an officer of the company` (JUST `I am an officer of the company who is in default`)

@export Under section 720B(8), am I guilty of an offence because my company did not comply with section 720B?
GIVEN `default was made in complying with section 720B` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did your company make default in complying with section 720B (delivering the documents, or the directors' confirmation, in time)?
      `I am an officer of the company who is in default` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are you an officer of the company who is in default (section 1121)?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 720B(8), am I guilty of an offence because my company did not comply with section 720B` IS
    `s 720B(8) the person commits an offence` `default was made in complying with section 720B` `s 658(2) an officer of the company` (JUST `I am an officer of the company who is in default`)

@export Under section 720B(9), what is the most I can be fined if convicted of an offence under section 720B?
GIVEN `where I am convicted` IS A `Mode of conviction` @desc Where would you be convicted? One of: on conviction on indictment; on summary conviction; on summary conviction in England and Wales; on summary conviction in Scotland; on summary conviction in Northern Ireland
GIVETH A MAYBE Penalty
DECIDE `Under section 720B(9), what is the most I can be fined if convicted of an offence under section 720B` IS
    `s 720B(9) the penalty on conviction` `where I am convicted`

@export Under section 721(1), may I apply to the court to cancel the resolution approving the payment out of capital?
GIVEN `the company is a private company` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the company a private company?
      `the resolution is a special resolution approving a payment out of capital` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the resolution a special resolution approving a payment out of capital for the redemption or purchase of its shares?
      `I am a member of the company` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are you a member of the company?
      `I consented to or voted in favour of the resolution` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did you consent to, or vote in favour of, the resolution?
      `I am a creditor of the company` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are you a creditor of the company?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 721(1), may I apply to the court to cancel the resolution approving the payment out of capital` IS
    `s 721(1) the person may apply to the court for the cancellation of the resolution` `the company is a private company` (JUST TRUE) `the resolution is a special resolution approving a payment out of capital`
        (IF `I am a member of the company` THEN `s 721(1)(a) a member of the company` `I consented to or voted in favour of the resolution`
         ELSE IF `I am a creditor of the company` THEN `s 721(1)(b) a creditor of the company` ELSE `s 721(1) any other person`)

@export Under section 721(2), by what date must I apply to the court to cancel the resolution?
GIVEN `the date the resolution was passed` IS A DATE @desc On what date was the resolution passed?
GIVETH A DATE
DECIDE `Under section 721(2), by what date must I apply to the court to cancel the resolution` IS
    `s 721(2)(a) the last day for applying to the court` `the date the resolution was passed`

@export Under section 722(3), by what date must my company deliver a copy of the court's order to the registrar?
GIVEN `the date the court made the order` IS A DATE @desc On what date did the court make its order?
      `the longer period the court directed in days, if it did` IS A MAYBE NUMBER @desc If the court directed a longer period than 15 days, how many days (leave out if it did not)?
GIVETH A DATE
DECIDE `Under section 722(3), by what date must my company deliver a copy of the court's order to the registrar` IS
    `s 722(3) the last day for delivering a copy of the order to the registrar` `the date the court made the order` `the longer period the court directed in days, if it did`

@export Under section 722(4), am I guilty of an offence because my company did not give the registrar notice of the court application or deliver a copy of the order?
GIVEN `the company failed to comply with section 722(2) or (3)` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did your company fail to comply with section 722(2) (immediate notice of the application) or (3) (a copy of the order in time)?
      `I am an officer of the company who is in default` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are you an officer of the company who is in default (section 1121)?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 722(4), am I guilty of an offence because my company did not give the registrar notice of the court application or deliver a copy of the order` IS
    `s 722(4) the person commits an offence` `the company failed to comply with section 722(2) or (3)` `s 658(2) an officer of the company` (JUST `I am an officer of the company who is in default`)

@export Under section 722(5), what is the most I can be fined if convicted of the offence of failing to give notice of the court application or to deliver the order?
GIVEN `where I am convicted` IS A `Mode of conviction` @desc Where would you be convicted? One of: on summary conviction; on summary conviction in England and Wales; on summary conviction in Scotland; on summary conviction in Northern Ireland; on conviction on indictment (the Act states no penalty on indictment for this offence)
GIVETH A MAYBE Penalty
DECIDE `Under section 722(5), what is the most I can be fined if convicted of the offence of failing to give notice of the court application or to deliver the order` IS
    `s 722(5) the penalty on conviction` `where I am convicted`

@export Under section 723, was my company's payment out of capital made within the window the section allows?
GIVEN `the date the resolution was passed` IS A DATE @desc On what date was the special resolution passed?
      `the date the payment out of capital was made` IS A DATE @desc On what date was the payment made?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 723, was my company's payment out of capital made within the window the section allows` IS
    `s 723(1) the payment out of capital was made in the window` `the date the resolution was passed` `the date the payment out of capital was made`

§§ `Chapter 6: treasury shares (ss 724 to 732)`

@export Under section 724(3), may my limited company hold, or deal with, the shares it purchased as treasury shares?
GIVEN `my limited company made a purchase of its own shares in accordance with Chapter 4` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did your limited company purchase its own shares in accordance with Chapter 4?
      `the purchase was made out of distributable profits` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Was the purchase made out of distributable profits?
      `what the company proposes to do with the shares` IS A `s 724(3) what the company does with the shares` @desc What does the company propose to do with the shares? One of: hold them; deal with them in accordance with section 727 or 729 (sell, transfer for an employees' share scheme, or cancel); deal with them in another way
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 724(3), may my limited company hold, or deal with, the shares it purchased as treasury shares` IS
    `s 724(3) the company may do it with the shares`
        (`s 724(1) this section applies` `my limited company made a purchase of its own shares in accordance with Chapter 4` `the purchase was made out of distributable profits`)
        `what the company proposes to do with the shares`

@export Under section 724(4), must my company be entered in its register of members as the member holding the shares?
GIVEN `the shares are held by the company` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are the shares held by the company?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 724(4), must my company be entered in its register of members as the member holding the shares` IS
    `s 724(4) the company must be entered in its register of members as the member holding the shares` `the shares are held by the company`

@export Under section 724(5), does my company hold these shares as treasury shares?
GIVEN `they were purchased by the company in circumstances in which section 724 applies` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Were they (or are they treated as having been) purchased by the company in circumstances in which section 724 applies (a purchase in accordance with Chapter 4 out of distributable profits)?
      `they have been held by the company continuously since` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Have they been held by the company continuously since they were so purchased (or treated as purchased)?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 724(5), does my company hold these shares as treasury shares` IS
    `s 724(5) the company holds the shares as treasury shares` `they were purchased by the company in circumstances in which section 724 applies` `they have been held by the company continuously since`

@export Under section 726(2), may my company exercise a right in respect of the treasury shares it holds?
GIVEN `the shares are held by the company as treasury shares` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are the shares held by the company as treasury shares?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 726(2), may my company exercise a right in respect of the treasury shares it holds` IS
    `s 726(2) the company may exercise a right in respect of the treasury shares` (`s 726(1) this section applies` `the shares are held by the company as treasury shares`)

@export Under section 726(2), is a purported exercise of a right in respect of treasury shares void?
GIVEN `the shares are held by the company as treasury shares` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are the shares held by the company as treasury shares?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 726(2), is a purported exercise of a right in respect of treasury shares void` IS
    `s 726(2) the purported exercise of the right is void` (`s 726(1) this section applies` `the shares are held by the company as treasury shares`)

@export Under section 726(3), may my company be paid a dividend or other distribution in respect of its treasury shares?
GIVEN `the shares are held by the company as treasury shares` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are the shares held by the company as treasury shares?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 726(3), may my company be paid a dividend or other distribution in respect of its treasury shares` IS
    `s 726(3) a dividend or other distribution may be paid or made to the company in respect of the treasury shares` (`s 726(1) this section applies` `the shares are held by the company as treasury shares`)

@export Under section 726(4), does section 726 prevent my company from doing this in respect of its treasury shares?
GIVEN `the shares are held by the company as treasury shares` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are the shares held by the company as treasury shares?
      `what is done` IS A `s 726(4) transaction` @desc What is done? One of: an allotment of shares as fully paid bonus shares in respect of the treasury shares; the payment of an amount payable on the redemption of the treasury shares; any other transaction
      `the treasury shares are redeemable shares` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are the treasury shares redeemable shares?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 726(4), does section 726 prevent my company from doing this in respect of its treasury shares` IS
    `s 726(4) section 726 prevents the transaction` (`s 726(1) this section applies` `the shares are held by the company as treasury shares`) `what is done` `the treasury shares are redeemable shares`

@export Under section 726(5), are the bonus shares allotted in respect of treasury shares treated as purchased by my company?
GIVEN `the shares are allotted as fully paid bonus shares in respect of treasury shares` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are the shares allotted as fully paid bonus shares in respect of the company's treasury shares?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 726(5), are the bonus shares allotted in respect of treasury shares treated as purchased by my company` IS
    `s 726(5) the shares are treated as purchased by the company, at the time they were allotted, in circumstances in which section 724(1) applied` `the shares are allotted as fully paid bonus shares in respect of treasury shares`

@export Under section 727(1), may my company dispose of its treasury shares in this way?
GIVEN `the shares are held as treasury shares` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are the shares held as treasury shares?
      `the disposal` IS A `s 727(1) disposal` @desc What is the disposal? One of: a sale of the shares for a cash consideration; a transfer of the shares for the purposes of or pursuant to an employees' share scheme; any other disposal
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 727(1), may my company dispose of its treasury shares in this way` IS
    `s 727(1) the company may dispose of the shares in that way` `the shares are held as treasury shares` `the disposal`

@export Under section 727(2), is what my company receives for the treasury shares a cash consideration?
GIVEN `it is cash received by the company` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the consideration cash received by the company?
      `it is a cheque` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it a cheque received by the company?
      `the cheque was received in good faith and the directors have no reason to suspect it will not be paid` IS A BOOLEAN @desc If it is a cheque: was it received in good faith, and have the directors no reason for suspecting that it will not be paid?
      `it is a release of a liability of the company for a liquidated sum` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it a release of a liability of the company for a liquidated sum?
      `it is an undertaking to pay cash` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it an undertaking to pay cash to the company?
      `the days after the agreement to sell by which the cash is to be paid` IS A NUMBER @desc If it is an undertaking to pay cash: within how many days after the date the company agrees to sell the shares is the cash to be paid?
      `it is payment by other means giving rise to an entitlement to a payment, or credit equivalent to payment, in cash` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it payment by any other means giving rise to a present or future entitlement (of the company or another company) to a payment, or credit equivalent to payment, in cash?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 727(2), is what my company receives for the treasury shares a cash consideration` IS
    `s 727(2) the consideration is a cash consideration` `the kind of consideration`
    WHERE
        `the kind of consideration` MEANS
            IF `it is cash received by the company`
            THEN `s 727(2)(a) cash received by the company`
            ELSE IF `it is a cheque`
                 THEN `s 727(2)(b) a cheque received by the company` `the cheque was received in good faith and the directors have no reason to suspect it will not be paid`
                 ELSE IF `it is a release of a liability of the company for a liquidated sum`
                      THEN `s 727(2)(c) a release of a liability of the company for a liquidated sum`
                      ELSE IF `it is an undertaking to pay cash`
                           THEN `s 727(2)(d) an undertaking to pay cash to the company` `the days after the agreement to sell by which the cash is to be paid`
                           ELSE IF `it is payment by other means giving rise to an entitlement to a payment, or credit equivalent to payment, in cash`
                                THEN `s 727(2)(e) payment by any other means giving rise to a present or future entitlement to a payment, or credit equivalent to payment, in cash`
                                ELSE `s 727(2) any other consideration`

@export Under section 727(2), is foreign currency cash for this purpose?
GIVEN `the money is foreign currency` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the money foreign currency?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 727(2), is foreign currency cash for this purpose` IS
    `s 727(2) the money is cash` `the money is foreign currency`

@export Under section 727(4), is my company barred from selling or transferring treasury shares to someone other than the person who gave a section 979 notice?
GIVEN `the company has received a notice under section 979 for the shares` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has the company received a notice under section 979 that a person desires to acquire the shares it holds as treasury shares?
      `the sale or transfer is to the person who gave the notice` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the sale or transfer to the person who gave the notice?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 727(4), is my company barred from selling or transferring treasury shares to someone other than the person who gave a section 979 notice` IS
    `s 727(4) the sale or transfer is barred` `the company has received a notice under section 979 for the shares` `the sale or transfer is to the person who gave the notice`

@export Under section 728(1), by what date must my company deliver the return of treasury shares it sold or transferred for an employees' share scheme?
GIVEN `the date the shares were disposed of` IS A DATE @desc On what date were the shares sold or transferred?
GIVETH A DATE
DECIDE `Under section 728(1), by what date must my company deliver the return of treasury shares it sold or transferred for an employees' share scheme` IS
    `s 728(1) the last day for delivering the return to the registrar` `the date the shares were disposed of`

@export Under section 728(4), am I guilty of an offence because my company did not deliver the return of shares disposed of?
GIVEN `default was made in complying with section 728` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did your company make default in complying with section 728 (the return of shares sold or transferred)?
      `I am an officer of the company who is in default` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are you an officer of the company who is in default (section 1121)?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 728(4), am I guilty of an offence because my company did not deliver the return of shares disposed of` IS
    `s 728(4) the person commits an offence` `default was made in complying with section 728` `s 658(2) an officer of the company` (JUST `I am an officer of the company who is in default`)

@export Under section 728(5), what is the most I can be fined if convicted of that offence?
GIVEN `where I am convicted` IS A `Mode of conviction` @desc Where would you be convicted? One of: on conviction on indictment; on summary conviction; on summary conviction in England and Wales; on summary conviction in Scotland; on summary conviction in Northern Ireland
      `the amended wording of the daily fine is in force` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN @desc Is the wording that substitutes one-tenth of the greater of 5,000 pounds and the level 4 amount for one-tenth of the statutory maximum in force? (leave out if you do not know)
GIVETH A MAYBE `s 707(7) penalty`
DECIDE `Under section 728(5), what is the most I can be fined if convicted of that offence` IS
    `s 728(5) the penalty on conviction` `where I am convicted` `the amended wording of the daily fine is in force`

@export Under section 729(1), may my company cancel the shares it holds as treasury shares?
GIVEN `the shares are held as treasury shares` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are the shares held as treasury shares?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 729(1), may my company cancel the shares it holds as treasury shares` IS
    `s 729(1) the company may cancel the shares` `the shares are held as treasury shares`

@export Under section 729(4), what is my company's share capital after it cancels treasury shares?
GIVEN `the company cancels shares held as treasury shares` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the company cancelling shares held as treasury shares?
      `the share capital before the cancellation in pounds` IS A NUMBER @desc What is the company's share capital before the cancellation, in pounds?
      `the nominal amount of the shares cancelled in pounds` IS A NUMBER @desc What is the nominal amount of the shares cancelled, in pounds?
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `Under section 729(4), what is my company's share capital after it cancels treasury shares` IS
    `s 729(4) the amount of the company's share capital after the cancellation` `the company cancels shares held as treasury shares` `the share capital before the cancellation in pounds` `the nominal amount of the shares cancelled in pounds`

@export Under section 729(5), may the directors take the steps needed to cancel the shares without complying with Chapter 10 of Part 17?
GIVEN `the company cancels shares under section 729` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the company cancelling shares under section 729?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 729(5), may the directors take the steps needed to cancel the shares without complying with Chapter 10 of Part 17` IS
    `s 729(5) the directors may take the steps without complying with Chapter 10 of Part 17` `the company cancels shares under section 729`

@export Under section 730(1), by what date must my company deliver the return of treasury shares it cancelled?
GIVEN `the date the shares were cancelled` IS A DATE @desc On what date were the shares cancelled?
GIVETH A DATE
DECIDE `Under section 730(1), by what date must my company deliver the return of treasury shares it cancelled` IS
    `s 730(1) the last day for delivering the return to the registrar` `the date the shares were cancelled`

@export Under section 730(5), does my company's statement of capital with the notice of cancellation state everything the section requires?
GIVEN `it states the total number of shares of the company` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does the statement state the total number of shares of the company?
      `it states the aggregate nominal value of those shares` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does it state their aggregate nominal value?
      `it states the aggregate amount unpaid on those shares` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does it state the aggregate amount (if any) unpaid on those shares?
      `for every class it states prescribed particulars of the rights attached to the shares` IS A BOOLEAN @desc For every class of shares, does it state the prescribed particulars of the rights attached to the shares?
      `for every class it states the total number of shares of that class` IS A BOOLEAN @desc For every class, does it state the total number of shares of that class?
      `for every class it states the aggregate nominal value of the shares of that class` IS A BOOLEAN @desc For every class, does it state the aggregate nominal value of the shares of that class?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 730(5), does my company's statement of capital with the notice of cancellation state everything the section requires` IS
    `s 730(5) the statement of capital states what the section requires` `the statement`
    WHERE
        `the statement` MEANS `s 663(3) statement of capital` WITH
            `s 663(3) states the total number of shares of the company` IS `it states the total number of shares of the company`
            `s 663(3) states the aggregate nominal value of those shares` IS `it states the aggregate nominal value of those shares`
            `s 663(3) states the aggregate amount unpaid on those shares` IS `it states the aggregate amount unpaid on those shares`
            `s 663(3) entries for the classes of shares` IS LIST (`s 663(3) class entry` WITH
                `s 663(3) states prescribed particulars of the rights attached to the shares of the class` IS `for every class it states prescribed particulars of the rights attached to the shares`
                `s 663(3) states the total number of shares of the class` IS `for every class it states the total number of shares of that class`
                `s 663(3) states the aggregate nominal value of the shares of the class` IS `for every class it states the aggregate nominal value of the shares of that class`)

@export Under section 730(6), am I guilty of an offence because my company did not deliver the return of shares cancelled?
GIVEN `default was made in complying with section 730` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did your company make default in complying with section 730 (the return of treasury shares cancelled, with a statement of capital)?
      `I am an officer of the company who is in default` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are you an officer of the company who is in default (section 1121)?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 730(6), am I guilty of an offence because my company did not deliver the return of shares cancelled` IS
    `s 730(6) the person commits an offence` `default was made in complying with section 730` `s 658(2) an officer of the company` (JUST `I am an officer of the company who is in default`)

@export Under section 730(7), what is the most I can be fined if convicted of that offence?
GIVEN `where I am convicted` IS A `Mode of conviction` @desc Where would you be convicted? One of: on conviction on indictment; on summary conviction; on summary conviction in England and Wales; on summary conviction in Scotland; on summary conviction in Northern Ireland
GIVETH A MAYBE Penalty
DECIDE `Under section 730(7), what is the most I can be fined if convicted of that offence` IS
    `s 730(7) the penalty on conviction` `where I am convicted`

@export Under section 731(2), what part of the proceeds of selling treasury shares is treated as my company's realised profit if they are no more than the purchase price?
GIVEN `the proceeds of sale in pounds` IS A NUMBER @desc What are the proceeds of the sale, in pounds?
      `the purchase price the company paid for the shares in pounds` IS A NUMBER @desc What purchase price did the company pay for the shares, in pounds?
GIVETH A MAYBE NUMBER
DECIDE `Under section 731(2), what part of the proceeds of selling treasury shares is treated as my company's realised profit if they are no more than the purchase price` IS
    `s 731(2) the amount treated as a realised profit of the company for the purposes of Part 23` `the proceeds of sale in pounds` `the purchase price the company paid for the shares in pounds`

@export Under section 731(3), how much of the proceeds above the purchase price goes to the share premium account?
GIVEN `the proceeds of sale in pounds` IS A NUMBER @desc What are the proceeds of the sale, in pounds?
      `the purchase price the company paid for the shares in pounds` IS A NUMBER @desc What purchase price did the company pay for the shares, in pounds?
GIVETH A MAYBE NUMBER
DECIDE `Under section 731(3), how much of the proceeds above the purchase price goes to the share premium account` IS
    `s 731(3)(b) the amount to be transferred to the company's share premium account` `the proceeds of sale in pounds` `the purchase price the company paid for the shares in pounds`

@export Under section 731(4), what purchase price is taken as paid for the shares sold, by the weighted average price method?
GIVEN `the total purchase price paid for all the treasury shares of the class held in pounds` IS A NUMBER @desc What total purchase price did the company pay for all the treasury shares of that class that it holds, in pounds?
      `the number of treasury shares of the class held` IS A NUMBER @desc How many treasury shares of that class does the company hold?
      `the number of shares sold` IS A NUMBER @desc How many of them are sold?
GIVETH A MAYBE NUMBER
DECIDE `Under section 731(4), what purchase price is taken as paid for the shares sold, by the weighted average price method` IS
    `s 731(4)(a) the purchase price paid by the company for the shares sold` `the total purchase price paid for all the treasury shares of the class held in pounds` `the number of treasury shares of the class held` `the number of shares sold`

@export Under section 732, am I guilty of an offence because my company contravened Chapter 6?
GIVEN `my company contravened a provision of Chapter 6 other than section 730` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did your company contravene a provision of Chapter 6 other than section 730?
      `I am an officer of the company who is in default` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are you an officer of the company who is in default (section 1121)?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 732, am I guilty of an offence because my company contravened Chapter 6` IS
    `s 732(1) the person commits an offence` `my company contravened a provision of Chapter 6 other than section 730` `s 658(2) an officer of the company` (JUST `I am an officer of the company who is in default`)

@export Under section 732(2), what is the most I can be fined if convicted of that offence?
GIVEN `where I am convicted` IS A `Mode of conviction` @desc Where would you be convicted? One of: on conviction on indictment; on summary conviction; on summary conviction in England and Wales; on summary conviction in Scotland; on summary conviction in Northern Ireland
GIVETH A MAYBE Penalty
DECIDE `Under section 732(2), what is the most I can be fined if convicted of that offence` IS
    `s 732(2) the penalty on conviction` `where I am convicted`

§§ `Chapter 7: supplementary provisions (ss 733 to 737)`

@export Under section 733(2), how much must my company transfer to the capital redemption reserve after redeeming or purchasing shares wholly out of profits?
GIVEN `shares were redeemed or purchased under Part 18 wholly out of the company's profits` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Were the company's shares redeemed or purchased under Part 18 wholly out of the company's profits?
      `the amount by which the issued share capital is diminished in pounds` IS A NUMBER @desc By how much is the company's issued share capital diminished by the redemption or purchase, in pounds?
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `Under section 733(2), how much must my company transfer to the capital redemption reserve after redeeming or purchasing shares wholly out of profits` IS
    `s 733(2) the amount to be transferred to the capital redemption reserve` `shares were redeemed or purchased under Part 18 wholly out of the company's profits` `the amount by which the issued share capital is diminished in pounds`

@export Under section 733(3), how much must my company transfer to the capital redemption reserve when the proceeds of a fresh issue are less than the nominal value of the shares redeemed or purchased?
GIVEN `the shares are redeemed or purchased wholly or partly out of the proceeds of a fresh issue` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are the shares redeemed or purchased wholly or partly out of the proceeds of a fresh issue of shares?
      `the aggregate amount of the proceeds in pounds` IS A NUMBER @desc What is the aggregate amount of the proceeds of the fresh issue, in pounds?
      `the aggregate nominal value of the shares redeemed or purchased in pounds` IS A NUMBER @desc What is the aggregate nominal value of the shares redeemed or purchased, in pounds?
      `the company is a private company` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the company a private company?
      `a payment out of capital is also applied` IS A BOOLEAN @desc In addition to the proceeds of the fresh issue, does the company apply a payment out of capital under Chapter 5 or section 692(1ZA) in making the redemption or purchase?
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `Under section 733(3), how much must my company transfer to the capital redemption reserve when the proceeds of a fresh issue are less than the nominal value of the shares redeemed or purchased` IS
    `s 733(3) the amount of the difference to be transferred to the capital redemption reserve` `the shares are redeemed or purchased wholly or partly out of the proceeds of a fresh issue` `the aggregate amount of the proceeds in pounds` `the aggregate nominal value of the shares redeemed or purchased in pounds` `the company is a private company` `a payment out of capital is also applied`

@export Under section 733(4), how much must my company transfer to the capital redemption reserve when it cancels treasury shares?
GIVEN `shares held as treasury shares are cancelled` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are shares held as treasury shares cancelled?
      `the amount by which the share capital is diminished in pounds` IS A NUMBER @desc By how much is the company's share capital diminished by the cancellation (section 729(4)), in pounds?
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `Under section 733(4), how much must my company transfer to the capital redemption reserve when it cancels treasury shares` IS
    `s 733(4) the amount to be transferred to the capital redemption reserve` `shares held as treasury shares are cancelled` `the amount by which the share capital is diminished in pounds`

@export Under section 733(5), may my company use the capital redemption reserve to pay up bonus shares?
GIVEN `the new shares are to be allotted to members as fully paid bonus shares` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are the new shares to be allotted to members as fully paid bonus shares?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 733(5), may my company use the capital redemption reserve to pay up bonus shares` IS
    `s 733(5) the company may use the capital redemption reserve to pay up the new shares` `the new shares are to be allotted to members as fully paid bonus shares`

@export Under section 733(6), how much share capital is counted for a reduction of capital once the capital redemption reserve is added?
GIVEN `the provision relates to the reduction of a company's share capital` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the provision one of the Companies Acts relating to the reduction of a company's share capital?
      `the paid up share capital in pounds` IS A NUMBER @desc What is the company's paid up share capital, in pounds?
      `the capital redemption reserve in pounds` IS A NUMBER @desc What is the capital redemption reserve, in pounds?
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `Under section 733(6), how much share capital is counted for a reduction of capital once the capital redemption reserve is added` IS
    `s 733(6) the paid up share capital to take for the provision` `the provision relates to the reduction of a company's share capital` `the paid up share capital in pounds` `the capital redemption reserve in pounds`

@export Under section 734, does the accounting section apply because my company made a payment out of capital?
GIVEN `a payment out of capital is made in accordance with Chapter 5` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is a payment out of capital made in accordance with Chapter 5?
      `a payment out of capital is made in accordance with section 692(1ZA)` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is a payment out of capital made in accordance with section 692(1ZA)?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 734, does the accounting section apply because my company made a payment out of capital` IS
    `s 734(1) this section applies` `a payment out of capital is made in accordance with Chapter 5` `a payment out of capital is made in accordance with section 692(1ZA)`

@export Under section 734(1A), what is the permissible capital payment for a payment under section 692(1ZA)?
GIVEN `the purchase price of the shares in pounds` IS A NUMBER @desc What is the purchase price of the shares, in pounds?
      `the payment under section 692(1ZA) in pounds` IS A NUMBER @desc What payment is made out of capital under section 692(1ZA), in pounds?
      `the proceeds of a fresh issue used in pounds` IS A NUMBER @desc What proceeds of a fresh issue are used to make the purchase, in pounds (0 if none)?
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `Under section 734(1A), what is the permissible capital payment for a payment under section 692(1ZA)` IS
    `s 734(1A) the permissible capital payment for a payment under section 692(1ZA)` `the purchase price of the shares in pounds` `the payment under section 692(1ZA) in pounds` `the proceeds of a fresh issue used in pounds`

@export Under section 734(2), how much must my company transfer to the capital redemption reserve because the permissible capital payment is less than the nominal amount?
GIVEN `the permissible capital payment in pounds` IS A NUMBER @desc What is the permissible capital payment (with any fresh-issue proceeds added, section 734(4)), in pounds?
      `the nominal amount of the shares redeemed or purchased in pounds` IS A NUMBER @desc What is the nominal amount of the shares redeemed or purchased, in pounds?
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `Under section 734(2), how much must my company transfer to the capital redemption reserve because the permissible capital payment is less than the nominal amount` IS
    `s 734(2) the amount to be transferred to the capital redemption reserve` `the permissible capital payment in pounds` `the nominal amount of the shares redeemed or purchased in pounds`

@export Under section 734(3), by how much at most may my company reduce its reserves and share capital because the permissible capital payment exceeds the nominal amount?
GIVEN `the permissible capital payment in pounds` IS A NUMBER @desc What is the permissible capital payment (with any fresh-issue proceeds added, section 734(4)), in pounds?
      `the nominal amount of the shares redeemed or purchased in pounds` IS A NUMBER @desc What is the nominal amount of the shares redeemed or purchased, in pounds?
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `Under section 734(3), by how much at most may my company reduce its reserves and share capital because the permissible capital payment exceeds the nominal amount` IS
    `s 734(3) the most by which the amounts may be reduced` `the permissible capital payment in pounds` `the nominal amount of the shares redeemed or purchased in pounds`

@export Under section 734(4), what amount is read as the permissible capital payment when a fresh issue is applied as well?
GIVEN `the proceeds of a fresh issue are applied in addition to a payment out of capital under Chapter 5` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are the proceeds of a fresh issue applied in addition to a payment out of capital under Chapter 5?
      `the permissible capital payment in pounds` IS A NUMBER @desc What is the permissible capital payment, in pounds?
      `the proceeds of the fresh issue in pounds` IS A NUMBER @desc What are the proceeds of the fresh issue, in pounds?
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `Under section 734(4), what amount is read as the permissible capital payment when a fresh issue is applied as well` IS
    `s 734(4) the amount to read as the permissible capital payment in subsections (2) and (3)` `the proceeds of a fresh issue are applied in addition to a payment out of capital under Chapter 5` `the permissible capital payment in pounds` `the proceeds of the fresh issue in pounds`

@export Under section 735(2), is my company liable in damages for failing to redeem or purchase its shares?
GIVEN `the company issued shares on terms that they are or are liable to be redeemed` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did the company issue shares on terms that they are or are liable to be redeemed?
      `the company agreed to purchase any of its shares` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did the company agree to purchase any of its shares?
      `the company has failed to redeem or purchase the shares` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has the company failed to redeem or purchase the shares?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 735(2), is my company liable in damages for failing to redeem or purchase its shares` IS
    `s 735(2) the company is liable in damages for the failure`
        (`s 735(1) this section applies` `the company issued shares on terms that they are or are liable to be redeemed` `the company agreed to purchase any of its shares`)
        `the company has failed to redeem or purchase the shares`

@export Under section 735(2), does the holder of the shares keep this right despite the company's failure to redeem or purchase?
GIVEN `the right` IS A `s 735(2) right of the holder` @desc What is the right? One of: a right to sue the company for damages in respect of its failure to redeem or purchase; any other right of the holder of the shares
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 735(2), does the holder of the shares keep this right despite the company's failure to redeem or purchase` IS
    `s 735(2) the holder's right survives the failure` `the right`

@export Under section 735(3), must the court refuse an order for specific performance of the company's terms of redemption or purchase?
GIVEN `the company shows that it is unable to meet the costs out of distributable profits` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does the company show that it is unable to meet the costs of redeeming or purchasing the shares in question out of distributable profits?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 735(3), must the court refuse an order for specific performance of the company's terms of redemption or purchase` IS
    `s 735(3) the court shall not grant specific performance` `the company shows that it is unable to meet the costs out of distributable profits`

@export Under section 735(4), may I enforce the terms of redemption or purchase against my company in its winding up?
GIVEN `the company is wound up` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the company wound up?
      `at the commencement of the winding up some of the shares have not been redeemed or purchased` IS A BOOLEAN @desc At the commencement of the winding up, had any of the shares not been redeemed or purchased?
      `the date the terms provided for the redemption or purchase` IS A DATE @desc On what date did the terms provide for the redemption or purchase to take place?
      `the date of the commencement of the winding up` IS A DATE @desc On what date did the winding up commence?
      `the company could not at any time have lawfully made a distribution equal to the price` IS A BOOLEAN @desc During the period from the date the redemption or purchase was to take place to the commencement of the winding up, could the company at no time lawfully have made a distribution equal in value to the price?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 735(4), may I enforce the terms of redemption or purchase against my company in its winding up` IS
    `s 735(4) the terms of redemption or purchase may be enforced against the company` `the company is wound up` `at the commencement of the winding up some of the shares have not been redeemed or purchased`
        (`s 735(5) subsection (4) does not apply` `the date the terms provided for the redemption or purchase` `the date of the commencement of the winding up` `the company could not at any time have lawfully made a distribution equal to the price`)

@export Under section 735(6), is this claim paid in priority to what my company must pay under section 735(4)?
GIVEN `the claim` IS A `s 735(6) other claim` @desc What is the claim? One of: a debt or liability of the company other than one due to members in their character as such; an amount due in satisfaction of rights as to capital or income preferred to the rights as to capital attaching to the shares; an amount due to members in satisfaction of their rights as members, other than preferred rights; a claim of another kind
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 735(6), is this claim paid in priority to what my company must pay under section 735(4)` IS
    `s 735(6) the claim is paid in priority to any amount the company is liable under subsection (4) to pay` `the claim`

@export Under section 736, are my company's profits distributable profits in relation to this payment?
GIVEN `the payment is one in Chapter 2 of Part 18 (financial assistance)` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the payment one made under Chapter 2 of Part 18 (financial assistance)? (For that Chapter section 683 gives the meaning.)
      `the profits available for distribution in pounds` IS A NUMBER @desc What are the profits available for distribution (section 830), in pounds?
      `the value of the payment in pounds` IS A NUMBER @desc What is the value of the payment, in pounds?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 736, are my company's profits distributable profits in relation to this payment` IS
    `s 736 the profits are distributable profits in relation to the payment` `the payment is one in Chapter 2 of Part 18 (financial assistance)` `the profits available for distribution in pounds` `the value of the payment in pounds`

-- ====================================================================================================
-- seat questions from part coa16 (merged by the lead on 2026-11-12; unchanged text follows)
-- ====================================================================================================
-- coa16-seat.l4: the Companies Act 2006, Parts 19 and 20 (ss 738 to 767), asked from the seat of an individual who is,
-- or is about to become, a director, a company secretary or a member (shareholder) of a company registered under the
-- Act, or who deals with one (a debenture holder, a creditor, a person offered the company's securities).
-- (Assumed, not ruled: the Act is addressed to companies, so the individual is whoever stands in a company's
-- management or ownership.)  There is never a seat for an official: the registrar and the court appear only as what
-- they mean for the person.
--
-- LAYER 2.  Every question takes plain inputs, one for each fact the person can state, each with an @desc worded as
-- that person would be asked, and calls the layer-1 rules of coa16-part19-general.l4, coa16-part19-register.l4,
-- coa16-part19-supplementary.l4, coa16-part20-public-offers.l4 and coa16-part20-minimum-capital.l4.  It restates no
-- rule.  A record field that the rule called never reads gets a fixed placeholder, with a comment saying so.
-- Every question's name begins "Under section N," with the Act's own numbering, and asks the question its body
-- answers, in the same direction as the layer-1 function it calls (NOTES.md lists each pair).
--
-- READING AN ANSWER.  A question answers JUST TRUE ("yes, the Act says so"), JUST FALSE ("no, the Act says no in its
-- own words") or NOTHING ("not covered": the Act does not decide the case, or points outside the sources).  Never read
-- NOTHING as no.  Questions about money answer a number of pounds, or NOTHING where the Act states no ceiling.
--
-- FIGURES.  The pounds that a level on the standard scale or the statutory maximum stands for, the prescribed euro
-- equivalent of the authorised minimum, and the fee for inspecting the register are not in the Act: inputs.  The
-- Act's own £50,000 (s 763(1)(a)) is used as it stands; an order under section 764 that substitutes another sterling
-- amount would change the answers of the questions that use it (the seat takes "no such order": NOTHING).

-- ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
-- Helpers (not exported): build layer-1 records from the plain inputs
-- ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------

-- Whose liability a question is about.
DECLARE `coa16 seat who is asked about` IS ONE OF
    `coa16 seat the company`
    `coa16 seat me, as an officer of the company`
    `coa16 seat me, in some other capacity`

GIVEN place IS A `Place of registration`
      liability IS A `Liability of members`
      capital IS A BOOLEAN
      certificate IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A `Company profile`
`coa16 seat the company profile` MEANS `Company profile` OF place, liability, capital, certificate

-- s 4(2)(b): the requirements for registration or re-registration as a public company complied with on or after the
-- relevant date, which is s 4(3) for the place of registration.
GIVEN place IS A `Place of registration`
      complied IS A DATE
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`coa16 seat the requirements were complied with on or after the relevant date` MEANS
    complied AT LEAST `s 4(3) the relevant date` place

GIVEN yes IS A BOOLEAN
      day IS A DATE
GIVETH A MAYBE DATE
`coa16 seat a date, if there is one` MEANS
    IF yes THEN JUST day ELSE NOTHING

GIVEN a IS A BOOLEAN, b IS A BOOLEAN, c IS A BOOLEAN, d IS A BOOLEAN, e IS A BOOLEAN, f IS A BOOLEAN, g IS A BOOLEAN, h IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A `s 756(5) facts about the person`
`coa16 seat the offeree` MEANS
    `s 756(5) facts about the person` OF (JUST a), b, (`s 756(6) relationship to another person` OF c, d, e), f, g, h

-- The offer, from the sixteen plain facts about it and the person it is made to (s 756(2) to (5)).
GIVEN publicOffer IS A BOOLEAN
      notCalculated IS A BOOLEAN
      privateConcern IS A BOOLEAN
      member IS A BOOLEAN
      employee IS A BOOLEAN
      spouse IS A BOOLEAN
      child IS A BOOLEAN
      descendant IS A BOOLEAN
      widow IS A BOOLEAN
      holder IS A BOOLEAN
      trustee IS A BOOLEAN
      renounce IS A BOOLEAN
      onlyConnected IS A BOOLEAN
      scheme IS A BOOLEAN
      onlyScheme IS A BOOLEAN
      contrary IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A `s 756 offer`
`coa16 seat the offer` MEANS
    `s 756 offer` OF
        publicOffer
        notCalculated
        privateConcern
        (`s 756(5) the person is already connected with the company` (`coa16 seat the offeree` member employee spouse child descendant widow holder trustee))
        renounce
        onlyConnected
        (JUST scheme)
        renounce
        onlyScheme
        contrary

-- The allotted shares, from the aggregate figures: shares not allotted under a scheme count as they stand; scheme
-- shares of each currency are taken as one group (NOTES.md, finding on the seat's grouping).
GIVEN sterling IS A NUMBER
      euros IS A NUMBER
      other IS A NUMBER
      sNominal IS A NUMBER
      sPaid IS A NUMBER
      sPremium IS A NUMBER
      sPremiumPaid IS A NUMBER
      eNominal IS A NUMBER
      ePaid IS A NUMBER
      ePremium IS A NUMBER
      ePremiumPaid IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A LIST OF `s 761(3) allotted share`
`coa16 seat the allotted shares` MEANS
    LIST
        (`s 761(3) allotted share` OF `s 765 sterling`, sterling, FALSE, 0, 0, 0)
        (`s 761(3) allotted share` OF `s 765 euros`, euros, FALSE, 0, 0, 0)
        (`s 761(3) allotted share` OF `s 765 another currency`, other, FALSE, 0, 0, 0)
        (`s 761(3) allotted share` OF `s 765 sterling`, sNominal, TRUE, sPaid, sPremium, sPremiumPaid)
        (`s 761(3) allotted share` OF `s 765 euros`, eNominal, TRUE, ePaid, ePremium, ePremiumPaid)

-- ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
§ `Debentures: what a debenture is, and registering an allotment (ss 738 to 742)`
-- Situation: you hold, are offered or are issuing the company's debentures.  Ask "Has this happened to you?" before
-- showing the questions about registration, the offence and the fine.
-- ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------

-- Layer-1: `s 738 the instrument is a debenture`.  Direction: JUST TRUE is "yes, it is a debenture".
@export Under section 738, is this instrument a debenture for the purposes of the Companies Acts?
GIVEN `the kind of instrument` IS A `s 738 kind of instrument` @desc What kind of instrument is it? One of: s 738 debenture stock; s 738 a bond; s 738 another security of a company; s 738 a share in a company; s 738 something that is not a security of a company.
      `the question arises in a provision of the Companies Acts` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the word "debenture" being used in a provision of the Companies Acts (as opposed to some other law or a contract's own definition)?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 738, is this instrument a debenture for the purposes of the Companies Acts` IS
    -- Placeholder FALSE: "whether or not constituting a charge on the assets of the company", so the rule does not read that fact.
    `s 738 the instrument is a debenture` `the kind of instrument` FALSE (JUST `the question arises in a provision of the Companies Acts`)

-- Layer-1: `s 739(1) the condition is invalid by reason only of ...`.  Direction: JUST FALSE is "no, not invalid for that reason alone".
@export Under section 739(1), is a condition in my debentures, or in the deed securing them, invalid only because the debentures are irredeemable or redeemable only on a contingency or after a period?
GIVEN `the condition is in the debentures or in a deed securing them` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the condition contained in the debentures, or in a deed for securing the debentures?
      `the debentures are irredeemable` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are the debentures made irredeemable?
      `the debentures are redeemable only on a contingency` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are the debentures made redeemable only on the happening of a contingency, however remote?
      `the debentures are redeemable only after a period` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are the debentures made redeemable only on the expiration of a period, however long?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 739(1), is a condition in my debentures, or in the deed securing them, invalid only because the debentures are irredeemable or redeemable only on a contingency or after a period` IS
    `s 739(1) the condition is invalid by reason only of how the debentures are made redeemable` `the condition is in the debentures or in a deed securing them` `the debentures are irredeemable` `the debentures are redeemable only on a contingency` `the debentures are redeemable only after a period`

-- Layer-1: `s 740 the contract may be enforced by an order for specific performance`.  Direction: JUST TRUE is "yes, it may be".
@export Under section 740, may a contract to take up and pay for a company's debentures be enforced by an order for specific performance?
GIVEN `the contract is with a company` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the contract made with a company?
      `the contract is to take up and pay for debentures of that company` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it a contract to take up and pay for debentures of that company?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 740, may a contract to take up and pay for a company's debentures be enforced by an order for specific performance` IS
    `s 740 the contract may be enforced by an order for specific performance` `the contract is with a company` `the contract is to take up and pay for debentures of that company`

-- Layer-1: `s 741(1) the last day for registering the allotment`.
@export Under section 741(1), by what date must the company register an allotment of debentures?
GIVEN `allotment date` IS A DATE @desc On what date were the debentures allotted (ISO 8601, for example 2024-03-15)?
GIVETH A DATE
DECIDE `Under section 741(1), by what date must the company register an allotment of debentures` IS
    `s 741(1) the last day for registering the allotment` `allotment date`

-- Layer-1: `s 741(1) the company has registered the allotment as the section requires`.  Direction: JUST TRUE is "yes, it has".
@export Under section 741(1), has the company registered the allotment of debentures as the section requires?
GIVEN `allotment date` IS A DATE @desc On what date were the debentures allotted (ISO 8601, for example 2024-03-15)?
      `allotment has been registered` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has the allotment been registered?
      `date registered` IS A DATE @desc On what date was it registered (ISO 8601)? Give any date if it has not been registered.
      `registered as soon as practicable` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Was (or will) the allotment be registered as soon as practicable?
      `date now` IS A DATE @desc What is today's date (ISO 8601)?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 741(1), has the company registered the allotment of debentures as the section requires` IS
    `s 741(1) the company has registered the allotment as the section requires` `allotment date` (`coa16 seat a date, if there is one` `allotment has been registered` `date registered`) `registered as soon as practicable` `date now`

-- Layer-1: `s 741(2) the person commits an offence`.  Direction: JUST TRUE is "yes, the offence is committed".
@export Under section 741(2), has the company, or have I as an officer of the company, committed an offence by not registering an allotment of debentures in time?
GIVEN `allotment date` IS A DATE @desc On what date were the debentures allotted (ISO 8601, for example 2024-03-15)?
      `allotment has been registered` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has the allotment been registered?
      `date registered` IS A DATE @desc On what date was it registered (ISO 8601)? Give any date if it has not been registered.
      `registered as soon as practicable` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Was (or will) the allotment be registered as soon as practicable?
      `date now` IS A DATE @desc What is today's date (ISO 8601)?
      `who is asked about` IS A `coa16 seat who is asked about` @desc Whose liability is this about? One of: coa16 seat the company; coa16 seat me, as an officer of the company; coa16 seat me, in some other capacity.
      `officer in default` IS A BOOLEAN @desc If you are asking as an officer: are you an officer in default of the company for this contravention (section 1121)? Answer false if you are not an officer.
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 741(2), has the company, or have I as an officer of the company, committed an offence by not registering an allotment of debentures in time` IS
    `s 741(2) the person commits an offence` `allotment date` (`coa16 seat a date, if there is one` `allotment has been registered` `date registered`) `registered as soon as practicable` `date now` person
    WHERE
        person MEANS
            CONSIDER `who is asked about`
            WHEN `coa16 seat the company` THEN `s 741(2) the company`
            WHEN `coa16 seat me, as an officer of the company` THEN `s 741(2) an officer of the company` (JUST `officer in default`)
            WHEN `coa16 seat me, in some other capacity` THEN `s 741(2) another person`

-- Layer-1: `s 741(3) the penalty for the offence` and `s 741(3) the most that a fine limit allows, in pounds`.
@export Under section 741(3), what is the most the court can fine, in pounds, on a conviction for not registering an allotment of debentures in time?
GIVEN `pounds that level 3 on the standard scale stands for` IS A NUMBER @desc How many pounds does level 3 on the standard scale stand for (the figure is set outside the Companies Act)?
GIVETH A MAYBE NUMBER
DECIDE `Under section 741(3), what is the most the court can fine, in pounds, on a conviction for not registering an allotment of debentures in time` IS
    CONSIDER (`s 741(3) the penalty for the offence`)'s `fine not exceeding`
    WHEN JUST limit THEN `s 741(3) the most that a fine limit allows, in pounds` limit `pounds that level 3 on the standard scale stands for` 0 -- placeholder 0: the statutory maximum is not read by a level fine
    WHEN NOTHING THEN NOTHING

-- Layer-1: `s 741(3) the penalty for the offence` (its daily default fine) and `s 741(3) the most that a fine limit allows, in pounds`.
@export Under section 741(3), what is the most the court can fine, in pounds for each day, as the daily default fine for continued contravention?
GIVEN `pounds that level 3 on the standard scale stands for` IS A NUMBER @desc How many pounds does level 3 on the standard scale stand for (the figure is set outside the Companies Act)?
GIVETH A MAYBE NUMBER
DECIDE `Under section 741(3), what is the most the court can fine, in pounds for each day, as the daily default fine for continued contravention` IS
    CONSIDER (`s 741(3) the penalty for the offence`)'s `daily default fine for continued contravention`
    WHEN JUST limit THEN `s 741(3) the most that a fine limit allows, in pounds` limit `pounds that level 3 on the standard scale stands for` 0 -- placeholder 0: the statutory maximum is not read by a level fine
    WHEN NOTHING THEN NOTHING

-- Layer-1: `s 742 the debentures are valid and binding according to their terms`.  Direction: JUST TRUE is "yes, valid and binding".
@export Under section 742, are debentures to bearer issued in Scotland valid and binding according to their terms?
GIVEN `the debentures are debentures to bearer` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are they debentures to bearer?
      `the debentures were issued in Scotland` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Were they issued in Scotland?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 742, are debentures to bearer issued in Scotland valid and binding according to their terms` IS
    `s 742 the debentures are valid and binding according to their terms` `the debentures are debentures to bearer` `the debentures were issued in Scotland`

-- ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
§ `The register of debenture holders (ss 743 to 748)`
-- Situation: the company keeps a register of debenture holders, or you want to see it.  Ask "Does your company keep a
-- register of debenture holders?" before showing the group.
-- ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------

-- Layer-1: `s 743(1) the register is kept available for inspection as the subsection requires`.  JUST TRUE is "yes, as required".
@export Under section 743(1), is the company keeping its register of debenture holders available for inspection where the subsection requires?
GIVEN `the document` IS A `s 743(6) kind of document` @desc What is the document? One of: a register of debenture holders; a duplicate of a register of debenture holders that is kept outside the United Kingdom; a duplicate of part of such a register; something else.
      `the register is kept by the company` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the register kept by the company?
      `kept at the registered office` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it kept available for inspection at the company's registered office?
      `kept at a place specified in regulations` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it kept available for inspection at a place specified in regulations under section 1136?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 743(1), is the company keeping its register of debenture holders available for inspection where the subsection requires` IS
    `s 743(1) the register is kept available for inspection as the subsection requires` `the document` `the register is kept by the company` `kept at the registered office` (JUST `kept at a place specified in regulations`)

-- Layer-1: `s 743(3) the company is excused from giving the notice`.  JUST TRUE is "yes, excused".
@export Under section 743(3), is the company excused from giving the registrar notice of where its register of debenture holders is kept?
GIVEN `always kept at the registered office` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has the register, at all times since it came into existence, been kept available for inspection at the company's registered office?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 743(3), is the company excused from giving the registrar notice of where its register of debenture holders is kept` IS
    `s 743(3) the company is excused from giving the notice` `always kept at the registered office`

-- Layer-1: `s 743(2) the company has given the notice to the registrar as the subsection requires`.  JUST TRUE is "yes, it has".
@export Under section 743(2), has the company done what the subsection requires about notifying the registrar of where its register of debenture holders is kept and of any change in that place?
GIVEN `the document` IS A `s 743(6) kind of document` @desc What is the document? One of: a register of debenture holders; a duplicate of a register of debenture holders that is kept outside the United Kingdom; a duplicate of part of such a register; something else.
      `always kept at the registered office` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has the register, at all times since it came into existence, been kept available for inspection at the company's registered office?
      `notice of the place has been given` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has notice of the place where the register is kept available for inspection been given to the registrar?
      `the place has changed` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has the place where the register is kept available for inspection changed?
      `notice of the change has been given` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has notice of that change been given to the registrar?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 743(2), has the company done what the subsection requires about notifying the registrar of where its register of debenture holders is kept and of any change in that place` IS
    `s 743(2) the company has given the notice to the registrar as the subsection requires` `the document` `always kept at the registered office` `notice of the place has been given` `the place has changed` `notice of the change has been given`

-- Layer-1: `s 743(4) the person commits an offence`.  JUST TRUE is "yes, the offence is committed".
@export Under section 743(4), has the company, or have I as an officer of the company, committed an offence by making default for 14 days in giving the registrar the notice that section 743(2) requires?
GIVEN `the document` IS A `s 743(6) kind of document` @desc What is the document? One of: a register of debenture holders; a duplicate of a register of debenture holders that is kept outside the United Kingdom; a duplicate of part of such a register; something else.
      `always kept at the registered office` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has the register, at all times since it came into existence, been kept available for inspection at the company's registered office?
      `notice of the place has been given` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has notice of the place where the register is kept available for inspection been given to the registrar?
      `the place has changed` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has the place where the register is kept available for inspection changed?
      `notice of the change has been given` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has notice of that change been given to the registrar?
      `days in default` IS A NUMBER @desc For how many days has the company been in default of its duty to give that notice?
      `who is asked about` IS A `coa16 seat who is asked about` @desc Whose liability is this about? One of: coa16 seat the company; coa16 seat me, as an officer of the company; coa16 seat me, in some other capacity.
      `officer in default` IS A BOOLEAN @desc If you are asking as an officer: are you an officer in default of the company for this contravention (section 1121)? Answer false if you are not an officer.
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 743(4), has the company, or have I as an officer of the company, committed an offence by making default for 14 days in giving the registrar the notice that section 743(2) requires` IS
    `s 743(4) the person commits an offence` `the document` `always kept at the registered office` `notice of the place has been given` `the place has changed` `notice of the change has been given` `days in default` person
    WHERE
        person MEANS
            CONSIDER `who is asked about`
            WHEN `coa16 seat the company` THEN `s 743(4) the company`
            WHEN `coa16 seat me, as an officer of the company` THEN `s 743(4) an officer of the company` (JUST `officer in default`)
            WHEN `coa16 seat me, in some other capacity` THEN `s 743(4) another person`

-- Layer-1: `s 743(5) the penalty for the offence`.
@export Under section 743(5), what is the most the court can fine, in pounds, on a conviction for failing to notify the registrar of where the register is kept?
GIVEN `pounds that level 3 on the standard scale stands for` IS A NUMBER @desc How many pounds does level 3 on the standard scale stand for (the figure is set outside the Companies Act)?
GIVETH A MAYBE NUMBER
DECIDE `Under section 743(5), what is the most the court can fine, in pounds, on a conviction for failing to notify the registrar of where the register is kept` IS
    CONSIDER (`s 743(5) the penalty for the offence`)'s `fine not exceeding`
    WHEN JUST limit THEN `s 741(3) the most that a fine limit allows, in pounds` limit `pounds that level 3 on the standard scale stands for` 0 -- placeholder 0: the statutory maximum is not read by a level fine
    WHEN NOTHING THEN NOTHING

-- Layer-1: `s 744(5) the register is duly closed`.  JUST TRUE is "yes, duly closed".
@export Under section 744(5), is the register of debenture holders duly closed?
GIVEN `register is closed` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the register of debenture holders closed?
      `closed under articles or debentures` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it closed in accordance with a provision contained in the company's articles or in the debentures?
      `closed under stock certificates` IS A BOOLEAN @desc For debenture stock, is it closed in accordance with a provision contained in the stock certificates?
      `closed under trust deed or other document` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it closed in accordance with a provision contained in the trust deed or other document securing the debentures or debenture stock?
      `days closed in the year` IS A NUMBER @desc For how many days in total is the register closed in the year?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 744(5), is the register of debenture holders duly closed` IS
    `s 744(5) the register is duly closed` (`s 744(5) closure of the register` OF `register is closed`, `closed under articles or debentures`, `closed under stock certificates`, `closed under trust deed or other document`, `days closed in the year`)

-- Layer-1: `s 744(1) the terms on which the person may inspect the register`.  The answer names the terms (or that the register is closed).
@export Under section 744(1), on what terms may I inspect the company's register of debenture holders?
GIVEN `the document` IS A `s 744(6) kind of document` @desc What is the document? One of: a register of debenture holders; a duplicate of a register of debenture holders that is kept outside the United Kingdom; a duplicate of part of such a register; something else.
      `register is closed` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the register of debenture holders closed?
      `closed under articles or debentures` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it closed in accordance with a provision contained in the company's articles or in the debentures?
      `closed under stock certificates` IS A BOOLEAN @desc For debenture stock, is it closed in accordance with a provision contained in the stock certificates?
      `closed under trust deed or other document` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it closed in accordance with a provision contained in the trust deed or other document securing the debentures or debenture stock?
      `days closed in the year` IS A NUMBER @desc For how many days in total is the register closed in the year?
      `I am the registered holder of debentures of the company` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are you the registered holder of any of the company's debentures?
      `I am a holder of shares in the company` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Do you hold shares in the company?
GIVETH A MAYBE `s 744(1) terms of inspection`
DECIDE `Under section 744(1), on what terms may I inspect the company's register of debenture holders` IS
    `s 744(1) the terms on which the person may inspect the register` `the document` (`s 744(5) closure of the register` OF `register is closed`, `closed under articles or debentures`, `closed under stock certificates`, `closed under trust deed or other document`, `days closed in the year`) `I am the registered holder of debentures of the company` `I am a holder of shares in the company`

-- Layer-1: `s 744(2) the person may require a copy of the register or any part of it`.  JUST TRUE is "yes, I may"; JUST FALSE is "no, not without paying the fee" (the text: "on payment of such fee as may be prescribed").
@export Under section 744(2), may I require a copy of the register of debenture holders, or any part of it?
GIVEN `the document` IS A `s 744(6) kind of document` @desc What is the document? One of: a register of debenture holders; a duplicate of a register of debenture holders that is kept outside the United Kingdom; a duplicate of part of such a register; something else.
      `I pay the prescribed fee` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Do you pay the fee that may be prescribed for a copy?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 744(2), may I require a copy of the register of debenture holders, or any part of it` IS
    `s 744(2) the person may require a copy of the register or any part of it` `the document` `I pay the prescribed fee`

-- Layer-1: `s 744(4) the request contains the information the subsection requires`.  JUST TRUE is "yes, it does".
@export Under section 744(4), does my request for the register contain the information the subsection requires?
GIVEN `requester is an individual` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are you making the request as an individual (rather than for an organisation)?
      `request gives requester's name and address` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does your request give your name and address?
      `request gives responsible individual for organisation` IS A BOOLEAN @desc For an organisation, does the request give the name and address of an individual responsible for making it on the organisation's behalf?
      `request states purpose` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does the request state the purpose for which the information is to be used?
      `request says whether disclosed` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does the request say whether the information will be disclosed to any other person?
      `information will be disclosed` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Will the information be disclosed to another person?
      `other person is an individual` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is that other person an individual (rather than an organisation)?
      `request gives other individual's name and address` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does the request give that other individual's name and address?
      `request gives responsible individual for other organisation` IS A BOOLEAN @desc If that other person is an organisation, does the request give the name and address of an individual responsible for receiving the information on its behalf?
      `request states other person's purpose` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does the request state the purpose for which that other person will use the information?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 744(4), does my request for the register contain the information the subsection requires` IS
    `s 744(4) the request contains the information the subsection requires` (`s 744(4) request for the register` OF `requester is an individual`, `request gives requester's name and address`, `request gives responsible individual for organisation`, `request states purpose`, `request says whether disclosed`, `information will be disclosed`, `other person is an individual`, `request gives other individual's name and address`, `request gives responsible individual for other organisation`, `request states other person's purpose`)

-- Layer-1: `s 745(1) the company has responded to the request in time`.  JUST TRUE is "yes, in time".
@export Under section 745(1), has the company responded to my request for the register in time?
GIVEN `the company has received my request` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has the company received your request under section 744?
      `the company has complied` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has the company complied with the request?
      `the company has applied to the court` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has the company applied to the court?
      `working days taken` IS A NUMBER @desc How many working days (not counting weekends or bank holidays) passed between the company receiving the request and the day it complied or applied to the court, or between receiving it and today if it has done neither?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 745(1), has the company responded to my request for the register in time` IS
    `s 745(1) the company has responded to the request in time` `the company has received my request` `the company has complied` `the company has applied to the court` `working days taken`

-- Layer-1: `s 745(3)(a) the court shall direct the company not to comply with the request`.  JUST TRUE is "yes, it must".
@export Under section 745(3), must the court direct the company not to comply with my request?
GIVEN `the court is satisfied that the inspection or copy is not sought for a proper purpose` IS A BOOLEAN @desc On the company's application, is the court satisfied that the inspection or copy is not sought for a proper purpose?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 745(3), must the court direct the company not to comply with my request` IS
    `s 745(3)(a) the court shall direct the company not to comply with the request` `the court is satisfied that the inspection or copy is not sought for a proper purpose`

-- Layer-1: `s 745(5) the company must comply with the request immediately`.  JUST TRUE is "yes, it must".
@export Under section 745(5), must the company comply with my request immediately?
GIVEN `the company applied to the court` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has the company made an application to the court under section 745?
      `the court has directed the company not to comply` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has the court directed the company not to comply with the request?
      `the court has decided or the proceedings have been discontinued` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has the court given its decision, or have the proceedings been discontinued?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 745(5), must the company comply with my request immediately` IS
    `s 745(5) the company must comply with the request immediately` `the company applied to the court` `the court has directed the company not to comply` `the court has decided or the proceedings have been discontinued`

-- Layer-1: `s 746(1) the person commits an offence`.  JUST TRUE is "yes, the offence is committed".
@export Under section 746(1), has the company, or have I as an officer of the company, committed an offence by refusing inspection of the register or failing to provide a copy?
GIVEN `inspection was refused` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Was an inspection of the register that section 744 requires refused?
      `default was made in providing a copy` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Was default made in providing a copy of the register that section 744 requires?
      `in accordance with an order of the court` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Was the refusal or default in accordance with an order of the court?
      `who is asked about` IS A `coa16 seat who is asked about` @desc Whose liability is this about? One of: coa16 seat the company; coa16 seat me, as an officer of the company; coa16 seat me, in some other capacity.
      `officer in default` IS A BOOLEAN @desc If you are asking as an officer: are you an officer in default of the company for this contravention (section 1121)? Answer false if you are not an officer.
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 746(1), has the company, or have I as an officer of the company, committed an offence by refusing inspection of the register or failing to provide a copy` IS
    `s 746(1) the person commits an offence` `inspection was refused` `default was made in providing a copy` `in accordance with an order of the court` person
    WHERE
        person MEANS
            CONSIDER `who is asked about`
            WHEN `coa16 seat the company` THEN `s 746(1) the company`
            WHEN `coa16 seat me, as an officer of the company` THEN `s 746(1) an officer of the company` (JUST `officer in default`)
            WHEN `coa16 seat me, in some other capacity` THEN `s 746(1) another person`

-- Layer-1: `s 747(1) the person commits an offence by a statement in a request`.  JUST TRUE is "yes, I have".
@export Under section 747(1), have I committed an offence by knowingly or recklessly making a misleading, false or deceptive statement in my request for the register?
GIVEN `I made a statement in a request under section 744` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did you make a statement in a request for the register of debenture holders?
      `the statement is misleading, false or deceptive in a material particular` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the statement misleading, false or deceptive in a material particular?
      `I made it knowingly` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did you make the statement knowing it was misleading, false or deceptive?
      `I made it recklessly` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did you make the statement recklessly?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 747(1), have I committed an offence by knowingly or recklessly making a misleading, false or deceptive statement in my request for the register` IS
    `s 747(1) the person commits an offence by a statement in a request` `I made a statement in a request under section 744` `the statement is misleading, false or deceptive in a material particular` `I made it knowingly` `I made it recklessly`

-- Layer-1: `s 747(2) the person commits an offence by disclosure of information`.  JUST TRUE is "yes, I have".
@export Under section 747(2), have I committed an offence by disclosing information from the register to a person, knowing or having reason to suspect that the person may use it for an improper purpose?
GIVEN `I have information obtained by exercising the section 744 rights` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are you in possession of information you obtained by exercising either of the rights in section 744 (to inspect the register or to have a copy)?
      `I did something that results in the information being disclosed` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did you do something that results in the information being disclosed to another person?
      `I failed to do something with the result that the information is disclosed` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did you fail to do something, with the result that the information is disclosed to another person?
      `I knew or had reason to suspect an improper purpose` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did you know, or have reason to suspect, that the other person may use the information for a purpose that is not a proper purpose?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 747(2), have I committed an offence by disclosing information from the register to a person, knowing or having reason to suspect that the person may use it for an improper purpose` IS
    `s 747(2) the person commits an offence by disclosure of information` `I have information obtained by exercising the section 744 rights` `I did something that results in the information being disclosed` `I failed to do something with the result that the information is disclosed` `I knew or had reason to suspect an improper purpose`

-- Layer-1: `s 747(3) the penalty for the offence` and `s 747(3) the number of months in the period`.
@export Under section 747(3), what is the longest term of imprisonment, in months, for an offence under section 747?
GIVEN `how I am convicted` IS A `Mode of conviction` @desc How are you convicted? One of: on conviction on indictment; on summary conviction in England and Wales; on summary conviction in Scotland; on summary conviction in Northern Ireland; on summary conviction.
GIVETH A MAYBE NUMBER
DECIDE `Under section 747(3), what is the longest term of imprisonment, in months, for an offence under section 747` IS
    CONSIDER `s 747(3) the penalty for the offence` `how I am convicted`
    WHEN JUST penalty THEN
        CONSIDER penalty's `imprisonment not exceeding`
        WHEN JUST term THEN `s 747(3) the number of months in the period` term
        WHEN NOTHING THEN NOTHING
    WHEN NOTHING THEN NOTHING

-- Layer-1: `s 747(3) the penalty for the offence` (its fine) and `s 741(3) the most that a fine limit allows, in pounds`.
@export Under section 747(3), what is the most the court can fine, in pounds, for an offence under section 747?
GIVEN `how I am convicted` IS A `Mode of conviction` @desc How are you convicted? One of: on conviction on indictment; on summary conviction in England and Wales; on summary conviction in Scotland; on summary conviction in Northern Ireland; on summary conviction.
      `pounds that the statutory maximum stands for` IS A NUMBER @desc How many pounds does the statutory maximum stand for (the figure is set outside the Companies Act)?
GIVETH A MAYBE NUMBER
DECIDE `Under section 747(3), what is the most the court can fine, in pounds, for an offence under section 747` IS
    CONSIDER `s 747(3) the penalty for the offence` `how I am convicted`
    WHEN JUST penalty THEN
        CONSIDER penalty's `fine not exceeding`
        WHEN JUST limit THEN `s 741(3) the most that a fine limit allows, in pounds` limit 0 `pounds that the statutory maximum stands for` -- placeholder 0: the level on the standard scale is not read by a statutory-maximum fine
        WHEN NOTHING THEN NOTHING
    WHEN NOTHING THEN NOTHING

-- Layer-1: `s 748(1) the liability is barred by the ten-year limit`.  JUST TRUE is "yes, barred".
@export Under section 748(1), is a liability of the company arising from making or deleting an entry in its register of debenture holders, or from failing to do so, barred by the ten-year limit?
GIVEN `the claim arises from the making or deletion of an entry in the register` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does the liability arise from the making or deletion of an entry in the register of debenture holders?
      `the claim arises from a failure to make or delete such an entry` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does the liability arise from a failure to make or delete such an entry?
      `date of the entry or the failure` IS A DATE @desc On what date was the entry made or deleted or, as the case may be, did the failure first occur (ISO 8601)?
      `date of enforcement` IS A DATE @desc On what date is the liability sought to be enforced (ISO 8601)?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 748(1), is a liability of the company arising from making or deleting an entry in its register of debenture holders, or from failing to do so, barred by the ten-year limit` IS
    `s 748(1) the liability is barred by the ten-year limit` `the claim arises from the making or deletion of an entry in the register` `the claim arises from a failure to make or delete such an entry` `date of the entry or the failure` `date of enforcement`

-- ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
§ `Debenture holders and trustees (ss 749 to 754)`
-- Situation: you hold debentures secured by a trust deed, are a trustee, or are dealing with redeemed debentures or a
-- floating charge.  Ask "Does this concern debentures?" before showing the group.
-- ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------

-- Layer-1: `s 749(1) the holder is entitled to be provided with a copy of the trust deed`.  JUST TRUE is "yes, entitled".
@export Under section 749(1), am I entitled to be provided with a copy of a trust deed securing the company's debentures?
GIVEN `I am a holder of debentures of the company` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are you a holder of debentures of the company?
      `there is a trust deed for securing the debentures` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is there a trust deed for securing the debentures?
      `I have made a request` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Have you made a request for a copy?
      `I have paid the fee that may be prescribed` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Have you paid the fee that may be prescribed?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 749(1), am I entitled to be provided with a copy of a trust deed securing the company's debentures` IS
    `s 749(1) the holder is entitled to be provided with a copy of the trust deed` `I am a holder of debentures of the company` `there is a trust deed for securing the debentures` `I have made a request` `I have paid the fee that may be prescribed`

-- Layer-1: `s 749(2) the person commits an offence`.  JUST TRUE is "yes, the offence is committed".  The subsection names
-- only officers in default, not the company, so the question is asked of the individual as an officer (F22).
@export Under section 749(2), have I committed an offence, as an officer of the company, by failing to provide a debenture holder with a copy of the trust deed?
GIVEN `default is made in complying with section 749` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has default been made in providing a debenture holder with a copy of the trust deed?
      `I am an officer of the company who is in default` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are you an officer of the company who is in default for this failure (section 1121)? Answer false if you are not an officer.
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 749(2), have I committed an offence, as an officer of the company, by failing to provide a debenture holder with a copy of the trust deed` IS
    `s 749(2) the person commits an offence` `default is made in complying with section 749` (`s 749(2) an officer of the company` (JUST `I am an officer of the company who is in default`))

-- Layer-1: `s 750(3) the provision is void, subject to subsection (2) and section 751`.  JUST TRUE is "yes, void".
@export Under section 750, is a provision in a trust deed securing debentures, or in a contract with their holders, void in so far as it exempts the trustee, or indemnifies him, against liability for breach of trust, subject to subsection (2) and section 751?
GIVEN `provision in a trust deed` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the provision contained in a trust deed for securing an issue of debentures?
      `provision in a contract with holders` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the provision contained in a contract with the holders of debentures secured by a trust deed?
      `provision exempts or indemnifies trustee` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Would the provision have the effect of exempting a trustee of the deed from, or indemnifying him against, liability for breach of trust?
      `trustee fails to show care and diligence` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does the trustee fail to show the degree of care and diligence required of him as trustee, having regard to the provisions of the trust deed conferring on him any powers, authorities or discretions?
      `release otherwise validly given` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it a release otherwise validly given?
      `release is for earlier acts` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the release in respect of anything done or omitted to be done by a trustee before the giving of the release?
      `provision enables a release` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it a provision enabling such a release to be given?
      `majority required in value` IS A NUMBER @desc What majority in value of the debenture holders present and voting does the provision require before a release is given (as a fraction: 0.75 is 75%)?
      `vote at a meeting summoned for the purpose` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does the provision require the vote to be taken at a meeting summoned for the purpose?
      `release for specific acts or omissions` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does the provision enable the release to be given with respect to specific acts or omissions?
      `release on trustee dying or ceasing to act` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does the provision enable the release to be given on the trustee dying or ceasing to act?
      `provision in force on the relevant date` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Was the provision in force on the relevant date (1 July 1948 where section 192 of the Companies Act 1985 applied; 1 July 1961 where Article 201 of the Companies (Northern Ireland) Order 1986 applied)?
      `a person then entitled remains a trustee` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does a person then entitled to the benefit of the provision remain a trustee of the deed in question?
      `a person later given the benefit remains a trustee` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does a person afterwards given the benefit of the provision under section 751(3) remain a trustee of the deed in question?
      `right relates to things done while in force` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the exemption or right to be indemnified in respect of anything done or omitted to be done by the person while any such provision was in force?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 750, is a provision in a trust deed securing debentures, or in a contract with their holders, void in so far as it exempts the trustee, or indemnifies him, against liability for breach of trust, subject to subsection (2) and section 751` IS
    `s 750(3) the provision is void, subject to subsection (2) and section 751`
        (`s 750(1) facts about the provision` OF `provision in a trust deed`, `provision in a contract with holders`, `provision exempts or indemnifies trustee`, `trustee fails to show care and diligence`)
        (`s 750(2) facts about the release or provision` OF `release otherwise validly given`, `release is for earlier acts`, `provision enables a release`, `majority required in value`, `vote at a meeting summoned for the purpose`, `release for specific acts or omissions`, `release on trustee dying or ceasing to act`)
        (`s 751(1) facts about an older provision` OF `provision in force on the relevant date`, `a person then entitled remains a trustee`, `a person later given the benefit remains a trustee`, `right relates to things done while in force`)

-- Layer-1: `s 751(3) the benefit of the saved provision may be given by resolution`.  JUST TRUE is "yes, it may"; JUST FALSE is "no, no trustee remains entitled to a saved provision" (the text: "While any trustee ... remains entitled").
@export Under section 751(3), may the benefit of a saved provision be given to trustees by a resolution of the debenture holders?
GIVEN `a trustee remains entitled to the benefit of a saved provision` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does a trustee of the trust deed remain entitled to the benefit of a provision saved by section 751(1)?
      `the benefit is to be given to all trustees, present and future` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the benefit to be given to all trustees of the deed, present and future?
      `the benefit is to be given to named or proposed trustees` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the benefit to be given to named trustees or proposed trustees of the deed?
      `the proportion in value who passed the resolution` IS A NUMBER @desc What proportion in value of the debenture holders present in person (or, where proxies are permitted, by proxy) passed the resolution (as a fraction: 0.75 is 75%)?
      `the meeting was summoned for the purpose` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Was the resolution passed at a meeting summoned for the purpose?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 751(3), may the benefit of a saved provision be given to trustees by a resolution of the debenture holders` IS
    `s 751(3) the benefit of the saved provision may be given by resolution` `a trustee remains entitled to the benefit of a saved provision` `the benefit is to be given to all trustees, present and future` `the benefit is to be given to named or proposed trustees` `the proportion in value who passed the resolution` `the meeting was summoned for the purpose`

-- Layer-1: `s 752(1) the company may re-issue the redeemed debentures`.  JUST TRUE is "yes, it may"; JUST FALSE is "no" (nothing has been redeemed, a provision to the contrary or an intention to cancel).
@export Under section 752(1), may the company re-issue debentures that it has redeemed?
GIVEN `the company has redeemed debentures previously issued` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has the company redeemed debentures it previously issued?
      `provision to the contrary is contained in the articles or a contract` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does the company's articles, or any contract made by the company, contain provision to the contrary (express or implied)?
      `the company has manifested its intention to cancel them` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has the company, by a resolution or some other act, manifested its intention that the debentures shall be cancelled?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 752(1), may the company re-issue debentures that it has redeemed` IS
    `s 752(1) the company may re-issue the redeemed debentures` `the company has redeemed debentures previously issued` `provision to the contrary is contained in the articles or a contract` `the company has manifested its intention to cancel them`

-- Layer-1: `s 752(4) the lender may give the debenture in evidence without payment of the stamp duty or any penalty`.  JUST TRUE is "yes, I may".
@export Under section 752(4), may I give in evidence, in proceedings to enforce my security, a debenture re-issued under section 752, without paying the stamp duty or any penalty on it?
GIVEN `I lent money on the security of a re-issued debenture` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did you lend money on the security of a debenture re-issued under section 752?
      `the debenture appears to be duly stamped` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does the debenture appear to be duly stamped?
      `I had notice that it was not duly stamped` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did you have notice that the debenture was not duly stamped?
      `but for my negligence I might have discovered it` IS A BOOLEAN @desc But for your negligence, might you have discovered that the debenture was not duly stamped?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 752(4), may I give in evidence, in proceedings to enforce my security, a debenture re-issued under section 752, without paying the stamp duty or any penalty on it` IS
    `s 752(4) the lender may give the debenture in evidence without payment of the stamp duty or any penalty` `I lent money on the security of a re-issued debenture` `the debenture appears to be duly stamped` `I had notice that it was not duly stamped` `but for my negligence I might have discovered it`

-- Layer-1: `s 753 the debentures are treated as redeemed by reason only that the account has ceased to be in debit`.  JUST FALSE is "no, not treated as redeemed".
@export Under section 753, are debentures deposited to secure advances treated as redeemed merely because the account has ceased to be in debit?
GIVEN `the debentures were deposited to secure advances` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has the company deposited any of its debentures to secure advances from time to time on current account or otherwise?
      `the account has ceased to be in debit` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has the account ceased to be in debit while the debentures remained so deposited?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 753, are debentures deposited to secure advances treated as redeemed merely because the account has ceased to be in debit` IS
    `s 753 the debentures are treated as redeemed by reason only that the account has ceased to be in debit` `the debentures were deposited to secure advances` `the account has ceased to be in debit`

-- Layer-1: `s 754(2) the company's preferential debts are to be paid in priority to the claims on the debentures`.  JUST TRUE is "yes, in priority".
@export Under section 754(2), are the company's preferential debts to be paid, out of assets coming to the hands of those who take possession, in priority to claims for principal or interest on its debentures?
GIVEN `where the company is registered` IS A `Place of registration` @desc Where is the company registered? One of: England and Wales, Scotland, Northern Ireland.
      `the debentures are secured by a charge` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are debentures of the company secured by a charge?
      `the charge was a floating charge as created` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Was the charge, as created, a floating charge?
      `possession has been taken` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has possession been taken, by or on behalf of the holders of the debentures, of any property comprised in or subject to the charge?
      `the company is being wound up` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the company at that time in the course of being wound up?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 754(2), are the company's preferential debts to be paid, out of assets coming to the hands of those who take possession, in priority to claims for principal or interest on its debentures` IS
    `s 754(2) the company's preferential debts are to be paid in priority to the claims on the debentures` `where the company is registered` `the debentures are secured by a charge` `the charge was a floating charge as created` `possession has been taken` `the company is being wound up`

-- ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
§ `Private companies: the ban on public offers of securities (ss 755 to 760)`
-- Situation: your company is a private company that is offering, or has allotted, shares or debentures.  Ask "Is your
-- company a private company, and has it offered or allotted shares or debentures?" before showing the group.
-- ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------

-- Layer-1: `s 755(1) the company is within the prohibition` (calls the keel's `s 4(1)`).  JUST TRUE is "yes, it binds the company".
@export Under section 755(1), is my company one that the prohibition on public offers of securities binds?
GIVEN `company registered in` IS A `Place of registration` @desc Where is your company registered? One of: England and Wales, Scotland, Northern Ireland.
      `members' liability` IS A `Liability of members` @desc How does your company's constitution limit its members' liability? One of: liability not limited; liability limited to the amount, if any, unpaid on the shares held; liability limited to the amount the members undertake to contribute on a winding up; liability limited in some other way by the constitution.
      `company has share capital` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does your company have a share capital?
      `certificate says public` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does your company's certificate of incorporation state that it is a public company?
      `date registration requirements complied with` IS A DATE @desc On what date were the requirements for registration or re-registration as a public company complied with (ISO 8601, for example 2008-10-01)? Give any date if the company has never been registered as a public company.
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 755(1), is my company one that the prohibition on public offers of securities binds` IS
    `s 755(1) the company is within the prohibition` (`coa16 seat the company profile` `company registered in` `members' liability` `company has share capital` `certificate says public`) (`coa16 seat the requirements were complied with on or after the relevant date` `company registered in` `date registration requirements complied with`)

-- Layer-1: `s 755(2) the presumption that the allotment was made with a view ... applies`.  JUST TRUE is "yes, it is presumed".
@export Under section 755(2), is an allotment of securities presumed to have been made with a view to their being offered to the public?
GIVEN `public offer made` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has an offer of the securities (or any of them) to the public been made?
      `allotment date` IS A DATE @desc On what date were the securities allotted, or agreed to be allotted (ISO 8601, for example 2024-03-15)?
      `offer date` IS A DATE @desc On what date was the offer to the public made, or first made (ISO 8601)?
      `whole consideration received` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has the company received the whole of the consideration to be received by it in respect of the securities?
      `date whole consideration received` IS A DATE @desc On what date did the company receive the whole of the consideration (ISO 8601)? Give any date if it has not.
      `contrary to presumption proved` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has it been proved that the allotment was not made with a view to the securities being offered to the public?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 755(2), is an allotment of securities presumed to have been made with a view to their being offered to the public` IS
    `s 755(2) the presumption that the allotment was made with a view to the securities being offered to the public applies` `public offer made` `allotment date` `offer date` (`coa16 seat a date, if there is one` `whole consideration received` `date whole consideration received`) `contrary to presumption proved`

-- Layer-1: `s 755(3) the company is excepted from the prohibition`.  JUST TRUE is "yes, excepted".
@export Under section 755(3), is my company excepted from the prohibition on public offers of securities?
GIVEN `acts in good faith` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does the company act in good faith?
      `arrangements to re-register before allotment` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does the company act in pursuance of arrangements under which it is to re-register as a public company before the securities are allotted?
      `undertaking to re-register in a specified period` IS A BOOLEAN @desc As part of the terms of the offer, does the company undertake to re-register as a public company within a specified period?
      `undertaking complied with` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is that undertaking complied with?
      `last day of specified period` IS A DATE @desc What is the last day of the specified period (ISO 8601)? Give any date if there is no such undertaking.
      `offer date` IS A DATE @desc On what date was the offer made, or first made (ISO 8601)?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 755(3), is my company excepted from the prohibition on public offers of securities` IS
    `s 755(3) the company is excepted from the prohibition` `acts in good faith` `arrangements to re-register before allotment` `undertaking to re-register in a specified period` `undertaking complied with` `offer date` `last day of specified period`

-- Layer-1: `s 755(1) the company contravenes the prohibition, subject to subsection (3)`.  JUST TRUE is "yes, it contravenes".
@export Under section 755(1), does my company contravene the prohibition on public offers of its securities?
GIVEN `company registered in` IS A `Place of registration` @desc Where is your company registered? One of: England and Wales, Scotland, Northern Ireland.
      `members' liability` IS A `Liability of members` @desc How does your company's constitution limit its members' liability? One of: liability not limited; liability limited to the amount, if any, unpaid on the shares held; liability limited to the amount the members undertake to contribute on a winding up; liability limited in some other way by the constitution.
      `company has share capital` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does your company have a share capital?
      `certificate says public` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does your company's certificate of incorporation state that it is a public company?
      `date registration requirements complied with` IS A DATE @desc On what date were the requirements for registration or re-registration as a public company complied with (ISO 8601, for example 2008-10-01)? Give any date if the company has never been registered as a public company.
      `the kind of instrument offered or allotted` IS A `s 738 kind of instrument` @desc What kind of instrument is offered or allotted? One of: s 738 debenture stock; s 738 a bond; s 738 another security of a company; s 738 a share in a company; s 738 something that is not a security of a company.
      `the company has made an offer of the securities` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has the company made an offer of the securities?
      `offer is to the public or a section of it` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the offer made to the public, or to any section of the public, however selected?
      `offer is not calculated to reach others` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Can the offer properly be regarded, in all the circumstances, as not being calculated to result, directly or indirectly, in securities of the company becoming available to persons other than those receiving the offer?
      `offer is otherwise a private concern` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Can the offer properly be regarded, in all the circumstances, as otherwise being a private concern of the person receiving it and the person making it?
      `offeree is an existing member` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the person to whom the offer is made an existing member of the company?
      `offeree is an existing employee` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the person to whom the offer is made an existing employee of the company?
      `offeree is spouse or civil partner of a member or employee` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the person to whom the offer is made the spouse or civil partner of a person who is or was a member or employee of the company?
      `offeree is child of a member or employee` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the person to whom the offer is made a child (including a step-child) of a person who is or was a member or employee of the company?
      `offeree is descendant of such a child` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the person to whom the offer is made a descendant of such a child?
      `offeree is widow, widower or surviving civil partner of a member or employee` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the person to whom the offer is made the widow or widower, or surviving civil partner, of a person who was a member or employee of the company?
      `offeree is an existing debenture holder` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the person to whom the offer is made an existing debenture holder of the company?
      `offeree is a trustee of a trust for one of those persons` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the person to whom the offer is made a trustee (acting in that capacity) of a trust whose principal beneficiary is an existing member or employee, a family member of a member or employee, a widow, widower or surviving civil partner of a member or employee, or an existing debenture holder?
      `offer allows renunciation` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does the offer allow the person to whom it is made to renounce his rights?
      `renunciation only to connected persons` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Do the terms of the offer allow the rights to be renounced only in favour of another person already connected with the company?
      `offer is for an employees' share scheme` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the offer an offer to subscribe for securities to be held under an employees' share scheme (section 1166)?
      `renunciation only to scheme or connected persons` IS A BOOLEAN @desc For an employees' share scheme offer, do the terms allow the rights to be renounced only in favour of another person entitled to hold securities under the scheme or a person already connected with the company?
      `contrary is proved` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has it been proved that the offer is not a private concern of the person receiving it and the person making it?
      `allotted or agreed to allot` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has the company allotted, or agreed to allot, any of the securities?
      `allotted with a view to public offer` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Was the allotment (or agreement to allot) in fact made with a view to the securities being offered to the public?
      `public offer made` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has an offer of the securities (or any of them) to the public been made?
      `allotment date` IS A DATE @desc On what date were the securities allotted, or agreed to be allotted (ISO 8601, for example 2024-03-15)?
      `offer date` IS A DATE @desc On what date was the offer to the public made, or first made (ISO 8601)?
      `whole consideration received` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has the company received the whole of the consideration to be received by it in respect of the securities?
      `date whole consideration received` IS A DATE @desc On what date did the company receive the whole of the consideration (ISO 8601)? Give any date if it has not.
      `contrary to presumption proved` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has it been proved that the allotment was not made with a view to the securities being offered to the public?
      `acts in good faith` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does the company act in good faith?
      `arrangements to re-register before allotment` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does the company act in pursuance of arrangements under which it is to re-register as a public company before the securities are allotted?
      `undertaking to re-register in a specified period` IS A BOOLEAN @desc As part of the terms of the offer, does the company undertake to re-register as a public company within a specified period?
      `undertaking complied with` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is that undertaking complied with?
      `last day of specified period` IS A DATE @desc What is the last day of the specified period (ISO 8601)? Give any date if there is no such undertaking.
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 755(1), does my company contravene the prohibition on public offers of its securities` IS
    `s 755(1) the company contravenes the prohibition, subject to subsection (3)` within offered allotted excepted
    WHERE
        within MEANS `s 755(1) the company is within the prohibition` (`coa16 seat the company profile` `company registered in` `members' liability` `company has share capital` `certificate says public`) (`coa16 seat the requirements were complied with on or after the relevant date` `company registered in` `date registration requirements complied with`)
        offered MEANS `s 755(1)(a) the company offers securities of the company to the public` `the company has made an offer of the securities` (`s 755(5) the instrument is a security for this Chapter` `the kind of instrument offered or allotted`) (`s 756(1) the offer is an offer of securities to the public` (`coa16 seat the offer` `offer is to the public or a section of it` `offer is not calculated to reach others` `offer is otherwise a private concern` `offeree is an existing member` `offeree is an existing employee` `offeree is spouse or civil partner of a member or employee` `offeree is child of a member or employee` `offeree is descendant of such a child` `offeree is widow, widower or surviving civil partner of a member or employee` `offeree is an existing debenture holder` `offeree is a trustee of a trust for one of those persons` `offer allows renunciation` `renunciation only to connected persons` `offer is for an employees' share scheme` `renunciation only to scheme or connected persons` `contrary is proved`))
        allotted MEANS `s 755(1)(b) the company allots or agrees to allot securities with a view to their being offered to the public` `allotted or agreed to allot` (`s 755(5) the instrument is a security for this Chapter` `the kind of instrument offered or allotted`) `allotted with a view to public offer` (`s 755(2) the presumption that the allotment was made with a view to the securities being offered to the public applies` `public offer made` `allotment date` `offer date` (`coa16 seat a date, if there is one` `whole consideration received` `date whole consideration received`) `contrary to presumption proved`)
        excepted MEANS `s 755(3) the company is excepted from the prohibition` `acts in good faith` `arrangements to re-register before allotment` `undertaking to re-register in a specified period` `undertaking complied with` `offer date` `last day of specified period`

-- Layer-1: `s 756(1) the offer is an offer of securities to the public`.  JUST TRUE is "yes, it is"; JUST FALSE "no, subsection (3) excludes it".
@export Under section 756(1), is this offer an offer of securities to the public?
GIVEN `offer is to the public or a section of it` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the offer made to the public, or to any section of the public, however selected?
      `offer is not calculated to reach others` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Can the offer properly be regarded, in all the circumstances, as not being calculated to result, directly or indirectly, in securities of the company becoming available to persons other than those receiving the offer?
      `offer is otherwise a private concern` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Can the offer properly be regarded, in all the circumstances, as otherwise being a private concern of the person receiving it and the person making it?
      `offeree is an existing member` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the person to whom the offer is made an existing member of the company?
      `offeree is an existing employee` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the person to whom the offer is made an existing employee of the company?
      `offeree is spouse or civil partner of a member or employee` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the person to whom the offer is made the spouse or civil partner of a person who is or was a member or employee of the company?
      `offeree is child of a member or employee` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the person to whom the offer is made a child (including a step-child) of a person who is or was a member or employee of the company?
      `offeree is descendant of such a child` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the person to whom the offer is made a descendant of such a child?
      `offeree is widow, widower or surviving civil partner of a member or employee` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the person to whom the offer is made the widow or widower, or surviving civil partner, of a person who was a member or employee of the company?
      `offeree is an existing debenture holder` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the person to whom the offer is made an existing debenture holder of the company?
      `offeree is a trustee of a trust for one of those persons` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the person to whom the offer is made a trustee (acting in that capacity) of a trust whose principal beneficiary is an existing member or employee, a family member of a member or employee, a widow, widower or surviving civil partner of a member or employee, or an existing debenture holder?
      `offer allows renunciation` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does the offer allow the person to whom it is made to renounce his rights?
      `renunciation only to connected persons` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Do the terms of the offer allow the rights to be renounced only in favour of another person already connected with the company?
      `offer is for an employees' share scheme` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the offer an offer to subscribe for securities to be held under an employees' share scheme (section 1166)?
      `renunciation only to scheme or connected persons` IS A BOOLEAN @desc For an employees' share scheme offer, do the terms allow the rights to be renounced only in favour of another person entitled to hold securities under the scheme or a person already connected with the company?
      `contrary is proved` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has it been proved that the offer is not a private concern of the person receiving it and the person making it?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 756(1), is this offer an offer of securities to the public` IS
    `s 756(1) the offer is an offer of securities to the public` (`coa16 seat the offer` `offer is to the public or a section of it` `offer is not calculated to reach others` `offer is otherwise a private concern` `offeree is an existing member` `offeree is an existing employee` `offeree is spouse or civil partner of a member or employee` `offeree is child of a member or employee` `offeree is descendant of such a child` `offeree is widow, widower or surviving civil partner of a member or employee` `offeree is an existing debenture holder` `offeree is a trustee of a trust for one of those persons` `offer allows renunciation` `renunciation only to connected persons` `offer is for an employees' share scheme` `renunciation only to scheme or connected persons` `contrary is proved`)

-- Layer-1: `s 757(3) the person may apply for an order under this section`.  JUST TRUE is "yes, I may".
@export Under section 757(3), may I apply to the court for an order under section 757 restraining a company from contravening section 755?
GIVEN `I am a member of the company` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are you a member of the company?
      `I am a creditor of the company` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are you a creditor of the company?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 757(3), may I apply to the court for an order under section 757 restraining a company from contravening section 755` IS
    -- Placeholder FALSE: the seat is an individual, so the person is not the Secretary of State.
    `s 757(3) the person may apply for an order under this section` (JUST `I am a member of the company`) `I am a creditor of the company` FALSE

-- Layer-1: `s 758(2) the court must make an order requiring the company to re-register as a public company`.  JUST TRUE is "yes, it must".
@export Under section 758(2), must the court order the company to re-register as a public company?
GIVEN `it appears to the court that the company has acted in contravention of section 755` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does it appear to the court that the company has acted in contravention of section 755?
      `the court is hearing an application under section 758` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the court hearing an application under section 758?
      `the court is hearing proceedings under Part 30` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the court hearing proceedings under Part 30 (protection of members against unfair prejudice)?
      `it appears that the company does not meet the requirements for re-registration` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does it appear to the court that the company does not meet the requirements for re-registration as a public company?
      `it appears impractical or undesirable to require re-registration` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does it appear to the court that it is impractical or undesirable to require the company to take steps to re-register?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 758(2), must the court order the company to re-register as a public company` IS
    `s 758(2) the court must make an order requiring the company to re-register as a public company` `it appears to the court that the company has acted in contravention of section 755` `the court is hearing an application under section 758` `the court is hearing proceedings under Part 30` `it appears that the company does not meet the requirements for re-registration` `it appears impractical or undesirable to require re-registration`

-- Layer-1: `s 758(4) the person may apply for an order under this section`.  JUST TRUE is "yes, I may".
@export Under section 758(4), may I apply to the court for an order under section 758?
GIVEN `I was a member when the offer was made` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Were you a member of the company at the time the offer was made (or, if it was made over a period, at any time during that period)?
      `I became a member as a result of the offer` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did you become a member of the company as a result of the offer?
      `I was a creditor when the offer was made` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Were you a creditor of the company at the time the offer was made (or, if it was made over a period, at any time during that period)?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 758(4), may I apply to the court for an order under section 758` IS
    -- Placeholder FALSE: the seat is an individual, so the person is not the Secretary of State.
    `s 758(4) the person may apply for an order under this section` `I was a member when the offer was made` `I became a member as a result of the offer` `I was a creditor when the offer was made` FALSE

-- Layer-1: `s 759(3) a remedial order may require the person to offer to purchase the securities`.  JUST TRUE is "yes, it may"; JUST FALSE is "no, the company is not a private company that has allotted as the subsection describes".
@export Under section 759(3), may a remedial order require me to offer to purchase any of a company's securities that it has allotted?
GIVEN `the company is a private company` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the company a private company?
      `the company allotted securities pursuant to an offer to the public` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did the company allot securities pursuant to an offer to the public?
      `the company allotted or agreed to allot with a view to a public offer` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did the company allot or agree to allot securities with a view to their being offered to the public?
      `I was knowingly concerned in the contravention` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Were you knowingly concerned in the contravention of section 755?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 759(3), may a remedial order require me to offer to purchase any of a company's securities that it has allotted` IS
    `s 759(3) a remedial order may require the person to offer to purchase the securities` `the company is a private company` `the company allotted securities pursuant to an offer to the public` `the company allotted or agreed to allot with a view to a public offer` `I was knowingly concerned in the contravention`

-- Layer-1: `s 760 this Chapter affects the validity of the transaction`.  JUST FALSE is "no, it does not affect it".
@export Under section 760, does the prohibition on public offers affect the validity of an allotment or sale of securities, or of an agreement to allot or sell them?
GIVEN `the transaction` IS A `s 760 transaction` @desc What is the transaction? One of: s 760 an allotment of securities; s 760 a sale of securities; s 760 an agreement to allot securities; s 760 an agreement to sell securities; s 760 any other transaction.
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 760, does the prohibition on public offers affect the validity of an allotment or sale of securities, or of an agreement to allot or sell them` IS
    `s 760 this Chapter affects the validity of the transaction` `the transaction`

-- ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
§ `Public companies: the trading certificate and the authorised minimum (ss 761 to 767)`
-- Situation: your company is a public company that is, or is about to start, doing business or borrowing.  Ask "Is your
-- company a public company that did not become public by re-registration?" before showing the group.
-- ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------

-- Layer-1: `s 761(1) the company is barred from doing business or exercising any borrowing powers` (calls the keel's `s 4(2)`).  JUST TRUE is "yes, barred".
@export Under section 761(1), is my company barred from doing business or exercising borrowing powers?
GIVEN `company registered in` IS A `Place of registration` @desc Where is your company registered? One of: England and Wales, Scotland, Northern Ireland.
      `members' liability` IS A `Liability of members` @desc How does your company's constitution limit its members' liability? One of: liability not limited; liability limited to the amount, if any, unpaid on the shares held; liability limited to the amount the members undertake to contribute on a winding up; liability limited in some other way by the constitution.
      `company has share capital` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does your company have a share capital?
      `certificate says public` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does your company's certificate of incorporation state that it is a public company?
      `date registration requirements complied with` IS A DATE @desc On what date were the requirements for registration or re-registration as a public company complied with (ISO 8601, for example 2008-10-01)? Give any date if the company has never been registered as a public company.
      `my company is public by virtue of re-registration` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is your company a public company by virtue of re-registration as a public company (rather than by being registered as one)?
      `the registrar has issued a trading certificate` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has the registrar issued your company with a trading certificate?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 761(1), is my company barred from doing business or exercising borrowing powers` IS
    `s 761(1) the company is barred from doing business or exercising any borrowing powers` (`coa16 seat the company profile` `company registered in` `members' liability` `company has share capital` `certificate says public`) (`coa16 seat the requirements were complied with on or after the relevant date` `company registered in` `date registration requirements complied with`) `my company is public by virtue of re-registration` `the registrar has issued a trading certificate`

-- Layer-1: `s 761(3) the scheme share is taken into account`.  JUST TRUE is "yes, taken into account".
@export Under section 761(3), is a share allotted under an employees' share scheme taken into account in my company's allotted share capital?
GIVEN `the share was allotted in pursuance of an employees' share scheme` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Was the share allotted in pursuance of an employees' share scheme (section 1166)?
      `nominal value of the share` IS A NUMBER @desc What is the nominal value of the share, in the currency of its denomination?
      `amount paid up on the nominal value` IS A NUMBER @desc How much of that nominal value has been paid up?
      `premium on the share` IS A NUMBER @desc What is the premium on the share (0 if none)?
      `amount of the premium paid` IS A NUMBER @desc How much of the premium has been paid?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 761(3), is a share allotted under an employees' share scheme taken into account in my company's allotted share capital` IS
    -- Placeholder sterling: the rule reads the share's currency only when it adds up share capital, not here.
    `s 761(3) the scheme share is taken into account` (`s 761(3) allotted share` OF `s 765 sterling`, `nominal value of the share`, `the share was allotted in pursuance of an employees' share scheme`, `amount paid up on the nominal value`, `premium on the share`, `amount of the premium paid`)

-- Layer-1: `s 761(2) the nominal value of the company's allotted share capital is not less than the authorised minimum` (calls s 765(1)).
@export Under section 761(2), is the nominal value of my company's allotted share capital not less than the authorised minimum?
GIVEN `sterling shares not under scheme` IS A NUMBER @desc What is the total nominal value, in pounds sterling, of the company's allotted shares denominated in sterling that were not allotted in pursuance of an employees' share scheme?
      `euro shares not under scheme` IS A NUMBER @desc What is the total nominal value, in euros, of the company's allotted shares denominated in euros that were not allotted in pursuance of an employees' share scheme?
      `shares in another currency` IS A NUMBER @desc What is the total nominal value of the company's allotted shares denominated in any other currency (any currency, 0 if none)?
      `sterling scheme shares nominal value` IS A NUMBER @desc What is the total nominal value, in pounds sterling, of the sterling shares allotted in pursuance of an employees' share scheme (0 if none)?
      `sterling scheme shares paid up` IS A NUMBER @desc How much of that nominal value has been paid up, in pounds sterling?
      `sterling scheme shares premium` IS A NUMBER @desc What is the total premium on those sterling scheme shares, in pounds sterling (0 if none)?
      `sterling scheme shares premium paid` IS A NUMBER @desc How much of that premium has been paid, in pounds sterling?
      `euro scheme shares nominal value` IS A NUMBER @desc What is the total nominal value, in euros, of the euro shares allotted in pursuance of an employees' share scheme (0 if none)?
      `euro scheme shares paid up` IS A NUMBER @desc How much of that nominal value has been paid up, in euros?
      `euro scheme shares premium` IS A NUMBER @desc What is the total premium on those euro scheme shares, in euros (0 if none)?
      `euro scheme shares premium paid` IS A NUMBER @desc How much of that premium has been paid, in euros?
      `prescribed euro equivalent` IS A NUMBER @desc What is the prescribed euro equivalent of the authorised minimum, in euros (set by order of the Secretary of State, not by the Act)?
      `the currency my company elects` IS A `s 765 currency` @desc In which currency does your company elect to measure its share capital? One of: s 765 sterling; s 765 euros; s 765 another currency.
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 761(2), is the nominal value of my company's allotted share capital not less than the authorised minimum` IS
    -- NOTHING: the seat assumes no order under section 764 has substituted another sterling amount.
    `s 761(2) the nominal value of the company's allotted share capital is not less than the authorised minimum` (`coa16 seat the allotted shares` `sterling shares not under scheme` `euro shares not under scheme` `shares in another currency` `sterling scheme shares nominal value` `sterling scheme shares paid up` `sterling scheme shares premium` `sterling scheme shares premium paid` `euro scheme shares nominal value` `euro scheme shares paid up` `euro scheme shares premium` `euro scheme shares premium paid`) `the currency my company elects` NOTHING `prescribed euro equivalent`

-- Layer-1: `s 761(2) the registrar shall issue a trading certificate`.  JUST TRUE is "yes, he must".
@export Under section 761(2), must the registrar issue my company a trading certificate?
GIVEN `an application has been made in accordance with section 762` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has an application been made in accordance with section 762?
      `the registrar is satisfied about the share capital` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the registrar satisfied that the nominal value of the company's allotted share capital is not less than the authorised minimum?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 761(2), must the registrar issue my company a trading certificate` IS
    `s 761(2) the registrar shall issue a trading certificate` `an application has been made in accordance with section 762` `the registrar is satisfied about the share capital`

-- Layer-1: `s 761(4) the certificate is conclusive evidence ...`.  JUST TRUE is "yes, conclusive evidence".
@export Under section 761(4), is my company's trading certificate conclusive evidence that it is entitled to do business and exercise borrowing powers?
GIVEN `a trading certificate has been issued` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has a trading certificate been issued to the company?
      `date the certificate was issued` IS A DATE @desc On what date was it issued (ISO 8601)? Give any date if none has been issued.
      `date of the question` IS A DATE @desc For what date are you asking whether the certificate is conclusive evidence (ISO 8601)?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 761(4), is my company's trading certificate conclusive evidence that it is entitled to do business and exercise borrowing powers` IS
    `s 761(4) the certificate is conclusive evidence that the company is entitled to do business and exercise any borrowing powers` (`coa16 seat a date, if there is one` `a trading certificate has been issued` `date the certificate was issued`) `date of the question`

-- Layer-1: `s 762(1) the application is made in accordance with section 762`.  JUST TRUE is "yes, it is".
@export Under section 762(1), is my application for a trading certificate made in accordance with section 762?
GIVEN `the application states that the allotted share capital is not less than the authorised minimum` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does the application state that the nominal value of the company's allotted share capital is not less than the authorised minimum?
      `the application specifies the preliminary expenses` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does the application specify the amount, or estimated amount, of the company's preliminary expenses?
      `the application specifies any payment or benefit to a promoter` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does the application specify any amount or benefit paid or given, or intended to be paid or given, to any promoter of the company, and the consideration for it (answer yes if there is none)?
      `the application is accompanied by a statement of compliance` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the application accompanied by a statement of compliance?
      `the application is accompanied by a statement of the amount paid up` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the application accompanied by a statement of the aggregate amount paid up on the shares of the company on account of their nominal value?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 762(1), is my application for a trading certificate made in accordance with section 762` IS
    `s 762(1) the application is made in accordance with section 762` `the application states that the allotted share capital is not less than the authorised minimum` `the application specifies the preliminary expenses` `the application specifies any payment or benefit to a promoter` `the application is accompanied by a statement of compliance` `the application is accompanied by a statement of the amount paid up`

-- Layer-1: `s 763(1) the authorised minimum in the currency`.
@export Under section 763(1), what is the authorised minimum, in the currency my company chooses?
GIVEN `the currency` IS A `s 765 currency` @desc In which currency is the minimum wanted? One of: s 765 sterling; s 765 euros; s 765 another currency.
      `the prescribed euro equivalent` IS A NUMBER @desc What is the prescribed euro equivalent of the authorised minimum, in euros (set by order of the Secretary of State, not by the Act)?
GIVETH A MAYBE NUMBER
DECIDE `Under section 763(1), what is the authorised minimum, in the currency my company chooses` IS
    -- NOTHING: the seat assumes no order under section 764 has substituted another sterling amount.
    `s 763(1) the authorised minimum in the currency` `the currency` NOTHING `the prescribed euro equivalent`

-- Layer-1: `s 765(4) the company has made the election the subsection requires`.  JUST TRUE is "yes, it has".
@export Under section 765(4), has my company made the election of currency that the subsection requires?
GIVEN `sterling shares not under scheme` IS A NUMBER @desc What is the total nominal value, in pounds sterling, of the company's allotted shares denominated in sterling that were not allotted in pursuance of an employees' share scheme?
      `euro shares not under scheme` IS A NUMBER @desc What is the total nominal value, in euros, of the company's allotted shares denominated in euros that were not allotted in pursuance of an employees' share scheme?
      `shares in another currency` IS A NUMBER @desc What is the total nominal value of the company's allotted shares denominated in any other currency (any currency, 0 if none)?
      `sterling scheme shares nominal value` IS A NUMBER @desc What is the total nominal value, in pounds sterling, of the sterling shares allotted in pursuance of an employees' share scheme (0 if none)?
      `sterling scheme shares paid up` IS A NUMBER @desc How much of that nominal value has been paid up, in pounds sterling?
      `sterling scheme shares premium` IS A NUMBER @desc What is the total premium on those sterling scheme shares, in pounds sterling (0 if none)?
      `sterling scheme shares premium paid` IS A NUMBER @desc How much of that premium has been paid, in pounds sterling?
      `euro scheme shares nominal value` IS A NUMBER @desc What is the total nominal value, in euros, of the euro shares allotted in pursuance of an employees' share scheme (0 if none)?
      `euro scheme shares paid up` IS A NUMBER @desc How much of that nominal value has been paid up, in euros?
      `euro scheme shares premium` IS A NUMBER @desc What is the total premium on those euro scheme shares, in euros (0 if none)?
      `euro scheme shares premium paid` IS A NUMBER @desc How much of that premium has been paid, in euros?
      `prescribed euro equivalent` IS A NUMBER @desc What is the prescribed euro equivalent of the authorised minimum, in euros (set by order of the Secretary of State, not by the Act)?
      `my company has elected, in its application, which currency is to be used` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has your company elected, in its application for a trading certificate or for re-registration as a public company, which currency is to be used?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 765(4), has my company made the election of currency that the subsection requires` IS
    `s 765(4) the company has made the election the subsection requires` (`coa16 seat the allotted shares` `sterling shares not under scheme` `euro shares not under scheme` `shares in another currency` `sterling scheme shares nominal value` `sterling scheme shares paid up` `sterling scheme shares premium` `sterling scheme shares premium paid` `euro scheme shares nominal value` `euro scheme shares paid up` `euro scheme shares premium` `euro scheme shares premium paid`) NOTHING `prescribed euro equivalent` `my company has elected, in its application, which currency is to be used`

-- Layer-1: `s 767(1) the person commits an offence`.  JUST TRUE is "yes, the offence is committed".
@export Under section 767(1), has the company, or have I as an officer of the company, committed an offence by doing business or exercising borrowing powers without a trading certificate?
GIVEN `company registered in` IS A `Place of registration` @desc Where is your company registered? One of: England and Wales, Scotland, Northern Ireland.
      `members' liability` IS A `Liability of members` @desc How does your company's constitution limit its members' liability? One of: liability not limited; liability limited to the amount, if any, unpaid on the shares held; liability limited to the amount the members undertake to contribute on a winding up; liability limited in some other way by the constitution.
      `company has share capital` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does your company have a share capital?
      `certificate says public` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does your company's certificate of incorporation state that it is a public company?
      `date registration requirements complied with` IS A DATE @desc On what date were the requirements for registration or re-registration as a public company complied with (ISO 8601, for example 2008-10-01)? Give any date if the company has never been registered as a public company.
      `my company is public by virtue of re-registration` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is your company a public company by virtue of re-registration as a public company (rather than by being registered as one)?
      `the registrar has issued a trading certificate` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has the registrar issued your company with a trading certificate?
      `the company does business or exercises borrowing powers` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has the company done business or exercised any borrowing powers?
      `who is asked about` IS A `coa16 seat who is asked about` @desc Whose liability is this about? One of: coa16 seat the company; coa16 seat me, as an officer of the company; coa16 seat me, in some other capacity.
      `officer in default` IS A BOOLEAN @desc If you are asking as an officer: are you an officer in default of the company for this contravention (section 1121)? Answer false if you are not an officer.
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 767(1), has the company, or have I as an officer of the company, committed an offence by doing business or exercising borrowing powers without a trading certificate` IS
    `s 767(1) the person commits an offence` (`coa16 seat the company profile` `company registered in` `members' liability` `company has share capital` `certificate says public`) (`coa16 seat the requirements were complied with on or after the relevant date` `company registered in` `date registration requirements complied with`) `my company is public by virtue of re-registration` `the registrar has issued a trading certificate` `the company does business or exercises borrowing powers` person
    WHERE
        person MEANS
            CONSIDER `who is asked about`
            WHEN `coa16 seat the company` THEN `s 767(1) the company`
            WHEN `coa16 seat me, as an officer of the company` THEN `s 767(1) an officer of the company` (JUST `officer in default`)
            WHEN `coa16 seat me, in some other capacity` THEN `s 767(1) another person`

-- Layer-1: `s 767(2) the penalty for the offence`.
@export Under section 767(2), what is the most the court can fine, in pounds, for doing business or exercising borrowing powers without a trading certificate?
GIVEN `how I am convicted` IS A `Mode of conviction` @desc How are you convicted? One of: on conviction on indictment; on summary conviction in England and Wales; on summary conviction in Scotland; on summary conviction in Northern Ireland; on summary conviction.
      `pounds that the statutory maximum stands for` IS A NUMBER @desc How many pounds does the statutory maximum stand for (the figure is set outside the Companies Act)?
GIVETH A MAYBE NUMBER
DECIDE `Under section 767(2), what is the most the court can fine, in pounds, for doing business or exercising borrowing powers without a trading certificate` IS
    CONSIDER (`s 767(2) the penalty for the offence` `how I am convicted`)'s `fine not exceeding`
    WHEN JUST limit THEN `s 741(3) the most that a fine limit allows, in pounds` limit 0 `pounds that the statutory maximum stands for` -- placeholder 0: the level on the standard scale is not read by a statutory-maximum fine
    WHEN NOTHING THEN NOTHING

-- Layer-1: `s 767(3) the contravention of section 761 affects the validity of the transaction`.  JUST FALSE is "no, it does not affect it".
@export Under section 767(3), does the company's contravention of section 761 affect the validity of a transaction it entered into?
GIVEN `the company entered into the transaction in contravention of section 761` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did the company enter into the transaction in contravention of section 761 (without a trading certificate)?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 767(3), does the company's contravention of section 761 affect the validity of a transaction it entered into` IS
    `s 767(3) the contravention of section 761 affects the validity of the transaction` `the company entered into the transaction in contravention of section 761`

-- Layer-1: `s 767(4) the director is liable to indemnify the other party to the transaction`.  JUST TRUE is "yes, liable".
@export Under section 767(4), am I jointly and severally liable, with the other directors, to indemnify the other party to a transaction the company entered into without a trading certificate?
GIVEN `the company entered into a transaction in contravention of section 761` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did the company enter into a transaction in contravention of section 761 (without a trading certificate)?
      `the company complied with its obligations` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has the company complied with its obligations in connection with the transaction?
      `days from being called on` IS A NUMBER @desc How many days passed between the company being called on to comply and the day it complied, or between being called on and today if it has not complied?
      `I was a director when the company entered into the transaction` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Were you a director of the company at the time it entered into the transaction (section 250)?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 767(4), am I jointly and severally liable, with the other directors, to indemnify the other party to a transaction the company entered into without a trading certificate` IS
    `s 767(4) the director is liable to indemnify the other party to the transaction` `the company entered into a transaction in contravention of section 761` `the company complied with its obligations` `days from being called on` (JUST `I was a director when the company entered into the transaction`)

-- ====================================================================================================
-- seat questions from part coa17 (merged by the lead on 2026-11-12; unchanged text follows)
-- ====================================================================================================
-- coa17-seat.l4: Companies Act 2006 (United Kingdom), Parts 21 and 21A (ss 768 to 790ZH) -- THE SEAT LAYER.
--
-- SEAT (assumed, not ruled: the Act is addressed to companies, so the individual is whoever stands in a company's
-- management or ownership): an individual who is, or is about to become, a director, a company secretary or a member
-- (shareholder) of a company registered under the Act, or who deals with one -- a transferee or a transferor of shares,
-- a person holding shares or debentures, a personal representative, a person with significant control over a company, or
-- a person who asks a company about its register. There is never a seat for an official: the registrar, the court and the
-- Secretary of State appear only as what they mean for that person.
--
-- This layer asks, on facts that person can state, what the Act requires or lets them do, what rights they have against the
-- company or its directors, what they must disclose, file, approve or vote on and by when, and what follows (liability,
-- offences, penalties) if it is not done. It calls the rules of the layer-1 modules and restates none of them: each
-- question builds the modules' records from plain inputs and calls the module's function. Nothing here is new law.
--
-- ANSWERS. Every yes/no answer is JUST TRUE (the text says yes), JUST FALSE (the text says no in its own words) or NOTHING
-- ("not covered": the text does not decide; it is never a no). A date answer is the last day of a period the text fixes.
--
-- WHERE THIS LAYER ASSUMES, AND WHAT WOULD CHANGE THE ANSWERS (recorded in NOTES.md):
--   * Whether Part 21A applies to the company (s 790B(1)) is asked as one yes/no, in the question's own words; the
--     question "Under section 790B(1), does Part 21A apply to my company?" works it out from the three facts.
--   * "Officer in default" (s 1121, another part's) is asked as a yes/no about the person asking.
--   * The pounds a level on the standard scale stands for are not in the Act: they are asked.
--   * Dates the Act does not give (the day s 84 of the Small Business, Enterprise and Employment Act 2015 came into force; the
--     appointed day) are asked.

§ `Companies Act 2006, Parts 21 and 21A: your questions`

§§ `Share certificates (s 768)`

-- s 768(1): a certificate under the common seal is "prima facie evidence" of a member's title (a company registered in
-- England and Wales or Northern Ireland).
@export Under section 768(1), is my share certificate prima facie evidence of my title to the shares?
GIVEN `the place where the company is registered` IS A `Place of registration` @desc Where is the company registered? One of: England and Wales, Scotland, Northern Ireland
      `my certificate is under the common seal of the company` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is your share certificate under the company's common seal?
      `my certificate specifies shares I hold as a member` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does your certificate specify shares that you hold as a member of the company?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 768(1), is my share certificate prima facie evidence of my title to the shares` IS
    `s 768(1) the certificate is prima facie evidence of the member's title to the shares` `the place where the company is registered` `my certificate is under the common seal of the company` `my certificate specifies shares I hold as a member`

-- s 768(2): in Scotland a certificate under the common seal, or subscribed under the Requirements of Writing (Scotland)
-- Act 1995, is "sufficient evidence, unless the contrary is shown".
@export Under section 768(2), is my share certificate from a Scottish company sufficient evidence of my title to the shares?
GIVEN `the place where the company is registered` IS A `Place of registration` @desc Where is the company registered? One of: England and Wales, Scotland, Northern Ireland
      `my certificate is under the common seal of the company` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is your share certificate under the company's common seal?
      `my certificate is subscribed in accordance with the Requirements of Writing (Scotland) Act 1995` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is your certificate subscribed by the company in accordance with the Requirements of Writing (Scotland) Act 1995?
      `my certificate specifies shares I hold as a member` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does your certificate specify shares that you hold as a member of the company?
      `someone has shown that my title is not what the certificate says` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has anyone shown the contrary, that is, that you are not entitled to the shares as the certificate says?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 768(2), is my share certificate from a Scottish company sufficient evidence of my title to the shares` IS
    `s 768(2) the certificate is sufficient evidence of the member's title to the shares` `the place where the company is registered` `my certificate is under the common seal of the company` `my certificate is subscribed in accordance with the Requirements of Writing (Scotland) Act 1995` `my certificate specifies shares I hold as a member` `someone has shown that my title is not what the certificate says`

§§ `When shares, debentures or debenture stock are allotted to you (s 769)`

-- s 769(1), (2): within two months after an allotment the company must complete and have ready for delivery the
-- certificates (shares, debenture stock) or the debentures, unless a listed exception applies.
@export Under section 769(1), must the company have my certificates or debentures ready for delivery after the allotment?
GIVEN `what was allotted to me` IS A `s 769(1) what was allotted` @desc What was allotted? One of: s 769(1) shares allotted, s 769(1) debentures allotted, s 769(1) debenture stock allotted
      `the conditions of issue provide otherwise` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Do the conditions of issue of the shares, debentures or debenture stock provide that the company need not do so?
      `the allotment was to a financial institution` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Was the allotment to a financial institution (a recognised clearing house, a recognised central securities depository or a designated nominee)?
      `the company has issued a share warrant in respect of the shares` IS A BOOLEAN @desc If shares were allotted, has the company since issued a share warrant in respect of them?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 769(1), must the company have my certificates or debentures ready for delivery after the allotment` IS
    `s 769(1) the company must complete and have ready for delivery the documents` `my allotment`
    WHERE
        `my allotment` MEANS `s 769 allotment` WITH
            `s 769(1) the thing allotted` IS `what was allotted to me`
            -- Placeholder: the duty rule does not read the day of the allotment.
            `s 769(1) the day of the allotment` IS Date 1 1 2000
            `s 769(2)(a) the conditions of issue provide otherwise` IS `the conditions of issue provide otherwise`
            `s 769(2)(b) the allotment is to a financial institution` IS `the allotment was to a financial institution`
            `s 769(2)(c) the company has issued a share warrant in respect of the shares allotted` IS `the company has issued a share warrant in respect of the shares`

@export Under section 769(1), by what day must the company have my certificates or debentures ready for delivery?
GIVEN `the day of the allotment` IS A DATE @desc On what day were the shares, debentures or debenture stock allotted to you?
GIVETH A DATE
DECIDE `Under section 769(1), by what day must the company have my certificates or debentures ready for delivery` IS
    `s 769(1) the last day of the period of two months after the day` `the day of the allotment`

-- s 769(3): default, and the offence of every officer of the company who is in default.
@export Under section 769(3), is the company in default over my certificates or debentures?
GIVEN `what was allotted to me` IS A `s 769(1) what was allotted` @desc What was allotted? One of: s 769(1) shares allotted, s 769(1) debentures allotted, s 769(1) debenture stock allotted
      `the day of the allotment` IS A DATE @desc On what day were they allotted to you?
      `the conditions of issue provide otherwise` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Do the conditions of issue provide that the company need not have the documents ready?
      `the allotment was to a financial institution` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Was the allotment to a financial institution?
      `the company has issued a share warrant in respect of the shares` IS A BOOLEAN @desc If shares were allotted, has the company since issued a share warrant in respect of them?
      `the documents have been ready for delivery` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has the company completed the documents and had them ready for delivery?
      `the day they were ready` IS A DATE @desc If so, on what day were they ready? (Any date if not yet ready.)
      `the day on which you ask` IS A DATE @desc What is today's date?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 769(3), is the company in default over my certificates or debentures` IS
    `s 769(3) default is made in complying with subsection (1)` `my allotment` `when they were ready` `the day on which you ask`
    WHERE
        `my allotment` MEANS `s 769 allotment` WITH
            `s 769(1) the thing allotted` IS `what was allotted to me`
            `s 769(1) the day of the allotment` IS `the day of the allotment`
            `s 769(2)(a) the conditions of issue provide otherwise` IS `the conditions of issue provide otherwise`
            `s 769(2)(b) the allotment is to a financial institution` IS `the allotment was to a financial institution`
            `s 769(2)(c) the company has issued a share warrant in respect of the shares allotted` IS `the company has issued a share warrant in respect of the shares`
        `when they were ready` MEANS IF `the documents have been ready for delivery` THEN JUST `the day they were ready` ELSE NOTHING

@export Under section 769(3), do I commit an offence as an officer of the company over a default on the certificates or debentures?
GIVEN `the company is in default (answer of the question: Under section 769(3), is the company in default)` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the company in default over the certificates or debentures (it did not have them ready within two months after the allotment, and no exception applies)?
      `I am an officer of the company who is in default` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are you an officer of the company who is in default (section 1121)?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 769(3), do I commit an offence as an officer of the company over a default on the certificates or debentures` IS
    `s 769(3) an offence is committed by the officer of the company who is in default` (JUST `the company is in default (answer of the question: Under section 769(3), is the company in default)`) (JUST `I am an officer of the company who is in default`)

@export Under section 769(4), what is the most the company's officer can be fined on summary conviction, in pounds?
GIVEN `the pounds that level 3 on the standard scale stands for` IS A NUMBER @desc How many pounds does level 3 on the standard scale stand for?
GIVETH A MAYBE NUMBER
DECIDE `Under section 769(4), what is the most the company's officer can be fined on summary conviction, in pounds` IS
    CONSIDER `s 769(4) the penalty`'s `fine not exceeding`
    WHEN JUST (`a fine not exceeding a level on the standard scale` OF level, fraction) THEN JUST (`the pounds that level 3 on the standard scale stands for` TIMES fraction)
    OTHERWISE NOTHING

§§ `Transfers of securities (ss 770 to 775)`

@export Under section 770(1), is the company barred from registering my transfer?
GIVEN `a proper instrument of transfer has been delivered to the company` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has a proper instrument of transfer been delivered to the company?
      `the transfer is an exempt transfer within the Stock Transfer Act 1982` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the transfer an exempt transfer within the Stock Transfer Act 1982?
      `the transfer is in accordance with regulations under Chapter 2 of Part 21` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the transfer in accordance with regulations made under Chapter 2 of Part 21 (transfer without a written instrument)?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 770(1), is the company barred from registering my transfer` IS
    `s 770(1) the bar on registering the transfer applies` `a proper instrument of transfer has been delivered to the company` `the transfer is an exempt transfer within the Stock Transfer Act 1982` `the transfer is in accordance with regulations under Chapter 2 of Part 21`

@export Under section 770(2), does section 770(1) leave unaffected the company's power to register me as shareholder or debenture holder where the right passed to me by operation of law?
GIVEN `the right to the shares or debentures has been transmitted to me by operation of law` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has the right to the shares or debentures been transmitted to you by operation of law (for example on a death or bankruptcy)?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 770(2), does section 770(1) leave unaffected the company's power to register me as shareholder or debenture holder where the right passed to me by operation of law` IS
    `s 770(2) subsection (1) does not affect the company's power to register the person` `the right to the shares or debentures has been transmitted to me by operation of law`

-- s 771: when a transfer is lodged, the company must register it or give the transferee notice of refusal with reasons,
-- as soon as practicable and within two months.
@export Under section 771(1), must the company register my transfer or give me notice of refusal with its reasons?
GIVEN `the transfer is of shares and the company has issued a share warrant in respect of them` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the transfer of shares in respect of which the company has issued a share warrant?
      `the transfer is a transmission of shares or debentures by operation of law` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it a transmission of shares or debentures by operation of law rather than a transfer?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 771(1), must the company register my transfer or give me notice of refusal with its reasons` IS
    `s 771(1) the company must register the transfer or give the transferee notice of refusal` `my transfer`
    WHERE
        `my transfer` MEANS `s 771 lodged transfer` WITH
            -- Placeholder: the duty rule does not read the day of lodging.
            `s 771(1) the day the transfer was lodged` IS Date 1 1 2000
            `s 771(5)(a) the transfer is of shares and the company has issued a share warrant in respect of the shares` IS `the transfer is of shares and the company has issued a share warrant in respect of them`
            `s 771(5)(b) the transfer is a transmission of shares or debentures by operation of law` IS `the transfer is a transmission of shares or debentures by operation of law`

@export Under section 771(1), by what day must the company register my transfer or give me notice of refusal?
GIVEN `the day my transfer was lodged with the company` IS A DATE @desc On what day was the transfer lodged with the company?
GIVETH A DATE
DECIDE `Under section 771(1), by what day must the company register my transfer or give me notice of refusal` IS
    `s 769(1) the last day of the period of two months after the day` `the day my transfer was lodged with the company`

@export Under section 771(1), has the company complied with its duty on my lodged transfer?
GIVEN `the transfer is of shares and the company has issued a share warrant in respect of them` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the transfer of shares in respect of which the company has issued a share warrant?
      `the transfer is a transmission of shares or debentures by operation of law` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it a transmission of shares or debentures by operation of law rather than a transfer?
      `the day my transfer was lodged with the company` IS A DATE @desc On what day was the transfer lodged with the company?
      `what the company did` IS A `s 771(1) what the company did with the lodged transfer` @desc What has the company done? One of: s 771(1)(a) registered the transfer, s 771(1)(b) gave the transferee notice of refusal with its reasons, s 771(1) did neither
      `the day it did so` IS A DATE @desc On what day did it do so? (Any date if it has done neither.)
      `it did so as soon as practicable` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did the company do it as soon as practicable?
      `the day on which you ask` IS A DATE @desc What is today's date?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 771(1), has the company complied with its duty on my lodged transfer` IS
    `s 771(1) the company has complied with subsection (1)` `my transfer` `what the company did` `the day it did so` `it did so as soon as practicable` `the day on which you ask`
    WHERE
        `my transfer` MEANS `s 771 lodged transfer` WITH
            `s 771(1) the day the transfer was lodged` IS `the day my transfer was lodged with the company`
            `s 771(5)(a) the transfer is of shares and the company has issued a share warrant in respect of the shares` IS `the transfer is of shares and the company has issued a share warrant in respect of them`
            `s 771(5)(b) the transfer is a transmission of shares or debentures by operation of law` IS `the transfer is a transmission of shares or debentures by operation of law`

@export Under section 771(1A), is the company barred from registering my transfer until it has the information for its register of members?
GIVEN `the company is satisfied that it has the information it must enter in its register of members about me as transferee` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the company satisfied that it has the information that it is required to enter in its register of members about the transferee?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 771(1A), is the company barred from registering my transfer until it has the information for its register of members` IS
    `s 771(1A) the bar on registering the transfer under subsection (1)(a) applies` `the company is satisfied that it has the information it must enter in its register of members about me as transferee`

@export Under section 771(2), must the company give me further information about its reasons for refusing to register my transfer?
GIVEN `the company has refused to register my transfer` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has the company refused to register the transfer?
      `my request for further information is one I may reasonably make` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the further information you ask for something you may reasonably request?
      `I am asking for copies of minutes of meetings of directors` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are you asking for copies of minutes of meetings of directors?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 771(2), must the company give me further information about its reasons for refusing to register my transfer` IS
    `s 771(2) the company must provide the transferee with the further information requested` `the company has refused to register my transfer` `my request for further information is one I may reasonably make` `I am asking for copies of minutes of meetings of directors`

@export Under section 771(3), do I commit an offence as an officer of the company that fails to deal with a lodged transfer?
GIVEN `the company has failed to comply with section 771` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has the company failed to comply with section 771 (it neither registered the transfer nor gave notice of refusal with reasons in time, or did not give the further information)?
      `I am an officer of the company who is in default` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are you an officer of the company who is in default (section 1121)?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 771(3), do I commit an offence as an officer of the company that fails to deal with a lodged transfer` IS
    `s 771(3)(b) an offence is committed by the officer of the company who is in default` (JUST `the company has failed to comply with section 771`) (JUST `I am an officer of the company who is in default`)

@export Under section 772, must the company enter the transferee's name in its register of members on my application as transferor?
GIVEN `I as transferor of a share or interest have applied to the company` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Have you, as transferor of a share or interest in the company, applied to the company to enter the transferee's name?
      `the conditions that would apply to the transferee's own application are met` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Would the conditions on which the company enters a name on the transferee's own application be met?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 772, must the company enter the transferee's name in its register of members on my application as transferor` IS
    `s 772 the company must enter the name of the transferee in its register of members` `I as transferor of a share or interest have applied to the company` `the conditions that would apply to the transferee's own application are met`

@export Under section 773(a), may I, as personal representative of a deceased member, make the instrument of transfer although I am not a member?
GIVEN `the instrument is of the share or other interest of a deceased member` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the instrument of transfer of the share or other interest of a deceased member of the company?
      `I am the personal representative of the deceased member and made it` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are you the deceased member's personal representative, and did you make the instrument?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 773(a), may I, as personal representative of a deceased member, make the instrument of transfer although I am not a member` IS
    `s 773(a) the personal representative may make the instrument of transfer although not a member` `the instrument is of the share or other interest of a deceased member` `I am the personal representative of the deceased member and made it`

@export Under section 774, must the company accept my grant of probate as sufficient evidence of the grant?
GIVEN `the grant my document evidences` IS A `s 774 grant` @desc What does the document evidence? One of: s 774(a) probate of the will of a deceased person, s 774(b) letters of administration of the estate of a deceased person, s 774(c) confirmation as executor of a deceased person, s 774 some other grant
      `the document is by law sufficient evidence of the grant` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the document one that is by law sufficient evidence of the grant?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 774, must the company accept my grant of probate as sufficient evidence of the grant` IS
    `s 774 the company must accept the document as sufficient evidence of the grant` `the grant my document evidences` `the document is by law sufficient evidence of the grant`

-- s 775: a company's certification of an instrument of transfer.
@export Under section 775(1), is the company's certification of my instrument of transfer a representation that documents showing a prima facie title have been produced?
GIVEN `the person who issued the instrument was authorised to issue certificated instruments of transfer on the company's behalf` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Was the person issuing the instrument authorised to issue certificated instruments of transfer on the company's behalf?
      `the certification was signed by a person authorised to certificate transfers on the company's behalf` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Was the certification signed by a person authorised to certificate transfers on the company's behalf?
      `the certification was signed by an officer or employee of the company or of a body corporate so authorised` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Was it signed by an officer or employee of the company or of a body corporate so authorised?
      `I acted on the faith of the certification` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did you act on the faith of the certification?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 775(1), is the company's certification of my instrument of transfer a representation that documents showing a prima facie title have been produced` IS
    `s 775(1) the certification is taken as a representation that documents showing a prima facie title in the transferor have been produced` (`s 775(4)(b) the certification of the instrument of transfer is made by the company` `the person who issued the instrument was authorised to issue certificated instruments of transfer on the company's behalf` `the certification was signed by a person authorised to certificate transfers on the company's behalf` `the certification was signed by an officer or employee of the company or of a body corporate so authorised` EQUALS JUST TRUE) `I acted on the faith of the certification`

@export Under section 775(3), is the company as liable to me for a negligent false certification as if it had acted fraudulently?
GIVEN `I acted on the faith of a false certification by the company` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did you act on the faith of a false certification by the company?
      `the company made the certification negligently` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did the company make the false certification negligently?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 775(3), is the company as liable to me for a negligent false certification as if it had acted fraudulently` IS
    `s 775(3) the company is under the same liability to the person as if the certification had been made fraudulently` `I acted on the faith of a false certification by the company` `the company made the certification negligently`

@export Under section 775(4)(a), is my instrument of transfer certificated?
GIVEN `the instrument bears the words "certificate lodged" or words to the like effect` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does the instrument of transfer bear the words "certificate lodged" or words to the like effect?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 775(4)(a), is my instrument of transfer certificated` IS
    `s 775(4)(a) the instrument of transfer is certificated` `the instrument bears the words "certificate lodged" or words to the like effect`

§§ `When shares, debentures or debenture stock are transferred to you (ss 776 to 778)`

@export Under section 776(1), must the company have my certificates or debentures ready for delivery after my transfer was lodged?
GIVEN `what was transferred` IS A `s 776(1) what was transferred` @desc What was transferred? One of: s 776(1) shares transferred, s 776(1) debentures transferred, s 776(1) debenture stock transferred
      `the transfer is duly stamped and otherwise valid` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the transfer duly stamped and otherwise valid?
      `the transfer is an exempt transfer within the Stock Transfer Act 1982` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it an exempt transfer within the Stock Transfer Act 1982?
      `the company is entitled to refuse to register it and does not register it` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the company entitled to refuse to register the transfer, and has it not registered it?
      `the conditions of issue provide otherwise` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Do the conditions of issue provide that the company need not do so?
      `the transfer is to a financial institution` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the transfer to a financial institution?
      `the company has issued a share warrant in respect of the shares` IS A BOOLEAN @desc If shares were transferred, has the company since issued a share warrant in respect of them?
      `the transferee is not entitled to a certificate under regulations made under section 3 of the Stock Transfer Act 1982` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the transferee not entitled to a certificate by virtue of regulations under section 3 of the Stock Transfer Act 1982?
      `the transferee has since become entitled to a certificate` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has the transferee since become entitled to a certificate under those regulations?
      `the transferee gave the company written notice of that` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has the transferee given the company notice in writing that they have become entitled?
      `the day of that notice` IS A DATE @desc On what day was that notice given? (Any date if none.)
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 776(1), must the company have my certificates or debentures ready for delivery after my transfer was lodged` IS
    `s 776(1) the company must complete and have ready for delivery the documents` `my transfer`
    WHERE
        `my transfer` MEANS `s 776 lodged transfer` WITH
            `s 776(1) the thing transferred` IS `what was transferred`
            -- Placeholder: the duty rule does not read the day of lodging.
            `s 776(1) the day the transfer was lodged` IS Date 1 1 2000
            `s 776(2)(a) the transfer is duly stamped and otherwise valid` IS `the transfer is duly stamped and otherwise valid`
            `s 776(2)(b) the transfer is an exempt transfer within the Stock Transfer Act 1982` IS `the transfer is an exempt transfer within the Stock Transfer Act 1982`
            `s 776(2) the company is entitled to refuse to register the transfer and does not register it` IS `the company is entitled to refuse to register it and does not register it`
            `s 776(3)(a) the conditions of issue provide otherwise` IS `the conditions of issue provide otherwise`
            `s 776(3)(b) the transfer is to a financial institution` IS `the transfer is to a financial institution`
            `s 776(3)(c) the company has issued a share warrant in respect of the shares transferred` IS `the company has issued a share warrant in respect of the shares`
            `s 777(1) the transferee is not entitled to a certificate by virtue of regulations under section 3 of the Stock Transfer Act 1982` IS `the transferee is not entitled to a certificate under regulations made under section 3 of the Stock Transfer Act 1982`
            `s 777(2)(a) the transferee has since become entitled to a certificate by virtue of a provision of those regulations` IS `the transferee has since become entitled to a certificate`
            `s 777(2)(b) the day on which the transferee gave the company notice in writing of that fact` IS IF `the transferee gave the company written notice of that` THEN JUST `the day of that notice` ELSE NOTHING

@export Under section 776(1), by what day must the company have my certificates or debentures ready for delivery?
GIVEN `the day my transfer was lodged with the company` IS A DATE @desc On what day was the transfer lodged with the company?
      `the transferee is not entitled to a certificate under regulations made under section 3 of the Stock Transfer Act 1982` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Was the transferee not entitled to a certificate by virtue of regulations under section 3 of the Stock Transfer Act 1982?
      `the transferee has since become entitled to a certificate` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has the transferee since become entitled to a certificate under those regulations?
      `the transferee gave the company written notice of that` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has the transferee given the company notice in writing that they have become entitled?
      `the day of that notice` IS A DATE @desc On what day was that notice given? (Any date if none.)
GIVETH A DATE
DECIDE `Under section 776(1), by what day must the company have my certificates or debentures ready for delivery` IS
    `s 776(1) the last day for completing the documents and having them ready for delivery` `my transfer`
    WHERE
        `my transfer` MEANS `s 776 lodged transfer` WITH
            -- Placeholder: the period rule does not read the kind of thing transferred.
            `s 776(1) the thing transferred` IS `s 776(1) shares transferred`
            `s 776(1) the day the transfer was lodged` IS `the day my transfer was lodged with the company`
            -- Placeholders: the period rule does not read subsection (2) or (3) facts.
            `s 776(2)(a) the transfer is duly stamped and otherwise valid` IS TRUE
            `s 776(2)(b) the transfer is an exempt transfer within the Stock Transfer Act 1982` IS FALSE
            `s 776(2) the company is entitled to refuse to register the transfer and does not register it` IS FALSE
            `s 776(3)(a) the conditions of issue provide otherwise` IS FALSE
            `s 776(3)(b) the transfer is to a financial institution` IS FALSE
            `s 776(3)(c) the company has issued a share warrant in respect of the shares transferred` IS FALSE
            `s 777(1) the transferee is not entitled to a certificate by virtue of regulations under section 3 of the Stock Transfer Act 1982` IS `the transferee is not entitled to a certificate under regulations made under section 3 of the Stock Transfer Act 1982`
            `s 777(2)(a) the transferee has since become entitled to a certificate by virtue of a provision of those regulations` IS `the transferee has since become entitled to a certificate`
            `s 777(2)(b) the day on which the transferee gave the company notice in writing of that fact` IS IF `the transferee gave the company written notice of that` THEN JUST `the day of that notice` ELSE NOTHING

@export Under section 776(5), do I commit an offence as an officer of the company that is in default over certificates or debentures on a transfer?
GIVEN `the company is in default over the certificates or debentures on the transfer` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the company in default (it did not have the documents ready within two months after the transfer was lodged, and no exception applies)?
      `I am an officer of the company who is in default` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are you an officer of the company who is in default (section 1121)?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 776(5), do I commit an offence as an officer of the company that is in default over certificates or debentures on a transfer` IS
    `s 776(5) an offence is committed by the officer of the company who is in default` (JUST `the company is in default over the certificates or debentures on the transfer`) (JUST `I am an officer of the company who is in default`)

@export Under section 778(2), is the person a financial institution for the purposes of sections 769 and 776?
GIVEN `the person is a recognised clearing house or recognised CSD acting in relation to a recognised investment exchange` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the person a recognised clearing house, or a recognised central securities depository, acting in relation to a recognised investment exchange (Part 18 of the Financial Services and Markets Act 2000)?
      `the person is a nominee of a recognised clearing house or recognised CSD acting in that way` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the person a nominee of such a clearing house or depository?
      `the person is a nominee of a recognised investment exchange` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the person a nominee of a recognised investment exchange?
      `the person is designated for these purposes in the rules of the exchange` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the nominee designated for the purposes of section 778 in the rules of the recognised investment exchange in question?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 778(2), is the person a financial institution for the purposes of sections 769 and 776` IS
    `s 778(2) the person is a financial institution` `the person is a recognised clearing house or recognised CSD acting in relation to a recognised investment exchange` `the person is a nominee of a recognised clearing house or recognised CSD acting in that way` `the person is a nominee of a recognised investment exchange` `the person is designated for these purposes in the rules of the exchange`

§§ `Share warrants (ss 779 and 781)`

@export Under section 779(1), may the company issue me a share warrant for my fully paid shares?
GIVEN `the liability of the company's members` IS A `Liability of members` @desc How is the members' liability limited? One of: liability not limited, liability limited to the amount, if any, unpaid on the shares held, liability limited to the amount the members undertake to contribute on a winding up, liability limited in some other way by the constitution
      `the articles authorise share warrants` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Do the company's articles authorise it to issue share warrants?
      `my shares are fully paid` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are the shares in question fully paid?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 779(1), may the company issue me a share warrant for my fully paid shares` IS
    `s 779(1) the company may issue a share warrant` `the liability of the company's members` `the articles authorise share warrants` `my shares are fully paid`

@export Under section 779(4), is the company barred from issuing a share warrant?
GIVEN `the day the warrant would be issued` IS A DATE @desc On what day would the share warrant be issued?
      `the day section 84 of the Small Business, Enterprise and Employment Act 2015 came into force` IS A DATE @desc On what day did section 84 of the Small Business, Enterprise and Employment Act 2015 come into force? (The Act does not give it.)
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 779(4), is the company barred from issuing a share warrant` IS
    `s 779(4) the bar on issuing a share warrant applies` `the day the warrant would be issued` `the day section 84 of the Small Business, Enterprise and Employment Act 2015 came into force`

@export Under section 779(2), does a share warrant entitle me, as bearer, to the shares specified in it?
GIVEN `the place where the company is registered` IS A `Place of registration` @desc Where is the company registered? One of: England and Wales, Scotland, Northern Ireland
      `the warrant is issued under the company's common seal` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the share warrant issued under the company's common seal?
      `the warrant is subscribed in accordance with the Requirements of Writing (Scotland) Act 1995` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it subscribed in accordance with the Requirements of Writing (Scotland) Act 1995?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 779(2), does a share warrant entitle me, as bearer, to the shares specified in it` IS
    `s 779(2) the share warrant entitles the bearer to the shares specified in it` `the place where the company is registered` `the warrant is issued under the company's common seal` `the warrant is subscribed in accordance with the Requirements of Writing (Scotland) Act 1995`

@export Under section 781(1), do I commit an offence in Scotland by forging or using a forged share warrant or coupon?
GIVEN `I acted in Scotland` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did you act in Scotland?
      `I acted with intent to defraud` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did you act with intent to defraud?
      `I forged or altered a share warrant or coupon, or a document purporting to be one` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did you forge or alter a share warrant or coupon, or a document purporting to be one issued under the Act?
      `I offered, uttered, disposed of or put off such a document` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did you offer, utter, dispose of or put off such a document?
      `I knew that document to be forged or altered` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did you know it to be forged or altered?
      `I acted by means of a forged or altered warrant, coupon or document` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did you act by means of a forged or altered share warrant, coupon or document?
      `I demanded or endeavoured to obtain a share or interest` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did you demand or endeavour to obtain or receive a share or interest in a company under the Act by that means?
      `I demanded or endeavoured to receive a dividend or money payment` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did you demand or endeavour to receive a dividend or money payment in respect of such a share or interest by that means?
      `I knew the warrant, coupon or document I used to be forged or altered` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did you know the warrant, coupon or document you used to be forged or altered?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 781(1), do I commit an offence in Scotland by forging or using a forged share warrant or coupon` IS
    `s 781(1) the person commits an offence` `I acted in Scotland` `I acted with intent to defraud` `I forged or altered a share warrant or coupon, or a document purporting to be one` `I offered, uttered, disposed of or put off such a document` `I knew that document to be forged or altered` `I acted by means of a forged or altered warrant, coupon or document` `I demanded or endeavoured to obtain a share or interest` `I demanded or endeavoured to receive a dividend or money payment` `I knew the warrant, coupon or document I used to be forged or altered`

§§ `When a company does not make good a default (s 782)`

@export Under section 782(1), may I apply to the court because the company has not made good its default on my certificates or debentures?
GIVEN `the default the notice required the company to make good` IS A `s 782(1) the default the notice requires the company to make good` @desc Which default did your notice require the company to make good? One of: s 782(1)(a) default in complying with section 769(1), s 782(1)(b) default in complying with section 776(1), s 782(1)(c) default in complying with section 780(1), s 782(1) some other default
      `the day the notice was served on the company` IS A DATE @desc On what day was your notice served on the company?
      `the company has made good the default` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has the company made good the default?
      `the day it made good the default` IS A DATE @desc If so, on what day? (Any date if not.)
      `I am the person entitled to have the certificates or debentures delivered to me` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are you the person entitled to have the certificates or the debentures delivered to you?
      `the day on which you ask` IS A DATE @desc What is today's date?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 782(1), may I apply to the court because the company has not made good its default on my certificates or debentures` IS
    `s 782(1) the person may apply to the court` `the default the notice required the company to make good` `the day the notice was served on the company` `when it made good` `the day on which you ask` `I am the person entitled to have the certificates or debentures delivered to me`
    WHERE
        `when it made good` MEANS IF `the company has made good the default` THEN JUST `the day it made good the default` ELSE NOTHING

@export Under section 782(1), by what day must the company make good the default after my notice was served?
GIVEN `the day the notice was served on the company` IS A DATE @desc On what day was your notice served on the company?
GIVETH A DATE
DECIDE `Under section 782(1), by what day must the company make good the default after my notice was served` IS
    `s 782(1) the last day for making good the default` `the day the notice was served on the company`

§§ `Securities without a written instrument (ss 783 to 790)`

@export Under section 783(a), is my holding a security for the purposes of Chapter 2 of Part 21?
GIVEN `what I hold` IS A `s 783(a) kind of instrument` @desc What do you hold? One of: s 783(a) shares, s 783(a) debentures, s 783(a) debenture stock, s 783(a) loan stock, s 783(a) bonds, s 783(a) units of a collective investment scheme within the meaning of the Financial Services and Markets Act 2000, s 783(a) an instrument of some other kind
      `it is a security of some other description` IS A BOOLEAN @desc If it is an instrument of some other kind, is it a security of any description?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 783(a), is my holding a security for the purposes of Chapter 2 of Part 21` IS
    `s 783(a) the instrument is a security for the purposes of this Chapter` `what I hold` `it is a security of some other description`

@export Under section 790, does Chapter 3 of Part 3 apply to the resolution I passed by virtue of regulations under Chapter 2 of Part 21?
GIVEN `the resolution was passed by virtue of regulations under Chapter 2 of Part 21` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Was the resolution passed by virtue of regulations made under Chapter 2 of Part 21?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 790, does Chapter 3 of Part 3 apply to the resolution I passed by virtue of regulations under Chapter 2 of Part 21` IS
    `s 790 Chapter 3 of Part 3 applies to the resolution` `the resolution was passed by virtue of regulations under Chapter 2 of Part 21`

§§ `Whether Part 21A (people with significant control) applies (ss 790B and 790C)`

@export Under section 790B(1), does Part 21A apply to my company?
GIVEN `the company has voting shares admitted to trading on a UK regulated market` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does the company have voting shares admitted to trading on a UK regulated market?
      `the company has voting shares admitted to trading on an EU regulated market` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does the company have voting shares admitted to trading on an EU regulated market?
      `the company is of a description specified by the Secretary of State by regulations` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the company of a description the Secretary of State has specified by regulations under section 790B?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 790B(1), does Part 21A apply to my company` IS
    `s 790B(1) this Part applies to the company` `the company has voting shares admitted to trading on a UK regulated market` `the company has voting shares admitted to trading on an EU regulated market` `the company is of a description specified by the Secretary of State by regulations`

@export Under section 790C(2), do I have significant control over the company?
GIVEN `I am an individual, or am read as one by section 790C(12)` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are you an individual (or one of the persons section 790C(12) reads as an individual)?
      `I meet at least one of the specified conditions in Part 1 of Schedule 1A` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Do you meet at least one of the specified conditions in Part 1 of Schedule 1A (more than 25% of the shares or voting rights, the right to appoint or remove a majority of the board, significant influence or control, or control of a trust or firm)?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 790C(2), do I have significant control over the company` IS
    `s 790C(2) the person has significant control over the company` `I am an individual, or am read as one by section 790C(12)` (JUST `I meet at least one of the specified conditions in Part 1 of Schedule 1A`)

@export Under section 790C(4), am I a registrable person, rather than a non-registrable individual, in relation to the company?
GIVEN `I meet at least one of the specified conditions in Part 1 of Schedule 1A` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Do you meet at least one of the specified conditions in Part 1 of Schedule 1A?
      `I hold an interest in the company directly, not only through legal entities` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Do you hold any interest in the company otherwise than through legal entities (determined under Part 2 of Schedule 1A)?
      `I hold my interest through a legal entity` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Do you hold an interest in the company through a legal entity?
      `I have significant control over that legal entity` IS A BOOLEAN @desc If so, do you have significant control over that legal entity (the specified conditions read with that entity as the company)?
      `I hold it through a chain of entities (paragraph 9(1)(b)(ii))` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Do you hold the interest through a chain of legal entities (paragraph 9(1)(b)(ii) of Schedule 1A), rather than through one entity (paragraph 9(1)(b)(i))?
      `that entity, or one in the chain, is a relevant legal entity` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the entity through which you hold it (or, for a chain, at least one entity in the chain) a relevant legal entity in relation to the company?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 790C(4), am I a registrable person, rather than a non-registrable individual, in relation to the company` IS
    `s 790C(4) the individual is a registrable person`
        (`s 790C(2) the person has significant control over the company` TRUE (JUST `I meet at least one of the specified conditions in Part 1 of Schedule 1A`))
        (`s 790C(4)(b) the individual with significant control is registrable` `I hold an interest in the company directly, not only through legal entities` `my holdings`)
    WHERE
        `my holdings` MEANS
            IF `I hold my interest through a legal entity`
            THEN LIST `my holding`
            ELSE EMPTY
        `my holding` MEANS `s 790C(4) holding through a legal entity` WITH
            `s 790C(4)(a) significant control over the legal entity (see s 790C(9)(b))` IS JUST `I have significant control over that legal entity`
            `s 790C(4)(a) how the shares or right are held indirectly` IS IF `I hold it through a chain of entities (paragraph 9(1)(b)(ii))` THEN `s 790C(4)(a)(ii) as described in paragraph 9(1)(b)(ii) of Schedule 1A` ELSE `s 790C(4)(a)(i) as described in paragraph 9(1)(b)(i) of Schedule 1A`
            `s 790C(4)(a)(i) the legal entity through which the shares or right are held is a relevant legal entity in relation to the company` IS JUST `that entity, or one in the chain, is a relevant legal entity`
            `s 790C(4)(a)(ii) at least one of the legal entities in the chain is a relevant legal entity in relation to the company` IS JUST `that entity, or one in the chain, is a relevant legal entity`

@export Under section 790C(7), is the legal entity subject to its own disclosure requirements?
GIVEN `Part 21A applies to the legal entity` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does Part 21A apply to the legal entity (a UK company that is not listed on a UK or EU regulated market and not of a specified description)?
      `it is an eligible Scottish partnership` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it an eligible Scottish partnership within regulation 3(2) of the Scottish Partnerships (Register of People with Significant Control) Regulations 2017?
      `it has voting shares admitted to trading on a UK or EU regulated market` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does it have voting shares admitted to trading on a UK regulated market or an EU regulated market?
      `it is of a description specified in regulations under section 790B` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it of a description specified in regulations under section 790B?
      `it is of a description specified by the Secretary of State under section 790C(7)(d)` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it of a description specified by the Secretary of State by regulations under section 790C(7)(d)?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 790C(7), is the legal entity subject to its own disclosure requirements` IS
    `s 790C(7) the legal entity is subject to its own disclosure requirements` (JUST `Part 21A applies to the legal entity`) `it is an eligible Scottish partnership` `it has voting shares admitted to trading on a UK or EU regulated market` `it is of a description specified in regulations under section 790B` `it is of a description specified by the Secretary of State under section 790C(7)(d)`

@export Under section 790CA, has the company had confirmation of the information I have supplied?
GIVEN `I have supplied the information to the company` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Have you supplied that information to the company (whether or not because this Part required it)?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 790CA, has the company had confirmation of the information I have supplied` IS
    `s 790CA the company has had confirmation of the information` `I have supplied the information to the company`

§§ `Finding out about people with significant control: duties on companies (ss 790CB to 790F)`

@export Under section 790CB, must my company take reasonable steps to find out who its people with significant control are?
GIVEN `my company is one to which Part 21A applies` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does Part 21A apply to your company? (It does not if its voting shares are admitted to trading on a UK or EU regulated market, or it is of a description the Secretary of State has specified.)
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 790CB, must my company take reasonable steps to find out who its people with significant control are` IS
    `s 790CB the company must take reasonable steps to find out if there is anyone who is a registrable person or a registrable relevant legal entity and, if so, to identify them` (JUST `my company is one to which Part 21A applies`)

@export Under section 790D(1), must my company give a notice to a person it believes has significant control?
GIVEN `my company is one to which Part 21A applies` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does Part 21A apply to your company?
      `the company knows or has cause to believe the person is a registrable person or registrable relevant legal entity` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does the company know, or have cause to believe, that the person is a registrable person or a registrable relevant legal entity?
      `the company has had confirmation of the person's status` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has the company had confirmation of the person's status?
      `the company has had confirmation of all the required particulars` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has the company had confirmation of all of the person's required particulars?
      `the incorporation statement named the person` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did the application to register the company contain a statement of initial significant control naming the person?
      `the company has no cause to believe the person has since ceased` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has the company no cause to believe the person has ceased to be a registrable person or registrable relevant legal entity since incorporation?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 790D(1), must my company give a notice to a person it believes has significant control` IS
    `s 790D(1) the company must give a notice to the person` (JUST `my company is one to which Part 21A applies`) `the company knows or has cause to believe the person is a registrable person or registrable relevant legal entity` `the company has had confirmation of the person's status` `the company has had confirmation of all the required particulars` `the incorporation statement named the person` `the company has no cause to believe the person has since ceased`

@export Under section 790D(3), by what day must I answer the company's notice to me?
GIVEN `the day the company gave me the notice` IS A DATE @desc On what day did the company give you the notice?
GIVETH A DATE
DECIDE `Under section 790D(3), by what day must I answer the company's notice to me` IS
    `s 790D(3) the last day for the person to comply with the notice` `the day the company gave me the notice`

@export Under section 790D(4), by what day must the company give the notice, after it becomes subject to the duty?
GIVEN `the day the company became subject to the duty` IS A DATE @desc On what day did the company become subject to the duty to give a notice?
GIVETH A DATE
DECIDE `Under section 790D(4), by what day must the company give the notice, after it becomes subject to the duty` IS
    `s 790D(4)(b) the last day for the company to give the notice` `the day the company became subject to the duty`

@export Under section 790DA(3), must my company give a notice to a third party who may know who a person with significant control is?
GIVEN `my company is one to which Part 21A applies` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does Part 21A apply to your company?
      `the company believes a person is a registrable person or registrable relevant legal entity` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does the company know, or have cause to believe, that a person is a registrable person or registrable relevant legal entity?
      `the company must give that person a notice under section 790D but cannot contact them` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the company under a duty to give that person a notice under section 790D but without the information it needs to contact them?
      `the third party knows who that person is` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does the company know, or have cause to believe, that the third party knows the identity of that person?
      `the third party knows someone likely to know who that person is` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does the company know, or have cause to believe, that the third party knows someone likely to have that knowledge?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 790DA(3), must my company give a notice to a third party who may know who a person with significant control is` IS
    `s 790DA(3) the company must give a notice to the third party` (JUST `my company is one to which Part 21A applies`) `the company believes a person is a registrable person or registrable relevant legal entity` `the company must give that person a notice under section 790D but cannot contact them` `the third party knows who that person is` `the third party knows someone likely to know who that person is`

@export Under section 790DA(6), am I not required by the company's notice to disclose information in respect of which a claim to legal professional privilege could be maintained?
GIVEN `a claim to legal professional privilege (in Scotland, confidentiality of communications) could be maintained` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Could a claim to legal professional privilege (in Scotland, to confidentiality of communications) be maintained in legal proceedings in respect of the information?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 790DA(6), am I not required by the company's notice to disclose information in respect of which a claim to legal professional privilege could be maintained` IS
    `s 790DA(6) the person is not required by the notice to disclose the information` `a claim to legal professional privilege (in Scotland, confidentiality of communications) could be maintained`

@export Under section 790E, must my company give a person a notice about a change in their particulars?
GIVEN `my company is one to which Part 21A applies` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does Part 21A apply to your company?
      `the company knows or has cause to believe there has been a change` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does the company know, or have cause to believe, that there has been a change in the required particulars of a registrable person or registrable relevant legal entity?
      `the company has not had confirmation that the change has occurred` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has the company not yet had confirmation that the change has occurred?
      `the company lacks confirmation of all the information for its notice of the change` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does the company lack confirmation of all the information it would need for a notice of the change to the registrar?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 790E, must my company give a person a notice about a change in their particulars` IS
    `s 790E(2) the company must give the person a notice` (`s 790E(1) this section applies to the company` (JUST `my company is one to which Part 21A applies`) `the company knows or has cause to believe there has been a change` `the company has not had confirmation that the change has occurred` `the company lacks confirmation of all the information for its notice of the change`)

@export Under section 790EA, must my company give a person a notice about ceasing to be a person with significant control?
GIVEN `my company is one to which Part 21A applies` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does Part 21A apply to your company?
      `the company knows or has cause to believe the person has ceased` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does the company know, or have cause to believe, that a person has ceased to be a registrable person or registrable relevant legal entity?
      `the company has not had confirmation that the person has ceased` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has the company not yet had confirmation that the person has ceased?
      `the company has not had confirmation of the date the person ceased` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has the company not yet had confirmation of the date on which the person ceased?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 790EA, must my company give a person a notice about ceasing to be a person with significant control` IS
    `s 790EA(2) the company must give the person a notice` (`s 790EA(1) this section applies to the company` (JUST `my company is one to which Part 21A applies`) `the company knows or has cause to believe the person has ceased` `the company has not had confirmation that the person has ceased` `the company has not had confirmation of the date the person ceased`)

@export Under section 790EB(1), must my company notify the registrar that a person has not answered its notice?
GIVEN `my company is one to which Part 21A applies` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does Part 21A apply to your company?
      `a person has failed to comply with the company's notice in time` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has a person failed to comply with a notice the company gave under section 790D, 790DA, 790E or 790EA within the period the notice specified?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 790EB(1), must my company notify the registrar that a person has not answered its notice` IS
    `s 790EB(1) the company must notify the registrar of the failure to comply with the notice` (JUST `my company is one to which Part 21A applies`) `a person has failed to comply with the company's notice in time`

@export Under section 790EB(2), by what day must my company tell the registrar that a person has not answered its notice?
GIVEN `the day the period specified in the company's notice ended` IS A DATE @desc On what day did the period specified in the company's notice end?
GIVETH A DATE
DECIDE `Under section 790EB(2), by what day must my company tell the registrar that a person has not answered its notice` IS
    `s 790EB(2) the last day for the company to give the notice to the registrar` `the day the period specified in the company's notice ended`

@export Under section 790EC(2), by what day must my company tell the registrar that a person has since complied with its notice?
GIVEN `the day the person complied with the company's notice` IS A DATE @desc On what day did the person comply with the company's notice, after the period had ended?
GIVETH A DATE
DECIDE `Under section 790EC(2), by what day must my company tell the registrar that a person has since complied with its notice` IS
    `s 790EC(2) the last day for the company to give the notice to the registrar` `the day the person complied with the company's notice`

@export Under section 790F(1), does my company commit an offence by failing to comply with an information duty?
GIVEN `the duty` IS A `s 790F(1) duty` @desc Which duty? One of: s 790F(1) the duty under section 790CB, s 790F(1) the duty under section 790D, s 790F(1) the duty under section 790DA(3), s 790F(1) the duty under section 790E, s 790F(1) the duty under section 790EA, s 790F(1) the duty under section 790EB, s 790F(1) the duty under section 790EC, s 790F(1) the duty under section 790ED, s 790F(1) the duty under section 790EE, s 790F(1) the duty under section 790EF, s 790F(1) another duty
      `the company failed to comply with the duty` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did the company fail to take the steps or give the notice that the duty requires?
      `the company has a reasonable excuse` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does the company have a reasonable excuse for the failure?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 790F(1), does my company commit an offence by failing to comply with an information duty` IS
    `s 790F(1)(a) an offence is committed by the company` `the duty` `the company failed to comply with the duty` `the company has a reasonable excuse`

@export Under section 790F(1), do I commit an offence as an officer of a company that fails to comply with an information duty?
GIVEN `the company commits an offence under section 790F(1)` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does the company commit an offence under section 790F(1) (it failed, without reasonable excuse, to comply with one of the listed information duties)?
      `I am an officer of the company who is in default` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are you an officer of the company who is in default (section 1121)?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 790F(1), do I commit an offence as an officer of a company that fails to comply with an information duty` IS
    `s 790F(1)(b) an offence is committed by the officer of the company who is in default` (JUST `the company commits an offence under section 790F(1)`) (JUST `I am an officer of the company who is in default`)

@export Under section 790F(2), what is the longest term of imprisonment on conviction of an information-duty offence, in months?
GIVEN `how I am convicted` IS A `Mode of conviction` @desc How is the person convicted? One of: on conviction on indictment, on summary conviction in England and Wales, on summary conviction in Scotland, on summary conviction in Northern Ireland
GIVETH A MAYBE NUMBER
DECIDE `Under section 790F(2), what is the longest term of imprisonment on conviction of an information-duty offence, in months` IS
    CONSIDER `s 790F(2) the penalty` `how I am convicted`
    WHEN JUST penalty THEN
        CONSIDER penalty's `imprisonment not exceeding`
        WHEN JUST period THEN
            CONSIDER period's unit
            WHEN Years THEN JUST (period's `number of units` TIMES 12)
            WHEN Months THEN JUST (period's `number of units`)
            OTHERWISE NOTHING
        WHEN NOTHING THEN NOTHING
    WHEN NOTHING THEN NOTHING

§§ `Your own duties as a person with significant control (ss 790G to 790K)`

@export Under section 790G, must I tell the company that I am a person with significant control over it?
GIVEN `the company is one to which Part 21A applies` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does Part 21A apply to the company?
      `I know that I am a registrable person or registrable relevant legal entity` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Do you know that you are a registrable person (or a registrable relevant legal entity) in relation to the company?
      `the public register indicates my status` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does the material in the register that is available for public inspection indicate your status?
      `I have informed the company of my status` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Have you informed the company of your status?
      `I have given the company all my required particulars` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Have you given the company all of your required particulars?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 790G, must I tell the company that I am a person with significant control over it` IS
    `s 790G(2) the person must inform the company of their status and give the company the required particulars` (`s 790G(1) this section applies to the person` (JUST `the company is one to which Part 21A applies`) `I know that I am a registrable person or registrable relevant legal entity` `the public register indicates my status` `I have informed the company of my status` `I have given the company all my required particulars`)

@export Under section 790G(3), by what day must I tell the company that I am a person with significant control?
GIVEN `the day the conditions in section 790G(1) were first met` IS A DATE @desc On what day did the conditions in section 790G(1) become met (you knew your status, the register did not show it, and you had not told the company)?
GIVETH A DATE
DECIDE `Under section 790G(3), by what day must I tell the company that I am a person with significant control` IS
    `s 790G(3) the last day for the person to comply with the duty in subsection (2)` `the day the conditions in section 790G(1) were first met`

@export Under section 790H, must I tell the company about a change in my particulars?
GIVEN `the company is one to which Part 21A applies` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does Part 21A apply to the company?
      `I know that I am a registrable person or registrable relevant legal entity` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Do you know that you are a registrable person (or a registrable relevant legal entity) in relation to the company?
      `there has been a change in my required particulars and I know it` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has there been a change in your required particulars, and do you know that?
      `I have informed the company of the change` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Have you informed the company of the change?
      `I have given the company all the information it needs for its notice of the change` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Have you given the company all the information it would need for a notice of the change to the registrar?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 790H, must I tell the company about a change in my particulars` IS
    `s 790H(2) the person must inform the company of the change and give the company the information` (`s 790H(1) this section applies to the person` (JUST `the company is one to which Part 21A applies`) `I know that I am a registrable person or registrable relevant legal entity` `there has been a change in my required particulars and I know it` `I have informed the company of the change` `I have given the company all the information it needs for its notice of the change`)

@export Under section 790HA, must I tell the company that I have ceased to be a person with significant control?
GIVEN `the company is one to which Part 21A applies` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does Part 21A apply to the company?
      `I know that I have ceased to be a registrable person or registrable relevant legal entity` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Do you know that you have ceased to be a registrable person (or a registrable relevant legal entity) in relation to the company?
      `the public register indicates that I have ceased` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does the material in the public register indicate that you have ceased?
      `I have informed the company that I have ceased` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Have you informed the company that you have ceased?
      `I have informed the company of the date I ceased` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Have you informed the company of the date on which you ceased?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 790HA, must I tell the company that I have ceased to be a person with significant control` IS
    `s 790HA(2) the person must inform the company that the person has ceased and of the date on which the person so ceased` (`s 790HA(1) this section applies to the person` (JUST `the company is one to which Part 21A applies`) `I know that I have ceased to be a registrable person or registrable relevant legal entity` `the public register indicates that I have ceased` `I have informed the company that I have ceased` `I have informed the company of the date I ceased`)

@export Under section 790J(2), having been exempted, am I not required to comply with a company's notice under section 790D, 790E or 790EA?
GIVEN `I have been exempted by the Secretary of State under section 790J` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has the Secretary of State exempted you under section 790J?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 790J(2), having been exempted, am I not required to comply with a company's notice under section 790D, 790E or 790EA` IS
    `s 790J(2)(a) the person is not required to comply with a notice under section 790D, 790E or 790EA` `I have been exempted by the Secretary of State under section 790J`

@export Under section 790K(1), what particulars must I give about myself as a registrable person?
GIVETH A LIST OF `s 790K particular`
DECIDE `Under section 790K(1), what particulars must I give about myself as a registrable person` IS
    `s 790K(1) the required particulars of an individual who is a registrable person`

@export Under section 790K(4A), may I give my title instead of my forename and surname?
GIVEN `I am a peer` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are you a peer?
      `I am usually known by a title` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are you usually known by a title?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 790K(4A), may I give my title instead of my forename and surname` IS
    `s 790K(4A) the requirement to provide the individual's name may be satisfied by providing the title instead of the forename and surname` `I am a peer` `I am usually known by a title`

§§ `Telling the registrar (ss 790LA to 790LL)`

@export Under section 790LA(1), must my company give a notice to the registrar of a person with significant control it has confirmed?
GIVEN `my company is one to which Part 21A applies` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does Part 21A apply to your company?
      `the company has had confirmation of the person's status` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has the company had confirmation of the person's status as a registrable person or registrable relevant legal entity?
      `the company has had confirmation of the required particulars` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has the company had confirmation of the person's required particulars?
      `the incorporation statement named the person` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did the application to register the company contain a statement of initial significant control naming the person?
      `the company has no cause to believe the person has since ceased` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has the company no cause to believe the person has ceased to be a registrable person or registrable relevant legal entity since incorporation?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 790LA(1), must my company give a notice to the registrar of a person with significant control it has confirmed` IS
    `s 790LA(1) the company must give a notice to the registrar` (JUST `my company is one to which Part 21A applies`) `the company has had confirmation of the person's status` `the company has had confirmation of the required particulars` `the incorporation statement named the person` `the company has no cause to believe the person has since ceased`

@export Under section 790LA(3), by what day must my company give the registrar a notice of a confirmed person with significant control?
GIVEN `the day the company had confirmation` IS A DATE @desc On what day did the company have confirmation of the person's status and required particulars?
GIVETH A DATE
DECIDE `Under section 790LA(3), by what day must my company give the registrar a notice of a confirmed person with significant control` IS
    `s 790LA(3) the last day for the company to give the notice to the registrar` `the day the company had confirmation`

@export Under section 790LC(1), must my company give the registrar a notice of a person it believes has become a person with significant control?
GIVEN `my company is one to which Part 21A applies` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does Part 21A apply to your company?
      `the company knows or has cause to believe a person has become a registrable person or registrable relevant legal entity` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does the company know, or have cause to believe, that a person has become a registrable person or registrable relevant legal entity?
      `the company has not yet had confirmation` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has the company not yet had confirmation of the person's status and required particulars?
      `this would be a notice on incorporation for a person in the statement of initial significant control` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Would the notice be one on the company's incorporation about a person included in the statement of initial significant control under section 12A?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 790LC(1), must my company give the registrar a notice of a person it believes has become a person with significant control` IS
    `s 790LC(1) the company must give a notice to the registrar` (JUST `my company is one to which Part 21A applies`) `the company knows or has cause to believe a person has become a registrable person or registrable relevant legal entity` `the company has not yet had confirmation` `this would be a notice on incorporation for a person in the statement of initial significant control`

@export Under section 790LD(1), must my company give the registrar a notice of a change in a person's required particulars?
GIVEN `my company is one to which Part 21A applies` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does Part 21A apply to your company?
      `the company has had confirmation of a change in the required particulars` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has the company had confirmation that there has been a change in the required particulars of a registrable person or registrable relevant legal entity?
      `the company has had confirmation of how and when they changed` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has the company had confirmation of how the particulars changed and the date on which they changed?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 790LD(1), must my company give the registrar a notice of a change in a person's required particulars` IS
    `s 790LD(1) the company must give a notice to the registrar of the change` (JUST `my company is one to which Part 21A applies`) `the company has had confirmation of a change in the required particulars` `the company has had confirmation of how and when they changed`

@export Under section 790LD(3), by what day must my company give the registrar a notice of the change?
GIVEN `the day the company had confirmation` IS A DATE @desc On what day did the company have confirmation of the change?
GIVETH A DATE
DECIDE `Under section 790LD(3), by what day must my company give the registrar a notice of the change` IS
    `s 790LD(3) the last day for the company to give the notice to the registrar` `the day the company had confirmation`

@export Under section 790LF(1), must my company give the registrar a notice that a person has ceased to have significant control?
GIVEN `my company is one to which Part 21A applies` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does Part 21A apply to your company?
      `the company has had confirmation that the person has ceased` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has the company had confirmation that a person has ceased to be a registrable person or registrable relevant legal entity?
      `the company has had confirmation of the date the person ceased` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has the company had confirmation of the date on which the person ceased?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 790LF(1), must my company give the registrar a notice that a person has ceased to have significant control` IS
    `s 790LF(1) the company must give a notice to the registrar that the person has ceased` (JUST `my company is one to which Part 21A applies`) `the company has had confirmation that the person has ceased` `the company has had confirmation of the date the person ceased`

@export Under section 790LH(1), must my company give the registrar a notice that it has no people with significant control?
GIVEN `my company is one to which Part 21A applies` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does Part 21A apply to your company?
      `the company knows or has cause to believe there is no registrable person or registrable relevant legal entity` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does the company know, or have cause to believe, that there is no registrable person or registrable relevant legal entity in relation to it?
      `the incorporation statement said there was no such person` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did the application to register the company contain a statement of initial significant control saying that, on incorporation, there was no such person?
      `the company has no cause to believe any person has since become one` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has the company no cause to believe that any person has become a registrable person or registrable relevant legal entity since incorporation?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 790LH(1), must my company give the registrar a notice that it has no people with significant control` IS
    `s 790LH(1) the company must give a notice to the registrar that it has no persons with significant control` (JUST `my company is one to which Part 21A applies`) `the company knows or has cause to believe there is no registrable person or registrable relevant legal entity` `the incorporation statement said there was no such person` `the company has no cause to believe any person has since become one`

@export Under section 790LJ(1), does my company commit an offence by failing to notify the registrar?
GIVEN `the duty` IS A `s 790LJ(1) duty` @desc Which duty? One of: s 790LJ(1) the duty under section 790LA, s 790LJ(1) the duty under section 790LC, s 790LJ(1) the duty under section 790LD, s 790LJ(1) the duty under section 790LE, s 790LJ(1) the duty under section 790LF, s 790LJ(1) the duty under section 790LG, s 790LJ(1) the duty under section 790LH, s 790LJ(1) the duty under regulations under section 790LI, s 790LJ(1) another duty
      `the company failed to comply with the duty` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did the company fail to comply with the duty?
      `the company has a reasonable excuse` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does the company have a reasonable excuse for the failure?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 790LJ(1), does my company commit an offence by failing to notify the registrar` IS
    `s 790LJ(1)(a) an offence is committed by the company` `the duty` `the company failed to comply with the duty` `the company has a reasonable excuse`

@export Under section 790LJ(1), do I commit an offence as an officer, or shadow director, of a company that fails to notify the registrar?
GIVEN `the company commits an offence under section 790LJ(1)` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does the company commit an offence under section 790LJ(1) (it failed, without reasonable excuse, to comply with one of the listed duties to notify the registrar)?
      `I am an officer of the company who is in default` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are you an officer of the company who is in default (section 1121)? A shadow director is treated as an officer for this purpose.
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 790LJ(1), do I commit an offence as an officer, or shadow director, of a company that fails to notify the registrar` IS
    `s 790LJ(1)(b) an offence is committed by the officer of the company who is in default` (JUST `the company commits an offence under section 790LJ(1)`) (JUST `I am an officer of the company who is in default`)

@export Under section 790LJ(3), what is the most a person can be fined on summary conviction for failing to notify the registrar, in pounds?
GIVEN `the pounds that level 3 on the standard scale stands for` IS A NUMBER @desc How many pounds does level 3 on the standard scale stand for?
GIVETH A MAYBE NUMBER
DECIDE `Under section 790LJ(3), what is the most a person can be fined on summary conviction for failing to notify the registrar, in pounds` IS
    CONSIDER `s 790LJ(3) the penalty`'s `fine not exceeding`
    WHEN JUST (`a fine not exceeding a level on the standard scale` OF level, fraction) THEN JUST (`the pounds that level 3 on the standard scale stands for` TIMES fraction)
    OTHERWISE NOTHING

@export Under section 790LK(2), may I apply to the court because a company has not notified the registrar?
GIVEN `the company has made default in complying with a duty to notify the registrar` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has the company made default in complying with section 790LA, 790LC, 790LD, 790LE, 790LF, 790LG or 790LH (or regulations under section 790LI)?
      `I am a person aggrieved by the default` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are you a person aggrieved by the default?
      `I am a member of the company` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are you a member of the company?
      `I am a registrable person or registrable relevant legal entity in relation to the company` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are you a registrable person or registrable relevant legal entity in relation to the company?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 790LK(2), may I apply to the court because a company has not notified the registrar` IS
    `s 790LK(2) the person may apply to the court` `the company has made default in complying with a duty to notify the registrar` `I am a person aggrieved by the default` `I am a member of the company` `I am a registrable person or registrable relevant legal entity in relation to the company`

@export Under section 790LL(1), may I ask the company whether all the information it must deliver to the registrar has been delivered?
GIVEN `the company is aware that the registrar must refrain from making the information available for public inspection` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the company aware that, by virtue of regulations under section 1088, the registrar is required to refrain from making that information available for public inspection?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 790LL(1), may I ask the company whether all the information it must deliver to the registrar has been delivered` IS
    `s 790LL(1) the person may request the company to tell them whether all of the information it is required to deliver under this Chapter has been delivered` `the company is aware that the registrar must refrain from making the information available for public inspection`

@export Under section 790LL(2), by what day must the company answer my request?
GIVEN `the day I made the request` IS A DATE @desc On what day did you make the request?
GIVETH A DATE
DECIDE `Under section 790LL(2), by what day must the company answer my request` IS
    `s 790LL(2) the last day for the company to comply with the request` `the day I made the request`

§§ `Verifying your identity (ss 790LM to 790LT)`

@export Under section 790LM(2), must the registrar direct me to deliver a statement that my identity is verified?
GIVEN `the company is one to which Part 21A applies` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does Part 21A apply to the company?
      `I was named in the application for registration as a person who would become a registrable person on incorporation` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Were you named in the statement of initial significant control in the application to register the company as someone who would become a registrable person on incorporation?
      `the application did not include my verification statement or it appears false` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did the application not include a statement under section 12B(2) about you, or does it appear to the registrar that it is false?
      `the company has not given notice that I did not become a registrable person` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has the company not given a notice under section 790LG(1) about you?
      `the registrar was notified that I have become a registrable person` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Was the registrar notified that you have become a registrable person in relation to the company?
      `that notice did not include my verification statement or it appears false` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did that notice not include a statement under section 790LB(1), or does it appear to the registrar that the statement is false?
      `I am a corporation sole, government, international organisation or local authority` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are you a person mentioned in section 790C(12)(a) to (d) (a corporation sole, a government or government department, an international organisation or a local authority)?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 790LM(2), must the registrar direct me to deliver a statement that my identity is verified` IS
    `s 790LM(2) the registrar must direct the registrable person to deliver a statement confirming that the person's identity is verified` (JUST `the company is one to which Part 21A applies`) (`s 790LM(1) Case 1 applies` `I was named in the application for registration as a person who would become a registrable person on incorporation` `the application did not include my verification statement or it appears false` FALSE `the company has not given notice that I did not become a registrable person`) (`s 790LM(1) Case 2 applies` `the registrar was notified that I have become a registrable person` `that notice did not include my verification statement or it appears false` FALSE) `I am a corporation sole, government, international organisation or local authority`

@export Under section 790LM(2), by what day must I deliver the statement that my identity is verified?
GIVEN `the date of the registrar's direction` IS A DATE @desc What is the date of the registrar's direction to you?
GIVETH A DATE
DECIDE `Under section 790LM(2), by what day must I deliver the statement that my identity is verified` IS
    `s 790LM(2) the last day for the registrable person to deliver the statement` `the date of the registrar's direction`

@export Under section 790LN(1), must I deliver a statement that my identity is verified because I was a registrable person before the verification rules began?
GIVEN `the company is one to which Part 21A applies` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does Part 21A apply to the company?
      `I was a registrable person on the appointed day` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Were you a registrable person in relation to a company at any time during the appointed day?
      `I became one on incorporation on an application delivered before section 12B(2) was fully in force` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did you become a registrable person on the company's incorporation, on an application for registration delivered before section 12B(2) came fully into force?
      `I became one otherwise before section 790LB(1) was fully in force` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did you become a registrable person, otherwise than on incorporation, before the day on which section 790LB(1) came fully into force?
      `I am a corporation sole, government, international organisation or local authority` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are you a person mentioned in section 790C(12)(a) to (d)?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 790LN(1), must I deliver a statement that my identity is verified because I was a registrable person before the verification rules began` IS
    `s 790LN(1) the person must deliver to the registrar the statement required by this section` (JUST `the company is one to which Part 21A applies`) `I was a registrable person on the appointed day` `I became one on incorporation on an application delivered before section 12B(2) was fully in force` `I became one otherwise before section 790LB(1) was fully in force` `I am a corporation sole, government, international organisation or local authority`

@export Under section 790LN(3), by what day must I deliver that statement?
GIVEN `the appointed day` IS A DATE @desc What is the appointed day (the day the Secretary of State appointed by regulations for section 790LN)?
GIVETH A DATE
DECIDE `Under section 790LN(3), by what day must I deliver that statement` IS
    `s 790LN(3) the last day for the person to deliver the statement` `the appointed day`

@export Under section 790LQ(1), am I in breach of my duty to keep my identity verified on a given day?
GIVEN `the day my relevant period began` IS A DATE @desc On what day did the relevant period begin (the incorporation, the delivery of your verification statement, or the end of the period for complying with a direction or with section 790LN)?
      `the registrar was told on a day that I have ceased to be a registrable person` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has the registrar been given a notice under section 790LF that you have ceased to be a registrable person?
      `the day that notice was given` IS A DATE @desc On what day was that notice given? (Any date if none.)
      `the day I am asking about` IS A DATE @desc Which day are you asking about?
      `I am a corporation sole, government, international organisation or local authority` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are you a person mentioned in section 790C(12)(a) to (d)?
      `my identity is verified on that day` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is your identity verified (within section 1110A) on that day?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 790LQ(1), am I in breach of my duty to keep my identity verified on a given day` IS
    `s 790LQ(1) the registrable person is in breach on the day` (`s 790LQ(1) the day falls in the relevant period` `the day my relevant period began` `when notice of ceasing was given` `the day I am asking about` `I am a corporation sole, government, international organisation or local authority`) (JUST `my identity is verified on that day`)
    WHERE
        `when notice of ceasing was given` MEANS IF `the registrar was told on a day that I have ceased to be a registrable person` THEN JUST `the day that notice was given` ELSE NOTHING

@export Under section 790LT(1), do I commit an offence by failing to comply with a duty or direction about verifying my identity?
GIVEN `the requirement` IS A `s 790LT(1) requirement` @desc Which requirement? One of: s 790LT(1)(a) section 790LN, s 790LT(1)(a) section 790LP, s 790LT(1)(a) section 790LQ, s 790LT(1)(a) section 790LR, s 790LT(1)(b) a direction under section 790LM, s 790LT(1)(b) a direction under section 790LO, s 790LT(1) another requirement
      `I fail to comply with it` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Do you fail to comply with the requirement?
      `I have a reasonable excuse` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Do you have a reasonable excuse?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 790LT(1), do I commit an offence by failing to comply with a duty or direction about verifying my identity` IS
    `s 790LT(1) the person commits an offence` `the requirement` `I fail to comply with it` `I have a reasonable excuse`

§§ `Protection of your address (ss 790ZF to 790ZH)`

@export Under section 790ZF, is information about my usual residential address protected from disclosure like a director's?
GIVEN `the information is my usual residential address` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the information your usual residential address?
      `the information is that my service address is my usual residential address` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the information that your service address is your usual residential address?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 790ZF, is information about my usual residential address protected from disclosure like a director's` IS
    `s 790ZF(1) sections 240 to 244 apply to the information as protected information` (`s 790ZF(2) the information is within this subsection` `the information is my usual residential address` `the information is that my service address is my usual residential address`)

@export Under section 790ZH(1), do I commit an offence as an officer of a company that breaches a restriction on using or disclosing information?
GIVEN `the company contravenes a restriction imposed by regulations under section 790ZG` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does the company contravene a restriction on the use or disclosure of information imposed by virtue of regulations under section 790ZG?
      `I am an officer of the company who is in default` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are you an officer of the company who is in default (section 1121)?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 790ZH(1), do I commit an offence as an officer of a company that breaches a restriction on using or disclosing information` IS
    `s 790ZH(1)(b) an offence is committed by the officer of the company who is in default` (`s 790ZH(1)(a) an offence is committed by the company` `the company contravenes a restriction imposed by regulations under section 790ZG`) (JUST `I am an officer of the company who is in default`)

-- ====================================================================================================
-- seat questions from part coa18 (merged by the lead on 2026-11-12; unchanged text follows)
-- ====================================================================================================
-- coa18-seat.l4: the SEAT LAYER over the layer-1 modules of lines 10757-11596 of the Companies Act 2006 (United Kingdom),
-- Parts 22 (information about interests in a company's shares), 23 (distributions) and 24 (annual confirmation of accuracy of
-- information on register), ss 791 to 859.
--
-- SEAT: an individual who is, or is about to become, a director, a company secretary or a member (shareholder) of a company
-- registered under the Act, or who deals with one, asking on facts they can state what the Act requires or lets them do, what
-- rights they have against the company or its directors, what they must disclose, file, approve or vote on and by when, and what
-- follows (liability, offences, penalties) if it is not done. (Assumed, not ruled: the Act is addressed to companies, so the
-- individual is whoever stands in a company's management or ownership.) There is no seat for an official: where a provision
-- addresses only the registrar, the Secretary of State or the court, it is asked here for what it means to this person.
--
-- READING AN ANSWER. Most questions answer true (JUST TRUE: the Act says yes), false (JUST FALSE: the Act says no in its own
-- words) or null (NOTHING: the Act does not decide the case on these facts, or the answer is in another provision this layer does
-- not hold). A null is never a "no". Where an answer is a number or a date it is the Act's own figure worked out from the facts.
-- Where the Act leaves a figure to others (the pounds that a level on the standard scale stands for, a prescribed fee) the person
-- supplies it; where the Act asks for a judgment (a reasonable period, a proper purpose) the person states whether it holds.
--
-- PLAIN INPUTS. Each question takes one input per fact the person can state. This layer builds nothing the layer-1 rules do not
-- read, and restates no rule: it asks the layer-1 functions. The gate of s 791 ("This Part applies only to public companies") is
-- put to the Part 22 questions about the company's powers here, by asking `s 791 this Part applies to the company` first.
-- Working days (s 827): the person lists the dates in the period that were not working days apart from weekends (Good Friday,
-- Christmas Day and bank holidays); weekends are taken from the library, the rest of the keel's "working day" rule being theirs.
-- A fact that is another section's answer (whether an officer is "in default", s 1121) is passed through as true, false or null.

§ `The Companies Act 2006, Parts 22 to 24 -- the questions of a director, secretary, member or person dealing with a company`

§ `Part 22 -- information about interests in a public company's shares`

§§ `A notice requiring information about interests in shares (ss 791 to 796)`

@export Does Part 22 (information about interests in a company's shares) apply to this company? True means yes; false means no, because it applies only to public companies.
GIVEN `the company is a public company` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the company a public company (not a private company)?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`Under section 791, does Part 22 apply to this company?` MEANS
    `s 791 this Part applies to the company` `the company is a public company`

@export May the company give me a notice requiring me to say whether I am, or was in the last three years, interested in its shares? True means it may; null means the Act does not say it may on these facts.
GIVEN `the company is a public company` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the company a public company?
      `the company knows or has reasonable cause to believe I am interested in its shares` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does the company know, or have reasonable cause to believe, that you are interested in its shares now?
      `the company knows or has reasonable cause to believe I was interested in its shares at some time in the three years before the notice` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does the company know, or have reasonable cause to believe, that you were interested in its shares at some time during the three years immediately before the date of the notice?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`Under section 793(1), may the company give me a notice requiring information about my interest in its shares?` MEANS
    CONSIDER `s 791 this Part applies to the company` `the company is a public company`
    WHEN JUST FALSE THEN JUST FALSE
    OTHERWISE `s 793(1) the company may give notice to the person` `the company knows or has reasonable cause to believe I am interested in its shares` `the company knows or has reasonable cause to believe I was interested in its shares at some time in the three years before the notice`

@export Was I interested in the shares at a time that falls within the three years immediately before the date of the notice?
GIVEN `the date on which I was interested` IS A DATE @desc On what date, if any, were you interested in the company's shares? (the date, for example 2024-05-31)
      `the date on which the notice is issued` IS A DATE @desc On what date is the notice issued?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`Under section 793(1)(b), was my interest within the three years before the notice?` MEANS
    `s 793(1)(b) the date is within the three years immediately preceding the date on which the notice is issued` `the date on which I was interested` `the date on which the notice is issued`

@export May the notice require me to give further information about my interest in the company's shares?
GIVEN `I hold, or have during the last three years held, an interest in the company's shares` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Do you hold, or have you during the three years before the notice held, an interest in the company's shares?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`Under section 793(2)(b), may the notice require me to give further information about my interest?` MEANS
    `s 793(2)(b) the notice may require the person to give further information` `I hold, or have during the last three years held, an interest in the company's shares`

@export May the notice require me to give particulars of another person's interest in the same shares?
GIVEN `my interest is a present interest and another interest in the shares subsists` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is your interest a present interest, and does another person's interest in the shares also exist now?
      `another interest in the shares existed during the last three years at a time when my interest existed` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did another person's interest in the shares exist, at a time in the three years before the notice when your interest also existed?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`Under section 793(4), may the notice require me to give particulars of another interest in the shares?` MEANS
    `s 793(4) the notice may require the person to give such particulars with respect to that other interest as the notice requires` `my interest is a present interest and another interest in the shares subsists` `another interest in the shares existed during the last three years at a time when my interest existed`

@export Did I give the information the notice required within the time the notice specified? True means yes; null means the time specified was not reasonable, which the Act does not answer.
GIVEN `the time the notice specified is reasonable` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the time the notice allows a reasonable time?
      `the last day the notice allows` IS A DATE @desc What is the last day the notice allows for giving the information?
      `the day I gave the information` IS A DATE @desc On what day did you give the information?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`Under section 793(7), did I give the information within the time the notice specified?` MEANS
    `s 793(7) the information required by the notice was given within the time specified` `the time the notice specified is reasonable` `the last day the notice allows` `the day I gave the information`

@export May the company apply to the court for an order that my shares be subject to restrictions?
GIVEN `the company served a notice under section 793 on a person who is or was interested in shares in the company` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did the company serve a notice under section 793 on a person who is or was interested in its shares?
      `that person has failed to give the information within the time specified in the notice` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has that person failed to give the company the information required within the time the notice specified?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`Under section 794(1), may the company apply to the court for an order restricting my shares?` MEANS
    `s 794(1) the company may apply to the court for an order directing that the shares in question be subject to restrictions` `the company served a notice under section 793 on a person who is or was interested in shares in the company` `that person has failed to give the information within the time specified in the notice`

@export Do I commit an offence by failing to comply with a notice requiring information about interests in shares? False includes the case where I prove the requirement was frivolous or vexatious.
GIVEN `I failed to comply with the notice` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did you fail to comply with the notice under section 793?
      `I can prove the requirement to give information was frivolous or vexatious` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Can you prove that the requirement to give you information was frivolous or vexatious?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`Under section 795(1)(a), do I commit an offence by failing to comply with the notice?` MEANS
    `s 795(1)(a) the person commits an offence by failing to comply with the notice` `I failed to comply with the notice` `I can prove the requirement to give information was frivolous or vexatious`

@export Do I commit an offence by making a false statement in purported compliance with the notice?
GIVEN `I made a statement in purported compliance with the notice` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did you make a statement in purported compliance with the notice?
      `I knew the statement was false in a material particular` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did you know the statement was false in a material particular?
      `I made the statement recklessly and it was false in a material particular` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did you make the statement recklessly, and was it false in a material particular?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`Under section 795(1)(b), do I commit an offence by a false statement in purported compliance with the notice?` MEANS
    `s 795(1)(b) the person commits an offence by a false statement in purported compliance with the notice` `I made a statement in purported compliance with the notice` `I knew the statement was false in a material particular` `I made the statement recklessly and it was false in a material particular`

@export What is the longest prison term, in months, for an offence under section 795 on the kind of conviction? Null where the Act gives none or does not divide the case this way.
GIVEN `the kind of conviction` IS A `Mode of conviction` @desc The kind of conviction: one of "on conviction on indictment", "on summary conviction in England and Wales", "on summary conviction in Scotland" or "on summary conviction in Northern Ireland"
GIVETH A MAYBE NUMBER
`Under section 795(3), what is the longest prison term, in months, on conviction?` MEANS
    CONSIDER `s 795(3) the penalty on conviction` `the kind of conviction`
    WHEN NOTHING THEN NOTHING
    WHEN JUST penalty THEN
        CONSIDER penalty's `imprisonment not exceeding`
        WHEN NOTHING THEN NOTHING
        WHEN JUST period THEN JUST (IF period's unit EQUALS Years THEN period's `number of units` TIMES 12 ELSE period's `number of units`)

@export Am I excused from the obligation to comply with a notice under section 793? True means I am, because the Secretary of State has exempted me for the time being.
GIVEN `the Secretary of State has for the time being exempted me from the operation of section 793` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has the Secretary of State, for the time being, exempted you from the operation of section 793?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`Under section 796(1), am I not obliged to comply with a notice under section 793?` MEANS
    `s 796(1) the person is not obliged to comply with a notice under section 793` `the Secretary of State has for the time being exempted me from the operation of section 793`

§§ `The effects of an order restricting shares, and the court's powers (ss 797 to 802)`

@export Is a transfer of my shares void because they are subject to an order restricting them? True means the transfer is void; false means a direction or the order's terms displace that; null means the shares are not under an order.
GIVEN `my shares are subject to restrictions by an order under section 794` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are your shares subject to restrictions by an order under section 794?
      `the transfer is within a direction under section 794(2) or 799(3)` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the transfer within a court direction (under section 794(2) or 799(3)) that it is not a breach of the restrictions?
      `the transfer is permitted by the terms of an interim order` IS A BOOLEAN @desc If the order is an interim order, do its terms permit the transfer?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`Under section 797(1)(a), is a transfer of my shares void?` MEANS
    `s 797(1)(a) any transfer of the shares is void` `my shares are subject to restrictions by an order under section 794` `the transfer is within a direction under section 794(2) or 799(3)` `the transfer is permitted by the terms of an interim order`

@export Are no voting rights exercisable in respect of my shares because they are subject to an order restricting them?
GIVEN `my shares are subject to restrictions by an order under section 794` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are your shares subject to restrictions by an order under section 794?
      `the voting is within a direction under section 794(2) or 799(3)` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the vote within a court direction (under section 794(2) or 799(3)) that it is not a breach of the restrictions?
      `the voting is permitted by the terms of an interim order` IS A BOOLEAN @desc If the order is an interim order, do its terms permit the vote?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`Under section 797(1)(b), are no voting rights exercisable in respect of my shares?` MEANS
    `s 797(1)(b) no voting rights are exercisable in respect of the shares` `my shares are subject to restrictions by an order under section 794` `the voting is within a direction under section 794(2) or 799(3)` `the voting is permitted by the terms of an interim order`

@export Is it the case that no payment may be made of sums due from the company on my shares (except in a liquidation) because they are subject to an order restricting them? True means payment is barred; false means a liquidation, a court direction or the terms of an interim order displaces the bar.
GIVEN `my shares are subject to restrictions by an order under section 794` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are your shares subject to restrictions by an order under section 794?
      `the payment is made in a liquidation` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the payment made in a liquidation of the company?
      `the payment is within a direction under section 794(2) or 799(3)` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the payment within a court direction (under section 794(2) or 799(3)) that it is not a breach of the restrictions?
      `the payment is permitted by the terms of an interim order` IS A BOOLEAN @desc If the order is an interim order, do its terms permit the payment?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`Under section 797(1)(d), is no payment to be made of sums due from the company on my shares?` MEANS
    `s 797(1)(d) no payment may be made of sums due from the company on the shares` `my shares are subject to restrictions by an order under section 794` `the payment is made in a liquidation` `the payment is within a direction under section 794(2) or 799(3)` `the payment is permitted by the terms of an interim order`

@export Do I commit an offence by disposing of shares that I know are subject to restrictions?
GIVEN `I exercise or purport to exercise a right to dispose of the shares` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Do you exercise, or purport to exercise, a right to dispose of shares?
      `I exercise or purport to exercise a right to dispose of a right to be issued with such shares` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Do you exercise, or purport to exercise, a right to dispose of a right to be issued with such shares?
      `I know the shares are for the time being subject to restrictions` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Do you know that the shares are for the time being subject to restrictions?
      `the act is within a direction or an interim order's terms` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the act within a court direction (under section 794(2), 799 or 800) or the terms of an interim order?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`Under section 798(2)(a), do I commit an offence by disposing of shares subject to restrictions?` MEANS
    `s 798(2)(a) the person commits an offence by exercising a right to dispose` `I exercise or purport to exercise a right to dispose of the shares` `I exercise or purport to exercise a right to dispose of a right to be issued with such shares` `I know the shares are for the time being subject to restrictions` `the act is within a direction or an interim order's terms`

@export Do I commit an offence by voting shares that I know are subject to restrictions, or by appointing a proxy to vote them?
GIVEN `I vote in respect of the shares, as holder or proxy` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Do you vote in respect of the shares, whether as holder or as proxy?
      `I appoint a proxy to vote in respect of the shares` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Do you appoint a proxy to vote in respect of the shares?
      `I know the shares are for the time being subject to restrictions` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Do you know that the shares are for the time being subject to restrictions?
      `the act is within a direction or an interim order's terms` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the act within a court direction (under section 794(2), 799 or 800) or the terms of an interim order?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`Under section 798(2)(b), do I commit an offence by voting shares subject to restrictions?` MEANS
    `s 798(2)(b) the person commits an offence by voting or appointing a proxy` `I vote in respect of the shares, as holder or proxy` `I appoint a proxy to vote in respect of the shares` `I know the shares are for the time being subject to restrictions` `the act is within a direction or an interim order's terms`

@export May I apply to the court to relax the restrictions on shares because the order unfairly affects my rights as a third party?
GIVEN `I am a person aggrieved by the order` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are you a person aggrieved by the order (for example a third party whose rights in the shares it unfairly affects)?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`Under section 799(2), may I apply to the court to relax the restrictions on shares?` MEANS
    `s 799(2) the person may make an application for an order under section 799` FALSE `I am a person aggrieved by the order`

@export Is the court barred from ordering that shares cease to be subject to restrictions? False means one of the two conditions that lift the bar is met.
GIVEN `the court is satisfied that the relevant facts about the shares have been disclosed to the company` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the court satisfied that the relevant facts about the shares have been disclosed to the company?
      `the court is satisfied that no unfair advantage has accrued to any person as a result of the earlier failure to disclose` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the court satisfied that no unfair advantage has accrued to anyone from the earlier failure to disclose?
      `the shares are to be transferred for valuable consideration` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are the shares to be transferred for valuable consideration?
      `the court approves the transfer` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does the court approve the transfer?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`Under section 800(3), is the court barred from ordering that the shares cease to be subject to restrictions?` MEANS
    `s 800(3) the court is barred from making an order under section 800` `the court is satisfied that the relevant facts about the shares have been disclosed to the company` `the court is satisfied that no unfair advantage has accrued to any person as a result of the earlier failure to disclose` `the shares are to be transferred for valuable consideration` `the court approves the transfer`

@export How much of the money from a court-ordered sale of restricted shares must the court order paid to me, in pounds? Null if the total value of the shares is nil.
GIVEN `the proceeds of sale paid into court` IS A NUMBER @desc How much, in pounds, were the proceeds of sale (less the costs of the sale)?
      `the interest on them` IS A NUMBER @desc How much interest, in pounds, has been earned on the proceeds?
      `another person had a beneficial interest in the shares at the time of the sale` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did another person have a beneficial interest in the shares when they were sold?
      `the value of my interest in the shares` IS A NUMBER @desc What was the value, in pounds, of your interest in the shares?
      `the total value of the shares` IS A NUMBER @desc What was the total value, in pounds, of the shares?
GIVETH A MAYBE NUMBER
`Under section 802(3), how much of the proceeds of sale must the court order paid to me?` MEANS
    `s 802(3) the amount the court shall order paid to the applicant` `the proceeds of sale paid into court` `the interest on them` `another person had a beneficial interest in the shares at the time of the sale` `the value of my interest in the shares` `the total value of the shares`

§§ `Members' power to require the company to investigate, and the report (ss 803 to 807)`

@export Is the company required to exercise its powers to investigate interests in its shares, because members holding enough of the voting capital have asked? True means it is required.
GIVEN `the requests are to the same effect` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are the requests the company has received to the same effect?
      `the paid-up voting capital held by the members who made the requests` IS A NUMBER @desc How much, in pounds, of the company's paid-up capital that carries a right to vote at general meetings do the requesting members hold?
      `the company's paid-up voting capital excluding treasury shares` IS A NUMBER @desc How much, in pounds, of the company's paid-up capital carries a right to vote at general meetings, excluding any voting rights attached to treasury shares?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`Under section 803(2), is the company required to investigate interests in its shares?` MEANS
    `s 803(2) the company is required to exercise its powers under section 793` `the requests are to the same effect` `the paid-up voting capital held by the members who made the requests` `the company's paid-up voting capital excluding treasury shares`

@export Does our request to the company meet the requirements for a members' request?
GIVEN `the form of the request` IS A `Form of document` @desc The form of the request: "hard copy form" or "electronic form"
      `the request states that the company is requested to exercise its powers under section 793` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does the request state that the company is requested to exercise its powers under section 793?
      `the request specifies the manner in which the company is requested to act` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does the request specify the manner in which the company is requested to act?
      `the request gives reasonable grounds` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does the request give reasonable grounds for requiring the company to exercise those powers in the manner specified?
      `the request is authenticated by the person or persons making it` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the request authenticated by the person or persons making it?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`Under section 803(3), does our request meet the requirements?` MEANS
    `s 803(3) the request meets the requirements of this subsection` `the form of the request` `the request states that the company is requested to exercise its powers under section 793` `the request specifies the manner in which the company is requested to act` `the request gives reasonable grounds` `the request is authenticated by the person or persons making it`

@export By what date must the company make the report on its investigation available for inspection, at the latest? Counted in working days (section 827).
GIVEN `the day the investigation concluded` IS A DATE @desc On what day did the investigation conclude?
      `dates in the period that were not working days apart from weekends` IS A LIST OF DATE @desc The dates, in the weeks after the investigation concluded, that were not working days apart from weekends: Good Friday, Christmas Day and bank holidays
GIVETH A DATE
`Under section 805(1), by what date must the company make the report available for inspection?` MEANS
    `s 805(1) the last day for making the report available for inspection` `the day the investigation concluded` (GIVEN d YIELD (NOT (`is weekend` d)) AND (NOT (elem d `dates in the period that were not working days apart from weekends`)))

@export How many interim reports must the company cause to be prepared on an investigation that runs on?
GIVEN `the day the company became subject to the requirement` IS A DATE @desc On what day did the company become subject to the members' requirement?
      `the day the investigation concluded` IS A DATE @desc On what day did the investigation conclude?
GIVETH A NUMBER
`Under section 805(2), how many interim reports must the company prepare?` MEANS
    `s 805(2) the number of interim reports the company must cause to be prepared` `the day the company became subject to the requirement` `the day the investigation concluded`

@export By what date must the company tell the members who made the requests where the report is available? Three working days after the report was made available.
GIVEN `the day the report was made available for inspection` IS A DATE @desc On what day was the report made available for inspection?
      `dates in the period that were not working days apart from weekends` IS A LIST OF DATE @desc The dates, in the days after that, that were not working days apart from weekends: Good Friday, Christmas Day and bank holidays
GIVETH A DATE
`Under section 805(6), by what date must the company notify the members where the report is available?` MEANS
    `s 805(6) the last day for notifying the members who made the requests` `the day the report was made available for inspection` (GIVEN d YIELD (NOT (`is weekend` d)) AND (NOT (elem d `dates in the period that were not working days apart from weekends`)))

@export Does the company commit an offence by failing to tell the registrar where the investigation reports are kept? True once it has been in default for 14 days.
GIVEN `the company has been in default for 14 days in giving the registrar notice of the place where the reports are kept` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has the company been in default for 14 days in giving the registrar notice of where the reports are kept (or of a change in that place)?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`Under section 806(1), does the company commit an offence by failing to notify the registrar of the place of the reports?` MEANS
    `s 806(1)(a) the company commits an offence` `the company has been in default for 14 days in giving the registrar notice of the place where the reports are kept`

@export Do I, as an officer of the company, commit an offence because the company has been in default for 14 days in notifying the registrar of the place of the reports?
GIVEN `the company has been in default for 14 days in giving the registrar notice of the place where the reports are kept` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has the company been in default for 14 days in giving the registrar notice of where the reports are kept?
      `I am an officer of the company who is in default` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN @desc Are you an officer of the company who is in default (section 1121)? true, false, or null if you do not know
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`Under section 806(1)(b), do I as an officer commit an offence?` MEANS
    `s 806(1)(b) the officer of the company commits an offence` `the company has been in default for 14 days in giving the registrar notice of the place where the reports are kept` `I am an officer of the company who is in default`

@export Must a report the company prepared on its investigation (section 805) be open to inspection by any person without charge? True means it must; false means the report is not one prepared under section 805.
GIVEN `the report was prepared under section 805` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Was the report prepared by the company under section 805 (the report on an investigation)?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`Under section 807(1), must a report the company prepared on its investigation be open to inspection by any person without charge?` MEANS
    `s 807(1) the report must be open to inspection by any person without charge` `the report was prepared under section 805`

@export Am I entitled to a copy of the report or part of it from the company?
GIVEN `I have asked the company for a copy` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Have you asked the company for a copy?
      `I have paid the prescribed fee` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Have you paid the fee that is prescribed?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`Under section 807(2), am I entitled to a copy of the report?` MEANS
    `s 807(2) the person is entitled to be provided with a copy of the report or any part of it` `I have asked the company for a copy` `I have paid the prescribed fee`

@export By what date must the company provide me with the copy I asked for? Ten working days after it received the request.
GIVEN `the day the company received my request` IS A DATE @desc On what day did the company receive your request?
      `dates in the period that were not working days apart from weekends` IS A LIST OF DATE @desc The dates, in the two weeks after that, that were not working days apart from weekends: Good Friday, Christmas Day and bank holidays
GIVETH A DATE
`Under section 807(2), by what date must the company provide the copy?` MEANS
    `s 807(2) the last day for providing the copy` `the day the company received my request` (GIVEN d YIELD (NOT (`is weekend` d)) AND (NOT (elem d `dates in the period that were not working days apart from weekends`)))

§§ `The register of interests disclosed (ss 808 to 819)`

@export By what date must the company enter the information it received about interests in its shares in its register? Three working days after receipt.
GIVEN `the day the company received the information` IS A DATE @desc On what day did the company receive the information?
      `dates in the period that were not working days apart from weekends` IS A LIST OF DATE @desc The dates, in the days after that, that were not working days apart from weekends: Good Friday, Christmas Day and bank holidays
GIVETH A DATE
`Under section 808(2), by what date must the company enter the information in the register?` MEANS
    `s 808(2) the last day for entering the information in the register` `the day the company received the information` (GIVEN d YIELD (NOT (`is weekend` d)) AND (NOT (elem d `dates in the period that were not working days apart from weekends`)))

@export Am I entitled to a copy of an entry in the register of interests disclosed?
GIVEN `I have made a request to the company` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Have you made a request to the company for a copy?
      `I have paid the prescribed fee` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Have you paid the fee that is prescribed?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`Under section 811(2), am I entitled to a copy of an entry in the register?` MEANS
    `s 811(2) the person is entitled to be provided with a copy of any entry in the register` `I have made a request to the company` `I have paid the prescribed fee`

@export Does my request to inspect the register or to have a copy of an entry contain the information the Act requires?
GIVEN `I am` IS A `s 811(4) kind of person` @desc Are you "s 811(4) an individual" or "s 811(4) an organisation"?
      `the request gives my name and address, or for an organisation the name and address of the individual responsible` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does the request give your name and address (or, for an organisation, the name and address of an individual responsible for making the request)?
      `the request states the purpose for which the information is to be used` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does the request state the purpose for which the information is to be used?
      `the request states whether the information will be disclosed to another person` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does the request state whether the information will be disclosed to any other person?
      `the information will be disclosed to another person` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Will the information be disclosed to another person?
      `the other person is` IS A `s 811(4) kind of person` @desc If so, is that person "s 811(4) an individual" or "s 811(4) an organisation"?
      `the request gives the other person's name and address` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does the request give that person's name and address (or, for an organisation, the name and address of the individual responsible for receiving the information)?
      `the request states the purpose for which the other person will use the information` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does the request state the purpose for which that person will use the information?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`Under section 811(4), does my request contain the information required?` MEANS
    `s 811(4) the request contains the information the subsection requires` `I am` `the request gives my name and address, or for an organisation the name and address of the individual responsible` `the request states the purpose for which the information is to be used` `the request states whether the information will be disclosed to another person` `the information will be disclosed to another person` `the other person is` `the request gives the other person's name and address` `the request states the purpose for which the other person will use the information`

@export Must the company comply with my request to inspect the register, or refuse it? It complies if it is satisfied the request is made for a proper purpose, and refuses if it is not.
GIVEN `the company is satisfied that my request is made for a proper purpose` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the company satisfied that your request is made for a proper purpose?
GIVETH A `s 812(1) what the company must do with the request`
`Under section 812(1), must the company comply with my request or refuse it?` MEANS
    `s 812(1) what the company must do with a request under section 811` `the company is satisfied that my request is made for a proper purpose`

@export Does the company commit an offence by refusing me inspection of the register or failing to give me a copy?
GIVEN `the company refused me inspection or failed to give me a copy` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did the company refuse you inspection, or fail to provide a copy you were entitled to?
      `the refusal or failure is in accordance with section 812` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Was the refusal or failure in accordance with section 812 (the company refusing because it was not satisfied of a proper purpose)?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`Under section 813(1)(a), does the company commit an offence by refusing me inspection of the register?` MEANS
    `s 813(1)(a) the company commits an offence` `the company refused me inspection or failed to give me a copy` `the refusal or failure is in accordance with section 812`

@export Do I commit an offence by passing on information I obtained from the register when I know or suspect it may be used for an improper purpose?
GIVEN `I am in possession of information obtained from the register or from a copy of an entry` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are you in possession of information obtained by inspecting the register or by obtaining a copy of an entry?
      `I do something that results in the information being disclosed to another person` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Do you do something that results in the information being disclosed to another person?
      `I fail to do something with the result that the information is disclosed to another person` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Do you fail to do something, with the result that the information is disclosed to another person?
      `I know or have reason to suspect the other person may use it for an improper purpose` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Do you know, or have reason to suspect, that the other person may use the information for a purpose that is not a proper purpose?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`Under section 814(2), do I commit an offence by disclosing information obtained from the register?` MEANS
    `s 814(2) the person commits an offence by disclosing the information` `I am in possession of information obtained from the register or from a copy of an entry` `I do something that results in the information being disclosed to another person` `I fail to do something with the result that the information is disclosed to another person` `I know or have reason to suspect the other person may use it for an improper purpose`

@export May the company remove an entry from the register because more than six years have passed since it was made?
GIVEN `the date the entry was made` IS A DATE @desc On what date was the entry made in the register?
      `today's date` IS A DATE @desc On what date are you asking?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`Under section 816, may the company remove an entry made more than six years ago?` MEANS
    `s 816 the company may remove the entry from the register` `the date the entry was made` `today's date`

@export May I apply to the company to have an entry that names me as interested in shares removed from its register, because someone gave my name in answer to a section 793 notice?
GIVEN `a person gave the company my name and address as interested in shares, in answer to a notice under section 793` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did someone, in answer to a notice under section 793, give the company your name and address as a person interested in shares in the company?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`Under section 817(2), may I apply to the company for the removal of an entry about me?` MEANS
    `s 817(2) that other person may apply to the company for the removal of the entry from the register` (`s 817(1) this section applies` `a person gave the company my name and address as interested in shares, in answer to a notice under section 793` EQUALS JUST TRUE)

@export Must a company that has stopped being a public company still keep its register of interests disclosed and its index?
GIVEN `the company has ceased to be a public company` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has the company ceased to be a public company?
      `the date it ceased to be a public company` IS A DATE @desc On what date did the company cease to be a public company?
      `today's date` IS A DATE @desc On what date are you asking?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`Under section 819(1), must the company that has ceased to be public keep the register?` MEANS
    `s 819(1) the company must continue to keep the register and any associated index` `the company has ceased to be a public company` `the date it ceased to be a public company` `today's date`

§§ `Whether a person has an interest in shares (ss 820 to 825)`

@export Am I treated as having an interest in shares because I contracted to acquire them, or because I am entitled to exercise or control the exercise of rights attached to them without being the registered holder?
GIVEN `I enter into a contract to acquire the shares` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Have you entered into a contract to acquire the shares?
      `I am the registered holder of the shares` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are you the registered holder of the shares?
      `I am entitled to exercise a right conferred by the holding of the shares` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are you entitled to exercise any right conferred by the holding of the shares?
      `I am entitled to control the exercise of such a right` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are you entitled to control the exercise of any such right?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`Under section 820(4), am I treated as having an interest in the shares?` MEANS
    `s 820(4) the person is treated as having an interest in the shares` `I enter into a contract to acquire the shares` `I am the registered holder of the shares` `I am entitled to exercise a right conferred by the holding of the shares` `I am entitled to control the exercise of such a right`

@export Am I taken to be interested in shares in which my spouse, civil partner or infant child or step-child is interested?
GIVEN `my spouse or civil partner is interested in the shares` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is your spouse or civil partner interested in the shares?
      `my infant child or step-child is interested in the shares` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is your infant child or step-child interested in the shares?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`Under section 822(1), am I taken to be interested in shares in which my family is interested?` MEANS
    `s 822(1) the person is taken to be interested in the shares` `my spouse or civil partner is interested in the shares` `my infant child or step-child is interested in the shares`

@export Am I taken to be interested in shares in which a company is interested because I direct it or control a third or more of its votes?
GIVEN `a body corporate is interested in the shares` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is a company (a body corporate) interested in the shares?
      `the body or its directors are accustomed to act on my directions or instructions` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the body, or are its directors, accustomed to act in accordance with your directions or instructions?
      `the fraction of the voting power at general meetings of the body I am entitled to exercise or control` IS A NUMBER @desc What fraction of the voting power at the body's general meetings are you entitled to exercise or control? (a number between 0 and 1, for example 0.35)
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`Under section 823(1), am I taken to be interested in shares in which a company I control is interested?` MEANS
    `s 823(1) the person is taken to be interested in the shares` `a body corporate is interested in the shares` `the body or its directors are accustomed to act on my directions or instructions` `the fraction of the voting power at general meetings of the body I am entitled to exercise or control`

@export Does section 824 apply to an agreement I am party to for acquiring interests in a particular public company? True means it applies, so each party is treated as interested in the shares the others hold.
GIVEN `the agreement is of the kind described in section 824(1)` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it an agreement between two or more persons that includes provision for any of them to acquire interests in shares of a particular public company?
      `the agreement imposes obligations or restrictions on a party about using, keeping or disposing of the interests acquired` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does the agreement include provision imposing obligations or restrictions on any party about the use, retention or disposal of the interests in the shares acquired under it?
      `an interest in the company's shares has in fact been acquired under the agreement` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has an interest in the company's shares in fact been acquired by any party in pursuance of the agreement?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`Under section 824(2), does section 824 apply to our agreement?` MEANS
    `s 824(2) this section applies to the agreement` `the agreement is of the kind described in section 824(1)` `the agreement imposes obligations or restrictions on a party about using, keeping or disposing of the interests acquired` `an interest in the company's shares has in fact been acquired under the agreement`

@export Does my notification to the company about my interest, as a party to a share acquisition agreement, contain everything required?
GIVEN `the notification states that I am a party to such an agreement` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does the notification state that you are a party to such an agreement?
      `the notification names the other parties and gives their addresses so far as known to me` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does it include the names and, so far as known to you, the addresses of the other parties, identifying them as such?
      `the notification states whether any of the shares are shares in which I am interested by virtue of section 824` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does it state whether any of the shares are shares in which you are interested by virtue of section 824?
      `some of the shares are shares in which I am interested by virtue of section 824` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are some of the shares shares in which you are interested by virtue of section 824?
      `the notification states the number of those shares` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does it state the number of those shares?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`Under section 825(4), does my notification contain what is required?` MEANS
    `s 825(4) the notification contains what the subsection requires` `the notification states that I am a party to such an agreement` `the notification names the other parties and gives their addresses so far as known to me` `the notification states whether any of the shares are shares in which I am interested by virtue of section 824` `some of the shares are shares in which I am interested by virtue of section 824` `the notification states the number of those shares`

§ `Part 23 -- distributions`

§§ `What a distribution is and what profits are available (ss 829 to 835)`

@export Is this payment or transfer to members a distribution for the purposes of Part 23? True means it is; false means it is not; null means the Act does not decide it on these facts.
GIVEN `the description of the act` IS A `s 829(2) description of act` @desc What is it? One of "s 829(2)(a) an issue of shares as fully or partly paid bonus shares", "s 829(2)(b)(i) a reduction of share capital by extinguishing or reducing the liability of any of the members on any of the company's shares in respect of share capital not paid up", "s 829(2)(b)(ii) a reduction of share capital by repaying paid-up share capital", "s 829(2)(c) the redemption or purchase of any of the company's own shares out of capital (including the proceeds of any fresh issue of shares) or out of unrealised profits", "s 829(2)(d) a distribution of assets to members of the company on its winding up", "s 829(1) another description of distribution of the company's assets to its members, whether in cash or otherwise", or "s 829(1) something that is not a distribution of the company's assets to its members"
      `the redemption or purchase is in accordance with Part 18 Chapter 3, 4 or 5` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN @desc For a redemption or purchase of the company's own shares: is it in accordance with Chapter 3, 4 or 5 of Part 18? true, false, or null if you do not know
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`Under section 829(1), is this a distribution?` MEANS
    `s 829(1) the act is a distribution` `the description of the act` `the redemption or purchase is in accordance with Part 18 Chapter 3, 4 or 5`

@export Is this distribution within the profits available for the purpose? False means it exceeds them, which the Act forbids.
GIVEN `the amount of the distribution` IS A NUMBER @desc How much, in pounds, is the distribution?
      `the profits available for distribution` IS A NUMBER @desc What are the company's profits available for distribution, in pounds (see section 830(2))?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`Under section 830(1), is the distribution within the profits available for the purpose?` MEANS
    `s 830(1) the distribution is within the profits available for the purpose` `the amount of the distribution` `the profits available for distribution`

@export What are the company's profits available for distribution, in pounds? Accumulated realised profits not previously used, less accumulated realised losses not previously written off. A negative figure means there are none.
GIVEN `the accumulated realised profits` IS A NUMBER @desc What are the company's accumulated, realised profits, in pounds?
      `the part of them previously used by distribution or capitalisation` IS A NUMBER @desc How much of those profits has already been used by distribution or capitalisation, in pounds?
      `the accumulated realised losses` IS A NUMBER @desc What are the company's accumulated, realised losses, in pounds?
      `the part of them previously written off in a reduction or reorganisation of capital` IS A NUMBER @desc How much of those losses has already been written off in a duly made reduction or reorganisation of capital, in pounds?
GIVETH A NUMBER
`Under section 830(2), what are the company's profits available for distribution?` MEANS
    `s 830(2) the profits available for distribution` `the accumulated realised profits` `the part of them previously used by distribution or capitalisation` `the accumulated realised losses` `the part of them previously written off in a reduction or reorganisation of capital`

@export Is a distribution by a public company within the net asset restriction? False means it would leave the company's net assets below its called-up share capital plus undistributable reserves.
GIVEN `the company is a public company` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the company a public company?
      `the amount of the company's net assets` IS A NUMBER @desc What are the company's net assets (its assets less its liabilities), in pounds?
      `the company's called-up share capital` IS A NUMBER @desc What is the company's called-up share capital, in pounds?
      `the company's undistributable reserves` IS A NUMBER @desc What are the company's undistributable reserves, in pounds (see section 831(4))?
      `the amount of the distribution` IS A NUMBER @desc How much, in pounds, is the distribution?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`Under section 831(1), is the distribution within the net asset restriction on public companies?` MEANS
    `s 831(1) the distribution is within the net asset restriction` `the company is a public company` `the amount of the company's net assets` `the company's called-up share capital` `the company's undistributable reserves` `the amount of the distribution`

@export What are the company's undistributable reserves, in pounds?
GIVEN `the amount of the share premium account` IS A NUMBER @desc What is the balance of the share premium account, in pounds?
      `the amount of the capital redemption reserve` IS A NUMBER @desc What is the capital redemption reserve, in pounds?
      `the accumulated unrealised profits` IS A NUMBER @desc What are the company's accumulated, unrealised profits, in pounds?
      `the part of them used by capitalisation, including transfers to the capital redemption reserve` IS A NUMBER @desc How much of those unrealised profits has been used by capitalisation (including any transfer to the capital redemption reserve), in pounds?
      `the part of that which was a transfer to the capital redemption reserve` IS A NUMBER @desc How much of that was a transfer of profits to the capital redemption reserve, in pounds?
      `the accumulated unrealised losses` IS A NUMBER @desc What are the company's accumulated, unrealised losses, in pounds?
      `the part of them written off in a reduction or reorganisation of capital` IS A NUMBER @desc How much of those unrealised losses has been written off in a duly made reduction or reorganisation of capital, in pounds?
      `any other reserve prohibited from distribution by an enactment` IS A NUMBER @desc How much is held in any other reserve the company is prohibited from distributing by an enactment (other than one in Part 23), in pounds?
      `any other reserve prohibited from distribution by the articles` IS A NUMBER @desc How much is held in any other reserve the company is prohibited from distributing by its articles, in pounds?
GIVETH A NUMBER
`Under section 831(4), what are the company's undistributable reserves?` MEANS
    `s 831(4) the company's undistributable reserves` `the amount of the share premium account` `the amount of the capital redemption reserve` `the accumulated unrealised profits` `the part of them used by capitalisation, including transfers to the capital redemption reserve` `the part of that which was a transfer to the capital redemption reserve` `the accumulated unrealised losses` `the part of them written off in a reduction or reorganisation of capital` `any other reserve prohibited from distribution by an enactment` `any other reserve prohibited from distribution by the articles`

@export Does the distribution by an investment company leave it with assets of at least one and a half times its liabilities to creditors?
GIVEN `the amount of the company's assets` IS A NUMBER @desc What is the amount of the company's assets, in pounds?
      `the aggregate of the company's liabilities to creditors` IS A NUMBER @desc What is the aggregate of the company's liabilities to creditors, in pounds?
      `the amount of the distribution` IS A NUMBER @desc How much, in pounds, is the distribution?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`Under section 832(3), does the distribution leave the investment company with enough assets?` MEANS
    `s 832(3) the distribution is within the asset cover the subsection requires` `the amount of the company's assets` `the aggregate of the company's liabilities to creditors` `the amount of the distribution`

§§ `The accounts that justify a distribution, and successive distributions (ss 836 to 840)`

@export May the company justify a distribution by interim accounts? True where the distribution would contravene Part 23 by reference to its last annual accounts.
GIVEN `the distribution would contravene Part 23 by reference to the last annual accounts` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Would the distribution be found to contravene Part 23 if the company's last annual accounts were used?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`Under section 836(2)(a), may the company justify the distribution by reference to interim accounts?` MEANS
    `s 836(2)(a) the distribution may be justified by reference to interim accounts` `the distribution would contravene Part 23 by reference to the last annual accounts`

@export May the company justify a distribution by initial accounts? True during the company's first accounting reference period, or before any accounts have been circulated for it.
GIVEN `the distribution is proposed to be declared during the company's first accounting reference period` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the distribution proposed to be declared during the company's first accounting reference period?
      `the distribution is proposed to be declared before any accounts have been circulated for that period` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it proposed to be declared before any accounts have been circulated in respect of that period?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`Under section 836(2)(b), may the company justify the distribution by reference to initial accounts?` MEANS
    `s 836(2)(b) the distribution may be justified by reference to initial accounts` `the distribution is proposed to be declared during the company's first accounting reference period` `the distribution is proposed to be declared before any accounts have been circulated for that period`

@export What amount counts as the proposed distribution once earlier distributions and relevant financial assistance and payments are added, in pounds?
GIVEN `the amount of the proposed distribution` IS A NUMBER @desc How much, in pounds, is the proposed distribution?
      `the amount of previous distributions by reference to the same accounts` IS A NUMBER @desc How much, in pounds, has already been distributed by reference to the same relevant accounts?
      `the amount of relevant financial assistance and other relevant payments since those accounts were prepared` IS A NUMBER @desc How much, in pounds, of financial assistance or other relevant payments (section 840(2)) has been given or made since those accounts were prepared?
GIVETH A NUMBER
`Under section 840(1), what amount counts as the proposed distribution?` MEANS
    `s 840(1) the amount of the proposed distribution as increased for the purposes of this Part` `the amount of the proposed distribution` `the amount of previous distributions by reference to the same accounts` `the amount of relevant financial assistance and other relevant payments since those accounts were prepared`

§§ `Distributions in kind, unlawful distributions and the savings (ss 841 to 853)`

@export What is the amount of a distribution made by selling or transferring a non-cash asset to a member, in pounds?
GIVEN `the amount or value of the consideration` IS A NUMBER @desc What amount or value of consideration did the company receive for the asset, in pounds?
      `the book value of the asset` IS A NUMBER @desc What is the book value of the asset (the amount at which it is stated in the relevant accounts, or nil), in pounds?
GIVETH A NUMBER
`Under section 845(2), what is the amount of the distribution in kind?` MEANS
    `s 845(2) the amount of the distribution or the relevant part of it` `the amount or value of the consideration` `the book value of the asset`

@export What am I liable to do about a distribution I received from the company that was made in contravention of Part 23: repay it, pay the company a sum equal to its value, or nothing under this subsection (not liable)?
GIVEN `the distribution made to me was made in contravention of Part 23` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Was the distribution made to you made in contravention of Part 23?
      `at the time I knew or had reasonable grounds for believing it was so made` IS A BOOLEAN @desc At the time of the distribution, did you know, or have reasonable grounds for believing, that it was made in contravention of Part 23?
      `the distribution was made in cash` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Was it made in cash (rather than in kind)?
      `it was financial assistance given in contravention of section 678 or 679, or a payment on the redemption or purchase of the company's own shares` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Was it financial assistance given in contravention of section 678 or 679, or a payment in respect of the company's redemption or purchase of its own shares?
GIVETH A `s 847(2) liability of the member`
`Under section 847(2), what am I liable to do about the distribution I received?` MEANS
    `s 847(2) what the member is liable to do` `the distribution made to me was made in contravention of Part 23` `at the time I knew or had reasonable grounds for believing it was so made` `the distribution was made in cash` `it was financial assistance given in contravention of section 678 or 679, or a payment on the redemption or purchase of the company's own shares`

@export May the company use an unrealised profit to pay up debentures or amounts unpaid on its issued shares? False means it must not.
GIVEN `the profit is an unrealised profit` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the profit an unrealised profit?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`Under section 849, may the company apply the profit in paying up debentures or unpaid amounts on its shares?` MEANS
    `s 849 the company may apply the profit in paying up debentures or any amounts unpaid on its issued shares` `the profit is an unrealised profit`

@export Is this asset a fixed asset for the purposes of Part 23?
GIVEN `the asset is intended for use on a continuing basis in the company's activities` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the asset intended for use on a continuing basis in the company's activities?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`Under section 853(6), is the asset a fixed asset?` MEANS
    `s 853(6) the asset is a fixed asset` `the asset is intended for use on a continuing basis in the company's activities`

§ `Part 24 -- annual confirmation of accuracy of information on register`

§§ `The confirmation statement and its timing (ss 853A to 853G)`

@export By what day must the company deliver its confirmation statement to the registrar? The fourteenth day after the end of the review period.
GIVEN `the last day of the review period` IS A DATE @desc On what day does the review period end?
GIVETH A DATE
`Under section 853A(1), by what day must the company deliver its confirmation statement?` MEANS
    `s 853A(1) the last day of the period of 14 days after the end of the review period` `the last day of the review period`

@export On what day does the company's review period end if it begins on the day I give? A review period is 12 months.
GIVEN `the first day of the review period` IS A DATE @desc On what day does the review period begin? (the company's incorporation day for the first, otherwise the day after the previous review period ended)
GIVETH A DATE
`Under section 853A(5), on what day does the review period end?` MEANS
    `s 853A(5) the last day of the review period beginning on the day` `the first day of the review period`

@export If the company delivers its confirmation statement early, on what day does its next review period begin?
GIVEN `the last day of the review period concerned` IS A DATE @desc On what day does the current review period end?
      `the confirmation date of the statement delivered` IS A DATE @desc What confirmation date does the statement specify?
GIVETH A DATE
`Under section 853A(6), on what day does the next review period begin?` MEANS
    `s 853A(6) the first day of the next review period` `the last day of the review period concerned` `the confirmation date of the statement delivered`

@export Must the company tell the registrar of a change in its principal business activities when it makes its confirmation statement?
GIVEN `the company is making a confirmation statement` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the company making a confirmation statement?
      `its principal business activities changed during the confirmation period` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did the company's principal business activities change during the confirmation period?
      `this is its first confirmation statement` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is this its first confirmation statement?
      `by the time of incorporation its principal business activities had changed from those stated when it was formed` IS A BOOLEAN @desc By the time the company was incorporated, had its principal business activities changed from those specified in the statement made on its formation?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`Under section 853C(2), must the company notify the registrar of a change in its principal business activities?` MEANS
    `s 853C(2) the company must give notice to the registrar of the change at the same time as it delivers the confirmation statement` (`s 853C(1) this section applies` `the company is making a confirmation statement` `its principal business activities changed during the confirmation period`) (`s 853C(1A) this section also applies` `this is its first confirmation statement` `by the time of incorporation its principal business activities had changed from those stated when it was formed`)

@export Must the company deliver a statement of capital with its confirmation statement?
GIVEN `the company has a share capital` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does the company have a share capital?
      `the company is making a confirmation statement` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the company making a confirmation statement?
      `nothing required in the statement of capital has changed since the last one` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has nothing that the statement of capital must deal with changed since the last statement of capital was delivered?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`Under section 853D(2), must the company deliver a statement of capital with its confirmation statement?` MEANS
    `s 853D(2) the company must deliver a statement of capital to the registrar at the same time as it delivers the confirmation statement` (`s 853D(1) this section applies` `the company has a share capital` `the company is making a confirmation statement`) `nothing required in the statement of capital has changed since the last one`

@export Must my name and address be delivered to the registrar as a holder of at least 5% of a class of the company's shares?
GIVEN `the number of shares of the class I held at the end of the confirmation date` IS A NUMBER @desc How many shares of the class did you hold at the end of the confirmation date?
      `the number of issued shares of the class` IS A NUMBER @desc How many issued shares of that class does the company have?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`Under section 853G(6)(a), must my name and address be delivered as a holder of 5% or more of a class?` MEANS
    `s 853G(6)(a) the person is a person whose name and address must be delivered` `the number of shares of the class I held at the end of the confirmation date` `the number of issued shares of the class`

§§ `Failing to deliver the confirmation statement (s 853L)`

@export Has the company committed an offence by failing to deliver its confirmation statement before the end of the 14 days after the review period?
GIVEN `the last day of the review period` IS A DATE @desc On what day did the review period end?
      `the day the confirmation statement was delivered, if it has been` IS A MAYBE DATE @desc On what day was the confirmation statement delivered? (leave empty if it has not been delivered)
      `today's date` IS A DATE @desc On what date are you asking?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`Under section 853L(1)(a), has the company committed an offence by not delivering its confirmation statement in time?` MEANS
    `s 853L(1)(a) the company commits an offence` (`s 853L(1) the company has failed to deliver a confirmation statement before the end of the period of 14 days after the end of the review period` `the last day of the review period` `the day the confirmation statement was delivered, if it has been` `today's date`)

@export Have I, as an officer of the company, committed an offence because the company did not deliver its confirmation statement in time? A shadow director is treated as a director for this purpose.
GIVEN `the last day of the review period` IS A DATE @desc On what day did the review period end?
      `the day the confirmation statement was delivered, if it has been` IS A MAYBE DATE @desc On what day was the confirmation statement delivered? (leave empty if it has not been delivered)
      `today's date` IS A DATE @desc On what date are you asking?
      `I am an officer of the company who is in default` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN @desc Are you an officer of the company who is in default (section 1121)? true, false, or null if you do not know
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`Under section 853L(1)(b), have I as an officer committed an offence by the company's late confirmation statement?` MEANS
    `s 853L(1)(b) the officer of the company commits an offence` (`s 853L(1) the company has failed to deliver a confirmation statement before the end of the period of 14 days after the end of the review period` `the last day of the review period` `the day the confirmation statement was delivered, if it has been` `today's date`) `I am an officer of the company who is in default`

@export What is the most the daily default fine can be, in pounds, for each day of continued contravention? The Act does not state what a level on the standard scale is in pounds: enter the amount for the level the penalty names (level 4 in England and Wales, level 5 in Scotland and Northern Ireland).
GIVEN `the kind of conviction` IS A `Mode of conviction` @desc The kind of conviction: one of "on summary conviction in England and Wales", "on summary conviction in Scotland" or "on summary conviction in Northern Ireland"
      `the pounds that level 4 stands for in England and Wales, or level 5 in Scotland and Northern Ireland` IS A NUMBER @desc How many pounds does the level on the standard scale that the penalty names stand for at present? (level 4 for England and Wales, level 5 for Scotland and Northern Ireland)
GIVETH A MAYBE NUMBER
`Under section 853L(6), what is the most the daily default fine can be in pounds?` MEANS
    CONSIDER `s 853L(6) the fine for each day on which the contravention continues and the person is in default does not exceed` `the kind of conviction`
    WHEN NOTHING THEN NOTHING
    WHEN JUST limit THEN JUST (`s 853L(2) the daily default fine limit in pounds` limit `the pounds that level 4 stands for in England and Wales, or level 5 in Scotland and Northern Ireland`)

-- ====================================================================================================
-- seat questions from part coa19 (merged by the lead on 2026-11-12; unchanged text follows)
-- ====================================================================================================
-- coa19-seat.l4: the seat layer over Part 25 of the Companies Act 2006 (Company charges), ss 859A to 894: coa19's ranges, lines 11597-12202 of ukpga-2006-46.txt.
--
-- SEAT: an individual who is, or is about to become, a director, a company secretary or a member (shareholder) of a company registered under the Act, or who deals with
-- one (a lender who takes a charge, a person who appoints a receiver, a creditor), asking on facts they can state what the Act requires or lets them do, what rights they have
-- against the company or its directors, what they must disclose, file, approve or vote on and by when, and what follows (liability, offences, penalties) if it is not done.
-- (Assumed, not ruled: the Act is addressed to companies, so the individual is whoever stands in a company's management or ownership.)
-- There is no seat for the registrar, the court or the Secretary of State: what they do appears only as what it means for this person.
--
-- PLAIN INPUTS: every question takes the facts the person can state (yes or no, a number, a date, a choice from a list), each with an @desc worded as that person is asked. The records
-- the layer-1 modules expect are built inside each question, from those answers, and the SAME layer-1 rule is then called: no rule is restated here.
-- A seam answer that another part of the Act owns (s 738 "debenture", s 1121 "officer in default", s 1136 places, s 1062 seal) is asked as a plain fact and passed as JUST fact; the answer NOTHING never reaches a caller as FALSE.
-- The prescribed fee, the pounds that level 3 on the standard scale and the statutory maximum stand for are not in the Act: they are inputs.
--
-- HOW TO READ AN ANSWER: every question that answers yes or no returns a MAYBE BOOLEAN. JUST TRUE: the Act says yes. JUST FALSE: the Act says no in its own words. NOTHING: the Act does not decide
-- the case (it is silent, lists without closing the list, says "includes", leaves a term undefined, points outside the text, or limits what it grants in its own wording). Never read NOTHING as no.
--
-- The text prints Chapter A1 and Chapters 1 and 2 side by side. A charge created by a company registered in England and Wales or Northern Ireland can be asked about under ss 859A to 859Q or under
-- ss 860 to 877; one by a company registered in Scotland under ss 859A to 859Q or ss 878 to 892. The questions are named for the section they answer, and the text does not say which governs (finding 1 in NOTES.md).

§ `Part 25 Company charges -- the questions of the individual (ss 859A to 894)`

§§ `Charges my company creates or acquires: registration under Chapter A1 (ss 859A to 859G)`

-- s 859A(1) and (6). Chapter A1 asks a UK-registered company that creates a charge to have it registered, except for three kinds of charge.
@export Under section 859A(1) and (6), does the registration requirement of section 859A apply to a charge my company creates?
GIVEN `my company is registered in England and Wales, Scotland or Northern Ireland` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is your company a UK-registered company (registered in England and Wales, Scotland or Northern Ireland)?
      `my company creates a charge` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is your company creating a charge over its property (a mortgage or, in Scotland, a standard security or other right in security)?
      `the charge is a landlord's charge on a cash deposit given as security for a lease of land` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it a charge in favour of a landlord on a cash deposit given as security in connection with the lease of land?
      `the charge is a Lloyd's member's charge for its underwriting business` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it a charge created by a member of Lloyd's to secure its obligations in connection with its underwriting business at Lloyd's?
      `the charge is excluded by another Act` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the charge excluded from section 859A by or under any other Act?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 859A(1) and (6), does the registration requirement of section 859A apply to a charge my company creates` IS
    `s 859A(1) this section applies` `my company is registered in England and Wales, Scotland or Northern Ireland` `my company creates a charge` (`s 859A(6) the charge` OF `the charge is a landlord's charge on a cash deposit given as security for a lease of land`, `the charge is a Lloyd's member's charge for its underwriting business`, `the charge is excluded by another Act`)

-- s 859E(1) Table. The date a charge is taken to be created depends on how it was created.
@export Under section 859E(1), on what date is my charge taken to be created?
GIVEN `how my charge was created` IS A `s 859E type of charge` @desc Which description in the section 859E Table fits your charge? (a standard security; a charge by a deed with immediate effect on execution and delivery, held in escrow, or held as undelivered; a charge by an instrument that is not a deed, with or without immediate effect on execution; a charge with no instrument; or a charge the Table does not describe)
      `the date of the event the Table names` IS A DATE @desc What is the date of the event the Table names for your kind of charge? (the recording or registration date for a standard security; the date of delivery for a deed with immediate effect or held as undelivered; the date of delivery into escrow for a deed in escrow; the date of execution for an instrument that is not a deed and takes effect on execution; the date it takes effect for one that does not; the date the charge comes into effect where there is no instrument)
GIVETH A MAYBE DATE
DECIDE `Under section 859E(1), on what date is my charge taken to be created` IS
    `s 859E(1) the date on which the charge is taken to be created` `how my charge was created` `the date of the event the Table names`

-- s 859A(4). 21 days beginning with the day after the date of creation, unless a court has extended the period.
@export Under section 859A(4), what is the last day for delivering the statement of particulars of my charge to the registrar?
GIVEN `how my charge was created` IS A `s 859E type of charge` @desc Which description in the section 859E Table fits your charge? (see the question on section 859E(1))
      `the date of the event the Table names` IS A DATE @desc What is the date of the event the Table names for your kind of charge?
      `a court has extended the period under section 859F(3)` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has a court ordered that the period allowed for delivery be extended?
      `the last day the court's order allows` IS A DATE @desc If so, what is the last day the court's order allows? (any date if there is no order)
GIVETH A MAYBE DATE
DECIDE `Under section 859A(4), what is the last day for delivering the statement of particulars of my charge to the registrar` IS
    CONSIDER `s 859E(1) the date on which the charge is taken to be created` `how my charge was created` `the date of the event the Table names`
    WHEN NOTHING THEN NOTHING
    WHEN JUST created THEN JUST (`s 859A(4) the last day of the period allowed for delivery` created (IF `a court has extended the period under section 859F(3)` THEN JUST `the last day the court's order allows` ELSE NOTHING))

-- s 859A(2) to (5). The registrar must register a charge if a section 859D statement is delivered in time, with a certified copy of any instrument (and a copy of any order extending time).
@export Under section 859A(2) to (5), must the registrar register the charge my company created?
GIVEN `my company is registered in England and Wales, Scotland or Northern Ireland` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is your company a UK-registered company?
      `my company created a charge` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did your company create the charge?
      `the charge is a landlord's charge on a cash deposit given as security for a lease of land` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it a charge in favour of a landlord on a cash deposit given as security in connection with the lease of land?
      `the charge is a Lloyd's member's charge for its underwriting business` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it a charge created by a member of Lloyd's to secure its obligations in connection with its underwriting business at Lloyd's?
      `the charge is excluded by another Act` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the charge excluded from section 859A by or under any other Act?
      `how my charge was created` IS A `s 859E type of charge` @desc Which description in the section 859E Table fits your charge?
      `the date of the event the Table names` IS A DATE @desc What is the date of the event the Table names for your kind of charge?
      `a court has extended the period under section 859F(3)` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has a court ordered that the period allowed for delivery be extended?
      `the last day the court's order allows` IS A DATE @desc If so, what is the last day the court's order allows? (any date if there is no order)
      `the company or a person interested in the charge delivered a statement of particulars to the registrar for registration` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did the company, or a person interested in the charge, deliver a statement of particulars to the registrar for registration?
      `my statement contains every particular section 859D requires` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does the statement contain every particular section 859D requires? (see the question on section 859D)
      `the day the statement was delivered` IS A DATE @desc On what day was the statement delivered to the registrar?
      `the charge is created or evidenced by an instrument` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the charge created or evidenced by an instrument?
      `a certified copy of the instrument was delivered with the statement` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Was a certified copy of the instrument delivered with the statement? (No if there is no instrument)
      `a copy of the court's order was delivered with the statement` IS A BOOLEAN @desc If a court extended the period, was a copy of its order delivered with the statement?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 859A(2) to (5), must the registrar register the charge my company created` IS
    CONSIDER `s 859E(1) the date on which the charge is taken to be created` `how my charge was created` `the date of the event the Table names`
    WHEN NOTHING THEN NOTHING
    WHEN JUST created THEN
        `s 859A(2) to (5) the registrar is required to register the charge`
            (`s 859A(2) the registrar must register the charge` (`s 859A(1) this section applies` `my company is registered in England and Wales, Scotland or Northern Ireland` `my company created a charge` (`s 859A(6) the charge` OF `the charge is a landlord's charge on a cash deposit given as security for a lease of land`, `the charge is a Lloyd's member's charge for its underwriting business`, `the charge is excluded by another Act`) EQUALS JUST TRUE) `the company or a person interested in the charge delivered a statement of particulars to the registrar for registration` `my statement contains every particular section 859D requires` `the day the statement was delivered` (`s 859A(4) the last day of the period allowed for delivery` created (IF `a court has extended the period under section 859F(3)` THEN JUST `the last day the court's order allows` ELSE NOTHING)))
            (`s 859A(3) the registrar is required to register the charge` `the charge is created or evidenced by an instrument` `a certified copy of the instrument was delivered with the statement`)
            (`s 859A(5) a copy of the order must be delivered to the registrar with the statement of particulars` `a court has extended the period under section 859F(3)`)
            `a copy of the court's order was delivered with the statement`

-- s 859B(1). A series of debentures giving holders a charge pari passu.
@export Under section 859B(1), does section 859B (a charge in a series of debentures) apply to the debentures my company creates?
GIVEN `the instruments are debentures` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are the instruments debentures (debenture stock, bonds or other securities of the company, whether or not they charge its assets)?
      `my company is registered in England and Wales, Scotland or Northern Ireland` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is your company a UK-registered company?
      `my company creates a series of debentures containing a charge, or giving a charge by reference to another instrument` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is your company creating a series of debentures that contain a charge, or give a charge by reference to another instrument?
      `the debenture holders of the series are entitled to the benefit of the charge equally (pari passu)` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are the debenture holders of that series entitled to the benefit of the charge equally (pari passu)?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 859B(1), does section 859B apply to the debentures my company creates` IS
    `s 859B(1) this section applies` (JUST `the instruments are debentures`) `my company is registered in England and Wales, Scotland or Northern Ireland` `my company creates a series of debentures containing a charge, or giving a charge by reference to another instrument` `the debenture holders of the series are entitled to the benefit of the charge equally (pari passu)`

-- s 859B(6). 21 days from the day after the deed (or, with no deed, the first debenture) is executed.
@export Under section 859B(6), what is the last day for delivering the statement of particulars for my series of debentures?
GIVEN `there is a deed containing the charge` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is there a deed containing the charge?
      `the day the deed was executed` IS A DATE @desc On what day was the deed executed? (any date if there is no deed)
      `the day the first debenture of the series was executed` IS A DATE @desc On what day was the first debenture of the series executed?
GIVETH A DATE
DECIDE `Under section 859B(6), what is the last day for delivering the statement of particulars for my series of debentures` IS
    `s 859B(6) the last day of the period allowed for delivery` `there is a deed containing the charge` `the day the deed was executed` `the day the first debenture of the series was executed`

-- s 859C. A company that acquires property or an undertaking already subject to a charge.
@export Under section 859C(1) to (3), must the registrar register a charge that already exists on property my company has acquired?
GIVEN `my company is registered in England and Wales, Scotland or Northern Ireland` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is your company a UK-registered company?
      `my company has acquired property or an undertaking` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has your company acquired property or an undertaking?
      `it is subject to a charge` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the property or undertaking subject to a charge?
      `the charge is a landlord's charge on a cash deposit given as security for a lease of land` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it a charge in favour of a landlord on a cash deposit given as security in connection with the lease of land?
      `the charge is a Lloyd's member's charge for its underwriting business` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it a charge created by a member of Lloyd's to secure its obligations in connection with its underwriting business at Lloyd's?
      `the charge is excluded by another Act` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the charge excluded from section 859A by or under any other Act?
      `the company or a person interested in the charge delivered a statement of particulars to the registrar for registration` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did the company, or a person interested in the charge, deliver a statement of particulars to the registrar for registration?
      `my statement contains every particular section 859D requires` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does the statement contain every particular section 859D requires, including the date of acquisition?
      `the charge is created or evidenced by an instrument` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the charge created or evidenced by an instrument?
      `a certified copy of the instrument was delivered with the statement` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Was a certified copy of the instrument delivered with the statement? (No if there is no instrument)
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 859C(1) to (3), must the registrar register a charge that already exists on property my company has acquired` IS
    `s 859C(2) and (3) the registrar is required to register the charge`
        (`s 859C(2) the registrar must register the charge` (`s 859C(1) this section applies` `my company is registered in England and Wales, Scotland or Northern Ireland` `my company has acquired property or an undertaking` `it is subject to a charge` (`s 859A(6) the charge` OF `the charge is a landlord's charge on a cash deposit given as security for a lease of land`, `the charge is a Lloyd's member's charge for its underwriting business`, `the charge is excluded by another Act`)) `the company or a person interested in the charge delivered a statement of particulars to the registrar for registration` `my statement contains every particular section 859D requires`)
        (`s 859C(3) the registrar is required to register the charge` `the charge is created or evidenced by an instrument` `a certified copy of the instrument was delivered with the statement`)

-- s 859D(1) to (3). What a statement of particulars must contain.
@export Under section 859D(1) to (3), is my statement of particulars a "section 859D statement of particulars"?
GIVEN `the charge is created or evidenced by an instrument` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the charge created or evidenced by an instrument?
      `the charge is one to which section 859C applies (it already existed on property my company acquired)` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it a charge that already existed on property or an undertaking your company acquired?
      `the number of persons, security agents or trustees in whose favour the charge is created or who hold it` IS A NUMBER @desc How many persons, security agents or trustees have the charge in their favour or hold it?
      `it gives the registered name and number of the company` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does the statement give the registered name and number of the company?
      `it gives the date of creation of the charge` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does it give the date of creation of the charge?
      `it gives the date of acquisition of the property or undertaking` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does it give the date of acquisition of the property or undertaking? (needed only for a charge that existed on acquired property)
      `it gives the name of each person, security agent or trustee` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does it give the name of each of the persons in whose favour the charge has been created, or of the security agents or trustees holding it?
      `it gives the names of any four of them and says that there are others` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Where there are more than four, does it give the names of any four listed in the charge instrument and say that there are others?
      `it says whether the instrument contains a floating charge and whether that covers all the property and undertaking` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does it say whether the instrument is expressed to contain a floating charge and, if so, whether it covers all the company's property and undertaking?
      `it says whether the terms prohibit or restrict further security ranking equally or ahead` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does it say whether any term of the charge prohibits or restricts the company creating further security that ranks equally with or ahead of the charge?
      `it says whether registered land, a ship, aircraft or intellectual property is subject to a fixed charge, with a short description` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does it say whether (and give a short description of) any land, ship, aircraft or intellectual property registered or required to be registered in the United Kingdom is subject to a fixed charge?
      `it says whether the instrument includes a fixed charge over other tangible or intangible property` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does it say whether the instrument includes a fixed charge over any other tangible (corporeal) or intangible (incorporeal) property?
      `it says that there is no instrument` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Where there is no instrument, does it say so?
      `it gives the names of the persons in whose favour the charge was created, or of the security agents or trustees` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Where there is no instrument, does it give the names of each person in whose favour the charge was created, or of the security agents or trustees holding it?
      `it gives the nature of the charge` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Where there is no instrument, does it give the nature of the charge?
      `it gives a short description of the property or undertaking charged` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Where there is no instrument, does it give a short description of the property or undertaking charged?
      `it gives the obligations secured by the charge` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Where there is no instrument, does it give the obligations secured by the charge?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 859D(1) to (3), is my statement of particulars a section 859D statement of particulars` IS
    `s 859D(1) the statement is a section 859D statement of particulars` `what my statement contains` `the number of persons, security agents or trustees in whose favour the charge is created or who hold it` `the charge is created or evidenced by an instrument` `the charge is one to which section 859C applies (it already existed on property my company acquired)`
    WHERE
        `what my statement contains` MEANS `s 859D what the statement contains` OF `it gives the registered name and number of the company`, `it gives the date of creation of the charge`, `it gives the date of acquisition of the property or undertaking`, `it gives the name of each person, security agent or trustee`, `it gives the names of any four of them and says that there are others`, `it says whether the instrument contains a floating charge and whether that covers all the property and undertaking`, `it says whether the terms prohibit or restrict further security ranking equally or ahead`, `it says whether registered land, a ship, aircraft or intellectual property is subject to a fixed charge, with a short description`, `it says whether the instrument includes a fixed charge over other tangible or intangible property`, `it says that there is no instrument`, `it gives the names of the persons in whose favour the charge was created, or of the security agents or trustees`, `it gives the nature of the charge`, `it gives a short description of the property or undertaking charged`, `it gives the obligations secured by the charge`

-- s 859F. Extension of the period by the court.
@export Under section 859F(1) to (3), may the court extend the period for delivering my charge to the registrar?
GIVEN `the court is satisfied that no one interested in the charge delivered the required documents before the end of the period` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the court satisfied that neither the company nor any other person interested in the charge delivered the documents required by section 859A or 859B before the end of the period allowed?
      `the court is satisfied that the failure was accidental, inadvertent or had another sufficient cause` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the court satisfied that the failure to deliver was accidental, or due to inadvertence or to some other sufficient cause?
      `the court is satisfied that the failure does not prejudice creditors or shareholders` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the court satisfied that the failure is not of a nature to prejudice the position of creditors or shareholders of the company?
      `the court is satisfied that on other grounds it is just and equitable to grant relief` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the court satisfied that on other grounds it is just and equitable to grant relief?
      `I apply as the company or as a person interested in the charge` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the application made by the company or by a person interested in the charge?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 859F(1) to (3), may the court extend the period for delivering my charge to the registrar` IS
    `s 859F(3) the court may order that the period allowed for delivery be extended`
        (`s 859F(1) subsection (3) applies` `the court is satisfied that no one interested in the charge delivered the required documents before the end of the period`
            (`s 859F(2) the requirement is met` `the court is satisfied that the failure was accidental, inadvertent or had another sufficient cause` `the court is satisfied that the failure does not prejudice creditors or shareholders` `the court is satisfied that on other grounds it is just and equitable to grant relief`))
        `I apply as the company or as a person interested in the charge`

-- s 859G(1). Information a certified copy need not contain.
@export Under section 859G(1), must a certified copy of an instrument delivered to the registrar include this item?
GIVEN `the item` IS A `s 859G item in a certified copy` @desc Which item is it? (personal information about an individual other than the individual's name; the name of an individual; the number or other identifier of a bank or securities account; a signature; or any other item)
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 859G(1), must a certified copy of an instrument delivered to the registrar include this item` IS
    `s 859G(1) the item is required to be included in a certified copy of an instrument or debenture` `the item`

§§ `What follows if a charge is not delivered, and what the register shows (ss 859H to 859O)`

-- s 859H(1) and (3). A charge that is not delivered in time is void, so far as it gives security over the company's property, against a liquidator, an administrator and a creditor.
@export Under section 859H(1) and (3), is the charge void against a liquidator, an administrator or a creditor of my company?
GIVEN `section 859A applies to the charge` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does section 859A apply to the charge (see the question on section 859A(1))?
      `section 859B applies to the charge` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does section 859B (a series of debentures) apply to the charge?
      `the documents were delivered` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has the company, or another person interested in the charge, delivered the documents section 859A or 859B requires?
      `the day they were delivered` IS A DATE @desc On what day were they delivered? (any date if they have not been)
      `the last day of the period allowed for delivery under the section in question` IS A DATE @desc What is the last day of the period allowed for delivery? (see the question on section 859A(4) or 859B(6))
      `the last day the court's order allows` IS A MAYBE DATE @desc If a court extended the period under section 859F(3), the last day its order allows (leave empty if there is no order)
      `the day I am asking` IS A DATE @desc What day is it today (or the day you are asking about)?
      `against whom` IS A `s 859H(3) party against whom the charge may be void` @desc Against whom do you ask? (a liquidator, an administrator or a creditor of the company, or any other person)
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 859H(1) and (3), is the charge void against a liquidator, an administrator or a creditor of my company` IS
    `s 859H(3) the charge is void against the party`
        (`s 859H(1) this section applies` `section 859A applies to the charge` `section 859B applies to the charge`
            (`s 859H(1)(b) the thing was done by the last day of the period` (IF `the documents were delivered` THEN JUST `the day they were delivered` ELSE NOTHING) (`s 859H(2) the last day of the relevant period allowed for delivery` `the last day of the period allowed for delivery under the section in question` `the last day the court's order allows`) `the day I am asking`))
        `against whom`

-- s 859H(4). If the charge becomes void, the money it secures becomes payable at once.
@export Under section 859H(4), does the money secured by a void charge become payable immediately?
GIVEN `the charge has become void against the party under section 859H` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has the charge become void against the person under section 859H(3) (see the previous question)?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 859H(4), does the money secured by a void charge become payable immediately` IS
    `s 859H(4) the money secured by the charge immediately becomes payable` (IF `the charge has become void against the party under section 859H` THEN JUST TRUE ELSE JUST FALSE)

-- s 859I(6). The registrar's certificate of registration.
@export Under section 859I(6), is the registrar's certificate conclusive evidence that the documents were delivered in time?
GIVEN `the charge was registered under section 859A or 859B` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Was the charge registered under section 859A or 859B?
      `the registrar gave a certificate of registration` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did the registrar give a certificate of the registration of the charge?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 859I(6), is the registrar's certificate conclusive evidence that the documents were delivered in time` IS
    `s 859I(6) the certificate is conclusive evidence that the documents were delivered before the end of the relevant period` `the charge was registered under section 859A or 859B` `the registrar gave a certificate of registration`

-- s 859J(1). A company that holds property as trustee.
@export Under section 859J(1), may I deliver a statement that my company holds the charged property as trustee?
GIVEN `my company is acting as trustee of property or undertaking that is the subject of a charge delivered for registration under Chapter A1` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is your company acting as trustee of property or an undertaking that is the subject of a charge delivered for registration?
      `I am the company or a person interested in the charge` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are you the company, or a person interested in the charge?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 859J(1), may I deliver a statement that my company holds the charged property as trustee` IS
    `s 859J(1) the person may deliver to the registrar a statement that the company is acting as trustee` `my company is acting as trustee of property or undertaking that is the subject of a charge delivered for registration under Chapter A1` `I am the company or a person interested in the charge`

-- s 859K(1), (8) and (9). Appointing a receiver or manager.
@export Under section 859K(1), (8) and (9), must I give the registrar notice that I obtained an order for, or made, an appointment of a receiver or manager?
GIVEN `I obtained an order for the appointment of a receiver or manager of a company's property or undertaking` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did you obtain an order for the appointment of a receiver or manager of a company's property or undertaking?
      `I appointed such a receiver or manager under powers contained in an instrument` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did you appoint such a receiver or manager under powers contained in an instrument?
      `a court in England and Wales or Northern Ireland appointed the receiver or manager` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Was the receiver or manager appointed by a court in England and Wales or Northern Ireland?
      `the instrument is governed by the law of England and Wales or Northern Ireland` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Was the receiver or manager appointed under an instrument governed by the law of England and Wales or Northern Ireland?
      `the receiver is appointed under Chapter 2 of Part 3 of the Insolvency Act 1986` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the receiver appointed under Chapter 2 of Part 3 of the Insolvency Act 1986 (receivers (Scotland))?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 859K(1), (8) and (9), must I give the registrar notice that I obtained an order for or made an appointment of a receiver or manager` IS
    `s 859K(1), (8) and (9) the person must give notice to the registrar`
        (`s 859K(1) subsection (2) applies` `I obtained an order for the appointment of a receiver or manager of a company's property or undertaking` `I appointed such a receiver or manager under powers contained in an instrument`)
        (`s 859K(8) this section applies to the receiver or manager` `a court in England and Wales or Northern Ireland appointed the receiver or manager` `the instrument is governed by the law of England and Wales or Northern Ireland`)
        (`s 859K(9) this section applies to the receiver` `the receiver is appointed under Chapter 2 of Part 3 of the Insolvency Act 1986`)

-- s 859K(2)(a). Within 7 days of the order or of the appointment.
@export Under section 859K(2)(a), did I give the registrar notice within 7 days of the order or of the appointment?
GIVEN `the day of the order or of the appointment` IS A DATE @desc On what day was the order made, or the appointment made under the instrument?
      `I have given the registrar notice` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Have you given the registrar notice of that fact?
      `the day I gave the registrar notice` IS A DATE @desc On what day did you give the registrar notice? (any date if you have not)
      `the day I am asking` IS A DATE @desc What day is it today (or the day you are asking about)?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 859K(2)(a), did I give the registrar notice within 7 days of the order or of the appointment` IS
    `s 859K(2)(a) the person gave the registrar notice within 7 days` `the day of the order or of the appointment` (IF `I have given the registrar notice` THEN JUST `the day I gave the registrar notice` ELSE NOTHING) `the day I am asking`

@export Under section 859K(2), what is the last day for giving the registrar notice of an order for, or an appointment of, a receiver or manager?
GIVEN `the day of the order or of the appointment` IS A DATE @desc On what day was the order made, or the appointment made under the instrument?
GIVETH A DATE
DECIDE `Under section 859K(2), what is the last day for giving the registrar notice of an order for or an appointment of a receiver or manager` IS
    `s 859K(2) the last day of 7 days after` `the day of the order or of the appointment`

-- s 859K(6). Default is an offence.
@export Under section 859K(6), do I commit an offence by failing to give the registrar notice of the receiver or manager?
GIVEN `the section requires me to give notice (see the question on section 859K(1), (8) and (9))` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN @desc The answer to the question on section 859K(1), (8) and (9): JUST TRUE, JUST FALSE or NOTHING
      `I made default in complying with subsection (2) or (3)` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did you fail to give the notice required by section 859K(2) or (3) in time?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 859K(6), do I commit an offence by failing to give the registrar notice of the receiver or manager` IS
    `s 859K(6) the person commits an offence` `the section requires me to give notice (see the question on section 859K(1), (8) and (9))` `I made default in complying with subsection (2) or (3)`

@export Under section 859K(7), what is the most I can be fined in pounds on summary conviction for that offence, and for each day it continues?
GIVEN `the pounds that level 3 on the standard scale stands for` IS A NUMBER @desc How many pounds does level 3 on the standard scale stand for? (the Act does not say: ask for the current figure)
GIVETH A LIST OF MAYBE NUMBER
DECIDE `Under section 859K(7), what is the most I can be fined in pounds on summary conviction for that offence and for each day it continues` IS
    LIST (`s 859K(7) the most in pounds that the fine limit allows` (fromMaybe `a fine without a stated limit` (`s 859K(7) the penalty for the offence`'s `fine not exceeding`)) `the pounds that level 3 on the standard scale stands for` 0)
       , (`s 859K(7) the most in pounds that the fine limit allows` (fromMaybe `a fine without a stated limit` (`s 859K(7) the penalty for the offence`'s `daily default fine for continued contravention`)) `the pounds that level 3 on the standard scale stands for` 0)

-- s 859L. Entering that a debt has been paid or property released.
@export Under section 859L(1) to (5), must the registrar enter that the debt has been satisfied, or the property released, once I deliver my statement?
GIVEN `my statement says that the debt for which the charge was given has been paid or satisfied in whole or in part` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does your statement say that the debt for which the charge was given has been paid or satisfied in whole or in part?
      `my statement says that all or part of the property has been released from the charge` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does it say that all or part of the property or undertaking charged has been released from the charge?
      `my statement says that all or part of the property has ceased to form part of the company's property` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does it say that all or part of the property or undertaking charged has ceased to form part of the company's property or undertaking?
      `the date the charge was created` IS A DATE @desc On what date was the charge created?
      `the charge is created or evidenced by an instrument` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the charge created or evidenced by an instrument?
      `I gave my name and address and my interest in the charge` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Do the particulars give your name and address and an indication of your interest in the charge?
      `I gave the registered name and number of the company` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Do the particulars give the registered name and number of the company that created the charge (or acquired the property subject to it)?
      `I gave the date of creation` IS A BOOLEAN @desc For a charge created before 6 April 2013: do the particulars give the date of creation?
      `I gave a description of the instrument` IS A BOOLEAN @desc For a charge created before 6 April 2013: do they describe the instrument by which the charge is created or evidenced?
      `I gave short particulars of the property or undertaking charged` IS A BOOLEAN @desc For a charge created before 6 April 2013: do they give short particulars of the property or undertaking charged?
      `I gave the unique reference code of the charge` IS A BOOLEAN @desc For a charge created on or after 6 April 2013: do they give the unique reference code allocated to the charge?
      `the statement and particulars were delivered to the registrar for a registered charge` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Were the statement and the particulars delivered to the registrar with respect to a registered charge?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 859L(1) to (5), must the registrar enter that the debt has been satisfied or the property released once I deliver my statement` IS
    `s 859L(5) the registrar must include the entry in the register`
        (`s 859L(1) subsection (5) applies`
            (`s 859L(2) the statement is the statement the section describes` `my statement says that the debt for which the charge was given has been paid or satisfied in whole or in part` `my statement says that all or part of the property has been released from the charge` `my statement says that all or part of the property has ceased to form part of the company's property`)
            (`s 859L(4) the particulars set out in subsection (4) are delivered` `I gave my name and address and my interest in the charge` `I gave the registered name and number of the company` `the date the charge was created` `the charge is created or evidenced by an instrument` `I gave the date of creation` `I gave a description of the instrument` `I gave short particulars of the property or undertaking charged` `I gave the unique reference code of the charge`)
            `the statement and particulars were delivered to the registrar for a registered charge`)
        `s 859L(5)(a) a statement of satisfaction in whole or in part`

-- s 859M(3) and s 859N(2). Court orders correcting the register.
@export Under section 859M(1) to (3), may the court order a mistake in a statement or notice about my charge to be rectified?
GIVEN `the court is satisfied that there has been an omission or mis-statement in a statement or notice delivered to the registrar under Chapter A1` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the court satisfied that there has been an omission or mis-statement in a statement or notice delivered to the registrar under Chapter A1?
      `the court is satisfied that it was accidental, inadvertent or had another sufficient cause` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the court satisfied that the omission or mis-statement was accidental, or due to inadvertence or to some other sufficient cause?
      `the court is satisfied that it does not prejudice creditors or shareholders` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the court satisfied that it is not of a nature to prejudice the position of creditors or shareholders of the company?
      `the court is satisfied that on other grounds it is just and equitable to grant relief` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the court satisfied that on other grounds it is just and equitable to grant relief?
      `I apply as the company or as a person interested` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the application made by the company or by a person interested?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 859M(1) to (3), may the court order a mistake in a statement or notice about my charge to be rectified` IS
    `s 859M(3) the court may order that the omission or mis-statement be rectified`
        (`s 859M(1) subsection (3) applies` `the court is satisfied that there has been an omission or mis-statement in a statement or notice delivered to the registrar under Chapter A1`
            (`s 859M(2) the requirement is met` `the court is satisfied that it was accidental, inadvertent or had another sufficient cause` `the court is satisfied that it does not prejudice creditors or shareholders` `the court is satisfied that on other grounds it is just and equitable to grant relief`))
        `I apply as the company or as a person interested`

@export Under section 859N(1) and (2), may the court order the copy of an instrument I delivered to be removed from the register and replaced?
GIVEN `the court is satisfied that the copy contains material that could have been omitted under section 859G` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the court satisfied that the copy contains material which could have been omitted under section 859G (personal information, account numbers or a signature)?
      `the court is satisfied that the wrong instrument or debenture was delivered` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the court satisfied that the wrong instrument or debenture was delivered to the registrar?
      `the court is satisfied that the copy was defective` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the court satisfied that the copy was defective?
      `I apply as the company or as a person interested` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the application made by the company or by a person interested?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 859N(1) and (2), may the court order the copy of an instrument I delivered to be removed from the register and replaced` IS
    `s 859N(2) the court may order that the copy be removed from the register and replaced`
        (`s 859N(1) subsection (2) applies` `the court is satisfied that the copy contains material that could have been omitted under section 859G` `the court is satisfied that the wrong instrument or debenture was delivered` `the court is satisfied that the copy was defective`)
        `I apply as the company or as a person interested`

-- s 859O. Telling the registrar that a charge has been amended.
@export Under section 859O(1) and (2), may I deliver to the registrar notice that my charge has been amended to restrict or rank other charges?
GIVEN `after the charge was created it was amended by adding or amending a term` IS A BOOLEAN @desc After the charge was created, was it amended by adding or amending a term?
      `the term prohibits or restricts a prior or equal ranking fixed security or charge` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does the term prohibit or restrict the creation of any fixed security or other charge having priority over, or ranking equally with, the charge?
      `the term varies or regulates the ranking of the charge` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does the term vary, or otherwise regulate the order of, the ranking of the charge in relation to any fixed security or other charge?
      `I am the company that created the charge` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are you the company that created the charge?
      `I am the person taking the benefit of the charge` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are you the person taking the benefit of the charge (or of another charge the term refers to)?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 859O(1) and (2), may I deliver to the registrar notice that my charge has been amended to restrict or rank other charges` IS
    `s 859O(2) the person may deliver to the registrar the certified copy and the statement of particulars`
        (`s 859O(1) this section applies` `after the charge was created it was amended by adding or amending a term` `the term prohibits or restricts a prior or equal ranking fixed security or charge` `the term varies or regulates the ranking of the charge`)
        `I am the company that created the charge` `I am the person taking the benefit of the charge`

§§ `Keeping copies of charges and letting people inspect them (ss 859P and 859Q)`

@export Under section 859P(1), must my company keep a copy of this instrument available for inspection?
GIVEN `the instrument creates a charge capable of registration under Chapter A1` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does the instrument create a charge that is capable of registration under Chapter A1?
      `the instrument varies or amends such a charge` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does the instrument vary or amend such a charge?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 859P(1), must my company keep a copy of this instrument available for inspection` IS
    `s 859P(1) the company must keep a copy of the instrument available for inspection` `the instrument creates a charge capable of registration under Chapter A1` `the instrument varies or amends such a charge`

@export Under section 859Q(2), is my company keeping the copies of its charges at a place the Act allows?
GIVEN `the copies are kept at the company's registered office` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are the copies kept at the company's registered office?
      `the copies are kept at a place specified in regulations under section 1136` IS A BOOLEAN @desc If not, are they kept at a place specified in regulations under section 1136?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 859Q(2), is my company keeping the copies of its charges at a place the Act allows` IS
    `s 859Q(2) the documents are kept at a place the subsection allows` `the copies are kept at the company's registered office` (JUST `the copies are kept at a place specified in regulations under section 1136`)

@export Under section 859Q(3), must my company give the registrar notice of the place where the copies of its charges are kept?
GIVEN `the copies have at all times been kept at the company's registered office` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Have the copies at all times been kept at the company's registered office?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 859Q(3), must my company give the registrar notice of the place where the copies of its charges are kept` IS
    `s 859Q(3) the company must give notice to the registrar of the place and of any change in that place` `the copies have at all times been kept at the company's registered office`

@export Under section 859Q(4), on what terms must the copies be open to my inspection?
GIVEN `I am a creditor or member of the company` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are you a creditor or a member of the company?
      `the fee prescribed for other persons, in pounds` IS A NUMBER @desc If you are neither, what fee has been prescribed for inspection, in pounds?
GIVETH A `s 859Q(4) terms of inspection`
DECIDE `Under section 859Q(4), on what terms must the copies be open to my inspection` IS
    `s 859Q(4) the terms on which the documents must be open to the inspection of the person` `I am a creditor or member of the company` `the fee prescribed for other persons, in pounds`

@export Under section 859Q(5), does my company, or do I as an officer, commit an offence over the place where the copies are kept or a refused inspection?
GIVEN `the number of days my company has been in default in telling the registrar the place` IS A NUMBER @desc For how many days has the company been in default of giving the registrar notice of the place where the copies are kept (or of a change in it)?
      `an inspection I am entitled to has been refused` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has an inspection that a creditor, member or other person is entitled to been refused?
      `my position in the company` IS A `s 1173(1) position in the body corporate` @desc What is your position in the company? (director, manager, secretary or another position)
      `I authorised, permitted, took part in or failed to take reasonable steps to prevent the default` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did you authorise or permit, take part in, or fail to take all reasonable steps to prevent, the default or the refusal (section 1121(3))?
GIVETH A LIST OF MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 859Q(5), does my company or do I as an officer commit an offence over the place where the copies are kept or a refused inspection` IS
    LIST (`s 859Q(5)(a) the company commits the offence` `the offence is committed`)
       , (`s 859Q(5)(b) the officer commits the offence` `the offence is committed` (`s 1173(1) the holder of the position is an officer of the body corporate` `my position in the company`) (JUST `I authorised, permitted, took part in or failed to take reasonable steps to prevent the default`))
    WHERE
        `the offence is committed` MEANS `s 859Q(5) an offence is committed` `the number of days my company has been in default in telling the registrar the place` `an inspection I am entitled to has been refused`

§§ `Chapter 1: a company registered in England and Wales or Northern Ireland (ss 860 to 877)`

@export Under section 860(1) and (7), must my company registered in England and Wales or Northern Ireland deliver particulars of this charge to the registrar?
GIVEN `the place where my company is registered` IS A `Place of registration` @desc Where is your company registered? (England and Wales, Scotland or Northern Ireland)
      `my company creates a charge` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is your company creating a charge?
      `it is a charge on land or an interest in land` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it a charge on land or any interest in land?
      `it is a charge for a rent or other periodical sum issuing out of land` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is that a charge for any rent or other periodical sum issuing out of land?
      `it is created by an instrument that would need registering as a bill of sale if an individual executed it` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it created or evidenced by an instrument which, if executed by an individual, would require registration as a bill of sale?
      `it secures an issue of debentures` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it a charge for the purposes of securing any issue of debentures?
      `it is a charge on uncalled share capital` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it a charge on uncalled share capital of the company?
      `it is a charge on calls made but not paid` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it a charge on calls made but not paid?
      `it is a charge on book debts` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it a charge on book debts of the company?
      `it is a floating charge` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it a floating charge on the company's property or undertaking?
      `it is a charge on a ship or aircraft` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it a charge on a ship or aircraft, or any share in a ship?
      `it is a charge on goodwill or intellectual property` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it a charge on goodwill or on any intellectual property?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 860(1) and (7), must my company registered in England and Wales or Northern Ireland deliver particulars of this charge to the registrar` IS
    `s 860(1) the company must deliver the prescribed particulars and the instrument to the registrar` `the place where my company is registered` `my company creates a charge`
        (`s 860(7) the charge is one to which section 860 applies` (`s 860(7) what the charge is` OF `it is a charge on land or an interest in land`, `it is a charge for a rent or other periodical sum issuing out of land`, `it is created by an instrument that would need registering as a bill of sale if an individual executed it`, `it secures an issue of debentures`, `it is a charge on uncalled share capital`, `it is a charge on calls made but not paid`, `it is a charge on book debts`, `it is a floating charge`, `it is a charge on a ship or aircraft`, `it is a charge on goodwill or intellectual property`))

@export Under section 870(1), what is the last day for registering a charge my company created?
GIVEN `the charge was created outside the United Kingdom` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Was the charge created outside the United Kingdom?
      `the day the charge was created` IS A DATE @desc On what day was the charge created?
      `the day the instrument could in due course of post have reached the United Kingdom` IS A DATE @desc If it was created outside the United Kingdom, on what day could the instrument (or a copy) have been received in the United Kingdom in due course of post, if despatched with due diligence? (any date otherwise)
GIVETH A DATE
DECIDE `Under section 870(1), what is the last day for registering a charge my company created` IS
    `s 870(1) the last day of the period allowed for registration of a charge created by a company` `the charge was created outside the United Kingdom` `the day the charge was created` `the day the instrument could in due course of post have reached the United Kingdom`

@export Under section 860(4), does my company commit an offence by not registering its charge in time?
GIVEN `my company must deliver the particulars (see the question on section 860(1) and (7))` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN @desc The answer to the question on section 860(1) and (7): JUST TRUE, JUST FALSE or NOTHING
      `the day the particulars and instrument were delivered` IS A MAYBE DATE @desc The day the company delivered the particulars and the instrument to the registrar (leave empty if it has not)
      `the last day of the period allowed for registration` IS A DATE @desc What is the last day of the period allowed for registration? (see the question on section 870(1))
      `the day I am asking` IS A DATE @desc What day is it today (or the day you are asking about)?
      `registration was effected on the application of some other person` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has registration of the charge been effected on the application of some other person?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 860(4), does my company commit an offence by not registering its charge in time` IS
    `s 860(4)(a) the company commits an offence`
        (`s 860(4) the company fails to comply with subsection (1), so that an offence is committed` `my company must deliver the particulars (see the question on section 860(1) and (7))`
            (`s 859H(1)(b) the thing was done by the last day of the period` `the day the particulars and instrument were delivered` `the last day of the period allowed for registration` `the day I am asking`)
            (`s 860(6) subsection (4) applies` `registration was effected on the application of some other person`))

@export Under section 860(4), do I commit an offence as an officer of my company that did not register its charge in time?
GIVEN `my company commits the offence (see the question on section 860(4))` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN @desc The answer to the question on whether the company commits the offence: JUST TRUE, JUST FALSE or NOTHING
      `my position in the company` IS A `s 1173(1) position in the body corporate` @desc What is your position in the company? (director, manager, secretary or another position)
      `I authorised, permitted, took part in or failed to take reasonable steps to prevent the default` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did you authorise or permit, take part in, or fail to take all reasonable steps to prevent, the failure to register (section 1121(3))?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 860(4), do I commit an offence as an officer of my company that did not register its charge in time` IS
    `s 860(4)(b) the officer commits an offence` `my company commits the offence (see the question on section 860(4))` (`s 1173(1) the holder of the position is an officer of the body corporate` `my position in the company`) (JUST `I authorised, permitted, took part in or failed to take reasonable steps to prevent the default`)

@export Under section 860(5), what is the most my company can be fined in pounds on summary conviction for not registering its charge?
GIVEN `the pounds that the statutory maximum stands for` IS A NUMBER @desc How many pounds does the statutory maximum stand for? (the Act does not say: ask for the current figure)
GIVETH A MAYBE NUMBER
DECIDE `Under section 860(5), what is the most my company can be fined in pounds on summary conviction for not registering its charge` IS
    CONSIDER filter (GIVEN penalty YIELD penalty's `how convicted` EQUALS `on summary conviction`) (`s 860(5) the penalties for the offence`)
    WHEN EMPTY THEN NOTHING
    WHEN penalty FOLLOWED BY rest THEN
        `s 859K(7) the most in pounds that the fine limit allows` (fromMaybe `a fine without a stated limit` (penalty's `fine not exceeding`)) 0 `the pounds that the statutory maximum stands for`

@export Under section 862(1) and (2), must my company deliver particulars of a charge that already exists on property it has acquired?
GIVEN `the place where my company is registered` IS A `Place of registration` @desc Where is your company registered? (England and Wales, Scotland or Northern Ireland)
      `my company has acquired property` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has your company acquired property?
      `the property is subject to a charge` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the property subject to a charge?
      `the charge is of a kind that would have had to be registered under Chapter 1 if my company had created it after the acquisition` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it a charge of a kind which would, if your company had created it after the acquisition, have had to be registered under Chapter 1 (see section 860(7))?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 862(1) and (2), must my company deliver particulars of a charge that already exists on property it has acquired` IS
    `s 862(2) the company must deliver the prescribed particulars and a certified copy of the instrument to the registrar`
        (`s 862(1) this section applies` `the place where my company is registered` `my company has acquired property` `the property is subject to a charge` (IF `the charge is of a kind that would have had to be registered under Chapter 1 if my company had created it after the acquisition` THEN JUST TRUE ELSE NOTHING))

@export Under section 865(1), must my company endorse a copy of the certificate of registration on this debenture?
GIVEN `the instruments are debentures` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it a debenture or certificate of debenture stock?
      `it is issued by my company` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it issued by your company?
      `its payment is secured by the charge that was registered` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is its payment secured by the charge that was registered?
      `it was issued before the charge was created` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Was it issued before the charge was created?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 865(1), must my company endorse a copy of the certificate of registration on this debenture` IS
    `s 865(1) the company must cause a copy of the certificate of registration to be endorsed on the debenture` (JUST `the instruments are debentures`) `it is issued by my company` `its payment is secured by the charge that was registered`
        (`s 865(2) the company is required to cause a copy of the certificate to be endorsed on the debenture` `it was issued before the charge was created`)

@export Under section 871(1), by what day must I give the registrar notice that I obtained an order for, or made an appointment of, a receiver or manager of a company's property?
GIVEN `the day of the order or of the appointment` IS A DATE @desc On what day was the order made, or the appointment made under the instrument?
GIVETH A DATE
DECIDE `Under section 871(1), by what day must I give the registrar notice that I obtained an order for or made an appointment of a receiver or manager of a company's property` IS
    `s 859K(2) the last day of 7 days after` `the day of the order or of the appointment`

@export Under section 874(1), is a charge my company created void against a liquidator, an administrator or a creditor?
GIVEN `my company created a charge to which section 860 applies` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did your company create a charge to which section 860 applies (see the question on section 860(1) and (7))?
      `section 860 has been complied with` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has section 860 been complied with (the particulars and instrument delivered in time, or registration effected on the application of another person)?
      `against whom` IS A `s 874(1) party against whom the charge may be void` @desc Against whom do you ask? (a liquidator, an administrator or a creditor of the company, or any other person)
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 874(1), is a charge my company created void against a liquidator, an administrator or a creditor` IS
    `s 874(1) the charge is void against the party` `my company created a charge to which section 860 applies` `section 860 has been complied with` `against whom`

@export Under section 876(1), must my company enter this charge in its own register of charges?
GIVEN `my company is a limited company` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is your company a limited company (the liability of its members is limited by its constitution)?
      `the kind of charge` IS A `s 876(1) kind of charge` @desc Which kind of charge is it? (a charge specifically affecting property of the company; a floating charge on the whole or part of its property or undertaking; or any other charge)
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 876(1), must my company enter this charge in its own register of charges` IS
    `s 876(1) the company must enter the charge in its register of charges` `my company is a limited company` `the kind of charge`

@export Under section 877(5), does my company, or do I as an officer, commit an offence over the place where its charge documents and register are kept, or a refused inspection?
GIVEN `the number of days my company has been in default in telling the registrar the place` IS A NUMBER @desc For how many days has the company been in default of giving the registrar notice of the place where the documents and register are kept (or of a change in it)?
      `an inspection I am entitled to has been refused` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has an inspection that a creditor, member or other person is entitled to been refused?
      `my position in the company` IS A `s 1173(1) position in the body corporate` @desc What is your position in the company? (director, manager, secretary or another position)
      `I authorised, permitted, took part in or failed to take reasonable steps to prevent the default` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did you authorise or permit, take part in, or fail to take all reasonable steps to prevent, the default or the refusal (section 1121(3))?
GIVETH A LIST OF MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 877(5), does my company or do I as an officer commit an offence over the place where its charge documents and register are kept or a refused inspection` IS
    LIST (`s 877(5)(a) the company commits the offence` `the offence is committed`)
       , (`s 877(5)(b) the officer commits the offence` `the offence is committed` (`s 1173(1) the holder of the position is an officer of the body corporate` `my position in the company`) (JUST `I authorised, permitted, took part in or failed to take reasonable steps to prevent the default`))
    WHERE
        `the offence is committed` MEANS `s 877(5) an offence is committed` `the number of days my company has been in default in telling the registrar the place` `an inspection I am entitled to has been refused`

§§ `Chapter 2: a company registered in Scotland (ss 878 to 892)`

@export Under section 878(1) and (7), must my company registered in Scotland deliver particulars of this charge to the registrar?
GIVEN `the place where my company is registered` IS A `Place of registration` @desc Where is your company registered? (England and Wales, Scotland or Northern Ireland)
      `my company is an incorporated company` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is your company an incorporated company?
      `my company creates a charge` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is your company creating a charge?
      `it is a charge on land or an interest in such land` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it a charge on land or any interest in such land?
      `it is a charge for a rent or other periodical sum payable in respect of the land` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is that a charge for any rent or other periodical sum payable in respect of the land?
      `it is a security over goodwill` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it a security over goodwill?
      `it is a security over a patent or a licence under a patent` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it a security over a patent or a licence under a patent?
      `it is a security over a trademark` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it a security over a trademark?
      `it is a security over a copyright or a licence under a copyright` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it a security over a copyright or a licence under a copyright?
      `it is a security over a registered design or a licence in respect of one` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it a security over a registered design or a licence in respect of such a design?
      `it is a security over a design right or a licence under one` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it a security over a design right or a licence under a design right?
      `it is a security over book debts` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it a security over the book debts (whether of the company or assigned to it)?
      `it is a security over uncalled share capital or calls made but not paid` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it a security over uncalled share capital of the company or calls made but not paid?
      `it is a security over a ship or aircraft` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it a security over a ship or aircraft or any share in a ship?
      `it is a floating charge` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it a floating charge?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 878(1) and (7), must my company registered in Scotland deliver particulars of this charge to the registrar` IS
    `s 878(1) the company must deliver the prescribed particulars and a certified copy of the instrument to the registrar` `the place where my company is registered` `my company is an incorporated company` `my company creates a charge`
        (`s 878(7) the charge is one to which section 878 applies` (`s 878(7) what the charge is` OF `it is a charge on land or an interest in such land`, `it is a charge for a rent or other periodical sum payable in respect of the land`, `it is a security over goodwill`, `it is a security over a patent or a licence under a patent`, `it is a security over a trademark`, `it is a security over a copyright or a licence under a copyright`, `it is a security over a registered design or a licence in respect of one`, `it is a security over a design right or a licence under one`, `it is a security over book debts`, `it is a security over uncalled share capital or calls made but not paid`, `it is a security over a ship or aircraft`, `it is a floating charge`))

@export Under section 886(1), what is the last day for registering a charge my company created?
GIVEN `the charge was created outside the United Kingdom` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Was the charge created outside the United Kingdom?
      `the day the charge was created` IS A DATE @desc On what day was the charge created?
      `the day a copy of the instrument could in due course of post have reached the United Kingdom` IS A DATE @desc If it was created outside the United Kingdom, on what day could a copy of the instrument have been received in the United Kingdom in due course of post, if despatched with due diligence? (any date otherwise)
GIVETH A DATE
DECIDE `Under section 886(1), what is the last day for registering a charge my company created` IS
    `s 886(1) the last day of the period allowed for registration of a charge created by a company` `the charge was created outside the United Kingdom` `the day the charge was created` `the day a copy of the instrument could in due course of post have reached the United Kingdom`

@export Under section 889(1), is a charge my company created void against the liquidator, an administrator or a creditor?
GIVEN `my company created a charge to which section 878 applies` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did your company create a charge to which section 878 applies (see the question on section 878(1) and (7))?
      `section 878 has been complied with` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has section 878 been complied with (the particulars and a certified copy delivered in time, or registration effected on the application of another person)?
      `against whom` IS A `s 889(1) party against whom the charge may be void` @desc Against whom do you ask? (the liquidator, an administrator or any creditor of the company, or any other person)
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 889(1), is a charge my company created void against the liquidator, an administrator or a creditor` IS
    `s 889(1) the charge is void against the party` `my company created a charge to which section 878 applies` `section 878 has been complied with` `against whom`

@export Under section 891(1), must my company registered in Scotland enter this charge in its own register of charges?
GIVEN `the kind of charge` IS A `s 891(1) kind of charge` @desc Which kind of charge is it? (a charge specifically affecting property of the company; a floating charge on any property of the company; or any other charge)
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 891(1), must my company registered in Scotland enter this charge in its own register of charges` IS
    `s 891(1) the company must enter the charge in its register of charges` `the kind of charge`

@export Under section 892(5), does my company, or do I as an officer, commit an offence over the place where its charge documents and register are kept, or a refused inspection?
GIVEN `the number of days my company has been in default in telling the registrar the place` IS A NUMBER @desc For how many days has the company been in default of giving the registrar notice of the place where the documents and register are kept (or of a change in it)?
      `an inspection I am entitled to has been refused` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has an inspection that a creditor, member or other person is entitled to been refused?
      `my position in the company` IS A `s 1173(1) position in the body corporate` @desc What is your position in the company? (director, manager, secretary or another position)
      `I authorised, permitted, took part in or failed to take reasonable steps to prevent the default` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did you authorise or permit, take part in, or fail to take all reasonable steps to prevent, the default or the refusal (section 1121(3))?
GIVETH A LIST OF MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 892(5), does my company or do I as an officer commit an offence over the place where its charge documents and register are kept or a refused inspection` IS
    LIST (`s 892(5)(a) the company commits the offence` `the offence is committed`)
       , (`s 892(5)(b) the officer commits the offence` `the offence is committed` (`s 1173(1) the holder of the position is an officer of the body corporate` `my position in the company`) (JUST `I authorised, permitted, took part in or failed to take reasonable steps to prevent the default`))
    WHERE
        `the offence is committed` MEANS `s 892(5) an offence is committed` `the number of days my company has been in default in telling the registrar the place` `an inspection I am entitled to has been refused`

§§ `Chapter 3: charges registered in a special register (s 893)`

@export Under section 893(3)(b), is my charge, registered in a special register, treated as if it had been registered under Chapter A1?
GIVEN `an order under section 893 is in force` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has the Secretary of State made an order under section 893 that covers charges of this kind?
      `my charge is of a description specified in the order` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is your charge of a description specified in the order?
      `my charge was registered in the special register within the period the order specifies` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Was it registered in the special register within the period the order specifies?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 893(3)(b), is my charge registered in a special register treated as if it had been registered under Chapter A1` IS
    `s 893(3)(b) the charge is to be treated as if it had been registered under Chapter A1` `an order under section 893 is in force` `my charge is of a description specified in the order` `my charge was registered in the special register within the period the order specifies`

-- ====================================================================================================
-- seat questions from part coa20 (merged by the lead on 2026-11-12; unchanged text follows)
-- ====================================================================================================
-- coa20-seat.l4: the SEAT LAYER over coa20's Parts of the Companies Act 2006 (United Kingdom): Part 26 (ss 895-901), Part 26A (ss 901A-901L) and
-- Part 27 (ss 902-941). SEAT: an individual who is, or is about to become, a director, a company secretary or a member (shareholder) of a company
-- registered under the Act, or who deals with one (as a creditor, a debenture trustee, a would-be expert), asking on facts they can state what the
-- Act requires or lets them do about a compromise, arrangement, merger or division, what rights they have, what they must disclose, deliver or vote
-- on and by when, and what follows (offences, penalties) if it is not done. (Assumed, not ruled: the Act is addressed to companies, so the individual
-- is whoever stands in a company's management or ownership.) No question has a seat for the court, the registrar or any official.
--
-- Each question takes plain inputs (yes/no, a number, a date, or a choice from the module's own list), one per fact the person can state, each with
-- an @desc worded as that person would be asked, builds the layer-1 inputs from them, and calls the layer-1 rule. Nothing here restates a rule.
-- Answers: JUST TRUE / JUST FALSE ("the text says no") / NOTHING ("not covered"; never to be read as no); a requirement is answered
-- "complied with", "not complied with", "does not apply" or "not covered"; a penalty is answered as the core's `Penalty` (the pounds a level or the
-- statutory maximum stands for are not in the Act); an amount is answered in pounds.
-- Where layer 1 takes the answer of a section that is in another part (s 1121 officer in default, s 4(2) public company, s 282 ordinary resolution,
-- s 399 group accounts, s 414 approval of accounts, s 1212 statutory auditor, s 1162 parent undertaking), the person states that fact and it is passed
-- as that section's answer. The court's own satisfaction (ss 901G, 916 to 918, 931, 932, 934) is asked as a fact ("the court is satisfied").

§ `Part 26 -- Arrangements and reconstructions: general`

§§ `Application of this Part and the meeting of creditors or members (ss 895-896)`

-- s 895(1). Ask this first: it says whether Part 26 is engaged by what is proposed.
@export Under section 895(1), does Part 26 (arrangements and reconstructions) apply to the compromise or arrangement that is proposed? (s 895(1))
GIVEN `proposed with creditors` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is a compromise or arrangement proposed between the company and its creditors, or any class of its creditors?
      `proposed with members` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is a compromise or arrangement proposed between the company and its members, or any class of its members?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 895(1), does Part 26 apply to the compromise or arrangement that is proposed` IS
    `s 895(1) the provisions of Part 26 apply` `proposed with creditors` `proposed with members`

-- s 896(2). The person is the one who asks the court for an order that a meeting be summoned.
@export Under section 896(2), may I apply to the court for an order that a meeting of the creditors or members be summoned? (s 896(2))
GIVEN `I am` IS A `s 896(2) applicant` @desc Who are you in relation to the company? Choose: the company, a creditor of the company, a member of the company, the liquidator of the company, the administrator of the company, or any other person.
      `the company is being wound up` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the company being wound up?
      `the company is in administration` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the company in administration?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 896(2), may I apply to the court for an order that a meeting be summoned` IS
    `s 896(2) the person may apply for an order for a meeting` `I am` `the company is being wound up` `the company is in administration`

§§ `The explanatory statement and the directors' duty to give information (ss 897-898)`

-- s 897(1). Asked by a director or secretary who is sending the notice, and by a creditor or member who has received it.
@export Under section 897(1), does the notice summoning the creditors' or members' meeting satisfy the requirement to give or offer the explanatory statement? (s 897(1))
GIVEN `a meeting is summoned under section 896` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has the court ordered a meeting to be summoned under section 896?
      `how the notice is given` IS A `s 897(1) how a notice summoning the meeting is given` @desc How is this notice given? Choose: sent to a creditor or member, or given by advertisement.
      `the notice is accompanied by a statement` IS A BOOLEAN @desc If the notice is sent to a creditor or member: is it accompanied by an explanatory statement that complies with section 897?
      `the advertisement includes the statement` IS A BOOLEAN @desc If the notice is given by advertisement: does it include the explanatory statement?
      `the advertisement says where to get copies` IS A BOOLEAN @desc If the notice is given by advertisement: does it state where and how creditors or members entitled to attend may obtain copies of the statement?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 897(1), does the notice summoning the meeting satisfy the requirement` IS
    `s 897(1) the notice summoning the meeting satisfies the requirement` `a meeting is summoned under section 896` `how the notice is given` `the notice is accompanied by a statement` `the advertisement includes the statement` `the advertisement says where to get copies`

-- s 897(2).
@export Under section 897(2), does the explanatory statement say what the section requires: the effect of the compromise or arrangement and the directors' interests? (s 897(2))
GIVEN `it explains the effect` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does the statement explain the effect of the compromise or arrangement?
      `it states directors' interests` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does the statement state any material interests of the directors of the company (as directors, members, creditors or otherwise)?
      `it states the effect on those interests` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does the statement state the effect of the compromise or arrangement on those interests, so far as it differs from its effect on the like interests of other persons?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 897(2), does the explanatory statement say what the section requires` IS
    `s 897(2) the statement complies` `it explains the effect` `it states directors' interests` `it states the effect on those interests`

-- s 897(4).
@export Under section 897(4), am I entitled to be given a copy of the explanatory statement free of charge? (s 897(4))
GIVEN `the advertisement says copies can be obtained` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does the advertised notice state that copies of an explanatory statement can be obtained by creditors or members entitled to attend the meeting?
      `I am entitled to attend` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are you a creditor or member entitled to attend the meeting?
      `I applied as the notice indicates` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Have you applied for a copy in the manner indicated by the notice?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 897(4), am I entitled to a free copy of the explanatory statement` IS
    `s 897(4) the person is entitled to be provided by the company with a copy of the statement free of charge` `the advertisement says copies can be obtained` `I am entitled to attend` `I applied as the notice indicates`

-- s 897(5) to (7).
@export Under section 897(5), am I guilty of an offence because the company made default in complying with the explanatory statement requirements? (ss 897(5)-(7))
GIVEN `the company made default` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did the company make default in complying with any requirement of section 897?
      `I am` IS A `s 897(5) person charged with the default` @desc Who are you? Choose: the company, an officer of the company, a liquidator or administrator of the company, a trustee of a deed securing the issue of debentures of the company, or any other person.
      `I am an officer in default` IS A BOOLEAN @desc If you are an officer (or a person treated as one): are you "in default" within section 1121, that is, did you authorise or permit, take part in, or fail to take all reasonable steps to prevent, the default?
      `I show the default was due to a refusal` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Can you show that the default was due to the refusal of a director or debenture trustee to supply the necessary particulars of his interests?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 897(5), am I guilty of an offence for a default in complying with section 897` IS
    `s 897(5) the person is guilty of an offence under section 897` `the company made default` `I am` (JUST `I am an officer in default`) `I show the default was due to a refusal`

-- s 897(8).
@export Under section 897(8), what is the most I can be fined for an offence under section 897? (s 897(8))
GIVEN `how I am convicted` IS A `Mode of conviction` @desc How would you be convicted? Choose: on conviction on indictment, on summary conviction (anywhere), or on summary conviction in England and Wales, in Scotland or in Northern Ireland.
GIVETH A MAYBE Penalty
DECIDE `Under section 897(8), what is the most I can be fined for an offence under section 897` IS
    `s 897(8) the penalty on conviction` `how I am convicted`

-- s 898(1).
@export Under section 898(1), must I, as a director or a debenture trustee, give the company notice of matters relating to myself? (s 898(1))
GIVEN `I am a director or a debenture trustee` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are you a director of the company or a trustee for its debenture holders?
      `the matter relates to me and is needed for the statement` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the matter one relating to yourself that may be necessary for the purposes of the explanatory statement under section 897?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 898(1), must I give the company notice of matters relating to myself` IS
    `s 898(1) the person is under a duty to give the company notice of the matter` `I am a director or a debenture trustee` `the matter relates to me and is needed for the statement`

-- s 898(2) and (3).
@export Under section 898(2), do I commit an offence if I make default in giving the company that notice? (ss 898(2)-(3))
GIVEN `I made default in complying with section 898` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did you make default in complying with section 898 (giving the company notice of matters relating to yourself)?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 898(2), do I commit an offence if I make default in giving the company notice` IS
    `s 898(2) the person commits an offence` `I made default in complying with section 898`

@export Under section 898(3), what is the most I can be fined for that offence? (s 898(3))
GIVEN `how I am convicted` IS A `Mode of conviction` @desc How would you be convicted? Choose: on summary conviction (in England and Wales, in Scotland or in Northern Ireland) or on conviction on indictment.
GIVETH A MAYBE Penalty
DECIDE `Under section 898(3), what is the most I can be fined for failing to give the company notice` IS
    `s 898(3) the penalty on conviction` `how I am convicted`

§§ `Court sanction, moratorium debts and the effect of the order (ss 899-899A)`

-- s 899(1).
@export Under section 899(1), may the court sanction the compromise or arrangement on the votes cast at the meeting? (s 899(1))
GIVEN `an application under section 899 has been made` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has an application been made to the court under section 899 to sanction the compromise or arrangement?
      `number present and voting` IS A NUMBER @desc How many creditors (or members) of the class were present and voting, in person or by proxy, at the meeting?
      `number who agree` IS A NUMBER @desc How many of them agreed the compromise or arrangement?
      `value present and voting` IS A NUMBER @desc What is the total value (in pounds of debt, or of shares) represented by those present and voting?
      `value who agree` IS A NUMBER @desc What is the total value represented by those who agreed?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 899(1), may the court sanction the compromise or arrangement` IS
    `s 899(1) the court may sanction the compromise or arrangement` `an application under section 899 has been made` `number present and voting` `number who agree` `value present and voting` `value who agree`

-- s 899(3).
@export Under section 899(3), is a sanctioned compromise or arrangement binding on me? (s 899(3))
GIVEN `the court has sanctioned it` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has the court sanctioned the compromise or arrangement?
      `I am` IS A `s 899(3) person said to be bound` @desc What are you? Choose: a creditor of the creditors or class concerned, a member of the members or class concerned, the company, the liquidator of a company in the course of being wound up, a contributory of a company in the course of being wound up, or any other person.
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 899(3), is the sanctioned compromise or arrangement binding on me` IS
    `s 899(3) the compromise or arrangement is binding on the person` `the court has sanctioned it` `I am`

-- s 899(4). "Has no effect until": the answer is TRUE while the order cannot yet have effect.
@export Under section 899(4), is the court's order still without effect because no copy has yet been delivered to the registrar? (s 899(4))
GIVEN `a copy of the order has been delivered to the registrar` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has a copy of the court's order been delivered to the registrar?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 899(4), is the court order still without effect` IS
    `s 899(4) the court's order cannot yet have effect` `a copy of the order has been delivered to the registrar`

-- s 899A(1) and (3). I am a creditor owed a moratorium debt.
@export Under section 899A(3), may I take part in the creditors' meeting if I am a creditor in respect of a moratorium debt or priority pre-moratorium debt? (ss 899A(1)-(3))
GIVEN `date of the application` IS A DATE @desc On what date was the application under section 896 for a meeting made?
      `last day of the moratorium` IS A DATE @desc On what day did the company's moratorium (under the Insolvency Act 1986 or the Insolvency (Northern Ireland) Order 1989) end?
      `relevant creditors are included` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Do the creditors with whom the compromise or arrangement is proposed include any creditor in respect of a moratorium debt or priority pre-moratorium debt?
      `I am a relevant creditor` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are you a creditor in respect of a moratorium debt or a priority pre-moratorium debt?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 899A(3), may I take part in the creditors meeting as a relevant creditor` IS
    `s 899A(3) the relevant creditor may participate in the meeting summoned under section 896` (`s 899A(1) this section applies` `date of the application` `last day of the moratorium` `relevant creditors are included`) `I am a relevant creditor`

@export Under section 899A(5), may the court sanction a compromise or arrangement that makes provision for a relevant creditor who has not agreed to it? (ss 899A(1), (5))
GIVEN `date of the application` IS A DATE @desc On what date was the application under section 896 for a meeting made?
      `last day of the moratorium` IS A DATE @desc On what day did the company's moratorium end?
      `relevant creditors are included` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Do the creditors with whom the compromise or arrangement is proposed include any relevant creditors (creditors in respect of a moratorium debt or a priority pre-moratorium debt)?
      `it makes provision for a relevant creditor` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does the compromise or arrangement include provision in respect of a relevant creditor?
      `that creditor has agreed` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has that relevant creditor agreed to it?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 899A(5), may the court sanction an arrangement that makes provision for a relevant creditor who has not agreed` IS
    `s 899A(5) the court may sanction the compromise or arrangement under section 899` (`s 899A(1) this section applies` `date of the application` `last day of the moratorium` `relevant creditors are included`) `it makes provision for a relevant creditor` `that creditor has agreed`

§§ `After the order: delivering it to the registrar, and the articles (ss 900-901)`

-- s 900(6). The seventh day after the order is made is the last day.
@export Under section 900(6), did the company deliver a copy of the order to the registrar within seven days after it was made? (s 900(6))
GIVEN `date the order was made` IS A DATE @desc On what date did the court make the order (under section 900)?
      `a copy has been delivered` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has a copy of the order been delivered to the registrar?
      `date it was delivered` IS A DATE @desc On what date was it delivered? (Ignored if it has not been delivered.)
      `today` IS A DATE @desc What is today's date?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 900(6), did the company deliver a copy of the order to the registrar in time` IS
    `s 900(6) the company delivered a copy of the order to the registrar in time` `date the order was made` (IF `a copy has been delivered` THEN JUST `date it was delivered` ELSE NOTHING) `today`

-- s 900(7).
@export Under section 900(7), am I guilty of an offence because the company did not deliver the copy of the order in time? (s 900(7))
GIVEN `default was made in complying with section 900(6)` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Was default made in complying with section 900(6) (delivering a copy of the order to the registrar within seven days)?
      `I am` IS A `s 897(5) person charged with the default` @desc Who are you? Choose: the company, an officer of the company, a liquidator or administrator of the company, a trustee of a deed securing the issue of debentures, or any other person.
      `I am an officer in default` IS A BOOLEAN @desc If you are an officer: are you "in default" within section 1121 (did you authorise or permit, take part in, or fail to take all reasonable steps to prevent, the default)?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 900(7), am I guilty of an offence for the late delivery of the order` IS
    `s 900(7) the person is guilty of an offence under section 900(7)` `default was made in complying with section 900(6)` `I am` (JUST `I am an officer in default`)

@export Under section 900(8), what is the most I can be fined for that offence, and what is the daily default fine? (s 900(8))
GIVEN `how I am convicted` IS A `Mode of conviction` @desc How would you be convicted? Choose: on summary conviction (in England and Wales, in Scotland or in Northern Ireland, or anywhere) or on conviction on indictment.
GIVETH A MAYBE Penalty
DECIDE `Under section 900(8), what is the most I can be fined for the late delivery of the order` IS
    `s 900(8) the penalty on conviction` `how I am convicted`

-- s 901(1) to (3).
@export Under section 901(2), is the copy of the order delivered to the registrar accompanied by a copy of the amended articles, resolution or agreement as the section requires? (ss 901(1)-(2))
GIVEN `the order is an order under section 899` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the order an order under section 899 sanctioning the compromise or arrangement?
      `it is an order under section 900 that alters the constitution` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the order an order under section 900 that alters the company's constitution?
      `the order amends the articles or a Chapter 3 resolution` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does the order amend the company's articles, or a resolution or agreement affecting the company's constitution (Chapter 3 of Part 3)?
      `the copy is accompanied by the amended text` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the copy of the order delivered to the registrar accompanied by a copy of the articles (or the resolution or agreement) as amended?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 901(2), is the copy of the order delivered to the registrar accompanied as required` IS
    `s 901(2) the copy of the order is accompanied as the section requires` (`s 901(1) this section applies to the order` `the order is an order under section 899` `it is an order under section 900 that alters the constitution`) `the order amends the articles or a Chapter 3 resolution` `the copy is accompanied by the amended text`

@export Under section 901(3), is each copy of the company's articles issued after the order is made accompanied by a copy of the order as the section requires? (ss 901(1), (3))
GIVEN `the order is an order under section 899` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the order an order under section 899 sanctioning the compromise or arrangement?
      `it is an order under section 900 that alters the constitution` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the order an order under section 900 that alters the company's constitution?
      `the copy is issued after the order is made` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is this copy of the articles issued by the company after the order is made?
      `the effect of the order is in the articles` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has the effect of the order been incorporated into the articles by amendment?
      `the copy is accompanied by a copy of the order` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is this copy of the articles accompanied by a copy of the order?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 901(3), is each copy of the articles accompanied by a copy of the order as the section requires` IS
    `s 901(3) the copy of the articles is accompanied as the section requires` (`s 901(1) this section applies to the order` `the order is an order under section 899` `it is an order under section 900 that alters the constitution`) `the copy is issued after the order is made` `the effect of the order is in the articles` `the copy is accompanied by a copy of the order`

§ `Part 26A -- Arrangements and reconstructions: companies in financial difficulty`

§§ `Application of this Part and the meeting (ss 901A-901C)`

-- s 901A(1) to (3).
@export Under section 901A(1), does Part 26A (companies in financial difficulty) apply to the compromise or arrangement that is proposed? (s 901A(1)-(3))
GIVEN `financial difficulties encountered` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has the company encountered financial difficulties?
      `financial difficulties likely` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the company likely to encounter financial difficulties?
      `affecting going concern` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are those difficulties affecting, or will or may they affect, the company's ability to carry on business as a going concern?
      `proposed with creditors` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is a compromise or arrangement proposed between the company and its creditors, or any class of them?
      `proposed with members` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is a compromise or arrangement proposed between the company and its members, or any class of them?
      `purpose is the difficulties` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the purpose of the compromise or arrangement to eliminate, reduce or prevent, or mitigate the effect of, those financial difficulties?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 901A(1), does Part 26A apply to the compromise or arrangement that is proposed` IS
    `s 901A(1) the provisions of Part 26A apply`
        (`s 901A(2) condition A is met` `financial difficulties encountered` `financial difficulties likely` `affecting going concern` EQUALS JUST TRUE)
        (`s 901A(3) condition B is met` `proposed with creditors` `proposed with members` `purpose is the difficulties` EQUALS JUST TRUE)

-- s 901C(3).
@export Under section 901C(3), must I be permitted to take part in the meeting of creditors or members? (s 901C(3))
GIVEN `a meeting is ordered to be summoned` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has the court ordered a meeting to be summoned under section 901C(1)?
      `my rights are affected` IS A BOOLEAN @desc As a creditor or member of the company, are your rights affected by the compromise or arrangement?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 901C(3), must I be permitted to participate in the meeting` IS
    `s 901C(3) the person must be permitted to participate in the meeting` `a meeting is ordered to be summoned` `my rights are affected`

@export Under section 901C(4), does section 901C(3) not apply to my class because the court is satisfied that none of its members has a genuine economic interest in the company? (s 901C(4))
GIVEN `the court is satisfied` IS A BOOLEAN @desc On an application under section 901C(4), is the court satisfied that none of the members of the class has a genuine economic interest in the company?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 901C(4), does the right to participate not apply to my class` IS
    `s 901C(4) subsection (3) does not apply in relation to the class` `the court is satisfied`

§§ `The explanatory statement (ss 901D-901E)`

@export Under section 901D(1), does the notice summoning the creditors' or members' meeting satisfy the requirement to give or offer the explanatory statement? (s 901D(1))
GIVEN `a meeting is summoned under section 901C` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has the court ordered a meeting to be summoned under section 901C?
      `how the notice is given` IS A `s 901D(1) how a notice summoning the meeting is given` @desc How is this notice given? Choose: sent to a creditor or member, or given by advertisement.
      `the notice is accompanied by a statement` IS A BOOLEAN @desc If the notice is sent to a creditor or member: is it accompanied by an explanatory statement that complies with section 901D?
      `the advertisement includes the statement` IS A BOOLEAN @desc If the notice is given by advertisement: does it include the explanatory statement?
      `the advertisement says where to get copies` IS A BOOLEAN @desc If the notice is given by advertisement: does it state where and how creditors or members entitled to attend may obtain copies?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 901D(1), does the notice summoning the meeting satisfy the requirement` IS
    `s 901D(1) the notice summoning the meeting satisfies the requirement` `a meeting is summoned under section 901C` `how the notice is given` `the notice is accompanied by a statement` `the advertisement includes the statement` `the advertisement says where to get copies`

@export Under section 901D(5), am I guilty of an offence because the company made default in complying with the explanatory statement requirements? (ss 901D(5)-(7))
GIVEN `the company made default` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did the company make default in complying with any requirement of section 901D?
      `I am` IS A `s 897(5) person charged with the default` @desc Who are you? Choose: the company, an officer of the company, a liquidator or administrator of the company, a trustee of a deed securing the issue of debentures, or any other person.
      `I am an officer in default` IS A BOOLEAN @desc If you are an officer (or a person treated as one): are you "in default" within section 1121?
      `I show the default was due to a refusal` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Can you show that the default was due to the refusal of a director or debenture trustee to supply the necessary particulars of his or her interests?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 901D(5), am I guilty of an offence for a default in complying with section 901D` IS
    `s 901D(5) the person is guilty of an offence under section 901D` `the company made default` `I am` (JUST `I am an officer in default`) `I show the default was due to a refusal`

@export Under section 901D(8), what is the most I can be fined for an offence under section 901D? (s 901D(8))
GIVEN `how I am convicted` IS A `Mode of conviction` @desc How would you be convicted? Choose: on conviction on indictment, on summary conviction in England and Wales, or on summary conviction in Scotland or Northern Ireland.
GIVETH A MAYBE Penalty
DECIDE `Under section 901D(8), what is the most I can be fined for an offence under section 901D` IS
    `s 901D(8) the penalty on conviction` `how I am convicted`

@export Under section 901E(1), must I, as a director or a debenture trustee, give the company notice of matters relating to myself for the explanatory statement? (s 901E(1))
GIVEN `I am a director or a debenture trustee` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are you a director of the company or a trustee for its debenture holders?
      `the matter relates to me and is needed for the statement` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the matter one relating to yourself that may be necessary for the purposes of section 901D?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 901E(1), must I give the company notice of matters relating to myself` IS
    `s 901E(1) the person is under a duty to give the company notice of the matter` `I am a director or a debenture trustee` `the matter relates to me and is needed for the statement`

§§ `Court sanction, dissenting classes and the effect of the order (ss 901F-901G)`

-- s 901F(1). No test of the number of persons voting: 75% in value only.
@export Under section 901F(1), may the court sanction the compromise or arrangement on the votes cast at the meeting (75% in value)? (s 901F(1))
GIVEN `an application under section 901F has been made` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has an application been made to the court under section 901F to sanction the compromise or arrangement?
      `value present and voting` IS A NUMBER @desc What is the total value (in pounds of debt, or of shares) represented by those present and voting, in person or by proxy, at the meeting?
      `value who agree` IS A NUMBER @desc What is the total value represented by those who agreed the compromise or arrangement?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 901F(1), may the court sanction the compromise or arrangement` IS
    `s 901F(1) the court may sanction the compromise or arrangement` `an application under section 901F has been made` `value present and voting` `value who agree`

-- s 901G.
@export Under section 901G(2), can the court sanction the compromise or arrangement although one class has not agreed it? (ss 901G(1)-(5))
GIVEN `class value present and voting` IS A NUMBER @desc What is the total value represented by the members of the dissenting class who were present and voting at the meeting?
      `class value who agree` IS A NUMBER @desc What is the total value represented by those of them who agreed?
      `court satisfied nobody worse off` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the court satisfied that, if sanctioned, none of the members of the dissenting class would be any worse off than in the event of the relevant alternative (what the court considers most likely to occur if it were not sanctioned)?
      `value of those who would be paid` IS A NUMBER @desc What is the total value represented by the members of a class present and voting who would receive a payment, or have a genuine economic interest in the company, in the event of the relevant alternative?
      `value of those who agree` IS A NUMBER @desc What is the total value represented by those of them who agreed the compromise or arrangement?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 901G(2), can the court sanction the compromise or arrangement although a class has not agreed it` IS
    `s 901G(2) the dissent of the dissenting class does not prevent the court from sanctioning under section 901F`
        (`s 901G(1) this section applies` `class value present and voting` `class value who agree`)
        (`s 901G(3) condition A is met` `court satisfied nobody worse off`)
        (`s 901G(5) condition B is met` `value of those who would be paid` `value of those who agree`)

-- s 901F(6). The step that lifts the bar depends on the company.
@export Under section 901F(6), is the court's order still without effect because the copy has not yet been published or delivered as required? (s 901F(6))
GIVEN `an overseas company not required to register under section 1046` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the company an overseas company that is not required to register particulars under section 1046?
      `a copy has been published in the Gazette` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has a copy of the order been published in the Gazette?
      `a copy has been delivered to the registrar` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has a copy of the order been delivered to the registrar?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 901F(6), is the court order still without effect` IS
    `s 901F(6) the court's order cannot yet have effect` `an overseas company not required to register under section 1046` `a copy has been published in the Gazette` `a copy has been delivered to the registrar`

§§ `Pension schemes and the order (ss 901I-901K)`

-- The question is "has it been sent as the section requires", and the name, the @export text and the body all ask that and nothing more (RECONCILED 2026-11-12: it was named "must a notice ... also be sent", which promised an answer about the duty that the body does not compute).
-- A "no" has two causes: the section's conditions are not met, so nothing has to be sent (fork F15), or the document is required but has not been sent. A "yes" means the conditions are met and it was sent.
@export Under section 901I(1), has the notice or document sent to a creditor also been sent to the Pensions Regulator as the section requires? (s 901I(1))
GIVEN `the company is or was an employer in a scheme that is not money purchase` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the company, or was it, an employer in respect of an occupational pension scheme that is not a money purchase scheme?
      `the document is required to be sent to a creditor` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is this notice or document required to be sent to a creditor of the company?
      `it has also been sent to the Pensions Regulator` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has it also been sent to the Pensions Regulator?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 901I(1), has the notice or document sent to a creditor also been sent to the Pensions Regulator as the section requires` IS
    `s 901I(1) the notice or other document has been sent to the Pensions Regulator as the section requires` `the company is or was an employer in a scheme that is not money purchase` `the document is required to be sent to a creditor` `it has also been sent to the Pensions Regulator`

-- The question is "has it been sent as the section requires", and the name, the @export text and the body all ask that and nothing more (RECONCILED 2026-11-12: it was named "must a notice ... also be sent", which promised an answer about the duty that the body does not compute).
-- A "no" has two causes: the section's conditions are not met, so nothing has to be sent (fork F15), or the document is required but has not been sent. A "yes" means the conditions are met and it was sent.
@export Under section 901I(2), has the notice or document sent to a creditor also been sent to the Board of the Pension Protection Fund as the section requires? (s 901I(2))
GIVEN `the company is an employer in an eligible scheme` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the company an employer in respect of an eligible scheme (within section 126 of the Pensions Act 2004 or Article 110 of the Pensions (Northern Ireland) Order 2005)?
      `the document is required to be sent to a creditor` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is this notice or document required to be sent to a creditor of the company?
      `it has also been sent to the Board` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has it also been sent to the Board of the Pension Protection Fund?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 901I(2), has the notice or document sent to a creditor also been sent to the Board of the Pension Protection Fund as the section requires` IS
    `s 901I(2) the notice or other document has been sent to the Board of the Pension Protection Fund as the section requires` `the company is an employer in an eligible scheme` `the document is required to be sent to a creditor` `it has also been sent to the Board`

@export Under section 901J(6), did the company deliver a copy of the order to the registrar within seven days after it was made? (s 901J(6))
GIVEN `date the order was made` IS A DATE @desc On what date did the court make the order (under section 901J)?
      `a copy has been delivered` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has a copy of the order been delivered to the registrar?
      `date it was delivered` IS A DATE @desc On what date was it delivered? (Ignored if it has not been delivered.)
      `today` IS A DATE @desc What is today's date?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 901J(6), did the company deliver a copy of the order to the registrar in time` IS
    `s 901J(6) the company delivered a copy of the order to the registrar in time` `date the order was made` (IF `a copy has been delivered` THEN JUST `date it was delivered` ELSE NOTHING) `today`

@export Under section 901K(3), is each copy of the company's articles issued after the order is made accompanied by a copy of the order as the section requires? (ss 901K(1), (3))
GIVEN `the order is an order under section 901F` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the order an order under section 901F sanctioning the compromise or arrangement?
      `it is an order under section 901J that alters the constitution` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the order an order under section 901J that alters the company's constitution?
      `the copy is issued after the order is made` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is this copy of the articles issued by the company after the order is made?
      `the effect of the order is in the articles` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has the effect of the order been incorporated into the articles by amendment?
      `the copy is accompanied by a copy of the order` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is this copy of the articles accompanied by a copy of the order?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 901K(3), is each copy of the articles accompanied by a copy of the order as the section requires` IS
    `s 901K(3) the copy of the articles is accompanied as the section requires` (`s 901K(1) this section applies to the order` `the order is an order under section 901F` `it is an order under section 901J that alters the constitution`) `the copy is issued after the order is made` `the effect of the order is in the articles` `the copy is accompanied by a copy of the order`

§ `Part 27 -- Mergers and divisions of public companies`

§§ `Whether Part 27 applies (ss 902-904, 919)`

@export Under section 902(1), does Part 27 (mergers and divisions of public companies) apply to the scheme that is proposed? (ss 902-904, 919)
GIVEN `the company is a public company` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the company in respect of which the compromise or arrangement is proposed a public company?
      `a compromise or arrangement is proposed` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is a compromise or arrangement proposed between that company and its creditors (or a class of them) or its members (or a class of them)?
      `for a reconstruction or amalgamation scheme` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it proposed for the purposes of, or in connection with, a scheme for the reconstruction of any company or companies or the amalgamation of any two or more companies?
      `shares are the consideration` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the consideration for each transfer to be shares in the transferee company (or companies) receivable by members of the transferor company (or companies), with or without a cash payment?
      `public companies transferred to an existing public company` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Under the scheme, are the undertaking, property and liabilities of one or more public companies (including the company in question) to be transferred to another existing public company?
      `public companies transferred to a new company` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Under the scheme, are the undertaking, property and liabilities of two or more public companies (including the company in question) to be transferred to a new company?
      `divided among two or more companies` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Under the scheme, are the undertaking, property and liabilities of the company in question to be divided among and transferred to two or more companies?
      `each is an existing public company or a new company` IS A BOOLEAN @desc If divided: is each of those companies either an existing public company or a new company (whether or not public)?
      `the company is being wound up` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the company in respect of which the compromise or arrangement is proposed being wound up?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 902(1), does Part 27 apply to the scheme that is proposed` IS
    IF `s 902(3) the winding up of the company takes the compromise or arrangement out of this Part` `the company is being wound up` EQUALS JUST TRUE
    THEN JUST FALSE
    ELSE `s 902(1) this Part applies` `the company is a public company` `a compromise or arrangement is proposed` `for a reconstruction or amalgamation scheme`
            (`s 904(1) the scheme involves a merger`
                (`s 904(1)(a) the scheme involves a merger by absorption` `public companies transferred to an existing public company` `public companies transferred to an existing public company`)
                (`s 904(1)(b) the scheme involves a merger by formation of a new company` `public companies transferred to a new company` `public companies transferred to a new company`))
            (`s 919(1) the scheme involves a division` `divided among two or more companies` `each is an existing public company or a new company`)
            `shares are the consideration`

§§ `Merger: the draft terms, publication and approval (ss 905-907)`

@export Under section 905(2), do the draft terms of the merger scheme give the particulars the section requires? (ss 905(2), 915(2))
GIVEN `a merger by absorption where all relevant securities of the transferor company are held by the transferee company` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the scheme a merger by absorption in which all of the relevant securities (voting shares or other securities) of the transferor company, or of each of them, are held by or on behalf of the transferee company (section 915)?
      `names given` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Do the draft terms give the name of each transferor company and of the transferee company?
      `registered offices given` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Do they give the address of the registered office of each?
      `kind of company given` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Do they say whether each is a company limited by shares or a company limited by guarantee and having a share capital?
      `share exchange ratio and cash given` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Do they give the number of shares in the transferee company to be allotted for a given number of shares in a transferor company (the share exchange ratio) and the amount of any cash payment?
      `allotment terms given` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Do they give the terms relating to the allotment of shares in the transferee company?
      `profit participation date given` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Do they give the date from which holding the new shares entitles the holders to participate in profits, and any special conditions?
      `accounting date given` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Do they give the date from which the transactions of a transferor company are treated for accounting purposes as those of the transferee company?
      `special rights measures given` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Do they give any rights or restrictions attaching to the new shares or securities for holders of securities with special rights or restrictions, or the measures proposed concerning them?
      `benefits given` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Do they give any benefit paid or given or intended to be paid or given to any of the experts or to any director of a merging company, and the consideration for it?
GIVETH A `s 903(1) status of a requirement`
DECIDE `Under section 905(2), do the draft terms of the merger give the particulars required` IS
    `s 905(2) the draft terms give the particulars required`
        (`s 915(2) the draft terms need not give the particulars in section 905(2)(b), (c) and (d)` (`s 915(1) this section applies` `a merger by absorption where all relevant securities of the transferor company are held by the transferee company` `a merger by absorption where all relevant securities of the transferor company are held by the transferee company`))
        `names given` `registered offices given` `kind of company given` `share exchange ratio and cash given` `allotment terms given` `profit participation date given` `accounting date given` `special rights measures given` `benefits given`

@export Under section 906(3), was the registrar's notice of receipt of the draft terms published in the Gazette at least one month before the members' meeting? (s 906(3))
GIVEN `date the notice was published` IS A DATE @desc On what date was the notice of receipt of the draft terms published in the Gazette?
      `a meeting is summoned` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has a meeting of the company been summoned for the purpose of approving the scheme?
      `date of the meeting` IS A DATE @desc On what date is the (first) meeting? (Ignored if no meeting is summoned.)
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 906(3), was the notice published at least one month before the meeting` IS
    `s 906(3) the notice was published at least one month before the meeting` `date the notice was published` (IF `a meeting is summoned` THEN JUST `date of the meeting` ELSE NOTHING)

@export Under section 907(1), has the merger scheme been approved by the members at the meeting (a majority in number representing 75% in value of each class)? (ss 907(1)-(2))
GIVEN `the meeting is excused` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is a meeting of the members excused under section 916, 917, 917A or 918?
      `number present and voting` IS A NUMBER @desc For the class of members: how many members were present and voting, in person or by proxy?
      `number for the scheme` IS A NUMBER @desc How many of them voted for the scheme?
      `value present and voting` IS A NUMBER @desc What is the total value of the shares of those present and voting?
      `value for the scheme` IS A NUMBER @desc What is the total value of the shares of those who voted for the scheme?
GIVETH A `s 903(1) status of a requirement`
DECIDE `Under section 907(1), has the merger scheme been approved by the members` IS
    `s 907(1) the scheme has been approved by the members of the merging company` (JUST `the meeting is excused`) (LIST (`s 907(1) votes of a class of members` OF `number present and voting`, `number for the scheme`, `value present and voting`, `value for the scheme`))

§§ `Merger: reports, accounts and inspection (ss 908-911B)`

@export Under section 908(1), must the directors of each merging company draw up and adopt an explanatory report, and have they? (ss 908(1)-(3))
GIVEN `section 915 applies` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does section 915 apply (a merger by absorption in which the transferee company holds all the relevant securities of each transferor company)?
      `section 915A exempts the report` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Do the conditions of section 915A apply (90% or more but not all held, a buy-out right and fair consideration) so that the report is not required?
      `all holders agreed to dispense` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Have all members and holders of other voting securities of the merging companies agreed to dispense with the report (section 918A)?
      `the directors drew up and adopted a report` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Have the directors drawn up and adopted a report?
GIVETH A `s 903(1) status of a requirement`
DECIDE `Under section 908(1), must the directors draw up and adopt an explanatory report and have they` IS
    `s 908(1) the directors have drawn up and adopted a report`
        (`s 908(3) the requirement in section 908 is excluded` (JUST `section 915 applies`) (JUST `section 915A exempts the report`) (JUST `all holders agreed to dispense`))
        `the directors drew up and adopted a report`

@export Under section 909(1), must an expert's report be drawn up on behalf of each merging company, and has it been? (ss 909(1)-(7))
GIVEN `section 915 applies` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does section 915 apply (a merger by absorption in which the transferee company holds all the relevant securities of each transferor company)?
      `section 915A exempts the report` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Do the conditions of section 915A apply so that the expert's report is not required?
      `all holders agreed to dispense` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Have all members and holders of other voting securities of the merging companies agreed to dispense with the report (section 918A)?
      `a written expert report has been drawn up` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has a written report on the draft terms to the members of the company been drawn up on its behalf by an expert?
GIVETH A `s 903(1) status of a requirement`
DECIDE `Under section 909(1), must an expert's report be drawn up for each merging company and has it been` IS
    `s 909(1) an expert's report has been drawn up on behalf of the company`
        (`s 909(7) the requirement in section 909 is excluded` (JUST `section 915 applies`) (JUST `section 915A exempts the report`) (JUST `all holders agreed to dispense`))
        `a written expert report has been drawn up`

-- s 909(4) with s 936(1).
@export Under section 909(4), may I act as the expert for a merging company: am I eligible as a statutory auditor and independent of the companies? (ss 909(4), 936(1))
GIVEN `I am eligible for appointment as a statutory auditor` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are you eligible for appointment as a statutory auditor (section 1212)?
      `I am an officer or employee of a company concerned` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are you an officer or employee of any of the companies concerned in the scheme (a transferor company or an existing transferee company)? An auditor of a company is not counted as its officer or employee.
      `I am a partner or employee of such a person` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are you a partner or employee of such a person, or a partnership of which such a person is a partner?
      `I am an officer or employee of an associated undertaking` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are you an officer or employee of an associated undertaking (a parent or subsidiary undertaking) of any of those companies?
      `I am a partner or employee of such an officer or employee` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are you a partner or employee of such a person, or a partnership of which such a person is a partner?
      `a connection specified by regulations exists` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does there exist, between you or an associate of yours and any of those companies or an associated undertaking, a connection of a description specified by regulations made by the Secretary of State?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 909(4), may I act as the expert` IS
    `s 909(4) the person may be the expert` (JUST `I am eligible for appointment as a statutory auditor`)
        (`s 936(1) the person meets the independence requirement` `I am an officer or employee of a company concerned` `I am a partner or employee of such a person` `I am an officer or employee of an associated undertaking` `I am a partner or employee of such an officer or employee` (JUST `a connection specified by regulations exists`))

@export Under section 910(1), must the directors prepare a supplementary accounting statement, and have they? (ss 910(1)-(6))
GIVEN `end of the financial year of the last annual accounts` IS A DATE @desc On what date did the financial year to which the last annual accounts relate end?
      `a meeting is required` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is a meeting of the company's members required to approve the scheme (it is not required where section 916, 917 or 918 applies)?
      `date of the first meeting` IS A DATE @desc On what date is the first meeting of the company summoned to approve the scheme? (Ignored if no meeting is required.)
      `date the directors adopt the draft terms` IS A DATE @desc On what date do (or did) the directors adopt the draft terms?
      `a recent half-yearly report was made public` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has the company made public a half-yearly financial report relating to a period ending on or after the date seven months before the meeting (or six months before adoption)?
      `section 915A or an agreement dispenses with it` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does section 915A apply, or have all holders of voting securities agreed to dispense with the statement (section 918A)?
      `the directors have prepared the statement` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Have the directors prepared a supplementary accounting statement?
GIVETH A `s 903(1) status of a requirement`
DECIDE `Under section 910(1), must the directors prepare a supplementary accounting statement and have they` IS
    `s 910(1A) the directors have prepared a supplementary accounting statement`
        (`s 910(1) this section applies` `end of the financial year of the last annual accounts` (IF `a meeting is required` THEN JUST `date of the first meeting` ELSE NOTHING) `date the directors adopt the draft terms`)
        (JUST `section 915A or an agreement dispenses with it`) `a recent half-yearly report was made public` `the directors have prepared the statement`

@export Under section 911(1), can the members of each merging company inspect the listed documents at the registered office and obtain copies free of charge throughout the month before the first meeting? (ss 911(1)-(2))
GIVEN `section 915 or 915A or an agreement excludes it` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the inspection requirement excluded by section 915A or 918A (or, for the reports, section 915)?
      `first day the members could inspect and get copies` IS A DATE @desc What is the first day on which the members could inspect the documents at the registered office and obtain copies on request free of charge?
      `last day the members could inspect and get copies` IS A DATE @desc What is the last day on which they could?
      `date of the first meeting` IS A DATE @desc On what date is the first meeting of the members (or any class of members) for the purposes of approving the scheme?
GIVETH A `s 903(1) status of a requirement`
DECIDE `Under section 911(1), can the members inspect the documents and obtain copies throughout the period` IS
    `s 911(1) the members could inspect the documents and obtain copies` (JUST `section 915 or 915A or an agreement excludes it`)
        (`s 911(2) the members could inspect and obtain copies throughout the period` `first day the members could inspect and get copies` `last day the members could inspect and get copies` `date of the first meeting`)
        (`s 911(2) the members could inspect and obtain copies throughout the period` `first day the members could inspect and get copies` `last day the members could inspect and get copies` `date of the first meeting`)

@export Under section 911B(1), must the directors report material changes in the company's property and liabilities to the members' meeting and to the other merging companies' directors, and have they? (s 911B(1))
GIVEN `section 915A or an agreement excludes the report` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the report excluded by section 915A or by the agreement of all holders of voting securities (section 918A)?
      `reported to every meeting` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Have the directors reported to every meeting of the members summoned to agree to the scheme any material changes in the property and liabilities of the company since the draft terms were adopted?
      `reported to the other directors` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Have they reported those changes to the directors of every other merging company?
GIVETH A `s 903(1) status of a requirement`
DECIDE `Under section 911B(1), have the directors reported material changes in property and liabilities` IS
    `s 911B(1) the directors have reported material changes in property and liabilities` (JUST `section 915A or an agreement excludes the report`) `reported to every meeting` `reported to the other directors`

§§ `Merger: articles, special rights and the exceptions (ss 912-918A)`

@export Under section 912, must the articles of the new transferee company be approved by ordinary resolution of each transferor company, and have they been? (s 912)
GIVEN `a merger by formation of a new company` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the scheme a merger by formation of a new company?
      `Part 26A and this is the company in respect of which it is proposed` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the compromise or arrangement to be sanctioned under Part 26A, and is this the company in respect of which it is proposed?
      `approved by an ordinary resolution` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has this transferor company approved the articles (or a draft of them) by ordinary resolution (section 282)?
GIVETH A `s 903(1) status of a requirement`
DECIDE `Under section 912, have the articles of the new transferee company been approved by ordinary resolution` IS
    `s 912(1) the articles of the transferee company have been approved by ordinary resolution` `a merger by formation of a new company` `Part 26A and this is the company in respect of which it is proposed` (JUST `approved by an ordinary resolution`)

@export Under section 913, must the merger scheme give me rights of equivalent value in the transferee company if I hold securities of a transferor company with special rights, and does it? (s 913)
GIVEN `I hold securities other than shares with special rights otherwise than as member or creditor` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Do you hold securities (other than shares) of a transferor company to which special rights are attached, otherwise than as a member or creditor of the company?
      `I have agreed otherwise` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Have you agreed otherwise?
      `I am entitled to have the securities purchased` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are you, or under the scheme will you be, entitled to have the securities purchased by the transferee company on terms that the court considers reasonable?
      `the scheme gives me rights of equivalent value` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does the scheme provide that you are to receive rights in the transferee company of equivalent value?
GIVETH A `s 903(1) status of a requirement`
DECIDE `Under section 913, does the merger scheme protect me as a holder of securities with special rights` IS
    `s 913(1) the scheme protects the holder of securities to which special rights are attached` `I hold securities other than shares with special rights otherwise than as member or creditor` `I have agreed otherwise` `I am entitled to have the securities purchased` `the scheme gives me rights of equivalent value`

@export Under section 914, does the merger scheme comply with the ban on allotting shares in the transferee company to a transferor company or its nominee in respect of its own shares? (s 914)
GIVEN `allotment to a transferor company for its own shares` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does the scheme provide for shares in the transferee company to be allotted to a transferor company (or its nominee) in respect of shares in the transferor company held by itself (or its nominee)?
      `allotment to the transferee company for shares it holds` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does the scheme provide for shares in the transferee company to be allotted to the transferee company (or its nominee) in respect of shares in a transferor company held by the transferee company (or its nominee)?
GIVETH A `s 903(1) status of a requirement`
DECIDE `Under section 914, does the merger scheme avoid allotting shares to a transferor company or its nominee` IS
    `s 914 the scheme does not provide for the allotment of shares the section forbids` `allotment to a transferor company for its own shares` `allotment to the transferee company for shares it holds`

@export Under section 915A(1), are the conditions met for the reports and inspection requirements to be dropped where the transferee company holds 90% or more (but not all) of a transferor company's voting securities? (ss 915A(1)-(4))
GIVEN `a merger by absorption` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the scheme a merger by absorption?
      `percentage held by the transferee company` IS A NUMBER @desc What percentage of the relevant securities (voting shares or other voting securities) of the transferor company is held by or on behalf of the transferee company? (If there are several transferor companies, ask for the lowest.)
      `the scheme gives every other holder a right to require the transferee to acquire` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does the scheme provide that every other holder of relevant securities has the right to require the transferee company to acquire those securities?
      `the consideration would be fair and reasonable` IS A BOOLEAN @desc If a holder exercises that right, will the consideration to be given for the securities be fair and reasonable?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 915A(1), do the reports and inspection requirements fall away where 90 percent or more but not all is held` IS
    `s 915A(2) the requirements of sections 908, 909, 910, 911 and 911B do not apply`
        (`s 915A(1) this section applies` `a merger by absorption` (LIST `percentage held by the transferee company`))
        (`s 915A(3) the first condition is met` `the scheme gives every other holder a right to require the transferee to acquire`)
        (`s 915A(4) the second condition is met` `the consideration would be fair and reasonable`)

@export Under section 916(2), is the meeting of the transferee company's members excused, on the court being satisfied the four conditions have been complied with? (ss 916(1)-(5))
GIVEN `a merger by absorption` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the scheme a merger by absorption?
      `percentage held by the transferee company` IS A NUMBER @desc What percentage of the relevant securities of the transferor company is held by or on behalf of the transferee company?
      `first condition met` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the first condition met (the registrar's notice of receipt of the draft terms was published at least one month before the transferor's first meeting, or the website route of section 916(3B) was followed)?
      `second condition met` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the second condition met (for each of the documents in section 911(3), the members could inspect it at the registered office, or it was on the transferee company's website, throughout the month)?
      `third condition met` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the third condition met (the members of the transferee company could obtain copies of the documents free of charge throughout the month)?
      `members holding 5 percent could have required a meeting` IS A NUMBER @desc What percentage of the transferee company's paid-up voting capital (excluding treasury shares) was held together by members who could have required a meeting of each class?
      `a meeting was required` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did any such members actually require a meeting of each class to be called?
      `the court is satisfied` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the court satisfied that the conditions have been complied with?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 916(2), is the meeting of the transferee company's members excused` IS
    `s 916(2) the meeting of members of the transferee company is not required`
        (`s 916(1) this section applies` `a merger by absorption` (LIST `percentage held by the transferee company`))
        (JUST `first condition met`) (JUST `second condition met`) (JUST `third condition met`)
        (`s 916(5) the fourth condition is met` `members holding 5 percent could have required a meeting` `a meeting was required`)
        `the court is satisfied`

@export Under section 918A(1), have all the members and holders of voting securities of the merging companies agreed to dispense with the reports and the inspection requirements? (s 918A(1))
GIVEN `all have so agreed` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Have all members holding shares in, and all persons holding other securities of, the merging companies (being shares or securities that carry a right to vote in general meetings) agreed to dispense with the reports?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 918A(1), are the reports and inspection requirements dispensed with by agreement` IS
    `s 918A(1) the requirements are dispensed with by agreement` `all have so agreed`

§§ `Division: the draft terms, approval, reports and the exceptions (ss 920-934)`

@export Under section 920(2), do the draft terms of the division scheme give the particulars the section requires? (s 920(2))
GIVEN `names given` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Do the draft terms give the name of the transferor company and of each transferee company?
      `registered offices given` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Do they give the address of the registered office of each?
      `kind of company given` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Do they say whether each is a company limited by shares or a company limited by guarantee and having a share capital?
      `share exchange ratio and cash given` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Do they give the number of shares in a transferee company to be allotted for a given number of shares in the transferor company (the share exchange ratio) and the amount of any cash payment?
      `allotment terms given` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Do they give the terms relating to the allotment of shares in a transferee company?
      `profit participation date given` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Do they give the date from which holding the new shares entitles the holders to participate in profits, and any special conditions?
      `accounting date given` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Do they give the date from which the transactions of the transferor company are treated for accounting purposes as those of a transferee company?
      `special rights measures given` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Do they give any rights or restrictions attaching to the new shares or securities for holders of securities with special rights or restrictions, or the measures proposed concerning them?
      `benefits given` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Do they give any benefit paid or given or intended to be paid or given to any of the experts or to any director of a company involved in the division, and the consideration for it?
GIVETH A `s 903(1) status of a requirement`
DECIDE `Under section 920(2), do the draft terms of the division give the particulars required` IS
    `s 920(2) the draft terms give the particulars required` `names given` `registered offices given` `kind of company given` `share exchange ratio and cash given` `allotment terms given` `profit participation date given` `accounting date given` `special rights measures given` `benefits given`

@export Under section 922(1), has the division scheme been approved by the members of the company at the meeting (a majority in number representing 75% in value of each class)? (ss 922(1)-(2))
GIVEN `the meeting is excused` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is a meeting of the members excused under section 931, 931A or 932?
      `number present and voting` IS A NUMBER @desc For the class of members: how many members were present and voting, in person or by proxy?
      `number for the scheme` IS A NUMBER @desc How many of them voted for the scheme?
      `value present and voting` IS A NUMBER @desc What is the total value of the shares of those present and voting?
      `value for the scheme` IS A NUMBER @desc What is the total value of the shares of those who voted for the scheme?
GIVETH A `s 903(1) status of a requirement`
DECIDE `Under section 922(1), has the division scheme been approved by the members` IS
    `s 922(1) the scheme has been approved by the members of a company involved in the division` (JUST `the meeting is excused`) (LIST (`s 922(1) votes of a class of members` OF `number present and voting`, `number for the scheme`, `value present and voting`, `value for the scheme`))

@export Under section 923(3), does the directors' report on the division say whether a report was made under section 593 and whether it was delivered to the registrar? (s 923(3))
GIVEN `the report states whether a section 593 report was made` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does the directors' report state whether a report has been made to any transferee company under section 593 (valuation of non-cash consideration for shares)?
      `a section 593 report was made` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has a report been made to a transferee company under section 593?
      `the report states whether it was delivered` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does the directors' report state whether that report has been delivered to the registrar of companies?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 923(3), does the directors report on the division say what the section requires about a section 593 report` IS
    `s 923(3) the report states what the section requires` `the report states whether a section 593 report was made` `a section 593 report was made` `the report states whether it was delivered`

@export Under section 926(1), can the members of each company involved in the division inspect the listed documents at the registered office and obtain copies free of charge throughout the month before the first meeting? (ss 926(1)-(2))
GIVEN `the court has directed that sections 921 and 926 do not apply` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has the court directed under section 934 that the inspection requirement of section 926 does not apply?
      `first day the members could inspect and get copies` IS A DATE @desc What is the first day on which the members could inspect the documents at the registered office and obtain copies on request free of charge?
      `last day the members could inspect and get copies` IS A DATE @desc What is the last day on which they could?
      `date of the first meeting` IS A DATE @desc On what date is the first meeting of the members (or any class of members) for the purposes of approving the scheme?
GIVETH A `s 903(1) status of a requirement`
DECIDE `Under section 926(1), can the members inspect the documents and obtain copies throughout the period` IS
    `s 926(1) the members could inspect the documents and obtain copies` (`s 934(1)(a) the court has directed that sections 921 and 926 do not apply` `the court has directed that sections 921 and 926 do not apply`)
        (`s 926(2) the members could inspect and obtain copies throughout the period` `first day the members could inspect and get copies` `last day the members could inspect and get copies` `date of the first meeting`)
        (`s 926(2) the members could inspect and obtain copies throughout the period` `first day the members could inspect and get copies` `last day the members could inspect and get copies` `date of the first meeting`)

@export Under section 928, must the articles of each new transferee company be approved by ordinary resolution of the transferor company, and have they been? (s 928)
GIVEN `Part 26A` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the compromise or arrangement to be sanctioned under Part 26A?
      `approved by an ordinary resolution` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has the transferor company approved the articles (or a draft of them) of every new transferee company by ordinary resolution (section 282)?
GIVETH A `s 903(1) status of a requirement`
DECIDE `Under section 928, have the articles of every new transferee company been approved by ordinary resolution` IS
    `s 928(1) the articles of every new transferee company have been approved by ordinary resolution of the transferor company` `Part 26A` (JUST `approved by an ordinary resolution`)

@export Under section 931(6), is the fourth condition for excusing the transferor's members' meeting met: has the board sent the report of material changes to every member and to the directors of every existing transferee company, covering changes up to a date no earlier than one month before the court's order? (s 931(6))
GIVEN `report sent to every member` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Have the directors of the transferor company sent a report of any material change in its property and liabilities to every member who would have been entitled to notice of a meeting?
      `report sent to the directors of the transferee companies` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Have they sent it to the directors of every existing transferee company?
      `report covers changes up to` IS A DATE @desc Up to what date does the report state material changes in the property and liabilities of the transferor company?
      `date of the court's order` IS A DATE @desc On what date is (or was) the court's order?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 931(6), has the fourth condition been met` IS
    `s 931(6) the fourth condition is met` `report sent to every member` `report sent to the directors of the transferee companies` `report covers changes up to` `date of the court's order`

@export Under section 933A(2), do the reports and accounts requirements fall away because each transferee company is new and its shares are allotted to the transferor company's members in proportion to their rights? (ss 933A(1)-(2))
GIVEN `a division` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the scheme a division?
      `each transferee company is new` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is each of the transferee companies a new company?
      `allotted in proportion to rights` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are all the shares in each of the transferee companies to be allotted to the members of the transferor company in proportion to their rights in the allotted share capital of the transferor company?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 933A(2), do the requirements of sections 923 to 925 and 927 fall away because shares are allotted proportionally` IS
    `s 933A(2) the requirements of sections 923, 924, 925 and 927 do not apply` (`s 933A(1) this section applies` `a division` `each transferee company is new`) `allotted in proportion to rights`

@export Under section 934(1), may the court direct that the publication and inspection requirements do not apply, or that the transferee company's meeting conditions are omitted? (ss 934(1)-(4))
GIVEN `members had the documents` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Will the members of the company have received, or been able to obtain free of charge, copies of the documents listed in section 926?
      `members in time to examine before the meeting` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Will that have been in time to examine them before the first meeting of the members?
      `no meeting is held` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is no meeting held, in the circumstances described in section 932?
      `members in time to require a meeting` IS A BOOLEAN @desc If no meeting is held: will they have had the documents in time to require a meeting as mentioned in section 932(4)?
      `creditors had the draft terms` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Will the creditors of the company have received, or been able to obtain free of charge, copies of the draft terms?
      `creditors in time to examine before the meeting` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Will that have been in time to examine them before the first meeting of the members?
      `creditors at the same time as the members` IS A BOOLEAN @desc If no meeting is held: will the creditors have had them at the same time as the members?
      `no prejudice` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Would no prejudice be caused to the members or creditors of the transferor company or any transferee company by making the order?
      `the court is satisfied` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the court satisfied that the conditions will be fulfilled in relation to that company?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 934(1), may the court direct that the requirements do not apply` IS
    `s 934(1) the court may by order direct that the requirements do not apply`
        (`s 934(2) the first condition is met` `members had the documents` `members in time to examine before the meeting` `no meeting is held` `members in time to require a meeting`)
        (`s 934(3) the second condition is met` `creditors had the draft terms` `creditors in time to examine before the meeting` `no meeting is held` `creditors at the same time as the members`)
        (`s 934(4) the third condition is met` `no prejudice`)
        `the court is satisfied`

§ `Part 27, Chapter 4 -- Supplementary provisions (ss 935-941)`

@export Under section 935(1), may I, as the expert, arrange for or accept a valuation made by another person? (s 935(1))
GIVEN `a valuation is reasonably necessary` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does it appear to you, as the expert, that a valuation is reasonably necessary to enable you to draw up your report?
      `reasonable for another person to make it` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does it appear to you that it is reasonable for that valuation, or part of it, to be made by (or for you to accept a valuation made by) another person?
      `the person has the knowledge and experience` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does that person appear to you to have the requisite knowledge and experience to make the valuation or that part of it?
      `the person meets the independence requirement` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does that person meet the independence requirement in section 936?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 935(1), may I arrange for or accept a valuation made by another person` IS
    `s 935(1) the expert may arrange for or accept the valuation` `a valuation is reasonably necessary` `reasonable for another person to make it` `the person has the knowledge and experience` (JUST `the person meets the independence requirement`)

@export Under section 936(1), do I meet the independence requirement to act as an expert or valuer for the companies concerned in the scheme? (s 936(1))
GIVEN `I am an officer or employee of a company concerned` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are you an officer or employee of any of the companies concerned in the scheme (every transferor and existing transferee company)? An auditor of a company is not counted as its officer or employee (section 936(2)).
      `I am a partner or employee of such a person` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are you a partner or employee of such a person, or a partnership of which such a person is a partner?
      `I am an officer or employee of an associated undertaking` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are you an officer or employee of an associated undertaking (a parent or subsidiary undertaking) of any of those companies?
      `I am a partner or employee of such an officer or employee` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are you a partner or employee of such a person, or a partnership of which such a person is a partner?
      `a connection specified by regulations exists` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does there exist, between you or an associate of yours and any of those companies or an associated undertaking, a connection of a description specified by regulations made by the Secretary of State?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 936(1), do I meet the independence requirement` IS
    `s 936(1) the person meets the independence requirement` `I am an officer or employee of a company concerned` `I am a partner or employee of such a person` `I am an officer or employee of an associated undertaking` `I am a partner or employee of such an officer or employee` (JUST `a connection specified by regulations exists`)

@export Under section 937, am I an associate of a person, for the purposes of the independence requirement? (s 937)
GIVEN `the other person is` IS A `s 937 kind of the person in relation to whom associate is defined` @desc What is the other person? Choose: an individual, a body corporate, a partnership that is a legal person, or a partnership that is not a legal person.
      `I am` IS A `s 937 relationship of the person to the other` @desc How are you related to the other person? Choose from the list (for example: a spouse, civil partner, minor child or step-child of the individual; an employee of the other; a partner of the other; a body corporate of which the other is a director; a body corporate in the same group; or any other relationship).
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 937, am I an associate of the other person` IS
    `s 937 the person is an associate` `the other person is` `I am`

@export Under section 938(2), may I apply to the court for an order that a meeting of the members or creditors of an existing transferee company be summoned? (ss 938(1)-(2))
GIVEN `I am` IS A `s 896(2) applicant` @desc Who are you in relation to the existing transferee company? Choose: the company, a creditor of the company, a member of the company, the liquidator of the company, the administrator of the company, or any other person.
      `the company is being wound up` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the company being wound up?
      `the company is in administration` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the company in administration?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 938(2), may I apply to the court for a meeting of the members or creditors of an existing transferee company` IS
    `s 938(2) the person may apply to the court` `I am` `the company is being wound up` `the company is in administration`

@export Under section 939(3), is the date the court fixed for the steps needed to complete the transfer within six months after the transfer date? (s 939(3))
GIVEN `steps are necessary` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it necessary for the transferor company to take steps to ensure that the undertaking, property and liabilities are fully transferred?
      `the transfer date` IS A DATE @desc What date did the court fix for the transfer?
      `the date for the steps` IS A DATE @desc What date did the court fix by which those steps must be taken?
GIVETH A `s 903(1) status of a requirement`
DECIDE `Under section 939(3), is the date the court fixed for the steps within six months` IS
    `s 939(3) the court has fixed a date for the steps within six months` `steps are necessary` `the transfer date` `the date for the steps`

-- s 940(2) and (3) feed s 940(1): the creditors' agreement and the net value.
@export Under section 940(1), how much may I claim, as a creditor of the transferor company in a division, from another transferee company for a liability that was transferred to a defaulting transferee company? (ss 940(1)-(3))
GIVEN `a division` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the scheme a division?
      `the liability was transferred to another transferee company` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Was the liability owed to you transferred to another transferee company under the scheme?
      `the creditors agreed by the majority` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did the creditors (or your class of creditors) agree to the scheme at the meeting by the majority section 940(2) or (2A) requires, so that section 940(1) does not apply to their liabilities?
      `the amount in default` IS A NUMBER @desc What amount of that liability has the other transferee company made default in satisfying (in pounds)?
      `value of the property transferred to this company` IS A NUMBER @desc For the transferee company you would look to: what was the value, at the time of the transfer, of the property transferred to it under the scheme (in pounds)?
      `liabilities transferred to this company` IS A NUMBER @desc What was the amount, at that date, of the liabilities transferred to it (in pounds)?
GIVETH A MAYBE NUMBER
DECIDE `Under section 940(1), how much may I claim from another transferee company for a liability transferred to a defaulting transferee company` IS
    `s 940(1) the amount for which the transferee company is liable` `a division` `the liability was transferred to another transferee company` (JUST `the creditors agreed by the majority`) `the amount in default` (`s 940(3) the net value transferred` `value of the property transferred to this company` `liabilities transferred to this company`)

@export Under section 940(2), did the creditors agree to the scheme by the majority that takes away their claim against the other transferee companies? (ss 940(2), (2A))
GIVEN `the compromise or arrangement is sanctioned under` IS A `s 940(2) Part under which the compromise or arrangement is sanctioned` @desc Under which Part is the compromise or arrangement to be sanctioned? Choose: Part 26 or Part 26A.
      `number present and voting` IS A NUMBER @desc How many creditors (of the class) were present and voting at the meeting summoned for the purposes of agreeing to the scheme?
      `number who agree` IS A NUMBER @desc How many of them agreed?
      `value present and voting` IS A NUMBER @desc What is the total value of the debts of those present and voting (in pounds)?
      `value who agree` IS A NUMBER @desc What is the total value of the debts of those who agreed (in pounds)?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 940(2), did the creditors agree by the majority that removes the joint and several liability` IS
    `s 940(2) subsection (1) does not apply in relation to the liabilities owed to those creditors` `the compromise or arrangement is sanctioned under` `number present and voting` `number who agree` `value present and voting` `value who agree`

@export Under section 940A(1), is the failure to keep the draft terms or document on the website throughout the period to be disregarded? (ss 940A(1)-(2))
GIVEN `the provision is` IS A `s 940A(2) provision` @desc Which provision requires the information or document to be available on the website throughout a period? Choose from the list (section 906A(6), 911A(4), 916(3B) and (4B), 917(3B) and (4B), 918(2B) and (3B), 921A(6), 926A(4), 931(3B) and (4B), 932(2B) and (3B)) or any other provision.
      `it was available for part of the period` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Was the information or document made available on the website for part of that period?
      `the failure was beyond the company's control` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the failure to make it available throughout that period wholly attributable to circumstances that it would not be reasonable to have expected the company to prevent or avoid?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 940A(1), is the failure to make the document available on the website throughout the period to be disregarded` IS
    `s 940A(1) the failure is to be disregarded` (`s 940A(2) the provision is one of those to which section 940A(1) applies` `the provision is`) `it was available for part of the period` `the failure was beyond the company's control`

-- ====================================================================================================
-- seat questions from part coa21 (merged by the lead on 2026-11-12; unchanged text follows)
-- ====================================================================================================
-- coa21-seat.l4: the Companies Act 2006 (United Kingdom), ss 942 to 993 (Part 28, Takeovers etc, and Part 29, Fraudulent trading) -- THE SEAT LAYER.
--
-- SEAT: an individual who is, or is about to become, a director, a company secretary or a member (shareholder) of a company registered under
-- the Act, or who deals with one, asking on facts they can state what the Act requires or lets them do, what rights they have against the
-- company or its directors, what they must disclose, file, approve or vote on and by when, and what follows (liability, offences, penalties)
-- if it is not done. (Assumed, not ruled: the Act is addressed to companies, so the individual is whoever stands in a company's management or
-- ownership.) In this range the person is a member who is bid for or squeezed out, a director of a company that is bid for or that opts in, an
-- offeror, or anyone who deals with the Takeover Panel. The Panel, the court and the Secretary of State have no seat.
--
-- PLAIN INPUTS. Every question takes plain inputs (yes or no, a number, a date, a choice from a list) worded as the person would be asked.
-- The records the layer-1 modules expect are built inside each question, in its WHERE, from those answers, and the SAME layer-1 rule is then
-- called; no rule is restated here. Where the Act turns a question on something the person cannot know from the Act (what the Panel's own
-- rules say, what Schedule 2 or Schedule 1C provide, whether an officer is "in default"), the question offers the choice "I do not know",
-- and the answer is then "not covered" (NOTHING), never "no".
-- Reading an answer: JUST TRUE is yes; JUST FALSE is the text's own "no"; NOTHING is "the Act's text does not answer this on these facts".

§ `Companies Act 2006 -- the questions of a director, member or other person dealing with a company (ss 942 to 993)`

DECLARE `Under sections 942 to 993 a fact the Act leaves to another source` IS ONE OF
    `Under sections 942 to 993 it is so`
    `Under sections 942 to 993 it is not so`
    `Under sections 942 to 993 I do not know`

GIVEN answer IS A `Under sections 942 to 993 a fact the Act leaves to another source`
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`Under sections 942 to 993 the fact as a yes, no or not known` MEANS
    CONSIDER answer
    WHEN `Under sections 942 to 993 it is so` THEN JUST TRUE
    WHEN `Under sections 942 to 993 it is not so` THEN JUST FALSE
    WHEN `Under sections 942 to 993 I do not know` THEN NOTHING

§§ `Chapter 1: the Takeover Panel (ss 942 to 965)`

-- s 944(4). A person is not taken to have contravened a Panel rule if he shows that, when he acted, the rule's text had not been made available to the public.
@export Under section 944(4), am I protected from being taken to have contravened a Takeover Panel rule because its text had not been made available to the public?
GIVEN `the text of the rule had not been made available to the public when I acted` IS A BOOLEAN @desc When the alleged contravention happened, had the text of the rule not yet been made available to the public (section 944(3) requires it immediately after the instrument containing the rules is made), and can you show that?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`Under section 944(4), am I protected from being taken to have contravened a Takeover Panel rule because its text had not been made available to the public` MEANS
    `s 944(4) the person is protected from being taken to have contravened the rule` `the text of the rule had not been made available to the public when I acted`

-- s 944(7). A person who wishes to rely on an instrument making rules in legal proceedings may require the Panel to endorse a copy with a certificate.
@export Under section 944(7), may I require the Takeover Panel to certify a copy of its rules instrument for use in legal proceedings?
GIVEN `I wish to rely on the instrument by which the rules are made in legal proceedings` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Do you wish to rely, in legal proceedings, on an instrument by which the Panel's rules are made?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`Under section 944(7), may I require the Takeover Panel to certify a copy of its rules instrument for use in legal proceedings` MEANS
    `s 944(7) the person may require the Panel to endorse a copy of the instrument with a certificate` `I wish to rely on the instrument by which the rules are made in legal proceedings`

-- s 945(2). A Panel ruling binds to the extent and in the circumstances the rules specify, and subject to any review or appeal.
@export Under section 945(2), is a Takeover Panel ruling binding on me?
GIVEN `the Panel's rules say that a ruling like this one binds, to this extent and in these circumstances` IS A `Under sections 942 to 993 a fact the Act leaves to another source` @desc Do the Panel's rules say that a ruling of this kind binds you, to this extent and in these circumstances? (The Act leaves that to the rules.)
      `a review of the ruling or an appeal from it is pending or has been decided` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is a review of the ruling, or an appeal from it, pending or already decided?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`Under section 945(2), is a Takeover Panel ruling binding on me` MEANS
    `s 945(2) the ruling has binding effect` (`Under sections 942 to 993 the fact as a yes, no or not known` `the Panel's rules say that a ruling like this one binds, to this extent and in these circumstances`) `a review of the ruling or an appeal from it is pending or has been decided`

-- s 947(1), (3), (10). The Panel's notice in writing requiring documents or information, and what limits it.
@export Under section 947, must I produce the documents or give the information the Takeover Panel has required by notice?
GIVEN `the Panel has required me by notice in writing` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has the Takeover Panel required you, by a notice in writing, to produce documents or provide information?
      `the notice specifies or describes what is required` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does the notice specify or describe the documents, or the information and the form and manner in which to provide it?
      `what is required is reasonably required in connection with the Panel's functions` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is what the notice requires reasonably required in connection with the exercise of the Panel's functions?
      `I could maintain a claim to legal professional privilege over it` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Could you maintain a claim to legal professional privilege (in Scotland, to confidentiality of communications) over the documents or information in legal proceedings?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`Under section 947, must I produce the documents or give the information the Takeover Panel has required by notice` MEANS
    `s 947 the person must comply with the Panel's requirement` `the Panel has required me by notice in writing` `the notice specifies or describes what is required` `what is required is reasonably required in connection with the Panel's functions` `I could maintain a claim to legal professional privilege over it`

-- s 947(2). Compliance must be at the place and before the end of the period the notice specifies.
@export Under section 947(2), did I comply with the Takeover Panel's notice at the right place and in time?
GIVEN `the last day of the period the notice allowed` IS A DATE @desc What was the last day of the period that the Panel's notice allowed you for compliance?
      `the day I complied` IS A DATE @desc On what day did you comply?
      `I complied at the place the notice specified` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did you comply at the place the notice specified?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`Under section 947(2), did I comply with the Takeover Panel's notice at the right place and in time` MEANS
    `s 947(2) the requirement has been complied with as the subsection requires` `the day I complied` `the last day of the period the notice allowed` `I complied at the place the notice specified`

-- s 948. The restriction on disclosing information given to the Panel, and its exceptions.
@export Under section 948, am I prohibited from disclosing this information that was given to the Takeover Panel?
GIVEN `it relates to the private affairs of an individual` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does the information relate to the private affairs of an individual?
      `it relates to a particular business` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does the information relate to a particular business?
      `it was provided to the Panel in connection with its functions` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Was the information provided to the Takeover Panel in connection with the exercise of its functions?
      `the individual is still living` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the individual still living?
      `the business is still carried on` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the business still being carried on?
      `the individual (or the person carrying on the business) has consented` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has the individual, or the person for the time being carrying on the business, consented to the disclosure?
      `the disclosure is to help the Panel carry out its functions` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the disclosure made for the purpose of facilitating the carrying out by the Panel of any of its functions?
      `the disclosure is to a person listed in Part 1 of Schedule 2` IS A `Under sections 942 to 993 a fact the Act leaves to another source` @desc Is the disclosure made to a person specified in Part 1 of Schedule 2 to the Act?
      `it is information of a description listed in Part 2 of Schedule 2` IS A `Under sections 942 to 993 a fact the Act leaves to another source` @desc Is the information of a description specified in Part 2 of Schedule 2?
      `the disclosure is made in accordance with Part 3 of Schedule 2` IS A `Under sections 942 to 993 a fact the Act leaves to another source` @desc Is the disclosure made in accordance with Part 3 of Schedule 2?
      `I am the Financial Conduct Authority, the Prudential Regulation Authority or the Bank of England` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are you (or the body you act for) the Financial Conduct Authority, the Prudential Regulation Authority or the Bank of England?
      `the Panel disclosed the information to that authority in reliance on section 948(3)` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did the Panel disclose the information to that authority in reliance on section 948(3)?
      `I obtained it, directly or indirectly, from one of those authorities` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did you obtain the information, directly or indirectly, from one of those authorities?
      `it is or has been available to the public from another source` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the information, or has it been, available to the public from any other source?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`Under section 948, am I prohibited from disclosing this information that was given to the Takeover Panel` MEANS
    `s 948 the disclosure is prohibited by section 948` `the answer under (2)` `the answer under (3)` `the answer under (6)` `the answer under (8)`
    WHERE
        `the answer under (2)` MEANS
            `s 948(2) the disclosure is prohibited` (`s 948(1) the section applies to the information` `it relates to the private affairs of an individual` `it relates to a particular business` `it was provided to the Panel in connection with its functions`) `it relates to the private affairs of an individual` `the individual is still living` `it relates to a particular business` `the business is still carried on` `the individual (or the person carrying on the business) has consented`
        `the answer under (3)` MEANS
            `s 948(3) subsection (2) does not apply to the disclosure` `the disclosure is to help the Panel carry out its functions` (`Under sections 942 to 993 the fact as a yes, no or not known` `the disclosure is to a person listed in Part 1 of Schedule 2`) (`Under sections 942 to 993 the fact as a yes, no or not known` `it is information of a description listed in Part 2 of Schedule 2`) (`Under sections 942 to 993 the fact as a yes, no or not known` `the disclosure is made in accordance with Part 3 of Schedule 2`)
        `the answer under (6)` MEANS
            `s 948(6) subsection (2) does not apply to the disclosure` (IF `I am the Financial Conduct Authority, the Prudential Regulation Authority or the Bank of England` THEN `s 948(7) the body is an authority within the subsection` `s 948(7)(a) the Financial Conduct Authority` ELSE JUST FALSE) `the Panel disclosed the information to that authority in reliance on section 948(3)` `I obtained it, directly or indirectly, from one of those authorities`
        `the answer under (8)` MEANS
            `s 948(8) the section prohibits the disclosure` `it is or has been available to the public from another source`

-- s 949(1). The offence of disclosing in contravention of section 948, unless the person did not know or took all reasonable steps.
@export Under section 949(1), am I guilty of the offence of disclosing information in contravention of section 948?
GIVEN `it relates to the private affairs of an individual` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does the information relate to the private affairs of an individual?
      `it relates to a particular business` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does the information relate to a particular business?
      `it was provided to the Panel in connection with its functions` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Was the information provided to the Takeover Panel in connection with the exercise of its functions?
      `the individual is still living` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the individual still living?
      `the business is still carried on` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the business still being carried on?
      `the individual (or the person carrying on the business) has consented` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has the individual, or the person for the time being carrying on the business, consented to the disclosure?
      `the disclosure is to help the Panel carry out its functions` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the disclosure made for the purpose of facilitating the carrying out by the Panel of any of its functions?
      `the disclosure is to a person listed in Part 1 of Schedule 2` IS A `Under sections 942 to 993 a fact the Act leaves to another source` @desc Is the disclosure made to a person specified in Part 1 of Schedule 2 to the Act?
      `it is information of a description listed in Part 2 of Schedule 2` IS A `Under sections 942 to 993 a fact the Act leaves to another source` @desc Is the information of a description specified in Part 2 of Schedule 2?
      `the disclosure is made in accordance with Part 3 of Schedule 2` IS A `Under sections 942 to 993 a fact the Act leaves to another source` @desc Is the disclosure made in accordance with Part 3 of Schedule 2?
      `I am the Financial Conduct Authority, the Prudential Regulation Authority or the Bank of England` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are you (or the body you act for) the Financial Conduct Authority, the Prudential Regulation Authority or the Bank of England?
      `the Panel disclosed the information to that authority in reliance on section 948(3)` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did the Panel disclose the information to that authority in reliance on section 948(3)?
      `I obtained it, directly or indirectly, from one of those authorities` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did you obtain the information, directly or indirectly, from one of those authorities?
      `it is or has been available to the public from another source` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the information, or has it been, available to the public from any other source?
      `I did not know, and had no reason to suspect, that it had been provided to the Panel` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it true that you did not know, and had no reason to suspect, that the information had been provided to the Panel as section 948(1) describes?
      `I took all reasonable steps and exercised all due diligence to avoid the offence` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did you take all reasonable steps and exercise all due diligence to avoid committing the offence?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`Under section 949(1), am I guilty of the offence of disclosing information in contravention of section 948` MEANS
    `s 949(1) the person is guilty of an offence` `the disclosure contravenes section 948` `I did not know, and had no reason to suspect, that it had been provided to the Panel` `I took all reasonable steps and exercised all due diligence to avoid the offence`
    WHERE
        `the disclosure contravenes section 948` MEANS
            `s 948 the disclosure is prohibited by section 948`
                (`s 948(2) the disclosure is prohibited` (`s 948(1) the section applies to the information` `it relates to the private affairs of an individual` `it relates to a particular business` `it was provided to the Panel in connection with its functions`) `it relates to the private affairs of an individual` `the individual is still living` `it relates to a particular business` `the business is still carried on` `the individual (or the person carrying on the business) has consented`)
                (`s 948(3) subsection (2) does not apply to the disclosure` `the disclosure is to help the Panel carry out its functions` (`Under sections 942 to 993 the fact as a yes, no or not known` `the disclosure is to a person listed in Part 1 of Schedule 2`) (`Under sections 942 to 993 the fact as a yes, no or not known` `it is information of a description listed in Part 2 of Schedule 2`) (`Under sections 942 to 993 the fact as a yes, no or not known` `the disclosure is made in accordance with Part 3 of Schedule 2`))
                (`s 948(6) subsection (2) does not apply to the disclosure` (IF `I am the Financial Conduct Authority, the Prudential Regulation Authority or the Bank of England` THEN `s 948(7) the body is an authority within the subsection` `s 948(7)(a) the Financial Conduct Authority` ELSE JUST FALSE) `the Panel disclosed the information to that authority in reliance on section 948(3)` `I obtained it, directly or indirectly, from one of those authorities`)
                (`s 948(8) the section prohibits the disclosure` `it is or has been available to the public from another source`)

-- s 949(2). The penalty for the offence.
@export Under section 949(2), what penalty may I face if I am convicted of disclosing information in contravention of section 948?
GIVEN `how I would be convicted` IS A `Mode of conviction` @desc How would you be convicted: on conviction on indictment, on summary conviction in England and Wales, in Scotland, or in Northern Ireland? (Choose "on summary conviction" only if the place is not known.)
GIVETH A MAYBE Penalty
`Under section 949(2), what penalty may I face if I am convicted of disclosing information in contravention of section 948` MEANS
    `s 949(2) the penalty` `how I would be convicted`

-- s 949(3). Every officer in default is also guilty where a company commits the offence.
@export Under section 949(3), am I, as an officer of a company that committed the offence, also guilty of it?
GIVEN `the company or other body corporate committed an offence under section 949` IS A `Under sections 942 to 993 a fact the Act leaves to another source` @desc Did the company or other body corporate commit an offence under section 949?
      `I am an officer of the company who is in default` IS A `Under sections 942 to 993 a fact the Act leaves to another source` @desc Are you an officer of the company who is "in default" (section 1121)?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`Under section 949(3), am I, as an officer of a company that committed the offence, also guilty of it` MEANS
    `s 949(3) the officer also commits the offence` (`Under sections 942 to 993 the fact as a yes, no or not known` `the company or other body corporate committed an offence under section 949`) (`Under sections 942 to 993 the fact as a yes, no or not known` `I am an officer of the company who is in default`)

-- s 951(1) and (3). Review by the Hearings Committee and appeal to the Takeover Appeal Board, as the Panel's rules provide.
@export Under section 951(1), may I have a Takeover Panel decision reviewed by the Hearings Committee?
GIVEN `I am affected by the decision` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are you a person affected by the Panel's decision?
      `the Panel's rules specify me as a person who may have the decision reviewed` IS A `Under sections 942 to 993 a fact the Act leaves to another source` @desc Do the Panel's rules specify you as a person who may have the decision reviewed by the Hearings Committee?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`Under section 951(1), may I have a Takeover Panel decision reviewed by the Hearings Committee` MEANS
    `s 951(1) the person may have the Panel's decision reviewed by the Hearings Committee` `I am affected by the decision` (`Under sections 942 to 993 the fact as a yes, no or not known` `the Panel's rules specify me as a person who may have the decision reviewed`)

@export Under section 951(3), may I appeal a Hearings Committee decision to the Takeover Appeal Board?
GIVEN `the decision is a decision of the Hearings Committee` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the decision one made by the Hearings Committee?
      `the Panel's rules give a right of appeal in these circumstances` IS A `Under sections 942 to 993 a fact the Act leaves to another source` @desc Do the Panel's rules give a right of appeal to the Takeover Appeal Board in these circumstances?
      `I meet the conditions the rules attach to the appeal` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Do you meet the conditions the rules attach to the right of appeal?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`Under section 951(3), may I appeal a Hearings Committee decision to the Takeover Appeal Board` MEANS
    `s 951(3) the person has a right of appeal to the Takeover Appeal Board` `the decision is a decision of the Hearings Committee` (`Under sections 942 to 993 the fact as a yes, no or not known` `the Panel's rules give a right of appeal in these circumstances`) `I meet the conditions the rules attach to the appeal`

-- s 952(1). The power to sanction a person for breach of the rules or failure to comply with a direction.
@export Under section 952(1), may the Takeover Panel impose a sanction on me?
GIVEN `the Panel's rules confer power to impose this sanction` IS A `Under sections 942 to 993 a fact the Act leaves to another source` @desc Do the Panel's rules confer on the Panel the power to impose this sanction?
      `I acted in breach of the rules` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did you act in breach of the Panel's rules?
      `I failed to comply with a direction the Panel gave under its rules` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did you fail to comply with a direction given by virtue of section 946?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`Under section 952(1), may the Takeover Panel impose a sanction on me` MEANS
    `s 952(1) the Panel may impose the sanction on the person` (`Under sections 942 to 993 the fact as a yes, no or not known` `the Panel's rules confer power to impose this sanction`) `I acted in breach of the rules` `I failed to comply with a direction the Panel gave under its rules`

-- s 953(2)-(3). The offence where an offer document does not comply with the offer document rules.
@export Under section 953(2) and (3), have I committed an offence over a bid's offer document?
GIVEN `a takeover bid is made for a company with voting securities on a UK regulated market` IS A `Under sections 942 to 993 a fact the Act leaves to another source` @desc Is a takeover bid (as paragraph 20(1) of Schedule 1C defines it) made for a company that has securities carrying voting rights admitted to trading on a regulated market in the United Kingdom?
      `the offer document does not comply with the offer document rules` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does the offer document published for the bid not comply with the offer document rules?
      `I am the person making the bid` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are you the person making the bid?
      `the person making the bid is a body of persons` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the person making the bid a body of persons (a company, partnership or other body)?
      `I am a director, officer or member of that body and caused the document to be published` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are you a director, officer or member of that body who caused the offer document to be published?
      `I knew it did not comply, or was reckless as to whether it did` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did you know that the offer document did not comply, or were you reckless as to whether it complied?
      `I failed to take all reasonable steps to secure that it did comply` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did you fail to take all reasonable steps to secure that the offer document did comply?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`Under section 953(2) and (3), have I committed an offence over a bid's offer document` MEANS
    `s 953(2)-(3) the person commits an offence in respect of the offer document` (`s 953(2) an offence is committed by the person` `the section applies` `the offer document does not comply with the offer document rules` `I am the person making the bid` `the person making the bid is a body of persons` `I am a director, officer or member of that body and caused the document to be published`) (`s 953(3) the person satisfies the conditions for committing the offence under subsection (2)` `I knew it did not comply, or was reckless as to whether it did` `I failed to take all reasonable steps to secure that it did comply`)
    WHERE
        `the section applies` MEANS
            `s 953(1) the section applies to the bid` (`Under sections 942 to 993 the fact as a yes, no or not known` `a takeover bid is made for a company with voting securities on a UK regulated market`) TRUE (`Under sections 942 to 993 the fact as a yes, no or not known` `a takeover bid is made for a company with voting securities on a UK regulated market`) TRUE

-- s 953(4). The offence where a response document does not comply, by a director or officer of the target.
@export Under section 953(4), have I, as a director or officer of the company bid for, committed an offence over its response document?
GIVEN `a takeover bid is made for a company with voting securities on a UK regulated market` IS A `Under sections 942 to 993 a fact the Act leaves to another source` @desc Is a takeover bid made for a company that has securities carrying voting rights admitted to trading on a regulated market in the United Kingdom?
      `the response document does not comply with the response document rules` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does the response document published for the bid not comply with the response document rules?
      `I am a director or other officer of that company` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are you a director or other officer of the company for which the bid is made?
      `I knew it did not comply, or was reckless as to whether it did` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did you know that the response document did not comply, or were you reckless as to whether it complied?
      `I failed to take all reasonable steps to secure that it did comply` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did you fail to take all reasonable steps to secure that the response document did comply?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`Under section 953(4), have I, as a director or officer of the company bid for, committed an offence over its response document` MEANS
    `s 953(4) an offence is committed by the person` (`s 953(1) the section applies to the bid` (`Under sections 942 to 993 the fact as a yes, no or not known` `a takeover bid is made for a company with voting securities on a UK regulated market`) TRUE (`Under sections 942 to 993 the fact as a yes, no or not known` `a takeover bid is made for a company with voting securities on a UK regulated market`) TRUE) `the response document does not comply with the response document rules` `I am a director or other officer of that company` `I knew it did not comply, or was reckless as to whether it did` `I failed to take all reasonable steps to secure that it did comply`

-- s 953(6). The penalty for the bid-documentation offence.
@export Under section 953(6), what penalty may I face for an offence over a bid's offer or response document?
GIVEN `how I would be convicted` IS A `Mode of conviction` @desc How would you be convicted: on conviction on indictment, or on summary conviction? (There is no difference by place.)
GIVETH A MAYBE Penalty
`Under section 953(6), what penalty may I face for an offence over a bid's offer or response document` MEANS
    `s 953(6) the penalty` `how I would be convicted`

-- s 954(1). The power to order compensation.
@export Under section 954(1), may the Takeover Panel order me to pay compensation?
GIVEN `the Panel's rules confer power to order compensation` IS A `Under sections 942 to 993 a fact the Act leaves to another source` @desc Do the Panel's rules confer on the Panel the power to order a person to pay compensation?
      `I am in breach of a rule the effect of which is to require the payment of money` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are you in breach of a rule the effect of which is to require the payment of money?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`Under section 954(1), may the Takeover Panel order me to pay compensation` MEANS
    `s 954(1) the Panel may order the person to pay compensation` (`Under sections 942 to 993 the fact as a yes, no or not known` `the Panel's rules confer power to order compensation`) `I am in breach of a rule the effect of which is to require the payment of money`

-- s 955(3). No person other than the Panel has a right to seek an injunction to prevent a contravention of the rules.
@export Under section 955(3), may I seek an injunction or interdict to stop someone contravening the Takeover Panel's rules?
GIVEN `I would be seeking it on the Panel's application under section 955(1)` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the remedy sought on the Panel's application under section 955(1)?
      `I would be seeking it to prevent a contravention of a rule-based requirement or a disclosure requirement` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Would you be seeking an injunction (in Scotland, an interdict or an order for specific performance) to prevent a person contravening, or continuing to contravene, a requirement imposed by or under the Panel's rules or by a Panel notice under section 947?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`Under section 955(3), may I seek an injunction or interdict to stop someone contravening the Takeover Panel's rules` MEANS
    `s 955(3) the person has a right to seek the remedy` `I would be seeking it on the Panel's application under section 955(1)` `I would be seeking it to prevent a contravention of a rule-based requirement or a disclosure requirement`

-- s 956(1) and (2). No action for breach of statutory duty, and no transaction void.
@export Under section 956(1), can I sue for breach of statutory duty because someone contravened a Takeover Panel rule or notice?
GIVEN `the contravention is of a requirement imposed by or under the Panel's rules, or by a Panel notice under section 947` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the contravention one of a requirement imposed by or under the Panel's rules, or of a requirement imposed by a Panel notice under section 947?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`Under section 956(1), can I sue for breach of statutory duty because someone contravened a Takeover Panel rule or notice` MEANS
    `s 956(1) the contravention gives rise to a right of action for breach of statutory duty` `the contravention is of a requirement imposed by or under the Panel's rules, or by a Panel notice under section 947`

@export Under section 956(2), is a transaction void or unenforceable because a Takeover Panel rule was contravened?
GIVEN `the contravention is of a requirement imposed by or under the Panel's rules` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the contravention one of a requirement imposed by or under the Panel's rules?
      `the thing in question is a transaction` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the thing whose validity is in question a transaction (rather than some other thing)?
      `the Panel's rules make provision about the validity of the thing` IS A `Under sections 942 to 993 a fact the Act leaves to another source` @desc Do the Panel's rules make provision about the validity of the thing?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`Under section 956(2), is a transaction void or unenforceable because a Takeover Panel rule was contravened` MEANS
    `s 956(2) the contravention makes the thing void or unenforceable or affects its validity` `the contravention is of a requirement imposed by or under the Panel's rules` `the thing in question is a transaction` (`Under sections 942 to 993 the fact as a yes, no or not known` `the Panel's rules make provision about the validity of the thing`)

-- s 959. Fees, charges and levy payable to the Panel are a debt.
@export Under section 959, is an amount I am asked to pay the Takeover Panel as a fee, charge or levy a debt I owe to it?
GIVEN `the amount is a fee or charge payable under rules the Panel made under section 957` IS A `Under sections 942 to 993 a fact the Act leaves to another source` @desc Is the amount a fee or charge that the Panel's rules (made under section 957) make payable to the Panel?
      `the amount is a levy payable under regulations made under section 958` IS A `Under sections 942 to 993 a fact the Act leaves to another source` @desc Is the amount a levy that regulations made under section 958 make payable to the Panel?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`Under section 959, is an amount I am asked to pay the Takeover Panel as a fee, charge or levy a debt I owe to it` MEANS
    `s 959 the amount is a debt due to the Panel` (`s 957(1) the fee or charge is payable to the Panel` (`Under sections 942 to 993 the fact as a yes, no or not known` `the amount is a fee or charge payable under rules the Panel made under section 957`)) (`Under sections 942 to 993 the fact as a yes, no or not known` `the amount is a levy payable under regulations made under section 958`)

-- s 961. No liability in damages for the Panel or those acting for it.
@export Under section 961, can I claim damages from the Takeover Panel or its staff for what they did in discharging its functions?
GIVEN `the defendant is the Panel itself` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the person you would sue the Panel itself?
      `the defendant is, or is acting as, a member, officer or member of staff of the Panel, or a person authorised under section 947(5)` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the person you would sue (or is acting as) a member, officer or member of staff of the Panel, or a person authorised under section 947(5) to exercise its power to require documents or information?
      `the thing was done or omitted in discharging or purporting to discharge the Panel's functions` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Was it done, or left undone, in or in connection with the discharge or purported discharge of the Panel's functions?
      `it is shown to have been done in bad faith` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it shown that the act or omission was in bad faith?
      `I claim on the ground that it was unlawful under section 6(1) of the Human Rights Act 1998` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are you claiming damages on the ground that the act or omission was unlawful as a result of section 6(1) of the Human Rights Act 1998?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`Under section 961, can I claim damages from the Takeover Panel or its staff for what they did in discharging its functions` MEANS
    `s 961(1) the defendant is liable in damages` `the defendant is the Panel itself` (`s 961(2) the person is within the subsection` `the defendant is, or is acting as, a member, officer or member of staff of the Panel, or a person authorised under section 947(5)` FALSE) `the thing was done or omitted in discharging or purporting to discharge the Panel's functions` `it is shown to have been done in bad faith` `I claim on the ground that it was unlawful under section 6(1) of the Human Rights Act 1998`

-- s 962. A statement made to the Panel may not be used against the person in criminal proceedings (except for the perjury offences).
@export Under section 962, may what I told the Takeover Panel be used against me in criminal proceedings?
GIVEN `I made the statement in response to a Panel requirement under section 947(1)` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did you make the statement in response to a requirement made by the Panel under section 947(1)?
      `I made it in response to a court order under section 955 to secure compliance with such a requirement` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did you make it in response to an order of the court under section 955 to secure compliance with such a requirement?
      `the offence charged` IS A `s 962(2) offence` @desc Which offence are you charged with: an offence under section 5 of the Perjury Act 1911, section 44(2) of the Criminal Law (Consolidation) (Scotland) Act 1995, Article 10 of the Perjury (Northern Ireland) Order 1979, or any other offence?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`Under section 962, may what I told the Takeover Panel be used against me in criminal proceedings` MEANS
    `s 962(1) the statement may be used against the person in the criminal proceedings` `I made the statement in response to a Panel requirement under section 947(1)` `I made it in response to a court order under section 955 to secure compliance with such a requirement` `the offence charged`

§§ `Chapter 2: Impediments to takeovers (ss 966 to 973)`

-- s 966(1) to (4). May the company opt in by special resolution?
@export Under section 966(1), may my company opt in to Chapter 2 of Part 28 by special resolution?
GIVEN `my company has voting shares admitted to trading on a UK regulated market` IS A `Under sections 942 to 993 a fact the Act leaves to another source` @desc Does your company have voting shares admitted to trading on a UK regulated market (Article 2.1.13A of Regulation (EU) No. 600/2014)?
      `the articles restrict the transfer of shares` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Do your company's articles of association contain any restrictions on the transfer of shares?
      `the articles disapply those restrictions to transfers to the offeror during the offer period` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Do the articles provide that the restrictions do not apply to transfers to the offeror (or at his direction to another person) during the offer period?
      `the articles disapply them to transfers when the offeror holds 75% of the voting shares` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Do the articles provide that the restrictions do not apply to transfers to any person during the offer period when the offeror holds shares worth not less than 75% of all the voting shares?
      `the articles restrict voting rights at general meetings` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Do the articles contain any restrictions on rights to vote at a general meeting?
      `the articles disapply them at a meeting deciding on frustrating action` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Do the articles provide that those restrictions have no effect at a general meeting that decides whether to take any action that might frustrate the takeover bid?
      `the articles disapply them at a meeting when the offeror holds 75%` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Do the articles provide that they have no effect at a general meeting held when the offeror holds not less than 75% in value of all the voting shares?
      `the voting restrictions are compensated by specific pecuniary advantages` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are the voting restrictions compensated for by specific pecuniary advantages?
      `an article is incompatible with one vote per multiple-vote share at a frustrating-action meeting` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is any other provision of the articles incompatible with multiple-vote shares carrying only one vote each at a general meeting that decides whether to take frustrating action?
      `an article is incompatible with one vote per multiple-vote share at the first meeting after the offer period` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is any other provision of the articles incompatible with multiple-vote shares carrying only one vote each at the first general meeting after the offer period (held when the offeror holds 75% and called at his request under section 969)?
      `an article is incompatible with no extraordinary board-appointment rights during the offer period` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is any other provision of the articles incompatible with shareholders having no extraordinary rights to appoint or remove directors during the offer period when the offeror holds 75%?
      `a minister holds shares with special rights` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are shares conferring special rights in the company held by a minister, a nominee or person acting for a minister, or a company controlled by a minister?
      `special rights are exercisable by a minister under an enactment` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are any special rights in the company exercisable by or on behalf of a minister under any enactment?
      `the resolution is a special resolution` IS A `Under sections 942 to 993 a fact the Act leaves to another source` @desc Is the resolution a special resolution within section 283?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`Under section 966(1), may my company opt in to Chapter 2 of Part 28 by special resolution` MEANS
    `s 966(1) the company may opt in by the resolution` (`s 966(2) the first condition is met` TRUE (`Under sections 942 to 993 the fact as a yes, no or not known` `my company has voting shares admitted to trading on a UK regulated market`)) (`s 966(3) the second condition is met` `the articles restrict the transfer of shares` `the articles disapply those restrictions to transfers to the offeror during the offer period` `the articles disapply them to transfers when the offeror holds 75% of the voting shares`) (`s 966(3A) the third condition is met` `the articles restrict voting rights at general meetings` `the articles disapply them at a meeting deciding on frustrating action` `the articles disapply them at a meeting when the offeror holds 75%` `the voting restrictions are compensated by specific pecuniary advantages`) (`s 966(3B) the fourth condition is met` `an article is incompatible with one vote per multiple-vote share at a frustrating-action meeting` `an article is incompatible with one vote per multiple-vote share at the first meeting after the offer period` `an article is incompatible with no extraordinary board-appointment rights during the offer period`) (`s 966(4) the fifth condition is met` `a minister holds shares with special rights` FALSE FALSE `special rights are exercisable by a minister under an enactment`) (`Under sections 942 to 993 the fact as a yes, no or not known` `the resolution is a special resolution`)

-- s 966(5). May the company revoke the opting-in resolution?
@export Under section 966(5), may my company revoke its opting-in resolution by a further special resolution?
GIVEN `my company has passed an opting-in resolution` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has your company passed an opting-in resolution?
      `the further resolution is a special resolution` IS A `Under sections 942 to 993 a fact the Act leaves to another source` @desc Is the further resolution a special resolution within section 283?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`Under section 966(5), may my company revoke its opting-in resolution by a further special resolution` MEANS
    `s 966(5) the company may revoke the opting-in resolution by the further resolution` `my company has passed an opting-in resolution` (`Under sections 942 to 993 the fact as a yes, no or not known` `the further resolution is a special resolution`)

-- s 967(2) and (6). The permitted effective dates.
@export Under section 967(2), is the effective date I put in my company's opting-in resolution allowed?
GIVEN `the effective date` IS A DATE @desc What effective date does the opting-in resolution specify?
      `the date the resolution is passed` IS A DATE @desc On what date is the resolution passed?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`Under section 967(2), is the effective date I put in my company's opting-in resolution allowed` MEANS
    `s 967(2) the effective date of the opting-in resolution is permitted` `the effective date` `the date the resolution is passed`

@export Under section 967(6), is the effective date I put in my company's opting-out resolution allowed?
GIVEN `the effective date of the opting-out resolution` IS A DATE @desc What effective date does the opting-out resolution specify?
      `the date a copy of the opting-in resolution was forwarded to the registrar` IS A DATE @desc On what date was a copy of the opting-in resolution forwarded to the registrar?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`Under section 967(6), is the effective date I put in my company's opting-out resolution allowed` MEANS
    `s 967(6) the effective date of the opting-out resolution is permitted` `the effective date of the opting-out resolution` `the date a copy of the opting-in resolution was forwarded to the registrar`

-- s 967(7). An alteration of the articles that would prevent a condition is of no effect until an opting-out resolution takes effect.
@export Under section 967(7), is my company's alteration of its articles still of no effect?
GIVEN `my company has passed an opting-in resolution` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has your company passed an opting-in resolution?
      `the alteration would prevent the second, third or fourth condition from being met` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Would the alteration of the articles prevent the second, third or fourth condition in section 966 from being met?
      `my company has passed an opting-out resolution` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has your company passed an opting-out resolution?
      `the effective date of the opting-out resolution` IS A DATE @desc What is the effective date of the opting-out resolution? (Any date if there is none.)
      `the day` IS A DATE @desc On what day are you asking?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`Under section 967(7), is my company's alteration of its articles still of no effect` MEANS
    `s 967(7) the alteration of the articles is still of no effect` `my company has passed an opting-in resolution` `the alteration would prevent the second, third or fourth condition from being met` (IF `my company has passed an opting-out resolution` THEN JUST `the effective date of the opting-out resolution` ELSE NOTHING) `the day`

-- s 968(2). Is my shareholder agreement invalid in so far as it restricts transfers or voting during a bid?
@export Under section 968(2), is my agreement invalid in so far as it restricts transferring shares or voting during a takeover bid?
GIVEN `a takeover bid is made for my company` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is a takeover bid made for the company?
      `my company is an opted-in company` IS A `Under sections 942 to 993 a fact the Act leaves to another source` @desc Is the company an opted-in company (an opting-in resolution has effect and the first and fifth conditions in section 966 continue to be met)?
      `the agreement is between two shareholders` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the agreement between a person holding shares in the company and another such person?
      `the date the agreement was entered into` IS A DATE @desc On what date was the agreement entered into?
      `the agreement is between a shareholder and the company` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the agreement between a shareholder and the company itself?
      `the restriction` IS A `s 968(2) restriction` @desc What does the agreement restrict: (a) transfer to the offeror during the offer period, (b) transfer to anyone when the offeror holds 75%, (c) voting at a meeting deciding on frustrating action, (d) voting at the first meeting after the offer period when the offeror holds 75%, or something else?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`Under section 968(2), is my agreement invalid in so far as it restricts transferring shares or voting during a takeover bid` MEANS
    `s 968(2) the agreement is invalid so far as it places the restriction` (`s 968(1) the provisions have effect` `a takeover bid is made for my company` (`Under sections 942 to 993 the fact as a yes, no or not known` `my company is an opted-in company`)) (`s 968(3) the section applies to the agreement` `the agreement is between two shareholders` `the date the agreement was entered into` `the agreement is between a shareholder and the company` TRUE) `the restriction`

-- s 968(6). Compensation for loss from an act that would, but for section 968, breach the agreement.
@export Under section 968(6), what compensation may I claim for loss from an act that would, but for section 968, breach an agreement?
GIVEN `I suffered loss from an act or omission that would but for section 968 breach the agreement` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did you suffer loss as a result of an act or omission that would (but for section 968) be a breach of an agreement to which that section applies?
      `the other person would but for section 968 be liable to me for the breach` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Would the person you claim against be liable to you, but for section 968, for committing or inducing the breach?
      `the amount the court considers just and equitable` IS A NUMBER @desc What amount does the court consider just and equitable, in pounds? (The Act leaves the amount to the court.)
GIVETH A MAYBE NUMBER
`Under section 968(6), what compensation may I claim for loss from an act that would, but for section 968, breach an agreement` MEANS
    `s 968(6) the compensation the person is entitled to` `I suffered loss from an act or omission that would but for section 968 breach the agreement` `the other person would but for section 968 be liable to me for the breach` `the amount the court considers just and equitable`

-- s 969(1). May the offeror require the directors to call a general meeting?
@export Under section 969(1), may the offeror require the directors of the company bid for to call a general meeting?
GIVEN `a takeover bid is made for my company` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is a takeover bid made for the company?
      `my company is an opted-in company` IS A `Under sections 942 to 993 a fact the Act leaves to another source` @desc Is the company an opted-in company?
      `the value of the shares the offeror holds when the request is made` IS A NUMBER @desc What is the value of the voting shares the offeror holds on the date the request is made? (Leave out debentures and shares that do not normally carry votes.)
      `the value of all the voting shares in the company` IS A NUMBER @desc What is the value of all the voting shares in the company? (Same units.)
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`Under section 969(1), may the offeror require the directors of the company bid for to call a general meeting` MEANS
    `s 969(1) the offeror may require the directors to call a general meeting` (`s 968(1) the provisions have effect` `a takeover bid is made for my company` (`Under sections 942 to 993 the fact as a yes, no or not known` `my company is an opted-in company`)) `the value of the shares the offeror holds when the request is made` `the value of all the voting shares in the company`

-- s 970. Notifying the Panel of an opting-in or opting-out resolution, in time; the offence and its penalty.
@export Under section 970(2), did my company notify the Takeover Panel of its opting-in or opting-out resolution in time?
GIVEN `the day the resolution was passed` IS A DATE @desc On what day was the opting-in or opting-out resolution passed?
      `the day the company notified the Panel` IS A DATE @desc On what day did the company notify the Panel?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`Under section 970(2), did my company notify the Takeover Panel of its opting-in or opting-out resolution in time` MEANS
    `s 970(2) the notification was given in time` `the day the resolution was passed` `the day the company notified the Panel`

@export Under section 970(2), by what day must my company notify the Takeover Panel of its opting-in or opting-out resolution?
GIVEN `the day the resolution was passed` IS A DATE @desc On what day was the opting-in or opting-out resolution passed?
GIVETH A DATE
`Under section 970(2), by what day must my company notify the Takeover Panel of its opting-in or opting-out resolution` MEANS
    `s 970(2) the last day for giving notification` `the day the resolution was passed`

@export Under section 970(3), am I, as an officer of the company, guilty of an offence because it did not notify the Takeover Panel?
GIVEN `the company failed to notify the Panel as section 970 requires` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did the company fail to comply with section 970 (notifying the Panel within 15 days after the resolution is passed)?
      `I am an officer of the company who is in default` IS A `Under sections 942 to 993 a fact the Act leaves to another source` @desc Are you an officer of the company who is "in default" (section 1121)?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`Under section 970(3), am I, as an officer of the company, guilty of an offence because it did not notify the Takeover Panel` MEANS
    `s 970(3) an offence is committed by` `the company failed to notify the Panel as section 970 requires` `s 970(3)(b) an officer of the company` (`Under sections 942 to 993 the fact as a yes, no or not known` `I am an officer of the company who is in default`)

@export Under section 970(4), what penalty may my company or I face for not notifying the Takeover Panel?
GIVEN `how I would be convicted` IS A `Mode of conviction` @desc How would you be convicted: on summary conviction (in England and Wales, in Scotland, or in Northern Ireland), or on indictment?
GIVETH A MAYBE Penalty
`Under section 970(4), what penalty may my company or I face for not notifying the Takeover Panel` MEANS
    `s 970(4) the penalty` `how I would be convicted`

-- s 972(3). 14 days' notice for a special resolution at the first meeting after the offer period.
@export Under section 972(3), how many days' notice does a special resolution need at the first meeting after the offer period?
GIVEN `a takeover bid is made for my company` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is a takeover bid made for the company?
      `my company is an opted-in company` IS A `Under sections 942 to 993 a fact the Act leaves to another source` @desc Is the company an opted-in company?
      `sections 368 and 378 of the Companies Act 1985 have been repealed by this Act` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Have sections 368 and 378 of the Companies Act 1985 been repealed by this Act? (The section applies only until their repeal.)
      `the meeting is the first general meeting after the end of the offer period` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the meeting the first general meeting of the company held after the end of the offer period?
      `the value of the voting shares the offeror holds when the meeting is held` IS A NUMBER @desc What is the value of the voting shares the offeror holds when the meeting is held?
      `the value of all the voting shares in the company` IS A NUMBER @desc What is the value of all the voting shares in the company? (Same units.)
GIVETH A MAYBE NUMBER
`Under section 972(3), how many days' notice does a special resolution need at the first meeting after the offer period` MEANS
    `s 972(3) the days' notice for a special resolution` (`s 972(1) the 1985 Act provisions have effect as the section provides` (`s 968(1) the provisions have effect` `a takeover bid is made for my company` (`Under sections 942 to 993 the fact as a yes, no or not known` `my company is an opted-in company`)) `sections 368 and 378 of the Companies Act 1985 have been repealed by this Act`) `the meeting is the first general meeting after the end of the offer period` `the value of the voting shares the offeror holds when the meeting is held` `the value of all the voting shares in the company`

§§ `Chapter 3: "Squeeze-out" and "Sell-out" (ss 974 to 991)`

-- s 974. Is the offer a takeover offer?
@export Under section 974, is the offer made for my company's shares a takeover offer?
GIVEN `the offer is to acquire all the shares, other than those the offeror already holds` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the offer to acquire all the shares in the company, other than shares already held by the offeror (including shares he has contracted to acquire)?
      `there is more than one class of shares` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is there more than one class of shares in the company?
      `the offer is to acquire all the shares of one or more classes` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the offer to acquire all the shares of one or more classes, other than shares already held by the offeror?
      `the terms are the same for all the shares the offer relates to` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are the terms of the offer the same for all the shares to which it relates?
      `the offer relates to shares of different classes` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does the offer relate to shares of different classes?
      `the terms are the same for all the shares of each class` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Where it relates to different classes, are the terms the same for all the shares of each class?
      `a later-allotted dividend explains a difference in the consideration` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is a difference in the consideration offered merely a reflection of a difference in dividend entitlement between shares allotted earlier and later (section 976(2))?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`Under section 974, is the offer made for my company's shares a takeover offer` MEANS
    `s 974(1) the offer is a takeover offer` (`s 974(2) the first condition is satisfied` `the offer is to acquire all the shares, other than those the offeror already holds` `there is more than one class of shares` `the offer is to acquire all the shares of one or more classes` (JUST FALSE)) (`s 974(3) the second condition is satisfied` `the terms are the same for all the shares the offer relates to` `the offer relates to shares of different classes` `the terms are the same for all the shares of each class` (`s 976(1) the condition in section 974(3) is treated as satisfied` (`s 976(2) the subsection applies` `a later-allotted dividend explains a difference in the consideration` `a later-allotted dividend explains a difference in the consideration` `a later-allotted dividend explains a difference in the consideration` `a later-allotted dividend explains a difference in the consideration`) (JUST FALSE)))

-- s 979(2). May the offeror give me, a minority shareholder, notice that he desires to acquire my shares?
@export Under section 979(2), may the offeror give me notice that he desires to acquire my shares?
GIVEN `the offer relates to shares of different classes` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does the takeover offer relate to shares of different classes?
      `the value of the shares the offer relates to` IS A NUMBER @desc What is the value of all the shares to which the offer relates, counting only those the offeror has not excluded (leave out shares the offeror, or an associate of his, acquired other than by acceptances unless section 979(8) or (9) applies)?
      `the value of those the offeror has acquired by acceptances` IS A NUMBER @desc What is the value of the shares the offeror has acquired, or unconditionally contracted to acquire, by virtue of acceptances of the offer?
      `the shares are voting shares` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are the shares to which the offer relates voting shares?
      `the voting rights the shares carry` IS A NUMBER @desc How many voting rights do the shares to which the offer relates carry?
      `the voting rights carried by those acquired by acceptances` IS A NUMBER @desc How many voting rights do the shares the offeror has acquired by acceptances carry?
      `the offeror holds shares contracted for subject to conditions` IS A NUMBER @desc What is the value of shares the offeror, or an associate of his, has contracted to acquire subject to conditions that has not yet become unconditional? (0 if none.)
      `my shares are among those the offeror has not acquired` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are your shares shares to which the offer relates that the offeror has not acquired or unconditionally contracted to acquire?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`Under section 979(2), may the offeror give me notice that he desires to acquire my shares` MEANS
    `s 979(2) the offeror may give notice to the holder of the shares` (`s 979(1) subsection (2) applies` `the offer relates to shares of different classes`) `the blocks` (Date 1 1 2100) `the shares are voting shares` `my shares are among those the offeror has not acquired`
    WHERE
        -- Placeholder: the date on which the entitlement is determined only matters for a block with an allotment date, and none is given here.
        `the blocks` MEANS LIST
            `s 979 block of shares` OF "ordinary", `the value of those the offeror has acquired by acceptances`, `the voting rights carried by those acquired by acceptances`, NOTHING, `s 979 acquired or unconditionally contracted to be acquired by virtue of acceptances of the offer`, FALSE
            `s 979 block of shares` OF "ordinary", (`the value of the shares the offer relates to` MINUS `the value of those the offeror has acquired by acceptances`), (`the voting rights the shares carry` MINUS `the voting rights carried by those acquired by acceptances`), NOTHING, `s 979 not acquired or contracted to be acquired`, FALSE
            `s 979 block of shares` OF "ordinary", `the offeror holds shares contracted for subject to conditions`, `the offeror holds shares contracted for subject to conditions`, NOTHING, `s 979 contracted to be acquired subject to conditions, not yet unconditional`, FALSE

-- s 980(2). By when may the offeror give the notice?
@export Under section 980(2), what is the last day on which the offeror may give me a squeeze-out notice?
GIVEN `the last day on which the offer can be accepted` IS A DATE @desc What is the last day on which the offer can be accepted?
      `the date of the offer` IS A DATE @desc What is the date of the offer (the date of publication, or when notices were first given)?
      `the time for acceptance is governed by the Panel's rules made under paragraph 13 or 14 of Schedule 1C` IS A `Under sections 942 to 993 a fact the Act leaves to another source` @desc Is the time allowed for acceptance of the offer governed by rules under section 943(1) made in accordance with paragraph 13 or 14 of Schedule 1C?
GIVETH A MAYBE DATE
`Under section 980(2), what is the last day on which the offeror may give me a squeeze-out notice` MEANS
    `s 980(2) the last day on which a notice may be given` `the last day on which the offer can be accepted` `the date of the offer` (`s 980(3) this subsection applies to the offer` (`Under sections 942 to 993 the fact as a yes, no or not known` `the time for acceptance is governed by the Panel's rules made under paragraph 13 or 14 of Schedule 1C`))

@export Under section 980(2), was the squeeze-out notice I received given in time?
GIVEN `the last day on which the offer can be accepted` IS A DATE @desc What is the last day on which the offer can be accepted?
      `the date of the offer` IS A DATE @desc What is the date of the offer?
      `the time for acceptance is governed by the Panel's rules made under paragraph 13 or 14 of Schedule 1C` IS A `Under sections 942 to 993 a fact the Act leaves to another source` @desc Is the time allowed for acceptance of the offer governed by rules under section 943(1) made in accordance with paragraph 13 or 14 of Schedule 1C?
      `the day the notice was given` IS A DATE @desc On what day was the notice given to you?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`Under section 980(2), was the squeeze-out notice I received given in time` MEANS
    `s 980(2) the notice is given in time` `the day the notice was given` (`s 980(2) the last day on which a notice may be given` `the last day on which the offer can be accepted` `the date of the offer` (`s 980(3) this subsection applies to the offer` (`Under sections 942 to 993 the fact as a yes, no or not known` `the time for acceptance is governed by the Panel's rules made under paragraph 13 or 14 of Schedule 1C`)))

-- s 980(6) and (7). The offeror's offence over the copy of the notice or the statutory declaration, and the defence.
@export Under section 980(6), have I, as an offeror, committed an offence over the squeeze-out notice or its statutory declaration?
GIVEN `I failed to send the company a copy of the notice or the statutory declaration as required` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did you fail to send the company a copy of the notice, or a statutory declaration in the prescribed form, at the time you first gave a notice under section 979?
      `I made the declaration knowing it to be false` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did you make the statutory declaration knowing it to be false?
      `I made the declaration without reasonable grounds for believing it true` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did you make the statutory declaration without having reasonable grounds for believing it to be true?
      `I am charged with failing to send a copy of a notice` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the charge one of failing to send a copy of a notice (rather than a missing or false declaration)?
      `I can prove that I took reasonable steps to secure compliance` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Can you prove that you took reasonable steps for securing compliance with section 980(4)?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`Under section 980(6), have I, as an offeror, committed an offence over the squeeze-out notice or its statutory declaration` MEANS
    `s 980(6)-(7) the person is guilty of the offence` (`s 980(6) the person commits an offence` `I failed to send the company a copy of the notice or the statutory declaration as required` `I made the declaration knowing it to be false` `I made the declaration without reasonable grounds for believing it true`) (`s 980(7) the section gives the person a defence` `I am charged with failing to send a copy of a notice` `I can prove that I took reasonable steps to secure compliance`)

-- s 981(3), (6). The six weeks after a squeeze-out notice.
@export Under section 981(3), by what day may I indicate my choice of consideration after a squeeze-out notice?
GIVEN `the date of the notice` IS A DATE @desc On what date was the squeeze-out notice dated?
GIVETH A DATE
`Under section 981(3), by what day may I indicate my choice of consideration after a squeeze-out notice` MEANS
    `s 981(3)(a) the last day for the shareholder to indicate his choice` `the date of the notice`

@export Under section 981(6), has the day come on which the offeror must send the company a copy of the notice and pay for my shares?
GIVEN `the date of the notice` IS A DATE @desc On what date was the squeeze-out notice dated?
      `the day` IS A DATE @desc On what day are you asking?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`Under section 981(6), has the day come on which the offeror must send the company a copy of the notice and pay for my shares` MEANS
    `s 981(6) the offeror's duty has arisen` `the date of the notice` `the day`

-- s 983. May I, a minority shareholder, require the offeror to buy my shares?
@export Under section 983(2), may I, a holder of voting shares who has not accepted the offer, require the offeror to buy my shares?
GIVEN `the offer is to acquire all the shares in the company` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the takeover offer an offer to acquire all the shares in the company (within the meaning of section 974)?
      `I have not accepted the offer` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Have you not accepted the offer?
      `the offeror holds some but not all the shares through acceptances` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has the offeror, by virtue of acceptances, acquired or unconditionally contracted to acquire some (but not all) of the shares to which the offer relates?
      `the day` IS A DATE @desc On what day do you require the offeror to acquire your shares?
      `the last day on which the offer can be accepted` IS A DATE @desc What is the last day on which the offer can be accepted?
      `the value of all the voting shares in the company` IS A NUMBER @desc What is the value of all the voting shares in the company?
      `the voting rights in the company` IS A NUMBER @desc How many voting rights does the company have?
      `the value acquired by acceptances` IS A NUMBER @desc What is the value of the shares the offeror has acquired, or unconditionally contracted to acquire, by virtue of acceptances?
      `the voting rights acquired by acceptances` IS A NUMBER @desc How many voting rights do those shares carry?
      `the value of other shares the offeror and his associates hold` IS A NUMBER @desc What is the value of any other shares in the company that the offeror, or an associate of his, has acquired or contracted to acquire (unconditionally or subject to conditions)?
      `the voting rights of those other shares` IS A NUMBER @desc How many voting rights do those other shares carry?
      `the value of treasury shares the company holds` IS A NUMBER @desc What is the value of the shares the company holds as treasury shares?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`Under section 983(2), may I, a holder of voting shares who has not accepted the offer, require the offeror to buy my shares` MEANS
    `s 983(2) the holder of voting shares may require the offeror to acquire them` (`s 983(1) subsections (2) and (3) apply` `the offer is to acquire all the shares in the company`) `I have not accepted the offer` `the offeror holds some but not all the shares through acceptances` `the day` `the last day on which the offer can be accepted` `the holdings` `the holdings`
    WHERE
        -- the same holdings are used with and without debentures treated as shares by section 990(1): the person is asked about voting shares only
        `the holdings` MEANS `s 983 holdings` OF `the value of all the voting shares in the company`, `the voting rights in the company`, `the value acquired by acceptances`, `the voting rights acquired by acceptances`, `the value of other shares the offeror and his associates hold`, `the voting rights of those other shares`, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, `the value of treasury shares the company holds`

-- s 984(2) and (3). The deadlines for the shareholder and for the offeror.
@export Under section 984(2), by what day must I exercise my right to require the offeror to buy my shares?
GIVEN `the last day on which the offer can be accepted` IS A DATE @desc What is the last day on which the offer can be accepted?
      `I have been sent the offeror's notice of my rights` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has the offeror sent you the notice of your rights that section 984(3) requires?
      `the date of that notice` IS A DATE @desc On what date was that notice given? (Any date if none has been given.)
GIVETH A DATE
`Under section 984(2), by what day must I exercise my right to require the offeror to buy my shares` MEANS
    `s 984(2) the last day on which the rights may be exercised` `the last day on which the offer can be accepted` (IF `I have been sent the offeror's notice of my rights` THEN JUST `the date of that notice` ELSE NOTHING)

@export Under section 984(3), by what day must the offeror give me notice of my right to be bought out?
GIVEN `the end of the period within which the offer can be accepted` IS A DATE @desc On what day does the period within which the offer can be accepted end?
GIVETH A DATE
`Under section 984(3), by what day must the offeror give me notice of my right to be bought out` MEANS
    `s 984(3) the last day for giving the notice` `the end of the period within which the offer can be accepted`

-- s 986(2). The six weeks to apply to the court against a squeeze-out notice.
@export Under section 986(2), am I still in time to apply to the court against the squeeze-out notice I was given?
GIVEN `the date on which the notice was given to me` IS A DATE @desc On what date was the squeeze-out notice given to you?
      `the day I apply` IS A DATE @desc On what day do you apply, or would you apply, to the court?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`Under section 986(2), am I still in time to apply to the court against the squeeze-out notice I was given` MEANS
    `s 986(2) the application is made in time` `the date on which the notice was given to me` `the day I apply`

-- s 988. Is a person an associate of the offeror?
@export Under section 988, is this person an associate of the offeror?
GIVEN `the person is a nominee of the offeror` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the person a nominee of the offeror?
      `the person is a holding company, subsidiary or fellow subsidiary of the offeror` IS A `Under sections 942 to 993 a fact the Act leaves to another source` @desc Is the person a holding company, subsidiary or fellow subsidiary of the offeror (section 1159)?
      `the person is a nominee of such a company` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the person a nominee of such a holding company, subsidiary or fellow subsidiary?
      `the person is accustomed to act on the offeror's directions` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the person a body corporate that, or whose directors, are accustomed to act in accordance with the offeror's directions or instructions?
      `the offeror controls this share of the person's voting power` IS A NUMBER @desc How much of the voting power at general meetings of the person (a body corporate) is the offeror entitled to exercise or control (counting as section 823(2) and (3) provide)? Use any units.
      `the total voting power of the person` IS A NUMBER @desc What is the total voting power at general meetings of the person (same units)? (0 if the person is not a body corporate.)
      `the person is a party to a share acquisition agreement with the offeror` IS A `Under sections 942 to 993 a fact the Act leaves to another source` @desc Is the person (or is the person a nominee of) a party to a share acquisition agreement with the offeror (an agreement for the acquisition of shares to which the offer relates, with obligations or restrictions on using, keeping or disposing of them, other than an excluded agreement)?
      `the offeror is an individual` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the offeror an individual?
      `the person is the offeror's spouse, civil partner or minor child or step-child` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the person the offeror's spouse or civil partner, or his minor child or step-child?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`Under section 988, is this person an associate of the offeror` MEANS
    `s 988(1) the person is an associate of the offeror` `the person is a nominee of the offeror` (`Under sections 942 to 993 the fact as a yes, no or not known` `the person is a holding company, subsidiary or fellow subsidiary of the offeror`) `the person is a nominee of such a company` (`s 988(3) the offeror has a substantial interest in the body corporate` `the person is accustomed to act on the offeror's directions` `the offeror controls this share of the person's voting power` `the total voting power of the person`) (`Under sections 942 to 993 the fact as a yes, no or not known` `the person is a party to a share acquisition agreement with the offeror`) `the offeror is an individual` `the person is the offeror's spouse, civil partner or minor child or step-child`

-- s 990(1). Debentures carrying voting rights are treated as shares in a company with listed voting shares or debentures.
@export Under section 990(1), are my company's debentures treated as shares for the purposes of Chapter 3?
GIVEN `my company's voting shares or voting debentures are admitted to trading on a regulated market` IS A `Under sections 942 to 993 a fact the Act leaves to another source` @desc Does your company have voting shares, or debentures carrying voting rights, admitted to trading on a regulated market (Article 2.1.13 of Regulation (EU) No. 600/2014)?
      `the debentures carry voting rights` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Do the debentures carry voting rights?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`Under section 990(1), are my company's debentures treated as shares for the purposes of Chapter 3` MEANS
    `s 990(1) the debentures are treated as shares in the company` (`s 990(2) the company is one to which the subsection applies` (`Under sections 942 to 993 the fact as a yes, no or not known` `my company's voting shares or voting debentures are admitted to trading on a regulated market`)) `the debentures carry voting rights`

§§ `Chapter 4 and Part 29: the directors' report (s 992) and fraudulent trading (s 993)`

-- s 992 (Schedule 7 paragraph 13 to the 1985 Act as inserted). What the directors' report of a listed company must contain.
@export Under section 992(2), must the directors' report of my company contain detailed information on this matter?
GIVEN `the first day of the financial year` IS A DATE @desc On what date did the financial year begin?
      `at the end of the year my company had voting securities admitted to trading on a regulated market` IS A `Under sections 942 to 993 a fact the Act leaves to another source` @desc At the end of the financial year, did your company have securities carrying voting rights admitted to trading on a regulated market?
      `the matter` IS A `s 992(2) para 13(2) matter` @desc Which matter are you asking about: (a) the structure of the capital, (b) restrictions on transfer, (c) significant holdings, (d) special control rights, (e) employees' share scheme control rights, (f) voting restrictions, (g) agreements between holders, (h) rules on directors and articles, (i) directors' powers, (j) change-of-control agreements, (k) compensation for loss of office on a takeover?
      `the person has a significant direct or indirect holding` IS A BOOLEAN @desc For paragraph (c): does the person have a significant direct or indirect holding of securities in the company?
      `the person holds securities with special control rights` IS A BOOLEAN @desc For paragraph (d): does the person hold securities carrying special rights with regard to control of the company?
      `the company has an employees' share scheme` IS A `Under sections 942 to 993 a fact the Act leaves to another source` @desc For paragraph (e): does the company have an employees' share scheme (section 1166)?
      `the scheme's shares have control rights not exercisable directly by the employees` IS A BOOLEAN @desc For paragraph (e): do shares to which the scheme relates have rights with regard to control of the company that are not exercisable directly by the employees?
      `disclosing the agreement would be seriously prejudicial to the company` IS A BOOLEAN @desc For paragraph (j): would disclosing the agreement be seriously prejudicial to the company?
      `the company is not under any other obligation to disclose it` IS A BOOLEAN @desc For paragraph (j): is the company not under any other obligation to disclose the agreement?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`Under section 992(2), must the directors' report of my company contain detailed information on this matter` MEANS
    `s 992(2) para 13(2) the report must contain detailed information on the matter` (`s 992(2) para 13(1) this Part of Schedule 7 applies to the directors' report` (`Under sections 942 to 993 the fact as a yes, no or not known` `at the end of the year my company had voting securities admitted to trading on a regulated market`)) `the matter` `the person has a significant direct or indirect holding` `the person holds securities with special control rights` (`Under sections 942 to 993 the fact as a yes, no or not known` `the company has an employees' share scheme`) `the scheme's shares have control rights not exercisable directly by the employees` `disclosing the agreement would be seriously prejudicial to the company` `the company is not under any other obligation to disclose it`

@export Under section 992(6), do the section 992 amendments apply to my company's directors' report?
GIVEN `the first day of the financial year` IS A DATE @desc On what date did the financial year to which the directors' report relates begin?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`Under section 992(6), do the section 992 amendments apply to my company's directors' report` MEANS
    `s 992(6) the amendments apply to the directors' report` `the first day of the financial year`

-- s 993. Fraudulent trading.
@export Under section 993(1), have I committed the offence of fraudulent trading?
GIVEN `a business of a company was carried on` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Was any business of a company carried on?
      `with intent to defraud the company's creditors` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Was it carried on with intent to defraud creditors of the company?
      `with intent to defraud another person's creditors` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Was it carried on with intent to defraud creditors of any other person?
      `for another fraudulent purpose` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Was it carried on for any fraudulent purpose?
      `I was knowingly a party to carrying it on in that way` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Were you knowingly a party to the carrying on of the business in that manner?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`Under section 993(1), have I committed the offence of fraudulent trading` MEANS
    `s 993(1) the person commits an offence` `a business of a company was carried on` `with intent to defraud the company's creditors` `with intent to defraud another person's creditors` `for another fraudulent purpose` `I was knowingly a party to carrying it on in that way`

@export Under section 993(3), what penalty may I face if I am convicted of fraudulent trading?
GIVEN `how I would be convicted` IS A `Mode of conviction` @desc How would you be convicted: on conviction on indictment, or on summary conviction in England and Wales, in Scotland or in Northern Ireland?
GIVETH A MAYBE Penalty
`Under section 993(3), what penalty may I face if I am convicted of fraudulent trading` MEANS
    `s 993(3) the penalty` `how I would be convicted`

-- ====================================================================================================
-- seat questions from part coa22 (merged by the lead on 2026-11-12; unchanged text follows)
-- ====================================================================================================
-- Companies Act 2006 (United Kingdom), ss 994 to 1043 (Parts 30 to 33) -- THE SEAT LAYER (layer 2).
--
-- SEAT: an individual who is, or is about to become, a director, a company secretary or a member (shareholder) of a
-- company registered under the Act, or who deals with one, asking on facts they can state what the Act requires or
-- lets them do, what rights they have against the company or its directors, what they must disclose, file, approve or
-- vote on and by when, and what follows (liability, offences, penalties) if it is not done.
-- (Assumed, not ruled: the Act is addressed to companies, so the individual is whoever stands in a company's management
-- or ownership.) There is never a seat for the registrar, the court, the Secretary of State or the Crown: where a provision
-- addresses only an official it is asked here for what it means to the person (what may be done to them, what they must
-- be given, by when).
--
-- This layer asks the questions the part-30-to-33 modules answer, in the order of the text. It restates no rule: every answer
-- is a call of a coa22-part*.l4 rule. Each question names the section it answers, begins "Under section N,", and takes plain
-- inputs, one per fact the person can state (yes/no, a number, a date, a choice from a list), each with an @desc worded as
-- that person would be asked. The modules' records, lists and seam inputs are built inside each question, in its WHERE, from
-- those answers. A fact a module's rule does not read is not asked.
--
-- WHAT AN ANSWER MEANS (the rule of 2026-10-29; see NOTES.md "Reading a result: FALSE and NOTHING").
--   JUST TRUE   the text says yes.            JUST FALSE   the text says no, in its own words.
--   NOTHING     the text does not say: not covered, never to be read as "no".
-- Answers other parts give (who is a member, who is an officer in default, what the registrar's Schedule 4 permits, whether
-- a name is the same as another) are asked here as plain facts and passed to the rules as JUST TRUE or JUST FALSE.
--
-- Pounds. A level on the standard scale and the statutory maximum are set outside the Act: where a question asks for an
-- amount of a fine, the person supplies what those stand for, and a later change would change the answer.
-- Where a group only arises in a situation the person may not be in (a petition, a striking-off application, a Crown
-- disclaimer, a restoration, a requirement to produce documents, registering a body formed outside the Companies Acts),
-- the group's heading says so ("only if ..."), so the form can first ask "Has this happened to you?".
-- The assumptions of this layer (seam statements, folded creditor kinds, defaults asked as plain facts, the event list of
-- s 1009, no seat for an inspector, penalties asked in pounds for ss 998 and 999 only) are S1 to S7 in the fork register of
-- NOTES.md.

§ `Companies Act 2006, Parts 30 to 33 -- the questions of a director, secretary, member or person dealing with a company`

§§ `Part 30: unfair prejudice (only if you are thinking of petitioning the court, or a petition or order is in play)`

-- s 994(1)-(3): a member (or a person to whom shares have passed by operation of law) petitions on either ground.
@export Under section 994(1), may I apply to the court by petition for an order under Part 30 on the ground of unfair prejudice?
GIVEN `I am a member of the company` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are you a member of the company?
      `shares in the company have been transferred or transmitted to me by operation of law` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Have shares in the company been transferred or transmitted to you by operation of law (for example on a death)?
      `the company is formed and registered under the Companies Act 2006` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the company one formed and registered under the Companies Act 2006 (or an earlier Companies Act, treated as formed under this one)?
      `the affairs are unfairly prejudicial to members generally` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are the company's affairs being, or have they been, conducted in a manner that is unfairly prejudicial to the interests of the members generally?
      `the affairs are unfairly prejudicial to some part of the members` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are the company's affairs being, or have they been, conducted in a manner that is unfairly prejudicial to the interests of some part of its members?
      `that part of the members includes me` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does that part of the members include you?
      `the auditor has been removed` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has the company's auditor been removed from office?
      `the auditor was removed over divergence of opinions` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Was the auditor removed on grounds of divergence of opinions on accounting treatments or audit procedures?
      `the auditor was removed on other improper grounds` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Was the auditor removed on any other improper grounds?
      `an act or omission is prejudicial` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is an actual or proposed act or omission of the company (including one on its behalf) unfairly prejudicial, or would it be, to the interests of members generally or of some part of its members?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 994(1), may I apply to the court by petition for an order under Part 30 on the ground of unfair prejudice` IS
    `s 994(1) the person may apply to the court by petition for an order under Part 30`
        (JUST `I am a member of the company`) -- the seam input for section 112 (who is a member): the person's own statement
        (`s 994(2) the person who is not a member is treated as a member for the purposes of Part 30` `shares in the company have been transferred or transmitted to me by operation of law`)
        (`s 994(3) the body is a company for the purposes of section 994` (JUST `the company is formed and registered under the Companies Act 2006`)) -- the seam input for section 1(1): the person's own statement
        (`s 994(1)(a) the ground of conduct of the company's affairs is made out` `the affairs are unfairly prejudicial to members generally` `the affairs are unfairly prejudicial to some part of the members` `that part of the members includes me`
            (`s 994(1A) the removal of the company's auditor is treated as unfairly prejudicial to some part of the members` `the auditor has been removed` `the auditor was removed over divergence of opinions` `the auditor was removed on other improper grounds`))
        (`s 994(1)(b) the ground of an actual or proposed act or omission of the company is made out` `an act or omission is prejudicial`)

-- s 995(2): the Secretary of State's petition about the person's company (an official's power, asked for what it means to the person).
@export Under section 995(2), may the Secretary of State apply to the court by petition for an order under Part 30 about my company?
GIVEN `a report under section 437 of the Companies Act 1985 has been received` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has the Secretary of State received an inspector's report on the company under section 437 of the Companies Act 1985?
      `powers under section 447 or 448 of the Companies Act 1985 have been used` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has the Secretary of State used his powers under section 447 or 448 of the Companies Act 1985 (to require documents and information, or to enter and search premises) in respect of the company?
      `Part 11 of the Financial Services and Markets Act 2000 powers have been used` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has the Secretary of State, the Financial Conduct Authority, the Prudential Regulation Authority or the Bank of England used its powers under Part 11 of the Financial Services and Markets Act 2000 (information gathering and investigations) in respect of the company?
      `an investigator's report has been received` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has the Secretary of State received a report from an investigator appointed under Part 11 of that Act?
      `the company is a body corporate` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the company a body corporate?
      `the company is liable to be wound up under the Insolvency Act 1986` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the company liable to be wound up under the Insolvency Act 1986 or the Insolvency (Northern Ireland) Order 1989?
      `it appears that the affairs are unfairly prejudicial` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does it appear to the Secretary of State that the company's affairs are being or have been conducted in a manner unfairly prejudicial to the interests of members generally or of some part of its members?
      `it appears that an act or omission is prejudicial` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does it appear to the Secretary of State that an actual or proposed act or omission of the company is or would be so prejudicial?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 995(2), may the Secretary of State apply to the court by petition for an order under Part 30 about my company` IS
    `s 995(2) the Secretary of State may apply to the court by petition for an order under Part 30`
        (`s 995(1) section 995 applies to the company` `a report under section 437 of the Companies Act 1985 has been received` `powers under section 447 or 448 of the Companies Act 1985 have been used` `Part 11 of the Financial Services and Markets Act 2000 powers have been used` `an investigator's report has been received`)
        (`s 995(4) the body is a company for the purposes of section 995` `the company is a body corporate` `the company is liable to be wound up under the Insolvency Act 1986`)
        `it appears that the affairs are unfairly prejudicial`
        `it appears that an act or omission is prejudicial`

-- s 996(1)-(2): what the court may order if it is satisfied that the petition is well founded.
@export Under section 996(2), may the court's order on a Part 30 petition contain a particular provision?
GIVEN `the court is satisfied that the petition is well founded` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the court satisfied that the petition under Part 30 is well founded?
      `the provision sought` IS A `s 996(2) kind of provision` @desc Which provision is sought: regulate the company's affairs in the future; require it to refrain from an act; require it to do an act it omitted; authorise civil proceedings in its name; restrict alterations to its articles; provide for a purchase of shares; or any other relief?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 996(2), may the court's order on a Part 30 petition contain a particular provision` IS
    `s 996(2) the court's order may contain the provision` (`s 996(1) the court may make such order as it thinks fit for giving relief in respect of the matters complained of` `the court is satisfied that the petition is well founded`) `the provision sought`

@export Under section 996(2)(e), where the order provides for the company itself to buy shares, does the order provide for the reduction of the company's capital accordingly?
GIVEN `the order provides for the purchase of shares by the company itself` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does the order provide for the company itself to purchase the shares of any of its members?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 996(2)(e), where the order provides for the company itself to buy shares, does the order provide for the reduction of the company's capital accordingly` IS
    `s 996(2)(e) the order provides for the reduction of the company's capital accordingly` `the order provides for the purchase of shares by the company itself`

-- s 998(1)-(4): the copy of the order for the registrar.
@export Under section 998(1), must my company deliver a copy of the court's Part 30 order to the registrar?
GIVEN `the order alters the company's constitution` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does the court's order under Part 30 alter the company's constitution?
      `the order gives leave to alter the constitution` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does the order give the company leave to make any, or any specified, alterations to its constitution?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 998(1), must my company deliver a copy of the court's Part 30 order to the registrar` IS
    `s 998(1) the company must deliver a copy of the order to the registrar` `the order alters the company's constitution` `the order gives leave to alter the constitution`

@export Under section 998(2), what is the last day for my company to deliver a copy of the court's Part 30 order to the registrar?
GIVEN `the date the order was made` IS A DATE @desc On what date did the court make the order?
      `the court allowed a longer period` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did the court allow a longer period than 14 days for delivering the copy?
      `the longer period in days` IS A NUMBER @desc If the court allowed a longer period, how many days from the making of the order did it allow? (Any number if it did not.)
GIVETH A DATE
DECIDE `Under section 998(2), what is the last day for my company to deliver a copy of the court's Part 30 order to the registrar` IS
    `s 998(2) the last day for delivering the copy of the order to the registrar` `the date the order was made` (IF `the court allowed a longer period` THEN JUST `the longer period in days` ELSE NOTHING)

@export Under section 998(3), have I, as an officer of the company, committed an offence by the company's default in delivering the copy of the order?
GIVEN `the order alters the company's constitution` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does the court's order under Part 30 alter the company's constitution?
      `the order gives leave to alter the constitution` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does the order give the company leave to make any, or any specified, alterations to its constitution?
      `the date the order was made` IS A DATE @desc On what date did the court make the order?
      `the court allowed a longer period` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did the court allow a longer period than 14 days for delivering the copy?
      `the longer period in days` IS A NUMBER @desc If the court allowed a longer period, how many days from the making of the order did it allow? (Any number if it did not.)
      `the copy has been delivered` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has a copy of the order been delivered to the registrar?
      `the date the copy was delivered` IS A DATE @desc On what date was it delivered? (Any date if it has not been.)
      `the date you are asking about` IS A DATE @desc What is the date you are asking about (usually today)?
      `I am an officer of the company` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are you an officer of the company (a director, manager or secretary)?
      `I authorised or permitted, participated in, or failed to take all reasonable steps to prevent, the default` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did you authorise or permit, take part in, or fail to take all reasonable steps to prevent, the company's default?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 998(3), have I, as an officer of the company, committed an offence by the company's default in delivering the copy of the order` IS
    CONSIDER `s 998(3) the company has made default in complying with section 998` `the order alters the company's constitution` `the order gives leave to alter the constitution` `the date the order was made` (IF `the court allowed a longer period` THEN JUST `the longer period in days` ELSE NOTHING) (IF `the copy has been delivered` THEN JUST `the date the copy was delivered` ELSE NOTHING) `the date you are asking about`
    WHEN JUST defaulted THEN `s 998(3)(b) the officer of the company commits an offence` defaulted `I am an officer of the company` (JUST `I authorised or permitted, participated in, or failed to take all reasonable steps to prevent, the default`) -- the seam input for section 1121 (officer in default): the person's own statement
    WHEN NOTHING THEN NOTHING -- not covered: the text does not decide whether the company is in default (NOTHING is kept, never turned into FALSE)

@export Under section 998(4), what is the most I can be fined on summary conviction for an offence under section 998, in pounds?
GIVEN `pounds that level 3 on the standard scale stands for` IS A NUMBER @desc How many pounds does level 3 on the standard scale stand for? (It is set outside the Act; give the current figure.)
GIVETH A MAYBE NUMBER
DECIDE `Under section 998(4), what is the most I can be fined on summary conviction for an offence under section 998, in pounds` IS
    `s 998(4) the amount in pounds of the fine limit` (penalty's `fine not exceeding`) `pounds that level 3 on the standard scale stands for` 0 -- placeholder 0: the statutory maximum is not read, because the limit is a level on the standard scale
    WHERE
        penalty MEANS `s 998(4) the penalty for a person guilty of an offence under section 998`

-- s 999: what must go with the copy of an order that alters the constitution.
@export Under section 999(2)(a), must the copy of the order delivered to the registrar be accompanied by a copy of the company's articles as amended?
GIVEN `the order alters the company's constitution` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does the court's order under Part 30 alter the company's constitution?
      `the order amends the company's articles` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does the order amend the company's articles?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 999(2)(a), must the copy of the order delivered to the registrar be accompanied by a copy of the company's articles as amended` IS
    `s 999(2)(a) the copy of the order delivered to the registrar must be accompanied by a copy of the company's articles as amended` (`s 999(1) section 999 applies` `the order alters the company's constitution`) `the order amends the company's articles`

@export Under section 999(2)(b), must the copy of the order delivered to the registrar be accompanied by a copy of the amended resolution or agreement?
GIVEN `the order alters the company's constitution` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does the court's order under Part 30 alter the company's constitution?
      `the order amends a resolution or agreement` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does the order amend a resolution or agreement?
      `Chapter 3 of Part 3 applies to that resolution or agreement` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it a resolution or agreement affecting the company's constitution to which Chapter 3 of Part 3 applies (sections 29 and 30)?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 999(2)(b), must the copy of the order delivered to the registrar be accompanied by a copy of the amended resolution or agreement` IS
    `s 999(2)(b) the copy of the order delivered to the registrar must be accompanied by a copy of the resolution or agreement as amended` (`s 999(1) section 999 applies` `the order alters the company's constitution`) `the order amends a resolution or agreement` (JUST `Chapter 3 of Part 3 applies to that resolution or agreement`) -- the seam input for section 29: the person's own statement

@export Under section 999(3), must every copy of the articles my company issues after the order carry a copy of the order?
GIVEN `the order alters the company's constitution` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does the court's order under Part 30 alter the company's constitution?
      `the copy of the articles is issued after the order is made` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the copy of the articles issued by the company after the order was made?
      `the effect of the order has been incorporated into the articles` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has the effect of the order been incorporated into the articles by amendment?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 999(3), must every copy of the articles my company issues after the order carry a copy of the order` IS
    `s 999(3) the copy of the articles issued by the company must be accompanied by a copy of the order` (`s 999(1) section 999 applies` `the order alters the company's constitution`) `the copy of the articles is issued after the order is made` `the effect of the order has been incorporated into the articles`

@export Under section 999(4), have I, as an officer of the company, committed an offence by the company's default in complying with section 999?
GIVEN `the company has defaulted in complying with section 999` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has the company made default in complying with section 999 (a copy of the order did not accompany the articles it issued, or the amended articles or resolution did not accompany the copy delivered to the registrar)?
      `I am an officer of the company` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are you an officer of the company (a director, manager or secretary)?
      `I authorised or permitted, participated in, or failed to take all reasonable steps to prevent, the default` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did you authorise or permit, take part in, or fail to take all reasonable steps to prevent, the company's default?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 999(4), have I, as an officer of the company, committed an offence by the company's default in complying with section 999` IS
    `s 999(4)(b) the officer of the company commits an offence` `the company has defaulted in complying with section 999` `I am an officer of the company` (JUST `I authorised or permitted, participated in, or failed to take all reasonable steps to prevent, the default`) -- the seam input for section 1121: the person's own statement

@export Under section 999(5), what is the most I can be fined on summary conviction for an offence under section 999, in pounds?
GIVEN `pounds that level 3 on the standard scale stands for` IS A NUMBER @desc How many pounds does level 3 on the standard scale stand for? (It is set outside the Act; give the current figure.)
GIVETH A MAYBE NUMBER
DECIDE `Under section 999(5), what is the most I can be fined on summary conviction for an offence under section 999, in pounds` IS
    `s 998(4) the amount in pounds of the fine limit` (penalty's `fine not exceeding`) `pounds that level 3 on the standard scale stands for` 0 -- placeholder 0: the statutory maximum is not read, because the limit is a level on the standard scale
    WHERE
        penalty MEANS `s 999(5) the penalty for a person guilty of an offence under section 999`

§§ `Part 31, Chapter 1: striking off (only if the registrar has written to your company, or your company is applying to be struck off)`

-- s 1000(2): when the registrar must send the second communication.
@export Under section 1000(2), by what date must the registrar send my company the second communication?
GIVEN `the date the registrar sent the first communication` IS A DATE @desc On what date did the registrar send your company the first communication asking whether it is carrying on business or in operation?
GIVETH A DATE
DECIDE `Under section 1000(2), by what date must the registrar send my company the second communication` IS
    `s 1000(2) the last day for the registrar to send the second communication` `the date the registrar sent the first communication`

-- s 1000(3): may the registrar now publish the notice of striking off?
@export Under section 1000(3), may the registrar now publish in the Gazette, and send my company, a notice that its name will be struck off?
GIVEN `my company has told the registrar it is not carrying on business or in operation` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has your company answered the registrar to the effect that it is not carrying on business or in operation?
      `the date the registrar sent the second communication` IS A DATE @desc On what date did the registrar send your company the second communication?
      `my company has answered the second communication` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has your company answered the second communication?
      `the date of that answer` IS A DATE @desc On what date was the answer received? (Any date if there has been none.)
      `the date you are asking about` IS A DATE @desc What is the date you are asking about (usually today)?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 1000(3), may the registrar now publish in the Gazette, and send my company, a notice that its name will be struck off` IS
    `s 1000(3) the registrar may publish in the Gazette, and send to the company, the notice of intended striking off`
        `my company has told the registrar it is not carrying on business or in operation`
        (`s 1000(3)(b) the registrar does not within 14 days after sending the second communication receive any answer` `the date the registrar sent the second communication` (IF `my company has answered the second communication` THEN JUST `the date of that answer` ELSE NOTHING) `the date you are asking about`)

-- s 1000(4): may the registrar now strike the name off?
@export Under section 1000(4), may the registrar now strike my company's name off the register?
GIVEN `the date of the registrar's notice in the Gazette` IS A DATE @desc On what date was the registrar's notice published in the Gazette that the name would be struck off?
      `my company has shown cause to the contrary` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did your company show cause to the contrary before the 2 months ended?
      `the date you are asking about` IS A DATE @desc What is the date you are asking about (usually today)?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 1000(4), may the registrar now strike my company's name off the register` IS
    `s 1000(4) the registrar may strike the company's name off the register` `the date of the registrar's notice in the Gazette` `my company has shown cause to the contrary` `the date you are asking about`

-- s 1000(6): is the company dissolved?
@export Under section 1000(6), has my company been dissolved by being struck off?
GIVEN `the registrar's notice of the striking off has been published in the Gazette` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has the registrar published in the Gazette a notice that the company's name has been struck off the register?
      `the date that notice was published` IS A DATE @desc On what date was it published? (Any date if it has not been.)
      `the date you are asking about` IS A DATE @desc What is the date you are asking about (usually today)?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 1000(6), has my company been dissolved by being struck off` IS
    `s 1000(6) the company is dissolved` (IF `the registrar's notice of the striking off has been published in the Gazette` THEN JUST `the date that notice was published` ELSE NOTHING) `the date you are asking about`

-- s 1000(7)(a): liability after striking off.
@export Under section 1000(7), does my liability as a director, managing officer or member continue after my company has been struck off?
GIVEN `the company has been dissolved on being struck off` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has the company been dissolved because the registrar struck its name off the register?
      `I am a director, managing officer or member of the company` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are you a director, managing officer or member of the company?
      `I have a liability` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Do you have any liability as a director, managing officer or member (for example a debt or a duty)?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 1000(7), does my liability as a director, managing officer or member continue after my company has been struck off` IS
    `s 1000(7)(a) the liability of the person continues and may be enforced as if the company had not been dissolved` (JUST `the company has been dissolved on being struck off`) `I am a director, managing officer or member of the company` `I have a liability`

-- s 1001(1): the registrar's duty to give notice where a company is being wound up.
@export Under section 1001(1), must the registrar give my company, or its liquidator, notice that it will be struck off?
GIVEN `my company is being wound up` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is your company being wound up?
      `the registrar has reasonable cause to believe that no liquidator is acting` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does the registrar have reasonable cause to believe that no liquidator is acting?
      `the registrar has reasonable cause to believe that the affairs are fully wound up` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does the registrar have reasonable cause to believe that the company's affairs are fully wound up?
      `the liquidator's returns have not been made for six consecutive months` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Have the returns the liquidator must make not been made for a period of six consecutive months?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 1001(1), must the registrar give my company, or its liquidator, notice that it will be struck off` IS
    `s 1001(1) the registrar must publish in the Gazette and send the notice of intended striking off` `my company is being wound up` `the registrar has reasonable cause to believe that no liquidator is acting` `the registrar has reasonable cause to believe that the affairs are fully wound up` `the liquidator's returns have not been made for six consecutive months`

-- s 1002(1)-(2): where the registrar may send a communication or notice.
@export Under section 1002(1), may the registrar send me, as an officer, a communication it could not send to the company under Schedule 4?
GIVEN `the registrar is able to send the communication to the company in accordance with Schedule 4` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the registrar able to send the communication or notice to the company in accordance with Schedule 4?
      `I have an address notified to the registrar by the company` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is there an address for you that your company has notified to the registrar?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 1002(1), may the registrar send me, as an officer, a communication it could not send to the company under Schedule 4` IS
    `s 1002(1) the communication may be sent to an officer of the company at the address notified` (JUST `the registrar is able to send the communication to the company in accordance with Schedule 4`) `I have an address notified to the registrar by the company` -- the seam input for Schedule 4: the person's own statement

@export Under section 1002(2), may the registrar send a communication or notice to me as a person who subscribed the company's memorandum?
GIVEN `an officer's name and address are known to the registrar` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is there an officer of the company whose name and address are known to the registrar?
      `my address is known to the registrar` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is your address (as a subscriber of the memorandum) known to the registrar?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 1002(2), may the registrar send a communication or notice to me as a person who subscribed the company's memorandum` IS
    `s 1002(2) the communication or notice may be sent to each of the persons who subscribed the memorandum` `an officer's name and address are known to the registrar` `my address is known to the registrar`

-- s 1002A: striking off a company registered on a false basis.
@export Under section 1002A(1), may the registrar strike my company's name off the register because it was registered on a false basis?
GIVEN `the registrar has reasonable cause to believe the registration or restoration application is misleading, false or deceptive` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does the registrar have reasonable cause to believe that information in the application to register the company (or to restore it) is misleading, false or deceptive in a material particular?
      `the registrar has reasonable cause to believe a statement made in connection with it is misleading, false or deceptive` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does the registrar have reasonable cause to believe that a statement made to the registrar in connection with such an application is misleading, false or deceptive in a material particular?
      `the registrar has published a notice in the Gazette that the name will be struck off` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has the registrar published a notice in the Gazette that, at the end of 28 days beginning with the date of the notice, the name will be struck off unless cause is shown?
      `the date of that notice` IS A DATE @desc On what date was that notice dated? (Any date if there has been none.)
      `the date you are asking about` IS A DATE @desc What is the date you are asking about (usually today)?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 1002A(1), may the registrar strike my company's name off the register because it was registered on a false basis` IS
    `s 1002A(1) the registrar may strike the company's name off the register` `the registrar has reasonable cause to believe the registration or restoration application is misleading, false or deceptive` `the registrar has reasonable cause to believe a statement made in connection with it is misleading, false or deceptive`
        (`s 1002A(3) the registrar may not yet exercise the power in subsection (1)` `the registrar has published a notice in the Gazette that the name will be struck off` `the date of that notice` `the date you are asking about`)

-- s 1003: my company applies to be struck off.
@export Under section 1003(2)(a), is my company's application to be struck off made on its behalf by its directors, or a majority of them?
GIVEN `the number of directors who make the application` IS A NUMBER @desc How many of the company's directors make the application on its behalf?
      `the number of directors of the company` IS A NUMBER @desc How many directors does the company have?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 1003(2)(a), is my company's application to be struck off made on its behalf by its directors, or a majority of them` IS
    `s 1003(2)(a) the application is made on the company's behalf by its directors or by a majority of them` `the number of directors who make the application` `the number of directors of the company`

@export Under section 1003(2)(b), does my company's application to be struck off contain the prescribed information?
GIVEN `the application contains the prescribed information` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does the application contain the information the Secretary of State has prescribed?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 1003(2)(b), does my company's application to be struck off contain the prescribed information` IS
    `s 1003(2)(b) the application contains the prescribed information` `the application contains the prescribed information`

@export Under section 1003(3), is the registrar still barred from striking my company off on its application?
GIVEN `a notice of the application has been published in the Gazette` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has the registrar published a notice in the Gazette?
      `the date the notice was published` IS A DATE @desc On what date was it published? (Any date if it has not been.)
      `the notice states that the registrar may strike the company off` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does the notice state that the registrar may exercise the power to strike the company off?
      `the notice invites any person to show cause why that should not be done` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does the notice invite any person to show cause why that should not be done?
      `the date you are asking about` IS A DATE @desc What is the date you are asking about (usually today)?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 1003(3), is the registrar still barred from striking my company off on its application` IS
    `s 1003(3) the registrar is barred from striking the company off under section 1003` (IF `a notice of the application has been published in the Gazette` THEN JUST `the date the notice was published` ELSE NOTHING) `the notice states that the registrar may strike the company off` `the notice invites any person to show cause why that should not be done` `the date you are asking about`

-- s 1004: when my company's application must not be made.
@export Under section 1004(1), must the application to strike my company off not be made because of what it has done in the last three months?
GIVEN `the company changed its name in the last three months` IS A BOOLEAN @desc In the three months before the application, did the company change its name?
      `the company traded or carried on business in the last three months` IS A BOOLEAN @desc In the three months before the application, did the company trade or otherwise carry on business?
      `the only reason is a payment of a liability from trading` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the only reason you might be treated as trading that the company made a payment in respect of a liability incurred in the course of trading?
      `the company made a disposal for value in the last three months` IS A BOOLEAN @desc In the three months before the application, did the company make a disposal for value of property or rights that, immediately before it ceased to trade, it held for the purpose of disposal for gain in the normal course of trading?
      `the company engaged in some other activity in the last three months` IS A BOOLEAN @desc In the three months before the application, did the company engage in any other activity?
      `that activity was for making the application` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Was that activity necessary or expedient for making the application, or deciding whether to?
      `that activity was for concluding the company's affairs` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Was that activity necessary or expedient for concluding the company's affairs?
      `that activity was for complying with a statutory requirement` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Was that activity necessary or expedient for complying with a statutory requirement?
      `that activity is specified by order` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is that activity one the Secretary of State has specified by order for this purpose?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 1004(1), must the application to strike my company off not be made because of what it has done in the last three months` IS
    `s 1004(1) the application must not be made` `the company changed its name in the last three months`
        (`s 1004(2) the company is to be treated as trading or otherwise carrying on business` `the company traded or carried on business in the last three months` `the only reason is a payment of a liability from trading`)
        `the company made a disposal for value in the last three months`
        (`s 1004(1)(d) the company engaged in an activity that is not an excepted one` `the company engaged in some other activity in the last three months` `that activity was for making the application` `that activity was for concluding the company's affairs` `that activity was for complying with a statutory requirement` `that activity is specified by order`)

@export Under section 1004(5), do I commit an offence by making the application when section 1004(1) forbids it?
GIVEN `section 1004(1) forbids the application` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does section 1004(1) forbid the application (see the previous question)?
      `I make the application` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Do you make the application?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 1004(5), do I commit an offence by making the application when section 1004(1) forbids it` IS
    `s 1004(5) the person commits an offence by making the application` (JUST `section 1004(1) forbids the application`) `I make the application`

@export Under section 1004(6), does section 1004 give me a defence because I did not know, and could not reasonably have known, the facts?
GIVEN `I did not know of the facts that led to the contravention` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Can you prove you did not know of the existence of the facts that led to the contravention?
      `I could not reasonably have known of those facts` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Can you prove you could not reasonably have known of them?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 1004(6), does section 1004 give me a defence because I did not know, and could not reasonably have known, the facts` IS
    `s 1004(6) section 1004 gives the accused a defence on these facts` `I did not know of the facts that led to the contravention` `I could not reasonably have known of those facts`

-- s 1005: other proceedings not concluded.
@export Under section 1005(1), must the application to strike my company off not be made because other proceedings are not concluded?
GIVEN `a Part 26 or 26A application for sanctioning a compromise or arrangement has been made` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has an application to the court under Part 26 or 26A been made on behalf of the company for the sanctioning of a compromise or arrangement?
      `that application has been withdrawn` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has that application been withdrawn?
      `that application has been finally dealt with without sanction` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has it been finally dealt with without a compromise or arrangement being sanctioned?
      `that arrangement has been sanctioned and fully carried out` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has a compromise or arrangement been sanctioned and (with anything the court ordered) fully carried out?
      `a voluntary arrangement has been proposed` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has a voluntary arrangement been proposed for the company under Part 1 of the Insolvency Act 1986 or Part 2 of the Insolvency (Northern Ireland) Order 1989?
      `no meetings are to be summoned on that proposal` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are no meetings to be summoned on that proposal?
      `the meetings summoned fail to approve the arrangement` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did the meetings summoned fail to approve the arrangement (with no, or the same, modifications)?
      `the arrangement approved has been fully implemented` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has the arrangement that was approved been fully implemented?
      `the court revoked approval of the arrangement` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has the court revoked the approval given at the meetings?
      `the company has done what the court directed` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has the company done whatever it must under any directions the court gave when revoking approval?
      `the company is in administration` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the company in administration?
      `the interim moratorium applies` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does the interim moratorium on proceedings (paragraph 44 or 45 of Schedule B1) apply?
      `the company is being wound up` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the company being wound up, voluntarily or by the court?
      `a winding-up petition is pending` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has a petition for winding up by the court been presented and not finally dealt with or withdrawn?
      `there is a receiver or manager of the company's property` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is there a receiver or manager of the company's property?
      `a judicial factor administers the company's estate` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the company's estate being administered by a judicial factor?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 1005(1), must the application to strike my company off not be made because other proceedings are not concluded` IS
    `s 1005(1) the application must not be made`
        `a Part 26 or 26A application for sanctioning a compromise or arrangement has been made`
        (`s 1005(2) the matter of the application to the court under Part 26 or 26A is finally concluded` `that application has been withdrawn` `that application has been finally dealt with without sanction` `that arrangement has been sanctioned and fully carried out`)
        `a voluntary arrangement has been proposed`
        (`s 1005(3) the matter of the voluntary arrangement is finally concluded` `no meetings are to be summoned on that proposal` `the meetings summoned fail to approve the arrangement` `the arrangement approved has been fully implemented` `the court revoked approval of the arrangement` `the company has done what the court directed`)
        `the company is in administration` `the interim moratorium applies` `the company is being wound up` `a winding-up petition is pending` `there is a receiver or manager of the company's property` `a judicial factor administers the company's estate`

-- s 1006: copy of the application to those affected.
@export Under section 1006(1), must I, as a director who makes the application, secure that a copy is given to a particular person?
GIVEN `the person is a member` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is that person a member of the company on the day the application is made?
      `the person is an employee` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is that person an employee of the company on that day?
      `the person is a creditor` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is that person a creditor of the company on that day? (A contingent or prospective creditor counts: say yes.)
      `the person is a director` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is that person a director of the company on that day?
      `the person is a pension fund manager or trustee` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is that person a manager or trustee of a pension fund established for the benefit of the company's employees?
      `the person is of a description specified by regulations` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is that person of a description specified by regulations of the Secretary of State for this purpose?
      `the person is a director who is a party to the application` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is that person a director who is a party to the application?
      `the day the application was made` IS A DATE @desc On what date was the application made?
      `the application has been withdrawn` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has the application been withdrawn?
      `the day the application was withdrawn` IS A DATE @desc On what date was it withdrawn? (Any date if it has not been.)
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 1006(1), must I, as a director who makes the application, secure that a copy is given to a particular person` IS
    `s 1006(1) the applicant must secure that a copy of the application is given to the person`
        (`s 1006(1) the person is one of those to whom a copy of the application must be given` `the person is a member` `the person is an employee` (`s 1011 the person is a creditor of the company for the purposes of Chapter 1 of Part 31` `the person is a creditor` FALSE FALSE) `the person is a director` `the person is a pension fund manager or trustee` `the person is of a description specified by regulations`) -- contingent and prospective creditors are folded into the one creditor question: section 1011 counts them, so asking them apart would add nothing
        (`s 1006(2) subsection (1) requires a copy of the application to be given to the director` `the person is a director` `the person is a director who is a party to the application`)
        (`s 1006(3) the duty imposed by section 1006 has ceased to apply` `the day the application was made` (IF `the application has been withdrawn` THEN JUST `the day the application was withdrawn` ELSE NOTHING))

@export Under section 1006(1), what is the last day for giving the copy of the application?
GIVEN `the day the application was made` IS A DATE @desc On what date was the application made?
GIVETH A DATE
DECIDE `Under section 1006(1), what is the last day for giving the copy of the application` IS
    `s 1006(1) the last day for giving the copy of the application` `the day the application was made`

@export Under section 1006(4), do I commit an offence by failing to give the copy of the application?
GIVEN `section 1006 required me to secure that a copy was given` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did section 1006(1) require you to secure that a copy of the application was given to the person (see the previous questions)?
      `I failed to perform the duty` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did you fail to perform that duty?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 1006(4), do I commit an offence by failing to give the copy of the application` IS
    `s 1006(4) the person commits an offence by failing to perform the duty` (JUST `section 1006 required me to secure that a copy was given`) `I failed to perform the duty`

@export Under section 1006(4), do I commit an aggravated offence by failing to give the copy of the application in order to conceal it?
GIVEN `section 1006 required me to secure that a copy was given` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did section 1006(1) require you to secure that a copy of the application was given to the person?
      `I failed to perform the duty` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did you fail to perform that duty?
      `I did so intending to conceal the application from the person` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did you fail with the intention of concealing the making of the application from the person concerned?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 1006(4), do I commit an aggravated offence by failing to give the copy of the application in order to conceal it` IS
    `s 1006(4) the person commits an aggravated offence by failing to perform the duty with the intention of concealing the application`
        (`s 1006(4) the person commits an offence by failing to perform the duty` (JUST `section 1006 required me to secure that a copy was given`) `I failed to perform the duty`)
        `I did so intending to conceal the application from the person`

@export Under section 1006(5), does section 1006 give me a defence because I took all reasonable steps to give the copy?
GIVEN `I took all reasonable steps to perform the duty` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Can you prove that you took all reasonable steps to perform the duty?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 1006(5), does section 1006 give me a defence because I took all reasonable steps to give the copy` IS
    `s 1006(5) section 1006 gives the accused a defence on these facts` `I took all reasonable steps to perform the duty`

-- s 1007: copy to those who become members, employees etc. while the application is pending.
@export Under section 1007(2), must I, as a director, secure that a copy of the pending application is given to a person who has just become a member, employee, creditor, director or pension trustee?
GIVEN `the day the company made the application` IS A DATE @desc On what date did the company make its application to be struck off?
      `the application has been dealt with or withdrawn` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has the application been finally dealt with or withdrawn?
      `the day it was dealt with or withdrawn` IS A DATE @desc On what date? (Any date if it has not been.)
      `the day that person became one of those listed` IS A DATE @desc On what date did that person become a member, employee, creditor, director or pension trustee?
      `the person becomes a member` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has that person just become a member of the company?
      `the person becomes an employee` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has that person just become an employee of the company?
      `the person becomes a creditor` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has that person just become a creditor of the company? (A contingent or prospective creditor counts: say yes.)
      `the person becomes a director` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has that person just become a director of the company?
      `the person becomes a pension fund manager or trustee` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has that person just become a manager or trustee of a pension fund established for the benefit of the company's employees?
      `the person becomes of a description specified by regulations` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has that person just become a person of a description specified by the Secretary of State's regulations for this purpose?
      `I am a director at the end of that day` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are you a director of the company at the end of the day on which that happened?
      `that person is someone other than me` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is that person someone other than yourself?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 1007(2), must I, as a director, secure that a copy of the pending application is given to a person who has just become a member, employee, creditor, director or pension trustee` IS
    `s 1007(2) the director must secure that a copy of the application is given to the other person`
        (`s 1007(1) section 1007 applies to the day asked about` `the day the company made the application` (IF `the application has been dealt with or withdrawn` THEN JUST `the day it was dealt with or withdrawn` ELSE NOTHING) `the day that person became one of those listed`)
        `I am a director at the end of that day`
        `that person is someone other than me`
        (`s 1007(2) the other person becomes one of those to whom a copy of the application must be given` `the person becomes a member` `the person becomes an employee` (`s 1011 the person is a creditor of the company for the purposes of Chapter 1 of Part 31` `the person becomes a creditor` FALSE FALSE) `the person becomes a director` `the person becomes a pension fund manager or trustee` `the person becomes of a description specified by regulations`) -- contingent and prospective creditors are folded into the one creditor question, as in section 1006

@export Under section 1007(2), what is the last day for giving the copy of the application to the new person?
GIVEN `the day that person became one of those listed` IS A DATE @desc On what date did that person become a member, employee, creditor, director or pension trustee?
GIVETH A DATE
DECIDE `Under section 1007(2), what is the last day for giving the copy of the application to the new person` IS
    `s 1007(2) the last day for giving the copy of the application` `the day that person became one of those listed`

@export Under section 1007(4), do I commit an offence by failing to give the copy of the application to the new person?
GIVEN `section 1007 required me to secure that a copy was given` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did section 1007(2) require you to secure that a copy of the application was given to the other person (see the previous questions)?
      `I failed to perform the duty` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did you fail to perform that duty?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 1007(4), do I commit an offence by failing to give the copy of the application to the new person` IS
    `s 1007(4) the person commits an offence by failing to perform the duty` (JUST `section 1007 required me to secure that a copy was given`) `I failed to perform the duty`

@export Under section 1007(5), does section 1007 give me a defence because I was unaware of the application or took all reasonable steps?
GIVEN `I was not aware that the company had made an application` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Can you prove that, at the time of the failure, you were not aware that the company had made an application to be struck off?
      `I took all reasonable steps to perform the duty` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Can you prove that you took all reasonable steps to perform the duty?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 1007(5), does section 1007 give me a defence because I was unaware of the application or took all reasonable steps` IS
    `s 1007(5) section 1007 gives the accused a defence on these facts` `I was not aware that the company had made an application` `I took all reasonable steps to perform the duty`

-- s 1008: how a copy is "given".
@export Under section 1008(2), is the copy of the application treated as given to a person I delivered it to, left at their address or posted?
GIVEN `I delivered it to the person` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did you deliver the copy to the person?
      `I left it at the person's proper address` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did you leave it at the person's proper address?
      `I sent it by post to the person at that address` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did you send it by post to the person at that address?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 1008(2), is the copy of the application treated as given to a person I delivered it to, left at their address or posted` IS
    `s 1008(2) the document is treated as given to the person` `I delivered it to the person` `I left it at the person's proper address` `I sent it by post to the person at that address`

@export Under section 1008(3), what is the proper address of the person to whom I must give the copy?
GIVEN `the person is an individual` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the person an individual (rather than a firm, company or other body)?
      `the firm was incorporated or formed in the United Kingdom` IS A BOOLEAN @desc If the person is a firm, was it incorporated or formed in the United Kingdom?
      `the firm has a place of business in the United Kingdom` IS A BOOLEAN @desc If the person is a firm incorporated or formed outside the United Kingdom, does it have a place of business in the United Kingdom?
GIVETH A `s 1008(3) proper address`
DECIDE `Under section 1008(3), what is the proper address of the person to whom I must give the copy` IS
    `s 1008(3) the proper address of the person` `the person is an individual` `the firm was incorporated or formed in the United Kingdom` `the firm has a place of business in the United Kingdom`

-- s 1009: when the application must be withdrawn.
@export Under section 1009(2), must I, as a director, secure that the company's application to be struck off is withdrawn forthwith?
GIVEN `the company changed its name` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Since the application, has the company changed its name?
      `the company traded or carried on business` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Since the application, has the company traded or otherwise carried on business?
      `the only reason is a payment of a liability from trading` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the only reason that the company made a payment in respect of a liability incurred in the course of trading?
      `the company made a disposal for value` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Since the application, has the company made a disposal for value of property or rights?
      `the property was needed for the application` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Was the property one it was necessary or expedient for the company to hold for making, or proceeding with, the application?
      `the company engaged in an activity` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Since the application, has the company engaged in any activity?
      `that activity was for the application` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Was it necessary or expedient for making or proceeding with the application?
      `that activity was for concluding outstanding affairs` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Was it for concluding affairs outstanding because of what was necessary or expedient for the application?
      `that activity was for a statutory requirement` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Was it for complying with a statutory requirement?
      `that activity is specified by order` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it an activity the Secretary of State has specified by order for this purpose?
      `a Part 26 or 26A application has been made` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has an application to the court been made under Part 26 or 26A for sanctioning a compromise or arrangement?
      `a voluntary arrangement has been proposed` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has a voluntary arrangement been proposed for the company?
      `an administration order has been applied for` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has an application for an administration order been made?
      `an administrator has been appointed or notice of intention filed` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has an administrator been appointed, or a notice of intention to appoint one filed with the court?
      `circumstances for voluntary winding up have arisen` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Have circumstances arisen in which the company may be voluntarily wound up?
      `a winding-up petition has been presented` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has a petition been presented for the winding up of the company by the court?
      `a receiver or manager has been appointed` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has a receiver or manager of the company's property been appointed?
      `a judicial factor has been appointed` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has a judicial factor been appointed to administer the company's estate?
      `I am a director at the end of a day on which one of these occurs` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are you a director of the company at the end of a day on which any of these occurs?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 1009(2), must I, as a director, secure that the company's application to be struck off is withdrawn forthwith` IS
    `s 1009(2) the director must secure that the company's application is withdrawn forthwith`
        (`s 1009(1) at least one of the events has occurred` events)
        `I am a director at the end of a day on which one of these occurs`
    WHERE
        -- An event is listed when the person states it occurred; for the three events the text qualifies (trading, a disposal, an activity), only when the module's rule counts it. A qualification the text does not decide leaves the event out of the list: see NOTES.md, seam note on s 1009.
        events MEANS
            concat (LIST
                (IF `the company changed its name` THEN LIST `s 1009(1)(a)(i) the company changes its name` ELSE EMPTY),
                (IF `s 1009(3) the company is treated as trading or otherwise carrying on business` `the company traded or carried on business` `the only reason is a payment of a liability from trading` EQUALS JUST TRUE THEN LIST `s 1009(1)(a)(ii) the company trades or otherwise carries on business` ELSE EMPTY),
                (IF `s 1009(1)(a)(iii) the disposal is one that requires the application to be withdrawn` `the company made a disposal for value` `the property was needed for the application` EQUALS JUST TRUE THEN LIST `s 1009(1)(a)(iii) the company makes a disposal for value of any property or rights other than those which it was necessary or expedient for it to hold for the purpose of making, or proceeding with, an application under section 1003` ELSE EMPTY),
                (IF `s 1009(1)(a)(iv) the activity is one that requires the application to be withdrawn` `the company engaged in an activity` (`s 1009(4) the activity is an excepted activity` `that activity was for the application` `that activity was for concluding outstanding affairs` `that activity was for a statutory requirement` `that activity is specified by order`) EQUALS JUST TRUE THEN LIST `s 1009(1)(a)(iv) the company engages in any activity, except one to which subsection (4) applies` ELSE EMPTY),
                (IF `a Part 26 or 26A application has been made` THEN LIST `s 1009(1)(b) an application is made to the court under Part 26 or 26A on behalf of the company for the sanctioning of a compromise or arrangement` ELSE EMPTY),
                (IF `a voluntary arrangement has been proposed` THEN LIST `s 1009(1)(c) a voluntary arrangement in relation to the company is proposed under Part 1 of the Insolvency Act 1986 or Part 2 of the Insolvency (Northern Ireland) Order 1989` ELSE EMPTY),
                (IF `an administration order has been applied for` THEN LIST `s 1009(1)(d) an application to the court for an administration order in respect of the company is made` ELSE EMPTY),
                (IF `an administrator has been appointed or notice of intention filed` THEN LIST `s 1009(1)(e) an administrator is appointed in respect of the company, or a copy of notice of intention to appoint an administrator is filed with the court` ELSE EMPTY),
                (IF `circumstances for voluntary winding up have arisen` THEN LIST `s 1009(1)(f) there arise circumstances in which the company may be voluntarily wound up under section 84(1) of that Act or Article 70 of that Order` ELSE EMPTY),
                (IF `a winding-up petition has been presented` THEN LIST `s 1009(1)(g) a petition is presented for the winding up of the company by the court under Part 4 of that Act or Part 5 of that Order` ELSE EMPTY),
                (IF `a receiver or manager has been appointed` THEN LIST `s 1009(1)(h) a receiver or manager of the company's property is appointed` ELSE EMPTY),
                (IF `a judicial factor has been appointed` THEN LIST `s 1009(1)(i) a judicial factor is appointed to administer the company's estate` ELSE EMPTY))

@export Under section 1009(5), do I commit an offence by failing to secure the withdrawal of the application?
GIVEN `section 1009 required me to secure the withdrawal` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did section 1009(2) require you to secure that the company's application was withdrawn (see the previous question)?
      `I failed to perform the duty` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did you fail to perform that duty?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 1009(5), do I commit an offence by failing to secure the withdrawal of the application` IS
    `s 1009(5) the person commits an offence by failing to perform the duty` (JUST `section 1009 required me to secure the withdrawal`) `I failed to perform the duty`

@export Under section 1009(6), does section 1009 give me a defence to failing to secure the withdrawal?
GIVEN `I was not aware that the company had made an application` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Can you prove that, at the time of the failure, you were not aware that the company had made an application to be struck off?
      `I took all reasonable steps to perform the duty` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Can you prove that you took all reasonable steps to perform the duty?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 1009(6), does section 1009 give me a defence to failing to secure the withdrawal` IS
    `s 1009(6) section 1009 gives the accused a defence on these facts` `I was not aware that the company had made an application` `I took all reasonable steps to perform the duty`

-- s 1010: how the application is withdrawn.
@export Under section 1010, is my company's application to be struck off withdrawn?
GIVEN `notice of withdrawal has been given to the registrar` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has notice of withdrawal of the application been given to the registrar?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 1010, is my company's application to be struck off withdrawn` IS
    `s 1010 the application under section 1003 is withdrawn` `notice of withdrawal has been given to the registrar`

-- s 1011: who is a creditor for this Chapter.
@export Under section 1011, am I a creditor of the company for the purposes of the striking-off provisions?
GIVEN `I am a creditor of the company` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are you a creditor of the company?
      `I am a contingent creditor` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are you a contingent creditor of the company?
      `I am a prospective creditor` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are you a prospective creditor of the company?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 1011, am I a creditor of the company for the purposes of the striking-off provisions` IS
    `s 1011 the person is a creditor of the company for the purposes of Chapter 1 of Part 31` `I am a creditor of the company` `I am a contingent creditor` `I am a prospective creditor`

§§ `Part 31, Chapter 2: property of a dissolved company (only if your company has been dissolved, or you claim an interest in property it held)`

-- s 1012(1): bona vacantia.
@export Under section 1012(1), is property the company held when it was dissolved deemed to be bona vacantia?
GIVEN `the company is dissolved` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has the company been dissolved?
      `the property was vested in or held on trust for the company immediately before dissolution` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Was the property or right vested in the company, or held on trust for it, immediately before its dissolution?
      `the company held the property on trust for another person` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did the company hold the property on trust for another person?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 1012(1), is property the company held when it was dissolved deemed to be bona vacantia` IS
    `s 1012(1) the property or right is deemed to be bona vacantia` `the company is dissolved` `the property was vested in or held on trust for the company immediately before dissolution` `the company held the property on trust for another person`

-- s 1013(5): is the Crown's disclaimer out of time?
@export Under section 1013(5), is the Crown's notice of disclaimer of no effect because it was executed too late?
GIVEN `the date the notice of disclaimer was executed` IS A DATE @desc On what date was the Crown's notice of disclaimer executed?
      `the date the fact first came to the Crown representative's notice` IS A DATE @desc On what date did the fact that the property may have vested in the Crown first come to the notice of the Crown representative?
      `ownership was established at that date` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Was ownership of the property established at that date?
      `the period needed to establish ownership has ended` IS A BOOLEAN @desc If ownership was not established then, has the period reasonably necessary to establish it ended?
      `the date the period needed to establish ownership ended` IS A DATE @desc On what date did it end? (Any date if it was established or has not ended.)
      `an interested person applied in writing for a decision` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did a person interested in the property apply in writing to the Crown representative requiring a decision whether to disclaim?
      `the date of that application` IS A DATE @desc On what date? (Any date if there was none.)
      `the court allowed a further period` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did the court allow a further period for the notice?
      `the date the further period ends` IS A DATE @desc On what date does it end? (Any date if there was none.)
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 1013(5), is the Crown's notice of disclaimer of no effect because it was executed too late` IS
    `s 1013(5) the notice of disclaimer is of no effect` `the date the notice of disclaimer was executed`
        (`s 1013(3) the last day for executing the notice of disclaimer` `the date the fact first came to the Crown representative's notice` `ownership was established at that date` (IF `the period needed to establish ownership has ended` THEN JUST `the date the period needed to establish ownership ended` ELSE NOTHING))
        (IF `an interested person applied in writing for a decision` THEN JUST (`s 1013(4) the last day for executing the notice of disclaimer after an application` `the date of that application` (IF `the court allowed a further period` THEN JUST `the date the further period ends` ELSE NOTHING)) ELSE NOTHING)

@export Under section 1013(7), must I be sent a copy of the Crown's notice of disclaimer because I claimed to be interested in the property?
GIVEN `a notice of disclaimer has been executed` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has a notice of disclaimer been executed under section 1013?
      `I have given the Crown representative notice that I claim to be interested` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Have you given the Crown representative notice that you claim to be interested in the property?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 1013(7), must I be sent a copy of the Crown's notice of disclaimer because I claimed to be interested in the property` IS
    `s 1013(7) a copy of the notice must be sent to the person` `a notice of disclaimer has been executed` `I have given the Crown representative notice that I claim to be interested`

-- s 1014(1): deemed not to have vested.
@export Under section 1014(1), is the property deemed not to have vested in the Crown because the Crown disclaimed it?
GIVEN `a notice of disclaimer was executed` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has a notice of disclaimer been executed under section 1013 as respects the property?
      `the notice is of no effect because it was late` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the notice of no effect under section 1013(5) because it was executed after the end of the time allowed?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 1014(1), is the property deemed not to have vested in the Crown because the Crown disclaimed it` IS
    `s 1014(1) the property is deemed not to have vested in the Crown under section 1012` `a notice of disclaimer was executed` (JUST `the notice is of no effect because it was late`)

-- s 1015(2): effect on other persons.
@export Under section 1015(2), does the Crown's disclaimer of property in England and Wales or Northern Ireland affect my rights or liabilities as another person?
GIVEN `the effect on me is necessary to release the company from a liability` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Would affecting your rights or liabilities be necessary for the purpose of releasing the company from any liability?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 1015(2), does the Crown's disclaimer of property in England and Wales or Northern Ireland affect my rights or liabilities as another person` IS
    `s 1015(2) the disclaimer affects the rights or liabilities of the other person` `the effect on me is necessary to release the company from a liability`

-- s 1016(1): disclaimer of leaseholds.
@export Under section 1016(1), is the Crown's disclaimer of leasehold property still barred from taking effect?
GIVEN `the property is of a leasehold character` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the property disclaimed of a leasehold character?
      `a copy was served on every underlessee and mortgagee` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has a copy of the disclaimer been served (so far as the Crown representative knows their addresses) on every person claiming under the company as underlessee or mortgagee?
      `the day the last notice was served` IS A DATE @desc On what date was the last such notice served?
      `an application for a vesting order was made` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has an application been made to the court for a vesting order under section 1017?
      `the day that application was made` IS A DATE @desc On what date was it made? (Any date if none was.)
      `the court directed that the disclaimer take effect` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has the court directed that the disclaimer shall take effect?
      `the date you are asking about` IS A DATE @desc What is the date you are asking about (usually today)?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 1016(1), is the Crown's disclaimer of leasehold property still barred from taking effect` IS
    `s 1016(1) the disclaimer of the leasehold property is barred from taking effect` `the property is of a leasehold character` `a copy was served on every underlessee and mortgagee` `the day the last notice was served` (IF `an application for a vesting order was made` THEN JUST `the day that application was made` ELSE NOTHING) `the court directed that the disclaimer take effect` `the date you are asking about`

-- s 1017: the vesting order.
@export Under section 1017(1), may the court make a vesting order for the disclaimed property on my application?
GIVEN `I claim an interest in the disclaimed property` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Do you claim an interest in the disclaimed property?
      `I am under a liability in respect of it that the disclaimer does not discharge` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are you under a liability in respect of the disclaimed property that the disclaimer does not discharge?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 1017(1), may the court make a vesting order for the disclaimed property on my application` IS
    `s 1017(1) the court may make a vesting order in respect of the property on the application of the person` `I claim an interest in the disclaimed property` `I am under a liability in respect of it that the disclaimer does not discharge`

@export Under section 1017(3), may the court make an order vesting the property in me, to compensate me for a liability?
GIVEN `it appears just to compensate me for the liability` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does it appear to the court that it would be just to make the order for the purpose of compensating you for your liability in respect of the disclaimer?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 1017(3), may the court make an order vesting the property in me, to compensate me for a liability` IS
    `s 1017(3) an order under subsection (2)(b) may be made` `it appears just to compensate me for the liability`

-- s 1018(3): an underlessee or mortgagee who declines.
@export Under section 1018(3), am I excluded from all interest in the property because I declined a vesting order on those terms?
GIVEN `I claim under the company as underlessee or mortgagee` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Do you claim under the company as underlessee or mortgagee?
      `I declined to accept a vesting order on such terms` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did you decline to accept a vesting order on the terms of section 1018(1)?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 1018(3), am I excluded from all interest in the property because I declined a vesting order on those terms` IS
    `s 1018(3) the person is excluded from all interest in the property` `I claim under the company as underlessee or mortgagee` `I declined to accept a vesting order on such terms`

-- s 1019: rentcharge liability.
@export Under section 1019, am I personally liable for a sum due under a rentcharge on land that vested in me because of the disclaimer?
GIVEN `land subject to a rentcharge vested in me in consequence of the disclaimer` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did land subject to a rentcharge vest in you in consequence of the disclaimer?
      `the sum became due after I took possession or control or went into occupation` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did the sum become due after you, or someone claiming under or through you, took possession or control of the land or entered into occupation of it?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 1019, am I personally liable for a sum due under a rentcharge on land that vested in me because of the disclaimer` IS
    `s 1019 the person or his successors in title are subject to personal liability for the sum due under the rentcharge` `land subject to a rentcharge vested in me in consequence of the disclaimer` `the sum became due after I took possession or control or went into occupation`

-- s 1020(2): effect on other persons (Scotland).
@export Under section 1020(2), does the Crown's disclaimer of property in Scotland affect my rights or liabilities as another person?
GIVEN `the effect on me is necessary to release the company from a liability` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Would affecting your rights or liabilities be necessary for the purpose of releasing the company from any liability?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 1020(2), does the Crown's disclaimer of property in Scotland affect my rights or liabilities as another person` IS
    `s 1020(2) the disclaimer affects the rights or liabilities of the other person` `the effect on me is necessary to release the company from a liability`

-- s 1021(1), s 1022: Scotland.
@export Under section 1021(1), may I apply to the court for an order vesting the disclaimed property in Scotland?
GIVEN `I claim an interest in the disclaimed property` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Do you claim an interest in the disclaimed property?
      `I am under a liability not discharged by the Act` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are you under a liability not discharged by the Act in respect of the disclaimed property?
      `the court has heard such persons as it thinks fit` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has the court heard such persons as it thinks fit?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 1021(1), may I apply to the court for an order vesting the disclaimed property in Scotland` IS
    `s 1021(1) the court may make a vesting order in respect of the property on the application of the person` `I claim an interest in the disclaimed property` `I am under a liability not discharged by the Act` `the court has heard such persons as it thinks fit`

@export Under section 1022(1), is the court barred from vesting a disclaimed lease in me as sub-lessee or heritable creditor except on the section 1022 terms?
GIVEN `the property disclaimed is held under a lease` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the property disclaimed held under a lease?
      `I claim under the company as sub-lessee` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Do you claim under the company as sub-lessee?
      `the heritable security is recorded in the Register of Sasines` IS A BOOLEAN @desc If you claim as creditor in a heritable security over a lease: is the security recorded in the Register of Sasines?
      `the heritable security is registered under the Land Registration etc. (Scotland) Act 2012` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it registered in accordance with the Land Registration etc. (Scotland) Act 2012?
      `I claim as creditor in a heritable security over a lease` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Do you claim under the company as creditor in a heritable security over a lease?
      `the order is on terms of the same liabilities and obligations as the company's` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the vesting order on terms making you subject to the same liabilities and obligations as those to which the company was subject under the lease?
      `the court thinks fit and the order is on terms as if the lease had been assigned to me` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does the court think fit to make you subject only to the same liabilities and obligations as if the lease had been assigned to you, and is the order on those terms?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 1022(1), is the court barred from vesting a disclaimed lease in me as sub-lessee or heritable creditor except on the section 1022 terms` IS
    `s 1022(1) the court is barred from making the vesting order in favour of the person` `the property disclaimed is held under a lease` `I claim under the company as sub-lessee` (`s 1022(6) the heritable security is duly recorded or duly registered` `the heritable security is recorded in the Register of Sasines` `the heritable security is registered under the Land Registration etc. (Scotland) Act 2012`) `I claim as creditor in a heritable security over a lease` `the order is on terms of the same liabilities and obligations as the company's` `the court thinks fit and the order is on terms as if the lease had been assigned to me`

@export Under section 1022(3), am I excluded from all interest in and security over the property because I declined a vesting order on those terms?
GIVEN `I am a sub-lessee or heritable creditor within section 1022(1)` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are you a sub-lessee, or a creditor in a heritable security over a lease, within section 1022(1)?
      `I declined to accept a vesting order on such terms` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did you decline to accept a vesting order on the terms of section 1022(1)?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 1022(3), am I excluded from all interest in and security over the property because I declined a vesting order on those terms` IS
    `s 1022(3) the person is excluded from all interest in and security over the property` `I am a sub-lessee or heritable creditor within section 1022(1)` `I declined to accept a vesting order on such terms`

-- s 1023(2): rentcharge liability where land vests on the dissolution.
@export Under section 1023(2), am I personally liable for a sum due under a rentcharge on land that vested in me by operation of law when the company was dissolved?
GIVEN `the person is a body corporate` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the person in whom the land vested a body corporate?
      `the company is dissolved` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has the company been dissolved?
      `land subject to a rentcharge vested by operation of law on the dissolution` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did land in England and Wales or Northern Ireland that is subject to a rentcharge vest by operation of law on the company's dissolution?
      `the sum became due after I took possession or control or went into occupation` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did the sum become due after you, or someone claiming under or through you, took possession or control of the land or entered into occupation of it?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 1023(2), am I personally liable for a sum due under a rentcharge on land that vested in me by operation of law when the company was dissolved` IS
    `s 1023(2) the proprietor or his successors in title are subject to personal liability for the sum due under the rentcharge` (`s 1023(1) section 1023 applies` (`s 1023(3) the person is a company for the purposes of section 1023` `the person is a body corporate`) `the company is dissolved` `land subject to a rentcharge vested by operation of law on the dissolution`) `the sum became due after I took possession or control or went into occupation`

§§ `Part 31, Chapter 3: restoration to the register (only if your company has been struck off or dissolved and you are thinking of restoring it)`

-- s 1024: who may apply to the registrar, and by when.
@export Under section 1024, may I apply to the registrar for administrative restoration of the company?
GIVEN `the company was struck off under section 1000 or 1001` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Was the company struck off the register under section 1000 or 1001 (not carrying on business, or a company being wound up)?
      `the company was struck off under section 1002A` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Was the company struck off the register under section 1002A (registered on a false basis)?
      `I am a former director of the company` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are you a former director of the company?
      `I am a former member of the company` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are you a former member of the company?
      `the date the company was dissolved` IS A DATE @desc On what date was the company dissolved?
      `the date the registrar receives my application` IS A DATE @desc On what date will the registrar receive (or did it receive) your application?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 1024, may I apply to the registrar for administrative restoration of the company` IS
    `s 1024 the person may make an application to the registrar for administrative restoration`
        (`s 1024(1) an application may be made to the registrar to restore the company to the register` `the company was struck off under section 1000 or 1001` `the company was struck off under section 1002A`)
        (`s 1024(3) the person may make the application to the registrar` `I am a former director of the company` `I am a former member of the company`)
        (`s 1024(4) the application is made within the period of six years from the date of the dissolution` `the date the company was dissolved` `the date the registrar receives my application`)

-- s 1025(1): must the registrar restore the company?
@export Under section 1025(1), must the registrar restore the company to the register on my application?
GIVEN `the company was struck off under section 1000 or 1001` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Was the company struck off under section 1000 or 1001 (rather than section 1002A)?
      `the company was carrying on business or in operation when struck off` IS A BOOLEAN @desc If it was struck off under section 1000 or 1001: was the company carrying on business or in operation at the time it was struck off?
      `the registrar had no reasonable cause to believe the false-basis matter` IS A BOOLEAN @desc If it was struck off under section 1002A: did the registrar, at the time, lack reasonable cause to believe the matter in section 1002A(1)(a) or (b)?
      `property has vested as bona vacantia` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has any property or right previously vested in or held on trust for the company vested as bona vacantia?
      `the Crown representative has consented in writing` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has the Crown representative signified to the registrar in writing consent to the company's restoration?
      `I have delivered the documents the registrar needs` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Have you delivered to the registrar such documents relating to the company as are necessary to make the registrar's records up to date?
      `outstanding section 453 penalties have been paid` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Have any outstanding penalties under section 453 (or earlier provisions) in relation to the company been paid?
      `each relevant person has paid outstanding fines and penalties` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has each relevant person (you; a director before dissolution who will be a director after restoration; their relevant officers) paid any outstanding fines or financial penalties for a Companies Acts offence relating to the company?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 1025(1), must the registrar restore the company to the register on my application` IS
    `s 1025(1) the registrar shall restore the company to the register`
        (`s 1025(2) the first condition is met` (IF `the company was struck off under section 1000 or 1001` THEN `s 1025(2)(a) struck off under section 1000 or 1001` ELSE `s 1025(2)(b) struck off under section 1002A`) `the company was carrying on business or in operation when struck off` `the registrar had no reasonable cause to believe the false-basis matter`)
        (`s 1025(3) the second condition is met` `property has vested as bona vacantia` `the Crown representative has consented in writing`)
        (`s 1025(5) the third condition is met` `I have delivered the documents the registrar needs`)
        (`s 1025(5A) the fourth condition is met` `outstanding section 453 penalties have been paid` `each relevant person has paid outstanding fines and penalties`)

@export Under section 1025(4), am I, as the applicant, responsible for the Crown representative's costs?
GIVEN `the cost is for dealing with the property while the company was dissolved` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the cost one of the Crown representative in dealing with the property during the period of dissolution?
      `the cost is for the proceedings on the application` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the cost one of the Crown representative in connection with the proceedings on the application?
      `the cost is demanded as a condition of giving consent` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the cost demanded as a condition of giving consent?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 1025(4), am I, as the applicant, responsible for the Crown representative's costs` IS
    `s 1025(4) the applicant is responsible for paying the cost` `the cost is for dealing with the property while the company was dissolved` `the cost is for the proceedings on the application` `the cost is demanded as a condition of giving consent`

-- s 1026(1): the statement of compliance.
@export Under section 1026(1), does my application for administrative restoration meet the requirement to be accompanied by a statement of compliance?
GIVEN `my application is accompanied by a statement of compliance` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is your application accompanied by a statement of compliance?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 1026(1), does my application for administrative restoration meet the requirement to be accompanied by a statement of compliance` IS
    `s 1026(1) the application meets the requirement to be accompanied by a statement of compliance` `my application is accompanied by a statement of compliance`

-- s 1027(2): when restoration takes effect.
@export Under section 1027(2), from what date does the company's administrative restoration take effect?
GIVEN `the registrar has decided that the company should be restored` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has the registrar decided that the company should be restored to the register?
      `the date the registrar sent notice of the decision` IS A DATE @desc On what date did the registrar send you notice of that decision?
GIVETH A MAYBE DATE
DECIDE `Under section 1027(2), from what date does the company's administrative restoration take effect` IS
    `s 1027(2) the date as from which the restoration takes effect` `the registrar has decided that the company should be restored` `the date the registrar sent notice of the decision`

-- s 1028(2), (4): effect of administrative restoration.
@export Under section 1028(2), is the restored company liable to a section 453 penalty for a financial year whose filing period ended while it was struck off?
GIVEN `the date the filing period for the financial year ended` IS A DATE @desc On what date did the period for filing the accounts and reports for that financial year end?
      `the date of dissolution or striking off` IS A DATE @desc On what date was the company dissolved or struck off?
      `the date of restoration` IS A DATE @desc On what date was the company restored to the register?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 1028(2), is the restored company liable to a section 453 penalty for a financial year whose filing period ended while it was struck off` IS
    `s 1028(2) the company is liable to a penalty under section 453 or any corresponding earlier provision for the financial year` `the date the filing period for the financial year ended` `the date of dissolution or striking off` `the date of restoration`

@export Under section 1028(4), what is the last day to apply to the court for directions after administrative restoration?
GIVEN `the date of restoration` IS A DATE @desc On what date was the company restored to the register?
GIVETH A DATE
DECIDE `Under section 1028(4), what is the last day to apply to the court for directions after administrative restoration` IS
    `s 1028(4) the last day for applying to the court for such directions or provision` `the date of restoration`

-- s 1028A: share warrants on administrative restoration.
@export Under section 1028A(3), must the restored company allot a share?
GIVEN `the company was struck off under section 1000, 1001 or 1002A` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Was the company struck off under section 1000, 1001 or 1002A?
      `the company had a share warrant in issue when struck off` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did the company have any share warrant in issue when it was struck off?
      `the registrar restored the company under section 1025` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has the registrar restored the company under section 1025?
      `the company has no issued share capital after the cancellation` IS A BOOLEAN @desc After the share warrant and the shares it specified are cancelled, does the company have no issued share capital?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 1028A(3), must the restored company allot a share` IS
    `s 1028A(3) the company must allot at least one share in the company`
        (`s 1028A(2) the share warrant and the shares specified in it are cancelled` (`s 1028A(1) section 1028A applies to the company` `the company was struck off under section 1000, 1001 or 1002A` `the company had a share warrant in issue when struck off`) `the registrar restored the company under section 1025`)
        `the company has no issued share capital after the cancellation`

@export Under section 1028A(3), what is the last day for the restored company to allot at least one share?
GIVEN `the date the restoration takes effect` IS A DATE @desc On what date does the restoration take effect?
GIVETH A DATE
DECIDE `Under section 1028A(3), what is the last day for the restored company to allot at least one share` IS
    `s 1028A(3) the last day for allotting at least one share` `the date the restoration takes effect`

@export Under section 1028A(4), what is the last day for the restored company to deliver a statement of capital to the registrar?
GIVEN `the date the restoration takes effect` IS A DATE @desc On what date does the restoration take effect?
GIVETH A DATE
DECIDE `Under section 1028A(4), what is the last day for the restored company to deliver a statement of capital to the registrar` IS
    `s 1028A(4) the last day for delivering the statement of capital` `the date the restoration takes effect`

@export Under section 1028A(10), have I, as an officer or shadow director of the restored company, committed an offence by its default?
GIVEN `the company has made default in complying with section 1028A(3) or (4)` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has the company made default in complying with section 1028A(3) (allotting a share) or (4) (delivering a statement of capital)?
      `I am an officer of the company` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are you an officer of the company (a director, manager or secretary)?
      `I am a shadow director of the company` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are you a shadow director of the company?
      `I authorised or permitted, participated in, or failed to take all reasonable steps to prevent, the default` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did you authorise or permit, take part in, or fail to take all reasonable steps to prevent, the company's default?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 1028A(10), have I, as an officer or shadow director of the restored company, committed an offence by its default` IS
    `s 1028A(10)(b) the officer of the company commits an offence` `the company has made default in complying with section 1028A(3) or (4)` `I am an officer of the company` `I am a shadow director of the company` (JUST `I authorised or permitted, participated in, or failed to take all reasonable steps to prevent, the default`) -- the seam input for section 1121: the person's own statement

-- s 1029(2): who may apply to the court.
@export Under section 1029(2), may I apply to the court to restore the company to the register?
GIVEN `I am the Secretary of State` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are you the Secretary of State?
      `I am a former director` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are you a former director of the company?
      `I have an interest in land in which the company had a superior or derivative interest` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Do you have an interest in land in which the company had a superior or derivative interest?
      `I have an interest in property subject to rights vested in the company` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Do you have an interest in land or other property that was subject to rights vested in the company?
      `I have an interest in property benefited by obligations owed by the company` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Do you have an interest in land or other property that was benefited by obligations owed by the company?
      `but for the dissolution I would be in a contractual relationship with the company` IS A BOOLEAN @desc But for the company's dissolution, would you have been in a contractual relationship with it?
      `I have a potential legal claim against the company` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Do you have a potential legal claim against the company?
      `I am a manager or trustee of a pension fund for the company's employees` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are you a manager or trustee of a pension fund established for the benefit of the company's employees?
      `I am a former member or a personal representative of one` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are you a former member of the company, or the personal representative of one?
      `I was a creditor at the time of striking off or dissolution` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Were you a creditor of the company at the time of its striking off or dissolution?
      `I am a former liquidator` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are you a former liquidator of the company?
      `it appears to the court that I have an interest in the matter` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does it appear to the court that you have an interest in the matter?
      `the company was struck off under section 1003` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Was the company struck off the register under section 1003 (voluntary striking off)?
      `I am of a description specified by regulations as entitled to notice of the application` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are you of a description specified by regulations as entitled to notice of the striking-off application?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 1029(2), may I apply to the court to restore the company to the register` IS
    `s 1029(2) the person may apply to the court for the restoration of the company to the register` grounds `the company was struck off under section 1003` `I am of a description specified by regulations as entitled to notice of the application`
    WHERE
        -- Each ground is listed when the person states it; the list is not closed (the last item of the section lets the court add another person), so a person with no listed ground is NOTHING, never FALSE.
        grounds MEANS
            concat (LIST
                (IF `I am the Secretary of State` THEN LIST `s 1029(2)(a) the Secretary of State` ELSE EMPTY),
                (IF `I am a former director` THEN LIST `s 1029(2)(b) a former director of the company` ELSE EMPTY),
                (IF `I have an interest in land in which the company had a superior or derivative interest` THEN LIST `s 1029(2)(c) a person having an interest in land in which the company had a superior or derivative interest` ELSE EMPTY),
                (IF `I have an interest in property subject to rights vested in the company` THEN LIST `s 1029(2)(d)(i) a person having an interest in land or other property that was subject to rights vested in the company` ELSE EMPTY),
                (IF `I have an interest in property benefited by obligations owed by the company` THEN LIST `s 1029(2)(d)(ii) a person having an interest in land or other property that was benefited by obligations owed by the company` ELSE EMPTY),
                (IF `but for the dissolution I would be in a contractual relationship with the company` THEN LIST `s 1029(2)(e) a person who but for the company's dissolution would have been in a contractual relationship with it` ELSE EMPTY),
                (IF `I have a potential legal claim against the company` THEN LIST `s 1029(2)(f) a person with a potential legal claim against the company` ELSE EMPTY),
                (IF `I am a manager or trustee of a pension fund for the company's employees` THEN LIST `s 1029(2)(g) a manager or trustee of a pension fund established for the benefit of employees of the company` ELSE EMPTY),
                (IF `I am a former member or a personal representative of one` THEN LIST `s 1029(2)(h) a former member of the company (or the personal representatives of such a person)` ELSE EMPTY),
                (IF `I was a creditor at the time of striking off or dissolution` THEN LIST `s 1029(2)(i) a person who was a creditor of the company at the time of its striking off or dissolution` ELSE EMPTY),
                (IF `I am a former liquidator` THEN LIST `s 1029(2)(j) a former liquidator of the company` ELSE EMPTY),
                (IF `it appears to the court that I have an interest in the matter` THEN LIST `s 1029(2) any other person appearing to the court to have an interest in the matter` ELSE EMPTY))

-- s 1030: when the application to the court may be made.
@export Under section 1030, is the time at which I apply to the court to restore the company not a bar to my application?
GIVEN `my purpose is bringing proceedings for damages for personal injury` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is your purpose bringing proceedings against the company for damages for personal injury?
      `my purpose is an insurer's proceedings in the company's name for personal injury damages` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is your purpose an insurer (within the Third Parties (Rights Against Insurers) Act 2010) bringing proceedings against a third party in the company's name in respect of the company's liability for damages for personal injury?
      `the date the company was dissolved` IS A DATE @desc On what date was the company dissolved?
      `the date of my application to the court` IS A DATE @desc On what date is (or was) your application to the court made?
      `the company was struck off under section 1000, 1001 or 1002A` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Was the company struck off under section 1000, 1001 or 1002A?
      `I applied to the registrar for administrative restoration in time` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did you apply to the registrar for administrative restoration within the time allowed?
      `the registrar refused` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did the registrar refuse the application?
      `the date notice of the registrar's decision was issued` IS A DATE @desc On what date was notice of the registrar's decision issued? (Any date if there was none.)
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 1030, is the time at which I apply to the court to restore the company not a bar to my application` IS
    `s 1030 the time at which the application to the court is made is not a bar` anytime
        (`s 1030(4) the application to the court is barred by the period of six years from the date of the dissolution` anytime `the date the company was dissolved` `the date of my application to the court`)
        (`s 1030(5) the application to the court may be made even though the period of six years has expired` `the company was struck off under section 1000, 1001 or 1002A` `I applied to the registrar for administrative restoration in time` `the registrar refused` `the date notice of the registrar's decision was issued` `the date of my application to the court`)
    WHERE
        anytime MEANS `s 1030(1) an application to the court for restoration may be made at any time` `my purpose is bringing proceedings for damages for personal injury` `my purpose is an insurer's proceedings in the company's name for personal injury damages`

-- s 1031(1): may the court order restoration?
@export Under section 1031(1), may the court order the restoration of the company to the register?
GIVEN `the way the company was removed from the register` IS A `s 1031(1) way the company was removed from the register` @desc How was the company removed from the register: struck off under section 1000 or 1001, struck off under section 1002A, struck off under section 1003, or in another way?
      `the company was carrying on business or in operation at the time` IS A BOOLEAN @desc If it was struck off under section 1000 or 1001: was the company carrying on business or in operation at the time?
      `the court considers the registrar had no reasonable cause to believe the false-basis matter` IS A BOOLEAN @desc If it was struck off under section 1002A: does the court consider that, at the time, the registrar did not have reasonable cause to believe the matter in section 1002A(1)(a) or (b)?
      `a requirement of sections 1004 to 1009 was not complied with` IS A BOOLEAN @desc If it was struck off under section 1003: was any of the requirements of sections 1004 to 1009 not complied with?
      `the court considers it just to restore the company` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does the court consider it just to restore the company?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 1031(1), may the court order the restoration of the company to the register` IS
    `s 1031(1) the court may order the restoration of the company to the register` `the way the company was removed from the register` `the company was carrying on business or in operation at the time` `the court considers the registrar had no reasonable cause to believe the false-basis matter` `a requirement of sections 1004 to 1009 was not complied with` `the court considers it just to restore the company`

-- s 1032A: share warrants on restoration by the court (the dates).
@export Under section 1032A(3), what is the last day for the company restored by the court to allot at least one share?
GIVEN `the date the restoration takes effect` IS A DATE @desc On what date does the court's restoration take effect (the date a copy of the order is delivered to the registrar)?
GIVETH A DATE
DECIDE `Under section 1032A(3), what is the last day for the company restored by the court to allot at least one share` IS
    `s 1032A(3) the last day for allotting at least one share` `the date the restoration takes effect`

@export Under section 1032A(6), what is the last day for the company restored by the court to deliver a statement of capital?
GIVEN `the date the restoration takes effect` IS A DATE @desc On what date does the court's restoration take effect (the date a copy of the order is delivered to the registrar)?
GIVETH A DATE
DECIDE `Under section 1032A(6), what is the last day for the company restored by the court to deliver a statement of capital` IS
    `s 1032A(6) the last day for delivering the statement of capital` `the date the restoration takes effect`

@export Under section 1032A(11), have I, as an officer or shadow director of the company restored by the court, committed an offence by its default?
GIVEN `the company has made default in complying with section 1032A(3) or (6)` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has the company made default in complying with section 1032A(3) (allotting a share) or (6) (delivering a statement of capital)?
      `I am an officer of the company` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are you an officer of the company (a director, manager or secretary)?
      `I am a shadow director of the company` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are you a shadow director of the company?
      `I authorised or permitted, participated in, or failed to take all reasonable steps to prevent, the default` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did you authorise or permit, take part in, or fail to take all reasonable steps to prevent, the company's default?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 1032A(11), have I, as an officer or shadow director of the company restored by the court, committed an offence by its default` IS
    `s 1032A(11)(b) the officer of the company commits an offence` `the company has made default in complying with section 1032A(3) or (6)` `I am an officer of the company` `I am a shadow director of the company` (JUST `I authorised or permitted, participated in, or failed to take all reasonable steps to prevent, the default`) -- the seam input for section 1121: the person's own statement

-- s 1033(1): the name on restoration.
@export Under section 1033(1), under what name is the company restored to the register?
GIVEN `the former name would contravene section 66` IS A BOOLEAN @desc At the date of restoration, could the company not be registered under its former name without contravening section 66 (a name the same as another in the registrar's index)?
      `the restoration is administrative` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the restoration administrative (on application to the registrar), rather than by order of the court?
      `another name is specified in the application or order` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is another name specified in the application to the registrar, or in the court's order?
GIVETH A MAYBE `s 1033(2) name on restoration`
DECIDE `Under section 1033(1), under what name is the company restored to the register` IS
    `s 1033(1) the name under which the company is restored to the register` (JUST `the former name would contravene section 66`) `the restoration is administrative` `another name is specified in the application or order` -- the seam input for section 66: the person's own statement

-- s 1033(5)-(6): where the registered number is the name.
@export Under section 1033(5)(a), what is the last day for my company, restored under its registered number, to change its name?
GIVEN `the date of the restoration` IS A DATE @desc On what date was the company restored to the register?
GIVETH A DATE
DECIDE `Under section 1033(5)(a), what is the last day for my company, restored under its registered number, to change its name` IS
    `s 1033(5)(a) the last day for changing the company's name` `the date of the restoration`

@export Under section 1033(6), have I, as an officer of the company, committed an offence by its failure to change its name or give notice?
GIVEN `the company has failed to comply with section 1033(5)(a) or (c)` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has the company failed to change its name within 14 days after restoration (section 1033(5)(a)), or failed to give notice of the change to the registrar (section 1033(5)(c))?
      `I am an officer of the company` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are you an officer of the company (a director, manager or secretary)?
      `I authorised or permitted, participated in, or failed to take all reasonable steps to prevent, the failure` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did you authorise or permit, take part in, or fail to take all reasonable steps to prevent, the company's failure?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 1033(6), have I, as an officer of the company, committed an offence by its failure to change its name or give notice` IS
    `s 1033(6)(b) the officer of the company commits an offence` `the company has failed to comply with section 1033(5)(a) or (c)` `I am an officer of the company` (JUST `I authorised or permitted, participated in, or failed to take all reasonable steps to prevent, the failure`) -- the seam input for section 1121: the person's own statement

-- s 1034: property disposed of before restoration.
@export Under section 1034(1), may I dispose of property that vested in me as bona vacantia, despite the company's possible restoration?
GIVEN `the property or right is vested in me by section 1012 or the Crown's title to it` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the property or right vested in you (as the person to whom it passed from the Crown, the Duchy of Lancaster or the Duke of Cornwall)?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 1034(1), may I dispose of property that vested in me as bona vacantia, despite the company's possible restoration` IS
    `s 1034(1) the person may dispose of the property or right, or of an interest in it, despite the possible restoration of the company` `the property or right is vested in me by section 1012 or the Crown's title to it`

@export Under section 1034(2)(b), what must the Crown or the Duke of Cornwall pay the restored company for property it disposed of, in pounds?
GIVEN `the company is restored to the register` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has the company been restored to the register?
      `consideration was received for the property` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Was any consideration received for the property or right, or the interest in it?
      `the consideration was an amount of money` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Was the consideration an amount of money?
      `the amount of the consideration, in pounds` IS A NUMBER @desc How much was the consideration, in pounds? (Any number if none was received.)
      `the value of the consideration at the time of the disposition, in pounds` IS A NUMBER @desc If it was not money, what was its value at the time of the disposition, in pounds? (Any number if it was money.)
      `the value of the property at the date of the disposition, in pounds` IS A NUMBER @desc If no consideration was received, what was the value of the property, right or interest disposed of at the date of the disposition, in pounds?
GIVETH A MAYBE NUMBER
DECIDE `Under section 1034(2)(b), what must the Crown or the Duke of Cornwall pay the restored company for property it disposed of, in pounds` IS
    `s 1034(2)(b) the amount the Crown or the Duke of Cornwall shall pay to the company, in pounds` `the company is restored to the register` `consideration was received for the property` `the consideration was an amount of money` `the amount of the consideration, in pounds` `the value of the consideration at the time of the disposition, in pounds` `the value of the property at the date of the disposition, in pounds`

@export Under section 1034(3), what is the least the Crown or the Duke of Cornwall must pay after deducting the Crown representative's reasonable costs, in pounds?
GIVEN `the amount payable under section 1034(2)(b), in pounds` IS A NUMBER @desc What is the amount payable to the company under section 1034(2)(b), in pounds?
      `the reasonable costs of the Crown representative, in pounds` IS A NUMBER @desc What are the Crown representative's reasonable costs in connection with the disposition, in pounds?
      `the part of those costs already paid, in pounds` IS A NUMBER @desc How much of those costs has already been paid as a condition of administrative restoration or under a court order for restoration, in pounds?
GIVETH A MAYBE NUMBER
DECIDE `Under section 1034(3), what is the least the Crown or the Duke of Cornwall must pay after deducting the Crown representative's reasonable costs, in pounds` IS
    `s 1034(3) the least the Crown or the Duke of Cornwall must pay to the company after the deduction, in pounds` (JUST `the amount payable under section 1034(2)(b), in pounds`) (`s 1034(3) the most that may be deducted from the amount payable under subsection (2)(b), in pounds` `the reasonable costs of the Crown representative, in pounds` `the part of those costs already paid, in pounds`)

§§ `Part 32: company investigations (there is no seat for an inspector or the Secretary of State; asked only for what a person required to produce documents can say)`

-- s 1038 (section 434 of the Companies Act 1985): what an inspector may require of a person who produces documents.
@export Under section 1038 (section 434(7) of the Companies Act 1985), does the inspector's power to require production of a document that is not in hard copy form include power to require a copy in hard copy form or in a form from which a hard copy can be readily obtained?
GIVEN `the document is not in hard copy form` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the document the inspector asks for not in hard copy form (for example, held on a computer)?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 1038 (section 434(7) of the Companies Act 1985), does the inspector's power to require production of a document that is not in hard copy form include power to require a copy in hard copy form or in a form from which a hard copy can be readily obtained` IS
    `s 1038 s 434(7) the power includes power to require a copy in hard copy form or readily convertible to it` `the document is not in hard copy form`

@export Under section 1038 (section 434(8) of the Companies Act 1985), may an inspector take copies of or extracts from a document I produce?
GIVEN `the document is produced in pursuance of section 434` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the document produced in pursuance of section 434 of the Companies Act 1985 (a requirement of an inspector)?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 1038 (section 434(8) of the Companies Act 1985), may an inspector take copies of or extracts from a document I produce` IS
    `s 1038 s 434(8) the inspector may take copies of or extracts from the document` `the document is produced in pursuance of section 434`

@export Under section 1038 (section 447(9) of the Companies Act 1985), does the Secretary of State's power to require production of a document that is not in hard copy form include power to require a copy in hard copy form or in a form from which a hard copy can be readily obtained?
GIVEN `the document is not in hard copy form` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the document asked for under section 447 of the Companies Act 1985 not in hard copy form (for example, held on a computer)?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 1038 (section 447(9) of the Companies Act 1985), does the Secretary of State's power to require production of a document that is not in hard copy form include power to require a copy in hard copy form or in a form from which a hard copy can be readily obtained` IS
    `s 1038 s 447(9) the power includes power to require a copy in hard copy form or readily convertible to it` `the document is not in hard copy form`

§§ `Part 33: companies not formed under companies legislation (only if your body was formed by an Act, by letters patent or otherwise outside the Companies Acts, and you are thinking of registering it)`

-- s 1040: registering under this Act.
@export Under section 1040, may my company register under this Act as the kind of company I choose?
GIVEN `the company was in existence on 2 November 1862` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Was the company in existence on 2 November 1862 (including a company registered under the Joint Stock Companies Acts)?
      `the company was formed later under another Act of Parliament` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Was the company formed after that date in pursuance of an Act of Parliament other than the Companies Act 2006 or any former Companies Act?
      `the company was formed later under letters patent` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Was the company formed after that date in pursuance of letters patent?
      `the company was otherwise duly constituted according to law` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Was the company formed after that date and is it otherwise duly constituted according to law?
      `the company is registered under Part 4 of the Risk Transformation Regulations 2017` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the company registered under Part 4 of the Risk Transformation Regulations 2017?
      `the company makes an application to register` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does the company make an application to register under the Companies Act 2006?
      `the members' liability is limited by Act of Parliament or letters patent` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the liability of the company's members limited by Act of Parliament or letters patent?
      `the company has fixed share capital` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does the company have a permanent paid-up or nominal share capital of fixed amount?
      `the capital is divided into fixed shares or stock` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the capital divided into shares, also of fixed amount, or held and transferable as stock, or divided and held partly in one way and partly in the other?
      `the members are only the holders of the shares or stock` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Was the company formed on the principle of having for its members the holders of those shares or that stock, and no other persons?
      `the kind of company it would register as` IS A `s 1040(3) kind of registration` @desc Which kind of company would it register as: an unlimited company, a company limited by shares, or a company limited by guarantee?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 1040, may my company register under this Act as the kind of company I choose` IS
    IF     `s 1040(4)(a) the company may register under section 1040` `the members' liability is limited by Act of Parliament or letters patent` joint EQUALS JUST FALSE
       OR  `s 1040(4)(b) the company may register as the kind of company` `the members' liability is limited by Act of Parliament or letters patent` `the kind of company it would register as` EQUALS JUST FALSE
       OR  `s 1040(5) the company may register as the kind of company` joint `the kind of company it would register as` EQUALS JUST FALSE
    THEN JUST FALSE
    ELSE `s 1040(3) the company may register as the kind of company, subject to the following provisions` (`s 1040(2) the company may register under this Act` (`s 1040(1) section 1040 applies to the company` `the company was in existence on 2 November 1862` `the company was formed later under another Act of Parliament` `the company was formed later under letters patent` `the company was otherwise duly constituted according to law` `the company is registered under Part 4 of the Risk Transformation Regulations 2017`) `the company makes an application to register`)
    WHERE
        joint MEANS `s 1041(1) the company is a joint stock company` `the company has fixed share capital` `the capital is divided into fixed shares or stock` `the members are only the holders of the shares or stock`

-- s 1043(1): unregistered companies.
@export Under section 1043(1), does the section on unregistered companies apply to my body?
GIVEN `the body is incorporated in the United Kingdom` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the body a body corporate incorporated in the United Kingdom?
      `the body has its principal place of business in the United Kingdom` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does the body have its principal place of business in the United Kingdom?
      `the body is incorporated by or registered under a public general Act` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the body incorporated by, or registered under, a public general Act of Parliament?
      `the body is not formed to carry on a business for gain` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the body one not formed for the purpose of carrying on a business that has for its object the acquisition of gain by the body or its individual members?
      `the body is exempted by direction of the Secretary of State` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the body for the time being exempted from section 1043 by direction of the Secretary of State?
      `the body is an open-ended investment company` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the body an open-ended investment company?
      `the body is a protected cell company registered under Part 4` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the body a protected cell company registered under Part 4 of the Risk Transformation Regulations 2017?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 1043(1), does the section on unregistered companies apply to my body` IS
    `s 1043(1) section 1043 applies to the body` `the body is incorporated in the United Kingdom` `the body has its principal place of business in the United Kingdom` `the body is incorporated by or registered under a public general Act` `the body is not formed to carry on a business for gain` `the body is exempted by direction of the Secretary of State` `the body is an open-ended investment company` `the body is a protected cell company registered under Part 4`

-- ====================================================================================================
-- seat questions from part coa23 (merged by the lead on 2026-11-12; unchanged text follows)
-- ====================================================================================================
-- coa23-seat.l4: the SEAT LAYER over the coa23 modules, for the Companies Act 2006 (United Kingdom), Part 34 (Overseas companies) and
-- Part 35 (The registrar of companies) up to section 1092B (lines 14666-15484 of ukpga-2006-46.txt).
--
-- SEAT: an individual who is, or is about to become, a director, a company secretary or a member (shareholder) of a company registered under
-- the Act, or who deals with one, asking on facts they can state what the Act requires or lets them do, what rights they have against the
-- company or its directors, what they must disclose, file, approve or vote on and by when, and what follows (liability, offences, penalties) if
-- it is not done. (Assumed, not ruled: the Act is addressed to companies, so the individual is whoever stands in a company's management or ownership.)
-- Provisions that address only an official (the registrar) appear here only for what they mean to that person: what is done with their documents,
-- what they may inspect or require, and what is kept from public view. There is no seat for an official.
--
-- PLAIN INPUTS. Every question takes plain inputs (yes or no, a number, a date, or a choice from the list in its description), one for each fact the
-- person can state. The records the layer-1 modules expect are built inside each question, and the SAME module rule is then called: no rule is restated
-- here. A fact that another part of the Act decides (identity verified under section 1110A, an authorised corporate service provider under section 1098A,
-- whether the registrar may disclose under section 1110F, an officer in default under section 1121, section 4(2) public company) is asked as a plain fact:
-- the person's yes or no is passed to the module as a known answer (JUST yes or JUST no), so a question cannot answer "not covered" for those inputs.
-- Every answer is MAYBE: a "not covered" (NOTHING) is the Act saying nothing, and a caller must never turn it into a no.
-- Figures the Act leaves to regulations or to other law (the general limit in a magistrates' court, fees, levels on the standard scale) are inputs.
--
-- GROUPS (the website groups by the section headings, in the text's order). Where a group arises only in a situation the person may not be in, its heading says so.

-- A choice of one of the three parts of the United Kingdom, from the words the person types. Anything else is not covered.
GIVEN place IS A STRING
GIVETH A MAYBE `Place of registration`
`Under section 1060(3), the part of the United Kingdom named` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF place EQUALS "England and Wales" THEN JUST `England and Wales`
        IF place EQUALS "Scotland" THEN JUST `Scotland`
        IF place EQUALS "Northern Ireland" THEN JUST `Northern Ireland`
        OTHERWISE NOTHING


§ `Part 34 - Overseas companies`
-- Only for a person whose company is incorporated outside the United Kingdom (an overseas company): ask "Is your company incorporated outside the United Kingdom?" before showing this group.

@ref s 1044
@export Under section 1044, is my company an overseas company?
GIVEN `my company is incorporated outside the United Kingdom` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is your company incorporated outside the United Kingdom?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 1044, is my company an overseas company` IS
    `s 1044 the company is an overseas company` `my company is incorporated outside the United Kingdom`

@ref s 1046(2)
@export Under section 1046(2), must the regulations require my overseas company to register its particulars?
GIVEN `my company is incorporated in Gibraltar` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is your company incorporated in Gibraltar?
      `my company opens a branch in the United Kingdom` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does your company open a branch in the United Kingdom?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 1046(2), must the regulations require my overseas company to register its particulars` IS
    `s 1046(2) the regulations must require the company to register particulars` `my company is incorporated in Gibraltar` `my company opens a branch in the United Kingdom`

@ref s 1047(2)
@export Under section 1047(2), may my overseas company register this name?
GIVEN `the name I want to register` IS A STRING @desc Which name do you want to register for your overseas company: "its corporate name" (its name under the law of the country or territory where it is incorporated), "an alternative name specified under section 1048", or "another name"?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 1047(2), may my overseas company register this name` IS
    `s 1047(2) the name may be the registered name of the overseas company` kind
    WHERE
        kind MEANS
            BRANCH
                IF `the name I want to register` EQUALS "its corporate name" THEN `s 1047(2)(a) the company's corporate name`
                IF `the name I want to register` EQUALS "an alternative name specified under section 1048" THEN `s 1047(2)(b) an alternative name specified in accordance with section 1048`
                OTHERWISE `s 1047(2) another name`

@ref s 1047(4)
@export Under section 1047(4), does this section of Part 5 (a company's name) apply to the registration of my overseas company's name?
GIVEN `the number of the section of Part 5` IS A NUMBER @desc What is the number of the section of Part 5 (a company's name) you are asking about, without any letter (for example 66)?
      `the letter after the section number` IS A STRING @desc Does the section number have a letter after it (for example "A" for section 53A)? Enter the letter, or leave it empty.
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 1047(4), does this section of Part 5 apply to the registration of my overseas company's name` IS
    `s 1047(4) the provision of Part 5 applies to the registration of the name of an overseas company` (`s 1047(4) the row of the list for the section of Part 5` `the number of the section of Part 5` `the letter after the section number`)

@ref s 1048(1)
@export Under section 1048(1), may my overseas company register an alternative name?
GIVEN `my overseas company is required to register particulars under section 1046` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is your overseas company required to register its particulars under section 1046?
      `the name is other than its corporate name` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the name you want to register a name other than your company's corporate name?
      `it is the name under which we propose to carry on business in the United Kingdom` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it the name under which you propose to carry on business in the United Kingdom?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 1048(1), may my overseas company register an alternative name` IS
    `s 1048(1) the company may deliver a statement of an alternative name` `my overseas company is required to register particulars under section 1046` `the name is other than its corporate name` `it is the name under which we propose to carry on business in the United Kingdom`

@ref s 1048(3)
@export Under section 1048(3), is the alternative name registered for my overseas company treated as its corporate name in United Kingdom law?
GIVEN `the name is the alternative name for the time being registered` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the name the alternative name now registered for your overseas company under section 1048?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 1048(3), is the alternative name registered for my overseas company treated as its corporate name` IS
    `s 1048(3) the name is treated for all purposes of the law applying in the United Kingdom as the company's corporate name` `the name is the alternative name for the time being registered`

@ref s 1048(5)
@export Under section 1048(5), can legal proceedings against my overseas company be continued or commenced by the name now registered for it?
GIVEN `the proceedings might have been continued or commenced by its corporate name or a name registered before` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Could the proceedings have been continued or commenced against your company by its corporate name, or by a name registered for it earlier?
      `they are continued or commenced by the name now registered` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are they continued or commenced by the name that is now registered for it?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 1048(5), can legal proceedings against my overseas company be continued or commenced by the name now registered for it` IS
    `s 1048(5) the proceedings may be continued or commenced against the company by its name for the time being registered` `the proceedings might have been continued or commenced by its corporate name or a name registered before` `they are continued or commenced by the name now registered`

@ref s 1051(2)(a)
@export Under section 1051(2)(a), must the regulations require my overseas company to disclose the name it has registered?
GIVEN `my overseas company has registered particulars under section 1046` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has your overseas company registered its particulars under section 1046?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 1051(2)(a), must the regulations require my overseas company to disclose the name it has registered` IS
    `s 1051(2)(a) the regulations must require the company to disclose the name registered by it under section 1047` `my overseas company has registered particulars under section 1046`

@ref s 1054(3)(a)
@export Under section 1054(3)(a), may the regulations make a failure by my overseas company punishable by imprisonment?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 1054(3)(a), may the regulations make a failure by my overseas company punishable by imprisonment` IS
    `s 1054(3)(a) the regulations may provide for imprisonment`

@ref s 1055
@export Under section 1055, must the regulations protect the usual residential address of an individual that my overseas company registers?
GIVEN `the regulations require my overseas company to register an individual's usual residential address` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Do the regulations under section 1046 require your overseas company to register the usual residential address of an individual?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 1055, must the regulations protect the usual residential address of an individual that my overseas company registers` IS
    `s 1055 the regulations must contain provision corresponding to that made by Chapter 8 of Part 10` `the regulations require my overseas company to register an individual's usual residential address`

@ref s 1056
@export Under section 1056, what must my overseas company register about people authorised to accept service of documents in the United Kingdom?
GIVEN `there is a person resident in the United Kingdom authorised to accept service of documents on our behalf` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is there a person resident in the United Kingdom who is authorised to accept service of documents on behalf of your overseas company?
GIVETH A STRING
DECIDE `Under section 1056, what must my overseas company register about people authorised to accept service of documents in the United Kingdom` IS
    CONSIDER `s 1056 what the regulations under section 1046 must require the overseas company to register` `there is a person resident in the United Kingdom authorised to accept service of documents on our behalf`
    WHEN `s 1056(a) particulars identifying every person resident in the United Kingdom authorised to accept service of documents on behalf of the company` THEN "particulars identifying every person resident in the United Kingdom authorised to accept service of documents on behalf of the company"
    WHEN `s 1056(b) a statement that there is no such person` THEN "a statement that there is no such person"

@ref s 1059
@export Under section 1059, does moving my overseas company's branch from one part of the United Kingdom to another count as closing one branch and opening another?
GIVEN `the part of the United Kingdom the branch moves from` IS A STRING @desc Which part of the United Kingdom does the branch move from: "England and Wales", "Scotland" or "Northern Ireland"?
      `the part of the United Kingdom the branch moves to` IS A STRING @desc Which part of the United Kingdom does the branch move to: "England and Wales", "Scotland" or "Northern Ireland"?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 1059, does moving my overseas company's branch from one part of the United Kingdom to another count as closing one branch and opening another` IS
    CONSIDER `Under section 1060(3), the part of the United Kingdom named` `the part of the United Kingdom the branch moves from`
    WHEN JUST fromPart THEN
        CONSIDER `Under section 1060(3), the part of the United Kingdom named` `the part of the United Kingdom the branch moves to`
        WHEN JUST toPart THEN `s 1059 the relocation counts as the closing of one branch and the opening of another` fromPart toPart
        WHEN NOTHING THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (silent): the part named is not one of the three parts of the United Kingdom
    WHEN NOTHING THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (silent): the part named is not one of the three parts of the United Kingdom


§ `Part 35 - The registrar of companies`
-- For any person dealing with the registrar of companies.

@ref s 1060(3)
@export Under section 1060(3), which registrar of companies is the registrar for my company?
GIVEN `the part of the United Kingdom where my company is registered` IS A STRING @desc Where is your company registered: "England and Wales", "Scotland" or "Northern Ireland"?
GIVETH A MAYBE STRING
DECIDE `Under section 1060(3), which registrar of companies is the registrar for my company` IS
    CONSIDER `Under section 1060(3), the part of the United Kingdom named` `the part of the United Kingdom where my company is registered`
    WHEN JUST p THEN
        CONSIDER `s 1060(3) the registrar of companies, as the case may require, for the place` p
        WHEN `s 1060(1)(a) the registrar of companies for England and Wales` THEN JUST "the registrar of companies for England and Wales"
        WHEN `s 1060(1)(b) the registrar of companies for Scotland` THEN JUST "the registrar of companies for Scotland"
        WHEN `s 1060(1)(c) the registrar of companies for Northern Ireland` THEN JUST "the registrar of companies for Northern Ireland"
    WHEN NOTHING THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (silent): the part named is not one of the three parts of the United Kingdom

@ref s 1064(1)
@export Under section 1064(1), must the registrar publish notice that a certificate of incorporation has been issued to my company?
GIVEN `a certificate of incorporation has been issued to my company` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has the registrar issued a certificate of incorporation to your company?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 1064(1), must the registrar publish notice that a certificate of incorporation has been issued to my company` IS
    `s 1064(1) the registrar must cause notice of the issue of the certificate to be published` `a certificate of incorporation has been issued to my company`

@ref s 1064(2)
@export Under section 1064(2), does the notice of my company's certificate of incorporation state what it must?
GIVEN `the notice states my company's name` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does the notice state your company's name?
      `the notice states my company's registered number` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does the notice state your company's registered number?
      `the notice states the date the certificate was issued` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does the notice state the date the certificate was issued?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 1064(2), does the notice of my company's certificate of incorporation state what it must` IS
    `s 1064(2) the notice states what it must state` `the notice states my company's name` `the notice states my company's registered number` `the notice states the date the certificate was issued`

@ref s 1064(3)
@export Under section 1064(3), does the registrar publish notice of this kind of certificate of incorporation?
GIVEN `the certificate is one issued` IS A STRING @desc Which certificate: "on the company's formation", "under section 80 (change of name)", "under section 88 (Welsh companies)", "under a provision of Part 7 (re-registration)", or "another certificate"?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 1064(3), does the registrar publish notice of this kind of certificate of incorporation` IS
    `s 1064(3) section 1064 applies to the certificate of incorporation` kind
    WHERE
        kind MEANS
            BRANCH
                IF `the certificate is one issued` EQUALS "on the company's formation" THEN `s 1064(3) the certificate issued on a company's formation`
                IF `the certificate is one issued` EQUALS "under section 80 (change of name)" THEN `s 1064(3)(a) a certificate issued under section 80 (change of name)`
                IF `the certificate is one issued` EQUALS "under section 88 (Welsh companies)" THEN `s 1064(3)(b) a certificate issued under section 88 (Welsh companies)`
                IF `the certificate is one issued` EQUALS "under a provision of Part 7 (re-registration)" THEN `s 1064(3)(c) a certificate issued under any provision of Part 7 (re-registration)`
                OTHERWISE `s 1064(3) another certificate`

@ref s 1065
@export Under section 1065, may I require the registrar to give me a copy of a company's certificate of incorporation?
GIVEN `the copy is of a certificate of incorporation of a company` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the copy you want one of a company's certificate of incorporation?
      `the copy is signed by the registrar or authenticated by the registrar's seal` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Do you want the copy signed by the registrar or authenticated by the registrar's seal?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 1065, may I require the registrar to give me a copy of a company's certificate of incorporation` IS
    `s 1065 the person may require the registrar to provide a copy of the certificate of incorporation` `the copy is of a certificate of incorporation of a company` `the copy is signed by the registrar or authenticated by the registrar's seal`

@ref s 1066(4)
@export Under section 1066(4), has the change of my company's registered number taken effect on this day?
GIVEN `the registrar has notified my company of the change` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has the registrar notified your company of the change of its registered number?
      `the date my company was notified` IS A DATE @desc On what date was your company notified of the change?
      `the day I am asking about` IS A DATE @desc Which day are you asking about?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 1066(4), has the change of my company's registered number taken effect on this day` IS
    `s 1066(4) the change of registered number has effect on the day` `the registrar has notified my company of the change` `the date my company was notified` `the day I am asking about`

@ref s 1066(5)
@export Under section 1066(5), can my company still use its old registered number to meet a trading disclosure requirement?
GIVEN `the date the change of number took effect` IS A DATE @desc On what date did the change of your company's registered number take effect (the date it was notified of the change)?
      `the day the number is disclosed` IS A DATE @desc On which day is the registered number disclosed?
      `the number disclosed is the old number or the new number` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the number disclosed either the old number or the new number?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 1066(5), can my company use the old or new registered number to meet a trading disclosure requirement on this day` IS
    `s 1066(5) the requirement to disclose the registered number imposed by regulations under section 82 or section 1051 is satisfied by the number disclosed` `the date the change of number took effect` `the day the number is disclosed` `the number disclosed is the old number or the new number`


§ `Delivering documents to the registrar`
-- Only for a person who is delivering, or has delivered, a document to the registrar: ask "Are you delivering or have you delivered a document to the registrar?" before showing this group.

@ref s 1067A(1)
@export Under section 1067A(1), am I barred from delivering a document to the registrar on my own behalf?
GIVEN `my identity is verified` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is your identity verified (section 1110A)?
      `the document is accompanied by a statement that my identity is verified` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the document accompanied by a statement that your identity is verified?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 1067A(1), am I barred from delivering a document to the registrar on my own behalf` IS
    `s 1067A(1) the individual is barred from delivering the document to the registrar on their own behalf` (JUST `my identity is verified`) `the document is accompanied by a statement that my identity is verified`

@ref s 1067A(2)
@export Under section 1067A(2), am I barred from delivering a document to the registrar on behalf of a firm or of another individual?
GIVEN `I am delivering the document for a firm` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are you delivering the document on behalf of a firm (answer no if you deliver it for another individual)?
      `I am an officer or employee of the firm` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are you an officer or employee of the firm?
      `I am an officer or employee of a corporate officer of the firm` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are you an officer or employee of a corporate officer of the firm?
      `I am an officer or employee of an authorised corporate service provider` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are you an officer or employee of an authorised corporate service provider?
      `my identity is verified` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is your identity verified (section 1110A)?
      `I am an authorised corporate service provider` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are you yourself an authorised corporate service provider (section 1098A)?
      `my statement says I am an officer or employee of the firm` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does your statement say that you are an officer or employee of the firm?
      `my statement says I am an officer or employee of a corporate officer of the firm` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does your statement say that you are an officer or employee of a corporate officer of the firm?
      `my statement says I am an authorised corporate service provider` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does your statement say that you are an authorised corporate service provider?
      `my statement says I am an officer or employee of an authorised corporate service provider` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does your statement say that you are an officer or employee of an authorised corporate service provider?
      `my statement says I am delivering on the firm's behalf` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does your statement say that you are delivering the document on the firm's behalf?
      `my statement says I am delivering on the other person's behalf` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does your statement say that you are delivering the document on the other person's behalf?
      `my statement says my identity is verified` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does your statement say that your identity is verified?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 1067A(2), am I barred from delivering a document to the registrar on behalf of a firm or of another individual` IS
    `s 1067A(2) the individual is barred from delivering the document to the registrar on behalf of B` whoB facts statements
    WHERE
        whoB MEANS
            IF `I am delivering the document for a firm`
            THEN `s 1067A(2) B is a firm`
            ELSE `s 1067A(2) B is an individual`
        facts MEANS `s 1067A(2) facts about the individual who delivers the document (A)` OF `I am an officer or employee of the firm`, `I am an officer or employee of a corporate officer of the firm`, `I am an officer or employee of an authorised corporate service provider`, (JUST `my identity is verified`), (JUST `I am an authorised corporate service provider`)
        statements MEANS
            concat (LIST
                (IF `my statement says I am an officer or employee of the firm` THEN LIST `s 1067A(2) statement that A is an officer or employee of the firm` ELSE EMPTY)
              , (IF `my statement says I am an officer or employee of a corporate officer of the firm` THEN LIST `s 1067A(2) statement that A is an officer or employee of a corporate officer of the firm` ELSE EMPTY)
              , (IF `my statement says I am an authorised corporate service provider` THEN LIST `s 1067A(2) statement that A is an authorised corporate service provider` ELSE EMPTY)
              , (IF `my statement says I am an officer or employee of an authorised corporate service provider` THEN LIST `s 1067A(2) statement that A is an officer or employee of an authorised corporate service provider` ELSE EMPTY)
              , (IF `my statement says I am delivering on the firm's behalf` THEN LIST `s 1067A(2) statement that A is delivering the document on the firm's behalf` ELSE EMPTY)
              , (IF `my statement says I am delivering on the other person's behalf` THEN LIST `s 1067A(2) statement that A is delivering the document on B's behalf` ELSE EMPTY)
              , (IF `my statement says my identity is verified` THEN LIST `s 1067A(2) statement that A's identity is verified` ELSE EMPTY))

@ref s 1067B(1)
@export Under section 1067B(1), am I barred from delivering documents to the registrar because I am disqualified?
GIVEN `I am disqualified under the directors disqualification legislation` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are you disqualified under the directors disqualification legislation (section 159A(2))?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 1067B(1), am I barred from delivering documents to the registrar because I am a disqualified person` IS
    `s 1067B(1) the individual is barred from delivering documents to the registrar on their own behalf or on behalf of another` `I am disqualified under the directors disqualification legislation`

@ref s 1067B(2)
@export Under section 1067B(2), am I barred from delivering a document to the registrar on behalf of a disqualified person?
GIVEN `the document is delivered on behalf of a disqualified person` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are you delivering the document on behalf of a disqualified person?
      `I am an authorised corporate service provider` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are you yourself an authorised corporate service provider (section 1098A)?
      `I am an officer or employee of an authorised corporate service provider` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are you an officer or employee of an authorised corporate service provider?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 1067B(2), am I barred from delivering a document to the registrar on behalf of a disqualified person` IS
    `s 1067B(2) the individual is barred from delivering the document to the registrar on behalf of the disqualified person` `the document is delivered on behalf of a disqualified person` (JUST `I am an authorised corporate service provider`) `I am an officer or employee of an authorised corporate service provider`

@ref s 1067B(3)
@export Under section 1067B(3), does my document carry the two statements it must?
GIVEN `the document carries my statement that I am not a disqualified person` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does the document carry your statement that you are not a disqualified person?
      `my second statement says` IS A STRING @desc What does your second statement say: "I am delivering on my own behalf", "I am delivering on behalf of another person who is not a disqualified person", "I am delivering on behalf of a disqualified person", or "none"?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 1067B(3), does my document carry the two statements it must` IS
    `s 1067B(3) the document is accompanied by the two statements` `the document carries my statement that I am not a disqualified person` second
    WHERE
        second MEANS
            BRANCH
                IF `my second statement says` EQUALS "I am delivering on my own behalf" THEN `s 1067B(5)(a) a statement that the individual is delivering the document on their own behalf`
                IF `my second statement says` EQUALS "I am delivering on behalf of another person who is not a disqualified person" THEN `s 1067B(5)(b) a statement that the individual is delivering the document on behalf of another person who is not a disqualified person`
                IF `my second statement says` EQUALS "I am delivering on behalf of a disqualified person" THEN `s 1067B(5)(c) a statement that the individual is delivering the document on behalf of a disqualified person`
                OTHERWISE `s 1067B(5) no second statement`

-- RENAMED 2026-11-12: was `Under section 1070(3), must my company deliver this document in accordance with its agreement with the registrar and has it done so`; the question now asks what the function answers (a bar or a duty, not its opposite)
@ref s 1070(3)
@export Under section 1070(3), has my company delivered this document as its electronic delivery agreement with the registrar requires?
GIVEN `an agreement for delivery by electronic means is in force for this document` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is an agreement with the registrar for delivery by electronic means in force for this document?
      `the document is delivered in accordance with the agreement` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the document delivered in accordance with the agreement?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 1070(3), has my company delivered this document as its agreement with the registrar requires` IS
    `s 1070(3) the document is delivered as the section requires` `an agreement for delivery by electronic means is in force for this document` `the document is delivered in accordance with the agreement`

@ref s 1071(1)
@export Under section 1071(1), is my document still not delivered to the registrar?
GIVEN `the registrar has received my document` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has the registrar received your document?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 1071(1), is my document still not delivered to the registrar` IS
    `s 1071(1) the document cannot yet count as delivered to the registrar` `the registrar has received my document`

@ref s 1071
@export Under section 1071, on what day did the registrar receive my document?
GIVEN `the registrar has received my document` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has the registrar received your document?
      `the day my document is regarded as received under the registrar's rules` IS A DATE @desc On what day is your document regarded as received under the registrar's rules?
GIVETH A MAYBE DATE
DECIDE `Under section 1071, on what day did the registrar receive my document` IS
    `s 1071 the day the registrar received the document` `the registrar has received my document` `the day my document is regarded as received under the registrar's rules`

@ref s 1072
@export Under section 1072, does my document meet the requirements for proper delivery?
GIVEN `the contents of my document meet the requirements of the provision I deliver it under` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Do the contents of your document meet the requirements of the provision under which you deliver it?
      `its form, authentication and manner of delivery meet that provision's requirements` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Do its form, authentication and manner of delivery meet that provision's requirements?
      `the person delivering it is one who may deliver it` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the person delivering it one who may deliver a document to the registrar (sections 1067A and 1067B)?
      `it meets the registrar's requirements under section 1068` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does it meet the registrar's requirements as to form, authentication and manner of delivery (section 1068)? Answer yes if none apply.
      `it meets the registrar's rules about delivery together under section 1068A` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does it meet the registrar's rules about documents delivered together (section 1068A)? Answer yes if none apply.
      `it meets any agreement for delivery by electronic means under section 1070` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does it meet any agreement for delivery by electronic means (section 1070)? Answer yes if none apply.
      `it meets the language requirements of the Act` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does it meet the Act's requirements as to language and any certified translation (sections 1102 to 1107)?
      `its names and addresses meet the requirements as to permitted characters` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Do its names and addresses meet the requirements as to permitted characters and any certificate of transliteration (sections 1108 to 1110)?
      `it meets the registrar's requirements as to certification or verification` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does it meet the registrar's requirements as to certification or verification (section 1111)?
      `it meets the requirements of regulations on unique identifiers` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does it meet the requirements of any regulations under section 1082 on unique identifiers? Answer yes if none apply.
      `the fee for its receipt has been paid` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has any fee for its receipt by the registrar been paid? Answer yes if none is due.
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 1072, does my document meet the requirements for proper delivery` IS
    `s 1072 the document meets the requirements for proper delivery` (JUST `the contents of my document meet the requirements of the provision I deliver it under`) (JUST `its form, authentication and manner of delivery meet that provision's requirements`) (JUST `the person delivering it is one who may deliver it`) `it meets the registrar's requirements under section 1068` `it meets the registrar's rules about delivery together under section 1068A` `it meets any agreement for delivery by electronic means under section 1070` (JUST `it meets the language requirements of the Act`) (JUST `its names and addresses meet the requirements as to permitted characters`) (JUST `it meets the registrar's requirements as to certification or verification`) (JUST `it meets the requirements of regulations on unique identifiers`) `the fee for its receipt has been paid`

@ref s 1073(1)
@export Under section 1073(1), may the registrar accept my document although it does not meet the requirements for proper delivery?
GIVEN `my document does not comply with the requirements for proper delivery` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does your document fail to comply with the requirements for proper delivery?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 1073(1), may the registrar accept my document although it does not meet the requirements for proper delivery` IS
    `s 1073(1) the registrar may accept and register the document` `my document does not comply with the requirements for proper delivery`

@ref s 1073(5)
@export Under section 1073(5), does this day count as a day of default for my company after the registrar accepted the document?
GIVEN `a daily default fine or section 453 applies to the failure to deliver` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the provision one that imposes a daily default fine for failing to deliver the document, or is it section 453 (civil penalty for failing to file accounts and reports)?
      `the day the registrar accepted the document` IS A DATE @desc On what day did the registrar accept the document?
      `the registrar issued a notice of administrative removal after accepting it` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did the registrar issue a notice of administrative removal from the register after accepting it?
      `the day the notice was issued` IS A DATE @desc On what day was that notice issued? (Any date if there was none.)
      `the requirements were complied with within 14 days of the notice` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Were the requirements for proper delivery complied with before the end of the 14 days after the notice was issued?
      `the day I am asking about` IS A DATE @desc Which day are you asking about?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 1073(5), does this day count as a day of default for my company after the registrar accepted the document` IS
    `s 1073(5) the day counts as a day of default in complying with the requirements for proper delivery` `a daily default fine or section 453 applies to the failure to deliver` `the day the registrar accepted the document` `the registrar issued a notice of administrative removal after accepting it` `the day the notice was issued` `the requirements were complied with within 14 days of the notice` `the day I am asking about`

@ref s 1073A(1)
@export Under section 1073A(1), may the registrar refuse to accept my document because it is inconsistent with other information?
GIVEN `it appears inconsistent with other information the registrar holds` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does the document appear to the registrar to be inconsistent with other information that the registrar holds or has available?
      `the registrar has reasonable grounds to doubt that it complies with a requirement as to its contents` IS A BOOLEAN @desc In light of the inconsistency, does the registrar have reasonable grounds to doubt that it complies with a requirement as to its contents?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 1073A(1), may the registrar refuse to accept my document because it is inconsistent with other information` IS
    `s 1073A(1) the registrar may refuse to accept and register the document` `it appears inconsistent with other information the registrar holds` `the registrar has reasonable grounds to doubt that it complies with a requirement as to its contents`

@ref s 1074(4)
@export Under section 1074(4), is my document treated as not properly delivered because it contains unnecessary material?
GIVEN `my document contains unnecessary material` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does your document contain material that is not necessary to comply with an obligation and not specifically authorised to be delivered?
      `the unnecessary material can readily be separated from the rest` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Can the unnecessary material readily be separated from the rest of the document?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 1074(4), is my document treated as not properly delivered because it contains unnecessary material` IS
    `s 1074(4) the document is treated as not meeting the requirements for proper delivery` `my document contains unnecessary material` `the unnecessary material can readily be separated from the rest`

@ref s 1076(2)
@export Under section 1076(2), is the registrar barred from accepting my replacement document?
GIVEN `the registrar is satisfied it comes from the person who delivered the original or the company` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the registrar satisfied that the replacement is delivered by the person who delivered the original, or by the company (or other body) the original relates to?
      `the registrar is satisfied it meets the requirements for proper delivery` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the registrar satisfied that the replacement complies with the requirements for proper delivery?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 1076(2), is the registrar barred from accepting my replacement document` IS
    `s 1076(2) the replacement document must not be accepted` `the registrar is satisfied it comes from the person who delivered the original or the company` `the registrar is satisfied it meets the requirements for proper delivery`


§ `Public notice and the register`
-- Public notice of filings, the effect of failing to give it, and what anyone may inspect, copy or have protected on the register. Parts of this group (new directors, a dissolved company, a failure to give the registrar information) arise only in those situations.

@ref s 1077(1)
@export Under section 1077(1), must the registrar publish notice that it has received the document I filed?
GIVEN `the document I filed is an enhanced disclosure document` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the document you filed an enhanced disclosure document (section 1078)?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 1077(1), must the registrar publish notice that it has received the document I filed` IS
    `s 1077(1) the registrar must cause notice of the receipt of the document to be published` (JUST `the document I filed is an enhanced disclosure document`)

@ref s 1078
@export Under section 1078, is the document I filed an enhanced disclosure document?
GIVEN `the subsection of section 1078 that lists it` IS A STRING @desc In which subsection of section 1078 is the document listed: "2", "3", "3A", "4", "4A", "4B" or "5"?
      `the heading of the list` IS A STRING @desc Under which heading is it listed in subsection (2) or (3) (for example "Directors", "Share capital")? Leave empty for other subsections.
      `the item number` IS A STRING @desc Which item number under that heading (for example "2" or "1A")? Leave empty for other subsections.
      `my company is a public company` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is your company a public company?
      `my company is a private company that has applied to re-register as a public company` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is your company a private company that has applied to re-register as a public company?
      `my company has re-registered as a public company` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has your company, a private company, re-registered as a public company?
      `my company must deliver a report under regulation 14 of the 2014 Regulations` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is your company required by regulation 14 of the Reports on Payments to Governments Regulations 2014 to deliver a report or consolidated report?
      `my company must deliver information under regulation 15 of the 2014 Regulations` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is your company required by regulation 15 of those Regulations to deliver information?
      `my company is an overseas company` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is your company an overseas company?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 1078, is the document I filed an enhanced disclosure document` IS
    `s 1078 the document is an enhanced disclosure document` (`s 1078 the head of the list named by its printed number` `the subsection of section 1078 that lists it` `the heading of the list` `the item number`) `my company is a public company` `my company is a private company that has applied to re-register as a public company` `my company has re-registered as a public company` `my company must deliver a report under regulation 14 of the 2014 Regulations` `my company must deliver information under regulation 15 of the 2014 Regulations` `my company is an overseas company`

-- RENAMED 2026-11-12: was `Under section 1079(1), can the company rely on this event against me if it was not officially notified`; the question now asks what the function answers (a bar or a duty, not its opposite)
@ref s 1079(1)
@export Under section 1079(1), is the company barred from relying on this event against me because it was not officially notified?
GIVEN `the event is` IS A STRING @desc What is the event: "an amendment of the company's articles", "a change among the company's directors", "a change of the company's registered office, as regards service of a document on the company", "the making of a winding-up order in respect of the company", "the appointment of a liquidator in a voluntary winding up of the company", or "another event"?
      `the event had been officially notified at the material time` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Had the event been officially notified at the material time?
      `the company shows that I knew of the event at the material time` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does the company show that you knew of the event at the material time?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 1079(1), is the company barred from relying on this event against me because it was not officially notified` IS
    `s 1079(1) the company is barred from relying against the person on the happening of the event` (`s 1079(2) the section applies to the event` kind) `the event had been officially notified at the material time` `the company shows that I knew of the event at the material time`
    WHERE
        kind MEANS
            BRANCH
                IF `the event is` EQUALS "an amendment of the company's articles" THEN `s 1079(2)(a) an amendment of the company's articles`
                IF `the event is` EQUALS "a change among the company's directors" THEN `s 1079(2)(b) a change among the company's directors`
                IF `the event is` EQUALS "a change of the company's registered office, as regards service of a document on the company" THEN `s 1079(2)(c) as regards service of any document on the company, a change of the company's registered office`
                IF `the event is` EQUALS "the making of a winding-up order in respect of the company" THEN `s 1079(2)(d) the making of a winding-up order in respect of the company`
                IF `the event is` EQUALS "the appointment of a liquidator in a voluntary winding up of the company" THEN `s 1079(2)(e) the appointment of a liquidator in a voluntary winding up of the company`
                OTHERWISE `s 1079(2) another event`

-- RENAMED 2026-11-12: was `Under section 1079(3), can the company rely on the event against me soon after official notification if I was unavoidably prevented from knowing of it`; the question now asks what the function answers (a bar or a duty, not its opposite)
@ref s 1079(3)
@export Under section 1079(3), is the company barred from relying on the event against me in the 15 days after official notification because I was unavoidably prevented from knowing of it?
GIVEN `the date of official notification` IS A DATE @desc On what date was the event officially notified?
      `the material time falls on the day` IS A DATE @desc On what day is the material time?
      `the 15th day after notification was a working day` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Was the 15th day after the date of official notification a working day?
      `the next working day after that 15th day` IS A DATE @desc What is the next day after that 15th day that was a working day?
      `I was unavoidably prevented from knowing of the event` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Can you show that you were unavoidably prevented from knowing of the event at that time?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 1079(3), is the company barred from relying on the event against me soon after official notification because I was unavoidably prevented from knowing of it` IS
    `s 1079(3) the company is barred from relying on the happening of the event against the person` `the date of official notification` `the material time falls on the day` `the 15th day after notification was a working day` `the next working day after that 15th day` `I was unavoidably prevented from knowing of the event`

@ref s 1079B(2)
@export Under section 1079B(2), must the registrar notify me that I am named as a director?
GIVEN `the document the registrar registered is` IS A STRING @desc What document did the registrar register: "the statement of proposed officers on formation of the company", "a notice under section 167G that a person has become a director", or "another document"?
      `I am named in it as a director` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are you named in it as a director of the company (or as having become one)?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 1079B(2), must the registrar notify me that I am named as a director` IS
    `s 1079B(2) the registrar must notify the person` kind `I am named in it as a director`
    WHERE
        kind MEANS
            BRANCH
                IF `the document the registrar registered is` EQUALS "the statement of proposed officers on formation of the company" THEN `s 1079B(1)(a) the statement of proposed officers required on formation of a company`
                IF `the document the registrar registered is` EQUALS "a notice under section 167G that a person has become a director" THEN `s 1079B(1)(b) notice under section 167G of a person having become a director of a company`
                OTHERWISE `s 1079B(1) another document`

@ref s 1083(1)
@export Under section 1083(1), may the registrar destroy the hard copy original of the document I filed?
GIVEN `I filed the document in hard copy form` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did you deliver the document to the registrar in hard copy form?
      `the day the registrar received it` IS A DATE @desc On what day did the registrar receive it?
      `the day I am asking about` IS A DATE @desc Which day are you asking about?
      `the information in it has been recorded` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has the information contained in it been recorded by the registrar?
      `a provision named in section 1083(1)(a) to (c) limits the obligation` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does section 1087(3), or section 16A(2) of the Limited Partnerships Act 1907, or section 22(5) of the Economic Crime (Transparency and Enforcement) Act 2022 limit the registrar's obligation to keep this original?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 1083(1), may the registrar destroy the hard copy original of the document I filed` IS
    `s 1083(1) the registrar may destroy the original` `I filed the document in hard copy form` `the day the registrar received it` `the day I am asking about` `the information in it has been recorded` `a provision named in section 1083(1)(a) to (c) limits the obligation`

-- RENAMED 2026-11-12: was `Under section 1084(1A), may the registrar stop making a dissolved company's records available for public inspection on this day`; the question now asks what the function answers (a bar or a duty, not its opposite)
@ref s 1084(1A)
@export Under section 1084(1A), is the registrar no longer required to make a dissolved company's records available for public inspection on this day?
GIVEN `the relevant date` IS A DATE @desc On what date was the company dissolved (or the overseas company ceased to have its connection, or the institution ceased to be within section 1050)?
      `the day I am asking about` IS A DATE @desc Which day are you asking about?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 1084(1A), is the registrar no longer required to make a dissolved company's records available for public inspection on this day` IS
    `s 1084(1A) the registrar need not make the information available for public inspection on the day` `the relevant date` `the day I am asking about`

@ref s 1085(1)
@export Under section 1085(1), may I inspect this material on the register?
GIVEN `the material forms part of the register` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does the material form part of the register?
      `a provision named in section 1085(3) restricts inspection of it` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does section 1087 (protected material), section 1084(1A), or a section about suppressed company names (sections 64(6A), 67(1A), 73(7), 75(4A), 76(5B), 76A(9), 76B(9)) restrict inspection of it?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 1085(1), may I inspect this material on the register` IS
    `s 1085(1) the person may inspect the material on the register` `the material forms part of the register` (JUST `a provision named in section 1085(3) restricts inspection of it`)

@ref s 1085(2)
@export Under section 1085(2), may I inspect the hard copy original of a document on the register?
GIVEN `the original was delivered in hard copy form` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Was the original delivered to the registrar in hard copy form?
      `the registrar's record of its contents is illegible` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the registrar's record of its contents illegible?
      `the registrar's record of its contents is unavailable` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the registrar's record of its contents unavailable?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 1085(2), may I inspect the hard copy original of a document on the register` IS
    `s 1085(2) the right of inspection extends to the original` `the original was delivered in hard copy form` `the registrar's record of its contents is illegible` `the registrar's record of its contents is unavailable`

@ref s 1086(1)
@export Under section 1086(1), may I require a copy of this material on the register?
GIVEN `the material is on the register` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the material on the register?
      `the material is available for public inspection` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the material available for public inspection?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 1086(1), may I require a copy of this material on the register` IS
    `s 1086(1) the person may require a copy of the material` `the material is on the register` `the material is available for public inspection`

@ref s 1086(2)
@export Under section 1086(2), is the fee I was charged for a copy of a company filing within the limit?
GIVEN `the copy is of material derived from an enhanced disclosure document` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the copy of material derived from an enhanced disclosure document (section 1078)?
      `the fee charged for the copy, in pounds` IS A NUMBER @desc What fee were you charged for the copy, in pounds?
      `the administrative cost of providing the copy, in pounds` IS A NUMBER @desc What is the administrative cost of providing the copy, in pounds?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 1086(2), is the fee I was charged for a copy of a company filing within the limit` IS
    `s 1086(2) the fee complies with the limit` `the copy is of material derived from an enhanced disclosure document` `the fee charged for the copy, in pounds` `the administrative cost of providing the copy, in pounds`

@ref s 1087(1)
@export Under section 1087(1), is this material protected from public inspection?
GIVEN `the paragraph of section 1087(1) that lists it` IS A STRING @desc Which paragraph of section 1087(1) lists the material, as printed (for example "za(i)", "b", "ba(ii)", "e(i)", "j(iii)", or "gd, section 12(2A)")?
      `the material forms part of the register` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does the material form part of the register?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 1087(1), is this material protected from public inspection` IS
    `s 1087(1) the registrar must not make the material available for public inspection` (`s 1087(1) the head of the list named by its paragraph` `the paragraph of section 1087(1) that lists it`) `the material forms part of the register`

-- RENAMED 2026-11-12: was `Under section 1087A(3), is this information about my date of birth protected as relevant date of birth information`; the question now asks what the function answers (a bar or a duty, not its opposite)
@ref s 1087A(3)
@export Under section 1087A(3), is this information about my date of birth relevant date of birth information (the kind that section 1087A keeps from public inspection)?
GIVEN `I am a director or proposed director of the company` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are you a director (or proposed director) of the company?
      `I am a registrable person in relation to the company` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are you a registrable person in relation to the company (section 790C(4))?
      `the information is only the day of the month I was born` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the information only the day of the month on which you were born (not the month or year)?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 1087A(3), is this information about my date of birth relevant date of birth information` IS
    `s 1087A(3) the information is relevant date of birth information` person `the information is only the day of the month I was born`
    WHERE
        person MEANS
            IF `I am a director or proposed director of the company`
            THEN `s 1087A(3)(a) a director (or proposed director)`
            ELSE IF `I am a registrable person in relation to the company`
                 THEN `s 1087A(3)(b) a registrable person in relation to the company`
                 ELSE `s 1087A(3) another person`

@ref s 1087C(1)
@export Under section 1087C(1), is the registrar barred from disclosing my date of birth information?
GIVEN `the information is made available for public inspection` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the information made available for public inspection?
      `the disclosure is to a credit reference agency` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the disclosure to a credit reference agency?
      `section 1110F permits the disclosure` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does section 1110F (the registrar's general powers of disclosure) permit the disclosure?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 1087C(1), is the registrar barred from disclosing my date of birth information` IS
    `s 1087C(1) the registrar is barred from disclosing the relevant date of birth information` `the information is made available for public inspection` `the disclosure is to a credit reference agency` (JUST `section 1110F permits the disclosure`)

@ref s 1091(1)
@export Under section 1091(1), must the registrar certify the copy I asked for as a true copy?
GIVEN `the copy is provided under section 1086` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the copy provided under section 1086?
      `I expressly asked for it to be certified` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did you expressly ask for the copy to be certified?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 1091(1), must the registrar certify the copy I asked for as a true copy` IS
    `s 1091(1) the registrar must certify the copy as a true copy` `the copy is provided under section 1086` `I expressly asked for it to be certified`

@ref s 1092B(1)
@export Under section 1092B(1), do I commit an offence by failing to give the registrar the information it required?
GIVEN `I failed to comply with the registrar's requirement under section 1092A` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did you fail to comply with the registrar's requirement under section 1092A?
      `I have a reasonable excuse for failing` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Do you have a reasonable excuse for failing to comply?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 1092B(1), do I commit an offence by failing to give the registrar the information it required` IS
    `s 1092B(1) the person commits an offence` `I failed to comply with the registrar's requirement under section 1092A` `I have a reasonable excuse for failing`

@ref s 1092B(2)
@export Under section 1092B(2), do I commit an offence as an officer of a firm in default when the firm fails to give the registrar the information?
GIVEN `the firm committed the offence under section 1092B` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has the firm committed an offence under section 1092B?
      `I am an officer of the firm` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are you an officer of the firm?
      `I am an officer in default` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are you an officer who is in default (section 1121)?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 1092B(2), do I commit an offence as an officer of a firm in default when the firm fails to give the registrar the information` IS
    `s 1092B(2) an offence is also committed by the officer` `the firm committed the offence under section 1092B` `I am an officer of the firm` (JUST `I am an officer in default`)

@ref s 1092B(3)
@export Under section 1092B(3), what is the longest term of imprisonment, in months, for failing to give the registrar the information?
GIVEN `how I am convicted` IS A STRING @desc How are you convicted: "on indictment", "on summary conviction in England and Wales", "on summary conviction in Scotland" or "on summary conviction in Northern Ireland"?
      `the general limit in a magistrates' court, in months` IS A NUMBER @desc If you are convicted summarily in England and Wales: what is the general limit on a term of imprisonment in a magistrates' court, in months? (The Act does not give the figure. Enter 0 elsewhere.)
GIVETH A MAYBE NUMBER
DECIDE `Under section 1092B(3), what is the longest term of imprisonment in months for failing to give the registrar the information` IS
    CONSIDER `s 1092B(3) the penalty for the offence` mode `the general limit in a magistrates' court, in months`
    WHEN JUST penalty THEN
        CONSIDER penalty's `imprisonment not exceeding`
        WHEN JUST period THEN
            IF period's unit EQUALS Years
            THEN JUST ((period's `number of units`) TIMES 12)
            ELSE JUST (period's `number of units`)
        WHEN NOTHING THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (silent): the text states no term of imprisonment for this conviction
    WHEN NOTHING THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (silent): the text states no penalty for a conviction of this kind
    WHERE
        mode MEANS
            BRANCH
                IF `how I am convicted` EQUALS "on indictment" THEN `on conviction on indictment`
                IF `how I am convicted` EQUALS "on summary conviction in England and Wales" THEN `on summary conviction in England and Wales`
                IF `how I am convicted` EQUALS "on summary conviction in Scotland" THEN `on summary conviction in Scotland`
                IF `how I am convicted` EQUALS "on summary conviction in Northern Ireland" THEN `on summary conviction in Northern Ireland`
                OTHERWISE `on summary conviction`

@ref s 1092B(3)
@export Under section 1092B(3), what fraction of the statutory maximum is the daily default fine for continued failure to give the registrar the information?
GIVEN `how I am convicted` IS A STRING @desc How are you convicted: "on indictment", "on summary conviction in England and Wales", "on summary conviction in Scotland" or "on summary conviction in Northern Ireland"?
GIVETH A MAYBE NUMBER
DECIDE `Under section 1092B(3), what fraction of the statutory maximum is the daily default fine for continued failure to give the registrar the information` IS
    CONSIDER `s 1092B(3) the penalty for the offence` mode 0
    WHEN JUST penalty THEN
        CONSIDER penalty's `daily default fine for continued contravention`
        WHEN JUST fine THEN
            CONSIDER fine
            WHEN `a fine not exceeding the statutory maximum` fraction THEN JUST fraction
            OTHERWISE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (silent): the text states a daily default fine only as a fraction of the statutory maximum
        WHEN NOTHING THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (silent): the text states no daily default fine for this conviction
    WHEN NOTHING THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (silent): the text states no penalty for a conviction of this kind
    WHERE
        mode MEANS
            BRANCH
                IF `how I am convicted` EQUALS "on indictment" THEN `on conviction on indictment`
                IF `how I am convicted` EQUALS "on summary conviction in England and Wales" THEN `on summary conviction in England and Wales`
                IF `how I am convicted` EQUALS "on summary conviction in Scotland" THEN `on summary conviction in Scotland`
                IF `how I am convicted` EQUALS "on summary conviction in Northern Ireland" THEN `on summary conviction in Northern Ireland`
                OTHERWISE `on summary conviction`

-- ====================================================================================================
-- seat questions from part coa24 (merged by the lead on 2026-11-12; unchanged text follows)
-- ====================================================================================================
-- Companies Act 2006 (United Kingdom), 2006 c. 46: the second half of Part 35 (the registrar of companies, ss 1092C to
-- 1120) and Part 36 (offences under the Companies Acts and financial penalties, ss 1121 to 1133) -- THE SEAT LAYER (coa24).
--
-- SEAT: an individual who is, or is about to become, a director, a company secretary or a member (shareholder) of a company
-- registered under the Act, or who deals with one, asking on facts they can state what the Act requires or lets them do, what
-- rights they have against the company or its directors, what they must disclose, file, approve or vote on and by when, and what
-- follows (liability, offences, penalties) if it is not done. (Assumed, not ruled: the Act is addressed to companies, so the
-- individual is whoever stands in a company's management or ownership.) There is no seat for the registrar, the Secretary of
-- State or a court: what they may do appears here only as what it means for this person.
--
-- This layer phrases the rules already encoded in the coa24 modules imported above as the questions that person would ask.
-- Nothing here is new law, and no rule is restated: each question builds the modules' records from plain inputs and calls
-- the module rule.
--
-- PLAIN INPUTS. Every input is a fact the person can state: yes or no, a number, a date, or a choice from the Act's own list.
-- A fact the Act leaves to regulations or to someone else (the amount of a level on the standard scale, the general limit
-- in a magistrates' court, whether regulations except a document) is asked as a plain fact where the person can state it,
-- and the amounts are never taken from memory: the person supplies them. The rules answer JUST TRUE, JUST FALSE or NOTHING
-- ("the Act does not decide this"): a caller must never read NOTHING as "no".
--
-- A PLACEHOLDER: where a module record has a field that no rule reads, a fixed value is given and a comment says so.
-- The one place this happens is `s 1125 amounts the Act leaves to other instruments`: only the level a rule names is read.

-- The three answers about an officer's conduct (s 1121(3)), as the record the modules take.
GIVEN a IS A BOOLEAN, b IS A BOOLEAN, c IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A `s 1121(3) conduct of the officer`
`s 1121(3) the officer's conduct as the person states it` MEANS `s 1121(3) conduct of the officer` WITH
    `s 1121(3) authorises or permits` IS a
    `s 1121(3) participates in` IS b
    `s 1121(3) fails to take all reasonable steps to prevent` IS c

-- The pounds the Act leaves to other instruments, with one amount in every slot. A rule reads only the level (or the
-- statutory maximum) it names, so the other slots are placeholders that no rule reads for that question.
GIVEN amount IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A `s 1125 amounts the Act leaves to other instruments`
`s 1125 the amounts with one figure in every slot` MEANS `s 1125 amounts the Act leaves to other instruments` WITH
    `s 1125 level 1 on the standard scale, in pounds` IS amount
    `s 1125 level 2 on the standard scale, in pounds` IS amount
    `s 1125 level 3 on the standard scale, in pounds` IS amount
    `s 1125 level 4 on the standard scale, in pounds` IS amount
    `s 1125 level 5 on the standard scale, in pounds` IS amount
    `s 1125 the statutory maximum, in pounds` IS amount

-- A period given in months and a flag saying whether the figure is known, as the MAYBE Period the modules take.
GIVEN known IS A BOOLEAN, months IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A MAYBE Period
`s 1131(2) the general limit as the person states it` MEANS
    IF known THEN JUST (Period OF months, Months) ELSE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (points outside the text): a date or limit the person does not know is passed to the rule as NOTHING, and the rule says whether it can decide without it

-- A MAYBE Period shown in months (years are twelve months; any other unit is not shown).
GIVEN term IS A MAYBE Period
GIVETH A MAYBE NUMBER
`s 1131(2) the term shown in months` MEANS
    CONSIDER term
    WHEN NOTHING THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (points outside the text): the term is not stated in the Act and was not supplied
    WHEN JUST p THEN
        CONSIDER p's unit
        WHEN Months THEN JUST (p's `number of units`)
        WHEN Years THEN JUST (p's `number of units` TIMES 12)
        OTHERWISE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (silent): only months and years are shown here

§ `Companies Act 2006: the registrar of companies, offences and penalties -- the questions of a director, secretary, member or person dealing with a company`

-- ======================================================================================================================
§§ `Part 35: statements to the registrar, notices and the register (ss 1092C to 1098)`

-- Arises only if the registrar has required you to give information (s 1092A) and a prosecution follows.
-- s 1092C(1)-(2). A statement you made because the registrar required it may not be used against you in a prosecution, except
-- for the false-statement and perjury offences and any offence of which a false delivery or statement is an element.
@ref s 1092C(1) (the section this question asks about)
@export Under section 1092C(1), is a statement I made in response to the registrar's requirement protected from use against me in criminal proceedings?
GIVEN `I made the statement in response to a requirement under section 1092A` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did you make the statement because the registrar required you to give information under section 1092A?
      `the offence I am charged with` IS A `s 1092C(2) offence` @desc Which kind of offence are you charged with? Choose the false-statement or perjury offence that applies, an offence of which delivering or making a false statement to the registrar is an element, or any other offence.
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 1092C(1), is a statement I made in response to the registrar's requirement protected from use against me in criminal proceedings` IS
    `s 1092C(1) the statement may not be used against the person in the criminal proceedings` `I made the statement in response to a requirement under section 1092A` `the offence I am charged with`

-- Arises only if the registrar has given your company a notice about inconsistent information (s 1093).
-- s 1093(1)(b). The 14 days begin on the day the notice is issued.
@ref s 1093(1)(b) (the section this question asks about)
@export Under section 1093(1)(b), by what date must my company resolve the inconsistency the registrar has told it about?
GIVEN `the date the registrar's notice was issued` IS A DATE @desc On what date was the registrar's notice issued (the date the notice itself states)?
GIVETH A DATE
DECIDE `Under section 1093(1)(b), by what date must my company resolve the inconsistency the registrar has told it about` IS
    `s 1093(1)(b) the last day of the period for resolving the inconsistency` `the date the registrar's notice was issued`

-- s 1093(3)(a). If the necessary documents are not delivered within the period, the company commits an offence.
@ref s 1093(3) (the section this question asks about)
@export Under section 1093(3), has my company committed an offence by not resolving the inconsistency in time?
GIVEN `the registrar gave my company a notice under section 1093(1)` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did the registrar give your company a notice under section 1093(1) about an inconsistency?
      `the notice states the date on which it was issued` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does the notice state the date on which it was issued?
      `the date the notice was issued` IS A DATE @desc On what date was the notice issued?
      `the necessary documents have been delivered` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Have the replacement or additional documents been delivered to the registrar?
      `the date the necessary documents were delivered` IS A DATE @desc On what date were they delivered? (Enter any date if they have not been delivered.)
      `the date on which you are asking` IS A DATE @desc What is today's date, or the date you want the question answered for?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 1093(3), has my company committed an offence by not resolving the inconsistency in time` IS
    `s 1093(3)(a) the company commits an offence` `the registrar gave my company a notice under section 1093(1)` `the notice states the date on which it was issued` `the date the notice was issued` (IF `the necessary documents have been delivered` THEN JUST `the date the necessary documents were delivered` ELSE NOTHING) `the date on which you are asking` -- NOTHING-kind (points outside the text): a date or limit the person does not know is passed to the rule as NOTHING, and the rule says whether it can decide without it

-- s 1093(3)(b). Every officer of the company who is in default also commits the offence.
@ref s 1093(3)(b) (the section this question asks about)
@export Under section 1093(3)(b), have I committed an offence as an officer of my company that did not resolve the inconsistency in time?
GIVEN `the registrar gave my company a notice under section 1093(1)` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did the registrar give your company a notice under section 1093(1) about an inconsistency?
      `the notice states the date on which it was issued` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does the notice state the date on which it was issued?
      `the date the notice was issued` IS A DATE @desc On what date was the notice issued?
      `the necessary documents have been delivered` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Have the replacement or additional documents been delivered to the registrar?
      `the date the necessary documents were delivered` IS A DATE @desc On what date were they delivered? (Enter any date if they have not been delivered.)
      `the date on which you are asking` IS A DATE @desc What is today's date, or the date you want the question answered for?
      `my position in the company` IS A `s 1121(2) position of the person` @desc What is your position: a director, a manager, a secretary, a person treated as an officer of the company for the purposes of section 1093, or none of these?
      `I authorised or permitted the failure` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did you authorise or permit the failure to deliver the documents?
      `I took part in the failure` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did you take part in the failure to deliver the documents?
      `I failed to take all reasonable steps to prevent the failure` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did you fail to take all reasonable steps to prevent the failure?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 1093(3)(b), have I committed an offence as an officer of my company that did not resolve the inconsistency in time` IS
    `s 1093(3)(b) the officer of the company commits an offence` `the registrar gave my company a notice under section 1093(1)` `the notice states the date on which it was issued` `the date the notice was issued` (IF `the necessary documents have been delivered` THEN JUST `the date the necessary documents were delivered` ELSE NOTHING) `the date on which you are asking` `my position in the company` (`s 1121(3) the officer's conduct as the person states it` `I authorised or permitted the failure` `I took part in the failure` `I failed to take all reasonable steps to prevent the failure`) -- NOTHING-kind (points outside the text): a date or limit the person does not know is passed to the rule as NOTHING, and the rule says whether it can decide without it

-- s 1093(4). The fine. The text as published runs two versions of the daily default fine together (one-tenth of level 5, and
-- one-tenth of the greater of 5,000 pounds or level 4), so the person chooses which version to apply, or leaves the choice open.
@ref s 1093(4) (the section this question asks about)
@export Under section 1093(4), what is the most I can be fined for the offence of not resolving the inconsistency?
GIVEN `which version of the text to apply` IS A `s 1093(4) version of the text` @desc The text of section 1093(4) as published runs two versions of the daily default fine together. Choose the version to apply: one-tenth of level 5, or one-tenth of the greater of 5,000 pounds or level 4; or choose the third value if you do not want to choose.
      `this is a second or subsequent summary conviction` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is this a second or subsequent summary conviction for the offence? (On a first conviction the limit is level 5; on a second or later one it is the daily default fine for each day of continued contravention.)
      `days on which the contravention is continued` IS A NUMBER @desc For how many days has the contravention continued?
      `the amount of level 4 on the standard scale, in pounds` IS A NUMBER @desc What is the amount of level 4 on the standard scale, in pounds? (The Act does not state it; only the second version reads it.)
      `the amount of level 5 on the standard scale, in pounds` IS A NUMBER @desc What is the amount of level 5 on the standard scale, in pounds? (The Act does not state it.)
GIVETH A MAYBE NUMBER
DECIDE `Under section 1093(4), what is the most I can be fined for the offence of not resolving the inconsistency` IS
    CONSIDER `s 1093(4) the punishment for the offence under subsection (3)` `which version of the text to apply` amounts
    WHEN JUST penalty THEN `s 1125(2) the most the person can be fined on this conviction, in pounds` penalty `this is a second or subsequent summary conviction` `days on which the contravention is continued` amounts
    WHEN NOTHING THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (silent): the text states two different daily default fines and does not say which applies
    WHERE
        amounts MEANS `s 1125 amounts the Act leaves to other instruments` WITH
            `s 1125 level 1 on the standard scale, in pounds` IS 0 -- Placeholder: no rule reads level 1 here.
            `s 1125 level 2 on the standard scale, in pounds` IS 0 -- Placeholder: no rule reads level 2 here.
            `s 1125 level 3 on the standard scale, in pounds` IS 0 -- Placeholder: no rule reads level 3 here.
            `s 1125 level 4 on the standard scale, in pounds` IS `the amount of level 4 on the standard scale, in pounds`
            `s 1125 level 5 on the standard scale, in pounds` IS `the amount of level 5 on the standard scale, in pounds`
            `s 1125 the statutory maximum, in pounds` IS 0 -- Placeholder: no rule reads the statutory maximum here.

-- s 1094. May the registrar remove material from the register?
@ref s 1094 (the section this question asks about)
@export Under section 1094, may the registrar remove this material from the register?
GIVEN `it appears to the registrar to be a document, or material derived from a document, accepted under section 1073` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does it appear to the registrar that the material is a document (or derived from a document) accepted although it did not meet the requirements for proper delivery (section 1073)?
      `it appears to the registrar to be unnecessary material` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does it appear to the registrar that the material is unnecessary material as defined by section 1074?
      `the registration of the material had legal consequences` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did the registration of the material have legal consequences?
      `the registrar is satisfied that the interest in removing it outweighs the interest of others in its staying` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the registrar satisfied that the interest of the company (or, if different, the applicant) in removing the material outweighs any interest of other persons in the material continuing to appear on the register?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 1094, may the registrar remove this material from the register` IS
    `s 1094(1) and (3) the registrar may remove the material from the register` `it appears to the registrar to be a document, or material derived from a document, accepted under section 1073` (JUST `it appears to the registrar to be unnecessary material`) `the registration of the material had legal consequences` `the registrar is satisfied that the interest in removing it outweighs the interest of others in its staying`

-- Arises only if the registrar has removed something from the register without a court order.
-- s 1094AB(1)-(2).
@ref s 1094AB(1) (the section this question asks about)
@export Under section 1094AB(1), may the court make consequential orders on my application now that the registrar has removed material from the register?
GIVEN `the registrar removed it from the register otherwise than under a court order` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did the registrar remove the material from the register other than because a court ordered it? (Count a registrar's decision that something purportedly delivered was not in fact delivered under an enactment.)
      `I have sufficient interest` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are you a person with sufficient interest in the removal?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 1094AB(1), may the court make consequential orders on my application now that the registrar has removed material from the register` IS
    `s 1094AB(1) the court may make consequential orders on the application` `the registrar removed it from the register otherwise than under a court order` `I have sufficient interest`

-- Arises only if a court has been asked to order material removed from the register.
-- s 1096.
@ref s 1096 (the section this question asks about)
@export Under section 1096, must the registrar remove material from the register under a court order?
GIVEN `the material derives from something the court has declared invalid, ineffective or done without the company's authority` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does the material derive from anything the court has declared to be invalid or ineffective, or to have been done without the authority of the company?
      `a court declares the material factually inaccurate, derived from something inaccurate, or forged` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does a court declare the material to be factually inaccurate, or derived from something factually inaccurate, or forged?
      `the court directs that the material be removed` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does the court direct that the material be removed from the register?
      `the material was delivered under Part 15` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Was the material delivered to the registrar under Part 15 (accounts and reports)?
      `the court has other, specific, powers to deal with the matter` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does the court have other, specific, powers to deal with the matter (for example section 859M on rectification of the register of charges)?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 1096, must the registrar remove material from the register under a court order` IS
    `s 1096 the registrar must remove the material from the register under a court order` `the material derives from something the court has declared invalid, ineffective or done without the company's authority` `a court declares the material factually inaccurate, derived from something inaccurate, or forged` `the court directs that the material be removed` `the material was delivered under Part 15` `the court has other, specific, powers to deal with the matter`

-- s 1097. After a removal order the court may keep a note, or its order, off the public register.
@ref s 1097 (the section this question asks about)
@export Under section 1097, may the court direct that its removal order, or a note about it, be kept from the public register?
GIVEN `the direction asked for` IS A `s 1097 direction` @desc Which direction is asked for: that any related note be removed from the register; that the order itself not be available for public inspection; that no note be made; or that any note be restricted?
      `the court has made an order for removal under section 1096` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has the court made an order for the removal of material from the register under section 1096?
      `a note on the register may cause damage to the company` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Might the presence on the register of the note (or of an unrestricted note) cause damage to the company?
      `public inspection of the order may cause damage to the company` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Might the availability of the court's order for public inspection cause damage to the company?
      `the company's interest in non-disclosure outweighs the interest in disclosure` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does the company's interest in non-disclosure outweigh any interest of other persons in disclosure?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 1097, may the court direct that its removal order, or a note about it, be kept from the public register` IS
    `s 1097(1)-(5) the court may give the direction on these facts` `the direction asked for` `the court has made an order for removal under section 1096` `a note on the register may cause damage to the company` `public inspection of the order may cause damage to the company` `the company's interest in non-disclosure outweighs the interest in disclosure`

-- s 1098. Public notice that a sensitive document has been taken off the register.
@ref s 1098(1) (the section this question asks about)
@export Under section 1098(1), must the registrar publish notice that an enhanced disclosure document has been removed from the register?
GIVEN `the material removed is an enhanced disclosure document, or was derived from one` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the material that was removed an enhanced disclosure document (see section 1078), or material derived from such a document?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 1098(1), must the registrar publish notice that an enhanced disclosure document has been removed from the register` IS
    `s 1098(1) the registrar must cause notice of the removal to be published` (JUST `the material removed is an enhanced disclosure document, or was derived from one`)

-- ======================================================================================================================
§§ `Part 35: authorised corporate service providers (ss 1098A to 1098H)`

-- Arises only if you are, or want to become, an authorised corporate service provider (a person who may verify identities for
-- Companies House filings).
-- s 1098A.
@ref s 1098A (the section this question asks about)
@export Under section 1098A, am I an authorised corporate service provider?
GIVEN `my application to become an authorised corporate service provider has been granted` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has the registrar granted your application to become an authorised corporate service provider?
      `I have since ceased to be one by virtue of section 1098F` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Have you since ceased to be an authorised corporate service provider by virtue of section 1098F?
      `my status is for the time being suspended by virtue of section 1098F` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is your status as an authorised corporate service provider for the time being suspended by virtue of section 1098F?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 1098A, am I an authorised corporate service provider` IS
    `s 1098A the person is an authorised corporate service provider` `my application to become an authorised corporate service provider has been granted` `I have since ceased to be one by virtue of section 1098F` `my status is for the time being suspended by virtue of section 1098F`

-- s 1098B(1).
@ref s 1098B(1) (the section this question asks about)
@export Under section 1098B(1), may I apply to become an authorised corporate service provider?
GIVEN `I am a relevant person as defined by regulation 8(1) of the Money Laundering Regulations` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are you a relevant person as defined by regulation 8(1) of the Money Laundering, Terrorist Financing and Transfer of Funds (Information on the Payer) Regulations 2017?
      `I am applying as an individual` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are you applying as an individual (and not as a firm)?
      `my identity is verified` IS A BOOLEAN @desc If you are an individual: is your identity verified within the meaning of section 1110A? (Ignored for a firm.)
      `I meet any other requirements imposed by regulations` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Do you meet any other requirements the Secretary of State has imposed by regulations for the purposes of section 1098B(1)(c)? (Answer yes if there are none.)
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 1098B(1), may I apply to become an authorised corporate service provider` IS
    `s 1098B(1) the person may apply to become an authorised corporate service provider` `I am a relevant person as defined by regulation 8(1) of the Money Laundering Regulations` `I am applying as an individual` (JUST `my identity is verified`) (JUST `I meet any other requirements imposed by regulations`)

-- s 1098B(4)-(5).
@ref s 1098B(4) (the section this question asks about)
@export Under section 1098B(4), must the registrar grant my application to become an authorised corporate service provider?
GIVEN `my supervisory authority has confirmed that I am known to and supervised by it` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has the supervisory authority (or at least one of them) specified in your application confirmed that you are known to and supervised by that authority?
      `I am applying as an individual` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are you applying as an individual (and not as a firm)?
      `the registrar is satisfied that my identity is verified` IS A BOOLEAN @desc If you are an individual: is the registrar satisfied that your identity is verified (section 1110A)? (Ignored for a firm.)
      `any other conditions specified by regulations are met` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are any other conditions the Secretary of State has specified by regulations for section 1098B(4)(c) met? (Answer yes if there are none.)
      `it appears to the registrar that I am not a fit and proper person` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does it appear to the registrar that you are not a fit and proper person to carry out the functions of an authorised corporate service provider?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 1098B(4), must the registrar grant my application to become an authorised corporate service provider` IS
    `s 1098B(4) the registrar must grant the application` `my supervisory authority has confirmed that I am known to and supervised by it` `I am applying as an individual` `the registrar is satisfied that my identity is verified` (JUST `any other conditions specified by regulations are met`) `it appears to the registrar that I am not a fit and proper person`

-- s 1098C(1).
@ref s 1098C(1) (the section this question asks about)
@export Under section 1098C(1), does my firm's application contain the required information about the firm?
GIVEN `the firm's name` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does the application give the firm name?
      `the firm's principal office` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does it give the firm's principal office?
      `a service address` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does it give a service address?
      `an email address` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does it give an email address?
      `the firm's legal form and governing law` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does it give the legal form of the firm and the law by which it is governed?
      `the firm's registration number under regulation 54 or 55` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does it give any registration number allocated to the firm under regulation 54 or 55 of the Money Laundering Regulations? (Answer yes if none was allocated.)
      `any other register the firm is entered in` IS A BOOLEAN @desc If the firm is entered in any other register, does it give details of the state and its registration number there? (Answer yes if it is not.)
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 1098C(1), does my firm's application contain the required information about the firm` IS
    `s 1098C(1) the application contains the required information about the firm` particulars
    WHERE
        particulars MEANS `s 1098C(1) particulars supplied for a firm` WITH
            `s 1098C(1)(a) firm name` IS `the firm's name`
            `s 1098C(1)(b) principal office` IS `the firm's principal office`
            `s 1098C(1)(c) a service address` IS `a service address`
            `s 1098C(1)(d) an email address` IS `an email address`
            `s 1098C(1)(e) the legal form of the firm and the law by which it is governed` IS `the firm's legal form and governing law`
            `s 1098C(1)(ea) any registration number allocated to the firm under regulation 54 or 55 of the Money Laundering Regulations` IS `the firm's registration number under regulation 54 or 55`
            `s 1098C(1)(f) if applicable, any other register in which it is entered (including details of the state) and its registration number in that register` IS `any other register the firm is entered in`

-- s 1098C(2)-(4).
@ref s 1098C(2) (the section this question asks about)
@export Under section 1098C(2), does my application contain the required information about me as an individual?
GIVEN `my forename and surname` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does the application give your forename and surname?
      `I am a peer or usually known by a title` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are you a peer, or an individual usually known by a title?
      `my title instead of my forename and surname` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does the application give your title instead of your forename and surname?
      `my nationality` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does it give your nationality?
      `my date of birth` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does it give your date of birth?
      `a service address` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does it give a service address?
      `an email address` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does it give an email address?
      `where I am usually resident` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does it give the part of the United Kingdom in which you are usually resident or, if you are usually resident outside the United Kingdom, that country or state?
      `my registration number under regulation 54 or 55` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does it give any registration number allocated to you under regulation 54 or 55 of the Money Laundering Regulations? (Answer yes if none was allocated.)
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 1098C(2), does my application contain the required information about me as an individual` IS
    `s 1098C(2) the application contains the required information about the individual` (`s 1098C(3) the name supplied meets the requirement to contain the applicant's name` `my forename and surname` `I am a peer or usually known by a title` `my title instead of my forename and surname` EQUALS JUST TRUE) particulars
    -- The name rule of s 1098C(3) and (4) answers only JUST TRUE or JUST FALSE, so reading it as a plain yes or no loses nothing.
    WHERE
        particulars MEANS `s 1098C(2) particulars supplied for an individual` WITH
            `s 1098C(2)(a) nationality` IS `my nationality`
            `s 1098C(2)(a) date of birth` IS `my date of birth`
            `s 1098C(2)(b) a service address` IS `a service address`
            `s 1098C(2)(c) an email address` IS `an email address`
            `s 1098C(2)(d) the part of the United Kingdom in which the person is usually resident or, if usually resident outside the United Kingdom, that country or state` IS `where I am usually resident`
            `s 1098C(2)(e) any registration number allocated to the individual under regulation 54 or 55 of the Money Laundering Regulations` IS `my registration number under regulation 54 or 55`

-- s 1098D.
@ref s 1098D (the section this question asks about)
@export Under section 1098D, is my firm's application delivered in the way the Act requires?
GIVEN `the kind of firm` IS A `s 1098D firm` @desc What kind of firm is applying: a company, a body corporate other than a company, a limited partnership, any other partnership, or an unincorporated body other than a partnership?
      `the body's affairs are managed by its members` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are the body's affairs managed by its members? (Ignored for a company and for a partnership.)
      `the position of the person who delivers it` IS A `s 1098D position of the individual` @desc What is the position of the person who delivers the application on the firm's behalf (director, member of the body, officer corresponding to a director, general partner, member of the partnership, member of the governing body, or another position)?
      `that person is an individual` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the person who delivers it an individual?
      `the application is accompanied by their statement of status` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the application accompanied by a statement by that individual confirming their status as a relevant officer of the firm?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 1098D, is my firm's application delivered in the way the Act requires` IS
    `s 1098D the application meets the delivery requirements of s 1098D` `the kind of firm` `the body's affairs are managed by its members` `the position of the person who delivers it` `that person is an individual` `the application is accompanied by their statement of status`

-- Arises only if you are an authorised corporate service provider whose supervisory authority has changed.
-- s 1098E(1)-(2).
@ref s 1098E(1) (the section this question asks about)
@export Under section 1098E(1), by what date must I notify the registrar of the change in my supervisory authority?
GIVEN `the change is the result of an agreement under regulation 7(2)` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the change the result of an agreement under regulation 7(2) of the Money Laundering Regulations (another authority agreeing to act)?
      `the date the change occurs` IS A DATE @desc On what date does the change occur?
      `the authority has notified me or published the agreement` IS A BOOLEAN @desc If the change is the result of such an agreement: has the authority that agreed to act notified you, or published the agreement (regulation 7(3))? (Ignored otherwise.)
      `the date it notified me or published the agreement` IS A DATE @desc On what date did it do so? (Enter any date if it has not.)
GIVETH A MAYBE DATE
DECIDE `Under section 1098E(1), by what date must I notify the registrar of the change in my supervisory authority` IS
    `s 1098E(1)-(2) the last day for notifying the registrar of the change` `the change is the result of an agreement under regulation 7(2)` `the date the change occurs` (IF `the authority has notified me or published the agreement` THEN JUST `the date it notified me or published the agreement` ELSE NOTHING) -- NOTHING-kind (points outside the text): a date or limit the person does not know is passed to the rule as NOTHING, and the rule says whether it can decide without it

-- s 1098E(1)-(3).
@ref s 1098E(3) (the section this question asks about)
@export Under section 1098E(3), have I committed an offence by not notifying the registrar of the change in my supervisory authority in time?
GIVEN `I am an authorised corporate service provider` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are you an authorised corporate service provider?
      `the change is the result of an agreement under regulation 7(2)` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the change the result of an agreement under regulation 7(2) of the Money Laundering Regulations?
      `the date the change occurs` IS A DATE @desc On what date does the change occur?
      `the authority has notified me or published the agreement` IS A BOOLEAN @desc If the change is the result of such an agreement: has the authority notified you, or published the agreement (regulation 7(3))? (Ignored otherwise.)
      `the date it notified me or published the agreement` IS A DATE @desc On what date did it do so? (Enter any date if it has not.)
      `I have notified the registrar` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Have you notified the registrar of the change?
      `the date I notified the registrar` IS A DATE @desc On what date did you notify the registrar? (Enter any date if you have not.)
      `the date on which you are asking` IS A DATE @desc What is today's date, or the date you want the question answered for?
      `I have no reasonable excuse` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it true that you have no reasonable excuse for failing to notify the registrar in time?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 1098E(3), have I committed an offence by not notifying the registrar of the change in my supervisory authority in time` IS
    `s 1098E(1)-(3) the person commits an offence by failing to notify the registrar in time` `I am an authorised corporate service provider` `the change is the result of an agreement under regulation 7(2)` `the date the change occurs` (IF `the authority has notified me or published the agreement` THEN JUST `the date it notified me or published the agreement` ELSE NOTHING) (IF `I have notified the registrar` THEN JUST `the date I notified the registrar` ELSE NOTHING) `the date on which you are asking` `I have no reasonable excuse` -- NOTHING-kind (points outside the text): a date or limit the person does not know is passed to the rule as NOTHING, and the rule says whether it can decide without it

-- s 1098E(4).
@ref s 1098E(4) (the section this question asks about)
@export Under section 1098E(4), as an officer of an authorised corporate service provider that is a firm, have I also committed the offence?
GIVEN `the offence was committed by` IS A `Kind of person` @desc What committed the offence: an individual, a company registered under the Companies Act 2006, another UK body corporate, a body corporate incorporated outside the UK, a corporation sole, a partnership or an unincorporated association?
      `the firm committed the offence of failing to notify the registrar in time` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did the firm commit the offence under section 1098E(3)?
      `my position in the firm` IS A `s 1121(2) position of the person` @desc What is your position: a director, a manager, a secretary, a person treated as an officer of the firm for the purposes of section 1098E, or none of these?
      `I authorised or permitted the failure` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did you authorise or permit the failure to notify the registrar?
      `I took part in the failure` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did you take part in the failure?
      `I failed to take all reasonable steps to prevent the failure` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did you fail to take all reasonable steps to prevent the failure?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 1098E(4), as an officer of an authorised corporate service provider that is a firm, have I also committed the offence` IS
    `s 1098E(4) the officer of the firm who is in default also commits the offence` `the offence was committed by` (JUST `the firm committed the offence of failing to notify the registrar in time`) `my position in the firm` (`s 1121(3) the officer's conduct as the person states it` `I authorised or permitted the failure` `I took part in the failure` `I failed to take all reasonable steps to prevent the failure`)

-- s 1098E(5) with s 1125(2). The fine for the offence. England and Wales: a fine with no stated limit, so no number.
@ref s 1098E(5) (the section this question asks about)
@export Under section 1098E(5), what is the most I can be fined on summary conviction for failing to notify the registrar of the change?
GIVEN `where I would be convicted` IS A `Place of registration` @desc Where would you be convicted: England and Wales, Scotland or Northern Ireland?
      `this is a second or subsequent summary conviction` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is this a second or subsequent summary conviction for the offence?
      `days on which the contravention is continued` IS A NUMBER @desc For how many days has the contravention continued?
      `the amount of level 5 on the standard scale, in pounds` IS A NUMBER @desc What is the amount of level 5 on the standard scale, in pounds? (The Act does not state it.)
GIVETH A MAYBE NUMBER
DECIDE `Under section 1098E(5), what is the most I can be fined on summary conviction for failing to notify the registrar of the change` IS
    `s 1125(2) the most the person can be fined on this conviction, in pounds` (`s 1098E(5) the punishment on summary conviction` `where I would be convicted`) `this is a second or subsequent summary conviction` `days on which the contravention is continued` (`s 1125 the amounts with one figure in every slot` `the amount of level 5 on the standard scale, in pounds`)

-- s 1098F(1).
@ref s 1098F(1) (the section this question asks about)
@export Under section 1098F(1), do I cease to be an authorised corporate service provider?
GIVEN `I cease to be a relevant person under regulation 8(1) of the Money Laundering Regulations` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Do you cease to be a relevant person as defined by regulation 8(1) of the Money Laundering Regulations?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 1098F(1), do I cease to be an authorised corporate service provider` IS
    `s 1098F(1) the person ceases to be an authorised corporate service provider` `I cease to be a relevant person under regulation 8(1) of the Money Laundering Regulations`

-- ======================================================================================================================
§§ `Part 35: the index of company names, languages and identity verification (ss 1099 to 1110D)`

-- s 1099.
@ref s 1099 (the section this question asks about)
@export Under section 1099, must the registrar keep my body's name in the index of company names?
GIVEN `my body is` IS A `s 1099 kind of body` @desc What is your body: a UK-registered company, an unregistered company under section 1043, an overseas company with registered particulars, a limited partnership, an LLP, a UK EEIG, an EEIG establishment, an OEIC, a registered society, a protected cell company, a charitable incorporated organisation, a Scottish CIO, or another body?
      `it appears to the registrar not to be required to register particulars` IS A BOOLEAN @desc If you are an overseas company: does it appear to the registrar that you are not required to register particulars under section 1046? (Ignored otherwise.)
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 1099, must the registrar keep my body's name in the index of company names` IS
    `s 1099(1) the registrar must keep the body's name in the index` (`s 1099(2)-(3) the section applies to the body` `my body is` `it appears to the registrar not to be required to register particulars`)

-- s 1100.
@ref s 1100 (the section this question asks about)
@export Under section 1100, may I inspect the registrar's index of company names?
GIVEN `I am` IS A `Kind of person` @desc What are you: an individual, a company registered under the Companies Act 2006, another UK body corporate, a body corporate incorporated outside the UK, a corporation sole, a partnership or an unincorporated association?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 1100, may I inspect the registrar's index of company names` IS
    `s 1100 the person may inspect the registrar's index of company names` `I am`

-- s 1103 with ss 1104(1) and 1105(2).
@ref s 1103 (the section this question asks about)
@export Under section 1103, must my document be drawn up and delivered in English?
GIVEN `the document relates to a Welsh company` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does the document relate to a Welsh company?
      `the kind of document` IS A `s 1105(2) description of document` @desc Is the document an agreement affecting the company's constitution (Chapter 3 of Part 3), group accounts under section 400 or 401, a certified copy of a company charge (Part 25), a document of a description specified in regulations, or another document?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 1103, must my document be drawn up and delivered in English` IS
    `s 1103 the document must be drawn up and delivered in English` (`s 1104(1) the document may be drawn up and delivered in Welsh` (JUST `the document relates to a Welsh company`)) (`s 1105(1) the document may be drawn up and delivered in a language other than English` (`s 1105(2) the section applies to the document` `the kind of document`))

-- Arises only if the document relates to a Welsh company and is delivered in Welsh.
-- s 1104(2).
@ref s 1104(2) (the section this question asks about)
@export Under section 1104(2), must my Welsh-language document be accompanied by a certified translation into English?
GIVEN `the document relating to a Welsh company is delivered in Welsh` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the document, which relates to a Welsh company, delivered in Welsh?
      `the document is of a description the regulations except` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the document of a description the Secretary of State's regulations except from the requirement of a certified translation?
      `the document is in a form prescribed in Welsh under section 26 of the Welsh Language Act 1993` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the document in a form prescribed in Welsh (or partly in Welsh and partly in English) by virtue of section 26 of the Welsh Language Act 1993?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 1104(2), must my Welsh-language document be accompanied by a certified translation into English` IS
    `s 1104(2) the document must be accompanied by a certified translation into English` `the document relating to a Welsh company is delivered in Welsh` (JUST `the document is of a description the regulations except`) `the document is in a form prescribed in Welsh under section 26 of the Welsh Language Act 1993`

-- s 1105(1)-(2).
@ref s 1105(1) (the section this question asks about)
@export Under section 1105(1), may I deliver my document to the registrar in a language other than English?
GIVEN `the kind of document` IS A `s 1105(2) description of document` @desc Is the document an agreement affecting the company's constitution (Chapter 3 of Part 3), group accounts under section 400 or 401, a certified copy of a company charge (Part 25), a document of a description specified in regulations, or another document?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 1105(1), may I deliver my document to the registrar in a language other than English` IS
    `s 1105(1) the document may be drawn up and delivered in a language other than English` (`s 1105(2) the section applies to the document` `the kind of document`)

@ref s 1105(1) (the section this question asks about)
@export Under section 1105(1), does my delivery in another language meet the requirement of a certified translation into English?
GIVEN `the kind of document` IS A `s 1105(2) description of document` @desc Is the document an agreement affecting the company's constitution (Chapter 3 of Part 3), group accounts under section 400 or 401, a certified copy of a company charge (Part 25), a document of a description specified in regulations, or another document?
      `the document is delivered in a language other than English` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the document delivered in a language other than English?
      `it is accompanied by a certified translation into English` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it accompanied by a certified translation into English?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 1105(1), does my delivery in another language meet the requirement of a certified translation into English` IS
    `s 1105(1) the delivery meets the requirement of s 1105(1)` (`s 1105(2) the section applies to the document` `the kind of document`) `the document is delivered in a language other than English` `it is accompanied by a certified translation into English`

-- s 1106(1).
@ref s 1106(1) (the section this question asks about)
@export Under section 1106(1), may my company deliver a certified translation of a document it has already delivered?
GIVEN `the document relates to my company and is or has been delivered to the registrar` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does the document relate to your company, and is it (or has it been) delivered to the registrar?
      `the regulations make the facility available for this language and kind of document` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Do the Secretary of State's regulations make the voluntary filing of translations available for this language and kind of document?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 1106(1), may my company deliver a certified translation of a document it has already delivered` IS
    `s 1106(1) the company may deliver certified translations of the document` `the document relates to my company and is or has been delivered to the registrar` (JUST `the regulations make the facility available for this language and kind of document`)

-- Arises only if a document and its certified translation differ.
-- s 1107(2).
@ref s 1107(2)(a) (the section this question asks about)
@export Under section 1107(2)(a), may my company rely on a certified translation against a third party where it differs from the original?
GIVEN `the translation differs from the original language version` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is there a discrepancy between the original language version of the document and the certified translation?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 1107(2)(a), may my company rely on a certified translation against a third party where it differs from the original` IS
    `s 1107(2)(a) the company may rely on the translation as against a third party` `the translation differs from the original language version`

@ref s 1107(2)(b) (the section this question asks about)
@export Under section 1107(2)(b), may I, as a third party, rely on a certified translation that differs from the original?
GIVEN `the translation differs from the original language version` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is there a discrepancy between the original language version of the document and the certified translation?
      `the company shows that I knew the original` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does the company show that you, as the third party, had knowledge of the original?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 1107(2)(b), may I, as a third party, rely on a certified translation that differs from the original` IS
    `s 1107(2)(b) the third party may rely on the translation` `the translation differs from the original language version` `the company shows that I knew the original`

-- s 1108(1).
@ref s 1108(1) (the section this question asks about)
@export Under section 1108(1), do the names and addresses in my document use only permitted letters, characters and symbols?
GIVEN `every letter, character and symbol is permitted` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is every letter, character and symbol in the names and addresses in your document (including accents and other diacritical marks) one that is permitted under the Secretary of State's regulations?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 1108(1), do the names and addresses in my document use only permitted letters, characters and symbols` IS
    `s 1108(1) the names and addresses meet the requirement of s 1108(1)` (JUST `every letter, character and symbol is permitted`)

-- s 1109(1).
@ref s 1109(1) (the section this question asks about)
@export Under section 1109(1), may my company deliver a transliteration of a name or address into Roman characters?
GIVEN `a name or address was delivered in a permitted form using other than Roman characters` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is a name or address of your company (or other body) delivered, or already delivered, to the registrar in a permitted form using other than Roman characters?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 1109(1), may my company deliver a transliteration of a name or address into Roman characters` IS
    `s 1109(1) the company or other body may deliver a transliteration into Roman characters` `a name or address was delivered in a permitted form using other than Roman characters`

-- Arises when you are a director, or deal with a company, and the question is whether your identity is verified for Companies House.
-- s 1110A(1).
@ref s 1110A(1) (the section this question asks about)
@export Under section 1110A(1), is my identity verified?
GIVEN `the registrar has verified my identity under the regulations` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has the registrar verified your identity in accordance with regulations under section 1110B?
      `a verification statement about me has been delivered to the registrar` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has an authorised corporate service provider's verification statement in respect of you been delivered to the registrar?
      `regulations have since ended my verified status` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Have regulations under section 1110A(6) since ended your status as an individual whose identity is verified?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 1110A(1), is my identity verified` IS
    `s 1110A(1) the individual's identity is verified` `the registrar has verified my identity under the regulations` `a verification statement about me has been delivered to the registrar` (JUST `regulations have since ended my verified status`)

-- Arises only if the Secretary of State has given you a written notice on grounds of national security or serious crime.
-- s 1110C(2).
@ref s 1110C(2) (the section this question asks about)
@export Under section 1110C(2), does the Secretary of State's notice relieve me of this identity-verification requirement?
GIVEN `the requirement` IS A `s 1110C(2) effect of the notice` @desc Which requirement: the statement of identity verification for a director named in a statement of proposed officers (section 12(2A)); section 167G(3)(c); section 167M; section 167N(1); section 1067A; or section 1098B(2)(c)?
      `the notice provides for that effect` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does the notice given to you provide for that effect?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 1110C(2), does the Secretary of State's notice relieve me of this identity-verification requirement` IS
    `s 1110C(2) the effect applies in relation to the person` `the requirement` `the notice provides for that effect`

-- ======================================================================================================================
§§ `Part 35: disclosure, false statements and delivering documents (ss 1110E to 1119)`

-- s 1110E.
@ref s 1110E (the section this question asks about)
@export Under section 1110E, may I disclose information to the registrar?
GIVEN `the disclosure is for the purposes of the exercise of any of the registrar's functions` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the disclosure for the purposes of the exercise of any of the registrar's functions?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 1110E, may I disclose information to the registrar` IS
    `s 1110E the person may disclose the information to the registrar` `the disclosure is for the purposes of the exercise of any of the registrar's functions`

-- s 1110G(1)-(2).
@ref s 1110G(1) (the section this question asks about)
@export Under section 1110G(1), does my disclosure to the registrar breach a duty of confidence or another restriction on disclosure?
GIVEN `the disclosure was made under section 1110E or 1110F` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Was the disclosure made to the registrar under section 1110E (or by the registrar under section 1110F)?
      `the disclosure would contravene the data protection legislation` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Would the disclosure contravene the data protection legislation (taking into account the powers conferred by sections 1110E and 1110F)?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 1110G(1), does my disclosure to the registrar breach a duty of confidence or another restriction on disclosure` IS
    `s 1110G(1) the disclosure breaches an obligation of confidence or any other restriction on the disclosure of information` `the disclosure was made under section 1110E or 1110F` `the disclosure would contravene the data protection legislation`

-- Arises only if the registrar disclosed to you information that HM Revenue and Customs had given the registrar.
-- s 1110G(5).
@ref s 1110G(5) (the section this question asks about)
@export Under section 1110G(5), have I committed an offence by disclosing HMRC information?
GIVEN `I disclosed revenue and customs information in contravention of section 1110G(3) or (4)` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did you disclose revenue and customs information in contravention of section 1110G(3) or (4) (without authorisation from HMRC)?
      `the information identifies a person or lets a person be identified` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does the information relate to a person whose identity is specified in the disclosure or can be deduced from it?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 1110G(5), have I committed an offence by disclosing HMRC information` IS
    `s 1110G(5) the person commits an offence` `I disclosed revenue and customs information in contravention of section 1110G(3) or (4)` `the information identifies a person or lets a person be identified`

-- s 1110G(6).
@ref s 1110G(6) (the section this question asks about)
@export Under section 1110G(6), do I have a defence to the offence of disclosing HMRC information?
GIVEN `I prove that I reasonably believed the disclosure was lawful` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Can you prove that you reasonably believed the disclosure was lawful?
      `I prove that I reasonably believed the information was already lawfully public` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Can you prove that you reasonably believed the information had already lawfully been made available to the public?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 1110G(6), do I have a defence to the offence of disclosing HMRC information` IS
    `s 1110G(6) this section gives a defence` `I prove that I reasonably believed the disclosure was lawful` `I prove that I reasonably believed the information was already lawfully public`

-- s 1112(1).
@ref s 1112(1) (the section this question asks about)
@export Under section 1112(1), have I committed an offence by giving the registrar a false, misleading or deceptive document or statement?
GIVEN `I delivered, or caused to be delivered, a document to the registrar for a purpose of the Companies Acts` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did you deliver, or cause to be delivered, a document to the registrar for a purpose of the Companies Acts?
      `I made a statement to the registrar for a purpose of the Companies Acts` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did you make a statement to the registrar for a purpose of the Companies Acts?
      `it is misleading, false or deceptive in a material particular` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the document or statement misleading, false or deceptive in a material particular?
      `I had a reasonable excuse` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did you have a reasonable excuse?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 1112(1), have I committed an offence by giving the registrar a false, misleading or deceptive document or statement` IS
    `s 1112(1) the person commits the offence` `I delivered, or caused to be delivered, a document to the registrar for a purpose of the Companies Acts` `I made a statement to the registrar for a purpose of the Companies Acts` `it is misleading, false or deceptive in a material particular` `I had a reasonable excuse`

-- s 1112(2).
@ref s 1112(2) (the section this question asks about)
@export Under section 1112(2), as an officer of a firm that gave the registrar a false document or statement, have I also committed the offence?
GIVEN `the offence was committed by` IS A `Kind of person` @desc What committed the offence: an individual, a company registered under the Companies Act 2006, another UK body corporate, a body corporate incorporated outside the UK, a corporation sole, a partnership or an unincorporated association?
      `the firm committed the offence under section 1112(1)` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did the firm commit the offence under section 1112(1)?
      `my position in the firm` IS A `s 1121(2) position of the person` @desc What is your position: a director, a manager, a secretary, a person treated as an officer of the firm for the purposes of section 1112, or none of these?
      `I authorised or permitted it` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did you authorise or permit the giving of the false document or statement?
      `I took part in it` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did you take part in it?
      `I failed to take all reasonable steps to prevent it` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did you fail to take all reasonable steps to prevent it?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 1112(2), as an officer of a firm that gave the registrar a false document or statement, have I also committed the offence` IS
    `s 1112(2) the officer of the firm who is in default also commits the offence` `the offence was committed by` (JUST `the firm committed the offence under section 1112(1)`) `my position in the firm` (`s 1121(3) the officer's conduct as the person states it` `I authorised or permitted it` `I took part in it` `I failed to take all reasonable steps to prevent it`)

-- s 1112(3). The fine. England and Wales: a fine with no stated limit, so no number.
@ref s 1112(3) (the section this question asks about)
@export Under section 1112(3), what is the most I can be fined on summary conviction for giving the registrar a false statement?
GIVEN `where I would be convicted` IS A `Place of registration` @desc Where would you be convicted: England and Wales, Scotland or Northern Ireland?
      `the amount of level 5 on the standard scale, in pounds` IS A NUMBER @desc What is the amount of level 5 on the standard scale, in pounds? (The Act does not state it.)
GIVETH A MAYBE NUMBER
DECIDE `Under section 1112(3), what is the most I can be fined on summary conviction for giving the registrar a false statement` IS
    CONSIDER (`s 1112(3) the punishment on summary conviction` `where I would be convicted`)'s `fine not exceeding`
    WHEN JUST limit THEN `s 1125(1) the fine limit in pounds` limit (`s 1125 the amounts with one figure in every slot` `the amount of level 5 on the standard scale, in pounds`)
    WHEN NOTHING THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (silent): the offence provision states no fine limit

-- s 1112A(1).
@ref s 1112A(1) (the section this question asks about)
@export Under section 1112A(1), have I committed the offence of knowingly giving the registrar a false, misleading or deceptive document or statement?
GIVEN `I delivered, or caused to be delivered, a document to the registrar for a purpose of the Companies Acts` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did you deliver, or cause to be delivered, a document to the registrar for a purpose of the Companies Acts?
      `I made a statement to the registrar for a purpose of the Companies Acts` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did you make a statement to the registrar for a purpose of the Companies Acts?
      `it is misleading, false or deceptive in a material particular` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the document or statement misleading, false or deceptive in a material particular?
      `I did it knowingly` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did you do it knowingly?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 1112A(1), have I committed the offence of knowingly giving the registrar a false, misleading or deceptive document or statement` IS
    `s 1112A(1) the person commits the offence` `I delivered, or caused to be delivered, a document to the registrar for a purpose of the Companies Acts` `I made a statement to the registrar for a purpose of the Companies Acts` `it is misleading, false or deceptive in a material particular` `I did it knowingly`

-- s 1112A(3) with s 1131(2). The longest imprisonment.
@ref s 1112A(3) (the section this question asks about)
@export Under section 1112A(3), what is the longest I can be imprisoned, in months, for knowingly giving the registrar a false document or statement?
GIVEN `how I would be convicted` IS A `Mode of conviction` @desc How would you be convicted: on indictment, or summarily in England and Wales, in Scotland or in Northern Ireland?
      `the date the offence was committed` IS A DATE @desc On what date was the offence committed?
      `the general limit in a magistrates' court is known` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Do you know the general limit on imprisonment in a magistrates' court (the Act does not state it)?
      `the general limit in a magistrates' court, in months` IS A NUMBER @desc What is that general limit, in months? (Ignored if you do not know it.)
GIVETH A MAYBE NUMBER
DECIDE `Under section 1112A(3), what is the longest I can be imprisoned, in months, for knowingly giving the registrar a false document or statement` IS
    CONSIDER `s 1112A(3) the punishment for the offence` `how I would be convicted` `the date the offence was committed` (`s 1131(2) the general limit as the person states it` `the general limit in a magistrates' court is known` `the general limit in a magistrates' court, in months`)
    WHEN JUST penalty THEN `s 1131(2) the term shown in months` (penalty's `imprisonment not exceeding`)
    WHEN NOTHING THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (points outside the text): the general limit in a magistrates' court is not stated in the Act, or no place of summary conviction was named

-- s 1112B(1).
@ref s 1112B(1) (the section this question asks about)
@export Under section 1112B(1), am I liable for a false-statement offence if the Secretary of State has issued me a certificate?
GIVEN `a certificate has been issued to me for the purposes of section 1112B` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has the Secretary of State issued you a certificate for the purposes of section 1112B?
      `the offence relates to a misleading, false or deceptive delivery or statement to the registrar` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does the offence relate to the delivery to the registrar, or the making of a statement to the registrar, that is misleading, false or deceptive?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 1112B(1), am I liable for a false-statement offence if the Secretary of State has issued me a certificate` IS
    `s 1112B(1) the person is liable for the commission of the offence` `a certificate has been issued to me for the purposes of section 1112B` `the offence relates to a misleading, false or deceptive delivery or statement to the registrar`

-- Arises only if your company has defaulted on a filing obligation (a document or a notice to the registrar).
-- s 1113(1)-(2).
@ref s 1113(2) (the section this question asks about)
@export Under section 1113(2), may I, as a member or creditor, give my company notice requiring it to deliver a document it has failed to deliver?
GIVEN `my company has defaulted in delivering a document to the registrar` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has your company made default in complying with an obligation under the Companies Acts to deliver a document to the registrar?
      `my company has defaulted in giving notice to the registrar` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has your company made default in complying with an obligation under the Companies Acts to give notice to the registrar of any matter?
      `I am` IS A `s 1113 person who may act` @desc What are you: the registrar, a member of the company, a creditor of the company, or some other person?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 1113(2), may I, as a member or creditor, give my company notice requiring it to deliver a document it has failed to deliver` IS
    `s 1113(2) the person may give notice to the company requiring it to comply with the obligation` (`s 1113(1) the section applies` `my company has defaulted in delivering a document to the registrar` `my company has defaulted in giving notice to the registrar`) `I am`

-- s 1113(3).
@ref s 1113(3) (the section this question asks about)
@export Under section 1113(3), by what date must my company make good its default after I served notice?
GIVEN `the date I served the notice` IS A DATE @desc On what date was the notice served on the company?
GIVETH A DATE
DECIDE `Under section 1113(3), by what date must my company make good its default after I served notice` IS
    `s 1113(3) the last day for the company to make good the default` `the date I served the notice`

@ref s 1113(3) (the section this question asks about)
@export Under section 1113(3), may I apply to the court for an order making my company file the document?
GIVEN `my company has defaulted in delivering a document to the registrar` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has your company made default in complying with an obligation under the Companies Acts to deliver a document to the registrar?
      `my company has defaulted in giving notice to the registrar` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has your company made default in complying with an obligation under the Companies Acts to give notice to the registrar of any matter?
      `I am` IS A `s 1113 person who may act` @desc What are you: the registrar, a member of the company, a creditor of the company, or some other person?
      `the date the notice was served` IS A DATE @desc On what date was the notice served on the company?
      `the company has made good the default` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has the company made good the default?
      `the date the company made good the default` IS A DATE @desc On what date did it do so? (Enter any date if it has not.)
      `the date on which you are asking` IS A DATE @desc What is today's date, or the date you want the question answered for?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 1113(3), may I apply to the court for an order making my company file the document` IS
    `s 1113(3) the person may apply to the court for an order` (`s 1113(1) the section applies` `my company has defaulted in delivering a document to the registrar` `my company has defaulted in giving notice to the registrar`) `I am` `the date the notice was served` (IF `the company has made good the default` THEN JUST `the date the company made good the default` ELSE NOTHING) `the date on which you are asking` -- NOTHING-kind (points outside the text): a date or limit the person does not know is passed to the rule as NOTHING, and the rule says whether it can decide without it

-- s 1114(1)(b).
@ref s 1114(1)(b) (the section this question asks about)
@export Under section 1114(1)(b), does what I am doing count as delivering a document to the registrar?
GIVEN `what I am doing` IS A `s 1114(1)(b) act` @desc What are you doing: forwarding, lodging, registering, sending, producing, submitting, giving a notice, providing information under section 1110E, or something else?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 1114(1)(b), does what I am doing count as delivering a document to the registrar` IS
    `s 1114(1)(b) the act is delivering a document` `what I am doing`

-- Arises only if the registrar has directed that a class of documents be delivered to a particular address.
-- s 1119(2).
@ref s 1119(2) (the section this question asks about)
@export Under section 1119(2), is a document I delivered to the wrong address treated as delivered?
GIVEN `a direction has been given for this class of documents` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has the registrar given a direction that documents of this class be delivered to a specified address of an authorised person?
      `I delivered it to an address other than the specified address` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did you deliver the document to an address other than the specified address?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 1119(2), is a document I delivered to the wrong address treated as delivered` IS
    `s 1119(2) the document is treated as delivered` `a direction has been given for this class of documents` `I delivered it to an address other than the specified address`

-- ======================================================================================================================
§§ `Part 36: officers in default, penalties and prosecution (ss 1121 to 1133)`

-- s 1121(2)-(3). Whether you are an officer in default (the person every "officer in default" offence names).
@ref s 1121 (the section this question asks about)
@export Under section 1121, am I an officer in default?
GIVEN `my position in the company` IS A `s 1121(2) position of the person` @desc What is your position: a director, a manager, a secretary, a person treated as an officer of the company for the purposes of the provision in question, or none of these?
      `I authorised or permitted the contravention` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did you authorise or permit the contravention?
      `I took part in the contravention` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did you take part in the contravention?
      `I failed to take all reasonable steps to prevent the contravention` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did you fail to take all reasonable steps to prevent the contravention?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 1121, am I an officer in default` IS
    `s 1121 the person is an officer in default` `my position in the company` (`s 1121(3) the officer's conduct as the person states it` `I authorised or permitted the contravention` `I took part in the contravention` `I failed to take all reasonable steps to prevent the contravention`)

-- s 1122(1).
@ref s 1122(1) (the section this question asks about)
@export Under section 1122(1), does my company commit an offence as an officer in default of another company?
GIVEN `my company is an officer of another company` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is your company an officer (for example a corporate director) of another company?
      `one of my company's officers is in default` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is one of your company's officers in default (section 1121(3))?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 1122(1), does my company commit an offence as an officer in default of another company` IS
    `s 1122(1) the company commits an offence as an officer in default` `my company is an officer of another company` `one of my company's officers is in default`

-- s 1123.
@ref s 1123 (the section this question asks about)
@export Under section 1123, am I treated as a director of this body for the purposes of the offence of an officer in default?
GIVEN `the kind of body` IS A `s 1123 kind of body` @desc What kind of body: a company, a body corporate other than a company, a partnership, or an unincorporated body other than a partnership?
      `the body's affairs are managed by its members` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are the body's affairs managed by its members?
      `my role in the body` IS A `s 1123 role of the person in the body` @desc What is your role: a member of the body, a corresponding officer of the body, a member of the partnership, a member of the governing body, a manager, secretary or similar officer, or some other role?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 1123, am I treated as a director of this body for the purposes of the offence of an officer in default` IS
    `s 1123 the person is read as a director for the purposes of section 1121(2)(a)` `the kind of body` `the body's affairs are managed by its members` `my role in the body`

-- s 1125(2). Any offence whose punishment is "a fine not exceeding [level] and, for continued contravention, a daily default fine".
@ref s 1125(2) (the section this question asks about)
@export Under section 1125(2), what is the most I can be fined on a second or later conviction for continuing the contravention?
GIVEN `the level on the standard scale of the first fine` IS A NUMBER @desc At what level on the standard scale (1 to 5) is the fine for a first conviction set?
      `the daily default fine as a fraction of that level` IS A NUMBER @desc What fraction of that level is the daily default fine (for example 0.1 for one-tenth)?
      `the amount of that level, in pounds` IS A NUMBER @desc What is the amount of that level on the standard scale, in pounds? (The Act does not state it.)
      `this is a second or subsequent summary conviction` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is this a second or subsequent summary conviction for the offence?
      `days on which the contravention is continued` IS A NUMBER @desc For how many days has the contravention continued?
GIVETH A MAYBE NUMBER
DECIDE `Under section 1125(2), what is the most I can be fined on a second or later conviction for continuing the contravention` IS
    `s 1125(2) the most the person can be fined on this conviction, in pounds` penalty `this is a second or subsequent summary conviction` `days on which the contravention is continued` (`s 1125 the amounts with one figure in every slot` `the amount of that level, in pounds`)
    WHERE
        penalty MEANS Penalty WITH
            `how convicted` IS `on summary conviction`
            `imprisonment not exceeding` IS NOTHING
            `fine not exceeding` IS JUST (`a fine not exceeding a level on the standard scale` OF `the level on the standard scale of the first fine`, 1)
            `daily default fine for continued contravention` IS JUST (`a fine not exceeding a level on the standard scale` OF `the level on the standard scale of the first fine`, `the daily default fine as a fraction of that level`)
            `imprisonment and fine together` IS FALSE

-- Arises only if you are charged with one of the offences that need a consent to prosecute.
-- s 1126.
@ref s 1126 (the section this question asks about)
@export Under section 1126, whose consent is needed before I can be prosecuted for this offence?
GIVEN `the offence` IS A `s 1126(1) offence` @desc Which offence: section 458, 460 or 949 (unauthorised disclosure); section 953 (takeover bid documents); sections 448 to 453A of the Companies Act 1985; section 798 (evading restrictions on shares); section 455 of the 1985 Act; section 1112 or 1112A (false statements); paragraph 5 or 6 of Schedule 1B; or another offence?
      `where the proceedings would be brought` IS A `Place of registration` @desc Where would the proceedings be brought: England and Wales, Scotland or Northern Ireland?
GIVETH A MAYBE `s 1126 consent required`
DECIDE `Under section 1126, whose consent is needed before I can be prosecuted for this offence` IS
    `s 1126(2)-(3) the consent required for the proceedings` `the offence` `where the proceedings would be brought`

@ref s 1126 (the section this question asks about)
@export Under section 1126, may the proceedings against me be brought with the consent that has been given?
GIVEN `the offence` IS A `s 1126(1) offence` @desc Which offence: section 458, 460 or 949 (unauthorised disclosure); section 953 (takeover bid documents); sections 448 to 453A of the Companies Act 1985; section 798 (evading restrictions on shares); section 455 of the 1985 Act; section 1112 or 1112A (false statements); paragraph 5 or 6 of Schedule 1B; or another offence?
      `where the proceedings would be brought` IS A `Place of registration` @desc Where would the proceedings be brought: England and Wales, Scotland or Northern Ireland?
      `the proceedings are brought by, or with the consent of` IS A `s 1126 consent of` @desc By whom, or with whose consent, are the proceedings brought: the Secretary of State, the Director of Public Prosecutions, the Director of Public Prosecutions for Northern Ireland, or no one?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 1126, may the proceedings against me be brought with the consent that has been given` IS
    `s 1126(2)-(3) the proceedings may be brought` `the offence` `where the proceedings would be brought` `the proceedings are brought by, or with the consent of`

-- s 1127(1).
@ref s 1127(1) (the section this question asks about)
@export Under section 1127(1), may summary proceedings for the offence be taken against me at this place?
GIVEN `the defendant is a body corporate` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the defendant a body corporate?
      `the place is a place of business of the body` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the place somewhere the body has a place of business?
      `the place is where the defendant is for the time being` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the place somewhere the defendant is for the time being?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 1127(1), may summary proceedings for the offence be taken against me at this place` IS
    `s 1127(1) summary proceedings for the offence may be taken at the place` `the defendant is a body corporate` `the place is a place of business of the body` `the place is where the defendant is for the time being`

-- s 1128(1).
@ref s 1128(1) (the section this question asks about)
@export Under section 1128(1), is an information laid on this date within the time the section allows for it to be tried in a magistrates' court in England and Wales?
GIVEN `the date the offence was committed` IS A DATE @desc On what date was the offence committed?
      `the date the information was or will be laid` IS A DATE @desc On what date was the information laid, or on what date will it be laid?
      `the prosecutor's date of knowledge is known` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Do you know the date on which evidence sufficient, in the opinion of the Director of Public Prosecutions or the Secretary of State, to justify the proceedings came to his knowledge (or is it stated in his certificate)?
      `the date the evidence came to the prosecutor's knowledge` IS A DATE @desc What is that date? (Ignored if you do not know it.)
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 1128(1), is an information laid on this date within the time the section allows for it to be tried in a magistrates' court in England and Wales` IS
    `s 1128(1) the information was laid in time` `the date the offence was committed` `the date the information was or will be laid` (IF `the prosecutor's date of knowledge is known` THEN JUST `the date the evidence came to the prosecutor's knowledge` ELSE NOTHING) -- NOTHING-kind (points outside the text): a date or limit the person does not know is passed to the rule as NOTHING, and the rule says whether it can decide without it

-- s 1128(2).
@ref s 1128(2) (the section this question asks about)
@export Under section 1128(2), are summary proceedings in Scotland commenced on this date within the time the section allows?
GIVEN `the date the offence was committed` IS A DATE @desc On what date was the offence committed?
      `the date the proceedings are or will be deemed commenced` IS A DATE @desc On what date are the proceedings deemed to be commenced under section 136(3) of the Criminal Procedure (Scotland) Act 1995, or on what date will they be?
      `the Lord Advocate's date of knowledge is known` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Do you know the date on which evidence sufficient, in the Lord Advocate's opinion, to justify the proceedings came to his knowledge?
      `the date the evidence came to the Lord Advocate's knowledge` IS A DATE @desc What is that date? (Ignored if you do not know it.)
      `the evidence was reported to the Lord Advocate by the Secretary of State` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Was the evidence reported to the Lord Advocate by the Secretary of State?
      `the Secretary of State's date of knowledge is known` IS A BOOLEAN @desc If it was, do you know the date on which it came to the Secretary of State's knowledge?
      `the date the evidence came to the Secretary of State's knowledge` IS A DATE @desc What is that date? (Ignored if you do not know it.)
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 1128(2), are summary proceedings in Scotland commenced on this date within the time the section allows` IS
    `s 1128(2) the proceedings in Scotland were commenced in time` `the date the offence was committed` `the date the proceedings are or will be deemed commenced` (IF `the Lord Advocate's date of knowledge is known` THEN JUST `the date the evidence came to the Lord Advocate's knowledge` ELSE NOTHING) `the evidence was reported to the Lord Advocate by the Secretary of State` (IF `the Secretary of State's date of knowledge is known` THEN JUST `the date the evidence came to the Secretary of State's knowledge` ELSE NOTHING) -- NOTHING-kind (points outside the text): a date or limit the person does not know is passed to the rule as NOTHING, and the rule says whether it can decide without it

-- s 1128(3).
@ref s 1128(3) (the section this question asks about)
@export Under section 1128(3), is a complaint made on this date within the time the section allows for a magistrates' court in Northern Ireland to hear it?
GIVEN `the date the offence was committed` IS A DATE @desc On what date was the offence committed?
      `the date the complaint was or will be made` IS A DATE @desc On what date was the complaint made, or on what date will it be made?
      `the prosecutor's date of knowledge is known` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Do you know the date on which evidence sufficient, in the opinion of the Director of Public Prosecutions for Northern Ireland or the Secretary of State, to justify the proceedings came to his knowledge (or is it stated in his certificate)?
      `the date the evidence came to the prosecutor's knowledge` IS A DATE @desc What is that date? (Ignored if you do not know it.)
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 1128(3), is a complaint made on this date within the time the section allows for a magistrates' court in Northern Ireland to hear it` IS
    `s 1128(3) the complaint was made in time` `the date the offence was committed` `the date the complaint was or will be made` (IF `the prosecutor's date of knowledge is known` THEN JUST `the date the evidence came to the prosecutor's knowledge` ELSE NOTHING) -- NOTHING-kind (points outside the text): a date or limit the person does not know is passed to the rule as NOTHING, and the rule says whether it can decide without it

-- s 1129.
@ref s 1129 (the section this question asks about)
@export Under section 1129, must I disclose information I am entitled to refuse to disclose on grounds of legal professional privilege?
GIVEN `the proceedings are against a person for an offence under the Companies Acts` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are the proceedings against a person for an offence under the Companies Acts?
      `I am entitled to refuse to disclose the information on grounds of legal professional privilege` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are you entitled to refuse to disclose the information on grounds of legal professional privilege (in Scotland, confidentiality of communications)?
