DECIDE `Under section 1130(1), may proceedings against my unincorporated body be brought in my name as one of its members` IS
    `s 1130(1) the proceedings meet the requirement of s 1130(1)` `the proceedings are for an offence under the Companies Acts alleged to have been committed by an unincorporated body` `s 1130(1) the name of a member of the body`

-- s 1130(3).
@ref s 1130(3) (the section this question asks about)
@export Under section 1130(3), may a fine imposed on my unincorporated body be taken from my own funds?
GIVEN `a fine is imposed on an unincorporated body on its conviction of an offence under the Companies Acts` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has a fine been imposed on an unincorporated body on its conviction of an offence under the Companies Acts?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 1130(3), may a fine imposed on my unincorporated body be taken from my own funds` IS
    `s 1130(3) the fine is paid as the subsection requires` `a fine is imposed on an unincorporated body on its conviction of an offence under the Companies Acts` `s 1130(3) the personal funds of a member of the body`

-- s 1131(2).
@ref s 1131(2) (the section this question asks about)
@export Under section 1131(2), what term of imprisonment on summary conviction in England and Wales applies to an offence committed on this date?
GIVEN `the date the offence was committed` IS A DATE @desc On what date was the offence committed?
      `the general limit in a magistrates' court is known` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Do you know the general limit on imprisonment in a magistrates' court (the Act does not state it)?
      `the general limit in a magistrates' court, in months` IS A NUMBER @desc What is that general limit, in months? (Ignored if you do not know it.)
GIVETH A MAYBE NUMBER
DECIDE `Under section 1131(2), what term of imprisonment on summary conviction in England and Wales applies to an offence committed on this date` IS
    `s 1131(2) the term shown in months` (`s 1131(2) the term of imprisonment the provision refers to` `the date the offence was committed` (`s 1131(2) the general limit as the person states it` `the general limit in a magistrates' court is known` `the general limit in a magistrates' court, in months`))

-- Arises only if the police, the Director of Public Prosecutions or the Secretary of State suspect an offence and want your company's documents.
-- s 1132(2).
@ref s 1132(2) (the section this question asks about)
@export Under section 1132(2), may a court order my company's documents to be inspected or produced?
GIVEN `there is reasonable cause to believe an officer committed an offence in connection with the management of the company's affairs` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is there shown to be reasonable cause to believe that a person has, while an officer of the company, committed an offence in connection with the management of the company's affairs?
      `there is reasonable cause to believe evidence of it is in the company's documents` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is there shown to be reasonable cause to believe that evidence of the offence is to be found in documents in the possession or control of the company?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 1132(2), may a court order my company's documents to be inspected or produced` IS
    `s 1132(2) an order under this section may be made` `there is reasonable cause to believe an officer committed an offence in connection with the management of the company's affairs` `there is reasonable cause to believe evidence of it is in the company's documents`

-- s 1132(3)-(4).
@ref s 1132(3) (the section this question asks about)
@export Under section 1132(3), may the order require me, as secretary or an officer of the company, to produce its documents?
GIVEN `an order under section 1132 is made` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has a court made an order under section 1132?
      `the documents are held by a person carrying on the business of banking` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are the documents in the possession or control of a person carrying on the business of banking (so far as they relate to the company's affairs)?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 1132(3), may the order require me, as secretary or an officer of the company, to produce its documents` IS
    `s 1132(3)-(4) the order may contain the provision` `s 1132(3)(b) a requirement that the secretary of the company, or such other officer of it as may be named in the order, produce the documents (or any of them) to a person named in the order at a place so named` `an order under section 1132 is made` `the documents are held by a person carrying on the business of banking`

-- s 1132(5).
@ref s 1132(5) (the section this question asks about)
@export Under section 1132(5), may I appeal against the decision to make an order for inspection or production of documents?
GIVEN `the decision is a decision under section 1132 of a High Court judge, a Lord Commissioner of Justiciary or the High Court` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the decision a decision under section 1132 of a judge of the High Court, any of the Lords Commissioners of Justiciary or the High Court?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 1132(5), may I appeal against the decision to make an order for inspection or production of documents` IS
    `s 1132(5) the decision may be appealed` `the decision is a decision under section 1132 of a High Court judge, a Lord Commissioner of Justiciary or the High Court`

-- s 1132A(2), (4), (5).
@ref s 1132A(2) (the section this question asks about)
@export Under section 1132A(2), is this offence one for which the registrar could be given power to impose a financial penalty?
GIVEN `where the offence provision is in the Act` IS A `s 1132A(2) place of the offence provision in the Act` @desc Where is the provision that creates the offence: Part 12 (company secretaries), Part 13 (resolutions and meetings), Part 16 (audit), some other provision of the Companies Act 2006, or a provision of another Act?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 1132A(2), is this offence one for which the registrar could be given power to impose a financial penalty` IS
    `s 1132A(2) the offence is a relevant offence under this Act` `where the offence provision is in the Act`

@ref s 1132A(4) (the section this question asks about)
@export Under section 1132A(4), may regulations giving the registrar power to impose a financial penalty provide for a maximum penalty of this amount?
GIVEN `the maximum financial penalty the regulations would allow, in pounds` IS A NUMBER @desc What is the maximum financial penalty, in pounds, that the regulations would provide for?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 1132A(4), may regulations giving the registrar power to impose a financial penalty provide for a maximum penalty of this amount` IS
    `s 1132A(4) the regulations may provide for this maximum financial penalty` `the maximum financial penalty the regulations would allow, in pounds`

@ref s 1132A(5) (the section this question asks about)
@export Under section 1132A(5), must the regulations provide that no proceedings may be brought against me for conduct for which I have been given a financial penalty?
GIVEN `I have been given a financial penalty under the regulations for that conduct` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Have you been given a financial penalty under the regulations in respect of that conduct?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 1132A(5), must the regulations provide that no proceedings may be brought against me for conduct for which I have been given a financial penalty` IS
    `s 1132A(5)(b) the regulations must provide that no proceedings may be brought against the person` `I have been given a financial penalty under the regulations for that conduct`

-- s 1133.
@ref s 1133 (the section this question asks about)
@export Under section 1133, do the provisions of Part 36 apply to an offence I committed before they came into force?
GIVEN `the provision is section 1132` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the provision in question section 1132 (production and inspection of documents)?
      `the offence was committed before the commencement of the relevant provision` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Was the offence committed before the commencement of the relevant provision of Part 36?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 1133, do the provisions of Part 36 apply to an offence I committed before they came into force` IS
    `s 1133 the provision of Part 36 applies to the offence` `the provision is section 1132` `the offence was committed before the commencement of the relevant provision`

-- ====================================================================================================
-- seat questions from part coa25 (merged by the lead on 2026-11-12; unchanged text follows)
-- ====================================================================================================
-- coa25-seat.l4: Companies Act 2006 (United Kingdom), ss 1134 to 1157 and 1175 to 1208 -- THE SEAT LAYER (part coa25).
--
-- SEAT: an individual who is, or is about to become, a director, a company secretary or a member (shareholder) of a
-- company registered under the Act, or who deals with one, asking on facts they can state what the Act requires or lets
-- them do, what rights they have against the company or its directors, what they must disclose, file, approve or vote
-- on and by when, and what follows (liability, offences, penalties) if it is not done. (Assumed, not ruled: the Act is
-- addressed to companies, so the individual is whoever stands in a company's management or ownership.)
-- ASSUMED, NOT RULED (Chapter 2 of Part 41, ss 1200 to 1206): that Chapter applies to an individual or a partnership
-- carrying on business under a business name, not to a company. Its questions are asked by the individual or partner who
-- carries on the business, and by a customer or supplier who deals with it (a person who "deals with" a business).
-- Provisions that address only an official (the Secretary of State, the court, the registrar) appear here only for what
-- they mean to the individual. Part 39 (amendments and repeals of other Acts) and the regulation-making powers of Parts
-- 37, 40 and 41 are machinery: no question is asked about them.
--
-- This layer IMPORTs the layer-1 modules and calls their rules; it never restates a rule. Every question takes plain
-- inputs, each with an @desc worded as the individual would be asked. Where a layer-1 rule takes the answer of another
-- part (s 1121 "officer in default", s 790C, Schedules 4 and 5, the working-day calendar of s 1173(1)), the question asks
-- the plain fact and passes it on as a MAYBE BOOLEAN. A "not covered" answer is NOTHING (null): it is never the same as "no".
-- The amounts the Act leaves to other law (the pounds a level on the standard scale stands for; the general limit in a
-- magistrates' court) are asked as inputs, never supplied here.
-- Questions are grouped under § headings in the text's order. Groups that arise only in a situation the person may not
-- be in are marked in the heading's comment, so that a form can ask "Has this happened to you?" first.

-- ---- the greatest fines for a conviction, shared by every offence question below --------------------------

DECLARE `Under section 1135(4), the greatest fines` HAS
    `the most on a first summary conviction, in pounds` IS A MAYBE NUMBER
    `the most for each day of continued contravention, in pounds` IS A MAYBE NUMBER

GIVEN limit IS A MAYBE `Fine limit`
      `the pounds that a level on the standard scale stands for` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A MAYBE NUMBER
`Under section 1135(4), the pounds that a fine limit stands for` MEANS
    CONSIDER limit
    WHEN NOTHING THEN NOTHING
    -- The statutory maximum is never reached by the penalties asked about here (levels on the standard scale only):
    -- a placeholder of 0 is passed for it.
    WHEN JUST l THEN `s 1135(4) the fine limit in pounds` l `the pounds that a level on the standard scale stands for` 0

GIVEN penalty IS A MAYBE Penalty
      `the pounds that a level on the standard scale stands for` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A `Under section 1135(4), the greatest fines`
`Under section 1135(4), the greatest fines for a penalty` MEANS
    CONSIDER penalty
    WHEN NOTHING THEN `Under section 1135(4), the greatest fines` OF NOTHING, NOTHING
    WHEN JUST p THEN
        `Under section 1135(4), the greatest fines` WITH
            `the most on a first summary conviction, in pounds` IS `Under section 1135(4), the pounds that a fine limit stands for` (p's `fine not exceeding`) `the pounds that a level on the standard scale stands for`
            `the most for each day of continued contravention, in pounds` IS `Under section 1135(4), the pounds that a fine limit stands for` (p's `daily default fine for continued contravention`) `the pounds that a level on the standard scale stands for`

§ `Companies Act 2006 -- questions from a director, secretary or member, or a person dealing with a company or business (ss 1134 to 1157, 1175 to 1208)`

§§ `Company records (ss 1134 to 1138)`

@export Under section 1134, is this document one of my company's "company records"?
GIVEN `a provision of the Companies Acts requires the company to keep this document` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does a provision of the Companies Acts require the company to keep this document (a register, index, accounting records, agreement, memorandum, minutes or other document)?
      `the requiring provision is one of the Companies Acts` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the provision that requires it one of the Companies Acts (the company law provisions of the 2006 Act, Part 2 of the 2004 Act, or the 1985 Act provisions still in force)?
      `it is a register of the company's debenture holders` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it a register kept by the company of its debenture holders?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 1134, is this document one of my company's company records` IS
    `s 1134 the document is a company record`
        `a provision of the Companies Acts requires the company to keep this document`
        (JUST `the requiring provision is one of the Companies Acts`)
        `it is a register of the company's debenture holders`

@export Under section 1135(1), may my company keep its records in this way?
GIVEN `the records are kept in` IS A `Form of document` @desc How does the company keep the records: in hard copy form or in electronic form?
      `the records are arranged as the directors think fit` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are the records arranged in the manner the directors of the company think fit?
      `the information is adequately recorded for future reference` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the information in the records adequately recorded for future reference?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 1135(1), may my company keep its records in this way` IS
    `s 1135(1) the company may keep its records in this way`
        `the records are kept in`
        `the records are arranged as the directors think fit`
        `the information is adequately recorded for future reference`

@export Under section 1135(2), have my company's electronic records met the requirement that they can be reproduced in hard copy form?
GIVEN `the records are kept in` IS A `Form of document` @desc How does the company keep the records: in hard copy form or in electronic form?
      `the electronic records can be reproduced in hard copy form` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Can the electronic records be reproduced in hard copy form? (Answer yes if the records are kept in hard copy.)
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 1135(2), have my company's electronic records met the requirement that they can be reproduced in hard copy form` IS
    `s 1135(2) the company has met the requirement of reproduction in hard copy form`
        `the records are kept in`
        `the electronic records can be reproduced in hard copy form`

@export Under section 1135(3), am I guilty of an offence, as an officer of my company, because of how it keeps its records?
GIVEN `the records are kept in` IS A `Form of document` @desc How does the company keep the records: in hard copy form or in electronic form?
      `the information is adequately recorded for future reference` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the information in the records adequately recorded for future reference?
      `the electronic records can be reproduced in hard copy form` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Can the electronic records be reproduced in hard copy form? (Answer yes if the records are kept in hard copy.)
      `I am an officer of the company who is in default` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are you an officer of the company who is in default within the meaning of section 1121 of the Act?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 1135(3), am I guilty of an offence, as an officer of my company, because of how it keeps its records` IS
    `s 1135(3) an officer of the company commits an offence`
        (`s 1135 the company has complied with this section`
            `the records are kept in`
            `the information is adequately recorded for future reference`
            `the electronic records can be reproduced in hard copy form`)
        (JUST `I am an officer of the company who is in default`)

@export Under section 1135(4), if I am convicted of the offence, what is the most I can be fined (in pounds)?
GIVEN `the amount in pounds that level 3 on the standard scale stands for` IS A NUMBER @desc The amount in pounds that level 3 on the standard scale stands for (the Act does not state it; it is set elsewhere)
GIVETH A `Under section 1135(4), the greatest fines`
DECIDE `Under section 1135(4), if I am convicted of the offence, what is the most I can be fined (in pounds)` IS
    `Under section 1135(4), the greatest fines for a penalty`
        (`s 1135(4) the penalty for an offence under s 1135` (JUST TRUE))
        `the amount in pounds that level 3 on the standard scale stands for`


@export Under section 1135(5), is an old instrument that requires the debenture register in hard copy now read as allowing electronic form?
GIVEN `the date the instrument was made` IS A DATE @desc On what date was the instrument (made by the company) made?
      `it requires the register of holders of the company's debentures to be kept in hard copy form` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does the instrument require the register of holders of the company's debentures to be kept in hard copy form?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 1135(5), is an old instrument that requires the debenture register in hard copy now read as allowing electronic form` IS
    `s 1135(5) the instrument's requirement is to be read as requiring hard copy or electronic form`
        `the date the instrument was made`
        `it requires the register of holders of the company's debentures to be kept in hard copy form`

@export Under section 1136(6), does keeping my company's records at this place satisfy the requirement to keep them available for inspection?
GIVEN `the place is one the regulations under section 1136 specify` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the place one that regulations under section 1136 specify as a place where the records may be kept available for inspection?
      `all the company's records subject to the requirement are kept there` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are all the company's records that are subject to that requirement kept at that place?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 1136(6), does keeping my company's records at this place satisfy the requirement to keep them available for inspection` IS
    `s 1136(6) keeping the records available for inspection at the place complies with the requirement`
        `the place is one the regulations under section 1136 specify`
        `all the company's records subject to the requirement are kept there`

@export Under section 1137(5)(b), is my company prevented by the Act or the regulations from charging less than the prescribed fee for inspection or copies, or nothing at all?
GIVEN `a fee may be charged` IS A BOOLEAN @desc May the company charge a fee for the inspection or the copies?
      `the fee I want to charge is lesser than the prescribed fee, or none at all` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the fee the company wants to charge less than the prescribed fee, or nothing at all?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 1137(5)(b), is my company prevented by the Act or the regulations from charging less than the prescribed fee for inspection or copies, or nothing at all` IS
    `s 1137(5)(b) the company is prevented from charging a lesser fee or none at all`
        `a fee may be charged`
        `the fee I want to charge is lesser than the prescribed fee, or none at all`

@export Under section 1138(1), has my company taken the precautions against falsification of its records that the Act requires?
GIVEN `what kind of record it is` IS A `s 1138 kind of company record` @desc Is the record a copy of a director's service contract or a memorandum of its terms (section 228), a qualifying indemnity provision (section 237), or another company record?
      `the records are kept otherwise than in bound books` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are the records kept otherwise than in bound books?
      `adequate precautions guard against falsification` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are adequate precautions taken to guard against falsification of the records?
      `adequate precautions facilitate the discovery of falsification` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are adequate precautions taken to facilitate the discovery of falsification?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 1138(1), has my company taken the precautions against falsification of its records that the Act requires` IS
    `s 1138 the company has complied with this section`
        `what kind of record it is`
        `the records are kept otherwise than in bound books`
        `adequate precautions guard against falsification`
        `adequate precautions facilitate the discovery of falsification`

@export Under section 1138(2), am I guilty of an offence, as an officer of my company, because its records are not protected against falsification?
GIVEN `what kind of record it is` IS A `s 1138 kind of company record` @desc Is the record a copy of a director's service contract or a memorandum of its terms (section 228), a qualifying indemnity provision (section 237), or another company record?
      `the records are kept otherwise than in bound books` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are the records kept otherwise than in bound books?
      `adequate precautions guard against falsification` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are adequate precautions taken to guard against falsification of the records?
      `adequate precautions facilitate the discovery of falsification` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are adequate precautions taken to facilitate the discovery of falsification?
      `I am an officer of the company who is in default` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are you an officer of the company who is in default within the meaning of section 1121 of the Act?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 1138(2), am I guilty of an offence, as an officer of my company, because its records are not protected against falsification` IS
    `s 1138(2) an officer of the company commits an offence`
        (`s 1138 the company has complied with this section`
            `what kind of record it is`
            `the records are kept otherwise than in bound books`
            `adequate precautions guard against falsification`
            `adequate precautions facilitate the discovery of falsification`)
        (JUST `I am an officer of the company who is in default`)

@export Under section 1138(3), if I am convicted of the offence, what is the most I can be fined (in pounds)?
GIVEN `the amount in pounds that level 3 on the standard scale stands for` IS A NUMBER @desc The amount in pounds that level 3 on the standard scale stands for (the Act does not state it; it is set elsewhere)
GIVETH A `Under section 1135(4), the greatest fines`
DECIDE `Under section 1138(3), if I am convicted of the offence, what is the most I can be fined (in pounds)` IS
    `Under section 1135(4), the greatest fines for a penalty`
        (`s 1138(3) the penalty for an offence under s 1138` (JUST TRUE))
        `the amount in pounds that level 3 on the standard scale stands for`


§§ `Service addresses (ss 1139 to 1142)`

@export Under section 1139(1), is a document validly served on my company if it is left at, or posted to, its registered office?
GIVEN `the company is registered under the Companies Act 2006` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the company a company registered under the Companies Act 2006?
      `the document is left at the registered office` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Was the document left at the company's registered office?
      `the document is sent by post to the registered office` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Was the document sent by post to the company's registered office?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 1139(1), is a document validly served on my company if it is left at, or posted to, its registered office` IS
    `s 1139(1) service of the document on the company is effected`
        `the company is registered under the Companies Act 2006`
        `the document is left at the registered office`
        `the document is sent by post to the registered office`

-- Section 1139(2) and (3) appear TWICE in the text (lines 16255-16264 of the source): two versions. The text does not say
-- which is in force, so the question asks which text to apply (fork F1 in NOTES.md).
@export Under section 1139(2), is a document validly served on an overseas company registered under section 1046?
GIVEN `which text of section 1139(2) to apply` IS A STRING @desc Which text of section 1139(2) and (3) applies: "first text" (a resident person's registered address, or a place of business in the United Kingdom if there is no such person) or "second text" (the company's registered address, or a resident person's registered address)? The Act as rendered shows both.
      `the overseas company's particulars are registered under section 1046` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are the overseas company's particulars registered under section 1046?
      `the document is left at or posted to the registered address of a resident person authorised to accept service` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Was the document left at, or posted to, the registered address of a person resident in the United Kingdom who is authorised to accept service on the company's behalf?
      `there is no such person, or the person refuses service, or service cannot otherwise be effected` IS A BOOLEAN @desc (First text only.) Is there no such person, or does such a person refuse service, or can service not for any other reason be effected on that person?
      `the document is left at or posted to a place of business of the company in the United Kingdom` IS A BOOLEAN @desc (First text only.) Was the document left at, or posted to, a place of business of the company in the United Kingdom?
      `the document is left at or posted to the company's registered address` IS A BOOLEAN @desc (Second text only.) Was the document left at, or posted to, the company's own registered address (the address registered for it under regulations under section 1048A)?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 1139(2), is a document validly served on an overseas company registered under section 1046` IS
    IF `which text of section 1139(2) to apply` EQUALS "second text"
    THEN `s 1139(2) second text: service of the document on the overseas company is effected`
            `the overseas company's particulars are registered under section 1046`
            `the document is left at or posted to the company's registered address`
            `the document is left at or posted to the registered address of a resident person authorised to accept service`
    ELSE IF `which text of section 1139(2) to apply` EQUALS "first text"
         THEN `s 1139(2) first text: service of the document on the overseas company is effected`
                 `the overseas company's particulars are registered under section 1046`
                 `the document is left at or posted to the registered address of a resident person authorised to accept service`
                 `there is no such person, or the person refuses service, or service cannot otherwise be effected`
                 `the document is left at or posted to a place of business of the company in the United Kingdom`
         ELSE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (silent): the answer to "which text" is neither "first text" nor "second text"

@export Under section 1139(4), is court process validly served on my company, registered in Scotland or Northern Ireland, at its principal place of business in England and Wales?
GIVEN `where the company is registered` IS A `Place of registration` @desc Where is the company registered: England and Wales, Scotland or Northern Ireland?
      `the company carries on business in England and Wales` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does the company carry on business in England and Wales?
      `the document is the process of a court in England and Wales` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the document the process of a court in England and Wales?
      `it was left at or posted to the principal place of business in England and Wales` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Was it left at, or sent by post to, the company's principal place of business in England and Wales?
      `it was addressed to the manager or other head officer in England and Wales` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Was it addressed to the manager or other head officer in England and Wales of the company?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 1139(4), is court process validly served on my company, registered in Scotland or Northern Ireland, at its principal place of business in England and Wales` IS
    `s 1139(4) service of the process on the company is effected`
        `where the company is registered`
        `the company carries on business in England and Wales`
        `the document is the process of a court in England and Wales`
        `it was left at or posted to the principal place of business in England and Wales`
        `it was addressed to the manager or other head officer in England and Wales`

@export Under section 1139(4), have I, as the person who issued the process, sent the company's registered office the copy the Act requires?
GIVEN `process was served on the company under section 1139(4)` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Was the process served on the company under section 1139(4) (a company registered in Scotland or Northern Ireland, served at its principal place of business in England and Wales)?
      `I sent a copy of it by post to the company's registered office` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did you send a copy of the process by post to the company's registered office?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 1139(4), have I, as the person who issued the process, sent the company's registered office the copy the Act requires` IS
    `s 1139(4) the person issuing out the process has complied with the duty to send a copy`
        `process was served on the company under section 1139(4)`
        `I sent a copy of it by post to the company's registered office`

@export Under section 1140(1), is a document validly served on me, as a director, secretary or other registered person, at my registered address?
GIVEN `what I am` IS A `s 1140 kind of person` @desc Which are you: a director or secretary of a company; a registrable person or registrable relevant legal entity; a person holding a specified position of a registered overseas company; a judicial factor; an interim manager (Charities Act); a manager under section 47 of the 2004 Act; or another kind of person?
      `I am a registrable person or registrable relevant legal entity under section 790C` IS A BOOLEAN @desc (Only if you are a registrable person or entity.) Are you a registrable person or a registrable relevant legal entity in relation to the company, within the meaning of section 790C?
      `my position is one specified by regulations under section 1046` IS A BOOLEAN @desc (Only for an overseas company's officer.) Is your position one that regulations under section 1046 specify for the purposes of section 1140?
      `the document was left at or posted to the address` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Was the document left at, or sent by post to, the address?
      `the address is shown as a current address for me in the public part of the register` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the address shown as a current address for you in the part of the register available for public inspection?
      `notice has been registered of the termination of the appointment for which the address was registered` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has notice been registered of the termination of the appointment in relation to which the address was registered?
      `the address is a registered address of mine for another appointment` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the address also a registered address of yours in relation to any other appointment?
      `the overseas company has ceased to have any connection with the United Kingdom requiring registration under section 1046` IS A BOOLEAN @desc (Overseas company position only.) Has the overseas company ceased to have any connection with the United Kingdom by virtue of which it must register particulars under section 1046?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 1140(1), is a document validly served on me, as a director, secretary or other registered person, at my registered address` IS
    `s 1140(1) service of the document on the person is effected`
        (`s 1140(2) the section applies to the person`
            `what I am`
            (JUST `I am a registrable person or registrable relevant legal entity under section 790C`)
            `my position is one specified by regulations under section 1046`)
        `the document was left at or posted to the address`
        (`s 1140(4) the address is the person's registered address` `the address is shown as a current address for me in the public part of the register`)
        (`s 1140(6) service may be effected by virtue of s 1140 at the address`
            `notice has been registered of the termination of the appointment for which the address was registered`
            `the address is a registered address of mine for another appointment`
            (`what I am` EQUALS `s 1140 a person holding a position of an overseas company whose particulars are registered under s 1046`)
            `the overseas company has ceased to have any connection with the United Kingdom requiring registration under section 1046`)

@export Under section 1140(5), a document was served at my previous address after I changed it: is the service still valid?
GIVEN `the date notice of the change of address was registered` IS A DATE @desc On what date was the notice of the change of your address registered?
      `the date the document was served at the previous address` IS A DATE @desc On what date was the document served at the address previously registered?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 1140(5), a document was served at my previous address after I changed it: is the service still valid` IS
    `s 1140(5) the document is validly served at the address previously registered`
        `the date notice of the change of address was registered`
        `the date the document was served at the previous address`

@export Under section 1141, is this address a service address for me?
GIVEN `documents may be effectively served on me at the address` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Can documents be effectively served on you at the address?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 1141, is this address a service address for me` IS
    `s 1141 the address is a service address` `documents may be effectively served on me at the address`

@export Under section 1142, must the address I am asked to give be a service address?
GIVEN `the obligation is under the Companies Acts to give a person's address` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the obligation one under the Companies Acts to give a person's address?
      `the Companies Acts expressly provide otherwise` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does the provision that requires the address expressly provide that it need not be a service address?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 1142, must the address I am asked to give be a service address` IS
    `s 1142 the address to be given is a service address`
        `the obligation is under the Companies Acts to give a person's address`
        `the Companies Acts expressly provide otherwise`

§§ `Sending or supplying documents or information (ss 1143 to 1148)`

@export Under section 1144, has the document or information I sent to, or received from, a company been sent or supplied as the Act requires?
GIVEN `who sent it to whom` IS A `s 1144 direction of the communication` @desc Was it sent to a company by someone who is not a company; by a company to someone who is not a company; or by one company to another company?
      `it was sent or supplied in accordance with Schedule 4` IS A BOOLEAN @desc (Sent to a company.) Was it sent or supplied in accordance with Schedule 4 (communications to a company)?
      `it was sent or supplied in accordance with Schedule 5` IS A BOOLEAN @desc (Sent by a company.) Was it sent or supplied in accordance with Schedule 5 (communications by a company)?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 1144, has the document or information I sent to, or received from, a company been sent or supplied as the Act requires` IS
    `s 1144 the document or information has been sent or supplied`
        `who sent it to whom`
        (JUST `it was sent or supplied in accordance with Schedule 4`)
        (JUST `it was sent or supplied in accordance with Schedule 5`)

@export Under section 1145(1), as a member or debenture holder, can I require my company to send me a hard copy of a document it sent me electronically?
GIVEN `what I am to the company` IS A `s 1145 holder` @desc Are you a member of the company, a holder of its debentures, or another person?
      `I received the document or information otherwise than in hard copy form` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did you receive the document or information from the company otherwise than in hard copy form (for example by e-mail or on a website)?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 1145(1), as a member or debenture holder, can I require my company to send me a hard copy of a document it sent me electronically` IS
    `s 1145(1) the person is entitled to require the company to send a hard copy version`
        `what I am to the company`
        `I received the document or information otherwise than in hard copy form`

@export Under section 1145(2), by what date must my company send me the hard copy I asked for?
GIVEN `the date the company received my request` IS A DATE @desc On what date did the company receive your request for a hard copy version?
GIVETH A DATE
DECIDE `Under section 1145(2), by what date must my company send me the hard copy I asked for` IS
    `s 1145(2) the last day for sending the hard copy version` `the date the company received my request`

@export Under section 1145(2), did my company send me the hard copy in time?
GIVEN `the date the company received my request` IS A DATE @desc On what date did the company receive your request for a hard copy version?
      `the date the company sent the hard copy` IS A DATE @desc On what date did the company send you the hard copy version?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 1145(2), did my company send me the hard copy in time` IS
    `s 1145(2) the company sent the hard copy version in time`
        `the date the company received my request`
        `the date the company sent the hard copy`

@export Under section 1145(3), may my company charge me for the hard copy version I asked for?
GIVEN `it is a version I am entitled to require under section 1145(1)` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it a hard copy version of a document or information that you are entitled to require under section 1145(1)?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 1145(3), may my company charge me for the hard copy version I asked for` IS
    `s 1145(3) the company may make a charge for providing the hard copy version` `it is a version I am entitled to require under section 1145(1)`

@export Under section 1145(4), am I guilty of an offence, as an officer of my company, because it did not send a requested hard copy as the Act requires?
GIVEN `what the requester is to the company` IS A `s 1145 holder` @desc Is the person who asked for the hard copy a member, a debenture holder, or another person?
      `the requester received the document otherwise than in hard copy form` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did the requester receive the document or information otherwise than in hard copy form?
      `the date the company received the request` IS A DATE @desc On what date did the company receive the request?
      `the date the company sent the hard copy` IS A DATE @desc On what date did the company send the hard copy version? (Give any date after the deadline if it was never sent.)
      `the company charged for it` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did the company make a charge for providing the hard copy version?
      `I am an officer of the company who is in default` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are you an officer of the company who is in default within the meaning of section 1121 of the Act?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 1145(4), am I guilty of an offence, as an officer of my company, because it did not send a requested hard copy as the Act requires` IS
    `s 1145(4) an officer of the company commits an offence`
        (`s 1145 the company has complied with this section`
            (`s 1145(1) the person is entitled to require the company to send a hard copy version` `what the requester is to the company` `the requester received the document otherwise than in hard copy form`)
            (`s 1145(2) the company sent the hard copy version in time` `the date the company received the request` `the date the company sent the hard copy`)
            `the company charged for it`)
        (JUST `I am an officer of the company who is in default`)

@export Under section 1145(5), if I am convicted of the offence, what is the most I can be fined (in pounds)?
GIVEN `the amount in pounds that level 3 on the standard scale stands for` IS A NUMBER @desc The amount in pounds that level 3 on the standard scale stands for (the Act does not state it; it is set elsewhere)
GIVETH A `Under section 1135(4), the greatest fines`
DECIDE `Under section 1145(5), if I am convicted of the offence, what is the most I can be fined (in pounds)` IS
    `Under section 1135(4), the greatest fines for a penalty`
        (`s 1145(5) the penalty for an offence under s 1145` (JUST TRUE))
        `the amount in pounds that level 3 on the standard scale stands for`


@export Under section 1146, is the document or information I sent to a company sufficiently authenticated?
GIVEN `it was sent in` IS A `Form of document` @desc Was it sent in hard copy form or in electronic form?
      `it is signed by me` IS A BOOLEAN @desc (Hard copy.) Is it signed by the person sending or supplying it?
      `the company specified a manner of confirming the sender's identity` IS A BOOLEAN @desc (Electronic.) Has the company specified a manner in which the sender's identity is to be confirmed?
      `my identity was confirmed in that manner` IS A BOOLEAN @desc (Electronic.) Was the sender's identity confirmed in the manner the company specified?
      `the communication contains or is accompanied by a statement of my identity` IS A BOOLEAN @desc (Electronic.) Does the communication contain, or is it accompanied by, a statement of the sender's identity?
      `the company has no reason to doubt that statement` IS A BOOLEAN @desc (Electronic.) Does the company have no reason to doubt the truth of that statement?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 1146, is the document or information I sent to a company sufficiently authenticated` IS
    CONSIDER `it was sent in`
    WHEN `hard copy form` THEN `s 1146(2) the hard copy document or information is sufficiently authenticated` `it is signed by me`
    WHEN `electronic form` THEN
        `s 1146(3) the electronic document or information is sufficiently authenticated`
            `the company specified a manner of confirming the sender's identity`
            `my identity was confirmed in that manner`
            `the communication contains or is accompanied by a statement of my identity`
            `the company has no reason to doubt that statement`

@export Under section 1147, on what day is a document my company sent me treated as received?
GIVEN `how it was sent` IS A `s 1147 how the document or information was sent` @desc Was it sent by post to an address in the United Kingdom, by electronic means, by means of a website, or in another way?
      `the company can show it was properly addressed` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Can the company show that it was properly addressed (and, if posted, prepaid and posted)?
      `the date it was posted or sent, or the material first made available on the website` IS A DATE @desc On what date was it posted or sent (or, for a website, first made available there)?
      `the hour of that day` IS A NUMBER @desc At what hour of that day (0 to 24)?
      `the date notice of the website material was received` IS A DATE @desc (Website only.) On what date did you receive, or are you deemed to have received, notice that the material was on the website?
      `the hour of that day for the notice` IS A NUMBER @desc (Website only.) At what hour of that day?
      `days that are not working days` IS A LIST OF DATE @desc List every day in the period that is not a working day because it is a bank holiday, Christmas Day or Good Friday (Saturdays and Sundays need not be listed)
GIVETH A MAYBE DATE
DECIDE `Under section 1147, on what day is a document my company sent me treated as received` IS
    `s 1147 the day the document is treated as delivered` deemed
    WHERE
        posted MEANS `s 1147 instant` OF `the date it was posted or sent, or the material first made available on the website`, `the hour of that day`
        noticed MEANS `s 1147 instant` OF `the date notice of the website material was received`, `the hour of that day for the notice`
        working MEANS GIVEN d YIELD (NOT (`is weekend` d)) AND NOT (elem d `days that are not working days`)
        deemed MEANS
            CONSIDER `how it was sent`
            WHEN `s 1147 by post to an address in the United Kingdom` THEN
                `s 1147(2) the instant at which the document or information is deemed received by post` TRUE `the company can show it was properly addressed` posted working
            WHEN `s 1147 by electronic means` THEN
                `s 1147(3) the instant at which the document or information is deemed received by electronic means` TRUE `the company can show it was properly addressed` posted working
            WHEN `s 1147 by means of a website` THEN
                JUST (`s 1147(4) the instant at which the document or information is deemed received by means of a website` posted noticed)
            WHEN `s 1147 in another way` THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): the deeming rules of subsections (2) to (4) name post, electronic means and a website only

@export Under section 1148(1), is this a "document" for the purposes of the company communications provisions?
GIVEN `what it is` IS A `s 1148 kind of document` @desc Is it a summons, a notice, an order, other legal process, a register, or any other document?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 1148(1), is this a document for the purposes of the company communications provisions` IS
    `s 1148(1) the thing is a document` `what it is`

§§ `Requirements as to independent valuation (ss 1149 to 1153): only if you are asked to value, or are an officer asked for information`

@export Under section 1150(1), may I make the valuation and report on non-cash consideration for a company?
GIVEN `I am eligible for appointment as a statutory auditor` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are you eligible for appointment as a statutory auditor (section 1212)?
      `I am an officer or employee of the company` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are you an officer or employee of the company? (An auditor of the company does not count.)
      `I am a partner or employee of such a person, or a partnership of which such a person is a partner` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are you a partner or employee of an officer or employee of the company, or a partnership of which such a person is a partner?
      `I am an officer or employee of an associated undertaking of the company` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are you an officer or employee of an associated undertaking of the company (a parent or subsidiary undertaking of it, or a subsidiary undertaking of its parent)?
      `I am a partner or employee of such an officer or employee of an associated undertaking, or a partnership of which such a person is a partner` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are you a partner or employee of such an officer or employee of an associated undertaking, or a partnership of which such a person is a partner?
      `a connection specified by regulations exists` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does a connection of a description specified by regulations exist between you or an associate of yours and the company or an associated undertaking of it?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 1150(1), may I make the valuation and report on non-cash consideration for a company` IS
    `s 1150(1) the person may make the valuation and report`
        (JUST `I am eligible for appointment as a statutory auditor`)
        (`s 1151(1) the person meets the independence requirement`
            `I am an officer or employee of the company`
            `I am a partner or employee of such a person, or a partnership of which such a person is a partner`
            `I am an officer or employee of an associated undertaking of the company`
            `I am a partner or employee of such an officer or employee of an associated undertaking, or a partnership of which such a person is a partner`
            `a connection specified by regulations exists`)

@export Under section 1151(1), do I meet the independence requirement for valuing a company's non-cash consideration?
GIVEN `I am an officer or employee of the company` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are you an officer or employee of the company? (An auditor of the company does not count.)
      `I am a partner or employee of such a person, or a partnership of which such a person is a partner` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are you a partner or employee of an officer or employee of the company, or a partnership of which such a person is a partner?
      `I am an officer or employee of an associated undertaking of the company` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are you an officer or employee of an associated undertaking of the company?
      `I am a partner or employee of such an officer or employee of an associated undertaking, or a partnership of which such a person is a partner` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are you a partner or employee of such an officer or employee of an associated undertaking, or a partnership of which such a person is a partner?
      `a connection specified by regulations exists` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does a connection of a description specified by regulations exist between you or an associate of yours and the company or an associated undertaking of it?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 1151(1), do I meet the independence requirement for valuing a company's non-cash consideration` IS
    `s 1151(1) the person meets the independence requirement`
        `I am an officer or employee of the company`
        `I am a partner or employee of such a person, or a partnership of which such a person is a partner`
        `I am an officer or employee of an associated undertaking of the company`
        `I am a partner or employee of such an officer or employee of an associated undertaking, or a partnership of which such a person is a partner`
        `a connection specified by regulations exists`

@export Under section 1152(2), is this person my "associate" for the independence requirement?
GIVEN `how the person is related to me` IS A `s 1152 relationship of the other person to the individual` @desc Is the person my spouse, civil partner, minor child or step-child; a body corporate of which I am a director; a limited liability partnership of which I am a member; my employee or partner; or none of these?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 1152(2), is this person my associate for the independence requirement` IS
    `s 1152(2) the other person is an associate of the individual` `how the person is related to me`

@export Under section 1153(1), may the valuer require information and explanation from me, as an officer of the company?
GIVEN `the person is carrying out a valuation or making a report on consideration to be accepted or given by the company` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the person carrying out a valuation, or making a report, on consideration proposed to be accepted or given by the company?
      `the information and explanation is what the person thinks necessary for the valuation, the report or a note under section 596(3) or 600(3)` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it information and explanation that the person thinks necessary to carry out the valuation or make the report, or to provide a note required by section 596(3) or 600(3)?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 1153(1), may the valuer require information and explanation from me, as an officer of the company` IS
    `s 1153(1) the person is entitled to require the information and explanation from the officers of the company`
        `the person is carrying out a valuation or making a report on consideration to be accepted or given by the company`
        `the information and explanation is what the person thinks necessary for the valuation, the report or a note under section 596(3) or 600(3)`

@export Under section 1153(2), have I committed an offence by what I told a valuer?
GIVEN `I made the statement knowingly or recklessly` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did you make the statement knowingly or recklessly?
      `it was misleading, false or deceptive in a material particular` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Was the statement misleading, false or deceptive in a material particular?
      `I made it, orally or in writing, to a person carrying out a valuation or making a report` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did you make it (orally or in writing) to a person carrying out a valuation or making a report?
      `it conveyed or purported to convey information or explanation that person requires or is entitled to require` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did it convey, or purport to convey, information or explanation that the person requires, or is entitled to require, under section 1153(1)?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 1153(2), have I committed an offence by what I told a valuer` IS
    `s 1153(2) the person commits an offence`
        `I made the statement knowingly or recklessly`
        `it was misleading, false or deceptive in a material particular`
        (`s 1153(3) the statement is one to which subsection (2) applies`
            `I made it, orally or in writing, to a person carrying out a valuation or making a report`
            `it conveyed or purported to convey information or explanation that person requires or is entitled to require`)

@export Under section 1153(4), what penalty can I face for making a false statement to a valuer?
GIVEN `how I would be convicted` IS A `Mode of conviction` @desc How would you be convicted: on conviction on indictment; on summary conviction in England and Wales; on summary conviction in Scotland; or on summary conviction in Northern Ireland?
GIVETH A MAYBE Penalty
DECIDE `Under section 1153(4), what penalty can I face for making a false statement to a valuer` IS
    `s 1153(4) the penalty for an offence under s 1153(2)` `how I would be convicted` (JUST TRUE)

§§ `Notice of appointment of certain officers, courts and legal proceedings (ss 1154 to 1157): only if you have been appointed judicial factor, interim manager or manager, or are sued for breach of duty`

@export Under section 1154(1) and (2), who must give the registrar notice of my appointment?
GIVEN `what I have been appointed` IS A `s 1154 appointment` @desc Which appointment: a judicial factor (Scotland); an interim manager under s 76 of the Charities Act 2011; an interim manager under s 33 of the Charities Act (Northern Ireland) 2008; a receiver or manager under that section; a manager under s 47 of the 2004 Act; or another appointment?
GIVETH A MAYBE `s 1154 party`
DECIDE `Under section 1154(1) and (2), who must give the registrar notice of my appointment` IS
    `s 1154(2) the person who must give the notice` `what I have been appointed`

@export Under section 1155(1), have I committed an offence as a judicial factor by not telling the registrar of my appointment within 14 days?
GIVEN `the date of my appointment` IS A DATE @desc On what date were you appointed?
      `I have given the registrar notice in accordance with section 1154` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Have you given the registrar notice of your appointment in accordance with section 1154?
      `the date I gave the notice` IS A DATE @desc On what date did you give the notice? (Any date if you have not.)
      `today's date` IS A DATE @desc What is today's date?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 1155(1), have I committed an offence as a judicial factor by not telling the registrar of my appointment within 14 days` IS
    `s 1155(1) the judicial factor commits an offence`
        `the date of my appointment`
        (IF `I have given the registrar notice in accordance with section 1154` THEN JUST `the date I gave the notice` ELSE NOTHING)
        `today's date`

@export Under section 1155(2), if I am convicted of the offence, what is the most I can be fined (in pounds)?
GIVEN `the amount in pounds that level 5 on the standard scale stands for` IS A NUMBER @desc The amount in pounds that level 5 on the standard scale stands for (the Act does not state it; it is set elsewhere)
GIVETH A `Under section 1135(4), the greatest fines`
DECIDE `Under section 1155(2), if I am convicted of the offence, what is the most I can be fined (in pounds)` IS
    `Under section 1135(4), the greatest fines for a penalty`
        (`s 1155(2) the penalty for an offence under s 1155` (JUST TRUE))
        `the amount in pounds that level 5 on the standard scale stands for`


@export Under section 1156(1), which courts are "the court" for my company?
GIVEN `where the company is registered` IS A `Place of registration` @desc Where is the company registered: England and Wales, Scotland or Northern Ireland?
GIVETH A LIST OF `s 1156 court`
DECIDE `Under section 1156(1), which courts are the court for my company` IS
    `s 1156(1) the courts that are "the court" in the part of the United Kingdom` `where the company is registered`

@export Under section 1157(1), as an officer or auditor sued for breach of duty, can the court relieve me from liability?
GIVEN `what I am` IS A `s 1157 defendant` @desc Are you an officer of a company; a person employed by a company as auditor (whether or not an officer); or another person?
      `the proceedings are for negligence, default, breach of duty or breach of trust` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are the proceedings against you for negligence, default, breach of duty or breach of trust?
      `it appears to the court that I am or may be liable` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does it appear to the court hearing the case that you are or may be liable?
      `it appears to the court that I acted honestly and reasonably` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does it appear to the court that you acted honestly and reasonably?
      `it appears to the court that I ought fairly to be excused` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does it appear to the court that, having regard to all the circumstances (including those connected with your appointment), you ought fairly to be excused?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 1157(1), as an officer or auditor sued for breach of duty, can the court relieve me from liability` IS
    `s 1157(1) the court may relieve the defendant from liability`
        `what I am`
        `the proceedings are for negligence, default, breach of duty or breach of trust`
        `it appears to the court that I am or may be liable`
        `it appears to the court that I acted honestly and reasonably`
        `it appears to the court that I ought fairly to be excused`

@export Under section 1157(2), may I apply to the court for relief now, because I fear a claim?
GIVEN `what I am` IS A `s 1157 defendant` @desc Are you an officer of a company; a person employed by a company as auditor (whether or not an officer); or another person?
      `I have reason to apprehend that a claim will or might be made against me` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Do you have reason to apprehend that a claim will or might be made against you in respect of negligence, default, breach of duty or breach of trust?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 1157(2), may I apply to the court for relief now, because I fear a claim` IS
    `s 1157(2)(a) the person may apply to the court for relief` `what I am` `I have reason to apprehend that a claim will or might be made against me`

@export Under section 1157(3), in a jury trial, may the judge direct judgment for me because I ought to be relieved?
GIVEN `the case is one to which section 1157(1) applies` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it a case to which section 1157(1) applies (proceedings for negligence, default, breach of duty or breach of trust against an officer or auditor)?
      `the case is being tried by a judge with a jury` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the case being tried by a judge with a jury?
      `the judge is satisfied that I ought to be relieved` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the judge, after hearing the evidence, satisfied that you ought to be relieved, wholly or in part, from the liability sought to be enforced against you?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 1157(3), in a jury trial, may the judge direct judgment for me because I ought to be relieved` IS
    `s 1157(3) the judge may withdraw the case from the jury and direct judgment for the defendant`
        `the case is one to which section 1157(1) applies`
        `the case is being tried by a judge with a jury`
        `the judge is satisfied that I ought to be relieved`

§§ `Company directors: foreign disqualification etc (ss 1182 to 1191): only if you are subject to restrictions abroad`

@export Under section 1182(2), am I "subject to foreign restrictions" because of a disqualification or undertaking abroad?
GIVEN `the restriction is under the law of a country or territory outside the United Kingdom` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the restriction, requirement or undertaking under the law of a country or territory outside the United Kingdom?
      `the activity concerned` IS A `s 1182 activity` @desc Which activity does it concern: being a director of a company; acting as receiver of a company's property; being concerned or taking part in the promotion, formation or management of a company; or any other activity?
      `I am disqualified to any extent from it, by reason of misconduct or unfitness` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are you, by reason of misconduct or unfitness, disqualified to any extent from that activity?
      `I must obtain permission or meet a condition before it, by reason of misconduct or unfitness` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are you, by reason of misconduct or unfitness, required to obtain permission from a court or other authority, or to meet any other condition, before that activity?
      `I have given undertakings about it, by reason of misconduct or unfitness` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Have you, by reason of misconduct or unfitness, given undertakings to a court or other authority outside the United Kingdom not to do it, or restricting how or how far you may do it?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 1182(2), am I subject to foreign restrictions because of a disqualification or undertaking abroad` IS
    `s 1182(2) the person is subject to foreign restrictions`
        `the restriction is under the law of a country or territory outside the United Kingdom`
        `the activity concerned`
        `I am disqualified to any extent from it, by reason of misconduct or unfitness`
        `I must obtain permission or meet a condition before it, by reason of misconduct or unfitness`
        `I have given undertakings about it, by reason of misconduct or unfitness`

@export Under section 1184(4), am I a "person disqualified under this Part"?
GIVEN `I am disqualified automatically by virtue of the regulations` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are you disqualified automatically by virtue of regulations under section 1184?
      `I am disqualified by an order of the court on the Secretary of State's application` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are you disqualified by order of the court on the Secretary of State's application under those regulations?
      `I have given and am subject to a disqualification undertaking` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Have you given, and are you subject to, a disqualification undertaking (an undertaking accepted by the Secretary of State not to do anything that would breach a disqualification)?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 1184(4), am I a person disqualified under this Part` IS
    `s 1184(4)(a) the person is a person disqualified under this Part`
        `I am disqualified automatically by virtue of the regulations`
        `I am disqualified by an order of the court on the Secretary of State's application`
        `I have given and am subject to a disqualification undertaking`

@export Under section 1186(2), what is the most the regulations may provide as a penalty for acting in breach of a disqualification?
GIVEN `how I would be convicted` IS A `Mode of conviction` @desc How would you be convicted: on conviction on indictment; on summary conviction in England and Wales; in Scotland; or in Northern Ireland?
      `the date the offence was committed` IS A DATE @desc On what date was the offence committed?
      `the general limit in a magistrates' court, in months` IS A NUMBER @desc How many months is "the general limit in a magistrates' court" (the Act does not state it; it is set elsewhere)?
GIVETH A MAYBE Penalty
DECIDE `Under section 1186(2), what is the most the regulations may provide as a penalty for acting in breach of a disqualification` IS
    `s 1186(2) the greatest penalty that the regulations may provide`
        `how I would be convicted`
        `the date the offence was committed`
        `the general limit in a magistrates' court, in months`

