@export Under section 1187(2), am I jointly and severally liable for a company's debts under regulations made under section 1187?
GIVEN `the regulations make me personally responsible for the company's debts and liabilities` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Do regulations under section 1187 make you personally responsible for debts and other liabilities of the company (because, while subject to foreign restrictions, you were its director or involved in its management)?
      `the other` IS A `s 1187 other person` @desc Jointly and severally liable with whom: the company; another person who is liable for the same debts and liabilities (by virtue of section 1187 or otherwise); or someone else?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 1187(2), am I jointly and severally liable for a company's debts under regulations made under section 1187` IS
    `s 1187(2) the person is jointly and severally liable with the other`
        `the regulations make me personally responsible for the company's debts and liabilities`
        `the other`

@export Under section 1187(3), am I "involved in the management" of a company?
GIVEN `I am concerned, directly or indirectly, in its management` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are you concerned, whether directly or indirectly, in the management of the company?
      `I take part in its management` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Do you take part in the management of the company?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 1187(3), am I involved in the management of a company` IS
    `s 1187(3) the person is involved in the management of the company`
        `I am concerned, directly or indirectly, in its management`
        `I take part in its management`

§§ `Business names: restricted or prohibited names (ss 1192 to 1199A): for an individual who carries on business, or a director of a company that does`

@export Under section 1192(2), does the Act stop me trading under my own surname with the additions I have?
GIVEN `what I am` IS A `s 1192 kind of business` @desc Are you an individual carrying on business; individuals carrying on business in partnership; or another person carrying on business?
      `my name consists of my surname, or of the surnames of all the partners` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does the name consist of your surname (or, for a partnership of individuals, the surnames of all the partners)?
      `it adds a forename or initial` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does the name add an individual's forename or initial, or (for a partnership) the forenames or initials of individual partners?
      `it adds an s to a surname that two or more partners share` IS A BOOLEAN @desc (Partnership only.) Does the name add an "s" at the end of a surname shared by two or more individual partners?
      `it adds only that the business succeeds a former owner` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does the name add something merely indicating that the business is carried on in succession to a former owner?
      `it adds anything else` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does the name add anything else at all?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 1192(2), does the Act stop me trading under my own surname with the additions I have` IS
    `s 1192(2) this Chapter prevents the business name`
        `what I am`
        `my name consists of my surname, or of the surnames of all the partners`
        (append (IF `it adds a forename or initial`
                 THEN (IF `what I am` EQUALS `s 1192 individuals carrying on business in partnership`
                       THEN LIST `s 1192 the forenames of individual partners or the initials of those forenames`
                       ELSE LIST `s 1192 an individual's forename or initial`)
                 ELSE EMPTY)
            (append (IF `it adds an s to a surname that two or more partners share` THEN LIST `s 1192 the addition of "s" at the end of a surname shared by two or more individual partners` ELSE EMPTY)
                (append (IF `it adds only that the business succeeds a former owner` THEN LIST `s 1192 an addition merely indicating that the business is carried on in succession to a former owner of the business` ELSE EMPTY)
                    (IF `it adds anything else` THEN LIST `s 1192 any other addition` ELSE EMPTY))))

@export Under section 1193(1), am I breaking the Act by trading under a name that suggests a connection with government or a public authority?
GIVEN `I carry on business in the United Kingdom under the name` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Do you carry on business in the United Kingdom under the name?
      `the body the name suggests a connection with` IS A `s 1193 body the name would suggest a connection with` @desc Does the name suggest a connection with the Government or a part of the Scottish, Welsh or Northern Ireland administration; with a local authority; with a public authority specified by regulations; or with none of these?
      `the name would be likely to give that impression` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Would the name be likely to give the impression that the business is connected with that body?
      `the Secretary of State has approved the name` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has the Secretary of State approved the name?
      `I carried on the business before the Chapter came into force under its lawful business name and still do` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did you carry on the business immediately before the date on which Chapter 1 of Part 41 came into force, and do you still carry it on under the name that was then its lawful business name?
      `the Secretary of State has given me a written notice that the prohibition does not apply` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has the Secretary of State given you a written notice, specifying the name, that the prohibition does not apply (national security or serious crime)?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 1193(1), am I breaking the Act by trading under a name that suggests a connection with government or a public authority` IS
    `s 1193(1) the person contravenes the prohibition on a name suggesting connection with government or a public authority`
        `I carry on business in the United Kingdom under the name`
        `the body the name suggests a connection with`
        `the name would be likely to give that impression`
        `the Secretary of State has approved the name`
        (`s 1199(2) sections 1192 to 1197 do not apply to the business` `I carried on the business before the Chapter came into force under its lawful business name and still do` `I carried on the business before the Chapter came into force under its lawful business name and still do`)
        -- One input answers both limbs of s 1199(2) ("carried on ... immediately before" and "continues ... under its lawful business name"), and one input answers the s 1199A(1) notice: a notice is effective only if the Secretary of State was satisfied of the national security or serious crime ground (assumed: see NOTES.md, Seams).
        (`s 1199A(1) the prohibitions of this Chapter do not apply to the business under the name` `the Secretary of State has given me a written notice that the prohibition does not apply` `the Secretary of State has given me a written notice that the prohibition does not apply` FALSE)

@export Under section 1193(4), am I guilty of an offence for trading under a name that suggests a connection with government or a public authority?
GIVEN `I carry on business in the United Kingdom under the name` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Do you carry on business in the United Kingdom under the name?
      `the body the name suggests a connection with` IS A `s 1193 body the name would suggest a connection with` @desc Does the name suggest a connection with the Government or a part of the Scottish, Welsh or Northern Ireland administration; with a local authority; with a public authority specified by regulations; or with none of these?
      `the name would be likely to give that impression` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Would the name be likely to give the impression that the business is connected with that body?
      `the Secretary of State has approved the name` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has the Secretary of State approved the name?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 1193(4), am I guilty of an offence for trading under a name that suggests a connection with government or a public authority` IS
    `s 1193(4) the person commits an offence`
        (`s 1193(1) the person contravenes the prohibition on a name suggesting connection with government or a public authority`
            `I carry on business in the United Kingdom under the name`
            `the body the name suggests a connection with`
            `the name would be likely to give that impression`
            `the Secretary of State has approved the name`
            NOTHING
            NOTHING)

