GIVEN `the amount in pounds that level 3 on the standard scale stands for` IS A NUMBER @desc The amount in pounds that level 3 on the standard scale stands for (the Act does not state it; it is set elsewhere)
GIVETH A `Under section 1135(4), the greatest fines`
DECIDE `Under section 1198B(6), if I am convicted of the offence, what is the most I can be fined (in pounds)` IS
    `Under section 1135(4), the greatest fines for a penalty`
        (`s 1198B(6) the penalty for an offence under s 1198B` (JUST TRUE))
        `the amount in pounds that level 3 on the standard scale stands for`


@export Under section 1199(3), do sections 1192 to 1197 not apply to my business, carried on under its existing lawful name, on a date within twelve months of my taking it over?
GIVEN `the business was transferred to me on or after the date Chapter 1 came into force` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Was the business transferred to you on or after the date on which Chapter 1 of Part 41 came into force?
      `I carry it on under the name that was its lawful business name immediately before the transfer` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Do you carry the business on under the name that was its lawful business name immediately before the transfer?
      `the date of the transfer` IS A DATE @desc On what date was the business transferred to you?
      `the date I am asking about` IS A DATE @desc For what date do you want to know?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 1199(3), do sections 1192 to 1197 not apply to my business, carried on under its existing lawful name, on a date within twelve months of my taking it over` IS
    `s 1199(3) sections 1192 to 1197 do not apply to the business carried on under that name on the date`
        `the business was transferred to me on or after the date Chapter 1 came into force`
        `I carry it on under the name that was its lawful business name immediately before the transfer`
        `the date of the transfer`
        `the date I am asking about`

@export Under section 1199A(1), do the prohibitions of Chapter 1 not apply to the business I carry on under my name, because the Secretary of State has given me a written notice?
GIVEN `the Secretary of State gave me a written notice specifying the name and lifting the prohibition` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has the Secretary of State given you a written notice, specifying the name, providing that a prohibition imposed by Chapter 1 does not apply to your business under it?
      `the Secretary of State is satisfied it is necessary for national security` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the Secretary of State satisfied that it is necessary in the interests of national security?
      `the Secretary of State is satisfied it is necessary to prevent or detect serious crime` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the Secretary of State satisfied that it is necessary for the purposes of preventing or detecting serious crime?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 1199A(1), do the prohibitions of Chapter 1 not apply to the business I carry on under my name, because the Secretary of State has given me a written notice` IS
    `s 1199A(1) the prohibitions of this Chapter do not apply to the business under the name`
        `the Secretary of State gave me a written notice specifying the name and lifting the prohibition`
        `the Secretary of State is satisfied it is necessary for national security`
        `the Secretary of State is satisfied it is necessary to prevent or detect serious crime`

§§ `Business names: disclosure by an individual or partnership (ss 1200 to 1208): asked by the individual or partner who carries on the business, and by a customer or supplier who deals with it`

@export Under section 1200(2), is the name I trade under a "business name"?
GIVEN `what I am` IS A `s 1200 kind of person` @desc Are you an individual, a partnership, or another kind of person?
      `my name consists of my surname, or of the surnames and corporate names of all the partners` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does the name consist of your surname (or, for a partnership, the surnames of all partners who are individuals and the corporate names of all partners who are bodies corporate)?
      `it adds a forename or initial` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does the name add an individual's forename or initial, or (for a partnership) the forenames or initials of individual partners?
      `it adds an s to a surname that two or more partners share` IS A BOOLEAN @desc (Partnership only.) Does the name add an "s" at the end of a surname shared by two or more individual partners?
      `it adds only that the business succeeds a former owner` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does the name add something merely indicating that the business is carried on in succession to a former owner?
      `it adds anything else` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does the name add anything else at all?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 1200(2), is the name I trade under a business name` IS
    `s 1200(2) the name is a business name`
        `what I am`
        `my name consists of my surname, or of the surnames and corporate names of all the partners`
        (append (IF `it adds a forename or initial`
                 THEN (IF `what I am` EQUALS `s 1200 a partnership`
                       THEN LIST `s 1200 the forenames of individual partners or the initials of those forenames`
                       ELSE LIST `s 1200 an individual's forename or initial`)
                 ELSE EMPTY)
            (append (IF `it adds an s to a surname that two or more partners share` THEN LIST `s 1200 the addition of "s" at the end of a surname shared by two or more individual partners` ELSE EMPTY)
                (append (IF `it adds only that the business succeeds a former owner` THEN LIST `s 1200 an addition merely indicating that the business is carried on in succession to a former owner of the business` ELSE EMPTY)
                    (IF `it adds anything else` THEN LIST `s 1200 any other addition` ELSE EMPTY))))

@export Under section 1201(1), does what I disclose contain the information Chapter 2 requires?
GIVEN `what I am` IS A `s 1200 kind of person` @desc Are you an individual, a partnership, or another kind of person?
      `it states my name, or the name of each member of the partnership` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does the disclosure state your name (or, for a partnership, the name of each member)?
      `it states an address for service for each person named` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does it state, for each person named, an address at which service of any document relating in any way to the business will be effective?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 1201(1), does what I disclose contain the information Chapter 2 requires` IS
    `s 1201(1) the disclosure contains the information required by this Chapter`
        `what I am`
        `it states my name, or the name of each member of the partnership`
        `it states an address for service for each person named`

@export Under section 1201(2), does the address I give meet the requirement to be in the United Kingdom where I have a place of business there?
GIVEN `I have a place of business in the United Kingdom` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Do you (or the partnership) have a place of business in the United Kingdom?
      `the address is in the United Kingdom` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the address in the United Kingdom?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 1201(2), does the address I give meet the requirement to be in the United Kingdom where I have a place of business there` IS
    `s 1201(2) the address meets the requirement as to place` `I have a place of business in the United Kingdom` `the address is in the United Kingdom`

@export Under section 1201(3), does the address I give meet the requirement of physical delivery and an acknowledgement of delivery where I have no place of business in the United Kingdom?
GIVEN `I have a place of business in the United Kingdom` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Do you (or the partnership) have a place of business in the United Kingdom?
      `service can be effected there by physical delivery` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Can service of documents be effected at the address by physical delivery?
      `delivery can be recorded by an acknowledgement` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the delivery of documents capable of being recorded by obtaining an acknowledgement of delivery?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 1201(3), does the address I give meet the requirement of physical delivery and an acknowledgement of delivery where I have no place of business in the United Kingdom` IS
    `s 1201(3) the address meets the requirement as to delivery`
        `I have a place of business in the United Kingdom`
        `service can be effected there by physical delivery`
        `delivery can be recorded by an acknowledgement`

@export Under section 1202(1), have I complied with the requirement to state my details, in legible characters, on this business document?
GIVEN `what kind of document it is` IS A `s 1202 kind of document` @desc Is it a business letter; a written order for goods or services to be supplied to the business; an invoice or receipt issued in the course of the business; a written demand for payment of a debt arising in the course of the business; or another document?
      `my partnership has more than 20 persons and meets the section 1203 conditions` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the document issued by a partnership of more than 20 persons that meets the conditions in section 1203(2) (a list of all partners kept at its principal place of business; no partner named except in the text or as signatory; the document states that address and that the list is open to inspection there)?
      `it states the information required by Chapter 2` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does the document state your name (or the name of each partner) and an address for service for each?
      `it is in legible characters` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it stated in legible characters?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 1202(1), have I complied with the requirement to state my details, in legible characters, on this business document` IS
    `s 1202(1) the person has complied with the requirement to state the information on the document`
        (`s 1202(1) the requirement to state the information applies to the document`
            `what kind of document it is`
            (IF `my partnership has more than 20 persons and meets the section 1203 conditions` THEN JUST TRUE ELSE NOTHING))
        `it states the information required by Chapter 2`
        `it is in legible characters`

@export Under section 1202(2), did the business I dealt with give me its owner's details when I asked, as the Act requires?
GIVEN `I asked for the information` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did you, as someone with whom anything was done or discussed in the course of the business, ask for the information (the owner's or each partner's name and an address for service)?
      `it was given to me immediately` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Was it given to you immediately?
      `it was given to me by written notice` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Was it given to you by written notice?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 1202(2), did the business I dealt with give me its owner's details when I asked, as the Act requires` IS
    `s 1202(2) the person has complied with the requirement to give the information on request`
        `I asked for the information`
        `it was given to me immediately`
        `it was given to me by written notice`

@export Under section 1203(1), is a document issued by our partnership of more than 20 persons exempt from the requirement to state the partners' names?
GIVEN `the number of persons in the partnership` IS A NUMBER @desc How many persons are in the partnership?
      `we keep a list of all partners at our principal place of business` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does the partnership maintain at its principal place of business a list of the names of all the partners?
      `no partner's name appears in the document except in the text or as a signatory` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does no partner's name appear in the document, except in the text or as a signatory?
      `the document states our principal place of business and that the list is open to inspection there` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does the document state, in legible characters, the address of the partnership's principal place of business and that the list of the partners' names is open to inspection there?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 1203(1), is a document issued by our partnership of more than 20 persons exempt from the requirement to state the partners' names` IS
    `s 1203(1) the exemption applies to the document`
        `the number of persons in the partnership`
        (`s 1203(2) the conditions for the exemption are met`
            `we keep a list of all partners at our principal place of business`
            `no partner's name appears in the document except in the text or as a signatory`
            `the document states our principal place of business and that the list is open to inspection there`)

@export Under section 1203(3), may I inspect the list of partners' names of a large partnership?
GIVEN `the partnership maintains a list of the partners' names for the purposes of section 1203` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does the partnership maintain a list of the partners' names for the purposes of section 1203?
      `I want to inspect it during office hours` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Do you want to inspect it during office hours?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 1203(3), may I inspect the list of partners' names of a large partnership` IS
    `s 1203(3) the person may inspect the list`
        `the partnership maintains a list of the partners' names for the purposes of section 1203`
        `I want to inspect it during office hours`

@export Under section 1203(4), have I, as a member of a partnership, committed an offence by refusing an inspection?
GIVEN `an inspection required in accordance with section 1203 was refused` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Was an inspection required by a person in accordance with section 1203 refused?
      `I refused it or permitted it to be refused` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did you refuse the inspection, or permit it to be refused?
      `I had a reasonable excuse` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did you have a reasonable excuse?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 1203(4), have I, as a member of a partnership, committed an offence by refusing an inspection` IS
    `s 1203(4) the member of the partnership commits an offence`
        `an inspection required in accordance with section 1203 was refused`
        `I refused it or permitted it to be refused`
        `I had a reasonable excuse`

@export Under section 1203(5), if I am convicted of the offence, what is the most I can be fined (in pounds)?
GIVEN `the amount in pounds that level 3 on the standard scale stands for` IS A NUMBER @desc The amount in pounds that level 3 on the standard scale stands for (the Act does not state it; it is set elsewhere)
GIVETH A `Under section 1135(4), the greatest fines`
DECIDE `Under section 1203(5), if I am convicted of the offence, what is the most I can be fined (in pounds)` IS
    `Under section 1135(4), the greatest fines for a penalty`
        (`s 1203(5) the penalty for an offence under s 1203` (JUST TRUE))
        `the amount in pounds that level 3 on the standard scale stands for`


@export Under section 1204(1), have I complied with the requirement to display a notice of my details at my business premises?
GIVEN `the premises are where the business is carried on` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are the premises ones where the business is carried on?
      `customers or suppliers have access to them` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Do customers of the business, or suppliers of goods or services to it, have access to the premises?
      `a notice with the required information is displayed in a prominent position` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is a notice containing the information required by Chapter 2 displayed in a prominent position, so that customers or suppliers can easily read it?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 1204(1), have I complied with the requirement to display a notice of my details at my business premises` IS
    `s 1204(1) the person has complied with the requirement to display the notice`
        (`s 1204(1) the requirement to display the notice applies to the premises` `the premises are where the business is carried on` `customers or suppliers have access to them`)
        `a notice with the required information is displayed in a prominent position`

@export Under section 1205(1), have I committed an offence by not making the disclosure Chapter 2 requires?
GIVEN `I stated my details on the document, legibly` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did you state the required information, in legible characters, on every business document the Act lists?
      `I gave my details immediately and in writing to anyone who asked` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did you immediately give the required information, by written notice, to anyone with whom anything was done or discussed in the course of the business who asked for it?
      `I displayed a notice at my premises` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did you display a notice containing the required information in a prominent position at premises to which customers or suppliers have access?
      `I had a reasonable excuse for any failure` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did you have a reasonable excuse for any failure?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 1205(1), have I committed an offence by not making the disclosure Chapter 2 requires` IS
    `s 1205(1) the person commits an offence`
        (IF `I stated my details on the document, legibly` THEN JUST TRUE ELSE JUST FALSE)
        (IF `I gave my details immediately and in writing to anyone who asked` THEN JUST TRUE ELSE JUST FALSE)
        (IF `I displayed a notice at my premises` THEN JUST TRUE ELSE JUST FALSE)
        `I had a reasonable excuse for any failure`

@export Under section 1205(3), if I am convicted of the offence, what is the most I can be fined (in pounds)?
GIVEN `the amount in pounds that level 3 on the standard scale stands for` IS A NUMBER @desc The amount in pounds that level 3 on the standard scale stands for (the Act does not state it; it is set elsewhere)
GIVETH A `Under section 1135(4), the greatest fines`
DECIDE `Under section 1205(3), if I am convicted of the offence, what is the most I can be fined (in pounds)` IS
    `Under section 1135(4), the greatest fines for a penalty`
        (`s 1205(3) the penalty for an offence under s 1205` (JUST TRUE))
        `the amount in pounds that level 3 on the standard scale stands for`


@export Under section 1206(2), must the court dismiss a claim brought against me by a business that did not make the disclosure Chapter 2 requires?
GIVEN `the claimant is an individual or partnership trading under a business name` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the claimant a person to whom Chapter 2 applies (an individual or partnership carrying on business under a business name) bringing proceedings to enforce a right under a contract made in the course of the business?
      `the claimant was in breach of section 1202(1) or (2) or section 1204(1) when the contract was made` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Was the claimant, when the contract was made, in breach of section 1202(1) or (2) or section 1204(1)?
      `I have a claim against the claimant that I have been unable to pursue because of that breach` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Do you have a claim against the claimant, arising out of the contract, that you have been unable to pursue by reason of the breach?
      `I have suffered financial loss in connection with the contract because of that breach` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Have you suffered some financial loss in connection with the contract by reason of the claimant's breach?
      `the court is satisfied that it is just and equitable to let the proceedings continue` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the court satisfied that it is just and equitable to permit the proceedings to continue?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 1206(2), must the court dismiss a claim brought against me by a business that did not make the disclosure Chapter 2 requires` IS
    `s 1206(2) the proceedings shall be dismissed`
        (`s 1206(1) this section applies to the proceedings`
            `the claimant is an individual or partnership trading under a business name`
            `the claimant was in breach of section 1202(1) or (2) or section 1204(1) when the contract was made`)
        `I have a claim against the claimant that I have been unable to pursue because of that breach`
        `I have suffered financial loss in connection with the contract because of that breach`
        `the court is satisfied that it is just and equitable to let the proceedings continue`

@export Under section 1207, do the general provisions about offences apply to an offence under Part 41?
GIVEN `the offence is an offence under Part 41` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it an offence under Part 41 (business names)?
      `the number of the section in question` IS A NUMBER @desc Which section of the Act are you asking about (for example 1121 on officers in default or 1125 on the daily default fine)?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 1207, do the general provisions about offences apply to an offence under Part 41` IS
    `s 1207 the provision applies in relation to the offence` `the offence is an offence under Part 41` `the number of the section in question`

@export Under section 1208, is this arrangement a "partnership" for Part 41?
GIVEN `what it is` IS A `s 1208 kind of arrangement` @desc Is it a partnership within the Partnership Act 1890; a limited partnership registered under the Limited Partnerships Act 1907; a firm or entity of a similar character formed under the law of a country or territory outside the United Kingdom; or another arrangement?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 1208, is this arrangement a partnership for Part 41` IS
    `s 1208 the arrangement is a partnership` `what it is`

-- ====================================================================================================
-- seat questions from part coa26 (merged by the lead on 2026-11-12; unchanged text follows)
-- ====================================================================================================
-- Companies Act 2006 (United Kingdom), Part 42 (Statutory Auditors), ss 1209-1238 -- THE SEAT LAYER (coa26).
--
-- SEAT: an individual who is, or is about to become, a director, a company secretary or a member (shareholder) of a company
-- registered under the Act, or who deals with one: here, the person who is asked to be (or is) a company's statutory auditor,
-- and the person who proposes to appoint one. (Assumed, not ruled: the Act is addressed to companies, so the individual is whoever
-- stands in a company's management or ownership, or deals with it. An Auditor General is an individual too, so ss 1226-1237 have
-- questions for that person.)
--
-- Every question takes plain inputs (yes or no, a number, a date, a choice from a list), one per fact the person can state, each
-- with an @desc worded for that person. The records and MAYBE answers the layer-1 modules expect are built inside each question
-- from those answers, and the SAME layer-1 rule is then called: no rule is restated here. A fact that the person cannot state
-- (what a borrowed Act or a regulation says) is asked as a yes/no fact, and the answer "not covered" (NOTHING) comes back only
-- where the text itself does not decide the case.
--
-- READING AN ANSWER: JUST TRUE = the text says yes; JUST FALSE = the text says no in its own words; NOTHING = not covered (the text
-- is silent, lists without closing, points outside the Act, or limits a grant by its own wording). Nothing here turns NOTHING into FALSE.
-- Figures the Act leaves to others (the statutory maximum, level 4 on the standard scale) are asked as inputs, in pounds.
--
-- NOT given a question: s 1209 (purposes), s 1210(4), s 1214(7), s 1228(7), s 1238 (machinery); ss 1223-1225G, 1228-1229, 1231, 1234,
-- 1236 address the Secretary of State, the competent authority, the Independent Supervisor, the court and the bodies, never a seat.
-- (The seat questions below use the parts of those sections that mean something to the person.)

§ `Part 42 -- Statutory Auditors: the individual's questions`

§§ `Who is a statutory auditor, and who is eligible (ss 1210-1212, 1226)`

-- s 1210(1). A statutory auditor is a person appointed under one of the routes listed (Part 16 of the Act, the Building Societies Act 1986,
-- a friendly society that is an insurer or an issuer on a UK regulated market, the two 2008 insurance regulations, or a prescribed route).
@export Under section 1210(1), am I a statutory auditor?
GIVEN `I was appointed as auditor of a company under Part 16 of the Companies Act 2006` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Were you appointed as auditor of a company under Part 16 of the Companies Act 2006?
      `I was appointed as auditor under the Building Societies Act 1986` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Were you appointed as auditor under section 77 of or Schedule 11 to the Building Societies Act 1986?
      `I was appointed as auditor of a friendly society` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Were you appointed as auditor of a friendly society under section 72 of or Schedule 14 to the Friendly Societies Act 1992?
      `that friendly society is an insurer` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is that friendly society an insurer (a person who would be an insurance undertaking under Article 2(1) of Council Directive 91/674/EEC)? Answer no if it is not a friendly society appointment.
      `that friendly society is an issuer on a UK regulated market` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is that friendly society an issuer whose transferable securities are admitted to trading on a UK regulated market? Answer no if it is not a friendly society appointment.
      `I was appointed for the Lloyd's syndicate or aggregate accounts regulations` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Were you appointed as auditor for the purposes of regulation 5 of the Insurance Accounts Directive (Lloyd's Syndicate and Aggregate Accounts) Regulations 2008, or to report on the aggregate accounts under those Regulations?
      `I was appointed as auditor of an insurance undertaking` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Were you appointed as auditor of an insurance undertaking for the purposes of the Insurance Accounts Directive (Miscellaneous Insurance Undertakings) Regulations 2008?
      `I was appointed as auditor of a prescribed person` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Were you appointed as auditor of a prescribed person under a prescribed enactment authorising or requiring the appointment (prescribed by order of the Secretary of State)?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 1210(1), am I a statutory auditor` IS
    `s 1210(1) the person is a statutory auditor`
        `I was appointed as auditor of a company under Part 16 of the Companies Act 2006`
        `I was appointed as auditor under the Building Societies Act 1986`
        `I was appointed as auditor of a friendly society`
        (JUST `that friendly society is an insurer`)
        (JUST `that friendly society is an issuer on a UK regulated market`)
        `I was appointed for the Lloyd's syndicate or aggregate accounts regulations`
        `I was appointed as auditor of an insurance undertaking`
        (JUST `I was appointed as auditor of a prescribed person`)

-- s 1210(2). An audited person is the person in respect of whom a statutory audit is conducted.
@export Under section 1210(2), is the company or other person I run an audited person?
GIVEN `an audit is being conducted of me or my company` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is an audit being conducted of you, or of the company you are a director, secretary or member of?
      `the auditor is a statutory auditor` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the person conducting that audit a statutory auditor (appointed under one of the routes in section 1210(1))?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 1210(2), is the company or other person I run an audited person` IS
    `s 1210(2) the person is an audited person` `an audit is being conducted of me or my company` (JUST `the auditor is a statutory auditor`)

-- s 1212(1). An individual or firm is eligible if it is a member of a recognised supervisory body and is eligible under that body's rules.
@export Under section 1212(1), is the individual or firm eligible for appointment as a statutory auditor?
GIVEN `I am subject to the rules of a supervisory body in seeking appointment or acting as a statutory auditor` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are you subject to the rules of a supervisory body when you seek appointment or act as a statutory auditor (whether or not you are formally one of its members)?
      `that supervisory body is a recognised supervisory body` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is that supervisory body recognised by the Secretary of State under Schedule 10?
      `I am eligible under that body's rules` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are you eligible for appointment as a statutory auditor under that body's rules?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 1212(1), is the individual or firm eligible for appointment as a statutory auditor` IS
    `s 1212(1) the individual or firm is eligible for appointment as a statutory auditor`
        `I am subject to the rules of a supervisory body in seeking appointment or acting as a statutory auditor`
        (JUST `that supervisory body is a recognised supervisory body`)
        `I am eligible under that body's rules`

-- s 1211 with ss 1212 and 1226. A person is eligible only if eligible by virtue of Chapter 2 (individuals and firms) or Chapter 3 (an Auditor General).
@export Under section 1211, can I be eligible for appointment as a statutory auditor at all?
GIVEN `I am subject to the rules of a supervisory body in seeking appointment or acting as a statutory auditor` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are you subject to the rules of a supervisory body when you seek appointment or act as a statutory auditor?
      `that supervisory body is a recognised supervisory body` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is that supervisory body recognised by the Secretary of State under Schedule 10?
      `I am eligible under that body's rules` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are you eligible for appointment as a statutory auditor under that body's rules?
      `I am an Auditor General` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are you the Comptroller and Auditor General, the Auditor General for Scotland, the Auditor General for Wales or the Comptroller and Auditor General for Northern Ireland?
      `a suspension notice suspends my eligibility` IS A BOOLEAN @desc If you are an Auditor General: does a suspension notice from the Independent Supervisor, having effect under section 1234, suspend your eligibility?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 1211, can I be eligible for appointment as a statutory auditor at all` IS
    `s 1211 the person is eligible for appointment as a statutory auditor` `by virtue of Chapter 2` `by virtue of Chapter 3`
    WHERE
        `by virtue of Chapter 2` MEANS
            `s 1212(1) the individual or firm is eligible for appointment as a statutory auditor`
                `I am subject to the rules of a supervisory body in seeking appointment or acting as a statutory auditor`
                (JUST `that supervisory body is a recognised supervisory body`)
                `I am eligible under that body's rules`
        `by virtue of Chapter 3` MEANS
            IF `I am an Auditor General`
            THEN `s 1226(2) the Auditor General is eligible for appointment as a statutory auditor` (JUST TRUE) `a suspension notice suspends my eligibility`
            ELSE JUST FALSE

§§ `Acting while ineligible, and the offences (s 1213)`

@export Under section 1213(1), may I act as statutory auditor of an audited person if I am ineligible?
GIVEN `I am ineligible for appointment as a statutory auditor` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are you ineligible for appointment as a statutory auditor (for example because you are no longer eligible under your supervisory body's rules)?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 1213(1), may I act as statutory auditor of an audited person if I am ineligible` IS
    `s 1213(1) the person may act as statutory auditor of an audited person` (JUST `I am ineligible for appointment as a statutory auditor`)

@export Under section 1213(2), must I resign and give written notice because I have become ineligible?
GIVEN `I am a statutory auditor` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are you currently a statutory auditor of an audited person?
      `I have become ineligible during my term of office` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Have you become ineligible for appointment as a statutory auditor at a time during your term of office?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 1213(2), must I resign and give written notice because I have become ineligible` IS
    `s 1213(2) the statutory auditor must immediately resign and give notice` `I am a statutory auditor` (JUST `I have become ineligible during my term of office`)

@export Under section 1213(3), am I guilty of an offence for acting while ineligible or for not giving the notice?
GIVEN `I acted as a statutory auditor although I was ineligible` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did you act as a statutory auditor of an audited person while you were ineligible for appointment?
      `I did not give the notice in writing that I had resigned` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did you fail to give the audited person, as required, written notice that you had resigned because you became ineligible?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 1213(3), am I guilty of an offence for acting while ineligible or for not giving the notice` IS
    `s 1213(3) the person is guilty of an offence` `I acted as a statutory auditor although I was ineligible` `I did not give the notice in writing that I had resigned`

@export Under section 1213(4), what is the most I can be fined for that offence, in pounds?
GIVEN `how I am convicted` IS A `Mode of conviction` @desc How are you convicted: on conviction on indictment, on summary conviction, or on summary conviction in England and Wales, Scotland or Northern Ireland?
      `the statutory maximum in pounds` IS A NUMBER @desc What is the statutory maximum fine in pounds (the figure the Act leaves to be set elsewhere)?
GIVETH A MAYBE NUMBER
DECIDE `Under section 1213(4), what is the most I can be fined for that offence, in pounds` IS
    `s 1213(4) the most the person can be fined, in pounds` `how I am convicted` `the statutory maximum in pounds`

@export Under section 1213(5), am I guilty of a further offence if I keep acting after a conviction?
GIVEN `I have been convicted of an offence of acting while ineligible` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Have you been convicted of an offence under section 1213(3)(a), or of the offence in section 1213(5)?
      `I continue to act after the conviction` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Do you continue to act as a statutory auditor, although ineligible, after the conviction?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 1213(5), am I guilty of a further offence if I keep acting after a conviction` IS
    `s 1213(5) the person is guilty of an offence` `I have been convicted of an offence of acting while ineligible` `I continue to act after the conviction`

@export Under section 1213(6), am I guilty of a further offence if I keep failing to give notice after a conviction?
GIVEN `I have been convicted of an offence of not giving the notice` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Have you been convicted of an offence under section 1213(3)(b), or of the offence in section 1213(6)?
      `I continue to fail to give the notice after the conviction` IS A BOOLEAN @desc After the conviction, do you continue to fail to give the audited person the written notice that you resigned?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 1213(6), am I guilty of a further offence if I keep failing to give notice after a conviction` IS
    `s 1213(6) the person is guilty of an offence` `I have been convicted of an offence of not giving the notice` `I continue to fail to give the notice after the conviction`

@export Under section 1213(7), what is the most I can be fined for each day I continue, in pounds?
GIVEN `how I am convicted` IS A `Mode of conviction` @desc How are you convicted: on conviction on indictment, on summary conviction, or on summary conviction in England and Wales, Scotland or Northern Ireland?
      `the amount corresponding to level 4 on the standard scale, in pounds` IS A NUMBER @desc What is the amount corresponding to level 4 on the standard scale for summary offences, in pounds (the figure the Act leaves to be set elsewhere)?
GIVETH A MAYBE NUMBER
DECIDE `Under section 1213(7), what is the most I can be fined for each day I continue, in pounds` IS
    CONSIDER `s 1213(7) the penalty for an offence under subsection (5) or (6)` `how I am convicted` `the amount corresponding to level 4 on the standard scale, in pounds`
    WHEN `s 1213(7) a fine without a stated limit` THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (silent): "to a fine" states no limit on indictment
    WHEN `s 1213(7) a fine not exceeding a sum for each day on which the act or the failure continues` pounds THEN JUST pounds

@export Under section 1213(8), do I have a defence to the offence of acting while ineligible?
GIVEN `I show that I did not know I was ineligible` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Can you show that you did not know that you were, or had become, ineligible for appointment as a statutory auditor?
      `I show that I had no reason to believe I was ineligible` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Can you show that you had no reason to believe that you were, or had become, ineligible?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 1213(8), do I have a defence to the offence of acting while ineligible` IS
    `s 1213(8) the defence is made out` `I show that I did not know I was ineligible` `I show that I had no reason to believe I was ineligible`

§§ `Independence (ss 1214-1215)`

-- s 1214(1). The answer is the module function's: JUST FALSE = no, I may not act (one of (2), (3), (4) applies to me);
-- NOTHING = none applies on these facts, and the section then neither bars me nor gives me leave (eligibility is s 1212).
@export Under section 1214(1), may I act as statutory auditor of the audited person, given my relationship to it?
GIVEN `my position with the audited company is that of its auditor` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the only position you hold with the audited company that of its auditor?
      `I am otherwise an officer or employee of the audited company` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are you an officer (for example a director or the secretary) or an employee of the audited company, apart from being its auditor?
      `I am a partner or employee of an officer or employee of the audited company` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are you a partner or employee of an officer or employee of the audited company?
      `I am a partnership of which an officer or employee of the audited company is a partner` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are you a partnership of which an officer or employee of the audited company is a partner?
      `I am an officer or employee of an associated undertaking` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are you an officer or employee of a parent or subsidiary undertaking of the audited company, or of a subsidiary undertaking of its parent?
      `I am a partner or employee of an officer or employee of an associated undertaking` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are you a partner or employee of an officer or employee of such an associated undertaking?
      `I am a partnership of which an officer or employee of an associated undertaking is a partner` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are you a partnership of which an officer or employee of such an associated undertaking is a partner?
      `a connection exists with the audited company or an associated undertaking` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does a connection exist between you (or an associate of yours) and the audited company (or an associated undertaking)?
      `the connection is of a description specified by regulations` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is that connection of a description specified by regulations made by the Secretary of State under section 1214(4)? Answer no if there is no connection.
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 1214(1), may I act as statutory auditor of the audited person, given my relationship to it` IS
    `s 1214(1) the person may act as statutory auditor of the audited person` `subsection (2)` `subsection (3)` `subsection (4)`
    WHERE
        `my position counts` MEANS
            `s 1214(5) the position counts as that of an officer or employee of the audited person for the purposes of subsections (2) and (3)` `my position with the audited company is that of its auditor` (JUST `I am otherwise an officer or employee of the audited company`)
        `subsection (2)` MEANS
            `s 1214(2) this subsection applies to the person` `my position counts` `I am a partner or employee of an officer or employee of the audited company` `I am a partnership of which an officer or employee of the audited company is a partner`
        `subsection (3)` MEANS
            `s 1214(3) this subsection applies to the person` (JUST `I am an officer or employee of an associated undertaking`) `I am a partner or employee of an officer or employee of an associated undertaking` `I am a partnership of which an officer or employee of an associated undertaking is a partner`
        `subsection (4)` MEANS
            `s 1214(4) this subsection applies to the person` `a connection exists with the audited company or an associated undertaking` (JUST `the connection is of a description specified by regulations`)

@export Under section 1215(1), must I resign and give written notice because I have lost my independence?
GIVEN `I am a statutory auditor` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are you currently a statutory auditor of an audited person?
      `I have become prohibited from acting by section 1214(1)` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Have you, at a time during your term of office, become prohibited by section 1214(1) from acting as its statutory auditor?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 1215(1), must I resign and give written notice because I have lost my independence` IS
    `s 1215(1) the statutory auditor must immediately resign and give notice` `I am a statutory auditor` (JUST `I have become prohibited from acting by section 1214(1)`)

@export Under section 1215(2), am I guilty of an offence for acting without independence or for not giving the notice?
GIVEN `I acted as a statutory auditor although section 1214(1) prohibited it` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did you act as a statutory auditor of an audited person although section 1214(1) prohibited you from acting?
      `I did not give the notice in writing that I had resigned` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did you fail to give the audited person, as required, written notice that you had resigned for lack of independence?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 1215(2), am I guilty of an offence for acting without independence or for not giving the notice` IS
    `s 1215(2) the person is guilty of an offence` `I acted as a statutory auditor although section 1214(1) prohibited it` `I did not give the notice in writing that I had resigned`

@export Under section 1215(7), do I have a defence to the offence of acting without independence?
GIVEN `I show that I did not know I was prohibited` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Can you show that you did not know that you were, or had become, prohibited from acting by section 1214(1)?
      `I show that I had no reason to believe I was prohibited` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Can you show that you had no reason to believe that you were, or had become, so prohibited?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 1215(7), do I have a defence to the offence of acting without independence` IS
    `s 1215(7) the defence is made out` `I show that I did not know I was prohibited` `I show that I had no reason to believe I was prohibited`

§§ `Appointment of a partnership (s 1216)`

@export Under section 1216(2), is my firm's appointment an appointment of the partnership as such and not of the partners?
GIVEN `the partnership is constituted under the law of England and Wales` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the partnership constituted under the law of England and Wales?
      `the partnership is constituted under the law of Northern Ireland` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the partnership constituted under the law of Northern Ireland?
      `the partnership is constituted under the law of another place where a partnership is not a legal person` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the partnership constituted under the law of another country or territory in which a partnership is not a legal person?
      `the partnership is appointed as statutory auditor` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the partnership appointed as statutory auditor of an audited person by virtue of Chapter 2 of Part 42?
      `a contrary intention appears` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does a contrary intention appear (for example in the terms of appointment)?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 1216(2), is my firm's appointment an appointment of the partnership as such and not of the partners` IS
    `s 1216(2) the appointment is an appointment of the partnership as such and not of the partners`
        (`s 1216(1) this section applies` `the partnership is constituted under the law of England and Wales` `the partnership is constituted under the law of Northern Ireland` `the partnership is constituted under the law of another place where a partnership is not a legal person` `the partnership is appointed as statutory auditor`)
        `a contrary intention appears`

@export Under section 1216(3), does the audited company's appointment pass to the firm that takes over when the partnership ceases?
GIVEN `the partnership has ceased` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has the partnership that was appointed ceased?
      `the successor is a partnership` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the successor a partnership (answer no if it is another person who carried the practice on in partnership)?
      `the successor in fact succeeds to the practice` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does the successor in fact succeed to the practice of the former partnership?
      `the successor's members are substantially the same` IS A BOOLEAN @desc If the successor is a partnership: are its members substantially the same as those of the former partnership?
      `the successor takes the whole or substantially the whole of the business` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does the successor take the whole or substantially the whole of the business of the former partnership?
      `the successor is eligible by virtue of Chapter 2` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the successor eligible for appointment as a statutory auditor by virtue of Chapter 2 of Part 42?
      `the successor is prohibited by section 1214(1)` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the successor prohibited by section 1214(1) (lack of independence) from acting as statutory auditor of the audited company?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 1216(3), does the audited company's appointment pass to the firm that takes over when the partnership ceases` IS
    `s 1216(3) the appointment is treated as extending to the successor`
        `the partnership has ceased`
        (IF `the successor is a partnership` THEN `the successor is appropriate and succeeds` ELSE JUST FALSE)
        (IF `the successor is a partnership` THEN JUST FALSE ELSE `the successor is appropriate and succeeds`)
        (`s 1216(4)(a) the partnership is regarded as succeeding to the practice of the former partnership` `the successor is a partnership` `the successor's members are substantially the same`)
        (`s 1216(4)(b) the partnership or other person is regarded as succeeding to the practice of the former partnership` `the successor takes the whole or substantially the whole of the business`)
    WHERE
        `the successor is appropriate and succeeds` MEANS
            `coa26 support both answers` (JUST `the successor in fact succeeds to the practice`) `the successor is appropriate`
        `the successor is appropriate` MEANS
            `s 1216(6) the partnership or other person is appropriate` (JUST `the successor is eligible by virtue of Chapter 2`) (IF `the successor is prohibited by section 1214(1)` THEN JUST FALSE ELSE NOTHING)

§§ `Supervisory bodies, damages and qualifications (ss 1217-1222)`

@export Under section 1217(2), am I a member of a supervisory body for the purposes of Part 42?
GIVEN `I am subject to the supervisory body's rules in seeking appointment or acting as a statutory auditor` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are you subject to the supervisory body's rules when you seek appointment or act as a statutory auditor (whether or not you are formally a member)?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 1217(2), am I a member of a supervisory body for the purposes of Part 42` IS
    `s 1217(2) the person is a member of the supervisory body` `I am subject to the supervisory body's rules in seeking appointment or acting as a statutory auditor`

@export Under section 1218(1), is a recognised supervisory body, or one of its officers, employees or governors, liable in damages to me for what it did?
GIVEN `it is a recognised supervisory body` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the person you complain of a recognised supervisory body?
      `it is an officer or employee of a recognised supervisory body` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the person you complain of an officer or employee of a recognised supervisory body?
      `it is a member of the governing body of a recognised supervisory body` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the person you complain of a member of the governing body of a recognised supervisory body?
      `the function related to Schedule 10 rules, practices, powers or arrangements` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did the act or omission arise from the body's rules, practices, powers or arrangements to which Part 2 of Schedule 10 applies?
      `the function related to the Schedule 10 paragraph 20 obligations` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did it arise from the obligations that paragraph 20 of Schedule 10 requires the body to comply with?
      `the function related to guidance issued by the body` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did it arise from guidance issued by the body?
      `the function related to obligations under Part 42 or the 2016 Regulations` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did it arise from obligations imposed on the body by or by virtue of Part 42 or the Statutory Auditors and Third Country Auditors Regulations 2016?
      `the function related to obligations under the Audit Regulation` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did it arise from obligations imposed on the body by or by virtue of the Audit Regulation?
      `the act or omission was in bad faith` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the act or omission shown to have been in bad faith?
      `damages are sought because the act was unlawful under the Human Rights Act 1998` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are damages sought on the ground that the act or omission was unlawful as a result of section 6(1) of the Human Rights Act 1998?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 1218(1), is a recognised supervisory body, or one of its officers, employees or governors, liable in damages to me for what it did` IS
    `s 1218(1) the person is liable in damages for anything done or omitted in the discharge or purported discharge of the function`
        (`s 1218(2) the person is within subsection (2)` `it is a recognised supervisory body` `it is an officer or employee of a recognised supervisory body` `it is a member of the governing body of a recognised supervisory body`)
        (`s 1218(3) subsection (1) applies to the function of the recognised supervisory body` `the function related to Schedule 10 rules, practices, powers or arrangements` `the function related to the Schedule 10 paragraph 20 obligations` `the function related to guidance issued by the body` `the function related to obligations under Part 42 or the 2016 Regulations` `the function related to obligations under the Audit Regulation`)
        (`s 1218(5) subsection (1) does not apply to the act or omission` `the act or omission was in bad faith` `damages are sought because the act was unlawful under the Human Rights Act 1998`)

@export Under section 1219(1), do I hold an appropriate qualification for the purposes of Chapter 2 of Part 42?
GIVEN `I hold a recognised professional qualification obtained in the United Kingdom` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Do you hold a recognised professional qualification obtained in the United Kingdom?
      `that qualification is recognised under Schedule 11` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is that qualification a recognised professional qualification under Schedule 11? Answer no if you hold none.
      `before the commencement I held an appropriate qualification under the Companies Act 1989` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Immediately before the commencement of Chapter 2 of Part 42, did you hold an appropriate qualification for the purposes of Part 2 of the Companies Act 1989 by virtue of section 31(1)(a) or (c), or were you treated as holding one by virtue of section 31(2), (3) or (4)?
      `before the commencement I held an appropriate qualification under the 1990 Northern Ireland Order` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Immediately before that commencement, did you hold an appropriate qualification for the purposes of Part III of the Companies (Northern Ireland) Order 1990 by virtue of Article 34(1)(a) or (c), or were you treated as holding one by virtue of Article 34(2), (3) or (4)?
      `the date I began my course of study or practical training` IS A DATE @desc On what date did you begin the course of study or practical training that led to your professional qualification in accountancy?
      `my qualification is in accountancy from a United Kingdom body` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is your professional qualification one in accountancy offered by a body established in the United Kingdom?
      `the date I obtained my qualification` IS A DATE @desc On what date did you obtain that qualification?
      `the Secretary of State approved my qualification` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did the Secretary of State approve your qualification as an appropriate qualification for the purposes of Chapter 2 of Part 42?
      `the date the Secretary of State approved it` IS A DATE @desc On what date did the Secretary of State approve it? (Any date if he did not.)
      `I am regarded as holding an approved third country qualification` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are you regarded, for the purposes of Chapter 2 of Part 42, as holding an approved third country qualification?
      `a direction under section 1221(5) applies to me` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does a direction of the Secretary of State under section 1221(5) require additional educational qualifications from you?
      `I hold the additional educational qualifications` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Do you hold the additional educational qualifications that direction specifies?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 1219(1), do I hold an appropriate qualification for the purposes of Chapter 2 of Part 42` IS
    `s 1219(1) the person holds an appropriate qualification`
        `I hold a recognised professional qualification obtained in the United Kingdom`
        (JUST `that qualification is recognised under Schedule 11`)
        `before the commencement I held an appropriate qualification under the Companies Act 1989`
        FALSE
        `before the commencement I held an appropriate qualification under the 1990 Northern Ireland Order`
        FALSE
        `within subsection (2)`
        (JUST `I am regarded as holding an approved third country qualification`)
        `a direction under section 1221(5) applies to me`
        `I hold the additional educational qualifications`
    WHERE
        -- (b)(i) and (b)(ii) are asked as one fact (and so are (c)(i) and (c)(ii)); the second slot of each pair is a fixed FALSE.
        `within subsection (2)` MEANS
            `s 1219(2) the person is within this subsection`
                `the date I began my course of study or practical training`
                `my qualification is in accountancy from a United Kingdom body`
                `the date I obtained my qualification`
                (IF `the Secretary of State approved my qualification` THEN JUST `the date the Secretary of State approved it` ELSE NOTHING)

@export Under section 1221(1B), have I met the requirement my third country declaration sets?
GIVEN `the way the declaration specifies` IS A `s 1221(1B) way the declaration specifies that the condition is satisfied` @desc How does the declaration say the condition is satisfied: only by an aptitude test, only by an adaptation period, or by either according to your choice?
      `I have passed an aptitude test in accordance with section 1221(7A)` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Have you passed an aptitude test in accordance with section 1221(7A)?
      `I have completed an adaptation period in accordance with section 1221(7C) and (7D)` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Have you completed an adaptation period in accordance with section 1221(7C) and (7D)?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 1221(1B), have I met the requirement my third country declaration sets` IS
    `s 1221(1B) the person has met the requirement the declaration specifies` `the way the declaration specifies` `I have passed an aptitude test in accordance with section 1221(7A)` `I have completed an adaptation period in accordance with section 1221(7C) and (7D)`

@export Under section 1221(7C), is my period of supervised practice an adaptation period?
GIVEN `the length of my period in months` IS A NUMBER @desc How long is your period of supervised practice, in months?
      `I pursue the profession under the supervision of a person holding an appropriate qualification` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Do you pursue the profession of statutory auditor under the supervision of another person who holds an appropriate qualification?
      `my pursuit is subject to an assessment of my ability` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is your pursuit subject to an assessment of your ability to pursue the profession of statutory auditor in the United Kingdom?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 1221(7C), is my period of supervised practice an adaptation period` IS
    `s 1221(7C) the period is an adaptation period` `the length of my period in months` `I pursue the profession under the supervision of a person holding an appropriate qualification` `my pursuit is subject to an assessment of my ability`

@export Under section 1222(1), may I be appointed auditor of this company if my only qualification is a retained 1967 Act authorisation?
GIVEN `my only appropriate qualification rests on a 1967 Act authorisation` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is your only appropriate qualification based on your retention of an authorisation originally granted by the Board of Trade or the Secretary of State under section 13(1) of the Companies Act 1967?
      `the company is a quoted company` IS A BOOLEAN @desc At the time of your appointment, is the company a quoted company within the meaning of section 385(2)?
      `a parent undertaking of the company is a quoted company` IS A BOOLEAN @desc At that time, is any parent undertaking of which the company is a subsidiary undertaking a quoted company within the meaning of section 385(2)?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 1222(1), may I be appointed auditor of this company if my only qualification is a retained 1967 Act authorisation` IS
    `s 1222(1) the person is eligible for appointment as auditor of the company` `my only appropriate qualification rests on a 1967 Act authorisation` (`s 1222(2) the company is unquoted` (JUST `the company is a quoted company`) (LIST JUST `a parent undertaking of the company is a quoted company`))

§§ `Information and disclosure (ss 1224-1224B)`

@export Under section 1224, can the Secretary of State require me to give information by written notice?
GIVEN `I am eligible for appointment as a statutory auditor by virtue of Chapter 2` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are you eligible for appointment as a statutory auditor by virtue of Chapter 2 of Part 42?
      `the requirement is made by notice in writing` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the requirement made by notice in writing?
      `the information is such as he may reasonably require for his functions under Part 42` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the information such as the Secretary of State may reasonably require for the exercise of his functions under Part 42?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 1224, can the Secretary of State require me to give information by written notice` IS
    `s 1224(1) the Secretary of State may by notice in writing require the person to give the information`
        (`s 1224(2) the person is within subsection (2)` (JUST FALSE) (JUST FALSE) (JUST `I am eligible for appointment as a statutory auditor by virtue of Chapter 2`))
        `the requirement is made by notice in writing`
        `the information is such as he may reasonably require for his functions under Part 42`

@export Under section 1224A(3), may a body holding information about my private affairs or business disclose it without my consent?
GIVEN `the information relates to my private affairs` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does the information relate to your private affairs (as an individual)?
      `the information relates to a particular business` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does the information relate to a particular business?
      `it is held by a body within section 1224A(2)` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it held by a recognised supervisory body, a recognised qualifying body, the competent authority, the Independent Supervisor, the Secretary of State or a body designated under section 1252?
      `it was provided in connection with the body's functions under Part 42` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Was it provided in connection with the body's functions under Part 42, sections 522 to 524, the 2016 Regulations or the Audit Regulation?
      `I am alive or the business continues to be carried on` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are you still alive (or, for a business, does it continue to be carried on)?
      `I consent to the disclosure` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Have you (or the person for the time being carrying on the business) consented to the disclosure?
      `the disclosure facilitates the body's functions` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the disclosure made for the purpose of facilitating the body's carrying out of any of its functions?
      `the disclosure is to a person specified in Part 1 of Schedule 11A` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the disclosure made to a person specified in Part 1 of Schedule 11A?
      `the information is of a description specified in Part 2 of Schedule 11A` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the information of a description specified in Part 2 of Schedule 11A?
      `the disclosure is made in accordance with Part 3 of Schedule 11A` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the disclosure made in accordance with Part 3 of Schedule 11A?
      `the information is or has been available to the public` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the information, or has it been, available to the public from any other source?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 1224A(3), may a body holding information about my private affairs or business disclose it without my consent` IS
    `s 1224A(3) the information may be disclosed`
        `subsection (1) applies`
        `I am alive or the business continues to be carried on`
        `I consent to the disclosure`
        (`s 1224A(4) subsection (3) does not apply to the disclosure` `the disclosure facilitates the body's functions` `the disclosure is to a person specified in Part 1 of Schedule 11A` `the information is of a description specified in Part 2 of Schedule 11A` `the disclosure is made in accordance with Part 3 of Schedule 11A`)
        (`s 1224A(6) the section does not prohibit the disclosure` `the information is or has been available to the public`)
    WHERE
        `subsection (1) applies` MEANS
            `s 1224A(1) the section applies to the information`
                `the information relates to my private affairs`
                `the information relates to a particular business`
                (IF `it is held by a body within section 1224A(2)` THEN JUST TRUE ELSE JUST FALSE)
                `it was provided in connection with the body's functions under Part 42`

@export Under section 1224B(1), am I guilty of an offence if I disclose information in contravention of section 1224A?
GIVEN `I disclosed the information` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did you disclose the information?
      `the disclosure was in contravention of section 1224A` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Was the disclosure made in contravention of section 1224A (that is, the restriction on disclosure applied and no exception did)?
      `I did not know and had no reason to suspect the information had been so provided` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did you not know, and have no reason to suspect, that the information had been provided to a body within section 1224A(1)?
      `I took all reasonable steps and exercised all due diligence` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did you take all reasonable steps and exercise all due diligence to avoid committing the offence?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 1224B(1), am I guilty of an offence if I disclose information in contravention of section 1224A` IS
    `s 1224B(1) the person is guilty of an offence` `I disclosed the information` (IF `the disclosure was in contravention of section 1224A` THEN JUST FALSE ELSE JUST TRUE) `I did not know and had no reason to suspect the information had been so provided` `I took all reasonable steps and exercised all due diligence`

@export Under section 1224B(2), what is the longest term of imprisonment I can be given for that offence, in months?
GIVEN `how I am convicted` IS A `Mode of conviction` @desc How are you convicted: on conviction on indictment, or on summary conviction in England and Wales, Scotland or Northern Ireland?
GIVETH A MAYBE NUMBER
DECIDE `Under section 1224B(2), what is the longest term of imprisonment I can be given for that offence, in months` IS
    CONSIDER `s 1224B(2) the penalty for an offence under section 1224B` `how I am convicted`
    WHEN NOTHING THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (silent): a summary conviction in no stated place
    WHEN JUST penalty THEN
        CONSIDER penalty's `imprisonment not exceeding`
        WHEN NOTHING THEN NOTHING
        WHEN JUST term THEN
            CONSIDER term's unit
            WHEN Years THEN JUST (term's `number of units` TIMES 12)
            WHEN Months THEN JUST (term's `number of units`)
            OTHERWISE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (silent): no other unit is used in the section

§§ `Auditors General (ss 1226-1235)`
-- These questions are for an Auditor General, who is an individual. Ask them only if you are one.

@export Under section 1226(2), am I, as an Auditor General, eligible for appointment as a statutory auditor?
GIVEN `I am the Comptroller and Auditor General` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are you the Comptroller and Auditor General?
      `I am the Auditor General for Scotland` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are you the Auditor General for Scotland?
      `I am the Auditor General for Wales` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are you the Auditor General for Wales?
      `I am the Comptroller and Auditor General for Northern Ireland` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are you the Comptroller and Auditor General for Northern Ireland?
      `a suspension notice suspends my eligibility` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does a suspension notice having effect under section 1234 suspend your eligibility for appointment as a statutory auditor?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 1226(2), am I, as an Auditor General, eligible for appointment as a statutory auditor` IS
    `s 1226(2) the Auditor General is eligible for appointment as a statutory auditor`
        (`s 1226(1) the person is an Auditor General` `I am the Comptroller and Auditor General` `I am the Auditor General for Scotland` `I am the Auditor General for Wales` `I am the Comptroller and Auditor General for Northern Ireland`)
        `a suspension notice suspends my eligibility`

@export Under section 1227, have I secured that each individual doing statutory audit work for me is eligible?
GIVEN `the individual is responsible for statutory audit work on my behalf` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the individual responsible for statutory audit work on your behalf?
      `the individual is eligible for appointment as a statutory auditor by virtue of Chapter 2` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is that individual eligible for appointment as a statutory auditor by virtue of Chapter 2 of Part 42?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 1227, have I secured that each individual doing statutory audit work for me is eligible` IS
    `s 1227 the Auditor General has secured that the individual is eligible for appointment as a statutory auditor by virtue of Chapter 2` `the individual is responsible for statutory audit work on my behalf` (JUST `the individual is eligible for appointment as a statutory auditor by virtue of Chapter 2`)

@export Under section 1230(1), have I complied with my duties under the supervision arrangements?
GIVEN `I complied with the standards determined under the arrangements` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Have you complied with any standards of professional integrity, independence or technical practice determined under the supervision arrangements?
      `I took the steps reasonably required to enable monitoring by inspection` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Have you taken such steps as may reasonably be required to enable your performance of statutory audits to be monitored by inspections under the arrangements?
      `I complied with any disciplinary decision made under the arrangements` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Have you complied with any decision on disciplinary action made under the supervision arrangements?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 1230(1), have I complied with my duties under the supervision arrangements` IS
    `s 1230(1) the Auditor General has complied with the duties in subsection (1)` `I complied with the standards determined under the arrangements` `I took the steps reasonably required to enable monitoring by inspection` `I complied with any disciplinary decision made under the arrangements`

@export Under section 1230(2), how much of the costs of the supervision arrangements must I pay, in pounds?
GIVEN `the costs incurred for the purposes of the arrangements, in pounds` IS A NUMBER @desc What costs have been incurred by the Independent Supervisor or the body for the purposes of the arrangements, in pounds?
      `the Independent Supervisor has notified me of a proportion` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has the Independent Supervisor notified you in writing of the proportion of those costs you must pay?
      `the proportion notified, as a fraction` IS A NUMBER @desc What proportion has it notified, as a fraction (for example 0.25 for a quarter)? Any number if none has been notified.
GIVETH A MAYBE NUMBER
DECIDE `Under section 1230(2), how much of the costs of the supervision arrangements must I pay, in pounds` IS
    `s 1230(2) the amount the Auditor General must pay, in pounds` `the costs incurred for the purposes of the arrangements, in pounds` (IF `the Independent Supervisor has notified me of a proportion` THEN JUST `the proportion notified, as a fraction` ELSE NOTHING)

@export Under section 1232(1), can the Independent Supervisor require me to notify it of events and give it information?
GIVEN `I am an Auditor General` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are you an Auditor General?
      `the requirement is to notify it immediately of specified events and give information about them` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the requirement to notify the Independent Supervisor immediately of events it specifies in writing, and to give it information about those events?
      `the requirement is to give information at specified times or for specified periods` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the requirement to give it, at times or for periods it specifies in writing, information so specified?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 1232(1), can the Independent Supervisor require me to notify it of events and give it information` IS
    `s 1232(1) the Independent Supervisor may require the body to notify or give information` `I am an Auditor General` `the requirement is to notify it immediately of specified events and give information about them` `the requirement is to give information at specified times or for specified periods`

@export Under section 1233(1), can the Independent Supervisor require me by written notice to give it information?
GIVEN `I am an Auditor General` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are you an Auditor General?
      `the requirement is made by notice in writing` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the requirement made by notice in writing?
      `the information is such as it may reasonably require for its functions` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the information such as the Independent Supervisor may reasonably require for the exercise of its functions under Part 42?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 1233(1), can the Independent Supervisor require me by written notice to give it information` IS
    `s 1233(1) the Independent Supervisor may by notice in writing require the person to give the information` (JUST `I am an Auditor General`) `the requirement is made by notice in writing` `the information is such as it may reasonably require for its functions`

@export Under section 1234(6), may I still make representations about a proposed suspension notice?
GIVEN `I am an Auditor General` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are you the Auditor General to whom the notice of intention was given?
      `the date the notice of intention was served or published` IS A DATE @desc On what date was the notice of intention (under section 1234(4)) served or published?
      `the day I make my representations` IS A DATE @desc On what day do you make (or propose to make) your representations?
      `the Independent Supervisor allowed a longer period` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has the Independent Supervisor allowed a longer period for representations?
      `the last day of that longer period` IS A DATE @desc What is the last day of that longer period? (Any date if none was allowed.)
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 1234(6), may I still make representations about a proposed suspension notice` IS
    `s 1234(6) the person may make written representations and, if desired, oral representations`
        (`s 1234(7) the person is within subsection (7)` `I am an Auditor General` FALSE)
        `the date the notice of intention was served or published`
        `the day I make my representations`
        (IF `the Independent Supervisor allowed a longer period` THEN JUST `the last day of that longer period` ELSE NOTHING)

@export Under section 1235(1), may I act as statutory auditor of an audited person while a suspension notice has effect?
GIVEN `a suspension notice issued to me in respect of the audited person has effect` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does a suspension notice issued to you in respect of the audited person have effect now?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 1235(1), may I act as statutory auditor of an audited person while a suspension notice has effect` IS
    `s 1235(1) the Auditor General may act as statutory auditor of the audited person` `a suspension notice issued to me in respect of the audited person has effect`

@export Under section 1235(2), must I resign and give written notice when a suspension notice takes effect?
GIVEN `I hold office as a statutory auditor` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Do you hold office as a statutory auditor of the audited person?
      `a suspension notice issued to me in respect of the audited person takes effect during my term of office` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does a suspension notice issued to you in respect of the audited person take effect at a time during your term of office?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 1235(2), must I resign and give written notice when a suspension notice takes effect` IS
    `s 1235(2) the Auditor General must immediately resign and give notice` `I hold office as a statutory auditor` `a suspension notice issued to me in respect of the audited person takes effect during my term of office`

@export Under section 1235(3), does a suspension notice make me ineligible for the purposes of the section 1213 offences?
GIVEN `a suspension notice has effect in relation to me` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does a suspension notice have effect in relation to you as an Auditor General?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 1235(3), does a suspension notice make me ineligible for the purposes of the section 1213 offences` IS
    `s 1235(3) the suspension notice makes the Auditor General ineligible for the purposes of section 1213` `a suspension notice has effect in relation to me`

-- ====================================================================================================
-- seat questions from part coa27 (merged by the lead on 2026-11-12; unchanged text follows)
-- ====================================================================================================
-- coa27-seat.l4: Companies Act 2006 (United Kingdom), Part 42 (second half: ss 1239 to 1264) and Part 43 (ss 1265 to 1273) -- THE SEAT LAYER.
--
-- SEAT: an individual who is, or is about to become, a director, a company secretary or a member (shareholder) of a company registered
-- under the Act, or who deals with one (an auditor, a person who holds shares or other securities in an issuer, a person served with a notice),
-- asking on facts they can state what the Act requires or lets them do, what rights they have against the company or its directors, what they
-- must disclose, file, approve or vote on and by when, and what follows (liability, offences, penalties) if it is not done.
-- (Assumed, not ruled: the Act is addressed to companies, so the individual is whoever stands in a company's management or ownership.)
--
-- This layer phrases the rules already encoded in the modules imported above as questions that person would ask. Nothing here is new law:
-- every question builds the modules' own records from plain inputs and calls the SAME module rule. Every question is named "Under section N,"
-- with the Act's own numbering and says the scope its answer claims. Provisions that address only an official (the Secretary of State's powers to
-- make regulations and orders, delegation, foreign cooperation) are encoded in layer 1 and have no question here, except for what they mean to the
-- person (s 1253D to 1253DC for a statutory auditor's transfers; ss 1267 and 1268, FSMA 89H to 89N, for a person on whom the competent authority acts).
-- The amounts a level on the standard scale stands for, the statutory maximum, the general limit in a magistrates' court and every fee the Secretary
-- of State prescribes are not in the Act: they are asked as numbers, never assumed.
--
-- HOW TO READ AN ANSWER. A question that answers BOOLEAN-like (MAYBE BOOLEAN) answers JUST TRUE (the text says yes), JUST FALSE (the text says no in
-- its own words) or NOTHING (the text does not decide: silent, limited by its own wording, a borrowed term, or a list that is not closed).
-- NOTHING must never be read as "no".

§ `Companies Act 2006, Part 42 -- the register of auditors and registered third country auditors`

§§ `The register and third country auditors (ss 1239 to 1245)`

-- s 1239(3). What the register entry of a firm eligible as a statutory auditor by virtue of Chapter 2 must show about the people behind it.
@export Under section 1239(3), what must the register entry of a firm that is a statutory auditor by virtue of Chapter 2 show about its directors, shareholders, members or partners?
GIVEN `my firm is` IS A `s 1239(3) kind of firm` @desc What kind of firm is it: a body corporate other than a limited liability partnership, a limited liability partnership, a corporation sole, or a partnership?
GIVETH A `s 1239(3) required information`
DECIDE `Under section 1239(3), what must the register entry of a firm show about its directors, shareholders, members or partners` IS
    `s 1239(3) the information referred to in subsection (2)(e) for a` `my firm is`

-- s 1241(1). A registered third country auditor is a third country auditor who is entered in the register.
@export Under section 1241(1), am I a registered third country auditor?
GIVEN `I am a third country auditor` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are you a third country auditor (a person who is not eligible for appointment as a statutory auditor but is eligible to audit accounts of bodies incorporated under the law of a third country)?
      `I am entered in the register of auditors kept under regulations under section 1239(1)` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are you entered in the register of auditors?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 1241(1), am I a registered third country auditor` IS
    `s 1241(1) the person is a registered third country auditor` `I am a third country auditor` `I am entered in the register of auditors kept under regulations under section 1239(1)`

-- s 1241(2). A UK-traded third country company.
@export Under section 1241(2), is the company I am dealing with a UK-traded third country company?
GIVEN `the company is incorporated or formed under the law of a third country` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the company incorporated or formed under the law of a country or territory other than the United Kingdom?
      `its transferable securities are admitted to trading on a UK regulated market` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are its transferable securities admitted to trading on a UK regulated market?
      `the Secretary of State has excluded it, or a description of company it belongs to, by order` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has the Secretary of State by order excluded the company, or the description of company it belongs to, from this definition?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 1241(2), is the company a UK-traded third country company` IS
    `s 1241(2) the body corporate is a UK-traded third country company` `the company is incorporated or formed under the law of a third country` `its transferable securities are admitted to trading on a UK regulated market` `the Secretary of State has excluded it, or a description of company it belongs to, by order`

-- s 1242(1), (4). A registered third country auditor of a UK-traded third country company must take part in the Schedule 12 arrangements, unless a direction disapplies it.
@export Under section 1242(1), must I, a registered third country auditor, take part in the independent monitoring and investigation arrangements in Schedule 12 for this audit?
GIVEN `I am a registered third country auditor` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are you a registered third country auditor?
      `I audit the accounts of a UK-traded third country company` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Do you audit the accounts of a UK-traded third country company?
      `the Secretary of State has directed in writing that this duty does not apply to this audit` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has the Secretary of State directed you in writing that subsection (1) does not apply to you or to this company or this audit?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 1242(1), must I take part in the Schedule 12 arrangements for this audit` IS
    `s 1242(1) the registered third country auditor must participate in the Schedule 12 arrangements` `I am a registered third country auditor` `I audit the accounts of a UK-traded third country company` `the Secretary of State has directed in writing that this duty does not apply to this audit`

-- s 1244(1). The Secretary of State's written demand for information.
@export Under section 1244(1), must I, a registered third country auditor, give the Secretary of State the information he has asked for in writing?
GIVEN `I am a registered third country auditor` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are you a registered third country auditor?
      `the Secretary of State has asked for the information by notice in writing` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has the Secretary of State required the information by a notice in writing?
      `the information is such as he may reasonably require for the exercise of his functions under Part 42` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the information something he may reasonably require for the exercise of his functions under this Part?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 1244(1), must I give the Secretary of State the information he has asked for` IS
    `s 1244(1) the registered third country auditor must give the information` `I am a registered third country auditor` `the Secretary of State has asked for the information by notice in writing` `the information is such as he may reasonably require for the exercise of his functions under Part 42`

-- s 1244(2). The time the Secretary of State specifies.
@export Under section 1244(2), did I give the Secretary of State the information within the time he specified?
GIVEN `the last day of the time the Secretary of State specified` IS A DATE @desc What is the last day of the time the Secretary of State specified (day, month, year)?
      `the day I gave the information` IS A DATE @desc On what day did you give him the information (day, month, year)?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 1244(2), did I give the information within the time specified` IS
    `s 1244(2) the information was given within the time specified` `the last day of the time the Secretary of State specified` `the day I gave the information`

-- s 1245(3). Which court the Secretary of State applies to for a compliance order.
@export Under section 1245(3), which court hears the Secretary of State's application for an order requiring a registered third country auditor to comply?
GIVEN `the proceedings are in Scotland` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are the proceedings in Scotland?
GIVETH A `s 1245(3) court`
DECIDE `Under section 1245(3), which court hears the application for a compliance order` IS
    `s 1245(3) the court is` `the proceedings are in Scotland`

§ `Companies Act 2006, Part 42 -- a second audit and the offences around it`

§§ `A second audit of my company (ss 1248 and 1249). Only arises if the Secretary of State has found, or is considering, that your company's auditor was not an appropriate person.`

-- s 1248(3). Whether a person is an "appropriate" person to be statutory auditor of the company.
@export Under section 1248(3), is the person appointed as my company's statutory auditor an appropriate person?
GIVEN `the person is an Auditor General` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the person an Auditor General?
      `the person is eligible for appointment as a statutory auditor` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the person eligible for appointment as a statutory auditor?
      `the person is eligible for appointment as statutory auditor of my company` IS A BOOLEAN @desc If the person is an Auditor General: is he eligible for appointment as statutory auditor of this company?
      `the person is prohibited by section 1214(1) from acting as statutory auditor of my company` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the person prohibited by the independence requirement (section 1214(1)) from acting as statutory auditor of the company?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 1248(3), is the person appointed as my company's statutory auditor an appropriate person` IS
    `s 1248(3) the person is appropriate` `the auditor`
    WHERE
        `the auditor` MEANS `s 1248(3) person` WITH
            `s 1248(3) is an Auditor General` IS `the person is an Auditor General`
            `s 1248(3) is eligible for appointment as a statutory auditor` IS `the person is eligible for appointment as a statutory auditor`
            `s 1248(3) is eligible for appointment as statutory auditor of the company` IS `the person is eligible for appointment as statutory auditor of my company`
            `s 1248(3) is prohibited by section 1214(1) from acting as statutory auditor of the company (the independence requirement: a seam answer)` IS JUST `the person is prohibited by section 1214(1) from acting as statutory auditor of my company`

-- s 1248(1), (2). The Secretary of State's direction to retain an appropriate person.
@export Under section 1248(2), can the Secretary of State direct my company to retain an appropriate person to carry out a second audit or review the first?
GIVEN `a person appointed as statutory auditor of my company was not an appropriate person for any part of the period during which the audit was conducted` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Was the person appointed as your company's statutory auditor not an appropriate person for any part of the period during which the audit was conducted?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 1248(2), can the Secretary of State direct my company to retain an appropriate person` IS
    `s 1248(2) the Secretary of State may direct the company to retain an appropriate person` (`s 1248(1) this section applies` `a person appointed as statutory auditor of my company was not an appropriate person for any part of the period during which the audit was conducted` EQUALS JUST TRUE)

-- s 1248(5)(a). The last day for complying with the direction.
@export Under section 1248(5)(a), what is the last day on which my company can comply with the Secretary of State's direction?
GIVEN `the day the direction was given to the company` IS A DATE @desc On what day was the direction given to your company (day, month, year)?
GIVETH A DATE
DECIDE `Under section 1248(5)(a), what is the last day on which my company can comply with the direction` IS
    `s 1248(5)(a) the last day of the period of 21 days beginning with the date the direction is given` `the day the direction was given to the company`

-- s 1248(5). Is the company guilty of an offence for not complying with the direction?
@export Under section 1248(5), is my company guilty of an offence for failing to comply with the Secretary of State's direction for a second audit?
GIVEN `the day the direction was given to the company` IS A DATE @desc On what day was the direction given to your company (day, month, year)?
      `my company has complied with the direction` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has your company complied with the direction?
      `the day my company complied (any day if it has not)` IS A DATE @desc On what day did your company comply (day, month, year)? Give any day if it has not complied.
      `the day I am asking about` IS A DATE @desc On what day are you asking (day, month, year)?
      `my company has been convicted of a previous offence under subsection (5)` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has your company been convicted of a previous offence under subsection (5)?
      `the failure which led to that conviction continues after the conviction` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does the failure to comply which led to that conviction continue after the conviction?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 1248(5), is my company guilty of an offence for failing to comply with the direction` IS
    `s 1248(5) the company is guilty of an offence`
        (`s 1248(5)(a) the company fails to comply with the direction within the period of 21 days`
            `the day the direction was given to the company` `complied on` `the day I am asking about`)
        (`s 1248(5)(b) the failure continues after a previous conviction`
            `my company has been convicted of a previous offence under subsection (5)` `the failure which led to that conviction continues after the conviction`)
    WHERE
        `complied on` MEANS IF `my company has complied with the direction` THEN JUST `the day my company complied (any day if it has not)` ELSE NOTHING

-- s 1248(6), (7). The report of a review of the first audit.
@export Under section 1248(7), is my company guilty of an offence in connection with the report of a review of the first audit?
GIVEN `the day my company received the report` IS A DATE @desc On what day did your company receive the report (day, month, year)?
      `my company has sent a copy of the report to the registrar of companies` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has your company sent a copy of the report to the registrar of companies?
      `the day my company sent the copy (any day if it has not)` IS A DATE @desc On what day did it send the copy (day, month, year)? Give any day if it has not.
      `the day I am asking about` IS A DATE @desc On what day are you asking (day, month, year)?
      `the report states that a second audit is needed` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does the report state that a second audit is needed?
      `my company took the necessary steps immediately it received the report` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did your company take the steps necessary for the second audit immediately it received the report?
      `my company has been convicted of a previous offence under subsection (7)` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has your company been convicted of a previous offence under subsection (7)?
      `the failure which led to that conviction continues after the conviction` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does the failure to send the copy or take the steps which led to that conviction continue after the conviction?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 1248(7), is my company guilty of an offence in connection with the report` IS
    `s 1248(7) the company is guilty of an offence`
        (`s 1248(7)(a) the company fails to send a copy of the report to the registrar within the period of 21 days`
            `the day my company received the report` `sent on` `the day I am asking about`)
        (`s 1248(7)(b) the company fails to take the steps immediately it receives the report`
            `the report states that a second audit is needed` `my company took the necessary steps immediately it received the report`)
        (`s 1248(7)(c) the failure continues after a previous conviction`
            `my company has been convicted of a previous offence under subsection (7)` `the failure which led to that conviction continues after the conviction`)
    WHERE
        `sent on` MEANS IF `my company has sent a copy of the report to the registrar of companies` THEN JUST `the day my company sent the copy (any day if it has not)` ELSE NOTHING

-- s 1248(8). The most my company can be fined.
@export Under section 1248(8), what is the most my company can be fined for the offence, in pounds?
GIVEN `the offence is` IS A `s 1248(8) case` @desc Which offence: failing to comply with the direction within 21 days (5)(a), continuing to fail after a conviction (5)(b), failing to send the copy of the report within 21 days (7)(a), failing to take the steps immediately (7)(b), or continuing to fail after a conviction (7)(c)?
      `what level 4 on the standard scale stands for, in pounds` IS A NUMBER @desc How many pounds does level 4 on the standard scale stand for?
      `what level 5 on the standard scale stands for, in pounds` IS A NUMBER @desc How many pounds does level 5 on the standard scale stand for?
GIVETH A MAYBE NUMBER
DECIDE `Under section 1248(8), what is the most my company can be fined for the offence, in pounds` IS
    `s 1248(8) the maximum fine in pounds for` `the offence is` `what level 4 on the standard scale stands for, in pounds` `what level 5 on the standard scale stands for, in pounds`

-- s 1249(1). Recovering the cost of the second audit from the auditor.
@export Under section 1249(1), can my company recover from the auditor the costs it incurred in complying with section 1248?
GIVEN `the auditor is an Auditor General` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the auditor an Auditor General?
      `the auditor is eligible for appointment as a statutory auditor` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the auditor eligible for appointment as a statutory auditor?
      `the auditor is eligible for appointment as statutory auditor of my company` IS A BOOLEAN @desc If the auditor is an Auditor General: is he eligible for appointment as statutory auditor of this company?
      `the auditor is prohibited by section 1214(1) from acting as statutory auditor of my company` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the auditor prohibited by the independence requirement (section 1214(1)) from acting as statutory auditor of the company?
      `the auditor accepted the appointment, or continued to act, as statutory auditor of my company` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did the auditor accept the appointment, or continue to act, as statutory auditor of your company?
      `the auditor knew he was not an appropriate person` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did the auditor know, when he accepted or continued, that he was not an appropriate person?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 1249(1), can my company recover from the auditor the costs of complying with section 1248` IS
    `s 1249(1) the company may recover from the person the costs it incurred in complying with section 1248` `the auditor` `the auditor accepted the appointment, or continued to act, as statutory auditor of my company` `the auditor knew he was not an appropriate person`
    WHERE
        `the auditor` MEANS `s 1248(3) person` WITH
            `s 1248(3) is an Auditor General` IS `the auditor is an Auditor General`
            `s 1248(3) is eligible for appointment as a statutory auditor` IS `the auditor is eligible for appointment as a statutory auditor`
            `s 1248(3) is eligible for appointment as statutory auditor of the company` IS `the auditor is eligible for appointment as statutory auditor of my company`
            `s 1248(3) is prohibited by section 1214(1) from acting as statutory auditor of the company (the independence requirement: a seam answer)` IS JUST `the auditor is prohibited by section 1214(1) from acting as statutory auditor of my company`

@export Under section 1249(1), how much of the cost of the second audit can my company recover from the auditor, in pounds?
GIVEN `my company can recover its costs from the auditor` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Can your company recover its costs from the auditor (the answer to the question under section 1249(1))?
      `the costs my company incurred in complying with section 1248, in pounds` IS A NUMBER @desc How many pounds did your company incur in complying with the requirements of section 1248?
GIVETH A MAYBE NUMBER
DECIDE `Under section 1249(1), how much of the cost of the second audit can my company recover from the auditor` IS
    `s 1249(1) the amount the company may recover from the person` `my company can recover its costs from the auditor` `the costs my company incurred in complying with section 1248, in pounds`

-- s 1249(3). How a direction is enforced.
@export Under section 1249(3), how can the Secretary of State enforce a direction for a second audit against my company?
GIVEN `the Secretary of State has applied for enforcement` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has the Secretary of State applied to enforce the direction?
      `the proceedings are in Scotland` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are the proceedings in Scotland?
GIVETH A MAYBE `s 1239(8) remedy`
DECIDE `Under section 1249(3), how can the Secretary of State enforce a direction for a second audit` IS
    `s 1249(3) the direction is enforceable by` TRUE `the Secretary of State has applied for enforcement` `the proceedings are in Scotland`

§§ `False statements and holding out (s 1250). Only arises if you have given information to the Secretary of State, or have described yourself as a registered auditor.`

-- s 1250(1). The offence of giving misleading, false or deceptive information.
@export Under section 1250(1), am I guilty of an offence for the information I gave in an application, or in answer to a requirement, under Part 42?
GIVEN `I gave the information for the purposes of or in connection with an application under Part 42` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did you give the information for the purposes of, or in connection with, an application under Part 42?
      `I gave the information in purported compliance with a requirement imposed on me by or by virtue of Part 42` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did you give the information in purported compliance with a requirement imposed on you by or by virtue of Part 42?
      `I gave it knowingly` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did you give it knowing it was misleading, false or deceptive?
      `I gave it recklessly` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did you give it recklessly as to whether it was misleading, false or deceptive?
      `it is misleading, false or deceptive in a material particular` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the information misleading, false or deceptive in a material particular?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 1250(1), am I guilty of an offence for the information I gave` IS
    `s 1250(1) the person is guilty of an offence` `I gave the information for the purposes of or in connection with an application under Part 42` `I gave the information in purported compliance with a requirement imposed on me by or by virtue of Part 42` `I gave it knowingly` `I gave it recklessly` `it is misleading, false or deceptive in a material particular`

-- s 1250(2). Calling myself a registered auditor.
@export Under section 1250(2), am I committing an offence by describing myself as a registered auditor?
GIVEN `my name does not appear on the register of auditors in an entry made under section 1239(1)(a)` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is your name missing from the register of auditors as a person eligible for appointment as a statutory auditor?
      `I describe myself as a registered auditor` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Do you describe yourself as a registered auditor?
      `I hold myself out as indicating, or being reasonably understood to indicate, that I am a registered auditor` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Do you hold yourself out in a way that indicates, or could reasonably be understood to indicate, that you are a registered auditor?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 1250(2), am I committing an offence by describing myself as a registered auditor` IS
    `s 1250(2) the person commits an offence by describing himself as a registered auditor` `my name does not appear on the register of auditors in an entry made under section 1239(1)(a)` `I describe myself as a registered auditor` `I hold myself out as indicating, or being reasonably understood to indicate, that I am a registered auditor`

-- s 1250(3). Calling myself a registered third country auditor.
@export Under section 1250(3), am I committing an offence by describing myself as a registered third country auditor?
GIVEN `my name does not appear on the register of auditors in an entry made under section 1239(1)(b)` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is your name missing from the register of auditors as a third country auditor?
      `I describe myself as a registered third country auditor` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Do you describe yourself as a registered third country auditor?
      `I hold myself out as indicating, or being reasonably understood to indicate, that I am a registered third country auditor` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Do you hold yourself out in a way that indicates, or could reasonably be understood to indicate, that you are a registered third country auditor?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 1250(3), am I committing an offence by describing myself as a registered third country auditor` IS
    `s 1250(3) the person commits an offence by describing himself as a registered third country auditor` `my name does not appear on the register of auditors in an entry made under section 1239(1)(b)` `I describe myself as a registered third country auditor` `I hold myself out as indicating, or being reasonably understood to indicate, that I am a registered third country auditor`

-- s 1250(4). A body calling itself a recognised body.
@export Under section 1250(4), is my body committing an offence by describing itself as a recognised supervisory body or recognised qualifying body?
GIVEN `my body is not a recognised supervisory body or a recognised qualifying body` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is your body neither a recognised supervisory body nor a recognised qualifying body?
      `my body describes itself as so recognised` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does your body describe itself as so recognised?
      `my body so describes itself or holds itself out as to indicate, or be reasonably understood to indicate, that it is so recognised` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does your body describe itself or hold itself out in a way that indicates, or could reasonably be understood to indicate, that it is so recognised?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 1250(4), is my body committing an offence by describing itself as a recognised body` IS
    `s 1250(4) the body commits an offence by describing itself as a recognised body` `my body is not a recognised supervisory body or a recognised qualifying body` `my body describes itself as so recognised` `my body so describes itself or holds itself out as to indicate, or be reasonably understood to indicate, that it is so recognised`

-- s 1250(5). The punishment for the false-information offence.
@export Under section 1250(5), what is the most I can be punished for giving misleading, false or deceptive information, if convicted?
GIVEN `how I am convicted` IS A `Mode of conviction` @desc How would you be convicted: on indictment, or summarily in England and Wales, in Scotland, or in Northern Ireland?
      `the day I committed the offence` IS A DATE @desc On what day was the offence committed (day, month, year)?
      `the general limit in a magistrates' court, in months` IS A NUMBER @desc For a summary conviction in England and Wales: how many months is the general limit on a term of imprisonment in a magistrates' court?
GIVETH A MAYBE Penalty
DECIDE `Under section 1250(5), what is the most I can be punished for giving misleading, false or deceptive information` IS
    `s 1250(5) the penalty for an offence under subsection (1)` `how I am convicted` `the day I committed the offence` `the general limit in a magistrates' court, in months`

-- s 1250(6). The punishment for holding out.
@export Under section 1250(6), what is the most I can be punished for describing myself as a registered auditor, a registered third country auditor or a recognised body when I am not, if convicted?
GIVEN `how I am convicted` IS A `Mode of conviction` @desc How would you be convicted: summarily in England and Wales, in Scotland, or in Northern Ireland?
      `I committed the offence before section 281(5) of the Criminal Justice Act 2003 came into force` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Was the offence committed before section 281(5) of the Criminal Justice Act 2003 came into force?
GIVETH A MAYBE Penalty
DECIDE `Under section 1250(6), what is the most I can be punished for holding myself out` IS
    `s 1250(6) the penalty for an offence under subsection (2), (3) or (4)` `how I am convicted` `I committed the offence before section 281(5) of the Criminal Justice Act 2003 came into force`

-- s 1250(7). The maximum fine where the description was publicly displayed.
@export Under section 1250(7), what is the most I can be fined if I publicly displayed the description, in pounds?
GIVEN `the contravention involves a public display of the description` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did the contravention involve a public display of the description (for example a sign or a website)?
      `what level 5 on the standard scale stands for, in pounds` IS A NUMBER @desc How many pounds does level 5 on the standard scale stand for?
      `the number of days for which the display has continued` IS A NUMBER @desc For how many days has the display continued?
GIVETH A MAYBE NUMBER
DECIDE `Under section 1250(7), what is the most I can be fined for a public display, in pounds` IS
    `s 1250(7) the maximum fine that may be imposed` `the contravention involves a public display of the description` `what level 5 on the standard scale stands for, in pounds` `the number of days for which the display has continued`

-- s 1250(8). The defence.
@export Under section 1250(8), do I have a defence to a charge of holding myself out, because I took all reasonable precautions and exercised all due diligence?
GIVEN `I am charged with an offence under subsection (2), (3) or (4)` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are you charged with an offence under section 1250(2), (3) or (4)?
      `I show that I took all reasonable precautions` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Can you show that you took all reasonable precautions to avoid the offence?
      `I show that I exercised all due diligence` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Can you show that you exercised all due diligence to avoid the offence?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 1250(8), do I have a defence to a charge of holding myself out` IS
    `s 1250(8) the section gives the person a defence` `I am charged with an offence under subsection (2), (3) or (4)` `I show that I took all reasonable precautions` `I show that I exercised all due diligence`

§ `Companies Act 2006, Part 42 -- fees, and papers going to a foreign authority`

§§ `Fees (s 1251). Only arises if you are applying for a recognition order.`

@export Under section 1251(1), is my application for a recognition order duly made if I have not paid the fee?
GIVEN `I have paid the fee the Secretary of State prescribed for the application` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Have you paid the fee the Secretary of State prescribed for your application?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 1251(1), is my application for a recognition order duly made` IS
    `s 1251(1) the application is duly made` `I have paid the fee the Secretary of State prescribed for the application`

@export Under section 1251(1), what fee must I pay with my application for a recognition order, in pounds?
GIVEN `I am applying for a recognition order under Part 42` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are you applying for a recognition order under Part 42?
      `the fee the Secretary of State prescribed by regulations, in pounds` IS A NUMBER @desc How many pounds is the fee the Secretary of State prescribed by regulations for the application?
GIVETH A MAYBE NUMBER
DECIDE `Under section 1251(1), what fee must I pay with my application for a recognition order` IS
    `s 1251(1) the fee the applicant must pay in pounds` `I am applying for a recognition order under Part 42` `the fee the Secretary of State prescribed by regulations, in pounds`

§§ `Handing audit working papers to a foreign authority (ss 1253D to 1253DC). Only arises if your auditor is asked to give audit working papers or investigation reports to a regulator outside the United Kingdom.`

-- s 1253D(1), 1253DB, 1253DC. A statutory auditor's transfer of audit working papers.
@export Under section 1253D(1), may our statutory auditor transfer audit working papers and investigation reports to a third country competent authority?
GIVEN `the authority is an approved third country competent authority` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the foreign authority an approved third country competent authority?
      `the transfer is for the purposes of an investigation of an auditor or audit firm` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the transfer for the purposes of an investigation of an auditor or audit firm? (If not, it is a transfer needing the Secretary of State's approval.)
      `the Secretary of State has approved the transfer in advance` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has the Secretary of State given prior approval to the transfer?
      `the transfer is made in accordance with the rules of our recognised supervisory body that meet the requirements of paragraph 16AA (approved transfers) or 16AB (investigations) of Schedule 10` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the transfer made in accordance with the rules of the auditor's recognised supervisory body that meet the requirements of paragraph 16AA of Schedule 10 (for a transfer approved by the Secretary of State) or paragraph 16AB (for a transfer for an investigation)?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 1253D(1), may our statutory auditor transfer audit working papers and investigation reports to a third country competent authority` IS
    `s 1253D(1) the transfer to the third country competent authority is permitted`
        `the authority is an approved third country competent authority`
        `my route`
        `the route's own answer`
    WHERE
        `my route` MEANS
            IF `the transfer is for the purposes of an investigation of an auditor or audit firm`
            THEN `s 1253D(1)(c) transfer by a statutory auditor for the purposes of investigation of an auditor (section 1253DC)`
            ELSE `s 1253D(1)(b) transfer by a statutory auditor with the approval of the Secretary of State (section 1253DB)`
        -- The two route sections answer NOTHING when their conditions are not met (the name test of 2026-11-12). Section 1253D(1) says the transfer "must not be
        -- transferred unless ... made in accordance with" the route's section, so a route whose conditions are not met is a transfer not made in accordance with it: JUST FALSE here.
        `the route's own answer` MEANS
            IF `the route's section answers` EQUALS JUST TRUE
            THEN JUST TRUE
            ELSE JUST FALSE
        `the route's section answers` MEANS
            IF `the transfer is for the purposes of an investigation of an auditor or audit firm`
            THEN `s 1253DC the statutory auditor may transfer the audit working papers and investigation reports to the third country competent authority`
                    `the transfer is for the purposes of an investigation of an auditor or audit firm`
                    `the transfer is made in accordance with the rules of our recognised supervisory body that meet the requirements of paragraph 16AA (approved transfers) or 16AB (investigations) of Schedule 10`
            ELSE `s 1253DB(1) the statutory auditor may transfer the audit working papers and investigation reports to the approved third country competent authority`
                    `the Secretary of State has approved the transfer in advance`
                    `the transfer is made in accordance with the rules of our recognised supervisory body that meet the requirements of paragraph 16AA (approved transfers) or 16AB (investigations) of Schedule 10`

-- s 1253D(3). Data protection.
@export Under section 1253D(3), do the sections that allow transfers of audit working papers authorise a disclosure that would break the data protection legislation?
GIVEN `the disclosure would be made in contravention of the data protection legislation` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Would the disclosure contravene the data protection legislation?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 1253D(3), do the transfer sections authorise a disclosure that would break the data protection legislation` IS
    `s 1253D(3) the sections referred to in subsection (1) authorise the disclosure` `the disclosure would be made in contravention of the data protection legislation`

§ `Companies Act 2006, Part 42 -- when officers are guilty, time limits, where proceedings are taken, and notices`

§§ `Offences by bodies corporate (s 1255). Only arises if the company or association you are involved with has committed an offence under Part 42.`

-- s 1255(1). The officer's own guilt.
@export Under section 1255(1), am I guilty of the offence as well as my company?
GIVEN `my company committed an offence under Part 42` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did your company commit an offence under Part 42?
      `it is proved that the offence was committed with my consent or connivance` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it proved that the offence was committed with your consent or connivance?
      `it is proved that the offence is attributable to my neglect` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it proved that the offence is attributable to any neglect on your part?
      `I purport to act as an officer of the company` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Do you purport to act as an officer of the company?
      `I am a director of the company` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are you a director of the company (including a person occupying the position of a director by whatever name)?
      `I am a manager of the company` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are you a manager of the company?
      `I am the secretary of the company` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are you the secretary of the company?
      `the company's affairs are managed by its members and I am a member` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are the company's affairs managed by its members, and are you a member?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 1255(1), am I guilty of the offence as well as my company` IS
    `s 1255(1) the officer is guilty of the offence as well as the body corporate`
        `my company committed an offence under Part 42`
        `it is proved that the offence was committed with my consent or connivance`
        `it is proved that the offence is attributable to my neglect`
        `I purport to act as an officer of the company`
        (`s 1261(1) the person is an officer of the body corporate` `I am a director of the company` `I am a manager of the company` `I am the secretary of the company` `the company's affairs are managed by its members and I am a member`)

-- s 1255(2).
@export Under section 1255(2), am I, a partner, guilty of the offence as well as the partnership?
GIVEN `the partnership committed an offence under Part 42` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did the partnership commit an offence under Part 42?
      `it is proved that the offence was committed with my consent or connivance` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it proved that the offence was committed with your consent or connivance?
      `it is proved that the offence is attributable to my neglect` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it proved that the offence is attributable to any neglect on your part?
      `I am a partner` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are you a partner in the partnership?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 1255(2), am I, a partner, guilty of the offence as well as the partnership` IS
    `s 1255(2) the partner is guilty of the offence as well as the partnership` `the partnership committed an offence under Part 42` `it is proved that the offence was committed with my consent or connivance` `it is proved that the offence is attributable to my neglect` `I am a partner`

-- s 1255(3).
@export Under section 1255(3), am I, an officer or a member of the governing body, guilty of the offence as well as the unincorporated association?
GIVEN `the association (other than a partnership) committed an offence under Part 42` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did the unincorporated association (other than a partnership) commit an offence under Part 42?
      `it is proved that the offence was committed with my consent or connivance` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it proved that the offence was committed with your consent or connivance?
      `it is proved that the offence is attributable to my neglect` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it proved that the offence is attributable to any neglect on your part?
      `I am an officer of the association or a member of its governing body` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are you an officer of the association or a member of its governing body?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 1255(3), am I guilty of the offence as well as the unincorporated association` IS
    `s 1255(3) the officer or member is guilty of the offence as well as the association` `the association (other than a partnership) committed an offence under Part 42` `it is proved that the offence was committed with my consent or connivance` `it is proved that the offence is attributable to my neglect` `I am an officer of the association or a member of its governing body`

§§ `Time limits for prosecution (s 1256). Only arises if you are being, or may be, prosecuted for an offence under Part 42.`

-- s 1256(1), (5). England and Wales.
@export Under section 1256(1), can the information against me still be tried in a magistrates' court in England and Wales?
GIVEN `the day the offence was committed` IS A DATE @desc On what day was the offence committed (day, month, year)?
      `the day the information was laid` IS A DATE @desc On what day was the information laid (day, month, year)?
      `the day evidence sufficient in the opinion of the Director of Public Prosecutions or the Secretary of State came to his knowledge` IS A DATE @desc On what day did evidence sufficient, in the opinion of the Director of Public Prosecutions or the Secretary of State, to justify the proceedings come to his knowledge (day, month, year)?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 1256(1), can the information against me still be tried in England and Wales` IS
    IF `s 1256(5) this section authorises the trial or the commencement` `the day the offence was committed` `the day the information was laid` EQUALS JUST FALSE
    THEN JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): section 1256(5), "This section does not authorise ... more than three years after the commission of the offence"
    ELSE `s 1256(1) the information may be tried in England and Wales` `the day the information was laid` `the day evidence sufficient in the opinion of the Director of Public Prosecutions or the Secretary of State came to his knowledge`

@export Under section 1256(1), what is the last day on which the information against me may be laid in England and Wales (apart from the three-year limit in subsection (5))?
GIVEN `the day evidence sufficient in the opinion of the Director of Public Prosecutions or the Secretary of State came to his knowledge` IS A DATE @desc On what day did evidence sufficient, in the opinion of the Director of Public Prosecutions or the Secretary of State, to justify the proceedings come to his knowledge (day, month, year)?
GIVETH A DATE
DECIDE `Under section 1256(1), what is the last day on which the information may be laid in England and Wales` IS
    `s 1256(1) the last day of the period of twelve months beginning with` `the day evidence sufficient in the opinion of the Director of Public Prosecutions or the Secretary of State came to his knowledge`

-- s 1256(2), (3), (5). Scotland.
@export Under section 1256(2), can proceedings against me still be commenced in Scotland?
GIVEN `the day the offence was committed` IS A DATE @desc On what day was the offence committed (day, month, year)?
      `the day proceedings were commenced` IS A DATE @desc On what day were (or would) the proceedings be commenced (day, month, year)? If a warrant to apprehend or cite you is granted and executed without undue delay, give the day it was granted.
      `the day evidence sufficient in the Lord Advocate's opinion came to his knowledge` IS A DATE @desc On what day did evidence sufficient, in the Lord Advocate's opinion, to justify proceedings come to his knowledge (day, month, year)?
      `the Secretary of State reported that evidence to the Lord Advocate` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did the Secretary of State report that evidence to the Lord Advocate?
      `the day it came to the knowledge of the Secretary of State` IS A DATE @desc If the Secretary of State reported it: on what day did the evidence come to his knowledge (day, month, year)? Give any day if he did not.
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 1256(2), can proceedings against me still be commenced in Scotland` IS
    IF `s 1256(5) this section authorises the trial or the commencement` `the day the offence was committed` `the day proceedings were commenced` EQUALS JUST FALSE
    THEN JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): section 1256(5), "This section does not authorise ... the commencement of proceedings ... more than three years after the commission of the offence"
    ELSE `s 1256(2) proceedings may be commenced in Scotland` `the day proceedings were commenced` `the day evidence sufficient in the Lord Advocate's opinion came to his knowledge` `the Secretary of State reported that evidence to the Lord Advocate` `the day it came to the knowledge of the Secretary of State`

-- s 1256(4), (5). Northern Ireland.
@export Under section 1256(4), can the complaint against me still be tried in a magistrates' court in Northern Ireland?
GIVEN `the day the offence was committed` IS A DATE @desc On what day was the offence committed (day, month, year)?
      `the day the complaint was made` IS A DATE @desc On what day was the complaint made (day, month, year)?
      `the day evidence sufficient in the opinion of the Director of Public Prosecutions for Northern Ireland or the Secretary of State came to his knowledge` IS A DATE @desc On what day did evidence sufficient, in the opinion of the Director of Public Prosecutions for Northern Ireland or the Secretary of State, to justify the proceedings come to his knowledge (day, month, year)?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 1256(4), can the complaint against me still be tried in Northern Ireland` IS
    IF `s 1256(5) this section authorises the trial or the commencement` `the day the offence was committed` `the day the complaint was made` EQUALS JUST FALSE
    THEN JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): section 1256(5), "This section does not authorise ... the trial of a complaint made ... more than three years after the commission of the offence"
    ELSE `s 1256(4) the complaint may be tried in Northern Ireland` `the day the complaint was made` `the day evidence sufficient in the opinion of the Director of Public Prosecutions for Northern Ireland or the Secretary of State came to his knowledge`

§§ `Where proceedings are taken (s 1257). Only arises if you are, or your unincorporated association is, charged with an offence under Part 42.`

@export Under section 1257(1), can summary proceedings for an offence under Part 42 be taken against me at the place where I am for the time being?
GIVEN `I am for the time being at the place` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are you for the time being at the place where the proceedings would be taken?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 1257(1), can summary proceedings be taken against me at the place where I am` IS
    `s 1257(1) summary proceedings may be taken at the place` `s 1257(1)(b) an individual` FALSE `I am for the time being at the place`

-- s 1257(2). Are the proceedings brought as the section requires? (The function answers whether they were; it does not state the duty itself.)
@export Under section 1257(2), are the proceedings against my unincorporated association brought in the name of the association, and not in the name of its members, as the section requires?
GIVEN `the proceedings are brought in the name of the association and not in that of any of its members` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are the proceedings against your association brought in the name of the association, and not in the name of any of its members (which is how section 1257(2) requires them to be brought)?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 1257(2), are the proceedings against my unincorporated association brought in the name of the association as the section requires` IS
    `s 1257(2) the proceedings against the unincorporated association are brought as the section requires` `the proceedings are brought in the name of the association and not in that of any of its members`

@export Under section 1257(6), must a fine imposed on my unincorporated association be paid out of the association's funds?
GIVEN `the fine was imposed on an unincorporated association on its conviction of an offence under Part 42` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Was the fine imposed on an unincorporated association on its conviction of an offence under Part 42?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 1257(6), must a fine imposed on my unincorporated association be paid out of its funds` IS
    `s 1257(6) the fine must be paid out of the funds of the association` `the fine was imposed on an unincorporated association on its conviction of an offence under Part 42`

§§ `Notices (ss 1258 and 1259). Only arises if a notice, direction or other document under Part 42 is given to you or to a body you run.`

-- s 1258(4). The proper address.
@export Under section 1258(4), is this a proper address for serving a notice on my company?
GIVEN `it is my company's last known address` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it your company's last known address (of its residence, or of a place where it carries on business or is employed)?
      `it is the address of my company's registered or principal office in the United Kingdom` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it the address of your company's registered or principal office in the United Kingdom?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 1258(4), is this a proper address for serving a notice on my company` IS
    `s 1258(4) the address is a proper address of the person` `it is my company's last known address` FALSE `it is the address of my company's registered or principal office in the United Kingdom` FALSE

-- s 1258(3). Service on an officer.
@export Under section 1258(3), does a notice served on me, as an officer of the company, count as served on the company?
GIVEN `I am an officer of the company` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are you an officer of the company (a director, manager, secretary or, where the company is managed by its members, a member)?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 1258(3), does a notice served on me as an officer count as served on the company` IS
    `s 1258(3) service on the person is service on the recipient` `s 1258(3)(a) a body corporate` `I am an officer of the company`

-- s 1259. Documents in electronic form.
@export Under section 1259(2), does a notice sent to me electronically count as delivered to me?
GIVEN `section 1258 authorises the notice to be given to me by delivery` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does section 1258 authorise the notice to be given to you by delivering it to you?
      `it was sent by means of an electronic communications network` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Was the notice sent to you by means of an electronic communications network?
      `it was sent by other means in a form I need apparatus to read` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Was it sent by other means, but in a form that you need apparatus to make intelligible?
      `I told the sender I was willing to receive it in that form and manner` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did you indicate to the sender that you were willing to receive the notice in the form and manner used?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 1259(2), does a notice sent to me electronically count as delivered to me` IS
    `s 1259(2) the transmission has effect as a delivery of the document to the recipient`
        (`s 1259(1) this section applies` `section 1258 authorises the notice to be given to me by delivery` `it was sent by means of an electronic communications network` `it was sent by other means in a form I need apparatus to read` EQUALS JUST TRUE)
        `I told the sender I was willing to receive it in that form and manner`

§ `Companies Act 2006, Part 42 -- what the terms mean (ss 1260 and 1261)`

§§ `Associates and officers (ss 1260 and 1261)`

-- s 1260(2). Whether another person is my associate, for Part 42, when I am an individual.
@export Under section 1260(2), is this person an associate of mine, as an individual?
GIVEN `the person is my spouse, civil partner, minor child or step-child` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the person your spouse, civil partner or minor child or step-child?
      `the person is a body corporate of which I am a director` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the person a body corporate (that is not a limited liability partnership) of which you are a director?
      `the person is a limited liability partnership of which I am a member` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the person a limited liability partnership of which you are a member?
      `the person is my employee or my partner` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the person your employee or your partner?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 1260(2), is this person an associate of mine, as an individual` IS
    `s 1260(1) the candidate is an associate of the subject` `s 1260 an individual` `the person`
    WHERE
        `the person` MEANS `s 1260 candidate` WITH
            `s 1260 is the spouse, civil partner or minor child or step-child of the subject` IS `the person is my spouse, civil partner, minor child or step-child`
            `s 1260 is a body corporate` IS `the person is a body corporate of which I am a director` OR `the person is a limited liability partnership of which I am a member`
            `s 1260 is a limited liability partnership` IS `the person is a limited liability partnership of which I am a member`
            `s 1260 the subject is a director of the candidate` IS `the person is a body corporate of which I am a director`
            `s 1260 the subject is a member of the candidate` IS `the person is a limited liability partnership of which I am a member`
            `s 1260 is an employee or partner of the subject` IS `the person is my employee or my partner`
            -- Placeholders: the rule for an individual does not read the next four fields.
            `s 1260 is a body corporate in the same group as the subject` IS FALSE
            `s 1260 is an employee or partner of a body corporate in the same group as the subject` IS FALSE
            `s 1260 is an employee of or partner in the partnership` IS FALSE
            `s 1260 is an associate of a partner in the partnership` IS FALSE

-- s 1261(1). Whether I am an officer of the body corporate, for Part 42.
@export Under section 1261(1), am I an officer of the body corporate for the purposes of Part 42?
GIVEN `I am a director of the body corporate` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are you a director of the body corporate?
      `I am a manager of the body corporate` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are you a manager of the body corporate?
      `I am a secretary of the body corporate` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are you a secretary of the body corporate?
      `the affairs of the body are managed by its members and I am a member` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are the affairs of the body managed by its members, and are you a member?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 1261(1), am I an officer of the body corporate for the purposes of Part 42` IS
    `s 1261(1) the person is an officer of the body corporate` `I am a director of the body corporate` `I am a manager of the body corporate` `I am a secretary of the body corporate` `the affairs of the body are managed by its members and I am a member`

-- s 1261(1). Whether I am a director of the body corporate, for Part 42 (the definition is extended to shadow directors).
@export Under section 1261(1), am I a director of the body corporate for the purposes of Part 42?
GIVEN `I am a director in the ordinary sense` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are you a director of the body corporate in the ordinary sense?
      `I occupy the position of a director, by whatever name called` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Do you occupy in relation to the body corporate the position of a director, by whatever name you are called?
      `the directors are accustomed to act in accordance with my directions or instructions` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are the directors of the body accustomed to act in accordance with your directions or instructions?
      `those directions or instructions are advice I give in a professional capacity` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is what you tell the directors advice you give in a professional capacity?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 1261(1), am I a director of the body corporate for the purposes of Part 42` IS
    `s 1261(1) the person is a director of the body corporate` `I am a director in the ordinary sense` `I occupy the position of a director, by whatever name called` `the directors are accustomed to act in accordance with my directions or instructions` `those directions or instructions are advice I give in a professional capacity`

§ `Companies Act 2006, Part 43 -- transparency obligations (sections of the Financial Services and Markets Act 2000 inserted by ss 1266 to 1271)`

§§ `Holding voting rights in an issuer (s 1266, FSMA ss 89B and 89F)`

-- s 1266, FSMA 89B(6). A notifiable change in the proportion of voting rights I hold.
@export Under section 1266 (inserting section 89B(6) of the Financial Services and Markets Act 2000), is the change in the proportion of voting rights I hold a notifiable change?
GIVEN `the proportion of voting rights I held before the change` IS A NUMBER @desc What proportion of the voting rights did you hold before the change (a fraction: 0.04 means 4%)?
      `the proportion of voting rights I hold after the change` IS A NUMBER @desc What proportion of the voting rights do you hold after the change (a fraction)?
      `the proportion designated by the transparency rules` IS A NUMBER @desc What is the designated proportion in the transparency rules (a fraction)?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 1266 (FSMA 89B(6)), is the change in the proportion of voting rights I hold a notifiable change` IS
    `s 1266 FSMA 89B(6) there is a notifiable change in the proportion of voting rights held by a person` `the proportion of voting rights I held before the change` `the proportion of voting rights I hold after the change` `the proportion designated by the transparency rules`

-- s 1266, FSMA 89F(1)(b). Am I regarded as holding the voting rights.
@export Under section 1266 (inserting section 89F(1)(b) of the Financial Services and Markets Act 2000), am I regarded as holding the voting rights in respect of the shares?
GIVEN `by virtue of those shares I am a shareholder within the meaning of Article 2.1(e) of the transparency obligations directive` IS A BOOLEAN @desc By virtue of the shares, are you a shareholder within the meaning of Article 2.1(e) of the transparency obligations directive?
      `I am entitled to acquire, dispose of or exercise the voting rights in a case mentioned in Article 10(a) to (h) of that directive` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are you entitled to acquire, dispose of or exercise the voting rights in one or more of the cases mentioned in Article 10(a) to (h) of that directive?
      `I hold, directly or indirectly, a financial instrument which results in an entitlement to acquire the shares` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Do you hold, directly or indirectly, a financial instrument which results in an entitlement to acquire the shares?
      `that instrument is of a type the European Commission determined under Article 13.2 of that directive` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is that financial instrument of a type determined by the European Commission under Article 13.2 of the directive (an Article 13 instrument)?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 1266 (FSMA 89F(1)(b)), am I regarded as holding the voting rights in respect of the shares` IS
    `s 1266 FSMA 89F(1)(b) the person is regarded as holding the voting rights in respect of the shares`
        (JUST `by virtue of those shares I am a shareholder within the meaning of Article 2.1(e) of the transparency obligations directive`)
        (JUST `I am entitled to acquire, dispose of or exercise the voting rights in a case mentioned in Article 10(a) to (h) of that directive`)
        `I hold, directly or indirectly, a financial instrument which results in an entitlement to acquire the shares`
        (`s 1266 FSMA 89F(4) the instrument is an Article 13 instrument` `that instrument is of a type the European Commission determined under Article 13.2 of that directive`)

§§ `Being asked for information by the competent authority (s 1267, FSMA ss 89H to 89J). Only arises if the competent authority has served a notice on you or your company.`

-- s 1267, FSMA 89H(1)-(3).
@export Under section 1267 (inserting section 89H of the Financial Services and Markets Act 2000), must I provide the information or documents the competent authority has asked for?
GIVEN `I am` IS A `s 1267 FSMA 89H(2) kind of person` @desc Which of these are you: an issuer on whom transparency rules have effect, a voteholder, an auditor of an issuer or voteholder, a person who controls a voteholder, a person controlled by a voteholder, a director or similar officer of an issuer, a director or similar officer (or a member where it is managed by its members) of a voteholder, or another kind of person?
      `the competent authority has given me a notice in writing` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has the competent authority given you a notice in writing requiring the information or documents?
      `they are reasonably required in connection with the competent authority's functions under sections 89A to 89G` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are the information and documents reasonably required in connection with the competent authority's functions under sections 89A to 89G (the transparency rules)?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 1267 (FSMA 89H), must I provide the information or documents the competent authority has asked for` IS
    `s 1267 FSMA 89H(1) the person must provide the information or produce the documents`
        `the competent authority has given me a notice in writing`
        (`s 1267 FSMA 89H(2) this section applies to the person` `I am`)
        `they are reasonably required in connection with the competent authority's functions under sections 89A to 89G`

-- s 1267, FSMA 89H(4).
@export Under section 1267 (inserting section 89H(4) of the Financial Services and Markets Act 2000), did I provide the information or documents in time and at the place the notice specified?
GIVEN `the last day of the period the notice specified` IS A DATE @desc What is the last day of the period the competent authority's notice specified (day, month, year)?
      `the day I provided or produced them` IS A DATE @desc On what day did you provide the information or produce the documents (day, month, year)?
      `I did so at the place the notice specified` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did you do so at the place the notice specified?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 1267 (FSMA 89H(4)), did I provide the information or documents in time and at the place specified` IS
    `s 1267 FSMA 89H(4) the information was provided or the documents were produced as the section requires` `the last day of the period the notice specified` `the day I provided or produced them` `I did so at the place the notice specified`

-- s 1267, FSMA 89H(5).
@export Under section 1267 (inserting section 89H(5) of the Financial Services and Markets Act 2000), does producing a document to the competent authority affect my lien on it?
GIVEN `I claim a lien on the document` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Do you claim a lien on the document?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 1267 (FSMA 89H(5)), does producing a document affect my lien on it` IS
    `s 1267 FSMA 89H(5) the production of the document under this section affects the lien` `I claim a lien on the document`

-- s 1267, FSMA 89J(4). Control.
@export Under section 1267 (inserting section 89J(4) of the Financial Services and Markets Act 2000), do I control the other person?
GIVEN `I hold a majority of the voting rights in the other person` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Do you hold a majority of the voting rights in the other person?
      `I am a member of the other person and hold, or am treated as holding, the right to appoint or remove a majority of its board` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are you a member of the other person, and do you hold (counting rights held by persons you control, or who act for you or for them) the right to appoint or remove a majority of its board of directors or equivalent management body?
      `I am a member and control alone, under an agreement with other shareholders or members, a majority of the voting rights` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are you a member of the other person and do you control alone, under an agreement with other shareholders or members, a majority of its voting rights?
      `I have the right to exercise, or actually exercise, dominant influence or control over the other person` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Do you have the right to exercise, or do you actually exercise, dominant influence or control over the other person?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 1267 (FSMA 89J(4)), do I control the other person` IS
    `s 1267 FSMA 89J(4) A controls B` `I hold a majority of the voting rights in the other person` `I am a member of the other person and hold, or am treated as holding, the right to appoint or remove a majority of its board` `I am a member and control alone, under an agreement with other shareholders or members, a majority of the voting rights` `I have the right to exercise, or actually exercise, dominant influence or control over the other person`

§§ `When the competent authority acts against an issuer (s 1268, FSMA ss 89K to 89N). Only arises if the competent authority has found, or suspects, that your company has infringed a transparency obligation.`

@export Under section 1268 (inserting section 89K of the Financial Services and Markets Act 2000), can the competent authority publish a statement that my company has failed to comply with a transparency obligation?
GIVEN `my company's securities are admitted to trading on a regulated market` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are your company's securities admitted to trading on a regulated market?
      `the competent authority finds that my company is failing or has failed to comply with an applicable transparency obligation` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has the competent authority found that your company is failing, or has failed, to comply with an applicable transparency obligation?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 1268 (FSMA 89K(1)), can the competent authority publish a statement that my company has failed to comply` IS
    `s 1268 FSMA 89K(1) the competent authority may publish a statement that the issuer has failed to comply` `my company's securities are admitted to trading on a regulated market` `the competent authority finds that my company is failing or has failed to comply with an applicable transparency obligation`

@export Under section 1268 (inserting section 89K(2) of the Financial Services and Markets Act 2000), must the competent authority give my company a warning notice before it publishes a statement?
GIVEN `the competent authority proposes to publish a statement` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does the competent authority propose to publish a statement that your company has failed to comply?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 1268 (FSMA 89K(2)), must the competent authority give my company a warning notice` IS
    `s 1268 FSMA 89K(2) the competent authority must give the issuer a warning notice` `the competent authority proposes to publish a statement`

@export Under section 1268 (inserting section 89L(2) of the Financial Services and Markets Act 2000), can the competent authority suspend or prohibit trading in my company's securities, or ask the market operator to?
GIVEN `my company's securities are admitted to trading on a regulated market` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are your company's securities admitted to trading on a regulated market?
      `the competent authority has reasonable grounds for suspecting that an applicable transparency obligation has been infringed by my company` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does the competent authority have reasonable grounds for suspecting that your company has infringed an applicable transparency obligation?
      `the measure is` IS A `s 1268 FSMA 89L(2) measure` @desc Which measure: suspend trading for a period, prohibit trading, ask the market operator to suspend trading for a period, or ask the market operator to prohibit trading?
      `the number of days of the suspension` IS A NUMBER @desc For a suspension: for how many days (use 0 for a prohibition)?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 1268 (FSMA 89L(2)), can the competent authority suspend or prohibit trading in my company's securities` IS
    `s 1268 FSMA 89L(2) the competent authority may take the measure` `my company's securities are admitted to trading on a regulated market` `the competent authority has reasonable grounds for suspecting that an applicable transparency obligation has been infringed by my company` `the measure is` `the number of days of the suspension`

@export Under section 1268 (inserting section 89M(2) of the Financial Services and Markets Act 2000), must the competent authority give me written notice that it proposes to, or has, suspended or prohibited trading?
GIVEN `the competent authority proposes to use its powers under section 89L in relation to me` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does the competent authority propose to use its powers to suspend or prohibit trading in relation to you?
      `the competent authority has used those powers in relation to me with immediate effect` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has the competent authority used those powers in relation to you with immediate effect?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 1268 (FSMA 89M(2)), must the competent authority give me written notice` IS
    `s 1268 FSMA 89M(2) the competent authority must give the person written notice` `the competent authority proposes to use its powers under section 89L in relation to me` `the competent authority has used those powers in relation to me with immediate effect`

@export Under section 1268 (inserting section 89N of the Financial Services and Markets Act 2000), may I refer the competent authority's decision to the Tribunal?
GIVEN `I was given a decision notice under section 89K (public censure)` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Were you given a decision notice about public censure under section 89K?
      `I was given a notice under section 89M about suspension or prohibition of trading` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Were you given a notice under section 89M about suspension or prohibition of trading?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 1268 (FSMA 89N), may I refer the matter to the Tribunal` IS
    `s 1268 FSMA 89N the person may refer the matter to the Tribunal` `I was given a decision notice under section 89K (public censure)` `I was given a notice under section 89M about suspension or prohibition of trading`

§§ `Compensation for a misleading published report (s 1270, FSMA s 90A). Only arises if you bought securities and lost money after a report or statement the issuer published was untrue, misleading or left something out.`

-- s 1270, FSMA 90A(1) to (5), (9)(b). The investor's claim against the issuer. The three base questions (the publication, the securities, the acquisition) are narrowed to "is JUST TRUE" before they reach 90A(3); this turns a NOTHING into FALSE on purpose and cannot change the outcome, because 90A(3) answers NOTHING whenever any base question fails, and the limits in (4) and (5) are read separately.
@export Under section 1270 (inserting section 90A of the Financial Services and Markets Act 2000), is the issuer liable to pay me compensation for my loss from a misleading or incomplete published report?
GIVEN `the report was published in response to a requirement implementing Article 4, 5 or 6 of the transparency obligations directive` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Was the report or statement published in response to a requirement imposed by a provision implementing Article 4, 5 or 6 of the transparency obligations directive?
      `it is a preliminary statement made in advance of a report that Article 4 requires` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it instead a preliminary statement made in advance of a report or statement that a provision implementing Article 4 requires?
      `the preliminary statement contains information intended to appear in the report` IS A BOOLEAN @desc If it is a preliminary statement: does it contain information that is intended to appear in the report or statement?
      `that information appears in substantially the same form` IS A BOOLEAN @desc If so: will that information be presented in the report or statement in substantially the same form?
      `the securities are traded on a regulated market in the United Kingdom` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are the securities traded on a regulated market situated or operating in the United Kingdom?
      `the securities are traded on a regulated market outside the United Kingdom` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are the securities traded on a regulated market situated or operating outside the United Kingdom?
      `the United Kingdom is the issuer's home Member State` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the United Kingdom the issuer's home Member State within the meaning of Article 2.1(i) of the transparency obligations directive?
      `I acquired the securities` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did you acquire the securities?
      `I contracted to acquire the securities` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did you contract to acquire the securities?
      `I contracted to acquire an interest in the securities` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did you contract to acquire an interest in the securities?
      `I suffered loss because of an untrue or misleading statement` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did you suffer loss in respect of the securities as a result of an untrue or misleading statement in the publication?
      `I suffered loss because a required matter was left out` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did you suffer loss in respect of the securities as a result of a matter required to be included in the publication being left out?
      `a person discharging managerial responsibilities knew the statement was untrue or misleading or was reckless about it` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did a person discharging managerial responsibilities within the issuer in relation to the publication know the statement was untrue or misleading, or was he reckless as to whether it was?
      `a person discharging managerial responsibilities knew the omission was dishonest concealment of a material fact` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did such a person know that the omission was dishonest concealment of a material fact?
      `I acquired the securities in reliance on the information in the publication` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did you acquire the securities in reliance on the information in the publication?
      `it was reasonable for me to rely on it when I acquired them` IS A BOOLEAN @desc At the time you acquired the securities, and in the circumstances, was it reasonable for you to rely on that information?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 1270 (FSMA 90A), is the issuer liable to pay me compensation for my loss` IS
    `s 1270 FSMA 90A(3)-(5) the issuer is liable to pay compensation`
        `base liability`
        (`s 1270 FSMA 90A(4) the limit on the issuer's liability is satisfied` `a person discharging managerial responsibilities knew the statement was untrue or misleading or was reckless about it` `a person discharging managerial responsibilities knew the omission was dishonest concealment of a material fact`)
        (`s 1270 FSMA 90A(5) the loss is regarded as suffered as a result of the statement or omission` `I acquired the securities in reliance on the information in the publication` `it was reasonable for me to rely on it when I acquired them`)
    WHERE
        `the publication is covered` MEANS
            `s 1270 FSMA 90A(1) the publication is one to which this section applies` `the report was published in response to a requirement implementing Article 4, 5 or 6 of the transparency obligations directive` `it is a preliminary statement made in advance of a report that Article 4 requires` `the preliminary statement contains information intended to appear in the report` `that information appears in substantially the same form` EQUALS JUST TRUE
        `the securities are covered` MEANS
            `s 1270 FSMA 90A(2) the securities are ones to which this section applies` `the securities are traded on a regulated market in the United Kingdom` `the securities are traded on a regulated market outside the United Kingdom` `the United Kingdom is the issuer's home Member State` EQUALS JUST TRUE
        `I acquired them` MEANS
            `s 1270 FSMA 90A(9)(b) the person has acquired securities` `I acquired the securities` `I contracted to acquire the securities` `I contracted to acquire an interest in the securities` EQUALS JUST TRUE
        `base liability` MEANS
            `s 1270 FSMA 90A(3) the issuer is liable to pay compensation to the person`
                `the securities are covered`
                `I acquired them`
                (`the publication is covered` AND `I suffered loss because of an untrue or misleading statement`)
                (`the publication is covered` AND `I suffered loss because a required matter was left out`)

-- s 1270, FSMA 90A(6)(b). Can I, as an investor, sue the directors?
@export Under section 1270 (inserting section 90A(6) of the Financial Services and Markets Act 2000), is a director of the issuer subject to any liability to an investor for the investor's loss from a misleading published report?
GIVEN `the loss was suffered as a result of reliance on an untrue or misleading statement in, or the omission of a required matter from, a publication to which the section applies` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Was the loss suffered as a result of reliance on an untrue or misleading statement in, or the omission of a required matter from, a publication to which section 90A applies?
      `the liability asked about is one of those mentioned in subsection (8) (restitution powers under sections 382 and 384, a civil penalty, or a criminal offence)` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the liability you are asking about one of those subsection (8) mentions: the powers of the court and the Authority to order restitution under sections 382 and 384, liability for a civil penalty, or liability for a criminal offence?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 1270 (FSMA 90A(6)), is a director of the issuer subject to any liability to an investor for the investor's loss` IS
    `s 1270 FSMA 90A(6)(b) a person other than the issuer is subject to a liability` `the loss was suffered as a result of reliance on an untrue or misleading statement in, or the omission of a required matter from, a publication to which the section applies` FALSE `the liability asked about is one of those mentioned in subsection (8) (restitution powers under sections 382 and 384, a civil penalty, or a criminal offence)`

§§ `Where the issuer's home State is another member State (s 1271, FSMA s 100A)`

@export Under section 1271 (inserting section 100A of the Financial Services and Markets Act 2000), can the UK competent authority act against my company, whose home State is another member State, for an infringement?
GIVEN `the competent authority is using a power under Part 6 of the Financial Services and Markets Act 2000 for an infringement of transparency rules or prospectus rules` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the competent authority using a power under Part 6 of the Financial Services and Markets Act 2000 for an infringement of a provision of prospectus rules or transparency rules (or another provision made in accordance with the prospectus directive or the transparency obligations directive)?
      `my company's home State is a member State other than the United Kingdom` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is your company's home State a member State other than the United Kingdom?
      `the infringement is of a provision required by the relevant directive` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the infringement of a provision required by the relevant directive?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 1271 (FSMA 100A(2)), can the competent authority act against my company for the infringement` IS
    `s 1271 FSMA 100A(2) the competent authority may act`
        (`s 1271 FSMA 100A(1) this section applies` `the competent authority is using a power under Part 6 of the Financial Services and Markets Act 2000 for an infringement of transparency rules or prospectus rules` `my company's home State is a member State other than the United Kingdom` EQUALS JUST TRUE)
        `the infringement is of a provision required by the relevant directive`

-- ====================================================================================================
-- seat questions from part coa28 (merged by the lead on 2026-11-12; unchanged text follows)
-- ====================================================================================================
-- Companies Act 2006 (United Kingdom), Parts 44 to 47 and Schedules 1, 1A, 1B and 1C -- THE SEAT LAYER.
--
-- SEAT: an individual who is, or is about to become, a director, a company secretary or a member (shareholder) of a
-- company registered under the Act, or who deals with one, asking on facts they can state what the Act requires or
-- lets them do, what rights they have against the company or its directors, what they must disclose, file, approve
-- or vote on and by when, and what follows (liability, offences, penalties) if it is not done.
-- (Assumed, not ruled: the Act is addressed to companies, so the individual is whoever stands in a company's
-- management or ownership.)
--
-- This layer asks, in the person's words, the questions that lines 18349-19081 of the Act answer for that person:
-- whether they have an interest in shares (Schedule 1), whether they control a company (Schedule 1A), what a company
-- may do to an interest it has not had disclosed to it (Schedule 1B), what an offeror, a board and a holder may
-- expect in a takeover bid (Schedule 1C), where winding-up expenses rank (s 1282), what happens when an institution
-- votes their shares (ss 1277-1280), whether the Acts extend to their Northern Ireland company (s 1284), and
-- whether regulations they rely on have lapsed (s 1291). Nothing here is new law: every question calls the rule of
-- the layer-1 module that owns it.
--
-- PLAIN INPUTS. Every question takes plain inputs (yes or no, a number, a date, or a choice from a list), each with an
-- @desc worded as the person would be asked. The records and lists the layer-1 rules expect are built inside each
-- question, in its WHERE, from those answers. Where a layer-1 rule takes an answer of another section (the officer-in-
-- default test of s 1121 is one), the question asks yes, no or "I do not know" and builds the answer from it.
--
-- READING AN ANSWER. Every question answers JUST TRUE (the Act says yes), JUST FALSE (the Act says no in its own words)
-- or NOTHING (the Act does not answer on these facts: not covered). NOTHING is never a no. A number question answers
-- a number; a penalty question answers the Penalty record of coa-core.l4, or NOTHING where the section gives none.
--
-- NAMES. Every question begins "Under section N," or "Under schedule N paragraph M," with the Act's own numbering,
-- so that no two parts' questions can share a name, and each question says the scope its answer claims.

-- A seat answer for a fact the person may not know. Built into a MAYBE BOOLEAN inside the question that asks it.
DECLARE `coa28 seat answer` IS ONE OF
    `coa28 seat yes`
    `coa28 seat no`
    `coa28 seat I do not know`

GIVEN answer IS A `coa28 seat answer`
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`coa28 seat the answer as a MAYBE BOOLEAN` MEANS
    CONSIDER answer
    WHEN `coa28 seat yes` THEN JUST TRUE
    WHEN `coa28 seat no` THEN JUST FALSE
    WHEN `coa28 seat I do not know` THEN NOTHING

§ `Companies Act 2006, Parts 44 to 47 and Schedules 1 to 1C -- the individual's questions`

-- =========================================================================================================
§§ `Part 44: miscellaneous provisions`
-- =========================================================================================================

-- GROUP: only if you deal with actuaries' regulation or a pension scheme's levy. The form can ask first "Does this
-- concern the regulation of actuaries, or the levy on pension schemes?" before showing these two questions.

@export Under section 1274(3), am I a member of a professional actuarial body?
GIVEN `I am a member of the Institute of Actuaries or the Faculty of Actuaries in Scotland` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are you a member of the body (the Institute of Actuaries or the Faculty of Actuaries in Scotland)?
      `I am subject to its rules when I perform actuarial functions` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Although not a member, are you subject to its rules when you perform actuarial functions?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 1274(3), am I a member of a professional actuarial body` IS
    `s 1274(3) the person is a member of a professional actuarial body` `I am a member of the Institute of Actuaries or the Faculty of Actuaries in Scotland` `I am subject to its rules when I perform actuarial functions`

-- Audit 2026-11-12: this question asks only whether the person is in the class of subsection (3A). Being in the class does not oblige anyone to pay: a levy needs regulations under section 17 of the 2004 Act, which are outside the sources.
@export Under section 1275(3), am I within subsection (3A) of section 17 of the 2004 Act (an administrator of a public service pension scheme, or a trustee or manager of an occupational or personal pension scheme)?
GIVEN `I am an administrator of a public service pension scheme` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are you an administrator of a public service pension scheme (within the meaning of section 1 of the Pension Schemes Act 1993)?
      `I am a trustee or manager of an occupational or personal pension scheme` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are you a trustee or manager of an occupational or personal pension scheme (within the meaning of that section)?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 1275(3), am I within subsection (3A) of section 17 of the 2004 Act` IS
    `s 1275(3) the person is within subsection (3A) of section 17 of the 2004 Act` `I am an administrator of a public service pension scheme` `I am a trustee or manager of an occupational or personal pension scheme`

-- GROUP: only if an institution (a pension scheme, unit trust, investment trust, insurer) holds shares for you or on
-- your behalf and voting-information regulations have been made. The form can ask first "Does an institution vote
-- shares on your behalf?" before showing these three questions.

@export Under section 1278(1), is the institution one to which the voting-information power of section 1277 applies?
GIVEN `it is a unit trust scheme with an order in force under section 243 of the Financial Services and Markets Act 2000` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it a unit trust scheme (within the meaning of the Financial Services and Markets Act 2000) in respect of which an order is in force under section 243 of that Act?
      `it is an open-ended investment company` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it an open-ended investment company incorporated by virtue of regulations under section 262 of that Act?
      `it is an approved investment trust` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it a company approved for the purposes of Chapter 4 of Part 24 of the Corporation Tax Act 2010 (investment trusts)?
      `it is a pension scheme` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it a pension scheme as defined in section 1(5) of the Pension Schemes Act 1993 or the Pension Schemes (Northern Ireland) Act 1993?
      `it is a long-term insurer` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it an undertaking authorised under the Financial Services and Markets Act 2000 to carry on long-term insurance business?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 1278(1), is the institution one to which section 1277 applies` IS
    `s 1278(1) the institution is one to which section 1277 applies` `it is a unit trust scheme with an order in force under section 243 of the Financial Services and Markets Act 2000` `it is an open-ended investment company` `it is an approved investment trust` `it is a pension scheme` `it is a long-term insurer`

@export Under section 1279(1), are these shares ones to which the voting-information power of section 1277 applies?
GIVEN `the shares are of a description traded on a market the regulations specify` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are the shares of a description traded on a market that the regulations specify?
      `the institution holds the shares, or a depositary certificate for them, or they are held on its behalf` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does the institution hold the shares, or a depositary certificate in respect of them, itself, or are they held on its behalf?
      `the institution has an interest in a specified collective investment scheme or vehicle` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does the institution have an interest in a collective investment scheme or vehicle of a description the regulations specify?
      `that scheme or vehicle holds the shares, or a depositary certificate for them, or they are held on its behalf` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does that scheme or vehicle hold the shares, or a depositary certificate in respect of them, or are they held on its behalf?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 1279(1), are the shares ones to which section 1277 applies` IS
    `s 1279(1) the shares are shares to which section 1277 applies` `the shares are of a description traded on a market the regulations specify` interest
    WHERE
        direct MEANS `s 1279(2) the institution has an interest in the shares` `the institution holds the shares, or a depositary certificate for them, or they are held on its behalf`
        viaScheme MEANS `s 1279(3) the institution is taken to have an interest in the shares` `the institution has an interest in a specified collective investment scheme or vehicle` (`s 1279(4) the scheme or vehicle is taken to have an interest in the shares` `that scheme or vehicle holds the shares, or a depositary certificate for them, or they are held on its behalf`)
        interest MEANS
            IF direct EQUALS JUST TRUE OR viaScheme EQUALS JUST TRUE
            THEN JUST TRUE
            ELSE NOTHING

@export Under section 1277(4), may I bring civil proceedings because an institution has not given me the information about its voting that the regulations require?
GIVEN `the obligation is imposed by regulations under section 1277` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Do regulations under section 1277 impose the obligation to give the information?
      `I am a person to whom the information should have been provided` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are you a person to whom the information should have been provided?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 1277(4), may I bring civil proceedings to enforce the obligation to provide information about voting` IS
    `s 1277(4) the person may bring civil proceedings to enforce the obligation` `the obligation is imposed by regulations under section 1277` `I am a person to whom the information should have been provided` FALSE

-- GROUP: only if a public authority holds information about you or your company that came to it under the Enterprise
-- Act 2002. The form can ask first "Has a public authority been given information about you under the Enterprise
-- Act 2002?" before showing these two questions.

@export Under section 1281 (section 241A(1) of the Enterprise Act 2002), may a public authority disclose information to me or for my case in civil proceedings?
GIVEN `the authority holds prescribed information to which section 237 applies` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the authority a public authority holding information that the Secretary of State has prescribed and to which section 237 of the Enterprise Act 2002 applies?
      purpose IS A `s 1281 241A(1) purpose` @desc What is the purpose of the disclosure? Choose one of the listed purposes, or "any other purpose".
      kind IS A `s 1281 241A(2) kind of information` @desc How did the information come to the authority? Choose the kind of information, or "any other information".
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 1281 (section 241A(1)), may a public authority disclose the information` IS
    `s 1281 241A(1) the public authority may disclose the information to any person` `the authority holds prescribed information to which section 237 applies` purpose (`s 1281 241A(2) subsection (1) does not apply to the information` kind)

@export Under section 1281 (section 241A(5) of the Enterprise Act 2002), am I barred from using information that was disclosed to me for this purpose?
GIVEN `the information was disclosed to me under section 241A` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Was the information disclosed to you under section 241A of the Enterprise Act 2002?
      `my purpose is one of those for which it may be disclosed under section 241A(1)` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is your purpose one of those in section 241A(1): prescribed civil proceedings (including prospective proceedings), obtaining legal advice about them, or establishing, enforcing or defending legal rights that are or may be the subject of such proceedings?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 1281 (section 241A(5)), am I barred from using the information for my purpose` IS
    `s 1281 241A(5) the person is barred from using the information for the purpose` `the information was disclosed to me under section 241A` TRUE `my purpose is one of those for which it may be disclosed under section 241A(1)`

-- GROUP: only if the company is being wound up. The form can ask first "Is a company you are owed money by, or hold
-- a charge over, in liquidation?" before showing these questions.

@export Under section 1282 (section 176ZA(1) of the Insolvency Act 1986), do the expenses of winding up rank ahead of my floating charge in an England and Wales winding up?
GIVEN `the winding up is in England and Wales` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the company being wound up in England and Wales?
      `the expenses of winding up` IS A NUMBER @desc What are the expenses of the winding up, in pounds (all expenses properly incurred in the winding up, including the liquidator's remuneration)?
      `the assets available to general creditors before any prescribed part is set aside` IS A NUMBER @desc What are the company's assets available for payment of general creditors, in pounds, before any amount is made available under section 176A(2)(a)?
      `the amount made available under section 176A(2)(a)` IS A NUMBER @desc What amount, in pounds, is made available under section 176A(2)(a) (the prescribed part for unsecured creditors)? Enter 0 if none.
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 1282 (section 176ZA(1)), do the expenses of winding up rank ahead of floating charge claims` IS
    `s 1282(1) 176ZA(1) the expenses of winding up have priority over claims to property comprised in or subject to a floating charge` `the winding up is in England and Wales` (`the expenses of winding up` GREATER THAN available)
    WHERE
        available MEANS `s 1282(1) 176ZA(2)(a) the assets of the company available for payment of general creditors` `the assets available to general creditors before any prescribed part is set aside` `the amount made available under section 176A(2)(a)`

@export Under section 1282 (section 176ZA(1) of the Insolvency Act 1986), how much of the expenses of an England and Wales winding up ranks ahead of floating charge claims, in pounds?
GIVEN `the expenses of winding up` IS A NUMBER @desc What are the expenses of the winding up, in pounds?
      `the assets available to general creditors before any prescribed part is set aside` IS A NUMBER @desc What are the company's assets available for payment of general creditors, in pounds, before any amount is made available under section 176A(2)(a)?
      `the amount made available under section 176A(2)(a)` IS A NUMBER @desc What amount, in pounds, is made available under section 176A(2)(a)? Enter 0 if none.
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `Under section 1282 (section 176ZA(1)), how much of the expenses of winding up ranks ahead of floating charge claims` IS
    `s 1282(1) 176ZA(1) the amount of the expenses that has priority over floating charge claims` `the expenses of winding up` available
    WHERE
        available MEANS `s 1282(1) 176ZA(2)(a) the assets of the company available for payment of general creditors` `the assets available to general creditors before any prescribed part is set aside` `the amount made available under section 176A(2)(a)`

@export Under section 1282 (Article 150ZA of the Insolvency (Northern Ireland) Order 1989), do the expenses of winding up rank ahead of my floating charge in a Northern Ireland winding up?
GIVEN `the expenses of winding up` IS A NUMBER @desc What are the expenses of the winding up, in pounds?
      `the assets available to general creditors before any prescribed part is set aside` IS A NUMBER @desc What are the company's assets available for payment of general creditors, in pounds, before any amount is made available under Article 150A(2)(a)?
      `the amount made available under Article 150A(2)(a)` IS A NUMBER @desc What amount, in pounds, is made available under Article 150A(2)(a)? Enter 0 if none.
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 1282 (Article 150ZA), do the expenses of winding up rank ahead of floating charge claims` IS
    `s 1282(2) 150ZA(1) the expenses of winding up have priority over claims to property comprised in or subject to a floating charge` (`the expenses of winding up` GREATER THAN available)
    WHERE
        available MEANS `s 1282(2) 150ZA(2)(a) the assets of the company available for payment of general creditors` `the assets available to general creditors before any prescribed part is set aside` `the amount made available under Article 150A(2)(a)`

@export Under section 1283, does paragraph 3(1) of Schedule 3 to the Commonhold and Leasehold Reform Act 2002 apply to my commonhold association's alteration of its memorandum or articles?
GIVEN `the association altered its memorandum or articles` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has your commonhold association altered its memorandum or articles of association?
      `the land specified in the memorandum was commonhold land at that time` IS A BOOLEAN @desc At the time of the alteration, was the land specified in its memorandum commonhold land?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 1283, does paragraph 3(1) of Schedule 3 to the Commonhold and Leasehold Reform Act 2002 apply to the alteration` IS
    `s 1283 paragraph 3(1) of Schedule 3 to the Commonhold and Leasehold Reform Act 2002 applies to the alteration` `the association altered its memorandum or articles` `the land specified in the memorandum was commonhold land at that time`

-- =========================================================================================================
§§ `Part 45: Northern Ireland`
-- =========================================================================================================

-- GROUP: only if your company, partnership or business name is registered in, or carries on business in, Northern
-- Ireland. The form can ask first "Is your company or business in Northern Ireland?" before showing these questions.

@export Under section 1284(1), do the Companies Acts provision I rely on extend to Northern Ireland?
GIVEN `the provision is one of the Companies Acts` IS A `coa28 seat answer` @desc Is the provision one of the Companies Acts (the company law provisions of the 2006 Act, Part 2 of the 2004 Act on community interest companies, and the remaining provisions of the 1985 Acts)? Answer yes, no, or I do not know.
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 1284(1), does the provision extend to Northern Ireland` IS
    `s 1284(1) the provision extends to Northern Ireland` (`coa28 seat the answer as a MAYBE BOOLEAN` `the provision is one of the Companies Acts`)

@export Under section 1284(2), does this Northern Ireland instrument cease to have effect (the Act says it shall)?
GIVEN instrument IS A `s 1284(2) instrument` @desc Which instrument? Choose one of the three named in section 1284(2), or "another instrument".
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 1284(2), does the instrument cease to have effect` IS
    `s 1284(2) the instrument ceases to have effect` instrument

@export Under section 1285(1), does this enactment on UK Societas extend to Northern Ireland?
GIVEN `the enactment is in force in Great Britain` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the enactment in force in Great Britain?
      `the enactment relates to UK Societas` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does it relate to UK Societas (a United Kingdom Societas within the meaning of Council Regulation 2157/2001/EC)?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 1285(1), does the enactment extend to Northern Ireland` IS
    `s 1285(1) the enactment extends to Northern Ireland` `the enactment is in force in Great Britain` `the enactment relates to UK Societas`

@export Under section 1285(2), does this Northern Ireland enactment on the European Company cease to have effect (the Act says it shall)?
GIVEN enactment IS A `s 1285(2) enactment` @desc Which enactment? Choose one of the two named in section 1285(2), or "another enactment".
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 1285(2), does the enactment cease to have effect` IS
    `s 1285(2) the enactment ceases to have effect` enactment

@export Under section 1286(1), does the Great Britain legislation on this form of business organisation extend to Northern Ireland?
GIVEN form IS A `s 1286(1) form of business organisation` @desc Which form of business organisation? Choose one of the five named in section 1286(1), or "another form of business organisation".
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 1286(1), does the Great Britain legislation on the form extend to Northern Ireland` IS
    `s 1286(1) the enactments in force in Great Britain relating to the form extend to Northern Ireland` form

@export Under section 1286(2), does this Northern Ireland enactment on a form of business organisation cease to have effect (the Act says it shall)?
GIVEN enactment IS A `s 1286(2) enactment` @desc Which enactment? Choose one of the four named in section 1286(2), or "another enactment".
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 1286(2), does the enactment cease to have effect` IS
    `s 1286(2) the enactment ceases to have effect` enactment

@export Under section 1287(1), do the business names provisions I rely on extend to Northern Ireland?
GIVEN `the provision is a provision of Part 41 of the Companies Act 2006` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the provision a provision of Part 41 of the Companies Act 2006 (business names)?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 1287(1), does the provision extend to Northern Ireland` IS
    `s 1287(1) the provision extends to Northern Ireland` `the provision is a provision of Part 41 of the Companies Act 2006`

@export Under section 1287(2), does the Business Names (Northern Ireland) Order 1986 cease to have effect (the Act says it shall)?
GIVEN instrument IS A `s 1287(2) instrument` @desc Which instrument? Choose the Business Names (Northern Ireland) Order 1986, or "another instrument".
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 1287(2), does the instrument cease to have effect` IS
    `s 1287(2) the instrument ceases to have effect` instrument

-- =========================================================================================================
§§ `Part 46: general supplementary provisions`
-- =========================================================================================================

-- GROUP: only if you rely on regulations or an order made under the Act. The form can ask first "Do you rely on
-- regulations or an order made under the Companies Act 2006?" before showing these questions.

@export Under section 1288, must the regulations or order I rely on have been made by statutory instrument?
GIVEN `the Act provides otherwise for these regulations or this order` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does the Act provide otherwise for these regulations or this order, for example by saying how else they are made?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 1288, must the regulations or order have been made by statutory instrument` IS
    `s 1288 the regulations or order under this Act must be made by statutory instrument` `the Act provides otherwise for these regulations or this order`

@export Under section 1291(1)(b), have the regulations or order I rely on, made under the "approval after being made" procedure, ceased to have effect?
GIVEN `the day they were made` IS A DATE @desc On what date were the regulations or order made?
      `the day I am asking about` IS A DATE @desc For which date do you want to know whether they are still in effect?
      `each House has approved them` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has each House of Parliament approved them by resolution?
      `the day on which the second House approved them` IS A DATE @desc If both Houses have approved them, on what date did the second of them do so? (Any date if not approved.)
      `there was a time when Parliament was dissolved or prorogued, or both Houses were adjourned for more than four days` IS A BOOLEAN @desc During the first 28 days, was there a time when Parliament was dissolved or prorogued, or both Houses were adjourned for more than four days?
      `that time began on` IS A DATE @desc On what date did that time begin? (Any date if there was none.)
      `that time ended on` IS A DATE @desc On what date did that time end? (Any date if there was none.)
      `that time was a dissolution or prorogation` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Was it a dissolution or prorogation (answer no if both Houses were adjourned instead)?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 1291(1)(b), have the regulations or order ceased to have effect` IS
    `s 1291(1)(b) the regulations or order have ceased to have effect` `the day they were made` intervals `the day I am asking about` approval
    WHERE
        approval MEANS IF `each House has approved them` THEN JUST `the day on which the second House approved them` ELSE NOTHING
        intervals MEANS
            IF `there was a time when Parliament was dissolved or prorogued, or both Houses were adjourned for more than four days`
            THEN LIST (`s 1291(2) interval` OF `that time began on`, `that time ended on`, intervalKind)
            ELSE EMPTY
        intervalKind MEANS
            IF `that time was a dissolution or prorogation`
            THEN `s 1291(2) Parliament dissolved or prorogued`
            ELSE `s 1291(2) both Houses adjourned`

@export Under section 1293, is the provision I am looking at an "enactment" for the purposes of the Act?
GIVEN kind IS A `s 1293 kind of provision` @desc What kind of provision is it? Choose one of the four kinds listed in section 1293, or "another kind of provision".
      `the context otherwise requires` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does the context in which the word is used otherwise require?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 1293, is the provision an enactment` IS
    `s 1293 the provision is an enactment` kind `the context otherwise requires`

-- GROUP: only if a provision of the 2006 Act re-enacts an enactment it repealed. The form can ask first "Does the
-- provision you rely on re-enact an earlier enactment?" before showing these three questions.

@export Under section 1297(3), does something done under a repealed provision have effect as if done under the corresponding provision of the 2006 Act?
GIVEN `a provision of the Act re-enacts an enactment repealed by the Act` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does a provision of the 2006 Act re-enact (with or without modification) an enactment that the Act repealed?
      `the thing was done under or for the purposes of the repealed provision` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Was the thing done (including subordinate legislation made), or does it have effect as if done, under or for the purposes of the repealed provision?
      `it could have been done under the corresponding provision` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Could it have been done under the corresponding provision of the 2006 Act, if that provision had been in force or effective immediately before it commenced?
      `a specific transitional provision or saving applies` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does a specific transitional provision or saving in the Act apply to the case?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 1297(3), does the thing have effect as if done under the corresponding provision` IS
    `s 1297(3) the thing has effect thereafter as if done under or for the purposes of the corresponding provision of this Act` (`s 1297(1) section 1297 applies` `a provision of the Act re-enacts an enactment repealed by the Act`) `the thing was done under or for the purposes of the repealed provision` `it could have been done under the corresponding provision` (`s 1297(6) section 1297 yields to a specific transitional provision or saving` `a specific transitional provision or saving applies`)

@export Under section 1297(4), is a reference to a provision of the 2006 Act read as including the corresponding repealed provision?
GIVEN `a provision of the Act re-enacts an enactment repealed by the Act` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does a provision of the 2006 Act re-enact (with or without modification) an enactment that the Act repealed?
      `the reference is to a provision of the 2006 Act` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the reference (express or implied), in the Act or any other enactment, instrument or document, to a provision of the 2006 Act?
      `the context permits` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does the context permit reading it that way?
      `it concerns a time, circumstance or purpose for which the repealed provision had effect` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does it concern a time, circumstance or purpose in relation to which the corresponding repealed provision had effect?
      `a specific transitional provision or saving applies` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does a specific transitional provision or saving in the Act apply to the case?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 1297(4), is the reference read as including the corresponding repealed provision` IS
    `s 1297(4) the reference to the provision of this Act is construed as including a reference to the corresponding repealed provision` (`s 1297(1) section 1297 applies` `a provision of the Act re-enacts an enactment repealed by the Act`) `the reference is to a provision of the 2006 Act` `the context permits` `it concerns a time, circumstance or purpose for which the repealed provision had effect` (`s 1297(6) section 1297 yields to a specific transitional provision or saving` `a specific transitional provision or saving applies`)

@export Under section 1297(5), is a reference to a repealed provision read as including the corresponding provision of the 2006 Act?
GIVEN `a provision of the Act re-enacts an enactment repealed by the Act` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does a provision of the 2006 Act re-enact (with or without modification) an enactment that the Act repealed?
      `the reference is to the repealed provision` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the reference (express or implied), in any enactment, instrument or document, to the repealed provision?
      `the context permits` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does the context permit reading it that way?
      `it concerns a time, circumstance or purpose for which the corresponding provision has effect` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does it concern a time, circumstance or purpose in relation to which the corresponding provision of the 2006 Act has effect?
      `a specific transitional provision or saving applies` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does a specific transitional provision or saving in the Act apply to the case?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 1297(5), is the reference read as including the corresponding provision of the 2006 Act` IS
    `s 1297(5) the reference to the repealed provision is construed as being or including a reference to the corresponding provision of this Act` (`s 1297(1) section 1297 applies` `a provision of the Act re-enacts an enactment repealed by the Act`) `the reference is to the repealed provision` `the context permits` `it concerns a time, circumstance or purpose for which the corresponding provision has effect` (`s 1297(6) section 1297 yields to a specific transitional provision or saving` `a specific transitional provision or saving applies`)

-- =========================================================================================================
§§ `Part 47: final provisions`
-- =========================================================================================================

@export Under section 1299, does this provision of the Act extend to the whole of the United Kingdom?
GIVEN `the Act otherwise provides for the provision` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does the Act otherwise provide for the provision's extent?
      `the context otherwise requires` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does the context otherwise require?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 1299, does the provision extend to the whole of the United Kingdom` IS
    `s 1299 the provision extends to the whole of the United Kingdom` `the Act otherwise provides for the provision` `the context otherwise requires`

-- =========================================================================================================
§§ `Schedule 1: interests in shares or debentures (the connected persons of sections 254 and 255)`
-- =========================================================================================================

-- GROUP: only if you are a director (or about to become one) asking whether you, or a body corporate you control, has
-- an interest in shares or debentures for sections 254 and 255. The form can ask first "Are you a director, and do
-- you hold or control shares or debentures of a body corporate?" before showing these questions. Each question is
-- about ONE interest in ONE holding; a "no" to a route is "not by this paragraph", not "no interest".

@export Under schedule 1 paragraph 3, am I taken to have an interest in shares because of a contract or a right to acquire them?
GIVEN `I entered into a contract to acquire the shares` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Have you entered into a contract to acquire the shares?
      `I have a right to call for delivery of the shares to myself or to my order` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Do you have a right to call for delivery of the shares to yourself or to your order?
      `I have a right to acquire an interest in shares, or I am under an obligation to take an interest in shares` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Do you have a right to acquire an interest in shares, or are you under an obligation to take an interest in shares (whether conditional or absolute)?
      `that right or obligation is only a right or obligation to subscribe for shares` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is that right or obligation only one to subscribe for shares?
      `the shares were delivered at my order in fulfilment of a contract for their acquisition by me` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Have the shares been delivered to another person at your order in fulfilment of a contract for their acquisition by you?
      `the shares were delivered at my order in satisfaction of my right to call for their delivery` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Have the shares been delivered to another person at your order in satisfaction of your right to call for their delivery?
      `the shares were not delivered as the contract or right required` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has there been a failure to deliver the shares in accordance with the terms of such a contract, or on which such a right falls to be satisfied?
      `my right to call for delivery has lapsed` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has your right to call for the delivery of the shares lapsed?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under schedule 1 paragraph 3, am I taken to have an interest in the shares by virtue of paragraph 3` IS
    `sch 1 para 3 the person has an interest in the shares by virtue of paragraph 3` (`sch 1 para 3(1) the person is taken to have an interest in the shares by entering into a contract to acquire them` `I entered into a contract to acquire the shares`) (`sch 1 para 3(2) the person is taken to have an interest in the shares by a right to call for delivery or a right or obligation to acquire an interest` `I have a right to call for delivery of the shares to myself or to my order` `I have a right to acquire an interest in shares, or I am under an obligation to take an interest in shares` `that right or obligation is only a right or obligation to subscribe for shares`) (`sch 1 para 3(4) the person ceases to have an interest in the shares by virtue of paragraph 3` `the shares were delivered at my order in fulfilment of a contract for their acquisition by me` `the shares were delivered at my order in satisfaction of my right to call for their delivery` `the shares were not delivered as the contract or right required` `my right to call for delivery has lapsed`)

@export Under schedule 1 paragraph 4, am I taken to have an interest in shares because I can exercise or control the exercise of the rights attached to them?
GIVEN `I am the registered holder of the shares` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are you the registered holder of the shares?
      `I am entitled to exercise a right conferred by the holding of the shares` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are you entitled to exercise any right conferred by the holding of the shares?
      `I am entitled to control the exercise of such a right` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are you entitled to control the exercise of any such right?
      `I have a right (even if conditional) that would make me so entitled` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Do you have a right (whether or not subject to conditions) the exercise of which would make you so entitled?
      `I am under an obligation that would make me so entitled` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are you under an obligation (whether or not so subject) the fulfilment of which would make you so entitled?
      `I have been appointed a proxy` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Have you been appointed a proxy to exercise any of the rights attached to the shares?
      `I have been appointed to represent a body corporate at a meeting` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Have you been appointed by a body corporate to act as its representative at any meeting of a company or of any class of its members?
      `that appointment is my only reason for being so entitled` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is that appointment the only reason you are entitled in this way?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under schedule 1 paragraph 4, am I taken to have an interest in the shares by virtue of paragraph 4` IS
    `sch 1 para 4 the person has an interest in the shares by virtue of paragraph 4` (`sch 1 para 4(1) the person is taken to have an interest in the shares by an entitlement to exercise or control the exercise of a right` `I am the registered holder of the shares` (`I am entitled to exercise a right conferred by the holding of the shares` OR `sch 1 para 4(2) the person is taken to be entitled to exercise or control the exercise of a right conferred by the holding of shares` `I have a right (even if conditional) that would make me so entitled` `I am under an obligation that would make me so entitled` EQUALS JUST TRUE) `I am entitled to control the exercise of such a right`) (`sch 1 para 4(3) the person is taken by virtue of paragraph 4 to be interested in the shares by reason only of the appointment` `I have been appointed a proxy` `I have been appointed to represent a body corporate at a meeting` `that appointment is my only reason for being so entitled`)

@export Under schedule 1 paragraph 5, am I taken to be interested in shares because a body corporate is interested in them?
GIVEN `a body corporate is interested in the shares` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is a body corporate interested in the shares?
      `the body corporate or its directors are accustomed to act on my directions or instructions` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are the body corporate or its directors accustomed to act in accordance with your directions or instructions?
      `the fraction of the voting power at the body corporate's general meetings that I can exercise or control directly` IS A NUMBER @desc What fraction (for example 0.3 for 30%) of the voting power at the body corporate's general meetings are you entitled to exercise or control yourself?
      `the fraction attributed to me through another body corporate I control more than half of` IS A NUMBER @desc What fraction of that voting power is exercisable by another body corporate in which you are entitled to exercise or control more than one-half of the voting power (the voting power then counts as yours)? Enter 0 if none.
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under schedule 1 paragraph 5, am I taken to be interested in the shares because a body corporate is interested in them` IS
    `sch 1 para 5(1) the person is taken to be interested in the shares because a body corporate is interested in them` `a body corporate is interested in the shares` `the body corporate or its directors are accustomed to act on my directions or instructions` (`sch 1 para 5(1)(b) the person is entitled to exercise or control the exercise of more than one-half of the voting power at general meetings of the body corporate` `the fraction of the voting power at the body corporate's general meetings that I can exercise or control directly` `the fraction attributed to me through another body corporate I control more than half of`)

@export Under schedule 1 paragraph 6, do I have an interest in shares as a beneficiary or trustee, once the exceptions are applied?
GIVEN `an interest in shares is comprised in property held on trust` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is an interest in the shares comprised in property held on trust?
      `I am a beneficiary of the trust` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are you a beneficiary of the trust?
      `my interest is in reversion, remainder or (in Scotland) fee` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is your interest an interest in the shares in reversion or remainder or (as regards Scotland) in fee?
      `a person is entitled to the income from the trust property comprising the shares` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is a person entitled to receive, during the lifetime of himself or another, income from the trust property comprising the shares?
      `I hold the shares as a bare trustee or custodian trustee` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Do you hold the shares under the law of any part of the United Kingdom as a bare trustee or custodian trustee?
      `I hold the shares as a simple trustee in Scotland` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Do you hold the shares under the law of Scotland as a simple trustee?
      `my interest subsists by virtue of one of these schemes` IS A `sch 1 para 6(4) basis of the interest` @desc Does your interest subsist by virtue of an authorised unit trust scheme, a scheme made under one of the charities or trustee investments enactments in paragraph 6(4)(b), or the Church Funds Investment Measure 1958 scheme? Choose one, or "another basis".
      `my interest is one of these Church of Scotland interests` IS A `sch 1 para 6(5) interest` @desc Is your interest one that paragraph 6(5) disregards (an interest of the Church of Scotland General Trustees or Trust in shares they hold, or of another person in shares they hold otherwise than as simple trustees)? Choose one, or "another interest".
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under schedule 1 paragraph 6, do I have an interest in the shares as a beneficiary or trustee` IS
    `sch 1 paras 2 to 6 the person has an interest in the shares or debentures for sections 254 and 255` (LIST `sch 1 para 6 the beneficiary has an interest in the shares by virtue of paragraph 6` (`sch 1 para 6(1) the beneficiary is taken to have an interest in the shares` `an interest in shares is comprised in property held on trust` `I am a beneficiary of the trust`) (`sch 1 para 6(2) the interest in reversion, remainder or fee is disregarded` `my interest is in reversion, remainder or (in Scotland) fee` `a person is entitled to the income from the trust property comprising the shares`)) (LIST (`sch 1 para 6(3) the person is treated as not interested in the shares` `I hold the shares as a bare trustee or custodian trustee` `I hold the shares as a simple trustee in Scotland`), (`sch 1 para 6(4) the interest is disregarded` `my interest subsists by virtue of one of these schemes`), (`sch 1 para 6(5) the interest is disregarded` `my interest is one of these Church of Scotland interests`))

@export Under schedule 1 paragraphs 2 to 6, am I interested in these shares or debentures for the purposes of sections 254 and 255?
GIVEN `I have some interest of any kind in them` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Do you have an interest of any kind whatsoever in the shares or debentures (restraints on the exercise of its rights, and the fact that the shares cannot be identified, make no difference)?
      `paragraph 3 applies to me` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did the question on paragraph 3 (contract or right to acquire) answer yes?
      `paragraph 4 applies to me` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did the question on paragraph 4 (entitlement to exercise or control rights) answer yes?
      `paragraph 5 applies to me` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did the question on paragraph 5 (a body corporate's interest) answer yes?
      `paragraph 6(1) applies to me` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did the question on paragraph 6 (trust beneficiary) answer yes before the exceptions?
      `I am treated as not interested, or the interest is disregarded, under paragraph 6(3), (4) or (5)` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the interest one that paragraph 6(3), (4) or (5) treats as not an interest (bare, custodian or simple trustee; an authorised unit trust, charity or Church fund scheme; Church of Scotland trustees)?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under schedule 1 paragraphs 2 to 6, am I interested in the shares or debentures for sections 254 and 255` IS
    `sch 1 paras 2 to 6 the person has an interest in the shares or debentures for sections 254 and 255` routes exclusions
    WHERE
        routes MEANS LIST `sch 1 para 2(1) the person has an interest in the shares` `I have some interest of any kind in them`, `coa28 seat route` `paragraph 3 applies to me`, `coa28 seat route` `paragraph 4 applies to me`, `coa28 seat route` `paragraph 5 applies to me`, `coa28 seat route` `paragraph 6(1) applies to me`
        exclusions MEANS LIST `coa28 seat exclusion` `I am treated as not interested, or the interest is disregarded, under paragraph 6(3), (4) or (5)`

-- A route the person says holds is JUST TRUE; a route the person says does not hold is "not by this paragraph" (NOTHING),
-- never "no interest": the first Schedule 1 paragraph 2(1) says the reference "includes any interest of any kind whatsoever".
GIVEN answer IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`coa28 seat route` MEANS IF answer THEN JUST TRUE ELSE NOTHING

GIVEN answer IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`coa28 seat exclusion` MEANS IF answer THEN JUST TRUE ELSE NOTHING

-- =========================================================================================================
§§ `Schedule 1A: people with significant control over a company`
-- =========================================================================================================

-- GROUP: only if you hold shares or voting rights in, or have influence over, a company and want to know whether you
-- are a person with significant control (section 790C). Each question is about ONE company, and amounts are in the
-- same unit: nominal value of shares, number of votes, or per cent of capital or profits where the company has no
-- share capital. The form can ask first "Do you hold or control shares, votes or board appointments in a company?".

@export Under schedule 1A paragraph 2, do I hold, directly or indirectly, more than 25% of the shares in the company?
GIVEN `the company has a share capital` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does the company have a share capital? (Answer no for a company limited by guarantee with no shares; then use per cent of capital or profits below.)
      `shares I hold in my own name` IS A NUMBER @desc How many shares (by nominal value, or as a per cent of capital or profits if the company has no share capital) do you hold in your own name?
      `shares I hold jointly with others` IS A NUMBER @desc How many do you hold jointly with one or more others (each joint holder counts the whole)?
      `shares held by a person who is party to a joint arrangement with me` IS A NUMBER @desc How many are held by another person who is party to a joint arrangement with you (an arrangement to exercise all or substantially all the rights jointly, in a pre-determined way)?
      `shares held by companies in which I have a majority stake` IS A NUMBER @desc How many are held by legal entities in which you have a majority stake, or by the last entity of a chain each of which has a majority stake in the next?
      `shares held by companies in which I have no majority stake` IS A NUMBER @desc How many are held by legal entities in which you have no majority stake (these do not count)?
      `shares held for me by a nominee` IS A NUMBER @desc How many are held for you by another person as your nominee?
      `shares I hold as nominee for someone else` IS A NUMBER @desc How many do you hold as nominee for someone else (these do not count)?
      `shares held in some other way` IS A NUMBER @desc How many are held in some other way that you are unsure counts?
      `the nominal value of the issued share capital` IS A NUMBER @desc What is the nominal value of the company's issued share capital? (Enter 100 if it has no share capital and you are using per cent.)
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under schedule 1A paragraph 2, do I hold, directly or indirectly, more than 25% of the shares in the company` IS
    `sch 1A para 2 the first condition is met` `the company has a share capital` (`sch 1A paras 11 to 23 the amount counted as held by X` blocks) (`sch 1A paras 11 to 23 the further amount that might be counted as held by X` blocks) `the nominal value of the issued share capital`
    WHERE
        blocks MEANS LIST
            `sch 1A block` OF `shares I hold in my own name`, `sch 1A para 2 held directly by X`
            `sch 1A block` OF `shares I hold jointly with others`, `sch 1A para 11 held jointly by X and one or more others`
            `sch 1A block` OF `shares held by a person who is party to a joint arrangement with me`, `sch 1A para 12 held by another person who is party to a joint arrangement with X`
            `sch 1A block` OF `shares held by companies in which I have a majority stake`, `sch 1A para 18 held by a legal entity in which X has a majority stake, or by the last entity of a chain each of which has a majority stake in the next`
            `sch 1A block` OF `shares held by companies in which I have no majority stake`, `sch 1A para 18 held by a legal entity in which X has no majority stake`
            `sch 1A block` OF `shares held for me by a nominee`, `sch 1A para 19 held by another person as nominee for X`
            `sch 1A block` OF `shares I hold as nominee for someone else`, `sch 1A para 19 held by X as nominee for another person`
            `sch 1A block` OF `shares held in some other way`, `sch 1A another way of holding`

@export Under schedule 1A paragraph 3, do I hold, directly or indirectly, more than 25% of the voting rights in the company?
GIVEN `the company has general meetings that decide matters by voting` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does the company hold general meetings at which matters are decided by the exercise of voting rights?
      `votes I hold in my own name` IS A NUMBER @desc How many votes (on all or substantially all matters) do you hold in your own name?
      `votes I hold jointly with others` IS A NUMBER @desc How many do you hold jointly with one or more others?
      `votes held by a person who is party to a joint arrangement with me` IS A NUMBER @desc How many are held by another person who is party to a joint arrangement with you?
      `votes held by companies in which I have a majority stake` IS A NUMBER @desc How many are held by legal entities in which you have a majority stake?
      `votes held by another that I control` IS A NUMBER @desc How many are rights held by another person but controlled by you (exercisable only by you, on your directions, or with your consent, by an arrangement)?
      `votes I hold but another person controls` IS A NUMBER @desc How many do you hold but another person controls (these do not count)?
      `votes attached to shares held by another as security that I provided` IS A NUMBER @desc How many are attached to shares held by another by way of security you provided, where apart from preserving or realising the security they are exercisable only on your instructions and only in your interests, and the shares are held in connection with loans in normal business?
      `votes held in some other way` IS A NUMBER @desc How many are held in some other way that you are unsure counts?
      `all the voting rights in the company` IS A NUMBER @desc How many voting rights are there in the company in all?
      `voting rights the company holds in itself` IS A NUMBER @desc How many of those are held by the company itself? Enter 0 if none.
      `I can block changes to policy or the constitution` IS A BOOLEAN @desc If the company has no general meetings: do you have the right under its constitution to block changes to its overall policy or to the terms of its constitution?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under schedule 1A paragraph 3, do I hold, directly or indirectly, more than 25% of the voting rights in the company` IS
    `sch 1A para 3 the second condition is met` `the company has general meetings that decide matters by voting` (`sch 1A paras 11 to 23 the amount counted as held by X` blocks) (`sch 1A paras 11 to 23 the further amount that might be counted as held by X` blocks) (`sch 1A para 15 the voting rights in the legal entity, reduced by the rights held by the entity itself` `all the voting rights in the company` `voting rights the company holds in itself`) `I can block changes to policy or the constitution`
    WHERE
        blocks MEANS LIST
            `sch 1A block` OF `votes I hold in my own name`, `sch 1A para 2 held directly by X`
            `sch 1A block` OF `votes I hold jointly with others`, `sch 1A para 11 held jointly by X and one or more others`
            `sch 1A block` OF `votes held by a person who is party to a joint arrangement with me`, `sch 1A para 12 held by another person who is party to a joint arrangement with X`
            `sch 1A block` OF `votes held by companies in which I have a majority stake`, `sch 1A para 18 held by a legal entity in which X has a majority stake, or by the last entity of a chain each of which has a majority stake in the next`
            `sch 1A block` OF `votes held by another that I control`, `sch 1A para 20 a right held by another person but controlled by X`
            `sch 1A block` OF `votes I hold but another person controls`, `sch 1A para 20 a right held by X but controlled by another person`
            `sch 1A block` OF `votes attached to shares held by another as security that I provided`, `sch 1A para 23 rights attached to shares held by another by way of security provided by X, meeting paragraph 23(a) and (b)`
            `sch 1A block` OF `votes held in some other way`, `sch 1A another way of holding`

@export Under schedule 1A paragraph 4, do I hold, directly or indirectly, the right to appoint or remove a majority of the company's board of directors?
GIVEN `board votes of the directors I can appoint or remove myself` IS A NUMBER @desc How many votes at board meetings (on all or substantially all matters) are held by directors you have the right to appoint or remove yourself?
      `board votes of the directors an entity I have a majority stake in can appoint or remove` IS A NUMBER @desc How many are held by directors that a legal entity in which you have a majority stake (or the last of a chain of such entities) has the right to appoint or remove?
      `board votes I am unsure count` IS A NUMBER @desc How many are held by directors that you may have the right to appoint or remove in some other way?
      `all the votes at board meetings` IS A NUMBER @desc How many votes are there at the company's board meetings in all, on all or substantially all matters?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under schedule 1A paragraph 4, do I hold, directly or indirectly, the right to appoint or remove a majority of the board` IS
    `sch 1A para 4 the third condition is met` (`sch 1A para 16 the person has the right to appoint or remove a majority of the board of directors` (`sch 1A paras 11 to 23 the amount counted as held by X` blocks) (`sch 1A paras 11 to 23 the further amount that might be counted as held by X` blocks) `all the votes at board meetings`)
    WHERE
        blocks MEANS LIST
            `sch 1A block` OF `board votes of the directors I can appoint or remove myself`, `sch 1A para 2 held directly by X`
            `sch 1A block` OF `board votes of the directors an entity I have a majority stake in can appoint or remove`, `sch 1A para 18 held by a legal entity in which X has a majority stake, or by the last entity of a chain each of which has a majority stake in the next`
            `sch 1A block` OF `board votes I am unsure count`, `sch 1A another way of holding`

@export Under schedule 1A paragraph 5, do I meet the fourth condition: the right to exercise, or actually exercising, significant influence or control over the company?
GIVEN `I have the right to exercise significant influence or control over the company` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Do you have the right to exercise significant influence or control over the company? (The Secretary of State's guidance on the phrase must be regarded.)
      `I actually exercise significant influence or control over the company` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Do you actually exercise significant influence or control over the company?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under schedule 1A paragraph 5, do I meet the fourth condition` IS
    `sch 1A para 5 the fourth condition is met` `I have the right to exercise significant influence or control over the company` `I actually exercise significant influence or control over the company`

@export Under schedule 1A paragraph 6, do I meet the fifth condition through a trust or a firm that is not a legal person?
GIVEN `the trustees or firm members meet another specified condition in their capacity as such` IS A `coa28 seat answer` @desc Do the trustees of the trust, or the members of the firm, meet (or would they, if individuals, meet) any of the other four conditions in relation to the company? Answer yes, no, or I do not know.
      `I have the right to exercise, or actually exercise, significant influence or control over the trust or firm` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Do you have the right to exercise, or actually exercise, significant influence or control over the activities of that trust or firm?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under schedule 1A paragraph 6, do I meet the fifth condition` IS
    `sch 1A para 6 the fifth condition is met` (`coa28 seat the answer as a MAYBE BOOLEAN` `the trustees or firm members meet another specified condition in their capacity as such`) `I have the right to exercise, or actually exercise, significant influence or control over the trust or firm`

@export Under schedule 1A paragraph 1, do I meet at least one of the specified conditions for significant control over the company?
GIVEN `I am an individual` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are you an individual (a natural person, not a company or other entity)?
      `the first condition: more than 25% of the shares` IS A `coa28 seat answer` @desc Did the paragraph 2 question answer yes? Answer yes, no, or I do not know.
      `the second condition: more than 25% of the voting rights` IS A `coa28 seat answer` @desc Did the paragraph 3 question answer yes? Answer yes, no, or I do not know.
      `the third condition: the right to appoint or remove a majority of the board` IS A `coa28 seat answer` @desc Did the paragraph 4 question answer yes? Answer yes, no, or I do not know.
      `the fourth condition: significant influence or control` IS A `coa28 seat answer` @desc Did the paragraph 5 question answer yes? Answer yes, no, or I do not know.
      `the fifth condition: through a trust or firm` IS A `coa28 seat answer` @desc Did the paragraph 6 question answer yes? Answer yes, no, or I do not know.
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under schedule 1A paragraph 1, do I meet at least one of the specified conditions` IS
    `sch 1A para 1 at least one of the specified conditions is met by X in relation to company Y` `I am an individual` conditions
    WHERE
        conditions MEANS LIST
            (`coa28 seat the answer as a MAYBE BOOLEAN` `the first condition: more than 25% of the shares`),
            (`coa28 seat the answer as a MAYBE BOOLEAN` `the second condition: more than 25% of the voting rights`),
            (`coa28 seat the answer as a MAYBE BOOLEAN` `the third condition: the right to appoint or remove a majority of the board`),
            (`coa28 seat the answer as a MAYBE BOOLEAN` `the fourth condition: significant influence or control`),
            (`coa28 seat the answer as a MAYBE BOOLEAN` `the fifth condition: through a trust or firm`)

-- Audit 2026-11-12: this question was titled "am I left out ..." (JUST TRUE would have meant left out) while the rule it calls answers whether the condition is MET once the carve-outs apply (JUST FALSE means left out). It now asks what the rule answers.
@export Under schedule 1A paragraph 25(1) and (2), do I meet the first, second or third condition once the carve-outs for a limited partner, and for holding only through one, are applied?
GIVEN `I meet that condition` IS A `coa28 seat answer` @desc Do you meet the condition in paragraph 2, 3 or 4 (more than 25% of the shares, more than 25% of the voting rights, or the right to appoint or remove a majority of the board)? Answer yes, no, or I do not know.
      `I meet it only by being a limited partner` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Do you meet it only by virtue of being a limited partner (in a limited partnership registered under the Limited Partnerships Act 1907, other than one who takes part in its management, or a foreign limited partner)?
      `I meet it only by holding shares or a right in or in relation to a limited partner` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Do you meet it only by virtue of directly or indirectly holding shares or a right in or in relation to a limited partner that would itself meet the condition if it were an individual?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under schedule 1A paragraph 25(1) and (2), do I meet the specified condition once limited partners are left out` IS
    `sch 1A paras 2 to 4 and 25 the individual meets the specified condition` (`coa28 seat the answer as a MAYBE BOOLEAN` `I meet that condition`) (`sch 1A para 25(1) the individual meets the specified condition by virtue only of being a limited partner` `I meet it only by being a limited partner`) (`sch 1A para 25(2) the individual meets the specified condition by virtue only of holding shares or a right in or in relation to a limited partner` `I meet it only by holding shares or a right in or in relation to a limited partner`)

@export Under schedule 1A paragraph 18(3), do I have a majority stake in the legal entity?
GIVEN `I hold more than half of the voting rights in it` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Do you hold a majority (more than half) of the voting rights in the entity?
      `I am a member and can appoint or remove a majority of its board` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are you a member of the entity with the right to appoint or remove a majority of its board of directors?
      `I am a member and alone control a majority of its votes by an agreement` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are you a member of the entity who alone controls, under an agreement with other shareholders or members, a majority of its voting rights?
      `I have or exercise dominant influence or control over it` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Do you have the right to exercise, or actually exercise, dominant influence or control over the entity?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under schedule 1A paragraph 18(3), do I have a majority stake in the legal entity` IS
    `sch 1A para 18(3) A has a majority stake in B` `I hold more than half of the voting rights in it` `I am a member and can appoint or remove a majority of its board` `I am a member and alone control a majority of its votes by an agreement` `I have or exercise dominant influence or control over it`

@export Under schedule 1A paragraph 22(1), are rights that can be exercised only in certain circumstances taken into account?
GIVEN `the rights are exercisable only in certain circumstances` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are the rights exercisable only in certain circumstances?
      `the circumstances have arisen and still continue` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Have the circumstances arisen, and do they still continue to obtain?
      `the circumstances are within the control of the person having the rights` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are the circumstances within the control of the person having the rights?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under schedule 1A paragraph 22(1), are rights exercisable only in certain circumstances taken into account` IS
    `sch 1A para 22(1) the rights are taken into account` `the rights are exercisable only in certain circumstances` `the circumstances have arisen and still continue` `the circumstances are within the control of the person having the rights`

@export Under schedule 1A paragraph 23, are rights attached to shares that I hold as security treated as held by the person who provided the security?
GIVEN `the rights are held by way of security provided by the person I am asking about` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are the rights attached to shares held by way of security provided by the person you are asking about?
      `apart from preserving or realising the security, they are exercisable only on that person's instructions` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Apart from the right to exercise them to preserve the value of the security or to realise it, are the rights exercisable only in accordance with that person's instructions?
      `the shares are held in connection with loans as part of normal business activities` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are the shares held in connection with the granting of loans as part of normal business activities?
      `apart from preserving or realising the security, they are exercisable only in that person's interests` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Apart from that, are the rights exercisable only in that person's interests?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under schedule 1A paragraph 23, are the rights treated as held by the person who provided the security` IS
    `sch 1A para 23 the rights are treated as held by the person who provided the security` `the rights are held by way of security provided by the person I am asking about` `apart from preserving or realising the security, they are exercisable only on that person's instructions` `the shares are held in connection with loans as part of normal business activities` `apart from preserving or realising the security, they are exercisable only in that person's interests`

@export Under schedule 1A paragraph 8(1), do I hold an interest in the company for the purposes of section 790C(4) or (8)?
GIVEN `I hold shares in the company, directly or indirectly` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Do you hold shares in the company, directly or indirectly?
      `I hold voting rights in the company, directly or indirectly` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Do you hold voting rights in the company, directly or indirectly?
      `I hold the right to appoint or remove a member of its board, directly or indirectly` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Do you hold, directly or indirectly, the right to appoint or remove any member of the company's board of directors?
      `I have or exercise significant influence or control over the company` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Do you have the right to exercise, or actually exercise, significant influence or control over the company?
      `trustees or firm members hold an interest in one of those ways` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Do the trustees of a trust, or the members of a firm that is not a legal person, hold an interest in the company in one of those ways (shares, voting rights, the right to appoint or remove a director, or influence or control)?
      `I have or exercise influence or control over that trust or firm` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Do you have the right to exercise, or actually exercise, significant influence or control over the activities of that trust or firm?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under schedule 1A paragraph 8(1), do I hold an interest in the company` IS
    `sch 1A para 8(1) V holds an interest in company W` `I hold shares in the company, directly or indirectly` `I hold voting rights in the company, directly or indirectly` `I hold the right to appoint or remove a member of its board, directly or indirectly` `I have or exercise significant influence or control over the company` (`sch 1A para 8(2) this sub-paragraph is satisfied` `trustees or firm members hold an interest in one of those ways` `I have or exercise influence or control over that trust or firm`)

@export Under schedule 1A paragraph 24(2), must regard be had to the Secretary of State's guidance on "significant influence or control"?
GIVEN `the guidance has been issued` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has the Secretary of State issued guidance under paragraph 24 about the meaning of "significant influence or control"?
      `I am interpreting those words in Schedule 1A` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are you interpreting a reference in Schedule 1A to "significant influence or control"?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under schedule 1A paragraph 24(2), must regard be had to the guidance` IS
    `sch 1A para 24(2) regard must be had to the guidance` `the guidance has been issued` `I am interpreting those words in Schedule 1A`

-- =========================================================================================================
§§ `Schedule 1B: enforcement of disclosure requirements (restrictions notices and offences)`
-- =========================================================================================================

-- GROUP: only if a company has served you with a notice asking who has an interest in or control over it (sections
-- 790D, 790DA, 790E, 790EA), or you hold an interest the company has restricted. The form can ask first "Has a
-- company served you with a notice about your interest in it?" before showing these questions.

@export Under schedule 1B paragraph 1(3), may the company issue a restrictions notice to me now?
GIVEN `the date the company gave me a warning notice` IS A DATE @desc On what date did the company give you the warning notice?
      `the day the company wants to issue the restrictions notice` IS A DATE @desc On what date does the company want to issue (send) the restrictions notice?
      `I still have not complied with the notice` IS A BOOLEAN @desc As at the end of the month that began on the date of the warning notice, had you still not complied with the notice served on you?
      `the company still has no valid reason for my failure` IS A BOOLEAN @desc As at the end of that month, had the company still not been given a valid reason sufficient to justify your failure to comply?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under schedule 1B paragraph 1(3), may the company issue the restrictions notice to me now` IS
    `sch 1B para 1(3) the company may issue the restrictions notice` `the date the company gave me a warning notice` `the day the company wants to issue the restrictions notice` `I still have not complied with the notice` `the company still has no valid reason for my failure`

@export Under schedule 1B paragraph 3(1), does the restrictions notice stop me doing this?
GIVEN act IS A `sch 1B para 3(1) act` @desc What do you want to do with the restricted interest? Choose: transfer it, exercise a right in respect of it, have shares issued in right of it or on an offer to you, be paid sums due in respect of it, or another act.
      `a restrictions notice issued under paragraph 1 is in force on my interest` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is a restrictions notice issued under paragraph 1 in force on your interest?
      `the company is in a liquidation` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the company in a liquidation?
      `the court has given a direction under paragraph 4 that covers this act` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has the court given a direction under paragraph 4 that covers this act?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under schedule 1B paragraph 3(1), does the restrictions notice stop me doing this` IS
    `sch 1B para 3(1) the effect of the restrictions notice applies to the act` act `a restrictions notice issued under paragraph 1 is in force on my interest` `the company is in a liquidation` (`sch 1B para 3(7) the provisions of paragraph 3 are subject to the direction` `the court has given a direction under paragraph 4 that covers this act`)

@export Under schedule 1B paragraph 3(2), is my agreement to transfer the restricted interest void?
GIVEN `my interest is subject to the restriction on transfers` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is your interest subject to the restriction in paragraph 3(1)(a) (no transfer of the interest)?
      `the agreement is to transfer it on a court order under paragraph 8 that approves the transfer` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the agreement one to transfer the interest on the making of an order under paragraph 8 that relaxes the restrictions because the transfer is for valuable consideration and the court approves it?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under schedule 1B paragraph 3(2), is my agreement to transfer the interest void` IS
    `sch 1B para 3(2) the agreement to transfer the interest is void` `my interest is subject to the restriction on transfers` (`sch 1B para 3(3) sub-paragraph (2) applies to the agreement` `the agreement is to transfer it on a court order under paragraph 8 that approves the transfer`)

@export Under schedule 1B paragraph 3(4), is my agreement to transfer an associated right void?
GIVEN `the agreement is to transfer a right to be issued with shares or to be paid sums due in respect of the interest` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the agreement one to transfer an associated right (a right to be issued with shares issued in right of the interest, or a right to payment of sums due from the company in respect of it)?
      `the transfer is in a liquidation` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the transfer in a liquidation?
      `the agreement is to transfer it on a court order under paragraph 8 that approves the transfer` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the agreement one to transfer the right on the making of an order under paragraph 8 that relaxes the restrictions because the transfer is for valuable consideration and the court approves it?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under schedule 1B paragraph 3(4), is my agreement to transfer the associated right void` IS
    `sch 1B para 3(4) the agreement to transfer the associated right is void` `the agreement is to transfer a right to be issued with shares or to be paid sums due in respect of the interest` `the transfer is in a liquidation` (`sch 1B para 3(5) sub-paragraph (4) applies to the agreement` `the agreement is to transfer it on a court order under paragraph 8 that approves the transfer`)

@export Under schedule 1B paragraph 4(1), may the court give a direction to protect my rights as a third party affected by a restrictions notice?
GIVEN `I am a person aggrieved and I have applied` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are you a person aggrieved, and have you applied to the court?
      `the court is satisfied that the notice unfairly affects third parties' rights` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the court satisfied that the restrictions notice unfairly affects the rights of third parties in respect of the relevant interest?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under schedule 1B paragraph 4(1), may the court give a direction to protect third party rights` IS
    `sch 1B para 4(1) the court may give a direction` `I am a person aggrieved and I have applied` `the court is satisfied that the notice unfairly affects third parties' rights`

@export Under schedule 1B paragraph 5(1), do I commit an offence by doing this with a restricted interest?
GIVEN thing IS A `sch 1B para 5(2) thing` @desc What did you do? Choose: exercise or purport to exercise a right to dispose of the interest, exercise or purport to exercise a right to dispose of a right to be issued with it, vote in respect of it (as holder or proxy) or appoint a proxy to vote, or another thing.
      `I knew the interest was subject to restrictions` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did you know the interest was subject to restrictions under a restrictions notice?
      `a direction under paragraph 4 or 8 covers what I did` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does a direction given under paragraph 4 or 8 cover what you did?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under schedule 1B paragraph 5(1), do I commit an offence by doing this with a restricted interest` IS
    `sch 1B para 5(1) the person commits an offence` thing `I knew the interest was subject to restrictions` (`sch 1B para 7(2) the provisions of paragraphs 5 and 6 are subject to the direction` `a direction under paragraph 4 or 8 covers what I did`)

@export Under schedule 1B paragraph 5(3), do I commit an offence by not telling a person entitled to vote that the interest is restricted?
GIVEN `I have a relevant interest that I know is subject to restrictions` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Do you have a relevant interest that you know to be subject to restrictions?
      `I know another person is entitled, apart from the restrictions, to vote in respect of it` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Do you know another person to be entitled (apart from the restrictions) to vote in respect of the interest, as holder or as proxy?
      `I do not know that person to be aware of the restrictions` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Do you not know that person to be aware that the interest is subject to restrictions?
      `I fail to notify that person` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Do you fail to notify that person that the interest is subject to restrictions?
      `a direction under paragraph 4 or 8 covers what I did` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does a direction given under paragraph 4 or 8 cover what you did?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under schedule 1B paragraph 5(3), do I commit an offence by not notifying a person entitled to vote` IS
    `sch 1B para 5(3) the person commits an offence` `I have a relevant interest that I know is subject to restrictions` `I know another person is entitled, apart from the restrictions, to vote in respect of it` `I do not know that person to be aware of the restrictions` `I fail to notify that person` (`sch 1B para 7(2) the provisions of paragraphs 5 and 6 are subject to the direction` `a direction under paragraph 4 or 8 covers what I did`)

@export Under schedule 1B paragraph 5(4), do I commit an offence by entering into an agreement that the restrictions make void?
GIVEN `I have a restricted interest I know of, or I am entitled to an associated right` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Do you either have a relevant interest that you know to be subject to restrictions, or are you entitled to an associated right?
      `I enter into an agreement that is void under paragraph 3(2) or (4)` IS A BOOLEAN @desc In that capacity, do you enter into an agreement that is void by virtue of paragraph 3(2) or (4)?
      `a direction under paragraph 4 or 8 covers what I did` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does a direction given under paragraph 4 or 8 cover what you did?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under schedule 1B paragraph 5(4), do I commit an offence by entering into a void agreement` IS
    `sch 1B para 5(4) the person commits an offence` `I have a restricted interest I know of, or I am entitled to an associated right` `I enter into an agreement that is void under paragraph 3(2) or (4)` (`sch 1B para 7(2) the provisions of paragraphs 5 and 6 are subject to the direction` `a direction under paragraph 4 or 8 covers what I did`)

@export Under schedule 1B paragraph 7(1), what is the penalty for an offence under paragraph 5 or 6?
GIVEN `how I am convicted` IS A `Mode of conviction` @desc How are you convicted? Choose: on conviction on indictment, or on summary conviction in England and Wales, in Scotland or in Northern Ireland.
GIVETH A MAYBE Penalty
DECIDE `Under schedule 1B paragraph 7(1), what is the penalty for an offence under paragraph 5 or 6` IS
    `sch 1B para 7(1) the penalty for an offence under paragraph 5 or 6` `how I am convicted`

@export Under schedule 1B paragraph 8(2), may I apply to the court for an order that my interest cease to be subject to restrictions?
GIVEN `I am the company in question` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are you the company in question?
      `I am a person aggrieved` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are you a person aggrieved?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under schedule 1B paragraph 8(2), may I apply for an order that the interest cease to be subject to restrictions` IS
    `sch 1B para 8(2) the person may apply for an order under paragraph 8` `I am the company in question` `I am a person aggrieved`

@export Under schedule 1B paragraph 8(3), is the court barred from lifting the restrictions on my interest?
GIVEN `the court is satisfied the information has been disclosed to the company` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the court satisfied that the information required by the notice has been disclosed to the company?
      `no unfair advantage has accrued to anyone from the earlier failure to disclose` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has no unfair advantage accrued to any person as a result of the earlier failure to make that disclosure?
      `the interest is to be transferred for valuable consideration and the court approves` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the interest to be transferred for valuable consideration, with the court's approval of the transfer?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under schedule 1B paragraph 8(3), is the court barred from making an order lifting the restrictions` IS
    `sch 1B para 8(3) the court is barred from making an order under paragraph 8` `the court is satisfied the information has been disclosed to the company` `no unfair advantage has accrued to anyone from the earlier failure to disclose` `the interest is to be transferred for valuable consideration and the court approves`

@export Under schedule 1B paragraph 10(3), how much of the proceeds of the court-ordered sale must the court order paid to me, in pounds?
GIVEN `the proceeds of sale paid into court` IS A NUMBER @desc What are the proceeds of the sale paid into court, in pounds (less the costs of the sale)?
      `the interest on the proceeds` IS A NUMBER @desc How much interest has the court received on the proceeds, in pounds? Enter 0 if none.
      `another person was also beneficially interested at the time of the sale` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Was another person also beneficially interested in the relevant interest at the time of the sale?
      `the value of my interest` IS A NUMBER @desc What was the value of your interest, in pounds?
      `the total value of the relevant interest` IS A NUMBER @desc What was the total value of the relevant interest, in pounds?
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `Under schedule 1B paragraph 10(3), how much of the proceeds must the court order paid to me` IS
    `sch 1B para 10(3) the amount the court must order to be paid to the applicant` `the proceeds of sale paid into court` `the interest on the proceeds` `another person was also beneficially interested at the time of the sale` `the value of my interest` `the total value of the relevant interest`

@export Under schedule 1B paragraph 11, must the company withdraw the restrictions notice it issued to me?
GIVEN `the company is satisfied there is a valid reason for my failure to comply` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the company satisfied that there is a valid reason sufficient to justify your failure to comply with the notice?
      `the notice served on me has now been complied with` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has the notice served on you been complied with?
      `the company discovers that a third party's rights are being unfairly affected` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does the company discover that the rights of a third party in respect of the relevant interest are being unfairly affected by the restrictions notice?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under schedule 1B paragraph 11, must the company by notice withdraw the restrictions notice` IS
    `sch 1B para 11 the company must by notice withdraw the restrictions notice` `the company is satisfied there is a valid reason for my failure to comply` `the notice served on me has now been complied with` `the company discovers that a third party's rights are being unfairly affected`

@export Under schedule 1B paragraph 13(1), do I commit an offence by not complying with the company's notice?
GIVEN `a notice under section 790D, 790DA, 790E or 790EA is addressed to me` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is a notice under section 790D, 790DA, 790E or 790EA addressed to you?
      `I fail to comply with it` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Do you fail to comply with the notice?
      `I have a reasonable excuse` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Do you have a reasonable excuse for failing to comply?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under schedule 1B paragraph 13(1), do I commit an offence by failing to comply with the notice` IS
    `sch 1B para 13(1) the person commits an offence by failing to comply with the notice` `a notice under section 790D, 790DA, 790E or 790EA is addressed to me` `I fail to comply with it` `I have a reasonable excuse`

@export Under schedule 1B paragraph 13(2), do I commit an offence as an officer of a legal entity that fails to comply with the notice?
GIVEN `the person the notice is addressed to is a legal entity` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the person to whom the notice is addressed a legal entity?
      `the entity commits the offence of failing to comply` IS A `coa28 seat answer` @desc Does the entity commit the offence of failing, without reasonable excuse, to comply with the notice? Answer yes, no, or I do not know.
      `I am an officer of the entity in default` IS A `coa28 seat answer` @desc Are you an officer of the entity who is in default (section 1121)? Answer yes, no, or I do not know.
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under schedule 1B paragraph 13(2), do I commit an offence as an officer of the entity` IS
    `sch 1B para 13(2) the officer of the entity commits an offence` `the person the notice is addressed to is a legal entity` (`coa28 seat the answer as a MAYBE BOOLEAN` `the entity commits the offence of failing to comply`) (`coa28 seat the answer as a MAYBE BOOLEAN` `I am an officer of the entity in default`)

@export Under schedule 1B paragraph 13(3), what is the penalty for failing to comply with a notice?
GIVEN `how I am convicted` IS A `Mode of conviction` @desc How are you convicted? Choose: on conviction on indictment, or on summary conviction in England and Wales, in Scotland or in Northern Ireland.
      `the general limit in a magistrates' court in England and Wales, in months` IS A NUMBER @desc If convicted in England and Wales on summary conviction: what is the general limit on imprisonment in a magistrates' court, in months? (The Act does not state it; enter any number otherwise.)
GIVETH A MAYBE Penalty
DECIDE `Under schedule 1B paragraph 13(3), what is the penalty for failing to comply with a notice` IS
    `sch 1B para 13(3) the penalty for an offence under paragraph 13` `how I am convicted` `the general limit in a magistrates' court in England and Wales, in months`

@export Under schedule 1B paragraph 14(1), do I commit an offence by not complying with a duty to provide information?
GIVEN `I fail to comply with a duty under section 790G, 790H or 790HA` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Do you fail to comply with a duty under section 790G, 790H or 790HA?
      `I have a reasonable excuse` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Do you have a reasonable excuse for failing to comply?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under schedule 1B paragraph 14(1), do I commit an offence by failing to comply with the duty` IS
    `sch 1B para 14(1) the person commits an offence by failing to comply with the duty` `I fail to comply with a duty under section 790G, 790H or 790HA` `I have a reasonable excuse`

@export Under schedule 1B paragraph 14B(1), do I commit an offence by knowingly making a false statement in answer to a notice or duty?
GIVEN `I make a statement I know is misleading, false or deceptive in a material particular, in purported compliance with a notice or duty` IS A BOOLEAN @desc In purported compliance with a notice under section 790D, 790DA, 790E or 790EA or a duty under section 790G, 790H or 790HA, do you make a statement that you know is misleading, false or deceptive in a material particular?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under schedule 1B paragraph 14B(1), do I commit the aggravated offence of making a false statement` IS
    `sch 1B para 14B(1) the person commits the aggravated offence of making a false statement` `I make a statement I know is misleading, false or deceptive in a material particular, in purported compliance with a notice or duty`

-- =========================================================================================================
§§ `Schedule 1C: rules of the Takeover Panel (general principles and other provision)`
-- =========================================================================================================

-- GROUP: only if a takeover bid is being made for a company whose securities are admitted to trading on a UK regulated
-- market. The form can ask first "Is a takeover bid being made for, or by, your company?" before showing these
-- questions. These answer what the Act requires the Panel's rules to require; the Takeover Code itself is outside
-- the sources.

@export Under schedule 1C paragraph 1(1), must the rules afford me, as a holder, the same treatment as every other holder of securities of the same class?
GIVEN `I hold securities of an offeree company` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Do you hold securities of an offeree company?
      `the rights attached to the securities are in all respects uniform` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are the rights attached to the securities in all respects uniform with those of the other securities (a difference only in dividend rights for the twelve months after their allotment does not count)?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under schedule 1C paragraph 1(1), must the rules afford me equivalent treatment as a holder` IS
    `sch 1C para 1(1) the rules must afford the holders equivalent treatment` `I hold securities of an offeree company` (`sch 1C para 20(2) the securities are of one class` `the rights attached to the securities are in all respects uniform`)

@export Under schedule 1C paragraph 3, does our board, as the board of the offeree company, comply with the principle?
GIVEN `our board is the board of directors of an offeree company` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is your board the board of directors of an offeree company?
      `our board acts in the interests of the company as a whole` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does your board act in the interests of the company as a whole?
      `our board denies the holders the opportunity to decide on the merits of the bid` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does your board deny the holders of securities the opportunity to decide on the merits of the takeover bid?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under schedule 1C paragraph 3, does the board of the offeree company comply with the principle` IS
    `sch 1C para 3 the board of the offeree company complies with the principle` `our board is the board of directors of an offeree company` `our board acts in the interests of the company as a whole` `our board denies the holders the opportunity to decide on the merits of the bid`

@export Under schedule 1C paragraph 5, am I, as offeror, barred from announcing the takeover bid yet?
GIVEN `I am offering cash` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is any of the consideration cash?
      `I have ensured I can fulfil the cash consideration in full` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Have you ensured that you can fulfil in full any cash consideration?
      `I am offering another type of consideration` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is any of the consideration of another type (securities, for example)?
      `I have taken all reasonable measures to secure the other consideration` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Have you taken all reasonable measures to secure the implementation of the other type of consideration?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under schedule 1C paragraph 5, am I barred from announcing the takeover bid yet` IS
    `sch 1C para 5 the offeror is barred from announcing the takeover bid yet` `I am offering cash` `I have ensured I can fulfil the cash consideration in full` `I am offering another type of consideration` `I have taken all reasonable measures to secure the other consideration`

@export Under schedule 1C paragraph 7(1), must the rules require me to make a mandatory takeover bid?
GIVEN `I or a person acting in concert with me has acquired securities in the company` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Have you, or a person acting in concert with you, acquired securities in the company?
      `with my existing securities they give me control` IS A BOOLEAN @desc When added to any existing securities held by you or by persons acting in concert with you, do the acquired securities directly or indirectly give you control of the company?
      `I acquired control following a voluntary bid to all holders for all their holdings` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did you acquire control following a voluntary takeover bid to all the holders of securities for all their holdings?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under schedule 1C paragraph 7(1), must the rules require me to make a mandatory takeover bid` IS
    `sch 1C para 7(1) the rules must require P to make a mandatory takeover bid` `I or a person acting in concert with me has acquired securities in the company` `with my existing securities they give me control` (`sch 1C para 7(3) the obligation to make a mandatory takeover bid no longer applies` `I acquired control following a voluntary bid to all holders for all their holdings`)

@export Under schedule 1C paragraph 8(1), what is the equitable price for my mandatory takeover bid, in pounds?
GIVEN `the day the mandatory takeover bid is announced` IS A DATE @desc On what date is the mandatory takeover bid announced?
      `the period the rules determine, in months` IS A NUMBER @desc How many months before the announcement do the rules look back? (The Act requires not less than 6 and not more than 12.)
      `the date of my first purchase` IS A DATE @desc On what date did you (or a person acting in concert with you) make your first purchase of the same securities? (Any date if none.)
      `the price I paid in the first purchase` IS A NUMBER @desc What price was paid in that purchase, in pounds? (0 if none.)
      `the date of my second purchase` IS A DATE @desc On what date was your second purchase? (Any date if none.)
      `the price I paid in the second purchase` IS A NUMBER @desc What price was paid in the second purchase, in pounds? (0 if none.)
      `the date of my third purchase` IS A DATE @desc On what date was your third purchase? (Any date if none.)
      `the price I paid in the third purchase` IS A NUMBER @desc What price was paid in the third purchase, in pounds? (0 if none.)
      `the first purchase was made` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Was there a first purchase?
      `the second purchase was made` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Was there a second purchase?
      `the third purchase was made` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Was there a third purchase?
GIVETH A MAYBE NUMBER
DECIDE `Under schedule 1C paragraph 8(1), what is the equitable price` IS
    `sch 1C para 8(1) the equitable price` purchases `the day the mandatory takeover bid is announced` `the period the rules determine, in months`
    WHERE
        purchases MEANS LIST
            `sch 1C para 8(1) purchase` OF `the date of my first purchase`, `the price I paid in the first purchase`, `the first purchase was made`, TRUE
            `sch 1C para 8(1) purchase` OF `the date of my second purchase`, `the price I paid in the second purchase`, `the second purchase was made`, TRUE
            `sch 1C para 8(1) purchase` OF `the date of my third purchase`, `the price I paid in the third purchase`, `the third purchase was made`, TRUE

@export Under schedule 1C paragraph 8(2), what is the lowest the consideration in my mandatory takeover bid may be raised to, in pounds?
GIVEN `the offer price` IS A NUMBER @desc What is the offer price, in pounds?
      `the highest price I paid after the bid was made public and before it closes` IS A NUMBER @desc What is the highest price you (or a person acting in concert with you) paid for securities after the bid was made public and before the offer closes for acceptance, in pounds? (0 if none.)
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `Under schedule 1C paragraph 8(2), what is the lowest the offer consideration may be` IS
    `sch 1C para 8(2) the offer consideration must not be less than` `the offer price` (LIST `the highest price I paid after the bid was made public and before it closes`)

@export Under schedule 1C paragraph 9(2), must the rules require cash to be offered as an alternative in my mandatory takeover bid?
GIVEN `my consideration is not liquid securities admitted to trading on a UK regulated market` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does the consideration you offer not consist of liquid securities admitted to trading on a UK regulated market?
      `the fraction of the voting rights carried by securities I bought for cash` IS A NUMBER @desc What fraction (for example 0.05 for 5%) of the voting rights in the offeree company do the securities you (and persons acting in concert with you) purchased for cash over the relevant period carry, taken together?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under schedule 1C paragraph 9(2), must the rules require cash to be offered as an alternative` IS
    `sch 1C para 9(2) the rules must ensure that cash is offered as an alternative` `my consideration is not liquid securities admitted to trading on a UK regulated market` `the fraction of the voting rights carried by securities I bought for cash`

@export Under schedule 1C paragraph 12(4), does the offer document state everything the rules must require it to state?
GIVEN `it states the terms of the bid` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does the offer document state the terms of the takeover bid? (For each question, answer yes if the item does not apply to this bid.)
      `it states the identity of the offeror and, for a company, its type, name and registered office` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does it state the identity of the offeror and, where the offeror is a company, its type, name and registered office?
      `it states the securities or classes for which the bid is made` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does it state the securities or, where appropriate, the class or classes of securities for which the bid is made?
      `it states the consideration and, for a mandatory bid, how it was determined and paid` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does it state the consideration offered for each security or class and, for a mandatory bid, the method used to determine it, with particulars of how it is to be paid?
      `it states the compensation for rights removed by an opting-in resolution` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does it state the compensation offered for the rights which might be removed as a result of a company's opting-in resolution under Chapter 2, how it is to be paid and how it was determined?
      `it states the maximum and minimum percentages or quantities the offeror undertakes to acquire` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does it state the maximum and minimum percentages or quantities of securities the offeror undertakes to acquire?
      `it states the existing holdings of the offeror and of persons acting in concert` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does it state details of any existing holdings of the offeror, and of any person acting in concert with the offeror, in the offeree company?
      `it states all the conditions of the bid` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does it state all the conditions to which the bid is subject?
      `it states the offeror's intentions for the offeree company's future business` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does it state the offeror's intentions with regard to the future business of the offeree company?
      `it states the offeror's intentions for jobs and conditions of employment` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does it state the offeror's intentions with regard to safeguarding the jobs of the employees and management of the offeree company, including any material change in the conditions of employment?
      `it states the offeror's strategic plans and their likely repercussions` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does it state the offeror's strategic plans for the offeree company and their likely repercussions on employment and the locations of its places of business?
      `it states the offeror's own intentions and plans, where the offeror is a company affected by the bid` IS A BOOLEAN @desc If the offeror is a company and in so far as it is affected by the bid, does it state the offeror's intentions as to its own future business and jobs and its strategic plans for itself?
      `it states the time allowed for acceptance` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does it state the time allowed for acceptance of the bid?
      `it states information on any securities offered as consideration` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Where the consideration includes securities of any kind, does it state information concerning those securities?
      `it states information on the financing of the bid` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does it state information concerning the financing for the bid?
      `it states the persons acting in concert and their relationships` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does it state the identity of persons acting in concert with the offeror or the offeree company and, for companies, their types, names, registered offices and relationships?
      `it states the national law governing the contracts and the competent courts` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does it state the national law which will govern contracts concluded between the offeror and the holders as a result of the bid, and the competent courts?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under schedule 1C paragraph 12(4), does the offer document state at least what the rules must require` IS
    `sch 1C para 12(4) the offer document states at least the information the rules must require` notStated EMPTY
    WHERE
        notStated MEANS concat (LIST
            (`coa28 seat the item if not stated` `it states the terms of the bid` `sch 1C para 12(4)(a) the terms of the takeover bid`),
            (`coa28 seat the item if not stated` `it states the identity of the offeror and, for a company, its type, name and registered office` `sch 1C para 12(4)(b) the identity of the offeror and, where the offeror is a company, the company's type, name and registered office`),
            (`coa28 seat the item if not stated` `it states the securities or classes for which the bid is made` `sch 1C para 12(4)(c) the securities or, where appropriate, the class or classes of securities for which the takeover bid is made`),
            (`coa28 seat the item if not stated` `it states the consideration and, for a mandatory bid, how it was determined and paid` `sch 1C para 12(4)(d) the consideration offered for each security or class of securities and, in the case of a mandatory takeover bid, the method employed in determining it, with particulars of the way in which that consideration is to be paid`),
            (`coa28 seat the item if not stated` `it states the compensation for rights removed by an opting-in resolution` `sch 1C para 12(4)(e) the compensation offered for the rights which might be removed as a result of a company's opting-in resolution under Chapter 2, with particulars of the way in which that compensation is to be paid and the method employed in determining it`),
            (`coa28 seat the item if not stated` `it states the maximum and minimum percentages or quantities the offeror undertakes to acquire` `sch 1C para 12(4)(f) the maximum and minimum percentages or quantities of securities which the offeror undertakes to acquire`),
            (`coa28 seat the item if not stated` `it states the existing holdings of the offeror and of persons acting in concert` `sch 1C para 12(4)(g) details of any existing holdings of the offeror, and of any person acting in concert with the offeror, in the offeree company`),
            (`coa28 seat the item if not stated` `it states all the conditions of the bid` `sch 1C para 12(4)(h) all the conditions to which the takeover bid is subject`),
            (`coa28 seat the item if not stated` `it states the offeror's intentions for the offeree company's future business` `sch 1C para 12(4)(i) the offeror's intentions with regard to the future business of the offeree company`),
            (`coa28 seat the item if not stated` `it states the offeror's intentions for jobs and conditions of employment` `sch 1C para 12(4)(j) the offeror's intentions with regard to the safeguarding of the jobs of the employees and management of the offeree company, including any material change in the conditions of employment`),
            (`coa28 seat the item if not stated` `it states the offeror's strategic plans and their likely repercussions` `sch 1C para 12(4)(k) the offeror's strategic plans for the offeree company, and their likely repercussions on employment and the locations of the company's places of business`),
            (`coa28 seat the item if not stated` `it states the offeror's own intentions and plans, where the offeror is a company affected by the bid` `sch 1C para 12(4)(l) if the offeror is a company and in so far as it is affected by the takeover bid, its intentions as to future business and jobs and its strategic plans for itself`),
            (`coa28 seat the item if not stated` `it states the time allowed for acceptance` `sch 1C para 12(4)(m) the time allowed for acceptance of the takeover bid`),
            (`coa28 seat the item if not stated` `it states information on any securities offered as consideration` `sch 1C para 12(4)(n) where the consideration offered includes securities of any kind, information concerning those securities`),
            (`coa28 seat the item if not stated` `it states information on the financing of the bid` `sch 1C para 12(4)(o) information concerning the financing for the takeover bid`),
            (`coa28 seat the item if not stated` `it states the persons acting in concert and their relationships` `sch 1C para 12(4)(p) the identity of persons acting in concert with the offeror or with the offeree company and, in the case of companies, the types, names, registered offices and relationships with the offeror and, where possible, with the offeree company`),
            (`coa28 seat the item if not stated` `it states the national law governing the contracts and the competent courts` `sch 1C para 12(4)(q) the national law which will govern contracts concluded between the offeror and the holders of the offeree company's securities as a result of the takeover bid and the competent courts`))

GIVEN stated IS A BOOLEAN
      item IS A `sch 1C para 12(4) item`
GIVETH A LIST OF `sch 1C para 12(4) item`
`coa28 seat the item if not stated` MEANS IF stated THEN EMPTY ELSE LIST item

@export Under schedule 1C paragraph 13(1), is the time allowed for acceptance of the takeover bid long enough and not too long?
GIVEN `the day the offer document was published` IS A DATE @desc On what date was the offer document published?
      `the last day on which the bid is open for acceptance` IS A DATE @desc What is the last day on which the bid is open for acceptance?
      `the rules make provision under paragraph 14 that changes the time allowed` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Do the rules make provision, in accordance with paragraph 14, that changes the time allowed for acceptance in this case?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under schedule 1C paragraph 13(1), is the time allowed for acceptance within the limits the rules must ensure` IS
    `sch 1C para 13(1) the time allowed for acceptance is within the limits the rules must ensure` `the day the offer document was published` `the last day on which the bid is open for acceptance` `the rules make provision under paragraph 14 that changes the time allowed`

@export Under schedule 1C paragraph 17(1), must the rules require our board to obtain a general meeting's prior authorisation before this action?
GIVEN `the day of the action` IS A DATE @desc On what date do you want to take the action?
      `the day our board received the information that a bid had been made public` IS A DATE @desc On what date did your board receive the information that a decision to make a takeover bid had been made public?
      `the rules fix an earlier stage` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Do the rules fix an earlier stage at which the relevant period begins?
      `that earlier stage` IS A DATE @desc If so, what date? (Any date if not.)
      `the result of the bid has been made public or the bid has lapsed` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has the result of the bid been made public, or the bid lapsed?
      `the day the result was made public or the bid lapsed` IS A DATE @desc If so, on what date? (Any date if not.)
      `we are only seeking alternative takeover bids` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the action only seeking alternative takeover bids?
      `the action may result in the frustration of the bid` IS A BOOLEAN @desc May the action result in the frustration of the bid?
      `the action is issuing shares that may be a lasting impediment to the offeror` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the action issuing shares which may result in a lasting impediment to the offeror's acquiring control of the offeree company?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under schedule 1C paragraph 17(1), must the rules require our board to obtain a general meeting's prior authorisation before the action` IS
    `sch 1C para 17(1) the rules must require the board to obtain the prior authorisation of a general meeting` (`sch 1C para 17(2) the day is within the relevant period` `the day of the action` `the day our board received the information that a bid had been made public` earlier ended) `we are only seeking alternative takeover bids` `the action may result in the frustration of the bid` `the action is issuing shares that may be a lasting impediment to the offeror`
    WHERE
        earlier MEANS IF `the rules fix an earlier stage` THEN JUST `that earlier stage` ELSE NOTHING
        ended MEANS IF `the result of the bid has been made public or the bid has lapsed` THEN JUST `the day the result was made public or the bid lapsed` ELSE NOTHING

@export Under schedule 1C paragraph 18(1), has our board met the requirement to draw up and make public its opinion of the takeover bid?
GIVEN `our board has made public a document setting out its opinion and reasons` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has your board drawn up and made public a document setting out its opinion of the takeover bid and the reasons for the opinion?
      `it includes our views on the effects on all the company's interests and on employment` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does it include your views on the effects of implementing the bid on all the company's interests and specifically employment?
      `it includes our views on the offeror's strategic plans and their repercussions` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does it include your views on the offeror's strategic plans for the company and their likely repercussions on employment and the locations of its places of business, as set out in the offer document?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under schedule 1C paragraph 18(1), has the board met the requirement to draw up and make public its opinion` IS
    `sch 1C para 18(1) the board has met the requirement to draw up and make public its opinion` `our board has made public a document setting out its opinion and reasons` `it includes our views on the effects on all the company's interests and on employment` `it includes our views on the offeror's strategic plans and their repercussions`

@export Under schedule 1C paragraph 20(1), is this offer a "takeover bid" for the purposes of the Schedule?
GIVEN `it is a public offer to the holders of the securities of a company` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it a public offer made to the holders of the securities of a company?
      `it is to acquire some or all of those securities` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it an offer to acquire some or all of those securities (whether mandatory or voluntary)?
      `it follows or aims at the acquisition of control` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does it follow, or have as its objective, the acquisition of control of that company?
      `the company itself makes the offer` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the offer made by the company itself?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under schedule 1C paragraph 20(1), is the offer a takeover bid` IS
    `sch 1C para 20(1) the offer is a takeover bid` `it is a public offer to the holders of the securities of a company` `it is to acquire some or all of those securities` `it follows or aims at the acquisition of control` `the company itself makes the offer`

@export Under schedule 1C paragraph 20(3), am I a person acting in concert with the offeror or the offeree company?
GIVEN `I co-operate with the offeror or the offeree company on the basis of an agreement or understanding` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Do you co-operate with the offeror or the offeree company on the basis of an agreement or understanding?
      `it is aimed at acquiring control of the offeree company` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is that agreement or understanding aimed at acquiring control of the offeree company?
      `it is aimed at frustrating the successful outcome of a takeover bid` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it aimed at frustrating the successful outcome of a takeover bid?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under schedule 1C paragraph 20(3), am I a person acting in concert` IS
    `sch 1C para 20(3) the person is a person acting in concert` `I co-operate with the offeror or the offeree company on the basis of an agreement or understanding` `it is aimed at acquiring control of the offeree company` `it is aimed at frustrating the successful outcome of a takeover bid`

-- ====================================================================================================
-- seat questions from part coa29 (merged by the lead on 2026-11-12; unchanged text follows)
-- ====================================================================================================
-- coa29-seat.l4: Companies Act 2006 (United Kingdom), 2006 c. 46, Schedules 2 to 9 -- THE SEAT LAYER (layer 2).
--
-- SEAT: an individual who is, or is about to become, a director, a company secretary or a member (shareholder) of a company registered under
-- the Act, or who deals with one, asking on facts they can state what the Act requires or lets them do, what rights they have against the
-- company or its directors, what they must disclose, file, approve or vote on and by when, and what follows if it is not done.
-- (Assumed, not ruled: the Act is addressed to companies, so the individual is whoever stands in a company's management or ownership.)
-- Officials appear only as parties the text names (the Takeover Panel, the registrar), never as a seat.
--
-- This layer asks, in the person's words, the questions that Schedules 2 to 9 answer for that person. It calls the layer-1 modules
-- (coa29-sch2-part1/2/3, coa29-sch4, coa29-sch5, coa29-sch6, coa29-sch7, coa29-sch8) and restates no rule. Schedule 3 (amendments of the
-- Companies Act 1985) and Schedule 9 (every paragraph blank in this text) have no question: see NOTES.md.
--
-- PLAIN INPUTS. Every question takes plain inputs (yes/no, a date, a number, a choice from a list), each with a `@desc` worded as the person
-- would be asked. The records and the answers of other sections the layer-1 rules expect are built inside each question from those answers:
-- a yes/no about a section that another part answers (s 86 the registered office, s 112 a member, s 250 a director, s 738 a debenture) becomes
-- JUST TRUE or JUST FALSE for that section's input; the person is never asked to read the Act. A field no rule reads is not asked.
--
-- READING AN ANSWER (rule of 2026-10-29, assumed, not ruled by a lawyer). The questions answer YES (true), NO (false) or "not covered"
-- (null: the Schedule does not decide the case). A "no" is the text saying no in its own words; "not covered" is never a "no".
-- The Schedules mostly say when something is VALIDLY done or is TAKEN to be so; they do not say what follows from an invalid act.

§ `Companies Act 2006 -- Schedules 2 to 9: the questions of a director, company secretary or member`

-- The one conversion this layer needs: a person's yes/no stands for the answer another section would give. NOTHING is never produced from a
-- yes/no; where the person does not know, the layer-1 rule has a NOTHING input and the question is simply not asked here.
GIVEN answer IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`coa29 seat the answer of another section from a yes or no` MEANS
    IF answer THEN JUST TRUE ELSE JUST FALSE

§§ `Schedule 2 -- when the Takeover Panel may pass on information about you or your business without your consent`

-- A group that only arises in a situation you may not be in. Ask first: "Has the Takeover Panel (the body that supervises takeovers of
-- companies) been given information about you, as an individual, or about your business?" Section 948 (not asked here: it belongs to another
-- part) bars the Panel from disclosing such information without your consent; Schedule 2 lists the exceptions: the persons it may tell (Part 1),
-- the descriptions of disclosure it may make (Part 2) and overseas regulators (Part 3).

@ref sch 2 Part 1, specified persons (s 948(3)(b))
@export The Takeover Panel holds information about me or my business: is the person it would pass it to one of the persons specified in Part 1 of Schedule 2? (yes or no)
GIVEN recipient IS A `sch 2 part 1 recipient` @desc Who would the Takeover Panel pass the information to? Pick the entry of Part 1 of Schedule 2 that describes the person (for example the Treasury, the Bank of England, a constable), or "none of the persons listed".
      `the person meets the meaning the entry borrows from another Act` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Some entries say "within the meaning of" another Act (a Jersey or Guernsey police officer, an Isle of Man constable or member of a Department). If you picked one, is the person within that Act's meaning? Otherwise answer false.
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under schedule 2 part 1, is the person the Takeover Panel would tell one of the persons specified there` IS
    `sch 2 part 1 the recipient is a specified person` recipient (`coa29 seat the answer of another section from a yes or no` `the person meets the meaning the entry borrows from another Act`)

@ref sch 2 Part 2, specified descriptions of disclosures (s 948(3)(c))
@export The Takeover Panel holds information about me or my business: is the disclosure it would make of a description specified in Part 2 of Schedule 2? (yes or no)
GIVEN description IS A `sch 2 part 2 description` @desc Which description in Part 2 of Schedule 2 fits the disclosure the Takeover Panel would make? Pick the paragraph (and, where the paragraph lists several Acts or kinds of person, the limb), or "none of the descriptions".
      `the person or body meets the meaning the description gives to a term` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Some descriptions depend on a definition in the paragraph's own sub-paragraph (2) (for example a "lawyer", a "public servant", a "recognised investment exchange"). If you picked one, does the person or body meet that definition? Otherwise answer false.
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under schedule 2 part 2, is the disclosure the Takeover Panel would make of a specified description` IS
    `sch 2 part 2 the disclosure is of a specified description` description (`coa29 seat the answer of another section from a yes or no` `the person or body meets the meaning the description gives to a term`)

@ref sch 2 Part 2, the words of a description
@export What are the words of the paragraph in Part 2 of Schedule 2 that I picked?
GIVEN description IS A `sch 2 part 2 description` @desc Which description in Part 2 of Schedule 2? Pick the paragraph (and the limb where there is one).
GIVETH A STRING
DECIDE `Under schedule 2 part 2, what are the words of the description` IS
    `sch 2 part 2 the words of the description` description

@ref sch 2 Part 2 para 52(2) and (3), lawyer
@export For disciplinary proceedings about a lawyer (Schedule 2 Part 2 paragraph 52): am I a lawyer within the paragraph's meaning? (yes or no)
GIVEN `section 18 of the Legal Services Act 2007 has come into force` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has section 18 of the Legal Services Act 2007 come into force? (The Schedule says "until" it does, a solicitor or barrister in England and Wales counts instead of an authorised person.)
      `I am an authorised person in relation to an activity that is a reserved legal activity` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are you an authorised person, for the purposes of the Legal Services Act 2007, in relation to an activity that is a reserved legal activity?
      `I am a solicitor or barrister in England and Wales` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are you a solicitor or barrister in England and Wales?
      `I am a solicitor or barrister in Northern Ireland` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are you a solicitor or barrister in Northern Ireland?
      `I am a solicitor or advocate in Scotland` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are you a solicitor or advocate in Scotland?
      `I am a member of a legal profession regulated outside the United Kingdom` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are you a member, and entitled to practise as such, of a legal profession regulated in a jurisdiction outside the United Kingdom?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under schedule 2 part 2 paragraph 52(2), am I a lawyer` IS
    `sch 2 part 2(A) para 52(2) the person is a lawyer`
        `section 18 of the Legal Services Act 2007 has come into force`
        `I am an authorised person in relation to an activity that is a reserved legal activity`
        `I am a solicitor or barrister in England and Wales`
        `I am a solicitor or barrister in Northern Ireland`
        `I am a solicitor or advocate in Scotland`
        `I am a member of a legal profession regulated outside the United Kingdom`

@ref sch 2 Part 2 para 53(2), public servant
@export For disciplinary proceedings about a public servant (Schedule 2 Part 2 paragraph 53): am I a public servant within the paragraph's meaning? (yes or no)
GIVEN `I am an officer or employee of the Crown` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are you an officer or employee of the Crown?
      `I am an officer or employee of an authority designated by the Secretary of State by order` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are you an officer or employee of a public or other authority that the Secretary of State has designated for this purpose by an order subject to negative resolution procedure?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under schedule 2 part 2 paragraph 53(2), am I a public servant` IS
    `sch 2 part 2(A) para 53(2) the person is a public servant` `I am an officer or employee of the Crown` `I am an officer or employee of an authority designated by the Secretary of State by order`

@ref sch 2 Part 3 para 1, overseas regulatory bodies
@export The Takeover Panel holds information about me or my business: would a disclosure to an overseas regulator be made in accordance with Part 3 of Schedule 2? (yes, no)
GIVEN `the disclosure is made to a person or body exercising functions under legislation in a country or territory outside the British Islands` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Would the information go to a person or body that exercises functions under legislation in a country or territory outside the British Islands?
      `the functions are functions of a public nature` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are those functions of a public nature?
      `it appears to the Panel that the functions are similar to the Panel's own functions` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does it appear to the Takeover Panel that those functions are similar to the Panel's own functions?
      `it appears to the Panel that the functions are similar to those of the Financial Conduct Authority or the Prudential Regulation Authority` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does it appear to the Panel that they are similar to the functions of the Financial Conduct Authority or the Prudential Regulation Authority?
      `it appears to the Panel that the functions are similar to the regulatory functions of the Bank of England` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does it appear to the Panel that they are similar to the regulatory functions of the Bank of England?
      `the disclosure is made for the purpose of enabling or assisting that person or body to exercise those functions` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Would the disclosure be made to enable or assist that person or body to exercise those functions?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under schedule 2 part 3 paragraph 1, would the disclosure be made in accordance with Part 3` IS
    `sch 2 part 3 para 1(1) the disclosure is made in accordance with this Part`
        `the disclosure is made to a person or body exercising functions under legislation in a country or territory outside the British Islands`
        `the functions are functions of a public nature`
        `it appears to the Panel that the functions are similar to the Panel's own functions`
        `it appears to the Panel that the functions are similar to those of the Financial Conduct Authority or the Prudential Regulation Authority`
        `it appears to the Panel that the functions are similar to the regulatory functions of the Bank of England`
        `the disclosure is made for the purpose of enabling or assisting that person or body to exercise those functions`

@ref sch 2 Part 3 para 2, what the Panel must consider
@export Before the Takeover Panel discloses information about me or my business to an overseas regulator, has it had regard to the two considerations Part 3 of Schedule 2 requires? (yes, no, or null if it is not deciding whether to disclose)
GIVEN `the Panel is determining whether to disclose information to a person or body in accordance with this Part` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the Takeover Panel deciding whether to disclose the information to an overseas person or body under Part 3 of Schedule 2?
      `the Panel has had regard to whether the use that the person or body is likely to make of the information is sufficiently important to justify making the disclosure` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has the Panel had regard to whether the use the overseas person or body is likely to make of the information is sufficiently important to justify the disclosure?
      `the Panel has had regard to whether the person or body has adequate arrangements to prevent the information from being used or further disclosed otherwise than for the purposes of carrying out the functions mentioned in paragraph 1(1)(a) or for other purposes substantially similar to those for which information disclosed to the Panel could be used or further disclosed` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has the Panel had regard to whether the overseas person or body has adequate arrangements to prevent the information being used or passed on otherwise than for the functions of that body or for substantially similar purposes?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under schedule 2 part 3 paragraph 2, has the Takeover Panel had regard to the considerations` IS
    `sch 2 part 3 para 2 the Panel has had regard to the considerations`
        `the Panel is determining whether to disclose information to a person or body in accordance with this Part`
        `the Panel has had regard to whether the use that the person or body is likely to make of the information is sufficiently important to justify making the disclosure`
        `the Panel has had regard to whether the person or body has adequate arrangements to prevent the information from being used or further disclosed otherwise than for the purposes of carrying out the functions mentioned in paragraph 1(1)(a) or for other purposes substantially similar to those for which information disclosed to the Panel could be used or further disclosed`

§§ `Schedule 4 -- documents and information you send to your company (or the registrar sends it)`

@ref sch 4 para 1, application of the Schedule
@export Does Schedule 4 govern a document or information I am sending to a company? (yes, no, or null if it is not being sent to a company)
GIVEN `the document or information is sent or supplied to a company` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are you sending or supplying the document or information to a company?
      `the document or information is sent or supplied by another company` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it being sent or supplied by another company (not by you, an individual)?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under schedule 4 paragraph 1, does the Schedule apply to the document or information` IS
    `sch 4 para 1 this Schedule applies to the document or information` `the document or information is sent or supplied to a company` `the document or information is sent or supplied by another company`

@ref sch 4 paras 2 to 4, hard copy form
@export I am sending my company a paper (hard copy) document: is it validly sent? (yes, no)
GIVEN `how I send it` IS A `sch 4 means of sending or supplying` @desc How do you send it? One of: sch 4 by hand, sch 4 by post, sch 4 by electronic means, sch 4 by some other means.
      `I post a prepaid envelope containing it` IS A BOOLEAN @desc If you send it by post, do you post a prepaid envelope containing it? Otherwise answer false.
      `the address is one the company specified for the purpose` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the address one that the company specified for receiving such documents?
      `the address is the company's registered office` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the address the company's registered office?
      `a provision of the Companies Acts authorises sending it to the address` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does a provision of the Companies Acts authorise this document to be sent to that address (for example the address the Act requires for that kind of document)?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under schedule 4 paragraph 2, is the paper document I send my company validly sent` IS
    `sch 4 para 2 the document or information is validly sent or supplied in hard copy form`
        `sch 4 hard copy form` `how I send it`
        `I post a prepaid envelope containing it`
        `the address is one the company specified for the purpose`
        (`coa29 seat the answer of another section from a yes or no` `the address is the company's registered office`)
        `a provision of the Companies Acts authorises sending it to the address`

@ref sch 4 paras 5 to 7, electronic form
@export I am sending my company a document in electronic form (an e-mail, or a disk): is it validly sent? (yes, no)
GIVEN `how I send it` IS A `sch 4 means of sending or supplying` @desc How do you send it? One of: sch 4 by hand, sch 4 by post, sch 4 by electronic means (e-mail, fax), sch 4 by some other means.
      `the company has agreed that I may send documents in electronic form` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has the company agreed, generally or for this document, that it may be sent or supplied to it in electronic form?
      `the company has revoked that agreement` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has the company withdrawn that agreement?
      `a provision of the Companies Acts deems the company to have agreed` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does a provision of the Companies Acts treat the company as having agreed to receive documents in electronic form?
      `the address is one the company specified for electronic documents` IS A BOOLEAN @desc If you send it by electronic means: is the address one the company specified for the purpose, generally or for this document?
      `a provision of the Companies Acts deems the address to be specified` IS A BOOLEAN @desc If you send it by electronic means: does a provision of the Companies Acts treat the address as specified by the company?
      `the address is one the company specified for paper documents` IS A BOOLEAN @desc If you hand over or post a disk: is the address one the company specified for receiving paper documents?
      `the address is the company's registered office` IS A BOOLEAN @desc If you hand over or post a disk: is the address the company's registered office?
      `a provision of the Companies Acts authorises sending it to the address` IS A BOOLEAN @desc If you hand over or post a disk: does a provision of the Companies Acts authorise a document to be sent to that address?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under schedule 4 paragraph 5, is the electronic document I send my company validly sent` IS
    `sch 4 para 5 the document or information is validly sent or supplied in electronic form by a person other than the registrar or the Secretary of State`
        FALSE `sch 4 electronic form` `how I send it`
        `the company has agreed that I may send documents in electronic form`
        `the company has revoked that agreement`
        `a provision of the Companies Acts deems the company to have agreed`
        `the address is one the company specified for electronic documents`
        `a provision of the Companies Acts deems the address to be specified`
        `the address is one the company specified for paper documents`
        (`coa29 seat the answer of another section from a yes or no` `the address is the company's registered office`)
        `a provision of the Companies Acts authorises sending it to the address`

@ref sch 4 para 4A, communications from the registrar or the Secretary of State
@export The registrar of companies (or the Secretary of State) has sent my company a document in electronic form: was it validly sent? (yes, no)
GIVEN `how it was sent` IS A `sch 4 means of sending or supplying` @desc How was it sent? One of: sch 4 by hand, sch 4 by post, sch 4 by electronic means (e-mail), sch 4 by some other means.
      `the company is registered under this Act` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the company registered under the Companies Act 2006?
      `it was sent to the company's registered email address` IS A BOOLEAN @desc If it was sent by electronic means: was it sent to the company's registered email address?
      `it was sent to an address the company specified for that purpose` IS A BOOLEAN @desc If it was sent by electronic means: was it sent to an address the company specified for that purpose (generally or for this document)?
      `the address is one the company specified for paper documents` IS A BOOLEAN @desc If a disk was handed over or posted: is the address one the company specified for receiving paper documents?
      `the address is the company's registered office` IS A BOOLEAN @desc If a disk was handed over or posted: is the address the company's registered office?
      `a provision of the Companies Acts authorises sending it to the address` IS A BOOLEAN @desc If a disk was handed over or posted: does a provision of the Companies Acts authorise a document to be sent to that address?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under schedule 4 paragraph 4A, was the electronic document the registrar sent my company validly sent` IS
    `sch 4 para 4A(1) the document or information is validly sent or supplied by the registrar or the Secretary of State in electronic form`
        TRUE `sch 4 electronic form` `how it was sent`
        `the company is registered under this Act`
        `it was sent to the company's registered email address`
        `it was sent to an address the company specified for that purpose`
        `the address is one the company specified for paper documents`
        (`coa29 seat the answer of another section from a yes or no` `the address is the company's registered office`)
        `a provision of the Companies Acts authorises sending it to the address`

@ref sch 4 para 8, other agreed forms of communication
@export I am sending my company something in a form that is neither paper nor electronic: is it validly sent? (yes, no)
GIVEN `the company has agreed that form or manner` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has the company agreed to receive documents or information in that form or manner?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under schedule 4 paragraph 8, is what I send my company in another agreed form validly sent` IS
    `sch 4 para 8 the document or information is validly sent or supplied in another agreed form or manner` `sch 4 neither hard copy form nor electronic form` `the company has agreed that form or manner`

§§ `Schedule 5 -- documents and information your company sends you`

@ref sch 5 paras 2 to 4, hard copy form
@export My company sent me a paper (hard copy) document: was it validly sent to me? (yes, no)
GIVEN `how the company sent it to me` IS A `sch 5 means of sending or supplying` @desc How did the company send it? One of: sch 5 handed to the intended recipient, sch 5 by hand to an address, sch 5 by post, sch 5 by electronic means, sch 5 by some other means.
      `the company posted a prepaid envelope containing it` IS A BOOLEAN @desc If it was sent by post: did the company post a prepaid envelope containing it?
      `the address is one I specified for the purpose` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the address one that you specified for the company to use?
      `I am a member of the company` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are you a member (shareholder) of the company?
      `the address is the one shown for me in the register of members` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the address the one shown for you in the company's register of members?
      `I am a director of the company` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are you a director of the company?
      `the address is the one shown for me in the register` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the address the one shown for you, as a director, in the register?
      `a provision of the Companies Acts authorises sending it to the address` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does a provision of the Companies Acts authorise this document to be sent to that address?
      `the company could not obtain an address of those kinds` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Was the company unable to obtain an address of the kinds above (one you specified, your address in the register, or an address a provision authorises)?
      `the address is my last address known to the company` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the address your last address known to the company?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under schedule 5 paragraph 2, was the paper document my company sent me validly sent` IS
    `sch 5 para 2 the document or information is validly sent or supplied in hard copy form` WITH
        `the form of the document or information` IS `sch 5 hard copy form`
        `the result of sch 5 para 3(1) the document or information in hard copy form is handed over or sent as the paragraph requires` IS `the method and address`
    WHERE
        `the method and address` MEANS
            `sch 5 para 3(1) the document or information in hard copy form is handed over or sent as the paragraph requires` WITH
                `the means of sending or supplying` IS `how the company sent it to me`
                `the person posts a prepaid envelope containing the document or information` IS `the company posted a prepaid envelope containing it`
                `the address is one to which hard copy may be sent or supplied under paragraph 4` IS `the address of paragraph 4`
        `the address of paragraph 4` MEANS
            `sch 5 para 4 the address is one to which hard copy may be sent or supplied` WITH
                `the address is specified for the purpose by the intended recipient` IS `the address is one I specified for the purpose`
                `the intended recipient is a company` IS FALSE -- the person in the seat is an individual, so limb (b), "to a company at its registered office", is not in question
                `s 86 the company has its registered office at the address` IS NOTHING -- not read: limb (b) needs a company
                `s 112 the person is a member of the company` IS `coa29 seat the answer of another section from a yes or no` `I am a member of the company`
                `the address is shown in the company's register of members` IS `the address is the one shown for me in the register of members`
                `s 250 the person occupies the position of director` IS `coa29 seat the answer of another section from a yes or no` `I am a director of the company`
                `the address is shown in the register` IS `the address is the one shown for me in the register`
                `a provision of the Companies Acts authorises the document or information to be sent or supplied to the address` IS `a provision of the Companies Acts authorises sending it to the address`
                `the company is unable to obtain an address falling within sub-paragraph (1)` IS `the company could not obtain an address of those kinds`
                `the address is the intended recipient's last address known to the company` IS `the address is my last address known to the company`

@ref sch 5 paras 5 to 7, electronic form
@export My company sent me a document in electronic form (an e-mail, or a disk): was it validly sent to me? (yes, no)
GIVEN `how the company sent it to me` IS A `sch 5 means of sending or supplying` @desc How did the company send it? One of: sch 5 handed to the intended recipient, sch 5 by hand to an address, sch 5 by post, sch 5 by electronic means (e-mail), sch 5 by some other means.
      `I have agreed that the company may send me documents in electronic form` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Have you agreed, generally or for this document, that the company may send it to you in electronic form?
      `I have revoked that agreement` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Have you withdrawn that agreement?
      `the address is one I specified for electronic documents` IS A BOOLEAN @desc If it was sent by electronic means: is the address one you specified for the purpose, generally or for this document?
      `the address is one I specified for the purpose` IS A BOOLEAN @desc If it was handed over or posted as a disk: is the address one you specified for the company to use?
      `I am a member of the company` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are you a member (shareholder) of the company?
      `the address is the one shown for me in the register of members` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the address the one shown for you in the company's register of members?
      `I am a director of the company` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are you a director of the company?
      `the address is the one shown for me in the register` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the address the one shown for you, as a director, in the register?
      `a provision of the Companies Acts authorises sending it to the address` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does a provision of the Companies Acts authorise a document to be sent to that address?
      `the company could not obtain an address of those kinds` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Was the company unable to obtain an address you specified, your address in the register, or an address a provision authorises?
      `the address is my last address known to the company` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the address your last address known to the company?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under schedule 5 paragraph 5, was the electronic document my company sent me validly sent` IS
    `sch 5 para 5 the document or information is validly sent or supplied in electronic form` WITH
        `the form of the document or information` IS `sch 5 electronic form`
        `the means of sending or supplying` IS `how the company sent it to me`
        `the result of sch 5 para 6 the document or information may be sent or supplied by the company in electronic form` IS `the agreement limb`
        `the result of sch 5 para 7(1) the address is one to which it may be sent or supplied by electronic means` IS `the electronic address limb`
        `the result of sch 5 para 7(2) the document or information in electronic form is handed over or sent as the paragraph requires` IS `the hand or post limb`
    WHERE
        `the agreement limb` MEANS
            `sch 5 para 6 the document or information may be sent or supplied by the company in electronic form` WITH
                `the intended recipient is a person who has agreed (generally or specifically) that the document or information may be sent or supplied in electronic form` IS `I have agreed that the company may send me documents in electronic form`
                `the intended recipient has revoked that agreement` IS `I have revoked that agreement`
                `the intended recipient is a company deemed by a provision in the Companies Acts to have so agreed` IS FALSE -- the person in the seat is an individual, so limb (b) (a company deemed to have agreed) is not in question
        `the electronic address limb` MEANS
            `sch 5 para 7(1) the address is one to which it may be sent or supplied by electronic means` WITH
                `the address is specified for the purpose by the intended recipient (generally or specifically)` IS `the address is one I specified for electronic documents`
                `the intended recipient is a company and a provision of the Companies Acts deems the address to have been so specified` IS FALSE -- the person in the seat is an individual
        `the hand or post limb` MEANS
            `sch 5 para 7(2) the document or information in electronic form is handed over or sent as the paragraph requires` WITH
                `the means of sending or supplying` IS `how the company sent it to me`
                `the address is one to which hard copy may be sent or supplied under paragraph 4` IS `the address of paragraph 4`
        `the address of paragraph 4` MEANS
            `sch 5 para 4 the address is one to which hard copy may be sent or supplied` WITH
                `the address is specified for the purpose by the intended recipient` IS `the address is one I specified for the purpose`
                `the intended recipient is a company` IS FALSE -- the person in the seat is an individual, so limb (b) is not in question
                `s 86 the company has its registered office at the address` IS NOTHING -- not read: limb (b) needs a company
                `s 112 the person is a member of the company` IS `coa29 seat the answer of another section from a yes or no` `I am a member of the company`
                `the address is shown in the company's register of members` IS `the address is the one shown for me in the register of members`
                `s 250 the person occupies the position of director` IS `coa29 seat the answer of another section from a yes or no` `I am a director of the company`
                `the address is shown in the register` IS `the address is the one shown for me in the register`
                `a provision of the Companies Acts authorises the document or information to be sent or supplied to the address` IS `a provision of the Companies Acts authorises sending it to the address`
                `the company is unable to obtain an address falling within sub-paragraph (1)` IS `the company could not obtain an address of those kinds`
                `the address is the intended recipient's last address known to the company` IS `the address is my last address known to the company`

@ref sch 5 para 10, deemed agreement of members to use of a website
@export My company asked me to agree that it may send me documents by making them available on a website, and I did not answer: am I taken to have agreed? (yes, no, or null if the 28 days have not yet ended or the paragraph does not apply to me)
GIVEN `the documents are to be sent to me as a member of the company` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are the documents to be sent to you as a member of the company?
      `the documents are to be sent to me as a person nominated by a member under the articles` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Or as a person nominated by a member, in accordance with the articles, to enjoy or exercise the member's rights?
      `the documents are to be sent to me as a person nominated by a member under section 146` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Or as a person nominated by a member under section 146 to enjoy information rights?
      `the members have resolved that the company may use a website` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Have the members resolved that the company may send or supply documents to members by making them available on a website?
      `the articles allow documents to be sent to members by a website` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Do the company's articles contain provision to that effect?
      `the company asked me individually to agree` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did the company ask you individually to agree that it may send you documents (generally, or the documents in question) by means of a website?
      `the date the company's request was sent` IS A DATE @desc On what date was the company's request sent?
      `I have responded` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Have you responded to the request?
      `the date of my response` IS A DATE @desc If you responded: on what date did the company receive your response? (Any date if you did not respond.)
      `today` IS A DATE @desc What is today's date (the day you are asking)?
      `the request said clearly what not responding would mean` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did the request state clearly what the effect of a failure to respond would be?
      `there was an earlier request about the same kind of documents` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Had the company made an earlier request to you for this purpose about the same or a similar class of documents or information?
      `the date of the earlier request` IS A DATE @desc If so, on what date was it sent? (Any date if there was none.)
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under schedule 5 paragraph 10, am I taken to have agreed that the company may send me documents by a website` IS
    `sch 5 para 10 the person is taken to have agreed that the company may send or supply documents or information to him by means of a website` WITH
        `the document or information is to be sent or supplied to the person as a member of the company` IS `the documents are to be sent to me as a member of the company`
        `the document or information is to be sent or supplied to the person as a person nominated by a member in accordance with the company's articles to enjoy or exercise all or any specified rights of the member in relation to the company` IS `the documents are to be sent to me as a person nominated by a member under the articles`
        `the document or information is to be sent or supplied to the person as a person nominated by a member under section 146 to enjoy information rights` IS `the documents are to be sent to me as a person nominated by a member under section 146`
        `the members of the company have resolved that the company may send or supply documents or information to members by making them available on a website` IS `the members have resolved that the company may use a website`
        `the company's articles contain provision that the company may send or supply documents or information to members by making them available on a website` IS `the articles allow documents to be sent to members by a website`
        `the company asked the person individually to agree that it may send or supply documents or information generally, or the documents or information in question, to him by means of a website` IS `the company asked me individually to agree`
        `the date on which the company's request was sent` IS `the date the company's request was sent`
        `the date on which the company received a response` IS IF `I have responded` THEN JUST `the date of my response` ELSE NOTHING
        `the date on which the question is asked` IS `today`
        `the request stated clearly what the effect of a failure to respond would be` IS `the request said clearly what not responding would mean`
        `the date on which a previous request was sent for the purposes of this paragraph in respect of the same or a similar class of documents or information` IS IF `there was an earlier request about the same kind of documents` THEN JUST `the date of the earlier request` ELSE NOTHING

@ref sch 5 para 11, deemed agreement of debenture holders to use of a website
@export My company asked me, as a holder of its debentures, to agree that it may send me documents by a website, and I did not answer: am I taken to have agreed? (yes, no, or null if the 28 days have not yet ended or the paragraph does not apply)
GIVEN `my instrument is a debenture` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is what you hold a debenture of the company?
      `the documents are to be sent to me as holder of the company's debentures` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are the documents to be sent to you as holder of the company's debentures?
      `the debenture holders agreed in accordance with their instruments` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Have the holders of debentures ranking equally with yours agreed, in accordance with the instruments creating the debentures, that the company may use a website?
      `my instrument contains provision for a website` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Or does the instrument creating your debenture contain provision to that effect?
      `the company asked me individually to agree` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did the company ask you individually to agree that it may send you documents by means of a website?
      `the date the company's request was sent` IS A DATE @desc On what date was the company's request sent?
      `I have responded` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Have you responded to the request?
      `the date of my response` IS A DATE @desc If you responded: on what date did the company receive your response? (Any date if you did not respond.)
      `today` IS A DATE @desc What is today's date (the day you are asking)?
      `the request said clearly what not responding would mean` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did the request state clearly what the effect of a failure to respond would be?
      `there was an earlier request about the same kind of documents` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Had the company made an earlier request to you for this purpose about the same or a similar class of documents or information?
      `the date of the earlier request` IS A DATE @desc If so, on what date was it sent? (Any date if there was none.)
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under schedule 5 paragraph 11, am I, as a debenture holder, taken to have agreed that the company may send me documents by a website` IS
    `sch 5 para 11 the debenture holder is taken to have agreed that the company may send or supply documents or information to him by means of a website` WITH
        `s 738 the instrument is a debenture` IS `coa29 seat the answer of another section from a yes or no` `my instrument is a debenture`
        `the document or information is to be sent or supplied to the person as holder of the company's debentures` IS `the documents are to be sent to me as holder of the company's debentures`
        `the relevant debenture holders agree in accordance with the provisions of the instruments creating the debentures that the company may send or supply documents or information to them by making them available on a website` IS `the debenture holders agreed in accordance with their instruments`
        `the instrument creating the debenture in question contains provision that the company may send or supply documents or information to debenture holders by making them available on a website` IS `my instrument contains provision for a website`
        `the company asked the debenture holder individually to agree that it may send or supply documents or information generally, or the documents or information in question, to him by means of a website` IS `the company asked me individually to agree`
        `the date on which the company's request was sent` IS `the date the company's request was sent`
        `the date on which the company received a response` IS IF `I have responded` THEN JUST `the date of my response` ELSE NOTHING
        `the date on which the question is asked` IS `today`
        `the request stated clearly what the effect of a failure to respond would be` IS `the request said clearly what not responding would mean`
        `the date on which a previous request was sent for the purposes of this paragraph in respect of the same or a similar class of documents or information` IS IF `there was an earlier request about the same kind of documents` THEN JUST `the date of the earlier request` ELSE NOTHING

@ref sch 5 para 9, agreement to use of a website
@export May my company send me a document by making it available on a website? (yes or no)
GIVEN `I have agreed that the company may use a website` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Have you agreed, generally or for this document, that the company may send it to you by making it available on a website?
      `I am taken to have agreed under paragraph 10 (as a member)` IS A BOOLEAN @desc As a member: are you taken to have agreed under paragraph 10 (the answer to the paragraph 10 question)?
      `I am taken to have agreed under paragraph 11 (as a debenture holder)` IS A BOOLEAN @desc As a debenture holder: are you taken to have agreed under paragraph 11 (the answer to the paragraph 11 question)?
      `I have revoked that agreement` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Have you revoked that agreement?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under schedule 5 paragraph 9, may my company send me the document by making it available on a website` IS
    `sch 5 para 9 the document or information may be sent or supplied by the company to the person by being made available on a website` WITH
        `the person has agreed (generally or specifically) that the document or information may be sent or supplied to him by being made available on a website` IS `I have agreed that the company may use a website`
        `the result of sch 5 para 10 the person is taken to have agreed that the company may send or supply documents or information to him by means of a website` IS `coa29 seat the answer of another section from a yes or no` `I am taken to have agreed under paragraph 10 (as a member)`
        `the result of sch 5 para 11 the debenture holder is taken to have agreed that the company may send or supply documents or information to him by means of a website` IS `coa29 seat the answer of another section from a yes or no` `I am taken to have agreed under paragraph 11 (as a debenture holder)`
        `the person has revoked that agreement` IS `I have revoked that agreement`

@ref sch 5 para 12(1), form and means of making the document available
@export Did my company make a document available on a website in a form and by a means that it reasonably considered would let me read it and keep a copy? (yes, no; the answer is about the company's reasonable view, not about whether I can in fact)
GIVEN `the company reasonably considered I could read it` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did the company reasonably consider that the form and means would enable you to read the document? (the company's view, not whether you can in fact)
      `the company reasonably considered I could keep a copy` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did the company reasonably consider that the form and means would enable you to retain a copy of it? (the company's view, not whether you can in fact)
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under schedule 5 paragraph 12(1), did my company make the document available in a form and by a means it reasonably considered would let me read it and keep a copy` IS
    `sch 5 para 12(1) the document or information has been made available in a form and by a means the paragraph allows` `the company reasonably considered I could read it` `the company reasonably considered I could keep a copy`

@ref sch 5 para 13(1), notification of availability
@export Did my company notify me of everything paragraph 13 requires when it put a document on a website? (yes, no)
GIVEN `it told me the document is on the website` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did the company notify you of the presence of the document or information on the website?
      `it told me the address of the website` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did it notify you of the address of the website?
      `it told me the place on the website where I can get it` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did it notify you of the place on the website where it may be accessed?
      `it told me how to get at it` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did it notify you how to access the document or information?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under schedule 5 paragraph 13(1), did my company notify me as the paragraph requires` IS
    `sch 5 para 13(1) the company has notified the intended recipient as the paragraph requires` `it told me the document is on the website` `it told me the address of the website` `it told me the place on the website where I can get it` `it told me how to get at it`

@ref sch 5 para 13(2), when the document is taken to be sent
@export On what date is a document on a website taken to have been sent to me? (a date, or null if it has not yet appeared on the website)
GIVEN `the date the company's notification was sent` IS A DATE @desc On what date did the company send you its notification that the document is on the website?
      `the document has appeared on the website` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has the document appeared on the website since that notification was sent?
      `the date it first appeared` IS A DATE @desc If so, on what date did it first appear? (Any date if it has not.)
GIVETH A MAYBE DATE
DECIDE `Under schedule 5 paragraph 13(2), on what date is the document taken to have been sent to me` IS
    `sch 5 para 13(2) the date on which the document or information is taken to be sent` WITH
        `the date on which the notification was sent` IS `the date the company's notification was sent`
        `the date on which the document or information first appears on the website after that notification is sent` IS IF `the document has appeared on the website` THEN JUST `the date it first appeared` ELSE NOTHING

@ref sch 5 para 14(1), the period of availability
@export Until what date must my company keep a document on its website? (a date)
GIVEN `a provision of the Companies Acts specifies a period` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does a provision of the Companies Acts specify a period for which this document must be available on the website?
      `the first day of that period` IS A DATE @desc If so, what is the first day of that period? (Any date if none.)
      `the last day of that period` IS A DATE @desc If so, what is the last day of that period? (Any date if none.)
      `the date the company's notification was sent` IS A DATE @desc On what date did the company send you its notification that the document is on the website?
GIVETH A DATE
DECIDE `Under schedule 5 paragraph 14(1), until what date must the company keep the document on the website` IS
    (`sch 5 para 14(1) the period throughout which the document or information must be available` WITH
        `an applicable provision of the Companies Acts specifies a period` IS `a provision of the Companies Acts specifies a period`
        `the first day of the period so specified` IS `the first day of that period`
        `the last day of the period so specified` IS `the last day of that period`
        `the date on which the notification required under paragraph 13 is sent to the person` IS `the date the company's notification was sent`)'s `sch 5 last day of the period`

@ref sch 5 para 14, keeping the document available throughout the period
@export Has my company kept a document on its website for as long as it had to? (yes or no)
GIVEN `a provision of the Companies Acts specifies a period` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does a provision of the Companies Acts specify a period for which the document must be available on the website?
      `the first day of that period` IS A DATE @desc If so, the first day of that period (any date if none).
      `the last day of that period` IS A DATE @desc If so, the last day of that period (any date if none).
      `the date the company's notification was sent` IS A DATE @desc On what date did the company send you its notification?
      `the first day on which it was on the website` IS A DATE @desc On what date did the document first appear on the website?
      `the last day on which it was on the website` IS A DATE @desc On what date was it last on the website?
      `it was on the website on every day in between` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Was it on the website on every day from the first to the last?
      `the failure was due to circumstances the company could not reasonably prevent` IS A BOOLEAN @desc If it was not there throughout: was the failure wholly attributable to circumstances it would not be reasonable to have expected the company to prevent or avoid?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under schedule 5 paragraph 14, has my company kept the document on the website for as long as it had to` IS
    `sch 5 para 14 the company has complied with the duty to keep the document or information available` WITH
        `the result of sch 5 para 14(1) the document or information was available on the website throughout the period` IS `throughout`
        `the result of sch 5 para 14(2) the failure to make the document or information available throughout the period is disregarded` IS `disregarded`
    WHERE
        period MEANS
            `sch 5 para 14(1) the period throughout which the document or information must be available` WITH
                `an applicable provision of the Companies Acts specifies a period` IS `a provision of the Companies Acts specifies a period`
                `the first day of the period so specified` IS `the first day of that period`
                `the last day of the period so specified` IS `the last day of that period`
                `the date on which the notification required under paragraph 13 is sent to the person` IS `the date the company's notification was sent`
        throughout MEANS
            `sch 5 para 14(1) the document or information was available on the website throughout the period` WITH
                `the first day of the period` IS period's `sch 5 first day of the period`
                `the last day of the period` IS period's `sch 5 last day of the period`
                `the first day on which it was available on the website` IS `the first day on which it was on the website`
                `the last day on which it was available on the website` IS `the last day on which it was on the website`
                `it was available on every day from the first to the last` IS `it was on the website on every day in between`
        disregarded MEANS
            `sch 5 para 14(2) the failure to make the document or information available throughout the period is disregarded` WITH
                `it was made available on the website for part of the period` IS (`the first day on which it was on the website` AT MOST period's `sch 5 last day of the period` AND `the last day on which it was on the website` AT LEAST period's `sch 5 first day of the period`)
                `the failure to make it available throughout the period is wholly attributable to circumstances that it would not be reasonable to have expected the company to prevent or avoid` IS `the failure was due to circumstances the company could not reasonably prevent`

@ref sch 5 para 8, validly sent by means of a website
@export My company put a document on a website instead of sending it: was it validly sent to me? (yes or no)
GIVEN `the answer to the paragraph 9 question is yes` IS A BOOLEAN @desc May the company send it to you by making it available on a website, because you have agreed or are taken to have agreed and have not revoked that agreement (the answer to the paragraph 9 question)?
      `the answer to the paragraph 12(1) question is yes` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did the company make it available in a form and by a means it reasonably considered would let you read it and keep a copy (the answer to the paragraph 12(1) question)?
      `the answer to the paragraph 13(1) question is yes` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did the company notify you as paragraph 13 requires (the paragraph 13(1) question)?
      `the answer to the paragraph 14 question is yes` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did the company keep it on the website for as long as it had to (the paragraph 14 question)?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under schedule 5 paragraph 8, was the document the company made available on a website validly sent to me` IS
    `sch 5 para 8 the document or information is validly sent or supplied by being made available on a website` WITH
        `the result of sch 5 para 9 the document or information may be sent or supplied by the company to the person by being made available on a website` IS `coa29 seat the answer of another section from a yes or no` `the answer to the paragraph 9 question is yes`
        `the result of sch 5 para 12(1) the document or information has been made available in a form and by a means the paragraph allows` IS `coa29 seat the answer of another section from a yes or no` `the answer to the paragraph 12(1) question is yes`
        `the result of sch 5 para 13(1) the company has notified the intended recipient as the paragraph requires` IS `coa29 seat the answer of another section from a yes or no` `the answer to the paragraph 13(1) question is yes`
        `the result of sch 5 para 14 the company has complied with the duty to keep the document or information available` IS `coa29 seat the answer of another section from a yes or no` `the answer to the paragraph 14 question is yes`

@ref sch 5 para 15, other agreed forms of communication
@export My company sent me something in a form that is not paper, electronic or a website: was it validly sent to me? (yes, no)
GIVEN `I have agreed that form or manner` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Have you agreed to receive documents or information from the company in that form or manner?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under schedule 5 paragraph 15, was what my company sent me in another agreed form validly sent` IS
    `sch 5 para 15 the document or information is validly sent or supplied in another agreed form or manner` `sch 5 none of those forms` `I have agreed that form or manner`

@ref sch 5 para 16, joint holders of shares or debentures
@export I hold shares or debentures jointly with others: has the agreement or specification been given by all of us, as the company needs? (yes, no, or null if we are not joint holders or the articles provide otherwise)
GIVEN `we are joint holders of shares or debentures` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Do you hold the shares or debentures jointly with others?
      `the number of joint holders` IS A NUMBER @desc How many joint holders are there (including you)?
      `the number of us who agreed or specified it` IS A NUMBER @desc How many of the joint holders have agreed or specified the matter (for example an address or agreement to electronic communications)?
      `the articles provide otherwise` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Do the company's articles contain provision to a different effect?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under schedule 5 paragraph 16(2), has the matter been agreed or specified by all the joint holders` IS
    `sch 5 para 16(2) the matter is agreed or specified by the joint holders as the paragraph requires` `we are joint holders of shares or debentures` `the number of joint holders` `the number of us who agreed or specified it` `the articles provide otherwise`

@ref sch 5 para 16(3), to which joint holder the document may be sent
@export I hold shares or debentures jointly with others: may the company send a document to each of us, or only to the holder named first? (yes, or null if the paragraph does not cover how it was sent)
GIVEN `we are joint holders of shares or debentures` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Do you hold the shares or debentures jointly with others?
      `it was sent to each of us` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Was the document sent to each of the joint holders?
      `it was sent to the holder named first in the register` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Was it sent to the holder whose name appears first in the register of members (or the register of debenture holders)?
      `the articles provide otherwise` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Do the company's articles contain provision to a different effect?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under schedule 5 paragraph 16(3), may the company send the document to each joint holder or to the first-named holder` IS
    `sch 5 para 16(3) the document or information may be sent or supplied to the joint holder` `we are joint holders of shares or debentures` `it was sent to each of us` `it was sent to the holder named first in the register` `the articles provide otherwise`

@ref sch 5 para 17(2), a holder of shares who has died or become bankrupt
@export The holder of shares has died or become bankrupt: may the company send documents to the people claiming the shares, by name or title, at the address in the United Kingdom they gave? (yes, or null where the paragraph does not cover how it was sent)
GIVEN `the holder has died or become bankrupt` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has the holder of the shares died or become bankrupt?
      `it is sent to those claiming by name or by title` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it sent to the persons claiming to be entitled to the shares by name, or by the title of representatives of the deceased or trustee of the bankrupt, or by any like description?
      `it is sent at the address they supplied in the United Kingdom` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it sent at the address in the United Kingdom they supplied for the purpose?
      `the articles provide otherwise` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Do the company's articles contain provision to a different effect?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under schedule 5 paragraph 17(2), may the company send the document to the persons claiming the shares` IS
    `sch 5 para 17(2) the document or information may be sent or supplied to the persons claiming to be entitled` `the holder has died or become bankrupt` `it is sent to those claiming by name or by title` `it is sent at the address they supplied in the United Kingdom` `the articles provide otherwise`

@ref sch 5 para 17(3), until an address has been supplied
@export The holder of shares has died or become bankrupt and the people claiming the shares have not yet given an address: may the company send documents in the way it could before? (yes, no once an address has been supplied, or null where the paragraph does not cover how it was sent)
GIVEN `the holder has died or become bankrupt` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has the holder of the shares died or become bankrupt?
      `those claiming have supplied an address in the United Kingdom` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Have the persons claiming to be entitled supplied an address in the United Kingdom?
      `it is sent in a manner open before the death or bankruptcy` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it sent in a manner in which it might have been sent if the death or bankruptcy had not occurred?
      `the articles provide otherwise` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Do the company's articles contain provision to a different effect?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under schedule 5 paragraph 17(3), may the company send the document in the way it could have before the death or bankruptcy` IS
    `sch 5 para 17(3) the document or information may be sent or supplied in the manner that applied before the death or bankruptcy` `the holder has died or become bankrupt` `those claiming have supplied an address in the United Kingdom` `it is sent in a manner open before the death or bankruptcy` `the articles provide otherwise`

§§ `Schedule 6 -- when another company is the holding company of my company (rights that count)`

-- A group that only arises where you ask whether another company is a "subsidiary" or "holding company" relation to yours (section 1159, not asked
-- here: it belongs to another part). Schedule 6 says which rights count towards that and whose they are treated as being.

@ref sch 6 para 2, voting rights in a company
@export Are the rights I am asking about "voting rights in the company" for the purposes of section 1159? (yes or no)
GIVEN `the company has a share capital` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does my company have a share capital?
      `the rights are conferred on shareholders in respect of their shares` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are the rights conferred on shareholders in respect of their shares?
      `the rights are conferred on members` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are the rights conferred on members (in a company with no share capital)?
      `the rights are to vote at general meetings of the company` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are they rights to vote at general meetings of the company?
      `the rights are to vote on all, or substantially all, matters` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Do they carry a vote on all, or substantially all, matters?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under schedule 6 paragraph 2, are the rights voting rights in my company` IS
    `sch 6 para 2 the rights are voting rights in the company` `the company has a share capital` `the rights are conferred on shareholders in respect of their shares` `the rights are conferred on members` `the rights are to vote at general meetings of the company` `the rights are to vote on all, or substantially all, matters`

@ref sch 6 para 3(1), a majority of the board of directors
@export Does the other company have the right to appoint or remove directors holding a majority of the votes at board meetings of mine? (yes or no)
GIVEN `the votes held by the directors it can appoint or remove` IS A NUMBER @desc How many votes at board meetings are held by the directors that the other company can appoint or remove?
      `all the votes at board meetings` IS A NUMBER @desc How many votes are there in all at meetings of the board?
      `the votes are on all, or substantially all, matters` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are the votes at board meetings on all, or substantially all, matters?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under schedule 6 paragraph 3(1), does the other company have the right to appoint or remove a majority of my board` IS
    `sch 6 para 3(1) the right is a right to appoint or remove a majority of the board of directors` `the votes held by the directors it can appoint or remove` `all the votes at board meetings` `the votes are on all, or substantially all, matters`

@ref sch 6 para 3(3), a right needing another person's consent
@export The other company's right to appoint or remove a director needs someone else's consent: is the right counted? (yes, no, or null if it does not need consent)
GIVEN `the right needs another person's consent or concurrence` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the right exercisable only with the consent or concurrence of another person?
      `no other person has a right to appoint or remove for that directorship` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does no other person have a right to appoint or, as the case may be, remove in relation to that directorship?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under schedule 6 paragraph 3(3), is a right that needs another person's consent counted` IS
    `sch 6 para 3(3) the right is taken into account` `the right needs another person's consent or concurrence` `no other person has a right to appoint or remove for that directorship`

@ref sch 6 paras 4 to 10, a block of rights seen from the other company
@export Counting the rights as Schedule 6 says, is this block of rights treated as held by the other company? (yes, no, or null where the Schedule does not decide)
GIVEN `who holds the rights` IS A `sch 6 who holds the rights` @desc Who holds the block of rights? One of: sch 6 the other company itself, sch 6 a subsidiary company of the other company, sch 6 someone else.
      `how the rights are held` IS A `sch 6 how the rights are held` @desc In what capacity are they held? One of: sch 6 held beneficially, sch 6 held in a fiduciary capacity, sch 6 held as nominee for the other company, sch 6 held as nominee for someone else, sch 6 held by way of security provided by the other company, sch 6 held by way of security provided by someone else.
      `the rights can be exercised only in certain circumstances` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Can the rights be exercised only in certain circumstances?
      `those circumstances have arisen and continue` IS A BOOLEAN @desc If so, have the circumstances arisen and do they continue?
      `those circumstances are within the control of the person having the rights` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Or are the circumstances within the control of the person who has the rights?
      `the rights are normally exercisable but temporarily cannot be` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are the rights normally exercisable but temporarily incapable of exercise?
      `the shares are held by way of security` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are the shares held by way of security?
      `exercisable only on the provider's instructions (apart from preserving or realising the security)` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Apart from the right to exercise them to preserve the value of the security or to realise it, are the rights exercisable only in accordance with the instructions of the person who provided the security?
      `exercisable only on the instructions of a company in the provider's group` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Or only in accordance with the instructions of a subsidiary or holding company of the provider, or a subsidiary of a holding company of the provider?
      `held in connection with loans as part of normal business activities` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are the shares held in connection with the granting of loans as part of normal business activities?
      `exercisable only in the provider's interests (apart from preserving or realising the security)` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Apart from that right, are the rights exercisable only in the interests of the person who provided the security?
      `exercisable only in the interests of a company in the provider's group` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Or only in the interests of a subsidiary or holding company of the provider, or a subsidiary of a holding company of the provider?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under schedule 6 paragraphs 4 to 10, is this block of rights treated as held by the other company` IS
    `sch 6 paras 4 to 10 the rights are treated as held by the other company` WITH
        `who holds the rights` IS `who holds the rights`
        `how the rights are held` IS `how the rights are held`
        `the result of sch 6 para 4` IS `the circumstances answer`
        `the result of sch 6 para 7` IS `the security answer`
    WHERE
        `the circumstances answer` MEANS
            `sch 6 para 4 the rights are taken into account` WITH
                `the rights are exercisable only in certain circumstances` IS `the rights can be exercised only in certain circumstances`
                `the circumstances have arisen and continue to obtain` IS `those circumstances have arisen and continue`
                `the circumstances are within the control of the person having the rights` IS `those circumstances are within the control of the person having the rights`
                `the rights are normally exercisable but are temporarily incapable of exercise` IS `the rights are normally exercisable but temporarily cannot be`
        `the security answer` MEANS
            `sch 6 para 7 the rights are treated as held by the person providing the security` WITH
                `the shares are held by way of security` IS `the shares are held by way of security`
                `apart from the right to exercise them for the purpose of preserving the value of the security, or of realising it, the rights are exercisable only in accordance with the instructions of the person providing the security` IS `exercisable only on the provider's instructions (apart from preserving or realising the security)`
                `apart from that right, the rights are exercisable only in accordance with the instructions of a subsidiary or holding company of the person providing the security, or of a subsidiary of a holding company of that person` IS `exercisable only on the instructions of a company in the provider's group`
                `the shares are held in connection with the granting of loans as part of normal business activities` IS `held in connection with loans as part of normal business activities`
                `apart from that right, the rights are exercisable only in the interests of the person providing the security` IS `exercisable only in the provider's interests (apart from preserving or realising the security)`
                `apart from that right, the rights are exercisable only in the interests of a subsidiary or holding company of the person providing the security, or of a subsidiary of a holding company of that person` IS `exercisable only in the interests of a company in the provider's group`

@ref sch 6 para 9, voting rights reduced by the company's own rights
@export How many voting rights are there in my company once those it holds in itself are taken off? (a number, or null if it cannot hold more than there are)
GIVEN `the voting rights in the company` IS A NUMBER @desc How many voting rights are there in my company in all?
      `the rights held by the company itself` IS A NUMBER @desc How many of those does the company itself hold?
GIVETH A MAYBE NUMBER
DECIDE `Under schedule 6 paragraph 9, how many voting rights are there in my company after the reduction` IS
    `sch 6 para 9 the voting rights in the company after the reduction` `the voting rights in the company` `the rights held by the company itself`

§§ `Schedule 7 -- when another undertaking is a parent undertaking of mine (rights that count)`

-- A group that only arises where you ask whether another undertaking is a "parent undertaking" of an undertaking you run or own (section 1162,
-- not asked here: it belongs to another part). Schedule 7 says which rights count towards that and whose they are treated as being.

@ref sch 7 para 2(1), voting rights in an undertaking
@export Are the rights I am asking about "voting rights in the undertaking" for the purposes of section 1162? (yes or no)
GIVEN `the undertaking has a share capital` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does the undertaking have a share capital?
      `the rights are conferred on shareholders in respect of their shares` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are the rights conferred on shareholders in respect of their shares?
      `the rights are conferred on members` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are the rights conferred on members (in an undertaking with no share capital)?
      `the rights are to vote at general meetings of the undertaking` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are they rights to vote at general meetings of the undertaking?
      `the rights are to vote on all, or substantially all, matters` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Do they carry a vote on all, or substantially all, matters?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under schedule 7 paragraph 2(1), are the rights voting rights in the undertaking` IS
    `sch 7 para 2(1) the rights are voting rights in the undertaking` `the undertaking has a share capital` `the rights are conferred on shareholders in respect of their shares` `the rights are conferred on members` `the rights are to vote at general meetings of the undertaking` `the rights are to vote on all, or substantially all, matters`

@ref sch 7 para 2(2), an undertaking with no general meetings
@export The undertaking has no general meetings that decide matters by votes: does the other undertaking "hold a majority of the voting rights" because of its rights under the constitution? (yes, no, or null if the undertaking does have such meetings)
GIVEN `the undertaking has general meetings that decide matters by votes` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does the undertaking have general meetings at which matters are decided by the exercise of voting rights?
      `the other undertaking has the right under the constitution to direct the overall policy` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does the other undertaking have the right, under the undertaking's constitution, to direct its overall policy?
      `the other undertaking has the right under the constitution to alter the constitution` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does the other undertaking have the right, under the undertaking's constitution, to alter the terms of the constitution?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under schedule 7 paragraph 2(2), does the other undertaking hold a majority of the voting rights in an undertaking with no general meetings` IS
    `sch 7 para 2(2) the undertaking holds a majority of the voting rights in the other undertaking` `the undertaking has general meetings that decide matters by votes` `the other undertaking has the right under the constitution to direct the overall policy` `the other undertaking has the right under the constitution to alter the constitution`

@ref sch 7 para 4(1), the bar on regarding an undertaking as having a dominant influence
@export Is the other undertaking barred from being regarded as having a right to exercise a dominant influence over mine? (yes where the bar applies, no where it does not, because it has a right to give directions its directors must obey)
GIVEN `it has a right to give directions on operating and financial policies` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does the other undertaking have a right to give directions with respect to the operating and financial policies of my undertaking?
      `my directors are obliged to comply with them whether or not they benefit my undertaking` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are my undertaking's directors obliged to comply with those directions whether or not they are for the benefit of my undertaking?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under schedule 7 paragraph 4(1), is the other undertaking barred from being regarded as having a dominant influence over mine` IS
    `sch 7 para 4(1) the undertaking cannot be regarded as having the right to exercise a dominant influence` `it has a right to give directions on operating and financial policies` `my directors are obliged to comply with them whether or not they benefit my undertaking`

@ref sch 7 para 4(2), a control contract
@export Is this contract a "control contract"? (yes or no)
GIVEN `the contract is in writing` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the contract in writing?
      `the contract gives the right to give directions on operating and financial policies` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does it confer a right to give directions with respect to operating and financial policies that the directors must obey whether or not they are for the undertaking's benefit?
      `my articles authorise a contract of that kind` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it a kind of contract authorised by the articles of the undertaking over which the right is exercisable?
      `the law that governs my undertaking permits it` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it permitted by the law under which that undertaking is established?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under schedule 7 paragraph 4(2), is the contract a control contract` IS
    `sch 7 para 4(2) the contract is a control contract` `the contract is in writing` `the contract gives the right to give directions on operating and financial policies` `my articles authorise a contract of that kind` `the law that governs my undertaking permits it`

@ref sch 7 paras 5 to 11, a block of rights seen from the parent undertaking
@export Counting the rights as Schedule 7 says, is this block of rights treated as held by the other undertaking? (yes, no, or null where the Schedule does not decide)
GIVEN `who holds the rights` IS A `sch 7 who holds the rights` @desc Who holds the block of rights? One of: sch 7 the parent undertaking itself, sch 7 a subsidiary undertaking of the parent undertaking, sch 7 someone else.
      `how the rights are held` IS A `sch 7 how the rights are held` @desc In what capacity are they held? One of: sch 7 held beneficially, sch 7 held in a fiduciary capacity, sch 7 held as nominee for the parent undertaking, sch 7 held as nominee for someone else, sch 7 held by way of security provided by the parent undertaking, sch 7 held by way of security provided by someone else.
      `the rights can be exercised only in certain circumstances` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Can the rights be exercised only in certain circumstances?
      `those circumstances have arisen and continue` IS A BOOLEAN @desc If so, have the circumstances arisen and do they continue?
      `those circumstances are within the control of the person having the rights` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Or are the circumstances within the control of the person who has the rights?
      `the rights are normally exercisable but temporarily cannot be` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are the rights normally exercisable but temporarily incapable of exercise?
      `the shares are held by way of security` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are the shares held by way of security?
      `exercisable only on the provider's instructions (apart from preserving or realising the security)` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Apart from the right to exercise them to preserve the value of the security or to realise it, are the rights exercisable only in accordance with the instructions of the person who provided the security?
      `exercisable only on the instructions of a group undertaking of the provider` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Or only in accordance with the instructions of a group undertaking of the provider?
      `held in connection with loans as part of normal business activities` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are the shares held in connection with the granting of loans as part of normal business activities?
      `exercisable only in the provider's interests (apart from preserving or realising the security)` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Apart from that right, are the rights exercisable only in the interests of the person who provided the security?
      `exercisable only in the interests of a group undertaking of the provider` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Or only in the interests of a group undertaking of the provider?
      `the instructing undertaking is a group undertaking of the provider` IS A BOOLEAN @desc If you relied on a group undertaking above: is it a "group undertaking" of the provider within section 1161(5)?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under schedule 7 paragraphs 5 to 11, is this block of rights treated as held by the other undertaking` IS
    `sch 7 paras 5 to 11 the rights are treated as held by the parent undertaking` WITH
        `who holds the rights` IS `who holds the rights`
        `how the rights are held` IS `how the rights are held`
        `the result of sch 7 para 5` IS `the circumstances answer`
        `the result of sch 7 para 8` IS `the security answer`
    WHERE
        `the circumstances answer` MEANS
            `sch 7 para 5 the rights are taken into account` WITH
                `the rights are exercisable only in certain circumstances` IS `the rights can be exercised only in certain circumstances`
                `the circumstances have arisen and continue to obtain` IS `those circumstances have arisen and continue`
                `the circumstances are within the control of the person having the rights` IS `those circumstances are within the control of the person having the rights`
                `the rights are normally exercisable but are temporarily incapable of exercise` IS `the rights are normally exercisable but temporarily cannot be`
        `the security answer` MEANS
            `sch 7 para 8 the rights are treated as held by the person providing the security` WITH
                `the shares are held by way of security` IS `the shares are held by way of security`
                `apart from the right to exercise them for the purpose of preserving the value of the security, or of realising it, the rights are exercisable only in accordance with the instructions of the person providing the security` IS `exercisable only on the provider's instructions (apart from preserving or realising the security)`
                `apart from that right, the rights are exercisable only in accordance with the instructions of a group undertaking of the person providing the security` IS `exercisable only on the instructions of a group undertaking of the provider`
                `the shares are held in connection with the granting of loans as part of normal business activities` IS `held in connection with loans as part of normal business activities`
                `apart from that right, the rights are exercisable only in the interests of the person providing the security` IS `exercisable only in the provider's interests (apart from preserving or realising the security)`
                `apart from that right, the rights are exercisable only in the interests of a group undertaking of the person providing the security` IS `exercisable only in the interests of a group undertaking of the provider`
                `s 1161(5) the undertaking is a group undertaking in relation to the other undertaking` IS `coa29 seat the answer of another section from a yes or no` `the instructing undertaking is a group undertaking of the provider`

@ref sch 7 para 10, voting rights reduced by the undertaking's own rights
@export How many voting rights are there in the undertaking once those it holds in itself are taken off? (a number, or null if it cannot hold more than there are)
GIVEN `the voting rights in the undertaking` IS A NUMBER @desc How many voting rights are there in the undertaking in all?
      `the rights held by the undertaking itself` IS A NUMBER @desc How many of those does the undertaking itself hold?
GIVETH A MAYBE NUMBER
DECIDE `Under schedule 7 paragraph 10, how many voting rights are there in the undertaking after the reduction` IS
    `sch 7 para 10 the voting rights in the undertaking after the reduction` `the voting rights in the undertaking` `the rights held by the undertaking itself`

§§ `Schedule 8 -- where the Act defines an expression`

@ref sch 8, index of defined expressions
@export Where does the Companies Act 2006 define or explain an expression? (the provisions the Act's own index names, with the part of the Act each covers; null if the index does not list it)
GIVEN expression IS A STRING @desc The expression as the Act's index prints it, for example director, shadow director, subsidiary undertaking, working day, quoted company.
GIVETH A MAYBE (LIST OF STRING)
DECIDE `Under schedule 8, which provisions define or explain the expression` IS
    `sch 8 the provisions that define or explain the expression` expression

-- ====================================================================================================
-- seat questions from part coa30 (merged by the lead on 2026-11-12; unchanged text follows)
-- ====================================================================================================
-- coa30-seat.l4: THE SEAT LAYER for Schedules 10 to 16 of the Companies Act 2006 (lines 20017-20928 of ukpga-2006-46.txt).
--
-- SEAT. An individual who is, or is about to become, a director, a company secretary or a member (shareholder) of a company
-- registered under the Act, or who deals with one, asking on facts they can state what the Act requires or lets them do, what rights
-- they have against the company or its directors, what they must disclose, file, approve or vote on and by when, and what
-- follows if it is not done (assumed, not ruled: the Act is addressed to companies, so the individual is whoever stands
-- in a company's management or ownership).
-- In these Schedules the people who deal with the company are: (1) its statutory auditor or a would-be auditor (and a
-- firm of auditors, a key audit partner, a third country auditor), whose appointment, independence, inspection and sanction
-- the supervisory bodies' rules govern; (2) a person who holds, or wants, a recognised professional qualification; (3) a member
-- of the body to which the Secretary of State delegates functions, or someone affected by its instruments; (4) a person
-- who holds information obtained under Part 42 and wants to know whom it may be given to; and (5) a director who asks
-- whether his company is a public interest entity or whether its former auditor may join the board. (Assumed, not ruled:
-- these are the individuals of the "who deals with one" limb of the seat for this range; the Schedules about the supervisory bodies
-- and the Secretary of State address those bodies and officials, and there is never a seat for an official.)
-- Schedules 14, 15 and 16 amend and repeal other Acts and have no question.
--
-- Every question takes plain inputs, one per fact the person can state, each with an @desc worded as that person would be asked, and
-- calls the layer-1 rules; no rule is restated. A fact that is a judgment of the Secretary of State ("appears to him") is asked as a
-- plain yes or no. A choice among the paragraphs of a list (Schedule 11A) is a choice from the list's own type.
-- ANSWERS. JUST TRUE is a yes the Act gives; JUST FALSE is a no the Act gives in its own words; NOTHING is "not covered": the Act does
-- not decide on these facts (see NOTES.md, "Reading a result: FALSE and NOTHING"). A caller must never turn NOTHING into FALSE.
-- Question names begin "Under schedule N paragraph M," so that no two parts' questions can share a name.


§ `Schedule 10 -- Recognised supervisory bodies: the people they audit and the auditors they supervise`

§§ `Part 1 -- Revocation of recognition (only if you have been told that the Secretary of State proposes to revoke the recognition of a supervisory body or has done so)`

-- sch 10 para 3(5), sch 10 para 3(6)
@export Under schedule 10 paragraph 3(5), may I still make representations to the Secretary of State on the proposed revocation of the recognition of a supervisory body?
GIVEN `I am a member of the supervisory body` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are you a member of the supervisory body whose recognition the Secretary of State proposes to revoke?
      `the Secretary of State considers that I am affected` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does it appear to the Secretary of State that you are affected by the proposed revocation?
      `the date the notice of the proposed revocation was served on me or published` IS A DATE @desc On what date was the notice of the proposed revocation served on you, or published?
      `the day I want to make representations` IS A DATE @desc On what day do you want to make your representations?
      `the Secretary of State has allowed a longer period` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has the Secretary of State allowed a period longer than three months for representations?
      `the last day of that longer period` IS A DATE @desc If so, what is the last day of the longer period? (Any date if there is none.)
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under schedule 10 paragraph 3(5), may I still make representations to the Secretary of State on the proposed revocation of the recognition of a supervisory body` IS
    `sch 10 para 3(5) the person may make written and oral representations`
        (`sch 10 para 3(6) the person is within this sub-paragraph` FALSE `I am a member of the supervisory body` `the Secretary of State considers that I am affected`)
        `the date the notice of the proposed revocation was served on me or published`
        `the day I want to make representations`
        (IF `the Secretary of State has allowed a longer period` THEN JUST `the last day of that longer period` ELSE NOTHING)

-- sch 10 para 3(2)
@export Under schedule 10 paragraph 3(2), does the order revoking the recognition of a supervisory body state a valid date for the revocation to take effect?
GIVEN `the revocation order states the date on which it takes effect` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does the order revoking the recognition state the date on which it takes effect?
      `the date the revocation order was made` IS A DATE @desc On what date was the revocation order made?
      `the date stated for the revocation to take effect` IS A DATE @desc What date does the order state for the revocation to take effect?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under schedule 10 paragraph 3(2), does the order revoking the recognition of a supervisory body state a valid date for the revocation to take effect` IS
    `sch 10 para 3(2) the revocation order states a valid date of effect` `the revocation order states the date on which it takes effect` `the date the revocation order was made` `the date stated for the revocation to take effect`

§§ `Part 2 -- Who may be appointed as a statutory auditor, independence, and inspection of auditors (for auditors and for the directors of audited companies)`

-- sch 10 para 6(1)
@export Under schedule 10 paragraph 6(1), do the rules that a recognised supervisory body must have bar me from appointment as a statutory auditor when I am an individual?
GIVEN `I am a third country auditor` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are you a third country auditor?
      `I hold an appropriate qualification` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Do you hold an appropriate qualification?
      `I was authorised on or before 5 April 2008 and fulfilled the requirements imposed under regulation 6 of the 2005 Regulations` IS A BOOLEAN @desc If you are a third country auditor: were you authorised on or before 5 April 2008 to practise as a company auditor under the 2005 Regulations, and have you fulfilled any requirements imposed under regulation 6 of them?
      `I meet the requirements of paragraph 6(1A)` IS A BOOLEAN @desc If you are a third country auditor: do you meet the requirements of paragraph 6(1A) (see the next question)?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under schedule 10 paragraph 6(1), do the rules that a recognised supervisory body must have bar me from appointment as a statutory auditor when I am an individual` IS
    `sch 10 para 6(1) the person is not eligible for appointment as a statutory auditor under the rule the body must have`
        TRUE `I am a third country auditor` `I hold an appropriate qualification`
        `I was authorised on or before 5 April 2008 and fulfilled the requirements imposed under regulation 6 of the 2005 Regulations`
        (JUST `I meet the requirements of paragraph 6(1A)`) FALSE NOTHING

-- sch 10 para 6(1), sch 10 para 7(3)
@export Under schedule 10 paragraph 6(1), do the rules that a recognised supervisory body must have bar my firm from appointment as a statutory auditor?
GIVEN `each individual responsible for statutory audit work on behalf of my firm is eligible for appointment as a statutory auditor` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is each individual responsible for statutory audit work on behalf of your firm eligible for appointment as a statutory auditor?
      `a majority of the members of my firm are qualified persons` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are a majority of the members of your firm qualified persons (see paragraph 7(2) and (4))?
      `my firm's affairs are managed by a board of directors, committee or other management body` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are the affairs of your firm managed by a board of directors, committee or other management body?
      `a majority of that management body are qualified persons` IS A BOOLEAN @desc If so, are a majority of that body qualified persons?
      `that management body consists of two persons only` IS A BOOLEAN @desc If so, does that body consist of two persons only?
      `at least one of those two is a qualified person` IS A BOOLEAN @desc If it consists of two persons only, is at least one of them a qualified person?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under schedule 10 paragraph 6(1), do the rules that a recognised supervisory body must have bar my firm from appointment as a statutory auditor` IS
    `sch 10 para 6(1) the person is not eligible for appointment as a statutory auditor under the rule the body must have`
        FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE NOTHING
        `each individual responsible for statutory audit work on behalf of my firm is eligible for appointment as a statutory auditor`
        (`sch 10 para 7(3) the firm is controlled by qualified persons` `a majority of the members of my firm are qualified persons` `my firm's affairs are managed by a board of directors, committee or other management body` `a majority of that management body are qualified persons` `that management body consists of two persons only` `at least one of those two is a qualified person`)

-- sch 10 para 7(4)
@export Under schedule 10 paragraph 7(4), do the qualified members of my firm hold a majority of the members of the firm?
GIVEN `matters are decided under the constitution of my firm by the exercise of voting rights` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does your firm's constitution decide matters by the exercise of voting rights?
      `the fraction of the rights to vote held by the qualified members` IS A NUMBER @desc What fraction (for example 0.6 for 60 per cent) of the rights to vote on all, or substantially all, matters do the qualified members hold, after attribution under Schedule 7 paragraphs 5 to 11?
      `the qualified members can direct the overall policy of my firm or alter its constitution` IS A BOOLEAN @desc If votes do not decide matters: can the qualified members, under the constitution, direct the firm's overall policy or alter its constitution?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under schedule 10 paragraph 7(4), do the qualified members of my firm hold a majority of the members of the firm` IS
    `sch 10 para 7(4) the qualified members are a majority of the members of the firm` `matters are decided under the constitution of my firm by the exercise of voting rights` `the fraction of the rights to vote held by the qualified members` `the qualified members can direct the overall policy of my firm or alter its constitution`

-- sch 10 para 6(1A)
@export Under schedule 10 paragraph 6(1A), do I meet the requirements for a third country auditor to be eligible for appointment as a statutory auditor?
GIVEN `I hold a professional qualification covering all the subjects covered by a recognised professional qualification and essential for the profession of statutory auditor` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Do you hold a professional qualification which covers all the subjects covered by a recognised professional qualification and essential for the profession of statutory auditor?
      `I am an EEA auditor` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are you an EEA auditor (an individual or firm approved under the Audit Directive by an EEA competent authority)?
      `on or before IP completion day I held a professional qualification that does not cover all those subjects` IS A BOOLEAN @desc On or before IP completion day, did you hold a professional qualification which does not cover all those subjects?
      `on or before IP completion day I had been approved by the body or was seeking approval` IS A BOOLEAN @desc On or before IP completion day, had you been approved by the supervisory body, or were you in the process of seeking its approval?
      `I have met the requirement of paragraph 6(1B) that the rules of the body specify` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Have you met whichever requirement of paragraph 6(1B) (aptitude test, adaptation period, or either at your choice) the body's rules specify?
      `I am a specified state auditor` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are you an individual eligible to audit the accounts of bodies corporate formed under the law of a specified state, in accordance with that state's law?
      `I hold professional qualifications obtained in a specified state comparable to an appropriate qualification` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Do you hold professional qualifications obtained in a specified state that are comparable to an appropriate qualification?
      `the body has imposed an aptitude test or adaptation period on me under the 2023 Regulations` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has the body imposed on you a requirement to take an aptitude test or complete an adaptation period (or both) under Part 2 of the 2023 Regulations?
      `I have met that requirement` IS A BOOLEAN @desc If so, have you met it?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under schedule 10 paragraph 6(1A), do I meet the requirements for a third country auditor to be eligible for appointment as a statutory auditor` IS
    `sch 10 para 6(1A) the requirements of this sub-paragraph are met` `I hold a professional qualification covering all the subjects covered by a recognised professional qualification and essential for the profession of statutory auditor` `I am an EEA auditor` `on or before IP completion day I held a professional qualification that does not cover all those subjects` `on or before IP completion day I had been approved by the body or was seeking approval` `I have met the requirement of paragraph 6(1B) that the rules of the body specify` `I am a specified state auditor` `I hold professional qualifications obtained in a specified state comparable to an appropriate qualification` `the body has imposed an aptitude test or adaptation period on me under the 2023 Regulations` `I have met that requirement`

-- sch 10 para 6(2)
@export Under schedule 10 paragraph 6(2), may the aptitude test that I am required to take test my knowledge of this matter?
GIVEN `the matter is a subject covered by a recognised professional qualification` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the matter a subject covered by a recognised professional qualification?
      `the matter is a subject not covered by the professional qualification I already hold` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it a subject that is not covered by the professional qualification you already hold?
      `knowledge of the matter is essential for the pursuit of the profession of statutory auditor` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is knowledge of it essential for the pursuit of the profession of statutory auditor?
      `the matter is a rule of professional conduct` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the matter a rule of professional conduct?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under schedule 10 paragraph 6(2), may the aptitude test that I am required to take test my knowledge of this matter` IS
    `sch 10 para 6(2) the aptitude test may test the person's knowledge of the matter` `the matter is a subject covered by a recognised professional qualification` `the matter is a subject not covered by the professional qualification I already hold` `knowledge of the matter is essential for the pursuit of the profession of statutory auditor` `the matter is a rule of professional conduct`

-- sch 10 para 6(2B)
@export Under schedule 10 paragraph 6(2B), is the period that I have been asked to complete an adaptation period?
GIVEN `the length of the period in months` IS A NUMBER @desc How many months long is the period?
      `I would pursue the profession of statutory auditor under the supervision of an individual who holds an appropriate qualification` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Would you pursue the profession of statutory auditor during it under the supervision of an individual who holds an appropriate qualification?
      `my ability to pursue the profession in the United Kingdom would be assessed` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Would your ability to pursue the profession of statutory auditor in the United Kingdom be assessed?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under schedule 10 paragraph 6(2B), is the period that I have been asked to complete an adaptation period` IS
    `sch 10 para 6(2B) the period is an adaptation period` `the length of the period in months` `I would pursue the profession of statutory auditor under the supervision of an individual who holds an appropriate qualification` `my ability to pursue the profession in the United Kingdom would be assessed`

-- sch 10 para 6(3)
@export Under schedule 10 paragraph 6(3), may my firm, which has ceased to comply with the conditions for eligibility, be permitted to remain eligible for appointment as a statutory auditor?
GIVEN `my firm has ceased to comply with the conditions in paragraph 6(1)(b)` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has your firm ceased to comply with the conditions mentioned in paragraph 6(1)(b) (each responsible individual eligible; firm controlled by qualified persons)?
      `the date my firm ceased to comply` IS A DATE @desc On what date did your firm cease to comply?
      `the day I ask about` IS A DATE @desc For what day do you want to know whether your firm may remain eligible?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under schedule 10 paragraph 6(3), may my firm, which has ceased to comply with the conditions for eligibility, be permitted to remain eligible for appointment as a statutory auditor` IS
    `sch 10 para 6(3) the firm may be permitted to remain eligible for appointment as a statutory auditor` `my firm has ceased to comply with the conditions in paragraph 6(1)(b)` `the date my firm ceased to comply` `the day I ask about`

-- sch 10 para 8(4)
@export Under schedule 10 paragraph 8(4), am I a controller of a body corporate for the purposes of the fit and proper test for its auditors?
GIVEN `the fraction of the rights to vote at general meetings that I alone or with associates can exercise or control` IS A NUMBER @desc What fraction (for example 0.15 for 15 per cent) of the rights to vote on all, or substantially all, matters at general meetings of the body corporate, or of another body corporate of which it is a subsidiary, are you entitled to exercise or control, alone or with an associate or associates?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under schedule 10 paragraph 8(4), am I a controller of a body corporate for the purposes of the fit and proper test for its auditors` IS
    `sch 10 para 8(4) the person is a controller of the body corporate` TRUE `the fraction of the rights to vote at general meetings that I alone or with associates can exercise or control`

-- sch 10 para 9(1A)
@export Under schedule 10 paragraph 9(1A), must the rules of a recognised supervisory body bar my company's former auditor from being appointed to its board or management on this date?
GIVEN `my company is a public interest entity` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is your company a public interest entity (see the question on paragraph 20A(1))?
      `the person was appointed as statutory auditor of my company or is a key audit partner of the firm that was` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Was the person appointed as statutory auditor of your company, or a key audit partner of a firm which was?
      `the date the appointment as statutory auditor ended` IS A DATE @desc On what date did the appointment as statutory auditor end?
      `the date of the appointment to the board or management` IS A DATE @desc On what date would the person be appointed a director or other officer, or become concerned in the management of your company?
      `the competent authority has set a longer period in standards` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Have the standards set by the competent authority fixed a bar longer than the minimum?
      `the number of months set in those standards` IS A NUMBER @desc If so, how many months? (Any number if none.)
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under schedule 10 paragraph 9(1A), must the rules of a recognised supervisory body bar my company's former auditor from being appointed to its board or management on this date` IS
    `sch 10 para 9(1A) the rules of the body must bar the appointment` `my company is a public interest entity` `the person was appointed as statutory auditor of my company or is a key audit partner of the firm that was` `the date the appointment as statutory auditor ended` `the date of the appointment to the board or management` (IF `the competent authority has set a longer period in standards` THEN JUST `the number of months set in those standards` ELSE NOTHING)

-- sch 10 para 10C(3)
@export Under schedule 10 paragraph 10C(3), must the rules of a recognised supervisory body bar the former auditor of my public interest entity from being appointed to its board or management on this date?
GIVEN `my company is a public interest entity` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is your company a public interest entity?
      `the person was appointed as statutory auditor of my company or is a key audit partner of the firm that was` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Was the person appointed as statutory auditor of your company, or a key audit partner of a firm which was?
      `the date the appointment as statutory auditor ended` IS A DATE @desc On what date did the appointment as statutory auditor end?
      `the date of the appointment to the board or management` IS A DATE @desc On what date would the person be appointed a director or other officer, or become concerned in the management of your company?
      `the competent authority has set a longer period in standards` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Have the standards set by the competent authority fixed a bar longer than the minimum?
      `the number of months set in those standards` IS A NUMBER @desc If so, how many months? (Any number if none.)
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under schedule 10 paragraph 10C(3), must the rules of a recognised supervisory body bar the former auditor of my public interest entity from being appointed to its board or management on this date` IS
    `sch 10 para 10C(3) the rules of the body must bar the appointment` `my company is a public interest entity` `the person was appointed as statutory auditor of my company or is a key audit partner of the firm that was` `the date the appointment as statutory auditor ended` `the date of the appointment to the board or management` (IF `the competent authority has set a longer period in standards` THEN JUST `the number of months set in those standards` ELSE NOTHING)

-- sch 10 para 9(5)
@export Under schedule 10 paragraph 9(5), is the auditor of my company regarded as an officer of the company for the purposes of the bar on a former auditor joining its board or management?
GIVEN `I am asking about the auditor of the company` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the person you ask about an auditor of the audited company?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under schedule 10 paragraph 9(5), is the auditor of my company regarded as an officer of the company for the purposes of the bar on a former auditor joining its board or management` IS
    `sch 10 para 9(5) the auditor is regarded as an officer of the audited person for the purposes of sub-paragraph (1A)(a) and (b)` `I am asking about the auditor of the company`

-- sch 10 para 9(4)
@export Under schedule 10 paragraph 9(4), is a fine imposed on me by my former supervisory body for breach of its independence or confidentiality rules recoverable by it as a debt?
GIVEN `the fine was imposed in the enforcement of the independence or confidentiality rules` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Was the fine imposed in the enforcement of the rules about appointment as a director or officer of the audited person (paragraph 9(1A)) or about confidentiality (paragraph 9(3)(b))?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under schedule 10 paragraph 9(4), is a fine imposed on me by my former supervisory body for breach of its independence or confidentiality rules recoverable by it as a debt` IS
    `sch 10 para 9(4) the fine is recoverable by the body as a debt due to it from the person obliged to pay it` `the fine was imposed in the enforcement of the independence or confidentiality rules`

-- sch 10 para 12(6)
@export Under schedule 10 paragraph 12(6), must my identity be kept from the public when the body publishes the sanction it imposed on me?
GIVEN `I am an individual and the body considers publishing my personal data would be disproportionate` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are you an individual, and does the body consider that publishing your personal data would be disproportionate?
      `publication would jeopardise the stability of financial markets` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Would publication jeopardise the stability of financial markets?
      `publication would jeopardise an ongoing criminal investigation` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Would publication jeopardise an ongoing criminal investigation?
      `publication would cause disproportionate damage to an institution or individual involved` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Would publication cause disproportionate damage to any institution or individual involved?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under schedule 10 paragraph 12(6), must my identity be kept from the public when the body publishes the sanction it imposed on me` IS
    `sch 10 para 12(6) the identity of the person sanctioned must not be made available to the public` `I am an individual and the body considers publishing my personal data would be disproportionate` `publication would jeopardise the stability of financial markets` `publication would jeopardise an ongoing criminal investigation` `publication would cause disproportionate damage to an institution or individual involved`

-- sch 10 para 12(7), sch 10 para 12(8)
@export Under schedule 10 paragraph 12(7), must the body still be publishing the sanction imposed on me on this day?
GIVEN `I appealed against the sanction` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did you appeal against the sanction?
      `the appeal has been determined` IS A BOOLEAN @desc If you appealed: has the appeal been determined?
      `the date the appeal was determined` IS A DATE @desc If it has: on what date was it determined? (Any date if not.)
      `the date by which any appeal was required to be lodged` IS A DATE @desc On what date did any appeal have to be lodged by?
      `the day I ask about` IS A DATE @desc For what day do you want to know whether the information must be on the body's website?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under schedule 10 paragraph 12(7), must the body still be publishing the sanction imposed on me on this day` IS
    CONSIDER `sch 10 para 12(8) the relevant date` `I appealed against the sanction` (IF `the appeal has been determined` THEN JUST `the date the appeal was determined` ELSE NOTHING) `the date by which any appeal was required to be lodged`
        WHEN NOTHING THEN NOTHING
        WHEN JUST relevantdate THEN `sch 10 para 12(7) the information must be published on the website of the body on the day` relevantdate `the day I ask about`

-- sch 10 para 12(4)
@export Under schedule 10 paragraph 12(4), does the temporary prohibition imposed by my former supervisory body still apply to me although I am no longer a member?
GIVEN `the sanction is a temporary prohibition of up to three years on exercising specified functions in a firm or public interest entity` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the sanction a temporary prohibition of up to three years preventing you from exercising specified functions in a firm eligible for appointment as a statutory auditor or in a public interest entity?
      `I am no longer a member of the body` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are you no longer a member of the body?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under schedule 10 paragraph 12(4), does the temporary prohibition imposed by my former supervisory body still apply to me although I am no longer a member` IS
    `sch 10 para 12(4) the sanction applies to the person as it applies to members` `the sanction is a temporary prohibition of up to three years on exercising specified functions in a firm or public interest entity` `I am no longer a member of the body`

-- sch 10 para 13(3)(b)(ii)
@export Under schedule 10 paragraph 13(3)(b)(ii), is another inspection of me due by this day?
GIVEN `in the previous five years I carried out a statutory audit of an entity` IS A BOOLEAN @desc In any of the previous five years, did you carry out a statutory audit of an entity?
      `that entity is subject to the small companies regime` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Was that entity subject to the small companies regime (section 381)?
      `the date of my previous inspection` IS A DATE @desc On what date was your last inspection?
      `the day I ask about` IS A DATE @desc For what day do you want to know whether another inspection is due?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under schedule 10 paragraph 13(3)(b)(ii), is another inspection of me due by this day` IS
    `sch 10 para 13(3)(b)(ii) another inspection of the person is due by the day asked about` `in the previous five years I carried out a statutory audit of an entity` (JUST `that entity is subject to the small companies regime`) `the date of my previous inspection` `the day I ask about`

-- sch 10 para 13(5)
@export Under schedule 10 paragraph 13(5), may this person conduct the inspection of me?
GIVEN `the inspector has an appropriate professional education` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does the inspector have an appropriate professional education?
      `the inspector has experience of statutory audit work` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does the inspector have experience of statutory audit work?
      `the inspector has experience of equivalent work in an EEA State before IP completion day` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does the inspector have experience of equivalent work, for an appointment to conduct inspections made before IP completion day, on the audit of accounts under the law of an EEA State?
      `the inspector has experience of equivalent work in an equivalent or transitional third country` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does the inspector have experience of equivalent work on the audit of accounts under the law of an equivalent or transitional third country?
      `the inspector has received adequate training in the conduct of inspections` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has the inspector received adequate training in the conduct of inspections?
      `the inspector has declared no interest likely to conflict with the proper conduct of the inspection` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has the inspector declared that they have no interest likely to conflict with the proper conduct of the inspection?
      `the inspector was ever my employee, partner, member of my management body or otherwise associated with me` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Was the inspector ever your employee or partner, a member of your management body, or otherwise associated with you?
      `the date that association last existed` IS A DATE @desc If so, on what date did it last exist? (Any date if never.)
      `the date of the inspection` IS A DATE @desc On what date will the inspection take place?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under schedule 10 paragraph 13(5), may this person conduct the inspection of me` IS
    `sch 10 para 13(5) the inspector is a person by whom the inspection may be conducted` `the inspector has an appropriate professional education` `the inspector has experience of statutory audit work` `the inspector has experience of equivalent work in an EEA State before IP completion day` `the inspector has experience of equivalent work in an equivalent or transitional third country` `the inspector has received adequate training in the conduct of inspections` `the inspector has declared no interest likely to conflict with the proper conduct of the inspection` (IF `the inspector was ever my employee, partner, member of my management body or otherwise associated with me` THEN JUST `the date that association last existed` ELSE NOTHING) `the date of the inspection`

-- sch 10 para 13(10)
@export Under schedule 10 paragraph 13(10), may the inspection of my firm be treated as an inspection of me as an individual responsible for its audit work?
GIVEN `the inspection was conducted in relation to my firm` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Was the inspection conducted in relation to your firm?
      `my firm has a common quality assurance policy that each responsible individual must comply with` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does your firm have a common quality assurance policy with which each individual responsible for its statutory audit work is required to comply?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under schedule 10 paragraph 13(10), may the inspection of my firm be treated as an inspection of me as an individual responsible for its audit work` IS
    `sch 10 para 13(10) the inspection of the firm may be treated as an inspection of all individuals responsible` `the inspection was conducted in relation to my firm` `my firm has a common quality assurance policy that each responsible individual must comply with`

-- sch 10 para 16A(1), sch 10 para 16AA, sch 10 para 16AB
@export Under schedule 10 paragraph 16A, may I transfer audit working papers and investigation reports to a third country competent authority?
GIVEN `the transfer is to an approved third country competent authority` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the transfer to an approved third country competent authority?
      `the Secretary of State has approved the transfer` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has the Secretary of State approved the transfer?
      `the transfer is for the purposes of an investigation of an auditor or audit firm` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the transfer made for the purposes of an investigation of an auditor or audit firm?
      `the authority requested the papers for an investigation begun by itself or another authority in the same third country` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has the authority requested the papers for an investigation initiated by itself or by another third country competent authority established in the same third country?
      `the papers relate to audits of companies that issued securities in that country` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Do the papers relate to audits of companies that have issued securities in that third country?
      `the papers relate to audits of companies in a group issuing consolidated accounts in that country` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Do they relate to audits of companies that form part of a group issuing statutory consolidated accounts in that third country?
      `the authority asked me directly for the papers` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did the authority make the request directly to you as statutory auditor?
      `the authority gave the Secretary of State advance notice with reasons` IS A BOOLEAN @desc If so, did the authority give the Secretary of State advance notice of the request, with the reasons for it?
      `the authority has entered into arrangements with the Secretary of State under section 1253E` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has the authority entered into arrangements with the Secretary of State in accordance with section 1253E?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under schedule 10 paragraph 16A, may I transfer audit working papers and investigation reports to a third country competent authority` IS
    `sch 10 para 16A(1) the person may transfer audit working papers and investigation reports to the third country competent authority`
        (`sch 10 para 16AA the requirements of this paragraph are met` `the transfer is to an approved third country competent authority` `the Secretary of State has approved the transfer`)
        (`sch 10 para 16AB the requirements of this paragraph are met` `the transfer is for the purposes of an investigation of an auditor or audit firm` `the authority requested the papers for an investigation begun by itself or another authority in the same third country` `the papers relate to audits of companies that issued securities in that country` `the papers relate to audits of companies in a group issuing consolidated accounts in that country` `the authority asked me directly for the papers` `the authority gave the Secretary of State advance notice with reasons` (JUST `the authority has entered into arrangements with the Secretary of State under section 1253E`))

-- sch 10 para 16A(2)
@export Under schedule 10 paragraph 16A(2), must I refuse to transfer audit working papers and investigation reports to a third country competent authority?
GIVEN `the Secretary of State has directed under section 1253E(6) that the transfer should not take place` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has the Secretary of State directed, under section 1253E(6), that the transfer should not take place?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under schedule 10 paragraph 16A(2), must I refuse to transfer audit working papers and investigation reports to a third country competent authority` IS
    `sch 10 para 16A(2) the person must refuse to transfer audit working papers and investigation reports to the third country competent authority` (JUST `the Secretary of State has directed under section 1253E(6) that the transfer should not take place`)

-- sch 10 para 17(2)
@export Under schedule 10 paragraph 17, am I able to meet claims against me arising out of my statutory audit work?
GIVEN `I have professional indemnity insurance` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Do you have professional indemnity insurance?
      `I have other arrangements that are appropriate` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Do you have other arrangements that are appropriate to meet such claims?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under schedule 10 paragraph 17, am I able to meet claims against me arising out of my statutory audit work` IS
    `sch 10 para 17(2) the person is able to meet claims arising out of statutory audit work` `I have professional indemnity insurance` `I have other arrangements that are appropriate`

-- sch 10 para 20A(1)
@export Under schedule 10 paragraph 20A(1), is my company a public interest entity?
GIVEN `my company is an issuer whose transferable securities are admitted to trading on a UK regulated market` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is your company an issuer whose transferable securities are admitted to trading on a UK regulated market?
      `my company is a CRR firm that is a credit institution` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is your company a credit institution within the meaning given by Article 4(1)(1) of Regulation (EU) No. 575/2013 which is a CRR firm within the meaning of Article 4(1)(2A) of that Regulation?
      `my company would be an insurance undertaking under the 1991 Directive were the United Kingdom a member State` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Would your company be an insurance undertaking as defined in Article 2(1) of Council Directive 91/674/EEC (as it had effect immediately before IP completion day) were the United Kingdom a member State?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under schedule 10 paragraph 20A(1), is my company a public interest entity` IS
    `sch 10 para 20A(1) the person is a public interest entity` `my company is an issuer whose transferable securities are admitted to trading on a UK regulated market` `my company is a CRR firm that is a credit institution` `my company would be an insurance undertaking under the 1991 Directive were the United Kingdom a member State`

-- sch 10 para 20A(1)
@export Under schedule 10 paragraph 20A(1), am I a key audit partner?
GIVEN `I am eligible for appointment as a statutory auditor` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are you an individual eligible for appointment as a statutory auditor?
      `I am designated by an audit firm as primarily responsible for a particular audit engagement` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are you designated by an audit firm for a particular audit engagement as primarily responsible for carrying out the statutory audit on behalf of the firm?
      `the audit is a group audit` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it a group audit?
      `I am designated as primarily responsible for the audit of the consolidated accounts of the group` IS A BOOLEAN @desc If so, are you designated as primarily responsible for the statutory audit of the consolidated accounts of the group on behalf of the audit firm?
      `I am designated as primarily responsible for the audit of a material subsidiary undertaking` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are you eligible to conduct the audit of the accounts of a material subsidiary undertaking and designated as primarily responsible for that audit?
      `I sign the audit report` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Do you sign the audit report?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under schedule 10 paragraph 20A(1), am I a key audit partner` IS
    `sch 10 para 20A(1) the individual is a key audit partner` `I am eligible for appointment as a statutory auditor` `I am designated by an audit firm as primarily responsible for a particular audit engagement` `the audit is a group audit` `I am designated as primarily responsible for the audit of the consolidated accounts of the group` `I am designated as primarily responsible for the audit of a material subsidiary undertaking` `I sign the audit report`


§ `Schedule 11 -- Recognised professional qualifications (for the person who holds, or wants, one)`

§§ `Part 1 and Part 2 -- Representations on revocation, and who may sit and be awarded a recognised qualification`

-- sch 11 para 3(5), sch 11 para 3(6)
@export Under schedule 11 paragraph 3(5), as a holder of or student for a recognised professional qualification, may I still make representations on the proposed revocation of its recognition?
GIVEN `I hold the qualification or am in the course of studying for it` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Do you hold the qualification, or are you in the course of studying for it?
      `the Secretary of State considers that I am affected` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does it appear to the Secretary of State that you are affected by the proposed revocation?
      `the date the notice of the proposed revocation was served on me or published` IS A DATE @desc On what date was the notice of the proposed revocation served on you, or published?
      `the day I want to make representations` IS A DATE @desc On what day do you want to make your representations?
      `the Secretary of State has allowed a longer period` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has the Secretary of State allowed a period longer than three months for representations?
      `the last day of that longer period` IS A DATE @desc If so, what is the last day of the longer period? (Any date if there is none.)
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under schedule 11 paragraph 3(5), as a holder of or student for a recognised professional qualification, may I still make representations on the proposed revocation of its recognition` IS
    `sch 11 para 3(5) the person may make written and oral representations`
        (`sch 11 para 3(6) the person is within this sub-paragraph` FALSE `I hold the qualification or am in the course of studying for it` `the Secretary of State considers that I am affected`)
        `the date the notice of the proposed revocation was served on me or published`
        `the day I want to make representations`
        (IF `the Secretary of State has allowed a longer period` THEN JUST `the last day of that longer period` ELSE NOTHING)

-- sch 11 para 6(1), sch 11 para 6(2), sch 11 para 6(4)
@export Under schedule 11 paragraph 6, may the qualification be open to me?
GIVEN `I have been admitted to a university or similar establishment in the United Kingdom` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Have you been admitted to a university or similar establishment in the United Kingdom?
      `my United Kingdom qualifications are recognised by the Secretary of State as of an appropriate standard for university entry` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is your education of a standard to be considered for admission on the basis of academic or professional qualifications obtained in the United Kingdom and recognised by the Secretary of State as of an appropriate standard?
      `my qualifications obtained outside the United Kingdom are considered equivalent` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it of such a standard on the basis of qualifications obtained outside the United Kingdom which the Secretary of State considers equivalent?
      `I have been assessed by written tests as of university entrance standard` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Have you been assessed, on the basis of written tests of a kind the Secretary of State considers adequate, as of the standard of ability that would entitle you to be considered for admission to a university?
      `my years of experience in a professional capacity in finance, law and accountancy` IS A NUMBER @desc How many years of experience in a professional capacity in the fields of finance, law and accountancy do you have?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under schedule 11 paragraph 6, may the qualification be open to me` IS
    `sch 11 para 6(1) the qualification may be open to the person`
        (`sch 11 para 6(2) the person has attained university entrance level` `I have been admitted to a university or similar establishment in the United Kingdom` `my United Kingdom qualifications are recognised by the Secretary of State as of an appropriate standard for university entry` `my qualifications obtained outside the United Kingdom are considered equivalent` `I have been assessed by written tests as of university entrance standard`)
        (`sch 11 para 6(4) the person has a sufficient period of professional experience` `my years of experience in a professional capacity in finance, law and accountancy`)

-- sch 11 para 7
@export Under schedule 11 paragraph 7, may the qualification be restricted to me because of my course of theoretical instruction or my professional experience?
GIVEN `I have completed a course of theoretical instruction in the prescribed subjects` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Have you completed a course of theoretical instruction in the subjects prescribed for the purposes of paragraph 8?
      `my years of experience in a professional capacity in finance, law and accountancy` IS A NUMBER @desc How many years of experience in a professional capacity in finance, law and accountancy do you have?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under schedule 11 paragraph 7, may the qualification be restricted to me because of my course of theoretical instruction or my professional experience` IS
    `sch 11 para 7 the qualification may be restricted to the person` `I have completed a course of theoretical instruction in the prescribed subjects` `my years of experience in a professional capacity in finance, law and accountancy`

-- sch 11 para 8(1), sch 11 para 8(2), sch 11 para 8(3)
@export Under schedule 11 paragraph 8, is the examination that I have passed of the kind that the qualification must require, allowing for sub-paragraphs (2) and (3)?
GIVEN `the examination I passed is at least in part in writing` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Was the examination you passed at least in part in writing?
      `it tested my theoretical knowledge of the prescribed subjects` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did it test your theoretical knowledge of the subjects prescribed for the purposes of paragraph 8?
      `I passed a university or other examination of equivalent standard in a subject, or hold a degree in it` IS A BOOLEAN @desc For a subject it did not test: have you passed a university or other examination of equivalent standard in that subject, or do you hold a university degree or equivalent qualification in it?
      `it tested my ability to apply that knowledge in practice` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did it test your ability to apply that knowledge in practice?
      `I received practical training attested by a recognised examination or diploma` IS A BOOLEAN @desc If not: did you receive practical training in the subject which is attested by an examination or diploma recognised by the Secretary of State?
      `it required a standard of attainment at least equivalent to a United Kingdom degree` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did it require a standard of attainment at least equivalent to that required to obtain a degree from a university or similar establishment in the United Kingdom?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under schedule 11 paragraph 8, is the examination that I have passed of the kind that the qualification must require, allowing for sub-paragraphs (2) and (3)` IS
    `sch 11 para 8(1) the examination is of the kind the qualification must require`
        `the examination I passed is at least in part in writing`
        (`it tested my theoretical knowledge of the prescribed subjects` OR (`sch 11 para 8(2) the qualification may be awarded without the theoretical knowledge of the subject being tested by examination` `I passed a university or other examination of equivalent standard in a subject, or hold a degree in it` `I passed a university or other examination of equivalent standard in a subject, or hold a degree in it` EQUALS JUST TRUE))
        (`it tested my ability to apply that knowledge in practice` OR (`sch 11 para 8(3) the qualification may be awarded without the ability to apply the theoretical knowledge of the subject in practice being tested by examination` `I received practical training attested by a recognised examination or diploma` EQUALS JUST TRUE))
        `it required a standard of attainment at least equivalent to a United Kingdom degree`

-- sch 11 para 9(1), sch 11 para 9(4)
@export Under schedule 11 paragraph 9, does my practical training meet the requirements of sub-paragraphs (1) and (4) (three years, audit work, and two-thirds given by eligible persons)?
GIVEN `the months of practical training I have completed` IS A NUMBER @desc How many months of practical training have you completed?
      `part of it was training in statutory audit work` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Was part of it spent being trained in statutory audit work?
      `a substantial part was training in statutory audit work or similar audit work` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Was a substantial part spent being trained in statutory audit work or other audit work approved by the Secretary of State as similar?
      `the months given by a person eligible for appointment as a statutory auditor` IS A NUMBER @desc How many months of the training were given by a person eligible for appointment as a statutory auditor?
      `the months given by a person eligible for a corresponding appointment outside the United Kingdom who meets the conditions in paragraph 9(4A)` IS A NUMBER @desc How many months were given by a person eligible for a corresponding appointment as an auditor outside the United Kingdom who meets the conditions in paragraph 9(4A)?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under schedule 11 paragraph 9, does my practical training meet the requirements of sub-paragraphs (1) and (4) (three years, audit work, and two-thirds given by eligible persons)` IS
    CONSIDER `sch 11 para 9(1) the practical training meets the requirement` `the months of practical training I have completed` `part of it was training in statutory audit work` `a substantial part was training in statutory audit work or similar audit work`
        WHEN JUST FALSE THEN JUST FALSE
        WHEN NOTHING THEN NOTHING
        WHEN JUST TRUE THEN `sch 11 para 9(4) at least two-thirds of the training is given by a person of the kind required` `the months given by a person eligible for appointment as a statutory auditor` `the months given by a person eligible for a corresponding appointment outside the United Kingdom who meets the conditions in paragraph 9(4A)` `the months of practical training I have completed`

-- sch 11 para 10(1)
@export Under schedule 11 paragraph 10(1), how many years of professional experience are required of me once my theoretical instruction is deducted?
GIVEN `the years of theoretical instruction in finance, law and accountancy I have had` IS A NUMBER @desc How many years of theoretical instruction in the fields of finance, law and accountancy have you had?
      `the instruction lasted at least one year` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did the instruction last at least one year?
      `the instruction is attested by an examination recognised by the Secretary of State` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the instruction attested by an examination recognised by the Secretary of State for these purposes?
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `Under schedule 11 paragraph 10(1), how many years of professional experience are required of me once my theoretical instruction is deducted` IS
    `sch 11 para 10(1) the years of professional experience required after the deduction` `the years of theoretical instruction in finance, law and accountancy I have had` `the instruction lasted at least one year` `the instruction is attested by an examination recognised by the Secretary of State`


§ `Schedule 11A -- Disclosure of information obtained under Part 42 (for a person who holds such information and wonders whom it may be given to)`

§§ `Parts 1 to 3 -- Specified persons, specified descriptions of disclosures, overseas bodies`

-- sch 11A part 1
@export Under schedule 11A paragraphs 1 to 17D, is the person I want to disclose the information to a specified person?
GIVEN `the person I want to disclose the information to` IS A `sch 11A part 1 specified person` @desc Which of the specified persons in Part 1 of Schedule 11A (paragraphs 1 to 17D) is the person you want to disclose to? Choose the paragraph; choose "a person that no paragraph names" if none fits.
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under schedule 11A paragraphs 1 to 17D, is the person I want to disclose the information to a specified person` IS
    `sch 11A part 1 the person is a specified person` `the person I want to disclose the information to`

-- sch 11A part 2
@export Under schedule 11A paragraphs 18 to 78, is my disclosure of the information one of the specified descriptions of disclosure?
GIVEN `the purpose and recipient of my disclosure` IS A `sch 11A part 2 specified description` @desc Which of the specified descriptions in Part 2 of Schedule 11A (paragraphs 18 to 78) fits your disclosure? Choose the paragraph; choose "a purpose that no paragraph names" if none fits.
      `the information I would make available identifies an audited person` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does the information you would make available identify any audited person? (This matters only for paragraph 62, public information about inspections.)
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under schedule 11A paragraphs 18 to 78, is my disclosure of the information one of the specified descriptions of disclosure` IS
    `sch 11A part 2 the disclosure is of a specified description` `the purpose and recipient of my disclosure` `the information I would make available identifies an audited person`

-- sch 11A para 79
@export Under schedule 11A paragraph 79, is my disclosure to an approved third country competent authority made in accordance with Part 3 of the Schedule?
GIVEN `I am disclosing to an approved third country competent authority` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are you disclosing to an approved third country competent authority?
      `the authority has made a request in accordance with section 1253B` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the disclosure made in accordance with section 1253B (requests from approved third country competent authorities)?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under schedule 11A paragraph 79, is my disclosure to an approved third country competent authority made in accordance with Part 3 of the Schedule` IS
    `sch 11A para 79 the disclosure is made in accordance with this Part of this Schedule` `I am disclosing to an approved third country competent authority` (JUST `the authority has made a request in accordance with section 1253B`)

-- sch 11A para 80
@export Under schedule 11A paragraph 80, is my disclosure to a third country competent authority made in accordance with Part 3 of the Schedule?
GIVEN `my disclosure is a transfer of audit working papers and investigation reports` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is your disclosure a transfer of audit working papers and investigation reports to a third country competent authority?
      `the transfer is in accordance with the rules imposed under paragraph 16A of Schedule 10` IS A BOOLEAN @desc If so, is it in accordance with the rules imposed under paragraph 16A of Schedule 10?
      `my disclosure is made to enable or assist the authority to exercise its functions` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the disclosure made to a third country competent authority for the purpose of enabling or assisting the authority to exercise its functions?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under schedule 11A paragraph 80, is my disclosure to a third country competent authority made in accordance with Part 3 of the Schedule` IS
    `sch 11A para 80 the disclosure is made in accordance with this Part of this Schedule` `my disclosure is a transfer of audit working papers and investigation reports` `the transfer is in accordance with the rules imposed under paragraph 16A of Schedule 10` `my disclosure is made to enable or assist the authority to exercise its functions`


§ `Schedule 12 -- Registered third country auditors (for a registered third country auditor)`

§§ `Funding, hearings and the choice of arrangements`

-- sch 12 para 4
@export Under schedule 12 paragraph 4, have I paid the costs of the monitoring and disciplinary arrangements that the arrangements provide I am to pay?
GIVEN `the arrangements are within paragraph 1 or 2 of Schedule 12` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are the arrangements arrangements for independent monitoring (paragraph 1) or for independent disciplinary investigations (paragraph 2)?
      `I am obliged to participate in the arrangements` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are you obliged to participate in them (section 1242)?
      `the arrangements provide that I am to pay those costs` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Do the arrangements provide that these costs are to be paid by you?
      `I have paid those costs` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Have you paid them?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under schedule 12 paragraph 4, have I paid the costs of the monitoring and disciplinary arrangements that the arrangements provide I am to pay` IS
    `sch 12 para 4 the registered third country auditor has paid the costs it must pay` `the arrangements are within paragraph 1 or 2 of Schedule 12` `I am obliged to participate in the arrangements` `the arrangements provide that I am to pay those costs` `I have paid those costs`

-- sch 12 para 2(1A)
@export Under schedule 12 paragraph 2(1A), may a decision on disciplinary action against me be made without a hearing because I agree in writing?
GIVEN `I agree in writing that a hearing need not be held` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Have you agreed in writing that a disciplinary hearing need not be held?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under schedule 12 paragraph 2(1A), may a decision on disciplinary action against me be made without a hearing because I agree in writing` IS
    `sch 12 para 2(1A) decisions to take disciplinary action may be made without a disciplinary hearing` `I agree in writing that a hearing need not be held`

-- sch 12 para 6(1)
@export Under schedule 12 paragraph 6(1), am I obliged to participate in this set of arrangements when there are two or more?
GIVEN `there are two or more sets of arrangements of the same kind` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are there two or more sets of arrangements within paragraph 1, or within paragraph 2?
      `the Secretary of State has specified a set by order` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has the Secretary of State specified a set by order?
      `this set is the one the Secretary of State specified` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is this the set the Secretary of State specified?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under schedule 12 paragraph 6(1), am I obliged to participate in this set of arrangements when there are two or more` IS
    `sch 12 para 6(1) the registered third country auditor is obliged to participate in the set of arrangements` `there are two or more sets of arrangements of the same kind` `the Secretary of State has specified a set by order` `this set is the one the Secretary of State specified`


§ `Schedule 13 -- The body to which the Secretary of State's functions are delegated (for a member, an employee, or a person affected by its instruments)`

§§ `Status, pay, instruments and appointment of its auditor`

-- sch 13 para 2
@export Under schedule 13 paragraph 2, am I, as a member, officer or employee of the body designated by a delegation order, to be regarded as a Crown servant?
GIVEN `I am a member, officer or employee of the body` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are you a member, officer or employee of the body designated by the delegation order?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under schedule 13 paragraph 2, am I, as a member, officer or employee of the body designated by a delegation order, to be regarded as a Crown servant` IS
    `sch 13 para 2 the person is regarded as acting on behalf of the Crown or as a Crown servant` FALSE `I am a member, officer or employee of the body`

-- sch 13 para 4(3)
@export Under schedule 13 paragraph 4(3), has the body paid me the compensation that it must pay for ceasing to be a member before the end of my term?
GIVEN `I ceased to be a member of the body before the end of my term of office` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did you cease to be a member of the body otherwise than on the expiry of your term of office?
      `it appears to the Secretary of State that there are special circumstances making compensation right` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does it appear to the Secretary of State that there are special circumstances which make it right for you to receive compensation?
      `the Secretary of State has determined an amount` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has the Secretary of State determined the amount of compensation?
      `the amount the Secretary of State determined` IS A NUMBER @desc What amount did the Secretary of State determine? (Any number if none.)
      `the amount the body has paid me` IS A NUMBER @desc How much has the body paid you?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under schedule 13 paragraph 4(3), has the body paid me the compensation that it must pay for ceasing to be a member before the end of my term` IS
    `sch 13 para 4(3) the body has paid the compensation it must pay` `I ceased to be a member of the body before the end of my term of office` `it appears to the Secretary of State that there are special circumstances making compensation right` (IF `the Secretary of State has determined an amount` THEN JUST `the amount the Secretary of State determined` ELSE NOTHING) `the amount the body has paid me`

-- sch 13 para 8(2)
@export Under schedule 13 paragraph 8(2), does the fact that an instrument of the body had not been made available give me a defence to an alleged contravention of it?
GIVEN `I can show that when the alleged contravention happened the instrument had not been made available as required` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Can you show that, at the time of the alleged contravention, the instrument containing the regulation or order had not been made available to the public as paragraph 8 requires?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under schedule 13 paragraph 8(2), does the fact that an instrument of the body had not been made available give me a defence to an alleged contravention of it` IS
    `sch 13 para 8(2) this paragraph gives a defence to the alleged contravention` `I can show that when the alleged contravention happened the instrument had not been made available as required`

-- sch 13 para 9(3)
@export Under schedule 13 paragraph 9(3), may I require the body to cause a copy of its instrument to be endorsed with a certificate for use in legal proceedings?
GIVEN `I wish to cite an instrument made by the body in legal proceedings` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Do you wish, in legal proceedings, to cite an instrument made by the body?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under schedule 13 paragraph 9(3), may I require the body to cause a copy of its instrument to be endorsed with a certificate for use in legal proceedings` IS
    `sch 13 para 9(3) the person may require the body to cause a copy of the instrument to be endorsed with a certificate` `I wish to cite an instrument made by the body in legal proceedings`

-- sch 13 para 10(6)
@export Under schedule 13 paragraph 10(6), may I be appointed as auditor of the body?
GIVEN `the body was established by the delegation order` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Was the body established by the delegation order?
      `I am eligible for appointment as a local auditor` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are you eligible for appointment as a local auditor?
      `I am eligible for appointment as a statutory auditor under this Part` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are you eligible for appointment as a statutory auditor in accordance with this Part of the Act (apart from its application by Schedule 5 to the Local Audit and Accountability Act 2014)?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under schedule 13 paragraph 10(6), may I be appointed as auditor of the body` IS
    `sch 13 para 10(6) the person may be appointed as auditor of the body` `the body was established by the delegation order` `I am eligible for appointment as a local auditor` `I am eligible for appointment as a statutory auditor under this Part`
